window.VOCAB_DATA = {"1":[["a/an","a(art.)一個、每一\nan(art.)一個(用於母音開頭的字前)\na lot of 許多\nan hour 一小時\nI have a dog and a cat.\n(我有一隻狗和一隻貓。)\nShe eats an apple every day.\n(她每天吃一顆蘋果。)"],["ability","ability(n.)能力、才能\nable(adj.)能夠的\nunable(adj.)不能的\nability to learn 學習能力\nnatural ability 天賦\nShe has the ability to speak three languages.\n(她有說三種語言的能力。)\nReading improves your ability to think.\n(閱讀能提升你的思考能力。)"],["able","able(adj.)能夠的、有能力的\nability(n.)能力\nunable(adj.)不能的\nbe able to 能夠\nable student 能幹的學生\nI am able to swim now.\n(我現在會游泳了。)\nWill you be able to come tomorrow?\n(你明天能來嗎？)"],["about","about(prep./adv.)關於、大約、到處\n(無詞性變化)\ntalk about 談論\nabout ten minutes 大約十分鐘\nThis book is about a brave girl.\n(這本書是關於一個勇敢的女孩。)\nIt takes about ten minutes to walk there.\n(走路到那裡大約要十分鐘。)"],["above","above(prep./adv./adj.)在……上方、超過、上述的\n(無詞性變化)\nabove all 最重要的是\nabove average 高於平均\nThe bird is flying above the tree.\n(鳥在樹的上方飛。)\nHis grades are above average.\n(他的成績高於平均。)"],["abroad","abroad(adv.)在國外、到國外\n(無詞性變化)\nstudy abroad 出國留學\ntravel abroad 出國旅行\nMy sister wants to study abroad.\n(我姊姊想出國留學。)\nWe travel abroad every summer.\n(我們每年夏天都出國旅行。)"],["across","across(prep./adv.)橫越、在對面\ncross(v.)越過\nacross the street 在街道對面\ncome across 偶然遇到\nThe bank is across the street.\n(銀行在街道對面。)\nWe walked across the bridge.\n(我們走過那座橋。)"],["act","act(n./v.)行為、法案、行動、表演\naction(n.)行動\nactive(adj.)活躍的\nactor(n.)演員\nact quickly 迅速行動\nan act of kindness 善舉\nWe must act now to save the earth.\n(我們必須現在就行動來拯救地球。)\nHe acts in a school play.\n(他在學校的話劇中演出。)"],["action","action(n.)行動、動作\nact(v.)行動\nactive(adj.)活躍的\ntake action 採取行動\naction movie 動作片\nIt is time to take action.\n(是時候採取行動了。)\nI love watching action movies.\n(我很愛看動作片。)"],["actor/actress","actor(n.)演員、男演員\nactress(n.)女演員\nact(v.)表演\nfamous actor 知名演員\nbest actress 最佳女主角\nThe actor is very popular in Taiwan.\n(這位演員在台灣很受歡迎。)\nShe wants to be an actress.\n(她想當一名女演員。)"],["add","add(v.)增加、加上、補充說\naddition(n.)加法、增加\nadd up 加總\nadd salt 加鹽\nPlease add some sugar to my tea.\n(請在我的茶裡加點糖。)\nIf you add two and three, you get five.\n(二加三等於五。)"],["afraid","afraid(adj.)害怕的、恐怕\n(無詞性變化)\nbe afraid of 害怕……\nI'm afraid 恐怕\nMy little brother is afraid of dogs.\n(我弟弟很怕狗。)\nI'm afraid I can't go with you.\n(恐怕我不能跟你去。)"],["after","after(prep./conj./adv.)在……之後\nafterward(adv.)之後\nafter school 放學後\nlook after 照顧\nLet's play basketball after school.\n(我們放學後去打籃球吧。)\nShe looks after her grandma every day.\n(她每天照顧她的奶奶。)"],["afternoon","afternoon(n.)下午\n(無詞性變化)\nin the afternoon 在下午\nthis afternoon 今天下午\nWe have a math test this afternoon.\n(我們今天下午有數學考試。)\nHe takes a nap in the afternoon.\n(他下午會睡個午覺。)"],["again","again(adv.)再一次、又\n(無詞性變化)\nagain and again 一再地\nonce again 再一次\nPlease say it again.\n(請再說一次。)\nI hope to see you again soon.\n(希望很快能再見到你。)"],["age","age(n./v.)年齡、時代、變老\naged(adj.)年老的、……歲的\nat the age of 在……歲時\nfor ages 很久\nHe started playing piano at the age of five.\n(他五歲時開始彈鋼琴。)\nWe are the same age.\n(我們同年紀。)"],["ago","ago(adv.)以前\n(無詞性變化)\nlong ago 很久以前\ntwo years ago 兩年前\nI moved to Taipei two years ago.\n(我兩年前搬到台北。)\nLong ago, people lived in caves.\n(很久以前，人們住在洞穴裡。)"],["agree(ment)","agree(v.)同意、agreement(n.)協議、同意\ndisagree(v.)不同意\nagree with 同意(某人)\nreach an agreement 達成協議\nI agree with you.\n(我同意你的看法。)\nThe two sides finally reached an agreement.\n(雙方終於達成協議。)"],["air","air(n.)空氣、天空\n(無詞性變化)\nfresh air 新鮮空氣\nby air 搭飛機\nLet's go outside for some fresh air.\n(我們去外面呼吸新鮮空氣吧。)\nThe air in the city is not clean.\n(城市裡的空氣不乾淨。)"],["airplane/plane","airplane(n.)飛機\nplane(n.)飛機\ntake a plane 搭飛機\npaper airplane 紙飛機\nThe airplane is taking off now.\n(飛機現在正在起飛。)\nWe took a plane to Japan.\n(我們搭飛機去日本。)"],["airport","airport(n.)機場\n(無詞性變化)\nat the airport 在機場\nairport bus 機場巴士\nMy dad will pick me up at the airport.\n(我爸爸會到機場接我。)\nThe airport is very busy today.\n(機場今天非常忙碌。)"],["all","all(adj./adv./pron./n.)全部、所有、完全\n(無詞性變化)\nall day 整天\nafter all 畢竟\nAll my friends came to the party.\n(我所有的朋友都來參加派對了。)\nIt rained all day.\n(下了一整天的雨。)"],["allow","allow(v.)允許、准許\nallowance(n.)零用錢、津貼\nallow sb. to 允許某人做……\nnot allowed 不准\nMy mom allows me to play games on weekends.\n(我媽媽允許我週末打電動。)\nSmoking is not allowed here.\n(這裡禁止吸菸。)"],["almost","almost(adv.)幾乎、差不多\n(無詞性變化)\nalmost all 幾乎全部\nalmost never 幾乎從不\nI almost missed the bus.\n(我差點錯過公車。)\nDinner is almost ready.\n(晚餐快準備好了。)"],["along","along(prep./adv.)沿著、一起\n(無詞性變化)\nalong the river 沿著河\nget along with 與……相處\nWe walked along the beach.\n(我們沿著海灘散步。)\nShe gets along with her classmates.\n(她和同學相處融洽。)"],["already","already(adv.)已經\n(無詞性變化)\nalready done 已經完成\nalready late 已經遲了\nI have already finished my homework.\n(我已經寫完功課了。)\nIt is already ten o'clock.\n(已經十點了。)"],["also","also(adv.)也、而且\n(無詞性變化)\nnot only... but also 不但……而且\nalso known as 又稱為\nI like music, and I also like sports.\n(我喜歡音樂，也喜歡運動。)\nShe is also a good singer.\n(她也是個很棒的歌手。)"],["although","although(conj.)雖然、儘管\n(無詞性變化)\nalthough it rained 雖然下了雨\nalthough tired 雖然累\nAlthough it was cold, we went swimming.\n(雖然天氣冷，我們還是去游泳了。)\nAlthough he is young, he is very smart.\n(雖然他年紀小，但他非常聰明。)"],["always","always(adv.)總是、一直\n(無詞性變化)\nas always 一如往常\nalways remember 永遠記得\nShe always gets up early.\n(她總是很早起床。)\nI will always remember you.\n(我會永遠記得你。)"],["am/a.m.","am(adv.)上午、午前\nAM(adv.)上午(也寫作 a.m.)\nat 7 a.m. 在上午七點\na.m. and p.m. 上午和下午\nSchool starts at 8 a.m.\n(學校早上八點開始上課。)\nI woke up at 6 a.m. today.\n(我今天早上六點起床。)"],["and","and(conj.)和、而且、然後\n(無詞性變化)\nand so on 等等\nboth A and B A 和 B 兩者\nI bought bread and milk.\n(我買了麵包和牛奶。)\nHe came home and took a shower.\n(他回到家然後洗了澡。)"],["angry","angry(adj.)生氣的\nanger(n.)憤怒\nangrily(adv.)生氣地\nget angry 生氣\nbe angry with 對某人生氣\nMy mom got angry because I was late.\n(因為我遲到，媽媽生氣了。)\nDon't be angry with me.\n(別生我的氣。)"],["animal","animal(n.)動物\n(無詞性變化)\nwild animal 野生動物\nfarm animal 家畜\nThe zoo has many animals.\n(動物園裡有很多動物。)\nDogs are my favorite animals.\n(狗是我最喜歡的動物。)"],["another","another(adj./pron.)另一個、再一個\n(無詞性變化)\none another 彼此\nanother day 改天\nCan I have another cookie?\n(我可以再吃一塊餅乾嗎？)\nLet's talk about it another day.\n(我們改天再談吧。)"],["answer","answer(n./v.)答案、回答、接(電話)\n(無詞性變化)\nanswer the phone 接電話\nthe right answer 正確答案\nCan you answer this question?\n(你能回答這個問題嗎？)\nPlease answer the phone for me.\n(請幫我接電話。)"],["ant","ant(n.)螞蟻\n(無詞性變化)\nred ant 紅螞蟻\na line of ants 一排螞蟻\nThere are ants on the cake!\n(蛋糕上有螞蟻！)\nAnts work very hard together.\n(螞蟻們一起努力工作。)"],["any","any(pron./adj./adv.)任何、一些\n(無詞性變化)\nany time 任何時候\nany more 再也(不)\nDo you have any questions?\n(你有任何問題嗎？)\nYou can call me any time.\n(你隨時可以打給我。)"],["anybody/anyone","anybody(pron.)任何人\nanyone(pron.)任何人\nanyone else 其他任何人\nanybody here 這裡有人\nIs anybody home?\n(有人在家嗎？)\nDon't tell anyone my secret.\n(別把我的祕密告訴任何人。)"],["anything","anything(pron.)任何事物\n(無詞性變化)\nanything else 其他任何東西\nanything but 絕不\nDo you need anything else?\n(你還需要什麼嗎？)\nI didn't eat anything this morning.\n(我今天早上什麼都沒吃。)"],["apartment","apartment(n.)公寓\n(無詞性變化)\nrent an apartment 租公寓\napartment building 公寓大樓\nWe live in a small apartment.\n(我們住在一間小公寓裡。)\nHe rented an apartment near school.\n(他在學校附近租了一間公寓。)"],["appear","appear(v.)出現、似乎\nappearance(n.)出現、外表\ndisappear(v.)消失\nappear on TV 上電視\nappear to be 似乎是\nA rainbow appeared after the rain.\n(雨後出現了一道彩虹。)\nShe appears to be very tired.\n(她看起來非常累。)"],["apple","apple(n.)蘋果\n(無詞性變化)\napple juice 蘋果汁\napple pie 蘋果派\nAn apple a day keeps the doctor away.\n(一天一蘋果，醫生遠離我。)\nI drink apple juice every morning.\n(我每天早上喝蘋果汁。)"],["area","area(n.)地區、區域、領域\n(無詞性變化)\nrural area 鄉村地區\nparking area 停車區\nThere are many shops in this area.\n(這個地區有很多商店。)\nPlease wait in the waiting area.\n(請在等候區等待。)"],["arm","arm(n./v.)手臂、武裝\narmy(n.)軍隊\narmed(adj.)武裝的\narm in arm 手挽著手\nbreak an arm 摔斷手臂\nHe broke his arm playing soccer.\n(他踢足球時摔斷了手臂。)\nThey walked arm in arm.\n(他們手挽著手走路。)"],["around","around(prep./adv.)在周圍、大約、到處\n(無詞性變化)\naround the world 全世界\nlook around 四處看看\nWe sat around the table.\n(我們圍著桌子坐。)\nHe traveled around the world.\n(他環遊了世界。)"],["arrive","arrive(v.)到達、抵達\narrival(n.)到達\narrive at/in 抵達(某地)\narrive on time 準時到達\nWe arrived at school at seven.\n(我們七點到達學校。)\nThe train arrived on time.\n(火車準時抵達。)"],["art","art(n.)藝術、美術、技巧\nartist(n.)藝術家\nartistic(adj.)藝術的\nwork of art 藝術品\nart class 美術課\nArt is my favorite subject.\n(美術是我最喜歡的科目。)\nThis painting is a great work of art.\n(這幅畫是一件偉大的藝術品。)"],["as","as(conj./adv./prep.)當……時、因為、像……一樣、作為\n(無詞性變化)\nas... as 和……一樣\nas soon as 一……就\nHe is as tall as his father.\n(他和他爸爸一樣高。)\nShe works as a nurse.\n(她的職業是護理師。)"],["ask","ask(v.)問、請求、邀請\n(無詞性變化)\nask for 要求\nask a question 提問\nMay I ask you a question?\n(我可以問你一個問題嗎？)\nHe asked for my help.\n(他請求我的幫忙。)"],["at","at(prep.)在(某地點、某時刻)、向\n(無詞性變化)\nat home 在家\nat night 在晚上\nI am at home now.\n(我現在在家。)\nLook at the stars in the sky.\n(看看天上的星星。)"],["attack","attack(n./v.)攻擊、(疾病)發作\nattacker(n.)攻擊者\nheart attack 心臟病發作\nattack on 對……的攻擊\nThe dog attacked the cat.\n(那隻狗攻擊了貓。)\nMy grandpa had a heart attack last year.\n(我爺爺去年心臟病發作。)"],["aunt","aunt(n.)阿姨、姑姑、伯母、嬸嬸、舅媽\n(無詞性變化)\nmy aunt 我的阿姨\naunt and uncle 叔叔阿姨\nMy aunt lives in Kaohsiung.\n(我阿姨住在高雄。)\nMy aunt gave me a birthday gift.\n(我姑姑送我一份生日禮物。)"],["away","away(adv.)離開、在遠處、不在\n(無詞性變化)\ngo away 走開\nfar away 很遠\nMy school is far away from my home.\n(我的學校離我家很遠。)\nThe cat ran away.\n(那隻貓跑走了。)"],["baby","baby(n.)嬰兒、寶寶\n(無詞性變化)\nbaby girl 女嬰\nhave a baby 生小孩\nThe baby is sleeping in her room.\n(寶寶正在她的房間裡睡覺。)\nMy aunt just had a baby boy.\n(我阿姨剛生了一個男寶寶。)"],["back","back(adv./n./v./adj.)向後、回原處、背部、支持\nbackward(adv.)向後地\ncome back 回來\nback door 後門\nPlease come back before dinner.\n(請在晚餐前回來。)\nMy back hurts after the long run.\n(長跑之後我的背很痛。)"],["bad","bad(adj.)壞的、不好的、嚴重的\nbadly(adv.)嚴重地、很差地\nbad news 壞消息\nbad habit 壞習慣\nI have some bad news for you.\n(我有一些壞消息要告訴你。)\nEating late at night is a bad habit.\n(深夜吃東西是個壞習慣。)"],["bag","bag(n.)袋子、包包\n(無詞性變化)\nschool bag 書包\nplastic bag 塑膠袋\nShe put her books in her school bag.\n(她把書放進書包裡。)\nPlease bring your own bag to the store.\n(請自備袋子到商店。)"],["ball","ball(n./v.)球、舞會、把…捏成球狀\n(無詞性變化)\nplay ball 打球\nkick the ball 踢球\nThe boys are playing ball in the park.\n(男孩們正在公園裡打球。)\nHe kicked the ball into the goal.\n(他把球踢進球門。)"],["banana","banana(n.)香蕉\n(無詞性變化)\nbanana peel 香蕉皮\na bunch of bananas 一串香蕉\nI eat a banana every morning.\n(我每天早上吃一根香蕉。)\nMom bought a bunch of bananas at the market.\n(媽媽在市場買了一串香蕉。)"],["band","band(n.)樂團、帶子、一群\n(無詞性變化)\nrock band 搖滾樂團\nrubber band 橡皮筋\nMy brother plays the drums in a band.\n(我哥哥在樂團裡打鼓。)\nShe tied her hair with a rubber band.\n(她用橡皮筋把頭髮綁起來。)"],["bank","bank(n./v.)銀行、河岸、存錢\nbanker(n.)銀行家\nbank account 銀行帳戶\nriver bank 河岸\nMy dad works at a bank downtown.\n(我爸爸在市中心的一家銀行工作。)\nWe sat on the river bank and talked.\n(我們坐在河岸邊聊天。)"],["baseball","baseball(n.)棒球\n(無詞性變化)\nbaseball game 棒球比賽\nbaseball player 棒球選手\nWe watched a baseball game on Sunday.\n(我們星期天看了一場棒球賽。)\nHe wants to be a baseball player.\n(他想成為一名棒球選手。)"],["basket","basket(n.)籃子、(籃球的)籃框\n(無詞性變化)\nshopping basket 購物籃\na basket of fruit 一籃水果\nShe carried a basket of apples.\n(她提著一籃蘋果。)\nPut the toys back in the basket.\n(把玩具放回籃子裡。)"],["basketball","basketball(n.)籃球\n(無詞性變化)\nplay basketball 打籃球\nbasketball court 籃球場\nWe play basketball after school.\n(我們放學後打籃球。)\nThe basketball court is full of students.\n(籃球場上滿是學生。)"],["bat","bat(n./v.)球棒、蝙蝠、用球棒擊球\n(無詞性變化)\nbaseball bat 棒球棒\nat bat 輪到打擊\nHe hit the ball with a wooden bat.\n(他用木製球棒擊球。)\nBats usually come out at night.\n(蝙蝠通常在晚上出沒。)"],["bath","bath(n.)洗澡、浴缸\nbathe(v.)洗澡、沐浴\ntake a bath 洗澡\nbath towel 浴巾\nI take a bath every night.\n(我每天晚上洗澡。)\nThe baby enjoys a warm bath.\n(寶寶喜歡洗溫水澡。)"],["bathroom","bathroom(n.)浴室、廁所\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to the bathroom 上廁所\nclean the bathroom 打掃浴室\nMay I go to the bathroom?\n(我可以去上廁所嗎？)\nIt is my turn to clean the bathroom.\n(輪到我打掃浴室了。)"],["be","be(v./aux.)是、在、存在\nbeing(n.)存在、生物\nbe late 遲到\nbe careful 小心\nPlease be careful when you cross the street.\n(過馬路時請小心。)\nDon't be late for school again.\n(上學不要再遲到了。)"],["beach","beach(n./v.)海灘、使(船)擱淺\n(無詞性變化)\nsandy beach 沙灘\non the beach 在海灘上\nWe played on the beach all day.\n(我們整天都在海灘上玩。)\nKenting has many beautiful beaches.\n(墾丁有許多美麗的海灘。)"],["bean","bean(n.)豆子\n(無詞性變化)\ngreen bean 四季豆\nred bean 紅豆\nGrandma makes red bean soup in winter.\n(奶奶冬天會煮紅豆湯。)\nI don't like green beans very much.\n(我不太喜歡四季豆。)"],["bear","bear(v./n.)忍受、承擔、熊\nbearable(adj.)可忍受的\ncan't bear 無法忍受\npolar bear 北極熊\nI can't bear the noise anymore.\n(我再也受不了這個噪音了。)\nWe saw a big brown bear at the zoo.\n(我們在動物園看到一隻大棕熊。)"],["beautiful","beautiful(adj.)美麗的、漂亮的\nbeauty(n.)美、美人\nbeautifully(adv.)美麗地\nbeautiful view 美麗的景色\nbeautiful day 美好的一天\nWhat a beautiful day it is today!\n(今天天氣真好！)\nThe view from the mountain is beautiful.\n(從山上看的景色很美。)"],["because","because(conj.)因為\n(無詞性變化)\nbecause of 由於\njust because 只因為\nI stayed home because I was sick.\n(我因為生病待在家裡。)\nThe game was canceled because of the rain.\n(比賽因為下雨而取消了。)"],["become","become(v.)變成、成為\n(無詞性變化)\nbecome friends 成為朋友\nbecome famous 成名\nShe wants to become a doctor.\n(她想成為醫生。)\nWe became good friends last year.\n(我們去年成了好朋友。)"],["bed","bed(n.)床\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to bed 上床睡覺\nmake the bed 整理床鋪\nI usually go to bed at eleven.\n(我通常十一點上床睡覺。)\nPlease make your bed every morning.\n(請每天早上整理床鋪。)"],["bedroom","bedroom(n.)臥室\n(無詞性變化)\nmaster bedroom 主臥室\nbedroom window 臥室窗戶\nMy bedroom is on the second floor.\n(我的臥室在二樓。)\nShe is cleaning her bedroom now.\n(她現在正在打掃臥室。)"],["bee","bee(n.)蜜蜂\n(無詞性變化)\nbusy as a bee 非常忙碌\nbee sting 蜂螫\nA bee is flying around the flowers.\n(一隻蜜蜂在花朵周圍飛舞。)\nBees make honey for us.\n(蜜蜂為我們製造蜂蜜。)"],["beef","beef(n.)牛肉\n(無詞性變化)\nbeef noodles 牛肉麵\nground beef 絞牛肉\nBeef noodles are popular in Taiwan.\n(牛肉麵在台灣很受歡迎。)\nI don't eat beef or pork.\n(我不吃牛肉也不吃豬肉。)"],["before","before(prep./conj./adv.)在…之前、以前\n(無詞性變化)\nbefore long 不久之後\nthe day before 前一天\nWash your hands before you eat.\n(吃東西前要洗手。)\nI have seen this movie before.\n(我以前看過這部電影。)"],["begin","begin(v.)開始\nbeginning(n.)開始、起點\nbeginner(n.)初學者\nbegin with 以…開始\nat the beginning 一開始\nClass begins at eight o'clock.\n(八點開始上課。)\nIt began to rain in the afternoon.\n(下午開始下雨了。)"],["behind","behind(prep./adv.)在…後面、落後\n(無詞性變化)\nbehind the door 在門後\nfall behind 落後\nThe cat is hiding behind the sofa.\n(貓躲在沙發後面。)\nDon't fall behind in your studies.\n(課業不要落後。)"],["believe","believe(v.)相信、認為\nbelief(n.)信念、相信\nbelieve in 信任、相信…存在\nhard to believe 難以置信\nI believe you can do it.\n(我相信你做得到。)\nIt's hard to believe he is only ten.\n(很難相信他只有十歲。)"],["bell","bell(n.)鈴、鐘\n(無詞性變化)\nring the bell 按鈴、敲鐘\nschool bell 學校鐘聲\nThe school bell rang at noon.\n(中午學校鐘聲響了。)\nPlease ring the bell at the door.\n(請按門口的電鈴。)"],["belong","belong(v.)屬於\nbelongings(n.)財物、隨身物品\nbelong to 屬於\nbelong together 是一對、很相配\nThis book belongs to Amy.\n(這本書是艾咪的。)\nDo these shoes belong to you?\n(這雙鞋是你的嗎？)"],["below","below(adv./prep.)在下方、低於\n(無詞性變化)\nbelow zero 零度以下\nsee below 見下文\nThe temperature fell below zero last night.\n(昨晚氣溫降到零度以下。)\nWrite your name in the box below.\n(把你的名字寫在下面的格子裡。)"],["belt","belt(n./v.)皮帶、腰帶、用帶子繫\n(無詞性變化)\nseat belt 安全帶\nleather belt 皮帶\nPlease fasten your seat belt.\n(請繫好安全帶。)\nHe wears a black leather belt.\n(他繫著一條黑色皮帶。)"],["bench","bench(n.)長椅、長凳\n(無詞性變化)\npark bench 公園長椅\nsit on a bench 坐在長椅上\nAn old man is sitting on the bench.\n(一位老先生坐在長椅上。)\nWe ate lunch on a park bench.\n(我們在公園長椅上吃午餐。)"],["beside","beside(prep.)在…旁邊\n(無詞性變化)\nbeside the window 在窗邊\nsit beside 坐在…旁邊\nCome and sit beside me.\n(過來坐在我旁邊。)\nThere is a lamp beside the bed.\n(床邊有一盞檯燈。)"],["best","best(adj./adv./v./n.)最好的、最好地、打敗、最佳\n(無詞性變化)\nbest friend 最好的朋友\ndo one's best 盡力\nTom is my best friend.\n(湯姆是我最好的朋友。)\nJust do your best on the test.\n(考試時盡力就好。)"],["between","between(prep./adv.)在…之間\n(無詞性變化)\nbetween A and B 在A和B之間\nin between 在中間\nThe bank is between the school and the park.\n(銀行位於學校和公園之間。)\nDon't eat between meals.\n(兩餐之間不要吃東西。)"],["bicycle/bike","bicycle(n.)腳踏車、自行車\nbike(n.)腳踏車(口語)\nride a bicycle 騎腳踏車\nbike lane 自行車道\nI ride my bicycle to school.\n(我騎腳踏車上學。)\nLet's go for a bike ride this weekend.\n(這個週末我們去騎腳踏車吧。)"],["big","big(adj.)大的、重要的\n(無詞性變化)\nbig city 大城市\nbig deal 了不起的事\nTaipei is a big city.\n(台北是個大城市。)\nDon't worry, it's no big deal.\n(別擔心，這沒什麼大不了。)"],["bird","bird(n.)鳥\n(無詞性變化)\nearly bird 早起的人\nbird watching 賞鳥\nThe birds are singing in the tree.\n(鳥兒在樹上唱歌。)\nThe early bird catches the worm.\n(早起的鳥兒有蟲吃。)"],["bite","bite(n./v.)咬、一口、叮咬\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a bite 咬一口\nmosquito bite 蚊子叮咬\nCan I take a bite of your apple?\n(我可以咬一口你的蘋果嗎？)\nThe dog bit my leg.\n(那隻狗咬了我的腿。)"],["black","black(adj./n.)黑色的、黑色\nblacken(v.)使變黑\nblack coffee 黑咖啡\nblack and white 黑白的\nHe drinks black coffee every morning.\n(他每天早上喝黑咖啡。)\nShe is wearing a black dress.\n(她穿著一件黑色洋裝。)"],["blind","blind(adj./v.)瞎的、盲目的、使失明\nblindness(n.)失明\nblind person 盲人\ngo blind 失明\nThe blind man walks with a dog.\n(那位盲人由狗陪著走路。)\nThe bright light blinded me for a moment.\n(強光讓我一時看不見。)"],["block","block(n./v.)街區、塊、阻擋\n(無詞性變化)\ntwo blocks away 兩個街區遠\nblock the road 擋住道路\nThe store is two blocks away.\n(那家店在兩個街區外。)\nA big tree blocked the road.\n(一棵大樹擋住了道路。)"],["blow","blow(v.)吹、颳(風)、吹氣\n(無詞性變化)\nblow out 吹熄\nblow one's nose 擤鼻涕\nMake a wish and blow out the candles.\n(許個願然後吹熄蠟燭。)\nThe wind is blowing hard today.\n(今天風颳得很大。)"],["blue","blue(adj./n.)藍色的、憂鬱的、藍色\n(無詞性變化)\nblue sky 藍天\nfeel blue 心情低落\nThe sky is blue and clear today.\n(今天天空湛藍晴朗。)\nShe feels blue on rainy days.\n(她在雨天會心情低落。)"],["boat","boat(n.)船、小船\n(無詞性變化)\nby boat 搭船\nfishing boat 漁船\nWe went to the island by boat.\n(我們搭船去那座島。)\nMany fishing boats are in the harbor.\n(港口裡有許多漁船。)"],["body","body(n.)身體、主體\n(無詞性變化)\nhuman body 人體\nbody language 肢體語言\nExercise is good for your body.\n(運動對身體有益。)\nBody language can show how you feel.\n(肢體語言能表現你的感受。)"],["book","book(n./v.)書、預訂\nbooking(n.)預訂\nread a book 看書\nbook a table 訂位\nI read a book before bed.\n(我睡前會看書。)\nLet's book a table for dinner.\n(我們預訂晚餐的位子吧。)"],["bored","bored(adj.)感到無聊的\nbore(v.)使厭煩\nboredom(n.)無聊\nget bored 覺得無聊\nbored with 對…感到厭煩\nI get bored when I stay home.\n(待在家裡我會覺得無聊。)\nThe kids were bored with the long movie.\n(孩子們對那部冗長的電影感到厭煩。)"],["boring","boring(adj.)無聊的、乏味的\nbore(v.)使厭煩\nboring class 無聊的課\nboring job 乏味的工作\nThis movie is so boring.\n(這部電影好無聊。)\nHe thinks history class is boring.\n(他覺得歷史課很無聊。)"],["born","born(adj.)出生的、天生的\nbear(v.)生(小孩)\nbe born 出生\nborn in 在…出生\nI was born in Taipei.\n(我在台北出生。)\nShe is a born singer.\n(她是天生的歌手。)"],["borrow","borrow(v.)借入、向…借\nborrower(n.)借用者\nborrow money 借錢\nborrow from 向…借\nCan I borrow your pen?\n(我可以借你的筆嗎？)\nI borrowed two books from the library.\n(我向圖書館借了兩本書。)"],["boss","boss(n./v.)老闆、上司、指揮\nbossy(adj.)愛指使人的\nmy boss 我的老闆\nboss around 對人頤指氣使\nMy boss is very kind to us.\n(我的老闆對我們很好。)\nStop bossing your little sister around.\n(不要再對你妹妹頤指氣使了。)"],["both","both(pron./adv./adj.)兩者、兩個都\n(無詞性變化)\nboth A and B 兩者都…\nboth of us 我們兩個\nBoth of my parents are teachers.\n(我的父母都是老師。)\nShe can speak both English and Japanese.\n(她會說英文和日文。)"],["bottle","bottle(n./v.)瓶子、裝瓶\n(無詞性變化)\nwater bottle 水瓶\na bottle of milk 一瓶牛奶\nI bring a water bottle to school.\n(我帶水瓶去學校。)\nPlease buy a bottle of milk.\n(請買一瓶牛奶。)"],["bottom","bottom(n./adj./v.)底部、最下面的、降到最低點\n(無詞性變化)\nat the bottom of 在…的底部\nfrom the bottom of my heart 打從心底\nThe keys are at the bottom of my bag.\n(鑰匙在我包包的底部。)\nThank you from the bottom of my heart.\n(打從心底感謝你。)"],["bow","bow(n./v.)鞠躬、弓、蝴蝶結\n(無詞性變化)\nbow to 向…鞠躬\nbow and arrow 弓箭\nThe students bowed to the teacher.\n(學生們向老師鞠躬。)\nShe tied a pink bow in her hair.\n(她在頭髮上繫了一個粉紅色蝴蝶結。)"],["bowl","bowl(n.)碗\n(無詞性變化)\na bowl of rice 一碗飯\nsoup bowl 湯碗\nI ate two bowls of rice tonight.\n(我今晚吃了兩碗飯。)\nPlease wash the bowls after dinner.\n(晚餐後請洗碗。)"],["box","box(n./v.)盒子、箱子、拳擊、裝箱\nboxing(n.)拳擊\nlunch box 便當盒\na box of 一盒…\nHe opened the box with a smile.\n(他微笑著打開盒子。)\nMom put my lunch box in my bag.\n(媽媽把我的便當盒放進包包。)"],["boy","boy(n.)男孩\nboyhood(n.)少年時期\nlittle boy 小男孩\nboy scout 童子軍\nThe little boy is crying.\n(那個小男孩在哭。)\nThere are twenty boys in our class.\n(我們班上有二十個男生。)"],["brave","brave(adj.)勇敢的\nbravery(n.)勇敢\nbravely(adv.)勇敢地\nbrave act 勇敢的行為\nbe brave 勇敢一點\nThe brave boy saved his friend.\n(那個勇敢的男孩救了他的朋友。)\nBe brave and try again.\n(勇敢一點，再試一次。)"],["bread","bread(n.)麵包\n(無詞性變化)\na slice of bread 一片麵包\nfresh bread 新鮮麵包\nI had bread and milk for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了麵包配牛奶。)\nThe bakery sells fresh bread.\n(那間麵包店賣新鮮麵包。)"],["break","break(n./v.)休息、打破、弄壞\nbroken(adj.)破的、壞掉的\ntake a break 休息一下\nbreak the rules 違反規則\nLet's take a break.\n(我們休息一下吧。)\nWho broke the window?\n(誰打破了窗戶？)"],["breakfast","breakfast(n./v.)早餐、吃早餐\n(無詞性變化)\nhave breakfast 吃早餐\nbreakfast shop 早餐店\nI have breakfast at seven.\n(我七點吃早餐。)\nThere is a breakfast shop near my house.\n(我家附近有一間早餐店。)"],["bridge","bridge(n./v.)橋、橋梁、彌合\n(無詞性變化)\ncross the bridge 過橋\nbuild a bridge 建造橋梁\nWe walked across the bridge.\n(我們走過那座橋。)\nThis bridge is very old.\n(這座橋非常古老。)"],["bright","bright(adj./adv.)明亮的、聰明的、光明的\nbrightly(adv.)明亮地\nbrighten(v.)使明亮\nbright future 光明的未來\nbright student 聰明的學生\nThe room is bright and clean.\n(這個房間明亮又乾淨。)\nShe is a bright student.\n(她是個聰明的學生。)"],["bring","bring(v.)帶來、拿來\n(無詞性變化)\nbring back 帶回來\nbring up 養育、提出\nDon't forget to bring your umbrella.\n(別忘了帶雨傘。)\nCan you bring me a glass of water?\n(你可以幫我拿一杯水來嗎？)"],["brother","brother(n.)兄弟、哥哥、弟弟\nbrotherhood(n.)兄弟情誼\nolder brother 哥哥\nyounger brother 弟弟\nMy older brother is in college.\n(我哥哥在讀大學。)\nI have one younger brother.\n(我有一個弟弟。)"],["brown","brown(adj./v./n.)棕色的、煎成褐色、棕色\n(無詞性變化)\nbrown hair 棕髮\nbrown sugar 紅糖、黑糖\nShe has long brown hair.\n(她有一頭棕色長髮。)\nBrown the onions in a pan first.\n(先把洋蔥放在鍋裡煎到金黃。)"],["bug","bug(n./v.)蟲子、程式錯誤、煩擾\n(無詞性變化)\nfix a bug 修正程式錯誤\nstomach bug 腸胃型感冒\nThere is a bug on the wall.\n(牆上有一隻蟲。)\nStop bugging me while I study.\n(我讀書時別來煩我。)"],["build","build(v.)建造、建立\nbuilding(n.)建築物\nbuilder(n.)建築工人\nbuild a house 蓋房子\nbuild up 逐步建立\nThey are building a new library.\n(他們正在蓋一座新圖書館。)\nReading helps you build your vocabulary.\n(閱讀能幫助你累積字彙。)"],["bus","bus(n.)公車、巴士\n(無詞性變化)\nbus stop 公車站\ntake a bus 搭公車\nI take the bus to school.\n(我搭公車上學。)\nLet's wait at the bus stop.\n(我們在公車站等吧。)"],["business","business(n.)生意、商業、事務\nbusinessman(n.)商人\non business 出差\nnone of your business 不關你的事\nMy father went to Japan on business.\n(我爸爸去日本出差。)\nShe runs a small business.\n(她經營一家小公司。)"],["busy","busy(adj.)忙碌的、熱鬧的、(電話)占線的\nbusily(adv.)忙碌地\nbusy with 忙於\nbusy street 熱鬧的街道\nI am busy with my homework.\n(我正忙著寫作業。)\nThis is a very busy street.\n(這是一條非常熱鬧的街道。)"],["but","but(conj./prep./adv.)但是、除了、只\n(無詞性變化)\nnot only...but also 不僅…而且\nall but 幾乎\nI like cats, but my sister likes dogs.\n(我喜歡貓，但我妹妹喜歡狗。)\nEveryone came but Tom.\n(除了湯姆，大家都來了。)"],["butter","butter(n./v.)奶油、塗奶油\n(無詞性變化)\npeanut butter 花生醬\nbread and butter 奶油麵包\nI like peanut butter on toast.\n(我喜歡在吐司上塗花生醬。)\nShe buttered the bread for me.\n(她幫我在麵包上塗了奶油。)"],["butterfly","butterfly(n.)蝴蝶\n(無詞性變化)\nbutterfly garden 蝴蝶園\nbutterflies in one's stomach 心裡七上八下\nA butterfly landed on the flower.\n(一隻蝴蝶停在花上。)\nI had butterflies in my stomach before the test.\n(考試前我緊張得心裡七上八下。)"],["button","button(n./v.)鈕扣、按鈕、扣上\n(無詞性變化)\npress the button 按下按鈕\nbutton up 扣好扣子\nPress the red button to start.\n(按紅色按鈕開始。)\nButton up your coat. It's cold.\n(把外套扣好，外面很冷。)"],["buy","buy(v./n.)買、購買、划算的東西\nbuyer(n.)買方\nbuy a gift 買禮物\na good buy 划算的東西\nI want to buy a gift for Mom.\n(我想買個禮物給媽媽。)\nThis bag was a good buy.\n(這個包包買得很划算。)"],["by","by(prep./adv.)在…旁邊、藉由、在…之前\n(無詞性變化)\nby bus 搭公車\nby the way 順便一提\nPlease finish it by Friday.\n(請在星期五前完成。)\nShe sat by the window.\n(她坐在窗邊。)"],["cake","cake(n.)蛋糕\n(無詞性變化)\nbirthday cake 生日蛋糕\na piece of cake 小事一樁、輕而易舉\nMom made a chocolate cake for me.\n(媽媽為我做了一個巧克力蛋糕。)\nThis test is a piece of cake.\n(這個考試簡直輕而易舉。)"],["call","call(v./n.)打電話、叫、稱呼\ncaller(n.)打電話的人、來訪者\ncall back 回電\nphone call 電話\nPlease call me after school.\n(放學後請打電話給我。)\nWe call our dog Lucky.\n(我們叫我們的狗 Lucky。)"],["camera","camera(n.)相機、攝影機\n(無詞性變化)\ndigital camera 數位相機\nsecurity camera 監視器\nI took this photo with my new camera.\n(我用新相機拍了這張照片。)\nSmile at the camera, please.\n(請對著鏡頭微笑。)"],["camp","camp(n./v.)營地、露營\ncamping(n.)露營活動\ncamper(n.)露營者\nsummer camp 夏令營\ngo camping 去露營\nWe went to summer camp last July.\n(我們去年七月參加了夏令營。)\nThey camped by the lake.\n(他們在湖邊露營。)"],["can","can(aux./n./v.)能夠、可以、罐頭、把…裝罐\ncould(aux.)能夠(過去式)、可以(委婉)\ncan of soda 一罐汽水\ntrash can 垃圾桶\nI can swim very fast.\n(我游泳游得很快。)\nHe drank a can of soda.\n(他喝了一罐汽水。)"],["cap","cap(n./v.)帽子(有帽舌)、蓋子、覆蓋\n(無詞性變化)\nbaseball cap 棒球帽\nbottle cap 瓶蓋\nHe always wears a red cap.\n(他總是戴著一頂紅色帽子。)\nPut the cap back on the pen.\n(把筆蓋蓋回去。)"],["car","car(n.)汽車\n(無詞性變化)\ndrive a car 開車\ncar accident 車禍\nMy dad drives a blue car.\n(我爸爸開一輛藍色的車。)\nWe went to the beach by car.\n(我們開車去海邊。)"],["card","card(n.)卡片、紙牌\n(無詞性變化)\nbirthday card 生日卡\nplay cards 玩撲克牌\nI sent her a birthday card.\n(我寄給她一張生日卡片。)\nLet's play cards after dinner.\n(晚餐後我們來玩撲克牌吧。)"],["care","care(n./v.)照顧、關心、在乎\ncareful(adj.)小心的\ncareless(adj.)粗心的\ntake care of 照顧\ncare about 在乎、關心\nShe takes care of her little brother.\n(她照顧她的弟弟。)\nI don't care about the price.\n(我不在乎價錢。)"],["careful","careful(adj.)小心的、仔細的\ncarefully(adv.)小心地\ncare(n./v.)照顧、關心\nbe careful with 小心處理…\ncareful driver 謹慎的駕駛\nBe careful when you cross the street.\n(過馬路時要小心。)\nShe is a careful student.\n(她是個細心的學生。)"],["carrot","carrot(n.)紅蘿蔔\n(無詞性變化)\ncarrot juice 紅蘿蔔汁\ncarrot cake 紅蘿蔔蛋糕\nRabbits love to eat carrots.\n(兔子很愛吃紅蘿蔔。)\nI don't like carrots in my soup.\n(我不喜歡湯裡有紅蘿蔔。)"],["carry","carry(v.)攜帶、搬運\ncarrier(n.)搬運者、運輸工具\ncarry a bag 提袋子\ncarry out 執行、實行\nCan you help me carry this box?\n(你可以幫我搬這個箱子嗎？)\nShe always carries an umbrella.\n(她總是隨身帶著雨傘。)"],["case","case(n./v.)情況、案件、盒子、把…裝箱\n(無詞性變化)\nin case 以防萬一\npencil case 鉛筆盒\nTake an umbrella in case it rains.\n(帶把傘以防下雨。)\nMy pencil case is on the desk.\n(我的鉛筆盒在桌上。)"],["cat","cat(n.)貓\nkitten(n.)小貓\nfeed the cat 餵貓\npet cat 寵物貓\nMy cat sleeps on my bed.\n(我的貓睡在我的床上。)\nThe cat is chasing a mouse.\n(那隻貓正在追老鼠。)"],["catch","catch(v./n.)抓住、接住、趕上、染上(疾病)\n(無詞性變化)\ncatch a cold 感冒\ncatch the bus 趕上公車\nHe caught the ball with one hand.\n(他用一隻手接住了球。)\nHurry, or we won't catch the bus.\n(快點，不然我們會趕不上公車。)"],["celebrate","celebrate(v.)慶祝\ncelebration(n.)慶祝、慶祝活動\ncelebrate a birthday 慶生\ncelebrate Christmas 慶祝聖誕節\nWe celebrated Grandma's birthday together.\n(我們一起慶祝了奶奶的生日。)\nHow do you celebrate the New Year?\n(你們怎麼慶祝新年？)"],["cellphone","cellphone(n.)手機\n(無詞性變化)\ncellphone number 手機號碼\nturn off your cellphone 把手機關機\nPlease turn off your cellphone in class.\n(上課時請把手機關機。)\nI left my cellphone at home.\n(我把手機忘在家裡了。)"],["cent","cent(n.)分(貨幣單位,一元的百分之一)\npercent(n.)百分比\nten cents 十分錢\nevery cent 每一分錢\nThis candy costs fifty cents.\n(這顆糖果要五十分錢。)\nHe saved every cent he earned.\n(他把賺到的每一分錢都存起來。)"],["center","center(n.)中心、中央\ncentral(adj.)中央的、主要的\nshopping center 購物中心\nin the center of 在…的中央\nThere is a big tree in the center of the park.\n(公園中央有一棵大樹。)\nLet's meet at the shopping center.\n(我們在購物中心碰面吧。)"],["certain","certain(adj./pron.)確定的、某些、某個\ncertainly(adv.)當然、無疑地\nbe certain of 確信…\na certain person 某個人\nAre you certain about the time?\n(你確定時間嗎？)\nCertain students did not do their homework.\n(某些學生沒寫作業。)"],["chair","chair(n./v.)椅子、主持(會議)\nchairman(n.)主席\nsit on a chair 坐在椅子上\nchair a meeting 主持會議\nPlease sit on this chair.\n(請坐這張椅子。)\nOur principal chaired the meeting.\n(我們校長主持了這場會議。)"],["chance","chance(n./v.)機會、可能性、碰巧\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a chance to 有機會…\nby chance 碰巧\nI had a chance to visit Japan.\n(我有機會去日本玩。)\nWe met by chance at the station.\n(我們在車站碰巧遇見。)"],["change","change(n./v.)改變、零錢、換\nchangeable(adj.)易變的\nchange one's mind 改變主意\nkeep the change 不用找零\nShe changed her mind at the last minute.\n(她在最後一刻改變了主意。)\nHere is your change.\n(這是找您的零錢。)"],["cheap","cheap(adj./adv.)便宜的、便宜地\ncheaply(adv.)便宜地\ncheap price 便宜的價格\nbuy something cheap 便宜買到東西\nThis shirt is very cheap.\n(這件襯衫很便宜。)\nFood here is cheap and good.\n(這裡的食物又便宜又好吃。)"],["check","check(v./n.)檢查、核對、支票、帳單\n(無詞性變化)\ncheck in 辦理登記、報到\ncheck the answer 核對答案\nPlease check your answers before you hand in.\n(交卷前請檢查答案。)\nCan I have the check, please?\n(請給我帳單好嗎？)"],["cheese","cheese(n.)起司、乳酪\n(無詞性變化)\na slice of cheese 一片起司\ncheese sandwich 起司三明治\nI want a sandwich with cheese.\n(我想要一個夾起司的三明治。)\nSay cheese for the photo!\n(拍照時說「cheese」！)"],["chicken","chicken(n.)雞、雞肉、膽小鬼\n(無詞性變化)\nfried chicken 炸雞\nchicken soup 雞湯\nWe had fried chicken for dinner.\n(我們晚餐吃炸雞。)\nGrandpa keeps ten chickens.\n(爺爺養了十隻雞。)"],["child","child(n.)小孩、孩子\nchildren(n.)小孩(複數)\nchildhood(n.)童年\nonly child 獨生子女\nchild care 托兒服務\nShe is an only child.\n(她是獨生女。)\nThe children are playing in the park.\n(孩子們正在公園玩。)"],["chocolate","chocolate(n.)巧克力\n(無詞性變化)\na bar of chocolate 一條巧克力\nhot chocolate 熱可可\nHe gave me a box of chocolates.\n(他送我一盒巧克力。)\nI drink hot chocolate in winter.\n(我冬天喝熱可可。)"],["choice","choice(n./adj.)選擇、精選的\nchoose(v.)選擇\nmake a choice 做選擇\nhave no choice 別無選擇\nYou made the right choice.\n(你做了正確的選擇。)\nWe had no choice but to wait.\n(我們別無選擇，只能等待。)"],["choose","choose(v.)選擇、挑選\nchoice(n.)選擇\nchoose between 在…之間選擇\nchoose to 決定、選擇做…\nYou can choose any color you like.\n(你可以選任何你喜歡的顏色。)\nShe chose to stay at home.\n(她選擇待在家裡。)"],["church","church(n.)教堂\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to church 上教堂(做禮拜)\nchurch bell 教堂鐘聲\nThey go to church every Sunday.\n(他們每週日上教堂。)\nThere is an old church in the town.\n(鎮上有一座古老的教堂。)"],["circle","circle(n./v.)圓圈、圈子、圈出、環繞\ncircular(adj.)圓形的\ndraw a circle 畫圓\ncircle the answer 圈出答案\nPlease circle the right answer.\n(請圈出正確答案。)\nThe kids sat in a circle.\n(孩子們圍成一圈坐著。)"],["city","city(n.)城市\n(無詞性變化)\nbig city 大城市\ncity hall 市政府\nTaipei is a big city.\n(台北是一座大城市。)\nI like living in the city.\n(我喜歡住在城市裡。)"],["class","class(n./v.)班級、課、等級、把…分類\nclassmate(n.)同班同學\nclassroom(n.)教室\nin class 上課中\nfirst class 頭等艙、一流的\nWe have English class today.\n(我們今天有英文課。)\nThere are thirty students in my class.\n(我們班上有三十個學生。)"],["clean","clean(adj./v./adv./n.)乾淨的、清潔、完全地\ncleaner(n.)清潔工、清潔劑\nclean up 清理乾淨\nkeep clean 保持乾淨\nPlease clean your room.\n(請打掃你的房間。)\nThe kitchen is very clean.\n(廚房非常乾淨。)"],["clear","clear(adj./v./adv.)清楚的、晴朗的、清除\nclearly(adv.)清楚地\nclear sky 晴朗的天空\nmake it clear 說清楚\nThe sky is clear today.\n(今天天空很晴朗。)\nPlease clear the table after dinner.\n(晚餐後請收拾桌子。)"],["clerk","clerk(n.)店員、職員\n(無詞性變化)\nbank clerk 銀行行員\noffice clerk 辦公室職員\nThe clerk helped me find a jacket.\n(店員幫我找到一件外套。)\nMy aunt works as a bank clerk.\n(我阿姨是銀行行員。)"],["climb","climb(v./n.)爬、攀登、攀爬\nclimber(n.)登山者、攀登者\nclimb a mountain 爬山\nclimb a tree 爬樹\nWe climbed Yangmingshan last weekend.\n(我們上週末去爬陽明山。)\nThe boy climbed up the tree.\n(那個男孩爬到樹上。)"],["clock","clock(n.)時鐘\n(無詞性變化)\nalarm clock 鬧鐘\naround the clock 日以繼夜地\nMy alarm clock rings at six.\n(我的鬧鐘六點響。)\nThe clock on the wall is slow.\n(牆上的時鐘慢了。)"],["close","close(adj./adv./v./n.)接近的、親密的、關閉、結束\nclosely(adv.)密切地、仔細地\nclosed(adj.)關著的、停止營業的\nclose friend 密友\nclose the door 關門\nPlease close the window.\n(請把窗戶關上。)\nShe is my close friend.\n(她是我的好朋友。)"],["clothes","clothes(n.)衣服\ncloth(n.)布料\nclothing(n.)衣物(總稱)\nchange clothes 換衣服\nwash clothes 洗衣服\nI need to buy some new clothes.\n(我需要買一些新衣服。)\nHe changed his clothes after the game.\n(比賽後他換了衣服。)"],["cloud","cloud(n.)雲\ncloudy(adj.)多雲的\ndark cloud 烏雲\nwhite cloud 白雲\nThere are dark clouds in the sky.\n(天空中有烏雲。)\nThe cloud looks like a rabbit.\n(那朵雲看起來像一隻兔子。)"],["club","club(n./v.)社團、俱樂部、棍棒、用棍棒打\n(無詞性變化)\njoin a club 加入社團\nclub activity 社團活動\nI joined the music club.\n(我加入了音樂社。)\nOur club meets every Friday.\n(我們社團每週五聚會。)"],["coat","coat(n./v.)外套、大衣、塗上一層\n(無詞性變化)\nput on a coat 穿上外套\nwinter coat 冬季大衣\nPut on your coat. It's cold.\n(穿上外套，天氣很冷。)\nShe bought a new winter coat.\n(她買了一件新的冬季大衣。)"],["coffee","coffee(n.)咖啡\n(無詞性變化)\na cup of coffee 一杯咖啡\ncoffee shop 咖啡店\nMy father drinks coffee every morning.\n(我爸爸每天早上喝咖啡。)\nLet's meet at the coffee shop.\n(我們在咖啡店見吧。)"],["cold","cold(adj./n.)冷的、冷淡的、感冒、寒冷\ncoldly(adv.)冷淡地\ncatch a cold 感冒\ncold water 冷水\nIt is very cold today.\n(今天非常冷。)\nI caught a cold last week.\n(我上週感冒了。)"],["collect","collect(v.)收集、收取\ncollection(n.)收藏品、收集\ncollector(n.)收藏家\ncollect stamps 集郵\ncollect money 募款、收錢\nMy brother likes to collect stamps.\n(我哥哥喜歡集郵。)\nThe teacher collected our homework.\n(老師收了我們的作業。)"],["color","color(n./v.)顏色、著色\ncolorful(adj.)色彩豐富的\nfavorite color 最喜歡的顏色\nbright color 鮮豔的顏色\nWhat is your favorite color?\n(你最喜歡什麼顏色？)\nThe children colored the pictures.\n(孩子們幫圖畫著色。)"],["come","come(v.)來、到來\n(無詞性變化)\ncome back 回來\ncome true 實現\nPlease come to my party.\n(請來參加我的派對。)\nI hope your dream will come true.\n(希望你的夢想會實現。)"],["comfortable","comfortable(adj.)舒服的、舒適的\ncomfort(n./v.)舒適、安慰\ncomfortably(adv.)舒服地\nfeel comfortable 感到舒服\ncomfortable shoes 舒適的鞋子\nThis sofa is very comfortable.\n(這張沙發非常舒服。)\nWear comfortable shoes for the trip.\n(旅行時要穿舒適的鞋子。)"],["common","common(adj./n.)常見的、共同的、公有地\ncommonly(adv.)普遍地\ncommon sense 常識\nin common 共同的\nChen is a common last name in Taiwan.\n(陳是台灣常見的姓氏。)\nWe have a lot in common.\n(我們有很多共同點。)"],["computer","computer(n.)電腦\n(無詞性變化)\ncomputer game 電腦遊戲\nuse a computer 使用電腦\nI do my homework on the computer.\n(我用電腦寫作業。)\nOur school has a new computer room.\n(我們學校有一間新的電腦教室。)"],["convenient","convenient(adj.)方便的、便利的\nconvenience(n.)方便、便利\nconveniently(adv.)方便地\nconvenience store 便利商店\nconvenient for 對…方便\nThe MRT is very convenient.\n(捷運非常方便。)\nIs Monday convenient for you?\n(星期一你方便嗎？)"],["cook","cook(v./n.)煮、烹飪、廚師\ncooker(n.)炊具\ncooking(n.)烹飪\ncook dinner 煮晚餐\na good cook 好廚師\nMy mom cooks dinner every day.\n(我媽媽每天煮晚餐。)\nHe is a very good cook.\n(他廚藝很好。)"],["cookie","cookie(n.)餅乾\n(無詞性變化)\nbake cookies 烤餅乾\nchocolate chip cookie 巧克力豆餅乾\nWe baked cookies for the party.\n(我們為派對烤了餅乾。)\nCan I have another cookie?\n(我可以再吃一片餅乾嗎？)"],["cool","cool(adj./v./n.)涼爽的、酷的、冷靜的、使變涼\ncooler(n.)冷藏箱\ncool down 冷卻、冷靜下來\nstay cool 保持冷靜\nIt is cool in the evening.\n(傍晚很涼爽。)\nYour new bike looks cool!\n(你的新腳踏車看起來好酷！)"],["copy","copy(n./v.)副本、一份(書報)、複製、抄襲\ncopier(n.)影印機\nmake a copy 影印一份\ncopy homework 抄作業\nPlease make ten copies of this page.\n(請把這一頁影印十份。)\nDon't copy your friend's homework.\n(不要抄朋友的作業。)"],["corner","corner(n.)角落、轉角\n(無詞性變化)\naround the corner 在附近、即將來臨\nstreet corner 街角\nThe bank is on the corner.\n(銀行在轉角處。)\nChristmas is just around the corner.\n(聖誕節快到了。)"],["correct","correct(adj./v.)正確的、改正、批改\ncorrection(n.)改正、訂正\ncorrectly(adv.)正確地\ncorrect answer 正確答案\ncorrect mistakes 改正錯誤\nYour answer is correct.\n(你的答案是正確的。)\nThe teacher corrected my mistakes.\n(老師改正了我的錯誤。)"],["cost","cost(n./v.)費用、成本、花費\ncostly(adj.)昂貴的\ncost of living 生活費\nat all costs 不惜任何代價\nHow much does this bag cost?\n(這個包包多少錢？)\nThe trip cost me a lot of money.\n(這趟旅行花了我很多錢。)"],["couch","couch(n./v.)長沙發、措辭表達\n(無詞性變化)\ncouch potato 整天窩在沙發看電視的人\nsit on the couch 坐在沙發上\nDad is sleeping on the couch.\n(爸爸正睡在沙發上。)\nDon't be a couch potato.\n(別整天窩在沙發上看電視。)"],["count","count(v./n.)數、計算、重要、計數\ncountless(adj.)數不清的\ncount to ten 數到十\ncount on 依靠、指望\nCan you count to ten in English?\n(你能用英文數到十嗎？)\nYou can count on me.\n(你可以依靠我。)"],["country","country(n.)國家、鄉下\ncountryside(n.)鄉間\nforeign country 外國\nin the country 在鄉下\nJapan is a beautiful country.\n(日本是個美麗的國家。)\nMy grandparents live in the country.\n(我的祖父母住在鄉下。)"],["course","course(n./v.)課程、路線、一道菜、(液體)流動\n(無詞性變化)\nof course 當然\ntake a course 修課\nOf course you can come with us.\n(你當然可以跟我們一起來。)\nShe is taking a cooking course.\n(她正在上烹飪課。)"],["cousin","cousin(n.)堂/表兄弟姊妹\n(無詞性變化)\nfirst cousin 嫡親堂/表兄弟姊妹\nvisit a cousin 拜訪堂/表親\nMy cousin lives in Tainan.\n(我的表哥住在台南。)\nI played games with my cousins.\n(我和堂兄弟姊妹們一起玩遊戲。)"],["cover","cover(v./n.)覆蓋、涵蓋、報導、封面、蓋子\ncovering(n.)覆蓋物\ncover with 用…覆蓋\nbook cover 書的封面\nSnow covered the mountain.\n(雪覆蓋了那座山。)\nI like the cover of this book.\n(我喜歡這本書的封面。)"],["cow","cow(n.)母牛、乳牛\n(無詞性變化)\nmilk a cow 擠牛奶\ndairy cow 乳牛\nThe cow is eating grass.\n(那頭牛正在吃草。)\nWe get milk from cows.\n(我們從乳牛身上取得牛奶。)"],["crazy","crazy(adj.)瘋狂的、著迷的\ncrazily(adv.)瘋狂地\nbe crazy about 對…著迷\ngo crazy 發瘋、抓狂\nHe is crazy about basketball.\n(他對籃球很著迷。)\nThe noise is driving me crazy.\n(這噪音快把我逼瘋了。)"],["cross","cross(n./v.)十字形、叉號、穿越、交叉\ncrossing(n.)十字路口、穿越處\ncross the street 過馬路\ncross one's arms 交叉雙臂\nLook both ways before you cross the street.\n(過馬路前要看兩邊。)\nPut a cross next to the wrong answers.\n(在錯誤的答案旁打叉。)"],["cry","cry(v./n.)哭、大叫、哭聲、叫聲\n(無詞性變化)\ncry for help 呼救\nstart to cry 開始哭\nThe baby cried all night.\n(那個嬰兒哭了一整晚。)\nWe heard a cry for help.\n(我們聽到一聲呼救。)"],["cup","cup(n.)杯子\n(無詞性變化)\na cup of tea 一杯茶\nWorld Cup 世界盃\nWould you like a cup of tea?\n(你要來杯茶嗎？)\nI broke my favorite cup.\n(我打破了我最喜歡的杯子。)"],["cut","cut(v./n.)切、剪、割、減少、傷口\n(無詞性變化)\ncut in line 插隊\nget a haircut 剪頭髮\nPlease cut the cake into eight pieces.\n(請把蛋糕切成八塊。)\nI cut my finger with a knife.\n(我被刀子割傷了手指。)"],["cute","cute(adj.)可愛的\n(無詞性變化)\ncute puppy 可愛的小狗\nlook cute 看起來很可愛\nYour little sister is so cute.\n(你妹妹好可愛。)\nLook at that cute puppy!\n(看那隻可愛的小狗！)"],["dance","dance(n./v.)舞蹈、跳舞\ndancer(n.)舞者\ndancing(n.)跳舞、舞蹈\ndance class 舞蹈課\ndance party 舞會\nLet's dance to this song together.\n(我們一起隨著這首歌跳舞吧。)\nShe takes a dance class every Saturday.\n(她每週六上一堂舞蹈課。)"],["dangerous","dangerous(adj.)危險的\ndanger(n.)危險\ndangerously(adv.)危險地\ndangerous animal 危險的動物\nextremely dangerous 極度危險\nIt is dangerous to swim here.\n(在這裡游泳很危險。)\nDriving too fast is very dangerous.\n(開車開太快非常危險。)"],["dark","dark(adj./n.)黑暗的、深色的、黑暗\ndarkness(n.)黑暗\ndarken(v.)使變暗\ndark blue 深藍色\nafter dark 天黑以後\nIt gets dark early in winter.\n(冬天天黑得很早。)\nDon't walk home alone after dark.\n(天黑以後不要獨自走路回家。)"],["date","date(n./v.)日期、約會、和……約會\n(無詞性變化)\ndue date 到期日\ngo on a date 去約會\nWhat is the date today?\n(今天是幾月幾號？)\nThey went on a date last Friday.\n(他們上週五去約會了。)"],["daughter","daughter(n.)女兒\n(無詞性變化)\nonly daughter 獨生女\neldest daughter 長女\nTheir daughter is five years old.\n(他們的女兒五歲了。)\nShe is the only daughter in her family.\n(她是家裡的獨生女。)"],["day","day(n.)天、日、白天\ndaily(adj./adv.)每日的、每天\nall day 一整天\nday off 休假日\nI study English every day.\n(我每天都讀英文。)\nWe stayed at home all day.\n(我們一整天都待在家。)"],["dead","dead(adj.)死的、無生命的、沒電的\ndie(v.)死亡\ndeath(n.)死亡\ndead body 屍體\ndead battery 沒電的電池\nMy phone is dead, so I can't call you.\n(我的手機沒電了，所以不能打給你。)\nThe fish in the tank are dead.\n(魚缸裡的魚死了。)"],["deal","deal(n./v.)交易、處理、對付\ndealer(n.)商人、經銷商\na great deal 大量、很多\ndeal with 處理\nIt's a deal!\n(就這麼說定了！)\nI need to deal with this problem now.\n(我現在需要處理這個問題。)"],["dear","dear(adj./n./adv.)親愛的、寶貴的、親愛的人\ndearly(adv.)深深地、非常\ndear friend 親愛的朋友\nOh dear 哎呀、天啊\nDear Tom, thank you for your letter.\n(親愛的湯姆，謝謝你的來信。)\nOh dear, I forgot my keys again!\n(哎呀，我又忘了帶鑰匙！)"],["death","death(n.)死亡、去世\ndie(v.)死亡\ndead(adj.)死的\nsudden death 猝死、驟死\nlife and death 生死\nHis death made everyone very sad.\n(他的去世讓大家都很難過。)\nThis is a matter of life and death.\n(這是攸關生死的事。)"],["decide","decide(v.)決定、下決心\ndecision(n.)決定\ndecide on 決定、選定\ndecide to do 決定做某事\nI decided to learn the guitar.\n(我決定學吉他。)\nWe can't decide where to eat.\n(我們決定不了要去哪裡吃飯。)"],["deep","deep(adj./adv.)深的、深深地\ndepth(n.)深度\ndeeply(adv.)深深地\ndeep breath 深呼吸\ndeep sleep 熟睡\nTake a deep breath and relax.\n(深呼吸，放輕鬆。)\nThe lake is very deep here.\n(這裡的湖水非常深。)"],["define","define(v.)下定義、界定\ndefinition(n.)定義\ndefined(adj.)明確的\ndefine a word 為字下定義\nclearly define 清楚界定\nCan you define this word for me?\n(你可以幫我解釋這個字的定義嗎？)\nIt is hard to define happiness.\n(幸福很難下定義。)"],["desk","desk(n.)書桌、辦公桌\n(無詞性變化)\nfront desk 櫃檯\ndesk lamp 檯燈\nMy books are on the desk.\n(我的書在書桌上。)\nPlease ask at the front desk.\n(請到櫃檯詢問。)"],["dictionary","dictionary(n.)字典、辭典\n(無詞性變化)\nEnglish dictionary 英文字典\nlook up in a dictionary 查字典\nI look up new words in my dictionary.\n(我在字典裡查新單字。)\nMay I borrow your English dictionary?\n(我可以借你的英文字典嗎？)"],["die","die(v.)死亡、枯死\ndeath(n.)死亡\ndead(adj.)死的\ndie of 死於（疾病等）\nbe dying to 渴望\nThe flowers died because I forgot to water them.\n(因為我忘了澆水，花都枯死了。)\nI'm dying to see the new movie.\n(我超想看那部新電影。)"],["different","different(adj.)不同的、各種的\ndifference(n.)差異、不同\ndiffer(v.)不同\ndifferent from 與……不同\ncompletely different 完全不同\nMy sister is very different from me.\n(我妹妹和我很不一樣。)\nWe visited many different places.\n(我們去了很多不同的地方。)"],["difficult","difficult(adj.)困難的、難相處的\ndifficulty(n.)困難\ndifficult question 困難的問題\ndifficult time 艱難時期\nThis math problem is very difficult.\n(這道數學題很難。)\nIt is difficult to wake up early.\n(早起很困難。)"],["dig","dig(v./n.)挖、掘、挖掘\n(無詞性變化)\ndig a hole 挖洞\ndig up 挖出\nThe dog is digging a hole in the yard.\n(那隻狗正在院子裡挖洞。)\nThey dug up some old coins.\n(他們挖出了一些古老的硬幣。)"],["dinner","dinner(n.)晚餐、正餐\n(無詞性變化)\nhave dinner 吃晚餐\ndinner party 晚宴\nWe have dinner at seven.\n(我們七點吃晚餐。)\nMom is cooking dinner in the kitchen.\n(媽媽正在廚房煮晚餐。)"],["dirty","dirty(adj./v.)髒的、弄髒\ndirt(n.)泥土、汙垢\ndirty clothes 髒衣服\ndirty work 苦差事\nYour shoes are dirty.\n(你的鞋子很髒。)\nPut your dirty clothes in the basket.\n(把你的髒衣服放進籃子裡。)"],["dish","dish(n./v.)盤子、菜餚、盛菜\n(無詞性變化)\nwash the dishes 洗碗\nmain dish 主菜\nI wash the dishes after dinner.\n(我晚餐後洗碗。)\nThis is my favorite dish.\n(這是我最喜歡的一道菜。)"],["do","do(aux./v.)做、從事、（助動詞）\ndoer(n.)實行者\ndo homework 做功課\ndo one's best 盡力\nDo you like apples?\n(你喜歡蘋果嗎？)\nI always do my homework after school.\n(我總是放學後寫功課。)"],["doctor/doc","doctor(n.)醫生、博士\ndoc(n.)醫生(口語)\nsee a doctor 看醫生\nfamily doctor 家庭醫師\nYou should see a doctor.\n(你應該去看醫生。)\nMy uncle is a doctor at that hospital.\n(我叔叔是那家醫院的醫生。)"],["dog","dog(n.)狗\ndoggy(n.)小狗(兒語)\nwalk the dog 遛狗\npet dog 寵物狗\nI walk my dog every morning.\n(我每天早上遛狗。)\nThe dog is sleeping under the table.\n(那隻狗在桌子底下睡覺。)"],["doll","doll(n.)洋娃娃、玩偶\n(無詞性變化)\nrag doll 布娃娃\nplay with dolls 玩洋娃娃\nMy little sister loves her doll.\n(我妹妹很愛她的洋娃娃。)\nThe girls are playing with dolls.\n(女孩們正在玩洋娃娃。)"],["dollar","dollar(n.)元(美元等貨幣單位)\n(無詞性變化)\nUS dollar 美元\ndollar bill 一元紙鈔\nThis pen costs two dollars.\n(這支筆要兩美元。)\nHe saved fifty dollars last month.\n(他上個月存了五十元。)"],["door","door(n.)門\ndoorway(n.)門口\nfront door 前門\nknock on the door 敲門\nPlease close the door.\n(請把門關上。)\nSomeone is knocking on the door.\n(有人在敲門。)"],["down","down(adv./prep./adj./n./v.)向下、沿著、沮喪的\ndownward(adj./adv.)向下的、向下\nsit down 坐下\nfeel down 心情低落\nPlease sit down here.\n(請坐在這裡。)\nShe feels a little down today.\n(她今天心情有點低落。)"],["dozen","dozen(n.)一打、十二個\n(無詞性變化)\na dozen eggs 一打蛋\ndozens of 數十個、很多\nI bought a dozen eggs.\n(我買了一打蛋。)\nDozens of people came to the party.\n(好幾十個人來參加派對。)"],["draw","draw(v./n.)畫、拉、抽籤、平手\ndrawing(n.)圖畫\ndrawer(n.)抽屜\ndraw a picture 畫一幅畫\ndraw attention 吸引注意\nI like to draw animals.\n(我喜歡畫動物。)\nThe game ended in a draw.\n(比賽以平手收場。)"],["dream","dream(n./v.)夢、夢想、做夢\ndreamer(n.)夢想家\ndream come true 夢想成真\nbad dream 惡夢\nI had a strange dream last night.\n(我昨晚做了一個奇怪的夢。)\nHer dream is to be a teacher.\n(她的夢想是當老師。)"],["dress","dress(n./v.)洋裝、服裝、穿衣\ndressing(n.)醬料、包紮\ndressed(adj.)穿好衣服的\nget dressed 穿好衣服\ndress up 盛裝打扮\nShe is wearing a red dress.\n(她穿著一件紅色洋裝。)\nHurry up and get dressed!\n(快點把衣服穿好！)"],["drink","drink(v./n.)喝、飲料\ndrinker(n.)飲酒者\nsoft drink 汽水、無酒精飲料\ndrink water 喝水\nDrink more water every day.\n(每天要多喝水。)\nWould you like a cold drink?\n(你想來杯冷飲嗎？)"],["drive","drive(v./n.)開車、駕駛、車程\ndriver(n.)駕駛人\ndriving(n.)駕駛\ndrive a car 開車\nan hour's drive 一小時車程\nMy father drives me to school.\n(我爸爸開車送我上學。)\nThe beach is a short drive from here.\n(海灘離這裡只有一小段車程。)"],["driver","driver(n.)駕駛人、司機\ndrive(v.)開車\ntaxi driver 計程車司機\nbus driver 公車司機\nThe bus driver is very friendly.\n(那位公車司機很友善。)\nMy uncle is a taxi driver.\n(我叔叔是計程車司機。)"],["drop","drop(v./n.)掉落、放下、滴\n(無詞性變化)\ndrop by 順道拜訪\na drop of water 一滴水\nDon't drop the glass!\n(別把杯子摔了！)\nPlease drop by my house tomorrow.\n(明天請順道來我家坐坐。)"],["drum","drum(n./v.)鼓、打鼓\ndrummer(n.)鼓手\nplay the drums 打鼓\ndrum set 爵士鼓組\nHe plays the drums in a band.\n(他在樂團裡打鼓。)\nThe children drummed on the table.\n(孩子們在桌上敲打。)"],["dry","dry(adj./v.)乾的、乾燥的、弄乾\ndryer(n.)烘乾機、吹風機\ndry season 乾季\ndry clothes 晾乾衣服\nThe towel is dry now.\n(毛巾現在乾了。)\nDry your hands before you eat.\n(吃飯前把手擦乾。)"],["duck","duck(n./v.)鴨子、閃避\nduckling(n.)小鴨\nroast duck 烤鴨\nduck down 低頭閃避\nThere are ducks in the pond.\n(池塘裡有鴨子。)\nHe ducked to avoid the ball.\n(他低頭閃避那顆球。)"],["during","during(prep.)在……期間\n(無詞性變化)\nduring the day 在白天\nduring the summer 在夏天期間\nPlease don't talk during the test.\n(考試期間請不要講話。)\nWe went to Japan during the summer vacation.\n(我們暑假期間去了日本。)"],["each","each(pron./adj./adv.)每個、各自\n(無詞性變化)\neach other 彼此、互相\neach time 每次\nEach student has a book.\n(每個學生都有一本書。)\nThe two friends help each other.\n(那兩個朋友互相幫忙。)"],["ear","ear(n.)耳朵、聽力\nearring(n.)耳環\near infection 耳朵發炎\nall ears 洗耳恭聽\nShe whispered in my ear.\n(她在我耳邊低語。)\nTell me your story. I'm all ears.\n(告訴我你的故事，我洗耳恭聽。)"],["early","early(adj./adv.)早的、提早地\n(無詞性變化)\nearly morning 清晨\nget up early 早起\nI get up early every day.\n(我每天都很早起床。)\nWe arrived ten minutes early.\n(我們提早十分鐘到達。)"],["earth","earth(n.)地球、土地、泥土\nearthquake(n.)地震\non earth 究竟、在世界上\nthe Earth's surface 地球表面\nThe Earth goes around the sun.\n(地球繞著太陽轉。)\nWhat on earth are you doing?\n(你到底在做什麼？)"],["east","east(n./adj./adv.)東方、東方的、向東\neastern(adj.)東方的、東部的\nthe Far East 遠東\neast coast 東海岸\nThe sun rises in the east.\n(太陽從東方升起。)\nHualien is on the east coast of Taiwan.\n(花蓮位於台灣東海岸。)"],["easy","easy(adj.)容易的、輕鬆的\neasily(adv.)容易地\nease(n./v.)容易、減輕\ntake it easy 放輕鬆\neasy question 簡單的問題\nThis test is very easy.\n(這次考試很簡單。)\nTake it easy. Everything will be fine.\n(放輕鬆，一切都會沒事的。)"],["eat","eat(v.)吃、吃飯\n(無詞性變化)\neat out 外出吃飯\neat breakfast 吃早餐\nWe often eat out on Sundays.\n(我們週日常常外出吃飯。)\nYou should eat more vegetables.\n(你應該多吃蔬菜。)"],["egg","egg(n.)蛋、卵\n(無詞性變化)\nboiled egg 水煮蛋\nfried egg 煎蛋\nI had two eggs for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了兩顆蛋。)\nThe bird laid three eggs in its nest.\n(那隻鳥在巢裡下了三顆蛋。)"],["either","either(adv./pron./adj./conj.)也（不）、兩者任一\n(無詞性變化)\neither A or B 不是A就是B\neither side 兩邊任一邊\nI don't like coffee either.\n(我也不喜歡咖啡。)\nYou can choose either of the two cakes.\n(這兩個蛋糕你可以任選一個。)"],["elephant","elephant(n.)大象\n(無詞性變化)\nbaby elephant 小象\nAfrican elephant 非洲象\nElephants have long noses.\n(大象有長長的鼻子。)\nWe saw a baby elephant at the zoo.\n(我們在動物園看到一隻小象。)"],["else","else(adv.)其他的、另外的\nelsewhere(adv.)在別處\nor else 否則\nsomeone else 別人\nWhat else do you need?\n(你還需要什麼別的嗎？)\nHurry up, or else you'll be late.\n(快一點，否則你會遲到。)"],["email","email(n./v.)電子郵件、寄電子郵件\n(無詞性變化)\nsend an email 寄電子郵件\nemail address 電子郵件地址\nPlease send me an email tonight.\n(今晚請寄電子郵件給我。)\nI'll email you the photos.\n(我會把照片用電子郵件寄給你。)"],["end","end(n./v.)結束、末端、終止\nending(n.)結局\nendless(adj.)無止境的\nin the end 最後\nat the end of 在……的末尾\nThe movie had a happy ending, and in the end everyone smiled.\n(這部電影有個快樂結局，最後大家都笑了。)\nThe class ends at noon.\n(這堂課在中午結束。)"],["engineer","engineer(n.)工程師\nengineering(n.)工程學\nsoftware engineer 軟體工程師\ncivil engineer 土木工程師\nMy father is an engineer.\n(我爸爸是一名工程師。)\nShe wants to be a software engineer.\n(她想成為一名軟體工程師。)"],["enjoy(ment)","enjoy(v.)享受、喜歡、enjoyment(n.)樂趣、享受\nenjoyable(adj.)令人愉快的\nenjoy oneself 玩得開心\nenjoy the view 欣賞風景\nDid you enjoy yourself at the party?\n(你在派對上玩得開心嗎？)\nI enjoy reading in my free time.\n(我空閒時喜歡看書。)"],["enough","enough(adv./adj./n.)足夠地、足夠的、足夠\n(無詞性變化)\nenough money 足夠的錢\nold enough 年紀夠大\nWe don't have enough time.\n(我們沒有足夠的時間。)\nHe is old enough to drive.\n(他已經到了可以開車的年紀。)"],["enter","enter(v.)進入、參加、輸入\nentrance(n.)入口\nentry(n.)進入、參賽作品\nenter a room 進入房間\nenter a contest 參加比賽\nPlease knock before you enter.\n(進來之前請先敲門。)\nShe entered a singing contest.\n(她參加了一場歌唱比賽。)"],["envelope","envelope(n.)信封\n(無詞性變化)\nred envelope 紅包\nseal an envelope 封信封\nPut the letter in the envelope.\n(把信放進信封裡。)\nKids get red envelopes during Chinese New Year.\n(孩子們在農曆新年會拿到紅包。)"],["eraser","eraser(n.)橡皮擦、板擦\nerase(v.)擦掉、消除\npencil eraser 鉛筆橡皮擦\nboard eraser 板擦\nCan I borrow your eraser?\n(我可以借你的橡皮擦嗎？)\nI lost my eraser at school.\n(我在學校弄丟了橡皮擦。)"],["error","error(n.)錯誤、失誤\n(無詞性變化)\nmake an error 犯錯\nspelling error 拼字錯誤\nThere is a spelling error here.\n(這裡有一個拼字錯誤。)\nEveryone makes errors sometimes.\n(每個人有時都會犯錯。)"],["even","even(adv./adj./v.)甚至、偶數的、平坦的、使平均\nevenly(adv.)均勻地\neven number 偶數\neven if 即使\nEven a child can do it.\n(連小孩子都會做。)\nTwo, four, and six are even numbers.\n(二、四、六是偶數。)"],["evening","evening(n.)傍晚、晚上\n(無詞性變化)\nthis evening 今晚\nin the evening 在傍晚\nI do my homework in the evening.\n(我在晚上做功課。)\nAre you free this evening?\n(你今晚有空嗎？)"],["ever","ever(adv.)曾經、從來、究竟\nforever(adv.)永遠\never since 自從……以後\nthan ever 比以往更\nHave you ever been to Japan?\n(你曾經去過日本嗎？)\nShe is happier than ever.\n(她比以往更快樂。)"],["every","every(adj.)每一、每個\n(無詞性變化)\nevery day 每天\nevery other day 每隔一天\nI brush my teeth every morning.\n(我每天早上刷牙。)\nEvery student must wear a uniform.\n(每位學生都必須穿制服。)"],["everyone/everybody","everyone(pron.)每個人、大家\neverybody(pron.)每個人、大家\neveryone else 其他所有人\nhello everyone 大家好\nHello, everyone! Welcome to class.\n(大家好！歡迎來上課。)\nEverybody likes her new song.\n(大家都喜歡她的新歌。)"],["everything","everything(pron.)每件事、一切\n(無詞性變化)\neverything else 其他一切\neverything is fine 一切都好\nThank you for everything.\n(謝謝你所做的一切。)\nDon't worry. Everything is fine.\n(別擔心，一切都很好。)"],["example","example(n.)例子、榜樣\n(無詞性變化)\nfor example 例如\nset an example 樹立榜樣\nCan you give me an example?\n(你可以給我舉個例子嗎？)\nI like fruit, for example, apples and bananas.\n(我喜歡水果，例如蘋果和香蕉。)"],["excellent","excellent(adj.)極好的、優秀的\nexcellence(n.)卓越\nexcel(v.)擅長、勝過\nexcellent student 優秀的學生\nexcellent idea 絕佳的點子\nThat's an excellent idea!\n(那真是個絕佳的點子！)\nShe is an excellent student.\n(她是一位優秀的學生。)"],["except","except(prep./conj.)除了……之外\nexception(n.)例外\nexcept for 除了……之外\nexcept that 只是、除了\nEveryone came except Tom.\n(除了湯姆之外，大家都來了。)\nThe store is open every day except Monday.\n(這家店除了週一之外每天都營業。)"],["excited","excited(adj.)興奮的、激動的\nexcite(v.)使興奮\nexcitement(n.)興奮\nget excited 變得興奮\nexcited about 對……感到興奮\nThe kids are excited about the trip.\n(孩子們對這趟旅行感到很興奮。)\nDon't get too excited.\n(別太激動。)"],["exciting","exciting(adj.)令人興奮的、刺激的\nexcite(v.)使興奮\nexcitement(n.)興奮\nexciting game 刺激的比賽\nexciting news 令人興奮的消息\nThe basketball game was very exciting.\n(那場籃球比賽非常刺激。)\nI have some exciting news for you.\n(我有個令人興奮的消息要告訴你。)"],["exercise","exercise(n./v.)運動、練習、做運動\n(無詞性變化)\ndo exercise 做運動\ngrammar exercise 文法練習\nI exercise in the park every morning.\n(我每天早上在公園運動。)\nPlease finish the exercises on page ten.\n(請完成第十頁的練習題。)"],["expect","expect(v.)預期、期待、預料\nexpectation(n.)期望\nexpected(adj.)預期的\nexpect a baby 懷孕、待產\nas expected 如預期\nI expect him to come soon.\n(我預期他很快就會來。)\nAs expected, it rained today.\n(如預期的一樣，今天下雨了。)"],["expensive","expensive(adj.)昂貴的\nexpense(n.)費用、開支\nexpensive car 昂貴的汽車\ntoo expensive 太貴\nThis bag is too expensive for me.\n(這個包包對我來說太貴了。)\nHe drives an expensive car.\n(他開一輛昂貴的汽車。)"],["experience","experience(n./v.)經驗、經歷、體驗\nexperienced(adj.)有經驗的\nwork experience 工作經驗\nlearn from experience 從經驗中學習\nThe trip was a wonderful experience.\n(這趟旅行是一次很棒的經驗。)\nHe has a lot of work experience.\n(他有豐富的工作經驗。)"],["explain","explain(v.)解釋、說明\nexplanation(n.)解釋、說明\nexplain to 向……解釋\nexplain why 解釋原因\nCan you explain this word to me?\n(你可以向我解釋這個字嗎？)\nPlease explain why you are late.\n(請解釋你為什麼遲到。)"],["eye","eye(n.)眼睛、眼光\neyesight(n.)視力\nkeep an eye on 留意、照看\nblue eyes 藍眼睛\nClose your eyes and make a wish.\n(閉上眼睛許個願。)\nPlease keep an eye on my bag.\n(請幫我看著我的包包。)"],["face","face(n./v.)臉、面對\nfacial(adj.)臉部的\nface to face 面對面\nface a problem 面對問題\nShe washes her face every morning.\n(她每天早上洗臉。)\nWe must face the problem together.\n(我們必須一起面對這個問題。)"],["fact","fact(n.)事實\nfactual(adj.)事實的\nin fact 事實上\na fun fact 有趣的事實\nIn fact, he is my cousin.\n(事實上，他是我的表哥。)\nIt is a fact that the earth is round.\n(地球是圓的，這是事實。)"],["factory","factory(n.)工廠\n(無詞性變化)\nfactory worker 工廠工人\ncar factory 汽車工廠\nMy uncle works in a car factory.\n(我叔叔在一家汽車工廠工作。)\nThe factory makes toys for children.\n(這家工廠生產兒童玩具。)"],["fail","fail(v./n.)失敗、不及格\nfailure(n.)失敗\nfail a test 考試不及格\nfail to do 未能做到\nHe failed the math test last week.\n(他上週數學考試不及格。)\nDon't give up if you fail once.\n(失敗一次也不要放棄。)"],["fall","fall(n./v.)落下、跌倒、秋天\nfallen(adj.)落下的\nfall down 跌倒\nfall asleep 睡著\nThe leaves fall from the trees in autumn.\n(秋天樹葉從樹上落下。)\nI fell asleep on the sofa.\n(我在沙發上睡著了。)"],["family","family(n.)家庭、家人\n(無詞性變化)\nfamily member 家庭成員\nfamily name 姓氏\nThere are four people in my family.\n(我家有四個人。)\nWe have a family dinner every Sunday.\n(我們每週日都有家庭聚餐。)"],["famous","famous(adj.)有名的\nfame(n.)名聲\nbe famous for 以……聞名\na famous singer 知名歌手\nTaipei 101 is a famous building.\n(台北101是一棟有名的建築。)\nThis town is famous for its tea.\n(這個小鎮以茶聞名。)"],["fan","fan(n./v.)風扇、粉絲、搧風\n(無詞性變化)\nelectric fan 電風扇\na big fan of 是……的忠實粉絲\nPlease turn on the fan. It's hot.\n(請打開電風扇，好熱。)\nI am a big fan of that band.\n(我是那個樂團的忠實粉絲。)"],["far","far(adv./adj.)遠的、遠地、非常\nfarther(adj./adv.)較遠的\nfar away 遙遠地\nso far 到目前為止\nMy school is not far from my home.\n(我的學校離我家不遠。)\nSo far, everything is going well.\n(到目前為止一切順利。)"],["farm","farm(n./v.)農場、耕種\nfarming(n.)農業、耕作\nwork on a farm 在農場工作\nfarm animals 農場動物\nMy grandparents live on a farm.\n(我的祖父母住在農場。)\nWe saw cows and pigs on the farm.\n(我們在農場看到牛和豬。)"],["farmer","farmer(n.)農夫\nfarm(n./v.)農場、耕種\nrice farmer 稻農\nlocal farmer 在地農民\nThe farmer gets up very early.\n(這位農夫起得很早。)\nWe buy fresh fruit from local farmers.\n(我們向在地農民買新鮮水果。)"],["fast","fast(adv./adj.)快的、快速地\n(無詞性變化)\nfast food 速食\nrun fast 跑得快\nHe can run very fast.\n(他可以跑得非常快。)\nDon't eat too much fast food.\n(不要吃太多速食。)"],["fat","fat(n./adj.)肥胖的、脂肪\nfatty(adj.)含脂肪的\nget fat 變胖\nlow fat 低脂\nMy cat is getting fat.\n(我的貓越來越胖了。)\nThis milk is low in fat.\n(這種牛奶脂肪含量低。)"],["father","father(n.)父親\n(無詞性變化)\nFather's Day 父親節\nlike father, like son 有其父必有其子\nMy father cooks dinner on weekends.\n(我爸爸週末會煮晚餐。)\nWe gave Dad a card on Father's Day.\n(我們在父親節送爸爸一張卡片。)"],["feed","feed(v./n.)餵食、飼料\n(無詞性變化)\nfeed the dog 餵狗\nfeed on 以……為食\nCan you feed the fish for me?\n(你可以幫我餵魚嗎？)\nPandas feed on bamboo.\n(貓熊以竹子為食。)"],["feel","feel(v./n.)感覺、覺得、觸感\nfeeling(n.)感覺、感情\nfeel like 想要\nfeel better 感覺好些\nI feel tired after school.\n(放學後我覺得很累。)\nDo you feel like going out tonight?\n(你今晚想出去嗎？)"],["festival","festival(n.)節日、慶典\nfestive(adj.)節慶的\nMoon Festival 中秋節\nmusic festival 音樂節\nWe eat mooncakes at the Moon Festival.\n(我們在中秋節吃月餅。)\nThe music festival starts this Friday.\n(音樂節這週五開始。)"],["few","few(adj./pron.)很少的、少數\nfewer(adj.)較少的\na few 一些、幾個\nquite a few 相當多\nI have a few friends in Tainan.\n(我在台南有幾個朋友。)\nFew students were late today.\n(今天很少學生遲到。)"],["fight","fight(v./n.)打架、奮戰、爭吵\nfighter(n.)戰士、鬥士\nfight for 為……而戰\nhave a fight 吵架\nThe two boys had a fight at school.\n(那兩個男孩在學校打了一架。)\nWe must fight for our dreams.\n(我們必須為夢想奮鬥。)"],["file","file(n./v.)檔案、文件夾、歸檔\n(無詞性變化)\nsave a file 儲存檔案\nfile folder 文件夾\nDon't forget to save the file.\n(別忘了儲存檔案。)\nShe put the papers in a file.\n(她把文件放進資料夾。)"],["fill","fill(v./n.)填滿、裝滿\nfull(adj.)滿的\nfill in 填寫\nfill up 裝滿\nPlease fill in this form.\n(請填寫這張表格。)\nHe filled the bottle with water.\n(他把瓶子裝滿水。)"],["finally","finally(adv.)最後、終於\nfinal(adj.)最後的\nfinally arrive 終於抵達\nfinally finish 終於完成\nThe bus finally came after an hour.\n(公車等了一小時終於來了。)\nI finally finished my homework.\n(我終於寫完功課了。)"],["find","find(v./n.)找到、發現\nfinding(n.)發現、研究結果\nfind out 查明、發現\nfind it hard to 覺得……很難\nI can't find my keys.\n(我找不到我的鑰匙。)\nLet's find out the answer together.\n(我們一起找出答案吧。)"],["fine","fine(adj./adv./v./n.)好的、晴朗的、罰款\n(無詞性變化)\nfine weather 好天氣\npay a fine 繳罰款\nI'm fine, thank you.\n(我很好，謝謝。)\nHe had to pay a fine for parking there.\n(他因為在那裡停車而被罰款。)"],["finger","finger(n./v.)手指、用手指觸摸\n(無詞性變化)\ncross my fingers 祈求好運\nlittle finger 小指\nShe cut her finger with a knife.\n(她被刀子割傷了手指。)\nI'll keep my fingers crossed for you.\n(我會為你祈求好運。)"],["finish","finish(v./n.)完成、結束、終點\nfinished(adj.)完成的\nfinish homework 完成功課\nfinish line 終點線\nDid you finish your dinner?\n(你吃完晚餐了嗎？)\nHe was the first to cross the finish line.\n(他第一個衝過終點線。)"],["fire","fire(n./v.)火、火災、開除\nfiery(adj.)火熱的\ncatch fire 著火\nfire station 消防局\nThe house caught fire last night.\n(那間房子昨晚失火了。)\nCall 119 if you see a fire.\n(如果看到火災請打119。)"],["first","first(n./adv./adj.)第一、首先、最初\nfirstly(adv.)首先\nat first 起初\nfirst of all 首先\nAt first, I didn't like the food.\n(起初我不喜歡這個食物。)\nFirst of all, wash your hands.\n(首先，洗手。)"],["fish","fish(n./v.)魚、釣魚\nfishing(n.)釣魚、漁業\ngo fishing 去釣魚\nfish market 魚市場\nWe went fishing by the river.\n(我們去河邊釣魚。)\nI don't like to eat fish.\n(我不喜歡吃魚。)"],["floor","floor(n./v.)地板、樓層\n(無詞性變化)\non the floor 在地板上\nfirst floor 一樓\nMy bag is on the floor.\n(我的包包在地板上。)\nOur classroom is on the third floor.\n(我們的教室在三樓。)"],["flower","flower(n./v.)花、開花\nflowery(adj.)多花的、華麗的\nflower shop 花店\na bunch of flowers 一束花\nHe gave his mom some flowers.\n(他送媽媽一些花。)\nThe flowers in the park are beautiful.\n(公園裡的花很漂亮。)"],["fly","fly(v./n.)飛、搭飛機、蒼蠅\nflight(n.)班機、飛行\nfly a kite 放風箏\nfly to 飛往\nBirds can fly high in the sky.\n(鳥能在天空高飛。)\nWe will fly to Tokyo next week.\n(我們下週要飛去東京。)"],["follow","follow(v.)跟隨、遵守、追蹤\nfollower(n.)追隨者、追蹤者\nfollowing(adj.)接下來的\nfollow the rules 遵守規則\nfollow me 跟我來\nPlease follow the school rules.\n(請遵守校規。)\nFollow me to the library.\n(跟我到圖書館。)"],["food","food(n.)食物\n(無詞性變化)\nfast food 速食\njunk food 垃圾食物\nTaiwan is famous for its street food.\n(台灣以街頭小吃聞名。)\nJunk food is bad for your health.\n(垃圾食物對健康有害。)"],["fool","fool(n./v.)傻瓜、愚弄\nfoolish(adj.)愚蠢的\nApril Fool's Day 愚人節\nmake a fool of 愚弄\nDon't be a fool.\n(別當傻瓜。)\nHe tried to fool me on April Fool's Day.\n(他在愚人節想捉弄我。)"],["foot","foot(n./v.)腳、英尺、支付(帳單)\nfeet(n.)腳(複數)\non foot 步行\nfoot the bill 付帳\nI go to school on foot.\n(我走路上學。)\nMy left foot hurts.\n(我的左腳很痛。)"],["for","for(prep./conj.)為了、給、因為\n(無詞性變化)\nfor example 例如\nfor a while 一會兒\nThis gift is for you.\n(這份禮物是給你的。)\nI waited for him for an hour.\n(我等了他一個小時。)"],["foreign","foreign(adj.)外國的\nforeigner(n.)外國人\nforeign language 外語\nforeign country 外國\nEnglish is a foreign language for us.\n(英文對我們來說是外語。)\nShe wants to study in a foreign country.\n(她想去國外讀書。)"],["foreigner","foreigner(n.)外國人\nforeign(adj.)外國的\ntalk to a foreigner 和外國人交談\nmany foreigners 許多外國人\nMany foreigners visit Taipei every year.\n(每年有許多外國人到台北觀光。)\nI helped a foreigner find the MRT station.\n(我幫一位外國人找到捷運站。)"],["forget","forget(v.)忘記\nforgetful(adj.)健忘的\nforget to do 忘記去做\nnever forget 永遠不會忘記\nDon't forget to bring your book.\n(別忘了帶你的書。)\nI will never forget this trip.\n(我永遠不會忘記這趟旅行。)"],["fork","fork(n.)叉子、岔路\n(無詞性變化)\nknife and fork 刀叉\na fork in the road 岔路\nCan I have a fork, please?\n(可以給我一支叉子嗎？)\nHe eats noodles with a fork.\n(他用叉子吃麵。)"],["free","free(adj./v./adv.)自由的、免費的、有空的、釋放\nfreedom(n.)自由\nfreely(adv.)自由地\nfree time 空閒時間\nfor free 免費\nWhat do you do in your free time?\n(你空閒時做什麼？)\nThe drinks are free today.\n(今天飲料免費。)"],["fresh","fresh(adj.)新鮮的、清新的\nfreshly(adv.)剛剛、新近地\nfresh air 新鮮空氣\nfresh fruit 新鮮水果\nLet's go out for some fresh air.\n(我們出去呼吸新鮮空氣吧。)\nThe fish here is very fresh.\n(這裡的魚很新鮮。)"],["friend","friend(n.)朋友\nfriendship(n.)友誼\nbest friend 最好的朋友\nmake friends 交朋友\nAmy is my best friend.\n(艾美是我最好的朋友。)\nIt's easy for him to make friends.\n(他很容易交到朋友。)"],["friendly","friendly(adj.)友善的\nfriend(n.)朋友\nbe friendly to 對……友善\neco-friendly 環保的\nThe people here are very friendly.\n(這裡的人非常友善。)\nShe is always friendly to new students.\n(她總是對新同學很友善。)"],["frog","frog(n.)青蛙\n(無詞性變化)\ngreen frog 綠色青蛙\na frog jumps 青蛙跳\nA frog jumped into the pond.\n(一隻青蛙跳進池塘。)\nWe heard frogs singing at night.\n(我們晚上聽到青蛙在叫。)"],["from","from(prep.)從、來自\n(無詞性變化)\nfrom A to B 從A到B\ncome from 來自\nWhere are you from?\n(你從哪裡來？)\nI walk from home to school.\n(我從家裡走路到學校。)"],["front","front(adj./n.)前面(的)、正面\n(無詞性變化)\nin front of 在……前面\nfront door 前門\nThere is a tree in front of my house.\n(我家前面有一棵樹。)\nPlease sit in the front row.\n(請坐在第一排。)"],["fruit","fruit(n.)水果、成果\nfruitful(adj.)富有成果的\nfresh fruit 新鮮水果\nfruit juice 果汁\nEat more fruit and vegetables.\n(多吃蔬菜水果。)\nMangoes are my favorite fruit.\n(芒果是我最喜歡的水果。)"],["full","full(adj.)滿的、吃飽的\nfully(adv.)完全地\nbe full of 充滿\nfull name 全名\nI'm full. I can't eat any more.\n(我吃飽了，再也吃不下了。)\nThe bus is full of students.\n(公車上擠滿了學生。)"],["fun","fun(n.)樂趣、好玩\nfunny(adj.)好笑的\nhave fun 玩得開心\nfor fun 為了好玩\nWe had a lot of fun at the beach.\n(我們在海邊玩得很開心。)\nLearning English can be fun.\n(學英文可以很有趣。)"],["funny","funny(adj.)好笑的、奇怪的\nfun(n.)樂趣\na funny story 好笑的故事\nlook funny 看起來很滑稽\nHe told us a funny story.\n(他跟我們說了一個好笑的故事。)\nThat movie was really funny.\n(那部電影真的很好笑。)"],["future","future(n./adj.)未來(的)、將來\n(無詞性變化)\nin the future 在未來\nfuture plans 未來計畫\nWhat do you want to be in the future?\n(你將來想做什麼？)\nLet's talk about our future plans.\n(我們來談談未來的計畫。)"],["game","game(n.)遊戲、比賽\n(無詞性變化)\nplay games 玩遊戲\nvideo game 電玩遊戲\nWe won the basketball game.\n(我們贏了籃球比賽。)\nHe plays video games after dinner.\n(他晚餐後玩電玩。)"],["garden","garden(n./v.)花園、園藝\ngardener(n.)園丁\ngardening(n.)園藝\nflower garden 花園\nin the garden 在花園裡\nMy mom grows roses in the garden.\n(我媽媽在花園裡種玫瑰。)\nThe kids are playing in the garden.\n(孩子們在花園裡玩。)"],["gate","gate(n.)大門、登機門\n(無詞性變化)\nschool gate 校門\nboarding gate 登機門\nLet's meet at the school gate.\n(我們在校門口見。)\nOur plane leaves from Gate 5.\n(我們的飛機從5號登機門出發。)"],["get","get(v.)得到、變得、抵達\n(無詞性變化)\nget up 起床\nget home 到家\nI get up at six every day.\n(我每天六點起床。)\nIt's getting cold outside.\n(外面變冷了。)"],["ghost","ghost(n.)鬼、幽靈\nghostly(adj.)幽靈般的\nghost story 鬼故事\nGhost Month 鬼月\nDo you believe in ghosts?\n(你相信有鬼嗎？)\nHe likes to tell ghost stories at night.\n(他喜歡在晚上講鬼故事。)"],["giant","giant(adj./n.)巨大的、巨人\n(無詞性變化)\ngiant panda 大貓熊\na giant tree 巨大的樹\nWe saw a giant panda at the zoo.\n(我們在動物園看到大貓熊。)\nThe giant lived in a castle.\n(那個巨人住在城堡裡。)"],["gift","gift(n.)禮物、天賦\ngifted(adj.)有天賦的\nbirthday gift 生日禮物\na gift for 對……的天賦\nThank you for the nice gift.\n(謝謝你的好禮物。)\nShe has a gift for music.\n(她有音樂天分。)"],["girl","girl(n.)女孩\ngirlfriend(n.)女朋友\nlittle girl 小女孩\ngirls' school 女校\nThe little girl is crying.\n(那個小女孩在哭。)\nThere are twenty girls in our class.\n(我們班上有二十個女生。)"],["give","give(v.)給、提供\n(無詞性變化)\ngive up 放棄\ngive back 歸還\nPlease give me a pen.\n(請給我一支筆。)\nNever give up on your dreams.\n(永遠不要放棄夢想。)"],["glad","glad(adj.)高興的\ngladly(adv.)樂意地\nbe glad to 很高興……\nglad to hear 很高興聽到\nI'm glad to see you again.\n(很高興再次見到你。)\nShe was glad to hear the good news.\n(她很高興聽到這個好消息。)"],["glass","glass(n.)玻璃、玻璃杯\n(無詞性變化)\na glass of water 一杯水\nbroken glass 碎玻璃\nCan I have a glass of water?\n(可以給我一杯水嗎？)\nBe careful of the broken glass.\n(小心碎玻璃。)"],["glasses","glasses(n.)眼鏡\nglass(n.)玻璃、玻璃杯\nwear glasses 戴眼鏡\na pair of glasses 一副眼鏡\nMy brother wears glasses.\n(我哥哥戴眼鏡。)\nI can't find my glasses.\n(我找不到我的眼鏡。)"],["glove(s)","glove(n.)手套\ngloves(n.)手套(複數)\na pair of gloves 一副手套\nwear gloves 戴手套\nWear your gloves. It's cold.\n(戴上手套，天氣很冷。)\nI lost one of my gloves.\n(我弄丟了一隻手套。)"],["go","go(v./n.)去、走、嘗試\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to school 上學\nhave a go 試一試\nI go to school by bus.\n(我搭公車上學。)\nLet's go to the park.\n(我們去公園吧。)"],["god/goddess","god(n.)神、上帝\ngoddess(n.)女神\nOh my God 我的天啊\nGreek gods 希臘眾神\nMany people pray to God.\n(許多人向上帝禱告。)\nShe looks like a goddess in that dress.\n(她穿那件洋裝看起來像女神。)"],["good","good(adj./adv./n.)好的、擅長的、益處\ngoodness(n.)善良\nbe good at 擅長\ngood luck 祝好運\nShe is good at math.\n(她數學很好。)\nGood luck on your test!\n(考試順利！)"],["goodbye","goodbye(n.)再見、告別\nbye(n.)再見(口語)\nsay goodbye 說再見\ngoodbye party 歡送會\nIt's time to say goodbye.\n(該說再見了。)\nWe had a goodbye party for our teacher.\n(我們為老師辦了歡送會。)"],["grade","grade(n./v.)年級、成績、評分\n(無詞性變化)\ngood grades 好成績\ntenth grade 十年級\nShe always gets good grades.\n(她總是拿到好成績。)\nMy sister is in the fifth grade.\n(我妹妹讀五年級。)"],["grandfather","grandfather(n.)祖父、外祖父\ngrandpa(n.)爺爺、外公(口語)\nvisit grandfather 探望祖父\nmy late grandfather 我已故的祖父\nMy grandfather is eighty years old.\n(我爺爺八十歲了。)\nI visit my grandfather every weekend.\n(我每週末去探望爺爺。)"],["grandmother","grandmother(n.)祖母、外祖母\ngrandma(n.)奶奶、外婆(口語)\nlive with grandmother 和祖母同住\ngrandmother's cooking 祖母的手藝\nMy grandmother makes great dumplings.\n(我奶奶包的水餃很好吃。)\nI live with my grandmother.\n(我和外婆住在一起。)"],["grass","grass(n.)草、草地\ngrassy(adj.)長滿草的\ncut the grass 割草\ngreen grass 綠草\nThe children are sitting on the grass.\n(孩子們坐在草地上。)\nMy dad cuts the grass every Sunday.\n(我爸爸每週日割草。)"],["gray","gray(adj./n./v.)灰色(的)、變白\ngrey(adj./n.)灰色(英式拼法)\ngray hair 白髮\ngray sky 灰暗的天空\nMy grandpa has gray hair.\n(我爺爺有白頭髮。)\nThe sky is gray today.\n(今天天空灰濛濛的。)"],["great","great(adj./n.)很棒的、偉大的、大的\ngreatly(adv.)大大地\na great idea 好主意\na great man 偉人\nThat's a great idea!\n(那是個好主意！)\nWe had a great time at the party.\n(我們在派對上玩得很愉快。)"],["green","green(adj./n./v.)綠色(的)、環保的\n(無詞性變化)\ngreen tea 綠茶\ngreen light 綠燈\nWait until the light turns green.\n(等到變綠燈。)\nI like green tea without sugar.\n(我喜歡無糖綠茶。)"],["ground","ground(n./v.)地面、場地、禁足\n(無詞性變化)\non the ground 在地上\nplayground 遊樂場、操場\nThe ball fell to the ground.\n(球掉到地上。)\nHe sat on the ground to rest.\n(他坐在地上休息。)"],["group","group(n./v.)群體、組、分組\n(無詞性變化)\nin groups 分組\na group of 一群\nPlease work in groups of four.\n(請四人一組合作。)\nA group of students is waiting outside.\n(一群學生在外面等。)"],["grow","grow(v.)成長、種植、變得\ngrowth(n.)成長\ngrow up 長大\ngrow vegetables 種菜\nI want to be a doctor when I grow up.\n(我長大後想當醫生。)\nMy grandma grows vegetables at home.\n(我奶奶在家種菜。)"],["guess","guess(v./n.)猜測\n(無詞性變化)\nguess what 你猜怎麼著\nmake a guess 猜一猜\nGuess what? I won the game!\n(你猜怎麼著？我贏了比賽！)\nCan you guess my age?\n(你能猜到我的年紀嗎？)"],["guitar","guitar(n.)吉他\nguitarist(n.)吉他手\nplay the guitar 彈吉他\nelectric guitar 電吉他\nHe plays the guitar very well.\n(他吉他彈得很好。)\nI want to learn the guitar.\n(我想學吉他。)"],["guy","guy(n.)傢伙、男人\nguys(n.)大家、各位(口語)\na nice guy 好人\nyou guys 你們\nHe is a really nice guy.\n(他真的是個好人。)\nHi, guys! Let's start the class.\n(大家好！我們開始上課吧。)"],["habit","habit(n.)習慣\nhabitual(adj.)習慣性的\nhabitually(adv.)習慣地\ngood habit 好習慣\nbreak a habit 戒掉習慣\nReading every night is a good habit.\n(每天晚上閱讀是一個好習慣。)\nIt is hard to break a bad habit.\n(改掉壞習慣很難。)"],["hair","hair(n.)頭髮、毛髮\nhairy(adj.)多毛的\ncomb hair 梳頭\nlong hair 長髮\nShe has long, dark hair.\n(她留著黑色的長髮。)\nRemember to comb your hair before going out.\n(出門前記得梳頭。)"],["half","half(n./adv./adj.)一半、二分之一\nhalve(v.)減半\nhalf an hour 半小時\ncut in half 切成兩半\nWe waited for half an hour.\n(我們等了半個小時。)\nPlease cut the apple in half.\n(請把蘋果切成兩半。)"],["ham","ham(n.)火腿\nham sandwich 火腿三明治\neggs and ham 蛋與火腿\nI had a ham sandwich for lunch.\n(我午餐吃了一個火腿三明治。)\nShe likes to eat eggs and ham in the morning.\n(她喜歡在早上吃蛋和火腿。)"],["hand","hand(n./v.)手、交給\nhandful(n.)一把、少數\nshake hands 握手\nby hand 手工製作\nThey shook hands when they met.\n(他們見面時握了手。)\nThis bag was made by hand.\n(這個包包是手工製作的。)"],["hang","hang(v.)懸掛、吊\nhanger(n.)衣架\nhang up 掛斷(電話)\nhang out 閒逛\nPlease hang your coat on the hook.\n(請把你的外套掛在鉤子上。)\nDon't hang up the phone yet.\n(先不要掛斷電話。)"],["happen","happen(v.)發生、碰巧\nhappening(n.)發生的事\nhappen to 發生在...身上\nwhat happened 發生了什麼事\nI happened to see him at the park.\n(我碰巧在公園見到他。)\nTell me what happened yesterday.\n(告訴我昨天發生了什麼事。)"],["happy","happy(adj.)快樂的、幸福的\nhappiness(n.)快樂\nhappily(adv.)快樂地\nhappy ending 快樂結局\nfeel happy 感到高興\nEveryone wants a happy ending.\n(每個人都想要一個快樂的結局。)\nI feel happy to see you again.\n(再次見到你我感到很高興。)"],["hard","hard(adj./adv.)辛苦的、困難的、努力地\nharden(v.)變硬\nwork hard 努力工作\nhard work 艱苦的工作\nHe works very hard to support his family.\n(他工作非常努力以養活家人。)\nPassing the exam requires a lot of hard work.\n(通過考試需要大量的努力。)"],["hat","hat(n.)帽子\nwear a hat 戴帽子\ntake off a hat 脫下帽子\nHe is wearing a straw hat.\n(他戴著一頂草帽。)\nShe took off her hat when she entered the room.\n(她進屋時脫下了帽子。)"],["hate","hate(v./n.)憎恨、討厭\nhatred(n.)仇恨\nhate to do something 討厭做某事\nhate doing something 討厭做某事\nI hate to see you so sad.\n(我討厭看到你這麼難過。)\nShe hates doing the dishes after dinner.\n(她討厭飯後洗碗。)"],["have","have(aux./v.)有、助動詞\nhave to 必須\nhave breakfast 吃早餐\nI have to go to school now.\n(我現在必須去學校。)\nWe had breakfast at seven o'clock.\n(我們七點鐘吃早餐。)"],["he (him, his, himself)","he(pron.)他\nhim(pron.)他(受格)\nhis(pron.)他的\nhimself(pron.)他自己\nhe says 他說\nby himself 他獨自\nHe is my brother.\n(他是我哥哥。)\nHe did the homework by himself.\n(他自己完成了功課。)"],["head","head(n./v.)頭、前往\nheading(n.)標題\nshake one's head 搖頭\nhead for 前往\nHe shook his head in disagreement.\n(他搖搖頭表示不同意。)\nWe are heading for the airport.\n(我們正前往機場。)"],["headache","headache(n.)頭痛、令人頭痛的事\nhave a headache 頭痛\na splitting headache 劇烈的頭痛\nI have a terrible headache today.\n(我今天頭痛得很厲害。)\nStress can often cause a headache.\n(壓力通常會導致頭痛。)"],["health","health(n.)健康\nhealthy(adj.)健康的\nin good health 身體健康\npublic health 公共衛生\nRegular exercise is good for your health.\n(規律運動對你的健康有益。)\nMy grandfather is still in good health.\n(我祖父身體仍然很健康。)"],["healthy","healthy(adj.)健康的\nhealth(n.)健康\nhealthily(adv.)健康地\nhealthy lifestyle 健康的生活方式\nhealthy diet 健康飲食\nShe maintains a very healthy lifestyle.\n(她保持著非常健康的生活方式。)\nEating vegetables is part of a healthy diet.\n(吃蔬菜是健康飲食的一部分。)"],["hear","hear(v.)聽見\nhearing(n.)聽覺\nhear of 聽說過\nhear from 收到某人的消息\nI have never heard of this movie.\n(我從未聽說過這部電影。)\nI hope to hear from you soon.\n(我希望能儘快收到你的消息。)"],["heart","heart(n.)心、心臟、中心\nhearty(adj.)熱誠的\nheart attack 心臟病發作\nlearn by heart 背誦\nYou should learn the poem by heart.\n(你應該把這首詩背下來。)\nExercise helps prevent a heart attack.\n(運動有助於預防心臟病發作。)"],["heat","heat(n./v.)熱度、加熱\nheater(n.)暖氣機\nheat up 加熱\nsummer heat 夏天的炎熱\nHeat the milk in the microwave.\n(在微波爐裡加熱牛奶。)\nI can't stand the summer heat anymore.\n(我再也受不了夏天的炎熱了。)"],["heavy","heavy(adj.)重的、沉重的\nheavily(adv.)重地、大量地\nheavy rain 大雨\nheavy traffic 交通擁擠\nBe careful, that box is very heavy.\n(當心，那個箱子很重。)\nWe were late because of heavy traffic.\n(因為交通擁擠我們遲到了。)"],["height","height(n.)高度、身高\nhigh(adj.)高的\nreach a height 達到...高度\nat the height of 在...的高峰期\nHe is six feet in height.\n(他的身高是六英尺。)\nShe was at the height of her career.\n(她當時正處於事業的高峰期。)"],["hello","hello(n.)哈囉、你好\nsay hello 說哈囉\na friendly hello 一聲友好的問候\nShe waved and said hello to me.\n(她揮揮手向我問好。)\nHe gave me a friendly hello as I walked by.\n(當我走過時，他親切地向我打了聲招呼。)"],["help","help(v./n.)幫助\nhelpful(adj.)有幫助的\nhelp with 幫助做某事\ncan't help 忍不住\nCan you help me with my homework?\n(你能幫我做功課嗎？)\nI can't help laughing at his jokes.\n(聽了他的笑話我忍不住笑了起來。)"],["helpful","helpful(adj.)有幫助的、有益的\nhelp(n./v.)幫助\nunhelpful(adj.)無助的\nhelpful advice 有用的建議\nbe helpful to 對...有幫助\nThe staff were very helpful and friendly.\n(工作人員非常熱心且友好。)\nThis book is helpful to English learners.\n(這本書對英語學習者很有幫助。)"],["hen","hen(n.)母雞\nrooster(n.)公雞\na mother hen 母雞\nlay an egg 下蛋\nThe hen is protecting her chicks.\n(母雞正在保護她的雛雞。)\nA hen can lay one egg a day.\n(母雞每天可以產一個蛋。)"],["here","here(adv./n.)這裡\naround here 這附近\nhere and there 到處\nIs there a supermarket around here?\n(這附近有超市嗎？)\nI've been looking for my keys here and there.\n(我一直在到處找我的鑰匙。)"],["hide","hide(v.)躲藏、隱瞞\nhidden(adj.)隱藏的\nhide from 躲避\nhide and seek 躲貓貓\nThey played hide and seek in the garden.\n(他們在花園裡玩躲貓貓。)\nYou can't hide from the truth forever.\n(你不能永遠逃避真相。)"],["high","high(adj./adv./n.)高的、高地\nheight(n.)高度\nhigh school 高中\nhigh speed 高速\nShe is a student in high school.\n(她是一名高中生。)\nThe train is traveling at a very high speed.\n(火車正以極高的速度行駛。)"],["hill","hill(n.)小山、丘陵\nhilly(adj.)多丘陵的\nup the hill 往山上\ndown the hill 往山下\nWe walked slowly up the hill.\n(我們慢慢地走上山。)\nThere is a small church on top of the hill.\n(山頂上有一座小教堂。)"],["history","history(n.)歷史\nhistorical(adj.)歷史的\nworld history 世界歷史\nmake history 創造歷史\nShe is very interested in ancient history.\n(她對古代歷史非常感興趣。)\nThis invention will make history.\n(這項發明將創造歷史。)"],["hit","hit(v./n.)打、打擊、受歡迎的人或物\nhit the target 擊中目標\na big hit 非常受歡迎\nHe hit the ball over the fence.\n(他把球打過了圍欄。)\nThe new song became a big hit.\n(這首新歌變得很受歡迎。)"],["hobby","hobby(n.)業餘愛好、嗜好\nhobbies(複數)\nfavorite hobby 最喜歡的愛好\npursue a hobby 從事愛好\nMy favorite hobby is playing guitar.\n(我最喜歡的愛好是彈吉他。)\nIt is important to have a hobby in your free time.\n(空閒時間有個愛好很重要。)"],["hold","hold(v./n.)握住、舉行\nholder(n.)持有者\nhold a meeting 舉行會議\nhold one's breath 屏息\nThey will hold a meeting tomorrow morning.\n(他們明天早上將舉行會議。)\nHe held his breath in excitement.\n(他興奮地屏住了呼吸。)"],["holiday","holiday(n.)假日、節日\nholidays(複數)\npublic holiday 國定假日\non holiday 在度假\nNext Monday is a public holiday.\n(下週一是以國定假日。)\nThey are going to Japan on holiday.\n(他們要去日本度假。)"],["home","home(n./adv./v./adj.)家、在家的\nhomework(n.)功課\nfeel at home 感覺自在\ngo home 回家\nI want to go home now.\n(我現在想回家。)\nPlease make yourself at home.\n(請不要客氣，當作在自己家。)"],["homework","homework(n.)功課、家庭作業\nhousework(n.)家事\ndo homework 做功課\nassign homework 布置作業\nI have a lot of homework to do tonight.\n(我今晚有很多功課要做。)\nThe teacher assigned some homework over the weekend.\n(老師布置了一些週末作業。)"],["honest","honest(adj.)誠實的\nhonesty(n.)誠實\nhonestly(adv.)誠實地\nto be honest 老實說\nan honest man 一個誠實的人\nTo be honest, I don't like this idea.\n(老實說，我不喜歡這個主意。)\nHe is known for being an honest man.\n(他以誠實著稱。)"],["honey","honey(n.)蜂蜜、親愛的(稱呼)\nhoneymoon(n.)蜜月\nsweet as honey 像蜂蜜一樣甜\nhoney bee 蜜蜂\nShe likes to add honey to her tea.\n(她喜歡在茶裡加蜂蜜。)\nDon't worry, honey, everything will be fine.\n(別擔心，親愛的，一切都會好起來的。)"],["hope","hope(v./n.)希望\nhopeful(adj.)充滿希望的\nhope for 希望得到\nlose hope 失去希望\nWe hope for better weather tomorrow.\n(我們希望明天天氣會好一點。)\nNever lose hope, no matter how hard it is.\n(無論多麼艱難，永遠不要失去希望。)"],["horse","horse(n.)馬\nride a horse 騎馬\nhorse racing 賽馬\nHe learned how to ride a horse.\n(他學會了如何騎馬。)\nThere are many horses on the farm.\n(農場裡有很多馬。)"],["hospital","hospital(n.)醫院\nhospitalize(v.)住院\nin hospital 住院(英式)\ngo to the hospital 去醫院\nHe had to go to the hospital after the accident.\n(事故發生後他不得不去醫院。)\nShe works as a nurse in a large hospital.\n(她在一家大醫院當護士。)"],["hot","hot(adj.)熱的、辣的\nheat(n.)熱度\nhot weather 炎熱的天氣\nhot sauce 辣醬\nIt is very hot outside today.\n(今天外面非常熱。)\nDo you like to eat hot and spicy food?\n(你喜歡吃又熱又辣的食物嗎？)"],["hotel","hotel(n.)旅館、飯店\nmotel(n.)汽車旅館\nbook a hotel 預訂飯店\nfive-star hotel 五星級飯店\nWe booked a hotel room for our vacation.\n(我們為假期預訂了一間飯店房間。)\nThey are staying in a five-star hotel.\n(他們正住在一間五星級飯店裡。)"],["hour","hour(n.)小時\nhourly(adj./adv.)每小時的\nhalf an hour 半小時\nrush hour 交通尖峰時段\nI spent an hour finishing the work.\n(我花了一個小時完成這項工作。)\nTraffic is always heavy during rush hour.\n(尖峰時段的交通總是很擁擠。)"],["house","house(n./v.)房屋、安置\nhousehold(n.)住戶\nhousewarming party 喬遷聚會\nlive in a house 住在房子裡\nThey are building a new house.\n(他們正在蓋一棟新房子。)\nShe invited us to her housewarming party.\n(她邀請我們參加她的喬遷聚會。)"],["housewife","housewife(n.)家庭主婦\nhousewives(複數)\na full-time housewife 全職家庭主婦\nhousehusband(n.)家庭主夫\nShe decided to be a housewife after her baby was born.\n(孩子出生後她決定當家庭主婦。)\nMy mother is a busy housewife.\n(我媽媽是一位忙碌的家庭主婦。)"],["how","how(adv.)如何、多麼\nhowever(adv.)然而\nhow are you 你好嗎\nhow many 多少(數量)\nHow are you doing today?\n(你今天過得怎麼樣？)\nHow many students are there in your class?\n(你們班有多少學生？)"],["however","however(adv.)然而、無論如何\nhow(adv.)如何\nhowever hard 無論多麼努力\nhowever much 無論多少\nHe was tired; however, he kept working.\n(他很累；然而，他繼續工作。)\nHowever hard she tried, she couldn't open the jar.\n(無論她多麼努力，都打不開那個罐子。)"],["hundred","hundred(n./adj.)一百\nhundreds of 數以百計的\none hundred 一百\nThere are over a hundred people in the hall.\n(大廳裡有一百多人。)\nHundreds of students attended the speech.\n(數百名學生參加了這場演講。)"],["hungry","hungry(adj.)飢餓的\nhunger(n.)飢餓\nfeel hungry 感到肚子餓\ngo hungry 挨餓\nI feel hungry after playing soccer.\n(踢完足球後我感到肚子餓。)\nNo child should have to go hungry.\n(不應該有孩子需要挨餓。)"],["hurt","hurt(v./n.)受傷、痛\nhurt oneself 受傷\nfeel hurt 感到傷心\nMy legs hurt after the long walk.\n(長途跋涉後我的腿很痛。)\nHe didn't mean to hurt your feelings.\n(他不是故意要傷你的心。)"],["husband","husband(n.)丈夫\nwife(n.)妻子\na loving husband 一位慈愛的丈夫\nhusband and wife 夫妻\nHer husband works in a bank.\n(她的丈夫在銀行工作。)\nThey are a very happy husband and wife.\n(他們是一對非常幸福的夫妻。)"],["I (me, my, mine, myself)","I(pron.)我\nme(pron.)我(受格)\nmy(pron.)我的\nmine(pron.)我的(東西)\nmyself(pron.)我自己\nI think 我認為\nby myself 我獨自\nI am a high school student.\n(我是一名高中生。)\nThis book is mine, not yours.\n(這本書是我的，不是你的。)"],["ice","ice(n.)冰\nicy(adj.)冰冷的\nice cream 冰淇淋\nice cube 冰塊\nWould you like some ice in your drink?\n(你的飲料裡要加點冰嗎？)\nWe went to get some ice cream after dinner.\n(我們飯後去吃冰淇淋。)"],["idea","idea(n.)想法、主意\nideal(adj.)理想的\nhave no idea 不知道\ngood idea 好主意\nI have no idea where my phone is.\n(我不知道我的手機在哪裡。)\nThat sounds like a great idea!\n(那聽起來是個棒透了的主意！)"],["if","if(conj.)如果、是否\nas if 彷彿\neven if 即使\nIf it rains tomorrow, the game will be canceled.\n(如果明天下雨，比賽將會取消。)\nLet me know if you need any help.\n(如果你需要幫助請告訴我。)"],["important","important(adj.)重要的\nimportance(n.)重要性\nplay an important role 扮演重要角色\nmost important 最重要的\nIt is important to brush your teeth every day.\n(每天刷牙是很重要的。)\nFamily is the most important thing to her.\n(家庭對她來說是最重要的。)"],["in","in(prep./adv./adj.)在...裡面\ninside(adv./prep.)在裡面\nin the morning 在早上\nin time 及時\nThe keys are in my bag.\n(鑰匙在我的包包裡。)\nWe arrived just in time for the movie.\n(我們剛好及時趕上電影。)"],["inch","inch(n.)英吋\ninches(複數)\nsquare inch 平方英吋\nby an inch 以些微之差\nThere are 12 inches in a foot.\n(一英尺有12英吋。)\nHe won the race by only an inch.\n(他僅以一英吋之差贏得了比賽。)"],["insect","insect(n.)昆蟲\ninsecticide(n.)殺蟲劑\ninsect bite 昆蟲叮咬\na tiny insect 一隻微小的昆蟲\nAn ant is a tiny insect.\n(螞蟻是一種微小的昆蟲。)\nBe careful not to get an insect bite.\n(當心不要被昆蟲叮咬。)"],["inside","inside(prep./adv./n./adj.)在...裡面\noutside(adv./prep.)在外面\ngo inside 進去\ninside out 翻過來\nIt started raining, so we went inside.\n(開始下雨了，所以我們進到了室內。)\nYou are wearing your shirt inside out.\n(你的衣服穿反了。)"],["interest","interest(n./v.)興趣、使感興趣\ninteresting(adj.)有趣的\ninterested(adj.)感興趣的\nshow interest in 對...表現出興趣\na sense of interest 興趣感\nHe showed no interest in the project.\n(他對這個企劃沒有表現出興趣。)\nGeography has always interested me.\n(地理總是能引起我的興趣。)"],["interested","interested(adj.)感興趣的\ninterest(n./v.)興趣\nbe interested in 對...感興趣\ninterested party 利害關係人\nAre you interested in learning Chinese?\n(你有興趣學中文嗎？)\nI am interested in buying this car.\n(我有興趣買這輛車。)"],["interesting","interesting(adj.)有趣的\ninterest(n./v.)興趣\nan interesting story 一個有趣的故事\nfind something interesting 覺得某事有趣\nI found the book very interesting.\n(我覺得這本書非常有趣。)\nHe told us an interesting story about his trip.\n(他跟我們講了一個關於他旅行的有趣故事。)"],["interview","interview(n./v.)面試、採訪\ninterviewer(n.)面試官\njob interview 工作面試\nconduct an interview 進行採訪\nI have a job interview tomorrow.\n(我明天有一個工作面試。)\nThe reporter will interview the famous singer.\n(記者將採訪那位著名的歌手。)"],["into","into(prep.)進入、到...裡面\ngo into 進入\nget into trouble 陷入麻煩\nHe walked into the room quietly.\n(他悄悄地走進了房間。)\nDon't get into trouble at school.\n(在學校不要惹麻煩。)"],["invite","invite(v.)邀請\ninvitation(n.)邀請函\ninvite someone to 邀請某人去...\ninvite someone over 邀請某人來家裡\nThey invited us to their wedding party.\n(他們邀請我們參加他們的婚禮派對。)\nLet's invite them over for dinner.\n(我們邀請他們過來吃晚餐吧。)"],["island","island(n.)島嶼\nislander(n.)島上居民\ndesert island 荒島\nmain island 主島\nTaiwan is a beautiful island.\n(台灣是一個美麗的島嶼。)\nThey were stranded on a desert island.\n(他們受困在一個荒島上。)"],["it (its, itself)","it(pron.)它、牠\nits(pron.)它的、牠的\nitself(pron.)它自己\nit is 它是\nby itself 自動地、單獨地\nIt is raining outside.\n(外面在下雨。)\nThe dog is wagging its tail.\n(那隻狗在搖尾巴。)"],["item","item(n.)項目、一件物品\nitems(複數)\na list of items 項目清單\nnew item 新項目\nThere are several new items on the menu.\n(菜單上有幾個新項目。)\nPlease check every item on the list.\n(請檢查清單上的每一個項目。)"],["jacket","jacket(n.)夾克、外套\nwear a jacket 穿夾克\nleather jacket 皮夾克\nYou should wear a jacket because it's cold.\n(你應該穿件夾克，因為天氣很冷。)\nHe looks cool in his new leather jacket.\n(他穿著新的皮夾克看起來很帥。)"],["jeans","jeans(n.)牛仔褲\na pair of jeans 一條牛仔褲\nblue jeans 藍色牛仔褲\nShe likes to wear jeans and a T-shirt.\n(她喜歡穿牛仔褲和 T 恤。)\nI need to buy a new pair of jeans.\n(我需要買一條新的牛仔褲。)"],["job","job(n.)工作\nfull-time job 全職工作\napply for a job 申請工作\nHe is looking for a new job.\n(他正在找一份新工作。)\nApplying for a job can be a long process.\n(申請工作可能是一個漫長的過程。)"],["join","join(v./n.)加入、連結\njoin a club 加入社團\njoin in 參加、加入\nWould you like to join us for lunch?\n(你想和我們一起吃午餐嗎？)\nPlease join in the games with everyone.\n(請和大家一起參加遊戲。)"],["joke","joke(n./v.)笑話、開玩笑\njoker(n.)愛開玩笑的人\ntell a joke 講笑話\nmake a joke 開玩笑\nHe told a funny joke that made everyone laugh.\n(他講了一個有趣的笑話，逗得大家哈哈大笑。)\nDon't be angry, I was only making a joke.\n(別生氣，我只是在開玩笑。)"],["joy","joy(n.)喜悅、歡樂\njoyful(adj.)喜悅的\nfull of joy 充滿喜悅\nweep for joy 喜極而泣\nHer face was full of joy when she won.\n(當她贏的時候，臉上充滿了喜悅。)\nThey wept for joy after seeing each other.\n(見面後，他們喜極而泣。)"],["juice","juice(n.)果汁\njuicy(adj.)多汁的\norange juice 柳橙汁\nfruit juice 果汁\nI'd like a glass of orange juice, please.\n(請給我一杯柳橙汁。)\nFresh fruit juice is better than soda.\n(新鮮果汁比汽水好。)"],["jump","jump(v./n.)跳躍\njumper(n.)跳躍者、套頭毛衣\njump over 跳過\nhigh jump 跳高\nThe cat jumped over the fence.\n(那隻貓跳過了圍欄。)\nHe won the first prize in the high jump.\n(他獲得了跳高比賽的第一名。)"],["just","just(adv./adj.)剛剛、僅僅、公正的\njustice(n.)正義\njust now 剛才\njust in time 及時\nI have just finished my dinner.\n(我剛吃完晚飯。)\nWe arrived at the station just in time.\n(我們及時趕到了車站。)"],["keep","keep(v./n.)保持、保留\nkeeper(n.)保管人\nkeep in touch 保持聯繫\nkeep a promise 遵守諾言\nPlease keep the room clean.\n(請保持房間整潔。)\nYou should keep your promise to your friends.\n(你應該遵守對朋友的諾言。)"],["key","key(adj./n./v.)鑰匙、關鍵的\nkey point 關鍵點\nkey factor 關鍵因素\nI can't find my house keys.\n(我找不到我家的鑰匙。)\nHard work is the key to success.\n(努力是成功的關鍵。)"],["kick","kick(v./n.)踢\nkick off 開始、開球\ngive a kick 踢一腳\nHe kicked the soccer ball into the goal.\n(他把足球踢進了球門。)\nThe donkey gave the gate a hard kick.\n(驢子狠狠地踢了門一腳。)"],["kid","kid(n./v.)小孩、開玩笑\nkidding(n./adj.)開玩笑\njust kidding 只是開玩笑\nsmart kid 聰明的孩子\nHe is a very smart kid.\n(他是一個非常聰明的孩子。)\nDon't take it seriously, I'm just kidding.\n(別當真，我只是在開玩笑。)"],["kill","kill(v./n.)殺死、殺害\nkiller(n.)殺手\nkill time 消磨時間\nkill off 殺光\nThe poison was strong enough to kill the insects.\n(這種毒藥強大到足以殺死昆蟲。)\nWe played cards to kill time at the airport.\n(我們在機場打牌以消磨時間。)"],["kind","kind(adj./n.)仁慈的、種類\nkindness(n.)仁慈\nwhat kind of 哪一種\nbe kind to 對...仁慈\nWhat kind of music do you like most?\n(你最喜歡哪種音樂？)\nIt was very kind of you to help me.\n(你人真好，願意幫助我。)"],["king","king(n.)國王\nkingdom(n.)王國\nking and queen 國王與王后\nthe Lion King 獅子王\nThe king ruled the country for many years.\n(國王統治了這個國家很多年。)\nHe is known as the king of pop music.\n(他被稱為流行音樂之王。)"],["kiss","kiss(n./v.)親吻\na goodnight kiss 晚安吻\nblow a kiss 吹一個吻\nShe gave her baby a kiss on the forehead.\n(她在寶寶的額頭上親了一下。)\nThey kissed each other goodbye at the station.\n(他們在車站吻別。)"],["kitchen","kitchen(n.)廚房\nkitchenware(n.)廚房用品\nin the kitchen 在廚房\nkitchen table 廚房餐桌\nMy mother is cooking dinner in the kitchen.\n(我媽媽正在廚房做晚飯。)\nWe sat around the kitchen table and talked.\n(我們坐在廚房餐桌旁聊天。)"],["kite","kite(n.)風箏\nfly a kite 放風箏\na paper kite 紙風箏\nThe children are flying kites in the park.\n(孩子們正在公園裡放風箏。)\nHe made a colorful paper kite by himself.\n(他自己做了一個色彩繽紛的紙風箏。)"],["knee","knee(n./v.)膝蓋\nkneel(v.)跪下\non one's knees 跪著\nknee injury 膝蓋受傷\nHe hurt his knee while playing basketball.\n(他在打籃球時傷到了膝蓋。)\nShe fell on her knees and started to pray.\n(她跪了下來，開始祈禱。)"],["knife","knife(n./v.)小刀、餐刀\nknives(複數)\nsharp knife 鋒利的刀\nknife and fork 刀叉\nPlease be careful with that sharp knife.\n(請小心使用那把鋒利的刀。)\nYou need a knife and fork to eat steak.\n(吃牛排需要刀叉。)"],["knock","knock(v./n.)敲、擊\nknock on 敲(門)\nknock down 撞倒\nSomeone is knocking on the door.\n(有人正在敲門。)\nThe old building was knocked down yesterday.\n(那棟舊建築昨天被拆除了。)"],["know","know(v.)知道、認識\nknown(adj.)已知的\nknow about 了解\nget to know 認識、了解\nDo you know about the secret meeting?\n(你知道那個秘密會議嗎？)\nI would like to get to know her better.\n(我想更深入地了解她。)"],["knowledge","knowledge(n.)知識、學問\nknowledgeable(adj.)博學的\ngeneral knowledge 常識\nhave a knowledge of 具備...知識\nReading helps us gain more knowledge.\n(閱讀有助於我們獲得更多知識。)\nShe has a wide knowledge of world history.\n(她對世界歷史有廣泛的了解。)"],["lake","lake(n.)湖\n(無詞性變化)\nSun Moon Lake 日月潭\nby the lake 在湖邊\nWe had a picnic by the lake.\n(我們在湖邊野餐。)\nSun Moon Lake is very beautiful.\n(日月潭非常美麗。)"],["lamp","lamp(n.)燈、檯燈\n(無詞性變化)\ndesk lamp 檯燈\nturn on the lamp 打開燈\nPlease turn on the lamp.\n(請把燈打開。)\nI read under the desk lamp.\n(我在檯燈下看書。)"],["land","land(n./v.)陸地、土地、降落、登陸\nlanding(n.)降落、著陸\nby land 經由陸路\nland safely 安全降落\nThe plane landed at ten o'clock.\n(飛機在十點降落。)\nFarmers work hard on the land.\n(農夫們在土地上辛勤工作。)"],["language","language(n.)語言\n(無詞性變化)\nforeign language 外語\nbody language 肢體語言\nEnglish is an international language.\n(英文是一種國際語言。)\nHow many languages can you speak?\n(你會說幾種語言？)"],["large","large(adj.)大的、大量的\nlargely(adv.)大部分、主要地\na large number of 大量的\nlarge size 大尺寸\nI'd like a large coffee, please.\n(我要一杯大杯咖啡。)\nThey live in a large house.\n(他們住在一棟大房子裡。)"],["last","last(n./v./adv./adj.)最後的、上一個的、持續、最後\nlasting(adj.)持久的\nlast week 上週\nat last 終於\nAt last, the rain stopped.\n(雨終於停了。)\nThe meeting lasted two hours.\n(會議持續了兩個小時。)"],["late","late(adj./adv.)遲的、晚的、已故的、晚地\nlately(adv.)最近\nbe late for 遲到\nstay up late 熬夜\nDon't be late for school.\n(上學不要遲到。)\nHe stayed up late last night.\n(他昨晚熬夜。)"],["later","later(adv.)稍後、後來\n(無詞性變化)\nsee you later 待會見\nsooner or later 遲早\nI will call you later.\n(我晚點打電話給你。)\nTwo days later, he came back.\n(兩天後，他回來了。)"],["laugh","laugh(v./n.)笑、笑聲\nlaughter(n.)笑聲\nlaugh at 嘲笑\nburst out laughing 突然大笑\nDon't laugh at other people.\n(不要嘲笑別人。)\nHis jokes always make us laugh.\n(他的笑話總是讓我們發笑。)"],["lawyer","lawyer(n.)律師\nlaw(n.)法律\nbecome a lawyer 成為律師\nhire a lawyer 請律師\nShe wants to be a lawyer.\n(她想當律師。)\nMy uncle is a lawyer in Taipei.\n(我叔叔是台北的律師。)"],["lazy","lazy(adj.)懶惰的\nlaziness(n.)懶惰\nlazy person 懶人\nfeel lazy 懶洋洋的\nDon't be so lazy!\n(別那麼懶惰！)\nI feel lazy on Sunday mornings.\n(星期天早上我總是懶洋洋的。)"],["lead","lead(v./n.)帶領、導致、領先、鉛\nleader(n.)領導者\nleadership(n.)領導能力\nlead to 導致、通往\ntake the lead 帶頭、領先\nThis road leads to the station.\n(這條路通往車站。)\nOur team took the lead.\n(我們隊伍取得領先。)"],["leader","leader(n.)領導者、隊長\nlead(v.)帶領\nleadership(n.)領導能力\nteam leader 組長、隊長\nworld leader 世界領袖\nShe is the leader of our group.\n(她是我們這組的組長。)\nA good leader listens to others.\n(好的領導者會傾聽別人。)"],["learn","learn(v.)學習、得知\nlearner(n.)學習者\nlearning(n.)學習\nlearn from 向…學習\nlearn a lesson 學到教訓\nI want to learn to play the guitar.\n(我想學彈吉他。)\nWe can learn from our mistakes.\n(我們可以從錯誤中學習。)"],["least","least(adv./pron./adj.)最少、最小\n(無詞性變化)\nat least 至少\nlast but not least 最後但同樣重要的\nYou should sleep at least eight hours.\n(你應該至少睡八個小時。)\nMath is my least favorite subject.\n(數學是我最不喜歡的科目。)"],["leave","leave(v./n.)離開、留下、遺忘、休假\n(無詞性變化)\nleave for 動身前往\nleave a message 留言\nThe train leaves at eight.\n(火車八點出發。)\nI left my bag on the bus.\n(我把包包忘在公車上了。)"],["left","left(adj./n./adv.)左邊的、左邊、向左\n(無詞性變化)\nturn left 左轉\non the left 在左邊\nTurn left at the corner.\n(在轉角處左轉。)\nThe library is on your left.\n(圖書館在你的左手邊。)"],["leg","leg(n.)腿\n(無詞性變化)\nbreak a leg 祝好運(演出前)\nlong legs 長腿\nHe hurt his leg playing soccer.\n(他踢足球時傷了腿。)\nA spider has eight legs.\n(蜘蛛有八隻腳。)"],["lemon","lemon(n.)檸檬\nlemonade(n.)檸檬汁、檸檬水\nlemon tea 檸檬茶\nlemon juice 檸檬汁\nI'd like a cup of lemon tea.\n(我想要一杯檸檬茶。)\nAdd some lemon juice to the fish.\n(在魚上加一點檸檬汁。)"],["less","less(pron./adv./adj./prep.)較少、更少、減去\nlessen(v.)減少\nless than 少於\nmore or less 或多或少、大約\nI spent less money this month.\n(我這個月花的錢比較少。)\nIt takes less than ten minutes.\n(這花不到十分鐘。)"],["lesson","lesson(n.)課、一堂課、教訓\n(無詞性變化)\npiano lesson 鋼琴課\nlearn a lesson 學到教訓\nI have a piano lesson on Monday.\n(我星期一有鋼琴課。)\nLet's begin Lesson Three.\n(我們開始上第三課。)"],["let","let(v.)讓、允許\n(無詞性變化)\nlet go 放手\nlet me know 讓我知道\nLet me help you.\n(讓我幫你。)\nMy parents let me go to the concert.\n(我爸媽讓我去聽演唱會。)"],["letter","letter(n.)信、字母\n(無詞性變化)\nwrite a letter 寫信\ncapital letter 大寫字母\nI wrote a letter to my pen pal.\n(我寫了一封信給我的筆友。)\nThere are 26 letters in English.\n(英文有二十六個字母。)"],["level","level(n./adj.)程度、等級、水平的、同高度的\n(無詞性變化)\nsea level 海平面\nhigh level 高水準\nMy English level is not high.\n(我的英文程度不高。)\nHe passed the first level of the game.\n(他通過了遊戲的第一關。)"],["library","library(n.)圖書館\nlibrarian(n.)圖書館員\nschool library 學校圖書館\nborrow books from the library 從圖書館借書\nI borrow books from the library.\n(我從圖書館借書。)\nPlease be quiet in the library.\n(在圖書館裡請保持安靜。)"],["lie","lie(v./n.)躺、位於、說謊、謊言\nliar(n.)說謊者\ntell a lie 說謊\nlie down 躺下\nDon't tell lies.\n(不要說謊。)\nI lay on the bed and rested.\n(我躺在床上休息。)"],["life","life(n.)生命、生活、人生\nlive(v.)生活、居住\nlively(adj.)活潑的、熱鬧的\ndaily life 日常生活\nsave one's life 救某人一命\nLife in the city is busy.\n(城市生活很忙碌。)\nThe doctor saved his life.\n(醫生救了他一命。)"],["light","light(n./adj./v./adv.)光、燈、輕的、明亮的、點燃\nlightly(adv.)輕輕地\nlighten(v.)減輕、照亮\nturn off the light 關燈\ntraffic light 紅綠燈\nPlease turn off the light.\n(請關燈。)\nThis bag is very light.\n(這個包包很輕。)"],["like","like(prep./v./n.)像、喜歡、喜好\nlikely(adj.)可能的\ndislike(v./n.)不喜歡\nlook like 看起來像\nwould like 想要\nI like to play basketball.\n(我喜歡打籃球。)\nShe looks like her mother.\n(她長得像她媽媽。)"],["line","line(n./v.)線、排隊的行列、台詞、排成一列\n(無詞性變化)\nstand in line 排隊\ndraw a line 畫一條線\nWe stood in line for the bus.\n(我們排隊等公車。)\nDraw a line under the new words.\n(在生字下面畫線。)"],["lion","lion(n.)獅子\nlioness(n.)母獅子\na pride of lions 一群獅子\nlion dance 舞獅\nThe lion is the king of animals.\n(獅子是萬獸之王。)\nWe saw a lion dance at the temple.\n(我們在廟口看了舞獅表演。)"],["lip","lip(n.)嘴唇\n(無詞性變化)\nlip balm 護唇膏\nbite one's lip 咬嘴唇\nMy lips are dry in winter.\n(冬天我的嘴唇很乾。)\nShe put on some lip balm.\n(她擦了一些護唇膏。)"],["list","list(n./v.)清單、名單、列出\n(無詞性變化)\nshopping list 購物清單\nmake a list 列清單\nMom made a shopping list.\n(媽媽列了一張購物清單。)\nPlease list three things you like.\n(請列出三件你喜歡的事。)"],["listen","listen(v.)聽、傾聽\nlistener(n.)聽眾、傾聽者\nlisten to 聽…\nlisten carefully 仔細聽\nI like to listen to music.\n(我喜歡聽音樂。)\nPlease listen to the teacher.\n(請聽老師說話。)"],["little","little(adj./adv./n.)小的、少的、稍微、一點點\n(無詞性變化)\na little 一點點\nlittle by little 逐漸地\nI can speak a little Japanese.\n(我會說一點日文。)\nShe has a little brother.\n(她有一個弟弟。)"],["live","live(v./adj.)居住、生活、活的、現場直播的\nliving(adj./n.)活的、生計\nlively(adj.)活潑的\nlive in 住在…\nlive music 現場音樂\nI live in Taipei.\n(我住在台北。)\nThey watched the game live on TV.\n(他們看電視上的比賽實況轉播。)"],["lonely","lonely(adj.)孤單的、寂寞的\nloneliness(n.)寂寞\nfeel lonely 感到寂寞\nlonely life 孤單的生活\nI feel lonely when you are away.\n(你不在時我感到寂寞。)\nThe old man lives a lonely life.\n(那位老人過著孤單的生活。)"],["long","long(adj./adv./v.)長的、長久地、渴望\nlength(n.)長度\na long time 很長的時間\nlong for 渴望\nShe has long hair.\n(她留著長頭髮。)\nI haven't seen you for a long time.\n(好久不見。)"],["look","look(v./n.)看、看起來、看一眼\n(無詞性變化)\nlook for 尋找\ntake a look 看一看\nWhat are you looking for?\n(你在找什麼？)\nYou look tired today.\n(你今天看起來很累。)"],["lose","lose(v.)遺失、輸掉、減少\nloss(n.)損失\nloser(n.)輸家\nlose weight 減重\nlose a game 輸掉比賽\nI lost my wallet yesterday.\n(我昨天弄丟了錢包。)\nOur team lost the game.\n(我們隊輸了比賽。)"],["lot","lot(n.)許多、一塊地、命運\n(無詞性變化)\na lot of 許多\nparking lot 停車場\nI have a lot of homework today.\n(我今天有很多作業。)\nThanks a lot!\n(非常感謝！)"],["loud","loud(adv./adj.)大聲地、大聲的、吵鬧的\nloudly(adv.)大聲地\nloud music 吵鬧的音樂\nread out loud 大聲朗讀\nThe music is too loud.\n(音樂太大聲了。)\nPlease read the story out loud.\n(請大聲朗讀這個故事。)"],["love","love(n./v.)愛、喜愛\nlovely(adj.)可愛的、美好的\nlover(n.)愛人、愛好者\nfall in love 墜入愛河\nlove to 很喜歡做…\nI love my family.\n(我愛我的家人。)\nShe loves to sing.\n(她很喜歡唱歌。)"],["lovely","lovely(adj.)可愛的、美好的、令人愉快的\nlove(n./v.)愛\nlovely day 美好的一天\nlovely smile 迷人的笑容\nWhat a lovely day!\n(天氣真好！)\nShe has a lovely smile.\n(她有迷人的笑容。)"],["low","low(adj./adv./n.)低的、低地、低點\nlower(v.)降低\nlow price 低價\nlow voice 低沉的聲音\nThe prices here are low.\n(這裡的價格很低。)\nHe spoke in a low voice.\n(他低聲說話。)"],["lucky","lucky(adj.)幸運的\nluck(n.)運氣\nluckily(adv.)幸運地\nlucky number 幸運數字\nlucky day 幸運日\nSeven is my lucky number.\n(七是我的幸運數字。)\nYou are lucky to have such good friends.\n(你很幸運有這麼好的朋友。)"],["lunch","lunch(n./v.)午餐、吃午餐\n(無詞性變化)\nhave lunch 吃午餐\nlunch box 便當盒\nWhat did you have for lunch?\n(你午餐吃了什麼？)\nWe eat lunch at school.\n(我們在學校吃午餐。)"],["machine","machine(n./v.)機器、用機器加工\nmachinery(n.)機械(總稱)\nwashing machine 洗衣機\nvending machine 自動販賣機\nI bought a drink from the vending machine.\n(我從自動販賣機買了一瓶飲料。)\nThe washing machine is broken.\n(洗衣機壞了。)"],["mad","mad(adj.)生氣的、瘋狂的、著迷的\nmadly(adv.)瘋狂地\nmadness(n.)瘋狂\nbe mad at 對…生氣\ngo mad 發瘋\nAre you still mad at me?\n(你還在生我的氣嗎？)\nHe is mad about soccer.\n(他對足球很著迷。)"],["magic","magic(adj./n.)魔術的、神奇的、魔術、魔法\nmagical(adj.)神奇的\nmagician(n.)魔術師\nmagic trick 魔術把戲\nlike magic 神奇地\nHe showed us a magic trick.\n(他表演了一個魔術給我們看。)\nThe medicine worked like magic.\n(這藥神奇地見效了。)"],["mail","mail(n./v.)郵件、郵寄\nmailbox(n.)信箱\nmailman(n.)郵差\nsend mail 寄信\nby mail 用郵寄方式\nI got some mail today.\n(我今天收到一些郵件。)\nPlease mail this letter for me.\n(請幫我寄這封信。)"],["main","main(adj./n.)主要的、總管道\nmainly(adv.)主要地\nmain idea 主旨\nmain road 幹道\nWhat is the main idea of this story?\n(這個故事的主旨是什麼？)\nThe main gate of the school is closed.\n(學校的大門關著。)"],["make","make(v.)做、製造、使得\nmaker(n.)製造者\nmake friends 交朋友\nmake a mistake 犯錯\nShe makes friends easily.\n(她很容易交到朋友。)\nThe movie made me cry.\n(這部電影讓我哭了。)"],["man","man(n./v.)男人、人類、為…配置人手\nmen(n.)男人(複數)\nmankind(n.)人類\nyoung man 年輕男子\nan old man 老先生\nThe man in the blue shirt is my teacher.\n(穿藍色襯衫的那位男士是我的老師。)\nAn old man sat on the bench.\n(一位老先生坐在長椅上。)"],["many","many(adj./pron.)許多的、許多人(事物)\n(無詞性變化)\nhow many 多少\nmany times 很多次\nHow many books do you have?\n(你有多少本書？)\nMany people like this song.\n(很多人喜歡這首歌。)"],["map","map(n./v.)地圖、繪製地圖\n(無詞性變化)\nworld map 世界地圖\nread a map 看地圖\nCan you read a map?\n(你會看地圖嗎？)\nThere is a world map on the wall.\n(牆上有一張世界地圖。)"],["mark","mark(n./v.)記號、分數、痕跡、標記\nmarker(n.)麥克筆、標記\nquestion mark 問號\nfull marks 滿分\nHe got full marks on the test.\n(他考試拿了滿分。)\nMark the important words in red.\n(用紅色標出重要的字。)"],["market","market(n./v.)市場、行銷、銷售\nmarketing(n.)行銷\nnight market 夜市\ngo to the market 去市場\nLet's go to the night market tonight.\n(我們今晚去逛夜市吧。)\nGrandma buys vegetables at the market.\n(奶奶在市場買菜。)"],["married","married(adj.)已婚的\nmarry(v.)結婚\nmarriage(n.)婚姻\nget married 結婚\nbe married to 與…結婚\nMy sister got married last year.\n(我姊姊去年結婚了。)\nAre your parents married?\n(你的父母結婚了嗎？)"],["mathematics/math","mathematics(n.)數學\nmath(n.)數學(口語)\nmathematical(adj.)數學的\nmath test 數學考試\ngood at math 擅長數學\nI am good at math.\n(我擅長數學。)\nWe have a math test tomorrow.\n(我們明天有數學考試。)"],["matter","matter(n./v.)事情、問題、物質、要緊\n(無詞性變化)\nWhat's the matter? 怎麼了?\nno matter what 無論什麼\nWhat's the matter with you?\n(你怎麼了？)\nIt doesn't matter.\n(沒關係。)"],["may","may(aux.)可以、可能、祝願\nmight(aux.)可能(may 的過去式)\nmay I...? 我可以…嗎?\nmay be 可能是\nMay I come in?\n(我可以進來嗎？)\nIt may rain tomorrow.\n(明天可能會下雨。)"],["maybe","maybe(adv.)也許、大概\n(無詞性變化)\nmaybe later 也許晚點\nmaybe not 也許不會\nMaybe he is sick today.\n(也許他今天生病了。)\nMaybe we can go tomorrow.\n(也許我們明天可以去。)"],["meal","meal(n.)一餐、餐點\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a meal 吃飯\nthree meals a day 一日三餐\nDon't skip your meals.\n(不要不吃正餐。)\nWe had a big meal at the restaurant.\n(我們在餐廳吃了一頓大餐。)"],["mean","mean(v./adj.)意思是、打算、刻薄的、小氣的\nmeaning(n.)意義\nmeaningful(adj.)有意義的\nmean to 打算、故意\nbe mean to 對…刻薄\nWhat does this word mean?\n(這個字是什麼意思？)\nDon't be mean to your sister.\n(不要對你妹妹那麼刻薄。)"],["meat","meat(n.)肉\n(無詞性變化)\neat meat 吃肉\nfresh meat 新鮮的肉\nShe doesn't eat meat.\n(她不吃肉。)\nThis meat is very fresh.\n(這塊肉很新鮮。)"],["media","media(n.)媒體\nmedium(n.)媒介(單數)\nsocial media 社群媒體\nmass media 大眾傳播媒體\nMany teens use social media every day.\n(很多青少年每天使用社群媒體。)\nThe news spread fast through the media.\n(這則新聞透過媒體迅速傳開。)"],["medicine","medicine(n.)藥、醫學\nmedical(adj.)醫療的、醫學的\ntake medicine 吃藥\nstudy medicine 讀醫科\nTake this medicine after meals.\n(這個藥飯後服用。)\nMy cousin studies medicine.\n(我表哥讀醫科。)"],["medium","medium(adj.)中等的、適中的\nmedia(n.)媒體(複數)\nmedium size 中等尺寸\nmedium rare 三分熟\nI want a medium coffee.\n(我要一杯中杯咖啡。)\nHe is of medium height.\n(他身高中等。)"],["meet","meet(v.)遇見、會面、認識\nmeeting(n.)會議\nmeet a friend 和朋友見面\nNice to meet you. 很高興認識你。\nNice to meet you.\n(很高興認識你。)\nLet's meet at the station at five.\n(我們五點在車站見面吧。)"],["meeting","meeting(n.)會議、集會\nmeet(v.)會面\nhave a meeting 開會\nclass meeting 班會\nWe have a class meeting on Friday.\n(我們星期五有班會。)\nThe meeting will start at nine.\n(會議九點開始。)"],["member","member(n.)成員、會員\nmembership(n.)會員資格\nfamily member 家庭成員\nclub member 社員\nThere are five members in my family.\n(我家有五個人。)\nHe is a member of the tennis club.\n(他是網球社的社員。)"],["menu","menu(n.)菜單\n(無詞性變化)\non the menu 在菜單上\nlook at the menu 看菜單\nCan I see the menu, please?\n(可以給我看一下菜單嗎？)\nFried rice is not on the menu.\n(炒飯不在菜單上。)"],["middle","middle(adj./n.)中間的、中間\n(無詞性變化)\nin the middle of 在…的中間\nmiddle school 國中\nThere is a table in the middle of the room.\n(房間中間有一張桌子。)\nHe woke up in the middle of the night.\n(他半夜醒來。)"],["milk","milk(n.)牛奶、乳汁\nmilky(adj.)乳白色的、含奶的\na glass of milk 一杯牛奶\nmilk tea 奶茶\nI drink a glass of milk every morning.\n(我每天早上喝一杯牛奶。)\nBubble milk tea is popular in Taiwan.\n(珍珠奶茶在台灣很受歡迎。)"],["million","million(n.)百萬\nmillionaire(n.)百萬富翁\nmillions of 數百萬的\none million dollars 一百萬元\nMillions of people visit Taipei every year.\n(每年有數百萬人造訪台北。)\nThe house costs ten million dollars.\n(那棟房子要價一千萬元。)"],["mind","mind(n./v.)心智、頭腦、介意\n(無詞性變化)\nchange one's mind 改變主意\nNever mind. 沒關係。\nDo you mind if I sit here?\n(你介意我坐這裡嗎？)\nNever mind. It's not your fault.\n(沒關係，不是你的錯。)"],["mine","mine(n./v.)我的(東西)、礦坑、採礦\nminer(n.)礦工\na friend of mine 我的一個朋友\ngold mine 金礦\nThis book is mine.\n(這本書是我的。)\nHe is a friend of mine.\n(他是我的一個朋友。)"],["minute","minute(n.)分鐘、片刻\n(無詞性變化)\nwait a minute 等一下\nin a minute 馬上\nWait a minute, please.\n(請等一下。)\nThe bus comes every ten minutes.\n(公車每十分鐘來一班。)"],["miss","miss(v./n.)想念、錯過、未擊中、失誤\nmissing(adj.)遺失的、失蹤的\nmiss the bus 錯過公車\nmiss home 想家\nI missed the bus this morning.\n(我今天早上錯過了公車。)\nI miss my grandma very much.\n(我非常想念我奶奶。)"],["mistake","mistake(n./v.)錯誤、誤會、弄錯\nmistaken(adj.)弄錯的\nmake a mistake 犯錯\nby mistake 錯誤地、不小心\nEveryone makes mistakes.\n(每個人都會犯錯。)\nI took your umbrella by mistake.\n(我不小心拿錯了你的雨傘。)"],["modern","modern(adj.)現代的、時髦的\nmodernize(v.)使現代化\nmodern art 現代藝術\nmodern life 現代生活\nTaipei 101 is a modern building.\n(台北101是一棟現代建築。)\nCellphones are part of modern life.\n(手機是現代生活的一部分。)"],["moment","moment(n.)片刻、時刻\n(無詞性變化)\nat the moment 此刻、目前\nfor a moment 一會兒\nPlease wait a moment.\n(請稍等一下。)\nHe is busy at the moment.\n(他此刻正在忙。)"],["money","money(n.)錢\n(無詞性變化)\nsave money 存錢\nspend money 花錢\nI want to save money for a new bike.\n(我想存錢買新腳踏車。)\nDon't spend too much money.\n(不要花太多錢。)"],["monkey","monkey(n.)猴子\n(無詞性變化)\nFormosan rock monkey 台灣獼猴\nmonkey around 胡鬧\nThe monkey is eating a banana.\n(那隻猴子正在吃香蕉。)\nStop monkeying around in class.\n(上課別胡鬧了。)"],["month","month(n.)月、月份\nmonthly(adj./adv.)每月的、每月一次\nnext month 下個月\nonce a month 一個月一次\nWe will move next month.\n(我們下個月要搬家。)\nI visit my grandparents once a month.\n(我一個月去看我的祖父母一次。)"],["moon","moon(n.)月亮\n(無詞性變化)\nfull moon 滿月\nMoon Festival 中秋節\nThe moon is very bright tonight.\n(今晚的月亮很亮。)\nWe eat moon cakes at the Moon Festival.\n(我們在中秋節吃月餅。)"],["more","more(adj./pron./adv.)更多的、更多、更\n(無詞性變化)\nmore and more 越來越多\nonce more 再一次\nWould you like some more rice?\n(你要再來點飯嗎？)\nPlease say it once more.\n(請再說一次。)"],["morning","morning(n.)早上、上午\n(無詞性變化)\ngood morning 早安\nin the morning 在早上\nGood morning, everyone!\n(大家早安！)\nI go jogging in the morning.\n(我早上去慢跑。)"],["most","most(adv./pron./adj.)最、大部分、最多的\nmostly(adv.)大多、主要地\nmost of 大部分的…\nat most 最多\nMost of my friends like music.\n(我大部分的朋友都喜歡音樂。)\nThis is the most beautiful park in town.\n(這是鎮上最漂亮的公園。)"],["mother","mother(n.)母親、媽媽\nmotherhood(n.)母親身分\nMother's Day 母親節\nmother tongue 母語\nMy mother is a nurse.\n(我媽媽是護理師。)\nWe bought flowers for Mother's Day.\n(我們買了花過母親節。)"],["mountain","mountain(n.)山、大量\nmountainous(adj.)多山的\nclimb a mountain 爬山\nmountain bike 登山車\nJade Mountain is the highest mountain in Taiwan.\n(玉山是台灣最高的山。)\nWe climbed the mountain on Sunday.\n(我們星期天去爬山。)"],["mouse","mouse(n.)老鼠、滑鼠\nmice(n.)老鼠(複數)\ncomputer mouse 電腦滑鼠\nclick the mouse 按滑鼠\nThe cat caught a mouse.\n(貓抓到一隻老鼠。)\nClick the mouse twice.\n(按兩下滑鼠。)"],["mouth","mouth(n./v.)嘴巴、出口、做嘴型說\n(無詞性變化)\nopen one's mouth 張開嘴\nword of mouth 口耳相傳\nOpen your mouth and say 'Ah.'\n(張開嘴巴說「啊」。)\nDon't talk with your mouth full.\n(嘴裡有食物時不要說話。)"],["move(ment)","move(v.)移動、搬家、感動\nmovement(n.)動作、運動、移動\nmoving(adj.)感人的\nmove to 搬到…\nmove on 繼續前進\nWe moved to Taichung last year.\n(我們去年搬到台中。)\nHer dance movements are beautiful.\n(她的舞蹈動作很優美。)"],["movie/film","movie(n.)電影\nfilm(n./v.)電影、底片、拍攝\ngo to the movies 去看電影\nmovie star 電影明星\nLet's go to the movies tonight.\n(我們今晚去看電影吧。)\nThis film is about a brave girl.\n(這部電影是關於一位勇敢的女孩。)"],["Mr./Mister","Mr.(n.)先生(用於男子姓氏前)\nMister(n.)先生(全稱)\nMr. Wang 王先生\nMr. Right 理想的另一半\nMr. Lin is our English teacher.\n(林老師是我們的英文老師。)\nExcuse me, Mr. Chen.\n(陳先生，不好意思。)"],["Mrs.","Mrs.(n.)太太、夫人(用於已婚女子姓氏前)\n(無詞性變化)\nMrs. Lee 李太太\nMr. and Mrs. Wang 王先生和王太太\nMrs. Brown lives next door.\n(布朗太太住在隔壁。)\nMr. and Mrs. Wang have two kids.\n(王先生和王太太有兩個孩子。)"],["Ms.","Ms.(n.)女士(用於女子姓氏前,不分婚否)\n(無詞性變化)\nMs. Chen 陳女士\nDear Ms. Smith 親愛的史密斯女士\nMs. Chang teaches us music.\n(張老師教我們音樂。)\nPlease give this to Ms. Lin.\n(請把這個交給林女士。)"],["much","much(adj./pron./adv.)許多的、許多、非常\n(無詞性變化)\nhow much 多少(錢)\ntoo much 太多\nHow much is this shirt?\n(這件襯衫多少錢？)\nThank you very much.\n(非常謝謝你。)"],["mud","mud(n.)泥巴、泥土\nmuddy(adj.)泥濘的\ncovered in mud 滿身泥巴\nmud bath 泥巴浴\nMy shoes are covered in mud.\n(我的鞋子沾滿了泥巴。)\nThe kids played in the mud.\n(孩子們在泥巴裡玩。)"],["museum","museum(n.)博物館、美術館\n(無詞性變化)\nNational Palace Museum 故宮博物院\nart museum 美術館\nWe visited the National Palace Museum.\n(我們參觀了故宮博物院。)\nThe museum opens at nine.\n(博物館九點開門。)"],["music","music(n.)音樂\nmusical(adj./n.)音樂的、音樂劇\nmusician(n.)音樂家\nlisten to music 聽音樂\npop music 流行音樂\nI listen to music every night.\n(我每天晚上聽音樂。)\nShe likes pop music.\n(她喜歡流行音樂。)"],["must","must(aux./n.)必須、一定、必備之物\n(無詞性變化)\nmust be 一定是\na must 必做之事、必備品\nYou must finish your homework first.\n(你必須先寫完作業。)\nHe must be tired after the long trip.\n(長途旅行後他一定很累。)"],["name","name(n./v.)名字、命名、說出名字\nnameless(adj.)無名的\nnamely(adv.)也就是\nfirst name 名字\nname after 以……命名\nWhat is your name, please?\n(請問你叫什麼名字？)\nThey named their baby after his grandfather.\n(他們以寶寶的祖父為他命名。)"],["national","national(adj.)國家的、全國的\nnation(n.)國家、民族\nnationality(n.)國籍\nnational park 國家公園\nnational holiday 國定假日\nWe visited a national park last summer.\n(我們去年夏天參觀了一座國家公園。)\nDouble Ten Day is a national holiday in Taiwan.\n(雙十節是臺灣的國定假日。)"],["nature","nature(n.)自然、大自然、本性\nnatural(adj.)自然的、天生的\nnaturally(adv.)自然地、當然\nhuman nature 人性\nin nature 本質上、在自然界\nI love to walk in nature on weekends.\n(我喜歡在週末到大自然中散步。)\nIt is human nature to want to be loved.\n(渴望被愛是人的天性。)"],["near","near(prep./adj./adv./v.)在……附近、近的、接近\nnearly(adv.)幾乎\nnearby(adj./adv.)附近的、在附近\nnear future 不久的將來\nnear here 在這附近\nIs there a bank near here?\n(這附近有銀行嗎？)\nMy school is very near my home.\n(我的學校離我家很近。)"],["neck","neck(n.)脖子、頸部\n(無詞性變化)\nlong neck 長脖子\nneck and neck 不分上下\nThe giraffe has a very long neck.\n(長頸鹿有很長的脖子。)\nShe wore a red scarf around her neck.\n(她在脖子上圍了一條紅色圍巾。)"],["need","need(v./n./aux.)需要、必須、需求\nneedy(adj.)貧困的\nneedless(adj.)不必要的\nin need 在困難中、有需要\nneed help 需要幫忙\nI need some water after running.\n(跑步之後我需要喝點水。)\nA friend in need is a friend indeed.\n(患難見真情。)"],["net","net(n./v.)網子、網路、用網捕\nnetwork(n.)網路、網絡\nfishing net 漁網\nsafety net 安全網、保障\nThe fisherman threw his net into the sea.\n(漁夫把他的網子撒進海裡。)\nThe ball hit the net and fell down.\n(球打到網子後掉了下來。)"],["never","never(adv.)從不、絕不\n(無詞性變化)\nnever mind 沒關係、不要緊\nnever again 再也不\nI have never been to Japan.\n(我從來沒去過日本。)\nNever give up on your dreams.\n(絕對不要放棄你的夢想。)"],["new","new(adj.)新的、陌生的\nnewly(adv.)新近地、最近\nbrand new 全新的\nnew year 新年\nI just bought a brand new bike.\n(我剛買了一台全新的腳踏車。)\nHe is new to this school.\n(他是這所學校的新生。)"],["news","news(n.)新聞、消息\n(無詞性變化)\ngood news 好消息\nbreaking news 即時新聞、突發新聞\nI have some good news for you.\n(我有一個好消息要告訴你。)\nMy dad watches the news every night.\n(我爸爸每天晚上都看新聞。)"],["newspaper","newspaper(n.)報紙、報社\n(無詞性變化)\ndaily newspaper 日報\nread the newspaper 看報紙\nMy grandpa reads the newspaper every morning.\n(我爺爺每天早上都看報紙。)\nHer photo was in the newspaper today.\n(她的照片今天登上了報紙。)"],["next","next(adj./adv.)下一個的、其次、接著\n(無詞性變化)\nnext to 在……旁邊\nnext time 下一次\nSee you next week!\n(下週見！)\nThe bookstore is next to the bakery.\n(書店就在麵包店旁邊。)"],["nice","nice(adj.)好的、令人愉快的、親切的\nnicely(adv.)好好地、和善地\nnice to meet you 很高興認識你\nnice weather 好天氣\nIt is nice to meet you.\n(很高興認識你。)\nOur new teacher is very nice to us.\n(我們的新老師對我們很親切。)"],["night","night(n.)夜晚、晚上\nnightly(adj./adv.)每夜的、每晚\nat night 在晚上\nlast night 昨晚\nI did my homework late last night.\n(我昨晚很晚才寫功課。)\nOwls usually hunt at night.\n(貓頭鷹通常在晚上獵食。)"],["no/nope","no(adj./adv./n.)沒有的、不、拒絕\nnope(adv.)不(口語)\nno longer 不再\nno way 不可能、沒門\nThere is no milk in the fridge.\n(冰箱裡沒有牛奶了。)\nNope, I don't want to go out tonight.\n(不要，我今晚不想出去。)"],["nobody","nobody(pron./n.)沒有人、無名小卒\n(無詞性變化)\nnobody else 沒有其他人\nnobody knows 沒人知道\nNobody was at home when I called.\n(我打電話時沒有人在家。)\nNobody knows the answer to this question.\n(沒有人知道這個問題的答案。)"],["noise","noise(n.)噪音、聲響\nnoisy(adj.)吵鬧的\nnoiseless(adj.)無聲的\nmake noise 製造噪音\nloud noise 很大的聲響\nPlease don't make any noise in the library.\n(請不要在圖書館製造噪音。)\nA loud noise woke me up last night.\n(昨晚一聲巨響把我吵醒了。)"],["noisy","noisy(adj.)吵鬧的、喧鬧的\nnoise(n.)噪音\nnoisily(adv.)吵鬧地\nnoisy street 吵雜的街道\nnoisy neighbors 吵鬧的鄰居\nThe classroom was very noisy before class.\n(上課前教室非常吵鬧。)\nI can't sleep because of my noisy neighbors.\n(因為鄰居很吵，我睡不著。)"],["noon","noon(n.)中午、正午\n(無詞性變化)\nat noon 在中午\nhigh noon 正午\nWe usually eat lunch at noon.\n(我們通常在中午吃午餐。)\nThe store closes at noon on Sundays.\n(這家店星期天中午就打烊。)"],["north","north(n./adj./adv.)北方、北方的、向北\nnorthern(adj.)北方的、北部的\nnorthward(adv.)向北\nNorth Pole 北極\nthe north of 在……的北部\nTaipei is in the north of Taiwan.\n(臺北位於臺灣北部。)\nThe birds fly north in spring.\n(這些鳥在春天往北飛。)"],["nose","nose(n.)鼻子\nnosy(adj.)愛管閒事的\nrunny nose 流鼻水\nblow your nose 擤鼻涕\nI have a cold and a runny nose.\n(我感冒了，還流鼻水。)\nThe dog has a very good nose.\n(這隻狗的嗅覺非常靈敏。)"],["not","not(adv.)不、沒有\n(無詞性變化)\nnot at all 一點也不、不客氣\nnot only... but also 不但……而且\nI am not hungry right now.\n(我現在不餓。)\nThank you. Not at all.\n(謝謝你。不客氣。)"],["note","note(n./v.)筆記、便條、注意、記下\nnotebook(n.)筆記本\nnoted(adj.)著名的\ntake notes 做筆記\nleave a note 留張便條\nPlease take notes during the class.\n(上課時請做筆記。)\nMom left a note on the table for me.\n(媽媽在桌上留了張紙條給我。)"],["nothing","nothing(pron./n.)沒有東西、沒什麼\n(無詞性變化)\nnothing but 只有、只不過\nfor nothing 免費、白白地\nThere is nothing in the box.\n(箱子裡什麼都沒有。)\nI have nothing to do this afternoon.\n(我今天下午沒什麼事可做。)"],["notice","notice(v./n.)注意到、察覺、通知、公告\nnoticeable(adj.)顯而易見的\nnotice board 布告欄\nwithout notice 未事先通知\nDid you notice her new haircut?\n(你有注意到她的新髮型嗎？)\nPlease read the notice on the board.\n(請閱讀布告欄上的公告。)"],["now","now(adv./n.)現在、目前\n(無詞性變化)\nright now 立刻、現在\nfrom now on 從現在開始\nI am busy right now.\n(我現在很忙。)\nFrom now on, I will get up early.\n(從現在起，我會早起。)"],["number","number(n./v.)數字、號碼、數量、編號\nnumerous(adj.)許多的\na number of 許多的\nphone number 電話號碼\nCan I have your phone number?\n(可以給我你的電話號碼嗎？)\nA number of students joined the club.\n(許多學生加入了這個社團。)"],["nurse","nurse(n./v.)護理師、看護、照顧\nnursing(n.)護理\nnursery(n.)托兒所、育嬰室\nschool nurse 學校護理師\nnurse back to health 照顧使恢復健康\nMy aunt works as a nurse in a hospital.\n(我阿姨在醫院當護理師。)\nShe nursed the sick bird back to health.\n(她細心照顧那隻生病的鳥直到牠康復。)"],["O.K./OK/okay","O.K.(adj./adv./n./v.)好、沒問題、同意、批准\nOK(adj./adv./n./v.)好、沒問題(同 O.K.)\nokay(adj./adv./n./v.)好、沒問題(同 O.K.)\nfeel O.K. 感覺還好\nget the O.K. 獲得同意\nAre you O.K.? You look tired.\n(你還好嗎？你看起來很累。)\nIs it okay if I sit here?\n(我可以坐在這裡嗎？)"],["o’clock","o’clock(adv.)……點鐘\n(無詞性變化)\nat seven o’clock 在七點鐘\none o’clock 一點鐘\nI get up at six o’clock every day.\n(我每天六點鐘起床。)\nThe movie starts at eight o’clock.\n(電影八點鐘開始。)"],["of","of(prep.)……的、屬於、由……組成\n(無詞性變化)\na cup of 一杯\nbecause of 因為\nI'd like a cup of tea, please.\n(請給我一杯茶。)\nShe is one of my best friends.\n(她是我最好的朋友之一。)"],["off","off(adv./prep./adj.)離開、脫離、關掉、休假的\n(無詞性變化)\nturn off 關掉\nday off 休假日\nPlease turn off the lights.\n(請把燈關掉。)\nI have a day off tomorrow.\n(我明天放假。)"],["office","office(n.)辦公室、職位\nofficer(n.)官員、警官\nofficial(adj./n.)官方的、官員\npost office 郵局\noffice hours 辦公時間\nMy father works in an office downtown.\n(我爸爸在市中心的辦公室上班。)\nI need to send a letter at the post office.\n(我需要到郵局寄一封信。)"],["officer","officer(n.)警官、官員、軍官\noffice(n.)辦公室\nofficial(adj./n.)官方的、官員\npolice officer 警察\narmy officer 陸軍軍官\nThe police officer helped the lost child.\n(警察幫助了那個走失的孩子。)\nHe wants to be an army officer someday.\n(他希望有一天成為陸軍軍官。)"],["often","often(adv.)常常、經常\n(無詞性變化)\nhow often 多久一次\nvery often 非常頻繁\nHow often do you play basketball?\n(你多久打一次籃球？)\nI often walk my dog after dinner.\n(我常常在晚餐後遛狗。)"],["oil","oil(n./v.)油、石油、上油\noily(adj.)油膩的\nolive oil 橄欖油\ncooking oil 食用油\nMom cooks vegetables with olive oil.\n(媽媽用橄欖油炒青菜。)\nThe price of oil went up again.\n(油價又上漲了。)"],["old","old(adj.)老的、舊的、……歲的\n(無詞性變化)\nold friend 老朋友\nyears old ……歲\nMy brother is ten years old.\n(我弟弟十歲。)\nI met an old friend at the station.\n(我在車站遇到一位老朋友。)"],["on","on(prep./adv.)在……上面、在(某日)、開著\n(無詞性變化)\non time 準時\nturn on 打開(電器)\nThe book is on the desk.\n(書在書桌上。)\nPlease turn on the TV.\n(請把電視打開。)"],["once","once(adv./conj./n.)一次、曾經、一旦\n(無詞性變化)\nat once 立刻\nonce a week 一週一次\nI go swimming once a week.\n(我一週去游泳一次。)\nOnce you start, you can't stop.\n(一旦你開始了，就停不下來。)"],["online","online(adj.)線上的、網路上的\n(無詞性變化)\nonline shopping 網路購物\nonline game 線上遊戲\nOnline shopping is very popular now.\n(網路購物現在非常流行。)\nHe plays online games with his friends.\n(他和朋友一起玩線上遊戲。)"],["only","only(adv./adj./conj.)只、唯一的、可是\n(無詞性變化)\nonly child 獨生子女\nnot only 不僅\nShe is an only child.\n(她是獨生女。)\nI only have ten dollars.\n(我只有十元。)"],["open","open(adj./v.)開著的、打開、開放\nopening(n.)開幕、空缺\nopenly(adv.)公開地\nopen the door 開門\nopen-minded 心胸開闊的\nCould you open the window, please?\n(可以請你打開窗戶嗎？)\nThe museum is open on Sundays.\n(博物館星期天有開放。)"],["or","or(conj.)或者、否則\n(無詞性變化)\nor else 否則\nsooner or later 遲早\nDo you want tea or coffee?\n(你要茶還是咖啡？)\nHurry up, or you will be late.\n(快一點，否則你會遲到。)"],["orange","orange(adj./n.)橘色的、柳橙、橘子\n(無詞性變化)\norange juice 柳橙汁\norange peel 橘子皮\nI drink orange juice every morning.\n(我每天早上都喝柳橙汁。)\nShe painted the wall orange.\n(她把牆漆成橘色。)"],["order","order(n./v.)順序、命令、訂購、點餐\norderly(adj.)整齊的、有秩序的\nin order to 為了\nplace an order 下訂單\nAre you ready to order?\n(您準備好點餐了嗎？)\nPut the words in the right order.\n(把這些字依正確順序排列。)"],["other","other(adj./pron.)其他的、另一個\notherwise(adv.)否則、不然\neach other 彼此\nthe other day 前幾天\nWe help each other with homework.\n(我們互相幫忙寫功課。)\nSome students like math, and others like art.\n(有些學生喜歡數學，其他人則喜歡美術。)"],["out","out(adv./prep./adj./n./v.)在外、出去、熄滅的、出局\nouter(adj.)外面的\ngo out 外出\nfind out 查明、發現\nLet's go out for dinner tonight.\n(我們今晚出去吃晚餐吧。)\nI need to find out the truth.\n(我必須查明真相。)"],["outside","outside(prep./adv./adj./n.)在外面、外面的、外部\noutsider(n.)局外人\noutside the door 在門外\ngo outside 到外面去\nThe children are playing outside.\n(孩子們正在外面玩。)\nIt is cold outside today.\n(今天外面很冷。)"],["over","over(prep./adv.)在……上方、超過、結束\n(無詞性變化)\nover there 在那裡\nall over 到處\nThe game is over.\n(比賽結束了。)\nThe plane flew over our house.\n(飛機從我們家上空飛過。)"],["own","own(adj./pron./v.)自己的、擁有\nowner(n.)擁有者、主人\nownership(n.)所有權\non your own 獨自、靠自己\nown a house 擁有房子\nI have my own room now.\n(我現在有自己的房間了。)\nWho owns this black car?\n(這輛黑色的車是誰的？)"],["pack","pack(n./v.)包、一包、打包、裝箱\npacking(n.)打包、包裝\npacked(adj.)擠滿的\npack a suitcase 收拾行李箱\na pack of cards 一副撲克牌\nI need to pack my bag tonight.\n(我今晚需要收拾我的包包。)\nHe bought a pack of gum at the store.\n(他在商店買了一包口香糖。)"],["package","package(n.)包裹、套裝\npack(v.)打包\npackaging(n.)包裝材料\nreceive a package 收到包裹\npackage tour 套裝旅遊\nA package came for you this morning.\n(今天早上有你的一個包裹寄來。)\nWe went to Japan on a package tour.\n(我們參加套裝旅遊去日本。)"],["page","page(n.)頁、頁面\n(無詞性變化)\nturn the page 翻頁\nfront page 頭版\nPlease turn to page ten.\n(請翻到第十頁。)\nHis picture was on the front page.\n(他的照片登上了頭版。)"],["paint","paint(n./v.)油漆、顏料、畫、粉刷\npainter(n.)畫家、油漆工\npainting(n.)畫作\npaint a picture 畫一幅畫\nwet paint 油漆未乾\nWe will paint the wall blue.\n(我們要把牆漆成藍色。)\nDon't touch the door. The paint is still wet.\n(別碰門，油漆還沒乾。)"],["pair","pair(n.)一雙、一對\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of shoes 一雙鞋\nin pairs 兩人一組\nI bought a new pair of shoes.\n(我買了一雙新鞋。)\nPlease work in pairs for this activity.\n(這個活動請兩人一組進行。)"],["pants","pants(n.)褲子\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of pants 一條褲子\nlong pants 長褲\nThese pants are too long for me.\n(這條褲子對我來說太長了。)\nHe wore black pants to the party.\n(他穿黑色褲子去參加派對。)"],["paper","paper(n./v.)紙、報紙、報告、貼壁紙\n(無詞性變化)\na piece of paper 一張紙\nwrite a paper 寫報告\nCan I have a piece of paper?\n(可以給我一張紙嗎？)\nMy dad reads the paper every morning.\n(我爸爸每天早上看報紙。)"],["parent(s)","parent(n.)父親或母親、parents(n.)雙親、父母\nparental(adj.)父母的\nsingle parent 單親\nparents' meeting 家長會\nMy parents both work in Taipei.\n(我的父母都在台北工作。)\nShe is a single parent with two kids.\n(她是帶著兩個孩子的單親家長。)"],["park","park(n./v.)公園、停車\nparking(n.)停車\npark a car 停車\nparking lot 停車場\nWe had a picnic in the park.\n(我們在公園野餐。)\nYou can't park your car here.\n(你不能把車停在這裡。)"],["part","part(n./v.)部分、角色、分開\npartly(adv.)部分地\npartial(adj.)部分的\ntake part in 參加\npart of 一部分\nPart of the cake is gone.\n(蛋糕有一部分不見了。)\nMany students took part in the game.\n(許多學生參加了比賽。)"],["party","party(n./v.)派對、政黨、開派對\n(無詞性變化)\nbirthday party 生日派對\nhave a party 舉辦派對\nWe had a party for Mom's birthday.\n(我們為媽媽的生日辦了派對。)\nAre you coming to my party tonight?\n(你今晚會來我的派對嗎？)"],["pass","pass(v./n.)經過、通過、傳遞、通行證\npassage(n.)通道、段落\npasser-by(n.)路人\npass the test 通過考試\npass the salt 把鹽遞過來\nCould you pass me the salt, please?\n(可以請你把鹽遞給我嗎？)\nShe studied hard and passed the test.\n(她努力讀書，通過了考試。)"],["past","past(adj./n./prep./adv.)過去的、過去、經過、超過\n(無詞性變化)\nin the past 在過去\nhalf past six 六點半\nIt's half past six now.\n(現在是六點半。)\nWe walked past the old school.\n(我們走過那間舊學校。)"],["pay(ment)","pay(v.)付錢、支付、payment(n.)付款\npaid(adj.)有薪的\npay for 為…付錢\npay attention to 注意\nI will pay for lunch today.\n(今天午餐我來付錢。)\nPlease pay attention to the teacher.\n(請注意聽老師講。)"],["pen","pen(n./v.)筆、原子筆、寫\n(無詞性變化)\npen pal 筆友\na red pen 一支紅筆\nMay I borrow your pen?\n(我可以借你的筆嗎？)\nI have a pen pal in Canada.\n(我在加拿大有一個筆友。)"],["pencil","pencil(n.)鉛筆\n(無詞性變化)\npencil case 鉛筆盒\nsharpen a pencil 削鉛筆\nPlease write your name in pencil.\n(請用鉛筆寫下你的名字。)\nMy pencil case is on the desk.\n(我的鉛筆盒在桌上。)"],["people","people(n./v.)人們、民族、居住於\n(無詞性變化)\nyoung people 年輕人\nmany people 許多人\nMany people like this song.\n(許多人喜歡這首歌。)\nThere were ten people in the room.\n(房間裡有十個人。)"],["perhaps","perhaps(adv.)或許、可能\n(無詞性變化)\nperhaps not 或許不\nperhaps tomorrow 也許明天\nPerhaps it will rain this afternoon.\n(今天下午或許會下雨。)\nPerhaps you are right about that.\n(關於那件事，也許你是對的。)"],["person","person(n.)人、個人\npersonal(adj.)個人的\nin person 親自\na kind person 一個好心的人\nShe is a very kind person.\n(她是一個非常善良的人。)\nI want to thank him in person.\n(我想親自向他道謝。)"],["pet","pet(n./v.)寵物、撫摸\n(無詞性變化)\npet dog 寵物狗\npet shop 寵物店\nDo you have any pets at home?\n(你家裡有養寵物嗎？)\nThe boy gently petted the cat.\n(那個男孩輕輕撫摸那隻貓。)"],["photograph/photo","photograph(n./v.)照片、拍照\nphoto(n.)照片(口語)\nphotographer(n.)攝影師\nphotography(n.)攝影\ntake a photo 拍照\nfamily photo 全家福\nLet's take a photo together.\n(我們一起拍張照吧。)\nThis is an old photo of my family.\n(這是我家人的一張舊照片。)"],["piano","piano(n.)鋼琴\npianist(n.)鋼琴家\nplay the piano 彈鋼琴\npiano lesson 鋼琴課\nMy sister can play the piano well.\n(我妹妹鋼琴彈得很好。)\nI have a piano lesson on Friday.\n(我星期五有鋼琴課。)"],["pick","pick(v./n.)挑選、摘、選擇\n(無詞性變化)\npick up 撿起、接(人)\npick out 挑出\nPlease pick up the trash on the floor.\n(請把地上的垃圾撿起來。)\nMy mom will pick me up at five.\n(我媽媽五點會來接我。)"],["picnic","picnic(n./v.)野餐、去野餐\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a picnic 野餐\npicnic basket 野餐籃\nLet's have a picnic by the river.\n(我們去河邊野餐吧。)\nShe packed sandwiches in the picnic basket.\n(她把三明治裝進野餐籃。)"],["picture","picture(n./v.)圖畫、照片、想像\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a picture 拍照\ndraw a picture 畫畫\nCan you take a picture of us?\n(你可以幫我們拍張照嗎？)\nThe little girl drew a picture of her dog.\n(那個小女孩畫了她的狗。)"],["pie","pie(n.)派、餡餅\n(無詞性變化)\napple pie 蘋果派\na piece of pie 一塊派\nGrandma made an apple pie for us.\n(奶奶為我們做了蘋果派。)\nWould you like a piece of pie?\n(你想來一塊派嗎？)"],["piece","piece(n./v.)一片、一塊、一件、拼湊\n(無詞性變化)\na piece of cake 一塊蛋糕、小事一樁\nin pieces 成碎片\nCan I have another piece of cake?\n(我可以再吃一塊蛋糕嗎？)\nThe glass fell and broke into pieces.\n(玻璃杯掉下去摔成碎片。)"],["pig","pig(n./v.)豬、狼吞虎嚥\npiggy(n.)小豬\npig out 大吃大喝\npiggy bank 小豬撲滿\nThe farmer has five pigs.\n(那個農夫養了五頭豬。)\nWe pigged out on pizza last night.\n(我們昨晚大吃披薩。)"],["pin","pin(n./v.)別針、大頭針、釘住\n(無詞性變化)\nsafety pin 安全別針\npin up 釘起來\nShe used a pin to fix her dress.\n(她用別針固定她的洋裝。)\nHe pinned the notice on the board.\n(他把公告釘在布告欄上。)"],["pink","pink(adj./n.)粉紅色的、粉紅色\n(無詞性變化)\npink dress 粉紅色洋裝\nlight pink 淺粉紅色\nShe is wearing a pink dress.\n(她穿著一件粉紅色洋裝。)\nPink is my favorite color.\n(粉紅色是我最喜歡的顏色。)"],["pipe","pipe(n./v.)管子、煙斗、用管輸送\npipeline(n.)管線\nwater pipe 水管\nsmoke a pipe 抽煙斗\nThe water pipe under the sink is broken.\n(水槽下面的水管破了。)\nMy grandpa used to smoke a pipe.\n(我爺爺以前會抽煙斗。)"],["place","place(n./v.)地方、位置、放置\n(無詞性變化)\ntake place 發生、舉行\nin place of 代替\nThis is a nice place to live.\n(這是一個適合居住的好地方。)\nThe meeting will take place on Monday.\n(會議將在星期一舉行。)"],["plan","plan(n./v.)計畫、打算\nplanner(n.)規劃者\nmake a plan 訂計畫\nplan to 打算\nWhat are your plans for the weekend?\n(你週末有什麼計畫？)\nWe plan to visit Tainan next month.\n(我們打算下個月去台南。)"],["planet","planet(n.)行星\nplanetary(adj.)行星的\nplanet Earth 地球\nanother planet 另一個星球\nEarth is the planet we live on.\n(地球是我們居住的行星。)\nMars is a red planet.\n(火星是一顆紅色的行星。)"],["plant","plant(n./v.)植物、工廠、種植\nplanter(n.)花盆\nplant trees 種樹\npower plant 發電廠\nWe plant trees every spring.\n(我們每年春天種樹。)\nWater the plants every morning.\n(每天早上替植物澆水。)"],["plate","plate(n.)盤子、一盤\n(無詞性變化)\na plate of rice 一盤飯\nclean plate 吃光盤中的食物\nPut the cake on a plate.\n(把蛋糕放在盤子上。)\nHe ate a whole plate of noodles.\n(他吃了一整盤麵。)"],["play","play(v./n.)玩、演奏、比賽、戲劇\nplayer(n.)球員、玩家\nplayful(adj.)愛玩的\nplay basketball 打籃球\nplay the guitar 彈吉他\nThe kids play in the park every day.\n(孩子們每天在公園裡玩。)\nWe went to see a play last night.\n(我們昨晚去看了一齣戲。)"],["player","player(n.)選手、球員、演奏者、播放器\nplay(v.)玩、比賽\nbasketball player 籃球員\nteam player 有團隊精神的人\nHe is the best player on our team.\n(他是我們隊上最好的選手。)\nShe is a famous piano player.\n(她是一位有名的鋼琴演奏者。)"],["please","please(v.)使高興、請\npleased(adj.)高興的\npleasant(adj.)令人愉快的\nplease sit down 請坐\nbe pleased with 對…滿意\nPlease close the door.\n(請把門關上。)\nIt is hard to please my boss.\n(要讓我的老闆滿意很難。)"],["pleasure","pleasure(n.)樂趣、愉快、榮幸\npleasant(adj.)令人愉快的\nwith pleasure 樂意\nmy pleasure 不客氣、我的榮幸\nReading gives me a lot of pleasure.\n(閱讀帶給我很多樂趣。)\n'Thank you for your help.' 'My pleasure.'\n(「謝謝你的幫忙。」「不客氣。」)"],["pm/p.m.","pm(adv.)下午、午後(亦寫作 p.m.)\n(無詞性變化)\nat 3 pm 下午三點\nfrom 2 to 5 pm 下午兩點到五點\nThe movie starts at 7 pm.\n(電影晚上七點開始。)\nThe store closes at 9 p.m.\n(這家店晚上九點關門。)"],["pocket","pocket(n./v.)口袋、放入口袋\npocketful(n.)一袋之量\npocket money 零用錢\nin my pocket 在我的口袋裡\nI put my phone in my pocket.\n(我把手機放進口袋。)\nHow much pocket money do you get?\n(你拿多少零用錢？)"],["point","point(n./v.)點、要點、分數、指\npointed(adj.)尖的\npoint at 指著\npoint of view 觀點\nIt's rude to point at people.\n(用手指著別人是不禮貌的。)\nOur team won by two points.\n(我們隊以兩分之差獲勝。)"],["police","police(n./v.)警察、警方、維持治安\npoliceman(n.)警察\ncall the police 報警\npolice station 警察局\nWe should call the police right now.\n(我們應該馬上報警。)\nThe police station is near my school.\n(警察局在我學校附近。)"],["polite","polite(adj.)有禮貌的\npolitely(adv.)有禮貌地\npoliteness(n.)禮貌\nbe polite to 對…有禮貌\npolite answer 有禮貌的回答\nYou should be polite to older people.\n(你應該對長輩有禮貌。)\nShe answered the question politely.\n(她有禮貌地回答了問題。)"],["pond","pond(n.)池塘\n(無詞性變化)\nfish pond 魚池\nduck pond 鴨池\nThere are many fish in the pond.\n(池塘裡有很多魚。)\nThe kids fed the ducks by the pond.\n(孩子們在池塘邊餵鴨子。)"],["pool","pool(n./v.)水池、游泳池、共同出資\n(無詞性變化)\nswimming pool 游泳池\ncar pool 共乘\nWe swim in the pool every Sunday.\n(我們每個星期天在游泳池游泳。)\nThe hotel has a big swimming pool.\n(那家飯店有一座大型游泳池。)"],["poor","poor(adj.)貧窮的、可憐的、差的\npoverty(n.)貧窮\npoorly(adv.)差勁地\npoor family 貧窮的家庭\npoor health 健康不佳\nHe grew up in a poor family.\n(他在一個貧窮的家庭長大。)\nThe poor dog was cold and hungry.\n(那隻可憐的狗又冷又餓。)"],["popcorn","popcorn(n.)爆米花\n(無詞性變化)\neat popcorn 吃爆米花\na bag of popcorn 一包爆米花\nWe ate popcorn at the movies.\n(我們在看電影時吃爆米花。)\nI bought a big bag of popcorn.\n(我買了一大包爆米花。)"],["popular","popular(adj.)受歡迎的、流行的\npopularity(n.)受歡迎、流行\nbe popular with 受…歡迎\npopular music 流行音樂\nThis game is popular with kids.\n(這個遊戲很受小孩歡迎。)\nShe is the most popular girl in class.\n(她是班上最受歡迎的女生。)"],["possible","possible(adj.)可能的\npossibly(adv.)可能地\npossibility(n.)可能性\nas soon as possible 盡快\nif possible 如果可能的話\nPlease call me back as soon as possible.\n(請盡快回電給我。)\nIs it possible to finish it today?\n(今天有可能完成嗎？)"],["pot","pot(n./v.)鍋、壺、盆、種在盆裡\n(無詞性變化)\na pot of tea 一壺茶\nhot pot 火鍋\nLet's have hot pot tonight.\n(我們今晚吃火鍋吧。)\nShe made a pot of tea for us.\n(她為我們泡了一壺茶。)"],["potato","potato(n.)馬鈴薯\n(無詞性變化)\nsweet potato 地瓜\nmashed potatoes 馬鈴薯泥\nI like sweet potatoes very much.\n(我非常喜歡地瓜。)\nMom made potato soup for dinner.\n(媽媽晚餐做了馬鈴薯湯。)"],["power","power(n./v.)力量、權力、電力、提供動力\npowerful(adj.)強大的\nin power 掌權\npower failure 停電\nThe storm caused a power failure.\n(暴風雨造成了停電。)\nKnowledge is power.\n(知識就是力量。)"],["practice","practice(n./v.)練習、實踐\npractical(adj.)實用的\npractice English 練習英文\nin practice 實際上\nPractice makes perfect.\n(熟能生巧。)\nI practice the piano every day.\n(我每天練習鋼琴。)"],["prepare","prepare(v.)準備\npreparation(n.)準備\nprepared(adj.)準備好的\nprepare for 為…做準備\nprepare dinner 準備晚餐\nWe are preparing for the final exam.\n(我們正在準備期末考。)\nDad is preparing dinner in the kitchen.\n(爸爸正在廚房準備晚餐。)"],["present","present(adj./n./v.)出席的、現在的、禮物、贈送、呈現\npresence(n.)出席\npresentation(n.)報告、簡報\nbirthday present 生日禮物\nat present 目前\nThank you for the birthday present.\n(謝謝你的生日禮物。)\nAll the students were present today.\n(今天所有學生都出席了。)"],["pretty","pretty(adv./adj.)相當、漂亮的\n(無詞性變化)\npretty good 相當好\npretty girl 漂亮的女孩\nThe test was pretty easy.\n(這次考試相當簡單。)\nWhat a pretty dress!\n(多漂亮的洋裝啊！)"],["price","price(n./v.)價格、定價\npriceless(adj.)無價的\nhigh price 高價\nprice tag 價格標籤\nThe price of this bag is too high.\n(這個包包的價格太高了。)\nLook at the price tag first.\n(先看一下價格標籤。)"],["probably","probably(adv.)大概、很可能\nprobable(adj.)很可能的\nprobably not 大概不會\nwill probably 很可能會\nIt will probably rain tomorrow.\n(明天很可能會下雨。)\nHe is probably at home now.\n(他現在大概在家。)"],["problem","problem(n.)問題\n(無詞性變化)\nsolve a problem 解決問題\nno problem 沒問題\nCan you help me solve this problem?\n(你可以幫我解決這個問題嗎？)\n'Can you help me?' 'No problem.'\n(「你可以幫我嗎？」「沒問題。」)"],["program","program(n./v.)節目、計畫、程式、設計程式\nprogrammer(n.)程式設計師\nprogramming(n.)程式設計\nTV program 電視節目\ncomputer program 電腦程式\nMy favorite TV program starts at eight.\n(我最喜歡的電視節目八點開始。)\nHe wrote a computer program for the game.\n(他為這個遊戲寫了一個電腦程式。)"],["proud","proud(adj.)驕傲的、自豪的\npride(n.)自豪、驕傲\nproudly(adv.)驕傲地\nbe proud of 以…為榮\nproud parents 引以為傲的父母\nMy parents are proud of me.\n(我的父母以我為榮。)\nShe proudly showed us her prize.\n(她驕傲地向我們展示她的獎品。)"],["public","public(adj./n.)公共的、公開的、大眾\npublicly(adv.)公開地\nin public 公開地、在公共場合\npublic library 公立圖書館\nDon't shout in public.\n(不要在公共場合大叫。)\nI often study at the public library.\n(我常在公立圖書館讀書。)"],["pull","pull(v./n.)拉、拖、拉力\n(無詞性變化)\npull out 拔出、退出\npull up 停車\nPull the door to open it.\n(把門拉開。)\nThe dentist pulled out my bad tooth.\n(牙醫把我的蛀牙拔掉了。)"],["push","push(v./n.)推、按、催促\npushy(adj.)強勢的、愛逼人的\npush the button 按按鈕\npush open 推開\nPush the button to start the machine.\n(按下按鈕啟動機器。)\nHe pushed open the heavy door.\n(他推開了那扇沉重的門。)"],["put","put(v.)放、擺\n(無詞性變化)\nput on 穿上\nput away 收起來\nPut your books on the desk.\n(把你的書放在桌上。)\nPut on your coat. It's cold outside.\n(穿上外套，外面很冷。)"],["quarter","quarter(n.)四分之一、一刻鐘、季、二十五分錢\nquarterly(adj.)每季的\na quarter past six 六點十五分\na quarter of 四分之一的\nIt's a quarter past seven.\n(現在是七點十五分。)\nA quarter of the students walk to school.\n(四分之一的學生走路上學。)"],["queen","queen(n.)女王、皇后\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Queen of England 英國女王\nbeauty queen 選美冠軍\nThe queen lived in a big castle.\n(女王住在一座大城堡裡。)\nShe played the queen in the school play.\n(她在學校話劇中演女王。)"],["question","question(n./v.)問題、詢問、質疑\nquestionable(adj.)可疑的\nask a question 問問題\nanswer the question 回答問題\nMay I ask you a question?\n(我可以問你一個問題嗎？)\nPlease answer the questions in English.\n(請用英文回答這些問題。)"],["quick","quick(adj./adv.)快的、迅速地\nquickly(adv.)快速地\nquick lunch 簡便的午餐\nbe quick 快一點\nBe quick, or we'll miss the bus.\n(快一點，不然我們會錯過公車。)\nShe gave a quick answer.\n(她很快地回答了。)"],["quiet","quiet(adj./n./v.)安靜的、寧靜、使安靜\nquietly(adv.)安靜地\nkeep quiet 保持安靜\nquiet place 安靜的地方\nPlease keep quiet in the library.\n(在圖書館裡請保持安靜。)\nShe walked quietly into the room.\n(她安靜地走進房間。)"],["quite","quite(adv.)相當、十分、完全\n(無詞性變化)\nquite a few 相當多\nnot quite 不完全\nThe movie was quite good.\n(那部電影相當好看。)\nQuite a few people came to the party.\n(相當多人來參加派對。)"],["rabbit","rabbit(n.)兔子\n(無詞性變化)\npet rabbit 寵物兔\nwhite rabbit 白兔\nMy sister has a cute pet rabbit.\n(我妹妹養了一隻可愛的寵物兔。)\nThe rabbit is eating a carrot.\n(那隻兔子正在吃紅蘿蔔。)"],["race","race(n./v.)賽跑、比賽、種族\nracer(n.)賽跑者、賽車手\nracial(adj.)種族的\nwin a race 贏得比賽\nhuman race 人類\nTom won the race at school today.\n(湯姆今天在學校贏得了賽跑。)\nLet's race to the park!\n(我們來比賽跑到公園吧！)"],["radio","radio(n./v.)收音機、廣播、用無線電通訊\n(無詞性變化)\nlisten to the radio 聽廣播\nradio station 廣播電台\nMy dad listens to the radio every morning.\n(我爸爸每天早上聽廣播。)\nI heard the news on the radio.\n(我在廣播上聽到這則新聞。)"],["rain","rain(n./v.)雨、下雨\nrainy(adj.)下雨的\nheavy rain 大雨\nrain hard 下大雨\nIt is going to rain this afternoon.\n(今天下午會下雨。)\nWe stayed home because of the heavy rain.\n(因為下大雨，我們待在家裡。)"],["rainbow","rainbow(n.)彩虹\n(無詞性變化)\nsee a rainbow 看見彩虹\nthe colors of the rainbow 彩虹的顏色\nLook! There is a rainbow in the sky.\n(你看！天空中有一道彩虹。)\nA rainbow has seven colors.\n(彩虹有七種顏色。)"],["rainy","rainy(adj.)下雨的、多雨的\nrain(n./v.)雨、下雨\nrainy day 雨天\nrainy season 雨季\nI don't like rainy days.\n(我不喜歡下雨天。)\nTaipei is often rainy in winter.\n(臺北冬天常常下雨。)"],["raise","raise(v./n.)舉起、提高、養育、加薪\n(無詞性變化)\nraise your hand 舉手\nraise money 募款\nPlease raise your hand if you know the answer.\n(如果你知道答案請舉手。)\nShe raised three children by herself.\n(她獨自養大三個孩子。)"],["reach","reach(v./n.)到達、伸手拿、聯絡上\n(無詞性變化)\nreach a goal 達成目標\nout of reach 拿不到、搆不著\nWe reached the station at noon.\n(我們中午抵達車站。)\nI can't reach the top shelf.\n(我搆不到最上層的架子。)"],["read","read(v.)讀、閱讀\nreader(n.)讀者\nreading(n.)閱讀\nread a book 看書\nread aloud 大聲朗讀\nI like to read books before bed.\n(我喜歡在睡前看書。)\nCan you read this word for me?\n(你能幫我念這個字嗎？)"],["ready","ready(adj./v.)準備好的、樂意的、使準備好\nreadiness(n.)準備就緒\nreadily(adv.)樂意地、容易地\nget ready 準備好\nbe ready to 準備好要⋯\nAre you ready for the test?\n(你準備好考試了嗎？)\nDinner is ready. Let's eat!\n(晚餐好了，我們來吃吧！)"],["real","real(adj.)真的、真實的\nreality(n.)現實\nreally(adv.)真正地、非常\nreal life 現實生活\na real friend 真正的朋友\nIs this a real diamond?\n(這是真的鑽石嗎？)\nHe is a real friend to me.\n(他是我真正的朋友。)"],["really","really(adv.)真正地、非常、真的嗎\nreal(adj.)真的、真實的\nreally good 非常好\nNot really. 不完全是、不太會。\nI really like this song.\n(我真的很喜歡這首歌。)\nThe movie was really funny.\n(這部電影真的很好笑。)"],["reason","reason(n./v.)理由、原因、推理\nreasonable(adj.)合理的\nreasoning(n.)推理\nfor this reason 因為這個原因\na good reason 好理由\nTell me the reason you were late.\n(告訴我你遲到的原因。)\nThere is no reason to be afraid.\n(沒有理由害怕。)"],["red","red(adj./n.)紅色的、紅色\n(無詞性變化)\nred light 紅燈\nturn red 變紅、臉紅\nShe is wearing a red dress today.\n(她今天穿著一件紅色洋裝。)\nHis face turned red with shame.\n(他羞得滿臉通紅。)"],["relative","relative(adj./n.)相對的、親戚\nrelatively(adv.)相對地\nrelate(v.)有關聯\nclose relative 近親\nrelative to 相對於\nWe visit our relatives during Chinese New Year.\n(我們在農曆新年拜訪親戚。)\nMy uncle is my only relative in Taipei.\n(我叔叔是我在臺北唯一的親戚。)"],["remember","remember(v.)記得、記住\n(無詞性變化)\nremember to 記得要⋯\nremember + V-ing 記得做過⋯\nRemember to bring your umbrella.\n(記得帶雨傘。)\nI remember meeting her last year.\n(我記得去年見過她。)"],["repeat","repeat(v.)重複、重說\nrepetition(n.)重複\nrepeated(adj.)重複的、反覆的\nrepeat after me 跟著我念\nrepeat a mistake 重蹈覆轍\nPlease repeat after me.\n(請跟著我念。)\nCould you repeat the question?\n(你可以再說一次問題嗎？)"],["report","report(n./v.)報告、報導\nreporter(n.)記者\nbook report 讀書報告\nnews report 新聞報導\nI have to write a book report.\n(我必須寫一篇讀書報告。)\nThe news reported a big fire last night.\n(新聞報導了昨晚的一場大火。)"],["reporter","reporter(n.)記者\nreport(n./v.)報告、報導\nnews reporter 新聞記者\nsports reporter 體育記者\nThe reporter asked the mayor many questions.\n(記者問了市長很多問題。)\nShe wants to be a news reporter.\n(她想當新聞記者。)"],["rest","rest(n./v.)休息、其餘部分\nrestful(adj.)寧靜的、使人放鬆的\ntake a rest 休息一下\nthe rest of 其餘的⋯\nLet's take a rest under the tree.\n(我們在樹下休息一下吧。)\nI will finish the rest of my homework later.\n(我晚點會完成其餘的作業。)"],["restaurant","restaurant(n.)餐廳\n(無詞性變化)\nChinese restaurant 中式餐廳\nfast-food restaurant 速食餐廳\nWe had dinner at a Chinese restaurant.\n(我們在一家中式餐廳吃晚餐。)\nThis restaurant is very popular.\n(這家餐廳非常受歡迎。)"],["rice","rice(n.)米、米飯、稻\n(無詞性變化)\na bowl of rice 一碗飯\nfried rice 炒飯\nI eat a bowl of rice every day.\n(我每天吃一碗飯。)\nMy mom makes great fried rice.\n(我媽媽做的炒飯很好吃。)"],["rich","rich(adj.)有錢的、富有的、豐富的\nrichness(n.)豐富\nriches(n.)財富\nrich in 富含⋯\nthe rich 有錢人\nHe became rich after his business grew.\n(他的生意擴大後就變得有錢了。)\nOranges are rich in vitamin C.\n(柳橙富含維他命C。)"],["ride","ride(n./v.)騎、搭乘、乘坐\nrider(n.)騎士、乘客\nride a bike 騎腳踏車\ngive someone a ride 載某人一程\nI ride my bike to school.\n(我騎腳踏車上學。)\nCan you give me a ride home?\n(你可以載我回家嗎？)"],["right","right(adv./adj./n.)正確的、右邊的、權利、立刻\nrightly(adv.)正確地、合理地\nright now 現在、立刻\nturn right 右轉\nYour answer is right.\n(你的答案是對的。)\nTurn right at the next corner.\n(在下一個轉角右轉。)"],["ring","ring(n./v.)戒指、環、鈴聲、(鈴)響、打電話\n(無詞性變化)\nwedding ring 婚戒\ngive someone a ring 打電話給某人\nThe phone is ringing.\n(電話在響。)\nShe wears a gold ring on her finger.\n(她手指上戴著一枚金戒指。)"],["rise","rise(n./v.)上升、升起、增加\nrising(adj.)上升的、新興的\nrise and fall 起落、興衰\non the rise 正在增加\nThe sun rises in the east.\n(太陽從東方升起。)\nPrices are on the rise again.\n(物價又在上漲了。)"],["river","river(n.)河、江\n(無詞性變化)\nriver bank 河岸\nalong the river 沿著河\nWe walked along the river.\n(我們沿著河邊散步。)\nThe river is very wide here.\n(這裡的河面非常寬。)"],["road","road(n.)路、道路\n(無詞性變化)\ncross the road 過馬路\non the road 在路上、在旅途中\nBe careful when you cross the road.\n(過馬路時要小心。)\nThis road goes to the beach.\n(這條路通往海灘。)"],["robot","robot(n.)機器人\nrobotic(adj.)機器人的、機械般的\nrobotics(n.)機器人學\nbuild a robot 製作機器人\nrobot vacuum 掃地機器人\nWe built a robot in science class.\n(我們在自然課做了一個機器人。)\nThe robot can clean the floor.\n(這台機器人會清潔地板。)"],["rock","rock(n./v.)岩石、搖滾樂、搖動\nrocky(adj.)多岩石的\nrock music 搖滾樂\nrock the boat 興風作浪\nHe sat on a big rock by the sea.\n(他坐在海邊的一塊大石頭上。)\nMy brother loves rock music.\n(我哥哥熱愛搖滾樂。)"],["roll","roll(v./n.)滾動、捲、捲狀物、名冊\nroller(n.)滾筒、滾輪\nroll up 捲起\negg roll 蛋捲\nThe ball rolled down the hill.\n(球滾下了山坡。)\nRoll up your sleeves before you wash.\n(洗東西前先把袖子捲起來。)"],["room","room(n./v.)房間、空間、同住\nroommate(n.)室友\nroomy(adj.)寬敞的\nliving room 客廳\nmake room for 騰出空間給⋯\nMy room is on the second floor.\n(我的房間在二樓。)\nThere is no room for the piano.\n(沒有空間放鋼琴了。)"],["root","root(n.)根、根源\n(無詞性變化)\nroot of the problem 問題的根源\ntake root 生根、紮根\nThe tree has deep roots.\n(這棵樹的根很深。)\nMoney is not the root of all problems.\n(錢不是一切問題的根源。)"],["rope","rope(n.)繩子\n(無詞性變化)\njump rope 跳繩\npull a rope 拉繩子\nThe kids like to jump rope.\n(孩子們喜歡跳繩。)\nHold the rope tightly.\n(抓緊繩子。)"],["rose","rose(n.)玫瑰\nrosy(adj.)玫瑰色的、樂觀的\nred rose 紅玫瑰\na bunch of roses 一束玫瑰\nHe gave her a red rose.\n(他送給她一朵紅玫瑰。)\nThese roses smell sweet.\n(這些玫瑰聞起來很香。)"],["round","round(adj./n./adv./prep./v.)圓的、一回合、環繞、繞過\n(無詞性變化)\nround trip 來回旅程\nall year round 一年到頭\nThe earth is round.\n(地球是圓的。)\nYou can swim here all year round.\n(你一年到頭都可以在這裡游泳。)"],["row","row(n./v.)一排、一列、划(船)\n(無詞性變化)\nin a row 連續地、成一排\nfront row 前排\nWe sat in the front row.\n(我們坐在前排。)\nThey rowed the boat across the lake.\n(他們划船橫越湖面。)"],["rule","rule(n./v.)規則、統治\nruler(n.)統治者、尺\nfollow the rules 遵守規則\nbreak a rule 違反規定\nWe must follow the school rules.\n(我們必須遵守校規。)\nThe king ruled the country for forty years.\n(國王統治這個國家四十年。)"],["ruler","ruler(n.)尺、統治者\nrule(n./v.)規則、統治\nuse a ruler 用尺\nwise ruler 賢明的統治者\nDraw a line with your ruler.\n(用你的尺畫一條線。)\nHe was a wise ruler.\n(他是一位賢明的統治者。)"],["run","run(v.)跑、經營、運轉\nrunner(n.)跑者\nrunning(n.)跑步\nrun fast 跑得快\nrun a business 經營事業\nHe runs very fast.\n(他跑得非常快。)\nMy aunt runs a small shop.\n(我阿姨經營一家小店。)"],["sad","sad(adj.)難過的、悲傷的\nsadness(n.)悲傷\nsadly(adv.)悲傷地、遺憾地\nfeel sad 感到難過\nsad news 令人難過的消息\nShe felt sad when her dog got sick.\n(她的狗生病時，她感到很難過。)\nIt was a sad movie about a lost boy.\n(那是一部關於一個走失男孩的悲傷電影。)"],["safe","safe(adj./n.)安全的、保險箱\nsafety(n.)安全\nsafely(adv.)安全地\nsafe and sound 平安無事\nkeep... safe 保護⋯安全\nPlease stay safe on your way home.\n(回家路上請注意安全。)\nHe keeps his money in a safe.\n(他把錢放在保險箱裡。)"],["salad","salad(n.)沙拉\n(無詞性變化)\nfruit salad 水果沙拉\nsalad dressing 沙拉醬\nI had a green salad for lunch.\n(我午餐吃了一份生菜沙拉。)\nMom made a big fruit salad for the party.\n(媽媽為派對做了一大盆水果沙拉。)"],["sale","sale(n.)出售、特價拍賣\nsell(v.)賣\non sale 特價中、出售中\nfor sale 待售\nThese shoes are on sale today.\n(這些鞋子今天特價。)\nThe old house is now for sale.\n(那棟老房子現在要出售。)"],["salt","salt(n./v./adj.)鹽、加鹽、鹹的\nsalty(adj.)鹹的\na pinch of salt 一小撮鹽\nsalt water 鹽水\nPlease pass me the salt.\n(請把鹽遞給我。)\nAdd a little salt to the soup.\n(在湯裡加一點鹽。)"],["same","same(adj./pron./adv.)相同的、同樣的事物\n(無詞性變化)\nthe same as 和⋯一樣\nat the same time 同時\nWe go to the same school.\n(我們上同一所學校。)\nMy bag is the same as yours.\n(我的包包跟你的一樣。)"],["save","save(v.)拯救、節省、儲存\nsaving(n.)節省、存款(常用複數 savings)\nsave money 存錢\nsave time 節省時間\nHe saved a little girl from the river.\n(他從河裡救起一個小女孩。)\nI want to save money for a new bike.\n(我想存錢買一台新腳踏車。)"],["say","say(v.)說\nsaying(n.)諺語、俗話\nsay hello to 向⋯問好\nsay goodbye 道別\nWhat did the teacher say?\n(老師說了什麼？)\nPlease say hello to your parents for me.\n(請替我向你父母問好。)"],["school","school(n./v.)學校、教育\nschooling(n.)學校教育\ngo to school 上學\nhigh school 高中\nI walk to school every morning.\n(我每天早上走路上學。)\nMy brother is a high school student.\n(我哥哥是高中生。)"],["science","science(n.)科學\nscientist(n.)科學家\nscientific(adj.)科學的\nscience class 自然科學課\ncomputer science 電腦科學\nScience is my favorite subject.\n(自然科學是我最喜歡的科目。)\nWe did a fun test in science class.\n(我們在自然課做了一個有趣的實驗。)"],["sea","sea(n.)海、海洋\n(無詞性變化)\nby the sea 在海邊\nsea level 海平面\nWe swam in the sea last summer.\n(我們去年夏天在海裡游泳。)\nThey live in a small house by the sea.\n(他們住在海邊的一間小房子裡。)"],["season","season(n.)季節\nseasonal(adj.)季節性的\nrainy season 雨季\nfour seasons 四季\nWhich season do you like best?\n(你最喜歡哪個季節？)\nTaiwan has a rainy season in May.\n(台灣在五月有梅雨季。)"],["seat","seat(n./v.)座位、使就座\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a seat 坐下\nwindow seat 靠窗座位\nPlease take a seat and wait here.\n(請坐下在這裡等一下。)\nI want a window seat on the plane.\n(我在飛機上想要靠窗的座位。)"],["second","second(adj./n./adv.)第二的、秒、第二地\nsecondly(adv.)其次\nsecond floor 二樓\nwait a second 等一下\nMy room is on the second floor.\n(我的房間在二樓。)\nWait a second, I can't find my key.\n(等一下，我找不到我的鑰匙。)"],["secretary","secretary(n.)祕書\n(無詞性變化)\npersonal secretary 私人祕書\nsecretary general 祕書長\nThe secretary answered the phone.\n(祕書接了電話。)\nShe works as a secretary in a bank.\n(她在一家銀行當祕書。)"],["see","see(v.)看見、明白、見面\nsight(n.)視力、景象\nsee a doctor 看醫生\nI see. 我明白了。\nI can see the mountains from my window.\n(我從窗戶可以看到山。)\nYou should see a doctor about your cough.\n(你應該為了咳嗽去看醫生。)"],["seed","seed(n.)種子\n(無詞性變化)\nplant seeds 播種\nsunflower seeds 葵花子\nWe planted some seeds in the garden.\n(我們在花園裡種了一些種子。)\nBirds like to eat sunflower seeds.\n(鳥喜歡吃葵花子。)"],["sell","sell(v.)賣、銷售\nseller(n.)賣方、銷售者\nsale(n.)出售\nsell out 賣完\nsell well 暢銷\nThat shop sells fresh bread.\n(那家店賣新鮮的麵包。)\nThe concert tickets sold out in one hour.\n(演唱會門票一小時內就賣完了。)"],["send","send(v.)寄、送、派遣\nsender(n.)寄件人\nsend a message 傳訊息\nsend for 派人去請\nI will send you a message tonight.\n(我今晚會傳訊息給你。)\nShe sent a card to her grandmother.\n(她寄了一張卡片給她奶奶。)"],["sentence","sentence(n./v.)句子、判決、宣判\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a sentence 造句\na prison sentence 徒刑\nPlease make a sentence with this word.\n(請用這個字造一個句子。)\nThe man was sentenced to two years in prison.\n(那名男子被判刑兩年。)"],["serious","serious(adj.)嚴重的、認真的、嚴肅的\nseriously(adv.)嚴重地、認真地\nserious problem 嚴重的問題\nbe serious about 對⋯認真\nAre you serious or just joking?\n(你是認真的還是在開玩笑？)\nAir pollution is a serious problem here.\n(空氣汙染在這裡是個嚴重的問題。)"],["service","service(n.)服務\nserve(v.)服務、供應\ncustomer service 客服\nservice station 加油站、服務站\nThe service in this restaurant is great.\n(這家餐廳的服務很好。)\nPlease call customer service for help.\n(請打電話給客服尋求協助。)"],["set","set(v./n.)放置、設定、一套\nsetting(n.)背景、設定\nset the table 擺餐具\nset up 設立、架設\nThe sun sets in the west.\n(太陽從西邊落下。)\nCan you help me set the table?\n(你可以幫我擺餐具嗎？)"],["several","several(adj./pron.)幾個、數個\n(無詞性變化)\nseveral times 好幾次\nseveral days 幾天\nI have read this book several times.\n(這本書我讀過好幾次。)\nSeveral students were late this morning.\n(今天早上有幾個學生遲到。)"],["shake","shake(v./n.)搖動、顫抖、搖晃\nshaky(adj.)搖晃的、不穩的\nshake hands 握手\nmilk shake 奶昔\nThey shook hands after the game.\n(比賽後他們握了手。)\nShake the bottle before you drink it.\n(喝之前先搖一搖瓶子。)"],["shall","shall(aux.)將、要(用於提議)\n(無詞性變化)\nShall we...? 我們要不要⋯？\nShall I...? 要我⋯嗎？\nShall we go to the park?\n(我們要不要去公園？)\nShall I open the window for you?\n(要我幫你開窗嗎？)"],["shape","shape(n.)形狀、狀態\n(無詞性變化)\nin good shape 狀況良好\nin the shape of 呈⋯形狀\nThe cake is in the shape of a heart.\n(這個蛋糕是心形的。)\nMy grandpa is still in good shape.\n(我爺爺身體狀況還很好。)"],["share","share(v./n.)分享、分擔、一份\n(無詞性變化)\nshare with 和⋯分享\nshare an idea 分享想法\nI share a room with my sister.\n(我和我妹妹共用一個房間。)\nLet's share this pizza together.\n(我們一起分這個披薩吧。)"],["sharp","sharp(adj./adv.)鋒利的、尖銳的、(時間)整\nsharpen(v.)削尖、磨利\nsharply(adv.)急劇地、嚴厲地\na sharp knife 一把鋒利的刀\nat seven sharp 七點整\nBe careful, the knife is very sharp.\n(小心，這把刀很鋒利。)\nThe class starts at eight sharp.\n(課程八點整開始。)"],["she (her, hers, herself)","she(pron.)她\nher(pron.)她(受格)、她的\nhers(pron.)她的(東西)\nherself(pron.)她自己\nby herself 她獨自\nshe and I 她和我\nShe is my best friend.\n(她是我最好的朋友。)\nShe made the cake by herself.\n(她自己做了這個蛋糕。)"],["sheep","sheep(n.)羊、綿羊(單複數同形)\n(無詞性變化)\na flock of sheep 一群羊\ncount sheep 數羊\nThere are many sheep on the farm.\n(農場上有很多綿羊。)\nI count sheep when I can't sleep.\n(我睡不著的時候會數羊。)"],["ship","ship(n./v.)船、運送\nshipping(n.)運輸、運費\nby ship 搭船\nship the goods 運送貨物\nThey went to the island by ship.\n(他們搭船去那座島。)\nThe store will ship the book to you.\n(店家會把書寄送給你。)"],["shirt","shirt(n.)襯衫\n(無詞性變化)\ndress shirt 正式襯衫\na white shirt 白襯衫\nHe wears a white shirt to work.\n(他穿白襯衫去上班。)\nI bought a new T-shirt yesterday.\n(我昨天買了一件新的T恤。)"],["shoe(s)","shoe(n.)鞋子(常用複數 shoes)\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of shoes 一雙鞋\nrunning shoes 跑鞋\nPlease take off your shoes at the door.\n(請在門口脫鞋。)\nI need a new pair of running shoes.\n(我需要一雙新的跑鞋。)"],["shop","shop(n./v.)商店、購物\nshopping(n.)購物\nshopper(n.)購物者\ngo shopping 去購物\ncoffee shop 咖啡店\nLet's go shopping this weekend.\n(這週末我們去購物吧。)\nThere is a coffee shop near my school.\n(我學校附近有一家咖啡店。)"],["short","short(adj.)短的、矮的、不足的\nshorten(v.)縮短\nshortly(adv.)不久\nbe short of 缺少\nfor short 簡稱\nMy little brother is short but strong.\n(我弟弟個子矮但很強壯。)\nWe are short of time, so hurry up.\n(我們時間不夠，所以快一點。)"],["shorts","shorts(n.)短褲\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of shorts 一件短褲\nwear shorts 穿短褲\nHe likes to wear shorts in summer.\n(他夏天喜歡穿短褲。)\nI bought a pair of blue shorts.\n(我買了一件藍色短褲。)"],["shoulder","shoulder(n.)肩膀\n(無詞性變化)\nshoulder to shoulder 肩並肩\nshrug one's shoulders 聳肩\nMy shoulder hurts after the game.\n(比賽後我的肩膀很痛。)\nShe put her hand on my shoulder.\n(她把手放在我的肩膀上。)"],["shout","shout(v./n.)大叫、喊叫\n(無詞性變化)\nshout at 對⋯吼叫\nshout for help 大聲呼救\nDon't shout at your little sister.\n(不要對你妹妹大吼。)\nHe shouted for help in the water.\n(他在水中大聲呼救。)"],["show","show(v./n.)展示、表演、節目\n(無詞性變化)\nshow... around 帶⋯參觀\nTV show 電視節目\nCan you show me the way to the station?\n(你可以告訴我去車站的路嗎？)\nThis TV show is very funny.\n(這個電視節目很好笑。)"],["shower","shower(n./v.)淋浴、陣雨、淋浴\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a shower 淋浴、洗澡\nrain shower 陣雨\nI take a shower every night.\n(我每天晚上洗澡。)\nThere may be showers this afternoon.\n(今天下午可能會有陣雨。)"],["sick","sick(adj.)生病的、噁心的、厭倦的\nsickness(n.)疾病\nget sick 生病\nbe sick of 厭倦⋯\nTom is sick, so he is at home today.\n(湯姆生病了，所以他今天在家。)\nI'm sick of eating noodles every day.\n(我厭倦每天吃麵了。)"],["side","side(n.)邊、側面、一方\n(無詞性變化)\nside by side 並排\non the other side 在另一邊\nThe bank is on the other side of the street.\n(銀行在街道的另一邊。)\nWe walked side by side in the park.\n(我們在公園並肩散步。)"],["sight","sight(n./v.)視力、景象、看見\nsee(v.)看見\nat first sight 一見(鍾情)\ncatch sight of 瞥見\nThe sunset was a beautiful sight.\n(夕陽是一幅美麗的景象。)\nThey fell in love at first sight.\n(他們一見鍾情。)"],["sign","sign(n./v.)標誌、跡象、簽名\nsignature(n.)簽名\nsignal(n.)信號\nsign up 報名\nroad sign 路標\nPlease sign your name here.\n(請在這裡簽名。)\nThe sign says 'No Parking'.\n(標誌上寫著「禁止停車」。)"],["simple","simple(adj.)簡單的、樸素的\nsimply(adv.)簡單地、只是\nsimplify(v.)簡化\nsimple question 簡單的問題\nsimple life 簡樸的生活\nThe answer is very simple.\n(答案非常簡單。)\nMy grandparents live a simple life.\n(我的祖父母過著簡樸的生活。)"],["since","since(conj./prep./adv.)自從、既然、從那時起\n(無詞性變化)\never since 從那時起一直\nsince then 從那時起\nI have lived here since 2015.\n(我從2015年起就住在這裡。)\nSince it's raining, let's stay home.\n(既然在下雨，我們就待在家吧。)"],["sing","sing(v.)唱歌\nsinger(n.)歌手\nsong(n.)歌曲\nsing a song 唱歌\nsing along 跟著唱\nShe sings very well.\n(她唱歌唱得很好。)\nLet's sing a song for Mom's birthday.\n(我們為媽媽的生日唱首歌吧。)"],["singer","singer(n.)歌手\nsing(v.)唱歌\npop singer 流行歌手\nlead singer 主唱\nThat singer has a beautiful voice.\n(那位歌手有一副美妙的嗓音。)\nShe wants to be a pop singer.\n(她想成為流行歌手。)"],["sir","sir(n.)先生、閣下(尊稱)\n(無詞性變化)\nYes, sir. 是的，先生。\nDear Sir 敬啟者\nExcuse me, sir, is this your bag?\n(不好意思，先生，這是您的包包嗎？)\nCan I help you, sir?\n(先生，需要幫忙嗎？)"],["sister","sister(n.)姐妹\n(無詞性變化)\nolder sister 姐姐\nyounger sister 妹妹\nMy older sister is a nurse.\n(我姐姐是護理師。)\nI play games with my little sister.\n(我和我妹妹一起玩遊戲。)"],["sit","sit(v.)坐\nseat(n.)座位\nsit down 坐下\nsit up 坐直\nPlease sit down and have some tea.\n(請坐下喝點茶。)\nThe cat is sitting on the sofa.\n(貓正坐在沙發上。)"],["size","size(n./v.)尺寸、大小、按大小分類\n(無詞性變化)\nshoe size 鞋子尺寸\nthe same size 同樣大小\nWhat size do you wear?\n(你穿什麼尺寸？)\nThese two boxes are the same size.\n(這兩個箱子一樣大。)"],["skirt","skirt(n.)裙子\n(無詞性變化)\nshort skirt 短裙\nlong skirt 長裙\nShe wore a red skirt to the party.\n(她穿了一件紅裙子去派對。)\nThis long skirt is very pretty.\n(這件長裙很漂亮。)"],["sky","sky(n.)天空\n(無詞性變化)\nblue sky 藍天\nin the sky 在天空中\nThe sky is clear and blue today.\n(今天的天空晴朗又湛藍。)\nI saw many stars in the sky.\n(我看到天空中有很多星星。)"],["sleep","sleep(n./v.)睡眠、睡覺\nsleepy(adj.)想睡的\nasleep(adj.)睡著的\ngo to sleep 去睡覺\nfall asleep 睡著\nI usually sleep eight hours a night.\n(我通常每晚睡八小時。)\nThe baby fell asleep in my arms.\n(寶寶在我懷裡睡著了。)"],["slim","slim(adj.)苗條的、微小的\n(無詞性變化)\nslim figure 苗條的身材\nslim chance 機會渺茫\nShe stays slim by running every day.\n(她靠每天跑步保持苗條。)\nOur chance of winning is slim.\n(我們獲勝的機會很渺茫。)"],["slow","slow(adj./v./adv.)慢的、減慢、慢慢地\nslowly(adv.)慢慢地\nslow down 放慢速度\nslow motion 慢動作\nPlease slow down, I can't follow you.\n(請慢一點，我跟不上你。)\nMy computer is very slow today.\n(我的電腦今天很慢。)"],["small","small(adj./n./adv.)小的、少的\n(無詞性變化)\nsmall town 小鎮\na small amount 少量\nHe lives in a small town.\n(他住在一個小鎮上。)\nThis shirt is too small for me.\n(這件襯衫對我來說太小了。)"],["smart","smart(adj.)聰明的、時髦的\n(無詞性變化)\nsmart phone 智慧型手機\nsmart choice 明智的選擇\nAmy is a smart girl.\n(艾咪是個聰明的女孩。)\nTaking the MRT was a smart choice.\n(搭捷運是個明智的選擇。)"],["smell","smell(n./v.)氣味、聞、聞起來\nsmelly(adj.)有臭味的\nsmell good 聞起來很香\nsense of smell 嗅覺\nThe flowers smell so sweet.\n(這些花聞起來好香。)\nI love the smell of fresh bread.\n(我愛新鮮麵包的味道。)"],["smile","smile(n./v.)微笑\n(無詞性變化)\nsmile at 對⋯微笑\na big smile 燦爛的笑容\nThe baby smiled at me.\n(寶寶對我微笑。)\nShe has a big smile on her face.\n(她臉上掛著燦爛的笑容。)"],["smoke","smoke(n./v.)煙、抽菸、冒煙\nsmoker(n.)吸菸者\nsmoking(n.)吸菸\ngive up smoking 戒菸\nNo Smoking 禁止吸菸\nMy dad stopped smoking last year.\n(我爸爸去年戒菸了。)\nBlack smoke came out of the kitchen.\n(黑煙從廚房冒出來。)"],["snake","snake(n./v.)蛇、蜿蜒\n(無詞性變化)\na poisonous snake 毒蛇\nsnake bite 蛇咬傷\nI am afraid of snakes.\n(我怕蛇。)\nThe river snakes through the valley.\n(那條河蜿蜒流過山谷。)"],["snow","snow(n./v.)雪、下雪\nsnowy(adj.)下雪的、多雪的\nheavy snow 大雪\nsnow-covered 被雪覆蓋的\nIt often snows in Japan in winter.\n(日本冬天常下雪。)\nThe kids played in the snow.\n(孩子們在雪地裡玩。)"],["so","so(adv./conj.)如此、非常、所以\n(無詞性變化)\nso far 到目前為止\nand so on 等等\nI am so happy to see you.\n(見到你我好開心。)\nIt was late, so we took a taxi.\n(時間晚了，所以我們搭計程車。)"],["sofa","sofa(n.)沙發\n(無詞性變化)\nsit on the sofa 坐在沙發上\nsofa bed 沙發床\nDad is sleeping on the sofa.\n(爸爸正在沙發上睡覺。)\nWe bought a new sofa for the living room.\n(我們為客廳買了一張新沙發。)"],["soldier","soldier(n.)軍人、士兵\n(無詞性變化)\nbrave soldier 勇敢的士兵\nbecome a soldier 當兵\nMy uncle was a soldier.\n(我叔叔以前是軍人。)\nThe soldiers helped people after the flood.\n(士兵們在水災後幫助民眾。)"],["some","some(adj./pron.)一些、某個\n(無詞性變化)\nsome day 將來某天\nsome of 其中一些\nI want some water, please.\n(我想要一些水，謝謝。)\nSome of my friends like basketball.\n(我的一些朋友喜歡籃球。)"],["someone/somebody","someone(pron./n.)某人、重要人物\nsomebody(pron./n.)某人(同 someone)\nsomeone else 別人\nsomeone special 特別的人\nSomeone is knocking on the door.\n(有人在敲門。)\nIs there someone who can help me?\n(有沒有人可以幫我？)"],["something","something(pron./n.)某事、某物\n(無詞性變化)\nsomething else 別的東西\nsomething to eat 吃的東西\nI want something to drink.\n(我想喝點東西。)\nThere is something wrong with my phone.\n(我的手機有點問題。)"],["sometimes","sometimes(adv.)有時候\n(無詞性變化)\nsometimes... sometimes... 有時⋯有時⋯\nonly sometimes 只是偶爾\nSometimes I walk to school.\n(我有時候走路上學。)\nHe sometimes forgets his homework.\n(他有時候會忘了帶作業。)"],["somewhere","somewhere(adv.)在某處\n(無詞性變化)\nsomewhere else 別的地方\nsomewhere near 附近某處\nI left my keys somewhere.\n(我把鑰匙忘在某個地方了。)\nLet's go somewhere quiet to talk.\n(我們去個安靜的地方談吧。)"],["son","son(n.)兒子\n(無詞性變化)\nonly son 獨子\noldest son 長子\nThey have two sons and a daughter.\n(他們有兩個兒子和一個女兒。)\nHer son is in the third grade.\n(她兒子讀三年級。)"],["song","song(n.)歌曲\nsing(v.)唱歌\nsing a song 唱首歌\nlove song 情歌\nThis is my favorite song.\n(這是我最喜歡的歌。)\nThe birds' songs woke me up.\n(鳥鳴聲把我吵醒了。)"],["soon","soon(adv.)很快、不久\n(無詞性變化)\nas soon as 一⋯就⋯\nSee you soon. 待會見。\nThe bus will come soon.\n(公車很快就會來。)\nCall me as soon as you get home.\n(你一到家就打電話給我。)"],["sore","sore(adj./n.)疼痛的、痛處\nsoreness(n.)疼痛\nsore throat 喉嚨痛\nsore eyes 眼睛痠痛\nI have a sore throat today.\n(我今天喉嚨痛。)\nMy legs are sore after the long walk.\n(走了很久之後我的腿很痠痛。)"],["sorry","sorry(adj.)抱歉的、難過的、遺憾的\n(無詞性變化)\nfeel sorry for 為⋯感到難過\nI'm sorry to hear that. 聽到這消息我很遺憾。\nI'm sorry I'm late.\n(對不起，我遲到了。)\nI feel sorry for the lost dog.\n(我替那隻走失的狗感到難過。)"],["sound","sound(n.)聲音\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a sound 發出聲音\nsound effect 音效\nI heard a strange sound outside.\n(我聽到外面有奇怪的聲音。)\nDon't make a sound, the baby is sleeping.\n(別出聲，寶寶在睡覺。)"],["soup","soup(n.)湯\n(無詞性變化)\nchicken soup 雞湯\na bowl of soup 一碗湯\nMom made chicken soup for me.\n(媽媽為我煮了雞湯。)\nWould you like a bowl of soup?\n(你想來一碗湯嗎？)"],["south","south(n./adj./adv.)南方、南方的、向南\nsouthern(adj.)南方的\nin the south of 在⋯的南部\nSouth Africa 南非\nKaohsiung is in the south of Taiwan.\n(高雄在台灣的南部。)\nBirds fly south in winter.\n(鳥在冬天往南飛。)"],["space","space(n./v.)空間、太空、隔開\nspacious(adj.)寬敞的\nouter space 外太空\nparking space 停車位\nThere is not enough space in my room.\n(我的房間空間不夠。)\nHe wants to travel into space someday.\n(他想有一天去太空旅行。)"],["speak","speak(v.)說話、說(某種語言)、演講\nspeaker(n.)說話者、喇叭\nspeech(n.)演說\nspeak English 說英文\nspeak to 和⋯說話\nCan you speak Japanese?\n(你會說日文嗎？)\nMay I speak to Mr. Lin, please?\n(請問我可以和林先生說話嗎？)"],["special","special(adj.)特別的、專門的\nspecially(adv.)特別地\nspecialist(n.)專家\nspecial gift 特別的禮物\nspecial offer 特價優惠\nToday is a special day for me.\n(今天對我來說是特別的日子。)\nThe store has a special offer this week.\n(這家店本週有特價優惠。)"],["spell","spell(v.)拼寫\nspelling(n.)拼字\nspell out 一個字母一個字母地拼出\nspelling test 拼字測驗\nHow do you spell your name?\n(你的名字怎麼拼？)\nI got full marks on the spelling test.\n(我拼字測驗拿到滿分。)"],["spend","spend(v.)花費(時間、金錢)、度過\nspending(n.)開銷\nspend money on 花錢在⋯\nspend time with 和⋯共度時光\nI spend an hour on homework every day.\n(我每天花一小時寫功課。)\nShe likes to spend time with her family.\n(她喜歡和家人共度時光。)"],["spring","spring(n./v.)春天、泉水、彈跳\n(無詞性變化)\nin spring 在春天\nhot spring 溫泉\nFlowers bloom in spring.\n(花在春天綻放。)\nWe went to a hot spring in Beitou.\n(我們去北投泡溫泉。)"],["square","square(n./adj.)正方形、廣場、正方形的\n(無詞性變化)\ntown square 城鎮廣場\nsquare meter 平方公尺\nDraw a square on your paper.\n(在你的紙上畫一個正方形。)\nMany people dance in the square at night.\n(晚上很多人在廣場上跳舞。)"],["stair","stair(n.)樓梯(常用複數 stairs)\nstaircase(n.)樓梯間\ngo up the stairs 上樓梯\nfall down the stairs 從樓梯跌下\nPlease walk up the stairs slowly.\n(請慢慢走上樓梯。)\nHe fell down the stairs and hurt his leg.\n(他從樓梯上摔下來，傷了腿。)"],["stand","stand(v./n.)站立、忍受、攤子\n(無詞性變化)\nstand up 站起來\ncan't stand 無法忍受\nPlease stand up when the teacher comes in.\n(老師進來時請起立。)\nI can't stand the noise anymore.\n(我再也受不了這噪音了。)"],["star","star(n./v.)星星、明星、主演\n(無詞性變化)\nmovie star 電影明星\nshooting star 流星\nThe stars are bright tonight.\n(今晚的星星很亮。)\nShe wants to be a movie star.\n(她想成為電影明星。)"],["start","start(v./n.)開始、出發、開端\n(無詞性變化)\nstart with 從⋯開始\nfrom start to finish 從頭到尾\nThe movie starts at seven.\n(電影七點開始。)\nLet's start with an easy question.\n(我們從簡單的問題開始吧。)"],["station","station(n.)車站、站、所\n(無詞性變化)\ntrain station 火車站\npolice station 警察局\nI'll meet you at the train station.\n(我會在火車站跟你碰面。)\nThe MRT station is near my home.\n(捷運站在我家附近。)"],["stay","stay(v./n.)停留、保持、逗留\n(無詞性變化)\nstay up 熬夜\nstay healthy 保持健康\nI stayed at home all day.\n(我一整天都待在家。)\nDon't stay up too late.\n(不要熬夜太晚。)"],["still","still(adv./adj.)仍然、靜止的\n(無詞性變化)\nstand still 站著不動\nstill water 靜水、無氣泡水\nHe is still at school.\n(他還在學校。)\nPlease sit still for a moment.\n(請坐著別動一下。)"],["stop","stop(v./n.)停止、阻止、站牌\n(無詞性變化)\nbus stop 公車站\nstop... from 阻止⋯做\nThe bus stop is across the street.\n(公車站在對街。)\nPlease stop talking in class.\n(上課時請不要說話。)"],["store","store(n./v.)商店、儲存\nstorage(n.)儲藏\nconvenience store 便利商店\ndepartment store 百貨公司\nI bought milk at the convenience store.\n(我在便利商店買了牛奶。)\nWe store old books in the box.\n(我們把舊書存放在箱子裡。)"],["story","story(n.)故事、樓層\n(無詞性變化)\ntell a story 講故事\nshort story 短篇故事\nGrandma told us a funny story.\n(奶奶跟我們講了一個好笑的故事。)\nHe lives in a three-story house.\n(他住在一棟三層樓的房子。)"],["straight","straight(adv./adj./n.)直直地、直的、直線\nstraighten(v.)弄直、整頓\ngo straight 直走\nstraight hair 直髮\nGo straight and turn left.\n(直走然後左轉。)\nShe has long straight hair.\n(她有一頭長直髮。)"],["strange","strange(adj.)奇怪的、陌生的\nstranger(n.)陌生人\nstrangely(adv.)奇怪地\nstrange sound 奇怪的聲音\nfeel strange 感覺怪怪的\nThat's strange, the door is open.\n(真奇怪，門是開著的。)\nI'm in a strange city alone.\n(我獨自在一個陌生的城市裡。)"],["street","street(n.)街道\n(無詞性變化)\ncross the street 過馬路\nstreet food 路邊小吃\nLook both ways before you cross the street.\n(過馬路前要看兩邊。)\nTaiwan is famous for its street food.\n(台灣以路邊小吃聞名。)"],["string","string(n.)線、細繩、弦\n(無詞性變化)\na piece of string 一條繩子\nguitar string 吉他弦\nTie the box with a string.\n(用一條繩子把箱子綁起來。)\nOne of the guitar strings broke.\n(其中一根吉他弦斷了。)"],["strong","strong(adj.)強壯的、強烈的、濃的\nstrength(n.)力量\nstrongly(adv.)強烈地\nstrong wind 強風\nstrong coffee 濃咖啡\nMy dad is tall and strong.\n(我爸爸又高又壯。)\nI don't like strong coffee.\n(我不喜歡濃咖啡。)"],["student","student(n.)學生\nstudy(v.)學習\nhigh school student 高中生\nexchange student 交換學生\nThere are thirty students in my class.\n(我們班有三十個學生。)\nShe is an exchange student from Japan.\n(她是來自日本的交換學生。)"],["study","study(n./v.)學習、研究、書房\nstudent(n.)學生\nstudy hard 用功讀書\nstudy abroad 出國留學\nI study English every day.\n(我每天學英文。)\nHe wants to study abroad in the future.\n(他將來想出國留學。)"],["stupid","stupid(adj.)愚蠢的、笨的\nstupidity(n.)愚蠢\nstupid question 蠢問題\nfeel stupid 覺得自己很笨\nThere are no stupid questions.\n(沒有所謂的蠢問題。)\nIt was stupid of me to lose my phone.\n(我把手機弄丟真是太笨了。)"],["subject","subject(n.)科目、主題、主詞\n(無詞性變化)\nfavorite subject 最喜歡的科目\nchange the subject 轉換話題\nMath is my favorite subject.\n(數學是我最喜歡的科目。)\nLet's change the subject.\n(我們換個話題吧。)"],["successful","successful(adj.)成功的\nsuccess(n.)成功\nsucceed(v.)成功\nsuccessfully(adv.)成功地\na successful business 成功的事業\nbe successful in 在⋯方面成功\nThe school party was very successful.\n(學校的派對非常成功。)\nHe is a successful writer.\n(他是一位成功的作家。)"],["sugar","sugar(n.)糖\nsugary(adj.)含糖的、甜的\nno sugar 無糖\nbrown sugar 黑糖\nI drink tea without sugar.\n(我喝茶不加糖。)\nToo much sugar is bad for your teeth.\n(吃太多糖對牙齒不好。)"],["sun","sun(n./v.)太陽、陽光、曬太陽\nsunny(adj.)晴朗的\nsunshine(n.)陽光\nin the sun 在陽光下\nthe rising sun 旭日\nThe sun rises in the east.\n(太陽從東方升起。)\nCats like to sleep in the sun.\n(貓喜歡在陽光下睡覺。)"],["sunny","sunny(adj.)晴朗的、陽光充足的、開朗的\nsun(n.)太陽\nsunny day 晴天\nsunny smile 開朗的笑容\nIt's a sunny day for a picnic.\n(今天是適合野餐的晴天。)\nShe always has a sunny smile.\n(她總是帶著開朗的笑容。)"],["supermarket","supermarket(n.)超級市場\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to the supermarket 去超市\nsupermarket shelf 超市貨架\nWe buy food at the supermarket.\n(我們在超市買食物。)\nThe supermarket opens at nine.\n(超市九點開門。)"],["sure","sure(adj./adv.)確定的、當然\nsurely(adv.)必定、當然\nmake sure 確定\nbe sure of 確信\nAre you sure about the answer?\n(你確定答案嗎？)\nMake sure you lock the door.\n(一定要鎖門。)"],["surprise","surprise(n./v.)驚喜、驚訝、使驚訝\nsurprising(adj.)令人驚訝的\nsurprised(adj.)感到驚訝的\nin surprise 驚訝地\nsurprise party 驚喜派對\nWe had a surprise party for Dad.\n(我們為爸爸辦了一場驚喜派對。)\nThe news surprised everyone.\n(這個消息讓大家都很驚訝。)"],["surprised","surprised(adj.)感到驚訝的\nsurprise(n./v.)驚喜、使驚訝\nsurprising(adj.)令人驚訝的\nbe surprised at 對⋯感到驚訝\npleasantly surprised 又驚又喜\nI was surprised at the big gift.\n(我對那份大禮感到很驚訝。)\nShe looked surprised to see me.\n(她看到我時一臉驚訝。)"],["sweet","sweet(adj.)甜的、可愛的、貼心的\nsweetness(n.)甜美\nsweeten(v.)使變甜\nsweet tooth 愛吃甜食\nsweet dreams 祝好夢\nThis cake is too sweet for me.\n(這個蛋糕對我來說太甜了。)\nIt's sweet of you to help me.\n(你幫我真是太貼心了。)"],["table","table(n.)桌子、表格\n(無詞性變化)\nset the table 擺餐具\ntable tennis 桌球\nPlease put the books on the table.\n(請把書放在桌上。)\nLook at the table on page ten.\n(請看第十頁的表格。)"],["tail","tail(n.)尾巴\n(無詞性變化)\nwag its tail 搖尾巴\nlong tail 長尾巴\nThe dog is wagging its tail.\n(那隻狗在搖尾巴。)\nA monkey has a long tail.\n(猴子有一條長尾巴。)"],["take","take(v.)拿、帶走、搭乘、花費(時間)\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a bus 搭公車\ntake a picture 拍照\nI take the MRT to school.\n(我搭捷運上學。)\nIt takes ten minutes to get there.\n(到那裡要花十分鐘。)"],["talk","talk(v./n.)說話、談論、演講\ntalkative(adj.)健談的\ntalk to 和……說話\ngive a talk 演講\nCan I talk to you for a minute?\n(我可以跟你談一下嗎？)\nWe talked about the movie all night.\n(我們整晚都在聊那部電影。)"],["tall","tall(adj.)高的\n(無詞性變化)\ntall building 高樓\ngrow tall 長高\nMy brother is very tall.\n(我哥哥很高。)\nHow tall are you?\n(你多高？)"],["tape","tape(n.)膠帶、錄音帶\n(無詞性變化)\ntape measure 捲尺\ntape recorder 錄音機\nI need some tape for this box.\n(我需要一些膠帶來封這個箱子。)\nFix the poster with tape.\n(用膠帶把海報貼好。)"],["taste","taste(n./v.)味道、品嚐、品味\ntasty(adj.)美味的\ntaste good 嚐起來很好吃\nsweet taste 甜味\nThis soup tastes great.\n(這湯很好喝。)\nShe has good taste in clothes.\n(她穿衣服很有品味。)"],["taxicab/taxi/cab","taxicab(n.)計程車\ntaxi(n.)計程車\ncab(n.)計程車(口語)\ntake a taxi 搭計程車\ntaxi driver 計程車司機\nLet's take a taxi to the station.\n(我們搭計程車去車站吧。)\nThe taxi driver was very kind.\n(那位計程車司機很親切。)"],["tea","tea(n.)茶\nteapot(n.)茶壺\nbubble tea 珍珠奶茶\na cup of tea 一杯茶\nWould you like a cup of tea?\n(你想喝杯茶嗎？)\nBubble tea is popular in Taiwan.\n(珍珠奶茶在台灣很受歡迎。)"],["teach","teach(v.)教\nteacher(n.)老師\nteaching(n.)教學\nteach English 教英文\nteach oneself 自學\nMy mom teaches English.\n(我媽媽教英文。)\nCan you teach me to swim?\n(你可以教我游泳嗎？)"],["teacher","teacher(n.)老師\nteach(v.)教\nEnglish teacher 英文老師\nTeacher's Day 教師節\nOur teacher is very nice.\n(我們的老師人很好。)\nWe gave our teacher a card on Teacher's Day.\n(我們在教師節送老師一張卡片。)"],["team","team(n./v.)隊伍、團隊、組隊\nteammate(n.)隊友\nteamwork(n.)團隊合作\nschool team 校隊\nteam up 組隊\nHe is on the school basketball team.\n(他是校籃球隊的隊員。)\nLet's team up for the project.\n(我們一起組隊做這個專題吧。)"],["teenager","teenager(n.)青少年\nteenage(adj.)青少年的\nteen(n.)青少年(口語)\na typical teenager 典型的青少年\nteenagers today 現今的青少年\nMany teenagers love social media.\n(許多青少年喜歡社群媒體。)\nAs a teenager, he loved music.\n(他青少年時期熱愛音樂。)"],["telephone/phone","telephone(n./v.)電話、打電話\nphone(n./v.)電話、打電話(口語)\nanswer the phone 接電話\nphone number 電話號碼\nCan you answer the phone, please?\n(可以請你接一下電話嗎？)\nWhat's your phone number?\n(你的電話號碼是多少？)"],["television/TV","television(n.)電視\nTV(n.)電視(縮寫)\nwatch TV 看電視\nTV show 電視節目\nI watch TV after dinner.\n(我晚餐後看電視。)\nWhat's your favorite TV show?\n(你最喜歡的電視節目是什麼？)"],["tell","tell(v.)告訴、講述、分辨\n(無詞性變化)\ntell a story 講故事\ntell the truth 說實話\nPlease tell me the truth.\n(請告訴我實話。)\nGrandma told us a story.\n(奶奶跟我們講了一個故事。)"],["temple","temple(n.)廟、寺院\n(無詞性變化)\nLongshan Temple 龍山寺\nvisit a temple 參拜寺廟\nWe visited a temple in Lukang.\n(我們參觀了鹿港的一間廟。)\nMany people go to the temple on New Year's Day.\n(許多人在新年去廟裡拜拜。)"],["tennis","tennis(n.)網球\n(無詞性變化)\nplay tennis 打網球\ntennis court 網球場\nLet's play tennis this weekend.\n(這個週末我們去打網球吧。)\nThere is a tennis court near my house.\n(我家附近有一座網球場。)"],["terrible","terrible(adj.)可怕的、糟糕的\nterribly(adv.)非常、極度地\nfeel terrible 感覺很糟\nterrible weather 糟糕的天氣\nThe weather is terrible today.\n(今天天氣糟透了。)\nI feel terrible about the mistake.\n(我對那個錯誤感到很難過。)"],["test","test(n./v.)測驗、考試、檢驗\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a test 參加考試\npass a test 考試及格\nWe have a math test tomorrow.\n(我們明天有數學考試。)\nShe passed the driving test.\n(她通過了駕照考試。)"],["than","than(conj./prep.)比\n(無詞性變化)\nmore than 超過\nrather than 而不是\nHe is taller than me.\n(他比我高。)\nMore than fifty people came.\n(超過五十個人來了。)"],["thank","thank(v./n.)感謝\nthankful(adj.)感激的\nthank you 謝謝你\nthanks to 多虧\nThank you for your help.\n(謝謝你的幫忙。)\nThanks to you, I passed the test.\n(多虧了你，我考試及格了。)"],["that","that(conj./pron./adv./adj.)那、那個、那麼\n(無詞性變化)\nthat is 也就是說\nthat way 那條路、那樣\nThat is my bike.\n(那是我的腳踏車。)\nI think that he is right.\n(我認為他是對的。)"],["the","the(art.)這、那(定冠詞)\n(無詞性變化)\nthe same 相同的\nthe best 最好的\nThe sun rises in the east.\n(太陽從東方升起。)\nPlease close the door.\n(請把門關上。)"],["theater","theater(n.)劇院、電影院\ntheatre(n.)劇院(英式拼法)\nmovie theater 電影院\ngo to the theater 去看戲\nLet's meet at the movie theater.\n(我們在電影院見。)\nThe theater was full of people.\n(劇院裡擠滿了人。)"],["then","then(adv./adj.)然後、那時、當時的\n(無詞性變化)\nsince then 從那時起\njust then 就在那時\nFinish your homework, then watch TV.\n(先寫完功課，再看電視。)\nI was only six then.\n(那時我才六歲。)"],["there","there(adv./n.)在那裡、那裡\n(無詞性變化)\nover there 在那邊\nthere is/are 有\nThere is a cat on the bed.\n(床上有一隻貓。)\nMy bag is over there.\n(我的包包在那邊。)"],["these","these(pron./adj.)這些\nthis(pron./adj.)這、這個\nthese days 最近\none of these 這些中的一個\nThese apples are very sweet.\n(這些蘋果很甜。)\nI am very busy these days.\n(我最近很忙。)"],["they (them, their, theirs, themselves)","they(pron.)他們、她們、它們\nthem(pron.)他們(受格)\ntheir(pron.)他們的\ntheirs(pron.)他們的(東西)\nthemselves(pron.)他們自己\nthey say 據說\nby themselves 他們獨自\nThey are my classmates.\n(他們是我的同學。)\nThe kids cleaned the room by themselves.\n(孩子們自己打掃了房間。)"],["thick","thick(adj.)厚的、濃的\nthickness(n.)厚度\nthick book 厚書\nthick fog 濃霧\nThis dictionary is very thick.\n(這本字典很厚。)\nThere was thick fog this morning.\n(今天早上起了濃霧。)"],["thin","thin(adj.)薄的、瘦的\n(無詞性變化)\nthin paper 薄紙\nget thin 變瘦\nShe is tall and thin.\n(她又高又瘦。)\nThe ice is too thin to walk on.\n(冰太薄了，不能在上面走。)"],["thing","thing(n.)東西、事情\n(無詞性變化)\nthe same thing 同樣的事\nfirst thing 第一件事\nWhat is that thing on the desk?\n(桌上那個東西是什麼？)\nI have many things to do today.\n(我今天有很多事要做。)"],["think","think(v.)想、認為\nthought(n.)想法\nthink about 考慮\nthink of 想到\nI think it will rain today.\n(我覺得今天會下雨。)\nLet me think about it.\n(讓我想一想。)"],["third","third(adj./n./adv.)第三(的)、三分之一\n(無詞性變化)\nthird floor 三樓\none third 三分之一\nHe came in third in the race.\n(他在賽跑中得到第三名。)\nMy office is on the third floor.\n(我的辦公室在三樓。)"],["this","this(pron./adv./adj.)這、這個、這麼\n(無詞性變化)\nthis morning 今天早上\nlike this 像這樣\nThis is my friend, Tom.\n(這是我的朋友湯姆。)\nDo it like this.\n(像這樣做。)"],["those","those(pron./adj.)那些\nthat(pron./adj.)那、那個\nthose days 那些日子\nthose who 那些……的人\nThose shoes are too big for me.\n(那些鞋子對我來說太大了。)\nI miss those days.\n(我懷念那些日子。)"],["though","though(conj./adv.)雖然、不過\nalthough(conj.)雖然\neven though 即使\nas though 好像\nThough it was raining, we went out.\n(雖然下著雨，我們還是出門了。)\nIt's hard. I like it, though.\n(很難，不過我喜歡。)"],["thousand","thousand(n./adj.)千\n(無詞性變化)\na thousand 一千\nthousands of 成千上萬的\nThis bike cost five thousand dollars.\n(這台腳踏車花了五千元。)\nThousands of people came to the concert.\n(成千上萬的人來參加演唱會。)"],["throat","throat(n.)喉嚨\n(無詞性變化)\nsore throat 喉嚨痛\nclear one's throat 清喉嚨\nI have a sore throat.\n(我喉嚨痛。)\nDrink warm water for your throat.\n(喝溫水對喉嚨好。)"],["through","through(prep./adv.)穿過、通過、透過\nthroughout(prep.)遍及、從頭到尾\ngo through 經歷、穿過\nthrough the window 透過窗戶\nThe train goes through a long tunnel.\n(火車穿過一條長隧道。)\nI learned about it through the news.\n(我是透過新聞得知這件事的。)"],["throw","throw(v./n.)丟、投擲\n(無詞性變化)\nthrow away 丟掉\nthrow a ball 丟球\nDon't throw trash on the street.\n(不要在街上亂丟垃圾。)\nHe threw the ball to me.\n(他把球丟給我。)"],["ticket","ticket(n.)票、罰單\n(無詞性變化)\nmovie ticket 電影票\nbuy a ticket 買票\nI bought two movie tickets.\n(我買了兩張電影票。)\nHe got a parking ticket.\n(他收到一張停車罰單。)"],["tidy","tidy(adj./v.)整齊的、整理\n(無詞性變化)\ntidy up 整理\na tidy room 整潔的房間\nPlease tidy up your room.\n(請整理你的房間。)\nHer desk is always tidy.\n(她的書桌總是很整齊。)"],["tie","tie(n./v.)領帶、平手、綁\n(無詞性變化)\nwear a tie 打領帶\ntie one's shoes 綁鞋帶\nMy dad wears a tie to work.\n(我爸爸打領帶上班。)\nThe game ended in a tie.\n(比賽以平手結束。)"],["tiger","tiger(n.)老虎\n(無詞性變化)\na wild tiger 野生老虎\nthe Year of the Tiger 虎年\nThe tiger is sleeping in the zoo.\n(老虎在動物園裡睡覺。)\nTigers are big and strong.\n(老虎又大又強壯。)"],["time","time(n./v.)時間、次數、計時\ntimer(n.)計時器\non time 準時\nhave a good time 玩得愉快\nWhat time is it now?\n(現在幾點？)\nPlease be on time for class.\n(上課請準時。)"],["tip","tip(n./v.)小費、訣竅、尖端、給小費\n(無詞性變化)\ngive a tip 給小費\nuseful tips 實用的訣竅\nHere are some tips for learning English.\n(這裡有一些學英文的訣竅。)\nWe left a tip for the waiter.\n(我們留了小費給服務生。)"],["tired","tired(adj.)累的、厭倦的\ntire(v.)使疲倦\nbe tired of 厭倦\nfeel tired 覺得累\nI'm too tired to go out.\n(我太累了，不想出門。)\nI'm tired of eating noodles.\n(我吃麵吃膩了。)"],["to","to(prep.)到、向、給\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to 去\nfrom A to B 從A到B\nI go to school at seven.\n(我七點去上學。)\nGive the book to Amy.\n(把書給艾美。)"],["today","today(adv./n.)今天、現今\n(無詞性變化)\ntoday's news 今日新聞\nyoung people today 現今的年輕人\nIt is very hot today.\n(今天很熱。)\nWhat day is today?\n(今天星期幾？)"],["toe","toe(n.)腳趾\n(無詞性變化)\nbig toe 大腳趾\non tiptoe 踮著腳\nI hurt my big toe.\n(我傷到了大腳趾。)\nThe water came up to my toes.\n(水淹到了我的腳趾。)"],["together","together(adv.)一起\n(無詞性變化)\nget together 聚會\nwork together 合作\nLet's eat lunch together.\n(我們一起吃午餐吧。)\nWe work together on the project.\n(我們一起合作做這個專題。)"],["toilet","toilet(n.)馬桶、廁所\n(無詞性變化)\ntoilet paper 衛生紙\nflush the toilet 沖馬桶\nWhere is the toilet?\n(廁所在哪裡？)\nDon't forget to flush the toilet.\n(別忘了沖馬桶。)"],["tomato","tomato(n.)番茄\ntomatoes(n.)番茄(複數)\ntomato sauce 番茄醬\ntomato juice 番茄汁\nI put some tomatoes in the salad.\n(我在沙拉裡放了一些番茄。)\nShe likes tomato juice.\n(她喜歡番茄汁。)"],["tomorrow","tomorrow(adv./n.)明天\n(無詞性變化)\nsee you tomorrow 明天見\ntomorrow morning 明天早上\nSee you tomorrow!\n(明天見！)\nWe have a test tomorrow morning.\n(我們明天早上有考試。)"],["tonight","tonight(adv./n.)今晚\n(無詞性變化)\ntonight's dinner 今晚的晚餐\nsee you tonight 今晚見\nWhat are you doing tonight?\n(你今晚要做什麼？)\nIt may rain tonight.\n(今晚可能會下雨。)"],["too","too(adv.)也、太\n(無詞性變化)\ntoo much 太多\nme too 我也是\nI like dogs, too.\n(我也喜歡狗。)\nThis shirt is too big for me.\n(這件襯衫對我來說太大了。)"],["tool","tool(n.)工具\n(無詞性變化)\nuseful tool 有用的工具\ntool box 工具箱\nA computer is a useful tool.\n(電腦是很有用的工具。)\nDad keeps his tools in the box.\n(爸爸把工具放在箱子裡。)"],["tooth","tooth(n.)牙齒\nteeth(n.)牙齒(複數)\nbrush one's teeth 刷牙\nsweet tooth 愛吃甜食\nBrush your teeth before bed.\n(睡前要刷牙。)\nI have a sweet tooth.\n(我很愛吃甜食。)"],["top","top(n./adj./v.)頂端、最高的、居首\n(無詞性變化)\non top of 在……上面\ntop student 頂尖學生\nWe climbed to the top of the hill.\n(我們爬到山頂。)\nShe is the top student in our class.\n(她是我們班的第一名。)"],["topic","topic(n.)話題、主題\n(無詞性變化)\na hot topic 熱門話題\nchange the topic 換話題\nWhat is the topic of your report?\n(你的報告主題是什麼？)\nLet's change the topic.\n(我們換個話題吧。)"],["total","total(adj./n./v.)總計(的)、完全的、合計\ntotally(adv.)完全地\nin total 總共\ntotal cost 總費用\nThe total is five hundred dollars.\n(總共是五百元。)\nThere are forty students in total.\n(總共有四十個學生。)"],["touch","touch(n./v.)接觸、觸摸、感動\ntouching(adj.)感人的\nkeep in touch 保持聯絡\nDon't touch 請勿觸摸\nPlease don't touch the paintings.\n(請勿觸摸畫作。)\nLet's keep in touch.\n(我們保持聯絡吧。)"],["towel","towel(n./v.)毛巾、用毛巾擦\n(無詞性變化)\nbath towel 浴巾\npaper towel 紙巾\nCan I use your towel?\n(我可以用你的毛巾嗎？)\nHe dried his hair with a towel.\n(他用毛巾擦乾頭髮。)"],["town","town(n.)城鎮\n(無詞性變化)\nsmall town 小鎮\ndowntown 市中心\nI grew up in a small town.\n(我在一個小鎮長大。)\nThere is a night market in this town.\n(這個小鎮有一個夜市。)"],["toy","toy(n.)玩具\n(無詞性變化)\ntoy car 玩具車\ntoy store 玩具店\nMy little brother has many toys.\n(我弟弟有很多玩具。)\nShe bought a toy car for her son.\n(她買了一台玩具車給兒子。)"],["traffic","traffic(n./v.)交通、車流\n(無詞性變化)\ntraffic jam 塞車\ntraffic light 紅綠燈\nWe were late because of a traffic jam.\n(我們因為塞車而遲到。)\nStop at the traffic light.\n(在紅綠燈前停下來。)"],["train","train(n./v.)火車、訓練\ntraining(n.)訓練\ntake a train 搭火車\ntrain station 火車站\nWe took a train to Hualien.\n(我們搭火車去花蓮。)\nHe trains hard every day.\n(他每天努力訓練。)"],["treat(ment)","treat(v.)對待、治療、請客、treatment(n.)對待、治療\n(無詞性變化)\ntreat someone to 請某人吃……\nmedical treatment 醫療\nLet me treat you to lunch.\n(讓我請你吃午餐。)\nShe treats her dog like a baby.\n(她把她的狗當成寶寶對待。)"],["tree","tree(n.)樹\n(無詞性變化)\nplant a tree 種樹\nChristmas tree 聖誕樹\nThere is a big tree in the park.\n(公園裡有一棵大樹。)\nWe planted trees on Arbor Day.\n(我們在植樹節種樹。)"],["trip","trip(n./v.)旅行、絆倒\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a trip 去旅行\nschool trip 校外教學\nWe took a trip to Kenting.\n(我們去墾丁旅行。)\nHe tripped over a rock.\n(他被一顆石頭絆倒。)"],["trouble","trouble(n./v.)麻煩、困擾、使煩惱\ntroublesome(adj.)麻煩的\nin trouble 有麻煩\nhave trouble 有困難\nHe is in big trouble.\n(他麻煩大了。)\nI have trouble sleeping at night.\n(我晚上睡不好。)"],["truck","truck(n.)卡車\n(無詞性變化)\ngarbage truck 垃圾車\ntruck driver 卡車司機\nThe garbage truck comes at eight.\n(垃圾車八點來。)\nA big truck is parked outside.\n(外面停了一台大卡車。)"],["try","try(v./n.)嘗試、努力、試穿\n(無詞性變化)\ntry on 試穿\ntry one's best 盡全力\nCan I try on this jacket?\n(我可以試穿這件外套嗎？)\nI will try my best.\n(我會盡全力。)"],["T-shirt","T-shirt(n.)T恤\n(無詞性變化)\nwhite T-shirt 白色T恤\nwear a T-shirt 穿T恤\nHe is wearing a white T-shirt.\n(他穿著一件白色T恤。)\nI bought a T-shirt at the shop.\n(我在店裡買了一件T恤。)"],["turn","turn(v./n.)轉、轉向、輪流\n(無詞性變化)\nturn on 打開(電器)\ntake turns 輪流\nTurn left at the corner.\n(在轉角左轉。)\nIt's your turn to sing.\n(輪到你唱了。)"],["twice","twice(adv.)兩次、兩倍\n(無詞性變化)\ntwice a week 一週兩次\nthink twice 三思\nI play basketball twice a week.\n(我一週打兩次籃球。)\nThink twice before you speak.\n(說話前要三思。)"],["type","type(n./v.)類型、打字\ntypical(adj.)典型的\nblood type 血型\ntype fast 打字很快\nWhat type of music do you like?\n(你喜歡哪種類型的音樂？)\nShe can type very fast.\n(她打字很快。)"],["uncle","uncle(n.)叔叔、伯伯、舅舅\n(無詞性變化)\nmy uncle 我的叔叔\nUncle Tom 湯姆叔叔\nMy uncle lives in Kaohsiung.\n(我舅舅住在高雄。)\nUncle Ben gave me a new bike.\n(班叔叔送我一台新腳踏車。)"],["under","under(prep./adv.)在……下面、少於\n(無詞性變化)\nunder the table 在桌子下面\nunder 18 未滿十八歲\nThe cat is under the bed.\n(貓在床底下。)\nKids under six can enter for free.\n(六歲以下的孩子可以免費入場。)"],["understand","understand(v.)了解、懂\nunderstanding(n.)理解\nunderstand English 聽得懂英文\nfully understand 完全了解\nDo you understand the question?\n(你懂這個問題嗎？)\nI can't understand what he said.\n(我聽不懂他說的話。)"],["uniform","uniform(n.)制服\n(無詞性變化)\nschool uniform 校服\nwear a uniform 穿制服\nWe wear school uniforms on Mondays.\n(我們週一穿校服。)\nThe nurse is in a white uniform.\n(那位護理師穿著白色制服。)"],["until","until(conj./prep.)直到\ntill(conj./prep.)直到\nuntil now 直到現在\nnot until 直到……才\nWait here until I come back.\n(在這裡等到我回來。)\nThe store is open until ten.\n(這家店營業到十點。)"],["up","up(adv./prep./adj./v./n.)向上、起來、在上面\n(無詞性變化)\nget up 起床\nlook up 抬頭、查詢\nStand up, please.\n(請站起來。)\nHe walked up the hill.\n(他走上山坡。)"],["use","use(v./n.)使用、用途\nuseful(adj.)有用的\nuser(n.)使用者\nmake use of 利用\nuse up 用完\nCan I use your phone?\n(我可以用你的手機嗎？)\nWe used up all the paper.\n(我們把紙都用完了。)"],["useful","useful(adj.)有用的\nuse(v./n.)使用、用途\nuseful information 有用的資訊\nbe useful for 對……有用\nThis app is very useful.\n(這個應用程式很有用。)\nA dictionary is useful for learning English.\n(字典對學英文很有幫助。)"],["usually","usually(adv.)通常\nusual(adj.)通常的\nas usual 照常\nusually go 通常去\nI usually go to bed at eleven.\n(我通常十一點睡覺。)\nShe usually walks to school.\n(她通常走路上學。)"],["vegetable","vegetable(n.)蔬菜\nvegetarian(n.)素食者\nfresh vegetables 新鮮蔬菜\nvegetable soup 蔬菜湯\nEat more vegetables.\n(多吃蔬菜。)\nMy mom makes good vegetable soup.\n(我媽媽煮的蔬菜湯很好喝。)"],["very","very(adv.)非常、很\n(無詞性變化)\nvery much 非常\nvery good 非常好\nThank you very much.\n(非常謝謝你。)\nThe test was very easy.\n(這次考試很簡單。)"],["video","video(n./v./adj.)影片、錄影(的)\n(無詞性變化)\nvideo game 電玩遊戲\nwatch a video 看影片\nI watched a funny video online.\n(我在網路上看了一部好笑的影片。)\nHe likes to play video games.\n(他喜歡玩電玩。)"],["violin","violin(n.)小提琴\nviolinist(n.)小提琴家\nplay the violin 拉小提琴\nviolin lessons 小提琴課\nShe plays the violin very well.\n(她小提琴拉得很好。)\nI take violin lessons every Saturday.\n(我每週六上小提琴課。)"],["visit","visit(v./n.)拜訪、參觀\nvisitor(n.)訪客\npay a visit 拜訪\nvisit a museum 參觀博物館\nWe visited my grandparents last week.\n(我們上週去探望祖父母。)\nLet's visit the museum tomorrow.\n(我們明天去參觀博物館吧。)"],["visitor","visitor(n.)訪客、遊客\nvisit(v./n.)拜訪、參觀\nforeign visitors 外國遊客\nvisitor center 遊客中心\nMany visitors come to Taipei 101.\n(許多遊客來到台北101。)\nWe have a visitor today.\n(我們今天有客人。)"],["voice","voice(n.)聲音、嗓音\n(無詞性變化)\nin a loud voice 大聲地\nlose one's voice 失聲\nShe has a beautiful voice.\n(她有一副好嗓子。)\nPlease speak in a low voice.\n(請小聲說話。)"],["wait","wait(v./n.)等待、等候\nwaiter(n.)服務生\nwaitress(n.)女服務生\nwait for 等待\ncan't wait 迫不及待\nPlease wait for me at the gate.\n(請在門口等我。)\nI can't wait to see you.\n(我等不及要見到你。)"],["wake","wake(v.)醒來、叫醒\nawake(adj.)醒著的\nwaken(v.)喚醒\nwake up 醒來、叫醒\nwake-up call 叫醒服務、警鐘\nI wake up at six every morning.\n(我每天早上六點起床。)\nPlease wake me up at seven.\n(請在七點叫醒我。)"],["walk","walk(v./n.)走路、散步、遛(狗)\nwalker(n.)步行者\ntake a walk 散步\nwalk the dog 遛狗\nLet's take a walk in the park.\n(我們去公園散步吧。)\nI walk to school every day.\n(我每天走路上學。)"],["wall","wall(n.)牆壁、城牆\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Great Wall 萬里長城\non the wall 在牆上\nThere is a clock on the wall.\n(牆上有一個時鐘。)\nWe visited the Great Wall in China.\n(我們參觀了中國的萬里長城。)"],["want","want(v./n.)想要、需要、缺乏\nwanted(adj.)被通緝的、受歡迎的\nwant to 想要做\nfor want of 因缺乏\nI want to be a doctor.\n(我想成為醫生。)\nDo you want some cake?\n(你想吃點蛋糕嗎？)"],["warm","warm(adj./v.)溫暖的、熱情的、使暖和\nwarmth(n.)溫暖\nwarmly(adv.)溫暖地、熱情地\nwarm up 暖身、加熱\nwarm welcome 熱烈歡迎\nIt is warm and sunny today.\n(今天溫暖又晴朗。)\nWe always warm up before running.\n(我們跑步前總會先暖身。)"],["watch","watch(v./n.)觀看、注意、手錶\n(無詞性變化)\nwatch TV 看電視\nwatch out 小心\nWatch out! A car is coming.\n(小心！有車子來了。)\nI got a new watch for my birthday.\n(我生日時收到一支新手錶。)"],["water","water(n./v.)水、澆水\nwatery(adj.)水分多的\ndrinking water 飲用水\nwater the plants 澆花\nDrink more water on hot days.\n(天氣熱時要多喝水。)\nI water the plants every morning.\n(我每天早上澆花。)"],["wave","wave(n./v.)波浪、揮手、揮動\nwavy(adj.)波浪狀的\nwave goodbye 揮手道別\nheat wave 熱浪\nShe waved goodbye to her friends.\n(她向朋友們揮手道別。)\nThe big waves hit the beach.\n(大浪拍打著海灘。)"],["way","way(n.)路、方法、方式、方向\n(無詞性變化)\nby the way 順帶一提\non the way 在路上\nIs this the way to the station?\n(這是往車站的路嗎？)\nBy the way, where is your sister?\n(順便問一下，你姊姊在哪裡？)"],["we (us, our, ours, ourselves)","we(pron.)我們\nus(pron.)我們(受格)\nour(pron.)我們的\nours(pron.)我們的(東西)、ourselves(pron.)我們自己\nwe all 我們大家\nby ourselves 我們自己、獨自\nWe are in the same class.\n(我們同班。)\nWe cleaned the classroom by ourselves.\n(我們自己打掃了教室。)"],["weak","weak(adj.)虛弱的、弱的、不擅長的\nweakness(n.)弱點\nweaken(v.)削弱\nweak point 弱點\nfeel weak 感到虛弱\nI feel weak after being sick.\n(生病後我覺得很虛弱。)\nMath is my weak subject.\n(數學是我不擅長的科目。)"],["wear","wear(v.)穿、戴、磨損\n(無詞性變化)\nwear glasses 戴眼鏡\nwear out 磨損、使疲憊\nShe wears glasses in class.\n(她上課時戴眼鏡。)\nWear a jacket. It's cold outside.\n(穿件外套，外面很冷。)"],["weather","weather(n./v.)天氣、安然度過\n(無詞性變化)\nweather forecast 天氣預報\nbad weather 惡劣天氣\nWhat's the weather like today?\n(今天天氣如何？)\nThe weather forecast says it will rain.\n(天氣預報說會下雨。)"],["week","week(n.)週、星期\nweekly(adj./adv.)每週的、每週一次\nlast week 上週\nonce a week 一週一次\nI visit my grandma once a week.\n(我一週去探望奶奶一次。)\nWe had a test last week.\n(我們上週考了一次試。)"],["weekend","weekend(n./v.)週末、度週末\n(無詞性變化)\non weekends 在週末\nweekend trip 週末旅行\nWhat do you do on weekends?\n(你週末都做些什麼？)\nWe went on a weekend trip to Yilan.\n(我們去宜蘭週末旅行。)"],["welcome","welcome(v./adj./n.)歡迎、受歡迎的\n(無詞性變化)\nyou're welcome 不客氣\nwelcome party 歡迎會\nWelcome to our school!\n(歡迎來到我們學校！)\nThank you. You're welcome.\n(謝謝你。不客氣。)"],["well","well(adv./adj./n.)好地、健康的、井\n(無詞性變化)\nas well 也\nwell done 做得好\nShe sings very well.\n(她唱歌唱得很好。)\nI don't feel well today.\n(我今天覺得不太舒服。)"],["west","west(n./adj./adv.)西方、西方的、向西\nwestern(adj.)西方的、西部的\nwestward(adv.)向西\nthe West 西方國家\nwest coast 西岸\nThe sun sets in the west.\n(太陽從西邊落下。)\nThey drove west to the beach.\n(他們往西開車去海邊。)"],["wet","wet(adj./v.)濕的、下雨的、弄濕\n(無詞性變化)\nget wet 弄濕、淋濕\nwet paint 油漆未乾\nI got wet in the rain.\n(我被雨淋濕了。)\nDon't touch it. The paint is still wet.\n(別碰，油漆還沒乾。)"],["what","what(pron./adj.)什麼、什麼樣的\nwhatever(pron./adj.)無論什麼\nwhat about ……怎麼樣\nwhat time 幾點\nWhat is your favorite food?\n(你最喜歡的食物是什麼？)\nWhat time is it now?\n(現在幾點？)"],["when","when(adv./conj./pron.)何時、當……時\nwhenever(conj.)每當、無論何時\nsince when 從何時起\nwhen to 何時該\nWhen is your birthday?\n(你的生日是什麼時候？)\nI was sleeping when you called.\n(你打電話來的時候我正在睡覺。)"],["where","where(conj./adv./pron./n.)哪裡、在……的地方\nwherever(conj.)無論哪裡\nwhere to 去哪裡\nfrom where 從哪裡\nWhere do you live?\n(你住在哪裡？)\nThis is the house where I grew up.\n(這是我長大的房子。)"],["whether","whether(conj.)是否、不論\n(無詞性變化)\nwhether or not 是否、不論是否\nwhether to 是否要\nI don't know whether he will come.\n(我不知道他是否會來。)\nWe will go whether it rains or not.\n(不論下不下雨，我們都會去。)"],["which","which(pron./adj.)哪一個、哪一些\nwhichever(pron./adj.)無論哪一個\nwhich one 哪一個\nwhich way 哪條路、哪個方向\nWhich one do you like better?\n(你比較喜歡哪一個？)\nWhich bus goes to the zoo?\n(哪一班公車到動物園？)"],["while","while(conj./n./v.)當……時、然而、一會兒、消磨\n(無詞性變化)\nfor a while 一會兒\nonce in a while 偶爾\nPlease wait for a while.\n(請稍等一會兒。)\nHe listens to music while he studies.\n(他一邊讀書一邊聽音樂。)"],["white","white(adj./n.)白色的、白色\nwhiten(v.)使變白\nwhite shirt 白襯衫\nblack and white 黑白的\nHe is wearing a white shirt today.\n(他今天穿著白襯衫。)\nSnow is white and cold.\n(雪又白又冷。)"],["who","who(pron.)誰、……的人\nwhom(pron.)誰(受格)\nwhoever(pron.)無論是誰\nwho else 還有誰\nwho knows 誰知道\nWho is that girl?\n(那個女孩是誰？)\nThe man who lives next door is a doctor.\n(住在隔壁的那位男士是醫生。)"],["whose","whose(pron.)誰的、那個人的\n(無詞性變化)\nwhose turn 輪到誰\nwhose fault 誰的錯\nWhose bag is this?\n(這是誰的包包？)\nI have a friend whose father is a pilot.\n(我有個朋友，他的爸爸是機師。)"],["why","why(adv./n.)為什麼、原因\n(無詞性變化)\nwhy not 為什麼不、好啊\nthat's why 那就是為什麼\nWhy are you late today?\n(你今天為什麼遲到？)\nLet's go to the movies. Why not?\n(我們去看電影吧。好啊！)"],["wide","wide(adj./adv.)寬的、廣泛的、完全地\nwidth(n.)寬度\nwidely(adv.)廣泛地\nwiden(v.)使變寬\nwide open 大開的\nwide range 廣泛的範圍\nThis river is very wide.\n(這條河非常寬。)\nThe door was wide open.\n(門大大地敞開著。)"],["wife","wife(n.)妻子、太太\n(無詞性變化)\nhusband and wife 夫妻\nhis wife 他的太太\nHe lives with his wife and two kids.\n(他和太太及兩個孩子住在一起。)\nHis wife is a teacher.\n(他的太太是一位老師。)"],["will","will(aux./n.)將會、願意、意志、遺囑\nwilling(adj.)願意的\nwillingness(n.)意願\nfree will 自由意志\nagainst one's will 違背某人的意願\nI will call you tomorrow.\n(我明天會打電話給你。)\nShe has a strong will to win.\n(她有強烈的求勝意志。)"],["win","win(v./n.)贏、獲勝、贏得、勝利\nwinner(n.)贏家、優勝者\nwin a prize 得獎\nwin the game 贏得比賽\nOur team won the game yesterday.\n(我們隊昨天贏了比賽。)\nShe won first prize in the contest.\n(她在比賽中得了第一名。)"],["wind","wind(n./v.)風、蜿蜒、上發條\nwindy(adj.)多風的\nstrong wind 強風\nwind up 結束、上發條\nThe wind is very strong today.\n(今天風很大。)\nThe road winds up the mountain.\n(這條路蜿蜒上山。)"],["window","window(n.)窗戶、視窗\n(無詞性變化)\nopen the window 開窗\nwindow seat 靠窗座位\nPlease close the window. It's cold.\n(請關窗，好冷。)\nI'd like a window seat, please.\n(我想要靠窗的座位，謝謝。)"],["wise","wise(adj.)聰明的、有智慧的、明智的\nwisdom(n.)智慧\nwisely(adv.)明智地\nwise choice 明智的選擇\nwise man 智者\nIt was a wise choice to bring an umbrella.\n(帶傘是個明智的選擇。)\nMy grandfather is a wise old man.\n(我爺爺是一位有智慧的老人。)"],["wish","wish(v./n.)希望、祝福、願望\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a wish 許願\nbest wishes 最誠摯的祝福\nClose your eyes and make a wish.\n(閉上眼睛許個願吧。)\nI wish you a happy birthday.\n(祝你生日快樂。)"],["with","with(prep.)和……一起、用、帶有\n(無詞性變化)\nwith care 小心地\nagree with 同意\nI went shopping with my mom.\n(我和媽媽一起去購物。)\nShe cut the paper with scissors.\n(她用剪刀剪紙。)"],["without","without(prep./adv.)沒有、不、在外面\n(無詞性變化)\nwithout doubt 毫無疑問\ndo without 沒有……也行\nI can't live without music.\n(沒有音樂我活不下去。)\nHe left without saying goodbye.\n(他沒說再見就離開了。)"],["woman","woman(n.)女人、婦女\nwomen(n.)女人(複數)\nyoung woman 年輕女子\nwomen's rights 女權\nThe woman in red is my aunt.\n(穿紅衣服的那位女士是我阿姨。)\nMany women work as engineers today.\n(現今有許多女性擔任工程師。)"],["wonderful","wonderful(adj.)極好的、精彩的\nwonder(n./v.)奇蹟、驚奇、想知道\nwonderfully(adv.)極好地\nwonderful time 美好時光\nwonderful idea 很棒的主意\nWe had a wonderful time at the beach.\n(我們在海邊度過了美好時光。)\nThat's a wonderful idea!\n(那真是個很棒的主意！)"],["word","word(n.)字、單字、話、諾言\nwordy(adj.)冗長的\nin other words 換句話說\nkeep one's word 遵守諾言\nWhat does this word mean?\n(這個字是什麼意思？)\nHe always keeps his word.\n(他總是信守承諾。)"],["work","work(n./v.)工作、作品、運作、有效\nworker(n.)工人\nworkable(adj.)可行的\nwork hard 努力工作\ngo to work 去上班\nMy dad goes to work by bus.\n(我爸爸搭公車上班。)\nThis old phone doesn't work anymore.\n(這支舊手機已經不能用了。)"],["worker","worker(n.)工人、工作者\nwork(n./v.)工作\nhard worker 工作勤奮的人\noffice worker 上班族\nHe is a hard worker.\n(他是個工作勤奮的人。)\nThe workers are building a new bridge.\n(工人們正在蓋一座新橋。)"],["world","world(n.)世界、領域\nworldwide(adj./adv.)全世界的、在世界各地\naround the world 世界各地\nworld record 世界紀錄\nI want to travel around the world.\n(我想環遊世界。)\nHe broke the world record.\n(他打破了世界紀錄。)"],["worry","worry(v./n.)擔心、煩惱\nworried(adj.)擔心的\nworrying(adj.)令人擔憂的\nworry about 擔心\ndon't worry 別擔心\nDon't worry. Everything will be fine.\n(別擔心，一切都會沒事的。)\nMy mom worries about my health.\n(我媽媽擔心我的健康。)"],["write","write(v.)寫、寫作、寫信\nwriter(n.)作家\nwriting(n.)寫作、筆跡\nwrite down 寫下\nwrite a letter 寫信\nPlease write down your name here.\n(請在這裡寫下你的名字。)\nI write in my diary every night.\n(我每天晚上寫日記。)"],["writer","writer(n.)作家、作者\nwrite(v.)寫\nwriting(n.)寫作\nfamous writer 知名作家\nwriter's block 寫作瓶頸\nShe wants to be a writer.\n(她想成為一位作家。)\nThe writer signed my book.\n(那位作家在我的書上簽名。)"],["wrong","wrong(adj./adv./n./v.)錯誤的、不對勁的、錯誤、冤枉\nwrongly(adv.)錯誤地\ngo wrong 出錯\nwhat's wrong 怎麼了\nWhat's wrong with you?\n(你怎麼了？)\nSorry, I took the wrong bus.\n(抱歉，我搭錯公車了。)"],["yard","yard(n.)院子、碼(長度單位)\n(無詞性變化)\nback yard 後院\nschool yard 校園操場\nThe kids are playing in the yard.\n(孩子們正在院子裡玩。)\nWe have a small garden in the back yard.\n(我們家後院有個小花園。)"],["year","year(n.)年、年紀、年度\nyearly(adj./adv.)每年的、每年一次\nlast year 去年\nall year round 一整年\nI started high school this year.\n(我今年開始讀高中。)\nIt is warm here all year round.\n(這裡一整年都很溫暖。)"],["yellow","yellow(adj./n./v.)黃色的、黃色、變黃\nyellowish(adj.)帶黃色的\nyellow card 黃牌\nturn yellow 變黃\nThe leaves turn yellow in fall.\n(葉子在秋天變黃。)\nShe has a yellow umbrella.\n(她有一把黃色的雨傘。)"],["yes/yeah","yes(adv./n.)是、對、好\nyeah(adv.)是、對(口語)\nsay yes 答應\nyes or no 是或不是\nYes, I'd love to come.\n(好，我很樂意來。)\nYeah, that sounds great.\n(對啊，聽起來很棒。)"],["yesterday","yesterday(adv./n.)昨天\n(無詞性變化)\nthe day before yesterday 前天\nyesterday morning 昨天早上\nI saw a movie yesterday.\n(我昨天看了一部電影。)\nIt rained hard yesterday morning.\n(昨天早上下了大雨。)"],["yet","yet(adv./conj.)還(沒)、已經、然而\n(無詞性變化)\nnot yet 還沒\nas yet 到目前為止\nHave you finished your homework yet?\n(你寫完功課了嗎？)\nHe is young, yet he is very wise.\n(他很年輕，卻很有智慧。)"],["you (your, yours, yourself, yourselves)","you(pron.)你、你們\nyour(pron.)你的、你們的\nyours(pron.)你的(東西)、你們的(東西)\nyourself(pron.)你自己、yourselves(pron.)你們自己\nhelp yourself 自己來、別客氣\nyours truly 敬上\nHelp yourself to some cookies.\n(請自己拿些餅乾吃。)\nIs this pen yours?\n(這支筆是你的嗎？)"],["young","young(adj./n.)年輕的、幼小的、幼崽\nyouth(n.)青春、年輕人\nyoungster(n.)年輕人、小孩\nyoung people 年輕人\nthe young 年輕人(總稱)、幼崽\nMy mom looks very young.\n(我媽媽看起來很年輕。)\nThe bird is feeding its young.\n(那隻鳥正在餵牠的雛鳥。)"],["zero","zero(n.)零、零度\n(無詞性變化)\nbelow zero 零度以下\nzero waste 零浪費\nIt is below zero outside.\n(外面低於零度。)\nHe got zero on the quiz.\n(他小考得了零分。)"],["zoo","zoo(n.)動物園\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to the zoo 去動物園\nzoo keeper 動物園管理員\nWe saw pandas at the zoo.\n(我們在動物園看到大貓熊。)\nLet's go to the zoo this Sunday.\n(這個星期天我們去動物園吧。)"]],"2":[["absence","absence(n.)缺席、不在、缺乏\nabsent(adj.)缺席的\nin one's absence 某人不在時\nabsence of 缺乏\nHis absence from class worried the teacher.\n(他缺課讓老師很擔心。)\nShe took care of the shop in my absence.\n(我不在時她幫忙照顧店。)"],["absent","absent(adj./v.)缺席的、不在的、使缺席\nabsence(n.)缺席\nbe absent from 缺席\nabsent-minded 心不在焉的\nThree students were absent from school today.\n(今天有三位學生缺席。)\nHe is absent because he has a cold.\n(他因為感冒而缺席。)"],["accept","accept(v.)接受、認可\nacceptable(adj.)可接受的\nacceptance(n.)接受\naccept an invitation 接受邀請\naccept a gift 收下禮物\nShe accepted my invitation to the party.\n(她接受了我的派對邀請。)\nI can't accept such an expensive gift.\n(我不能收這麼貴的禮物。)"],["accident","accident(n.)意外、事故\naccidental(adj.)意外的\naccidentally(adv.)意外地\ncar accident 車禍\nby accident 偶然地\nHe was hurt in a car accident.\n(他在一場車禍中受傷。)\nI met an old friend by accident.\n(我偶然遇見一位老朋友。)"],["account","account(n./v.)帳戶、帳號、說明、占(比例)\naccountant(n.)會計師\nbank account 銀行帳戶\ntake into account 考慮到\nI opened a bank account last week.\n(我上週開了一個銀行帳戶。)\nStudents account for half of the visitors.\n(學生占了遊客的一半。)"],["active","active(adj.)活躍的、積極的\nactivity(n.)活動\nactively(adv.)積極地\nan active role 積極的角色\nstay active 保持活躍\nMy grandpa stays active by walking every day.\n(我爺爺每天散步保持活力。)\nShe takes an active part in school clubs.\n(她積極參與學校社團。)"],["activity","activity(n.)活動\nactive(adj.)活躍的\noutdoor activities 戶外活動\nclub activities 社團活動\nHiking is my favorite outdoor activity.\n(健行是我最喜歡的戶外活動。)\nOur school has many club activities.\n(我們學校有很多社團活動。)"],["actual","actual(adj.)實際的、真實的\nactually(adv.)實際上、其實\nactual cost 實際費用\nin actual fact 事實上\nThe actual cost was higher than we thought.\n(實際費用比我們想的高。)\nWhat is the actual reason for his absence?\n(他缺席的真正原因是什麼？)"],["addition","addition(n.)增加、加法、增添的人事物\nadd(v.)增加\nadditional(adj.)額外的\nin addition 此外\nin addition to 除了……之外\nIn addition to English, she speaks Japanese.\n(除了英文，她還會說日文。)\nThe new library is a great addition to our school.\n(新圖書館為我們學校增色不少。)"],["address","address(v./n.)地址、演說、處理、向……講話\n(無詞性變化)\nemail address 電子郵件地址\naddress a problem 處理問題\nPlease write your address on the form.\n(請在表格上寫下你的地址。)\nThe principal addressed the students this morning.\n(校長今天早上對學生發表談話。)"],["admit","admit(v.)承認、准許進入\nadmission(n.)入場、入學許可\nadmit a mistake 承認錯誤\nbe admitted to 獲准進入\nHe finally admitted his mistake.\n(他終於承認了自己的錯誤。)\nShe was admitted to a good university.\n(她被一所好大學錄取了。)"],["adult","adult(n./adj.)成年人、成年的\nadulthood(n.)成年期\nadult ticket 全票\nyoung adult 年輕成人\nAn adult ticket costs three hundred dollars.\n(一張全票三百元。)\nChildren must come with an adult.\n(兒童須由成人陪同。)"],["advance","advance(n./v.)前進、進步、預先\nadvanced(adj.)先進的、高級的\nin advance 事先\nadvance in technology 科技進步\nPlease book your tickets in advance.\n(請事先訂票。)\nScience has advanced quickly in recent years.\n(近年來科學進步得很快。)"],["advice","advice(n.)建議、忠告\nadvise(v.)建議、勸告\ngive advice 給建議\na piece of advice 一則建議\nCan you give me some advice?\n(你能給我一些建議嗎？)\nI took my teacher's advice and studied harder.\n(我聽了老師的建議，更加用功。)"],["affair","affair(n.)事務、事件、風流韻事\n(無詞性變化)\ncurrent affairs 時事\nforeign affairs 外交事務\nHe likes to read about current affairs.\n(他喜歡閱讀時事。)\nThat is my private affair.\n(那是我的私事。)"],["affect","affect(v.)影響、感動\naffection(n.)喜愛、情感\ndeeply affect 深深影響\naffect health 影響健康\nLack of sleep can affect your grades.\n(睡眠不足會影響你的成績。)\nThe bad weather affected our plans.\n(壞天氣影響了我們的計畫。)"],["against","against(prep.)反對、對抗、倚靠\n(無詞性變化)\nbe against 反對\nagainst the wall 靠著牆\nMany people are against the new rule.\n(許多人反對新規定。)\nHe leaned his bike against the wall.\n(他把腳踏車靠在牆上。)"],["ahead","ahead(adv.)在前方、提前\n(無詞性變化)\ngo ahead 請便、繼續\nahead of time 提前\nGo ahead and ask your question.\n(請說出你的問題吧。)\nWe finished the work ahead of time.\n(我們提前完成了工作。)"],["aid","aid(n./v.)幫助、援助\n(無詞性變化)\nfirst aid 急救\nhearing aid 助聽器\nEvery student should learn first aid.\n(每個學生都應該學急救。)\nMany countries sent aid after the earthquake.\n(地震後許多國家送來援助。)"],["aim","aim(n./v.)目標、瞄準、旨在\naimless(adj.)沒有目標的\naim at 瞄準、針對\nachieve one's aim 達成目標\nMy aim is to pass the exam.\n(我的目標是通過考試。)\nThis program aims to help poor children.\n(這個計畫旨在幫助貧困兒童。)"],["aircraft","aircraft(n.)飛機、航空器\n(無詞性變化)\nmilitary aircraft 軍機\naircraft carrier 航空母艦\nThe aircraft landed safely.\n(那架飛機安全降落。)\nThis aircraft can carry 300 passengers.\n(這架飛機可載運三百名乘客。)"],["alarm","alarm(n./v.)警報、鬧鐘、使驚慌\nalarming(adj.)令人擔憂的\nalarm clock 鬧鐘\nfire alarm 火災警報\nI set my alarm clock for six.\n(我把鬧鐘設在六點。)\nThe fire alarm went off during class.\n(上課時火災警報響了。)"],["album","album(n.)相簿、專輯\n(無詞性變化)\nphoto album 相簿\nnew album 新專輯\nWe looked through the old photo album.\n(我們翻看舊相簿。)\nThe singer will release a new album.\n(那位歌手將發行新專輯。)"],["alike","alike(adv./adj.)相似的、同樣地\n(無詞性變化)\nlook alike 看起來很像\nyoung and old alike 老少皆然\nThe twins look alike.\n(那對雙胞胎長得很像。)\nThe game is loved by young and old alike.\n(這個遊戲老少皆愛。)"],["alive","alive(adj.)活著的、有活力的\n(無詞性變化)\nstay alive 存活\ncome alive 活躍起來\nThe fish is still alive.\n(那條魚還活著。)\nThe city comes alive at night.\n(這座城市到了晚上就熱鬧起來。)"],["alone","alone(adv./adj.)單獨的、獨自地\nlonely(adj.)寂寞的\nlive alone 獨居\nleave me alone 別管我\nMy grandmother lives alone.\n(我奶奶獨居。)\nPlease leave me alone for a while.\n(請讓我自己靜一靜。)"],["aloud","aloud(adv.)出聲地、大聲地\n(無詞性變化)\nread aloud 朗讀\nthink aloud 自言自語地思考\nPlease read the passage aloud.\n(請把這段文章唸出來。)\nShe laughed aloud at the joke.\n(她聽到笑話大笑出聲。)"],["altogether","altogether(adv.)總共、完全\n(無詞性變化)\naltogether different 完全不同\nfive altogether 總共五個\nThat will be 200 dollars altogether.\n(總共是兩百元。)\nThe new plan is altogether different.\n(新計畫完全不同。)"],["among","among(prep.)在……之中\n(無詞性變化)\namong friends 在朋友之間\namong the best 名列前茅\nShe is popular among her classmates.\n(她在同學之間很受歡迎。)\nHe is among the best students in school.\n(他是全校最優秀的學生之一。)"],["amount","amount(n./v.)數量、總額、總計\n(無詞性變化)\na large amount of 大量的\namount to 總計達\nHe spent a large amount of money on games.\n(他在遊戲上花了一大筆錢。)\nThe bill amounted to 1,000 dollars.\n(帳單總計一千元。)"],["ancient","ancient(adj.)古代的、古老的\n(無詞性變化)\nancient times 古代\nancient history 古代史\nWe learned about ancient Egypt in class.\n(我們在課堂上學了古埃及。)\nThis temple is very ancient.\n(這間廟非常古老。)"],["anger","anger(n.)憤怒\nangry(adj.)生氣的\nangrily(adv.)生氣地\nin anger 憤怒地\ncontrol one's anger 控制怒氣\nHe shouted in anger.\n(他憤怒地大叫。)\nYou should learn to control your anger.\n(你應該學著控制怒氣。)"],["angle","angle(n.)角度、觀點\n(無詞性變化)\nright angle 直角\nfrom a different angle 從不同角度\nA square has four right angles.\n(正方形有四個直角。)\nLet's look at the problem from a different angle.\n(我們從不同的角度看這個問題。)"],["ankle","ankle(n.)腳踝\n(無詞性變化)\ntwist one's ankle 扭傷腳踝\nankle socks 短襪\nI twisted my ankle playing basketball.\n(我打籃球時扭傷了腳踝。)\nThe water was only ankle deep.\n(水只淹到腳踝。)"],["anytime","anytime(adv.)任何時候\n(無詞性變化)\ncall me anytime 隨時打給我\nanytime soon 短期內\nYou can call me anytime.\n(你隨時都可以打給我。)\nThe rain won't stop anytime soon.\n(這場雨短期內不會停。)"],["anyway","anyway(adv.)無論如何、反正\nanyhow(adv.)無論如何\nthanks anyway 還是謝謝你\ndo it anyway 還是去做\nIt was raining, but we went out anyway.\n(雖然下雨，我們還是出門了。)\nI don't need it, but thanks anyway.\n(我不需要，但還是謝謝你。)"],["anywhere/anyplace","anywhere(adv.)任何地方\nanyplace(adv.)任何地方(美式口語)\ngo anywhere 去任何地方\nanywhere else 其他任何地方\nI can't find my phone anywhere.\n(我到處都找不到我的手機。)\nYou can sit anywhere you like.\n(你想坐哪裡都可以。)"],["ape","ape(n.)猿\n(無詞性變化)\ngreat ape 大型猿類\napes and monkeys 猿猴\nApes have no tails.\n(猿沒有尾巴。)\nGorillas are the largest apes.\n(大猩猩是體型最大的猿類。)"],["appearance","appearance(n.)外表、出現\nappear(v.)出現、似乎\nphysical appearance 外貌\nmake an appearance 露面\nDon't judge people by their appearance.\n(不要以貌取人。)\nThe singer made a short appearance at the party.\n(那位歌手在派對上短暫露面。)"],["appetite","appetite(n.)食慾、慾望\n(無詞性變化)\nlose one's appetite 沒有食慾\na big appetite 胃口很大\nI lost my appetite when I was sick.\n(我生病時沒有食慾。)\nTeenage boys often have a big appetite.\n(青少年男生的胃口常常很大。)"],["apply","apply(v.)申請、應用、塗抹\napplication(n.)申請、應用\napplicant(n.)申請者\napply for 申請\napply to 適用於\nShe applied for a summer job.\n(她申請了一份暑期工作。)\nThese rules apply to all students.\n(這些規定適用於所有學生。)"],["appreciate","appreciate(v.)感激、欣賞、了解\nappreciation(n.)感激、欣賞\nreally appreciate 非常感激\nappreciate art 欣賞藝術\nI really appreciate your help.\n(我非常感謝你的幫忙。)\nHe learned to appreciate classical music.\n(他學會欣賞古典音樂。)"],["approach","approach(n./v.)方法、接近\n(無詞性變化)\na new approach 新方法\napproach to 對……的方法\nThe exam is approaching quickly.\n(考試很快就要到了。)\nWe need a new approach to this problem.\n(我們需要用新方法處理這個問題。)"],["argue(argument)","argue(v.)爭吵、主張、argument(n.)爭吵、論點\n(無詞性變化)\nargue with 和……爭吵\nhave an argument 吵架\nMy sister and I often argue about small things.\n(我和姊姊常為小事爭吵。)\nHe had an argument with his parents.\n(他和父母吵了一架。)"],["army","army(n.)軍隊、陸軍\n(無詞性變化)\njoin the army 從軍\nan army of 一大群\nHe joined the army after high school.\n(他高中畢業後從軍。)\nAn army of fans waited outside the hotel.\n(一大群粉絲在飯店外等候。)"],["arrange(ment)","arrange(v.)安排、整理、arrangement(n.)安排、布置\n(無詞性變化)\narrange a meeting 安排會議\nflower arrangement 插花\nMy mom arranged a party for my birthday.\n(媽媽為我的生日安排了派對。)\nWe made arrangements for the school trip.\n(我們為校外教學做了安排。)"],["arrival","arrival(n.)到達、抵達的人或物\narrive(v.)到達\non arrival 抵達時\nnew arrival 新到的人或貨\nPlease call me on your arrival.\n(你抵達時請打電話給我。)\nThe arrival of the train was delayed.\n(火車到站時間延誤了。)"],["arrow","arrow(n.)箭、箭頭\n(無詞性變化)\nbow and arrow 弓箭\nfollow the arrows 跟著箭頭走\nFollow the arrows to the exit.\n(跟著箭頭走到出口。)\nHe shot an arrow at the target.\n(他朝靶子射了一支箭。)"],["article","article(n.)文章、物品、冠詞\n(無詞性變化)\nnewspaper article 報紙文章\nan article of clothing 一件衣物\nI read an interesting article about space.\n(我讀了一篇有關太空的有趣文章。)\nPlease write an article for the school paper.\n(請為校刊寫一篇文章。)"],["artist","artist(n.)藝術家、畫家\nart(n.)藝術\nartistic(adj.)藝術的\nfamous artist 知名藝術家\nstreet artist 街頭藝術家\nShe wants to become an artist.\n(她想成為一位藝術家。)\nThe artist painted a picture of the sea.\n(那位畫家畫了一幅海的畫。)"],["asleep","asleep(adj.)睡著的\nsleep(v./n.)睡覺\nfall asleep 睡著\nfast asleep 熟睡\nThe baby is fast asleep.\n(寶寶睡得很熟。)\nI fell asleep in class yesterday.\n(我昨天上課睡著了。)"],["attempt","attempt(n./v.)嘗試、企圖\n(無詞性變化)\nmake an attempt 嘗試\nattempt to do 試圖做\nHe passed the test on his first attempt.\n(他第一次嘗試就通過了考試。)\nShe attempted to climb the mountain alone.\n(她試圖獨自攀登那座山。)"],["attend","attend(v.)參加、出席、上(學)\nattendance(n.)出席\nattention(n.)注意\nattend a meeting 出席會議\nattend school 上學\nAll students must attend the meeting.\n(所有學生都必須出席這場集會。)\nShe attends a high school in Taipei.\n(她在台北上高中。)"],["attention","attention(n.)注意、注意力\nattentive(adj.)專心的\npay attention to 注意\nattract attention 吸引注意\nPlease pay attention to the teacher.\n(請專心聽老師講。)\nThe strange noise attracted my attention.\n(奇怪的聲音引起了我的注意。)"],["author","author(n./v.)作者、作家、著作\n(無詞性變化)\nfamous author 知名作家\nthe author of 的作者\nWho is the author of this book?\n(這本書的作者是誰？)\nThe author signed books for her fans.\n(那位作家為書迷簽書。)"],["available","available(adj.)可用的、有空的、可取得的\navailability(n.)可用性\navailable seats 空位\nbe available for 有空做\nAre you available this afternoon?\n(你今天下午有空嗎？)\nThere are no seats available on the train.\n(火車上已經沒有空位了。)"],["average","average(adj./n./v.)平均(的)、普通的、平均為\n(無詞性變化)\non average 平均而言\nabove average 高於平均\nOn average, I sleep seven hours a night.\n(我平均每晚睡七小時。)\nHis grades are above average.\n(他的成績高於平均。)"],["avoid","avoid(v.)避免、躲開\navoidable(adj.)可避免的\navoid mistakes 避免犯錯\navoid doing 避免做\nTry to avoid eating too much sugar.\n(盡量避免吃太多糖。)\nWe left early to avoid the traffic.\n(我們提早出發以避開車潮。)"],["backpack","backpack(n./v.)背包、背包旅行\nbackpacker(n.)背包客\nschool backpack 書包\ngo backpacking 去自助旅行\nHe put his books in his backpack.\n(他把書放進背包裡。)\nThey went backpacking around Europe last summer.\n(他們去年夏天到歐洲自助旅行。)"],["backward","backward(adj.)向後的、落後的\n(無詞性變化)\na backward step 倒退的一步\nbackward area 落後地區\nHe left the room without a backward look.\n(他頭也不回地離開了房間。)\nThe village was once poor and backward.\n(那個村莊以前既貧窮又落後。)"],["backward/backwards","backward(adv.)向後地、倒著\nbackwards(adv.)向後地、倒著(同 backward)\nwalk backward 倒著走\ncount backward 倒數\nShe took a step backward in surprise.\n(她驚訝地向後退了一步。)\nCan you say the alphabet backwards?\n(你可以倒著唸英文字母嗎？)"],["badminton","badminton(n.)羽毛球\n(無詞性變化)\nplay badminton 打羽毛球\nbadminton court 羽球場\nWe play badminton after school.\n(我們放學後打羽毛球。)\nTai Tzu-ying is a famous badminton player.\n(戴資穎是知名的羽球選手。)"],["bake","bake(v.)烘烤\nbaker(n.)麵包師傅\nbakery(n.)麵包店\nbake a cake 烤蛋糕\nfreshly baked 剛烤好的\nMy mom bakes cookies on weekends.\n(我媽媽週末會烤餅乾。)\nI love the smell of freshly baked bread.\n(我喜歡剛出爐麵包的香味。)"],["bakery","bakery(n.)麵包店、烘焙坊\nbake(v.)烘烤\nbaker(n.)麵包師傅\nlocal bakery 當地麵包店\nbakery shop 麵包店\nI buy bread at the bakery every morning.\n(我每天早上在麵包店買麵包。)\nThe new bakery sells delicious pineapple cakes.\n(新開的麵包店賣美味的鳳梨酥。)"],["balance","balance(n./v.)平衡、餘額、使平衡\nbalanced(adj.)均衡的\nkeep one's balance 保持平衡\nbalanced diet 均衡飲食\nShe lost her balance and fell off the bike.\n(她失去平衡從腳踏車上摔下來。)\nIt's important to balance study and rest.\n(兼顧讀書和休息很重要。)"],["balcony","balcony(n.)陽台\n(無詞性變化)\non the balcony 在陽台上\nbalcony door 陽台門\nWe grow flowers on our balcony.\n(我們在陽台上種花。)\nHe hung his clothes on the balcony to dry.\n(他把衣服晾在陽台上。)"],["balloon","balloon(n.)氣球\n(無詞性變化)\nblow up a balloon 吹氣球\nhot-air balloon 熱氣球\nThe kids blew up balloons for the party.\n(孩子們為派對吹氣球。)\nWe rode a hot-air balloon in Taitung.\n(我們在台東搭了熱氣球。)"],["bar","bar(n./v.)酒吧、條、棒、阻擋\n(無詞性變化)\nchocolate bar 巧克力棒\nsnack bar 小吃店\nHe ate a chocolate bar after the run.\n(他跑完步後吃了一條巧克力棒。)\nThey met at a small bar downtown.\n(他們在市中心一家小酒吧見面。)"],["barbecue","barbecue(n./v.)烤肉、燒烤\nBBQ(n.)烤肉(縮寫)\nhave a barbecue 烤肉\nbarbecue sauce 烤肉醬\nMany families have a barbecue at Moon Festival.\n(許多家庭在中秋節烤肉。)\nDad barbecued some chicken in the yard.\n(爸爸在院子裡烤了一些雞肉。)"],["barber","barber(n.)理髮師\nbarbershop(n.)理髮店\ngo to the barber 去理髮\nbarber shop 理髮店\nI go to the barber once a month.\n(我每個月去理髮一次。)\nThe barber cut my hair too short.\n(理髮師把我的頭髮剪得太短了。)"],["bark","bark(n./v.)吠叫、狗吠聲、樹皮\n(無詞性變化)\nbark at 對⋯吠叫\ntree bark 樹皮\nThe dog barks at every stranger.\n(這隻狗對每個陌生人吠叫。)\nThe bark of this tree is very rough.\n(這棵樹的樹皮很粗糙。)"],["base","base(n./v.)基礎、底部、基地、以⋯為根據\nbasic(adj.)基本的\nbasis(n.)基礎、根據\nbe based on 根據⋯\nmilitary base 軍事基地\nThe movie is based on a true story.\n(這部電影是根據真實故事改編的。)\nPut the lamp on a strong base.\n(把檯燈放在穩固的底座上。)"],["basic","basic(adj.)基本的、基礎的\nbase(n.)基礎\nbasics(n.)基本原理\nbasically(adv.)基本上\nbasic skills 基本技能\nbasic needs 基本需求\nFood and water are basic needs.\n(食物和水是基本需求。)\nYou need basic computer skills for this job.\n(這份工作需要基本的電腦技能。)"],["basics","basics(n.)基礎、基本原理\nbasic(adj.)基本的\nlearn the basics 學習基礎\nback to basics 回歸基本\nFirst, let's learn the basics of cooking.\n(首先，我們來學烹飪的基礎。)\nThe coach taught us the basics of tennis.\n(教練教我們網球的基本功。)"],["basis","basis(n.)基礎、根據\nbase(n.)基礎\nbasic(adj.)基本的\non a daily basis 每天\non the basis of 根據⋯\nI check my email on a daily basis.\n(我每天都會查看電子郵件。)\nTrust is the basis of friendship.\n(信任是友誼的基礎。)"],["bathe","bathe(v.)洗澡、給⋯洗澡、沐浴\nbath(n.)洗澡\nbathe a baby 幫嬰兒洗澡\nbathed in sunlight 沐浴在陽光中\nShe bathes her dog every week.\n(她每週幫狗洗澡。)\nThe garden was bathed in morning sunlight.\n(花園沐浴在早晨的陽光中。)"],["battle","battle(n./v.)戰役、戰鬥、奮鬥\n(無詞性變化)\nfight a battle 打仗\nbattle against 和⋯奮戰\nMany soldiers died in the battle.\n(很多士兵在那場戰役中喪生。)\nShe won her battle against illness.\n(她戰勝了病魔。)"],["beard","beard(n.)鬍子、絡腮鬍\nbearded(adj.)有鬍子的\ngrow a beard 留鬍子\nshave one's beard 刮鬍子\nMy uncle has a long gray beard.\n(我叔叔留著灰色長鬍子。)\nHe decided to grow a beard this winter.\n(他決定今年冬天留鬍子。)"],["beat","beat(v./n.)打敗、敲打、(心臟)跳動、節拍\n(無詞性變化)\nbeat the record 打破紀錄\nheart beat 心跳\nOur team beat them 3 to 1.\n(我們隊以三比一打敗他們。)\nMy heart beat fast before the test.\n(考試前我的心跳得很快。)"],["beauty","beauty(n.)美、美人\nbeautiful(adj.)美麗的\nbeautify(v.)美化\nnatural beauty 自然美景\nbeauty salon 美容院\nTaroko is famous for its natural beauty.\n(太魯閣以自然美景聞名。)\nShe is a real beauty.\n(她真是個美人。)"],["beer","beer(n.)啤酒\n(無詞性變化)\na glass of beer 一杯啤酒\ndraft beer 生啤酒\nDad had a cold beer after work.\n(爸爸下班後喝了一杯冰啤酒。)\nYou must be eighteen to buy beer.\n(你必須滿十八歲才能買啤酒。)"],["beg","beg(v.)乞討、懇求\nbeggar(n.)乞丐\nbeg for 乞求\nI beg your pardon. 請再說一次。\nThe child begged his mom for a toy.\n(那個孩子懇求媽媽買玩具。)\nAn old man was begging for food.\n(一位老人在乞討食物。)"],["beginner","beginner(n.)初學者\nbegin(v.)開始\nbeginning(n.)開始\nbeginner level 初級程度\nbeginner's luck 新手運\nThis class is for beginners.\n(這堂課是給初學者上的。)\nI'm a beginner at swimming.\n(我是游泳的初學者。)"],["behave","behave(v.)表現、行為舉止、守規矩\nbehavior(n.)行為\nbehave oneself 守規矩\nbehave well 表現良好\nPlease behave yourself in class.\n(上課時請守規矩。)\nThe kids behaved well at the party.\n(孩子們在派對上表現得很好。)"],["being","being(n.)存在、生物、人\n(無詞性變化)\nhuman being 人類\ncome into being 形成、出現\nEvery human being needs love.\n(每個人都需要愛。)\nThe school came into being in 1950.\n(這所學校成立於1950年。)"],["belief","belief(n.)信念、信仰、相信\nbelieve(v.)相信\nbelievable(adj.)可信的\nreligious belief 宗教信仰\nstrong belief 堅定的信念\nHe has a strong belief in hard work.\n(他堅信努力的價值。)\nPeople have different beliefs.\n(人們有不同的信仰。)"],["bend","bend(v./n.)彎曲、彎腰、轉彎處\n(無詞性變化)\nbend down 彎下腰\na sharp bend 急轉彎\nShe bent down to pick up the pen.\n(她彎下腰撿起筆。)\nDrive slowly around the sharp bend.\n(在急轉彎處要慢慢開。)"],["better","better(adj./adv./n./v.)較好的、更好地、改善\n(無詞性變化)\nget better 好轉\nhad better 最好\nI hope you get better soon.\n(希望你早日康復。)\nYou had better finish your homework first.\n(你最好先寫完功課。)"],["beyond","beyond(prep./adv.)超出、在⋯的另一邊、更遠處\n(無詞性變化)\nbeyond one's reach 超出能力範圍\nbeyond belief 難以置信\nThe mountains lie beyond the river.\n(那些山就在河的另一邊。)\nThis math problem is beyond me.\n(這道數學題超出我的能力範圍。)"],["bill","bill(n./v.)帳單、鈔票、法案、開帳單\n(無詞性變化)\npay the bill 付帳\na hundred-dollar bill 一張百元鈔票\nLet me pay the bill this time.\n(這次讓我付帳吧。)\nThe phone bill is too high this month.\n(這個月的電話費太高了。)"],["billion","billion(n.)十億\n(無詞性變化)\nbillions of 數十億的\none billion dollars 十億元\nThere are about eight billion people on Earth.\n(地球上大約有八十億人。)\nThe company is worth a billion dollars.\n(這家公司價值十億美元。)"],["birth","birth(n.)出生、誕生\nbirthday(n.)生日\ngive birth to 生(孩子)\ndate of birth 出生日期\nPlease write your date of birth here.\n(請在這裡寫下你的出生日期。)\nThe cat gave birth to four kittens.\n(那隻貓生了四隻小貓。)"],["biscuit","biscuit(n.)餅乾(英式)、小圓麵包(美式)\n(無詞性變化)\nchocolate biscuit 巧克力餅乾\ntea and biscuits 茶和餅乾\nGrandma served tea and biscuits.\n(奶奶端出茶和餅乾。)\nHe ate a whole box of biscuits.\n(他吃掉了一整盒餅乾。)"],["bit","bit(n.)一點、小片\n(無詞性變化)\na bit 有點\nbit by bit 一點一點地\nI'm a bit tired today.\n(我今天有點累。)\nShe improved her English bit by bit.\n(她的英文一點一點地進步。)"],["blackboard","blackboard(n.)黑板\n(無詞性變化)\nwrite on the blackboard 在黑板上寫字\nclean the blackboard 擦黑板\nThe teacher wrote the answer on the blackboard.\n(老師把答案寫在黑板上。)\nIt's my turn to clean the blackboard.\n(輪到我擦黑板了。)"],["blame","blame(v./n.)責怪、歸咎、責任\n(無詞性變化)\nblame... for 因⋯責怪\ntake the blame 承擔責任\nDon't blame me for your mistake.\n(不要把你的錯怪到我頭上。)\nThe captain took the blame for the loss.\n(隊長為輸球承擔了責任。)"],["blank","blank(adj./n.)空白的、茫然的、空格\n(無詞性變化)\nfill in the blanks 填空\ngo blank 腦袋一片空白\nFill in the blanks with the right words.\n(用正確的字填空。)\nMy mind went blank during the test.\n(考試時我腦袋一片空白。)"],["blanket","blanket(n./v.)毯子、覆蓋\n(無詞性變化)\na warm blanket 保暖的毯子\na blanket of snow 一層厚雪\nShe put a blanket over the sleeping baby.\n(她在熟睡的寶寶身上蓋了毯子。)\nThe ground was covered with a blanket of snow.\n(地面覆蓋著一層厚厚的雪。)"],["blood","blood(n.)血、血液\nbloody(adj.)流血的、血腥的\nbleed(v.)流血\nblood type 血型\ngive blood 捐血\nWhat is your blood type?\n(你的血型是什麼？)\nMy father gives blood twice a year.\n(我爸爸一年捐血兩次。)"],["board","board(n./v.)木板、布告欄、董事會、登上(交通工具)\nboarding(n.)登機、寄宿\non board 在船(機、車)上\nbulletin board 布告欄\nPlease check the bulletin board for news.\n(請查看布告欄上的消息。)\nPassengers are now boarding the plane.\n(乘客正在登機。)"],["boil","boil(n./v.)沸騰、煮沸\nboiling(adj.)沸騰的、極熱的\nboiled(adj.)煮過的\nboil water 燒開水\nboiled egg 水煮蛋\nWater boils at 100 degrees Celsius.\n(水在攝氏一百度沸騰。)\nI had a boiled egg for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了一顆水煮蛋。)"],["bone","bone(n.)骨頭\nbony(adj.)骨瘦如柴的、多骨的\nbreak a bone 骨折\nbone marrow 骨髓\nHe broke a bone in his arm.\n(他的手臂骨折了。)\nThe dog is chewing on a bone.\n(那隻狗正在啃骨頭。)"],["bookstore","bookstore(n.)書店\n(無詞性變化)\nused bookstore 二手書店\nonline bookstore 網路書店\nI bought this novel at a bookstore.\n(我在書店買了這本小說。)\nThere is a used bookstore near the station.\n(車站附近有一家二手書店。)"],["border","border(n./v.)邊界、邊緣、與⋯接壤\n(無詞性變化)\ncross the border 越過邊界\nborder on 與⋯接壤\nThey crossed the border into Canada.\n(他們越過邊界進入加拿大。)\nFrance borders on Spain.\n(法國與西班牙接壤。)"],["bother","bother(v./n.)打擾、使煩惱、麻煩\n(無詞性變化)\nSorry to bother you. 抱歉打擾你。\ndon't bother 不必費心\nSorry to bother you, but where is the library?\n(抱歉打擾你，請問圖書館在哪裡？)\nThe noise didn't bother him at all.\n(這噪音一點也沒打擾到他。)"],["brain","brain(n.)腦、頭腦、智囊\nbrainy(adj.)聰明的\nuse your brain 動動腦\nbrain power 腦力\nReading is good for your brain.\n(閱讀對大腦有益。)\nUse your brain to solve the puzzle.\n(動動腦解開這個謎題。)"],["branch","branch(n./v.)樹枝、分店、分支、分岔\n(無詞性變化)\nbranch office 分公司\nbranch out 拓展\nA bird is sitting on the branch.\n(一隻鳥停在樹枝上。)\nThe bank has a branch near my school.\n(那家銀行在我學校附近有分行。)"],["brand","brand(n.)品牌、商標\n(無詞性變化)\nbrand name 品牌名稱\nbrand-new 全新的\nWhat brand is your phone?\n(你的手機是什麼牌子？)\nHe bought a brand-new bike.\n(他買了一台全新的腳踏車。)"],["brief","brief(adj./n./v.)簡短的、摘要、向⋯簡報\nbriefly(adv.)簡短地\nin brief 簡言之\na brief talk 簡短的談話\nThe teacher gave a brief speech.\n(老師做了簡短的致詞。)\nIn brief, we need more time.\n(簡單地說，我們需要更多時間。)"],["brilliant","brilliant(adj.)出色的、聰穎的、燦爛的\nbrilliance(n.)光輝、才華\nbrilliant idea 絕妙的主意\nbrilliant sunshine 燦爛的陽光\nWhat a brilliant idea!\n(真是個絕妙的主意！)\nShe is a brilliant young scientist.\n(她是一位才華洋溢的年輕科學家。)"],["broad","broad(adj.)寬闊的、廣泛的\nbreadth(n.)寬度\nbroaden(v.)拓寬\nbroad shoulders 寬肩膀\na broad range of 範圍廣泛的\nHe has broad shoulders.\n(他有寬闊的肩膀。)\nThe library has a broad range of books.\n(圖書館有種類廣泛的書。)"],["brush","brush(n./v.)刷子、刷\n(無詞性變化)\nbrush one's teeth 刷牙\npaint brush 畫筆\nBrush your teeth before bed.\n(睡前要刷牙。)\nShe painted the wall with a big brush.\n(她用一把大刷子粉刷牆壁。)"],["building","building(n.)建築物、大樓\nbuild(v.)建造\nbuilder(n.)建築工人\ntall building 高樓\noffice building 辦公大樓\nTaipei 101 is a very tall building.\n(台北101是一棟非常高的大樓。)\nMy dad works in that office building.\n(我爸爸在那棟辦公大樓上班。)"],["bun","bun(n.)小圓麵包、包子、(頭髮)髻\n(無詞性變化)\nsteamed bun 饅頭、包子\nhot dog bun 熱狗麵包\nI had two steamed buns for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了兩個包子。)\nShe wears her hair in a bun.\n(她把頭髮盤成一個髻。)"],["burden","burden(n./v.)負擔、重擔、使負擔\n(無詞性變化)\na heavy burden 沉重的負擔\nbe a burden to 成為⋯的負擔\nHe doesn't want to be a burden to his family.\n(他不想成為家人的負擔。)\nToo much homework is a burden on students.\n(太多功課對學生是一種負擔。)"],["burn","burn(v./n.)燃燒、燒傷、燒傷處\nburning(adj.)燃燒的、熾熱的\nburn down 燒毀\nget burned 被燙傷、曬傷\nThe old house burned down last night.\n(那棟老房子昨晚被燒毀了。)\nBe careful not to burn your hand.\n(小心別燙到手。)"],["burst","burst(n./v.)爆炸、破裂、突然發生\n(無詞性變化)\nburst into tears 突然哭出來\nburst out laughing 突然大笑\nThe balloon burst with a loud bang.\n(氣球砰的一聲爆了。)\nShe burst into tears when she heard the news.\n(她聽到消息後突然哭了出來。)"],["businessman","businessman(n.)商人、生意人\nbusiness(n.)生意\nbusinesswoman(n.)女商人\nsuccessful businessman 成功的商人\na businessman from Japan 一位日本商人\nHis father is a successful businessman.\n(他父親是一位成功的商人。)\nThe businessman travels to China often.\n(那位商人經常到中國出差。)"],["cabbage","cabbage(n.)高麗菜、甘藍菜\n(無詞性變化)\nChinese cabbage 大白菜\ncabbage soup 高麗菜湯\nMy mom bought a big cabbage at the market.\n(我媽媽在市場買了一顆大高麗菜。)\nCabbage is cheap and healthy.\n(高麗菜便宜又健康。)"],["café/cafe","café(n.)咖啡館、小餐館\ncafe(n.)咖啡館(同 café)\ninternet café 網咖\na small café 一間小咖啡館\nLet's meet at the café near the station.\n(我們在車站附近的咖啡館碰面吧。)\nShe often studies in a quiet café.\n(她常在一間安靜的咖啡館讀書。)"],["cage","cage(n./v.)籠子、把⋯關進籠子\ncaged(adj.)關在籠中的\nbird cage 鳥籠\nin a cage 在籠子裡\nThe bird is singing in its cage.\n(那隻鳥在籠子裡唱歌。)\nThe lion was caged at the zoo.\n(那隻獅子被關在動物園的籠子裡。)"],["calendar","calendar(n.)日曆、行事曆\n(無詞性變化)\nlunar calendar 農曆\nmark the calendar 在日曆上做記號\nI marked her birthday on my calendar.\n(我在日曆上標記了她的生日。)\nChinese New Year follows the lunar calendar.\n(農曆新年是依照農曆來定的。)"],["calm","calm(v./adj./n.)使平靜、冷靜的、平靜\ncalmly(adv.)冷靜地\ncalmness(n.)平靜、鎮定\ncalm down 冷靜下來\nstay calm 保持冷靜\nPlease calm down and tell me what happened.\n(請冷靜下來，告訴我發生了什麼事。)\nThe sea is calm this morning.\n(今天早上海面很平靜。)"],["camel","camel(n.)駱駝\n(無詞性變化)\nride a camel 騎駱駝\ncamel hump 駝峰\nCamels can live in the desert for days without water.\n(駱駝可以在沙漠中好幾天不喝水。)\nWe rode a camel in Egypt.\n(我們在埃及騎了駱駝。)"],["cancel","cancel(v.)取消\ncancellation(n.)取消\ncancel a meeting 取消會議\ncancel an order 取消訂單\nThe game was canceled because of the rain.\n(比賽因為下雨被取消了。)\nI had to cancel my trip to Japan.\n(我不得不取消去日本的旅行。)"],["cancer","cancer(n.)癌症\n(無詞性變化)\nlung cancer 肺癌\ncancer patient 癌症病患\nSmoking can cause lung cancer.\n(抽菸可能導致肺癌。)\nMy uncle beat cancer two years ago.\n(我舅舅兩年前戰勝了癌症。)"],["candle","candle(n.)蠟燭\ncandlelight(n.)燭光\nlight a candle 點蠟燭\nblow out the candles 吹熄蠟燭\nShe blew out the candles on her birthday cake.\n(她吹熄了生日蛋糕上的蠟燭。)\nWe lit a candle when the power went out.\n(停電時我們點了一根蠟燭。)"],["capital","capital(n./adj.)首都、資本、大寫字母、主要的\ncapitalism(n.)資本主義\ncapital city 首都\ncapital letter 大寫字母\nTokyo is the capital of Japan.\n(東京是日本的首都。)\nStart each sentence with a capital letter.\n(每個句子的開頭要用大寫字母。)"],["cartoon","cartoon(n./v.)卡通、漫畫、畫漫畫\ncartoonist(n.)漫畫家\ncartoon character 卡通人物\nwatch cartoons 看卡通\nKids love to watch cartoons on Saturday morning.\n(孩子們喜歡在星期六早上看卡通。)\nMickey Mouse is a famous cartoon character.\n(米老鼠是一個有名的卡通人物。)"],["cash","cash(n./v.)現金、兌現\ncashier(n.)收銀員\npay in cash 用現金付款\ncash a check 兌現支票\nCan I pay in cash?\n(我可以付現金嗎？)\nI don't have any cash with me.\n(我身上沒有帶任何現金。)"],["castle","castle(n.)城堡\n(無詞性變化)\nsand castle 沙堡\nold castle 古堡\nThe children built a sand castle on the beach.\n(孩子們在海灘上蓋了一座沙堡。)\nThe king lived in a huge castle.\n(國王住在一座巨大的城堡裡。)"],["cause","cause(n./v.)原因、起因、導致\n(無詞性變化)\ncause and effect 因果\ncause trouble 惹麻煩\nThe heavy rain caused a flood.\n(大雨造成了水災。)\nWhat was the cause of the fire?\n(火災的原因是什麼？)"],["ceiling","ceiling(n.)天花板\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh ceiling 挑高的天花板\nceiling fan 吊扇\nThere is a spider on the ceiling.\n(天花板上有一隻蜘蛛。)\nThe room has a ceiling fan.\n(這個房間有一台吊扇。)"],["cell","cell(n.)細胞、牢房、小隔間\ncellular(adj.)細胞的、行動電話的\ncell phone 手機\nblood cell 血球\nOur bodies are made of millions of cells.\n(我們的身體是由數百萬個細胞組成的。)\nPlease turn off your cell phone in class.\n(上課時請把手機關機。)"],["centimeter","centimeter(n.)公分\n(無詞性變化)\nten centimeters long 十公分長\nsquare centimeter 平方公分\nThis ruler is thirty centimeters long.\n(這把尺有三十公分長。)\nShe grew five centimeters this year.\n(她今年長高了五公分。)"],["central","central(adj.)中央的、主要的\ncenter(n.)中心\ncentral heating 中央暖氣\ncentral idea 主旨\nOur school is in central Taipei.\n(我們學校在臺北市中心。)\nWhat is the central idea of this story?\n(這個故事的主旨是什麼？)"],["century","century(n.)世紀、一百年\n(無詞性變化)\nthe 21st century 二十一世紀\nfor centuries 好幾個世紀以來\nWe live in the twenty-first century.\n(我們生活在二十一世紀。)\nThis temple is over three centuries old.\n(這座廟已有三百多年的歷史。)"],["cereal","cereal(n.)穀類、麥片\n(無詞性變化)\nbreakfast cereal 早餐麥片\na bowl of cereal 一碗麥片\nI eat a bowl of cereal with milk every morning.\n(我每天早上吃一碗加牛奶的麥片。)\nRice and wheat are common cereals.\n(稻米和小麥是常見的穀物。)"],["chain","chain(n./v.)鏈條、連鎖店、用鏈子拴住\n(無詞性變化)\nchain store 連鎖店\nfood chain 食物鏈\nHe chained his bike to the tree.\n(他用鏈條把腳踏車鎖在樹上。)\nThere are many chain stores in this city.\n(這個城市有很多連鎖店。)"],["chalk","chalk(n./v.)粉筆、用粉筆寫\n(無詞性變化)\na piece of chalk 一支粉筆\ncolored chalk 彩色粉筆\nThe teacher wrote the answer in chalk.\n(老師用粉筆寫下答案。)\nCan you give me a piece of chalk?\n(你能給我一支粉筆嗎？)"],["challenge","challenge(n./v.)挑戰、向⋯挑戰\nchallenging(adj.)有挑戰性的\nface a challenge 面對挑戰\nmeet a challenge 迎接挑戰\nLearning English is a big challenge for him.\n(學英文對他來說是很大的挑戰。)\nShe challenged me to a game of chess.\n(她向我挑戰下一盤西洋棋。)"],["channel","channel(n./v.)頻道、海峽、管道、引導\n(無詞性變化)\nTV channel 電視頻道\nchange the channel 轉台\nWhat channel is the game on?\n(比賽在哪一台播？)\nPlease don't change the channel.\n(請不要轉台。)"],["chapter","chapter(n.)(書的)章、回\n(無詞性變化)\nthe first chapter 第一章\na new chapter 新的篇章\nPlease read Chapter 3 before the next class.\n(下次上課前請讀完第三章。)\nGoing to college is a new chapter in her life.\n(上大學是她人生的新篇章。)"],["character","character(n.)性格、角色、文字\ncharacteristic(n./adj.)特徵、特有的\nmain character 主角\nChinese character 中文字\nThe main character of the movie is a little girl.\n(這部電影的主角是一個小女孩。)\nHe has a strong character.\n(他個性很堅強。)"],["charge","charge(n./v.)收費、費用、充電、控告、負責\ncharger(n.)充電器\nin charge of 負責⋯\nfree of charge 免費\nI need to charge my phone.\n(我需要幫手機充電。)\nMr. Lin is in charge of the school library.\n(林老師負責學校圖書館。)"],["chart","chart(n.)圖表\n(無詞性變化)\npie chart 圓餅圖\ntop the charts 登上排行榜冠軍\nThe chart shows our sales this year.\n(這張圖表顯示我們今年的銷售量。)\nHer new song topped the charts.\n(她的新歌登上排行榜冠軍。)"],["chase","chase(n./v.)追逐、追趕\n(無詞性變化)\nchase after 追趕\nchase a dream 追夢\nThe dog is chasing a cat.\n(狗正在追一隻貓。)\nNever stop chasing your dreams.\n(永遠不要停止追逐你的夢想。)"],["cheat","cheat(v./n.)作弊、欺騙、騙子\ncheater(n.)作弊者、騙子\ncheat on a test 考試作弊\ncheat someone out of 騙走某人的⋯\nIt is wrong to cheat on a test.\n(考試作弊是不對的。)\nThe man cheated her out of her money.\n(那個男人騙走了她的錢。)"],["cheer","cheer(v./n.)歡呼、喝采、使振奮\ncheerful(adj.)開心的、令人愉快的\ncheer up 振作起來\ncheer for 為⋯加油\nCheer up! Things will get better.\n(振作起來！事情會好轉的。)\nWe cheered for our team.\n(我們為我們的隊伍加油。)"],["chemical","chemical(adj./n.)化學的、化學物質\nchemistry(n.)化學\nchemist(n.)化學家\nchemical change 化學變化\ntoxic chemicals 有毒化學物質\nSome chemicals are dangerous to touch.\n(有些化學物質碰觸是危險的。)\nBurning paper is a chemical change.\n(燒紙是一種化學變化。)"],["chess","chess(n.)西洋棋\n(無詞性變化)\nplay chess 下西洋棋\nchess player 棋手\nMy grandfather taught me how to play chess.\n(我爺爺教我怎麼下西洋棋。)\nHe is a good chess player.\n(他是個很厲害的西洋棋手。)"],["chief","chief(adj./n.)主要的、首領、主管\nchiefly(adv.)主要地\nchief reason 主要原因\npolice chief 警察局長\nMoney is the chief reason for his choice.\n(錢是他做這個選擇的主要原因。)\nThe chief of the village is very kind.\n(這個村子的村長非常和善。)"],["childhood","childhood(n.)童年\nchild(n.)小孩\nchildhood memory 童年回憶\nhappy childhood 快樂的童年\nI had a happy childhood in the countryside.\n(我在鄉下度過了快樂的童年。)\nThis song brings back my childhood memories.\n(這首歌喚起了我的童年回憶。)"],["childish","childish(adj.)幼稚的、孩子氣的\nchild(n.)小孩\nchildlike(adj.)天真的\nchildish behavior 幼稚的行為\nDon't be childish. 別那麼幼稚。\nStop being so childish!\n(別再那麼幼稚了！)\nHis childish behavior made his mom angry.\n(他幼稚的行為讓他媽媽很生氣。)"],["china","china(n.)瓷器\n(無詞性變化)\nfine china 精緻瓷器\nchina cup 瓷杯\nBe careful with that china cup.\n(小心那個瓷杯。)\nMy grandma keeps her best china in the cabinet.\n(我奶奶把她最好的瓷器放在櫃子裡。)"],["chopstick(s)","chopstick(n.)筷子(單支)、chopsticks(n.)筷子(一雙)\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of chopsticks 一雙筷子\nuse chopsticks 用筷子\nCan you eat noodles with chopsticks?\n(你會用筷子吃麵嗎？)\nI need a new pair of chopsticks.\n(我需要一雙新筷子。)"],["claim","claim(n./v.)聲稱、要求、認領、主張\n(無詞性變化)\nclaim to be 聲稱是\nbaggage claim 行李提領處\nHe claims to be a famous singer.\n(他聲稱自己是有名的歌手。)\nLet's pick up our bags at baggage claim.\n(我們去行李提領處拿行李吧。)"],["clap","clap(v./n.)拍手、鼓掌\n(無詞性變化)\nclap your hands 拍手\na clap of thunder 一聲雷響\nEveryone clapped after her speech.\n(她演講完大家都鼓掌了。)\nClap your hands to the music.\n(跟著音樂拍手。)"],["classic","classic(adj./n.)經典的、典型的、經典作品\nclassical(adj.)古典的\nclassic movie 經典電影\na classic example 典型的例子\nThis is a classic movie from the 1950s.\n(這是一部 1950 年代的經典電影。)\nRomeo and Juliet is a classic.\n(《羅密歐與茱麗葉》是一部經典作品。)"],["classical","classical(adj.)古典的\nclassic(adj./n.)經典的、經典作品\nclassical music 古典音樂\nclassical Chinese 文言文\nShe listens to classical music when she studies.\n(她讀書時聽古典音樂。)\nWe are learning classical Chinese this semester.\n(我們這學期在學文言文。)"],["classmate","classmate(n.)同學\n(無詞性變化)\nold classmate 老同學\nnew classmate 新同學\nShe is my classmate.\n(她是我的同學。)\nI met an old classmate at the mall.\n(我在購物中心遇到一位老同學。)"],["clever","clever(adj.)聰明的、靈巧的\ncleverly(adv.)聰明地、巧妙地\ncleverness(n.)聰明\nclever idea 好點子\nclever with one's hands 手巧\nThat's a clever idea!\n(那是個好點子！)\nThe clever boy solved the puzzle quickly.\n(那個聰明的男孩很快就解開了謎題。)"],["click","click(v./n.)點擊、發出喀嚓聲、喀嚓聲\n(無詞性變化)\nclick on 點擊⋯\ndouble-click 點兩下\nClick on the link to see more.\n(點擊連結看更多內容。)\nI heard a click at the door.\n(我聽到門口傳來喀嚓一聲。)"],["climate","climate(n.)氣候\n(無詞性變化)\nclimate change 氣候變遷\nwarm climate 溫暖的氣候\nTaiwan has a warm climate.\n(臺灣氣候溫暖。)\nClimate change is a big problem today.\n(氣候變遷是當今一大問題。)"],["cloth","cloth(n.)布、布料、抹布\nclothes(n.)衣服\nclothing(n.)衣物、服裝\na piece of cloth 一塊布\ncotton cloth 棉布\nShe wiped the table with a wet cloth.\n(她用濕抹布擦桌子。)\nThis bag is made of cotton cloth.\n(這個袋子是用棉布做的。)"],["clothing","clothing(n.)衣物、服裝(總稱)\ncloth(n.)布、布料\nclothes(n.)衣服\nwarm clothing 保暖衣物\nclothing store 服飾店\nBring warm clothing for the mountain trip.\n(這趟登山行程要帶保暖衣物。)\nShe works at a clothing store.\n(她在一家服飾店工作。)"],["cloudy","cloudy(adj.)多雲的、陰天的\ncloud(n.)雲\ncloudy day 陰天\ncloudy sky 多雲的天空\nIt is cloudy today, but it won't rain.\n(今天是陰天，但不會下雨。)\nI like to read on cloudy days.\n(我喜歡在陰天看書。)"],["coal","coal(n.)煤、煤炭\n(無詞性變化)\ncoal mine 煤礦\nburn coal 燒煤\nBurning coal makes the air dirty.\n(燒煤會讓空氣變髒。)\nHis grandfather worked in a coal mine.\n(他的祖父曾在煤礦工作。)"],["coast","coast(n.)海岸、海濱\ncoastal(adj.)沿海的\neast coast 東海岸\nalong the coast 沿著海岸\nWe drove along the east coast of Taiwan.\n(我們沿著臺灣東海岸開車。)\nThey live in a small town on the coast.\n(他們住在海邊的一個小鎮。)"],["cockroach/roach","cockroach(n.)蟑螂\nroach(n.)蟑螂(口語)\nkill a cockroach 打死蟑螂\nflying cockroach 會飛的蟑螂\nI saw a cockroach in the kitchen.\n(我在廚房看到一隻蟑螂。)\nShe screamed when the cockroach flew.\n(蟑螂飛起來時她尖叫了。)"],["cocoa","cocoa(n.)可可粉、熱可可\n(無詞性變化)\nhot cocoa 熱可可\ncocoa beans 可可豆\nA cup of hot cocoa is nice on a cold day.\n(冷天喝一杯熱可可很舒服。)\nChocolate is made from cocoa beans.\n(巧克力是用可可豆做的。)"],["coin","coin(n./v.)硬幣、創造(新詞)\n(無詞性變化)\ntoss a coin 擲硬幣\ncoin a word 創造新詞\nLet's toss a coin to decide.\n(我們擲硬幣決定吧。)\nI put a ten-dollar coin into the machine.\n(我把一枚十元硬幣投進機器。)"],["cola/Coke","cola(n.)可樂\nCoke(n.)可口可樂(商標名)\na can of cola 一罐可樂\ndiet cola 健怡可樂\nToo much cola is bad for your teeth.\n(喝太多可樂對牙齒不好。)\nI'd like a burger and a Coke, please.\n(我要一個漢堡和一杯可樂，謝謝。)"],["college","college(n.)大學、學院\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to college 上大學\ncollege student 大學生\nMy brother is going to college next year.\n(我哥哥明年要上大學。)\nShe is a college student in Tainan.\n(她是臺南的大學生。)"],["comb","comb(n./v.)梳子、梳(頭髮)\n(無詞性變化)\ncomb one's hair 梳頭髮\nfine-tooth comb 細齒梳\nComb your hair before you go out.\n(出門前梳一下頭髮。)\nI can't find my comb.\n(我找不到我的梳子。)"],["combine","combine(v.)結合、混合\ncombination(n.)結合、組合\ncombine A with B 把 A 和 B 結合\ncombined effort 共同努力\nCombine the flour with the eggs.\n(把麵粉和蛋混合在一起。)\nShe combines work with fun.\n(她把工作和娛樂結合在一起。)"],["comic(s)","comic(adj./n.)滑稽的、喜劇演員、comics(n.)漫畫\ncomical(adj.)滑稽可笑的\ncomic book 漫畫書\nread comics 看漫畫\nMy little brother loves reading comics.\n(我弟弟很愛看漫畫。)\nHe bought a new comic book yesterday.\n(他昨天買了一本新漫畫書。)"],["command","command(n./v.)命令、指揮、掌握\ncommander(n.)指揮官\ngive a command 下命令\ncommand of English 英語能力\nThe dog obeys every command.\n(那隻狗會服從每個指令。)\nShe has a good command of English.\n(她英語能力很好。)"],["commercial","commercial(adj./n.)商業的、廣告\ncommerce(n.)商業\nTV commercial 電視廣告\ncommercial area 商業區\nI don't like long TV commercials.\n(我不喜歡很長的電視廣告。)\nThis is a busy commercial area.\n(這是個熱鬧的商業區。)"],["company","company(n.)公司、陪伴、同伴\ncompanion(n.)同伴\nkeep someone company 陪伴某人\nwork for a company 在公司工作\nMy father works for a computer company.\n(我爸爸在一家電腦公司上班。)\nI'll keep you company tonight.\n(今晚我會陪你。)"],["compare","compare(v.)比較、比作\ncomparison(n.)比較\ncompare A with B 把 A 和 B 比較\ncompare A to B 把 A 比作 B\nDon't compare yourself with others.\n(不要拿自己和別人比較。)\nLife is often compared to a journey.\n(人生常被比作一段旅程。)"],["complete","complete(adj./v.)完整的、完成\ncompletely(adv.)完全地\ncompletion(n.)完成\ncomplete a task 完成任務\na complete set 一整套\nPlease complete the form.\n(請填完這張表格。)\nI completely forgot about the meeting.\n(我完全忘了那場會議。)"],["complex","complex(adj./n.)複雜的、綜合大樓\ncomplexity(n.)複雜性\ncomplex problem 複雜的問題\nsports complex 綜合運動中心\nThis math problem is too complex for me.\n(這道數學題對我來說太複雜了。)\nThere is a new sports complex near my home.\n(我家附近有一座新的綜合運動中心。)"],["concern","concern(n./v.)關心、擔心、與⋯有關\nconcerned(adj.)擔心的、有關的\nbe concerned about 擔心⋯\nas far as I'm concerned 就我而言\nMy parents are concerned about my health.\n(我父母很擔心我的健康。)\nThank you for your concern.\n(謝謝你的關心。)"],["conclude","conclude(v.)下結論、結束\nconclusion(n.)結論\nconclude that 推斷出⋯\nin conclusion 總而言之\nThe police concluded that it was an accident.\n(警方斷定那是一場意外。)\nThe meeting concluded at five.\n(會議在五點結束。)"],["condition","condition(n./v.)情況、狀態、條件\nconditional(adj.)有條件的\nin good condition 狀況良好\non one condition 在一個條件下\nMy old bike is still in good condition.\n(我的舊腳踏車狀況還很好。)\nYou can go, on one condition.\n(你可以去，但有一個條件。)"],["confident","confident(adj.)有信心的、自信的\nconfidence(n.)信心、自信\nconfidently(adv.)有信心地\nbe confident of 對⋯有信心\nfeel confident 覺得有信心\nI am confident that we will win.\n(我有信心我們會贏。)\nShe looked confident on the stage.\n(她在台上看起來很有自信。)"],["conflict","conflict(n./v.)衝突、抵觸\n(無詞性變化)\nin conflict with 與⋯衝突\nconflict of interest 利益衝突\nThe two countries are in conflict.\n(這兩個國家處於衝突之中。)\nMy class schedule conflicts with my piano lesson.\n(我的課表和鋼琴課時間衝突。)"],["congratulation(s)","congratulation(n.)祝賀、congratulations(n.)恭喜\ncongratulate(v.)祝賀、恭喜\nCongratulations on ⋯ 恭喜⋯\nsend congratulations 致上祝賀\nCongratulations on your new job!\n(恭喜你找到新工作！)\nWe sent our congratulations to the happy couple.\n(我們向那對新人致上祝賀。)"],["connection","connection(n.)連接、關聯、人脈\nconnect(v.)連接\nInternet connection 網路連線\nin connection with 關於⋯\nThe Internet connection here is slow.\n(這裡的網路連線很慢。)\nThere is a connection between sleep and health.\n(睡眠和健康之間有關聯。)"],["consider","consider(v.)考慮、認為\nconsideration(n.)考慮、體貼\nconsiderate(adj.)體貼的\nconsider + V-ing 考慮做⋯\nbe considered (to be) 被認為是\nI am considering studying abroad.\n(我正在考慮出國念書。)\nHe is considered a great writer.\n(他被認為是一位偉大的作家。)"],["consideration","consideration(n.)考慮、體貼\nconsider(v.)考慮、認為\nconsiderate(adj.)體貼的\ntake into consideration 把⋯列入考慮\nunder consideration 考慮中\nWe should take the weather into consideration.\n(我們應該把天氣列入考慮。)\nYour plan is still under consideration.\n(你的計畫仍在考慮中。)"],["contact","contact(n./v.)聯絡、接觸\n(無詞性變化)\nkeep in contact with 和⋯保持聯絡\ncontact lenses 隱形眼鏡\nPlease contact me if you need help.\n(如果需要幫忙請和我聯絡。)\nI still keep in contact with my old classmates.\n(我仍和老同學保持聯絡。)"],["contain","contain(v.)包含、容納\ncontainer(n.)容器\ncontain sugar 含糖\ncontain information 包含資訊\nThis drink contains a lot of sugar.\n(這杯飲料含有很多糖。)\nThe box contains old photos.\n(這個盒子裡裝著舊照片。)"],["continue","continue(v.)繼續、持續\ncontinuous(adj.)連續不斷的\ncontinuation(n.)繼續\ncontinue to 繼續⋯\nto be continued 未完待續\nThe rain continued all day.\n(雨下了一整天。)\nLet's continue our lesson.\n(我們繼續上課吧。)"],["contract","contract(n./v.)合約、訂約、收縮、感染\ncontractor(n.)承包商\nsign a contract 簽合約\nbreak a contract 違約\nThe singer signed a contract with a big company.\n(那位歌手和一家大公司簽了合約。)\nMetal contracts when it gets cold.\n(金屬遇冷會收縮。)"],["control","control(n./v.)控制、管理\ncontroller(n.)控制器、管理者\nunder control 在控制之中\nlose control 失控\nEverything is under control.\n(一切都在掌控之中。)\nHe lost control of his car.\n(他的車失控了。)"],["conversation","conversation(n.)對話、會話\nconverse(v.)交談\nhave a conversation 談話\nEnglish conversation 英語會話\nI had a long conversation with my teacher.\n(我和老師進行了一場長談。)\nShe takes an English conversation class.\n(她上英語會話課。)"],["corn","corn(n.)玉米\n(無詞性變化)\ncorn soup 玉米濃湯\ngrilled corn 烤玉米\nI'd like a bowl of corn soup.\n(我想要一碗玉米濃湯。)\nWe bought grilled corn at the night market.\n(我們在夜市買了烤玉米。)"],["countryside","countryside(n.)鄉間、鄉下\n(無詞性變化)\nin the countryside 在鄉下\nbeautiful countryside 美麗的鄉間\nMy grandparents live in the countryside.\n(我的祖父母住在鄉下。)\nWe rode bikes through the countryside.\n(我們騎腳踏車穿過鄉間。)"],["couple","couple(n./v.)一對、夫妻、情侶、連結\n(無詞性變化)\na couple of 幾個、兩三個\nmarried couple 已婚夫妻\nI'll be back in a couple of days.\n(我過兩三天就回來。)\nThe young couple just bought a house.\n(那對年輕夫妻剛買了房子。)"],["courage","courage(n.)勇氣\ncourageous(adj.)勇敢的\nencourage(v.)鼓勵\nhave the courage to 有勇氣去⋯\nlose courage 失去勇氣\nIt takes courage to say sorry.\n(說對不起需要勇氣。)\nShe had the courage to speak up.\n(她有勇氣說出來。)"],["court","court(n.)法院、法庭、球場\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to court 上法院、打官司\nbasketball court 籃球場\nWe play on the basketball court after school.\n(我們放學後在籃球場打球。)\nThe case went to court.\n(這個案子鬧上了法院。)"],["cowboy","cowboy(n.)牛仔\n(無詞性變化)\ncowboy hat 牛仔帽\ncowboy boots 牛仔靴\nThe cowboy rode his horse across the field.\n(牛仔騎著馬穿越田野。)\nHe wore a cowboy hat to the party.\n(他戴著一頂牛仔帽去參加派對。)"],["crayon","crayon(n.)蠟筆\n(無詞性變化)\na box of crayons 一盒蠟筆\ndraw with crayons 用蠟筆畫畫\nThe kids drew pictures with crayons.\n(孩子們用蠟筆畫圖。)\nI bought her a box of crayons.\n(我買了一盒蠟筆給她。)"],["cream","cream(n./adj.)奶油、乳霜、米色的\ncreamy(adj.)含奶油的、滑順的\nice cream 冰淇淋\nface cream 面霜\nI'd like some cream in my coffee.\n(我的咖啡想加點奶精。)\nLet's get some ice cream!\n(我們去買冰淇淋吧！)"],["create","create(v.)創造、建立\ncreation(n.)創造、創作物\ncreative(adj.)有創意的\ncreate jobs 創造工作機會\ncreate a new account 建立新帳號\nThe artist created a beautiful painting.\n(這位藝術家創作了一幅美麗的畫。)\nYou need to create a password first.\n(你得先建立一組密碼。)"],["crime","crime(n.)罪、犯罪\ncriminal(n./adj.)罪犯、犯罪的\ncommit a crime 犯罪\ncrime rate 犯罪率\nStealing is a crime.\n(偷竊是一種犯罪。)\nThe crime rate in this city is low.\n(這座城市的犯罪率很低。)"],["crisis","crisis(n.)危機\n(無詞性變化)\neconomic crisis 經濟危機\nin crisis 處於危機中\nThe country faced an economic crisis.\n(這個國家面臨經濟危機。)\nStay calm in a crisis.\n(在危機中要保持冷靜。)"],["crow","crow(n./v.)烏鴉、(公雞)啼叫\n(無詞性變化)\nas the crow flies 直線距離\na black crow 黑色的烏鴉\nA crow is sitting on the roof.\n(一隻烏鴉停在屋頂上。)\nThe school is two kilometers away as the crow flies.\n(學校直線距離兩公里遠。)"],["crowd","crowd(n./v.)人群、群眾、擠滿\ncrowded(adj.)擁擠的\na crowd of 一群⋯\ncrowd into 擠進⋯\nA large crowd watched the parade.\n(一大群人觀看遊行。)\nThe MRT is crowded in the morning.\n(早上捷運很擁擠。)"],["cultural","cultural(adj.)文化的\nculture(n.)文化\ncultural difference 文化差異\ncultural heritage 文化遺產\nThere are many cultural differences between the two countries.\n(這兩個國家之間有很多文化差異。)\nThe old temple is an important cultural site.\n(這座古廟是重要的文化遺址。)"],["culture","culture(n.)文化\ncultural(adj.)文化的\npop culture 流行文化\nChinese culture 中華文化\nI want to learn about Japanese culture.\n(我想了解日本文化。)\nK-pop is part of pop culture today.\n(韓國流行音樂是現今流行文化的一部分。)"],["cure","cure(n./v.)治療、治癒、療法\ncurable(adj.)可治癒的\ncure for 治療⋯的方法\ncure a disease 治好疾病\nThere is no cure for the common cold.\n(普通感冒沒有藥可以根治。)\nThe doctor cured her quickly.\n(醫生很快就治好了她。)"],["curious","curious(adj.)好奇的\ncuriosity(n.)好奇心\ncuriously(adv.)好奇地\nbe curious about 對⋯好奇\ncurious child 好奇的孩子\nBabies are curious about everything.\n(嬰兒對一切都很好奇。)\nI'm curious to know the answer.\n(我很想知道答案。)"],["current","current(adj./n.)目前的、現行的、水流、電流\ncurrently(adv.)目前\ncurrent events 時事\nocean current 洋流\nWhat is your current address?\n(你目前的地址是什麼？)\nThe river has a strong current.\n(這條河的水流很強。)"],["curtain","curtain(n./v.)窗簾、布幕、裝上簾子\n(無詞性變化)\ndraw the curtains 拉上(或拉開)窗簾\nthe curtain falls 落幕\nPlease close the curtains.\n(請把窗簾拉上。)\nThe curtain rose and the show began.\n(幕升起，表演開始了。)"],["custom","custom(n.)習俗、風俗、(customs)海關\ncustomary(adj.)習慣上的、慣例的\nlocal custom 當地習俗\ngo through customs 通過海關\nIt is a custom to give red envelopes at New Year.\n(過年發紅包是一種習俗。)\nWe went through customs at the airport.\n(我們在機場通過海關。)"],["customer","customer(n.)顧客\n(無詞性變化)\ncustomer service 客服\nregular customer 常客\nThe store has many customers on weekends.\n(這家店週末有很多顧客。)\nPlease call customer service for help.\n(請打電話給客服尋求協助。)"],["cycle","cycle(n./v.)循環、週期、騎腳踏車\ncycling(n.)騎自行車運動\ncyclist(n.)騎自行車的人\nlife cycle 生命週期\nwater cycle 水循環\nWe learned about the water cycle in science class.\n(我們在自然課學到水循環。)\nThey cycled around the lake.\n(他們騎腳踏車環湖。)"],["daily","daily(adj./adv./n.)每日的、每天、日報\nday(n.)天、日\ndaily life 日常生活\ndaily newspaper 日報\nExercise is part of my daily life.\n(運動是我日常生活的一部分。)\nThe store is open daily from nine to ten.\n(這家店每天從九點營業到十點。)"],["damage","damage(n./v.)損害、損壞、毀損\ndamaged(adj.)受損的\ncause damage 造成損害\nbrain damage 腦部損傷\nThe typhoon caused serious damage to the farms.\n(颱風對農田造成嚴重損害。)\nToo much sun can damage your skin.\n(過度曬太陽會傷害你的皮膚。)"],["dancer","dancer(n.)舞者\ndance(n./v.)舞蹈、跳舞\nballet dancer 芭蕾舞者\ngood dancer 很會跳舞的人\nShe wants to become a ballet dancer.\n(她想成為一名芭蕾舞者。)\nMy brother is a really good dancer.\n(我哥哥真的很會跳舞。)"],["danger","danger(n.)危險、威脅\ndangerous(adj.)危險的\nendanger(v.)危及\nin danger 處於危險中\nout of danger 脫離險境\nMany wild animals are in danger.\n(許多野生動物正處於危險之中。)\nThe doctor said he is out of danger now.\n(醫生說他現在已經脫離險境了。)"],["data","data(n.)資料、數據\n(無詞性變化)\ncollect data 收集資料\ndata analysis 數據分析\nWe need more data for the report.\n(我們需要更多資料來寫報告。)\nThe scientists collected data for two years.\n(科學家們收集了兩年的數據。)"],["deaf","deaf(adj.)聾的、充耳不聞的\ndeafness(n.)耳聾\ndeafen(v.)使聾、震耳欲聾\ngo deaf 變聾\nturn a deaf ear to 對……充耳不聞\nThe old man is a little deaf.\n(那位老先生有點重聽。)\nHe turned a deaf ear to my advice.\n(他對我的建議充耳不聞。)"],["debate","debate(n./v.)辯論、討論\ndebater(n.)辯論者\ndebate team 辯論隊\nheated debate 激烈的辯論\nOur class held a debate about school uniforms.\n(我們班舉辦了一場關於制服的辯論。)\nThey debated the plan for hours.\n(他們針對這個計畫辯論了好幾個小時。)"],["debt","debt(n.)債務、欠款\ndebtor(n.)債務人\nin debt 負債\npay off a debt 還清債務\nHe worked hard to pay off his debt.\n(他努力工作以還清債務。)\nMany students are in debt after college.\n(許多學生大學畢業後背負債務。)"],["decision","decision(n.)決定、決心\ndecide(v.)決定\ndecisive(adj.)果斷的、決定性的\nmake a decision 做決定\nfinal decision 最後的決定\nIt was a hard decision to make.\n(那是一個很難做的決定。)\nYou need to make a decision now.\n(你現在必須做出決定。)"],["deer","deer(n.)鹿(單複數同形)\n(無詞性變化)\na herd of deer 一群鹿\nsika deer 梅花鹿\nWe saw two deer in the forest.\n(我們在森林裡看到兩隻鹿。)\nThe deer ran away when it heard us.\n(那隻鹿聽到我們的聲音就跑走了。)"],["degree","degree(n.)度數、程度、學位\n(無詞性變化)\nto some degree 在某種程度上\nbachelor's degree 學士學位\nIt is 35 degrees today.\n(今天氣溫三十五度。)\nShe has a degree in English.\n(她擁有英文學位。)"],["delay","delay(n./v.)延誤、延期、耽擱\ndelayed(adj.)延誤的\nwithout delay 立刻、毫不延遲\nflight delay 班機延誤\nOur flight was delayed because of the storm.\n(我們的班機因為暴風雨而延誤。)\nPlease reply without delay.\n(請立即回覆。)"],["delicious","delicious(adj.)美味的、好吃的\n(無詞性變化)\ndelicious food 美食\nsmell delicious 聞起來很香\nThe beef noodles are delicious.\n(這碗牛肉麵很好吃。)\nSomething smells delicious in the kitchen.\n(廚房裡有東西聞起來好香。)"],["deliver","deliver(v.)遞送、運送、發表(演說)\ndelivery(n.)遞送\ndeliverer(n.)遞送者\ndeliver a package 送包裹\ndeliver a speech 發表演說\nThe mailman delivers letters every day.\n(郵差每天送信。)\nThe principal delivered a speech on stage.\n(校長在台上發表了演說。)"],["delivery","delivery(n.)遞送、投遞、分娩\ndeliver(v.)遞送\nhome delivery 宅配、送貨到府\nfree delivery 免運費\nThe store offers free delivery.\n(這家店提供免運費。)\nWe ordered pizza for home delivery.\n(我們訂了外送披薩。)"],["dentist","dentist(n.)牙醫\ndental(adj.)牙齒的\ngo to the dentist 去看牙醫\ndentist appointment 牙醫預約\nI go to the dentist twice a year.\n(我一年看兩次牙醫。)\nI have a dentist appointment this afternoon.\n(我今天下午有牙醫預約。)"],["deny","deny(v.)否認、拒絕給予\ndenial(n.)否認\ndeny the fact 否認事實\ndeny doing 否認做了某事\nHe denied breaking the window.\n(他否認打破了窗戶。)\nNo one can deny that she works hard.\n(沒有人能否認她很努力。)"],["department","department(n.)部門、科系\ndepartmental(adj.)部門的\ndepartment store 百貨公司\nsales department 業務部\nWe went shopping at the department store.\n(我們去百貨公司購物。)\nMy mother works in the sales department.\n(我媽媽在業務部工作。)"],["depend","depend(v.)依賴、取決於\ndependent(adj.)依賴的\ndependence(n.)依賴\ndepend on 依靠、取決於\nIt depends. 看情況。\nYou can always depend on me.\n(你永遠可以依靠我。)\nOur plan depends on the weather.\n(我們的計畫取決於天氣。)"],["depth","depth(n.)深度、深處\ndeep(adj.)深的\nin depth 深入地、徹底地\nthe depth of the sea 海的深度\nThe pool has a depth of two meters.\n(這個游泳池深兩公尺。)\nWe discussed the problem in depth.\n(我們深入討論了這個問題。)"],["describe","describe(v.)描述、形容\ndescription(n.)描述\ndescriptive(adj.)描述性的\ndescribe in detail 詳細描述\ndescribe oneself 描述自己\nCan you describe the man you saw?\n(你能描述你看到的那個男人嗎？)\nWords cannot describe how happy I am.\n(言語無法形容我有多開心。)"],["description","description(n.)描述、說明\ndescribe(v.)描述\njob description 工作說明\ndetailed description 詳細的描述\nThe police asked for a description of the thief.\n(警方要求描述小偷的長相。)\nRead the job description carefully.\n(仔細閱讀工作說明。)"],["desert","desert(n./v.)沙漠、拋棄、離棄\ndeserted(adj.)荒蕪的、無人的\ndesert island 荒島\nthe Sahara Desert 撒哈拉沙漠\nCamels can live in the desert.\n(駱駝能在沙漠中生存。)\nHe would never desert his friends.\n(他絕不會拋棄他的朋友。)"],["design","design(n./v.)設計、圖案、設計\ndesigner(n.)設計師\ngraphic design 平面設計\ndesign a website 設計網站\nI love the design of this dress.\n(我很喜歡這件洋裝的設計。)\nShe designed the poster for our club.\n(她為我們社團設計了海報。)"],["detail","detail(n./v.)細節、詳述\ndetailed(adj.)詳細的\nin detail 詳細地\npay attention to details 注意細節\nTell me the story in detail.\n(把那件事詳細地告訴我。)\nShe always pays attention to small details.\n(她總是注意小細節。)"],["develop(ment)","develop(v.)發展、培養、研發、development(n.)發展\ndeveloped(adj.)已開發的\ndeveloping(adj.)開發中的\ndevelop a habit 養成習慣\neconomic development 經濟發展\nReading can help you develop good habits.\n(閱讀能幫助你養成好習慣。)\nThe city has seen fast development in recent years.\n(這座城市近年來發展迅速。)"],["dial","dial(n./v.)錶盤、撥號\n(無詞性變化)\ndial a number 撥號碼\ndial tone 撥號音\nDial 119 if there is a fire.\n(如果發生火災，請撥打119。)\nThe dial of my watch is blue.\n(我的手錶錶盤是藍色的。)"],["dialogue","dialogue(n.)對話、對白\n(無詞性變化)\npractice a dialogue 練習對話\nopen dialogue 公開對話\nLet's practice the dialogue in pairs.\n(我們兩人一組練習這段對話。)\nThe dialogue in this movie is funny.\n(這部電影的對白很好笑。)"],["diamond","diamond(n.)鑽石、菱形\n(無詞性變化)\ndiamond ring 鑽戒\ndiamond shape 菱形\nHe gave her a diamond ring.\n(他送給她一枚鑽戒。)\nDiamonds are very hard and expensive.\n(鑽石非常堅硬又昂貴。)"],["diary","diary(n.)日記、日記本\n(無詞性變化)\nkeep a diary 寫日記\ndiary entry 一則日記\nI keep a diary in English.\n(我用英文寫日記。)\nShe wrote about her trip in her diary.\n(她在日記裡寫下了她的旅行。)"],["diet","diet(n./v.)飲食、節食\ndietary(adj.)飲食的\non a diet 節食中\nbalanced diet 均衡飲食\nA balanced diet keeps you healthy.\n(均衡飲食讓你保持健康。)\nNo cake for me. I'm on a diet.\n(我不吃蛋糕，我在節食。)"],["difference","difference(n.)差異、不同、差額\ndifferent(adj.)不同的\ndiffer(v.)不同\nmake a difference 有影響、有差別\ntime difference 時差\nCan you tell the difference between them?\n(你能分辨它們的差別嗎？)\nYour help made a big difference.\n(你的幫忙起了很大的作用。)"],["difficulty","difficulty(n.)困難、難題\ndifficult(adj.)困難的\nhave difficulty (in) doing 做某事有困難\nwithout difficulty 毫不費力地\nI have difficulty remembering names.\n(我很難記住別人的名字。)\nShe passed the test without difficulty.\n(她毫不費力地通過了考試。)"],["direct","direct(adj./v./adv.)直接的、指引、直接地\ndirection(n.)方向\ndirectly(adv.)直接地\ndirect flight 直飛班機\ndirect contact 直接接觸\nIs there a direct flight to Paris?\n(有直飛巴黎的班機嗎？)\nCan you direct me to the station?\n(你能告訴我去車站怎麼走嗎？)"],["direction","direction(n.)方向、指示、指導\ndirect(v.)指引\nin the direction of 朝……方向\nask for directions 問路\nWe walked in the wrong direction.\n(我們走錯方向了。)\nLet's stop and ask for directions.\n(我們停下來問路吧。)"],["director","director(n.)導演、主任、董事\ndirect(v.)導演、指導\nmovie director 電影導演\ndirector of the department 部門主任\nAng Lee is a famous movie director.\n(李安是一位有名的電影導演。)\nThe director of the museum gave a short talk.\n(博物館館長做了簡短的演講。)"],["disagree(ment)","disagree(v.)不同意、意見不合、disagreement(n.)意見不合\nagree(v.)同意\ndisagree with 不同意某人\nstrong disagreement 強烈的反對\nI disagree with you on this point.\n(在這一點上我不同意你的看法。)\nThey had a disagreement about money.\n(他們在金錢方面意見不合。)"],["disappear","disappear(v.)消失、不見\ndisappearance(n.)消失\nappear(v.)出現\ndisappear from view 從視線中消失\nsuddenly disappear 突然消失\nThe sun disappeared behind the clouds.\n(太陽消失在雲層後面。)\nMy cat disappeared for two days.\n(我的貓不見了兩天。)"],["discover","discover(v.)發現、發覺\ndiscovery(n.)發現\ndiscoverer(n.)發現者\ndiscover the truth 發現真相\ndiscover a new species 發現新物種\nScientists discovered a new kind of frog.\n(科學家發現了一種新的青蛙。)\nI discovered a nice café near school.\n(我在學校附近發現一家不錯的咖啡店。)"],["discovery","discovery(n.)發現、被發現的事物\ndiscover(v.)發現\nmake a discovery 有所發現\nscientific discovery 科學發現\nThe discovery of fire changed human life.\n(火的發現改變了人類的生活。)\nShe made an important discovery in the lab.\n(她在實驗室裡有了重要發現。)"],["discuss","discuss(v.)討論、商討\ndiscussion(n.)討論\ndiscuss a problem 討論問題\ndiscuss with 與……討論\nLet's discuss the plan after class.\n(我們下課後討論這個計畫吧。)\nI need to discuss this with my parents.\n(我需要和我爸媽討論這件事。)"],["discussion","discussion(n.)討論、商討\ndiscuss(v.)討論\ngroup discussion 小組討論\nunder discussion 討論中\nWe had a group discussion in class.\n(我們在課堂上進行了小組討論。)\nThe new rule is still under discussion.\n(新規定仍在討論中。)"],["disease","disease(n.)疾病\n(無詞性變化)\nheart disease 心臟病\ncatch a disease 染病\nWashing hands can prevent disease.\n(洗手可以預防疾病。)\nHeart disease is a serious health problem.\n(心臟病是一個嚴重的健康問題。)"],["display","display(n./v.)展示、陳列、顯示\n(無詞性變化)\non display 展示中\ndisplay screen 顯示螢幕\nThe paintings are on display at the museum.\n(這些畫作正在博物館展出。)\nThe store displays new shoes in the window.\n(這家店在櫥窗裡陳列新鞋。)"],["distance","distance(n.)距離、遠處\ndistant(adj.)遙遠的\nin the distance 在遠處\nlong distance 長距離\nWe saw a mountain in the distance.\n(我們看到遠處有一座山。)\nThe school is within walking distance.\n(學校在步行可到的距離內。)"],["distant","distant(adj.)遙遠的、疏遠的\ndistance(n.)距離\ndistant future 遙遠的未來\ndistant relative 遠親\nHe is a distant relative of mine.\n(他是我的遠房親戚。)\nWe heard distant thunder.\n(我們聽到遠方的雷聲。)"],["divide","divide(v./n.)分開、劃分、除、分歧\ndivision(n.)分割、除法、部門\ndivide into 分成\ndivided by 除以\nThe teacher divided us into four groups.\n(老師把我們分成四組。)\nTen divided by two is five.\n(十除以二等於五。)"],["division","division(n.)分割、除法、部門\ndivide(v.)分開、除\nlong division 長除法\ndivision of labor 分工\nWe learned division in math class.\n(我們在數學課學了除法。)\nHe works in the sales division.\n(他在業務部門工作。)"],["domestic","domestic(adj.)國內的、家庭的、馴養的\n(無詞性變化)\ndomestic flight 國內班機\ndomestic animal 家畜\nWe took a domestic flight to Kinmen.\n(我們搭國內班機去金門。)\nCows and pigs are domestic animals.\n(牛和豬是家畜。)"],["dot","dot(n./v.)點、圓點、點綴\ndotted(adj.)有點的、虛線的\npolka dots 圓點花紋\ndotted line 虛線\nShe wore a dress with white dots.\n(她穿著一件白色圓點洋裝。)\nSign your name on the dotted line.\n(請在虛線上簽名。)"],["double","double(adj./v./n./adv.)兩倍的、雙人的、加倍\n(無詞性變化)\ndouble room 雙人房\ndouble the price 價格翻倍\nWe booked a double room at the hotel.\n(我們在飯店訂了一間雙人房。)\nThe price of eggs has doubled.\n(雞蛋的價格漲了一倍。)"],["doubt","doubt(n./v.)懷疑、疑慮\ndoubtful(adj.)懷疑的、不確定的\nno doubt 無疑地\nwithout a doubt 毫無疑問\nThere is no doubt that he is right.\n(毫無疑問他是對的。)\nI doubt that he will come today.\n(我懷疑他今天會來。)"],["dove","dove(n.)鴿子\n(無詞性變化)\nwhite dove 白鴿\ndove of peace 和平鴿\nThe white dove is a symbol of peace.\n(白鴿是和平的象徵。)\nA dove landed on the roof.\n(一隻鴿子停在屋頂上。)"],["download","download(v.)下載\nupload(v.)上傳\ndownload an app 下載應用程式\nfree download 免費下載\nYou can download the app for free.\n(你可以免費下載這個應用程式。)\nIt took ten minutes to download the file.\n(下載這個檔案花了十分鐘。)"],["downstairs","downstairs(adv./n./adj.)在樓下、往樓下、樓下\nupstairs(adv.)在樓上\ngo downstairs 下樓\ndownstairs neighbor 樓下鄰居\nDinner is ready. Come downstairs!\n(晚餐好了，快下樓來！)\nOur downstairs neighbor has a cute dog.\n(我們樓下的鄰居養了一隻可愛的狗。)"],["dragon","dragon(n.)龍\n(無詞性變化)\nDragon Boat Festival 端午節\ndragon dance 舞龍\nWe eat rice dumplings on the Dragon Boat Festival.\n(我們在端午節吃粽子。)\nThe dragon in the story can breathe fire.\n(故事裡的龍會噴火。)"],["drama","drama(n.)戲劇、戲劇性事件\ndramatic(adj.)戲劇性的、劇烈的\ndrama club 戲劇社\nTV drama 電視劇\nShe joined the drama club this year.\n(她今年加入了戲劇社。)\nMy mom watches Korean dramas every night.\n(我媽媽每晚都看韓劇。)"],["drawer","drawer(n.)抽屜\ndraw(v.)拉、畫\ntop drawer 最上層抽屜\nopen a drawer 打開抽屜\nThe keys are in the top drawer.\n(鑰匙在最上層的抽屜裡。)\nShe put the letters in a drawer.\n(她把信放進抽屜裡。)"],["drawing","drawing(n.)圖畫、素描、繪畫\ndraw(v.)畫\nmake a drawing 畫一幅畫\npencil drawing 鉛筆素描\nYour drawing of the cat is great.\n(你畫的貓真棒。)\nHe is good at drawing.\n(他很擅長畫畫。)"],["drug","drug(n./v.)藥、毒品、下藥\ndruggist(n.)藥劑師\ntake drugs 吸毒、服藥\ndrug store 藥局\nNever take drugs from strangers.\n(絕對不要拿陌生人給的藥物。)\nThis new drug can treat the flu.\n(這種新藥可以治療流感。)"],["dryer","dryer(n.)烘乾機、吹風機\ndry(adj./v.)乾的、弄乾\nhair dryer 吹風機\nclothes dryer 乾衣機\nCan I use your hair dryer?\n(我可以用你的吹風機嗎？)\nPut the wet clothes in the dryer.\n(把濕衣服放進烘乾機。)"],["due","due(adj./adv./n.)到期的、預定的、應得之物\n(無詞性變化)\ndue to 由於、因為\ndue date 截止日、預產期\nThe report is due next Monday.\n(報告下週一截止。)\nThe game was canceled due to rain.\n(比賽因雨取消了。)"],["dull","dull(adj./v.)無聊的、遲鈍的、鈍的、使變鈍\ndullness(n.)無趣、遲鈍\ndull knife 鈍刀\ndull life 乏味的生活\nThe movie was so dull that I fell asleep.\n(這部電影無聊到我睡著了。)\nThis knife is too dull to cut meat.\n(這把刀太鈍了，切不動肉。)"],["duty","duty(n.)責任、義務、職務、稅\n(無詞性變化)\non duty 值班\nduty-free 免稅的\nIt is our duty to protect the earth.\n(保護地球是我們的責任。)\nWho is on duty today?\n(今天誰值日？)"],["eagle","eagle(n.)老鷹\n(無詞性變化)\nbald eagle 白頭鷹\neagle eye 銳利的眼光\nAn eagle flew high above the mountain.\n(一隻老鷹在山的上空高飛。)\nThe bald eagle is a symbol of the United States.\n(白頭鷹是美國的象徵。)"],["earn","earn(v.)賺取、贏得\nearnings(n.)收入、所得\nearn money 賺錢\nearn a living 謀生\nShe earns money by teaching piano.\n(她靠教鋼琴賺錢。)\nHe earned the respect of his classmates.\n(他贏得了同學們的尊敬。)"],["earring(s)","earring(n.)耳環、earrings(n.)一對耳環\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of earrings 一對耳環\ngold earrings 金耳環\nShe wore a pair of silver earrings.\n(她戴了一對銀耳環。)\nI lost one of my earrings at the party.\n(我在派對上弄丟了一隻耳環。)"],["earthquake","earthquake(n.)地震\n(無詞性變化)\nstrong earthquake 強烈地震\nearthquake drill 地震演習\nTaiwan has many earthquakes every year.\n(台灣每年都有許多地震。)\nOur school held an earthquake drill today.\n(我們學校今天舉行了地震演習。)"],["ease","ease(n./v.)容易、舒適、減輕\neasy(adj.)容易的\neasily(adv.)容易地\nwith ease 輕鬆地\nat ease 自在、放鬆\nShe passed the test with ease.\n(她輕鬆地通過了考試。)\nThis medicine will ease the pain.\n(這種藥可以減輕疼痛。)"],["eastern","eastern(adj.)東方的、東部的\neast(n.)東方\neastern Taiwan 東台灣\nEastern culture 東方文化\nHualien is a city in eastern Taiwan.\n(花蓮是東台灣的一個城市。)\nHe is interested in Eastern culture.\n(他對東方文化很有興趣。)"],["edge","edge(n./v.)邊緣、優勢、側身移動\nedgy(adj.)緊張不安的\non the edge of 在…的邊緣\nhave an edge over 比…佔優勢\nDon't stand too close to the edge of the cliff.\n(不要站得離懸崖邊緣太近。)\nHer English skills give her an edge over others.\n(她的英文能力讓她比別人更有優勢。)"],["edition","edition(n.)版本、版次\nedit(v.)編輯\neditor(n.)編輯\nfirst edition 初版\nlimited edition 限量版\nThis is the first edition of the book.\n(這是這本書的初版。)\nHe bought a limited edition of the sneakers.\n(他買了一雙限量版的運動鞋。)"],["education","education(n.)教育\neducate(v.)教育\neducational(adj.)教育的\nhigher education 高等教育\nreceive an education 接受教育\nEducation is the key to a better future.\n(教育是通往更好未來的關鍵。)\nEvery child should receive a good education.\n(每個孩子都應該受到良好的教育。)"],["effect","effect(n./v.)影響、效果、產生\neffective(adj.)有效的\nhave an effect on 對…有影響\nside effect 副作用\nMusic has a strong effect on our mood.\n(音樂對我們的心情有很大的影響。)\nThis medicine has no side effects.\n(這種藥沒有副作用。)"],["effective","effective(adj.)有效的、生效的\neffect(n.)效果\neffectively(adv.)有效地\neffective way 有效的方法\nhighly effective 非常有效\nExercise is an effective way to lose weight.\n(運動是減重的有效方法。)\nThe new rule becomes effective next month.\n(新規定下個月生效。)"],["effort","effort(n.)努力、費力\neffortless(adj.)不費力的\nmake an effort 努力\na waste of effort 白費力氣\nShe made a great effort to win the race.\n(她為了贏得比賽付出極大的努力。)\nLearning English takes time and effort.\n(學英文需要時間和努力。)"],["elder","elder(n./adj.)長輩、年長的\nelderly(adj.)年長的\nelder brother 哥哥\nrespect your elders 尊敬長輩\nMy elder sister studies in Taichung.\n(我姊姊在台中讀書。)\nWe should respect our elders.\n(我們應該尊敬長輩。)"],["electric","electric(adj.)電的、電動的\nelectricity(n.)電、電力\nelectric car 電動車\nelectric fan 電風扇\nMore people are driving electric cars now.\n(現在越來越多人開電動車。)\nPlease turn off the electric fan.\n(請把電風扇關掉。)"],["electrical","electrical(adj.)電的、與電有關的\nelectrician(n.)電工\nelectrical engineer 電機工程師\nelectrical problem 電路問題\nMy uncle is an electrical engineer.\n(我叔叔是一名電機工程師。)\nThe fire was caused by an electrical problem.\n(那場火災是電路問題引起的。)"],["emotion","emotion(n.)情緒、情感\nemotional(adj.)情緒的、激動的\nshow emotion 表露情感\ncontrol one's emotions 控制情緒\nHe tried hard to control his emotions.\n(他努力控制自己的情緒。)\nHer voice was full of emotion.\n(她的聲音充滿了情感。)"],["emphasize","emphasize(v.)強調\nemphasis(n.)強調、重點\nemphasize the importance 強調重要性\nstrongly emphasize 特別強調\nThe teacher emphasized the importance of reading.\n(老師強調閱讀的重要性。)\nOur coach always emphasizes teamwork.\n(我們教練總是強調團隊合作。)"],["employ(ment)","employ(v.)雇用、使用、employment(n.)雇用、就業\nemployee(n.)員工\nemployer(n.)雇主\nemploy workers 雇用員工\nfull-time employment 全職工作\nThe factory employs over 500 workers.\n(這家工廠雇用了五百多名員工。)\nIt is hard to find employment in this area.\n(在這個地區很難找到工作。)"],["employee","employee(n.)員工、受雇者\nemploy(v.)雇用\nemployer(n.)雇主\nfull-time employee 全職員工\nnew employee 新進員工\nThe company has about 200 employees.\n(這家公司大約有兩百名員工。)\nThe new employee started work on Monday.\n(新進員工星期一開始上班。)"],["employer","employer(n.)雇主、老闆\nemploy(v.)雇用\nemployee(n.)員工\ngood employer 好雇主\nformer employer 前雇主\nMy employer gave me a day off.\n(我的老闆給了我一天假。)\nShe asked her former employer for a letter.\n(她請前雇主幫她寫一封推薦信。)"],["empty","empty(adj./v.)空的、倒空\nemptiness(n.)空虛\nempty bottle 空瓶\nempty the trash 倒垃圾\nThe classroom was empty after school.\n(放學後教室空無一人。)\nCould you empty the trash can?\n(你可以把垃圾桶倒乾淨嗎？)"],["encourage(ment)","encourage(v.)鼓勵、encouragement(n.)鼓勵\nencouraging(adj.)令人鼓舞的\nencourage sb. to 鼓勵某人去\nwords of encouragement 鼓勵的話\nMy teacher encouraged me to join the contest.\n(老師鼓勵我參加比賽。)\nThank you for your encouragement.\n(謝謝你的鼓勵。)"],["ending","ending(n.)結局、結尾\nend(n./v.)結束\nhappy ending 快樂的結局\nsurprise ending 出人意料的結局\nI like movies with happy endings.\n(我喜歡有快樂結局的電影。)\nThe story has a surprise ending.\n(這個故事有一個出人意料的結局。)"],["enemy","enemy(n.)敵人\n(無詞性變化)\nmake enemies 樹敵\nnatural enemy 天敵\nCats are natural enemies of mice.\n(貓是老鼠的天敵。)\nHe is kind and has no enemies.\n(他很和善，沒有任何敵人。)"],["energy","energy(n.)精力、能源、能量\nenergetic(adj.)精力充沛的\nfull of energy 充滿活力\nsolar energy 太陽能\nThe kids are full of energy.\n(孩子們精力充沛。)\nSolar energy is clean and safe.\n(太陽能乾淨又安全。)"],["engine","engine(n.)引擎、發動機\nengineer(n.)工程師\nstart the engine 發動引擎\nsearch engine 搜尋引擎\nHe started the engine and drove away.\n(他發動引擎後開車離去。)\nGoogle is a popular search engine.\n(Google 是一個很受歡迎的搜尋引擎。)"],["entire","entire(adj.)全部的、整個的\nentirely(adv.)完全地\nthe entire class 全班\nentire day 一整天\nThe entire class passed the test.\n(全班都通過了考試。)\nI spent the entire day at home.\n(我一整天都待在家。)"],["entrance","entrance(n.)入口、進入、入學\nenter(v.)進入\nmain entrance 正門\nentrance exam 入學考試\nLet's meet at the main entrance.\n(我們在正門碰面吧。)\nShe is preparing for the entrance exam.\n(她正在準備入學考試。)"],["environment","environment(n.)環境\nenvironmental(adj.)環境的\nprotect the environment 保護環境\nlearning environment 學習環境\nWe should protect the environment.\n(我們應該保護環境。)\nThe school offers a good learning environment.\n(這所學校提供良好的學習環境。)"],["environmental","environmental(adj.)環境的\nenvironment(n.)環境\nenvironmentally(adv.)環境上\nenvironmental protection 環境保護\nenvironmental problem 環境問題\nAir pollution is a serious environmental problem.\n(空氣汙染是嚴重的環境問題。)\nShe works for an environmental group.\n(她在一個環保團體工作。)"],["equal","equal(adj./v./n.)相等的、平等的、等於、同等的人\nequality(n.)平等\nequally(adv.)平等地\nequal rights 平等權利\nbe equal to 等於\nTwo plus three equals five.\n(二加三等於五。)\nMen and women should have equal rights.\n(男女應享有平等的權利。)"],["escape","escape(v./n.)逃脫、逃避、逃跑\n(無詞性變化)\nescape from 從…逃出\nnarrow escape 九死一生\nThe bird escaped from its cage.\n(那隻鳥從籠子裡逃了出來。)\nThey had a narrow escape in the fire.\n(他們在火災中死裡逃生。)"],["especially","especially(adv.)特別、尤其\nespecial(adj.)特別的\nespecially for 特別為了\nespecially when 尤其是當\nI love fruit, especially mangoes.\n(我愛水果，尤其是芒果。)\nThis gift is especially for you.\n(這份禮物是特別為你準備的。)"],["essay","essay(n.)論說文、散文、短文\nessayist(n.)散文家\nwrite an essay 寫文章\nessay question 申論題\nWe have to write an essay about our hometown.\n(我們必須寫一篇關於家鄉的文章。)\nThe essay question was the hardest part.\n(申論題是最難的部分。)"],["eve","eve(n.)前夕、前一天\n(無詞性變化)\nChristmas Eve 聖誕夜\nNew Year's Eve 跨年夜\nWe had a big dinner on Christmas Eve.\n(我們在聖誕夜吃了一頓大餐。)\nWhere will you spend New Year's Eve?\n(你要在哪裡跨年？)"],["event","event(n.)事件、活動、比賽項目\neventful(adj.)多事的\nsports event 運動賽事\nschool event 學校活動\nThe school sports event is next Friday.\n(學校運動會在下週五舉行。)\nHer wedding was a big event in the village.\n(她的婚禮是村裡的一件大事。)"],["evil","evil(n./adj.)邪惡、罪惡、邪惡的\n(無詞性變化)\ngood and evil 善與惡\nevil spirit 惡靈\nThe story is about good and evil.\n(這個故事是關於善與惡的。)\nThe evil witch wanted to hurt the princess.\n(邪惡的巫婆想要傷害公主。)"],["exact","exact(adj.)確切的、精確的\nexactly(adv.)確切地、正是\nexact time 確切的時間\nexact same 完全相同的\nWhat is the exact time now?\n(現在確切的時間是幾點？)\nWe wore the exact same shirt today.\n(我們今天穿了一模一樣的上衣。)"],["examination/exam","examination(n.)考試、檢查\nexam(n.)考試(口語)\nexamine(v.)檢查、測驗\nfinal exam 期末考\nmedical examination 健康檢查\nI have to study for the final exam.\n(我得為期末考讀書。)\nAll new students need a medical examination.\n(所有新生都需要做健康檢查。)"],["examine","examine(v.)檢查、審查、測驗\nexamination(n.)檢查、考試\nexaminer(n.)主考官\nexamine carefully 仔細檢查\nexamine a patient 為病人看診\nThe doctor examined my throat.\n(醫生檢查了我的喉嚨。)\nPlease examine the report carefully.\n(請仔細檢查這份報告。)"],["excite(ment)","excite(v.)使興奮、excitement(n.)興奮、刺激\nexcited(adj.)興奮的\nexciting(adj.)令人興奮的\nget excited 變得興奮\nin excitement 興奮地\nThe kids got excited about the trip.\n(孩子們對這次旅行感到很興奮。)\nShe jumped up and down in excitement.\n(她興奮地跳上跳下。)"],["excuse","excuse(v./n.)原諒、藉口\n(無詞性變化)\nexcuse me 對不起、打擾一下\nmake an excuse 找藉口\nExcuse me, where is the library?\n(打擾一下，請問圖書館在哪裡？)\nStop making excuses for being late.\n(別再為遲到找藉口了。)"],["exist","exist(v.)存在、生存\nexistence(n.)存在\nexisting(adj.)現有的\nstill exist 仍然存在\ncannot exist without 沒有…就無法生存\nDo you think ghosts really exist?\n(你覺得鬼真的存在嗎？)\nFish cannot exist without water.\n(魚沒有水就無法生存。)"],["existence","existence(n.)存在、生存\nexist(v.)存在\ncome into existence 開始存在、產生\nthe existence of 存在著…\nScientists question the existence of life on Mars.\n(科學家質疑火星上是否有生命存在。)\nThe company came into existence in 1990.\n(這家公司成立於 1990 年。)"],["exit","exit(n./v.)出口、離開\n(無詞性變化)\nemergency exit 緊急出口\nexit the room 離開房間\nPlease use the emergency exit in a fire.\n(火災時請走緊急出口。)\nHe quietly exited the room.\n(他悄悄地離開了房間。)"],["expense","expense(n.)費用、支出\nexpensive(adj.)昂貴的\nliving expenses 生活費\nat the expense of 以…為代價\nMy living expenses are high in Taipei.\n(我在台北的生活費很高。)\nHe worked hard at the expense of his health.\n(他犧牲健康拼命工作。)"],["expert","expert(n./adj.)專家、熟練的\nexpertise(n.)專業知識\nexpert in 在…方面的專家\nexpert advice 專家建議\nShe is an expert in computer science.\n(她是電腦科學的專家。)\nYou should ask for expert advice.\n(你應該尋求專家的建議。)"],["express","express(v./adj./adv./n.)表達、快速的、以快遞、快車\nexpression(n.)表達、表情\nexpressive(adj.)富表現力的\nexpress oneself 表達自己\nexpress train 快車\nIt's hard for me to express my feelings.\n(要表達我的感受對我來說很難。)\nWe took the express train to Kaohsiung.\n(我們搭快車去高雄。)"],["expression","expression(n.)表達、表情、措辭\nexpress(v.)表達\nfacial expression 臉部表情\nfreedom of expression 言論自由\nHer facial expression showed she was angry.\n(她的臉部表情顯示她很生氣。)\nLearn this expression and use it often.\n(學會這個說法並且常常使用它。)"],["extra","extra(adj./adv./n.)額外的、特別地、額外的東西\n(無詞性變化)\nextra money 額外的錢\nextra charge 額外收費\nCan I have an extra blanket?\n(我可以多要一條毯子嗎？)\nThere is no extra charge for drinks.\n(飲料不另外收費。)"],["eyebrow/brow","eyebrow(n.)眉毛\nbrow(n.)眉毛、額頭\nraise an eyebrow 揚起眉毛(表示驚訝)\nthick eyebrows 濃眉\nHe has thick black eyebrows.\n(他有濃黑的眉毛。)\nShe raised an eyebrow when she heard the news.\n(她聽到這個消息時揚起了眉毛。)"],["factor","factor(n.)因素、要素\n(無詞性變化)\nkey factor 關鍵因素\nimportant factor 重要因素\nHard work is a key factor in success.\n(努力是成功的關鍵因素。)\nPrice is an important factor when shopping.\n(購物時價格是一個重要因素。)"],["failure","failure(n.)失敗、失敗者、故障\nfail(v.)失敗\nend in failure 以失敗告終\npower failure 停電\nFailure is the mother of success.\n(失敗為成功之母。)\nThe plan ended in failure.\n(這個計畫以失敗告終。)"],["fair","fair(adj./n./adv.)公平的、晴朗的、博覽會、公平地\nfairly(adv.)相當、公平地\nfairness(n.)公平\nfair play 公平競爭\nbook fair 書展\nThat's not fair to the other players.\n(那樣對其他選手不公平。)\nWe went to the book fair last weekend.\n(我們上週末去了書展。)"],["false","false(adj.)錯誤的、假的\nfalsely(adv.)錯誤地\ntrue or false 是非題\nfalse teeth 假牙\nIs this sentence true or false?\n(這個句子是對還是錯？)\nHe gave the police false information.\n(他給警方提供了錯誤的資訊。)"],["fashion","fashion(n./v.)時尚、流行、方式、塑造\nfashionable(adj.)流行的、時髦的\nin fashion 流行\nfashion show 時裝秀\nShort hair is in fashion this year.\n(今年流行短髮。)\nShe wants to be a fashion designer.\n(她想成為服裝設計師。)"],["fate","fate(n.)命運\nfatal(adj.)致命的\nby fate 命中注定\naccept one's fate 接受命運\nIt was fate that we met again.\n(我們再次相遇是命中注定。)\nHe refused to accept his fate.\n(他拒絕接受自己的命運。)"],["fault","fault(n./v.)錯誤、過錯、缺點、挑剔\nfaulty(adj.)有缺陷的\nmy fault 我的錯\nfind fault with 挑剔\nIt's not your fault.\n(這不是你的錯。)\nMy boss always finds fault with my work.\n(我老闆總是挑剔我的工作。)"],["favor","favor(n./v.)恩惠、幫忙、偏愛、支持\nfavorable(adj.)有利的、贊同的\ndo sb. a favor 幫某人一個忙\nin favor of 支持、贊成\nCould you do me a favor?\n(你可以幫我一個忙嗎？)\nMost students are in favor of the plan.\n(大部分學生都支持這個計畫。)"],["favorite","favorite(adj./n.)最喜愛的、最喜愛的人事物\nfavor(v.)偏愛\nfavorite food 最喜歡的食物\nall-time favorite 一直以來的最愛\nPizza is my favorite food.\n(披薩是我最喜歡的食物。)\nThis song is my all-time favorite.\n(這首歌是我一直以來的最愛。)"],["fear","fear(n./v.)恐懼、害怕\nfearful(adj.)害怕的\nfearless(adj.)無畏的\nin fear 恐懼地\nfear of heights 懼高症\nShe has a fear of heights.\n(她有懼高症。)\nThe boy shook in fear.\n(那男孩害怕得發抖。)"],["feature","feature(n./v.)特色、特徵、五官、以…為特色\n(無詞性變化)\nmain feature 主要特色\nspecial feature 特點\nThe phone has many new features.\n(這支手機有許多新功能。)\nThe show features young singers.\n(這個節目以年輕歌手為主打。)"],["fee","fee(n.)費用、酬勞\n(無詞性變化)\nschool fees 學費\nentrance fee 入場費\nThe entrance fee is 100 dollars.\n(入場費是一百元。)\nParents pay school fees every term.\n(家長每學期要繳學費。)"],["feeling","feeling(n.)感覺、感情、感受\nfeel(v.)感覺\nhurt one's feelings 傷害某人的感情\nhave a feeling 有預感\nI didn't mean to hurt your feelings.\n(我不是故意要傷害你的感情。)\nI have a feeling he won't come.\n(我有預感他不會來。)"],["fellow","fellow(n.)傢伙、夥伴、同伴\nfellowship(n.)夥伴關係、交情\nfellow students 同學\nnice fellow 好人\nHe is a nice fellow.\n(他是個好人。)\nShe gets along well with her fellow students.\n(她和同學們相處得很好。)"],["female","female(adj./n.)女性的、雌性的、女性\n(無詞性變化)\nfemale student 女學生\nfemale animal 雌性動物\nOur class has twenty female students.\n(我們班有二十個女學生。)\nThe female bird is sitting on the eggs.\n(那隻母鳥正在孵蛋。)"],["fever","fever(n.)發燒、狂熱\nfeverish(adj.)發燒的\nhave a fever 發燒\nhigh fever 高燒\nShe stayed home because she had a fever.\n(她因為發燒待在家裡。)\nThe baby has a high fever.\n(那個嬰兒發高燒。)"],["field","field(n.)田野、場地、領域\n(無詞性變化)\nrice field 稻田\nfield trip 校外教學\nWe went on a field trip to the zoo.\n(我們去動物園校外教學。)\nHe is an expert in the field of science.\n(他是科學領域的專家。)"],["figure","figure(n./v.)數字、身材、人物、認為\n(無詞性變化)\nfigure out 想出、理解\nkeep one's figure 保持身材\nI can't figure out this math problem.\n(我想不出這道數學題。)\nHe is an important figure in history.\n(他是歷史上的重要人物。)"],["final","final(adj./n.)最後的、決賽、期末考\nfinally(adv.)最後、終於\nfinal exam 期末考\nmake the final 打進決賽\nThis is the final chapter of the book.\n(這是這本書的最後一章。)\nOur team made it to the final.\n(我們隊打進了決賽。)"],["fireman/firewoman","fireman(n.)消防員\nfirewoman(n.)女消防員\nfirefighter(n.)消防員\nbrave fireman 英勇的消防員\nfireman's uniform 消防員制服\nThe fireman saved a child from the fire.\n(那位消防員從火場中救出一個小孩。)\nMy aunt is a firewoman in Taipei.\n(我阿姨是台北的女消防員。)"],["firm","firm(n./adj./v./adv.)公司、堅定的、穩固的、使堅固\nfirmly(adv.)堅定地\nlaw firm 律師事務所\nfirm decision 堅定的決定\nMy father works for a law firm.\n(我爸爸在一家律師事務所工作。)\nShe held my hand firmly.\n(她緊緊握住我的手。)"],["fisherman","fisherman(n.)漁夫\nfish(v.)釣魚、捕魚\nfishing(n.)釣魚、漁業\nold fisherman 老漁夫\nfisherman's boat 漁夫的船\nThe fisherman caught a big fish.\n(那個漁夫捕到一條大魚。)\nMany fishermen live in this small town.\n(許多漁夫住在這個小鎮上。)"],["fit","fit(v./adj./n./adv.)適合、合身、健康的、合身\nfitness(n.)健康、體能\nkeep fit 保持健康\nfit in 融入\nThese shoes don't fit me.\n(這雙鞋我穿不合腳。)\nI go jogging to keep fit.\n(我慢跑來保持健康。)"],["fix","fix(v./n.)修理、固定、安排\nfixed(adj.)固定的\nfix a bike 修腳踏車\nfix a time 定下時間\nMy dad can fix almost anything.\n(我爸爸幾乎什麼都會修。)\nLet's fix a time for the meeting.\n(我們來定個開會時間吧。)"],["flag","flag(n.)旗子、旗幟\n(無詞性變化)\nnational flag 國旗\nwave a flag 揮舞旗子\nThe fans waved flags at the game.\n(球迷們在比賽中揮舞旗子。)\nEvery country has its own national flag.\n(每個國家都有自己的國旗。)"],["flat","flat(adj./adv./n.)平的、扁平的、洩氣的、平直地、公寓\nflatten(v.)使變平\nflat tire 洩氣的輪胎\nlie flat 平躺\nMy bike has a flat tire.\n(我的腳踏車輪胎沒氣了。)\nPeople once thought the Earth was flat.\n(人們曾經以為地球是平的。)"],["flight","flight(n.)飛行、班機、航班\nfly(v.)飛\nflight attendant 空服員\nbook a flight 訂機票\nOur flight to Tokyo leaves at nine.\n(我們飛往東京的班機九點起飛。)\nShe wants to be a flight attendant.\n(她想當空服員。)"],["flow","flow(n./v.)流動、流量\n(無詞性變化)\nflow into 流入\ntraffic flow 車流量\nThe river flows into the sea.\n(這條河流入大海。)\nThe police control the traffic flow.\n(警察管制車流。)"],["flu","flu(n.)流行性感冒\n(無詞性變化)\ncatch the flu 得流感\nflu shot 流感疫苗\nI caught the flu last week.\n(我上週得了流感。)\nYou should get a flu shot every year.\n(你應該每年打流感疫苗。)"],["focus","focus(n./v.)焦點、重點、集中\n(無詞性變化)\nfocus on 專注於\nin focus 焦點清楚\nFocus on your work, please.\n(請專心做你的事。)\nThe photo is not in focus.\n(這張照片沒對準焦。)"],["fog","fog(n./v.)霧、起霧\nfoggy(adj.)多霧的\nheavy fog 濃霧\nfog up 起霧\nThe heavy fog made it hard to see.\n(濃霧讓人很難看清楚。)\nMy glasses fogged up in the cold.\n(我的眼鏡在寒冷中起霧了。)"],["folk","folk(n.)人們、民族、家人\n(無詞性變化)\nfolk song 民謠\nold folks 老人家\nWe sang a Taiwanese folk song.\n(我們唱了一首台灣民謠。)\nHow are your folks doing?\n(你的家人都好嗎？)"],["following","following(adj./prep./n.)接著的、在…之後、下列\nfollow(v.)跟隨\nthe following day 隔天\nthe following 下列事物\nAnswer the following questions.\n(回答下列問題。)\nWe left the following morning.\n(我們隔天早上離開了。)"],["foolish","foolish(adj.)愚蠢的\nfool(n.)傻瓜\nfoolishly(adv.)愚蠢地\nfoolish mistake 愚蠢的錯誤\nfeel foolish 覺得自己很傻\nIt was foolish of me to believe him.\n(我相信他真是太傻了。)\nI made a foolish mistake on the test.\n(我在考試中犯了一個愚蠢的錯誤。)"],["football","football(n.)美式足球、足球(英式)\n(無詞性變化)\nplay football 踢足球、打美式足球\nfootball team 足球隊\nThe boys play football after school.\n(男孩們放學後踢足球。)\nHe joined the school football team.\n(他加入了學校足球隊。)"],["force","force(n./v.)力量、武力、強迫\nforceful(adj.)強而有力的\nair force 空軍\nforce sb. to 強迫某人\nNobody can force you to do it.\n(沒有人能強迫你做這件事。)\nMy cousin joined the air force.\n(我表哥加入了空軍。)"],["forest","forest(n.)森林\n(無詞性變化)\nrain forest 雨林\nforest fire 森林大火\nMany animals live in the forest.\n(許多動物住在森林裡。)\nThe forest fire burned for three days.\n(那場森林大火燒了三天。)"],["forgive","forgive(v.)原諒、寬恕\nforgiveness(n.)原諒\nforgive and forget 既往不咎\nforgive sb. for 原諒某人做了…\nPlease forgive me for being late.\n(請原諒我遲到了。)\nShe can't forgive him for lying.\n(她無法原諒他說謊。)"],["form","form(n./v.)形式、表格、形成\nformation(n.)形成\nfill in a form 填表格\nform a team 組成隊伍\nPlease fill in this form.\n(請填寫這張表格。)\nWe formed a team for the contest.\n(我們組隊參加比賽。)"],["formal","formal(adj.)正式的\nformally(adv.)正式地\ninformal(adj.)非正式的\nformal dress 正式服裝\nformal letter 正式信函\nYou need to wear formal dress to the dinner.\n(你需要穿正式服裝出席晚宴。)\nPlease write a formal letter to the school.\n(請寫一封正式信函給學校。)"],["former","former(adj.)以前的、前者的\nformerly(adv.)以前\nformer president 前總統\nthe former 前者\nHe is a former student of mine.\n(他是我以前的學生。)\nOf the two plans, I like the former.\n(這兩個計畫中，我比較喜歡前者。)"],["forth","forth(adv.)向前、往外\n(無詞性變化)\nback and forth 來回地\nand so forth 等等\nHe walked back and forth in the room.\n(他在房間裡來回踱步。)\nWe bought pens, books, and so forth.\n(我們買了筆、書等等。)"],["forward","forward(adj./n./v.)向前的、前鋒、轉寄\n(無詞性變化)\nlook forward to 期待\nforward an email 轉寄電子郵件\nI look forward to seeing you again.\n(我期待再次見到你。)\nPlease forward this email to Tom.\n(請把這封電子郵件轉寄給湯姆。)"],["forward/forwards","forward(adv.)向前、往前\nforwards(adv.)向前(英式)\nmove forward 向前進\nstep forward 向前一步\nPlease step forward when I call your name.\n(我叫到你的名字時請往前一步。)\nThe car moved slowly forwards.\n(車子慢慢地往前移動。)"],["found","found(v.)創立、建立\nfounder(n.)創辦人\nfoundation(n.)基礎、基金會\nfound a company 創立公司\nbe founded in 創立於\nThe school was founded in 1950.\n(這所學校創立於 1950 年。)\nHe founded his own company at 25.\n(他二十五歲時創立了自己的公司。)"],["fox","fox(n.)狐狸\n(無詞性變化)\nred fox 赤狐\nsly fox 狡猾的狐狸\nThe fox ran into the forest.\n(那隻狐狸跑進了森林。)\nHe is as sly as a fox.\n(他像狐狸一樣狡猾。)"],["freedom","freedom(n.)自由\nfree(adj.)自由的\nfreedom of speech 言論自由\nfight for freedom 爭取自由\nPeople fought hard for their freedom.\n(人們為了自由而努力奮鬥。)\nTeenagers want more freedom.\n(青少年想要更多自由。)"],["friendship","friendship(n.)友誼\nfriend(n.)朋友\nfriendly(adj.)友善的\nclose friendship 深厚的友誼\nbuild a friendship 建立友誼\nOur friendship began in high school.\n(我們的友誼始於高中。)\nTrue friendship lasts forever.\n(真正的友誼會永遠長存。)"],["fries","fries(n.)薯條\nfry(v.)油炸\nFrench fries 薯條\nlarge fries 大薯\nI'd like a burger and French fries.\n(我要一個漢堡和薯條。)\nCan I have some of your fries?\n(我可以吃一些你的薯條嗎？)"],["fry","fry(v./n.)油炸、煎、炸物\nfried(adj.)油炸的\nfried rice 炒飯\nstir-fry 快炒\nMom is frying eggs for breakfast.\n(媽媽正在煎蛋當早餐。)\nI had fried rice for lunch.\n(我午餐吃了炒飯。)"],["function","function(n./v.)功能、作用、運作\nfunctional(adj.)實用的、功能的\nmain function 主要功能\nfunction well 運作良好\nWhat is the main function of the heart?\n(心臟的主要功能是什麼？)\nThe machine is not functioning well.\n(這台機器運作得不太好。)"],["furniture","furniture(n.)家具\nfurnish(v.)布置家具\na piece of furniture 一件家具\noffice furniture 辦公家具\nWe bought new furniture for the living room.\n(我們為客廳買了新家具。)\nA sofa is a piece of furniture.\n(沙發是一件家具。)"],["further","further(adv./adj./v.)更進一步地、更遠的、促進\nfurthermore(adv.)此外\nfurther information 進一步的資訊\ngo further 更進一步\nFor further information, please call us.\n(如需進一步資訊，請來電。)\nShe wants to further her studies abroad.\n(她想出國深造。)"],["gain","gain(v./n.)獲得、增加、收穫\n(無詞性變化)\ngain weight 體重增加\ngain experience 獲得經驗\nShe gained a lot of experience from her part-time job.\n(她從打工中獲得了許多經驗。)\nMy brother gained three kilograms during the winter vacation.\n(我哥哥在寒假期間胖了三公斤。)"],["garbage","garbage(n.)垃圾\n(無詞性變化)\ngarbage truck 垃圾車\ntake out the garbage 倒垃圾\nPlease take out the garbage before you go to bed.\n(睡覺前請把垃圾拿出去倒。)\nThe garbage truck comes to our street every evening.\n(垃圾車每天傍晚都會來我們這條街。)"],["gardener","gardener(n.)園丁、園藝工作者\ngarden(n./v.)花園、從事園藝\ngardening(n.)園藝\nprofessional gardener 專業園丁\nkeen gardener 熱愛園藝的人\nThe gardener waters the flowers in the park every morning.\n(園丁每天早上替公園裡的花澆水。)\nMy grandmother is a keen gardener who grows her own vegetables.\n(我奶奶熱愛園藝，自己種蔬菜。)"],["garlic","garlic(n.)大蒜\n(無詞性變化)\ngarlic bread 大蒜麵包\na clove of garlic 一瓣大蒜\nMy mom adds a lot of garlic to the fried vegetables.\n(我媽媽在炒青菜裡加很多大蒜。)\nWe ordered garlic bread and soup for lunch.\n(我們午餐點了大蒜麵包和湯。)"],["gather","gather(v.)聚集、收集\ngathering(n.)聚會、集會\ngather information 收集資料\ngather together 聚在一起\nThe whole family gathers together for dinner on Lunar New Year's Eve.\n(除夕夜全家人會聚在一起吃年夜飯。)\nStudents gathered information about the city for their report.\n(學生們為了報告收集有關這座城市的資料。)"],["general","general(adj./n.)一般的、大體的、將軍\ngenerally(adv.)一般地、通常\ngeneralize(v.)概括、歸納\nin general 一般來說\ngeneral public 一般大眾\nIn general, students in our class are friendly and helpful.\n(一般來說，我們班的學生都友善又樂於助人。)\nThe general led his army into a long battle.\n(那位將軍率領軍隊投入一場漫長的戰役。)"],["generous","generous(adj.)慷慨的、大方的\ngenerosity(n.)慷慨、大方\ngenerously(adv.)慷慨地\ngenerous gift 慷慨的禮物\nbe generous with 對……很大方\nMy uncle is very generous with his time and money.\n(我叔叔對他的時間和金錢都很大方。)\nThank you for your generous gift on my birthday.\n(謝謝你在我生日時送的大方禮物。)"],["gentle","gentle(adj.)溫和的、溫柔的、輕柔的\ngently(adv.)輕輕地、溫柔地\ngentleness(n.)溫和、溫柔\ngentle breeze 微風\ngentle voice 溫柔的聲音\nThe nurse spoke to the child in a gentle voice.\n(護理師用溫柔的聲音跟孩子說話。)\nA gentle breeze blew across the quiet lake.\n(一陣微風吹過寧靜的湖面。)"],["gentleman","gentleman(n.)紳士、先生\ngentlemen(n.)紳士、先生(複數)\nladies and gentlemen 各位女士先生\na true gentleman 真正的紳士\nLadies and gentlemen, welcome to our school concert.\n(各位女士先生，歡迎來到我們學校的音樂會。)\nHe always opens the door for others like a true gentleman.\n(他總是像真正的紳士一樣替別人開門。)"],["giraffe","giraffe(n.)長頸鹿\n(無詞性變化)\nbaby giraffe 長頸鹿寶寶\ngiraffe's neck 長頸鹿的脖子\nThe giraffe ate leaves from the top of the tree.\n(長頸鹿吃著樹頂的葉子。)\nWe saw a baby giraffe at the zoo last Sunday.\n(上星期天我們在動物園看到一隻長頸鹿寶寶。)"],["glue","glue(n./v.)膠水、黏貼\n(無詞性變化)\nglue stick 口紅膠\nglue together 黏在一起\nI used glue to fix the broken cup.\n(我用膠水把破掉的杯子修好。)\nPlease glue the picture onto the card.\n(請把圖片黏在卡片上。)"],["goal","goal(n.)目標、得分、球門\n(無詞性變化)\nreach a goal 達成目標\nscore a goal 射門得分\nMy goal this year is to read twenty books.\n(我今年的目標是讀二十本書。)\nHe scored the winning goal in the last minute.\n(他在最後一分鐘踢進致勝的一球。)"],["goat","goat(n.)山羊\n(無詞性變化)\ngoat milk 羊奶\nmountain goat 野山羊\nThe farmer keeps ten goats on his farm.\n(那位農夫在他的農場養了十隻山羊。)\nSome people drink goat milk instead of cow milk.\n(有些人喝羊奶而不喝牛奶。)"],["gold","gold(n./adj.)黃金、金的\ngolden(adj.)金色的、黃金的\ngold medal 金牌\ngold ring 金戒指\nShe won a gold medal at the Olympic Games.\n(她在奧運會上贏得一面金牌。)\nMy father gave my mother a gold ring.\n(我爸爸送給我媽媽一枚金戒指。)"],["golden","golden(adj.)金色的、黃金的、極好的\ngold(n./adj.)黃金、金的\ngolden chance 大好機會\ngolden hair 金髮\nThe little girl has long golden hair.\n(那個小女孩有一頭長長的金髮。)\nThis trip is a golden chance to practice English.\n(這趟旅行是練習英文的大好機會。)"],["goose","goose(n.)鵝\ngeese(n.)鵝(複數)\nroast goose 烤鵝\nwild goose 野雁\nA goose was swimming slowly in the pond.\n(一隻鵝在池塘裡慢慢地游著。)\nThe restaurant is famous for its roast goose.\n(那家餐廳以烤鵝聞名。)"],["govern","govern(v.)統治、治理、管理\ngovernment(n.)政府\ngovernor(n.)州長、總督\ngovern a country 治理國家\nbe governed by 受……支配\nIt is not easy to govern a large country.\n(治理一個大國並不容易。)\nThe school is governed by strict rules.\n(這所學校受嚴格的規定管理。)"],["government","government(n.)政府\ngovern(v.)統治、治理\ngovernmental(adj.)政府的\nlocal government 地方政府\ngovernment official 政府官員\nThe government plans to build a new hospital here.\n(政府計劃在這裡蓋一間新醫院。)\nThe local government cleaned up the river last year.\n(地方政府去年整治了這條河。)"],["gradual","gradual(adj.)逐漸的、漸進的\ngradually(adv.)逐漸地\ngradual change 逐漸的改變\ngradual increase 逐步增加\nThere has been a gradual change in the weather.\n(天氣已經逐漸在改變。)\nHis English improved gradually after he moved to London.\n(搬到倫敦後，他的英文逐漸進步。)"],["grain","grain(n.)穀物、顆粒\n(無詞性變化)\nwhole grain 全穀物\na grain of sand 一粒沙\nRice is the most important grain in Asia.\n(稻米是亞洲最重要的穀物。)\nThere was a grain of sand in my shoe.\n(我的鞋子裡有一粒沙。)"],["gram","gram(n.)公克\n(無詞性變化)\ngrams of sugar 幾公克的糖\nper gram 每公克\nAdd 200 grams of flour to the bowl.\n(在碗裡加入兩百公克的麵粉。)\nThis letter weighs about twenty grams.\n(這封信大約重二十公克。)"],["grand","grand(adj.)盛大的、宏偉的、極好的\n(無詞性變化)\ngrand opening 盛大開幕\ngrand prize 頭獎\nThe new mall will have its grand opening next week.\n(新的購物中心下週將盛大開幕。)\nShe won the grand prize in the singing contest.\n(她在歌唱比賽中贏得首獎。)"],["grape","grape(n.)葡萄\n(無詞性變化)\ngrape juice 葡萄汁\na bunch of grapes 一串葡萄\nI bought a bunch of grapes at the market.\n(我在市場買了一串葡萄。)\nThe kids drank grape juice at the party.\n(孩子們在派對上喝葡萄汁。)"],["greet","greet(v.)問候、迎接、打招呼\ngreeting(n.)問候、致意\ngreet guests 迎接客人\ngreet each other 互相問候\nThe teacher greets every student at the classroom door.\n(老師在教室門口跟每位學生打招呼。)\nThey greeted each other with a big smile.\n(他們帶著燦爛的笑容互相問候。)"],["growth","growth(n.)成長、增長\ngrow(v.)生長、成長\neconomic growth 經濟成長\nrapid growth 快速成長\nSleep is important for a child's growth.\n(睡眠對孩子的成長很重要。)\nThe city has seen rapid growth in recent years.\n(這座城市近年來快速成長。)"],["guard","guard(n./v.)警衛、守衛、看守\nguardian(n.)監護人、守護者\nsecurity guard 保全人員\nguard against 防範\nA security guard stands at the bank door.\n(一名保全人員站在銀行門口。)\nThe dog guards the house at night.\n(那隻狗在晚上看守房子。)"],["guava","guava(n.)芭樂、番石榴\n(無詞性變化)\nguava juice 芭樂汁\nfresh guava 新鮮芭樂\nGuava is a popular fruit in Taiwan.\n(芭樂在台灣是很受歡迎的水果。)\nMy aunt gave us a bag of fresh guavas.\n(我阿姨給了我們一袋新鮮芭樂。)"],["guest","guest(n.)客人、來賓\n(無詞性變化)\nguest room 客房\nspecial guest 特別來賓\nWe have a special guest on our show tonight.\n(我們今晚的節目有一位特別來賓。)\nMy cousin stayed in our guest room for a week.\n(我表哥在我們家的客房住了一星期。)"],["guide","guide(n./v.)導遊、指南、引導\nguidance(n.)指導、輔導\ntour guide 導遊\ntravel guide 旅遊指南\nOur tour guide told us many stories about the old town.\n(我們的導遊告訴我們許多關於老城區的故事。)\nThe teacher guided us through the science museum.\n(老師帶領我們參觀科學博物館。)"],["gun","gun(n./v.)槍、開槍射擊\ngunman(n.)持槍歹徒\nfire a gun 開槍\ntoy gun 玩具槍\nThe little boy plays with a toy gun.\n(那個小男孩在玩玩具槍。)\nThe police officer did not fire his gun.\n(那名警察沒有開槍。)"],["gymnasium/gym","gymnasium(n.)體育館、健身房\ngym(n.)體育館、健身房(口語)\nschool gym 學校體育館\ngo to the gym 上健身房\nOur graduation ceremony was held in the school gymnasium.\n(我們的畢業典禮在學校體育館舉行。)\nMy father goes to the gym three times a week.\n(我爸爸一週去健身房三次。)"],["haircut","haircut(n.)理髮、髮型\n(無詞性變化)\nget a haircut 剪頭髮\nshort haircut 短髮\nI need to get a haircut before the school trip.\n(校外教學前我需要去剪頭髮。)\nDo you like my new short haircut?\n(你喜歡我新剪的短髮嗎？)"],["hall","hall(n.)大廳、會堂、走廊\n(無詞性變化)\nconcert hall 音樂廳\ncity hall 市政府\nWe listened to a concert in the new concert hall.\n(我們在新的音樂廳聽了一場音樂會。)\nThe students waited in the hall for the test.\n(學生們在走廊等待考試。)"],["hamburger/burger","hamburger(n.)漢堡\nburger(n.)漢堡(口語)\nhamburger shop 漢堡店\nhamburger meat 漢堡肉\nI ate a hamburger and fries for lunch.\n(我午餐吃了一個漢堡和薯條。)\nThis shop sells the best burgers in town.\n(這家店賣全城最好吃的漢堡。)"],["handle","handle(v./n.)處理、應付、把手\n(無詞性變化)\nhandle a problem 處理問題\ndoor handle 門把\nShe knows how to handle difficult customers.\n(她知道如何應付難纏的顧客。)\nThe door handle is broken, so be careful.\n(門把壞了，所以要小心。)"],["handsome","handsome(adj.)英俊的、帥氣的\n(無詞性變化)\nhandsome man 英俊的男子\ntall and handsome 又高又帥\nThe actor is tall and handsome.\n(那位演員又高又帥。)\nYou look very handsome in that suit.\n(你穿那套西裝看起來很帥。)"],["hardly","hardly(adv.)幾乎不\nhard(adj./adv.)困難的、努力地\nhardly ever 幾乎從不\ncan hardly believe 簡直無法相信\nI can hardly believe that summer vacation is over.\n(我簡直無法相信暑假已經結束了。)\nHe hardly ever eats breakfast at home.\n(他幾乎從不在家吃早餐。)"],["heaven","heaven(n.)天堂、天國\nheavenly(adj.)天堂的、美妙的\ngo to heaven 上天堂\nheaven on earth 人間天堂\nThis beautiful island is heaven on earth.\n(這座美麗的島嶼是人間天堂。)\nMany people believe good people go to heaven.\n(許多人相信好人會上天堂。)"],["hero/heroine","hero(n.)英雄、男主角\nheroine(n.)女英雄、女主角\nheroic(adj.)英勇的\nnational hero 民族英雄\nbecome a hero 成為英雄\nThe firefighter became a hero after saving the child.\n(那位消防員救了孩子後成為英雄。)\nThe heroine of the story is a brave young girl.\n(這個故事的女主角是一位勇敢的年輕女孩。)"],["highly","highly(adv.)非常、高度地\nhigh(adj./adv.)高的、高地\nhighly recommend 強力推薦\nhighly likely 非常可能\nI highly recommend this book to everyone.\n(我強力推薦這本書給每個人。)\nIt is highly likely to rain this afternoon.\n(今天下午非常可能會下雨。)"],["highway","highway(n.)公路、高速公路\n(無詞性變化)\nhighway exit 高速公路出口\non the highway 在公路上\nThere was a traffic jam on the highway this morning.\n(今天早上高速公路上塞車。)\nTake the next highway exit to get to the airport.\n(下一個高速公路出口下去就能到機場。)"],["hike","hike(n./v.)健行、遠足、徒步旅行\nhiker(n.)健行者\nhiking(n.)健行\ngo hiking 去健行\nhiking trail 健行步道\nWe went hiking in the mountains last weekend.\n(我們上週末去山上健行。)\nThe hike to the top took three hours.\n(健行到山頂花了三個小時。)"],["hip","hip(n.)臀部、髖部\n(無詞性變化)\nhands on hips 雙手叉腰\nhip bone 髖骨\nShe stood with her hands on her hips.\n(她雙手叉腰站著。)\nMy grandfather fell and hurt his hip.\n(我爺爺跌倒傷了髖部。)"],["hippopotamus/hippo","hippopotamus(n.)河馬\nhippo(n.)河馬(口語)\nbaby hippo 河馬寶寶\na herd of hippos 一群河馬\nA hippopotamus spends most of the day in the water.\n(河馬白天大部分時間都待在水裡。)\nThe baby hippo at the zoo is very popular.\n(動物園裡的河馬寶寶很受歡迎。)"],["historical","historical(adj.)歷史的、有關歷史的\nhistory(n.)歷史\nhistoric(adj.)有歷史意義的\nhistorical event 歷史事件\nhistorical site 歷史遺跡\nWe visited several historical sites in Tainan.\n(我們參觀了台南幾處歷史遺跡。)\nThis movie is based on a historical event.\n(這部電影是根據一個歷史事件改編的。)"],["hole","hole(n.)洞、坑\n(無詞性變化)\ndig a hole 挖洞\na hole in 在……上的破洞\nThere is a hole in my sock.\n(我的襪子破了一個洞。)\nThe dog dug a hole in the garden.\n(那隻狗在花園裡挖了一個洞。)"],["hop","hop(v./n.)單腳跳、跳躍\n(無詞性變化)\nhop on 跳上(車)\nhop around 跳來跳去\nThe rabbit hopped across the grass.\n(兔子跳過草地。)\nHop on the bus, or we will be late.\n(快上公車，不然我們會遲到。)"],["host/hostess","host(n.)主人、主持人\nhostess(n.)女主人、女主持人\nhost family 寄宿家庭\ntalk show host 脫口秀主持人\nI stayed with a host family in Canada last summer.\n(去年夏天我在加拿大住在寄宿家庭。)\nThe hostess welcomed every guest at the door.\n(女主人在門口迎接每一位客人。)"],["huge","huge(adj.)巨大的、龐大的\n(無詞性變化)\nhuge amount 大量\nhuge success 巨大的成功\nAn elephant is a huge animal.\n(大象是一種巨大的動物。)\nThe school concert was a huge success.\n(學校音樂會非常成功。)"],["human","human(adj./n.)人類的、人\nhumanity(n.)人性、人類\nhuman being 人類\nhuman rights 人權\nDogs can hear sounds that humans cannot.\n(狗能聽到人類聽不到的聲音。)\nEvery human being needs love and care.\n(每個人都需要愛與關懷。)"],["humble","humble(adj.)謙虛的、卑微的\nhumbly(adv.)謙虛地\nstay humble 保持謙虛\nhumble beginnings 卑微的出身\nEven after winning, he stayed humble.\n(即使贏了，他仍保持謙虛。)\nThe famous singer came from humble beginnings.\n(那位知名歌手出身卑微。)"],["hunt","hunt(v./n.)打獵、搜尋\nhunter(n.)獵人\nhunting(n.)打獵\njob hunt 找工作\nhunt for 搜尋\nLions usually hunt at night.\n(獅子通常在夜間獵食。)\nMy sister is hunting for a new apartment.\n(我姊姊正在找新公寓。)"],["hunter","hunter(n.)獵人、搜尋者\nhunt(v./n.)打獵、搜尋\nskilled hunter 熟練的獵人\nbargain hunter 喜歡撿便宜的人\nThe hunter walked quietly through the forest.\n(獵人靜悄悄地走過森林。)\nMy mom is a real bargain hunter at sales.\n(我媽媽在特價時真是個撿便宜高手。)"],["hurry","hurry(v./n.)趕快、匆忙\nhurried(adj.)匆忙的\nin a hurry 匆忙地\nhurry up 快一點\nHurry up, or we will miss the train.\n(快一點，不然我們會錯過火車。)\nHe left home in a hurry this morning.\n(他今天早上匆忙離開家。)"],["ideal","ideal(adj./n.)理想的、理想\nideally(adv.)理想地\nidealistic(adj.)理想主義的\nideal place 理想的地方\nideal job 理想的工作\nThis park is an ideal place for a picnic.\n(這座公園是野餐的理想地點。)\nTeaching is my ideal job.\n(教書是我理想的工作。)"],["identity","identity(n.)身分、特性\nidentify(v.)確認、辨認\nidentification(n.)身分證明、辨認\nidentity card 身分證\ncultural identity 文化認同\nPlease show your identity card at the counter.\n(請在櫃檯出示你的身分證。)\nLanguage is part of our cultural identity.\n(語言是我們文化認同的一部分。)"],["ignore","ignore(v.)忽視、不理會\nignorance(n.)無知\nignorant(adj.)無知的\nignore the advice 不理會建議\ncompletely ignore 完全忽視\nHe ignored my message and did not reply.\n(他不理會我的訊息，也沒有回覆。)\nDo not ignore your teacher's advice.\n(不要忽視老師的建議。)"],["ill","ill(adj./adv./n.)生病的、壞地、災難\nillness(n.)疾病\nfall ill 生病\nseriously ill 病重\nShe fell ill and stayed in bed for two days.\n(她生病了，在床上躺了兩天。)\nPlease do not speak ill of others.\n(請不要說別人的壞話。)"],["image","image(n.)影像、形象、印象\nimagine(v.)想像\npublic image 公眾形象\nclear image 清晰的影像\nThe camera takes very clear images.\n(這台相機拍出的影像非常清晰。)\nThe singer cares a lot about her public image.\n(那位歌手非常在意她的公眾形象。)"],["imagine","imagine(v.)想像、設想\nimagination(n.)想像力\nimaginary(adj.)想像的、虛構的\nimagine life without 想像沒有……的生活\ncan't imagine 無法想像\nCan you imagine life without cell phones?\n(你能想像沒有手機的生活嗎？)\nI can't imagine how tired you must be.\n(我無法想像你一定有多累。)"],["importance","importance(n.)重要性\nimportant(adj.)重要的\nthe importance of ……的重要性\nof great importance 非常重要\nOur teacher talked about the importance of sleep.\n(我們老師談到睡眠的重要性。)\nThis meeting is of great importance to our team.\n(這場會議對我們的團隊非常重要。)"],["impressive","impressive(adj.)令人印象深刻的\nimpress(v.)使印象深刻\nimpression(n.)印象\nimpressive performance 精彩的表現\nvery impressive 非常令人佩服\nHer piano performance was very impressive.\n(她的鋼琴演奏令人印象非常深刻。)\nThe view from the mountain top is impressive.\n(從山頂看出去的景色令人讚嘆。)"],["improve(ment)","improve(v.)改善、進步、improvement(n.)改進、進步\n(無詞性變化)\nimprove skills 提升技能\nmake improvements 做改進\nReading every day can improve your English.\n(每天閱讀可以提升你的英文。)\nThere is a big improvement in your writing.\n(你的寫作有很大的進步。)"],["include","include(v.)包含、包括\nincluding(prep.)包括\ninclusive(adj.)包含的、包容的\nbe included in 被包含在……裡\ninclude tax 含稅\nThe price includes breakfast and dinner.\n(這個價格包含早餐和晚餐。)\nYour name is included in the list.\n(你的名字在名單裡。)"],["income","income(n.)收入、所得\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh income 高收入\nincome tax 所得稅\nHis family has a low income.\n(他的家庭收入不高。)\nEveryone with an income must pay income tax.\n(每個有收入的人都必須繳所得稅。)"],["increase","increase(v./n.)增加、增長\nincreasingly(adv.)越來越\nincrease in ……的增加\nsharp increase 急遽增加\nThe number of students has increased this year.\n(今年學生人數增加了。)\nThere was a sharp increase in oil prices.\n(油價急遽上漲。)"],["indeed","indeed(adv.)確實、的確\n(無詞性變化)\nyes, indeed 的確如此\nindeed very 確實非常\nThe movie was indeed very exciting.\n(這部電影確實非常刺激。)\nA friend in need is a friend indeed.\n(患難見真情。)"],["independence","independence(n.)獨立、自主\nindependent(adj.)獨立的\nindependently(adv.)獨立地\nIndependence Day 獨立紀念日\ngain independence 獲得獨立\nAmericans celebrate Independence Day on July 4.\n(美國人在七月四日慶祝獨立紀念日。)\nLiving alone taught me independence.\n(獨自生活教會我獨立。)"],["independent","independent(adj.)獨立的、自主的\nindependence(n.)獨立、自主\nindependently(adv.)獨立地\nbe independent of 不依賴……\nindependent thinking 獨立思考\nShe became independent of her parents after college.\n(她大學畢業後就不再依賴父母。)\nTeachers encourage independent thinking in class.\n(老師在課堂上鼓勵獨立思考。)"],["indicate","indicate(v.)指出、顯示、表明\nindication(n.)跡象、指示\nindicator(n.)指標\nindicate that 顯示……\nclearly indicate 清楚表明\nThe study indicates that exercise is good for the brain.\n(研究顯示運動對大腦有益。)\nDark clouds indicate that it will rain soon.\n(烏雲顯示快要下雨了。)"],["individual","individual(adj./n.)個別的、個人\nindividually(adv.)個別地\nindividual needs 個人需求\neach individual 每一個人\nThe teacher pays attention to each student's individual needs.\n(老師注意每位學生的個別需求。)\nEvery individual has the right to be happy.\n(每個人都有追求幸福的權利。)"],["industry","industry(n.)工業、產業、勤勉\nindustrial(adj.)工業的\nindustrious(adj.)勤勉的\ntourism industry 觀光業\nheavy industry 重工業\nThe tourism industry is important to Taiwan.\n(觀光業對台灣很重要。)\nMy father works in the car industry.\n(我爸爸在汽車業工作。)"],["influence","influence(n./v.)影響、影響力\ninfluential(adj.)有影響力的\nhave an influence on 對……有影響\nunder the influence of 在……的影響下\nMy grandmother had a great influence on me.\n(我奶奶對我有很大的影響。)\nThe weather can influence our mood.\n(天氣會影響我們的心情。)"],["ink","ink(n./v.)墨水、用墨水寫\n(無詞性變化)\nblack ink 黑色墨水\nin ink 用墨水(筆)寫\nPlease write your answers in black ink.\n(請用黑色墨水筆寫答案。)\nMy printer has run out of ink.\n(我的印表機沒墨水了。)"],["insist","insist(v.)堅持、堅決要求\ninsistence(n.)堅持\ninsist on 堅持\ninsist that 堅持認為\nMy mother insists on cooking dinner every night.\n(我媽媽堅持每晚自己煮晚餐。)\nHe insisted that he was right.\n(他堅持認為自己是對的。)"],["instance","instance(n.)例子、實例\n(無詞性變化)\nfor instance 例如\nin this instance 在這個例子中\nSome fruits, for instance oranges, are rich in vitamin C.\n(有些水果，例如柳橙，富含維他命C。)\nIn this instance, you should ask your teacher for help.\n(在這種情況下，你應該向老師求助。)"],["instant","instant(adj./n.)立即的、速食的、瞬間\ninstantly(adv.)立即地\ninstant noodles 泡麵\nfor an instant 一瞬間\nI ate instant noodles for dinner last night.\n(我昨晚晚餐吃了泡麵。)\nFor an instant, I thought I saw a ghost.\n(有一瞬間，我以為我看到了鬼。)"],["instead","instead(adv.)作為替代、反而\n(無詞性變化)\ninstead of 而不是、代替\ngo instead 代替去\nLet's walk instead of taking the bus.\n(我們走路去，而不要搭公車吧。)\nI was busy, so my brother went instead.\n(我很忙，所以我弟弟代替我去。)"],["instruction","instruction(n.)指示、說明、教導\ninstruct(v.)指示、教導\ninstructor(n.)教練、講師\nfollow instructions 遵照指示\ninstruction manual 使用說明書\nPlease read the instructions carefully before the test.\n(考試前請仔細閱讀說明。)\nFollow the instructions to set up the new computer.\n(按照說明來設定新電腦。)"],["instrument","instrument(n.)樂器、儀器、工具\ninstrumental(adj.)樂器的、起作用的\nmusical instrument 樂器\nplay an instrument 演奏樂器\nCan you play any musical instruments?\n(你會演奏任何樂器嗎？)\nDoctors use special instruments to check your heart.\n(醫生用特殊儀器檢查你的心臟。)"],["internal","internal(adj.)內部的、體內的、國內的\ninternally(adv.)在內部\ninternal organs 內臟\ninternal problem 內部問題\nThe heart is one of our internal organs.\n(心臟是我們的內臟之一。)\nThe company had some internal problems last year.\n(那間公司去年有一些內部問題。)"],["international","international(adj.)國際的\ninternationally(adv.)國際上\ninternational student 國際學生\ninternational trade 國際貿易\nThere are many international students at this university.\n(這所大學有許多國際學生。)\nTaiwan depends a lot on international trade.\n(台灣非常依賴國際貿易。)"],["Internet/internet","Internet(n.)網際網路\ninternet(n.)網際網路(小寫寫法)\non the Internet 在網路上\nInternet access 上網\nI found the information on the Internet.\n(我在網路上找到這項資料。)\nThe hotel offers free internet access.\n(這家飯店提供免費上網。)"],["introduce","introduce(v.)介紹、引進\nintroduction(n.)介紹、引進\nintroductory(adj.)介紹的、入門的\nintroduce oneself 自我介紹\nintroduce A to B 把A介紹給B\nLet me introduce myself to the class.\n(讓我向全班自我介紹。)\nShe introduced her best friend to her parents.\n(她把她最好的朋友介紹給她的父母。)"],["introduction","introduction(n.)介紹、引言、引進\nintroduce(v.)介紹、引進\nself-introduction 自我介紹\nbrief introduction 簡短介紹\nEach student gave a short self-introduction.\n(每位學生都做了簡短的自我介紹。)\nThe introduction of the book is very interesting.\n(這本書的引言非常有趣。)"],["iron","iron(n./v./adj.)鐵、熨斗、熨燙、鐵的\n(無詞性變化)\niron a shirt 燙襯衫\niron gate 鐵門\nMy father irons his shirts every Sunday.\n(我爸爸每個星期天燙他的襯衫。)\nSpinach is rich in iron.\n(菠菜富含鐵質。)"],["jam","jam(n./v.)果醬、擁擠、阻塞\n(無詞性變化)\ntraffic jam 塞車\nstrawberry jam 草莓果醬\nWe were stuck in a traffic jam for an hour.\n(我們塞車塞了一個小時。)\nI like to put strawberry jam on my toast.\n(我喜歡在吐司上塗草莓果醬。)"],["jog","jog(v./n.)慢跑\njogger(n.)慢跑者\njogging(n.)慢跑\ngo jogging 去慢跑\njog in the park 在公園慢跑\nMy parents go jogging every morning.\n(我父母每天早上去慢跑。)\nI jog in the park after school.\n(我放學後在公園慢跑。)"],["joint","joint(adj./n.)共同的、聯合的、關節\njointly(adv.)共同地\njoint effort 共同努力\nknee joint 膝關節\nThe party was a joint effort by the whole class.\n(這場派對是全班共同努力的成果。)\nMy grandmother has pain in her knee joints.\n(我奶奶的膝關節會痛。)"],["journal","journal(n.)日誌、期刊\njournalist(n.)記者\nkeep a journal 寫日誌\nscience journal 科學期刊\nI keep a journal to write down my feelings.\n(我寫日誌記錄自己的感受。)\nHis paper was published in a science journal.\n(他的論文刊登在一本科學期刊上。)"],["judge","judge(n./v.)法官、裁判、評審、判斷\njudgment(n.)判斷、判決\njudge by 根據……判斷\nact as a judge 擔任評審\nDon't judge a person by his looks.\n(不要以貌取人。)\nThe judge listened carefully to both sides.\n(法官仔細聆聽雙方的說法。)"],["judgment/judgement","judgment(n.)判斷、判決、看法\njudgement(n.)判斷(英式拼法)\njudge(v./n.)判斷、法官\ngood judgment 良好的判斷力\nmake a judgment 做出判斷\nYou should use good judgment when you make friends online.\n(在網路上交朋友時，你應該運用良好的判斷力。)\nIt is too early to make a judgment.\n(現在下判斷還太早。)"],["justice","justice(n.)正義、公平、司法\njust(adj.)公正的\nbring to justice 繩之以法\nsense of justice 正義感\nHe has a strong sense of justice.\n(他有強烈的正義感。)\nThe police finally brought the thief to justice.\n(警方終於將小偷繩之以法。)"],["keeper","keeper(n.)看守人、管理員、守門員\nkeep(v.)保持、保存\ngoalkeeper 守門員\nzoo keeper 動物園管理員\nThe zoo keeper feeds the lions every afternoon.\n(動物園管理員每天下午餵獅子。)\nOur goalkeeper stopped the ball.\n(我們的守門員擋下了那顆球。)"],["ketchup","ketchup(n.)番茄醬\n(無詞性變化)\ntomato ketchup 番茄醬\nwith ketchup 加番茄醬\nWould you like some ketchup with your fries?\n(你的薯條要加點番茄醬嗎？)\nHe put too much ketchup on his hot dog.\n(他在熱狗上加了太多番茄醬。)"],["kilogram","kilogram(n.)公斤\nkilo(n.)公斤(口語)\na kilogram of 一公斤的\nper kilogram 每公斤\nThis bag of rice weighs five kilograms.\n(這袋米重五公斤。)\nApples are sold at 100 dollars per kilogram.\n(蘋果每公斤賣一百元。)"],["lack","lack(n./v.)缺乏、缺少\nlacking(adj.)缺乏的\nlack of sleep 睡眠不足\nlack confidence 缺乏自信\nHe is tired because of lack of sleep.\n(他因為睡眠不足而很累。)\nShe lacks confidence when she speaks English.\n(她說英文時缺乏自信。)"],["lady","lady(n.)女士、淑女\n(無詞性變化)\nladies and gentlemen 各位先生女士\nold lady 老太太\nLadies and gentlemen, welcome to the show.\n(各位先生女士，歡迎蒞臨本節目。)\nI helped an old lady cross the street.\n(我幫一位老太太過馬路。)"],["ladybug","ladybug(n.)瓢蟲\n(無詞性變化)\nred ladybug 紅色瓢蟲\nladybug spots 瓢蟲的斑點\nA ladybug landed on my finger.\n(一隻瓢蟲停在我的手指上。)\nLadybugs eat small insects on plants.\n(瓢蟲會吃植物上的小蟲。)"],["lamb","lamb(n./v.)小羊、羔羊肉、生小羊\n(無詞性變化)\nroast lamb 烤羊肉\nas gentle as a lamb 溫順如羔羊\nThe lamb is following its mother.\n(那隻小羊跟著牠的媽媽。)\nWe had roast lamb for dinner.\n(我們晚餐吃烤羊肉。)"],["lane","lane(n.)巷子、小路、車道\n(無詞性變化)\nbus lane 公車專用道\nfast lane 快車道\nMy house is in a quiet lane.\n(我家在一條安靜的巷子裡。)\nCars cannot drive in the bus lane.\n(汽車不能開進公車專用道。)"],["lantern","lantern(n.)燈籠、提燈\n(無詞性變化)\nLantern Festival 元宵節\nsky lantern 天燈\nWe saw many lanterns at the Lantern Festival.\n(我們在元宵節看到很多燈籠。)\nPeople release sky lanterns in Pingxi.\n(人們在平溪施放天燈。)"],["lap","lap(n.)膝上、(跑道的)一圈\n(無詞性變化)\nsit on one's lap 坐在某人腿上\nrun a lap 跑一圈\nThe cat is sleeping on my lap.\n(那隻貓在我腿上睡覺。)\nWe ran three laps around the field.\n(我們繞操場跑了三圈。)"],["latest","latest(adj.)最新的、最近的\nlate(adj.)遲的、晚的\nlatest news 最新消息\nthe latest model 最新款\nHave you heard the latest news?\n(你聽說最新消息了嗎？)\nHe bought the latest model of the phone.\n(他買了最新款的手機。)"],["latter","latter(adj.)後者的、後半的\n(無詞性變化)\nthe latter 後者\nthe latter half 後半\nOf the two plans, I prefer the latter.\n(這兩個計畫中，我比較喜歡後者。)\nThe latter half of the movie is exciting.\n(這部電影的後半段很精彩。)"],["law","law(n.)法律、法則、定律\nlawyer(n.)律師\nlawful(adj.)合法的\nbreak the law 犯法\nby law 依法\nEveryone must obey the law.\n(每個人都必須遵守法律。)\nDriving without a license is against the law.\n(無照駕駛是違法的。)"],["lay","lay(v.)放置、下(蛋)、鋪設\n(無詞性變化)\nlay eggs 下蛋\nlay the table 擺餐具\nOur hens lay eggs every day.\n(我們的母雞每天都下蛋。)\nShe laid the baby on the bed.\n(她把嬰兒放在床上。)"],["leadership","leadership(n.)領導能力、領導地位\nlead(v.)帶領\nleader(n.)領導者\nleadership skills 領導技巧\nunder the leadership of 在……的領導下\nShe showed great leadership as class leader.\n(她擔任班長時展現了出色的領導能力。)\nThe team won under his leadership.\n(這支隊伍在他的領導下獲勝。)"],["leaf","leaf(n.)葉子、(書的)一頁\nleaves(n.)葉子(複數)\nfallen leaves 落葉\nturn over a new leaf 改過自新\nThe leaves turn red in fall.\n(葉子在秋天變紅。)\nHe promised to turn over a new leaf.\n(他保證會改過自新。)"],["legal","legal(adj.)合法的、法律的\nillegal(adj.)非法的\nlegally(adv.)合法地\nlegal age 法定年齡\nlegal advice 法律諮詢\nIt is not legal to drive at sixteen here.\n(在這裡十六歲開車是不合法的。)\nYou should get legal advice first.\n(你應該先尋求法律諮詢。)"],["lend","lend(v.)借出、借給\nlender(n.)出借人\nlend a hand 幫忙\nlend money 借錢給人\nCan you lend me your pen?\n(你可以借我你的筆嗎？)\nCould you lend me a hand with these boxes?\n(你可以幫我搬這些箱子嗎？)"],["length","length(n.)長度、時間長短\nlong(adj.)長的\nlengthen(v.)加長\nat length 詳細地、最後\nthe length of …的長度\nThe length of the bridge is 500 meters.\n(這座橋的長度是五百公尺。)\nThey talked about the plan at length.\n(他們詳細地討論了這個計畫。)"],["lens","lens(n.)鏡片、鏡頭、透鏡\n(無詞性變化)\ncontact lens 隱形眼鏡\ncamera lens 相機鏡頭\nShe wears contact lenses instead of glasses.\n(她戴隱形眼鏡而不是一般眼鏡。)\nDon't touch the camera lens.\n(不要碰相機鏡頭。)"],["liberal","liberal(adj.)開明的、自由主義的、大方的\nliberty(n.)自由\nliberate(v.)解放\nliberal arts 人文學科\nliberal attitude 開明的態度\nMy parents have liberal ideas about dating.\n(我父母對交往的想法很開明。)\nShe studies liberal arts in college.\n(她在大學讀人文學科。)"],["lid","lid(n.)蓋子、眼瞼\neyelid(n.)眼皮\nput the lid on 蓋上蓋子\njar lid 瓶蓋\nPut the lid on the pot.\n(把鍋蓋蓋上。)\nI can't open the lid of this jar.\n(我打不開這個罐子的蓋子。)"],["lift","lift(v./n.)舉起、提起、搭便車、電梯(英)\n(無詞性變化)\ngive someone a lift 讓某人搭便車\nlift weights 舉重\nCan you help me lift this box?\n(你能幫我抬起這個箱子嗎？)\nMy dad gave me a lift to school.\n(我爸爸順路載我去學校。)"],["likely","likely(adj./adv.)可能的、很可能\nlikelihood(n.)可能性\nunlikely(adj.)不太可能的\nbe likely to 很可能\nmost likely 極有可能\nIt is likely to rain tomorrow.\n(明天很可能會下雨。)\nHe will most likely be late again.\n(他極有可能又會遲到。)"],["limit","limit(n./v.)限制、極限、限定\nlimited(adj.)有限的\nlimitation(n.)限制\nspeed limit 速限\ntime limit 時間限制\nThe speed limit here is 50 kilometers per hour.\n(這裡的速限是每小時五十公里。)\nPlease limit your speech to three minutes.\n(請把你的演講限制在三分鐘內。)"],["link","link(n./v.)連結、關聯、連接\n(無詞性變化)\nlink between …之間的關聯\nclick the link 點擊連結\nClick the link to watch the video.\n(點這個連結觀看影片。)\nThere is a link between diet and health.\n(飲食和健康之間有關聯。)"],["liquid","liquid(n.)液體\n(無詞性變化)\nliquid soap 洗手乳\nclear liquid 透明液體\nWater is a liquid at room temperature.\n(水在室溫下是液體。)\nYou can't bring liquids on the plane.\n(你不能帶液體上飛機。)"],["listener","listener(n.)聽者、聽眾\nlisten(v.)聽\ngood listener 好的傾聽者\nradio listener 電台聽眾\nShe is a good listener.\n(她是很好的傾聽者。)\nThe radio show has many listeners.\n(這個廣播節目有很多聽眾。)"],["liver","liver(n.)肝臟\n(無詞性變化)\nliver cancer 肝癌\npork liver 豬肝\nDrinking too much is bad for your liver.\n(喝太多酒對肝臟不好。)\nGrandma cooked pork liver soup for me.\n(奶奶為我煮了豬肝湯。)"],["load","load(n./v.)負荷、裝載物、裝載\n(無詞性變化)\nheavy load 沉重的負擔\nloads of 大量的\nThe truck carries a heavy load.\n(那輛卡車載著沉重的貨物。)\nThey loaded the boxes into the car.\n(他們把箱子裝上車。)"],["local","local(adj./n.)當地的、本地的、當地人\nlocally(adv.)在當地\nlocal food 當地美食\nlocal time 當地時間\nWe tried some local food in Tainan.\n(我們在台南吃了一些當地美食。)\nAsk a local for directions.\n(向當地人問路吧。)"],["lone","lone(adj.)孤單的、唯一的\nlonely(adj.)寂寞的\nalone(adj./adv.)獨自的\nlone wolf 獨行俠\na lone tree 一棵孤零零的樹\nA lone tree stood on the hill.\n(山丘上有一棵孤零零的樹。)\nHe is a lone wolf and seldom joins others.\n(他是個獨行俠，很少和別人一起行動。)"],["loss","loss(n.)損失、喪失、失敗\nlose(v.)失去、輸\nlost(adj.)迷路的、遺失的\nweight loss 減重\nat a loss 不知所措\nThe team had a big loss last night.\n(這支隊伍昨晚大敗。)\nI was at a loss for words.\n(我不知道該說什麼。)"],["lower","lower(v.)降低、放下\nlow(adj.)低的\nlower the price 降價\nlower one's voice 壓低聲音\nPlease lower your voice in the library.\n(在圖書館請壓低音量。)\nThe store lowered the price of the shoes.\n(這家店調降了鞋子的價格。)"],["luck","luck(n.)運氣、好運\nlucky(adj.)幸運的\nluckily(adv.)幸運地\ngood luck 祝好運\nbad luck 壞運氣\nGood luck on your exam!\n(祝你考試順利！)\nIt was just bad luck.\n(那只是運氣不好。)"],["magazine","magazine(n.)雜誌\n(無詞性變化)\nfashion magazine 時尚雜誌\nread a magazine 看雜誌\nShe reads a fashion magazine every month.\n(她每個月都看時尚雜誌。)\nI saw your photo in a magazine.\n(我在雜誌上看到你的照片。)"],["maintain","maintain(v.)維持、保養、主張\nmaintenance(n.)維修、保養\nmaintain a balance 維持平衡\nmaintain contact 保持聯絡\nIt is important to maintain a healthy weight.\n(維持健康的體重很重要。)\nHe maintains his car very well.\n(他把車子保養得很好。)"],["major","major(adj./n./v.)主要的、主修科目、主修\nmajority(n.)大多數\nmajor in 主修\nmajor problem 主要問題\nShe wants to major in history.\n(她想主修歷史。)\nTraffic is a major problem in big cities.\n(交通是大城市的主要問題。)"],["male","male(adj./n.)男性的、雄性的、男性\nfemale(adj./n.)女性的、女性\nmale student 男學生\nmale lion 公獅\nThe male lion has a big mane.\n(公獅有一大圈鬃毛。)\nThere are more male students in this class.\n(這個班的男學生比較多。)"],["manage(ment)","manage(v.)管理、設法完成、management(n.)管理\nmanager(n.)經理\nmanage to do 設法做到\ntime management 時間管理\nHe managed to finish the work on time.\n(他設法準時完成了工作。)\nGood time management helps students study better.\n(良好的時間管理有助於學生讀書。)"],["manager","manager(n.)經理、經營者\nmanage(v.)管理\ngeneral manager 總經理\nstore manager 店長\nI want to speak to the manager.\n(我想和經理談談。)\nShe became a store manager at twenty-five.\n(她二十五歲就當上了店長。)"],["mango","mango(n.)芒果\n(無詞性變化)\nmango shaved ice 芒果冰\nripe mango 熟透的芒果\nMango shaved ice is popular in summer.\n(芒果冰在夏天很受歡迎。)\nThis mango is sweet and juicy.\n(這顆芒果又甜又多汁。)"],["manner","manner(n.)方式、態度、(複數)禮貌\nmannered(adj.)有……舉止的\ntable manners 餐桌禮儀\ngood manners 有禮貌\nIt's bad manners to talk with your mouth full.\n(嘴裡有食物時說話是沒禮貌的。)\nHe spoke in a friendly manner.\n(他以友善的態度說話。)"],["marriage","marriage(n.)婚姻、結婚\nmarry(v.)結婚\nmarried(adj.)已婚的\nhappy marriage 幸福的婚姻\nmarriage proposal 求婚\nMy parents have a happy marriage.\n(我的父母婚姻幸福。)\nHe made a marriage proposal at the beach.\n(他在海邊求婚。)"],["marry","marry(v.)結婚、嫁、娶\nmarriage(n.)婚姻\nmarried(adj.)已婚的\nget married 結婚\nmarry someone 和某人結婚\nWill you marry me?\n(你願意嫁給我嗎？)\nThey got married last spring.\n(他們去年春天結婚了。)"],["mask","mask(n./v.)面具、口罩、掩飾\nmasked(adj.)戴面具的\nwear a mask 戴口罩\nface mask 面膜、口罩\nPlease wear a mask on the bus.\n(在公車上請戴口罩。)\nHe masked his fear with a smile.\n(他用微笑掩飾恐懼。)"],["mass","mass(n.)大量、團、質量、群眾\nmassive(adj.)巨大的\nmass media 大眾傳播媒體\na mass of 大量的\nThe mass media has a strong influence on teens.\n(大眾媒體對青少年影響很大。)\nA mass of people gathered in the square.\n(一大群人聚集在廣場上。)"],["master","master(n./v.)主人、大師、精通\nmastery(n.)精通\nmaster's degree 碩士學位\nmaster a skill 精通一項技能\nIt takes years to master a language.\n(精通一種語言需要好幾年。)\nThe dog waited for its master at the door.\n(那隻狗在門口等牠的主人。)"],["mat","mat(n.)墊子、地墊\n(無詞性變化)\nyoga mat 瑜伽墊\ndoor mat 門口腳踏墊\nWipe your feet on the mat.\n(在墊子上擦擦腳。)\nI bought a new yoga mat.\n(我買了一張新的瑜伽墊。)"],["match","match(n.)比賽、火柴、相配的人或物\n(無詞性變化)\ntennis match 網球比賽\na perfect match 天生一對、完美搭配\nWe watched a tennis match on TV.\n(我們在電視上看了一場網球比賽。)\nYour shoes and bag are a perfect match.\n(你的鞋子和包包搭配得很完美。)"],["mate","mate(n./v.)夥伴、配偶、交配\n(無詞性變化)\nfind a mate 尋找伴侶\nbest mate 最好的朋友(英式口語)\nMy roommate and I get along well.\n(我和室友相處得很好。)\nBirds look for mates in spring.\n(鳥類在春天尋找伴侶。)"],["material","material(n.)材料、資料、布料\n(無詞性變化)\nraw material 原料\nteaching material 教材\nThis bag is made of soft material.\n(這個包包是用柔軟的材料做的。)\nShe is collecting material for her report.\n(她正在為報告蒐集資料。)"],["mature","mature(adj.)成熟的\nmaturity(n.)成熟\nimmature(adj.)不成熟的\nmature attitude 成熟的態度\nmentally mature 心智成熟\nHe is very mature for his age.\n(以他的年紀來說，他非常成熟。)\nShe handled the problem in a mature way.\n(她用成熟的方式處理了這個問題。)"],["meaning","meaning(n.)意思、意義\nmean(v.)意指\nmeaningful(adj.)有意義的\nmeaningless(adj.)無意義的\nfind meaning in 在……中找到意義\nthe meaning of life 人生的意義\nWhat is the meaning of this word?\n(這個字是什麼意思？)\nHelping others gives my life meaning.\n(幫助別人讓我的人生有意義。)"],["means","means(n.)方法、手段、財力\n(無詞性變化)\nby means of 藉由\nby no means 絕不\nThe bus is the main means of transportation here.\n(公車是這裡主要的交通工具。)\nThis is by no means easy.\n(這絕不容易。)"],["measure(ment)","measure(v.)測量、衡量、measurement(n.)測量、尺寸\n(無詞性變化)\nmeasure the length 測量長度\ntake measurements 量尺寸\nThe nurse measured my height and weight.\n(護理師幫我量了身高和體重。)\nThe tailor took my measurements for a suit.\n(裁縫師幫我量尺寸做西裝。)"],["medical","medical(adj.)醫學的、醫療的\nmedicine(n.)藥、醫學\nmedic(n.)醫護人員\nmedical school 醫學院\nmedical care 醫療照護\nShe wants to go to medical school.\n(她想讀醫學院。)\nTaiwan has good medical care.\n(台灣有良好的醫療照護。)"],["melody","melody(n.)旋律、曲調\nmelodic(adj.)旋律的、悅耳的\nsweet melody 甜美的旋律\ncatchy melody 朗朗上口的旋律\nThe song has a catchy melody.\n(這首歌的旋律很好記。)\nShe hummed a simple melody.\n(她哼著一段簡單的曲調。)"],["membership","membership(n.)會員身分、會員資格\nmember(n.)成員、會員\nmembership card 會員卡\nmembership fee 會費\nShow your membership card at the counter.\n(在櫃台出示你的會員卡。)\nThe gym membership fee is not cheap.\n(健身房的會費不便宜。)"],["memory","memory(n.)記憶、回憶、記憶力\nmemorize(v.)記住\nmemorial(adj./n.)紀念的、紀念碑\ngood memory 好記性\nin memory of 紀念\nMy grandma has a very good memory.\n(我奶奶的記性非常好。)\nI have happy memories of my childhood.\n(我有許多快樂的童年回憶。)"],["mention","mention(v./n.)提到、說起、提及\n(無詞性變化)\ndon't mention it 不客氣\nas mentioned 如前所述\nDid he mention his new job?\n(他有提到他的新工作嗎？)\n'Thanks for your help.' 'Don't mention it.'\n('謝謝你的幫忙。' '不客氣。')"],["message","message(n.)訊息、留言、要旨\nmessenger(n.)信差、傳訊者\nleave a message 留言\ntext message 簡訊\nCan I leave a message for her?\n(我可以留言給她嗎？)\nI sent you a text message last night.\n(我昨晚傳了簡訊給你。)"],["metal","metal(n./adj.)金屬、金屬的\nmetallic(adj.)金屬的\nheavy metal 重金屬\nmetal box 金屬盒\nGold and silver are metals.\n(金和銀都是金屬。)\nThe cookies come in a metal box.\n(餅乾裝在金屬盒裡。)"],["meter","meter(n.)公尺、計量器\n(無詞性變化)\nsquare meter 平方公尺\nparking meter 停車計時器\nThe pool is 50 meters long.\n(這座游泳池長五十公尺。)\nHe ran 100 meters in 12 seconds.\n(他十二秒跑完一百公尺。)"],["method","method(n.)方法、方式\nmethodical(adj.)有條理的\nteaching method 教學方法\nscientific method 科學方法\nThis is a good method for learning words.\n(這是學單字的好方法。)\nWe used a new method in the experiment.\n(我們在實驗中使用了一種新方法。)"],["midnight","midnight(n.)午夜、半夜十二點\n(無詞性變化)\nat midnight 在午夜\nmidnight snack 宵夜\nI went to bed after midnight.\n(我過了半夜才去睡覺。)\nLet's have a midnight snack.\n(我們來吃宵夜吧。)"],["mile","mile(n.)英里、哩\nmileage(n.)里程數\nmiles away 遠在數英里外\nmiles per hour 每小時英里數\nThe beach is two miles from here.\n(海灘離這裡兩英里。)\nHe walks three miles every day.\n(他每天走三英里。)"],["military","military(adj./n.)軍事的、軍隊\n(無詞性變化)\nmilitary service 兵役\nmilitary base 軍事基地\nMy brother is doing his military service.\n(我哥哥正在服兵役。)\nThere is a military base near the coast.\n(海岸附近有一個軍事基地。)"],["minor","minor(adj./n.)較小的、次要的、未成年人\nminority(n.)少數\nminor problem 小問題\nminor injury 輕傷\nIt's only a minor problem.\n(這只是個小問題。)\nHe had a minor injury in the game.\n(他在比賽中受了輕傷。)"],["minority","minority(n.)少數、少數族群\nminor(adj.)較小的\nin the minority 屬於少數\nminority group 少數族群\nOnly a minority of students voted no.\n(只有少數學生投反對票。)\nWe should respect minority groups.\n(我們應該尊重少數族群。)"],["mirror","mirror(n./v.)鏡子、反映\n(無詞性變化)\nlook in the mirror 照鏡子\nrearview mirror 後照鏡\nShe looked at herself in the mirror.\n(她照鏡子看著自己。)\nThe lake mirrored the blue sky.\n(湖面倒映著藍天。)"],["mix","mix(n./v.)混合、混合物、相處\nmixture(n.)混合物\nmixed(adj.)混合的、複雜的\nmix up 混淆、搞混\nmixed feelings 百感交集\nMix the flour and the eggs together.\n(把麵粉和蛋混在一起。)\nI always mix up the twins.\n(我總是把那對雙胞胎搞混。)"],["mixture","mixture(n.)混合物、混合\nmix(v.)混合\na mixture of …的混合\ncake mixture 蛋糕糊\nPour the mixture into the pan.\n(把混合物倒進烤盤。)\nI felt a mixture of joy and fear.\n(我感到既開心又害怕。)"],["model","model(n./v.)模型、模範、模特兒、做模型\n(無詞性變化)\nrole model 榜樣\nfashion model 時裝模特兒\nMy father is my role model.\n(我爸爸是我的榜樣。)\nHe built a model of a ship.\n(他做了一個船的模型。)"],["mood","mood(n.)心情、情緒、氣氛\nmoody(adj.)喜怒無常的\nin a good mood 心情好\nin the mood for 有心情做……\nShe is in a good mood today.\n(她今天心情很好。)\nI'm not in the mood for jokes.\n(我現在沒心情開玩笑。)"],["mop","mop(n./v.)拖把、用拖把拖\n(無詞性變化)\nmop the floor 拖地\nmop up 擦乾\nI mop the floor every weekend.\n(我每個週末拖地。)\nPlease mop up the spilled milk.\n(請把灑出來的牛奶擦乾。)"],["motion","motion(n.)動作、移動、提議\nmotionless(adj.)靜止不動的\nin slow motion 以慢動作\nmotion sickness 暈車、暈船\nThey showed the goal in slow motion.\n(他們用慢動作重播了那次進球。)\nI always get motion sickness on boats.\n(我搭船總是會暈船。)"],["motorcycle","motorcycle(n.)機車、摩托車\nmotorcyclist(n.)騎機車的人\nride a motorcycle 騎機車\nmotorcycle helmet 機車安全帽\nMy father rides a motorcycle to work.\n(我爸爸騎機車上班。)\nAlways wear a helmet on a motorcycle.\n(騎機車一定要戴安全帽。)"],["mug","mug(n.)馬克杯\n(無詞性變化)\ncoffee mug 咖啡杯\na mug of 一杯……\nHe drinks a mug of coffee every morning.\n(他每天早上喝一杯咖啡。)\nI bought a mug as a gift.\n(我買了一個馬克杯當禮物。)"],["musical","musical(adj./n.)音樂的、有音樂天分的、音樂劇\nmusic(n.)音樂\nmusician(n.)音樂家\nmusical instrument 樂器\nBroadway musical 百老匯音樂劇\nCan you play any musical instruments?\n(你會演奏任何樂器嗎？)\nWe saw a musical in New York.\n(我們在紐約看了一齣音樂劇。)"],["musician","musician(n.)音樂家、樂手\nmusic(n.)音樂\nmusical(adj.)音樂的\nstreet musician 街頭藝人\ntalented musician 有天分的音樂家\nA street musician was playing the violin.\n(一位街頭藝人在拉小提琴。)\nHer dream is to become a musician.\n(她的夢想是成為音樂家。)"],["nail","nail(n.)指甲、釘子\n(無詞性變化)\nnail polish 指甲油\nbite one's nails 咬指甲\nStop biting your nails.\n(別再咬指甲了。)\nHe hit the nail with a hammer.\n(他用鐵鎚敲釘子。)"],["narrow","narrow(adj./v.)狹窄的、勉強的、使變窄\nnarrowly(adv.)勉強地、險些\nnarrow street 狹窄的街道\nnarrow escape 九死一生\nThe street is too narrow for buses.\n(這條街太窄，公車開不進來。)\nThey won by a narrow margin.\n(他們險勝。)"],["nation","nation(n.)國家、民族\nnational(adj.)國家的、全國的\nnationality(n.)國籍\nthe whole nation 全國\ndeveloping nation 開發中國家\nThe whole nation watched the game.\n(全國人民都在看這場比賽。)\nThe United Nations has many member nations.\n(聯合國有許多會員國。)"],["natural","natural(adj.)自然的、天然的、天生的\nnature(n.)自然\nnaturally(adv.)自然地\nnatural resources 天然資源\nnatural disaster 天災\nEarthquakes are natural disasters.\n(地震是天然災害。)\nIt's natural to feel nervous before a test.\n(考試前感到緊張是很自然的。)"],["naughty","naughty(adj.)頑皮的、淘氣的\n(無詞性變化)\nnaughty boy 頑皮的男孩\nnaughty behavior 淘氣的行為\nThe naughty boy broke the window.\n(那個頑皮的男孩打破了窗戶。)\nDon't be naughty in class.\n(上課不要調皮。)"],["nearby","nearby(adj./adv.)附近的、在附近\nnear(prep./adj.)在……附近、近的\nnearby store 附近的商店\nlive nearby 住在附近\nIs there a bank nearby?\n(附近有銀行嗎？)\nWe went to a nearby park.\n(我們去了附近的公園。)"],["nearly","nearly(adv.)幾乎、差不多\nnear(adj.)近的\nnearly all 幾乎全部\nnearly forget 差點忘記\nIt's nearly ten o'clock.\n(快十點了。)\nI nearly missed the bus.\n(我差點錯過公車。)"],["necessary","necessary(adj.)必要的、必需的\nnecessity(n.)必需品、必要\nnecessarily(adv.)必然地\nif necessary 必要的話\nnecessary for 對……是必要的\nWater is necessary for life.\n(水是生命所必需的。)\nCall me if necessary.\n(必要的話打電話給我。)"],["necklace","necklace(n.)項鍊\n(無詞性變化)\nsilver necklace 銀項鍊\ngold necklace 金項鍊\nShe wears a gold necklace.\n(她戴著一條金項鍊。)\nHe bought his mom a necklace.\n(他買了一條項鍊給媽媽。)"],["needle","needle(n.)針、指針\n(無詞性變化)\nneedle and thread 針線\nlike looking for a needle in a haystack 大海撈針\nShe sewed the button with a needle.\n(她用針把鈕扣縫上。)\nFinding him in this crowd is like looking for a needle in a haystack.\n(在這人群中找他就像大海撈針。)"],["negative","negative(adj./n.)負面的、否定的、陰性的\nnegatively(adv.)負面地\nnegative effect 負面影響\ntest negative 檢驗呈陰性\nToo much screen time has a negative effect.\n(太多螢幕時間會有負面影響。)\nDon't be so negative about everything.\n(不要對每件事都這麼消極。)"],["neighbor","neighbor(n.)鄰居\nneighborhood(n.)街坊、鄰近地區\nnext-door neighbor 隔壁鄰居\nfriendly neighbor 友善的鄰居\nOur neighbors are very friendly.\n(我們的鄰居很友善。)\nMy next-door neighbor has a big dog.\n(我隔壁鄰居養了一隻大狗。)"],["neither","neither(adj./adv./pron./conj.)兩者都不、也不\n(無詞性變化)\nneither A nor B 既不是A也不是B\nme neither 我也不\nNeither of my parents can swim.\n(我爸媽兩個都不會游泳。)\n'I don't like it.' 'Me neither.'\n('我不喜歡。' '我也不喜歡。')"],["nephew","nephew(n.)姪子、外甥\nniece(n.)姪女、外甥女\nlittle nephew 小姪子\nmy nephew's birthday 我姪子的生日\nMy nephew is three years old.\n(我的姪子三歲了。)\nI bought a toy for my nephew.\n(我買了一個玩具給我外甥。)"],["nerve","nerve(n.)神經、勇氣、膽量\nnervous(adj.)緊張的\nget on one's nerves 惹某人心煩\nhave the nerve to 有膽量做……\nHis loud music gets on my nerves.\n(他大聲的音樂讓我很煩。)\nI didn't have the nerve to ask her.\n(我沒有勇氣問她。)"],["nervous","nervous(adj.)緊張的、神經的\nnerve(n.)神經\nnervously(adv.)緊張地\nfeel nervous 感到緊張\nnervous system 神經系統\nI always feel nervous before exams.\n(我考試前總是很緊張。)\nDon't be nervous. You'll do fine.\n(別緊張，你會表現得很好。)"],["network","network(n./v.)網路、網絡、建立人脈\nnetworking(n.)建立人脈\nsocial network 社群網絡\nnetwork connection 網路連線\nThe network connection is very slow today.\n(今天網路連線非常慢。)\nTaipei has a good MRT network.\n(台北有完善的捷運網。)"],["niece","niece(n.)姪女、外甥女\nnephew(n.)姪子、外甥\nlittle niece 小姪女\nmy niece's school 我外甥女的學校\nMy niece loves drawing.\n(我的姪女很愛畫畫。)\nI took my niece to the zoo.\n(我帶外甥女去動物園。)"],["nod","nod(n./v.)點頭、打瞌睡\n(無詞性變化)\nnod one's head 點頭\nnod off 打瞌睡\nHe nodded his head to say yes.\n(他點頭表示同意。)\nI nodded off in class.\n(我上課時打瞌睡了。)"],["none","none(pron./adv.)沒有任何人或物、一點也不\n(無詞性變化)\nnone of 沒有一個\nnone of your business 不關你的事\nNone of my friends came.\n(我的朋友一個都沒來。)\nThat's none of your business.\n(那不關你的事。)"],["noodle","noodle(n.)麵條\n(無詞性變化)\nbeef noodles 牛肉麵\ninstant noodles 泡麵\nBeef noodles are my favorite food.\n(牛肉麵是我最喜歡的食物。)\nDon't eat instant noodles every day.\n(不要每天都吃泡麵。)"],["nor","nor(conj.)也不\n(無詞性變化)\nneither A nor B 既非A也非B\nnor do I 我也不\nHe can neither read nor write.\n(他既不會讀也不會寫。)\n'I don't eat meat.' 'Nor do I.'\n('我不吃肉。' '我也不吃。')"],["northern","northern(adj.)北方的、北部的\nnorth(n.)北方\nnorthern Taiwan 北台灣\nNorthern Hemisphere 北半球\nKeelung is in northern Taiwan.\n(基隆位在北台灣。)\nIt is winter in the Northern Hemisphere now.\n(北半球現在是冬天。)"],["notebook","notebook(n.)筆記本、筆記型電腦\n(無詞性變化)\nnotebook computer 筆記型電腦\nwrite in a notebook 寫在筆記本上\nWrite the new words in your notebook.\n(把新單字寫在筆記本上。)\nI left my notebook at school.\n(我把筆記本留在學校了。)"],["novel","novel(n./adj.)小說、新穎的\nnovelist(n.)小說家\nnovelty(n.)新奇\nread a novel 讀小說\nnovel idea 新穎的想法\nI'm reading a novel by Jin Yong.\n(我正在讀金庸的小說。)\nThat's a novel idea!\n(那是個新穎的點子！)"],["nut","nut(n.)堅果、螺帽、怪人\nnutty(adj.)有堅果味的、古怪的\nnut allergy 堅果過敏\na hard nut to crack 難題、難搞的人\nSquirrels like to eat nuts.\n(松鼠喜歡吃堅果。)\nThis math problem is a hard nut to crack.\n(這道數學題是個難題。)"],["obey","obey(v.)服從、遵守\nobedient(adj.)順從的\nobedience(n.)服從\nobey the rules 遵守規則\nobey the law 守法\nStudents must obey the school rules.\n(學生必須遵守校規。)\nThe dog always obeys its owner.\n(那隻狗總是聽主人的話。)"],["object","object(n./v.)物體、目標、受詞、反對\nobjection(n.)反對\nobjective(adj./n.)客觀的、目標\nobject to 反對\nflying object 飛行物體\nMy parents objected to the plan.\n(我爸媽反對這個計畫。)\nThere is a strange object in the sky.\n(天空中有一個奇怪的物體。)"],["obvious","obvious(adj.)明顯的\nobviously(adv.)明顯地\nobvious reason 明顯的理由\nit is obvious that 很明顯的是\nIt is obvious that he is lying.\n(很明顯他在說謊。)\nShe was obviously very tired.\n(她顯然非常累。)"],["occur","occur(v.)發生、出現、想到\noccurrence(n.)發生、事件\noccur to 想到\naccidents occur 意外發生\nThe accident occurred late at night.\n(那起意外發生在深夜。)\nIt never occurred to me to ask him.\n(我從沒想過要問他。)"],["ocean","ocean(n.)海洋\noceanic(adj.)海洋的\nPacific Ocean 太平洋\nocean view 海景\nTaiwan is in the Pacific Ocean.\n(台灣位於太平洋。)\nWe stayed in a room with an ocean view.\n(我們住在有海景的房間。)"],["offer","offer(v./n.)提供、提議、出價\n(無詞性變化)\njob offer 工作機會\noffer help 提供幫助\nHe offered me a cup of tea.\n(他請我喝一杯茶。)\nShe got a job offer from a big company.\n(她得到了一家大公司的工作機會。)"],["official","official(adj./n.)官方的、正式的、官員\nofficially(adv.)正式地\noffice(n.)辦公室、職位\nofficial language 官方語言\ngovernment official 政府官員\nEnglish is an official language in India.\n(英語是印度的官方語言之一。)\nTwo government officials visited our school.\n(兩位政府官員參訪了我們學校。)"],["operate","operate(v.)操作、運轉、動手術\noperation(n.)手術、操作\noperator(n.)操作員\noperate a machine 操作機器\noperate on 為…動手術\nDo you know how to operate this machine?\n(你知道怎麼操作這台機器嗎？)\nThe doctor will operate on him tomorrow.\n(醫生明天將為他動手術。)"],["operator","operator(n.)操作員、接線生、業者\noperate(v.)操作\ntelephone operator 電話接線生\ntour operator 旅行業者\nThe operator connected my call.\n(接線生幫我接通了電話。)\nHe works as a machine operator.\n(他的工作是機器操作員。)"],["opinion","opinion(n.)意見、看法\n(無詞性變化)\nin my opinion 依我看\npublic opinion 輿論\nIn my opinion, the movie was too long.\n(依我看，那部電影太長了。)\nWhat is your opinion about this?\n(你對這件事有什麼看法？)"],["ordinary","ordinary(adj.)普通的、平常的\nordinarily(adv.)通常\nordinary people 普通人\nout of the ordinary 不尋常的\nIt was just an ordinary day.\n(那只是平凡的一天。)\nNothing out of the ordinary happened.\n(沒有發生什麼不尋常的事。)"],["organ","organ(n.)器官、風琴\norganic(adj.)有機的、器官的\ninternal organs 內臟\norgan donation 器官捐贈\nThe heart is an important organ.\n(心臟是一個重要的器官。)\nShe plays the organ at church.\n(她在教堂彈風琴。)"],["organization","organization(n.)組織、機構、團體\norganize(v.)組織、安排\norganizer(n.)主辦者\nnon-profit organization 非營利組織\ninternational organization 國際組織\nShe works for a non-profit organization.\n(她在一個非營利組織工作。)\nThe WHO is an international organization.\n(世界衛生組織是一個國際組織。)"],["origin","origin(n.)起源、出身\noriginal(adj.)原始的、原創的\noriginally(adv.)原本\ncountry of origin 原產國\nthe origin of 起源\nDo you know the origin of this word?\n(你知道這個字的起源嗎？)\nThe country of origin is on the label.\n(原產國標示在標籤上。)"],["owner","owner(n.)擁有者、主人\nown(v.)擁有\nownership(n.)所有權\nshop owner 店主\ndog owner 狗主人\nThe shop owner is very friendly.\n(那位店主很友善。)\nWho is the owner of this bike?\n(這台腳踏車的主人是誰？)"],["pain","pain(n./v.)疼痛、痛苦、使痛苦\npainful(adj.)疼痛的\npainless(adj.)無痛的\nfeel pain 感到疼痛\na pain in the neck 討厭的人事物\nI have a pain in my back.\n(我背痛。)\nNo pain, no gain.\n(不勞則無獲。)"],["painful","painful(adj.)疼痛的、令人痛苦的\npain(n.)疼痛\npainfully(adv.)痛苦地\npainful memory 痛苦的回憶\npainful experience 痛苦的經驗\nMy leg is still painful after the fall.\n(跌倒之後我的腿還在痛。)\nLosing her pet was a painful experience.\n(失去寵物對她來說是痛苦的經驗。)"],["painting","painting(n.)畫、繪畫\npaint(v.)畫\npainter(n.)畫家\noil painting 油畫\nfamous painting 名畫\nThis oil painting is very old.\n(這幅油畫非常古老。)\nPainting is my favorite hobby.\n(畫畫是我最喜歡的嗜好。)"],["pajamas","pajamas(n.)睡衣褲\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of pajamas 一套睡衣\nin pajamas 穿著睡衣\nHe came down in his pajamas.\n(他穿著睡衣走下樓來。)\nI bought a new pair of pajamas.\n(我買了一套新睡衣。)"],["pale","pale(adj.)蒼白的、淺色的\npaleness(n.)蒼白\nturn pale 臉色發白\npale blue 淺藍色\nYou look pale. Are you sick?\n(你臉色蒼白，生病了嗎？)\nShe turned pale when she heard the news.\n(她聽到消息時臉色發白。)"],["pan","pan(n.)平底鍋\n(無詞性變化)\nfrying pan 平底煎鍋\npots and pans 鍋碗瓢盆\nHeat some oil in a frying pan.\n(在平底鍋裡加熱一些油。)\nDad washed all the pots and pans.\n(爸爸洗了所有的鍋子。)"],["panda","panda(n.)貓熊\n(無詞性變化)\ngiant panda 大貓熊\nbaby panda 貓熊寶寶\nWe saw a giant panda at the zoo.\n(我們在動物園看到一隻大貓熊。)\nThe baby panda is very cute.\n(那隻貓熊寶寶非常可愛。)"],["papaya","papaya(n.)木瓜\n(無詞性變化)\npapaya milk 木瓜牛奶\nripe papaya 熟木瓜\nI love drinking papaya milk.\n(我很喜歡喝木瓜牛奶。)\nThis papaya is sweet and ripe.\n(這顆木瓜又甜又熟。)"],["pardon","pardon(n./v.)原諒、赦免\n(無詞性變化)\npardon me 對不起、請再說一遍\nI beg your pardon 請再說一次\nPardon me, could you say that again?\n(對不起，你可以再說一次嗎？)\nThe king pardoned the prisoner.\n(國王赦免了那名囚犯。)"],["participate","participate(v.)參與、參加\nparticipation(n.)參與\nparticipant(n.)參加者\nparticipate in 參加\nactively participate 積極參與\nAll students should participate in class.\n(所有學生都應該參與課堂活動。)\nOver 100 teams participated in the contest.\n(超過一百隊參加了這場比賽。)"],["particular","particular(adj.)特定的、特別的、挑剔的\nparticularly(adv.)特別地\nin particular 特別、尤其\nbe particular about 對…挑剔\nIs there anything in particular you want?\n(你有特別想要什麼嗎？)\nShe is very particular about food.\n(她對食物非常挑剔。)"],["partner","partner(n.)夥伴、搭檔、合夥人\npartnership(n.)合夥關係\nbusiness partner 生意夥伴\ndance partner 舞伴\nFind a partner and practice the dialogue.\n(找個搭檔練習這段對話。)\nHe is my business partner.\n(他是我的生意夥伴。)"],["password","password(n.)密碼、口令\n(無詞性變化)\nenter a password 輸入密碼\nchange one's password 更改密碼\nPlease enter your password.\n(請輸入你的密碼。)\nYou should change your password often.\n(你應該經常更換密碼。)"],["paste","paste(n./v.)漿糊、醬、貼上\n(無詞性變化)\ncopy and paste 複製貼上\ntomato paste 番茄醬(糊)\nCopy and paste the text into the file.\n(把文字複製貼上到檔案裡。)\nAdd some tomato paste to the soup.\n(在湯裡加一些番茄糊。)"],["path","path(n.)小徑、道路、路線\n(無詞性變化)\nbike path 自行車道\ncareer path 職涯道路\nWe walked along the path by the river.\n(我們沿著河邊的小徑散步。)\nHe chose a different career path.\n(他選擇了一條不同的職涯道路。)"],["patient","patient(n./adj.)病人、有耐心的\npatience(n.)耐心\npatiently(adv.)耐心地\nbe patient with 對…有耐心\ncancer patient 癌症病人\nOur teacher is patient with us.\n(我們老師對我們很有耐心。)\nThe doctor has many patients today.\n(醫生今天有很多病人。)"],["pattern","pattern(n./v.)模式、圖案、仿造\n(無詞性變化)\nsleep pattern 睡眠模式\nflower pattern 花朵圖案\nHer dress has a flower pattern.\n(她的洋裝有花朵圖案。)\nTry to find the pattern in these numbers.\n(試著找出這些數字的規律。)"],["peace","peace(n.)和平、平靜\npeaceful(adj.)和平的、寧靜的\nworld peace 世界和平\npeace of mind 心安\nWe all hope for world peace.\n(我們都希望世界和平。)\nLeave me in peace, please.\n(請讓我靜一靜。)"],["peaceful","peaceful(adj.)和平的、寧靜的\npeace(n.)和平\npeacefully(adv.)平靜地\npeaceful life 平靜的生活\npeaceful village 寧靜的村莊\nThey live a peaceful life in the country.\n(他們在鄉下過著平靜的生活。)\nThe baby is sleeping peacefully.\n(寶寶正安詳地睡著。)"],["peach","peach(n.)桃子\n(無詞性變化)\npeach tree 桃樹\npeach juice 桃子汁\nThese peaches are sweet and juicy.\n(這些桃子又甜又多汁。)\nThere is a peach tree in our yard.\n(我們院子裡有一棵桃樹。)"],["peak","peak(n./v.)山頂、高峰、達到頂點\n(無詞性變化)\npeak hours 尖峰時段\nreach the peak 達到高峰\nThe MRT is crowded during peak hours.\n(捷運在尖峰時段很擁擠。)\nThey finally reached the peak of the mountain.\n(他們終於登上了山頂。)"],["pear","pear(n.)梨子\n(無詞性變化)\nAsian pear 水梨\npear tree 梨樹\nI bought some pears at the market.\n(我在市場買了一些梨子。)\nThis pear is very juicy.\n(這顆梨子很多汁。)"],["per","per(prep.)每、每一\n(無詞性變化)\nper hour 每小時\nper person 每人\nThe tickets cost 300 dollars per person.\n(門票每人三百元。)\nThe car was going 80 kilometers per hour.\n(那輛車以每小時八十公里行駛。)"],["perfect","perfect(adj./v./n.)完美的、使完美、完成式\nperfectly(adv.)完美地、完全地\nperfection(n.)完美\nperfect weather 完美的天氣\nperfectly fine 完全沒問題\nPractice makes perfect.\n(熟能生巧。)\nThe weather is perfect for a picnic.\n(這種天氣最適合野餐。)"],["period","period(n.)時期、期間、節課、句點\nperiodic(adj.)週期性的\na period of time 一段時間\nclass period 一節課\nHe lived in Japan for a short period.\n(他在日本住了一小段時間。)\nWe have math in the third period.\n(我們第三節是數學課。)"],["personal","personal(adj.)個人的、私人的\npersonally(adv.)就個人而言、親自\nperson(n.)人\npersonal information 個人資料\npersonal opinion 個人意見\nDon't share your personal information online.\n(不要在網路上分享你的個人資料。)\nPersonally, I prefer tea to coffee.\n(就我個人而言，我比較喜歡茶而不是咖啡。)"],["personality","personality(n.)個性、人格、名人\npersonal(adj.)個人的\nstrong personality 個性強烈\nTV personality 電視名人\nShe has a warm and friendly personality.\n(她個性溫暖又友善。)\nThe twins have very different personalities.\n(那對雙胞胎個性非常不同。)"],["phrase","phrase(n./v.)片語、措辭、用言語表達\n(無詞性變化)\nuseful phrase 實用片語\nphrase book 常用語手冊\nLearn these useful English phrases.\n(學會這些實用的英文片語。)\nHe phrased his question very politely.\n(他用很有禮貌的措辭提出問題。)"],["pillow","pillow(n.)枕頭\n(無詞性變化)\nsoft pillow 柔軟的枕頭\npillow fight 枕頭大戰\nI can't sleep without my pillow.\n(沒有我的枕頭我睡不著。)\nThe kids had a pillow fight.\n(孩子們玩枕頭大戰。)"],["pizza","pizza(n.)披薩\n(無詞性變化)\norder a pizza 訂披薩\na slice of pizza 一片披薩\nLet's order a pizza for dinner.\n(我們晚餐訂披薩吧。)\nI ate three slices of pizza.\n(我吃了三片披薩。)"],["plain","plain(adj./n.)簡單的、樸素的、清楚的、平原\nplainly(adv.)清楚地、樸素地\nplain white 素白色\nplain English 淺白的英文\nShe wore a plain white shirt.\n(她穿了一件素白的襯衫。)\nPlease explain it in plain English.\n(請用淺白的英文解釋。)"],["platform","platform(n.)月台、平台、講台\n(無詞性變化)\ntrain platform 火車月台\nonline platform 線上平台\nThe train leaves from Platform 3.\n(火車從第三月台發車。)\nThis online platform helps students learn.\n(這個線上平台幫助學生學習。)"],["playground","playground(n.)遊樂場、操場\n(無詞性變化)\nschool playground 學校操場\nplay on the playground 在操場玩\nThe children are playing on the playground.\n(孩子們在操場上玩。)\nThere is a new playground in the park.\n(公園裡有一個新的遊樂場。)"],["pleasant","pleasant(adj.)令人愉快的、宜人的\nplease(v.)使高興\npleasure(n.)愉快\npleasant weather 宜人的天氣\npleasant surprise 驚喜\nWe had a pleasant time at the beach.\n(我們在海邊度過了愉快的時光。)\nThe weather is pleasant today.\n(今天天氣很宜人。)"],["plus","plus(prep./n./adj.)加上、加號、優點、正的\n(無詞性變化)\nplus sign 加號\na big plus 一大優點\nTwo plus two is four.\n(二加二等於四。)\nSpeaking English is a big plus for this job.\n(會說英文是這份工作的一大加分。)"],["poem","poem(n.)詩\npoet(n.)詩人\npoetry(n.)詩(總稱)\nwrite a poem 寫詩\nlove poem 情詩\nShe wrote a poem about her mother.\n(她寫了一首關於母親的詩。)\nWe read a famous poem in class.\n(我們在課堂上讀了一首名詩。)"],["poet","poet(n.)詩人\npoem(n.)詩\npoetic(adj.)詩意的\nfamous poet 著名詩人\nyoung poet 年輕詩人\nLi Bai was a great Chinese poet.\n(李白是一位偉大的中國詩人。)\nShe dreams of becoming a poet.\n(她夢想成為一名詩人。)"],["poetry","poetry(n.)詩(總稱)、詩歌\npoem(n.)一首詩\npoetic(adj.)詩意的\nwrite poetry 寫詩\nmodern poetry 現代詩\nHe loves reading poetry.\n(他喜歡讀詩。)\nWe studied modern poetry this term.\n(我們這學期學了現代詩。)"],["poison","poison(n./v.)毒藥、毒物、下毒\npoisonous(adj.)有毒的\nfood poisoning 食物中毒\npoison gas 毒氣\nSome snakes use poison to kill their prey.\n(有些蛇用毒液殺死獵物。)\nHe got food poisoning from bad fish.\n(他吃了壞掉的魚而食物中毒。)"],["policeman/cop","policeman(n.)警察\ncop(n.)警察(口語)\npolice(n.)警方\ntraffic policeman 交通警察\ncall a cop 叫警察\nThe policeman helped the old lady cross the street.\n(警察幫老太太過馬路。)\nA cop stopped the car on the road.\n(一名警察在路上攔下那輛車。)"],["policy","policy(n.)政策、方針\n(無詞性變化)\ngovernment policy 政府政策\nschool policy 學校規定\nThe new policy helps poor families.\n(新政策幫助了貧困家庭。)\nHonesty is the best policy.\n(誠實為上策。)"],["pop","pop(n./adj.)流行音樂、砰的一聲、流行的\npopular(adj.)流行的\npop music 流行音樂\npop star 流行歌星\nI like listening to pop music.\n(我喜歡聽流行音樂。)\nShe wants to be a pop star.\n(她想成為流行歌星。)"],["population","population(n.)人口\npopulate(v.)居住於\nlarge population 人口眾多\npopulation growth 人口成長\nTaipei has a large population.\n(台北人口眾多。)\nThe population of Taiwan is about 23 million.\n(台灣的人口約兩千三百萬。)"],["pork","pork(n.)豬肉\n(無詞性變化)\nbraised pork rice 滷肉飯\npork chop 豬排\nBraised pork rice is a famous Taiwanese dish.\n(滷肉飯是有名的台灣料理。)\nI had a pork chop for lunch.\n(我午餐吃了豬排。)"],["port","port(n.)港口、港市\nportable(adj.)手提的\nfishing port 漁港\nport city 港口城市\nKaohsiung is a big port city.\n(高雄是一個大型港口城市。)\nThe ship arrived at the port in the morning.\n(那艘船早上抵達港口。)"],["pose","pose(v./n.)擺姿勢、造成、姿勢\n(無詞性變化)\npose for a photo 擺姿勢拍照\npose a problem 造成問題\nWe posed for a photo in front of the castle.\n(我們在城堡前擺姿勢拍照。)\nSmoking poses a danger to health.\n(抽菸對健康構成危險。)"],["position","position(n./v.)位置、職位、立場、放置\n(無詞性變化)\nin position 在適當位置\njob position 職位\nShe applied for the position of manager.\n(她應徵了經理的職位。)\nPlease stay in your position.\n(請待在你的位置上。)"],["positive","positive(adj./n.)正面的、積極的、確定的、陽性\npositively(adv.)積極地、肯定地\npositive attitude 積極的態度\ntest positive 檢驗呈陽性\nTry to keep a positive attitude.\n(試著保持積極的態度。)\nAre you positive that he said that?\n(你確定他說了那句話嗎？)"],["possibility","possibility(n.)可能性\npossible(adj.)可能的\npossibly(adv.)可能地\na strong possibility 很大的可能性\nthe possibility of ……的可能性\nThere is a possibility of rain tonight.\n(今晚有下雨的可能。)\nWe talked about the possibility of moving.\n(我們討論了搬家的可能性。)"],["post","post(n./v./adv.)郵件、職位、柱子、張貼、郵寄、快速地\npostal(adj.)郵政的\npost office 郵局\npost a message 發布訊息\nI need to go to the post office.\n(我需要去郵局。)\nShe posted a photo online.\n(她在網路上貼了一張照片。)"],["postcard","postcard(n.)明信片\n(無詞性變化)\nsend a postcard 寄明信片\npicture postcard 風景明信片\nI sent my friend a postcard from Japan.\n(我從日本寄了一張明信片給朋友。)\nShe collects postcards from many countries.\n(她收集許多國家的明信片。)"],["pound","pound(n.)磅(重量單位)、英鎊\n(無詞性變化)\nfive pounds 五磅\nBritish pound 英鎊\nThis bag weighs ten pounds.\n(這個袋子重十磅。)\nThe ticket costs twenty pounds.\n(這張票要二十英鎊。)"],["powerful","powerful(adj.)強大的、有權勢的、有效力的\npower(n.)力量\npowerfully(adv.)強有力地\npowerful country 強國\npowerful engine 強力引擎\nAmerica is a powerful country.\n(美國是一個強大的國家。)\nThis car has a powerful engine.\n(這輛車有強大的引擎。)"],["praise","praise(n./v.)稱讚、讚美\npraiseworthy(adj.)值得稱讚的\npraise sb. for 稱讚某人…\nhigh praise 高度讚揚\nThe teacher praised him for his hard work.\n(老師稱讚他很用功。)\nHer new book received high praise.\n(她的新書獲得高度讚揚。)"],["pray","pray(v.)祈禱、祈求\nprayer(n.)禱告、禱文\npray for 為…祈禱\npray to God 向上帝祈禱\nWe prayed for his safe return.\n(我們祈禱他平安歸來。)\nShe prays before every meal.\n(她每餐飯前都會禱告。)"],["prayer","prayer(n.)禱告、禱文、祈禱者\npray(v.)祈禱\nsay a prayer 做禱告\nmorning prayer 早禱\nShe said a prayer before bed.\n(她睡前做了禱告。)\nOur prayers were answered.\n(我們的禱告應驗了。)"],["prefer","prefer(v.)較喜歡、偏好\npreference(n.)偏好\npreferable(adj.)較好的\nprefer A to B 喜歡 A 勝過 B\nprefer to 寧願\nI prefer tea to coffee.\n(比起咖啡，我比較喜歡茶。)\nShe prefers to stay at home on weekends.\n(她週末比較喜歡待在家。)"],["president","president(n.)總統、總裁、校長、會長\npresidential(adj.)總統的\nvice president 副總統、副總裁\nelect a president 選出總統\nShe was elected president of the student council.\n(她被選為學生會會長。)\nThe president gave a speech on TV.\n(總統在電視上發表了演說。)"],["press","press(n./v.)新聞界、出版社、壓、按\npressure(n.)壓力\npress the button 按按鈕\npress conference 記者會\nPress the button to start.\n(按下按鈕開始。)\nThe mayor held a press conference today.\n(市長今天召開了記者會。)"],["pressure","pressure(n./v.)壓力、施壓\npress(v.)壓\npressure from 來自…的壓力\nblood pressure 血壓\nStudents are under a lot of pressure before exams.\n(考試前學生承受很大的壓力。)\nHis parents pressured him to study law.\n(他的父母逼他讀法律。)"],["pride","pride(n./v.)自豪、驕傲、以…自豪\nproud(adj.)自豪的\ntake pride in 以…為傲\npride oneself on 以…自豪\nHe takes pride in his work.\n(他以自己的工作為傲。)\nShe prides herself on being on time.\n(她以自己守時為傲。)"],["priest","priest(n.)神父、牧師、祭司\n(無詞性變化)\nCatholic priest 天主教神父\nbecome a priest 成為神父\nThe priest gave a talk at the church.\n(神父在教堂發表談話。)\nHe decided to become a priest.\n(他決定成為神父。)"],["primary","primary(adj.)主要的、初級的\nprimarily(adv.)主要地\nprimary school 小學\nprimary reason 主要原因\nMy brother is in primary school.\n(我弟弟在讀小學。)\nMoney was not the primary reason.\n(錢不是主要原因。)"],["prince/princess","prince(n.)王子\nprincess(n.)公主\nPrince Charming 白馬王子\nfairy-tale princess 童話公主\nThe prince fell in love with a poor girl.\n(王子愛上了一個貧窮的女孩。)\nThe little girl dressed up as a princess.\n(那個小女孩打扮成公主。)"],["principal","principal(adj./n.)主要的、校長\nprincipally(adv.)主要地\nschool principal 校長\nprincipal reason 主要原因\nThe principal gave a speech at the meeting.\n(校長在集會上發表了演說。)\nCost is the principal reason for the change.\n(成本是改變的主要原因。)"],["principle","principle(n.)原則、原理\n(無詞性變化)\nin principle 原則上\nbasic principle 基本原理\nIn principle, I agree with you.\n(原則上我同意你。)\nHe never acts against his principles.\n(他從不違背自己的原則。)"],["print","print(n./v.)印刷、列印、字體、印記\nprinter(n.)印表機\nprint out 列印出來\nin print 已出版\nPlease print out the report for me.\n(請幫我把報告印出來。)\nThe print in this book is too small.\n(這本書的字體太小了。)"],["printer","printer(n.)印表機、印刷業者\nprint(v.)列印\nlaser printer 雷射印表機\nprinter ink 印表機墨水\nThe printer is out of paper.\n(印表機沒紙了。)\nWe need to buy new printer ink.\n(我們需要買新的印表機墨水。)"],["prison","prison(n.)監獄\nprisoner(n.)囚犯\nimprison(v.)監禁\ngo to prison 入獄\nin prison 在獄中\nThe thief was sent to prison.\n(那個小偷被送進監獄。)\nHe spent five years in prison.\n(他坐了五年牢。)"],["prisoner","prisoner(n.)囚犯、俘虜\nprison(n.)監獄\nprisoner of war 戰俘\nrelease a prisoner 釋放囚犯\nThe prisoner escaped last night.\n(那名囚犯昨晚逃獄了。)\nThey took him prisoner during the war.\n(他在戰爭中被俘虜。)"],["private","private(adj.)私人的、私立的、隱私的\nprivacy(n.)隱私\nprivately(adv.)私下地\nprivate school 私立學校\nin private 私下\nShe goes to a private school.\n(她就讀私立學校。)\nCan I talk to you in private?\n(我可以私下跟你談談嗎？)"],["prize","prize(n./v.)獎品、獎、重視\n(無詞性變化)\nwin a prize 得獎\nfirst prize 首獎\nShe won first prize in the speech contest.\n(她在演講比賽中得到第一名。)\nThe Nobel Prize is a great honor.\n(諾貝爾獎是一項很高的榮譽。)"],["produce","produce(v./n.)生產、製造、農產品\nproduct(n.)產品\nproduction(n.)生產\nproducer(n.)製作人、生產者\nproduce goods 生產商品\nfresh produce 新鮮農產品\nThis factory produces cars.\n(這家工廠生產汽車。)\nThe market sells fresh produce.\n(這個市場販售新鮮農產品。)"],["production","production(n.)生產、產量、製作\nproduce(v.)生產\nproductive(adj.)多產的、有成效的\nmass production 大量生產\nproduction line 生產線\nProduction of rice was high this year.\n(今年稻米的產量很高。)\nThe factory started mass production.\n(那家工廠開始大量生產。)"],["progress","progress(n./v.)進步、進展、前進\nprogressive(adj.)進步的\nmake progress 進步\nin progress 進行中\nYou have made great progress in English.\n(你的英文進步很多。)\nThe meeting is still in progress.\n(會議仍在進行中。)"],["project","project(n.)計畫、專案、專題\n(無詞性變化)\nschool project 學校專題\nwork on a project 進行專案\nWe are working on a science project.\n(我們正在做一個科學專題。)\nThe project will take two months.\n(這個計畫將花兩個月。)"],["promise","promise(n./v.)承諾、答應\npromising(adj.)有前途的\nkeep a promise 遵守承諾\nbreak a promise 違背承諾\nI promise I won't be late again.\n(我保證不會再遲到了。)\nHe always keeps his promises.\n(他總是遵守承諾。)"],["proper","proper(adj.)適當的、正確的\nproperly(adv.)適當地、正確地\nproper way 正確的方法\nproper clothes 合適的衣服\nYou need proper shoes for hiking.\n(你健行需要合適的鞋子。)\nPlease do your homework properly.\n(請好好地做你的功課。)"],["propose","propose(v.)提議、求婚\nproposal(n.)提議、求婚\npropose a plan 提出計畫\npropose to sb. 向某人求婚\nHe proposed a new plan at the meeting.\n(他在會議上提出了一個新計畫。)\nTom proposed to his girlfriend last night.\n(湯姆昨晚向女友求婚。)"],["protect","protect(v.)保護\nprotection(n.)保護\nprotective(adj.)保護的\nprotect from 保護…免於\nprotect the environment 保護環境\nSunglasses protect your eyes from the sun.\n(太陽眼鏡保護你的眼睛不受陽光傷害。)\nWe must protect wild animals.\n(我們必須保護野生動物。)"],["protective","protective(adj.)保護的、防護的\nprotect(v.)保護\nprotection(n.)保護\nprotective clothing 防護衣\nbe protective of 對…保護欲強\nWorkers must wear protective clothing.\n(工人必須穿防護衣。)\nShe is very protective of her little brother.\n(她對弟弟非常保護。)"],["prove","prove(v.)證明、證實\nproof(n.)證據\nprove oneself 證明自己\nprove sb. wrong 證明某人錯了\nCan you prove that you were at home?\n(你能證明你當時在家嗎？)\nShe worked hard to prove herself.\n(她努力工作證明自己。)"],["provide","provide(v.)提供\nprovision(n.)供應、規定\nprovide A with B 提供 B 給 A\nprovide for 供養\nThe school provides students with free lunch.\n(學校提供學生免費午餐。)\nHe works hard to provide for his family.\n(他努力工作養家。)"],["pudding","pudding(n.)布丁\n(無詞性變化)\negg pudding 雞蛋布丁\nchocolate pudding 巧克力布丁\nI had some pudding for dessert.\n(我吃了一些布丁當甜點。)\nMy sister loves chocolate pudding.\n(我妹妹很愛巧克力布丁。)"],["pumpkin","pumpkin(n.)南瓜\n(無詞性變化)\npumpkin pie 南瓜派\npumpkin soup 南瓜湯\nWe made a pumpkin lantern for Halloween.\n(我們為萬聖節做了南瓜燈。)\nMom cooked pumpkin soup today.\n(媽媽今天煮了南瓜湯。)"],["punish(ment)","punish(v.)懲罰、punishment(n.)懲罰、處罰\n(無詞性變化)\npunish sb. for 因…懲罰某人\nsevere punishment 嚴厲的處罰\nThe teacher punished him for cheating.\n(老師因為他作弊而處罰他。)\nThe punishment was too severe.\n(這個處罰太嚴厲了。)"],["pupil","pupil(n.)學生、小學生、瞳孔\n(無詞性變化)\nprimary school pupil 小學生\nformer pupil 以前的學生\nThere are 30 pupils in the class.\n(這個班有三十名學生。)\nHer pupils got bigger in the dark.\n(她的瞳孔在黑暗中放大了。)"],["puppy","puppy(n.)小狗、幼犬\n(無詞性變化)\ncute puppy 可愛的小狗\npuppy love 初戀、青澀的愛\nWe adopted a puppy from the shelter.\n(我們從收容所領養了一隻小狗。)\nThe puppy is playing with a ball.\n(那隻小狗正在玩球。)"],["purple","purple(adj./n.)紫色的、紫色\n(無詞性變化)\npurple flowers 紫色的花\ndark purple 深紫色\nShe bought a purple umbrella.\n(她買了一把紫色的雨傘。)\nPurple is a mix of red and blue.\n(紫色是紅色和藍色混合而成的。)"],["purpose","purpose(n.)目的、用途\npurposely(adv.)故意地\non purpose 故意地\nthe purpose of ……的目的\nHe broke the window on purpose.\n(他故意打破窗戶。)\nWhat is the purpose of your visit?\n(你來訪的目的是什麼？)"],["puzzle","puzzle(n./v.)謎題、拼圖、使困惑\npuzzled(adj.)困惑的\njigsaw puzzle 拼圖\ncrossword puzzle 填字遊戲\nWe finished a 1,000-piece jigsaw puzzle.\n(我們完成了一幅一千片的拼圖。)\nHis strange answer puzzled me.\n(他奇怪的回答讓我很困惑。)"],["quality","quality(n.)品質、特質\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh quality 高品質\nquality of life 生活品質\nThis shop sells high-quality goods.\n(這家店販售高品質的商品。)\nPatience is an important quality for a teacher.\n(耐心是當老師的重要特質。)"],["quantity","quantity(n.)數量、份量\n(無詞性變化)\nlarge quantity 大量\nquality and quantity 質與量\nQuality is more important than quantity.\n(品質比數量更重要。)\nThey bought a large quantity of rice.\n(他們買了大量的米。)"],["quiz","quiz(n.)小考、測驗\n(無詞性變化)\npop quiz 突擊小考\nhave a quiz 小考\nWe have a math quiz tomorrow.\n(我們明天有數學小考。)\nThe teacher gave us a pop quiz.\n(老師給我們來了一次突擊小考。)"],["railroad/railway","railroad(n.)鐵路、鐵道\nrailway(n.)鐵路(英式)\nrailroad station 火車站\nrailroad track 鐵軌\nThe old railroad runs along the river.\n(那條老鐵路沿著河流延伸。)\nDo not walk on the railway tracks.\n(不要在鐵軌上行走。)"],["raincoat","raincoat(n.)雨衣\n(無詞性變化)\nwear a raincoat 穿雨衣\na yellow raincoat 黃色雨衣\nPut on your raincoat before you go out.\n(出門前先穿上雨衣。)\nThe little boy wore a yellow raincoat to school.\n(那個小男孩穿著黃色雨衣上學。)"],["range","range(n./v.)範圍、山脈、(在範圍內)變動\n(無詞性變化)\na wide range of 各式各樣的\nmountain range 山脈\nThe shop sells a wide range of shoes.\n(這家店賣各式各樣的鞋子。)\nPrices range from 100 to 500 dollars.\n(價格從一百元到五百元不等。)"],["rapid","rapid(adj.)快速的、迅速的\nrapidly(adv.)快速地\nrapid growth 快速成長\nrapid change 快速的變化\nThe city has seen rapid growth.\n(這座城市經歷了快速成長。)\nThe river flows rapidly after the rain.\n(下雨後河水流得很快。)"],["rare","rare(adj.)稀有的、罕見的、(肉)三分熟的\nrarely(adv.)很少、難得\na rare chance 難得的機會\nrare animals 稀有動物\nPandas are rare animals.\n(貓熊是稀有動物。)\nHe rarely eats breakfast at home.\n(他很少在家吃早餐。)"],["rat","rat(n.)老鼠、大老鼠\n(無詞性變化)\na big rat 一隻大老鼠\nrat poison 老鼠藥\nA big rat ran across the kitchen.\n(一隻大老鼠跑過廚房。)\nRats like to live in dirty places.\n(老鼠喜歡住在骯髒的地方。)"],["rather","rather(adv.)相當、寧願、而不是\n(無詞性變化)\nwould rather 寧願\nrather than 而不是\nI would rather stay home tonight.\n(我今晚寧願待在家。)\nThe test was rather easy.\n(這次考試相當簡單。)"],["reality","reality(n.)現實、真實\nreal(adj.)真實的\nrealistic(adj.)實際的、寫實的\nin reality 實際上\nface reality 面對現實\nYour dream can become a reality.\n(你的夢想可以成真。)\nIn reality, he is very shy.\n(實際上，他非常害羞。)"],["realize","realize(v.)了解、意識到、實現\nrealization(n.)領悟、實現\nrealize a dream 實現夢想\nsuddenly realize 突然意識到\nI didn't realize it was so late.\n(我沒意識到已經這麼晚了。)\nShe worked hard to realize her dream.\n(她努力實現自己的夢想。)"],["receive","receive(v.)收到、接受\nreceiver(n.)接收者、聽筒\nreceipt(n.)收據\nreceive a letter 收到信\nreceive a gift 收到禮物\nI received a letter from my aunt.\n(我收到阿姨寄來的信。)\nShe received many gifts on her birthday.\n(她生日時收到很多禮物。)"],["recent","recent(adj.)最近的、近來的\nrecently(adv.)最近\nin recent years 近幾年\nrecent news 最近的消息\nHave you seen his recent photos?\n(你看過他最近的照片嗎？)\nI have been very busy recently.\n(我最近很忙。)"],["record","record(n./v.)紀錄、唱片、記錄、錄製\nrecorder(n.)錄音機、直笛\nrecording(n.)錄音、錄影\nbreak a record 打破紀錄\nkeep a record 做紀錄\nHe broke the school record.\n(他打破了學校紀錄。)\nShe recorded the song on her phone.\n(她用手機錄下了這首歌。)"],["recover","recover(v.)恢復、康復、找回\nrecovery(n.)康復、恢復\nrecover from 從…中恢復\nfully recover 完全康復\nHe recovered from a bad cold.\n(他從重感冒中康復了。)\nThe police recovered the stolen bike.\n(警方找回了被偷的腳踏車。)"],["refrigerator/fridge","refrigerator(n.)冰箱\nfridge(n.)冰箱(口語)\nin the fridge 在冰箱裡\nfridge door 冰箱門\nPut the milk in the refrigerator.\n(把牛奶放進冰箱。)\nThere is some cake in the fridge.\n(冰箱裡有一些蛋糕。)"],["refuse","refuse(v.)拒絕\nrefusal(n.)拒絕\nrefuse to 拒絕做…\nrefuse an offer 拒絕提議\nHe refused to answer the question.\n(他拒絕回答這個問題。)\nShe refused my offer of help.\n(她拒絕了我的幫忙。)"],["regard","regard(n./v.)關心、尊重、將…視為\nregarding(prep.)關於\nregard A as B 把A視為B\nbest regards 敬祝安好(信末用語)\nWe regard him as our leader.\n(我們把他視為我們的領袖。)\nShe has great regard for her teacher.\n(她非常尊敬她的老師。)"],["region","region(n.)地區、區域\nregional(adj.)地區的\nmountain region 山區\na cold region 寒冷地區\nThis region is famous for tea.\n(這個地區以茶聞名。)\nFew people live in that cold region.\n(很少人住在那個寒冷地區。)"],["regular","regular(adj./n.)規律的、定期的、一般的、常客\nregularly(adv.)規律地、定期地\nregular exercise 規律運動\na regular customer 常客\nRegular exercise keeps you healthy.\n(規律運動讓你保持健康。)\nHe is a regular at this coffee shop.\n(他是這家咖啡店的常客。)"],["reject","reject(v.)拒絕、駁回\nrejection(n.)拒絕\nreject an idea 否決一個想法\nreject a plan 否決計畫\nThe teacher rejected my idea.\n(老師否決了我的想法。)\nHer story was rejected by the magazine.\n(她的故事被雜誌退稿了。)"],["relate","relate(v.)使有關聯、敘述\nrelated(adj.)有關的、有親屬關係的\nrelate to 與…有關、能理解\nbe related to 與…有關\nThis movie relates to real life.\n(這部電影和真實生活有關。)\nI can relate to how you feel.\n(我能理解你的感受。)"],["relation","relation(n.)關係、親戚\nrelative(n./adj.)親戚、相對的\nin relation to 關於、與…相比\nclose relations 密切的關係\nThe two countries have good relations.\n(這兩個國家關係良好。)\nIs he a relation of yours?\n(他是你的親戚嗎？)"],["relationship","relationship(n.)關係、人際關係\n(無詞性變化)\na close relationship 親密的關係\nbuild a relationship 建立關係\nShe has a good relationship with her parents.\n(她和父母的關係很好。)\nTrust is important in any relationship.\n(信任在任何關係中都很重要。)"],["religion","religion(n.)宗教\nreligious(adj.)宗教的、虔誠的\nfreedom of religion 宗教自由\nworld religions 世界各大宗教\nPeople of many religions live here.\n(許多不同宗教的人住在這裡。)\nReligion is part of their culture.\n(宗教是他們文化的一部分。)"],["remove","remove(v.)移除、拿走、脫掉\nremoval(n.)移除\nremove a stain 去除汙漬\nremove your shoes 脫鞋\nPlease remove your shoes at the door.\n(請在門口脫鞋。)\nThis soap can remove the stain.\n(這種肥皂可以去除汙漬。)"],["rent","rent(n./v.)租金、租用、出租\nrental(n./adj.)租金、出租的\npay the rent 付房租\nrent a car 租車\nWe rented a car for the trip.\n(我們為這趟旅行租了一輛車。)\nThe rent here is very high.\n(這裡的房租很高。)"],["repair","repair(n./v.)修理、修補\n(無詞性變化)\nrepair shop 修理店\nunder repair 修理中\nMy father repaired the broken chair.\n(我爸爸修好了那張壞掉的椅子。)\nThe road is under repair now.\n(這條路正在整修中。)"],["reply","reply(n./v.)回答、回覆\n(無詞性變化)\nreply to 回覆…\nin reply 作為回答\nPlease reply to my email soon.\n(請盡快回覆我的電子郵件。)\nI am still waiting for his reply.\n(我還在等他的回覆。)"],["require(ment)","require(v.)需要、要求、requirement(n.)需求、必要條件\nrequired(adj.)必需的、必修的\nbe required to 被要求做…\nmeet the requirements 符合要求\nStudents are required to wear uniforms.\n(學生被要求穿制服。)\nHe meets all the job requirements.\n(他符合所有的工作條件。)"],["respect","respect(n./v.)尊敬、尊重、方面\nrespectful(adj.)恭敬的\nrespectable(adj.)值得尊敬的、體面的\nshow respect 表示尊敬\nin many respects 在許多方面\nWe should respect our parents.\n(我們應該尊敬父母。)\nHe has the respect of all his students.\n(他受到所有學生的尊敬。)"],["respond","respond(v.)回應、回答、反應\nresponse(n.)回應、反應\nrespond to 回應…\nrespond quickly 迅速回應\nShe didn't respond to my message.\n(她沒有回應我的訊息。)\nThe doctors responded quickly.\n(醫生們迅速做出反應。)"],["responsible","responsible(adj.)負責的、應負責任的\nresponsibility(n.)責任\nbe responsible for 對…負責\na responsible person 負責任的人\nI am responsible for cleaning the room.\n(我負責打掃房間。)\nHe is a very responsible student.\n(他是個很負責的學生。)"],["restroom","restroom(n.)廁所、洗手間\n(無詞性變化)\npublic restroom 公共廁所\ngo to the restroom 上廁所\nExcuse me, where is the restroom?\n(不好意思，請問洗手間在哪裡？)\nThe restroom is on the second floor.\n(洗手間在二樓。)"],["result","result(n./v.)結果、成績、導致、起因於\n(無詞性變化)\nas a result 結果、因此\nresult in 導致\nI was happy with my test results.\n(我對我的考試成績很滿意。)\nToo much rain resulted in floods.\n(雨量過多導致了水災。)"],["return","return(v./n.)回來、歸還、返回\n(無詞性變化)\nreturn home 回家\nin return 作為回報\nPlease return the book by Friday.\n(請在星期五前還書。)\nHe returned home late last night.\n(他昨晚很晚才回家。)"],["review","review(n./v.)複習、評論、檢討\nreviewer(n.)評論者\nreview a lesson 複習課程\nbook review 書評\nI need to review for the test.\n(我需要為考試複習。)\nThe movie got good reviews.\n(這部電影得到好評。)"],["riches","riches(n.)財富、財產\nrich(adj.)有錢的、豐富的\ngreat riches 鉅額財富\nfrom rags to riches 從貧窮到致富\nRiches cannot buy happiness.\n(財富買不到快樂。)\nThe king had great riches.\n(那位國王擁有龐大的財富。)"],["rocky","rocky(adj.)多岩石的、坎坷的\nrock(n.)岩石\na rocky beach 岩石海灘\na rocky road 崎嶇的道路\nWe walked along the rocky beach.\n(我們沿著多岩石的海灘散步。)\nThe path up the hill is rocky.\n(上山的小路多岩石。)"],["role","role(n.)角色、作用\n(無詞性變化)\nplay a role 扮演角色、發揮作用\nrole model 模範、榜樣\nShe played the main role in the play.\n(她在這齣戲裡演主角。)\nMy mother is my role model.\n(我媽媽是我的榜樣。)"],["roof","roof(n./v.)屋頂、給…蓋屋頂\n(無詞性變化)\non the roof 在屋頂上\na red roof 紅色屋頂\nA cat is sleeping on the roof.\n(一隻貓在屋頂上睡覺。)\nThe house has a red roof.\n(那棟房子有紅色的屋頂。)"],["rooster","rooster(n.)公雞\n(無詞性變化)\na rooster crows 公雞啼叫\nYear of the Rooster 雞年\nThe rooster crows every morning.\n(那隻公雞每天早上都會啼叫。)\nMy grandpa keeps a rooster on his farm.\n(我爺爺在農場養了一隻公雞。)"],["royal","royal(adj.)皇家的、王室的\nroyalty(n.)王室成員、版稅\nroyal family 皇室\nroyal palace 王宮\nThe royal family lives in that palace.\n(皇室住在那座宮殿裡。)\nWe visited a royal palace in London.\n(我們參觀了倫敦的一座王宮。)"],["rub","rub(v./n.)摩擦、揉、擦\n(無詞性變化)\nrub your eyes 揉眼睛\nrub your hands 搓手\nDon't rub your eyes with dirty hands.\n(不要用髒手揉眼睛。)\nHe rubbed his hands to keep warm.\n(他搓手取暖。)"],["rubber","rubber(n.)橡膠、橡皮擦(英式)\n(無詞性變化)\nrubber band 橡皮筋\nrubber boots 雨鞋\nThese boots are made of rubber.\n(這雙靴子是用橡膠做的。)\nCan I borrow a rubber band?\n(可以借我一條橡皮筋嗎？)"],["rude","rude(adj.)無禮的、粗魯的\nrudely(adv.)無禮地\nrudeness(n.)無禮\nbe rude to 對…無禮\na rude remark 無禮的話\nIt is rude to talk with food in your mouth.\n(嘴裡有食物時說話很沒禮貌。)\nDon't be rude to your teacher.\n(不要對老師沒禮貌。)"],["runner","runner(n.)跑者\nrun(v.)跑\na fast runner 跑得快的人\nmarathon runner 馬拉松跑者\nShe is the fastest runner in our class.\n(她是我們班跑得最快的人。)\nThousands of runners joined the race.\n(數千名跑者參加了這場賽跑。)"],["safety","safety(n.)安全\nsafe(adj.)安全的\nsafely(adv.)安全地\nsafety belt 安全帶\nfor safety reasons 基於安全理由\nSafety comes first.\n(安全第一。)\nWear a helmet for your own safety.\n(為了你自己的安全，請戴安全帽。)"],["sail","sail(v./n.)航行、帆\nsailing(n.)帆船運動、航行\nset sail 啟航\nsail across 航行橫越\nThe ship sailed across the ocean.\n(那艘船橫越大海。)\nThey set sail early in the morning.\n(他們一大早就啟航了。)"],["sailor","sailor(n.)水手、船員\nsail(v./n.)航行、帆\na young sailor 年輕水手\nsailor suit 水手服\nThe sailor has been to many countries.\n(那位水手去過很多國家。)\nThe sailors worked hard on the ship.\n(水手們在船上辛勤工作。)"],["salesperson/salesman/saleswoman","salesperson(n.)售貨員、業務員\nsalesman(n.)男售貨員、男業務員\nsaleswoman(n.)女售貨員、女業務員\ncar salesperson 汽車業務\na friendly salesperson 親切的店員\nThe salesperson showed me some new phones.\n(那位店員給我看了一些新手機。)\nMy uncle works as a car salesman.\n(我舅舅是汽車業務員。)"],["salty","salty(adj.)鹹的\nsalt(n.)鹽\nsalty food 鹹的食物\ntaste salty 嚐起來鹹\nThis soup is too salty.\n(這湯太鹹了。)\nEating salty food is bad for your health.\n(吃太鹹的食物對健康不好。)"],["sample","sample(n./v.)樣品、試吃、抽樣\n(無詞性變化)\nfree sample 免費試用品\nblood sample 血液樣本\nThe store gave out free samples of cake.\n(那家店發送蛋糕試吃品。)\nYou can sample the food before you buy it.\n(你可以先試吃再買。)"],["sand","sand(n./v.)沙、用砂紙磨\nsandy(adj.)沙質的\nsand castle 沙堡\nwhite sand 白沙\nThe kids built a sand castle on the beach.\n(孩子們在沙灘上蓋沙堡。)\nI got sand in my shoes.\n(我的鞋子裡跑進了沙子。)"],["sandwich","sandwich(n./v.)三明治、夾在中間\n(無詞性變化)\nham sandwich 火腿三明治\nbe sandwiched between 被夾在……之間\nI had a sandwich for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了一個三明治。)\nMy seat was sandwiched between two big men.\n(我的座位被夾在兩個大塊頭中間。)"],["satisfy","satisfy(v.)使滿意、滿足\nsatisfaction(n.)滿意\nsatisfied(adj.)感到滿意的\nsatisfy needs 滿足需求\nbe satisfied with 對……滿意\nNothing can satisfy him.\n(沒有什麼能讓他滿意。)\nI'm satisfied with my test score.\n(我對我的考試成績很滿意。)"],["saw","saw(v./n.)鋸、鋸子\n(無詞性變化)\nsaw wood 鋸木頭\nelectric saw 電鋸\nHe used a saw to cut the wood.\n(他用鋸子鋸木頭。)\nDad sawed the branch off the tree.\n(爸爸把樹枝鋸了下來。)"],["scare","scare(v./n.)驚嚇、恐慌\nscary(adj.)可怕的\nscared(adj.)害怕的\nscare away 嚇跑\ngive someone a scare 嚇某人一跳\nThe loud noise scared the birds away.\n(巨大的聲響把鳥嚇跑了。)\nYou gave me a scare!\n(你嚇了我一跳！)"],["scared","scared(adj.)害怕的\nscare(v./n.)驚嚇\nbe scared of 害怕\nscared to death 嚇得要死\nMy little sister is scared of dogs.\n(我妹妹怕狗。)\nI was scared to walk home alone at night.\n(我很怕晚上獨自走路回家。)"],["scene","scene(n.)場景、現場、景色\nscenery(n.)風景\nscenic(adj.)風景優美的\nbehind the scenes 在幕後\nthe scene of the accident 事故現場\nThe police arrived at the scene quickly.\n(警察很快就抵達現場。)\nThis is my favorite scene in the movie.\n(這是我在電影中最喜歡的一幕。)"],["schedule","schedule(n./v.)時間表、行程、安排\n(無詞性變化)\non schedule 按時\nbusy schedule 忙碌的行程\nThe train arrived on schedule.\n(火車準時抵達。)\nThe meeting is scheduled for Friday.\n(會議安排在週五。)"],["scooter","scooter(n.)機車、速克達\n(無詞性變化)\nride a scooter 騎機車\nelectric scooter 電動機車\nMany people in Taiwan ride scooters to work.\n(台灣很多人騎機車上班。)\nMy dad bought an electric scooter.\n(我爸爸買了一台電動機車。)"],["score","score(n./v.)分數、得分\nscorer(n.)得分者\nhigh score 高分\nscore a goal 射門得分\nShe got a high score on the English test.\n(她英文考試考了高分。)\nHe scored two goals in the game.\n(他在比賽中踢進兩球。)"],["screen","screen(n.)螢幕、屏風\n(無詞性變化)\ncomputer screen 電腦螢幕\nbig screen 大螢幕\nDon't look at the screen for too long.\n(不要盯著螢幕太久。)\nWe watched the game on a big screen.\n(我們在大螢幕上看比賽。)"],["seafood","seafood(n.)海鮮\n(無詞性變化)\nseafood restaurant 海鮮餐廳\nfresh seafood 新鮮海鮮\nKeelung is famous for its seafood.\n(基隆以海鮮聞名。)\nWe had dinner at a seafood restaurant.\n(我們在一家海鮮餐廳吃晚餐。)"],["search","search(n./v.)搜尋、尋找\n(無詞性變化)\nsearch for 尋找\nin search of 尋找\nI searched for the word online.\n(我上網搜尋這個字。)\nThey went in search of the lost dog.\n(他們去尋找走失的狗。)"],["secondary","secondary(adj.)次要的、中等(教育)的\n(無詞性變化)\nsecondary school 中學\nof secondary importance 次要的\nMoney is of secondary importance to him.\n(對他來說錢是次要的。)\nShe teaches at a secondary school.\n(她在一所中學教書。)"],["secret","secret(adj./n.)祕密(的)\nsecretly(adv.)祕密地\nkeep a secret 保守祕密\nin secret 祕密地\nCan you keep a secret?\n(你能保守祕密嗎？)\nThey had a secret meeting after school.\n(他們放學後開了一場祕密會議。)"],["section","section(n.)部分、區域、段落\n(無詞性變化)\nsports section 體育版\nthe first section 第一部分\nPlease read the first section of the book.\n(請讀這本書的第一部分。)\nThe library has a large science section.\n(圖書館有一個很大的科學書區。)"],["seek","seek(v.)尋找、尋求\n(無詞性變化)\nseek help 尋求協助\nhide-and-seek 捉迷藏\nYou should seek help from your teacher.\n(你應該向老師尋求協助。)\nThe children are playing hide-and-seek.\n(孩子們在玩捉迷藏。)"],["seem","seem(v.)似乎、看起來\n(無詞性變化)\nseem to 似乎\nit seems that 看來\nYou seem tired today.\n(你今天看起來很累。)\nIt seems that it will rain soon.\n(看來快要下雨了。)"],["seesaw","seesaw(n.)蹺蹺板\n(無詞性變化)\nplay on the seesaw 玩蹺蹺板\nride a seesaw 坐蹺蹺板\nThe kids are playing on the seesaw.\n(孩子們在玩蹺蹺板。)\nThere is a seesaw in the park.\n(公園裡有一座蹺蹺板。)"],["seldom","seldom(adv.)很少、不常\n(無詞性變化)\nseldom see 很少見到\nseldom go out 很少出門\nMy father seldom watches TV.\n(我爸爸很少看電視。)\nIt seldom snows in Taipei.\n(台北很少下雪。)"],["select","select(v./adj.)選擇、挑選、精選的\nselection(n.)選擇、精選\nselective(adj.)有選擇性的\nselect a team 挑選隊伍\na select group 精選的一群人\nShe was selected for the school team.\n(她被選入校隊。)\nPlease select one answer.\n(請選出一個答案。)"],["selection","selection(n.)選擇、選拔、精選品\nselect(v.)選擇、挑選\na wide selection of 種類繁多的\nnatural selection 天擇\nThe store has a wide selection of shoes.\n(那家店的鞋子種類很多。)\nThe selection of the new captain took a week.\n(選出新隊長花了一個星期。)"],["self","self(n.)自己、自我\nselfish(adj.)自私的\none's true self 真正的自我\nself-confidence 自信\nJust be your true self.\n(做真正的自己就好。)\nHe's back to his old self again.\n(他又恢復了原來的樣子。)"],["selfish","selfish(adj.)自私的\nselfishness(n.)自私\nunselfish(adj.)無私的\na selfish person 自私的人\nselfish behavior 自私的行為\nDon't be so selfish. Share your snacks.\n(別那麼自私，分享你的零食吧。)\nIt was selfish of him to take all the cake.\n(他把蛋糕全拿走真是太自私了。)"],["sense","sense(n./v.)感覺、意義、察覺\nsensible(adj.)明智的\nsense of humor 幽默感\nmake sense 有道理\nHe has a great sense of humor.\n(他很有幽默感。)\nWhat you said doesn't make sense.\n(你說的話沒有道理。)"],["sensitive","sensitive(adj.)敏感的、體貼的\nsensitivity(n.)敏感度\nsensitive skin 敏感肌膚\nbe sensitive to 對……敏感\nMy skin is sensitive to the sun.\n(我的皮膚對陽光很敏感。)\nShe is sensitive to other people's feelings.\n(她很能體察別人的感受。)"],["separate","separate(adj./v.)分開的、分開\nseparation(n.)分離\nseparately(adv.)分別地\nseparate from 和……分開\nseparate rooms 分開的房間\nPlease separate the trash for recycling.\n(請把垃圾分類以便回收。)\nMy brother and I have separate rooms.\n(我和哥哥各有自己的房間。)"],["servant","servant(n.)僕人、傭人\nserve(v.)服務\ncivil servant 公務員\na loyal servant 忠實的僕人\nThe rich man had many servants.\n(那個富人有很多僕人。)\nMy aunt is a civil servant.\n(我阿姨是公務員。)"],["serve","serve(v.)服務、供應(餐點)、任職\nservice(n.)服務\nserver(n.)服務生、伺服器\nserve food 上菜\nserve as 擔任\nBreakfast is served from seven to ten.\n(早餐供應時間是七點到十點。)\nHe served as class leader last year.\n(他去年擔任班長。)"],["settle(ment)","settle(v.)解決、定居、安頓、settlement(n.)解決、協議、定居地\n(無詞性變化)\nsettle down 安頓下來\nsettle a problem 解決問題\nThey settled the problem quickly.\n(他們很快就解決了問題。)\nHis family settled in Tainan many years ago.\n(他的家人多年前在台南定居。)"],["sex","sex(n.)性別、性\nsexual(adj.)性的\nsex education 性教育\nthe opposite sex 異性\nPlease write your name, age, and sex.\n(請寫下你的姓名、年齡和性別。)\nOur school offers sex education classes.\n(我們學校有開性教育課程。)"],["shame","shame(n./v.)羞恥、可惜、使丟臉\nshameful(adj.)可恥的\nashamed(adj.)感到羞恥的\nWhat a shame! 真可惜！\nfeel shame 感到羞愧\nWhat a shame you can't come!\n(你不能來真可惜！)\nHe felt shame for lying to his mom.\n(他對媽媽說謊感到羞愧。)"],["shark","shark(n.)鯊魚\n(無詞性變化)\nshark attack 鯊魚攻擊\ngreat white shark 大白鯊\nWe saw a shark at the aquarium.\n(我們在水族館看到一隻鯊魚。)\nSharks have very sharp teeth.\n(鯊魚有非常銳利的牙齒。)"],["sheet","sheet(n.)床單、一張(紙)\n(無詞性變化)\na sheet of paper 一張紙\nchange the sheets 換床單\nPlease take out a sheet of paper.\n(請拿出一張紙。)\nI change my bed sheets every week.\n(我每週換床單。)"],["shelf","shelf(n.)架子、書架\nshelves(n.)架子(複數)\nbook shelf 書架\non the shelf 在架子上\nPut the books back on the shelf.\n(把書放回書架上。)\nThe top shelf is too high for me.\n(最上層的架子對我來說太高了。)"],["shell","shell(n.)殼、貝殼\n(無詞性變化)\nsea shell 貝殼\negg shell 蛋殼\nWe collected shells on the beach.\n(我們在海灘上撿貝殼。)\nA turtle can hide in its shell.\n(烏龜可以躲進殼裡。)"],["shine","shine(v./n.)發光、照耀、擦亮、光澤\nshiny(adj.)閃亮的\nthe sun shines 陽光照耀\nshine a light 照亮\nThe sun is shining brightly today.\n(今天陽光燦爛。)\nHer eyes shone with joy.\n(她的眼睛閃耀著喜悅。)"],["shock","shock(n./v.)震驚、衝擊、使震驚\nshocking(adj.)令人震驚的\nshocked(adj.)感到震驚的\nin shock 處於震驚中\nculture shock 文化衝擊\nThe news came as a shock to us.\n(這個消息令我們震驚。)\nI was shocked by his rude words.\n(我被他無禮的話嚇到了。)"],["shoot","shoot(v./n.)射擊、投籃、拍攝、嫩芽\nshooter(n.)射手\nshoot a film 拍電影\nshoot the ball 投籃\nHe shot the ball and scored.\n(他投籃得分。)\nThey are shooting a movie in our town.\n(他們正在我們鎮上拍電影。)"],["shopkeeper","shopkeeper(n.)店主\n(無詞性變化)\na friendly shopkeeper 親切的店主\nlocal shopkeepers 在地店家\nThe shopkeeper gave me a discount.\n(店主給了我折扣。)\nThe shopkeeper knows all his customers.\n(店主認識他所有的顧客。)"],["shore","shore(n.)岸、海岸\n(無詞性變化)\non the shore 在岸上\nwalk along the shore 沿著海岸走\nWe walked along the shore at sunset.\n(我們在日落時沿著海岸散步。)\nThe boat came back to shore.\n(那艘船回到岸邊。)"],["shot","shot(n.)射擊、投籃、照片、注射\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a shot 試一試、投籃\nflu shot 流感疫苗\nHe made the winning shot.\n(他投進致勝的一球。)\nI got a flu shot last week.\n(我上週打了流感疫苗。)"],["shut","shut(v./adj.)關閉、關上的\n(無詞性變化)\nshut down 關閉\nshut up 閉嘴\nPlease shut the door.\n(請把門關上。)\nThe store was shut for the holiday.\n(那家店因假期關門。)"],["shy","shy(adj.)害羞的\nshyness(n.)害羞\nshyly(adv.)害羞地\nbe shy with 對……害羞\ntoo shy to 太害羞而不敢\nShe is too shy to speak in class.\n(她太害羞了，不敢在課堂上發言。)\nHe smiled shyly at the girl.\n(他害羞地對那女孩微笑。)"],["sidewalk","sidewalk(n.)人行道\n(無詞性變化)\non the sidewalk 在人行道上\nwalk on the sidewalk 走人行道\nPlease walk on the sidewalk.\n(請走在人行道上。)\nScooters should not park on the sidewalk.\n(機車不應該停在人行道上。)"],["silence","silence(n./v.)寂靜、沉默、使安靜\nsilent(adj.)安靜的\nin silence 沉默地\nbreak the silence 打破沉默\nWe ate dinner in silence.\n(我們默默地吃晚餐。)\nHer joke broke the silence.\n(她的笑話打破了沉默。)"],["silent","silent(adj.)安靜的、沉默的\nsilence(n.)寂靜、沉默\nsilently(adv.)默默地\nkeep silent 保持沉默\nsilent film 默片\nPlease keep silent in the library.\n(在圖書館請保持安靜。)\nHe stayed silent during the meeting.\n(他在會議中一直保持沉默。)"],["silly","silly(adj.)愚蠢的、傻的\n(無詞性變化)\nsilly question 蠢問題\ndon't be silly 別傻了\nDon't be silly. You can do it!\n(別傻了，你做得到的！)\nIt was silly of me to forget my keys.\n(我真傻，竟然忘了帶鑰匙。)"],["silver","silver(n./adj.)銀、銀色(的)\n(無詞性變化)\nsilver medal 銀牌\nsilver ring 銀戒指\nShe won a silver medal in swimming.\n(她在游泳比賽中贏得銀牌。)\nMy mom has a silver ring.\n(我媽媽有一枚銀戒指。)"],["similar","similar(adj.)相似的\nsimilarity(n.)相似處\nsimilarly(adv.)同樣地\nbe similar to 和……相似\nsimilar taste 相似的品味\nMy bag is similar to yours.\n(我的包包和你的很像。)\nWe have similar interests.\n(我們有相似的興趣。)"],["simply","simply(adv.)簡單地、只是、簡直\nsimple(adj.)簡單的\nsimply put 簡單地說\nsimply because 只因為\nSimply put, we need more time.\n(簡單地說，我們需要更多時間。)\nThe view was simply beautiful.\n(景色簡直美極了。)"],["single","single(adj./n./v.)單一的、單身的、單人的、挑出\n(無詞性變化)\nsingle room 單人房\nevery single day 每一天\nI'd like to book a single room.\n(我想訂一間單人房。)\nHe practices piano every single day.\n(他每一天都練鋼琴。)"],["skill","skill(n.)技能、技巧\nskillful(adj.)熟練的\nskilled(adj.)熟練的\nlanguage skills 語言能力\ndevelop skills 培養技能\nCooking is a useful life skill.\n(烹飪是一項實用的生活技能。)\nShe wants to improve her English skills.\n(她想加強她的英文能力。)"],["skilled","skilled(adj.)熟練的、有技術的\nskill(n.)技能\nskilled worker 技術工人\nbe skilled at 擅長\nHe is skilled at fixing computers.\n(他很擅長修電腦。)\nThe factory needs more skilled workers.\n(這間工廠需要更多技術工人。)"],["skin","skin(n.)皮膚、皮\n(無詞性變化)\ndry skin 乾性皮膚\nbanana skin 香蕉皮\nUse sunscreen to protect your skin.\n(用防曬乳保護你的皮膚。)\nHe slipped on a banana skin.\n(他踩到香蕉皮滑倒了。)"],["sleepy","sleepy(adj.)想睡的、寧靜的\nsleep(v./n.)睡覺\nfeel sleepy 想睡\na sleepy town 寧靜的小鎮\nI always feel sleepy after lunch.\n(我午餐後總是很想睡。)\nThey live in a sleepy little town.\n(他們住在一個寧靜的小鎮。)"],["slide","slide(n./v.)滑梯、投影片、滑動\n(無詞性變化)\nslide down 滑下\nslide show 投影片放映\nThe kids slid down the slide.\n(孩子們從溜滑梯上滑下來。)\nLet's look at the next slide.\n(我們來看下一張投影片。)"],["slip","slip(v./n.)滑倒、溜走、紙條、小錯誤\nslippery(adj.)滑的\nslip on 踩到……滑倒\nslip of the tongue 口誤\nBe careful not to slip on the wet floor.\n(小心別在濕地板上滑倒。)\nSorry, it was just a slip of the tongue.\n(抱歉，那只是口誤。)"],["slipper(s)","slipper(n.)拖鞋\nslippers(n.)拖鞋(複數)\na pair of slippers 一雙拖鞋\nput on slippers 穿上拖鞋\nPlease put on your slippers inside.\n(在室內請穿上拖鞋。)\nI bought a new pair of slippers.\n(我買了一雙新拖鞋。)"],["smooth","smooth(adj./v.)光滑的、順利的、使平滑\nsmoothly(adv.)順利地\nsmooth skin 光滑的肌膚\ngo smoothly 進行順利\nThe baby has smooth skin.\n(寶寶的皮膚很光滑。)\nI hope everything goes smoothly.\n(希望一切順利。)"],["snack","snack(n./v.)點心、零食、吃點心\n(無詞性變化)\nsnack bar 小吃店\nlate-night snack 宵夜\nI often eat snacks while watching TV.\n(我常常邊看電視邊吃零食。)\nLet's have a late-night snack.\n(我們來吃宵夜吧。)"],["snail","snail(n.)蝸牛\n(無詞性變化)\nat a snail's pace 慢吞吞地\nsnail mail 傳統郵件\nA snail moves very slowly.\n(蝸牛移動得很慢。)\nThe traffic moved at a snail's pace.\n(車流慢吞吞地前進。)"],["snowy","snowy(adj.)下雪的、積雪的\nsnow(n./v.)雪、下雪\nsnowy day 下雪天\nsnowy mountain 雪山\nIt was a cold and snowy day.\n(那是一個寒冷的下雪天。)\nWe saw snowy mountains in Japan.\n(我們在日本看到了雪山。)"],["soap","soap(n./v.)肥皂、用肥皂洗\nsoapy(adj.)含肥皂的\na bar of soap 一塊肥皂\nsoap opera 肥皂劇\nWash your hands with soap.\n(用肥皂洗手。)\nMy grandma loves watching soap operas.\n(我奶奶很愛看連續劇。)"],["soccer","soccer(n.)足球\n(無詞性變化)\nplay soccer 踢足球\nsoccer team 足球隊\nWe play soccer after school.\n(我們放學後踢足球。)\nHe is on the school soccer team.\n(他是學校足球隊的一員。)"],["social","social(adj.)社會的、社交的\nsociety(n.)社會\nsocially(adv.)社交上\nsocial media 社群媒體\nsocial skills 社交能力\nMany teens spend hours on social media.\n(許多青少年花好幾個小時在社群媒體上。)\nGood social skills help you make friends.\n(良好的社交能力幫助你交朋友。)"],["society","society(n.)社會、協會\nsocial(adj.)社會的\nmodern society 現代社會\nmember of society 社會的一份子\nComputers play a big role in modern society.\n(電腦在現代社會中扮演重要角色。)\nHe joined the school's music society.\n(他加入了學校的音樂社。)"],["sock(s)","sock(n.)短襪、socks(n.)一雙襪子\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of socks 一雙襪子\nwool socks 羊毛襪\nI need a new pair of socks.\n(我需要一雙新襪子。)\nHe wore one red sock and one blue sock.\n(他穿了一隻紅襪和一隻藍襪。)"],["soda","soda(n.)汽水、蘇打水\n(無詞性變化)\na can of soda 一罐汽水\nsoda water 蘇打水\nToo much soda is bad for your teeth.\n(喝太多汽水對牙齒不好。)\nHe ordered a can of soda with his burger.\n(他點漢堡時配了一罐汽水。)"],["soft","soft(adj.)柔軟的、輕柔的、溫和的\nsoften(v.)使變軟\nsoftly(adv.)輕柔地\nsoft drink 不含酒精的飲料\nsoft voice 輕柔的聲音\nThis pillow is very soft.\n(這個枕頭非常柔軟。)\nShe spoke in a soft voice.\n(她用輕柔的聲音說話。)"],["soil","soil(n.)土壤、土地\n(無詞性變化)\nrich soil 肥沃的土壤\nsoil pollution 土壤汙染\nPlants grow well in rich soil.\n(植物在肥沃的土壤中長得很好。)\nThe farmer checked the soil before planting.\n(農夫在種植前檢查土壤。)"],["solution","solution(n.)解決辦法、答案、溶液\nsolve(v.)解決\nfind a solution 找到解決辦法\nsolution to ……的解決辦法\nWe need to find a solution quickly.\n(我們需要盡快找到解決辦法。)\nIs there a solution to this problem?\n(這個問題有解決辦法嗎？)"],["solve","solve(v.)解決、解答\nsolution(n.)解決辦法\nsolve a problem 解決問題\nsolve a mystery 解開謎團\nCan you solve this math problem?\n(你會解這道數學題嗎？)\nThe police finally solved the case.\n(警方終於破案了。)"],["somewhat","somewhat(adv.)有點、稍微\n(無詞性變化)\nsomewhat different 有點不同\nsomewhat surprised 有點驚訝\nI was somewhat surprised by the news.\n(我對這個消息有點驚訝。)\nThe test was somewhat harder than I expected.\n(這次考試比我預期的難一點。)"],["sort","sort(n./v.)種類、分類、整理\n(無詞性變化)\nsort of 有點\nsort out 整理、解決\nWhat sort of music do you like?\n(你喜歡哪一種音樂？)\nPlease sort the trash before you throw it away.\n(丟垃圾前請先分類。)"],["soul","soul(n.)靈魂、心靈、人\n(無詞性變化)\nbody and soul 全心全意\nnot a soul 一個人也沒有\nThere was not a soul on the street.\n(街上一個人也沒有。)\nMusic is food for the soul.\n(音樂是心靈的食糧。)"],["sour","sour(adj./n./v.)酸的、酸味、變酸\n(無詞性變化)\nsweet and sour 糖醋的\nturn sour 變酸、變糟\nThe milk has gone sour.\n(牛奶已經酸掉了。)\nI love sweet and sour pork.\n(我很愛吃糖醋里肌。)"],["source","source(n.)來源、根源、出處\n(無詞性變化)\nsource of income 收入來源\nenergy source 能源\nFruit is a good source of vitamins.\n(水果是維他命的良好來源。)\nThe sun is our main energy source.\n(太陽是我們主要的能源。)"],["southern","southern(adj.)南方的、南部的\nsouth(n.)南方\nsouthern Taiwan 南台灣\nsouthern part 南部\nKaohsiung is in southern Taiwan.\n(高雄位於南台灣。)\nIt is warmer in the southern part of the island.\n(島嶼的南部比較溫暖。)"],["soybean","soybean(n.)黃豆、大豆\n(無詞性變化)\nsoybean milk 豆漿\nsoybean oil 大豆油\nTofu is made from soybeans.\n(豆腐是由黃豆做成的。)\nI drink soybean milk every morning.\n(我每天早上喝豆漿。)"],["speaker","speaker(n.)演講者、說話者、喇叭\nspeak(v.)說話\nnative speaker 母語人士\nguest speaker 客座講者\nOur teacher is a native speaker of English.\n(我們的老師是以英文為母語的人。)\nTurn up the speaker, please.\n(請把喇叭的音量調大。)"],["speech","speech(n.)演講、說話能力\nspeak(v.)說話\ngive a speech 發表演說\nspeech contest 演講比賽\nThe principal gave a speech this morning.\n(校長今天早上發表了演說。)\nShe won first place in the speech contest.\n(她在演講比賽中得了第一名。)"],["speed","speed(n./v.)速度、加速、超速\nspeedy(adj.)快速的\nspeed limit 速限\nat full speed 全速\nThe speed limit here is 50 kilometers per hour.\n(這裡的速限是每小時五十公里。)\nThe train ran at full speed.\n(火車全速行駛。)"],["spelling","spelling(n.)拼字、拼法\nspell(v.)拼寫\nspelling mistake 拼字錯誤\nspelling test 拼字測驗\nCheck your spelling before you hand it in.\n(交出去之前檢查一下你的拼字。)\nI got full marks on the spelling test.\n(我拼字測驗拿了滿分。)"],["spider","spider(n.)蜘蛛\n(無詞性變化)\nspider web 蜘蛛網\npoisonous spider 毒蜘蛛\nThere is a big spider on the wall.\n(牆上有一隻大蜘蛛。)\nThe spider is making a web.\n(蜘蛛正在結網。)"],["spirit","spirit(n.)精神、心情、靈魂\nspiritual(adj.)精神上的\nteam spirit 團隊精神\nin high spirits 興高采烈\nOur class has great team spirit.\n(我們班很有團隊精神。)\nEveryone was in high spirits at the party.\n(派對上每個人都興高采烈。)"],["spoon","spoon(n.)湯匙\nspoonful(n.)一匙的量\na spoon of sugar 一匙糖\nsoup spoon 湯匙\nCan I have a spoon, please?\n(可以給我一支湯匙嗎？)\nShe added a spoon of sugar to her tea.\n(她在茶裡加了一匙糖。)"],["sport","sport(n./v.)運動、運動會、穿戴(展示)\nsporty(adj.)愛運動的\nsports(adj.)運動的\nplay sports 做運動\nsports car 跑車\nBasketball is my favorite sport.\n(籃球是我最喜歡的運動。)\nHe plays sports every day after school.\n(他每天放學後都做運動。)"],["spot","spot(n./v.)地點、斑點、看見、認出\nspotless(adj.)一塵不染的\ntourist spot 觀光景點\non the spot 當場\nSun Moon Lake is a famous tourist spot.\n(日月潭是有名的觀光景點。)\nI spotted my friend in the crowd.\n(我在人群中認出了我的朋友。)"],["spread","spread(v./n.)散布、傳播、塗、展開、蔓延\n(無詞性變化)\nspread the news 散播消息\nspread butter 塗奶油\nThe news spread quickly at school.\n(這個消息在學校裡很快傳開。)\nShe spread butter on her toast.\n(她在吐司上塗奶油。)"],["stage","stage(n./v.)舞台、階段、上演\n(無詞性變化)\non stage 在舞台上\nearly stage 早期階段\nShe sang a song on stage.\n(她在舞台上唱了一首歌。)\nThe project is still at an early stage.\n(這個計畫仍處於早期階段。)"],["stamp","stamp(n./v.)郵票、印章、蓋章、跺腳\n(無詞性變化)\ncollect stamps 集郵\nstamp one's foot 跺腳\nMy grandpa likes to collect stamps.\n(我爺爺喜歡集郵。)\nThe officer stamped my passport.\n(那位官員在我的護照上蓋了章。)"],["standard","standard(adj./n.)標準的、標準、水準\nstandardize(v.)使標準化\nhigh standard 高標準\nstandard of living 生活水準\nThe school has high standards for students.\n(這所學校對學生要求很高。)\nTheir standard of living has improved.\n(他們的生活水準提高了。)"],["state(ment)","state(v.)陳述、說明、statement(n.)聲明、陳述\nstate(n.)州、狀態、國家\nmake a statement 發表聲明\nclearly state 清楚說明\nPlease state your name and age.\n(請說出你的姓名和年齡。)\nThe company made a statement about the problem.\n(公司就這個問題發表了聲明。)"],["steak","steak(n.)牛排\n(無詞性變化)\nrare steak 三分熟的牛排\nsteak house 牛排館\nHow would you like your steak?\n(你的牛排要幾分熟？)\nWe had steak for my dad's birthday.\n(我們為爸爸慶生吃了牛排。)"],["steel","steel(n./v.)鋼、鋼鐵、使堅強\n(無詞性變化)\nstainless steel 不鏽鋼\nsteel oneself 使自己堅強起來\nThe bridge is made of steel.\n(這座橋是用鋼鐵建造的。)\nHe steeled himself for the bad news.\n(他做好心理準備面對壞消息。)"],["step","step(n./v.)步、步驟、台階、踏\n(無詞性變化)\nstep by step 一步一步地\ntake a step 採取一步\nLearn English step by step.\n(一步一步地學英文。)\nWatch your step. The floor is wet.\n(小心腳步，地板是濕的。)"],["stick","stick(v./n.)黏貼、刺、堅持、棍子\nsticky(adj.)黏的\nsticker(n.)貼紙\nstick to 堅持\nwalking stick 手杖\nStick the stamp on the envelope.\n(把郵票貼在信封上。)\nYou should stick to your plan.\n(你應該堅持你的計畫。)"],["stomachache","stomachache(n.)胃痛、肚子痛\nstomach(n.)胃、肚子\nhave a stomachache 胃痛\nbad stomachache 嚴重的胃痛\nI have a stomachache after eating too much.\n(我吃太多之後肚子痛。)\nHe missed school because of a bad stomachache.\n(他因為嚴重的胃痛沒去上學。)"],["stone","stone(n./v.)石頭、寶石、向…扔石頭\nstony(adj.)多石的、冷漠的\nthrow a stone 丟石頭\nstone wall 石牆\nDon't throw stones at the dogs.\n(不要向狗丟石頭。)\nThe old house has a stone wall.\n(那棟老房子有一道石牆。)"],["storm","storm(n./v.)暴風雨、猛攻、怒氣沖沖地走\nstormy(adj.)暴風雨的\nheavy storm 強烈暴風雨\nstorm out 氣沖沖地離開\nThe storm knocked down many trees.\n(暴風雨吹倒了許多樹。)\nShe stormed out of the room angrily.\n(她氣沖沖地走出房間。)"],["stranger","stranger(n.)陌生人、外地人\nstrange(adj.)奇怪的、陌生的\ncomplete stranger 完全陌生的人\ntalk to strangers 和陌生人說話\nDon't talk to strangers.\n(不要和陌生人說話。)\nI'm a stranger here myself.\n(我自己也是初來乍到。)"],["strawberry","strawberry(n.)草莓\n(無詞性變化)\nstrawberry jam 草莓果醬\nstrawberry farm 草莓園\nWe picked strawberries in Dahu.\n(我們去大湖採草莓。)\nI'd like some strawberry jam on my bread.\n(我想在麵包上塗一些草莓果醬。)"],["stream","stream(n./v.)小溪、一連串、流動、串流\nstreaming(n.)串流\nmountain stream 山澗\nlive stream 直播\nThe children played in the mountain stream.\n(孩子們在山澗中玩水。)\nWe watched a live stream of the concert.\n(我們看了演唱會的直播。)"],["stress","stress(n./v.)壓力、重音、強調\nstressful(adj.)壓力大的\nstressed(adj.)感到壓力的\nunder stress 承受壓力\nreduce stress 減輕壓力\nExercise can help reduce stress.\n(運動可以幫助減輕壓力。)\nThe teacher stressed the importance of sleep.\n(老師強調睡眠的重要性。)"],["stretch","stretch(n./v.)伸展、延伸、一段\nstretchy(adj.)有彈性的\nstretch out 伸展\nstretch one's legs 舒展筋骨、散步\nStretch your arms before you swim.\n(游泳前先伸展手臂。)\nThe beach stretches for miles.\n(這片海灘綿延數英里。)"],["strict","strict(adj.)嚴格的\nstrictly(adv.)嚴格地\nbe strict with 對…嚴格\nstrict rules 嚴格的規定\nMy parents are very strict with me.\n(我的父母對我很嚴格。)\nThe school has strict rules about phones.\n(學校對手機有嚴格的規定。)"],["strike","strike(n./v.)罷工、打擊、襲擊、突然想到\nstriking(adj.)顯著的、引人注目的\ngo on strike 罷工\nstrike sb. as 給某人…的印象\nThe workers went on strike for higher pay.\n(工人們為了加薪而罷工。)\nThe house was struck by lightning.\n(那棟房子被閃電擊中。)"],["struggle","struggle(n./v.)奮鬥、掙扎、努力\n(無詞性變化)\nstruggle with 與…奮鬥\nstruggle for 為…奮鬥\nHe struggled with math in high school.\n(他高中時數學學得很吃力。)\nLife was a struggle for the poor family.\n(對那個貧窮的家庭來說，生活很艱辛。)"],["style","style(n./v.)風格、樣式、時尚、設計\nstylish(adj.)時髦的\nin style 流行、有氣派\nhair style 髮型\nI like your new hair style.\n(我喜歡你的新髮型。)\nHer writing style is simple and clear.\n(她的寫作風格簡單明瞭。)"],["subway/underground/metro","subway(n.)地下鐵、捷運(美式)\nunderground(n.)地下鐵(英式)\nmetro(n.)地鐵、捷運\ntake the subway 搭地鐵\nsubway station 地鐵站\nI take the subway to school every day.\n(我每天搭捷運上學。)\nThe subway station is near my house.\n(地鐵站在我家附近。)"],["succeed","succeed(v.)成功、繼承\nsuccess(n.)成功\nsuccessful(adj.)成功的\nsucceed in 在…方面成功\nsucceed to 繼承\nShe succeeded in passing the exam.\n(她成功通過了考試。)\nIf at first you don't succeed, try again.\n(如果一開始不成功，就再試一次。)"],["success","success(n.)成功、成功的人事物\nsucceed(v.)成功\nsuccessful(adj.)成功的\ngreat success 極大的成功\nthe key to success 成功的關鍵\nHard work is the key to success.\n(努力是成功的關鍵。)\nThe concert was a great success.\n(這場音樂會非常成功。)"],["such","such(adj./pron.)如此的、這樣的、這樣的人事物\n(無詞性變化)\nsuch as 例如\nsuch a 如此的\nIt was such a nice day.\n(那是如此美好的一天。)\nI like fruits such as apples and bananas.\n(我喜歡蘋果和香蕉之類的水果。)"],["sudden","sudden(adj./n.)突然的、意外的\nsuddenly(adv.)突然地\nall of a sudden 突然\nsudden change 突然的改變\nAll of a sudden, the lights went out.\n(突然間，燈全熄了。)\nThere was a sudden change in the weather.\n(天氣突然變了。)"],["suggest","suggest(v.)建議、暗示\nsuggestion(n.)建議\nsuggest doing 建議做…\nstrongly suggest 強烈建議\nI suggest taking the bus.\n(我建議搭公車。)\nThe doctor suggested that I get more sleep.\n(醫生建議我多睡一點。)"],["suit","suit(n./v.)西裝、套裝、適合\nsuitable(adj.)適合的\nsuit sb. well 很適合某人\nwear a suit 穿西裝\nMy dad wears a suit to work.\n(我爸爸穿西裝上班。)\nThat color suits you well.\n(那個顏色很適合你。)"],["suitable","suitable(adj.)適合的、適當的\nsuit(v.)適合\nsuitably(adv.)適當地\nsuitable for 適合…\nsuitable time 適當的時間\nThis movie is not suitable for children.\n(這部電影不適合兒童觀看。)\nIs now a suitable time to talk?\n(現在方便談話嗎？)"],["super","super(adj./adv.)極好的、超級地\n(無詞性變化)\nsuper easy 超級簡單\nsuper cool 超酷\nThe test was super easy.\n(這次考試超級簡單。)\nWe had a super time at the party.\n(我們在派對上玩得超開心。)"],["supper","supper(n.)晚餐、宵夜\n(無詞性變化)\nhave supper 吃晚餐\nlate supper 宵夜\nWe have supper at seven every evening.\n(我們每天晚上七點吃晚餐。)\nWhat's for supper tonight?\n(今晚晚餐吃什麼？)"],["supply","supply(n./v.)供應、補給品、提供\nsupplier(n.)供應商\nsupply A with B 提供 B 給 A\nschool supplies 學校用品\nThe farm supplies the city with milk.\n(這座農場為城市供應牛奶。)\nI need to buy some school supplies.\n(我需要買一些學校用品。)"],["support","support(n./v.)支持、支撐、扶養\nsupporter(n.)支持者\nsupportive(adj.)支持的\nsupport a team 支持一支球隊\nfinancial support 經濟支援\nMy parents always support my dreams.\n(我的父母總是支持我的夢想。)\nThank you for your support.\n(謝謝你的支持。)"],["suppose","suppose(v.)假定、認為、應該\nsupposedly(adv.)據說\nbe supposed to 應該\nI suppose so 我想是吧\nYou are supposed to be in class now.\n(你現在應該在上課。)\nI suppose he is right.\n(我想他是對的。)"],["surf","surf(v.)衝浪、上網瀏覽\nsurfer(n.)衝浪者\nsurfing(n.)衝浪\ngo surfing 去衝浪\nsurf the Internet 上網\nWe went surfing in Taitung.\n(我們去台東衝浪。)\nHe surfs the Internet for news every day.\n(他每天上網看新聞。)"],["surface","surface(n./v.)表面、外表、浮出水面\n(無詞性變化)\non the surface 表面上\nthe Earth's surface 地球表面\nWater covers most of the Earth's surface.\n(水覆蓋了地球表面大部分的地方。)\nOn the surface, she seemed calm.\n(表面上她看起來很冷靜。)"],["survival","survival(n.)生存、存活\nsurvive(v.)生存\nsurvivor(n.)倖存者\nsurvival skills 求生技能\nfight for survival 為生存而戰\nWater is necessary for survival.\n(水是生存所必需的。)\nWe learned survival skills at camp.\n(我們在營隊學了求生技能。)"],["survive","survive(v.)存活、倖存、度過\nsurvival(n.)生存\nsurvivor(n.)倖存者\nsurvive an accident 在意外中倖存\nsurvive on 靠…維生\nOnly two people survived the crash.\n(只有兩個人在墜機事故中倖存。)\nPlants cannot survive without sunlight.\n(植物沒有陽光就無法存活。)"],["swallow","swallow(v./n.)吞下、燕子\n(無詞性變化)\nswallow food 吞嚥食物\nswallow one's pride 放下自尊\nIt hurts when I swallow.\n(我吞東西的時候會痛。)\nA swallow built a nest under the roof.\n(一隻燕子在屋簷下築了巢。)"],["sweater","sweater(n.)毛衣\n(無詞性變化)\nwool sweater 羊毛衣\nwear a sweater 穿毛衣\nIt's cold. Put on your sweater.\n(天氣很冷，穿上你的毛衣。)\nGrandma knitted me a sweater.\n(奶奶為我織了一件毛衣。)"],["sweep","sweep(v.)掃、清掃、席捲\nsweeper(n.)清掃者、掃地機\nsweep the floor 掃地\nsweep away 掃除、沖走\nPlease sweep the floor after class.\n(下課後請掃地。)\nThe flood swept away many houses.\n(洪水沖走了許多房屋。)"],["swim","swim(v./n.)游泳\nswimmer(n.)游泳者\nswimming(n.)游泳\ngo for a swim 去游泳\nswim across 游過\nCan you swim across the river?\n(你能游過這條河嗎？)\nLet's go for a swim this afternoon.\n(我們今天下午去游泳吧。)"],["swimsuit","swimsuit(n.)泳裝、泳衣\n(無詞性變化)\none-piece swimsuit 連身泳衣\nbring a swimsuit 帶泳衣\nDon't forget to bring your swimsuit.\n(別忘了帶你的泳衣。)\nShe bought a new swimsuit for the trip.\n(她為了這趟旅行買了一件新泳衣。)"],["swing","swing(n./v.)鞦韆、搖擺、揮動\n(無詞性變化)\nswing a bat 揮棒\nmood swings 情緒起伏\nThe kids are playing on the swings.\n(孩子們在盪鞦韆。)\nHe swung the bat and hit the ball.\n(他揮棒擊中了球。)"],["switch","switch(n./v.)開關、轉換、切換\n(無詞性變化)\nswitch on/off 打開/關掉\nlight switch 電燈開關\nPlease switch off the lights.\n(請把燈關掉。)\nThe light switch is next to the door.\n(電燈開關在門旁邊。)"],["symbol","symbol(n.)象徵、符號\nsymbolic(adj.)象徵性的\nsymbolize(v.)象徵\nsymbol of peace 和平的象徵\nchemical symbol 化學符號\nThe dove is a symbol of peace.\n(鴿子是和平的象徵。)\nWhat does this symbol mean?\n(這個符號代表什麼意思？)"],["system","system(n.)系統、制度、體系\nsystematic(adj.)有系統的\neducation system 教育制度\ncomputer system 電腦系統\nThe computer system is down.\n(電腦系統當機了。)\nTaiwan's education system is changing.\n(台灣的教育制度正在改變。)"],["tale","tale(n.)故事、傳說\n(無詞性變化)\nfairy tale 童話故事\nfolk tale 民間故事\nMy grandma told me a fairy tale every night.\n(我奶奶每天晚上都講一個童話故事給我聽。)\nThis old tale is about a brave young farmer.\n(這個古老的故事是關於一位勇敢的年輕農夫。)"],["target","target(n./v.)目標、靶子、以…為目標\n(無詞性變化)\nsales target 銷售目標\ntarget audience 目標觀眾\nOur team finally reached the sales target this month.\n(我們團隊這個月終於達到了銷售目標。)\nThis TV show targets young children.\n(這個電視節目以幼童為目標觀眾。)"],["task","task(n./v.)任務、工作、分派任務\n(無詞性變化)\na difficult task 困難的任務\ncomplete a task 完成任務\nCleaning the whole house is not an easy task.\n(打掃整間房子不是件容易的工作。)\nEach student must complete the task by Friday.\n(每位學生都必須在星期五前完成這項任務。)"],["tax","tax(n./v.)稅、課稅\ntaxation(n.)課稅、稅制\npay taxes 繳稅\ntax-free 免稅的\nEveryone with a job has to pay taxes.\n(每個有工作的人都必須繳稅。)\nYou can buy tax-free goods at the airport.\n(你可以在機場買到免稅商品。)"],["teapot","teapot(n.)茶壺\n(無詞性變化)\na china teapot 瓷茶壺\nfill the teapot 把茶壺裝滿\nShe poured hot water into the teapot.\n(她把熱水倒進茶壺裡。)\nMy aunt bought a beautiful teapot in Japan.\n(我阿姨在日本買了一個漂亮的茶壺。)"],["tear","tear(n./v.)眼淚、撕破\ntore(v.)撕破(過去式)\ntorn(adj.)撕破的\nin tears 流著淚\ntear up 撕碎\nThe little girl was in tears after losing her doll.\n(小女孩弄丟洋娃娃之後哭了起來。)\nPlease don't tear the pages out of the book.\n(請不要把書頁撕下來。)"],["technology","technology(n.)科技、技術\ntechnological(adj.)科技的\nmodern technology 現代科技\ninformation technology 資訊科技\nModern technology makes our lives much easier.\n(現代科技讓我們的生活便利許多。)\nMy brother wants to study information technology in college.\n(我哥哥想在大學念資訊科技。)"],["teens","teens(n.)十幾歲(13到19歲)\nteenager(n.)青少年\nteenage(adj.)青少年的\nin one's teens 在某人十幾歲時\nlate teens 快二十歲時\nShe started playing the guitar in her teens.\n(她十幾歲時開始彈吉他。)\nMany people in their late teens learn to drive.\n(許多快二十歲的人會去學開車。)"],["temperature","temperature(n.)溫度、體溫\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh temperature 高溫\ntake one's temperature 量體溫\nThe temperature dropped quickly after the rain.\n(下雨後氣溫迅速下降。)\nThe nurse took my temperature this morning.\n(護理師今天早上幫我量了體溫。)"],["term","term(n./v.)學期、術語、期限、稱為\nterms(n.)條件、關係\nin terms of 就…而言\na technical term 專業術語\nWe will have three tests this term.\n(這學期我們會有三次考試。)\nIn terms of price, this phone is a good choice.\n(就價格而言，這支手機是個好選擇。)"],["terrorism","terrorism(n.)恐怖主義、恐怖行動\nterrorist(n.)恐怖分子\nterror(n.)恐懼、恐怖\nfight terrorism 打擊恐怖主義\nan act of terrorism 恐怖行動\nMany countries work together to fight terrorism.\n(許多國家攜手合作打擊恐怖主義。)\nThe attack was called an act of terrorism.\n(這次攻擊被稱為恐怖行動。)"],["terrorist","terrorist(adj.)恐怖分子的、恐怖主義的\nterrorist(n.)恐怖分子\nterrorism(n.)恐怖主義\nterrorist attack 恐怖攻擊\nterrorist group 恐怖組織\nThe terrorist attack shocked the whole world.\n(那起恐怖攻擊震驚了全世界。)\nThe police arrested two members of a terrorist group.\n(警方逮捕了兩名恐怖組織成員。)"],["text","text(n.)文字、內文、簡訊\ntext(v.)傳簡訊\nsend a text 傳簡訊\ntext message 簡訊\nI will send you a text when I get home.\n(我到家時會傳簡訊給你。)\nRead the text carefully before you answer.\n(回答之前請仔細閱讀內文。)"],["textbook","textbook(n.)教科書、課本\n(無詞性變化)\nEnglish textbook 英文課本\nopen your textbook 打開課本\nPlease open your textbook to page twenty.\n(請把課本翻到第二十頁。)\nI forgot to bring my math textbook today.\n(我今天忘了帶數學課本。)"],["therefore","therefore(adv.)因此、所以\n(無詞性變化)\nand therefore 因此\ntherefore, ... 因此，…\nIt was raining; therefore, we stayed at home.\n(當時在下雨，因此我們待在家裡。)\nHe studied hard and therefore passed the exam.\n(他用功讀書，因此通過了考試。)"],["thief","thief(n.)小偷、竊賊\nthieves(n.)小偷(複數)\ntheft(n.)偷竊\ncar thief 偷車賊\ncatch a thief 抓小偷\nThe police finally caught the thief last night.\n(警方昨晚終於抓到了小偷。)\nA thief stole my bike in front of the store.\n(有小偷在商店前偷了我的腳踏車。)"],["thirsty","thirsty(adj.)口渴的、渴望的\nthirst(n.)口渴\nfeel thirsty 覺得口渴\nthirsty for knowledge 渴望知識\nI feel thirsty after running in the sun.\n(在太陽下跑步之後我覺得口渴。)\nCan I have some water? I'm very thirsty.\n(可以給我一些水嗎？我好渴。)"],["thought","thought(n.)想法、思考\nthoughtful(adj.)體貼的、深思的\nthink(v.)想、認為\non second thought 再想一想\nlost in thought 陷入沉思\nThat's a good thought. Let's try it.\n(那是個好主意，我們試試看吧。)\nHe sat by the window, lost in thought.\n(他坐在窗邊，陷入沉思。)"],["throughout","throughout(prep./adv.)遍及、從頭到尾\n(無詞性變化)\nthroughout the year 一整年\nthroughout the world 全世界\nThis shop is open throughout the year.\n(這家店全年無休。)\nThe singer is famous throughout the world.\n(這位歌手聞名全世界。)"],["thunder","thunder(n./v.)雷、打雷\nthunderstorm(n.)雷雨\na clap of thunder 一聲雷響\nthunder and lightning 雷電\nMy dog is afraid of thunder.\n(我的狗很怕打雷。)\nIt thundered all night, so I couldn't sleep.\n(整晚都在打雷，所以我睡不著。)"],["thus","thus(adv.)因此、如此\n(無詞性變化)\nand thus 因而\nthus far 到目前為止\nHe didn't study and thus failed the test.\n(他沒有讀書，因而考試不及格。)\nThus far, everything has gone well.\n(到目前為止，一切都很順利。)"],["till","till(conj./prep.)直到\n(無詞性變化)\ntill now 直到現在\nfrom morning till night 從早到晚\nWait here till I come back.\n(在這裡等到我回來。)\nShe works from morning till night.\n(她從早工作到晚。)"],["tiny","tiny(adj.)極小的、微小的\n(無詞性變化)\na tiny bit 一點點\ntiny room 很小的房間\nThe baby has tiny hands and feet.\n(這個寶寶有小小的手和腳。)\nThey live in a tiny apartment in the city.\n(他們住在城裡一間很小的公寓。)"],["tire","tire(v./n.)使疲倦、輪胎\ntired(adj.)疲倦的、厭倦的\ntiring(adj.)令人疲倦的\nflat tire 爆胎、沒氣的輪胎\nbe tired of 厭倦\nOur car got a flat tire on the way.\n(我們的車在路上爆胎了。)\nLong walks tire my grandfather easily.\n(長距離散步很容易讓我爺爺疲累。)"],["tissue","tissue(n.)面紙、(生物)組織\n(無詞性變化)\na box of tissues 一盒面紙\nbody tissue 身體組織\nCan you pass me a tissue, please?\n(可以請你遞一張面紙給我嗎？)\nMuscle tissue needs time to heal after exercise.\n(肌肉組織在運動後需要時間修復。)"],["title","title(n./v.)標題、頭銜、給…加標題\n(無詞性變化)\nbook title 書名\nwin the title 贏得冠軍頭銜\nWhat is the title of this song?\n(這首歌的歌名是什麼？)\nOur team won the title last year.\n(我們隊去年贏得了冠軍。)"],["toast","toast(n./v.)吐司、敬酒、烤\ntoaster(n.)烤麵包機\na slice of toast 一片吐司\nmake a toast 敬酒\nI had toast and milk for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了吐司配牛奶。)\nLet's make a toast to the happy couple.\n(讓我們向這對新人敬酒。)"],["tofu","tofu(n.)豆腐\n(無詞性變化)\nstinky tofu 臭豆腐\nfried tofu 炸豆腐\nStinky tofu is a famous Taiwanese snack.\n(臭豆腐是有名的台灣小吃。)\nMy mom made soup with tofu and fish.\n(我媽媽用豆腐和魚煮了湯。)"],["tone","tone(n.)語氣、音調、色調\n(無詞性變化)\ntone of voice 說話的語氣\nin a friendly tone 用友善的語氣\nDon't talk to me in that tone.\n(不要用那種語氣跟我說話。)\nThe teacher spoke in a friendly tone.\n(老師用友善的語氣說話。)"],["tongue","tongue(n.)舌頭、語言\n(無詞性變化)\nmother tongue 母語\nstick out one's tongue 吐舌頭\nChinese is my mother tongue.\n(中文是我的母語。)\nThe boy stuck out his tongue at his sister.\n(男孩對他妹妹吐舌頭。)"],["toothache","toothache(n.)牙痛\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a toothache 牙痛\na bad toothache 嚴重牙痛\nI have a toothache, so I can't eat candy.\n(我牙痛，所以不能吃糖果。)\nHe went to the dentist because of a bad toothache.\n(他因為牙痛得厲害去看牙醫。)"],["toothbrush","toothbrush(n.)牙刷\n(無詞性變化)\nelectric toothbrush 電動牙刷\na new toothbrush 新牙刷\nYou should change your toothbrush every three months.\n(你應該每三個月換一次牙刷。)\nI forgot to pack my toothbrush for the trip.\n(我旅行時忘了帶牙刷。)"],["tour","tour(n./v.)旅行、參觀、巡迴\ntourist(n.)觀光客\ntourism(n.)觀光業\nguided tour 有導覽的遊覽\ngo on a tour 去旅遊\nWe went on a tour of the old city.\n(我們去遊覽了古城。)\nThe band will tour Asia next year.\n(那個樂團明年將在亞洲巡迴演出。)"],["toward/towards","toward(prep.)朝向、對於\ntowards(prep.)朝向、對於(英式拼法)\nwalk toward 朝…走去\nattitude toward 對…的態度\nThe dog ran toward me happily.\n(那隻狗開心地朝我跑來。)\nHer attitude toward work is very good.\n(她對工作的態度非常好。)"],["track","track(n./v.)軌道、跑道、足跡、追蹤\n(無詞性變化)\nkeep track of 記錄、掌握…的動態\non the right track 方向正確\nI use an app to keep track of my spending.\n(我用一個應用程式記錄我的花費。)\nThe runners are warming up on the track.\n(跑者們正在跑道上暖身。)"],["trade","trade(n./v.)貿易、交易、交換\ntrader(n.)商人\ntrade with 與…貿易\ntrade A for B 用A換B\nTaiwan has close trade with many countries.\n(台灣與許多國家有密切的貿易往來。)\nI traded my comic book for his toy car.\n(我用我的漫畫書換了他的玩具車。)"],["tradition","tradition(n.)傳統、慣例\ntraditional(adj.)傳統的\nfamily tradition 家族傳統\nfollow a tradition 遵循傳統\nEating moon cakes is a Mid-Autumn tradition.\n(吃月餅是中秋節的傳統。)\nIt is our family tradition to eat together on Sundays.\n(星期天一起吃飯是我們家的傳統。)"],["traditional","traditional(adj.)傳統的\ntradition(n.)傳統\ntraditionally(adv.)傳統上\ntraditional food 傳統食物\ntraditional culture 傳統文化\nBeef noodles are a traditional food in Taiwan.\n(牛肉麵是台灣的傳統食物。)\nShe wore a traditional dress at the festival.\n(她在節慶上穿了傳統服裝。)"],["trap","trap(n./v.)陷阱、困住、誘捕\n(無詞性變化)\nset a trap 設陷阱\nbe trapped in 被困在\nThe farmer set a trap to catch the mouse.\n(農夫設了陷阱來抓老鼠。)\nWe were trapped in the elevator for an hour.\n(我們被困在電梯裡一個小時。)"],["trash","trash(n./v.)垃圾、丟棄\n(無詞性變化)\ntake out the trash 倒垃圾\ntrash can 垃圾桶\nIt's your turn to take out the trash.\n(輪到你倒垃圾了。)\nPlease throw the paper cup into the trash can.\n(請把紙杯丟進垃圾桶。)"],["travel","travel(n./v.)旅行、行進\ntraveler(n.)旅客\ntravel abroad 出國旅行\ntravel agency 旅行社\nMy family likes to travel abroad in summer.\n(我家人喜歡在夏天出國旅行。)\nLight travels faster than sound.\n(光速比音速快。)"],["treasure","treasure(n./v.)寶藏、寶物、珍惜\n(無詞性變化)\nhidden treasure 隱藏的寶藏\ntreasure map 藏寶圖\nThe pirates buried their treasure on an island.\n(海盜把他們的寶藏埋在一座島上。)\nI treasure the time I spend with my friends.\n(我很珍惜和朋友相處的時光。)"],["trial","trial(n.)審判、試驗、試用\ntry(v.)嘗試、審判\non trial 受審\ntrial and error 反覆嘗試、試誤\nThe man is on trial for stealing a car.\n(那名男子因偷車而受審。)\nI learned to cook by trial and error.\n(我是靠反覆嘗試學會做菜的。)"],["triangle","triangle(n.)三角形\ntriangular(adj.)三角形的\ndraw a triangle 畫一個三角形\nlove triangle 三角戀\nPlease draw a triangle on the board.\n(請在黑板上畫一個三角形。)\nThe movie is about a love triangle.\n(這部電影是關於一段三角戀。)"],["trick","trick(n./v.)詭計、把戲、竅門、欺騙\ntricky(adj.)棘手的、狡猾的\nplay a trick on 捉弄某人\nmagic trick 魔術把戲\nMy brother likes to play tricks on me.\n(我弟弟喜歡捉弄我。)\nThe man tricked her into giving him money.\n(那個男人騙她給他錢。)"],["true","true(adj./adv./v.)真的、真實的、正確地、校準\ntruly(adv.)真正地、真誠地\ntruth(n.)事實、真相\ncome true 實現\ntrue or false 是非題、對或錯\nI hope your dream will come true.\n(我希望你的夢想會實現。)\nIs it true that he moved to Japan?\n(他搬到日本是真的嗎？)"],["trust","trust(v./n.)信任、相信\ntrustworthy(adj.)值得信賴的\ntrust in 信賴…\nbuild trust 建立信任\nYou can trust me with your secret.\n(你可以放心把祕密告訴我。)\nIt takes time to build trust between friends.\n(朋友之間建立信任需要時間。)"],["truth","truth(n.)事實、真相、真理\ntrue(adj.)真的\ntruthful(adj.)誠實的\ntell the truth 說實話\nthe truth is 事實是\nPlease tell me the truth.\n(請告訴我實話。)\nThe truth is that I forgot your birthday.\n(事實是我忘了你的生日。)"],["tube","tube(n.)管子、管狀容器、(英國)地鐵\n(無詞性變化)\na tube of toothpaste 一條牙膏\ntest tube 試管\nI need to buy a new tube of toothpaste.\n(我需要買一條新的牙膏。)\nThe scientist put the liquid into a test tube.\n(科學家把液體倒進試管裡。)"],["turtle","turtle(n.)烏龜、海龜\n(無詞性變化)\nsea turtle 海龜\nas slow as a turtle 像烏龜一樣慢\nWe saw a sea turtle while swimming.\n(我們游泳時看到了一隻海龜。)\nMy little brother keeps a turtle as a pet.\n(我弟弟養了一隻烏龜當寵物。)"],["typhoon","typhoon(n.)颱風\n(無詞性變化)\ntyphoon day off 颱風假\nstrong typhoon 強烈颱風\nSchool was closed because of the typhoon.\n(因為颱風，學校停課了。)\nA strong typhoon hit Taiwan last week.\n(上週一個強烈颱風侵襲台灣。)"],["typical","typical(adj.)典型的、一向如此的\ntype(n.)類型\ntypically(adv.)通常、典型地\na typical day 典型的一天\ntypical of 是…的特點\nLet me tell you about a typical day at school.\n(讓我告訴你我在學校典型的一天。)\nIt's typical of him to be late.\n(遲到是他一貫的作風。)"],["ugly","ugly(adj.)醜的、難看的、令人不快的\nugliness(n.)醜陋\nugly duckling 醜小鴨\nturn ugly 變得難看、惡化\nI think this sweater is really ugly.\n(我覺得這件毛衣真的很醜。)\nThe argument turned ugly very quickly.\n(這場爭吵很快就變得很難看。)"],["umbrella","umbrella(n.)雨傘\n(無詞性變化)\nopen an umbrella 打開雨傘\nbring an umbrella 帶傘\nDon't forget to bring an umbrella today.\n(今天別忘了帶傘。)\nShe shared her umbrella with me in the rain.\n(她在雨中和我共撐一把傘。)"],["unit","unit(n.)單位、單元、一組\nunite(v.)團結、聯合\nunit of measurement 計量單位\nUnit One 第一單元\nWe will have a test on Unit Three tomorrow.\n(我們明天要考第三單元。)\nThe meter is a unit of length.\n(公尺是長度的單位。)"],["universe","universe(n.)宇宙、全世界\nuniversal(adj.)普遍的、全世界的\nthe whole universe 整個宇宙\nthe origin of the universe 宇宙的起源\nScientists still study the origin of the universe.\n(科學家們仍在研究宇宙的起源。)\nIs there other life in the universe?\n(宇宙中還有其他生命嗎？)"],["university","university(n.)大學\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to university 上大學\nuniversity student 大學生\nMy sister is a university student in Taipei.\n(我姊姊是台北的大學生。)\nHe hopes to go to university abroad.\n(他希望去國外念大學。)"],["unless","unless(conj.)除非、如果不\n(無詞性變化)\nunless otherwise noted 除非另有註明\nnot... unless 除非…否則不\nYou will miss the bus unless you hurry.\n(除非你快一點，否則會錯過公車。)\nDon't call me unless it's important.\n(除非有重要的事，否則別打電話給我。)"],["upload","upload(v.)上傳\ndownload(v.)下載\nupload photos 上傳照片\nupload a video 上傳影片\nShe uploaded the photos to her blog.\n(她把照片上傳到她的部落格。)\nPlease upload your homework before Friday.\n(請在星期五之前上傳你的作業。)"],["upon","upon(prep.)在…之上、一…就\n(無詞性變化)\nonce upon a time 從前\nupon arrival 一抵達就\nOnce upon a time, there lived a kind king.\n(從前，有一位仁慈的國王。)\nPlease call me upon arrival.\n(抵達後請馬上打電話給我。)"],["upper","upper(adj.)上面的、較高的\n(無詞性變化)\nupper floor 樓上\nupper class 上流社會\nMy office is on the upper floor.\n(我的辦公室在樓上。)\nHe hurt his upper arm while playing basketball.\n(他打籃球時傷到了上臂。)"],["upset","upset(adj./v./n.)心煩的、使心煩、打亂、(比賽)爆冷\n(無詞性變化)\nget upset 生氣、難過\nupset stomach 腸胃不適\nShe got upset when she lost her phone.\n(她弄丟手機時很難過。)\nDon't upset your mother with bad news.\n(別用壞消息讓你媽媽心煩。)"],["upstairs","upstairs(adv./adj./n.)在樓上、樓上的、樓上\ndownstairs(adv.)在樓下\ngo upstairs 上樓\nupstairs neighbor 樓上鄰居\nMy bedroom is upstairs.\n(我的臥室在樓上。)\nOur upstairs neighbor is very noisy at night.\n(我們樓上的鄰居晚上很吵。)"],["used","used(adj.)用過的、二手的、習慣的\nuse(v.)使用\nused car 二手車\nbe used to 習慣於\nMy father bought a used car last month.\n(我爸爸上個月買了一輛二手車。)\nI am used to getting up early.\n(我習慣早起。)"],["user","user(n.)使用者、用戶\nuse(v.)使用\nuser-friendly 容易使用的\ninternet user 網路使用者\nThis app is very user-friendly.\n(這個應用程式非常容易使用。)\nThe number of internet users is growing fast.\n(網路使用者的數量成長得很快。)"],["usual","usual(adj.)平常的、通常的\nusually(adv.)通常\nas usual 照常、一如往常\nthan usual 比平常\nHe was late for class as usual.\n(他一如往常上課遲到了。)\nIt is colder than usual today.\n(今天比平常冷。)"],["vacation","vacation(n./v.)假期、度假\n(無詞性變化)\nsummer vacation 暑假\non vacation 在度假\nWhat did you do during summer vacation?\n(你暑假做了什麼？)\nMy parents are on vacation in Japan.\n(我爸媽正在日本度假。)"],["valley","valley(n.)山谷、溪谷\n(無詞性變化)\na deep valley 深谷\nriver valley 河谷\nThere is a small village in the valley.\n(山谷裡有一個小村莊。)\nWe hiked down into the deep valley.\n(我們徒步走下深谷。)"],["valuable","valuable(adj.)貴重的、有價值的\nvalue(n.)價值\nvaluables(n.)貴重物品\nvaluable experience 寶貴的經驗\nvaluable information 有價值的資訊\nWorking part-time gave me valuable experience.\n(打工給了我寶貴的經驗。)\nDon't leave valuable things in your car.\n(別把貴重物品留在車上。)"],["value","value(n./v.)價值、價值觀、重視\nvaluable(adj.)有價值的\nvalue friendship 重視友誼\nfamily values 家庭價值觀\nI value my friends very much.\n(我非常重視我的朋友。)\nThis old coin has a high value.\n(這枚古錢幣價值很高。)"],["victory","victory(n.)勝利\nvictorious(adj.)勝利的\nwin a victory 獲勝\nvictory over 戰勝…\nOur team celebrated the victory together.\n(我們隊一起慶祝勝利。)\nThey won a great victory over the champions.\n(他們大勝了冠軍隊伍。)"],["view","view(n./v.)景色、觀點、看待、觀看\nviewer(n.)觀眾\npoint of view 觀點\na view of the sea 海景\nThe hotel room has a great view of the sea.\n(這間飯店房間有很棒的海景。)\nEveryone has a different point of view.\n(每個人都有不同的觀點。)"],["village","village(n.)村莊\nvillager(n.)村民\na small village 小村莊\nvillage life 鄉村生活\nMy grandparents live in a small village.\n(我的祖父母住在一個小村莊裡。)\nThe whole village came to the party.\n(全村的人都來參加了派對。)"],["vote","vote(n./v.)投票、選票\nvoter(n.)投票者、選民\nvote for 投票支持\ncast a vote 投下一票\nWe voted for a new class leader today.\n(我們今天投票選出新班長。)\nEvery vote counts in an election.\n(選舉中每一票都很重要。)"],["waist","waist(n.)腰、腰部\n(無詞性變化)\nslim waist 纖細的腰\nwaist size 腰圍\nShe tied a belt around her waist.\n(她在腰間繫了一條腰帶。)\nThe water came up to my waist.\n(水淹到了我的腰部。)"],["waiter/waitress","waiter(n.)服務生、男服務生\nwaitress(n.)女服務生\nwait(v.)等待、服侍\ncall the waiter 叫服務生\ntip the waitress 給女服務生小費\nThe waiter brought us the menu.\n(服務生拿菜單給我們。)\nThe waitress was very kind to us.\n(那位女服務生對我們很親切。)"],["wallet","wallet(n.)皮夾、錢包\n(無詞性變化)\nlose a wallet 遺失皮夾\nleather wallet 皮製錢包\nI left my wallet at home.\n(我把皮夾忘在家裡了。)\nHe found a wallet on the street.\n(他在街上撿到一個錢包。)"],["war","war(n.)戰爭\nwarrior(n.)戰士\nworld war 世界大戰\nat war 處於戰爭狀態\nMany people died in the war.\n(很多人死於那場戰爭。)\nWe all hope for a world without war.\n(我們都希望有一個沒有戰爭的世界。)"],["wash","wash(v./n.)洗、洗滌\nwashing(n.)洗滌、待洗衣物\nwasher(n.)洗衣機\nwash the dishes 洗碗\nwash your hands 洗手\nPlease wash your hands before dinner.\n(晚餐前請洗手。)\nIt's my turn to wash the dishes.\n(輪到我洗碗了。)"],["waste","waste(n./v.)浪費、廢棄物\nwasteful(adj.)浪費的\nwaste time 浪費時間\na waste of money 浪費錢\nDon't waste your time on video games.\n(別把時間浪費在電玩上。)\nBuying that toy was a waste of money.\n(買那個玩具真是浪費錢。)"],["watermelon","watermelon(n.)西瓜\n(無詞性變化)\nwatermelon juice 西瓜汁\na slice of watermelon 一片西瓜\nWatermelon is my favorite summer fruit.\n(西瓜是我最愛的夏季水果。)\nWe shared a big watermelon at the beach.\n(我們在海邊分吃了一顆大西瓜。)"],["wealth","wealth(n.)財富、大量\nwealthy(adj.)富有的\ngreat wealth 巨大財富\na wealth of 大量的、豐富的\nHealth is more important than wealth.\n(健康比財富更重要。)\nThe book has a wealth of information.\n(這本書有豐富的資訊。)"],["wedding","wedding(n.)婚禮\nwed(v.)結婚\nwedding dress 婚紗\nwedding ring 結婚戒指\nMy cousin's wedding is next Sunday.\n(我表姊的婚禮在下週日。)\nShe looked beautiful in her wedding dress.\n(她穿婚紗看起來很美。)"],["weekday","weekday(n.)平日、工作日\n(無詞性變化)\non weekdays 在平日\nweekday mornings 平日早上\nI get up at six on weekdays.\n(我平日六點起床。)\nThe museum is less crowded on weekdays.\n(博物館平日比較不擁擠。)"],["weigh","weigh(v.)稱重、重達、權衡\nweight(n.)重量\nweigh oneself 量體重\nweigh the pros and cons 權衡利弊\nHow much do you weigh?\n(你體重多少？)\nThe baby weighs three kilograms.\n(這個嬰兒重三公斤。)"],["weight","weight(n.)重量、體重\nweigh(v.)稱重、重達\nlose weight 減重\ngain weight 體重增加\nHe wants to lose weight before summer.\n(他想在夏天前減重。)\nThe weight of the box is ten kilograms.\n(這個箱子的重量是十公斤。)"],["western","western(adj./n.)西方的、西部的、西部片\nwest(n.)西方\nWestern culture 西方文化\nwestern part 西部\nShe is interested in Western art.\n(她對西方藝術很感興趣。)\nThe western part of Taiwan is very crowded.\n(台灣西部人口很稠密。)"],["whale","whale(n.)鯨魚\n(無詞性變化)\nwhale watching 賞鯨\nblue whale 藍鯨\nWe went whale watching in Hualien.\n(我們到花蓮去賞鯨。)\nThe blue whale is the largest animal on earth.\n(藍鯨是地球上最大的動物。)"],["whatever","whatever(adj./pron.)無論什麼、任何……的事物\n(無詞性變化)\nwhatever happens 無論發生什麼事\nwhatever you like 任何你喜歡的\nYou can eat whatever you like.\n(你喜歡吃什麼就吃什麼。)\nWhatever happens, I will support you.\n(無論發生什麼事，我都會支持你。)"],["wheel","wheel(n.)輪子、方向盤\n(無詞性變化)\nsteering wheel 方向盤\nbehind the wheel 開車\nOne of the bike's wheels is broken.\n(腳踏車的一個輪子壞了。)\nKeep both hands on the steering wheel.\n(雙手要握住方向盤。)"],["whenever","whenever(conj./adv.)每當、無論何時\n(無詞性變化)\nwhenever possible 只要有可能\nwhenever you want 隨時\nWhenever I feel sad, I listen to music.\n(每當我難過時，我就聽音樂。)\nCome and visit us whenever you want.\n(你隨時都可以來找我們。)"],["wherever","wherever(adv./conj.)無論何處、在任何地方\n(無詞性變化)\nwherever you go 無論你去哪裡\nwherever possible 盡可能\nMy dog follows me wherever I go.\n(無論我去哪裡，我的狗都跟著我。)\nYou can sit wherever you like.\n(你想坐哪裡都可以。)"],["whisper","whisper(n./v.)低語、耳語\n(無詞性變化)\nin a whisper 小聲地\nwhisper to sb. 對某人耳語\nShe whispered something in my ear.\n(她在我耳邊低聲說了些話。)\nThey talked in a whisper in the library.\n(他們在圖書館裡小聲交談。)"],["whoever","whoever(pron.)無論是誰、任何……的人\n(無詞性變化)\nwhoever comes 無論誰來\nwhoever wins 無論誰贏\nWhoever finishes first will get a prize.\n(誰先完成就能得到獎品。)\nYou can invite whoever you like.\n(你想邀請誰都可以。)"],["whole","whole(adj./n.)整個的、全部的、整體\nwholly(adv.)完全地\nthe whole day 一整天\nas a whole 整體而言\nI spent the whole day studying.\n(我花了一整天讀書。)\nHe ate the whole pizza by himself.\n(他一個人吃掉了整個披薩。)"],["whom","whom(pron.)誰(受格)\n(無詞性變化)\nto whom 給誰\nwith whom 和誰\nTo whom should I send this letter?\n(我應該把這封信寄給誰？)\nThe man whom you met is my uncle.\n(你見到的那個人是我叔叔。)"],["width","width(n.)寬度\nwide(adj.)寬的\nwiden(v.)加寬\nthe width of 的寬度\nin width 寬度為\nThe road is ten meters in width.\n(這條路寬十公尺。)\nMeasure the width of the window.\n(量一下窗戶的寬度。)"],["wild","wild(adj./adv./n.)野生的、狂野的、荒野\nwildlife(n.)野生動物\nwildly(adv.)瘋狂地\nwild animals 野生動物\nin the wild 在野外\nTigers live in the wild in Asia.\n(老虎在亞洲的野外生活。)\nThe fans went wild after the goal.\n(進球後球迷們都瘋狂了。)"],["willing","willing(adj.)願意的、樂意的\nwillingness(n.)意願\nunwilling(adj.)不願意的\nbe willing to 願意\nwilling helper 熱心的幫手\nI am willing to help you.\n(我很樂意幫你。)\nAre you willing to try something new?\n(你願意嘗試新事物嗎？)"],["windy","windy(adj.)颳風的、風大的\nwind(n.)風\nwindy day 颳風的日子\ncold and windy 又冷風又大\nIt's too windy to fly a kite today.\n(今天風太大，不能放風箏。)\nHsinchu is famous for its windy weather.\n(新竹以風大聞名。)"],["wine","wine(n.)葡萄酒、酒\n(無詞性變化)\nred wine 紅酒\na glass of wine 一杯葡萄酒\nMy parents had a glass of red wine.\n(我爸媽喝了一杯紅酒。)\nThis wine is made from grapes.\n(這種酒是用葡萄釀的。)"],["wing","wing(n.)翅膀、機翼、側翼\nwinged(adj.)有翅膀的\nspread its wings 展翅\nchicken wings 雞翅\nThe bird spread its wings and flew away.\n(那隻鳥展開翅膀飛走了。)\nWe ordered some fried chicken wings.\n(我們點了一些炸雞翅。)"],["wire","wire(n.)金屬線、電線\nwireless(adj.)無線的\nelectric wire 電線\nwire fence 鐵絲網\nDon't touch that electric wire.\n(別碰那條電線。)\nThe wire connects the speaker to the computer.\n(這條線把喇叭連到電腦上。)"],["within","within(prep./adv.)在……之內\n(無詞性變化)\nwithin a week 一週內\nwithin reach 伸手可及\nPlease reply within three days.\n(請在三天內回覆。)\nThe school is within walking distance.\n(學校在步行可到的距離內。)"],["wolf","wolf(n.)狼\nwolves(n.)狼(複數)\na pack of wolves 一群狼\nlone wolf 獨來獨往的人\nThe wolf howled at the moon.\n(那隻狼對著月亮嚎叫。)\nWolves usually hunt in groups.\n(狼通常成群獵食。)"],["wonder","wonder(v./n.)想知道、納悶、驚奇、奇蹟\nwonderful(adj.)極好的\nno wonder 難怪\nI wonder if 我想知道是否\nI wonder why he is late.\n(我想知道他為什麼遲到。)\nNo wonder you are tired; you slept so late.\n(難怪你很累，你那麼晚睡。)"],["wood(s)","wood(n.)木頭、木材、woods(n.)樹林、森林\nwooden(adj.)木製的\nmade of wood 木製的\nin the woods 在樹林裡\nThis table is made of wood.\n(這張桌子是木頭做的。)\nWe went for a walk in the woods.\n(我們去樹林裡散步。)"],["wooden","wooden(adj.)木製的、呆板的\nwood(n.)木頭\nwooden box 木箱\nwooden floor 木地板\nGrandpa made me a wooden toy.\n(爺爺做了一個木頭玩具給我。)\nThe house has a wooden floor.\n(這間房子是木地板。)"],["wool","wool(n.)羊毛、毛線\nwoolen(adj.)羊毛製的\nwool sweater 羊毛毛衣\nball of wool 毛線球\nThis sweater is made of wool.\n(這件毛衣是羊毛做的。)\nGrandma knitted a scarf with red wool.\n(奶奶用紅色毛線織了一條圍巾。)"],["workbook","workbook(n.)練習簿、作業簿\n(無詞性變化)\nEnglish workbook 英文習作\nfinish the workbook 完成習作\nPlease do page ten in your workbook.\n(請寫你習作的第十頁。)\nI forgot to bring my math workbook.\n(我忘了帶數學習作。)"],["worm","worm(n./v.)蟲、蠕蟲、蠕行\n(無詞性變化)\nearly bird catches the worm 早起的鳥兒有蟲吃\nworm one's way 慢慢擠進\nThe bird caught a worm.\n(那隻鳥抓到一隻蟲。)\nThere are many worms in the soil after rain.\n(下雨後土裡有很多蟲。)"],["worse","worse(adj./adv./n.)更壞的、更糟地、更糟的事\nworsen(v.)惡化\nget worse 變得更糟\nworse than 比……更糟\nThe weather is getting worse.\n(天氣愈來愈糟了。)\nMy cold is worse than yesterday.\n(我的感冒比昨天更嚴重。)"],["worst","worst(adj./adv./n.)最壞的、最糟地、最壞的情況\n(無詞性變化)\nat worst 在最壞的情況下\nthe worst day 最糟的一天\nToday was the worst day of my life.\n(今天是我人生中最糟的一天。)\nPrepare for the worst and hope for the best.\n(做最壞的打算，抱最好的希望。)"],["worth","worth(adj./n.)值得的、價值\nworthy(adj.)值得的\nworthless(adj.)無價值的\nbe worth it 值得\nworth a visit 值得一遊\nThis movie is worth watching.\n(這部電影值得一看。)\nThe trip was long, but it was worth it.\n(旅程很長，但很值得。)"],["wound","wound(n./v.)傷口、使受傷\nwounded(adj.)受傷的\ndeep wound 很深的傷口\nheal a wound 治癒傷口\nThe nurse cleaned the wound on his leg.\n(護理師清理了他腿上的傷口。)\nTwo soldiers were wounded in the fight.\n(兩名士兵在戰鬥中受傷。)"],["yam","yam(n.)山藥、番薯\n(無詞性變化)\nsweet yam 甜番薯\nyam soup 山藥湯\nMy grandma cooked yam soup for us.\n(奶奶為我們煮了山藥湯。)\nRoasted yams are popular in winter.\n(烤番薯在冬天很受歡迎。)"],["youth","youth(n.)青春、年輕時代、年輕人\nyoung(adj.)年輕的\nyouthful(adj.)年輕的、有朝氣的\nin one's youth 在年輕時\nyouth hostel 青年旅館\nHe was a good swimmer in his youth.\n(他年輕時是游泳好手。)\nThe program is designed for local youth.\n(這個計畫是為當地年輕人設計的。)"],["zebra","zebra(n.)斑馬\n(無詞性變化)\nzebra crossing 斑馬線\na herd of zebras 一群斑馬\nZebras have black and white stripes.\n(斑馬有黑白相間的條紋。)\nAlways cross the road at the zebra crossing.\n(過馬路一定要走斑馬線。)"]],"3":[["aboard","aboard(prep./adv.)在(船、飛機、車)上\n(無詞性變化)\ngo aboard 上船/飛機/車\nwelcome aboard 歡迎搭乘\nWelcome aboard Flight 802 to New York.\n(歡迎搭乘前往紐約的 802 班次。)\nThe passengers are already aboard the ship.\n(乘客們已經在船上了。)"],["acceptable","acceptable(adj.)可接受的、滿意的\naccept(v.)接受\nacceptance(n.)接受、承認\nsocially acceptable 社會可接受的\nacceptable behavior 可接受的行為\nWe are looking for a solution that is acceptable to everyone.\n(我們正在尋找一個大家都能接受的解決方案。)\nHis performance was acceptable, but not outstanding.\n(他的表現尚可，但並不傑出。)"],["accurate","accurate(adj.)準確的、精確的\naccuracy(n.)準確性\naccurately(adv.)準確地\naccurate information 準確的資訊\nhighly accurate 高度精確的\nScientists need to provide accurate data for the experiment.\n(科學家需要為實驗提供準確的數據。)\nThe report gives an accurate account of what happened.\n(這份報告準確地描述了發生的事情。)"],["ache","ache(n./v.)疼痛\nheadache(n.)頭痛\ntoothache(n.)牙痛\nstomach ache 胃痛\nmuscle ache 肌肉痠痛\nMy legs ache after walking all day.\n(走了一整天路後，我的腿很痠痛。)\nHe has a dull ache in his shoulder.\n(他的肩膀隱隱作痛。)"],["achieve(ment)","achieve(v.)達成、achievement(n.)成就\nachievable(adj.)可達成的\nachieve a goal 達成目標\nsense of achievement 成就感\nYou can achieve anything if you work hard enough.\n(如果你夠努力，你可以達成任何事。)\nWinning the gold medal was a great achievement.\n(贏得金牌是一項偉大的成就。)"],["additional","additional(adj.)附加的、額外的\naddition(n.)增加、加法\nadd(v.)增加、添加\nadditional information 額外資訊\nadditional costs 額外費用\nWe need additional information before making a decision.\n(我們在做決定之前需要額外的資訊。)\nThere will be an additional charge for delivery.\n(運送將會收取額外費用。)"],["admire","admire(v.)欽佩、欣賞\nadmiration(n.)欽佩、仰慕\nadmirable(adj.)令人欽佩的\nadmire someone for something 因某事欽佩某人\nadmire the view 欣賞風景\nI really admire him for his courage.\n(我真的很佩服他的勇氣。)\nThey stopped to admire the sunset.\n(他們停下來欣賞日落。)"],["advanced","advanced(adj.)先進的、高等的\nadvance(v./n.)進步、前進\nadvancement(n.)前進、提升\nadvanced technology 先進科技\nadvanced level 高階程度\nThe hospital uses advanced methods to treat patients.\n(這間醫院使用先進的方法來治療病人。)\nShe is taking an advanced English course this semester.\n(她這學期選修了高階英文課程。)"],["advantage","advantage(n.)優點、優勢\nadvantageous(adj.)有利的\ntake advantage of 利用、佔便宜\nhave an advantage 具有優勢\nBeing tall is a great advantage in basketball.\n(長得高在籃球運動中是一大優勢。)\nHe took advantage of the good weather to go hiking.\n(他趁著天氣好去健行。)"],["adventure","adventure(n.)冒險\nadventurous(adj.)愛冒險的\nadventurer(n.)冒險家\nsense of adventure 冒險精神\noutdoor adventure 戶外冒險\nThey went on an adventure in the Amazon rainforest.\n(他們去亞馬遜雨林進行了一場冒險。)\nTraveling alone in a foreign country is a real adventure.\n(獨自在外國旅行是一場真正的冒險。)"],["advertise(ment)/ad","advertise(v.)登廣告、advertisement(n.)廣告\nadvertiser(n.)廣告商\nadvertising(n.)廣告業\nadvertise a product 為產品打廣告\nplace an advertisement 刊登廣告\nThey advertise their new products on television.\n(他們在電視上為新產品打廣告。)\nI saw an ad for a cheap flight to Japan.\n(我看到一張去日本廉價機票的廣告。)"],["advise","advise(v.)建議、忠告\nadvice(n.)建議、忠告\nadvisor(n.)顧問、指導老師\nadvise someone to do something 建議某人做某事\nadvise against 建議不要...\nI would advise you to see a doctor immediately.\n(我會建議你立即去看醫生。)\nMy teacher advised me against skipping classes.\n(老師建議我不要翹課。)"],["adviser/advisor","adviser/advisor(n.)顧問、指導老師\nadvise(v.)建議\nadvice(n.)建議\nlegal adviser 法律顧問\nfinancial advisor 財務顧問\nHe works as a technical adviser for the government.\n(他在政府擔任技術顧問。)\nYou should talk to your academic advisor about your grades.\n(你應該和你的學業指導老師談談你的成績。)"],["afford","afford(v.)負擔得起\naffordable(adj.)負擔得起的\ncan afford to do something 負擔得起做某事\nafford the cost 負擔費用\nI can't afford to buy a new car right now.\n(我現在負擔不起買新車。)\nWe can't afford to lose any more time.\n(我們不能再浪費任何時間了。)"],["afterward/afterwards","afterward/afterwards(adv.)之後、後來\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nshortly afterward 不久之後\nsoon afterward 很快地之後\nThey went to the movie and had dinner afterward.\n(他們去看電影，之後去吃晚餐。)\nWe met for coffee, and she left shortly afterwards.\n(我們見面喝咖啡，不久後她就離開了。)"],["agriculture","agriculture(n.)農業\nagricultural(adj.)農業的\nmodern agriculture 現代農業\norganic agriculture 有機農業\nMost of the people in this area depend on agriculture.\n(這個地區的大多數人依靠農業維生。)\nAdvances in agriculture have increased food production.\n(農業的進步增加了糧食產量。)"],["airline","airline(n.)航空公司\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nairline industry 航空業\ninternational airline 國際航空公司\nWhich airline are you flying with to Paris?\n(你搭哪家航空公司去巴黎？)\nThe airline offers direct flights to many major cities.\n(這家航空公司提供直飛許多主要城市的航班。)"],["alley","alley(n.)小巷、弄、胡同\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nbowling alley 保齡球館\nnarrow alley 狹窄的小巷\nThe thief disappeared into a dark alley.\n(小偷消失在一條黑暗的小巷裡。)\nOur house is located in a quiet alley behind the park.\n(我們的房子位於公園後方的一條安靜小巷裡。)"],["almond","almond(n.)杏仁\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nalmond milk 杏仁奶\ntoasted almonds 烤杏仁\nShe added some sliced almonds to the salad.\n(她在沙拉裡加了一些杏仁片。)\nAlmonds are a healthy source of protein.\n(杏仁是健康的蛋白質來源。)"],["alphabet","alphabet(n.)字母表\nalphabetical(adj.)字母順序的\nalphabetically(adv.)按字母順序地\nEnglish alphabet 英文字母表\nin alphabetical order 依字母順序\nThere are 26 letters in the English alphabet.\n(英文字母表中有 26 個字母。)\nThe books are arranged on the shelf in alphabetical order.\n(書架上的書是按字母順序排列的。)"],["amaze(ment)","amaze(v.)使驚奇、amazement(n.)驚奇\namazing(adj.)令人驚奇的\namazed(adj.)感到驚奇的\nto one's amazement 令某人驚奇的是\nlook in amazement 驚訝地看著\nTo my amazement, he finished the work in ten minutes.\n(令我驚訝的是，他在十分鐘內完成了工作。)\nShe stared at the scene in total amazement.\n(她完全驚訝地盯著那個場景。)"],["ambassador","ambassador(n.)大使\nembassy(n.)大使館\nambassador to ... 派駐於...的大使\ngoodwill ambassador 親善大使\nHe was appointed as the British ambassador to Japan.\n(他被任命為英國駐日本大使。)\nShe serves as a goodwill ambassador for the UN.\n(她擔任聯合國的親善大使。)"],["ambition","ambition(n.)抱負、野心\nambitious(adj.)有野心的、抱負不凡的\ncareer ambition 事業抱負\nfulfill an ambition 實現抱負\nHis main ambition is to become a famous actor.\n(他的主要抱負是成為一名著名的演員。)\nShe has the ambition to start her own company.\n(她有創辦自己公司的抱負。)"],["ambulance","ambulance(n.)救護車\n(無明顯詞性變化)\ncall an ambulance 叫救護車\nambulance crew 救護人員\nSomeone call an ambulance! There's been an accident.\n(有人快叫救護車！發生事故了。)\nThe ambulance arrived at the scene within minutes.\n(救護車在幾分鐘內就到達了現場。)"],["angel","angel(n.)天使\nangelic(adj.)天使般的\nguardian angel 守護天使\nlike an angel 像天使一樣\nShe has the voice of an angel.\n(她擁有天使般的嗓音。)\nThank you for helping me; you are a real angel.\n(謝謝你幫助我；你真是個天使。)"],["announce(ment)","announce(v.)宣佈、announcement(n.)宣佈、公告\nannouncer(n.)播報員、宣告者\nmake an announcement 做出宣佈\nannounce a plan 宣佈一項計畫\nThe government will announce the new policy tomorrow.\n(政府明天將宣佈新政策。)\nThe headmaster made an important announcement during the assembly.\n(校長在集會期間做出了一項重要宣佈。)"],["anxious","anxious(adj.)焦慮的、渴望的\nanxiety(n.)焦慮\nanxiously(adv.)焦慮地\nanxious about 對...感到焦慮\nfeel anxious 感到焦慮\nParents are often anxious about their children's future.\n(父母經常對孩子的未來感到焦慮。)\nShe was anxious to finish the project on time.\n(她渴望能準時完成這項企劃。)"],["anyhow","anyhow(adv.)無論如何、總之\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nget there anyhow 無論如何到達那裡\ndo it anyhow 無論如何都要做\nIt might rain, but we are going anyhow.\n(可能會下雨，但我們無論如何都要去。)\nAnyhow, let's forget about the past and move on.\n(總之，讓我們忘記過去，繼續前進吧。)"],["apart","apart(adv.)分開地、相隔地\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nfall apart 破碎、倒塌\ntell them apart 分辨他們\nThe two houses are built 500 meters apart.\n(這兩棟房子相隔 500 公尺。)\nThe toy came apart after he dropped it.\n(這個玩具在他摔到後就散架了。)"],["apologize","apologize(v.)道歉\napology(n.)道歉\napologetic(adj.)道歉的、愧疚的\napologize to someone 向某人道歉\napologize for something 為某事道歉\nYou should apologize to her for being late.\n(你應該因為遲到向她道歉。)\nHe apologized for his rude behavior at the party.\n(他為他在派對上的粗魯行為道歉。)"],["appeal","appeal(n./v.)吸引力、呼籲、上訴\nappealing(adj.)有吸引力的\nappeal to 吸引、向...呼籲\nlose one's appeal 失去吸引力\nThe idea of working abroad appeals to many young people.\n(在國外工作的想法吸引了許多年輕人。)\nThe police made an appeal for witnesses to the crime.\n(警方呼籲該犯罪行為的目擊者提供資訊。)"],["approve","approve(v.)贊成、批准\napproval(n.)贊同、批准\napprove of 贊成、同意\napprove the plan 批准計畫\nMy parents don't approve of me staying out late.\n(我的父母不贊成我太晚回家。)\nThe committee finally approved the budget for next year.\n(委員會終於批准了明年的預算。)"],["apron","apron(n.)圍裙\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nkitchen apron 廚房圍裙\nwear an apron 穿圍裙\nShe put on her apron and started cooking dinner.\n(她穿上圍裙開始煮晚餐。)\nThe baker's apron was covered in flour.\n(麵包師傅的圍裙上沾滿了麵粉。)"],["armed","armed(adj.)武裝的、持械的\narms(n.)武器\narm(v.)武裝\narmed forces 武裝部隊\narmed robbery 持械搶劫\nThe guards were armed with guns.\n(守衛配有槍枝。)\nThe armed forces are ready to defend the country.\n(武裝部隊已準備好保衛國家。)"],["arrest","arrest(n./v.)逮捕\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nunder arrest 被逮捕\narrest someone for 為...逮捕某人\nThe police arrested the man for stealing a car.\n(警方因偷車逮捕了那名男子。)\nHe is currently under arrest and waiting for trial.\n(他目前被捕並等待審判。)"],["ash","ash(n.)灰、灰燼\n(無明顯詞性變化)\ncigarette ash 煙灰\nvolcanic ash 火山灰\nHe tapped the cigarette ash into the tray.\n(他把煙灰彈進托盤裡。)\nThe village was covered in volcanic ash after the eruption.\n(噴發後，村莊被火山灰覆蓋。)"],["aside","aside(adv.)在旁邊、撇開\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nset aside 撥出、留出\nstep aside 讓位、避開\nShe set some money aside for her vacation.\n(她存了一些錢準備度假用。)\nJoking aside, we really need to finish this work.\n(撇開玩笑不談，我們真的需要完成這項工作。)"],["assist","assist(v.)協助、幫助\nassistance(n.)協助、幫助\nassistant(n.)助手\nassist someone with 協助某人某事\nassist in doing 協助做某事\nThe computer program can assist you in translating texts.\n(這個電腦程式可以協助你翻譯文本。)\nWe are here to assist you with your travel plans.\n(我們在這裡協助您安排旅遊計畫。)"],["assistant","assistant(n.)助手、助理\nassist(v.)協助\nassistance(n.)協助\nresearch assistant 研究助理\nshop assistant 店員\nShe works as a personal assistant to the manager.\n(她擔任經理的私人助理。)\nCan I speak to the shop assistant for help?\n(我可以找店員幫忙嗎？)"],["assume","assume(v.)假設、承擔\nassumption(n.)假設\nassume responsibility 承擔責任\nassume that 假設...\nI assume that you have already finished the report.\n(我假設你已經完成了報告。)\nHe is willing to assume responsibility for the mistake.\n(他願意為這個錯誤承擔責任。)"],["athlete","athlete(n.)運動員\nathletic(adj.)體育的、運動健壯的\nathletics(n.)田徑、體育運動\nprofessional athlete 職業運動員\nstar athlete 明星運動員\nHe is a gifted athlete who excels in many sports.\n(他是一位在許多運動項目上都很出色的天才運動員。)\nMany young athletes dream of competing in the Olympics.\n(許多運動員夢想能參加奧運。)"],["attitude","attitude(n.)態度\n(無明顯詞性變化)\npositive attitude 正面態度\nattitude toward 對於...的態度\nYou need to change your negative attitude toward work.\n(你需要改變你對工作的消極態度。)\nShe always maintains a positive attitude, even in difficult times.\n(即使在困難時期，她也總是保持正面的態度。)"],["attract","attract(v.)吸引\nattraction(n.)吸引力、景點\nattractive(adj.)有吸引力的\nattract attention 引起注意\nattract tourists 吸引遊客\nThe bright lights attract insects at night.\n(夜晚亮光會吸引昆蟲。)\nThe museum attracts thousands of visitors every year.\n(這間博物館每年吸引數千名遊客。)"],["attractive","attractive(adj.)有吸引力的、迷人的\nattract(v.)吸引\nattraction(n.)吸引力、景點\nattractive features 吸引人的特徵\nhighly attractive 很有吸引力的\nShe is an attractive woman with a great personality.\n(她是一位非常有魅力且個性很好的女性。)\nThe company offers an attractive salary to new employees.\n(這間公司為新員工提供優渥的薪水。)"],["audience","audience(n.)觀眾、聽眾\n(無明顯詞性變化)\ntarget audience 目標觀眾\nlive audience 現場觀眾\nThe singer performed in front of a large audience.\n(這位歌手在大批觀眾面前表演。)\nThe audience cheered and clapped at the end of the show.\n(演出結束時，觀眾歡呼並鼓掌。)"],["automatic","automatic(adj.)自動的\nautomatically(adv.)自動地\nautomatic doors 自動門\nautomatic system 自動系統\nThe car has an automatic transmission.\n(這輛車有自動變速器。)\nThe lights go on and off through an automatic system.\n(燈光透過自動系統開啟和關閉。)"],["automobile/auto","automobile/auto(n.)汽車\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nautomobile industry 汽車產業\ndrive an automobile 開汽車\nThe invention of the automobile changed the way we travel.\n(汽車的發明改變了我們旅行的方式。)\nHe works in a factory that manufactures automobile parts.\n(他在一家製造汽車零件的工廠工作。)"],["avenue","avenue(n.)大道、管道\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nFifth Avenue 第五大道\nbroad avenue 寬闊的大道\nThe hotel is located on a beautiful avenue lined with trees.\n(這間飯店坐落在一條綠樹成蔭的美麗大道上。)\nWe are exploring every avenue to solve the problem.\n(我們正嘗試各種管道來解決問題。)"],["awake","awake(adj./v.)醒著的、喚醒\nawaken(v.)喚醒\nstay awake 保持清醒\nwide awake 完全清醒的\nI was wide awake all night thinking about the exam.\n(我想著考試的事情，整晚都清醒著。)\nIs the baby awake yet?\n(寶寶醒了嗎？)"],["awaken","awaken(v.)喚醒、意識到\nawake(adj.)醒著的\nawaken from a dream 從夢中醒來\nawaken interest 引起興趣\nThe loud noise awakened me from a deep sleep.\n(大聲的噪音把我從深睡中喚醒。)\nHis speech awakened our interest in environmental issues.\n(他的演講喚起了我們對環境議題的興趣。)"],["award","award(n./v.)獎賞、頒發\n(無明顯詞性變化)\nwin an award 獲獎\nacademy award 奧斯卡獎\nShe received an award for her bravery.\n(她因勇敢而獲得獎項。)\nThe judge awarded the first prize to the young pianist.\n(評審將一等獎頒發給了那位年輕鋼琴家。)"],["aware","aware(adj.)意識到的、察覺到的\nawareness(n.)意識、察覺\naware of 意識到...\nenvironmentally aware 有環保意識的\nMost people are aware of the dangers of smoking.\n(大多數人都意識到抽煙的危險。)\nHe wasn't aware that the meeting had been canceled.\n(他沒察覺到會議已經取消了。)"],["awful","awful(adj.)糟糕的、可怕的\nawfully(adv.)非常地、糟糕地\nawful weather 糟糕的天氣\nsound awful 聽起來很糟\nThe food was awful, so we didn't finish it.\n(食物很難吃，所以我們沒吃完。)\nI feel awful about forgetting your birthday.\n(我對忘記你的生日感到很抱歉。)"],["awkward","awkward(adj.)尷尬的、笨拙的\nawkwardly(adv.)尷尬地、笨拙地\nawkward silence 尷尬的沉默\nawkward position 尷尬的境地\nThere was an awkward silence after she asked the question.\n(她問完問題後，現場陷入了一陣尷尬的沉默。)\nHe felt awkward dancing in front of so many people.\n(在這麼多人面前跳舞讓他感到很尷尬。)"],["background","background(n.)背景、背景經歷\n(無詞性變化)\ncultural background 文化背景\nbackground music 背景音樂\nShe comes from a diverse cultural background with rich traditions.\n(她來自一個擁有豐富傳統的多元文化背景。)\nSoft background music was playing while we enjoyed our dinner.\n(在我們享用晚餐時，放著柔和的背景音樂。)"],["bacon","bacon(n.)培根\n(無詞性變化)\ncrispy bacon 酥脆培根\nbacon and eggs 培根煎蛋\nHe ordered a plate of crispy bacon and scrambled eggs for breakfast.\n(他早餐點了一盤酥脆培根和炒蛋。)\nThe delicious smell of frying bacon filled the entire kitchen.\n(煎培根的美味香氣瀰漫了整間廚房。)"],["bacteria","bacteria(n.)細菌 (複數)\nbacterium(n.)細菌 (單數)\nbacterial(adj.)細菌的\nharmful bacteria 有害細菌\ngrow bacteria 滋生細菌\nWashing your hands frequently with soap helps kill harmful bacteria.\n(常用肥皂洗手有助於殺死有害細菌。)\nWarm and humid conditions allow bacteria to multiply rapidly.\n(溫暖潮濕的環境會讓細菌迅速滋生。)"],["badly","badly(adv.)嚴重地、非常\nbad(adj.)壞的、差的\nbadly hurt 受傷嚴重\nbadly needed 迫切需要\nSeveral passengers were badly injured in the highway car accident.\n(幾名乘客在高速公路車禍中嚴重受傷。)\nClean drinking water is badly needed in the disaster area.\n(災區迫切需要乾淨的飲用水。)"],["baggage","baggage(n.)行李\n(無詞性變化)\nbaggage claim 行李提領處\nexcess baggage 超重行李\nPassengers can collect their suitcases at the baggage claim area.\n(旅客可以在行李提領處領取他們的行李箱。)\nYou will have to pay an extra fee if you have excess baggage.\n(如果你的行李超重，將必須支付額外費用。)"],["bait","bait(n./v.)餌、誘餌、引誘\n(無詞性變化)\nfishing bait 魚餌\ntake the bait 上當、咬餌\nHe placed a fresh earthworm on the hook as fishing bait.\n(他把一條新鮮的蚯蚓鉤在魚鉤上當作魚餌。)\nThe detective laid a trap and waited for the criminal to take the bait.\n(刑警設下陷阱，等待罪犯上當咬餌。)"],["bamboo","bamboo(n.)竹子\n(無詞性變化)\nbamboo forest 竹林\nbamboo shoots 竹筍\nGiant pandas feed almost exclusively on fresh green bamboo.\n(大貓熊幾乎完全以新鮮翠綠的竹子為食。)\nWalking through the peaceful bamboo forest brought calmness to her mind.\n(漫步在寧靜的竹林中讓她的心情平靜下來。)"],["bang","bang(n./v.)砰擊、猛擊、砰的一聲\n(無詞性變化)\nbig bang 宇宙大爆炸、巨響\nbang on the door 猛敲門\nThe wooden door closed with a loud bang due to the strong wind.\n(因為強風，木門發出砰的一聲巨響關上了。)\nHe started to bang on the locked door asking for help.\n(他開始用力猛敲反鎖的門大聲求救。)"],["banker","banker(n.)銀行家、銀行主管\nbank(n./v.)銀行、存款\nbanking(n.)銀行業\ninvestment banker 投資銀行家\nsuccessful banker 成功的銀行家\nAfter graduating from business school, he became a successful investment banker.\n(商學院畢業後，他成了一名成功的投資銀行家。)\nThe banker carefully reviewed the loan application before approving it.\n(銀行經理在批准貸款申請前仔細地進行了審查。)"],["bare","bare(adj.)赤裸的、光禿禿的\nbarely(adv.)勉強、幾乎不\nbarefoot(adj./adv.)赤腳的\nbare feet 赤腳\nbare hands 赤手空拳\nThe children enjoyed running on the sandy beach with bare feet.\n(孩子們喜歡赤腳在沙灘上奔跑。)\nHe managed to climb up the rocky cliff with his bare hands.\n(他僅憑赤手空拳就爬上了那座陡峭的岩壁。)"],["barely","barely(adv.)勉強、幾乎不\nbare(adj.)赤裸的\nbarely audible 幾乎聽不見\nbarely escape 險些逃脫\nHer voice was trembling and barely audible in the crowded room.\n(在擁擠的房間裡，她的聲音顫抖著，幾乎聽不見。)\nThe driver barely escaped being hit by the falling tree branch.\n(司機差一點就被掉落的樹枝砸中，險象環生。)"],["barn","barn(n.)穀倉、牲口棚\n(無詞性變化)\nred barn 紅色穀倉\nbarn owl 倉鴞\nThe farmer stored bales of dry hay inside the large wooden barn.\n(農夫把一捆捆乾燥的乾草存放在大型木造穀倉裡。)\nDuring the heavy rainstorm, horses were led safely into the barn.\n(暴風雨期間，馬匹被安全地牽進了牲口棚裡。)"],["barrel","barrel(n.)木桶、大圓桶、槍管\n(無詞性變化)\noil barrel 油桶\nwooden barrel 木桶\nTraditional wine is aged inside oak barrels to enhance its flavor.\n(傳統葡萄酒在橡木桶中陳釀以增添其風味。)\nThe factory produces thousands of barrels of refined oil every day.\n(這家工廠每天生產數千桶精煉石油。)"],["basement","basement(n.)地下室\nbase(n./v.)基礎、基於\nbasement parking 地下停車場\ndark basement 昏暗的地下室\nThey converted their spacious basement into a home theater.\n(他們把寬敞的地下室改造成了家庭劇院。)\nDuring the fierce tornado warning, the family took shelter in the basement.\n(在強烈的龍捲風警報期間，全家人在地下室躲避。)"],["bay","bay(n.)海灣\n(無詞性變化)\nSan Francisco Bay 舊金山灣\nkeep at bay 牽制、阻擋\nSailboats were drifting peacefully across the blue water of the bay.\n(帆船在海灣湛藍的水面上平靜地漂流。)\nEating healthy food helps keep seasonal colds and illness at bay.\n(健康飲食有助於預防季節性感冒與疾病。)"],["bead","bead(n.)珠子、小水滴\nbeaded(adj.)飾有珠子的\nglass bead 玻璃珠\nbeads of sweat 汗珠\nShe strung colorful glass beads together to make a pretty necklace.\n(她把五顏六色的玻璃珠串在一起做成一條漂亮的項鍊。)\nBeads of sweat formed on his forehead after the strenuous marathon.\n(跑完艱苦的馬拉松後，他的額頭上冒出了汗珠。)"],["beam","beam(n./v.)光線、橫梁、眉開眼笑\n(無詞性變化)\nbeam of light 一束光線\nbeam with joy 喜形於色\nA bright beam of sunlight shone through the gaps in the window curtains.\n(一道耀眼的陽光穿透窗簾縫隙照射進來。)\nThe proud mother beamed with joy when she saw her daughter graduate.\n(當看見女兒畢業時，驕傲的母親喜笑顏開。)"],["beast","beast(n.)野獸\nbeastly(adj.)殘暴的、討厭的\nwild beast 猛獸\nBeauty and the Beast 美女與野獸\nThe ancient forest was believed to be inhabited by mythical wild beasts.\n(這片古老的森林傳說中棲息著神話中的猛獸。)\nThe famous fairy tale Beauty and the Beast carries a heartwarming message.\n(著名的童話《美女與野獸》傳達了溫暖人心的啟示。)"],["beetle","beetle(n.)甲蟲\n(無詞性變化)\nstag beetle 鍬形蟲\nrhinoceros beetle 獨角仙\nThe little boy loves observing the shiny shell of the rhinoceros beetle.\n(小男孩非常喜歡觀察獨角仙有光澤的外殼。)\nMany species of beetles play an important role in forest ecosystems.\n(許多種甲蟲在森林生態系中扮演著重要的角色。)"],["beneath","beneath(prep./adv.)在...之下、在下方\n(無詞性變化)\nbeneath the surface 在表面之下\nbeneath the trees 在樹蔭下\nMuch of the huge iceberg remains hidden beneath the ocean surface.\n(巨大的冰山大部分隱藏在海洋表面之下。)\nWe sat on the bench beneath the shady trees to escape the afternoon heat.\n(我們坐在綠樹成蔭的長椅下避暑。)"],["benefit","benefit(n./v.)利益、好處、受惠\nbeneficial(adj.)有益的\nbeneficiary(n.)受益人\nhealth benefits 健康益處\nbenefit from 從...中獲益\nRegular physical exercise offers numerous long-term health benefits.\n(規律的體能鍛鍊帶來許多長期的健康益處。)\nStudents will greatly benefit from participating in practical internship programs.\n(學生將從參與實習計畫中大幅獲益。)"],["berry","berry(n.)漿果、莓果\n(無詞性變化)\npick berries 採莓果\nwild berries 野生漿果\nThe hikers picked wild berries along the sunny mountain trail.\n(登山客沿著陽光明媚的山徑採摘野生莓果。)\nStrawberries and blueberries are rich in antioxidants and vitamins.\n(草莓和藍莓富含抗氧化劑與維生素。)"],["besides","besides(prep./adv.)除...之外、此外\nbeside(prep.)在...旁邊\nbesides that 除此之外\nwho else besides 除...之外還有誰\nBesides English, she can speak fluent French and conversational Japanese.\n(除了英語之外，她還能說流利的法語和基礎日語。)\nI don't really want to go out tonight; besides, it is starting to rain.\n(我今晚不是很想出門；此外，天也開始下雨了。)"],["bet","bet(v./n.)打賭、下注、把握的事\n(無詞性變化)\nplace a bet 下注\nI bet 我敢肯定、我敢打賭\nHe placed a small bet on his favorite football team in the final.\n(他在決賽中給自己最喜歡的足球隊下了一筆小注。)\nI bet that you will pass the final English exam with flying colors.\n(我敢肯定你一定會以優異的成績通過英文期末考。)"],["bind","bind(v.)綑綁、束縛、約束\nbinding(adj./n.)有約束力的、裝訂\nbind together 連結在一起\nlegally binding 具法律約束力的\nShared cultural values and mutual respect bind the community together.\n(共同的文化價值觀與相互尊重將整個社區連結在一起。)\nBoth parties signed the contract, making it a legally binding agreement.\n(雙方均簽署了合約，使其成為具法律約束力的協議。)"],["bitter","bitter(adj.)苦的、嚴寒的、痛苦怨恨的\nbitterly(adv.)痛苦地、極其\nbitterness(n.)苦味、怨恨\nbitter taste 苦味\nbitter cold 刺骨嚴寒\nDark chocolate usually has a rich aroma and a slightly bitter taste.\n(黑巧克力通常具有濃郁的香氣和微苦的滋味。)\nThe soldiers marched forward through the bitter cold wind and heavy snow.\n(士兵們冒著刺骨的寒風與大雪向前行軍。)"],["bleed","bleed(v.)流血\nblood(n.)血液\nbloody(adj.)血腥的\nbleed heavily 大量流血\nnosebleed(n.)流鼻血\nPress firmly on the wound with a clean cloth if it starts to bleed.\n(如果傷口開始流血，請用乾淨的布用力壓住止血。)\nThe deep paper cut on his finger bled for several minutes.\n(他手指上被紙張劃出的深傷口流了好幾分鐘的血。)"],["bless","bless(v.)祝福、保佑\nblessing(n.)祝福、幸事\nblessed(adj.)有福的\nGod bless you 上帝保佑你\nblessed with 幸運享有\nThe priest raised his hands to bless the newly married couple.\n(神父舉起雙手為這對新婚夫婦祈福。)\nShe feels truly blessed with good health and supportive friends.\n(她覺得自己非常幸運，享有健康的體魄和支持她的朋友。)"],["bloody","bloody(adj.)血腥的、流血的\nblood(n.)血液\nbleed(v.)流血\nbloody battle 慘烈的血戰\nbloody nose 流鼻血\nThe historic movie portrayed the horrors of the bloody battle realistically.\n(這部歷史電影寫實地描繪了血腥戰役的殘酷面貌。)\nHe got a bloody nose after accidentally running into the glass door.\n(他不小心撞上玻璃門後流了鼻血。)"],["blouse","blouse(n.)女襯衫\n(無詞性變化)\nsilk blouse 絲綢女襯衫\nwhite blouse 白襯衫\nShe wore a formal white blouse and a dark skirt to the job interview.\n(她穿著正式的白襯衫和深色裙子去參加求職面試。)\nThe delicate silk blouse should be washed by hand with gentle care.\n(這件精緻的絲質女襯衫應該用手輕柔清洗。)"],["bold","bold(adj.)大膽的、勇敢的、粗體的\nboldly(adv.)大膽地\nboldness(n.)大膽、魄力\nbold move 大膽的舉動\nin bold font 粗體字\nStarting his own technology company at age twenty was a bold move.\n(他在二十歲時創立自己的科技公司是一次大膽的嘗試。)\nKey terms in the textbook are printed in bold font for easy review.\n(教科書中的關鍵術語以粗體字印出以便於複習。)"],["bomb","bomb(n./v.)炸彈、轟炸\nbomber(n.)轟炸機\nbombing(n.)轟炸事件\ntime bomb 定時炸彈\nbomb threat 炸彈威脅\nThe security squad was called in to safely defuse the unexploded bomb.\n(防爆小組受命前來安全拆除未引爆的炸彈。)\nThe police evacuated the busy airport terminal after receiving a bomb threat.\n(警方接到炸彈威脅後，疏散了繁忙的機場航廈。)"],["bookcase","bookcase(n.)書架、書櫃\nbook(n.)書\ncase(n.)箱、盒\nwooden bookcase 木質書櫃\nshelf of a bookcase 書架層板\nHe organized his extensive novel collection neatly on the wooden bookcase.\n(他把數量豐富的小說收藏整齊地排列在木質書櫃上。)\nThe heavy bookcase took up most of the space along the living room wall.\n(沉重的書櫃佔據了客廳牆面大部分的空間。)"],["boot","boot(n.)靴子、(車輛)後車廂\n(無詞性變化)\nhiking boots 登山靴\nrain boots 雨靴\nMake sure to wear sturdy waterproof hiking boots when climbing rough mountains.\n(攀登崎嶇山路時務必穿著堅固防水的登山靴。)\nThe little boy put on his yellow boots to splash happily in muddy puddles.\n(小男孩穿上黃色雨靴，開心地在泥水坑裡踏水。)"],["bore","bore(v./n.)使厭煩、令人討厭的人事物\nbored(adj.)感到厭煩的\nboring(adj.)無聊的\nboredom(n.)無聊\nbored to death 無聊得要死\nbore tears 令人無聊至極\nLong speeches with unnecessary details often bore the restless audience.\n(冗長且充斥不必要細節的演講常使坐立難安的聽眾感到厭煩。)\nI hope my endless travel stories do not bore you too much.\n(我希望我那些講個沒完的旅行故事沒有讓你覺得太無聊。)"],["bowling","bowling(n.)保齡球運動\nbowl(v.)打保齡球\nbowler(n.)保齡球選手\ngo bowling 去打保齡球\nbowling alley 保齡球館\nWe decided to go bowling at the recreation center on Saturday evening.\n(我們決定週六晚上去育樂中心打保齡球。)\nHe scored three strikes in a row at the crowded bowling alley.\n(他在熱鬧的保齡球館裡連續擊出了三次全倒。)"],["brake","brake(n./v.)煞車、制動器、煞車減速\n(無詞性變化)\nhit the brakes 踩煞車\nbrake suddenly 緊急煞車\nThe driver hit the brakes hard to avoid hitting the crossing dog.\n(司機猛踩煞車以避免撞上過馬路的狗。)\nYou should regularly check your bicycle brakes before riding downhill.\n(下坡前你應該定期檢查腳踏車的煞車功能。)"],["brass","brass(n.)黃銅、黃銅樂器\n(無詞性變化)\nbrass instrument 銅管樂器\nbrass band 銅管樂隊\nThe antique door handle was crafted from shiny polished brass.\n(這款復古門把是由光澤閃亮的拋光黃銅製成的。)\nTrumpets and trombones belong to the brass section of the orchestra.\n(小號和長號屬於管弦樂團中的銅管樂器組。)"],["bravery","bravery(n.)英勇、勇氣\nbrave(adj.)勇敢的\nbravely(adv.)英勇地\nmedal for bravery 英勇勳章\nact of bravery 勇敢行徑\nThe brave firefighter was awarded a medal for extraordinary bravery.\n(英勇的消防員因其非凡的勇氣而獲頒勳章。)\nRescuing the drowning child from the rushing river was an inspiring act of bravery.\n(從湍急的河流中救起溺水孩童是令人感佩的英勇行徑。)"],["breast","breast(n.)乳房、胸膛、胸部\n(無詞性變化)\nbreast cancer 乳癌\nchicken breast 雞胸肉\nRegular medical screenings are essential for early detection of breast cancer.\n(定期健康篩檢對於及早發現乳癌至關重要。)\nGrilled chicken breast is a popular healthy meal choice for athletes.\n(烤雞胸肉是運動員常見且喜愛的健康餐點選擇。)"],["breath","breath(n.)呼吸、氣息\nbreathe(v.)呼吸\nbreathless(adj.)喘不過氣的\ntake a deep breath 深吸一口氣\nout of breath 上氣不接下氣\nTake a deep breath and relax before beginning your oral presentation.\n(在開始口頭簡報前，深吸一口氣並放鬆身心。)\nHe was completely out of breath after running up five flights of stairs.\n(在跑上五層樓梯後，他喘得完全上氣不接下氣。)"],["breathe","breathe(v.)呼吸、吸入\nbreath(n.)呼吸\nbreathing(n.)呼吸\nbreathe in 吸氣\nbreathe out 呼氣\nIt feels wonderful to step outside and breathe the fresh morning air.\n(走進戶外大口呼吸清晨的新鮮空氣令人心曠神怡。)\nThe yoga instructor told the students to breathe in slowly through their nose.\n(瑜伽教練囑咐學員用鼻子緩慢地吸氣。)"],["breeze","breeze(n.)微風、輕而易舉的事\nbreezy(adj.)有微風的、輕快的\ngentle breeze 微風\nsea breeze 海風\nA cool gentle breeze blew across the lake, making the summer heat bearable.\n(一陣涼爽的微風拂過湖面，使夏天的炎熱變得好受些。)\nThanks to thorough preparation, the math test was an absolute breeze for him.\n(由於準備充足，那場數學考試對他來說完全是輕而易舉。)"],["brick","brick(n.)磚塊\n(無詞性變化)\nbrick wall 磚牆\nred brick 紅磚\nThe historic cottage was built with solid red bricks over a century ago.\n(這座歷史悠久的小屋是一百多年前用堅固的紅磚砌成的。)\nHe stacked the remaining bricks neatly beside the garage.\n(他把剩下的磚塊整齊地堆放在車庫旁邊。)"],["bride","bride(n.)新娘\nbridal(adj.)婚禮的、新娘的\nbridegroom(n.)新郎\nbride and groom 新娘與新郎\nblushing bride 嬌羞幸福的新娘\nThe smiling bride walked down the church aisle accompanied by her father.\n(面帶微笑的新娘在父親的陪伴下走過教堂紅毯。)\nGuests cheered enthusiastically as the bride and groom shared their first dance.\n(當新娘與新郎共舞第一支舞時，賓客們熱情地歡呼。)"],["broadcast","broadcast(n./v.)廣播、播送\nbroadcaster(n.)廣播員、廣播公司\nlive broadcast 現場直播\nbroadcast live 現場播出\nThe Olympic opening ceremony was broadcast live to millions of viewers worldwide.\n(奧運開幕典禮向全球數百萬觀眾進行了現場直播。)\nTune in to the local radio station for the latest weather broadcast.\n(請鎖定當地廣播電台以收聽最新的天氣廣播。)"],["brunch","brunch(n.)早午餐\n(無詞性變化)\nSunday brunch 週日早午餐\nhave brunch 吃早午餐\nWe decided to meet friends for a relaxing Sunday brunch at a cozy café.\n(我們決定和朋友在一間溫馨的咖啡館共進悠閒的週日早午餐。)\nBrunch typically combines breakfast items like pancakes with savory lunch dishes.\n(早午餐通常結合了煎餅等早餐品項與美味的午餐菜色。)"],["bubble","bubble(n./v.)氣泡、水泡、冒泡\nbubbly(adj.)起泡的、活潑的\nsoap bubble 肥皂泡\neconomic bubble 經濟泡沫\nChildren had fun blowing colorful soap bubbles in the sunny park.\n(孩子們在陽光明媚的公園裡開心地吹著五彩繽紛的肥皂泡。)\nWater began to bubble and steam when it reached boiling point.\n(水達到沸點時開始冒泡並產生蒸汽。)"],["bucket","bucket(n.)水桶\nbucketful(n.)滿滿一桶\nbucket list 人生願望清單\na bucket of water 一桶水\nTraveling to see the northern lights is at the very top of my bucket list.\n(去欣賞北極光位居我人生願望清單的第一位。)\nHe filled the plastic bucket with warm water to wash the family car.\n(他把塑膠水桶裝滿溫水來清洗家裡的汽車。)"],["bud","bud(n./v.)花蕾、芽、發芽\nbudding(adj.)萌芽的、有發展潛力的\nrose bud 玫瑰花蕾\nnip in the bud 防患於未然、扼殺在萌芽階段\nIn early spring, tiny flower buds begin to appear on the bare branches.\n(初春時節，微小的花蕾開始出現在光禿禿的枝頭上。)\nParents and teachers should work together to nip bad behavioral habits in the bud.\n(家長和老師應該共同努力，將不良行為習慣防患於未然。)"],["budget","budget(n./v.)預算、編列預算\nbudgetary(adj.)預算的\non a budget 預算有限\nannual budget 年度預算\nTraveling on a tight budget requires careful planning and smart choices.\n(在預算吃緊的情況下旅行需要周詳的規劃與明智的選擇。)\nThe school board approved the annual budget for the upcoming academic year.\n(校董會審批了即將到來學年的年度預算。)"],["buffalo","buffalo(n.)水牛、野牛\n(無詞性變化)\nwater buffalo 水牛\nherd of buffalo 一群野牛\nIn traditional Taiwanese farming, water buffaloes were indispensable helpers.\n(在台灣傳統農業中，水牛是不可或缺的得力幫手。)\nA large herd of wild buffalo grazed peacefully across the open grassland.\n(一大群野生水牛在遼闊的草原上悠閒吃草。)"],["buffet","buffet(n.)自助餐\n(無詞性變化)\nbuffet dinner 自助晚餐\nall-you-can-eat buffet 吃到飽自助餐\nThe luxury hotel offers a wonderful seafood buffet dinner on weekends.\n(這家豪華飯店在週末提供豐盛的海鮮自助晚餐。)\nYou can help yourself to a wide variety of fresh dishes at the buffet counter.\n(你可以在自助餐檯隨意享用各式各樣的新鮮菜餚。)"],["bulb","bulb(n.)電燈泡、球莖\n(無詞性變化)\nlight bulb 電燈泡\nplant bulbs 種植球莖\nReplacing old incandescent bulbs with LED bulbs saves significant electricity.\n(將老舊白熾燈泡更換為 LED 燈泡可大幅節省電力。)\nShe planted tulip bulbs in the garden before the first winter frost.\n(她在入冬第一道霜降前在花園裡種下了鬱金香球莖。)"],["bull","bull(n.)公牛、看漲行情\nbullish(adj.)樂觀的、看漲的\nbull market 牛市(股市大漲)\ngrab the bull by the horns 挺身面對困難\nInvestors were excited as the stock market entered a strong bull market.\n(隨著股市進入強勁的牛市行情，投資者感到興奮不已。)\nInstead of avoiding the difficult challenge, she decided to grab the bull by the horns.\n(她決定挺身直接面對困難，而不是逃避這項艱鉅的挑戰。)"],["bullet","bullet(n.)子彈、圓形點標記\nbulletproof(adj.)防彈的\nbullet train 高速火車、子彈列車\nbullet point 條列項目符號\nRiding the high-speed bullet train between Tokyo and Osaka is extremely convenient.\n(搭乘往返東京與大阪的高速子彈列車極為便利。)\nUse bullet points in your presentation slides to make key ideas easier to read.\n(在簡報投影片中使用條列式圓點標記，能讓重點更加一目了然。)"],["bump","bump(n./v.)碰撞、腫塊、隆起、撞擊\nbumpy(adj.)顛簸的\nspeed bump 減速丘\nbump into 偶遇、巧遇\nDrivers are required to slow down before passing over the speed bump.\n(駕駛人在駛過減速丘之前必須放慢車速。)\nI was surprised to bump into an old middle school classmate at the supermarket.\n(我很驚喜在超市巧遇了一位國中老同學。)"],["bunch","bunch(n.)一束、一串、一群\n(無詞性變化)\na bunch of flowers 一束花\na bunch of keys 一串鑰匙\nHe bought a beautiful bunch of fresh red roses for his mother's birthday.\n(他買了一束漂亮的鮮紅玫瑰慶祝母親的生日。)\nThanks a bunch for helping me move the heavy furniture into the new room.\n(非常感謝你幫我把沉重的家具搬進新房間。)"],["bundle","bundle(n./v.)包裹、一捆、捆綁\n(無詞性變化)\nbundle up 穿暖和\na bundle of sticks 一捆木棍\nRemember to bundle up warmly before going outside into the freezing snowy weather.\n(在走入酷寒的大雪天之前，記得多穿點衣服保暖。)\nThe mail carrier delivered a neat bundle of letters and magazines this morning.\n(郵差今天早晨送來了一整捆整齊的信件與雜誌。)"],["bury","bury(v.)埋葬、埋藏、埋首於\nburial(n.)葬禮、埋葬\nbury the hatchet 言歸於好、和解\nbury oneself in 埋首於、專心於\nAfter a long feud, the two rival families finally decided to bury the hatchet.\n(在長期的不和之後，這兩個宿怨家族終於決定冰釋前嫌、言歸於好。)\nDuring exam week, students bury themselves in textbooks and class notes.\n(在考試週期間，學生們全身心埋首於教科書與課堂筆記中。)"],["bush","bush(n.)灌木、矮樹叢\nbushy(adj.)茂密的、濃密的\nrose bush 玫瑰花叢\nbeat around the bush 拐彎抹角\nA tiny brown bird built its cozy nest deep inside the thick rose bush.\n(一隻棕色小鳥在茂密的玫瑰花叢深處築起了溫馨的巢。)\nPlease stop beating around the bush and tell us directly what happened.\n(請別再拐彎抹角了，直接告訴我們到底發生了什麼事。)"],["buzz","buzz(n./v.)嗡嗡聲、蜂鳴、嗡嗡作響、熱議\nbuzzer(n.)蜂鳴器\nbuzz of bees 蜜蜂的嗡嗡聲\nbuzz with excitement 興奮熱絡\nThe garden was filled with the gentle buzz of honeybees gathering sweet nectar.\n(花園裡充滿了採集甜美花蜜的蜜蜂發出的輕柔嗡嗡聲。)\nThe entire school auditorium was buzzing with excitement before the concert began.\n(在音樂會開始前，整個學校禮堂充滿了興奮熱烈的氣氛。)"],["cabin","cabin(n.)小木屋、船艙、機艙\n(無詞性變化)\nlog cabin 小木屋\ncabin crew 空服人員\nWe stayed in a small cabin in the mountains.\n(我們住在山上的一間小木屋。)\nThe cabin crew served drinks during the flight.\n(空服人員在飛行途中提供飲料。)"],["cable","cable(n./v.)纜線、電纜、有線電視、發電報\n(無詞性變化)\ncable TV 有線電視\ncable car 纜車\nWe took a cable car up to Maokong.\n(我們搭纜車上貓空。)\nThis cable connects the printer to the computer.\n(這條線把印表機連接到電腦。)"],["cafeteria","cafeteria(n.)自助餐廳、學生餐廳\n(無詞性變化)\nschool cafeteria 學校餐廳\ncafeteria food 餐廳伙食\nWe usually eat lunch in the school cafeteria.\n(我們通常在學校餐廳吃午餐。)\nThe cafeteria is crowded at noon.\n(中午時自助餐廳很擁擠。)"],["campus","campus(n.)校園\n(無詞性變化)\non campus 在校園內\ncampus life 校園生活\nStudents are not allowed to smoke on campus.\n(學生不得在校園內吸菸。)\nShe enjoys her campus life very much.\n(她非常享受她的校園生活。)"],["canyon","canyon(n.)峽谷\n(無詞性變化)\nGrand Canyon 大峽谷\ndeep canyon 深谷\nThe river flows through a deep canyon.\n(這條河流經一座深谷。)\nTaroko is famous for its marble canyon.\n(太魯閣以大理石峽谷聞名。)"],["capable","capable(adj.)有能力的、能幹的\ncapability(n.)能力\nincapable(adj.)無能力的\nbe capable of 有能力做……\nhighly capable 非常能幹\nShe is capable of solving difficult problems.\n(她有能力解決困難的問題。)\nWe need a capable leader for this project.\n(這個計畫需要一位能幹的領導者。)"],["captain","captain(n.)船長、機長、隊長\n(無詞性變化)\nteam captain 隊長\nship captain 船長\nHe was chosen as the captain of the basketball team.\n(他被選為籃球隊隊長。)\nThe captain told the passengers to stay calm.\n(機長要求乘客保持冷靜。)"],["capture","capture(v./n.)捕捉、俘虜、吸引(注意)\ncaptive(n.)俘虜\ncapture attention 吸引注意\ncapture the moment 捕捉那一刻\nThe photographer captured the beautiful sunset.\n(攝影師捕捉到美麗的夕陽。)\nThe story captured the hearts of many readers.\n(這個故事擄獲了許多讀者的心。)"],["career","career(n.)職業、生涯\n(無詞性變化)\ncareer goal 職涯目標\ncareer choice 職業選擇\nShe wants to have a career in medicine.\n(她想從事醫療方面的職業。)\nHe spent his whole career as a teacher.\n(他整個職業生涯都在當老師。)"],["carpenter","carpenter(n.)木匠\ncarpentry(n.)木工\nskilled carpenter 熟練的木匠\nhire a carpenter 請木匠\nThe carpenter made a new table for us.\n(木匠為我們做了一張新桌子。)\nMy grandfather was a skilled carpenter.\n(我祖父是一位手藝精湛的木匠。)"],["carpet","carpet(n./v.)地毯、鋪地毯\n(無詞性變化)\nred carpet 紅地毯\ncarpet floor 地毯地板\nThe stars walked down the red carpet.\n(明星們走過紅地毯。)\nThe cat is sleeping on the carpet.\n(貓正睡在地毯上。)"],["carriage","carriage(n.)馬車、車廂\ncarry(v.)攜帶、運送\nhorse-drawn carriage 馬車\nbaby carriage 嬰兒車\nThe princess rode in a golden carriage.\n(公主坐在一輛金色馬車裡。)\nThe train has eight carriages.\n(這列火車有八節車廂。)"],["cart","cart(n./v.)手推車、運貨馬車、用車運送\n(無詞性變化)\nshopping cart 購物車\npush a cart 推車\nHe put the groceries in the shopping cart.\n(他把雜貨放進購物車。)\nThe workers carted the bricks away.\n(工人們用推車把磚塊運走。)"],["cast","cast(v./n.)投擲、投射、演員陣容、石膏\n(無詞性變化)\ncast a shadow 投下陰影\ncast a vote 投票\nThe tall tree cast a long shadow.\n(那棵高大的樹投下長長的影子。)\nThe movie has an amazing cast.\n(這部電影的演員陣容很強。)"],["casual","casual(adj.)隨意的、非正式的、偶然的\ncasually(adv.)隨意地\ncasual clothes 便服\ncasual conversation 閒聊\nYou can wear casual clothes on Friday.\n(星期五你可以穿便服。)\nWe had a casual chat over coffee.\n(我們邊喝咖啡邊隨意聊天。)"],["cattle","cattle(n.)牛(集合名詞)\n(無詞性變化)\nraise cattle 養牛\nherd of cattle 一群牛\nThe farmer raises cattle and sheep.\n(這位農夫養牛和羊。)\nA herd of cattle was eating grass in the field.\n(一群牛在田野上吃草。)"],["cave","cave(n./v.)洞穴、塌陷\ncaveman(n.)穴居人\ncave in 塌陷\nexplore a cave 探索洞穴\nThe bats live in a dark cave.\n(蝙蝠住在一個黑暗的洞穴裡。)\nThe roof of the old house caved in.\n(那棟老房子的屋頂塌了。)"],["champion","champion(n.)冠軍、擁護者\nchampionship(n.)冠軍賽、冠軍頭銜\nworld champion 世界冠軍\ndefending champion 衛冕冠軍\nShe became the national tennis champion.\n(她成為全國網球冠軍。)\nOur team is the defending champion.\n(我們隊是衛冕冠軍。)"],["charm","charm(n./v.)魅力、吸引、護身符\ncharming(adj.)迷人的\nlucky charm 幸運物\ncharm sb. 迷住某人\nThe old town has a special charm.\n(這座古鎮有種特別的魅力。)\nShe charmed everyone with her smile.\n(她的笑容迷倒了每個人。)"],["chat","chat(n./v.)聊天、閒談\nchatty(adj.)愛聊天的\nhave a chat 聊一聊\nchat online 線上聊天\nWe had a nice chat after class.\n(下課後我們愉快地聊了一下。)\nI often chat with my friends online.\n(我常常和朋友在網路上聊天。)"],["cheek","cheek(n.)臉頰\ncheeky(adj.)厚臉皮的\nrosy cheeks 紅潤的臉頰\nkiss on the cheek 親吻臉頰\nTears ran down her cheeks.\n(淚水從她的臉頰流下。)\nThe baby has round, rosy cheeks.\n(這個寶寶有圓圓紅潤的臉頰。)"],["cheerful","cheerful(adj.)開朗的、愉快的\ncheer(v.)歡呼、使高興\ncheerfully(adv.)愉快地\ncheerful smile 開朗的笑容\ncheerful mood 愉快的心情\nOur teacher is always cheerful and kind.\n(我們的老師總是開朗又親切。)\nThe bright colors make the room look cheerful.\n(明亮的色彩讓房間看起來很愉快。)"],["cherry","cherry(n./adj.)櫻桃、櫻花樹、櫻桃色的\n(無詞性變化)\ncherry blossom 櫻花\ncherry tree 櫻花樹\nWe went to Alishan to see the cherry blossoms.\n(我們去阿里山看櫻花。)\nThere is a cherry on top of the cake.\n(蛋糕上面有一顆櫻桃。)"],["chest","chest(n.)胸部、箱子\n(無詞性變化)\nchest pain 胸痛\ntreasure chest 寶箱\nHe felt a sharp pain in his chest.\n(他感到胸口一陣劇痛。)\nThe pirates hid a treasure chest on the island.\n(海盜們把寶箱藏在島上。)"],["chill","chill(n./v./adj.)寒意、使變冷、冷的\nchilly(adj.)寒冷的\nchill out 放輕鬆\ncatch a chill 著涼\nThere is a chill in the air this morning.\n(今天早上空氣中有股寒意。)\nChill the juice in the fridge before serving.\n(上桌前把果汁放冰箱冰一下。)"],["chilly","chilly(adj.)寒冷的、冷淡的\nchill(n.)寒意\nchilly morning 寒冷的早晨\nchilly wind 冷風\nIt's chilly outside, so take a jacket.\n(外面很冷，帶件外套吧。)\nHe received a chilly welcome from his neighbors.\n(他受到鄰居們冷淡的接待。)"],["chimney","chimney(n.)煙囪\n(無詞性變化)\nfactory chimney 工廠煙囪\ncome down the chimney 從煙囪下來\nSmoke was rising from the chimney.\n(煙從煙囪裡冒出來。)\nSanta Claus comes down the chimney on Christmas Eve.\n(聖誕老人在平安夜從煙囪下來。)"],["chin","chin(n.)下巴\n(無詞性變化)\nchin up 振作起來\ndouble chin 雙下巴\nHe rested his chin on his hand.\n(他用手托著下巴。)\nKeep your chin up and try again.\n(振作起來再試一次。)"],["chip","chip(n./v.)碎片、晶片、洋芋片、削下\n(無詞性變化)\npotato chips 洋芋片\ncomputer chip 電腦晶片\nWe ate potato chips while watching the movie.\n(我們一邊看電影一邊吃洋芋片。)\nTaiwan is famous for making computer chips.\n(台灣以製造電腦晶片聞名。)"],["chop","chop(n./v.)砍、剁、切碎、排骨\nchopper(n.)切肉刀、直升機(口語)\nchop up 切碎\npork chop 豬排\nChop the onions into small pieces.\n(把洋蔥切成小塊。)\nI had a pork chop with rice for lunch.\n(我午餐吃排骨飯。)"],["cigarette","cigarette(n.)香菸\n(無詞性變化)\nsmoke a cigarette 抽菸\ncigarette butt 菸蒂\nSmoking cigarettes is bad for your health.\n(抽菸對健康有害。)\nDon't throw cigarette butts on the street.\n(不要把菸蒂丟在街上。)"],["cinema","cinema(n.)電影院、電影\ncinematic(adj.)電影的\ngo to the cinema 去看電影\ncinema ticket 電影票\nLet's go to the cinema this weekend.\n(這個週末我們去看電影吧。)\nThe new cinema has very comfortable seats.\n(新電影院的座位非常舒適。)"],["circus","circus(n.)馬戲團\n(無詞性變化)\ncircus clown 馬戲團小丑\ncircus performer 馬戲團表演者\nThe children laughed at the circus clown.\n(孩子們被馬戲團小丑逗得哈哈大笑。)\nThe circus comes to town every summer.\n(馬戲團每年夏天都會來鎮上。)"],["citizen","citizen(n.)公民、市民\ncitizenship(n.)公民身分\nsenior citizen 年長者\ngood citizen 好公民\nEvery citizen has the right to vote.\n(每位公民都有投票權。)\nSenior citizens can take the bus for free.\n(年長者可以免費搭公車。)"],["civil","civil(adj.)公民的、民用的、有禮貌的\ncivilian(n.)平民\ncivil war 內戰\ncivil rights 公民權\nThe country suffered from a long civil war.\n(這個國家飽受長期內戰之苦。)\nMartin Luther King fought for civil rights.\n(馬丁‧路德‧金恩為公民權利奮鬥。)"],["clay","clay(n.)黏土、陶土\n(無詞性變化)\nclay pot 陶罐\nmodeling clay 黏土\nThe children made animals out of clay.\n(孩子們用黏土做動物。)\nThis clay pot was made by hand.\n(這個陶罐是手工做的。)"],["cleaner","cleaner(n.)清潔工、清潔劑、吸塵器\nclean(v./adj.)清潔、乾淨的\nvacuum cleaner 吸塵器\nglass cleaner 玻璃清潔劑\nThe cleaner comes to clean our office every night.\n(清潔工每晚都會來打掃我們的辦公室。)\nUse a vacuum cleaner to clean the carpet.\n(用吸塵器清理地毯。)"],["client","client(n.)客戶、委託人\nclientele(n.)客戶群\nmeet a client 會見客戶\nregular client 常客\nThe lawyer is meeting with a client now.\n(律師現在正在會見一位委託人。)\nWe must keep our clients happy.\n(我們必須讓客戶滿意。)"],["clinic","clinic(n.)診所\nclinical(adj.)臨床的\ndental clinic 牙醫診所\ngo to the clinic 去診所\nI went to the clinic because I had a fever.\n(我因為發燒去了診所。)\nThe dental clinic opens at nine.\n(那間牙醫診所九點開門。)"],["clip","clip(n./v.)夾子、片段、修剪、夾住\nclipper(n.)指甲剪、剪刀\npaper clip 迴紋針\nvideo clip 影片片段\nUse a paper clip to hold these pages together.\n(用迴紋針把這幾頁夾在一起。)\nHe watched a funny video clip online.\n(他在網路上看了一段搞笑影片。)"],["closet","closet(n.)衣櫥、壁櫥\n(無詞性變化)\nwalk-in closet 更衣間\nclothes closet 衣櫃\nHang your coat in the closet.\n(把你的外套掛進衣櫥。)\nHer closet is full of dresses.\n(她的衣櫥裡滿是洋裝。)"],["clothe","clothe(v.)給……穿衣、提供衣服\nclothes(n.)衣服\nclothing(n.)衣物(總稱)\nfeed and clothe 供吃供穿\nbe clothed in 穿著……\nParents work hard to feed and clothe their children.\n(父母努力工作供孩子吃穿。)\nThe bride was clothed in white.\n(新娘身穿白衣。)"],["clown","clown(n./v.)小丑、搞笑的人、扮小丑\n(無詞性變化)\nclass clown 班上的開心果\nclown around 胡鬧\nHe is the class clown and always makes us laugh.\n(他是班上的開心果，總是逗我們笑。)\nStop clowning around and do your homework.\n(別再胡鬧了，去寫功課。)"],["clue","clue(n.)線索、提示\nclueless(adj.)毫無頭緒的\nfind a clue 找到線索\nhave no clue 毫無頭緒\nThe police found an important clue.\n(警方找到一個重要線索。)\nI have no clue what he is talking about.\n(我完全不知道他在說什麼。)"],["coach","coach(n./v.)教練、長途巴士、指導\n(無詞性變化)\nhead coach 總教練\ncoach a team 指導球隊\nOur coach makes us run every morning.\n(我們教練每天早上要我們跑步。)\nShe coaches the school volleyball team.\n(她指導學校的排球隊。)"],["cock","cock(n.)公雞\n(無詞性變化)\ncock crow 雞鳴\nfighting cock 鬥雞\nThe cock crowed at dawn.\n(公雞在黎明時啼叫。)\nA cock was walking around the farmyard.\n(一隻公雞在農家院子裡走來走去。)"],["cocktail","cocktail(n.)雞尾酒\n(無詞性變化)\ncocktail party 雞尾酒會\nfruit cocktail 什錦水果\nThey served fruit cocktail as dessert.\n(他們端上什錦水果當甜點。)\nMy parents went to a cocktail party last night.\n(我爸媽昨晚去參加了雞尾酒會。)"],["coconut","coconut(n.)椰子\n(無詞性變化)\ncoconut milk 椰奶\ncoconut tree 椰子樹\nWe drank fresh coconut water on the beach.\n(我們在海灘上喝新鮮的椰子水。)\nCoconut trees line the road in Kenting.\n(墾丁的道路兩旁種滿椰子樹。)"],["collar","collar(n.)衣領、項圈\n(無詞性變化)\nshirt collar 襯衫領子\ndog collar 狗項圈\nThere is a stain on your shirt collar.\n(你的襯衫領子上有汙漬。)\nThe dog wears a red collar.\n(那隻狗戴著紅色項圈。)"],["collection","collection(n.)收集、收藏品、募捐\ncollect(v.)收集\ncollector(n.)收藏家\nstamp collection 集郵\ngarbage collection 垃圾收集\nHe has a large collection of stamps.\n(他收藏了大量郵票。)\nThe museum has a famous collection of Chinese art.\n(這間博物館有著名的中國藝術收藏。)"],["colony","colony(n.)殖民地、群體\ncolonial(adj.)殖民的\ncolonize(v.)殖民\nformer colony 前殖民地\nant colony 蟻群\nHong Kong was once a British colony.\n(香港曾經是英國的殖民地。)\nAn ant colony can have thousands of ants.\n(一個蟻群可以有數千隻螞蟻。)"],["colorful","colorful(adj.)色彩繽紛的、多采多姿的\ncolor(n.)顏色\ncolorful flowers 色彩繽紛的花\ncolorful life 多采多姿的生活\nThe garden is full of colorful flowers.\n(花園裡開滿了色彩繽紛的花。)\nMy grandfather has had a colorful life.\n(我祖父有著多采多姿的人生。)"],["column","column(n.)圓柱、專欄、(表格)直行\ncolumnist(n.)專欄作家\nstone column 石柱\nnewspaper column 報紙專欄\nThe temple is supported by huge stone columns.\n(這座廟由巨大的石柱支撐。)\nShe writes a weekly column for a newspaper.\n(她每週為一家報紙寫專欄。)"],["comfort","comfort(n./v.)舒適、安慰\ncomfortable(adj.)舒適的\ncomfortably(adv.)舒適地\ncomfort zone 舒適圈\nin comfort 舒適地\nShe tried to comfort her crying friend.\n(她試著安慰哭泣的朋友。)\nTry to step out of your comfort zone.\n(試著走出你的舒適圈。)"],["comma","comma(n.)逗號\n(無詞性變化)\nput a comma 加逗號\ncomma splice 逗號誤接\nPut a comma after the word 'however'.\n(在 however 這個字後面加逗號。)\nYou forgot a comma in this sentence.\n(你在這個句子裡漏了一個逗號。)"],["committee","committee(n.)委員會\n(無詞性變化)\nstudent committee 學生委員會\ncommittee meeting 委員會會議\nThe committee will make a decision next week.\n(委員會將在下週做出決定。)\nShe is a member of the school committee.\n(她是學校委員會的成員。)"],["communicate","communicate(v.)溝通、傳達\ncommunication(n.)溝通\ncommunicative(adj.)健談的、溝通的\ncommunicate with 與……溝通\ncommunicate ideas 傳達想法\nIt is important to communicate with your parents.\n(和父母溝通很重要。)\nWe communicate by email most of the time.\n(我們大多透過電子郵件聯絡。)"],["comparison","comparison(n.)比較、比喻\ncompare(v.)比較\ncomparative(adj.)比較的\nin comparison with 與……相比\nmake a comparison 做比較\nIn comparison with last year, sales have increased.\n(和去年相比，銷售量增加了。)\nThere is no comparison between the two phones.\n(這兩支手機根本無法相比。)"],["compete","compete(v.)競爭、參賽\ncompetition(n.)競爭、比賽\ncompetitive(adj.)競爭的\ncompete with 與……競爭\ncompete for 爭奪\nTen teams will compete for the prize.\n(十支隊伍將爭奪這個獎項。)\nSmall shops find it hard to compete with big stores.\n(小商店很難與大賣場競爭。)"],["complain","complain(v.)抱怨、投訴\ncomplaint(n.)抱怨、投訴\ncomplain about 抱怨……\ncomplain to 向……投訴\nHe always complains about the weather.\n(他總是抱怨天氣。)\nWe complained to the manager about the noise.\n(我們向經理投訴噪音問題。)"],["complaint","complaint(n.)抱怨、投訴\ncomplain(v.)抱怨\nmake a complaint 投訴\ncustomer complaint 客訴\nThe hotel received many complaints about the noise.\n(飯店收到許多關於噪音的投訴。)\nIf you are not happy, you can make a complaint.\n(如果你不滿意，可以提出投訴。)"],["concert","concert(n.)音樂會、演唱會\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to a concert 去聽演唱會\nconcert hall 音樂廳\nWe went to Mayday's concert last night.\n(我們昨晚去看了五月天的演唱會。)\nThe orchestra will perform at the concert hall.\n(管弦樂團將在音樂廳演出。)"],["conclusion","conclusion(n.)結論、結尾\nconclude(v.)下結論、結束\nconclusive(adj.)決定性的\nin conclusion 總而言之\ncome to a conclusion 得出結論\nIn conclusion, exercise is good for everyone.\n(總而言之，運動對每個人都有益。)\nDon't jump to conclusions too quickly.\n(不要太快下結論。)"],["cone","cone(n.)圓錐體、甜筒、毬果\n(無詞性變化)\nice cream cone 冰淇淋甜筒\ntraffic cone 交通錐\nShe bought a chocolate ice cream cone.\n(她買了一支巧克力冰淇淋甜筒。)\nTraffic cones were placed around the hole.\n(洞的周圍擺放了交通錐。)"],["confirm","confirm(v.)確認、證實\nconfirmation(n.)確認\nconfirm a booking 確認預訂\nconfirm the news 證實消息\nPlease call to confirm your reservation.\n(請打電話確認您的訂位。)\nThe doctor confirmed that the bone was broken.\n(醫生證實骨頭斷了。)"],["confuse","confuse(v.)使困惑、混淆\nconfusion(n.)困惑、混亂\nconfused(adj.)困惑的\nconfusing(adj.)令人困惑的\nconfuse A with B 把 A 和 B 搞混\nconfusing instructions 令人困惑的說明\nI always confuse him with his twin brother.\n(我總是把他和他的雙胞胎弟弟搞混。)\nThe teacher's explanation confused the students.\n(老師的解釋讓學生們很困惑。)"],["connect","connect(v.)連接、聯繫\nconnection(n.)連接、關聯\nconnect to 連接到\nbe connected with 與……有關\nConnect your phone to the Wi-Fi.\n(把你的手機連上無線網路。)\nThis bridge connects the two islands.\n(這座橋連接兩座島嶼。)"],["conscious","conscious(adj.)有意識的、察覺到的、刻意的\nconsciousness(n.)意識\nunconscious(adj.)無意識的\nbe conscious of 意識到\nhealth-conscious 注重健康的\nShe is conscious of her weight.\n(她很在意自己的體重。)\nHe was still conscious after the accident.\n(意外發生後他仍然有意識。)"],["considerable","considerable(adj.)相當大的、可觀的\nconsiderably(adv.)相當地\nconsiderable amount 相當大的數量\nconsiderable effort 相當大的努力\nThe project took a considerable amount of time.\n(這個計畫花了相當多的時間。)\nHe made considerable progress in English.\n(他的英文有相當大的進步。)"],["constant","constant(adj./n.)持續的、不變的、常數\nconstantly(adv.)不斷地\nconstant noise 持續的噪音\nconstant temperature 恆溫\nThe baby needs constant care.\n(嬰兒需要持續不斷的照顧。)\nKeep the room at a constant temperature.\n(讓房間保持恆溫。)"],["continent","continent(n.)大陸、洲\ncontinental(adj.)大陸的\nseven continents 七大洲\nthe African continent 非洲大陸\nAsia is the largest continent in the world.\n(亞洲是世界上最大的洲。)\nShe has traveled to every continent.\n(她已經去過每一個洲。)"],["controller","controller(n.)控制器、管理者\ncontrol(v./n.)控制\ngame controller 遊戲手把\nair traffic controller 航管人員\nMy game controller stopped working.\n(我的遊戲手把壞了。)\nAir traffic controllers have a very stressful job.\n(航管人員的工作壓力非常大。)"],["cooker","cooker(n.)炊具、爐具\ncook(v./n.)烹調、廚師\nrice cooker 電鍋\npressure cooker 壓力鍋\nAlmost every Taiwanese family has a rice cooker.\n(幾乎每個台灣家庭都有一個電鍋。)\nShe made the soup in a pressure cooker.\n(她用壓力鍋煮湯。)"],["costly","costly(adj.)昂貴的、代價高的\ncost(n./v.)費用、花費\ncostly mistake 代價高昂的錯誤\ncostly repairs 昂貴的修理費\nFixing the car will be very costly.\n(修那台車會非常貴。)\nIt was a costly mistake for the team.\n(那對球隊來說是個代價高昂的錯誤。)"],["cotton","cotton(n.)棉花、棉布\n(無詞性變化)\ncotton shirt 棉質襯衫\ncotton candy 棉花糖\nThis T-shirt is made of 100% cotton.\n(這件T恤是百分之百純棉。)\nThe kids bought cotton candy at the night market.\n(孩子們在夜市買了棉花糖。)"],["cough","cough(n./v.)咳嗽\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a cough 咳嗽\ncough medicine 咳嗽藥\nI have had a bad cough for a week.\n(我已經咳得很厲害一個星期了。)\nCover your mouth when you cough.\n(咳嗽時要遮住嘴巴。)"],["countable","countable(adj.)可數的\ncount(v.)數、計算\nuncountable(adj.)不可數的\ncountable noun 可數名詞\ncountable and uncountable 可數與不可數\n'Apple' is a countable noun.\n('Apple' 是可數名詞。)\nUse 'many' with countable nouns.\n(可數名詞要用 many。)"],["county","county(n.)縣、郡\n(無詞性變化)\ncounty government 縣政府\nYilan County 宜蘭縣\nHualien County is on the east coast of Taiwan.\n(花蓮縣位於台灣東海岸。)\nThe county government built a new library.\n(縣政府蓋了一座新圖書館。)"],["crab","crab(n.)螃蟹\n(無詞性變化)\ncrab meat 蟹肉\nhermit crab 寄居蟹\nWe saw many small crabs on the beach.\n(我們在海灘上看到許多小螃蟹。)\nSteamed crab is a popular dish in autumn.\n(清蒸螃蟹是秋天很受歡迎的菜。)"],["cradle","cradle(n./v.)搖籃、發源地、輕抱\n(無詞性變化)\nfrom the cradle to the grave 從生到死\ncradle of civilization 文明的搖籃\nThe baby is sleeping in the cradle.\n(寶寶正在搖籃裡睡覺。)\nShe cradled the kitten in her arms.\n(她把小貓輕輕抱在懷裡。)"],["crane","crane(n./v.)鶴、起重機、伸長(脖子)\n(無詞性變化)\npaper crane 紙鶴\ncrane one's neck 伸長脖子\nShe folded a thousand paper cranes.\n(她摺了一千隻紙鶴。)\nA huge crane lifted the steel beams.\n(一部巨大的起重機吊起鋼樑。)"],["crash","crash(n./v.)撞擊、墜毀、(電腦)當機\n(無詞性變化)\ncar crash 車禍\nplane crash 墜機\nTwo cars crashed at the crossroads.\n(兩輛車在十字路口相撞。)\nMy computer crashed and I lost my report.\n(我的電腦當機，報告不見了。)"],["crawl","crawl(v./n.)爬行、緩慢行進\n(無詞性變化)\ncrawl into 爬進\nat a crawl 緩慢地\nThe baby is learning to crawl.\n(寶寶正在學爬。)\nTraffic was moving at a crawl this morning.\n(今天早上車流移動得非常緩慢。)"],["creative","creative(adj.)有創意的、創造性的\ncreate(v.)創造\ncreativity(n.)創造力\ncreative thinking 創意思考\ncreative writing 創意寫作\nShe is a very creative designer.\n(她是一位非常有創意的設計師。)\nTeachers encourage creative thinking in class.\n(老師們在課堂上鼓勵創意思考。)"],["creator","creator(n.)創造者、創作者\ncreate(v.)創造\ncreation(n.)創造、作品\ncontent creator 內容創作者\nthe creator of 某物的創造者\nHe is the creator of this popular game.\n(他是這款熱門遊戲的創作者。)\nMany young people want to be content creators.\n(很多年輕人想成為內容創作者。)"],["creature","creature(n.)生物、動物\n(無詞性變化)\nliving creature 生物\nsea creature 海洋生物\nThe ocean is home to many strange creatures.\n(海洋是許多奇特生物的家。)\nWe should respect all living creatures.\n(我們應該尊重所有生物。)"],["credit","credit(n./v.)信用、讚揚、學分、歸功於\n(無詞性變化)\ncredit card 信用卡\ntake credit for 把功勞歸於自己\nCan I pay by credit card?\n(我可以刷卡嗎？)\nShe deserves credit for her hard work.\n(她的努力值得讚揚。)"],["crew","crew(n.)全體船員、機組人員、工作人員\n(無詞性變化)\ncabin crew 空服人員\nfilm crew 拍攝團隊\nThe ship's crew worked through the storm.\n(船員們在暴風雨中持續工作。)\nA film crew came to our school yesterday.\n(昨天有個拍攝團隊來我們學校。)"],["cricket","cricket(n.)蟋蟀、板球\n(無詞性變化)\nplay cricket 打板球\ncricket chirping 蟋蟀鳴叫\nWe could hear crickets chirping at night.\n(晚上我們能聽到蟋蟀的鳴叫聲。)\nCricket is very popular in India.\n(板球在印度非常受歡迎。)"],["criminal","criminal(adj./n.)犯罪的、罪犯\ncrime(n.)罪行\ncriminal record 犯罪紀錄\ncatch a criminal 抓到罪犯\nThe police finally caught the criminal.\n(警方終於抓到了那名罪犯。)\nStealing is a criminal act.\n(偷竊是犯罪行為。)"],["crispy","crispy(adj.)酥脆的\ncrisp(adj.)脆的、清新的\ncrispy fried chicken 酥脆炸雞\ncrispy skin 脆皮\nI love the crispy fried chicken at this shop.\n(我很愛這家店的酥脆炸雞。)\nThe roast duck has crispy skin.\n(這隻烤鴨的皮很酥脆。)"],["crop","crop(n./v.)農作物、收成、修剪\n(無詞性變化)\ncrop failure 歉收\ngrow crops 種植作物\nRice is the main crop in this area.\n(稻米是這個地區的主要作物。)\nThe typhoon destroyed most of the crops.\n(颱風摧毀了大部分的農作物。)"],["crown","crown(n./v.)王冠、加冕\n(無詞性變化)\nwear a crown 戴王冠\ncrown prince 王儲\nThe king wore a golden crown.\n(國王戴著一頂金色王冠。)\nShe was crowned the winner of the contest.\n(她被封為比賽的冠軍。)"],["cruel","cruel(adj.)殘忍的、殘酷的\ncruelty(n.)殘忍\ncruelly(adv.)殘忍地\ncruel to animals 虐待動物\ncruel world 殘酷的世界\nIt is cruel to keep a dog in a small cage.\n(把狗關在小籠子裡是很殘忍的。)\nLife can sometimes be cruel.\n(人生有時候是很殘酷的。)"],["cupboard","cupboard(n.)碗櫥、櫥櫃\n(無詞性變化)\nkitchen cupboard 廚房櫥櫃\nin the cupboard 在櫃子裡\nThe cups are in the kitchen cupboard.\n(杯子在廚房的櫥櫃裡。)\nThere is nothing to eat in the cupboard.\n(櫃子裡沒有東西可以吃。)"],["dairy","dairy(n.)乳製品、乳品店、酪農場\n(無詞性變化)\ndairy products 乳製品\ndairy farm 酪農場\nMilk, cheese, and yogurt are dairy products.\n(牛奶、起司和優格都是乳製品。)\nHis family runs a dairy farm in Changhua.\n(他家在彰化經營一座酪農場。)"],["dam","dam(n./v.)水壩、築壩攔(水)\n(無詞性變化)\nbuild a dam 建造水壩\ndam a river 在河上築壩\nThe government plans to build a dam on the river.\n(政府計畫在這條河上建一座水壩。)\nThe dam provides water for the whole city.\n(這座水壩供應全市的用水。)"],["dare","dare(aux./v.)敢、膽敢、向⋯挑戰\ndaring(adj.)大膽的\ndare to 敢於⋯\nHow dare you! 你怎麼敢！\nI didn't dare to tell my parents the truth.\n(我不敢告訴爸媽真相。)\nHe dared me to jump into the cold river.\n(他激我跳進冰冷的河裡。)"],["darling","darling(n./adj.)親愛的、寶貝、可愛的\n(無詞性變化)\nmy darling 我親愛的\na darling little girl 可愛的小女孩\nGood night, my darling.\n(晚安，我的寶貝。)\nShe was everyone's darling at the party.\n(她是派對上大家的寵兒。)"],["dash","dash(n./v.)猛衝、急奔、少量、破折號\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a dash for 衝向⋯\na dash of salt 一點點鹽\nHe dashed to the bus stop to catch the bus.\n(他衝向公車站去趕公車。)\nAdd a dash of salt to the soup.\n(在湯裡加一點點鹽。)"],["database","database(n.)資料庫\n(無詞性變化)\nonline database 線上資料庫\nsearch the database 搜尋資料庫\nThe library has a large online database.\n(圖書館有一個大型的線上資料庫。)\nAll student records are kept in a database.\n(所有學生的紀錄都存在資料庫裡。)"],["dawn","dawn(n./v.)黎明、開端、(天)破曉\n(無詞性變化)\nat dawn 黎明時\nfrom dawn to dusk 從早到晚\nThe farmers start working at dawn.\n(農夫們天一亮就開始工作。)\nIt suddenly dawned on me that I had left my keys at home.\n(我突然想到我把鑰匙留在家裡了。)"],["dealer","dealer(n.)商人、經銷商、(牌局)發牌者\ndeal(v./n.)處理、交易\ncar dealer 汽車經銷商\ndrug dealer 毒販\nHe bought a used car from a local dealer.\n(他向當地的經銷商買了一輛二手車。)\nThe dealer gave each player five cards.\n(發牌員發給每位玩家五張牌。)"],["decade","decade(n.)十年\n(無詞性變化)\nfor decades 數十年來\nin the past decade 過去十年間\nThe city has changed a lot in the past decade.\n(這座城市在過去十年間改變很多。)\nMy parents have lived here for decades.\n(我爸媽已經在這裡住了數十年。)"],["deck","deck(n.)甲板、一副(紙牌)、平台\n(無詞性變化)\non deck 在甲板上\na deck of cards 一副撲克牌\nWe stood on the deck and watched the sunset.\n(我們站在甲板上看夕陽。)\nCan you bring a deck of cards to the trip?\n(你可以帶一副撲克牌去旅行嗎？)"],["decorate","decorate(v.)裝飾、布置\ndecoration(n.)裝飾、裝飾品\ndecorative(adj.)裝飾用的\ndecorate the room 布置房間\ndecorate with 用⋯裝飾\nWe decorated the classroom for Christmas.\n(我們為了聖誕節布置教室。)\nShe decorated the cake with strawberries.\n(她用草莓裝飾蛋糕。)"],["decrease","decrease(v./n.)減少、降低\n(無詞性變化)\ndecrease by 減少了(多少)\na decrease in 在⋯方面的減少\nThe number of students has decreased this year.\n(今年學生人數減少了。)\nThere was a sharp decrease in sales last month.\n(上個月銷售量大幅下滑。)"],["deed","deed(n.)行為、事蹟、契據\n(無詞性變化)\ngood deed 善行\ndo a good deed 做好事\nHelping the old man was a good deed.\n(幫助那位老先生是一件善行。)\nActions speak louder than words, so judge people by their deeds.\n(行動勝於言語，所以要從行為來評斷一個人。)"],["deepen","deepen(v.)加深、使變深\ndeep(adj.)深的\ndepth(n.)深度\ndeepen understanding 加深理解\ndeepen a friendship 加深友誼\nTraveling abroad deepened my understanding of other cultures.\n(出國旅行加深了我對其他文化的理解。)\nTheir friendship deepened over the years.\n(他們的友誼隨著歲月加深。)"],["definition","definition(n.)定義、清晰度\ndefine(v.)下定義\ndefinite(adj.)明確的\nby definition 按照定義、本質上\nhigh definition 高畫質\nLook up the definition of this word in the dictionary.\n(在字典裡查這個字的定義。)\nThis TV shows pictures in high definition.\n(這台電視能顯示高畫質影像。)"],["democracy","democracy(n.)民主、民主政治\ndemocratic(adj.)民主的\ndemocrat(n.)民主主義者\nfreedom and democracy 自由與民主\nfight for democracy 爭取民主\nTaiwan is a young democracy in Asia.\n(臺灣是亞洲一個年輕的民主國家。)\nPeople in a democracy can vote for their leaders.\n(在民主國家，人民可以投票選出領導人。)"],["democratic","democratic(adj.)民主的\ndemocracy(n.)民主\ndemocrat(n.)民主主義者\ndemocratic country 民主國家\ndemocratic process 民主程序\nEveryone has the right to vote in a democratic country.\n(在民主國家每個人都有投票權。)\nThe class made the decision in a democratic way.\n(全班用民主的方式做出決定。)"],["deposit","deposit(n./v.)存款、訂金、押金、存放\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a deposit 存款\npay a deposit 付訂金\nI need to deposit some money in the bank.\n(我需要去銀行存一些錢。)\nWe paid a deposit to rent the apartment.\n(我們付了押金租下這間公寓。)"],["designer","designer(n.)設計師\ndesign(n./v.)設計\nfashion designer 服裝設計師\ngraphic designer 平面設計師\nShe wants to become a fashion designer.\n(她想成為服裝設計師。)\nThe designer created a new logo for the company.\n(設計師為公司設計了新的標誌。)"],["desirable","desirable(adj.)令人嚮往的、值得擁有的\ndesire(n./v.)慾望、渴望\nhighly desirable 非常令人嚮往的\ndesirable result 理想的結果\nA house near the MRT station is very desirable.\n(靠近捷運站的房子非常搶手。)\nGood communication skills are desirable for this job.\n(這份工作最好具備良好的溝通能力。)"],["desire","desire(n./v.)慾望、渴望、想要\ndesirable(adj.)令人嚮往的\na strong desire 強烈的渴望\ndesire for 對⋯的渴望\nHe has a strong desire to travel around the world.\n(他非常渴望環遊世界。)\nEveryone desires happiness and peace.\n(人人都渴望幸福與和平。)"],["dessert","dessert(n.)甜點\n(無詞性變化)\nfor dessert 當甜點\ndessert shop 甜點店\nWe had mango ice for dessert.\n(我們吃芒果冰當甜點。)\nLet's save some room for dessert.\n(我們留點胃吃甜點吧。)"],["destroy","destroy(v.)破壞、毀滅\ndestruction(n.)破壞\ndestructive(adj.)破壞性的\ncompletely destroy 徹底摧毀\ndestroy the environment 破壞環境\nThe typhoon destroyed many houses in the village.\n(颱風摧毀了村裡許多房屋。)\nPlastic waste is destroying our oceans.\n(塑膠垃圾正在破壞我們的海洋。)"],["detect","detect(v.)察覺、偵測\ndetective(n.)偵探\ndetection(n.)偵查、察覺\ndetect a problem 發現問題\nsmoke detector 煙霧偵測器\nThe machine can detect metal in your bag.\n(這台機器可以偵測你包包裡的金屬。)\nI detected a hint of anger in her voice.\n(我察覺到她的聲音裡帶著一絲怒氣。)"],["determine","determine(v.)決定、確定、查明\ndetermination(n.)決心\ndetermined(adj.)下定決心的\ndetermine the cause 查明原因\nbe determined to 決心要⋯\nYour attitude determines your success.\n(你的態度決定你的成功。)\nThe police are trying to determine the cause of the fire.\n(警方正試著查明火災的原因。)"],["devil","devil(n.)魔鬼、惡魔\ndevilish(adj.)惡魔般的\nspeak of the devil 說曹操曹操就到\nthe devil is in the details 魔鬼藏在細節裡\nSpeak of the devil! Here comes Jason.\n(說曹操曹操就到！傑森來了。)\nThe little boy is a real devil at home.\n(那個小男孩在家裡真是個小惡魔。)"],["dim","dim(adj./v.)昏暗的、模糊的、使變暗\ndimly(adv.)昏暗地、模糊地\ndim light 昏暗的光線\ndim the lights 調暗燈光\nDon't read in such dim light.\n(不要在這麼昏暗的光線下看書。)\nThe theater dimmed the lights before the movie started.\n(電影開始前戲院把燈光調暗。)"],["dime","dime(n.)(美國、加拿大的)一角硬幣\n(無詞性變化)\na dime a dozen 多得很、不值錢\nnot a dime 一毛錢也沒有\nA dime is worth ten cents.\n(一角硬幣價值十分錢。)\nCheap phone cases are a dime a dozen.\n(便宜的手機殼到處都是。)"],["dine","dine(v.)用餐、進餐\ndinner(n.)晚餐\ndiner(n.)用餐者、小餐館\ndine out 外出用餐\ndine in 在家用餐、內用\nWe usually dine out on Friday nights.\n(我們通常週五晚上外出用餐。)\nWould you like to dine in or take out?\n(您要內用還是外帶？)"],["dinosaur","dinosaur(n.)恐龍\n(無詞性變化)\ndinosaur fossil 恐龍化石\ndinosaur museum 恐龍博物館\nDinosaurs lived millions of years ago.\n(恐龍生活在數百萬年前。)\nWe saw a huge dinosaur fossil at the museum.\n(我們在博物館看到一具巨大的恐龍化石。)"],["dip","dip(v./n.)浸、沾、下降、短暫游泳\n(無詞性變化)\ndip into 浸入、沾\ntake a dip 泡一下水、游個泳\nDip the fries into the ketchup.\n(把薯條沾番茄醬。)\nLet's take a quick dip in the pool.\n(我們去游泳池泡一下水吧。)"],["dirt","dirt(n.)灰塵、泥土、汙垢\ndirty(adj.)髒的\ndirt road 泥土路\ncovered in dirt 滿是泥土\nHis shoes were covered in dirt after the hike.\n(健行後他的鞋子沾滿了泥土。)\nWe drove down a narrow dirt road.\n(我們沿著一條窄窄的泥土路開車。)"],["discount","discount(n./v.)折扣、打折\n(無詞性變化)\nstudent discount 學生折扣\nat a discount 打折(出售)\nStudents can get a ten percent discount here.\n(學生在這裡可以打九折。)\nThe store discounts winter clothes in March.\n(這家店三月會把冬裝打折。)"],["dishonest","dishonest(adj.)不誠實的\ndishonesty(n.)不誠實\nhonest(adj.)誠實的\ndishonest behavior 不誠實的行為\nit is dishonest to 做⋯是不誠實的\nIt is dishonest to copy someone else's homework.\n(抄別人的作業是不誠實的。)\nHe lost his job because he was dishonest.\n(他因為不誠實而丟了工作。)"],["disk/disc","disk(n.)磁碟、圓盤\ndisc(n.)光碟、圓盤(同 disk)\nhard disk 硬碟\ncompact disc 光碟(CD)\nSave the file on the hard disk.\n(把檔案存在硬碟裡。)\nMy dad still keeps his old music discs.\n(我爸爸還留著他的舊音樂光碟。)"],["dislike","dislike(v./n.)不喜歡、厭惡\nlike(v.)喜歡\ndislike + V-ing 不喜歡做⋯\nlikes and dislikes 好惡\nI dislike waiting in long lines.\n(我不喜歡排長長的隊。)\nEveryone has different likes and dislikes.\n(每個人都有不同的好惡。)"],["ditch","ditch(n./v.)水溝、溝渠、拋棄\n(無詞性變化)\ndig a ditch 挖溝\nditch class 翹課\nThe car slid off the road into a ditch.\n(車子滑出路面掉進水溝裡。)\nHe ditched his old phone for a new one.\n(他丟掉舊手機換了一支新的。)"],["dive","dive(n./v.)跳水、潛水、俯衝\ndiver(n.)潛水員、跳水者\ndiving(n.)潛水、跳水\ndive into 跳入、投入\nscuba diving 水肺潛水\nShe dove into the pool without fear.\n(她毫不害怕地跳進泳池。)\nWe went scuba diving in Kenting.\n(我們去墾丁玩水肺潛水。)"],["dizzy","dizzy(adj.)頭暈的、暈眩的\ndizziness(n.)頭暈\nfeel dizzy 覺得頭暈\nmake someone dizzy 使某人頭暈\nI felt dizzy after the roller coaster ride.\n(坐完雲霄飛車後我覺得頭暈。)\nStanding up too fast can make you dizzy.\n(站起來太快可能會讓你頭暈。)"],["dock","dock(n./v.)碼頭、船塢、(船)停靠\n(無詞性變化)\nat the dock 在碼頭\ndock at 停靠在⋯\nThe ship docked at Keelung Harbor this morning.\n(那艘船今天早上停靠在基隆港。)\nFishermen were selling fish at the dock.\n(漁夫們在碼頭賣魚。)"],["dolphin","dolphin(n.)海豚\n(無詞性變化)\ndolphin watching 賞海豚\na pod of dolphins 一群海豚\nWe went dolphin watching in Hualien.\n(我們去花蓮賞海豚。)\nDolphins are known to be very smart.\n(海豚以非常聰明著稱。)"],["donkey","donkey(n.)驢子\n(無詞性變化)\nride a donkey 騎驢\ndonkey work 苦差事\nThe farmer used a donkey to carry the bags.\n(農夫用驢子來搬運袋子。)\nHe is as stubborn as a donkey.\n(他固執得像頭驢。)"],["dose","dose(n./v.)(藥的)一劑、劑量、給⋯服藥\ndosage(n.)劑量\na dose of medicine 一劑藥\ndaily dose 每日劑量\nTake one dose of this medicine after each meal.\n(每餐飯後服用一劑這種藥。)\nA small dose of humor can make a class more fun.\n(一點點幽默就能讓課堂更有趣。)"],["doubtful","doubtful(adj.)懷疑的、不確定的\ndoubt(n./v.)懷疑\ndoubtfully(adv.)懷疑地\nbe doubtful about 對⋯存疑\nit is doubtful whether ⋯ 是否⋯令人懷疑\nIt is doubtful whether he will come today.\n(他今天會不會來還很難說。)\nMy parents were doubtful about my plan.\n(我爸媽對我的計畫存疑。)"],["doughnut","doughnut(n.)甜甜圈\ndonut(n.)甜甜圈(美式拼法)\nchocolate doughnut 巧克力甜甜圈\na box of doughnuts 一盒甜甜圈\nI had a doughnut and coffee for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了一個甜甜圈配咖啡。)\nShe bought a box of doughnuts for the class.\n(她買了一盒甜甜圈給全班。)"],["downtown","downtown(adj./adv./n.)市中心(的)、在市中心\n(無詞性變化)\ngo downtown 去市區\ndowntown area 市中心區\nLet's go downtown and see a movie.\n(我們去市區看電影吧。)\nThe new hotel is in the downtown area.\n(那家新飯店在市中心區。)"],["drag","drag(v./n.)拖、拉、拖累、無聊的事\n(無詞性變化)\ndrag on 拖延、拖拖拉拉\ndrag and drop 拖放(電腦操作)\nHe dragged the heavy box across the floor.\n(他把重箱子拖過地板。)\nThe meeting dragged on for three hours.\n(會議拖了三個小時。)"],["dragonfly","dragonfly(n.)蜻蜓\n(無詞性變化)\nred dragonfly 紅蜻蜓\ncatch a dragonfly 抓蜻蜓\nA dragonfly landed on the tip of the grass.\n(一隻蜻蜓停在草尖上。)\nWhen I was little, I liked to catch dragonflies by the pond.\n(我小時候喜歡在池塘邊抓蜻蜓。)"],["drain","drain(v./n.)排水、耗盡、排水管\ndrainage(n.)排水系統\ndrain away 逐漸流失\nbrain drain 人才外流\nDrain the water from the noodles before adding the sauce.\n(加醬料前先把麵的水瀝乾。)\nThe long exam drained all my energy.\n(那場漫長的考試耗盡了我所有精力。)"],["dramatic","dramatic(adj.)戲劇性的、劇烈的、引人注目的\ndrama(n.)戲劇\ndramatically(adv.)戲劇性地、大幅地\ndramatic change 劇烈的變化\ndramatic increase 大幅增加\nThere has been a dramatic change in the weather.\n(天氣出現了劇烈的變化。)\nDon't be so dramatic. It's just a small cut.\n(別那麼誇張，只是個小傷口而已。)"],["drip","drip(n./v.)滴、滴下、水滴聲\n(無詞性變化)\ndrip coffee 滴濾咖啡\nthe drip of water 滴水聲\nWater is dripping from the ceiling.\n(水正從天花板滴下來。)\nI couldn't sleep because of the drip of the faucet.\n(水龍頭的滴水聲讓我睡不著。)"],["drown","drown(v.)淹死、溺水、淹沒\ndrowning(n.)溺水\ndrown in 淹沒在⋯之中\ndrown out 蓋過(聲音)\nNever swim alone, or you might drown.\n(絕對不要獨自游泳，否則可能會溺水。)\nThe loud music drowned out our voices.\n(大聲的音樂蓋過了我們的聲音。)"],["drugstore","drugstore(n.)藥房、藥妝店\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to the drugstore 去藥局\ndrugstore chain 連鎖藥妝店\nI bought some cold medicine at the drugstore.\n(我在藥局買了一些感冒藥。)\nThe drugstore on the corner is open until midnight.\n(轉角那家藥妝店營業到半夜。)"],["drunk","drunk(adj./n.)喝醉的、醉漢\ndrunken(adj.)酒醉的\ndrink(v.)喝\nget drunk 喝醉\ndrunk driving 酒駕\nDrunk driving is very dangerous.\n(酒駕非常危險。)\nHe got drunk at the party and fell asleep.\n(他在派對上喝醉後睡著了。)"],["dumb","dumb(adj.)笨的、啞的、說不出話的\n(無詞性變化)\na dumb question 蠢問題\nplay dumb 裝傻\nThere is no such thing as a dumb question.\n(沒有所謂的蠢問題。)\nDon't play dumb. I know you broke the vase.\n(別裝傻，我知道是你打破了花瓶。)"],["dump","dump(v./n.)傾倒、拋棄、垃圾場\n(無詞性變化)\ndump garbage 傾倒垃圾\ngarbage dump 垃圾場\nIt is illegal to dump garbage in the river.\n(把垃圾倒進河裡是違法的。)\nShe dumped her boyfriend last week.\n(她上星期甩了男朋友。)"],["dumpling","dumpling(n.)餃子、湯圓、麵糰子\n(無詞性變化)\nsteamed dumplings 蒸餃\nsoup dumplings 小籠包\nWe make dumplings together every Chinese New Year.\n(我們每年過年都會一起包餃子。)\nThis restaurant is famous for its soup dumplings.\n(這家餐廳以小籠包聞名。)"],["dust","dust(n./v.)灰塵、撢去灰塵\ndusty(adj.)滿是灰塵的\ncovered with dust 布滿灰塵\ndust off 撢去灰塵、重新拿出來用\nThe old books on the shelf were covered with dust.\n(架上的舊書布滿了灰塵。)\nPlease dust the furniture before the guests arrive.\n(客人到之前請把家具的灰塵撢一撢。)"],["eager","eager(adj.)渴望的、熱切的\neagerly(adv.)熱切地\neagerness(n.)渴望\nbe eager to 渴望去⋯\nbe eager for 渴望得到⋯\nThe students are eager to start the summer vacation.\n(學生們渴望暑假趕快開始。)\nShe is eager for her parents' approval.\n(她渴望得到父母的認可。)"],["echo","echo(n./v.)回聲、回音、發出回聲、附和\n(無詞性變化)\nhear an echo 聽到回音\necho someone's words 附和某人的話\nWe heard the echo of our voices in the cave.\n(我們在山洞裡聽到自己聲音的回音。)\nMany students echoed his opinion.\n(許多學生附和他的意見。)"],["edit","edit(v.)編輯、校訂、剪輯\neditor(n.)編輯\nedition(n.)版本\nedit a video 剪輯影片\nedit an article 編輯文章\nI spent the whole night editing my video.\n(我花了一整晚剪輯我的影片。)\nPlease edit your essay before you hand it in.\n(交作文之前請先修改一下。)"],["editor","editor(n.)編輯、主編\nedit(v.)編輯\neditorial(n./adj.)社論、編輯的\nchief editor 總編輯\nmagazine editor 雜誌編輯\nShe works as an editor for a fashion magazine.\n(她在一家時尚雜誌擔任編輯。)\nThe editor asked me to make the story shorter.\n(編輯要我把故事寫短一點。)"],["educate","educate(v.)教育\neducation(n.)教育\neducational(adj.)教育的\neducated(adj.)受過教育的\neducate the public 教育大眾\nwell educated 受過良好教育的\nParents should educate their children about online safety.\n(父母應該教育孩子網路安全的知識。)\nThe campaign aims to educate the public about recycling.\n(這項活動旨在教育大眾關於回收的知識。)"],["educational","educational(adj.)教育的、有教育意義的\neducation(n.)教育\neducate(v.)教育\neducational system 教育制度\neducational value 教育價值\nThis TV program is both fun and educational.\n(這個電視節目既有趣又有教育意義。)\nThe museum offers many educational activities for kids.\n(博物館為孩子們提供許多教育活動。)"],["efficient","efficient(adj.)有效率的、效能高的\nefficiency(n.)效率\nefficiently(adv.)有效率地\nenergy-efficient 節能的\nefficient use of 有效利用⋯\nShe is an efficient worker who always finishes on time.\n(她是個有效率的員工，總是準時完成工作。)\nWe should buy an energy-efficient air conditioner.\n(我們應該買一台節能冷氣。)"],["elbow","elbow(n./v.)手肘、用手肘推擠\n(無詞性變化)\nelbow room 活動空間\nelbow one's way 用手肘擠過去\nI hurt my elbow while playing tennis.\n(我打網球時傷到了手肘。)\nHe elbowed his way through the crowd.\n(他用手肘擠過了人群。)"],["elderly","elderly(adj.)年長的、上了年紀的\nelder(adj./n.)年長的、長輩\nthe elderly 老年人\nelderly people 長者\nWe should give our seats to the elderly on the bus.\n(我們在公車上應該讓座給老年人。)\nMy grandmother takes care of an elderly neighbor.\n(我奶奶照顧一位年長的鄰居。)"],["elect","elect(v./adj.)選舉、推選、當選而未就任的\nelection(n.)選舉\nelective(adj./n.)選修的、選修課\nelect a president 選出總統\nbe elected (as) 當選為\nShe was elected class leader this semester.\n(她這學期被選為班長。)\nCitizens elect the mayor every four years.\n(市民每四年選一次市長。)"],["election","election(n.)選舉\nelect(v.)選舉\nelectoral(adj.)選舉的\npresidential election 總統大選\nwin an election 贏得選舉\nThe presidential election will be held next January.\n(總統大選將在明年一月舉行。)\nHe won the election by a small margin.\n(他以些微差距贏得選舉。)"],["electricity","electricity(n.)電、電力\nelectric(adj.)電的、用電的\nelectrical(adj.)與電有關的\nsave electricity 省電\nelectricity bill 電費帳單\nTurn off the lights to save electricity.\n(關燈以節省用電。)\nOur electricity bill is very high in summer.\n(我們夏天的電費很高。)"],["electronic","electronic(adj.)電子的\nelectronics(n.)電子學、電子產品\nelectron(n.)電子\nelectronic device 電子裝置\nelectronic music 電子音樂\nPlease turn off all electronic devices during the exam.\n(考試期間請關閉所有電子裝置。)\nMore and more people read electronic books.\n(越來越多人閱讀電子書。)"],["element","element(n.)元素、要素、成分\nelementary(adj.)基本的、初級的\nkey element 關鍵要素\nchemical element 化學元素\nHard work is a key element of success.\n(努力是成功的關鍵要素。)\nOxygen is a chemical element.\n(氧是一種化學元素。)"],["elevator","elevator(n.)電梯\n(無詞性變化)\ntake the elevator 搭電梯\nelevator button 電梯按鈕\nLet's take the elevator to the tenth floor.\n(我們搭電梯到十樓吧。)\nDon't use the elevator during an earthquake.\n(地震時不要搭電梯。)"],["emergency","emergency(n.)緊急情況、突發事件\n(無詞性變化)\nin case of emergency 萬一發生緊急情況\nemergency room 急診室\nIn case of emergency, call 119.\n(萬一發生緊急狀況，請撥 119。)\nHe was taken to the emergency room last night.\n(他昨晚被送進急診室。)"],["emotional","emotional(adj.)情緒的、情感的、易動感情的\nemotion(n.)情緒、情感\nemotionally(adv.)情感上地\nemotional support 情感支持\nget emotional 變得激動\nFriends can give us emotional support.\n(朋友能給我們情感上的支持。)\nShe got emotional when she said goodbye.\n(她道別時情緒激動起來。)"],["emperor","emperor(n.)皇帝\nempire(n.)帝國\nempress(n.)女皇、皇后\nthe first emperor 開國皇帝\nRoman emperor 羅馬皇帝\nThe emperor lived in a huge palace.\n(皇帝住在一座巨大的宮殿裡。)\nQin Shi Huang was the first emperor of China.\n(秦始皇是中國第一位皇帝。)"],["enable","enable(v.)使能夠\nable(adj.)能夠的\nenable someone to 使某人能夠⋯\nenable a function 啟用功能\nThe Internet enables us to learn anything at home.\n(網路讓我們能在家學習任何東西。)\nYou need to enable location services on your phone.\n(你需要在手機上啟用定位服務。)"],["energetic","energetic(adj.)精力充沛的、充滿活力的\nenergy(n.)能量、精力\nenergetically(adv.)精力充沛地\nenergetic young people 充滿活力的年輕人\nfeel energetic 覺得精力充沛\nThe energetic kids ran around the park all afternoon.\n(精力充沛的孩子們整個下午在公園裡跑來跑去。)\nI feel more energetic after a good night's sleep.\n(睡個好覺後我覺得更有精神。)"],["engage(ment)","engage(v.)從事、使參與、吸引、訂婚、engagement(n.)訂婚、約定、參與\nengaged(adj.)已訂婚的、忙碌的\nengage in 從事、參與\nengagement ring 訂婚戒指\nStudents should engage in more outdoor activities.\n(學生應該多參與戶外活動。)\nThey announced their engagement last month.\n(他們上個月宣布訂婚。)"],["enjoyable","enjoyable(adj.)令人愉快的、有樂趣的\nenjoy(v.)享受、喜愛\nenjoyment(n.)樂趣\nan enjoyable experience 愉快的經驗\nmake ⋯ enjoyable 讓⋯變得愉快\nWe had an enjoyable evening at the night market.\n(我們在夜市度過了愉快的夜晚。)\nGood music makes the long drive more enjoyable.\n(好音樂讓長途開車變得更愉快。)"],["entry","entry(n.)進入、入口、參賽作品、條目\nenter(v.)進入\nentrance(n.)入口\nNo Entry 禁止進入\nentry fee 入場費\nThe sign on the door says 'No Entry'.\n(門上的標誌寫著「禁止進入」。)\nHer entry won first prize in the drawing contest.\n(她的參賽作品在繪畫比賽中得到第一名。)"],["envy","envy(n./v.)羨慕、嫉妒\nenvious(adj.)羨慕的、嫉妒的\nbe the envy of 是⋯羨慕的對象\ngreen with envy 非常嫉妒\nI envy you for having such a nice family.\n(我很羨慕你有這麼好的家庭。)\nHer new phone is the envy of all her classmates.\n(她的新手機讓全班同學都很羨慕。)"],["erase","erase(v.)擦掉、抹去、刪除\neraser(n.)橡皮擦\nerase a mistake 擦掉錯誤\nerase the board 擦黑板\nPlease erase the board after class.\n(下課後請把黑板擦乾淨。)\nI accidentally erased all the photos on my phone.\n(我不小心刪掉了手機裡所有的照片。)"],["excellence","excellence(n.)卓越、傑出\nexcellent(adj.)極好的\nexcel(v.)擅長、勝過\nacademic excellence 學業上的優異表現\npursue excellence 追求卓越\nThe school is known for its academic excellence.\n(這所學校以學業表現優異聞名。)\nWe should always pursue excellence in what we do.\n(我們做事應該始終追求卓越。)"],["exchange","exchange(n./v.)交換、兌換、交流\n(無詞性變化)\nexchange student 交換學生\nin exchange for 作為⋯的交換\nShe went to Germany as an exchange student.\n(她以交換學生的身分去了德國。)\nCan I exchange this shirt for a bigger size?\n(我可以把這件襯衫換成大一號的嗎？)"],["exhibition","exhibition(n.)展覽、展覽會\nexhibit(v./n.)展示、展覽品\nart exhibition 藝術展覽\non exhibition 展出中\nWe visited an art exhibition at the museum last weekend.\n(我們上週末去博物館參觀一場藝術展覽。)\nHer paintings are now on exhibition in Taichung.\n(她的畫作目前正在臺中展出。)"],["expectation","expectation(n.)期望、預期\nexpect(v.)期望、預期\nmeet someone's expectations 達到某人的期望\nbeyond expectation 超出預期\nI tried hard to meet my parents' expectations.\n(我努力達到父母的期望。)\nThe movie was beyond my expectations.\n(這部電影超出我的預期。)"],["experiment","experiment(n./v.)實驗、做實驗、嘗試\nexperimental(adj.)實驗性的\ndo an experiment 做實驗\nexperiment with 試驗、嘗試⋯\nWe did an interesting experiment in chemistry class.\n(我們在化學課做了一個有趣的實驗。)\nThe chef likes to experiment with new recipes.\n(這位主廚喜歡嘗試新食譜。)"],["explode","explode(v.)爆炸、激增、勃然大怒\nexplosion(n.)爆炸\nexplosive(adj./n.)爆炸性的、炸藥\nexplode with anger 勃然大怒\npopulation explosion 人口爆炸\nThe bomb exploded in the middle of the night.\n(炸彈在半夜爆炸。)\nHe exploded with anger when he heard the news.\n(他聽到消息時勃然大怒。)"],["explore","explore(v.)探索、探險、探究\nexploration(n.)探索、探險\nexplorer(n.)探險家\nexplore the world 探索世界\nexplore possibilities 探究可能性\nWe spent the day exploring the old streets of Tainan.\n(我們花了一天探索臺南的老街。)\nScientists are exploring new ways to produce clean energy.\n(科學家正在探究生產乾淨能源的新方法。)"],["export","export(n./v.)出口、輸出、出口品\nexporter(n.)出口商\nexport goods 出口貨物\nmajor export 主要出口品\nTaiwan exports a lot of computer chips.\n(臺灣出口大量的電腦晶片。)\nRice is the country's major export.\n(稻米是該國主要的出口品。)"],["expressive","expressive(adj.)富於表情的、有表現力的\nexpress(v.)表達\nexpression(n.)表達、表情\nexpressive eyes 會說話的眼睛\nexpressive face 表情豐富的臉\nThe actress has very expressive eyes.\n(那位女演員有一雙會說話的眼睛。)\nHis expressive way of speaking keeps everyone interested.\n(他生動的說話方式讓大家都聽得津津有味。)"],["extreme","extreme(adj./n.)極端的、極度的、極端\nextremely(adv.)極度地、非常\ngo to extremes 走極端\nextreme weather 極端天氣\nExtreme weather is becoming more common.\n(極端天氣變得越來越常見。)\nIt was extremely cold in the mountains last night.\n(昨晚山上非常冷。)"],["fade","fade(v.)褪色、逐漸消失、凋謝\n(無詞性變化)\nfade away 逐漸消失\nfade out 淡出\nThe colors of my old T-shirt have faded after many washes.\n(我那件舊T恤洗了很多次後已經褪色了。)\nAs night came, the sound of the music slowly faded away.\n(夜晚降臨時，音樂聲漸漸消失了。)"],["faint","faint(adj./v./n.)微弱的、模糊的、昏倒、昏厥\nfaintly(adv.)微弱地、模糊地\nfaint light 微弱的光\nfaint from 因…而昏倒\nShe fainted from the heat during the school assembly.\n(她在朝會時因為太熱而昏倒了。)\nWe could see a faint light at the end of the tunnel.\n(我們可以看見隧道盡頭有一絲微弱的光線。)"],["fairly","fairly(adv.)相當地、公平地\nfair(adj.)公平的\nfairness(n.)公平\nfairly easy 相當簡單\ntreat someone fairly 公平對待某人\nThe test was fairly easy, so most students passed.\n(考試相當簡單，所以大部分學生都及格了。)\nA good teacher treats every student fairly.\n(好老師會公平對待每個學生。)"],["fairy","fairy(n./adj.)仙女、小精靈、仙女的\n(無詞性變化)\nfairy tale 童話故事\ntooth fairy 牙仙子\nMy grandmother told me fairy tales before bed.\n(我奶奶在睡前講童話故事給我聽。)\nIn the story, a fairy gave the girl three wishes.\n(故事中，一位仙女給了女孩三個願望。)"],["faith","faith(n.)信任、信心、信仰\nfaithful(adj.)忠實的、忠誠的\nhave faith in 對…有信心\nlose faith 失去信心\nI have faith in my teammates.\n(我對我的隊友有信心。)\nDon't lose faith in yourself after one failure.\n(不要因為一次失敗就對自己失去信心。)"],["fake","fake(adj./v./n.)假的、偽造、假裝、冒牌貨\n(無詞性變化)\nfake news 假新聞\nfake smile 假笑\nBe careful not to share fake news online.\n(小心不要在網路上分享假新聞。)\nHe faked an illness to stay home from school.\n(他裝病不去上學。)"],["familiar","familiar(adj.)熟悉的、常見的\nfamiliarity(n.)熟悉\nbe familiar with 熟悉…\nfamiliar face 熟悉的面孔\nAre you familiar with this part of the city?\n(你熟悉城市的這一區嗎？)\nI saw a familiar face in the crowd.\n(我在人群中看到一張熟悉的面孔。)"],["fancy","fancy(adj./n./v.)花俏的、高級的、想像、喜歡\n(無詞性變化)\nfancy restaurant 高級餐廳\nfancy dress 化裝服\nWe had dinner at a fancy restaurant for Dad's birthday.\n(我們在一間高級餐廳為爸爸慶生。)\nHer dress is too fancy for a school party.\n(她的洋裝對學校派對來說太花俏了。)"],["fare","fare(n.)車費、票價\n(無詞性變化)\nbus fare 公車票價\ntaxi fare 計程車費\nStudents can get a discount on the bus fare.\n(學生搭公車可以享有票價優惠。)\nThe taxi fare from the airport was quite high.\n(從機場出發的計程車費相當貴。)"],["farther","farther(adv./adj.)更遠地、更遠的\nfar(adj./adv.)遠的、遠地\nfarthest(adj./adv.)最遠的、最遠地\nfarther away 更遠處\nwalk farther 走得更遠\nThe station is farther than I thought.\n(車站比我想的還要遠。)\nWe can't walk any farther; let's take a rest.\n(我們走不動了，休息一下吧。)"],["fashionable","fashionable(adj.)流行的、時髦的\nfashion(n.)時尚、流行\nfashionably(adv.)時髦地\nfashionable clothes 時髦的服裝\nbecome fashionable 開始流行\nWide-leg pants have become fashionable again.\n(寬褲又重新流行起來了。)\nShe always wears fashionable clothes.\n(她總是穿著時髦的衣服。)"],["faucet","faucet(n.)水龍頭\n(無詞性變化)\nturn on the faucet 打開水龍頭\nleaky faucet 漏水的水龍頭\nPlease turn off the faucet while you brush your teeth.\n(刷牙時請關掉水龍頭。)\nDad fixed the leaky faucet in the kitchen.\n(爸爸修好了廚房漏水的水龍頭。)"],["fearful","fearful(adj.)害怕的、可怕的\nfear(n./v.)恐懼、害怕\nfearless(adj.)無畏的\nfearful of 害怕…\nfearful look 害怕的神情\nThe little boy was fearful of the dark.\n(那個小男孩很怕黑。)\nShe gave me a fearful look when the lights went out.\n(燈熄滅時她露出害怕的神情看著我。)"],["feather","feather(n.)羽毛\n(無詞性變化)\nas light as a feather 輕如鴻毛\nBirds of a feather flock together. 物以類聚。\nThis pillow is filled with soft feathers.\n(這個枕頭裡填滿了柔軟的羽毛。)\nThe parrot has bright green feathers.\n(那隻鸚鵡有鮮綠色的羽毛。)"],["fence","fence(n.)籬笆、圍牆、柵欄\n(無詞性變化)\nbuild a fence 築圍籬\nsit on the fence 保持中立、觀望\nThere is a white fence around the garden.\n(花園四周有一圈白色的籬笆。)\nThe dog jumped over the fence and ran away.\n(那隻狗跳過柵欄跑走了。)"],["fighter","fighter(n.)戰士、鬥士、戰鬥機\nfight(v./n.)打架、戰鬥\nfire fighter 消防員\nfighter jet 戰鬥機\nThe fire fighters saved the family from the burning house.\n(消防員從失火的房子裡救出了那一家人。)\nShe is a real fighter and never gives up.\n(她是個真正的鬥士，從不放棄。)"],["firework","firework(n.)煙火\n(無詞性變化)\nfireworks show 煙火表演\nset off fireworks 放煙火\nWe watched the New Year's fireworks at Taipei 101.\n(我們在台北101看跨年煙火。)\nPeople set off fireworks to celebrate the festival.\n(人們放煙火慶祝節日。)"],["fist","fist(n./v.)拳頭、握拳\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a fist 握拳\nshake one's fist 揮舞拳頭\nHe made a fist and hit the table angrily.\n(他握緊拳頭生氣地捶桌子。)\nThe baby held my finger in her tiny fist.\n(那個寶寶用小小的拳頭握住我的手指。)"],["flame","flame(n./v.)火焰、燃燒、發紅\nflaming(adj.)燃燒的\nin flames 著火、燃燒中\ncandle flame 燭火\nThe old building was in flames within minutes.\n(那棟老舊建築在幾分鐘內就陷入火海。)\nShe blew out the candle flame.\n(她吹熄了燭火。)"],["flash","flash(n./v.)閃光、閃現、閃耀\nflashy(adj.)浮華的、俗豔的\nin a flash 瞬間\nflash of lightning 一道閃電\nA flash of lightning lit up the sky.\n(一道閃電照亮了天空。)\nThe summer vacation went by in a flash.\n(暑假一眨眼就過去了。)"],["flashlight","flashlight(n.)手電筒\n(無詞性變化)\nturn on a flashlight 打開手電筒\nshine a flashlight 用手電筒照\nKeep a flashlight at home in case of a power outage.\n(家裡要準備手電筒以防停電。)\nHe shined his flashlight into the dark cave.\n(他用手電筒照進漆黑的山洞。)"],["flavor","flavor(n./v.)味道、口味、調味\nflavorful(adj.)美味的、風味十足的\nice cream flavor 冰淇淋口味\nadd flavor 增添風味\nWhat's your favorite ice cream flavor?\n(你最喜歡哪種冰淇淋口味？)\nGarlic adds a lot of flavor to the dish.\n(大蒜為這道菜增添許多風味。)"],["flesh","flesh(n.)肉、果肉、肉體\nfleshy(adj.)多肉的\nflesh and blood 血肉之軀、親骨肉\nin the flesh 本人、親自\nThe flesh of this mango is sweet and juicy.\n(這顆芒果的果肉香甜多汁。)\nI finally saw my favorite singer in the flesh.\n(我終於見到我最喜歡的歌手本人了。)"],["float","float(v./n.)漂浮、浮起、浮板、遊行花車\nfloating(adj.)漂浮的\nfloat on water 浮在水面上\nfloat in the air 飄在空中\nLeaves were floating on the surface of the pond.\n(葉子漂浮在池塘水面上。)\nThe kids used floats to learn to swim.\n(孩子們用浮板學游泳。)"],["flock","flock(n./v.)(鳥、羊)群、成群結隊而行\n(無詞性變化)\na flock of sheep 一群羊\nflock to 湧向、蜂擁至\nA flock of birds flew over the rice fields.\n(一群鳥飛過稻田。)\nTourists flock to the night market every weekend.\n(每到週末觀光客就湧向夜市。)"],["flood","flood(n./v.)洪水、大量、淹沒、湧入\nflooding(n.)淹水\nheavy flood 大洪水\nbe flooded with 充滿、湧入大量的\nThe typhoon caused serious floods in the south.\n(颱風在南部造成嚴重水災。)\nThe office was flooded with phone calls.\n(辦公室湧進大量的電話。)"],["flour","flour(n.)麵粉\n(無詞性變化)\nwheat flour 小麥麵粉\na bag of flour 一袋麵粉\nMix the flour with milk and eggs to make pancakes.\n(把麵粉跟牛奶和蛋混合來做鬆餅。)\nWe need two cups of flour for this cake.\n(做這個蛋糕需要兩杯麵粉。)"],["flute","flute(n.)長笛\nflutist(n.)長笛演奏者\nplay the flute 吹長笛\nflute solo 長笛獨奏\nMy sister plays the flute in the school band.\n(我妹妹在學校樂隊吹長笛。)\nThe flute solo in the concert was beautiful.\n(音樂會中的長笛獨奏非常優美。)"],["foggy","foggy(adj.)有霧的、模糊的\nfog(n.)霧\nfoggy morning 起霧的早晨\nfoggy weather 有霧的天氣\nDrive slowly on foggy mornings.\n(起霧的早晨要慢慢開車。)\nIt was so foggy that we couldn't see the mountain.\n(霧大到我們看不到那座山。)"],["fold","fold(v./n.)摺疊、對摺、摺痕\nfolder(n.)資料夾\nfold clothes 摺衣服\nfold one's arms 雙臂交叉\nPlease fold your clothes and put them away.\n(請把你的衣服摺好收起來。)\nHe folded the paper into a plane.\n(他把紙摺成一架飛機。)"],["follower","follower(n.)追隨者、跟隨者、(社群)追蹤者\nfollow(v.)跟隨、遵循\nhave followers 擁有追蹤者\nloyal follower 忠實追隨者\nThe singer has millions of followers on Instagram.\n(那位歌手在 Instagram 上有數百萬追蹤者。)\nHe is a loyal follower of the team.\n(他是這支球隊的忠實支持者。)"],["fond","fond(adj.)喜歡的、喜愛的\nfondness(n.)喜愛\nbe fond of 喜歡…\nfond memories 美好的回憶\nMy grandfather is fond of gardening.\n(我爺爺喜歡園藝。)\nI have fond memories of my childhood.\n(我對童年有美好的回憶。)"],["forever","forever(adv.)永遠\n(無詞性變化)\nlast forever 永遠持續\nforever young 永遠年輕\nNothing lasts forever.\n(沒有什麼是永遠不變的。)\nI will remember this trip forever.\n(我會永遠記得這趟旅行。)"],["fortune","fortune(n.)財富、運氣、命運\nfortunate(adj.)幸運的\nfortunately(adv.)幸運地\nmake a fortune 發大財\ntell one's fortune 算命\nHe made a fortune by selling his app.\n(他靠賣掉他的應用程式發了大財。)\nThe old woman offered to tell my fortune.\n(那位老婦人說要幫我算命。)"],["fountain","fountain(n.)噴泉、泉源\n(無詞性變化)\ndrinking fountain 飲水機\nwater fountain 噴水池、飲水機\nThe children played around the fountain in the park.\n(孩子們在公園的噴水池旁玩耍。)\nThere is a drinking fountain near the gym.\n(體育館附近有一台飲水機。)"],["frank","frank(adj.)坦白的、直率的\nfrankly(adv.)坦白地\nto be frank 坦白說\nfrank opinion 坦率的意見\nTo be frank, I don't like this plan.\n(坦白說，我不喜歡這個計畫。)\nThank you for your frank opinion.\n(謝謝你坦率的意見。)"],["freeze","freeze(v./n.)結冰、冷凍、僵住、凍結\nfreezing(adj.)極冷的\nfrozen(adj.)冷凍的、結冰的\nfreeze to death 凍死\nfrozen food 冷凍食品\nWater freezes at zero degrees Celsius.\n(水在攝氏零度時結冰。)\nThe cat froze when it saw the dog.\n(那隻貓看到狗時僵住了。)"],["freezer","freezer(n.)冷凍庫、冰櫃\nfreeze(v.)冷凍\nin the freezer 在冷凍庫裡\nfreezer bag 冷凍保鮮袋\nPut the ice cream back in the freezer.\n(把冰淇淋放回冷凍庫。)\nThere is some frozen chicken in the freezer.\n(冷凍庫裡有一些冷凍雞肉。)"],["frequent","frequent(adj./v.)頻繁的、常去(某地)\nfrequently(adv.)經常\nfrequency(n.)頻率\nfrequent visitor 常客\nfrequent flyer 飛行常客\nHe is a frequent visitor to the library.\n(他是圖書館的常客。)\nEarthquakes are frequent in Taiwan.\n(台灣經常發生地震。)"],["fright","fright(n.)驚嚇、恐懼\nfrighten(v.)使驚嚇\nfrightened(adj.)受驚的\nin fright 驚恐地\nstage fright 怯場\nShe screamed in fright when she saw the snake.\n(她看到蛇時嚇得尖叫。)\nMany students have stage fright before giving a speech.\n(許多學生在演講前會怯場。)"],["frighten","frighten(v.)使驚嚇、使害怕\nfrightened(adj.)受驚的、害怕的\nfrightening(adj.)可怕的\nfrighten away 嚇跑\nbe frightened of 害怕…\nThe loud thunder frightened the little girl.\n(轟隆的雷聲嚇壞了那個小女孩。)\nDon't make noise, or you'll frighten the birds away.\n(別出聲，不然你會把鳥嚇跑。)"],["fuel","fuel(n./v.)燃料、加燃料、助長\n(無詞性變化)\nfossil fuel 化石燃料\nrun out of fuel 燃料耗盡\nOur car is running out of fuel.\n(我們的車快沒油了。)\nWe should use less fossil fuel to protect the earth.\n(我們應該少用化石燃料來保護地球。)"],["fund","fund(n./v.)基金、資金、提供資金\nfunding(n.)資金、經費\nraise funds 募款\nschool fund 學校基金\nThe students held a sale to raise funds for the trip.\n(學生們舉辦義賣為旅行募款。)\nThe project is funded by the government.\n(這個計畫由政府出資。)"],["fur","fur(n.)毛皮、軟毛\nfurry(adj.)毛茸茸的\nsoft fur 柔軟的毛\nfur coat 毛皮大衣\nMy cat has soft white fur.\n(我的貓有柔軟的白色毛。)\nMany people refuse to wear fur coats.\n(許多人拒絕穿毛皮大衣。)"],["gallon","gallon(n.)加侖(容量單位)\n(無詞性變化)\na gallon of milk 一加侖牛奶\nmiles per gallon 每加侖可行駛的英里數\nDad bought a gallon of milk at the supermarket.\n(爸爸在超市買了一加侖的牛奶。)\nGas prices are over four dollars a gallon in the US.\n(美國的油價每加侖超過四美元。)"],["gamble","gamble(n./v.)賭博、冒險、打賭\ngambler(n.)賭徒\ngambling(n.)賭博\ngamble away 賭輸(錢財)\ntake a gamble 冒險一試\nHe gambled away all his money.\n(他把錢全都賭光了。)\nStarting a business is always a gamble.\n(創業總是一種冒險。)"],["gang","gang(n./v.)幫派、一夥人、結夥\ngangster(n.)歹徒、幫派分子\nstreet gang 街頭幫派\ngang up on 聯合起來對付\nThe police arrested members of the gang.\n(警方逮捕了幫派成員。)\nIt's not fair to gang up on one student.\n(聯合起來欺負一個學生是不公平的。)"],["gap","gap(n.)缺口、差距、間隔\n(無詞性變化)\ngeneration gap 代溝\ngap year 空檔年\nThere is a generation gap between my parents and me.\n(我和父母之間有代溝。)\nMind the gap between the train and the platform.\n(注意列車與月台間的空隙。)"],["garage","garage(n.)車庫、汽車修理廠\n(無詞性變化)\ngarage sale 車庫拍賣(舊物拍賣)\npark in the garage 停在車庫\nDad parked the car in the garage.\n(爸爸把車停在車庫裡。)\nOur neighbors are having a garage sale this Saturday.\n(我們鄰居這星期六要舉辦車庫拍賣。)"],["gasoline/gas","gasoline(n.)汽油\ngas(n.)汽油(口語)、氣體、瓦斯\ngas station 加油站\nnatural gas 天然氣\nWe stopped at a gas station to fill up the tank.\n(我們在加油站停下來把油加滿。)\nThe price of gasoline has gone up again.\n(汽油價格又上漲了。)"],["geography","geography(n.)地理、地理學\ngeographic(adj.)地理的\ngeographer(n.)地理學家\ngeography class 地理課\nphysical geography 自然地理\nI learned about mountains and rivers in geography class.\n(我在地理課學到山脈和河流的知識。)\nThe geography of Taiwan is very diverse.\n(台灣的地形非常多樣。)"],["gesture","gesture(n./v.)手勢、姿態、表示、做手勢\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a gesture 做手勢\na kind gesture 友善的表示\nHe made a gesture for me to sit down.\n(他做手勢要我坐下。)\nSending flowers was a kind gesture.\n(送花是一種貼心的表示。)"],["glance","glance(n./v.)一瞥、看一眼\n(無詞性變化)\nat a glance 一眼就\nglance at 瞥一眼\nShe glanced at the clock and hurried out.\n(她看了一眼時鐘就匆忙出門。)\nI recognized him at a glance.\n(我一眼就認出了他。)"],["global","global(adj.)全球的、全面的\nglobe(n.)地球、地球儀\nglobalization(n.)全球化\nglobal warming 全球暖化\nglobal economy 全球經濟\nGlobal warming is a serious problem for everyone.\n(全球暖化對每個人來說都是嚴重的問題。)\nEnglish is a global language.\n(英文是一種全球通用的語言。)"],["glory","glory(n.)光榮、榮耀、壯麗\nglorious(adj.)光榮的、輝煌的\nwin glory 贏得榮耀\nbring glory to 為…帶來榮耀\nThe team brought glory to our school.\n(這支隊伍為我們學校帶來榮耀。)\nThe soldiers fought for the glory of their country.\n(士兵們為國家的榮耀而戰。)"],["glow","glow(n./v.)光輝、發光、(臉)發紅\nglowing(adj.)熱烈的、發光的\nglow in the dark 在黑暗中發光\nwarm glow 溫暖的光芒\nThe stars on my ceiling glow in the dark.\n(我天花板上的星星會在黑暗中發光。)\nHer face glowed with happiness.\n(她的臉上洋溢著幸福的光彩。)"],["golf","golf(n./v.)高爾夫球、打高爾夫球\ngolfer(n.)高爾夫球員\nplay golf 打高爾夫球\ngolf course 高爾夫球場\nMy uncle plays golf every Sunday.\n(我叔叔每個星期天都打高爾夫球。)\nThe hotel is next to a golf course.\n(那間飯店就在高爾夫球場旁邊。)"],["gossip","gossip(n./v.)閒話、八卦、說閒話\n(無詞性變化)\ngossip about 說…的閒話\noffice gossip 辦公室八卦\nDon't gossip about others behind their backs.\n(不要在背後說別人閒話。)\nShe loves reading celebrity gossip online.\n(她很愛在網路上看名人八卦。)"],["governor","governor(n.)州長、總督、主管\ngovern(v.)統治、治理\ngovernment(n.)政府\nstate governor 州長\nelect a governor 選出州長\nThe governor of California gave a speech today.\n(加州州長今天發表了演說。)\nHe was elected governor last year.\n(他去年當選州長。)"],["grab","grab(v./n.)抓取、趕緊吃(喝)、攫取\n(無詞性變化)\ngrab a bite 隨便吃點東西\ngrab someone's attention 吸引某人注意\nLet's grab a bite before the movie.\n(看電影前我們先隨便吃點東西吧。)\nHe grabbed my arm to stop me from falling.\n(他抓住我的手臂以免我跌倒。)"],["graduate","graduate(n./v.)畢業生、畢業\ngraduation(n.)畢業、畢業典禮\ngraduate from 從…畢業\ncollege graduate 大學畢業生\nMy brother will graduate from high school next June.\n(我哥哥明年六月將從高中畢業。)\nMany college graduates find it hard to get a job.\n(許多大學畢業生很難找到工作。)"],["grasp","grasp(v./n.)抓緊、理解、掌握\n(無詞性變化)\ngrasp the meaning 理解意思\ngrasp a chance 抓住機會\nIt took me a while to grasp the main idea of the article.\n(我花了一段時間才理解這篇文章的主旨。)\nShe grasped my hand tightly.\n(她緊緊抓住我的手。)"],["grasshopper","grasshopper(n.)蚱蜢\n(無詞性變化)\ncatch a grasshopper 抓蚱蜢\ngreen grasshopper 綠色蚱蜢\nA grasshopper jumped out of the grass.\n(一隻蚱蜢從草叢裡跳出來。)\nThe kids tried to catch grasshoppers in the field.\n(孩子們試著在田野裡抓蚱蜢。)"],["grassy","grassy(adj.)長滿草的、草綠色的\ngrass(n.)草\ngrassy field 草地\ngrassy hill 長滿草的山丘\nWe sat on a grassy hill and watched the sunset.\n(我們坐在長滿草的山丘上看夕陽。)\nThe children ran across the grassy field.\n(孩子們跑過草地。)"],["greedy","greedy(adj.)貪心的、貪婪的\ngreed(n.)貪婪\ngreedily(adv.)貪婪地\ngreedy for 渴望得到…\ngreedy person 貪心的人\nDon't be greedy; leave some cake for others.\n(別貪心，留一些蛋糕給別人。)\nThe greedy man wanted more and more money.\n(那個貪婪的人想要越來越多錢。)"],["greenhouse","greenhouse(n.)溫室\n(無詞性變化)\ngreenhouse effect 溫室效應\ngreenhouse gas 溫室氣體\nGreenhouse gases cause the earth to get warmer.\n(溫室氣體使地球變得更暖。)\nThe farmer grows tomatoes in a greenhouse.\n(那位農夫在溫室裡種番茄。)"],["grin","grin(n./v.)露齒而笑、咧嘴笑\n(無詞性變化)\ngrin from ear to ear 笑得合不攏嘴\na big grin 燦爛的笑容\nHe grinned from ear to ear when he heard the news.\n(他聽到這個消息時笑得合不攏嘴。)\nShe walked in with a big grin on her face.\n(她滿臉笑容地走了進來。)"],["grocery","grocery(n.)食品雜貨、雜貨店\ngrocer(n.)雜貨商\ngrocery store 雜貨店、超市\nbuy groceries 買日用食品\nMom goes grocery shopping every Saturday.\n(媽媽每個星期六去採買食品雜貨。)\nCan you help me carry the groceries?\n(你可以幫我提這些買來的東西嗎？)"],["guidance","guidance(n.)指導、輔導\nguide(v./n.)引導、導遊\nunder the guidance of 在…的指導下\nguidance counselor 輔導老師\nUnder the teacher's guidance, we finished the project.\n(在老師的指導下，我們完成了專題。)\nYou can ask the guidance counselor for advice.\n(你可以向輔導老師尋求建議。)"],["gum","gum(n.)口香糖、牙齦、膠\n(無詞性變化)\nchewing gum 口香糖\nbubble gum 泡泡糖\nChewing gum is not allowed in class.\n(上課時不准嚼口香糖。)\nBrush gently so you don't hurt your gums.\n(輕輕刷牙，以免傷到牙齦。)"],["hairdresser","hairdresser(n.)美髮師\nhairdressing(n.)美髮業\ngo to the hairdresser 去美髮院\nskilled hairdresser 技術好的美髮師\nI go to the hairdresser to get my hair cut every month.\n(我每個月都去美髮院剪頭髮。)\nThe hairdresser suggested a shorter style for summer.\n(美髮師建議我夏天剪短一點的髮型。)"],["hallway","hallway(n.)走廊、玄關\nhall(n.)大廳、會堂\nlong hallway 長廊\nin the hallway 在走廊上\nStudents are not allowed to run in the hallway.\n(學生不准在走廊上奔跑。)\nShe left her wet shoes in the hallway.\n(她把濕鞋子留在玄關。)"],["hammer","hammer(n./v.)鐵鎚、用鎚子敲打\n(無詞性變化)\nhammer a nail 釘釘子\nhammer home 反覆強調\nHe used a hammer to fix the broken chair.\n(他用鐵鎚修理壞掉的椅子。)\nDad hammered a nail into the wall to hang the picture.\n(爸爸在牆上釘了一根釘子來掛畫。)"],["handful","handful(n.)一把、少數、難管的人\n(無詞性變化)\na handful of 一把、少數的\nquite a handful 很難管教\nOnly a handful of students came to the meeting.\n(只有少數幾個學生來參加會議。)\nShe gave the birds a handful of rice.\n(她給那些鳥一把米。)"],["handkerchief","handkerchief(n.)手帕\n(無詞性變化)\ncotton handkerchief 棉質手帕\nwipe with a handkerchief 用手帕擦\nHe wiped his face with a handkerchief.\n(他用手帕擦了擦臉。)\nMy grandfather always carries a handkerchief in his pocket.\n(我爺爺口袋裡總是帶著一條手帕。)"],["handy","handy(adj.)方便的、手巧的、手邊的\nhandily(adv.)輕易地\ncome in handy 派上用場\nkeep... handy 把……放在手邊\nA small flashlight will come in handy during a blackout.\n(停電時一支小手電筒就會派上用場。)\nMy uncle is very handy and can fix almost anything.\n(我叔叔手很巧，幾乎什麼都會修。)"],["hanger","hanger(n.)衣架、掛鉤\nhang(v.)掛、懸掛\ncoat hanger 衣架\nhang on a hanger 掛在衣架上\nPlease put your coat on a hanger.\n(請把你的外套掛在衣架上。)\nWe need more hangers for all these new clothes.\n(我們需要更多衣架來掛這些新衣服。)"],["harbor","harbor(n./v.)港口、避難所、懷有(想法)、窩藏\n(無詞性變化)\nfishing harbor 漁港\nharbor a grudge 懷恨在心\nMany fishing boats are resting in the harbor.\n(許多漁船停泊在港口裡。)\nShe still harbors hope that her lost dog will return.\n(她仍懷抱著走失的狗會回來的希望。)"],["harm","harm(n./v.)傷害、損害\nharmful(adj.)有害的\nharmless(adj.)無害的\ndo harm to 對……有害\nno harm done 沒造成傷害、沒關係\nToo much sugar can do harm to your teeth.\n(太多糖會傷害你的牙齒。)\nThe storm did not harm anyone in the village.\n(這場暴風雨沒有傷到村裡任何人。)"],["harmful","harmful(adj.)有害的\nharm(n./v.)傷害\nharmless(adj.)無害的\nharmful effects 有害影響\nharmful to health 對健康有害\nSmoking is harmful to your health.\n(抽菸對你的健康有害。)\nSome chemicals are harmful to plants and animals.\n(有些化學物質對動植物有害。)"],["harvest","harvest(n./v.)收成、收穫、收割\n(無詞性變化)\nrice harvest 稻米收成\nharvest season 收穫季節\nFarmers are busy during the harvest season.\n(農夫們在收穫季節很忙碌。)\nWe harvested a lot of tomatoes from our garden this year.\n(今年我們從菜園收成了許多番茄。)"],["hasty","hasty(adj.)匆忙的、草率的\nhaste(n.)急忙、倉促\nhastily(adv.)匆忙地\nhasty decision 草率的決定\nhasty meal 匆忙的一餐\nDon't make a hasty decision when you are angry.\n(生氣時不要做草率的決定。)\nHe ate a hasty breakfast and ran to the bus stop.\n(他匆匆吃完早餐就跑向公車站。)"],["hatch","hatch(n./v.)孵化、策劃、艙口\n(無詞性變化)\nhatch a plan 策劃計畫\nhatch from an egg 從蛋中孵出\nThe baby chicks hatched from their eggs this morning.\n(小雞今天早上從蛋裡孵出來了。)\nThe kids hatched a plan to surprise their mother.\n(孩子們策劃了一個要給媽媽驚喜的計畫。)"],["hateful","hateful(adj.)可恨的、充滿仇恨的\nhate(v./n.)討厭、仇恨\nhatred(n.)憎恨\nhateful words 充滿惡意的話\nhateful attitude 惡劣的態度\nPosting hateful comments online can hurt people deeply.\n(在網路上發表充滿惡意的留言會深深傷害他人。)\nI don't like his hateful attitude toward others.\n(我不喜歡他對別人那種惡劣的態度。)"],["hay","hay(n.)乾草\n(無詞性變化)\nmake hay while the sun shines 把握時機\nbale of hay 一捆乾草\nThe farmer fed the horses some fresh hay.\n(農夫餵馬吃了一些新鮮的乾草。)\nThe barn was filled with bales of hay.\n(穀倉裡堆滿了一捆捆乾草。)"],["headline","headline(n./v.)標題、頭條、擔任主角\n(無詞性變化)\nfront-page headline 頭版頭條\nmake headlines 成為頭條新聞\nThe news about the earthquake made headlines around the world.\n(那則地震新聞登上了全球的頭條。)\nI only had time to read the headlines this morning.\n(今天早上我只有時間看新聞標題。)"],["headquarters","headquarters(n.)總部、總公司\n(無詞性變化)\ncompany headquarters 公司總部\npolice headquarters 警察總局\nThe company's headquarters is located in Taipei.\n(這家公司的總部位於臺北。)\nHe was sent to work at the headquarters for a year.\n(他被派到總部工作一年。)"],["heal","heal(v.)治癒、癒合\nhealer(n.)治療者\nhealing(n.)治療、癒合\nheal a wound 使傷口癒合\ntime heals 時間會撫平一切\nIt took two weeks for the cut on my finger to heal.\n(我手指上的傷口花了兩週才癒合。)\nThey say time heals all wounds.\n(人們說時間會撫平所有的傷痛。)"],["heap","heap(n./v.)一堆、堆積、大量\n(無詞性變化)\na heap of 一堆\nheap up 堆起來\nThere is a heap of dirty clothes on his bed.\n(他床上有一堆髒衣服。)\nShe heaped food onto my plate.\n(她在我的盤子上堆滿了食物。)"],["heater","heater(n.)暖氣機、加熱器\nheat(n./v.)熱、加熱\nwater heater 熱水器\nturn on the heater 打開暖氣\nWe turned on the heater because it was freezing.\n(因為天氣很冷，我們打開了暖氣。)\nThe water heater in our house is broken.\n(我們家的熱水器壞了。)"],["heel","heel(n./v.)腳跟、鞋跟、緊跟\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh heels 高跟鞋\non the heels of 緊接在……之後\nShe wore high heels to the party.\n(她穿高跟鞋去參加派對。)\nMy new shoes rubbed against my heel and hurt.\n(我的新鞋磨到腳跟，很痛。)"],["hell","hell(n.)地獄、苦境\nhellish(adj.)地獄般的、可怕的\ngo through hell 歷經磨難\na living hell 人間地獄\nBeing stuck in traffic for four hours was hell.\n(塞車塞了四個小時簡直是地獄。)\nHe went through hell before he finally recovered.\n(他歷經了許多磨難才終於康復。)"],["helmet","helmet(n.)安全帽、頭盔\n(無詞性變化)\nwear a helmet 戴安全帽\nbike helmet 自行車頭盔\nYou must wear a helmet when riding a scooter.\n(騎機車時你必須戴安全帽。)\nThe helmet saved his life in the accident.\n(那頂安全帽在意外中救了他一命。)"],["hesitate","hesitate(v.)猶豫、遲疑\nhesitation(n.)猶豫\nhesitant(adj.)猶豫的\ndon't hesitate to 別猶豫、儘管\nwithout hesitation 毫不猶豫\nDon't hesitate to ask me if you have any questions.\n(如果你有任何問題，儘管問我。)\nShe hesitated for a moment before answering.\n(她猶豫了一下才回答。)"],["hint","hint(n./v.)暗示、提示、線索\n(無詞性變化)\ngive a hint 給提示\ndrop a hint 暗示\nCan you give me a hint about the answer?\n(你可以給我一點答案的提示嗎？)\nShe hinted that she wanted a new phone for her birthday.\n(她暗示自己生日想要一支新手機。)"],["hire","hire(v./n.)僱用、租用、受僱者\n(無詞性變化)\nhire a car 租車\nnew hire 新進員工\nThe restaurant plans to hire two more waiters.\n(那家餐廳打算再僱用兩名服務生。)\nWe hired a boat to visit the small island.\n(我們租了一艘船去那座小島。)"],["historian","historian(n.)歷史學家\nhistory(n.)歷史\nhistorical(adj.)歷史的、史學的\nart historian 藝術史學家\nfamous historian 知名歷史學家\nThe historian wrote a book about ancient Rome.\n(那位歷史學家寫了一本關於古羅馬的書。)\nHistorians still argue about the cause of the war.\n(歷史學家們仍在爭論那場戰爭的起因。)"],["historic","historic(adj.)有歷史意義的、歷史上著名的\nhistory(n.)歷史\nhistorical(adj.)歷史的、史學的\nhistoric building 古蹟建築\nhistoric moment 歷史性的時刻\nTainan has many historic temples and buildings.\n(臺南有許多具歷史意義的廟宇和建築。)\nLanding on the moon was a historic moment.\n(登陸月球是一個歷史性的時刻。)"],["holder","holder(n.)持有者、支架、容器\nhold(v./n.)握住、舉行\nrecord holder 紀錄保持人\ncup holder 杯架\nShe is the national record holder in the 100-meter race.\n(她是百公尺賽跑的全國紀錄保持人。)\nHe put his pen back into the pen holder.\n(他把筆放回筆筒裡。)"],["hollow","hollow(adj./n./v.)中空的、空洞的、凹處、挖空\n(無詞性變化)\nhollow tree 空心樹\nhollow promise 空洞的承諾\nThe squirrel hid its nuts in a hollow tree.\n(松鼠把堅果藏在一棵空心的樹裡。)\nHis words sounded hollow to everyone.\n(他的話對大家來說聽起來很空洞。)"],["holy","holy(adj.)神聖的\nholiness(n.)神聖\nholy place 聖地\nHoly Bible 聖經\nVisitors should be quiet in this holy place.\n(遊客在這個神聖的地方應保持安靜。)\nJerusalem is a holy city for several religions.\n(耶路撒冷是好幾個宗教的聖城。)"],["homesick","homesick(adj.)想家的、思鄉的\nhomesickness(n.)思鄉病\nfeel homesick 想家\nget homesick 開始想家\nI felt homesick during my first week at summer camp.\n(夏令營的第一週我很想家。)\nMany exchange students get homesick at the beginning.\n(許多交換學生一開始都會想家。)"],["hometown","hometown(n.)家鄉、故鄉\n(無詞性變化)\nreturn to one's hometown 回鄉\nhometown hero 家鄉英雄\nHe returned to his hometown after graduating from college.\n(他大學畢業後回到了家鄉。)\nMy hometown is famous for its beautiful beaches.\n(我的家鄉以美麗的海灘聞名。)"],["honesty","honesty(n.)誠實、正直\nhonest(adj.)誠實的\nhonestly(adv.)老實說、誠實地\nin all honesty 老實說\nHonesty is the best policy. 誠實為上策\nHonesty is the most important quality in a friend.\n(誠實是朋友最重要的特質。)\nThe teacher praised the boy for his honesty.\n(老師稱讚那個男孩很誠實。)"],["honor","honor(n./v.)榮譽、尊敬、使增光\nhonorable(adj.)光榮的、正直的\nin honor of 為紀念、向……致敬\nan honor 一項殊榮\nIt is a great honor to meet you.\n(能見到您是我莫大的榮幸。)\nA party was held in honor of the retiring teacher.\n(為了向即將退休的老師致敬，舉辦了一場派對。)"],["hopeful","hopeful(adj.)抱有希望的、有希望的\nhope(n./v.)希望\nhopefully(adv.)但願、有希望地\nfeel hopeful 感到充滿希望\nhopeful sign 好兆頭\nWe are hopeful that the weather will improve tomorrow.\n(我們希望明天天氣會好轉。)\nThe doctor gave us some hopeful news.\n(醫生給了我們一些令人振奮的消息。)"],["horn","horn(n.)角、喇叭、號角\n(無詞性變化)\nhonk the horn 按喇叭\nFrench horn 法國號\nThe driver honked the horn at the slow car.\n(那位駕駛對著開得很慢的車按喇叭。)\nA rhino has one or two horns on its nose.\n(犀牛的鼻子上有一或兩隻角。)"],["horrible","horrible(adj.)可怕的、糟透的\nhorror(n.)恐怖\nhorribly(adv.)可怕地、非常\nhorrible accident 可怕的意外\nhorrible smell 難聞的氣味\nThere was a horrible smell coming from the trash can.\n(垃圾桶傳來一股難聞的氣味。)\nWe had horrible weather during our trip.\n(我們旅行時天氣糟透了。)"],["horror","horror(n.)恐怖、震驚\nhorrible(adj.)可怕的\nhorrify(v.)使驚嚇\nhorror movie 恐怖片\nin horror 驚恐地\nI can't sleep after watching a horror movie.\n(看完恐怖片後我就睡不著。)\nShe screamed in horror when she saw the snake.\n(她看到那條蛇時驚恐地尖叫。)"],["hourly","hourly(adj./adv.)每小時的、每小時一次\nhour(n.)小時\nhourly wage 時薪\nhourly update 每小時更新\nThe buses to the airport run hourly.\n(往機場的公車每小時一班。)\nHer hourly wage at the coffee shop is quite low.\n(她在咖啡店的時薪相當低。)"],["housekeeper","housekeeper(n.)管家、女管家\nhousekeeping(n.)家務管理、房務\nhire a housekeeper 請管家\nhotel housekeeper 飯店房務人員\nThe housekeeper cleans the house twice a week.\n(管家一週打掃房子兩次。)\nThey hired a housekeeper to help take care of the kids.\n(他們請了一位管家幫忙照顧孩子。)"],["hug","hug(n./v.)擁抱\n(無詞性變化)\ngive someone a hug 擁抱某人\nbig hug 大大的擁抱\nShe gave her mother a big hug at the airport.\n(她在機場給了媽媽一個大大的擁抱。)\nThe two friends hugged each other after the game.\n(比賽結束後，兩個朋友互相擁抱。)"],["hum","hum(v.)哼歌、發出嗡嗡聲\n(無詞性變化)\nhum a song 哼歌\nhum along 跟著哼\nShe always hums a song while she cooks.\n(她做菜時總是哼著歌。)\nThe old refrigerator hums all night long.\n(那台舊冰箱整晚都發出嗡嗡聲。)"],["humid","humid(adj.)潮濕的\nhumidity(n.)濕度\nhot and humid 濕熱的\nhumid climate 潮濕的氣候\nSummer in Taiwan is usually hot and humid.\n(臺灣的夏天通常又熱又潮濕。)\nBread goes bad quickly in humid weather.\n(潮濕的天氣裡麵包很快就會壞掉。)"],["humor","humor(n.)幽默、幽默感、心情\nhumorous(adj.)幽默的\nsense of humor 幽默感\nin good humor 心情好\nMy English teacher has a great sense of humor.\n(我的英文老師很有幽默感。)\nHis speech was full of humor and everyone laughed.\n(他的演講充滿幽默，大家都笑了。)"],["humorous","humorous(adj.)幽默的、滑稽的\nhumor(n.)幽默\nhumorously(adv.)幽默地\nhumorous story 幽默的故事\nhumorous remark 風趣的話\nHe told a humorous story about his first day at school.\n(他講了一個關於自己上學第一天的有趣故事。)\nThe book is both humorous and touching.\n(這本書既幽默又感人。)"],["hunger","hunger(n.)飢餓、渴望\nhungry(adj.)飢餓的\nhungrily(adv.)飢餓地\ndie of hunger 餓死\nhunger for knowledge 渴望知識\nMillions of people around the world still suffer from hunger.\n(全世界仍有數百萬人飽受飢餓之苦。)\nShe has a strong hunger for knowledge.\n(她非常渴望求知。)"],["hut","hut(n.)小屋、茅舍\n(無詞性變化)\nwooden hut 木屋\nmountain hut 山屋\nThe hikers spent the night in a mountain hut.\n(登山客在山屋裡過夜。)\nThe old fisherman lives in a small wooden hut.\n(那位老漁夫住在一間小木屋裡。)"],["icy","icy(adj.)結冰的、冰冷的、冷淡的\nice(n.)冰\nicy road 結冰的路面\nicy stare 冷淡的目光\nDrive slowly because the roads are icy.\n(開慢一點，因為路面結冰了。)\nAn icy wind blew through the valley.\n(一陣冰冷的風吹過山谷。)"],["imagination","imagination(n.)想像力、想像\nimagine(v.)想像\nimaginative(adj.)富有想像力的\nuse your imagination 發揮想像力\nbeyond imagination 超乎想像\nChildren often have a rich imagination.\n(孩子們通常有豐富的想像力。)\nUse your imagination to finish the story.\n(發揮你的想像力把故事寫完。)"],["immediate","immediate(adj.)立即的、直接的、最接近的\nimmediately(adv.)立刻\nimmediate action 立即行動\nimmediate family 直系親屬\nThe problem needs immediate action.\n(這個問題需要立即採取行動。)\nOnly immediate family members were invited to the wedding.\n(只有直系親屬受邀參加婚禮。)"],["import","import(n./v.)進口、進口貨\nimporter(n.)進口商\nimport goods 進口商品\nimport tax 進口稅\nTaiwan imports a lot of oil from other countries.\n(臺灣從其他國家進口大量石油。)\nThe price of imports has risen this year.\n(今年進口商品的價格上漲了。)"],["impress","impress(v.)使印象深刻、使欽佩\nimpression(n.)印象\nimpressive(adj.)令人印象深刻的\nbe impressed by 對……印象深刻\nimpress on 使銘記\nI was impressed by her excellent English.\n(她出色的英文讓我印象深刻。)\nHe tried hard to impress his new boss.\n(他努力想讓新老闆留下好印象。)"],["indoor","indoor(adj.)室內的\nindoors(adv.)在室內\nindoor activity 室內活動\nindoor pool 室內游泳池\nOur school has a large indoor swimming pool.\n(我們學校有一座大型室內游泳池。)\nReading is a good indoor activity on rainy days.\n(閱讀是雨天很好的室內活動。)"],["indoors","indoors(adv.)在室內、進屋內\nindoor(adj.)室內的\nstay indoors 待在室內\ngo indoors 進到屋內\nWe stayed indoors because of the typhoon.\n(因為颱風，我們待在室內。)\nIt started to rain, so the children went indoors.\n(開始下雨了，所以孩子們進到屋內。)"],["industrial","industrial(adj.)工業的、產業的\nindustry(n.)工業、產業\nindustrialize(v.)使工業化\nindustrial area 工業區\nIndustrial Revolution 工業革命\nThe Industrial Revolution changed the way people lived.\n(工業革命改變了人們的生活方式。)\nThere are many factories in the industrial area.\n(工業區裡有許多工廠。)"],["inferior","inferior(adj./n.)較差的、低等的、部屬\ninferiority(n.)劣等、自卑\ninferior to 比……差\ninferior quality 品質低劣\nThis cheap bag is inferior to the original one.\n(這個便宜的包包品質比正品差。)\nNever let anyone make you feel inferior.\n(絕對不要讓任何人使你感到自卑。)"],["inform","inform(v.)通知、告知\ninformation(n.)資訊、消息\ninformative(adj.)提供資訊的、有益的\ninform someone of 通知某人某事\nkeep someone informed 讓某人隨時了解狀況\nPlease inform us of any changes to your address.\n(若您的地址有任何變更，請通知我們。)\nThe teacher informed the students that the test was canceled.\n(老師告知學生考試取消了。)"],["information","information(n.)資訊、消息、資料\ninform(v.)通知\ninformative(adj.)提供資訊的\na piece of information 一則資訊\ninformation desk 服務臺、詢問處\nYou can find more information on our website.\n(您可以在我們的網站上找到更多資訊。)\nPlease ask at the information desk.\n(請到服務臺詢問。)"],["injury","injury(n.)傷害、受傷\ninjure(v.)使受傷\ninjured(adj.)受傷的\nserious injury 重傷\nsuffer an injury 受傷\nHe missed the game because of a knee injury.\n(他因為膝傷錯過了比賽。)\nLuckily, nobody suffered serious injuries in the accident.\n(幸運的是，沒有人在意外中受重傷。)"],["inn","inn(n.)小旅館、客棧\ninnkeeper(n.)旅館老闆\ncountry inn 鄉間旅館\nstay at an inn 住在小旅館\nWe stayed at a small inn near the lake.\n(我們住在湖邊的一間小旅館。)\nThe old inn has been open for over a hundred years.\n(那間老旅館已經開業超過一百年了。)"],["inner","inner(adj.)內部的、內心的\ninnermost(adj.)最深處的\ninner peace 內心的平靜\ninner city 市中心(貧困區)\nYoga helps me find inner peace.\n(瑜伽幫助我找到內心的平靜。)\nThe inner walls of the castle are very thick.\n(城堡的內牆非常厚。)"],["innocent","innocent(adj.)無罪的、天真的、無辜的\ninnocence(n.)無罪、天真\ninnocent victim 無辜的受害者\ninnocent smile 天真的笑容\nThe man said he was innocent of the crime.\n(那名男子說他沒有犯罪。)\nThe baby gave us an innocent smile.\n(那個寶寶對我們露出天真的笑容。)"],["inspect","inspect(v.)檢查、視察\ninspection(n.)檢查、視察\ninspector(n.)檢查員、督察\ninspect carefully 仔細檢查\nsafety inspection 安全檢查\nThe mechanic inspected the car before the long trip.\n(長途旅行前，技師檢查了這輛車。)\nOfficials came to inspect the new school building.\n(官員們前來視察新校舍。)"],["inspector","inspector(n.)檢查員、督察、巡官\ninspect(v.)檢查\ninspection(n.)檢查\npolice inspector 警察督察\nsafety inspector 安全檢查員\nThe safety inspector checked every fire exit in the building.\n(安全檢查員檢查了大樓裡的每一個逃生出口。)\nA police inspector was sent to solve the case.\n(一位警察督察被派來偵辦這起案件。)"],["intelligent","intelligent(adj.)聰明的、有才智的\nintelligence(n.)智力、情報\nintelligently(adv.)聰明地\nhighly intelligent 非常聰明的\nintelligent design 智慧型設計\nDolphins are highly intelligent animals.\n(海豚是非常聰明的動物。)\nShe asked an intelligent question in class.\n(她在課堂上問了一個很有見地的問題。)"],["interrupt","interrupt(v.)打斷、中斷\ninterruption(n.)打斷、中斷\ninterrupt a conversation 打斷談話\nwithout interruption 不間斷地\nIt's rude to interrupt someone while they are speaking.\n(在別人說話時打斷是很沒禮貌的。)\nThe TV program was interrupted by breaking news.\n(電視節目被即時新聞中斷。)"],["invent","invent(v.)發明、捏造\ninvention(n.)發明、發明物\ninventor(n.)發明家\ninventive(adj.)有創意的\ninvent a machine 發明機器\ninvent an excuse 編造藉口\nWho invented the telephone?\n(誰發明了電話？)\nHe invented an excuse for being late.\n(他編了一個遲到的藉口。)"],["inventor","inventor(n.)發明家、發明者\ninvent(v.)發明\ninvention(n.)發明\nfamous inventor 著名發明家\nyoung inventor 年輕發明家\nThomas Edison was a famous American inventor.\n(愛迪生是一位著名的美國發明家。)\nThe young inventor won a prize for her smart robot.\n(那位年輕發明家以她的智慧機器人得獎。)"],["investigate","investigate(v.)調查、研究\ninvestigation(n.)調查\ninvestigator(n.)調查員\ninvestigate a case 調查案件\nunder investigation 調查中\nThe police are investigating the cause of the fire.\n(警方正在調查這場火災的起因。)\nThe case is still under investigation.\n(此案仍在調查中。)"],["invitation","invitation(n.)邀請、請帖\ninvite(v.)邀請\naccept an invitation 接受邀請\nwedding invitation 喜帖\nThank you for your kind invitation.\n(謝謝您的盛情邀請。)\nWe received a wedding invitation from my cousin.\n(我們收到表哥寄來的喜帖。)"],["ivory","ivory(n./adj.)象牙、象牙色的\n(無詞性變化)\nivory trade 象牙貿易\nivory tower 象牙塔\nThe ivory trade has caused many elephants to be killed.\n(象牙貿易導致許多大象遭到獵殺。)\nShe wore a beautiful ivory dress.\n(她穿著一件美麗的象牙色洋裝。)"],["jail","jail(n./v.)監獄、拘留所、監禁\njailer(n.)獄卒\nin jail 坐牢\ngo to jail 入獄\nThe thief was sent to jail for two years.\n(那名小偷被判入獄兩年。)\nHe was jailed for drunk driving.\n(他因酒駕而被關。)"],["jar","jar(n.)罐子、廣口瓶\n(無詞性變化)\ncookie jar 餅乾罐\na jar of jam 一罐果醬\nGrandma keeps cookies in a glass jar.\n(奶奶把餅乾放在一個玻璃罐裡。)\nCan you open this jar of jam for me?\n(你可以幫我打開這罐果醬嗎？)"],["jaw","jaw(n.)下巴、顎\n(無詞性變化)\nlower jaw 下顎\njaw drop 驚訝得張大嘴\nThe boxer was hit hard on the jaw.\n(那名拳擊手的下巴被重重擊中。)\nSharks have very strong jaws.\n(鯊魚有非常強壯的顎。)"],["jazz","jazz(n.)爵士樂\njazzy(adj.)爵士風格的、花俏的\njazz music 爵士樂\njazz band 爵士樂團\nMy father loves listening to jazz music.\n(我爸爸很喜歡聽爵士樂。)\nA jazz band played at the café on Friday night.\n(星期五晚上有一個爵士樂團在咖啡廳表演。)"],["jealous","jealous(adj.)嫉妒的、吃醋的\njealousy(n.)嫉妒\njealously(adv.)嫉妒地\njealous of 嫉妒\nfeel jealous 感到嫉妒\nShe was jealous of her sister's new dress.\n(她嫉妒姊姊的新洋裝。)\nDon't feel jealous of other people's success.\n(不要嫉妒別人的成功。)"],["jeep","jeep(n.)吉普車\n(無詞性變化)\ndrive a jeep 開吉普車\narmy jeep 軍用吉普車\nWe rode in a jeep through the mountain roads.\n(我們搭吉普車穿越山路。)\nThe soldiers arrived in an army jeep.\n(士兵們搭著軍用吉普車抵達。)"],["jelly","jelly(n.)果凍、果醬\n(無詞性變化)\njelly beans 雷根糖\npeanut butter and jelly 花生醬果醬\nThe kids love eating strawberry jelly after lunch.\n(孩子們很愛在午餐後吃草莓果凍。)\nHe made a peanut butter and jelly sandwich.\n(他做了一個花生醬果醬三明治。)"],["jet","jet(n./v.)噴射機、噴射、搭噴射機旅行\n(無詞性變化)\njet lag 時差\nprivate jet 私人噴射機\nI suffered from jet lag after flying to New York.\n(飛到紐約之後我飽受時差之苦。)\nA jet of water shot out of the broken pipe.\n(一道水柱從破掉的水管噴出。)"],["jewel","jewel(n.)寶石、寶物\njewelry(n.)珠寶\njeweler(n.)珠寶商\nprecious jewel 貴重的寶石\ncrown jewels 王冠上的寶石\nThe queen's crown was covered with jewels.\n(女王的王冠上鑲滿了寶石。)\nThis small island is the jewel of the region.\n(這座小島是該地區的瑰寶。)"],["jewelry","jewelry(n.)珠寶、首飾\njewel(n.)寶石\njeweler(n.)珠寶商\njewelry box 珠寶盒\nwear jewelry 戴首飾\nShe keeps her jewelry in a small wooden box.\n(她把首飾放在一個小木盒裡。)\nMy mom doesn't like to wear much jewelry.\n(我媽媽不喜歡戴太多首飾。)"],["journey","journey(n./v.)旅程、旅行\n(無詞性變化)\nlong journey 長途旅行\njourney of life 人生旅程\nThe journey from Taipei to Kaohsiung takes about two hours by high-speed rail.\n(搭高鐵從臺北到高雄大約要兩個小時。)\nLife is a journey full of surprises.\n(人生是一段充滿驚奇的旅程。)"],["joyful","joyful(adj.)充滿喜悅的、歡樂的\njoy(n.)喜悅\njoyfully(adv.)愉快地\njoyful moment 歡樂時刻\njoyful celebration 歡樂的慶祝\nThe wedding was a joyful celebration for the whole family.\n(那場婚禮對全家人而言是一場歡樂的慶祝。)\nThe children sang joyful songs at the party.\n(孩子們在派對上唱著歡樂的歌。)"],["juicy","juicy(adj.)多汁的、有趣的(八卦)\njuice(n.)果汁\njuicy fruit 多汁的水果\njuicy gossip 有趣的八卦\nThese peaches are sweet and juicy.\n(這些桃子又甜又多汁。)\nShe couldn't wait to share the juicy gossip.\n(她迫不及待想分享那個有趣的八卦。)"],["jungle","jungle(n.)叢林\n(無詞性變化)\ntropical jungle 熱帶叢林\nlaw of the jungle 弱肉強食\nMany wild animals live in the tropical jungle.\n(許多野生動物住在熱帶叢林裡。)\nThe explorers got lost in the thick jungle.\n(探險家們在茂密的叢林中迷路了。)"],["junior","junior(adj./n.)年少的、資淺的、三年級學生\n(無詞性變化)\njunior high school 國中\njunior member 資淺成員\nMy younger brother is a student in junior high school.\n(我弟弟是國中生。)\nShe is two years my junior.\n(她比我小兩歲。)"],["junk","junk(n./v.)廢物、垃圾、丟棄\n(無詞性變化)\njunk food 垃圾食物\njunk mail 垃圾郵件\nEating too much junk food is bad for your health.\n(吃太多垃圾食物對健康不好。)\nThe garage is full of old junk.\n(車庫裡堆滿了舊的廢物。)"],["kangaroo","kangaroo(n.)袋鼠\n(無詞性變化)\nred kangaroo 紅袋鼠\nbaby kangaroo 袋鼠幼崽\nA kangaroo can leap great distances with its powerful hind legs.\n(袋鼠可以用強壯的後腿跳躍很長的距離。)\nThe baby kangaroo stayed safely inside its mother's pouch.\n(小袋鼠安全地待在媽媽的育兒袋裡。)"],["keyboard","keyboard(n.)鍵盤\nkeyboardist(n.)鍵盤樂手\ncomputer keyboard 電腦鍵盤\nkeyboard shortcut 鍵盤快捷鍵\nHe cleaned the dust between the keys of his computer keyboard.\n(他清理了電腦鍵盤按鍵之間的灰塵。)\nLearning keyboard shortcuts can greatly improve your typing speed.\n(學習鍵盤快捷鍵可以大幅提升你的打字速度。)"],["kidney","kidney(n.)腎臟\n(無詞性變化)\nkidney disease 腎臟疾病\nkidney transplant 腎臟移植\nDrinking enough water every day helps maintain healthy kidneys.\n(每天補充足夠的水分有助於維持腎臟健康。)\nThe patient is waiting for a suitable donor for a kidney transplant.\n(該名病患正在等待合適的捐贈者進行腎臟移植。)"],["kilometer","kilometer(n.)公里\n(無詞性變化)\nper kilometer 每公里\nsquare kilometer 平方公里\nThe school is about two kilometers away from my house.\n(學校離我家大約有兩公里的距離。)\nThe speed limit on this highway is one hundred kilometers per hour.\n(這條高速公路的速限是每小時一百公里。)"],["kindergarten","kindergarten(n.)幼兒園\nkindergartner(n.)幼兒園學童\nattend kindergarten 就讀幼兒園\nkindergarten teacher 幼兒園老師\nChildren usually start kindergarten at around five years old.\n(孩童通常在五歲左右開始就讀幼兒園。)\nThe kindergarten teacher planned fun activities to keep the kids engaged.\n(幼兒園老師規劃了有趣的活動來吸引孩子們參與。)"],["kingdom","kingdom(n.)王國、界(生物分類)\nking(n.)國王\nkingship(n.)王位、王權\nUnited Kingdom 英國(聯合王國)\nanimal kingdom 動物界\nThe fairy tale tells a story of a prosperous and peaceful kingdom.\n(這篇童話講述了一個繁榮且和平的王國的故事。)\nLions are often considered the kings of the animal kingdom.\n(獅子通常被認為是動物界的王者。)"],["kit","kit(n.)成套工具、配套元件\n(無詞性變化)\nfirst-aid kit 急救箱\ntool kit 工具組\nEvery home should have a basic first-aid kit in case of emergencies.\n(每個家庭都應該準備基本急救箱以備不時之需。)\nHe bought a model airplane kit and spent hours putting it together.\n(他買了一組模型飛機套件，並花了數小時組裝。)"],["knight","knight(n.)騎士、爵士\nknighthood(n.)騎士頭銜\nbrave knight 勇敢的騎士\nknight in shining armor 救星、救難英雄\nThe brave knight fought valiantly to protect his kingdom.\n(那位英勇的騎士英勇奮戰以保護他的王國。)\nShe was waiting for a knight in shining armor to rescue her from trouble.\n(她在等待一位救星出現，將她從困境中拯救出來。)"],["knit","knit(v./n.)編織、毛線衣\nknitting(n.)編織物\nknitted(adj.)針織的\nknit a sweater 編織毛衣\nclose-knit 緊密團結的\nMy grandmother likes to knit warm scarves for us in winter.\n(我祖母喜歡在冬天為我們編織溫暖的圍巾。)\nThey grew up in a close-knit community where everyone helped each other.\n(他們在一個彼此互助的緊密社區中長大。)"],["knot","knot(n./v.)結、打結\nknotty(adj.)多節的、棘手的\ntie a knot 打結\ntie the knot 結婚\nMake sure to tie a tight knot so that the boat will not drift away.\n(務必打一個緊緊的結，以免船隻漂走。)\nAfter dating for seven years, they finally decided to tie the knot.\n(交往七年後，他們終於決定步入禮堂結婚。)"],["koala","koala(n.)無尾熊\n(無詞性變化)\nkoala bear 無尾熊\ncuddle a koala 擁抱無尾熊\nThe koala spends most of its day sleeping on eucalyptus trees.\n(無尾熊一整天的大部分時間都在尤加利樹上睡覺。)\nAustralia is famous for its unique wildlife, such as the koala and kangaroo.\n(澳洲以其獨特的野生動物聞名，例如無尾熊和袋鼠。)"],["label","label(n./v.)標籤、貼標籤於\n(無詞性變化)\nwarning label 警告標籤\nprice label 價格標籤\nAlways read the nutrition label before buying packaged food.\n(在購買包裝食品之前，務必閱讀營養標籤。)\nYou should not label people based on stereotypes.\n(你不應該根據刻板印象給人們貼上標籤。)"],["lace","lace(n./v.)蕾絲、鞋帶、繫鞋帶\nlacy(adj.)蕾絲的\nshoe laces 鞋帶\ntie one's laces 繫鞋帶\nThe bride wore an elegant white gown trimmed with delicate lace.\n(新娘穿著一件飾有精緻蕾絲的優雅白紗禮服。)\nHe knelt down on the sidewalk to tie his loose shoe laces.\n(他在人行道上蹲下身子繫緊鬆開的鞋帶。)"],["ladder","ladder(n.)梯子\n(無詞性變化)\nclimb a ladder 爬梯子\ncareer ladder 職場晉升階梯\nHe used a tall ladder to clean the leaves out of the roof gutter.\n(他用一把長梯清理屋頂排水溝裡的落葉。)\nShe worked diligently for ten years to climb the corporate career ladder.\n(她勤勉地工作了十年，在企業晉升階梯上步步高升。)"],["lately","lately(adv.)最近、近來\nlate(adj./adv.)遲的、晚的\njust lately 就在最近\nas of lately 最近以來\nHave you seen any good movies lately?\n(你最近有看過什麼好看的電影嗎？)\nShe has been feeling under great pressure at work lately.\n(她近來在工作上感到壓力很大。)"],["laughter","laughter(n.)笑聲、歡笑\nlaugh(v./n.)笑\nlaughable(adj.)可笑的\nburst into laughter 爆發笑聲\nroar of laughter 哄堂大笑\nThe room was filled with joy and laughter during the family party.\n(在家庭聚會期間，房間裡充滿了歡樂與笑聲。)\nHis funny impression of the teacher made everyone burst into laughter.\n(他模仿老師的滑稽模樣讓每個人都哄堂大笑。)"],["laundry","laundry(n.)待洗衣物、洗衣店\nlaunder(v.)洗滌、洗黑錢\ndo the laundry 洗衣服\nlaundry detergent 洗衣精\nI usually do the laundry on Sunday mornings so my clothes are ready for school.\n(我通常在週日早上洗衣服，這樣上學要穿的衣服就準備好了。)\nHe hung the wet laundry outside on the balcony to dry in the sun.\n(他把洗好的濕衣服晾在陽台外曬太陽。)"],["lawn","lawn(n.)草坪、草地\n(無詞性變化)\nmow the lawn 修剪草坪\nfront lawn 前院草坪\nMy father spends every Saturday morning mowing the front lawn.\n(我父親每週六早上都花時間修剪前院的草坪。)\nThe children enjoyed having a picnic and playing games on the green lawn.\n(孩子們喜歡在綠油油的草坪上野餐和玩遊戲。)"],["leak","leak(n./v.)漏洞、洩漏\nleakage(n.)滲漏、洩漏\nleaky(adj.)有漏洞的\ngas leak 瓦斯外洩\nwater leak 漏水\nThe old water pipe began to leak after the freezing winter storm.\n(在嚴寒的冬季風暴過後，老舊的水管開始漏水。)\nImportant confidential documents were leaked to the press last night.\n(重要的機密文件昨晚被洩漏給了媒體。)"],["leap","leap(n./v.)跳躍、躍進\n(無詞性變化)\nleap year 閏年\nleap of faith 放手一搏、大膽一試\nThe cat made a graceful leap from the table onto the top of the bookshelf.\n(那隻貓優雅地從桌上一躍跳到了書架頂端。)\nTaking this new job was a leap of faith for her career.\n(接受這份新工作是她職業生涯中的一次大膽嘗試。)"],["learning","learning(n.)學習、學問\nlearn(v.)學習\nlearned(adj.)博學的\nlifelong learning 終身學習\nlearning process 學習過程\nMaking mistakes is an unavoidable part of the learning process.\n(犯錯是學習過程中不可避免的一部分。)\nOnline courses have made lifelong learning much more accessible to everyone.\n(線上課程讓每個人都更容易實踐終身學習。)"],["leather","leather(n.)皮革\nleathery(adj.)像皮革的、粗糙的\nleather jacket 皮夾克\ngenuine leather 真皮\nHe bought a stylish brown leather jacket for the cold autumn days.\n(他買了一件帥氣的棕色皮夾克來度過寒冷的秋日。)\nThese expensive shoes are made of high-quality genuine leather.\n(這雙昂貴的鞋子是由優質真皮製成的。)"],["leisure","leisure(n.)閒暇、休閒\nleisurely(adj./adv.)悠閒的、悠閒地\nleisure time 閒暇時間\nat one's leisure 有空時、閒暇時\nIn his leisure time, he enjoys reading novels and listening to classical music.\n(在閒暇時間，他喜歡閱讀小說和聆聽古典音樂。)\nYou can review this contract at your leisure and sign it tomorrow.\n(您可以在有空時審閱這份合約，並在明天簽署。)"],["lemonade","lemonade(n.)檸檬水\n(無詞性變化)\nglass of lemonade 一杯檸檬水\nlemonade stand 檸檬水攤位\nNothing is more refreshing on a hot summer afternoon than an icy glass of lemonade.\n(在炎熱的夏日午後，沒有什麼比一杯冰涼的檸檬水更消暑了。)\nThe kids set up a lemonade stand on the street corner to raise money for charity.\n(孩子們在街角擺了一個檸檬水攤位，為慈善機構募款。)"],["leopard","leopard(n.)花豹、豹\n(無詞性變化)\nsnow leopard 雪豹\nspots of a leopard 豹的斑點\nThe leopard is famous for its speed, agility, and spotted coat.\n(花豹以其速度、敏捷度以及斑紋皮毛聞名。)\nA leopard can easily drag heavy prey up into a tall tree.\n(花豹可以輕鬆地將沉重的獵物拖到高高的樹上。)"],["lettuce","lettuce(n.)萵苣、生菜\n(無詞性變化)\nhead of lettuce 一球萵苣\ncrisp lettuce 爽脆的生菜\nShe made a fresh salad with crisp lettuce, sliced tomatoes, and cucumber.\n(她用爽脆的生菜、番茄切片和小黃瓜做了一道新鮮沙拉。)\nWould you like an extra slice of cheese and some lettuce in your burger?\n(你的漢堡裡想要多一片起司和一些生菜嗎？)"],["liberty","liberty(n.)自由\nliberate(v.)解放、使自由\nliberation(n.)解放\nStatue of Liberty 自由女神像\nreligious liberty 宗教自由\nThe Statue of Liberty is a worldwide symbol of freedom and democracy.\n(自由女神像是全球公認的自由與民主象徵。)\nCitizens fought courageously for their civil liberties and equal rights.\n(公民們英勇奮戰，為了爭取自身的公民自由與平等權利。)"],["lick","lick(v./n.)舔、舐\n(無詞性變化)\nlick one's lips 舔嘴唇\ngive a lick 舔一下\nThe friendly puppy ran up and began to lick my face enthusiastically.\n(那隻親人的小狗跑過來，熱情地舔我的臉。)\nThe little boy licked his melting ice cream before it dripped on his shirt.\n(小男孩在冰淇淋滴到襯衫之前趕緊舔了一口融化的冰淇淋。)"],["lifetime","lifetime(n.)一生、終身\n(無詞性變化)\nopportunity of a lifetime 一生一次的機會\nin one's lifetime 在某人一生中\nWinning a trip around the world was truly the opportunity of a lifetime.\n(贏得環遊世界的旅行確實是一生難得的良機。)\nHe dedicated his entire lifetime to researching renewable energy sources.\n(他將畢生精力都奉獻給了再生能源的研究。)"],["lighthouse","lighthouse(n.)燈塔\n(無詞性變化)\nlighthouse keeper 燈塔管理員\nbeam of a lighthouse 燈塔光束\nThe lighthouse on the cliff warned passing ships of the hazardous rocks below.\n(懸崖上的燈塔警告過往船隻注意下方的危險暗礁。)\nThe beacon from the lighthouse guided the fishermen safely back to the harbor.\n(燈塔的光芒引導著漁民安全返回港口。)"],["lightning","lightning(n.)閃電\n(無詞性變化)\nflash of lightning 一道閃電\nstruck by lightning 被雷擊中\nA flash of lightning lit up the entire night sky during the thunderstorm.\n(雷雨交加之際，一道閃電照亮了整片夜空。)\nThe old oak tree was struck by lightning and split down the middle.\n(那棵老橡樹被閃電擊中，從中間裂成了兩半。)"],["lily","lily(n.)百合花\n(無詞性變化)\nwater lily 睡蓮\nwhite lily 白百合\nThe white lily is often regarded as a symbol of pure love and innocence.\n(白百合常被視為純潔愛情與天真無邪的象徵。)\nBeautiful water lilies were floating peacefully across the surface of the pond.\n(美麗的睡蓮平靜地漂浮在池塘水面上。)"],["limb","limb(n.)肢、臂、大樹枝\n(無詞性變化)\nupper limbs 上肢\ntree limb 大樹枝\nRegular stretching exercises help keep your limbs flexible and strong.\n(規律的伸展運動有助於保持四肢靈活與強健。)\nA heavy tree limb snapped and fell onto the car during the gale.\n(大風中，一根粗重的大樹枝斷裂並掉落在汽車上。)"],["litter","litter(n./v.)垃圾、亂扔垃圾、一窩(幼獸)\n(無詞性變化)\nlitter bin 垃圾桶\ndrop litter 亂扔垃圾\nPeople who drop litter in the public park will be fined heavily.\n(在公園亂丟垃圾的人將被處以重罰。)\nOur cat gave birth to a healthy litter of five adorable kittens yesterday.\n(我們的貓昨天生了一窩共五隻健康的可愛小貓。)"],["lively","lively(adj.)充滿活力的、生氣勃勃的\nlive(v./adj.)居住、活的\nliveliness(n.)活力\nlively discussion 熱烈的討論\nlively imagination 豐富活躍的想像力\nThe professor encouraged a lively discussion among the students in class.\n(教授在課堂上鼓勵學生之間進行熱烈的討論。)\nDespite her old age, she still retains a lively and cheerful personality.\n(儘管年事已高，她仍然保持著活潑開朗的性格。)"],["loaf","loaf(n.)一條(麵包)\nloaves(n.)麵包條(複數)\nloafer(n.)遊手好閒者\na loaf of bread 一條麵包\nmeat loaf 肉捲、肉糕\nShe bought a loaf of freshly baked whole wheat bread from the bakery.\n(她從烘焙坊買了一條剛出爐的全麥麵包。)\nHalf a loaf is better than no bread when you are truly hungry.\n(聊勝於無；肚子餓時，半條麵包總比完全沒有麵包好。)"],["lobby","lobby(n./v.)大廳、遊說\nlobbyist(n.)遊說者\nhotel lobby 飯店大廳\nlobby for 遊說支持\nWe agreed to meet our tour guide in the hotel lobby at eight o'clock.\n(我們約定好八點在飯店大廳與導遊會合。)\nEnvironmental groups are actively lobbying for stricter laws against pollution.\n(環保團體正積極遊說制定更嚴格的反污染法規。)"],["locate","locate(v.)找出...的位置、座落於\nlocation(n.)位置、地點\nlocated(adj.)位於的\nbe located in 位於\nlocate the problem 找出問題所在\nThe rescue team used GPS devices to locate the missing hikers on the mountain.\n(搜救隊利用 GPS 設備在山上找出了失蹤登山客的位置。)\nThe new library is conveniently located near the central train station.\n(新圖書館地理位置便利，就座落在中央火車站附近。)"],["location","location(n.)位置、地點\nlocate(v.)找出位置、使座落\nprime location 黃金地段\ncurrent location 目前位置\nThe restaurant is situated in a prime location with a scenic ocean view.\n(這家餐廳位於黃金地段，享有美麗的海景。)\nPlease enable GPS on your mobile phone to share your current location.\n(請在手機上開啟 GPS 以分享您目前的位置。)"],["lock","lock(n./v.)鎖、鎖上\nlocked(adj.)上鎖的\nunlock(v.)解鎖、開鎖\nlock the door 鎖門\nunder lock and key 妥善鎖藏\nRemember to lock the front door and windows before leaving home.\n(離家前記得將大門和窗戶鎖好。)\nImportant contracts and valuables should be kept safely under lock and key.\n(重要合約和貴重物品應當妥善鎖藏保管。)"],["log","log(n./v.)原木、航海日誌、記錄\nlogger(n.)伐木工人\nlogging(n.)伐木業\nlog cabin 小木屋\nlog into 登入\nThey built a cozy log cabin in the woods to spend their winter vacation.\n(他們在森林裡建了一座溫馨的小木屋來度過寒假。)\nYou need to enter your username and password to log into your account.\n(你需要輸入使用者名稱和密碼才能登入你的帳號。)"],["lollipop","lollipop(n.)棒棒糖\n(無詞性變化)\nstrawberry lollipop 草莓棒棒糖\nsuck a lollipop 舔棒棒糖\nThe doctor gave the little girl a sweet lollipop after her vaccination.\n(醫生在小女孩打完疫苗後給了她一支甜甜的棒棒糖。)\nHe bought a colorful strawberry lollipop for his younger brother at the candy store.\n(他在糖果店為弟弟買了一支色彩繽紛的草莓棒棒糖。)"],["loose","loose(adj.)鬆的、寬鬆的、未束縛的\nloosen(v.)鬆開、放寬\nloosely(adv.)寬鬆地\nloose clothing 寬鬆衣物\nbreak loose 掙脫、逃脫\nYou should wear loose and comfortable clothing when exercising outdoors.\n(在戶外運動時，你應該穿著寬鬆舒適的衣服。))\nThe fierce dog broke loose from its chain and ran into the backyard.\n(那隻兇猛的狗掙脫了鐵鍊，跑進了後院。)"],["lord","lord(n.)貴族、領主、主\nlordship(n.)貴族統治、大人\nfeudal lord 封建領主\nLord of the Rings 魔戒\nIn medieval times, peasants worked on the land owned by the noble lord.\n(在中世紀，農民在貴族領主擁有的土地上耕作。)\nThe brave warriors swore an oath of eternal loyalty to their lord.\n(勇敢的戰士們向他們的領主宣誓永恆效忠。)"],["loser","loser(n.)輸家、失敗者\nlose(v.)輸、失去\nloss(n.)損失\ngood loser 有風度的輸家\nsore loser 輸不起的人\nSports teach us how to be a gracious winner and a good loser.\n(運動教會我們如何做一個有風度的贏家，以及輸得起的人。)\nNobody likes playing games with a sore loser who complains constantly.\n(沒有人喜歡和一個總是抱怨、輸不起的人一起玩遊戲。)"],["lover","lover(n.)情人、愛好者\nlove(v./n.)喜愛、愛\nlovely(adj.)可愛的\nmusic lover 音樂愛好者\nnature lover 大自然愛好者\nAs a dedicated nature lover, she spends almost every weekend hiking in the mountains.\n(身為一個熱愛大自然的人，她幾乎每個週末都在登山。)\nThe famous concert drew thousands of enthusiastic classical music lovers.\n(這場著名的音樂會吸引了成千上萬熱情的古典音樂愛好者。)"],["luggage","luggage(n.)行李\n(無詞性變化)\nhand luggage 手提行李\npack luggage 收拾行李\nPlease make sure your hand luggage fits into the overhead compartment on the plane.\n(請確保您的手提行李能放進飛機上的頭頂行李架置物箱中。)\nShe carefully packed her luggage the evening before departure.\n(她在出發前一天晚上仔細地收拾好了行李。)"],["lung","lung(n.)肺、肺部\n(無詞性變化)\nlung cancer 肺癌\nhealthy lungs 健康的肺部\nSmoking causes severe damage to human lungs and increases the risk of heart disease.\n(吸煙會對人體的肺部造成嚴重損害，並增加心臟病的風險。)\nThe excited fans shouted at the top of their lungs when their team scored a goal.\n(當球隊進球時，興奮的球迷們竭盡全力扯開嗓子高聲歡呼。)"],["magical","magical(adj.)神奇的、魔法的、迷人的\nmagic(n./adj.)魔術、魔法\nmagician(n.)魔術師\nmagical power 魔力\nmagical moment 美妙的時刻\nThe night view of the city was magical.\n(這座城市的夜景美得令人著迷。)\nIn the story, the old woman has magical powers.\n(故事中，那位老婦人擁有魔力。)"],["magician","magician(n.)魔術師、魔法師\nmagic(n.)魔術、魔法\nmagical(adj.)神奇的\nstreet magician 街頭魔術師\na famous magician 知名魔術師\nThe magician pulled a rabbit out of his hat.\n(那位魔術師從帽子裡拉出一隻兔子。)\nLouis Liu is a famous magician from Taiwan.\n(劉謙是台灣有名的魔術師。)"],["magnet","magnet(n.)磁鐵、有吸引力的人(事物)\nmagnetic(adj.)有磁性的、有吸引力的\nfridge magnet 冰箱磁鐵\na magnet for 吸引…的地方\nShe put a photo on the fridge with a magnet.\n(她用磁鐵把照片貼在冰箱上。)\nThe night market is a magnet for tourists.\n(夜市是吸引觀光客的地方。)"],["maid","maid(n.)女僕、女傭\n(無詞性變化)\nhotel maid 飯店清潔人員\nmaid of honor 伴娘\nThe hotel maid cleans our room every morning.\n(飯店清潔人員每天早上打掃我們的房間。)\nMy cousin asked me to be her maid of honor.\n(我表姊請我當她的伴娘。)"],["majority","majority(n.)大多數、多數\nmajor(adj.)主要的\nthe majority of 大多數的…\nmajority vote 多數決\nThe majority of students voted for the class trip.\n(大多數學生投票贊成班級旅行。)\nWe made the decision by majority vote.\n(我們以多數決做出決定。)"],["mall","mall(n.)購物中心、商場\n(無詞性變化)\nshopping mall 購物中心\ngo to the mall 去逛街\nLet's go to the mall this weekend.\n(這個週末我們去購物中心逛逛吧。)\nThe new shopping mall has a big movie theater.\n(新的購物中心有一間大電影院。)"],["mankind/humankind","mankind(n.)人類\nhumankind(n.)人類(性別中立的說法)\nhuman(n./adj.)人、人類的\nthe history of mankind 人類歷史\nfor the good of mankind 為了全人類的福祉\nThe invention of the Internet changed mankind forever.\n(網際網路的發明永遠改變了人類。)\nClimate change is a threat to all humankind.\n(氣候變遷是全人類的威脅。)"],["marble","marble(n.)大理石、彈珠\n(無詞性變化)\nmarble floor 大理石地板\nplay marbles 玩彈珠\nThe hall has a beautiful marble floor.\n(大廳有美麗的大理石地板。)\nTaroko Gorge is famous for its marble cliffs.\n(太魯閣峽谷以大理石峭壁聞名。)"],["march","march(n./v.)行軍、遊行、前進、示威遊行\n(無詞性變化)\nmarch past 列隊行進通過\npeace march 和平遊行\nThe band marched down the street.\n(樂隊沿著街道行進。)\nThousands of people joined the march.\n(數千人參加了這場遊行。)"],["marker","marker(n.)麥克筆、記號筆、標記\nmark(v./n.)標記、記號\nwhiteboard marker 白板筆\npermanent marker 油性筆\nThe teacher wrote on the board with a red marker.\n(老師用紅色白板筆在白板上寫字。)\nWrite your name on the box with a permanent marker.\n(用油性筆在箱子上寫下你的名字。)"],["marvelous","marvelous(adj.)令人驚嘆的、非凡的、極好的\nmarvel(v./n.)驚嘆、奇蹟\nmarvelous view 絕佳的景色\nmarvelous idea 絕妙的主意\nWe had a marvelous time at the beach.\n(我們在海邊玩得非常愉快。)\nThat's a marvelous idea!\n(那真是個絕妙的主意！)"],["mathematical","mathematical(adj.)數學的、精確的\nmathematics(n.)數學\nmathematician(n.)數學家\nmathematical problem 數學問題\nmathematical skills 數學能力\nCoding requires good mathematical skills.\n(寫程式需要良好的數學能力。)\nHe solved the mathematical problem in five minutes.\n(他在五分鐘內解出了這道數學題。)"],["mayor","mayor(n.)市長\n(無詞性變化)\nthe mayor of Taipei 台北市長\nelect a mayor 選舉市長\nThe mayor visited our school yesterday.\n(市長昨天參訪了我們學校。)\nPeople will elect a new mayor next year.\n(人們明年將選出新市長。)"],["meadow","meadow(n.)草地、牧草地\n(無詞性變化)\ngreen meadow 綠色草原\nflower meadow 花草地\nCows were eating grass in the meadow.\n(牛群在草地上吃草。)\nWe had a picnic in a meadow full of flowers.\n(我們在開滿花的草地上野餐。)"],["meaningful","meaningful(adj.)有意義的、意味深長的\nmeaning(n.)意義\nmeaningless(adj.)無意義的\nmeaningful experience 有意義的經驗\nmeaningful life 有意義的人生\nVolunteering at the hospital was a meaningful experience.\n(在醫院當志工是一段有意義的經驗。)\nShe gave me a meaningful look.\n(她意味深長地看了我一眼。)"],["meanwhile","meanwhile(n./adv.)同時、其間\n(無詞性變化)\nin the meanwhile 在這期間\nmeanwhile at home 與此同時在家裡\nDad cooked dinner; meanwhile, I set the table.\n(爸爸煮晚餐，同時我擺好餐具。)\nThe bus will come in twenty minutes. In the meanwhile, let's get a drink.\n(公車二十分鐘後才來，這段時間我們去買杯飲料吧。)"],["medal","medal(n.)獎牌、勳章\nmedalist(n.)獎牌得主\ngold medal 金牌\nwin a medal 贏得獎牌\nShe won a gold medal at the Olympics.\n(她在奧運贏得一面金牌。)\nEvery runner got a medal after the race.\n(每位跑者賽後都獲得一面獎牌。)"],["medium/media","medium(n.)媒介、方法、中間\nmedia(n.)媒體(medium 的複數)\nmass media 大眾傳播媒體\na medium of communication 溝通媒介\nEnglish is used as a medium of teaching in this class.\n(這堂課用英文作為教學媒介。)\nThe mass media has a strong influence on young people.\n(大眾媒體對年輕人有很大的影響。)"],["melon","melon(n.)甜瓜、瓜\nwatermelon(n.)西瓜\nslice of melon 一片瓜\nhoneydew melon 哈密瓜\nWe ate cold watermelon on a hot day.\n(我們在大熱天吃冰涼的西瓜。)\nThis melon is sweet and juicy.\n(這顆甜瓜又甜又多汁。)"],["melt","melt(v.)融化、熔化、(感情)軟化\n(無詞性變化)\nmelt away 逐漸消失\nmelting pot 大熔爐\nThe ice cream melted quickly in the sun.\n(冰淇淋在陽光下很快就融化了。)\nHer smile melted my heart.\n(她的笑容融化了我的心。)"],["mend","mend(v.)修補、修理、改善\n(無詞性變化)\nmend clothes 縫補衣服\nmend a relationship 修補關係\nGrandma mended the hole in my jeans.\n(奶奶幫我補好牛仔褲上的破洞。)\nThey tried to mend their friendship after the fight.\n(吵架後他們試著修補友誼。)"],["mental","mental(adj.)心理的、精神的、智力的\nmentally(adv.)心理上、精神上\nmentality(n.)心態\nmental health 心理健康\nmental age 心智年齡\nExercise is good for both physical and mental health.\n(運動對身心健康都有益。)\nTaking the exam was a great mental challenge.\n(考試是一大心理挑戰。)"],["merry","merry(adj.)愉快的、歡樂的\nmerrily(adv.)愉快地\nMerry Christmas 聖誕快樂\nmerry-go-round 旋轉木馬\nWe wish you a Merry Christmas!\n(祝你聖誕快樂！)\nThe children laughed merrily on the merry-go-round.\n(孩子們在旋轉木馬上開心地笑著。)"],["mess","mess(n./v.)雜亂、混亂、弄亂\nmessy(adj.)凌亂的\nin a mess 一團亂\nmess up 弄亂、搞砸\nYour room is in a mess!\n(你的房間亂七八糟！)\nI messed up my speech because I was nervous.\n(我因為緊張把演講搞砸了。)"],["microphone/mike","microphone(n.)麥克風\nmike(n.)麥克風(口語)\nspeak into the microphone 對著麥克風講話\nwireless microphone 無線麥克風\nPlease speak into the microphone so everyone can hear.\n(請對著麥克風說話，這樣大家才聽得到。)\nThe singer held the mike and started to sing.\n(那位歌手拿起麥克風開始唱歌。)"],["microwave","microwave(n./v.)微波爐、微波、用微波爐加熱\n(無詞性變化)\nmicrowave oven 微波爐\nmicrowave food 微波食品\nHeat the rice in the microwave for two minutes.\n(把飯放進微波爐加熱兩分鐘。)\nI microwaved my lunch at the convenience store.\n(我在便利商店把午餐微波加熱。)"],["mighty","mighty(adj.)強大的、巨大的\nmight(n.)力量、權力\nmightily(adv.)強而有力地\nmighty river 大河\nmighty power 強大的力量\nThe mighty river flows into the sea.\n(那條大河流入大海。)\nThe pen is mightier than the sword.\n(筆的力量勝過劍。)"],["minus","minus(prep./n./adj.)減去、負號、零下的、負的\n(無詞性變化)\nminus sign 減號\nminus ten degrees 零下十度\nTen minus four is six.\n(十減四等於六。)\nIt was minus five degrees in Seoul last night.\n(首爾昨晚氣溫零下五度。)"],["miracle","miracle(n.)奇蹟\nmiraculous(adj.)奇蹟般的\nwork miracles 創造奇蹟\nby a miracle 奇蹟般地\nIt was a miracle that no one was hurt in the accident.\n(那場車禍沒有人受傷真是奇蹟。)\nThe doctors worked miracles to save his life.\n(醫生們創造奇蹟救回了他的性命。)"],["misery","misery(n.)痛苦、悲慘、不幸\nmiserable(adj.)悲慘的、痛苦的\nlive in misery 生活悲慘\nput someone out of misery 讓某人解脫\nThe war brought misery to millions of people.\n(戰爭為數百萬人帶來苦難。)\nMany families still live in misery after the earthquake.\n(許多家庭在地震後仍過著悲慘的生活。)"],["missile","missile(n.)飛彈、導彈\n(無詞性變化)\nlaunch a missile 發射飛彈\nmissile test 飛彈試射\nThe country launched a missile into the sea.\n(該國向海上發射了一枚飛彈。)\nThe news reported a new missile test this morning.\n(新聞報導今天早上有一次新的飛彈試射。)"],["missing","missing(adj.)失蹤的、遺失的、缺少的\nmiss(v.)錯過、想念、遺漏\nmissing person 失蹤人口\ngo missing 失蹤、不見\nMy cat went missing last week.\n(我的貓上週不見了。)\nTwo pages are missing from this book.\n(這本書少了兩頁。)"],["mission","mission(n.)任務、使命、使節團\nmissionary(n.)傳教士\non a mission 執行任務\nmission impossible 不可能的任務\nThe astronauts completed their mission successfully.\n(太空人們成功完成了他們的任務。)\nOur mission is to help children in need.\n(我們的使命是幫助需要幫助的孩子。)"],["mist","mist(n./v.)薄霧、霧氣、起霧、(眼睛)變模糊\nmisty(adj.)有霧的、朦朧的\nmorning mist 晨霧\ncovered in mist 被霧籠罩\nThe mountains were covered in morning mist.\n(群山被晨霧籠罩。)\nHer eyes misted over when she said goodbye.\n(她道別時眼眶泛起淚光。)"],["mob","mob(n./v.)暴民、一群人、成群圍住\n(無詞性變化)\nangry mob 憤怒的群眾\nbe mobbed by fans 被粉絲團團圍住\nAn angry mob gathered outside the building.\n(一群憤怒的群眾聚集在大樓外。)\nThe singer was mobbed by fans at the airport.\n(那位歌手在機場被粉絲團團圍住。)"],["mobile","mobile(adj.)可移動的、行動的\nmobility(n.)移動性、流動性\nmobile phone 手機\nmobile game 手機遊戲\nPlease turn off your mobile phone during the test.\n(考試時請關掉你的手機。)\nMany students spend hours playing mobile games.\n(許多學生花好幾個小時玩手遊。)"],["moist","moist(adj.)潮濕的、濕潤的\nmoisture(n.)濕氣、水分\nmoisten(v.)弄濕、使濕潤\nmoist soil 濕潤的土壤\nmoist air 潮濕的空氣\nKeep the soil moist, but don't water the plant too much.\n(保持土壤濕潤，但不要澆太多水。)\nThis chocolate cake is soft and moist.\n(這個巧克力蛋糕鬆軟又濕潤。)"],["moisture","moisture(n.)濕氣、水分\nmoist(adj.)潮濕的\nmoisturize(v.)保濕\nabsorb moisture 吸收水分\nlose moisture 流失水分\nThis cream helps your skin keep its moisture.\n(這款乳霜幫助你的肌膚保持水分。)\nRice can absorb moisture from the air.\n(米能吸收空氣中的濕氣。)"],["monk","monk(n.)和尚、僧侶\n(無詞性變化)\nBuddhist monk 佛教僧侶\nbecome a monk 出家\nA Buddhist monk lives in the temple on the hill.\n(一位僧侶住在山丘上的寺廟裡。)\nHe decided to become a monk at the age of thirty.\n(他三十歲時決定出家。)"],["monster","monster(n.)怪物、巨大的東西\nmonstrous(adj.)巨大的、駭人的\nsea monster 海怪\nlittle monster 小怪物、小搗蛋\nThe movie is about a monster living under the sea.\n(這部電影是關於一隻住在海底的怪物。)\nMy little brother is a real monster when he's hungry.\n(我弟弟肚子餓時真是個小搗蛋。)"],["monthly","monthly(adj./adv./n.)每月的、每月一次、月刊\nmonth(n.)月\nmonthly payment 月付款\nmonthly magazine 月刊\nMy monthly phone bill is about five hundred dollars.\n(我每月的電話費大約五百元。)\nThe club meets monthly to share books.\n(讀書會每月聚會一次分享書籍。)"],["moral","moral(adj./n.)道德的、寓意、道德規範\nmorality(n.)道德\nmorally(adv.)道德上\nmoral of the story 故事的寓意\nmoral support 精神支持\nThe moral of the story is that honesty is the best policy.\n(這個故事的寓意是誠實為上策。)\nMy friends came to give me moral support.\n(我的朋友們來給我精神上的支持。)"],["mosquito","mosquito(n.)蚊子\n(無詞性變化)\nmosquito bite 蚊子叮咬\nmosquito net 蚊帳\nI got a lot of mosquito bites in the park.\n(我在公園被蚊子叮了好多包。)\nMosquitoes can spread dengue fever.\n(蚊子會傳播登革熱。)"],["mostly","mostly(adv.)大多、主要地\nmost(adj./adv.)大部分的、最\nmostly sunny 大致晴朗\nconsist mostly of 主要由…組成\nThe weather will be mostly sunny tomorrow.\n(明天天氣大致晴朗。)\nThe audience was mostly teenagers.\n(觀眾大多是青少年。)"],["motel","motel(n.)汽車旅館\n(無詞性變化)\nstay at a motel 住汽車旅館\ncheap motel 便宜的汽車旅館\nWe stayed at a motel near the highway.\n(我們住在公路附近的一間汽車旅館。)\nThe motel was cheap but clean.\n(那間汽車旅館便宜又乾淨。)"],["moth","moth(n.)蛾\n(無詞性變化)\nlike a moth to a flame 飛蛾撲火般地\nmoth wings 蛾的翅膀\nA moth flew around the lamp all night.\n(一隻蛾整晚繞著燈飛。)\nFans were drawn to the star like moths to a flame.\n(粉絲們像飛蛾撲火般被那位明星吸引。)"],["motor","motor(n.)馬達、發動機\nmotorcycle(n.)機車、摩托車\nelectric motor 電動馬達\nmotor vehicle 機動車輛\nThe fan has a small electric motor.\n(這台電風扇有一個小型電動馬達。)\nThe boat's motor stopped in the middle of the lake.\n(船的馬達在湖中央熄火了。)"],["multiply","multiply(v.)乘、增加、繁殖\nmultiplication(n.)乘法、增加\nmultiply by 乘以\nmultiply rapidly 迅速增加\nThree multiplied by four equals twelve.\n(三乘以四等於十二。)\nBacteria multiply quickly in warm weather.\n(細菌在溫暖的天氣中會迅速繁殖。)"],["murder","murder(n./v.)謀殺、兇殺\nmurderer(n.)殺人兇手\ncommit murder 犯下謀殺罪\nmurder case 兇殺案\nThe police are investigating the murder case.\n(警方正在調查這起兇殺案。)\nThe novel is about a murder on a train.\n(這本小說是關於一起火車上的謀殺案。)"],["muscle","muscle(n.)肌肉、力量\nmuscular(adj.)肌肉發達的\nbuild muscle 鍛鍊肌肉\npull a muscle 拉傷肌肉\nHe goes to the gym to build muscle.\n(他去健身房鍛鍊肌肉。)\nI pulled a muscle while playing basketball.\n(我打籃球時拉傷了肌肉。)"],["mushroom","mushroom(n./v.)蘑菇、迅速增長\n(無詞性變化)\nmushroom soup 蘑菇湯\nwild mushroom 野生菇類\nNever eat wild mushrooms you can't identify.\n(千萬不要吃無法辨識的野生菇類。)\nCoffee shops have mushroomed in our neighborhood.\n(我們這一區的咖啡店如雨後春筍般冒出來。)"],["mystery","mystery(n.)謎、神祕的事物、推理小說\nmysterious(adj.)神祕的\nsolve a mystery 解開謎團\nmystery novel 推理小說\nHow the pyramids were built is still a mystery.\n(金字塔是如何建造的至今仍是一個謎。)\nShe loves reading mystery novels.\n(她很愛看推理小說。)"],["naked","naked(adj.)裸體的、赤裸的、無遮蔽的\n(無詞性變化)\nnaked eye 肉眼\nnaked truth 赤裸裸的事實\nSome stars can be seen with the naked eye.\n(有些星星用肉眼就看得見。)\nThe baby ran around the room naked after his bath.\n(那個寶寶洗完澡後光著身子在房間裡跑來跑去。)"],["nap","nap(n./v.)小睡、午睡、打盹\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a nap 小睡一下\nafternoon nap 午睡\nI usually take a short nap after lunch.\n(我通常午餐後小睡一下。)\nGrandpa is napping on the sofa.\n(爺爺正在沙發上打盹。)"],["napkin","napkin(n.)餐巾、餐巾紙\n(無詞性變化)\npaper napkin 紙巾\nfold a napkin 摺餐巾\nCould you pass me a napkin, please?\n(可以請你遞給我一張餐巾紙嗎？)\nHe wiped his mouth with a paper napkin.\n(他用紙巾擦嘴。)"],["native","native(adj./n.)本國的、出生地的、本地人\n(無詞性變化)\nnative speaker 母語人士\nnative language 母語\nOur English teacher is a native speaker from Canada.\n(我們的英文老師是來自加拿大的母語人士。)\nFormosan black bears are native to Taiwan.\n(台灣黑熊是台灣的原生物種。)"],["navy","navy(n.)海軍、海軍藍\nnaval(adj.)海軍的\njoin the navy 加入海軍\nnavy blue 海軍藍、深藍色\nMy uncle served in the navy for ten years.\n(我叔叔在海軍服役了十年。)\nOur school uniform is navy blue.\n(我們的校服是深藍色的。)"],["neat","neat(adj.)整潔的、整齊的、很棒的\nneatly(adv.)整齊地\nneat and tidy 整齊乾淨\nneat handwriting 工整的字跡\nHer room is always neat and tidy.\n(她的房間總是整齊乾淨。)\nYour handwriting is very neat.\n(你的字跡非常工整。)"],["necessity","necessity(n.)必需品、必要性\nnecessary(adj.)必要的\nnecessarily(adv.)必然地\ndaily necessities 日常必需品\nout of necessity 出於必要\nWater and food are basic necessities of life.\n(水和食物是生活的基本必需品。)\nSmartphones have become a necessity for students.\n(智慧型手機已成為學生的必需品。)"],["necktie","necktie(n.)領帶\ntie(n./v.)領帶、綁\nwear a necktie 打領帶\ntie a necktie 繫領帶\nDad wears a necktie to work every day.\n(爸爸每天打領帶上班。)\nI bought my father a necktie for Father's Day.\n(我買了一條領帶送爸爸當父親節禮物。)"],["neighborhood","neighborhood(n.)鄰近地區、街坊、社區\nneighbor(n.)鄰居\nin the neighborhood 在附近\nquiet neighborhood 安靜的社區\nIs there a post office in the neighborhood?\n(這附近有郵局嗎？)\nWe live in a quiet neighborhood.\n(我們住在一個安靜的社區。)"],["nest","nest(n./v.)巢、窩、築巢\n(無詞性變化)\nbird's nest 鳥巢\nbuild a nest 築巢\nTwo birds are building a nest in the tree.\n(兩隻鳥正在樹上築巢。)\nChildren leave the nest when they grow up.\n(孩子長大後就會離家獨立。)"],["nickname","nickname(n./v.)綽號、暱稱、取綽號\n(無詞性變化)\ngive someone a nickname 幫某人取綽號\nbe nicknamed 被暱稱為\nHis classmates gave him the nickname 'Little Bear.'\n(他的同學幫他取了「小熊」這個綽號。)\nChicago is nicknamed 'the Windy City.'\n(芝加哥被暱稱為「風城」。)"],["normal","normal(adj.)正常的、平常的\nnormally(adv.)通常、正常地\nabnormal(adj.)不正常的\nback to normal 恢復正常\nnormal temperature 正常溫度\nIt's normal to feel nervous before a test.\n(考試前感到緊張是正常的。)\nLife went back to normal after the typhoon.\n(颱風過後生活恢復了正常。)"],["novelist","novelist(n.)小說家\nnovel(n./adj.)小說、新奇的\nfamous novelist 著名小說家\nyoung novelist 年輕小說家\nJ.K. Rowling is a famous British novelist.\n(J.K. 羅琳是一位著名的英國小說家。)\nShe dreams of becoming a novelist.\n(她夢想成為一名小說家。)"],["nun","nun(n.)修女、尼姑\n(無詞性變化)\nBuddhist nun 尼姑\nCatholic nun 天主教修女\nThe nun has worked at the orphanage for years.\n(那位修女在孤兒院服務了很多年。)\nA Buddhist nun lives in the small temple.\n(一位尼姑住在那間小廟裡。)"],["oak","oak(n.)橡樹、橡木\n(無詞性變化)\noak tree 橡樹\noak table 橡木桌\nA tall oak tree stands in front of the church.\n(教堂前有一棵高大的橡樹。)\nThis table is made of oak.\n(這張桌子是橡木做的。)"],["observe","observe(v.)觀察、注意到、遵守\nobservation(n.)觀察\nobserver(n.)觀察者\nobserve the rules 遵守規則\nobserve the stars 觀察星象\nStudents observed the plants for a week and took notes.\n(學生們觀察植物一個星期並做筆記。)\nAll players must observe the rules of the game.\n(所有選手都必須遵守比賽規則。)"],["occasion","occasion(n.)場合、時機、特殊的大事\noccasional(adj.)偶爾的\noccasionally(adv.)偶爾\nspecial occasion 特殊場合\non occasion 有時、偶爾\nShe only wears that dress on special occasions.\n(她只在特殊場合穿那件洋裝。)\nWe should celebrate this happy occasion.\n(我們應該慶祝這個喜慶的時刻。)"],["odd","odd(adj.)奇怪的、奇數的、零星的\noddly(adv.)奇怪地\nodd number 奇數\nodd job 零工\nOne, three, and five are odd numbers.\n(一、三、五都是奇數。)\nIt's odd that he hasn't called me yet.\n(他到現在還沒打給我，真奇怪。)"],["omit","omit(v.)省略、遺漏\nomission(n.)省略、遺漏\nomit a word 漏掉一個字\nomit details 省略細節\nYou can omit the word 'that' in this sentence.\n(這個句子裡你可以省略 that 這個字。)\nMy name was omitted from the list by mistake.\n(我的名字被誤漏在名單之外。)"],["ongoing","ongoing(adj.)進行中的、持續的\n(無詞性變化)\nongoing project 進行中的計畫\nongoing problem 持續存在的問題\nThe research is still ongoing.\n(這項研究仍在進行中。)\nAir pollution is an ongoing problem in many cities.\n(空氣汙染是許多城市持續存在的問題。)"],["onion","onion(n.)洋蔥\n(無詞性變化)\ngreen onion 青蔥\nonion rings 洋蔥圈\nCutting onions always makes me cry.\n(切洋蔥總是讓我流眼淚。)\nI'd like some onion rings with my burger.\n(我的漢堡要搭配一些洋蔥圈。)"],["onto","onto(prep.)到…之上\n(無詞性變化)\njump onto 跳上\nget onto 上(車、船等)\nThe cat jumped onto the table.\n(那隻貓跳到桌子上。)\nShe stepped onto the stage and began to sing.\n(她走上舞台開始唱歌。)"],["operation","operation(n.)手術、操作、運作\noperate(v.)操作、動手術\noperator(n.)操作員\nhave an operation 動手術\nrescue operation 救援行動\nMy grandfather had an operation on his knee.\n(我爺爺膝蓋動了手術。)\nThe rescue operation lasted three days.\n(救援行動持續了三天。)"],["opportunity","opportunity(n.)機會\n(無詞性變化)\ntake the opportunity 把握機會\nequal opportunity 平等的機會\nI took the opportunity to practice my English with tourists.\n(我把握機會和觀光客練習英文。)\nStudying abroad is a great opportunity.\n(出國留學是一個很好的機會。)"],["opposite","opposite(adj./n./prep./adv.)相反的、對面的、相反的事物、在對面\noppose(v.)反對\nopposition(n.)反對\nthe opposite of …的相反\nopposite side 對面\nThe bank is opposite the post office.\n(銀行在郵局對面。)\nThe opposite of 'happy' is 'sad.'\n(happy 的相反詞是 sad。)"],["optimistic","optimistic(adj.)樂觀的\noptimism(n.)樂觀主義\noptimist(n.)樂觀的人\nbe optimistic about 對…感到樂觀\nstay optimistic 保持樂觀\nShe is optimistic about her future.\n(她對自己的未來很樂觀。)\nTry to stay optimistic even when things are hard.\n(即使事情很困難，也要試著保持樂觀。)"],["oral","oral(adj./n.)口頭的、口腔的、口試\norally(adv.)口頭地\noral test 口試\noral report 口頭報告\nWe have an English oral test next week.\n(我們下週有英文口試。)\nEach group has to give an oral report in class.\n(每一組都必須在課堂上做口頭報告。)"],["organic","organic(adj.)有機的、器官的\norganism(n.)有機體、生物\norganic food 有機食品\norganic farming 有機農業\nOrganic vegetables are more expensive than regular ones.\n(有機蔬菜比一般蔬菜貴。)\nThe farm uses no chemicals; it practices organic farming.\n(那座農場不使用化學藥劑，採用有機耕作。)"],["organize","organize(v.)組織、籌辦、整理\norganization(n.)組織、機構\norganizer(n.)籌辦者\norganize a party 籌辦派對\norganize one's thoughts 整理思緒\nOur class organized a party for the teacher.\n(我們班為老師籌辦了一場派對。)\nTake a moment to organize your thoughts before you write.\n(寫作前先花點時間整理思緒。)"],["original","original(adj./n.)原始的、原創的、原作\norigin(n.)起源\noriginally(adv.)原本\noriginal idea 原創的想法\noriginal plan 原本的計畫\nOur original plan was to go hiking.\n(我們原本的計畫是去健行。)\nThis painting is a copy, not the original.\n(這幅畫是複製品，不是原作。)"],["outdoor","outdoor(adj.)戶外的\noutdoors(adv.)在戶外\noutdoor activities 戶外活動\noutdoor concert 戶外音樂會\nHiking is my favorite outdoor activity.\n(健行是我最喜歡的戶外活動。)\nThe outdoor concert was canceled because of the rain.\n(那場戶外音樂會因雨取消。)"],["outdoors","outdoors(adv.)在戶外、在野外\noutdoor(adj.)戶外的\nplay outdoors 在戶外玩\nthe great outdoors 大自然\nChildren should spend more time playing outdoors.\n(孩子們應該多花時間在戶外玩耍。)\nWe ate outdoors because the weather was nice.\n(因為天氣很好，我們在戶外用餐。)"],["outer","outer(adj.)外部的、外層的\n(無詞性變化)\nouter space 外太空\nouter layer 外層\nAstronauts travel into outer space.\n(太空人前往外太空。)\nRemove the outer layer of the onion first.\n(先剝掉洋蔥的外層。)"],["outline","outline(n./v.)大綱、輪廓、概述、畫出輪廓\n(無詞性變化)\nwrite an outline 寫大綱\noutline a plan 概述計畫\nWrite an outline before you start your essay.\n(開始寫作文前先擬好大綱。)\nWe could see the outline of the mountains at sunset.\n(日落時我們可以看到山的輪廓。)"],["oven","oven(n.)烤箱、爐\n(無詞性變化)\nmicrowave oven 微波爐\nbake in the oven 用烤箱烘烤\nBake the cookies in the oven for fifteen minutes.\n(把餅乾放進烤箱烤十五分鐘。)\nThe bread just came out of the oven.\n(麵包剛出爐。)"],["overseas","overseas(adv./adj.)在海外、海外的、外國的\n(無詞性變化)\nstudy overseas 出國留學\noverseas students 海外留學生\nMy sister plans to study overseas after college.\n(我姊姊打算大學畢業後出國留學。)\nOur school welcomes many overseas students.\n(我們學校歡迎許多海外學生。)"],["owe","owe(v.)欠(錢、人情)、歸功於\n(無詞性變化)\nowe someone money 欠某人錢\nowe... to... 把…歸功於…\nI still owe you a hundred dollars.\n(我還欠你一百元。)\nI owe my success to my parents.\n(我把我的成功歸功於我的父母。)"],["owl","owl(n.)貓頭鷹\n(無詞性變化)\nnight owl 夜貓子\nas wise as an owl 像貓頭鷹般睿智\nOwls usually hunt at night.\n(貓頭鷹通常在夜間獵食。)\nMy brother is a night owl who often studies until 2 a.m.\n(我哥哥是個夜貓子，常讀書讀到凌晨兩點。)"],["ownership","ownership(n.)所有權、擁有\nown(v./adj.)擁有、自己的\nowner(n.)主人、擁有者\nhome ownership 擁有房屋\ntake ownership of 對…負起責任\nThe ownership of the house passed to his son.\n(那棟房子的所有權轉移給了他兒子。)\nStudents should take ownership of their learning.\n(學生應該為自己的學習負起責任。)"],["ox","ox(n.)牛、閹牛\noxen(n.)牛(複數)\nas strong as an ox 力大如牛\nYear of the Ox 牛年\nIn the past, farmers used oxen to plow the fields.\n(過去，農夫用牛來犁田。)\nMy uncle is as strong as an ox.\n(我叔叔力大如牛。)"],["pad","pad(n./v.)墊子、便條本、填塞\npadding(n.)填充物\nmouse pad 滑鼠墊\nknee pad 護膝\nHe wrote the phone number on a note pad.\n(他把電話號碼寫在便條本上。)\nSkaters should wear knee pads for safety.\n(溜冰的人應該戴護膝以策安全。)"],["painter","painter(n.)畫家、油漆工\npaint(v./n.)畫、油漆\npainting(n.)畫作\nfamous painter 著名畫家\nhouse painter 油漆工\nVan Gogh is one of my favorite painters.\n(梵谷是我最喜歡的畫家之一。)\nWe hired a painter to paint the walls.\n(我們請了一位油漆工來粉刷牆壁。)"],["pal","pal(n.)朋友、夥伴(口語)\n(無詞性變化)\npen pal 筆友\nold pal 老朋友\nI have a pen pal in Canada.\n(我在加拿大有一位筆友。)\nMike and I have been pals since childhood.\n(麥克和我從小就是好朋友。)"],["palace","palace(n.)宮殿\n(無詞性變化)\nroyal palace 皇宮\nthe National Palace Museum 國立故宮博物院\nThe king lived in a beautiful palace.\n(國王住在一座美麗的宮殿裡。)\nWe visited the National Palace Museum last weekend.\n(我們上週末參觀了國立故宮博物院。)"],["palm","palm(n.)手掌、棕櫚樹\n(無詞性變化)\npalm tree 棕櫚樹\nread one's palm 看手相\nPalm trees line the beach road.\n(海灘路旁種滿了棕櫚樹。)\nShe held the tiny bird in her palm.\n(她把那隻小鳥捧在手掌心。)"],["pancake","pancake(n.)鬆餅、煎餅\n(無詞性變化)\nmake pancakes 做鬆餅\npancake with syrup 淋糖漿的鬆餅\nDad makes pancakes every Sunday morning.\n(爸爸每個星期天早上都做鬆餅。)\nI like my pancakes with honey and butter.\n(我喜歡在鬆餅上加蜂蜜和奶油。)"],["panic","panic(n./v.)恐慌、驚慌\npanicky(adj.)驚慌的\nin a panic 驚慌失措\nDon't panic. 別慌。\nPeople ran out of the building in a panic.\n(人們驚慌失措地跑出大樓。)\nDon't panic if you forget a word in your speech.\n(演講時忘詞也別慌張。)"],["parade","parade(n./v.)遊行、列隊行進\n(無詞性變化)\nhold a parade 舉行遊行\nparade float 遊行花車\nThousands of people watched the holiday parade.\n(數千人觀看了節日遊行。)\nThe team paraded through the city after winning.\n(球隊獲勝後在城市中遊行。)"],["paradise","paradise(n.)天堂、樂園\n(無詞性變化)\nshopping paradise 購物天堂\na paradise for 對⋯來說是天堂\nThis island is a paradise for divers.\n(這座島是潛水者的天堂。)\nTaipei is a food paradise for tourists.\n(台北對觀光客來說是美食天堂。)"],["parcel","parcel(n./v.)包裹、分配\n(無詞性變化)\nsend a parcel 寄包裹\nparcel out 分配\nI went to the post office to send a parcel.\n(我去郵局寄包裹。)\nA parcel arrived for you this morning.\n(今天早上有一個你的包裹寄到了。)"],["parrot","parrot(n./v.)鸚鵡、鸚鵡學舌般地重複\n(無詞性變化)\npet parrot 寵物鸚鵡\nparrot fashion 死記硬背地\nOur pet parrot can say 'hello'.\n(我們的寵物鸚鵡會說「哈囉」。)\nDon't just parrot the textbook; use your own words.\n(不要只是照著課本背，要用自己的話說。)"],["passage","passage(n.)通道、(文章的)段落、流逝\npass(v.)通過\nreading passage 閱讀短文\nthe passage of time 時間的流逝\nRead the passage and answer the questions.\n(閱讀這篇短文並回答問題。)\nA narrow passage leads to the garden.\n(一條狹窄的通道通往花園。)"],["passenger","passenger(n.)乘客\n(無詞性變化)\npassenger seat 副駕駛座\npassenger train 客運列車\nThe bus can carry fifty passengers.\n(這輛公車可以載五十名乘客。)\nAll passengers must wear seat belts.\n(所有乘客都必須繫安全帶。)"],["passion","passion(n.)熱情、熱愛\npassionate(adj.)熱情的\nhave a passion for 熱愛⋯\nfollow your passion 追隨你的熱情\nShe has a passion for music.\n(她熱愛音樂。)\nHe spoke about science with great passion.\n(他充滿熱情地談論科學。)"],["passport","passport(n.)護照\n(無詞性變化)\napply for a passport 申請護照\npassport control 護照查驗處\nDon't forget to bring your passport.\n(別忘了帶你的護照。)\nYou need a passport to travel abroad.\n(出國旅行需要護照。)"],["pat","pat(v./n.)輕拍\n(無詞性變化)\npat someone on the back 拍某人的背(表示鼓勵)\ngive... a pat 輕拍⋯\nThe coach patted me on the back after the game.\n(比賽後教練拍拍我的背鼓勵我。)\nShe gave the dog a gentle pat.\n(她輕輕拍了拍那隻狗。)"],["patience","patience(n.)耐心\npatient(adj./n.)有耐心的、病人\npatiently(adv.)耐心地\nlose patience 失去耐心\nwith patience 有耐心地\nLearning a language takes patience.\n(學習語言需要耐心。)\nThe teacher never loses patience with us.\n(老師對我們從不失去耐心。)"],["pause","pause(n./v.)暫停、停頓\n(無詞性變化)\npause button 暫停鍵\na short pause 短暫的停頓\nShe paused for a moment before answering.\n(她回答之前停頓了一下。)\nPress the pause button to stop the video.\n(按暫停鍵讓影片停下來。)"],["pave(ment)","pave(v.)鋪(路)、pavement(n.)人行道、鋪過的路面\n(無詞性變化)\npave the way for 為⋯鋪路\npaved road 柏油路\nThe village road was paved last year.\n(那條村莊道路去年鋪好了。)\nHard work paves the way for success.\n(努力為成功鋪路。)"],["pea","pea(n.)豌豆\n(無詞性變化)\ngreen peas 青豆\nlike two peas in a pod 一模一樣\nHe doesn't like green peas.\n(他不喜歡吃青豆。)\nThe twins are like two peas in a pod.\n(那對雙胞胎長得一模一樣。)"],["peanut","peanut(n.)花生\n(無詞性變化)\npeanut butter 花生醬\nroasted peanuts 烤花生\nI had a peanut butter sandwich for lunch.\n(我午餐吃了一份花生醬三明治。)\nSome people can't eat peanuts.\n(有些人不能吃花生。)"],["pearl","pearl(n.)珍珠\n(無詞性變化)\npearl necklace 珍珠項鍊\npearl milk tea 珍珠奶茶\nShe wore a pearl necklace to the party.\n(她戴著一條珍珠項鍊參加派對。)\nPearl milk tea is popular around the world.\n(珍珠奶茶在全世界都很受歡迎。)"],["peel","peel(v./n.)剝皮、削皮、果皮\npeeler(n.)削皮器\npeel an apple 削蘋果皮\norange peel 橘子皮\nCan you peel the potatoes for me?\n(你可以幫我削馬鈴薯皮嗎？)\nDon't throw the banana peel on the floor.\n(別把香蕉皮丟在地上。)"],["penguin","penguin(n.)企鵝\n(無詞性變化)\nemperor penguin 皇帝企鵝\na group of penguins 一群企鵝\nPenguins cannot fly, but they swim well.\n(企鵝不會飛，但很會游泳。)\nWe saw cute penguins at the zoo.\n(我們在動物園看到可愛的企鵝。)"],["penny","penny(n.)一分錢、便士\n(無詞性變化)\nevery penny 每一分錢\nnot a penny 一毛錢也沒有\nHe saved every penny for a new phone.\n(他為了買新手機存下每一分錢。)\nThe old toy isn't worth a penny.\n(這個舊玩具一毛錢也不值。)"],["pepper","pepper(n.)胡椒、辣椒、甜椒\npeppery(adj.)胡椒味的、辛辣的\nsalt and pepper 鹽和胡椒\ngreen pepper 青椒\nAdd some salt and pepper to the soup.\n(在湯裡加一些鹽和胡椒。)\nMy little brother refuses to eat green peppers.\n(我弟弟拒絕吃青椒。)"],["perform","perform(v.)表演、執行、表現\nperformance(n.)表演、表現\nperformer(n.)表演者\nperform a task 執行任務\nperform well 表現良好\nThe band will perform at the school festival.\n(那個樂團將在校慶表演。)\nOur team performed well in the contest.\n(我們隊在比賽中表現良好。)"],["performance","performance(n.)表演、表現、性能\nperform(v.)表演、執行\nperformer(n.)表演者\nlive performance 現場表演\nacademic performance 學業表現\nHer performance in the play was amazing.\n(她在那齣戲中的表演很驚人。)\nSleep can affect your academic performance.\n(睡眠會影響你的學業表現。)"],["permission","permission(n.)許可、允許\npermit(v.)允許\nask for permission 請求許可\nwithout permission 未經許可\nYou need permission to leave the classroom.\n(你需要得到許可才能離開教室。)\nDon't use my computer without permission.\n(未經許可不要用我的電腦。)"],["permit","permit(v./n.)允許、許可證\npermission(n.)許可\nweather permitting 天氣允許的話\nwork permit 工作許可證\nSmoking is not permitted in the building.\n(大樓內禁止吸菸。)\nWe will go hiking, weather permitting.\n(天氣允許的話，我們會去爬山。)"],["persuade","persuade(v.)說服\npersuasion(n.)說服\npersuasive(adj.)有說服力的\npersuade... to 說服⋯去做\npersuade... into 說服⋯做\nI persuaded my dad to buy a dog.\n(我說服爸爸買一隻狗。)\nShe tried to persuade him to stay, but he left.\n(她試著說服他留下，但他還是走了。)"],["photographer","photographer(n.)攝影師\nphotograph(n./v.)照片、拍照\nphotography(n.)攝影\nprofessional photographer 專業攝影師\nwedding photographer 婚禮攝影師\nThe photographer took pictures of the wedding.\n(攝影師拍攝了婚禮的照片。)\nHe wants to become a nature photographer.\n(他想成為一名自然生態攝影師。)"],["pigeon","pigeon(n.)鴿子\n(無詞性變化)\nfeed the pigeons 餵鴿子\nracing pigeon 賽鴿\nChildren are feeding the pigeons in the park.\n(孩子們在公園裡餵鴿子。)\nA pigeon landed on my window.\n(一隻鴿子停在我的窗台上。)"],["pile","pile(n./v.)一堆、堆積\n(無詞性變化)\na pile of 一堆\npile up 堆積\nThere is a pile of books on my desk.\n(我書桌上有一堆書。)\nDirty dishes piled up in the sink.\n(髒碗盤在水槽裡堆積如山。)"],["pill","pill(n.)藥丸\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a pill 吃藥丸\nsleeping pill 安眠藥\nTake one pill after each meal.\n(每餐飯後吃一顆藥。)\nThe pill was too big to swallow.\n(那顆藥丸大到難以吞下。)"],["pilot","pilot(n./v.)飛行員、駕駛、試驗性的(計畫)\n(無詞性變化)\nairline pilot 民航機師\npilot program 試辦計畫\nMy cousin wants to be an airline pilot.\n(我表哥想當民航機師。)\nThe pilot landed the plane safely.\n(機師讓飛機安全降落。)"],["pine","pine(n.)松樹\n(無詞性變化)\npine tree 松樹\npine cone 松果\nTall pine trees grow on the mountain.\n(山上長著高大的松樹。)\nThe kids collected pine cones in the forest.\n(孩子們在森林裡撿松果。)"],["pineapple","pineapple(n.)鳳梨\n(無詞性變化)\npineapple cake 鳳梨酥\npineapple juice 鳳梨汁\nPineapple cakes are a popular gift from Taiwan.\n(鳳梨酥是台灣很受歡迎的伴手禮。)\nThis pineapple is sweet and juicy.\n(這顆鳳梨又甜又多汁。)"],["pint","pint(n.)品脫(容量單位)\n(無詞性變化)\na pint of milk 一品脫牛奶\nhalf a pint 半品脫\nHe bought a pint of milk at the store.\n(他在店裡買了一品脫牛奶。)\nA pint is a little less than half a liter.\n(一品脫比半公升少一點。)"],["pit","pit(n.)坑、洞、(水果的)核\n(無詞性變化)\nfire pit 火坑、烤火台\npeach pit 桃核\nThe workers dug a deep pit.\n(工人們挖了一個深坑。)\nBe careful not to swallow the cherry pit.\n(小心別吞下櫻桃核。)"],["pitch","pitch(n./v.)投球、音調、球場、搭(帳篷)\npitcher(n.)投手、水壺\npitch a tent 搭帳篷\nhigh pitch 高音調\nWe pitched our tent near the lake.\n(我們在湖邊搭帳篷。)\nHe pitched the ball very fast.\n(他把球投得很快。)"],["pity","pity(n./v.)遺憾、同情、憐憫\npitiful(adj.)可憐的\nWhat a pity! 真可惜！\ntake pity on 同情⋯\nWhat a pity that you missed the concert!\n(你錯過了演唱會真可惜！)\nI pity the people who lost their homes.\n(我同情那些失去家園的人。)"],["plastic","plastic(n./adj.)塑膠、塑膠的\n(無詞性變化)\nplastic bag 塑膠袋\nplastic surgery 整形手術\nPlease bring your own bag instead of using plastic bags.\n(請自備購物袋，不要使用塑膠袋。)\nPlastic waste is harmful to sea animals.\n(塑膠垃圾對海洋動物有害。)"],["playful","playful(adj.)愛玩的、開玩笑的\nplay(v.)玩\nplayfully(adv.)開玩笑地、頑皮地\nplayful puppy 愛玩的小狗\nplayful mood 頑皮的心情\nThe playful kitten chased the ball all day.\n(那隻愛玩的小貓整天追著球跑。)\nHe gave her a playful smile.\n(他對她露出頑皮的微笑。)"],["plenty","plenty(pron./n./adv.)大量、充足、很\nplentiful(adj.)豐富的\nplenty of 很多的\nplenty of time 充裕的時間\nDon't worry, we have plenty of time.\n(別擔心，我們時間很充裕。)\nDrink plenty of water on hot days.\n(大熱天要多喝水。)"],["plug","plug(n./v.)插頭、塞子、插上插頭\n(無詞性變化)\nplug in 插上電源\npull the plug 拔掉插頭、終止\nPlug in the charger before you go to bed.\n(睡前先把充電器插上電源。)\nThe sink plug is missing.\n(水槽的塞子不見了。)"],["pole","pole(n.)竿、柱、(地球的)極\npolar(adj.)極地的\nthe North Pole 北極\nfishing pole 釣竿\nA bird is sitting on the telephone pole.\n(一隻鳥停在電線桿上。)\nPolar bears live near the North Pole.\n(北極熊住在北極附近。)"],["political","political(adj.)政治的\npolitics(n.)政治\npolitician(n.)政治人物\npolitical party 政黨\npolitical issue 政治議題\nTaiwan has several major political parties.\n(台灣有幾個主要政黨。)\nThey avoid talking about political issues at dinner.\n(他們吃飯時避免談論政治議題。)"],["politician","politician(n.)政治人物、政客\npolitics(n.)政治\npolitical(adj.)政治的\nlocal politician 地方政治人物\nhonest politician 誠實的政治人物\nThe politician promised to build a new park.\n(那位政治人物承諾要建一座新公園。)\nMany people don't trust politicians.\n(很多人不信任政客。)"],["politics","politics(n.)政治、政治學\npolitical(adj.)政治的\npolitician(n.)政治人物\nenter politics 從政\nbe interested in politics 對政治感興趣\nMy uncle has been interested in politics since college.\n(我叔叔從大學起就對政治很感興趣。)\nShe plans to study politics at university.\n(她打算在大學念政治學。)"],["poll","poll(n./v.)民意調查、投票、對⋯進行民調\n(無詞性變化)\nopinion poll 民意調查\ngo to the polls 去投票\nThe latest poll shows he is in the lead.\n(最新的民調顯示他領先。)\nWe polled fifty students about their lunch habits.\n(我們針對五十名學生的午餐習慣做了調查。)"],["pollute","pollute(v.)汙染\npollution(n.)汙染\npolluted(adj.)受汙染的\npollute the air 汙染空氣\npolluted water 受汙染的水\nFactories should not pollute the rivers.\n(工廠不應該汙染河川。)\nCars pollute the air in big cities.\n(汽車汙染了大城市的空氣。)"],["pollution","pollution(n.)汙染\npollute(v.)汙染\npolluted(adj.)受汙染的\nair pollution 空氣汙染\nnoise pollution 噪音汙染\nAir pollution is bad for our health.\n(空氣汙染對我們的健康有害。)\nWe should reduce plastic pollution in the ocean.\n(我們應該減少海洋中的塑膠汙染。)"],["porcelain","porcelain(n.)瓷器、瓷\n(無詞性變化)\nporcelain vase 瓷花瓶\nfine porcelain 精緻瓷器\nThe museum has a collection of Chinese porcelain.\n(博物館收藏了一批中國瓷器。)\nShe broke a porcelain cup by accident.\n(她不小心打破了一個瓷杯。)"],["portion","portion(n./v.)部分、一份、分配\n(無詞性變化)\na large portion of 大部分的\na portion of food 一份食物\nThe restaurant serves large portions.\n(這家餐廳的份量很大。)\nA large portion of my money goes to food.\n(我大部分的錢都花在食物上。)"],["portrait","portrait(n.)肖像、人像畫\nportray(v.)描繪\nself-portrait 自畫像\nportrait painter 肖像畫家\nA portrait of the king hangs on the wall.\n(牆上掛著一幅國王的肖像。)\nThe artist painted a self-portrait.\n(那位畫家畫了一幅自畫像。)"],["poster","poster(n.)海報\n(無詞性變化)\nmovie poster 電影海報\nput up a poster 張貼海報\nHe has a movie poster on his bedroom wall.\n(他臥室牆上貼著一張電影海報。)\nWe put up posters for the school concert.\n(我們為學校音樂會張貼海報。)"],["postpone(ment)","postpone(v.)延期、postponement(n.)延期\n(無詞性變化)\npostpone the meeting 延後會議\npostpone until 延到⋯\nThe game was postponed because of the typhoon.\n(比賽因颱風而延期。)\nWe had to postpone our trip until next month.\n(我們不得不把旅行延到下個月。)"],["pottery","pottery(n.)陶器、陶藝\npotter(n.)陶藝家\nmake pottery 做陶藝\npottery class 陶藝課\nWe made pottery bowls in art class.\n(我們在美術課做了陶碗。)\nYingge is famous for its pottery.\n(鶯歌以陶瓷聞名。)"],["pour","pour(v.)倒、灌、(雨)傾盆而下\n(無詞性變化)\npour water 倒水\npour down 傾盆而下\nCould you pour me a glass of water?\n(你可以幫我倒一杯水嗎？)\nIt is pouring outside, so take an umbrella.\n(外面正下著大雨，帶把傘吧。)"],["poverty","poverty(n.)貧窮\npoor(adj.)貧窮的\nlive in poverty 生活貧困\npoverty line 貧窮線\nMany children around the world live in poverty.\n(全世界有許多孩子生活在貧困中。)\nEducation can help people escape poverty.\n(教育能幫助人們擺脫貧窮。)"],["powder","powder(n./v.)粉、粉末、撲粉\npowdery(adj.)粉狀的\nmilk powder 奶粉\nwashing powder 洗衣粉\nMix the milk powder with warm water.\n(把奶粉和溫水混合。)\nThe baking powder makes the cake rise.\n(泡打粉讓蛋糕膨脹起來。)"],["practical","practical(adj.)實際的、實用的\npractice(n./v.)實踐、練習\npractically(adv.)實際上、幾乎\npractical skills 實用技能\npractical advice 實用的建議\nThis bag is cheap and practical.\n(這個包包便宜又實用。)\nShe gave me some practical advice.\n(她給了我一些實用的建議。)"],["precious","precious(adj.)珍貴的、寶貴的\n(無詞性變化)\nprecious time 寶貴的時間\nprecious stone 寶石\nTime with family is precious.\n(和家人相處的時光很寶貴。)\nDon't waste your precious time on games.\n(不要把寶貴的時間浪費在遊戲上。)"],["preparation","preparation(n.)準備\nprepare(v.)準備\nprepared(adj.)準備好的\nin preparation for 為⋯做準備\nmake preparations 做準備\nThe students are busy in preparation for the exam.\n(學生們正忙著準備考試。)\nGood preparation is the key to success.\n(充分的準備是成功的關鍵。)"],["presence","presence(n.)出席、在場、存在\npresent(adj.)出席的、現在的\nin the presence of 在⋯面前\npresence of mind 沉著、鎮定\nThank you for your presence at the meeting.\n(謝謝你出席會議。)\nDon't say that in the presence of children.\n(別在孩子面前說那種話。)"],["pretend","pretend(v.)假裝\npretense(n.)假裝、藉口\npretend to 假裝⋯\npretend that 假裝⋯\nHe pretended to be asleep.\n(他假裝睡著了。)\nShe pretended that nothing had happened.\n(她假裝什麼事都沒發生。)"],["prevent","prevent(v.)預防、阻止\nprevention(n.)預防\npreventive(adj.)預防的\nprevent... from 阻止⋯做\nprevent disease 預防疾病\nWashing your hands can prevent colds.\n(洗手可以預防感冒。)\nThe heavy rain prevented us from going out.\n(大雨讓我們無法出門。)"],["previous","previous(adj.)先前的、以前的\npreviously(adv.)先前\nprevious day 前一天\nprevious experience 先前的經驗\nDo you have any previous work experience?\n(你有任何先前的工作經驗嗎？)\nI met him the previous day.\n(我前一天遇見了他。)"],["probable","probable(adj.)很可能的\nprobably(adv.)大概\nprobability(n.)可能性\nhighly probable 極有可能的\nprobable cause 可能的原因\nIt is probable that it will rain tomorrow.\n(明天很可能會下雨。)\nWhat is the most probable reason for the delay?\n(延誤最可能的原因是什麼？)"],["process","process(n./v.)過程、程序、處理、加工\nprocessor(n.)處理器\nin the process of 在⋯過程中\nprocessed food 加工食品\nLearning is a slow process.\n(學習是一個緩慢的過程。)\nTry to eat less processed food.\n(試著少吃加工食品。)"],["producer","producer(n.)生產者、製作人\nproduce(v.)生產\nproduct(n.)產品\nfilm producer 電影製片人\nmajor producer 主要生產者\nBrazil is a major producer of coffee.\n(巴西是咖啡的主要生產國。)\nThe producer of this movie won an award.\n(這部電影的製片人得了獎。)"],["product","product(n.)產品、成果\nproduce(v.)生產\nproduction(n.)生產\nproductive(adj.)有生產力的\nnew product 新產品\ndairy products 乳製品\nThe company will launch a new product next month.\n(那家公司下個月將推出新產品。)\nMilk and cheese are dairy products.\n(牛奶和起司是乳製品。)"],["professor","professor(n.)教授\n(無詞性變化)\ncollege professor 大學教授\nprofessor of history 歷史教授\nMy aunt is a professor at National Taiwan University.\n(我阿姨是台大的教授。)\nThe professor answered our questions patiently.\n(教授耐心地回答我們的問題。)"],["profit","profit(n./v.)利潤、獲利、得益\nprofitable(adj.)有利潤的\nmake a profit 獲利\nprofit from 從⋯中得益\nThe shop made a big profit this year.\n(這家店今年賺了很多錢。)\nYou can profit from reading good books.\n(閱讀好書能讓你獲益。)"],["promote","promote(v.)促進、推廣、使升職\npromotion(n.)升遷、促銷\npromote health 促進健康\nbe promoted to 被升為\nThe campaign promotes healthy eating.\n(這項活動推廣健康飲食。)\nShe was promoted to manager last year.\n(她去年被升為經理。)"],["pronounce","pronounce(v.)發音、宣布\npronunciation(n.)發音\npronounce a word 唸一個字\nhard to pronounce 難發音\nHow do you pronounce this word?\n(這個字怎麼發音？)\nSome English names are hard to pronounce.\n(有些英文名字很難發音。)"],["proof","proof(n.)證據、證明\nprove(v.)證明\nproof of 證明⋯\nwaterproof 防水的\nDo you have any proof that he took it?\n(你有任何證據證明是他拿的嗎？)\nPlease bring proof of your age.\n(請攜帶年齡證明。)"],["property","property(n.)財產、房地產、特性\n(無詞性變化)\nprivate property 私人財產\npublic property 公共財產\nThis land is private property.\n(這塊地是私人產業。)\nPlease take care of public property.\n(請愛護公物。)"],["protection","protection(n.)保護\nprotect(v.)保護\nprotective(adj.)保護的\nenvironmental protection 環境保護\nprotection from 免於⋯的保護\nSunscreen gives protection from the sun.\n(防曬乳能防止陽光曬傷。)\nEnvironmental protection is everyone's job.\n(環境保護是每個人的責任。)"],["pub","pub(n.)酒吧、酒館\n(無詞性變化)\ngo to the pub 去酒吧\nlocal pub 當地酒館\nThey watched the soccer game at a pub.\n(他們在酒吧看足球賽。)\nThe old pub is popular with tourists.\n(那家老酒館很受觀光客歡迎。)"],["pump","pump(n./v.)幫浦、抽水機、打氣\n(無詞性變化)\nbicycle pump 打氣筒\npump up 打氣\nI used a pump to fill my bike tires.\n(我用打氣筒幫腳踏車輪胎打氣。)\nThe heart pumps blood around the body.\n(心臟把血液輸送到全身。)"],["punch","punch(n./v.)拳打、打孔、水果酒\n(無詞性變化)\npunch in the face 打臉一拳\nfruit punch 水果調酒\nHe punched the bag hard in the gym.\n(他在健身房用力打沙包。)\nThe fruit punch at the party was delicious.\n(派對上的水果潘趣酒很好喝。)"],["puppet","puppet(n.)木偶、傀儡\n(無詞性變化)\npuppet show 木偶戲\nhand puppet 手偶\nGlove puppet shows are a traditional art in Taiwan.\n(布袋戲是台灣的傳統藝術。)\nThe government was just a puppet of the army.\n(那個政府只是軍方的傀儡。)"],["pure","pure(adj.)純粹的、純淨的\npurity(n.)純淨\npurely(adv.)純粹地\npure water 純淨的水\nby pure chance 純屬巧合\nThe air in the mountains is pure.\n(山上的空氣很純淨。)\nWe met by pure chance.\n(我們純屬巧合碰面。)"],["purse","purse(n.)錢包、手提包\n(無詞性變化)\ncoin purse 零錢包\nleather purse 皮製錢包\nShe took some money out of her purse.\n(她從錢包裡拿出一些錢。)\nI lost my purse on the bus.\n(我在公車上掉了錢包。)"],["queer","queer(adj.)奇怪的、古怪的、酷兒的\n(無詞性變化)\na queer feeling 奇怪的感覺\nqueer behavior 古怪的行為\nI had a queer feeling that someone was watching me.\n(我有一種奇怪的感覺，好像有人在看我。)\nThe old man's queer behavior worried his neighbors.\n(那位老人古怪的舉動讓鄰居很擔心。)"],["quit","quit(v.)停止、放棄、辭職\n(無詞性變化)\nquit smoking 戒菸\nquit one's job 辭職\nHe quit smoking for his health.\n(為了健康，他戒菸了。)\nShe quit her job to travel the world.\n(她辭職去環遊世界。)"],["quote","quote(v./n.)引用、引述、報價、引文\nquotation(n.)引文、報價\nquote from 引自\nfamous quote 名言\nShe likes to quote famous people in her essays.\n(她喜歡在作文中引用名人的話。)\nThe garage gave us a quote for the repair.\n(修車廠給了我們修理費的報價。)"],["racial","racial(adj.)種族的\nrace(n.)種族、賽跑\nracism(n.)種族歧視\nracial discrimination 種族歧視\nracial equality 種族平等\nRacial discrimination should not be allowed in any school.\n(任何學校都不應容許種族歧視。)\nMartin Luther King Jr. fought for racial equality in America.\n(馬丁‧路德‧金恩為美國的種族平等奮鬥。)"],["rag","rag(n.)破布、抹布\nragged(adj.)破爛的\nin rags 衣衫襤褸\nfrom rags to riches 從貧窮到致富\nShe wiped the dirty table with an old rag.\n(她用一條舊抹布擦髒桌子。)\nHis life story is a true tale of rags to riches.\n(他的人生故事是一個白手起家的真實例子。)"],["rank","rank(n./v.)等級、階級、排名\nranking(n.)排名\nrank first 排名第一\nhigh rank 高階級\nOur school ranks first in the city basketball league.\n(我們學校在全市籃球聯賽中排名第一。)\nHe was promoted to a higher rank in the army.\n(他在軍中晉升到更高的軍階。)"],["rate","rate(n./v.)比率、速度、費用、評價\nrating(n.)評分、等級\nbirth rate 出生率\nat any rate 無論如何\nTaiwan's birth rate has dropped in recent years.\n(台灣的出生率近年來下降了。)\nMany viewers rated the new drama very highly.\n(許多觀眾給這部新劇很高的評價。)"],["raw","raw(adj.)生的、未加工的\n(無詞性變化)\nraw fish 生魚\nraw materials 原料\nSome people do not like to eat raw fish.\n(有些人不喜歡吃生魚。)\nThe factory imports raw materials from other countries.\n(那間工廠從其他國家進口原料。)"],["ray","ray(n.)光線、射線\n(無詞性變化)\nrays of sunlight 陽光\nget an X-ray 照X光\nThe first rays of sunlight came through the window.\n(第一道陽光透過窗戶照進來。)\nThe doctor asked me to take an X-ray of my arm.\n(醫生要我的手臂照X光。)"],["razor","razor(n.)剃刀、刮鬍刀\n(無詞性變化)\nelectric razor 電動刮鬍刀\nrazor blade 刮鬍刀片\nMy father uses an electric razor every morning.\n(我爸爸每天早上用電動刮鬍刀。)\nBe careful, the razor blade is very sharp.\n(小心，這個刮鬍刀片非常鋒利。)"],["react","react(v.)反應、回應\nreaction(n.)反應\nreactor(n.)反應爐\nreact to 對……做出反應\nreact quickly 迅速反應\nHow did your parents react to the news?\n(你父母對這個消息有什麼反應？)\nThe driver reacted quickly and avoided the accident.\n(司機迅速反應，避開了車禍。)"],["reaction","reaction(n.)反應\nreact(v.)反應、回應\nchemical reaction 化學反應\nreaction to 對……的反應\nFire is the result of a chemical reaction.\n(火是化學反應的結果。)\nHer first reaction to the gift was surprise.\n(她對這份禮物的第一個反應是驚訝。)"],["reasonable","reasonable(adj.)合理的、講理的、價格公道的\nreason(n.)理由、理性\nreasonably(adv.)合理地、相當\nreasonable price 合理的價格\nreasonable request 合理的要求\nThe restaurant serves good food at reasonable prices.\n(那家餐廳以合理的價格提供美味的食物。)\nIt is reasonable to ask for more time to finish the project.\n(要求更多時間完成這項專題是合理的。)"],["receipt","receipt(n.)收據、收到\nreceive(v.)收到\nkeep the receipt 保留收據\non receipt of 一收到……就\nPlease keep the receipt in case you want to return it.\n(請保留收據，以防你想退貨。)\nTaiwanese people often check their receipts for the lottery.\n(台灣人常常對發票看有沒有中獎。)"],["receiver","receiver(n.)接收者、聽筒、接收器\nreceive(v.)收到\npick up the receiver 拿起聽筒\nthe receiver of 收件人\nShe picked up the receiver and said hello.\n(她拿起聽筒說聲哈囉。)\nThe receiver of the letter must sign for it.\n(收件人必須簽收這封信。)"],["recognize","recognize(v.)認出、承認、認可\nrecognition(n.)認出、認可\nrecognizable(adj.)可辨認的\nrecognize someone 認出某人\nbe recognized as 被公認為\nI didn't recognize you with your new haircut.\n(你剪了新髮型，我都認不出你了。)\nShe is recognized as one of the best writers in Taiwan.\n(她被公認為台灣最優秀的作家之一。)"],["recorder","recorder(n.)錄音機、記錄器、直笛\nrecord(v./n.)記錄、紀錄\nrecording(n.)錄音、錄影\nvoice recorder 錄音筆\nplay the recorder 吹直笛\nThe reporter used a voice recorder during the interview.\n(記者在訪問時使用錄音筆。)\nMost students in Taiwan learn to play the recorder in elementary school.\n(台灣大部分學生在國小學吹直笛。)"],["rectangle","rectangle(n.)長方形、矩形\nrectangular(adj.)長方形的\ndraw a rectangle 畫長方形\narea of a rectangle 長方形的面積\nPlease draw a rectangle on the board.\n(請在黑板上畫一個長方形。)\nWe learned how to find the area of a rectangle.\n(我們學了如何求長方形的面積。)"],["reduce","reduce(v.)減少、降低\nreduction(n.)減少、降低\nreduce waste 減少浪費\nreduce the risk 降低風險\nWe should reduce plastic waste to protect the ocean.\n(我們應該減少塑膠垃圾以保護海洋。)\nRegular exercise can reduce the risk of heart disease.\n(規律運動可以降低心臟病的風險。)"],["regional","regional(adj.)地區的、區域的\nregion(n.)地區、區域\nregional food 地方特色料理\nregional differences 地區差異\nEvery county in Taiwan has its own regional food.\n(台灣每個縣市都有自己的地方特色料理。)\nThere are regional differences in the way people speak.\n(人們說話的方式有地區上的差異。)"],["regret","regret(v./n.)後悔、遺憾\nregretful(adj.)後悔的\nregrettable(adj.)令人遺憾的\nregret doing 後悔做了……\nhave no regrets 不後悔\nI regret not studying harder for the exam.\n(我後悔沒有更用功準備考試。)\nShe has no regrets about choosing this school.\n(她對選擇這所學校一點也不後悔。)"],["relax","relax(v.)放鬆、休息\nrelaxation(n.)放鬆、休閒\nrelaxed(adj.)放鬆的\nrelaxing(adj.)令人放鬆的\nrelax and enjoy 放鬆享受\nfeel relaxed 感到放鬆\nTake a deep breath and try to relax before the speech.\n(演講前深呼吸，試著放輕鬆。)\nListening to soft music helps me relax after school.\n(聽輕柔的音樂幫助我在放學後放鬆。)"],["release","release(n./v.)釋放、發行、發布\n(無詞性變化)\nrelease a new album 發行新專輯\npress release 新聞稿\nThe singer will release a new album next month.\n(那位歌手下個月將發行新專輯。)\nThe injured bird was released after it got better.\n(那隻受傷的鳥康復後被放生了。)"],["reliable","reliable(adj.)可靠的、可信賴的\nrely(v.)依賴、信賴\nreliability(n.)可靠性\nreliable source 可靠的來源\nreliable friend 可靠的朋友\nMake sure your information comes from a reliable source.\n(要確定你的資訊來自可靠的來源。)\nThis old car is still very reliable.\n(這輛舊車仍然非常可靠。)"],["relief","relief(n.)放心、緩解、救濟\nrelieve(v.)減輕、緩和\nrelieved(adj.)放心的\nto one's relief 令某人鬆一口氣的是\npain relief 止痛\nTo my relief, everyone arrived home safely.\n(令我鬆一口氣的是，大家都平安到家了。)\nThe government sent food and water as relief for the flood victims.\n(政府送去食物和飲水救濟水災災民。)"],["religious","religious(adj.)宗教的、虔誠的\nreligion(n.)宗教\nreligious belief 宗教信仰\nreligious festival 宗教節慶\nMazu's birthday is an important religious festival in Taiwan.\n(媽祖誕辰是台灣重要的宗教節慶。)\nPeople should respect each other's religious beliefs.\n(人們應該尊重彼此的宗教信仰。)"],["rely","rely(v.)依賴、信賴\nreliable(adj.)可靠的\nreliance(n.)依賴\nrely on 依賴、信賴\ncan rely on 可以信賴\nYou can always rely on me when you need help.\n(你需要幫忙時隨時可以信賴我。)\nMany students rely too much on their cell phones.\n(許多學生太過依賴手機。)"],["remain","remain(v.)保持、仍然是、留下\nremains(n.)遺跡、剩餘物\nremaining(adj.)剩下的\nremain silent 保持沉默\nremain calm 保持冷靜\nPlease remain calm during the earthquake.\n(地震時請保持冷靜。)\nOnly a few cookies remained after the party.\n(派對後只剩下幾片餅乾。)"],["remind","remind(v.)提醒、使想起\nreminder(n.)提醒物、提示\nremind A of B 使A想起B\nremind A to do 提醒A做某事\nPlease remind me to bring my textbook tomorrow.\n(請提醒我明天要帶課本。)\nThis song reminds me of my childhood.\n(這首歌讓我想起我的童年。)"],["remote","remote(adj.)遙遠的、偏僻的、遠端的\nremotely(adv.)遙遠地、遠端地\nremote control 遙控器\nremote area 偏遠地區\nCan you pass me the remote control?\n(你可以把遙控器遞給我嗎？)\nSome volunteers teach children in remote areas.\n(有些志工在偏遠地區教小朋友。)"],["replace(ment)","replace(v.)取代、替換、replacement(n.)替換、替代品\n(無詞性變化)\nreplace A with B 用B取代A\nfind a replacement 找人接替\nWe need to replace the old light bulb with a new one.\n(我們需要把舊燈泡換成新的。)\nThe coach is looking for a replacement for the injured player.\n(教練正在找受傷球員的替補人選。)"],["represent","represent(v.)代表、象徵、表示\nrepresentative(n./adj.)代表、代表性的\nrepresentation(n.)代表、表現\nrepresent the school 代表學校\nrepresent peace 象徵和平\nShe will represent our school in the speech contest.\n(她將代表我們學校參加演講比賽。)\nThe white dove represents peace.\n(白鴿象徵和平。)"],["representative","representative(adj./n.)代表性的、代表\nrepresent(v.)代表\nclass representative 班代\nsales representative 業務代表\nOur class representative will attend the student meeting.\n(我們的班代將出席學生會議。)\nThis painting is representative of his early works.\n(這幅畫可以代表他早期的作品。)"],["republic","republic(n.)共和國\nrepublican(adj./n.)共和國的、共和主義者\nRepublic of China 中華民國\ndemocratic republic 民主共和國\nThe Republic of China was founded in 1912.\n(中華民國成立於一九一二年。)\nFrance is a republic, not a kingdom.\n(法國是共和國，不是王國。)"],["request","request(n./v.)請求、要求\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a request 提出請求\non request 應要求\nThe teacher agreed to our request for more time.\n(老師答應了我們延長時間的請求。)\nVisitors are requested to turn off their phones.\n(參觀者請關閉手機。)"],["reserve","reserve(n./v.)預訂、保留、儲備\nreservation(n.)預訂\nreserved(adj.)預訂的、內向的\nreserve a table 訂位\nnature reserve 自然保護區\nWe reserved a table for six at the restaurant.\n(我們在餐廳訂了六人的位子。)\nThis seat is reserved for the elderly.\n(這個座位是保留給年長者的。)"],["resist","resist(v.)抵抗、抗拒、忍住\nresistance(n.)抵抗\nresistant(adj.)有抵抗力的\nresist temptation 抵抗誘惑\ncan't resist 忍不住\nI can't resist eating chocolate when I see it.\n(我看到巧克力就忍不住要吃。)\nThe village people resisted the enemy for many days.\n(村民抵抗敵人好幾天。)"],["resource","resource(n.)資源\nresourceful(adj.)足智多謀的\nnatural resources 天然資源\nhuman resources 人力資源\nTaiwan does not have many natural resources.\n(台灣沒有很多天然資源。)\nThe library is a great resource for students.\n(圖書館對學生來說是很好的資源。)"],["response","response(n.)回應、反應、答覆\nrespond(v.)回應、回答\nresponsive(adj.)反應靈敏的\nin response to 回應……\nquick response 快速回應\nIn response to the heavy rain, schools were closed.\n(因應豪大雨，學校停課了。)\nI sent an email but got no response.\n(我寄了電子郵件，但沒有收到回覆。)"],["responsibility","responsibility(n.)責任、職責\nresponsible(adj.)負責的\ntake responsibility for 為……負責\nsense of responsibility 責任感\nYou must take responsibility for your own actions.\n(你必須為自己的行為負責。)\nTaking care of a pet teaches children a sense of responsibility.\n(照顧寵物能教導孩子責任感。)"],["restrict","restrict(v.)限制、約束\nrestriction(n.)限制\nrestricted(adj.)受限制的\nrestrict to 限制在……\nrestricted area 管制區\nThe use of phones is restricted during class.\n(上課期間限制使用手機。)\nVisitors are not allowed in the restricted area.\n(訪客不准進入管制區。)"],["reveal","reveal(v.)揭露、透露、顯示\nrevelation(n.)揭露、啟示\nreveal a secret 洩漏秘密\nreveal the truth 揭露真相\nShe refused to reveal the secret to anyone.\n(她拒絕向任何人透露這個秘密。)\nThe report revealed that many teens do not get enough sleep.\n(報告顯示許多青少年睡眠不足。)"],["ribbon","ribbon(n.)緞帶、絲帶\n(無詞性變化)\ntie a ribbon 繫緞帶\ncut the ribbon 剪綵\nShe tied a red ribbon around the gift box.\n(她在禮物盒上繫了一條紅色緞帶。)\nThe mayor cut the ribbon at the opening of the new library.\n(市長在新圖書館開幕時剪綵。)"],["rid","rid(adj./v.)擺脫的、使擺脫、除去\n(無詞性變化)\nget rid of 擺脫、丟掉\nbe rid of 擺脫\nI want to get rid of my bad habit of staying up late.\n(我想改掉熬夜的壞習慣。)\nWe finally got rid of all the old furniture.\n(我們終於把所有舊家具處理掉了。)"],["ripe","ripe(adj.)成熟的\nripen(v.)使成熟、變成熟\nripe fruit 成熟的水果\nripe old age 高齡\nThese bananas are not ripe yet.\n(這些香蕉還沒熟。)\nMy great-grandmother lived to a ripe old age of 98.\n(我曾祖母活到九十八歲的高齡。)"],["risk","risk(n./v.)風險、冒險\nrisky(adj.)有風險的\ntake a risk 冒險\nat risk 有危險\nHe took a big risk by starting his own business.\n(他自己創業冒了很大的風險。)\nSmoking puts your health at risk.\n(抽菸會讓你的健康陷入危險。)"],["roar","roar(n./v.)吼叫、咆哮、轟鳴\n(無詞性變化)\nroar of laughter 哄堂大笑\nroar of the engine 引擎的轟鳴聲\nThe lion roared loudly in its cage.\n(獅子在籠子裡大聲吼叫。)\nHis joke was followed by a roar of laughter.\n(他的笑話引起一陣哄堂大笑。)"],["roast","roast(adj./n./v.)烤的、烤肉、烘烤\n(無詞性變化)\nroast chicken 烤雞\nroast duck 烤鴨\nWe had roast chicken for dinner on Christmas.\n(我們聖誕節晚餐吃烤雞。)\nMy father roasts sweet potatoes in the oven.\n(我爸爸用烤箱烤地瓜。)"],["rob","rob(v.)搶劫、剝奪\nrobber(n.)強盜、搶匪\nrobbery(n.)搶劫\nrob a bank 搶銀行\nrob A of B 搶走A的B\nTwo men robbed the bank last night.\n(兩名男子昨晚搶劫了那家銀行。)\nThe thief robbed the old woman of her purse.\n(小偷搶走那位老婦人的錢包。)"],["robbery","robbery(n.)搶劫、搶案\nrob(v.)搶劫\nrobber(n.)強盜、搶匪\narmed robbery 持械搶劫\nbank robbery 銀行搶案\nThe police are looking into the bank robbery.\n(警方正在調查那起銀行搶案。)\nThe store was the scene of an armed robbery.\n(這家店發生過一起持械搶劫案。)"],["robe","robe(n.)長袍、浴袍\n(無詞性變化)\nbathrobe 浴袍\ngraduation robe 畢業袍\nShe put on a robe after taking a shower.\n(她洗完澡後穿上浴袍。)\nAll the graduates wore black graduation robes.\n(所有畢業生都穿著黑色的畢業袍。)"],["rocket","rocket(n.)火箭\n(無詞性變化)\nlaunch a rocket 發射火箭\nrocket science 高深的學問\nThe rocket was launched into space this morning.\n(火箭今天早上發射升空。)\nDon't worry, cooking pasta isn't rocket science.\n(別擔心，煮義大利麵又不是什麼高深的學問。)"],["romantic","romantic(adj./n.)浪漫的、浪漫的人\nromance(n.)愛情、浪漫\nromantic dinner 浪漫晚餐\nromantic comedy 浪漫喜劇\nThey had a romantic dinner by the sea.\n(他們在海邊享用浪漫的晚餐。)\nMy sister loves watching romantic comedies.\n(我姊姊很愛看浪漫喜劇。)"],["rot","rot(v./n.)腐爛、腐壞\nrotten(adj.)腐爛的\nrot away 爛掉\nstart to rot 開始腐爛\nThe apples began to rot after a week in the hot room.\n(蘋果在悶熱的房間裡放了一週後開始腐爛。)\nToo much sugar can cause your teeth to rot.\n(吃太多糖可能導致蛀牙。)"],["rotten","rotten(adj.)腐爛的、糟糕的\nrot(v./n.)腐爛\nrotten egg 臭雞蛋\nfeel rotten 感覺很糟\nThe kitchen smelled like rotten eggs.\n(廚房聞起來像臭雞蛋。)\nI felt rotten after eating too much fried food.\n(吃了太多油炸食物後我覺得很不舒服。)"],["rough","rough(adj./adv./n.)粗糙的、粗略的、艱難的\nroughly(adv.)大約、粗暴地\nrough idea 大概的想法\nrough day 辛苦的一天\nI had a rough day at school today.\n(我今天在學校過得很辛苦。)\nHis hands are rough from years of farm work.\n(他的雙手因多年務農而粗糙。)"],["roughly","roughly(adv.)大約、粗略地、粗暴地\nrough(adj.)粗糙的、粗略的\nroughly speaking 大致說來\nroughly half 大約一半\nRoughly half of the students take the bus to school.\n(大約一半的學生搭公車上學。)\nRoughly speaking, the trip will take three hours.\n(大致說來，這趟旅程要花三個小時。)"],["routine","routine(n./adj.)例行公事、慣例、例行的\nroutinely(adv.)例行地\ndaily routine 日常作息\nroutine check 例行檢查\nExercise is part of my daily routine.\n(運動是我日常作息的一部分。)\nThe doctor gave me a routine check.\n(醫生幫我做了例行檢查。)"],["rug","rug(n.)小地毯\n(無詞性變化)\nsweep under the rug 掩蓋\nsoft rug 柔軟的地毯\nThe cat is sleeping on the rug by the fire.\n(貓咪睡在爐火旁的地毯上。)\nDon't sweep your problems under the rug.\n(不要把你的問題掩蓋起來。)"],["rumor","rumor(n./v.)謠言、傳聞、謠傳\nrumour(n.)謠言(英式拼法)\nspread a rumor 散播謠言\nrumor has it that 謠傳……\nSomeone spread a rumor that our teacher was leaving.\n(有人散播謠言說我們老師要離職了。)\nRumor has it that the singer will visit Taiwan.\n(謠傳那位歌手將來台灣。)"],["rush","rush(n./v.)匆忙、急速、衝\n(無詞性變化)\nrush hour 尖峰時間\nin a rush 匆忙地\nThe MRT is very crowded during rush hour.\n(捷運在尖峰時間非常擁擠。)\nHe rushed to the hospital after hearing the news.\n(他聽到消息後趕到醫院。)"],["rust","rust(n./v.)鐵鏽、生鏽\nrusty(adj.)生鏽的、生疏的\ncovered in rust 布滿鐵鏽\nrusty English 生疏的英文\nThe old bike was covered in rust.\n(那台舊腳踏車布滿鐵鏽。)\nIron will rust if you leave it out in the rain.\n(鐵如果放在外面淋雨就會生鏽。)"],["sack","sack(n.)大袋子、麻袋\n(無詞性變化)\na sack of rice 一袋米\nget the sack 被開除\nThe farmer carried a heavy sack of rice on his back.\n(農夫背著一大袋沉重的米。)\nHe got the sack for being late too often.\n(他因為太常遲到而被開除了。)"],["sake","sake(n.)緣故、利益\n(無詞性變化)\nfor the sake of 為了……\nfor one's own sake 為了某人自己好\nShe quit smoking for the sake of her children.\n(她為了孩子而戒菸。)\nPlease get some rest for your own sake.\n(為了你自己好，請休息一下。)"],["salary","salary(n.)薪水、薪資\nsalaried(adj.)領薪水的\nmonthly salary 月薪\nraise one's salary 加薪\nHis monthly salary is enough to support his family.\n(他的月薪足夠養家。)\nThe company decided to raise everyone's salary this year.\n(公司決定今年替每個人加薪。)"],["satisfactory","satisfactory(adj.)令人滿意的、符合要求的\nsatisfy(v.)使滿意\nsatisfaction(n.)滿意\nsatisfactory result 令人滿意的結果\nsatisfactory answer 滿意的答覆\nThe test results were satisfactory.\n(考試結果令人滿意。)\nHe could not give a satisfactory answer to the question.\n(他無法對這個問題給出令人滿意的答覆。)"],["sauce","sauce(n.)醬汁、調味醬\nsaucer(n.)茶碟、淺碟\nsoy sauce 醬油\ntomato sauce 番茄醬汁\nAdd a little soy sauce to the fried rice.\n(在炒飯裡加一點醬油。)\nThe pasta tastes better with fresh tomato sauce.\n(義大利麵配上新鮮番茄醬汁更好吃。)"],["saucer","saucer(n.)茶碟、淺碟\nsauce(n.)醬汁\ncup and saucer 一套杯碟\nflying saucer 飛碟\nShe placed the cup carefully on the saucer.\n(她小心地把杯子放在茶碟上。)\nThe boy claimed he saw a flying saucer in the sky.\n(那個男孩聲稱他在天空看到了飛碟。)"],["sausage","sausage(n.)香腸、臘腸\n(無詞性變化)\ngrilled sausage 烤香腸\nsausage roll 香腸捲\nGrilled sausage is a popular snack at Taiwan's night markets.\n(烤香腸是台灣夜市受歡迎的小吃。)\nWe had eggs and sausages for breakfast.\n(我們早餐吃了蛋和香腸。)"],["saving(s)","saving(n.)節省、savings(n.)存款、積蓄\nsave(v.)節省、儲蓄、拯救\nsavings account 儲蓄帳戶\nlife savings 畢生積蓄\nShe spent all her savings on a trip to Japan.\n(她把所有的積蓄都花在日本之旅上。)\nTurning off the lights can make a big saving on electricity.\n(隨手關燈可以省下大量電費。)"],["scale(s)","scale(n.)規模、比例、刻度、scales(n.)秤、天平\n(無詞性變化)\non a large scale 大規模地\nbathroom scales 體重計\nThe company produces toys on a large scale.\n(那間公司大規模生產玩具。)\nShe stepped on the scales to check her weight.\n(她站上體重計量體重。)"],["scarce","scarce(adj.)稀少的、缺乏的\nscarcely(adv.)幾乎不\nscarcity(n.)缺乏、稀少\nscarce resources 稀少的資源\nwater is scarce 水資源缺乏\nWater becomes scarce in the dry season.\n(乾季時水變得很缺乏。)\nFood was scarce during the war.\n(戰爭期間糧食短缺。)"],["scarf","scarf(n.)圍巾、披巾\nscarves(n.)圍巾(複數)\nwool scarf 羊毛圍巾\nwear a scarf 圍圍巾\nShe wore a warm wool scarf on the cold day.\n(她在寒冷的日子圍著一條溫暖的羊毛圍巾。)\nMy grandmother knitted a scarf for me.\n(我奶奶替我織了一條圍巾。)"],["scary","scary(adj.)可怕的、嚇人的\nscare(v./n.)驚嚇、恐慌\nscared(adj.)害怕的\nscary movie 恐怖電影\nscary experience 可怕的經歷\nWe watched a scary movie last night and couldn't sleep.\n(我們昨晚看了一部恐怖片，結果睡不著。)\nBeing stuck in the elevator was a scary experience.\n(被困在電梯裡是一次可怕的經歷。)"],["scatter","scatter(v./n.)散布、撒、驅散\nscattered(adj.)分散的、零星的\nscatter seeds 撒種子\nscattered showers 零星陣雨\nThe farmer scattered seeds across the field.\n(農夫在田裡撒下種子。)\nToys were scattered all over the floor.\n(玩具散落了一地。)"],["scholar","scholar(n.)學者\nscholarship(n.)獎學金\nscholarly(adj.)學術的、博學的\nfamous scholar 知名學者\nChinese scholar 漢學家\nHe is a famous scholar of Chinese history.\n(他是一位知名的中國史學者。)\nMany scholars came to the conference to share their research.\n(許多學者來參加研討會分享研究。)"],["scholarship","scholarship(n.)獎學金\nscholar(n.)學者\nwin a scholarship 獲得獎學金\nfull scholarship 全額獎學金\nShe won a full scholarship to study in the US.\n(她獲得全額獎學金到美國留學。)\nGood grades can help you get a scholarship.\n(好成績可以幫助你獲得獎學金。)"],["scientific","scientific(adj.)科學的\nscience(n.)科學\nscientifically(adv.)科學地\nscientific research 科學研究\nscientific method 科學方法\nThe scientific method helps us find answers step by step.\n(科學方法幫助我們一步一步找到答案。)\nThere is no scientific evidence for the story.\n(這個說法沒有科學證據。)"],["scientist","scientist(n.)科學家\nscience(n.)科學\nscientific(adj.)科學的\ncomputer scientist 電腦科學家\nbecome a scientist 成為科學家\nMy little brother wants to become a scientist.\n(我弟弟想成為科學家。)\nScientists are working hard to find a cure for the disease.\n(科學家正努力尋找治療這種疾病的方法。)"],["scissors","scissors(n.)剪刀\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of scissors 一把剪刀\nsharp scissors 鋒利的剪刀\nCan I borrow your scissors to cut the paper?\n(我可以借你的剪刀剪紙嗎？)\nChildren should be careful when using sharp scissors.\n(小孩使用鋒利的剪刀時應該小心。)"],["scout","scout(n./v.)童子軍、偵察員、偵察\n(無詞性變化)\nboy scout 童子軍\ntalent scout 星探\nMy brother joined the scouts in junior high school.\n(我哥哥國中時參加了童子軍。)\nA talent scout noticed her singing in the park.\n(一位星探注意到她在公園唱歌。)"],["scream","scream(v./n.)尖叫、大叫\n(無詞性變化)\nscream for help 尖叫求救\nlet out a scream 發出一聲尖叫\nShe screamed when she saw a big spider.\n(她看到一隻大蜘蛛時尖叫起來。)\nWe heard someone scream for help outside.\n(我們聽到外面有人尖叫求救。)"],["screw","screw(v./n.)旋緊、用螺絲固定、螺絲\nscrewdriver(n.)螺絲起子\ntighten a screw 鎖緊螺絲\nscrew up 搞砸\nHe used a screwdriver to tighten the screws.\n(他用螺絲起子鎖緊螺絲。)\nI really screwed up my math test.\n(我數學考試真的考砸了。)"],["scrub","scrub(n./v.)刷洗、擦洗、灌木叢\n(無詞性變化)\nscrub the floor 刷地板\ngive a good scrub 好好刷洗\nWe scrubbed the classroom floor before the holiday.\n(我們在放假前把教室地板刷洗乾淨。)\nThe pot needs a good scrub.\n(這個鍋子需要好好刷洗。)"],["seal","seal(n./v.)海豹、封條、印章、密封\n(無詞性變化)\nseal the envelope 封好信封\nbaby seal 小海豹\nDon't forget to seal the envelope before mailing it.\n(寄出前別忘了把信封封好。)\nWe watched seals playing on the rocks.\n(我們看著海豹在岩石上玩耍。)"],["security","security(n.)安全、保全、保障\nsecure(adj./v.)安全的、確保\nsecurity guard 保全人員\nsecurity check 安全檢查\nAll passengers must go through a security check.\n(所有乘客都必須通過安全檢查。)\nThe building has twenty-four-hour security.\n(這棟大樓有二十四小時保全。)"],["semester","semester(n.)學期\n(無詞性變化)\nfall semester 上學期\nfinal exam of the semester 期末考\nThe new semester starts in September.\n(新學期在九月開始。)\nI plan to join the drama club this semester.\n(我打算這學期加入戲劇社。)"],["senior","senior(adj./n.)年長的、資深的、高年級生、長者\nseniority(n.)年資\nsenior high school 高中\nsenior citizen 年長者\nMy sister is a senior in high school.\n(我姊姊是高三學生。)\nSenior citizens can take the MRT at a lower price.\n(年長者可以用較低的價格搭捷運。)"],["sensible","sensible(adj.)明智的、合理的\nsense(n.)感覺、判斷力\nsensibly(adv.)明智地\nsensible decision 明智的決定\nsensible shoes 實用好走的鞋子\nIt was a sensible decision to bring an umbrella.\n(帶雨傘是個明智的決定。)\nWear sensible shoes for the long walk.\n(長途步行要穿好走的鞋子。)"],["separation","separation(n.)分開、分離\nseparate(v./adj.)分開、分開的\nseparately(adv.)分開地\nseparation from 與……分離\nseparation of powers 三權分立\nThe children cried at the separation from their parents.\n(孩子們和父母分開時哭了。)\nAfter years of separation, the two brothers finally met again.\n(分離多年後，兩兄弟終於重逢。)"],["sexual","sexual(adj.)性的、性別的\nsex(n.)性別、性\nsexuality(n.)性向、性慾\nsexual harassment 性騷擾\nsexual equality 性別平等\nOur school has clear rules against sexual harassment.\n(我們學校有反性騷擾的明確規定。)\nThe class discussed sexual equality in the workplace.\n(班上討論職場中的性別平等。)"],["sexy","sexy(adj.)性感的、迷人的\nsex(n.)性別、性\nsexy voice 性感的嗓音\nlook sexy 看起來性感\nThe singer is famous for her sexy voice.\n(那位歌手以性感的嗓音聞名。)\nSome people think fast cars are sexy.\n(有些人覺得跑車很有魅力。)"],["shadow","shadow(n./v.)影子、陰影、跟蹤\nshadowy(adj.)陰暗的、模糊的\nin the shadow of 在……的陰影下\ncast a shadow 投下陰影\nThe tall building casts a long shadow in the afternoon.\n(這棟高樓在下午投下長長的影子。)\nHe grew up in the shadow of his famous brother.\n(他在知名哥哥的光環下長大。)"],["shallow","shallow(adj.)淺的、膚淺的\n(無詞性變化)\nshallow water 淺水\nshallow person 膚淺的人\nChildren should swim in shallow water.\n(小孩應該在淺水區游泳。)\nIt is shallow to judge people only by their looks.\n(只憑外表評斷別人是很膚淺的。)"],["shampoo","shampoo(n./v.)洗髮精、洗頭\n(無詞性變化)\na bottle of shampoo 一瓶洗髮精\nshampoo and conditioner 洗髮精和潤髮乳\nI need to buy a new bottle of shampoo.\n(我需要買一瓶新的洗髮精。)\nShe shampoos her hair every night.\n(她每天晚上洗頭。)"],["shepherd","shepherd(n.)牧羊人\n(無詞性變化)\nGerman shepherd 德國牧羊犬\ngood shepherd 好牧人\nThe shepherd led his sheep across the hill.\n(牧羊人帶著羊群越過山丘。)\nOur neighbor keeps a German shepherd as a guard dog.\n(我們的鄰居養了一隻德國牧羊犬當看門狗。)"],["shiny","shiny(adj.)閃亮的、有光澤的\nshine(v./n.)發光、光澤\nshiny hair 有光澤的頭髮\nshiny new car 閃亮的新車\nHe drove a shiny new car to the party.\n(他開著一輛閃亮的新車去參加派對。)\nHer long hair is soft and shiny.\n(她的長髮柔順又有光澤。)"],["shorten","shorten(v.)縮短、變短\nshort(adj.)短的\nshortly(adv.)不久\nshorten the time 縮短時間\nshorten a skirt 改短裙子\nThe new bridge will shorten the travel time.\n(新的橋梁將縮短交通時間。)\nPlease shorten your speech to three minutes.\n(請把你的演講縮短到三分鐘。)"],["shortly","shortly(adv.)不久、立刻\nshort(adj.)短的\nshortly after 在……之後不久\nshortly before 在……之前不久\nThe train will arrive shortly.\n(火車很快就會到站。)\nShortly after the game started, it began to rain.\n(比賽開始後不久就下起雨了。)"],["shovel","shovel(n./v.)鏟子、用鏟子挖\n(無詞性變化)\nshovel snow 鏟雪\ndig with a shovel 用鏟子挖\nThey shoveled snow off the road in the morning.\n(他們早上把路上的雪鏟掉。)\nHe dug a hole in the garden with a shovel.\n(他用鏟子在花園挖了一個洞。)"],["shrimp","shrimp(n.)蝦子\n(無詞性變化)\nfried shrimp 炸蝦\nshrimp fried rice 蝦仁炒飯\nI ordered shrimp fried rice for dinner.\n(我晚餐點了蝦仁炒飯。)\nSome people are allergic to shrimp.\n(有些人對蝦子過敏。)"],["shrink","shrink(v.)縮小、縮水、退縮\nshrinkage(n.)收縮、縮水\nshrink in the wash 洗後縮水\nshrink from 逃避、退縮\nMy new sweater shrank in the wash.\n(我的新毛衣洗了之後縮水了。)\nThe number of farmers in the village continues to shrink.\n(村裡的農夫人數持續減少。)"],["sigh","sigh(n./v.)嘆氣、嘆息\n(無詞性變化)\nsigh of relief 鬆了一口氣\nsigh deeply 深深地嘆氣\nShe breathed a sigh of relief after the exam.\n(考完試後她鬆了一口氣。)\nHe sighed and looked out the window.\n(他嘆了一口氣，望向窗外。)"],["signal","signal(n./v.)信號、訊號、發信號\n(無詞性變化)\ntraffic signal 交通號誌\nno signal 沒有訊號\nThere is no phone signal in the mountains.\n(山裡沒有手機訊號。)\nThe coach signaled the players to stop.\n(教練示意球員停下來。)"],["significant","significant(adj.)重要的、顯著的、有意義的\nsignificance(n.)重要性、意義\nsignificantly(adv.)顯著地\nsignificant change 重大的改變\nsignificant role 重要的角色\nSocial media plays a significant role in teenagers' lives.\n(社群媒體在青少年的生活中扮演重要角色。)\nThere has been a significant increase in online shopping.\n(網路購物有顯著的增加。)"],["silk","silk(n.)絲、絲綢\nsilky(adj.)柔滑如絲的\nsilk scarf 絲巾\nSilk Road 絲路\nMy mother bought a silk scarf in Thailand.\n(我媽媽在泰國買了一條絲巾。)\nThe Silk Road connected China with Europe long ago.\n(很久以前，絲路連接了中國與歐洲。)"],["similarity","similarity(n.)相似、相似處\nsimilar(adj.)相似的\nsimilarly(adv.)同樣地\nsimilarity between ……之間的相似處\nbear a similarity to 與……相似\nThere are many similarities between the two languages.\n(這兩種語言之間有許多相似處。)\nThe twins bear a strong similarity to their father.\n(這對雙胞胎長得很像他們的父親。)"],["sin","sin(n./v.)罪、罪過、犯罪\nsinful(adj.)有罪的\nsinner(n.)罪人\ncommit a sin 犯罪\noriginal sin 原罪\nIn some religions, lying is considered a sin.\n(在某些宗教裡，說謊被視為一種罪。)\nIt's a sin to waste so much good food.\n(浪費這麼多好食物真是罪過。)"],["sincere","sincere(adj.)真誠的、誠摯的\nsincerely(adv.)真誠地、誠摯地\nsincerity(n.)真誠\nsincere apology 誠摯的道歉\nsincere thanks 由衷的感謝\nPlease accept my sincere apology.\n(請接受我誠摯的道歉。)\nShe gave him a sincere smile.\n(她給了他一個真誠的微笑。)"],["sink","sink(n./v.)水槽、洗手台、下沉\n(無詞性變化)\nkitchen sink 廚房水槽\nsink to the bottom 沉到底部\nPlease put the dirty dishes in the sink.\n(請把髒碗盤放進水槽。)\nThe ship hit a rock and began to sink.\n(那艘船撞上岩石，開始下沉。)"],["sip","sip(v./n.)啜飲、小口喝\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a sip 喝一小口\nsip tea 啜飲茶\nShe took a sip of hot tea and smiled.\n(她喝了一小口熱茶，露出微笑。)\nWe sat on the balcony sipping coffee.\n(我們坐在陽台上慢慢喝咖啡。)"],["situation","situation(n.)情況、處境、形勢\nsituated(adj.)位於……的\ndifficult situation 困境\nin this situation 在這種情況下\nWhat would you do in this situation?\n(在這種情況下你會怎麼做？)\nShe stayed calm in a difficult situation.\n(她在困境中保持冷靜。)"],["skate","skate(v./n.)溜冰、溜冰鞋\nskater(n.)溜冰者\nskating(n.)溜冰\nice skate 溜冰\nroller skates 直排輪鞋\nWe went ice skating at the mall last weekend.\n(上週末我們去購物中心溜冰。)\nShe skates very well for her age.\n(以她的年紀來說，她溜冰溜得很好。)"],["ski","ski(n./v.)滑雪板、滑雪\nskier(n.)滑雪者\nskiing(n.)滑雪\ngo skiing 去滑雪\nski resort 滑雪勝地\nWe plan to go skiing in Japan this winter.\n(我們計劃今年冬天去日本滑雪。)\nHe learned to ski when he was ten.\n(他十歲時學會滑雪。)"],["skillful","skillful(adj.)熟練的、有技巧的\nskill(n.)技能\nskillfully(adv.)熟練地\nskillful player 技術純熟的選手\nskillful at 擅長……\nHe is a skillful player on the basketball team.\n(他是籃球隊裡技術純熟的球員。)\nMy grandmother is skillful at making dumplings.\n(我奶奶很擅長包水餃。)"],["skinny","skinny(adj.)極瘦的、皮包骨的、緊身的\nskin(n.)皮膚\nskinny jeans 緊身牛仔褲\ntall and skinny 又高又瘦\nHe was tall and skinny when he was a teenager.\n(他青少年時又高又瘦。)\nSkinny jeans were very popular a few years ago.\n(緊身牛仔褲幾年前非常流行。)"],["skip","skip(v./n.)跳過、略過、蹺(課)、蹦跳\n(無詞性變化)\nskip class 蹺課\nskip breakfast 不吃早餐\nIt's not healthy to skip breakfast.\n(不吃早餐是不健康的。)\nIf you don't know the answer, skip the question.\n(如果你不知道答案，就跳過那一題。)"],["slave","slave(n./v.)奴隸、苦幹\nslavery(n.)奴隸制度\nslave trade 奴隸買賣\nslave to 受……支配的人\nAbraham Lincoln worked to free the slaves.\n(林肯致力於解放奴隸。)\nDon't become a slave to your cell phone.\n(不要被你的手機給綁架了。)"],["sleeve","sleeve(n.)袖子\nsleeveless(adj.)無袖的\nlong sleeves 長袖\nroll up one's sleeves 捲起袖子、準備大幹一場\nIt's cold today, so wear a shirt with long sleeves.\n(今天很冷，穿件長袖襯衫吧。)\nLet's roll up our sleeves and clean the classroom.\n(我們捲起袖子來打掃教室吧。)"],["slender","slender(adj.)苗條的、纖細的\n(無詞性變化)\nslender figure 苗條的身材\nslender fingers 纖細的手指\nThe dancer has a tall, slender figure.\n(那位舞者身材高挑苗條。)\nShe played the piano with her long, slender fingers.\n(她用修長纖細的手指彈鋼琴。)"],["slice","slice(n./v.)薄片、一片、切片\n(無詞性變化)\na slice of bread 一片麵包\nslice the cake 切蛋糕\nI had a slice of bread and a cup of milk for breakfast.\n(我早餐吃了一片麵包和一杯牛奶。)\nMy mother sliced the cake into eight pieces.\n(我媽媽把蛋糕切成八塊。)"],["slippery","slippery(adj.)滑的、易滑的\nslip(v./n.)滑倒、滑\nslippery floor 滑溜的地板\nslippery road 濕滑的路面\nBe careful, the floor is slippery after cleaning.\n(小心，地板剛拖過很滑。)\nThe roads are slippery on rainy days.\n(雨天路面很濕滑。)"],["slope","slope(n.)斜坡、坡度\nsloping(adj.)傾斜的\nsteep slope 陡坡\nski slope 滑雪坡道\nThe house was built on a steep slope.\n(那棟房子蓋在陡坡上。)\nThe children ran down the grassy slope.\n(孩子們跑下長滿青草的斜坡。)"],["snap","snap(v./n.)啪地折斷、猛咬、厲聲說、快照\n(無詞性變化)\nsnap one's fingers 彈手指\nsnap at 厲聲責罵\nThe branch snapped under his weight.\n(樹枝被他的體重壓得啪一聲斷了。)\nI'm sorry I snapped at you this morning.\n(很抱歉我今天早上對你大聲說話。)"],["solid","solid(adj.)固體的、堅固的、可靠的\nsolidly(adv.)堅固地\nsolid food 固體食物\nsolid evidence 確鑿的證據\nIce is water in a solid state.\n(冰是固態的水。)\nThe police have solid evidence against the man.\n(警方握有那名男子的確鑿證據。)"],["someday","someday(adv.)總有一天、將來某天\n(無詞性變化)\nsomeday soon 不久的某天\nhope to someday 希望有一天\nSomeday I want to travel around the world.\n(總有一天我想環遊世界。)\nI hope we can meet again someday.\n(我希望有一天我們能再見面。)"],["somehow","somehow(adv.)以某種方式、不知怎麼地\n(無詞性變化)\nsomehow manage 設法做到\nsomehow or other 不知怎麼地\nSomehow, we finished the project on time.\n(不知怎麼地，我們準時完成了專題。)\nSomehow I feel that something is wrong.\n(不知為什麼，我覺得有些不對勁。)"],["sometime","sometime(adv.)某個時候\n(無詞性變化)\nsometime next week 下週某個時候\nsometime soon 近期某時\nLet's have lunch together sometime next week.\n(我們下週找個時間一起吃午餐吧。)\nThe package will arrive sometime this afternoon.\n(包裹會在今天下午某個時候送到。)"],["sorrow","sorrow(n.)悲傷、哀痛\nsorrowful(adj.)悲傷的\ndeep sorrow 深深的悲傷\nto one's sorrow 令某人難過的是\nShe felt deep sorrow when her dog died.\n(她的狗死去時她感到非常悲傷。)\nThe song is about love and sorrow.\n(這首歌是關於愛與哀愁。)"],["spaghetti","spaghetti(n.)義大利麵\n(無詞性變化)\nspaghetti with meatballs 肉丸義大利麵\ncook spaghetti 煮義大利麵\nWe had spaghetti with tomato sauce for dinner.\n(我們晚餐吃了番茄醬汁義大利麵。)\nIt only takes ten minutes to cook spaghetti.\n(煮義大利麵只需要十分鐘。)"],["specific","specific(adj.)明確的、具體的、特定的\nspecifically(adv.)明確地、特別地\nspecify(v.)具體說明\nspecific example 具體的例子\nspecific purpose 特定目的\nCan you give me a specific example?\n(你可以給我一個具體的例子嗎？)\nThe money is for a specific purpose.\n(這筆錢有特定用途。)"],["spice","spice(n./v.)香料、調味料、增添趣味\nspicy(adj.)辛辣的\nspice up 增添趣味\nherbs and spices 香草和香料\nIndian food uses a lot of spices.\n(印度料理使用大量香料。)\nA little music can spice up the party.\n(一點音樂可以讓派對更熱鬧。)"],["spill","spill(v./n.)灑出、溢出\n(無詞性變化)\nspill coffee 灑出咖啡\noil spill 漏油事件\nI accidentally spilled coffee on my homework.\n(我不小心把咖啡灑在作業上。)\nThe oil spill killed many sea birds.\n(漏油事件造成許多海鳥死亡。)"],["spin","spin(n./v.)旋轉、紡紗\n(無詞性變化)\nspin around 轉來轉去\ngo for a spin 開車兜風\nThe dancer spun around on one foot.\n(那位舞者單腳旋轉。)\nMy head is spinning after the long test.\n(長時間考試後我的頭昏腦脹。)"],["spinach","spinach(n.)菠菜\n(無詞性變化)\nfresh spinach 新鮮菠菜\nspinach salad 菠菜沙拉\nPopeye eats spinach to become strong.\n(大力水手吃菠菜變強壯。)\nMy mom cooks spinach with garlic.\n(我媽媽用蒜頭炒菠菜。)"],["spit","spit(v./n.)吐口水、吐出、口水\n(無詞性變化)\nspit out 吐出來\nspit on 對……吐口水\nIt is rude to spit on the street.\n(在街上吐口水很沒禮貌。)\nThe baby spat out the medicine.\n(那個嬰兒把藥吐了出來。)"],["spite","spite(n.)惡意、怨恨\nspiteful(adj.)懷恨的\nin spite of 儘管\nout of spite 出於惡意\nIn spite of the rain, we still went hiking.\n(儘管下雨，我們還是去健行了。)\nHe broke her pen out of spite.\n(他出於惡意弄壞了她的筆。)"],["splash","splash(n./v.)潑水聲、濺、潑\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a splash 引起轟動\nsplash water 潑水\nThe kids splashed water at each other in the pool.\n(孩子們在游泳池裡互相潑水。)\nHer first movie made a big splash.\n(她的第一部電影引起很大的轟動。)"],["spoil","spoil(v.)破壞、寵壞、(食物)變壞\nspoiled(adj.)被寵壞的、變質的\nspoil the fun 掃興\nspoil a child 寵壞孩子\nThe rain spoiled our picnic.\n(這場雨破壞了我們的野餐。)\nGrandparents often spoil their grandchildren.\n(祖父母常常寵壞孫子女。)"],["spray","spray(n./v.)噴霧、噴劑、噴灑\nsprayer(n.)噴霧器\nhair spray 髮膠噴霧\nspray paint 噴漆\nFarmers spray their crops to kill insects.\n(農夫在農作物上噴藥殺蟲。)\nShe used some hair spray before the party.\n(她在派對前噴了一些髮膠。)"],["spy","spy(n./v.)間諜、暗中監視\n(無詞性變化)\nspy on 暗中監視\nspy movie 間諜片\nThe man was caught spying for another country.\n(那名男子因替他國從事間諜活動被捕。)\nI love watching spy movies like James Bond.\n(我很喜歡看像〇〇七那樣的間諜片。)"],["squeeze","squeeze(v./n.)擠、榨、緊握\n(無詞性變化)\nsqueeze juice 榨汁\nsqueeze into 擠進\nShe squeezed some lemon juice into her tea.\n(她在茶裡擠了一些檸檬汁。)\nFive of us squeezed into the small car.\n(我們五個人擠進那輛小車裡。)"],["squirrel","squirrel(n.)松鼠\n(無詞性變化)\nred squirrel 紅松鼠\nsquirrel away 儲藏\nA squirrel ran up the tree with a nut.\n(一隻松鼠叼著堅果跑上樹。)\nWe saw many squirrels in the park.\n(我們在公園看到很多松鼠。)"],["stable","stable(adj.)穩定的、穩固的\nstability(n.)穩定\nstabilize(v.)使穩定\nstable job 穩定的工作\nstable condition 狀況穩定\nMy father has a stable job at a bank.\n(我爸爸在銀行有份穩定的工作。)\nThe patient is now in stable condition.\n(病人現在狀況穩定。)"],["stadium","stadium(n.)體育場、運動場\n(無詞性變化)\nbaseball stadium 棒球場\nfootball stadium 足球場\nThe baseball stadium was full of fans.\n(棒球場坐滿了球迷。)\nThe concert will be held at the stadium.\n(演唱會將在體育場舉行。)"],["staff","staff(n./v.)全體職員、工作人員、配置職員\n(無詞性變化)\nstaff member 職員\nteaching staff 教職員\nPlease ask a staff member if you need help.\n(如果需要幫忙，請詢問工作人員。)\nThe hospital is staffed by many experienced nurses.\n(這家醫院配置了許多有經驗的護理師。)"],["stale","stale(adj.)不新鮮的、陳腐的\n(無詞性變化)\nstale bread 不新鮮的麵包\nstale air 不流通的空氣\nThis bread is stale; let's buy some fresh bread.\n(這麵包不新鮮了，我們去買新鮮的吧。)\nOpen the window to let the stale air out.\n(打開窗戶讓悶濁的空氣出去。)"],["stare","stare(v./n.)盯著看、凝視\n(無詞性變化)\nstare at 盯著看\nblank stare 茫然的目光\nIt is rude to stare at strangers.\n(盯著陌生人看是不禮貌的。)\nHe stared out of the window for a long time.\n(他望著窗外看了很久。)"],["starve","starve(v.)挨餓、餓死\nstarvation(n.)飢餓、餓死\nstarve to death 餓死\nbe starving 餓壞了\nI'm starving. Let's eat now.\n(我快餓死了，我們現在去吃東西吧。)\nMany animals starved during the long winter.\n(許多動物在漫長的冬季中餓死。)"],["statue","statue(n.)雕像\n(無詞性變化)\nStatue of Liberty 自由女神像\nbronze statue 銅像\nWe took photos in front of the Statue of Liberty.\n(我們在自由女神像前拍照。)\nThere is a bronze statue in the middle of the park.\n(公園中央有一座銅像。)"],["steady","steady(adj./v./adv./n.)穩定的、平穩的、使穩定\nsteadily(adv.)穩定地\nsteady progress 穩定的進步\nhold steady 保持穩定\nShe has made steady progress in English this year.\n(她今年英文穩定進步。)\nHold the ladder steady while I climb up.\n(我爬上去的時候，請把梯子扶穩。)"],["steal","steal(v.)偷竊、偷取\nstealing(n.)偷竊\nsteal from 從……偷東西\nsteal the show 搶盡風頭\nSomeone stole my bike outside the library.\n(有人在圖書館外偷了我的腳踏車。)\nThe little dog stole the show at the wedding.\n(那隻小狗在婚禮上搶盡風頭。)"],["steam","steam(n./v.)蒸汽、蒸\nsteamy(adj.)蒸氣瀰漫的\nsteamed(adj.)蒸的\nsteamed buns 包子、饅頭\nlet off steam 發洩情緒\nMy grandmother steams fish with ginger.\n(我奶奶用薑清蒸魚。)\nPlaying basketball helps me let off steam after exams.\n(打籃球幫助我在考試後發洩情緒。)"],["steep","steep(adj.)陡峭的、急劇的\nsteeply(adv.)陡峭地、急劇地\nsteep hill 陡峭的山坡\nsteep rise 急遽上升\nWe climbed a steep hill to see the sunrise.\n(我們爬上陡峭的山坡看日出。)\nThere has been a steep rise in house prices.\n(房價急遽上漲。)"],["sticky","sticky(adj.)黏的、濕熱的\nstick(v./n.)黏貼、棍子\nsticky rice 糯米\nsticky weather 悶熱潮濕的天氣\nMy hands are sticky after eating the candy.\n(吃完糖果後我的手黏黏的。)\nTaiwan's summer weather is hot and sticky.\n(台灣夏天的天氣又熱又悶濕。)"],["stiff","stiff(adj.)僵硬的、硬的、激烈的\nstiffen(v.)變僵硬\nstiff neck 脖子僵硬\nstiff competition 激烈的競爭\nI woke up with a stiff neck this morning.\n(我今天早上醒來脖子僵硬。)\nThere is stiff competition for the scholarship.\n(這份獎學金競爭很激烈。)"],["sting","sting(n./v.)刺、螫、刺痛\nstinger(n.)螫針\nbee sting 蜂螫\nsting like 刺痛如……\nA bee stung me on the arm.\n(一隻蜜蜂螫了我的手臂。)\nThe smoke made my eyes sting.\n(煙讓我的眼睛刺痛。)"],["stir","stir(v./n.)攪拌、激起、騷動\n(無詞性變化)\nstir the soup 攪拌湯\ncause a stir 引起騷動\nStir the soup slowly so it doesn't burn.\n(慢慢攪拌湯，以免燒焦。)\nThe news caused a stir in the school.\n(這則消息在學校引起一陣騷動。)"],["stitch","stitch(n./v.)一針、縫線、縫\n(無詞性變化)\nneed stitches 需要縫針\nstitch up 縫合\nHe cut his finger and needed five stitches.\n(他割傷手指，需要縫五針。)\nA stitch in time saves nine.\n(及時縫一針，可省九針；小洞不補，大洞吃苦。)"],["stomach","stomach(n.)胃、肚子\n(無詞性變化)\nstomachache 胃痛、肚子痛\non an empty stomach 空腹\nDon't take this medicine on an empty stomach.\n(不要空腹吃這種藥。)\nI have a pain in my stomach after eating too fast.\n(我吃太快之後肚子痛。)"],["stool","stool(n.)凳子、高腳椅\n(無詞性變化)\nbar stool 吧台高腳椅\nsit on a stool 坐在凳子上\nThe old man sat on a small stool outside his shop.\n(老先生坐在店外的小凳子上。)\nWe sat on bar stools and ordered drinks.\n(我們坐在吧台高腳椅上點飲料。)"],["stormy","stormy(adj.)暴風雨的、激烈的\nstorm(n./v.)暴風雨\nstormy weather 暴風雨天氣\nstormy relationship 風波不斷的關係\nThe boats stayed in the harbor because of the stormy weather.\n(因為暴風雨的天氣，船隻都停在港內。)\nIt was a dark and stormy night.\n(那是一個黑暗又狂風暴雨的夜晚。)"],["stove","stove(n.)爐子、火爐\n(無詞性變化)\ngas stove 瓦斯爐\non the stove 在爐子上\nThere is a pot of soup on the stove.\n(爐子上有一鍋湯。)\nTurn off the gas stove before you leave.\n(離開前要把瓦斯爐關掉。)"],["strategy","strategy(n.)策略、戰略\nstrategic(adj.)策略上的、戰略的\nlearning strategy 學習策略\nmarketing strategy 行銷策略\nMaking flashcards is a useful learning strategy.\n(做字卡是一種有用的學習策略。)\nThe coach changed the team's strategy at halftime.\n(教練在中場時改變球隊的戰術。)"],["straw","straw(n.)稻草、吸管\n(無詞性變化)\nplastic straw 塑膠吸管\nstraw hat 草帽\nMany shops no longer give out plastic straws.\n(許多店家已不再提供塑膠吸管。)\nThe farmer wore a straw hat in the sun.\n(農夫在太陽下戴著草帽。)"],["strength","strength(n.)力量、力氣、長處\nstrong(adj.)強壯的\nstrengthen(v.)加強\nstrengths and weaknesses 優缺點\nphysical strength 體力\nEveryone has their own strengths and weaknesses.\n(每個人都有自己的優缺點。)\nHe didn't have the strength to lift the box.\n(他沒有力氣抬起那個箱子。)"],["strip","strip(n./v.)條、帶、剝去\n(無詞性變化)\na strip of paper 一張紙條\ncomic strip 連環漫畫\nCut the paper into long strips.\n(把紙剪成長條。)\nHe reads the comic strips in the newspaper every day.\n(他每天看報紙上的連環漫畫。)"],["structure","structure(n.)結構、建築物\nstructural(adj.)結構上的\nsentence structure 句子結構\nfamily structure 家庭結構\nThe teacher explained the sentence structure clearly.\n(老師清楚地解釋了句子結構。)\nTaipei 101 is a tall structure that can resist earthquakes.\n(台北一〇一是一棟能抵抗地震的高聳建築。)"],["stubborn","stubborn(adj.)固執的、頑固的\nstubbornly(adv.)固執地\nstubbornness(n.)固執\nstubborn as a mule 非常固執\nstubborn child 固執的孩子\nMy grandfather is as stubborn as a mule.\n(我爺爺非常固執。)\nThe stubborn boy refused to say sorry.\n(那個固執的男孩拒絕道歉。)"],["studio","studio(n.)工作室、攝影棚、錄音室\n(無詞性變化)\nrecording studio 錄音室\nart studio 畫室\nThe band recorded their new song in a studio.\n(樂團在錄音室錄製新歌。)\nShe opened an art studio for children.\n(她為孩子們開設了一間畫室。)"],["stuff","stuff(n./v.)東西、物品、塞滿\nstuffed(adj.)塞滿的、填充的\nstuffy(adj.)悶熱的、不通風的\nstuffed animal 填充玩偶\npack one's stuff 收拾東西\nPlease pack your stuff before we leave.\n(我們出發前請收拾好你的東西。)\nShe stuffed her clothes into the small bag.\n(她把衣服塞進那個小袋子裡。)"],["substance","substance(n.)物質、實質\nsubstantial(adj.)大量的、實質的\nharmful substance 有害物質\nillegal substance 違禁物品\nSome plastic products contain harmful substances.\n(有些塑膠產品含有有害物質。)\nHis speech lacked substance.\n(他的演講缺乏實質內容。)"],["subtract","subtract(v.)減去、扣除\nsubtraction(n.)減法\nsubtract A from B 從B減去A\nadd and subtract 加減\nIf you subtract 3 from 10, you get 7.\n(十減三等於七。)\nYoung children learn to add and subtract.\n(小朋友學習加減法。)"],["suburb","suburb(n.)郊區\nsuburban(adj.)郊區的\nlive in the suburbs 住在郊區\nquiet suburb 寧靜的郊區\nMany families move to the suburbs for cheaper housing.\n(許多家庭搬到郊區以找到較便宜的住處。)\nThey live in a quiet suburb of Taipei.\n(他們住在台北一個寧靜的郊區。)"],["suck","suck(v./n.)吸、吸吮\n(無詞性變化)\nsuck one's thumb 吸吮拇指\nsuck up 吸起\nThe baby likes to suck his thumb.\n(那個嬰兒喜歡吸吮拇指。)\nThe machine sucks up dust from the floor.\n(這台機器把地上的灰塵吸起來。)"],["suffer","suffer(v.)受苦、遭受、患病\nsuffering(n.)痛苦、苦難\nsuffer from 受……之苦、患……\nsuffer a loss 遭受損失\nMany people suffer from back pain.\n(許多人受背痛之苦。)\nThe farmers suffered a big loss after the typhoon.\n(颱風過後農民遭受巨大損失。)"],["sufficient","sufficient(adj.)足夠的、充分的\nsufficiently(adv.)足夠地\nsufficiency(n.)充足\nsufficient time 足夠的時間\nsufficient evidence 充分的證據\nWe don't have sufficient time to finish the project.\n(我們沒有足夠的時間完成這個專題。)\nMake sure you get sufficient sleep before the exam.\n(考試前要確保睡眠充足。)"],["suicide","suicide(n.)自殺、自毀的行為\nsuicidal(adj.)想自殺的、自毀的\nsuicide prevention 自殺防治\npolitical suicide 政治自殺\nThe school holds talks on suicide prevention every year.\n(學校每年舉辦自殺防治講座。)\nSkipping the final exam would be academic suicide.\n(缺考期末考等於自毀學業。)"],["sum","sum(n./v.)總數、金額、總結\nsummary(n.)摘要\nsummarize(v.)總結\na large sum of money 一大筆錢\nsum up 總結\nHe spent a large sum of money on his new phone.\n(他花了一大筆錢買新手機。)\nLet me sum up the main points of today's lesson.\n(讓我總結一下今天課程的重點。)"],["summary","summary(n.)摘要、總結\nsummarize(v.)總結、摘要\nin summary 總之\nwrite a summary 寫摘要\nPlease write a summary of the story in 100 words.\n(請用一百字寫出這個故事的摘要。)\nIn summary, exercise is good for both body and mind.\n(總之，運動對身心都有益。)"],["summit","summit(n.)山頂、高峰、高峰會\n(無詞性變化)\nreach the summit 登頂\nsummit meeting 高峰會議\nWe reached the summit of Jade Mountain at sunrise.\n(我們在日出時登上玉山頂峰。)\nWorld leaders met at the summit meeting.\n(世界各國領袖在高峰會中會面。)"],["superior","superior(adj./n.)較好的、優越的、上司\nsuperiority(n.)優越\nsuperior to 比……好\nimmediate superior 直屬上司\nThis phone is superior to the old model in many ways.\n(這支手機在許多方面都比舊型號好。)\nYou should report the problem to your superior.\n(你應該向你的上司報告這個問題。)"],["surround","surround(v.)包圍、圍繞\nsurroundings(n.)環境\nsurrounding(adj.)周圍的\nbe surrounded by 被……圍繞\nsurrounding area 周遭地區\nTaiwan is surrounded by the sea.\n(台灣四面環海。)\nThe singer was surrounded by fans.\n(那位歌手被歌迷團團圍住。)"],["survey","survey(n./v.)調查、民調、俯瞰\n(無詞性變化)\nconduct a survey 進行調查\nsurvey shows 調查顯示\nOur class conducted a survey about students' sleep habits.\n(我們班進行了一項關於學生睡眠習慣的調查。)\nThe survey shows that most teens use social media every day.\n(調查顯示大部分青少年每天使用社群媒體。)"],["survivor","survivor(n.)倖存者、生還者\nsurvive(v.)存活、倖存\nsurvival(n.)生存\nsole survivor 唯一的倖存者\nearthquake survivor 地震倖存者\nRescue workers searched for survivors after the earthquake.\n(地震後救難人員搜尋倖存者。)\nShe was the only survivor of the plane crash.\n(她是那場墜機事故中唯一的生還者。)"],["suspect","suspect(v./n./adj.)懷疑、嫌疑犯、可疑的\nsuspicion(n.)懷疑\nsuspicious(adj.)可疑的\nmain suspect 主要嫌疑犯\nsuspect that 懷疑……\nThe police arrested the main suspect last night.\n(警方昨晚逮捕了主要嫌疑犯。)\nI suspect that he forgot about the meeting.\n(我懷疑他忘了這場會議。)"],["suspicion","suspicion(n.)懷疑、嫌疑\nsuspect(v./n.)懷疑、嫌疑犯\nsuspicious(adj.)可疑的\nunder suspicion 受到懷疑\narouse suspicion 引起懷疑\nHis strange behavior aroused the guard's suspicion.\n(他奇怪的舉動引起警衛的懷疑。)\nThe new worker is under suspicion of stealing money.\n(那位新員工涉嫌偷錢。)"],["swan","swan(n.)天鵝\n(無詞性變化)\nblack swan 黑天鵝\nSwan Lake 天鵝湖\nTwo white swans were swimming on the lake.\n(兩隻白天鵝在湖上游著。)\nWe watched the ballet Swan Lake last night.\n(我們昨晚看了芭蕾舞劇《天鵝湖》。)"],["swear","swear(v.)發誓、咒罵\nswearing(n.)咒罵、發誓\nswear to 對……發誓\nswear at 咒罵某人\nI swear I didn't tell anyone your secret.\n(我發誓我沒有把你的秘密告訴任何人。)\nIt's rude to swear at other people.\n(對別人罵髒話很沒禮貌。)"],["sweat","sweat(n./v.)汗水、流汗\nsweaty(adj.)汗濕的\nbreak a sweat 流汗\nno sweat 小事一樁\nI was covered in sweat after running.\n(跑步後我滿身大汗。)\nCan you help me move this desk? No sweat.\n(你可以幫我搬這張桌子嗎？小事一樁。)"],["swell","swell(v./n.)腫脹、增大、膨脹\nswelling(n.)腫脹處\nswollen(adj.)腫起來的\nswell up 腫起來\nswollen ankle 腫脹的腳踝\nMy ankle began to swell after I fell down.\n(我跌倒後腳踝開始腫起來。)\nThe river swelled after days of heavy rain.\n(連日大雨後河水暴漲。)"],["swift","swift(adj.)迅速的、敏捷的\nswiftly(adv.)迅速地\nswift action 迅速的行動\nswift reply 迅速的回覆\nThanks to the firefighters' swift action, no one was hurt.\n(多虧消防員迅速行動，沒有人受傷。)\nThe swift river is dangerous for swimmers.\n(湍急的河流對游泳者很危險。)"],["sword","sword(n.)劍、刀\n(無詞性變化)\ndraw a sword 拔劍\ndouble-edged sword 雙面刃\nThe knight drew his sword to fight the dragon.\n(騎士拔劍與龍搏鬥。)\nThe Internet is a double-edged sword.\n(網路是一把雙面刃。)"],["tablet","tablet(n.)平板電腦、藥片、碑\n(無詞性變化)\ntablet computer 平板電腦\ntake a tablet 吃一顆藥\nMany students take notes on their tablets.\n(許多學生用平板電腦做筆記。)\nTake two tablets after each meal.\n(每餐飯後服用兩顆藥片。)"],["tag","tag(n./v.)標籤、貼標籤、標記\n(無詞性變化)\nprice tag 價格標籤\nname tag 名牌\nDon't forget to remove the price tag from the gift.\n(別忘了把禮物上的價格標籤撕掉。)\nShe tagged her friends in the photo.\n(她在照片中標記了她的朋友。)"],["tailor","tailor(n.)裁縫師\ntailored(adj.)量身訂做的\ntailor-made 量身訂做的\nlocal tailor 當地裁縫師\nThe tailor made a suit for my father.\n(裁縫師為我爸爸做了一套西裝。)\nThe program is tailor-made for beginners.\n(這個課程是專為初學者量身打造的。)"],["talent","talent(n.)天分、才能、人才\ntalented(adj.)有天分的\ntalent show 才藝表演\na talent for 有……的天分\nShe has a real talent for music.\n(她在音樂方面很有天分。)\nOur class won first prize in the talent show.\n(我們班在才藝表演中得到第一名。)"],["talkative","talkative(adj.)健談的、多話的\ntalk(v.)說話\ntalkative person 多話的人\nbecome talkative 變得話多\nMy little brother is very talkative at dinner.\n(我弟弟吃晚餐時話很多。)\nShe is shy at first but becomes talkative later.\n(她一開始很害羞，但後來就變得很健談。)"],["tame","tame(adj./v.)溫馴的、馴服\n(無詞性變化)\ntame animal 溫馴的動物\ntame a horse 馴服一匹馬\nThe deer in Nara are so tame that you can feed them.\n(奈良的鹿非常溫馴，你可以餵牠們。)\nIt took him months to tame the wild horse.\n(他花了好幾個月才馴服那匹野馬。)"],["tangerine","tangerine(n.)橘子、柑橘\n(無詞性變化)\npeel a tangerine 剝橘子\ntangerine juice 橘子汁\nPeople give tangerines as gifts during Chinese New Year.\n(人們在農曆新年送橘子當禮物。)\nShe peeled a tangerine and shared it with me.\n(她剝了一顆橘子和我分享。)"],["tank","tank(n.)槽、箱、坦克\n(無詞性變化)\nfish tank 魚缸\ngas tank 油箱\nThere are five goldfish in the fish tank.\n(魚缸裡有五隻金魚。)\nWe need to fill up the gas tank before the trip.\n(出發前我們需要把油箱加滿。)"],["tap","tap(v./n.)輕拍、輕敲、水龍頭\n(無詞性變化)\ntap water 自來水\ntap on the shoulder 輕拍肩膀\nSomeone tapped me on the shoulder on the bus.\n(在公車上有人輕拍我的肩膀。)\nTap the screen twice to open the app.\n(在螢幕上點兩下打開這個應用程式。)"],["tasty","tasty(adj.)美味的、可口的\ntaste(n./v.)味道、品嘗\ntasteful(adj.)有品味的\ntasty food 美味的食物\ntasty snack 好吃的點心\nThe night market has lots of tasty snacks.\n(夜市裡有很多好吃的小吃。)\nThis soup is healthy and tasty.\n(這碗湯既健康又美味。)"],["tease","tease(v.)取笑、捉弄\nteasing(n.)取笑、戲弄\ntease someone about 拿……取笑某人\njust teasing 只是開玩笑\nStop teasing your sister about her haircut.\n(別再拿你妹妹的髮型取笑她了。)\nDon't be angry. I was just teasing you.\n(別生氣，我只是在逗你。)"],["technical","technical(adj.)技術的、專門的\ntechnique(n.)技巧\ntechnically(adv.)技術上、嚴格來說\ntechnical problem 技術問題\ntechnical school 技術學校\nThe concert was delayed because of a technical problem.\n(演唱會因為技術問題而延遲。)\nThe article has too many technical terms.\n(這篇文章有太多專業術語。)"],["technique","technique(n.)技巧、技術、手法\ntechnical(adj.)技術的\nlearning technique 學習技巧\ndevelop a technique 發展技巧\nShe uses a special technique to remember new words.\n(她用一種特別的技巧記新單字。)\nThe coach taught us a new swimming technique.\n(教練教我們一種新的游泳技巧。)"],["teenage","teenage(adj.)十幾歲的、青少年的\nteenager(n.)青少年\nteen(n.)青少年\nteenage years 青少年時期\nteenage girl 十幾歲的女孩\nMany teenage students spend hours on their phones.\n(許多青少年學生花好幾個小時在手機上。)\nHe enjoyed his teenage years in Tainan.\n(他在台南度過了愉快的青少年時期。)"],["temper","temper(n.)脾氣、情緒\ntemperament(n.)性情、氣質\nlose one's temper 發脾氣\nbad temper 壞脾氣\nMy dad never loses his temper with us.\n(我爸爸從來不對我們發脾氣。)\nHe has a bad temper when he is hungry.\n(他肚子餓時脾氣很差。)"],["temporary","temporary(adj.)暫時的、臨時的\ntemporarily(adv.)暫時地\ntemporary job 臨時工作\ntemporary solution 權宜之計\nShe found a temporary job during summer vacation.\n(她在暑假找到一份臨時工作。)\nThe road is temporarily closed for repairs.\n(這條路因整修暫時封閉。)"],["tend","tend(v.)傾向、往往會、照料\ntendency(n.)傾向、趨勢\ntend to 往往、傾向於\ntend to the sick 照顧病人\nI tend to feel sleepy after lunch.\n(我午餐後往往會覺得想睡。)\nNurses tend to patients day and night.\n(護理師日夜照顧病人。)"],["tender","tender(adj.)嫩的、溫柔的、疼痛的\ntenderness(n.)溫柔、柔軟\ntenderly(adv.)溫柔地\ntender meat 嫩肉\ntender care 細心照顧\nThe steak was tender and juicy.\n(這塊牛排又嫩又多汁。)\nShe spoke to the child in a tender voice.\n(她用溫柔的聲音對孩子說話。)"],["tent","tent(n.)帳篷\n(無詞性變化)\nput up a tent 搭帳篷\ncamping tent 露營帳篷\nWe put up our tent near the lake.\n(我們在湖邊搭起帳篷。)\nIt rained all night, but we stayed dry in the tent.\n(雨下了一整晚，但我們在帳篷裡很乾爽。)"],["terrific","terrific(adj.)極好的、了不起的、極大的\nterrifically(adv.)極其\nterrific job 做得太棒了\nterrific idea 絕佳的主意\nYou did a terrific job on the project.\n(你這個專題做得太棒了。)\nWe had a terrific time at the beach.\n(我們在海邊玩得很開心。)"],["territory","territory(n.)領土、領域、地盤\nterritorial(adj.)領土的\nenemy territory 敵方領土\nnew territory 新領域\nSome animals mark their territory with smells.\n(有些動物會用氣味標記地盤。)\nFor me, cooking is new territory.\n(對我來說，烹飪是個全新的領域。)"],["thankful","thankful(adj.)感謝的、慶幸的\nthank(v.)感謝\nthankfully(adv.)幸好、感激地\nthankful for 對……感激\nbe thankful that 慶幸……\nI am thankful for my parents' support.\n(我很感謝父母的支持。)\nWe were thankful that no one was hurt.\n(我們很慶幸沒有人受傷。)"],["theory","theory(n.)理論、學說\ntheoretical(adj.)理論上的\nin theory 理論上\ntheory of evolution 演化論\nIn theory, the plan should work.\n(理論上，這個計畫應該行得通。)\nDarwin is famous for his theory of evolution.\n(達爾文因他的演化論而聞名。)"],["thirst","thirst(n.)口渴、渴望\nthirsty(adj.)口渴的\nquench one's thirst 解渴\nthirst for knowledge 求知慾\nA glass of cold water will quench your thirst.\n(一杯冰水就能幫你解渴。)\nShe has a strong thirst for knowledge.\n(她有強烈的求知慾。)"],["thread","thread(n./v.)線、思路、穿線\n(無詞性變化)\nneedle and thread 針線\nlose the thread 失去思路\nGrandma threaded the needle without glasses.\n(奶奶不戴眼鏡就把針穿上了線。)\nI lost the thread of the story halfway through.\n(故事聽到一半我就跟不上了。)"],["threat","threat(n.)威脅、恐嚇\nthreaten(v.)威脅\nthreatening(adj.)威脅的\nserious threat 嚴重威脅\na threat to …的威脅\nPlastic waste is a serious threat to sea life.\n(塑膠垃圾對海洋生物是嚴重的威脅。)\nHe ignored the threat and kept walking.\n(他不理會威脅，繼續往前走。)"],["threaten","threaten(v.)威脅、恐嚇、可能危及\nthreat(n.)威脅\nthreatened(adj.)受威脅的\nthreaten to 揚言要\nthreaten one's life 危及生命\nThe man threatened to call the police.\n(那個男人揚言要報警。)\nClimate change threatens many animals.\n(氣候變遷威脅著許多動物。)"],["thumb","thumb(n./v.)拇指、用拇指翻\n(無詞性變化)\nthumbs up 讚、豎起大拇指\nthumb through 快速翻閱\nHe gave me a thumbs up after my speech.\n(我演講完後他對我豎起大拇指。)\nShe thumbed through the magazine while waiting.\n(她在等待時隨手翻閱雜誌。)"],["tide","tide(n.)潮汐、潮流\ntidal(adj.)潮汐的\nhigh tide 漲潮\nlow tide 退潮\nYou can find crabs on the beach at low tide.\n(退潮時你可以在海灘上找到螃蟹。)\nThe tide is coming in, so let's go back.\n(開始漲潮了，我們回去吧。)"],["tight","tight(adj./adv.)緊的、緊密的、緊緊地\ntightly(adv.)緊緊地\ntighten(v.)拉緊\ntight schedule 緊湊的行程\nhold tight 抓緊\nThese jeans are too tight for me.\n(這條牛仔褲對我來說太緊了。)\nHold tight, or you'll fall off.\n(抓緊，不然你會掉下去。)"],["tighten","tighten(v.)拉緊、加強、收緊\ntight(adj.)緊的\ntighten one's belt 勒緊褲帶、節省開支\ntighten security 加強安全措施\nPlease tighten your seat belt.\n(請繫緊你的安全帶。)\nThe airport tightened security after the incident.\n(事件發生後，機場加強了安檢。)"],["timber","timber(n.)木材、木料\n(無詞性變化)\ntimber house 木屋\ntimber industry 木材業\nThe old house was built of timber.\n(這棟老房子是用木材建造的。)\nTaiwan once had a large timber industry.\n(台灣過去曾有龐大的木材業。)"],["tobacco","tobacco(n.)菸草、菸\n(無詞性變化)\ntobacco smoke 菸草煙霧\ntobacco company 菸草公司\nTobacco is harmful to your health.\n(菸草對你的健康有害。)\nSelling tobacco to teenagers is against the law.\n(賣菸給青少年是違法的。)"],["ton","ton(n.)噸、大量\n(無詞性變化)\ntons of 大量的\nweigh a ton 很重\nThis truck can carry ten tons of sand.\n(這輛卡車可以載十噸的沙。)\nI have tons of homework this weekend.\n(我這個週末有一大堆功課。)"],["toss","toss(v./n.)扔、拋、擲硬幣\n(無詞性變化)\ntoss a coin 擲硬幣\ntoss and turn 輾轉反側\nLet's toss a coin to decide who goes first.\n(我們擲硬幣決定誰先開始吧。)\nI tossed and turned all night before the exam.\n(考試前一晚我整夜輾轉難眠。)"],["tough","tough(adj.)困難的、堅強的、(肉)老的\ntoughness(n.)堅韌\ntoughen(v.)使堅強\ntough decision 艱難的決定\ntough guy 硬漢\nIt was a tough decision to leave my hometown.\n(離開家鄉是個艱難的決定。)\nThis meat is too tough to chew.\n(這塊肉太老了，咬不動。)"],["tourism","tourism(n.)觀光業、旅遊業\ntour(n./v.)旅行\ntourist(n.)觀光客\ntourism industry 觀光產業\neco-tourism 生態旅遊\nTourism is important to Hualien's economy.\n(觀光業對花蓮的經濟很重要。)\nThe government is trying to promote tourism.\n(政府正努力推廣觀光。)"],["tourist","tourist(n.)觀光客、遊客\ntour(n./v.)旅行\ntourism(n.)觀光業\ntourist attraction 觀光景點\nforeign tourist 外國遊客\nTaipei 101 is a popular tourist attraction.\n(台北101是熱門的觀光景點。)\nMany foreign tourists visit the night markets.\n(許多外國遊客造訪夜市。)"],["tow","tow(n./v.)拖、拖吊\n(無詞性變化)\ntow truck 拖吊車\nbe towed away 被拖吊\nMy car was towed away because I parked illegally.\n(我的車因為違規停車被拖吊了。)\nWe called a tow truck after the accident.\n(車禍後我們叫了拖吊車。)"],["tower","tower(n.)塔、高樓\ntowering(adj.)高聳的\nclock tower 鐘樓\nwater tower 水塔\nThe Eiffel Tower is a symbol of Paris.\n(艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎的象徵。)\nThere is an old clock tower in the center of town.\n(鎮中心有一座古老的鐘樓。)"],["trace","trace(n./v.)痕跡、追蹤、描摹\n(無詞性變化)\nwithout a trace 無影無蹤\ntrace back to 追溯到\nThe thief disappeared without a trace.\n(小偷消失得無影無蹤。)\nThis custom can be traced back to the Qing Dynasty.\n(這個習俗可以追溯到清朝。)"],["trader","trader(n.)商人、交易者\ntrade(n./v.)貿易、交易\nstock trader 股票交易員\nfur trader 毛皮商\nThe Dutch traders came to Taiwan in the 17th century.\n(荷蘭商人在十七世紀來到台灣。)\nMy uncle works as a stock trader.\n(我叔叔是一名股票交易員。)"],["trail","trail(n./v.)小徑、蹤跡、拖曳、落後\ntrailer(n.)預告片、拖車\nhiking trail 登山步道\ntrail behind 落後\nWe followed the hiking trail up the mountain.\n(我們沿著登山步道上山。)\nOur team was trailing by ten points at halftime.\n(我們隊在中場時落後十分。)"],["transport","transport(n./v.)運輸、交通工具、運送\ntransportation(n.)交通運輸\npublic transport 大眾運輸\ntransport goods 運送貨物\nPublic transport in Taipei is very convenient.\n(台北的大眾運輸非常方便。)\nTrucks transport fruit from the farms to the markets.\n(卡車把水果從農場運送到市場。)"],["traveler","traveler(n.)旅行者、旅客\ntravel(v./n.)旅行\nsolo traveler 獨自旅行者\nbusiness traveler 商務旅客\nMore and more young travelers like to travel alone.\n(越來越多年輕旅客喜歡獨自旅行。)\nThe hotel offers free breakfast to all travelers.\n(這家飯店為所有旅客提供免費早餐。)"],["tray","tray(n.)托盤、盤子\n(無詞性變化)\nice tray 製冰盒\nfood tray 餐盤\nThe waiter carried drinks on a tray.\n(服務生用托盤端飲料。)\nPlease return your food tray after eating.\n(用餐後請歸還你的餐盤。)"],["trend","trend(n.)趨勢、潮流\ntrendy(adj.)時髦的\nfashion trend 流行趨勢\nfollow the trend 跟隨潮流\nShe always follows the latest fashion trends.\n(她總是跟隨最新的流行趨勢。)\nThere is a growing trend of working from home.\n(在家工作的趨勢越來越明顯。)"],["tribe","tribe(n.)部落、種族\ntribal(adj.)部落的\ntribe member 部落成員\nindigenous tribe 原住民部落\nWe visited an Amis tribe in Hualien.\n(我們拜訪了花蓮的一個阿美族部落。)\nEach tribe has its own language and culture.\n(每個部落都有自己的語言和文化。)"],["tricky","tricky(adj.)棘手的、狡猾的\ntrick(n./v.)詭計、欺騙\ntricky question 棘手的問題\ntricky situation 棘手的情況\nThat was a tricky question on the test.\n(那是考試中一道很刁鑽的題目。)\nDriving in heavy rain can be tricky.\n(在大雨中開車可能很棘手。)"],["troop","troop(n.)(複數)部隊、軍隊、一群\ntrooper(n.)騎兵、州警\nsend troops 派遣部隊\na troop of 一群\nThe government sent troops to help after the earthquake.\n(地震後政府派遣部隊協助救災。)\nA troop of monkeys came down from the mountain.\n(一群猴子從山上下來。)"],["tropical","tropical(adj.)熱帶的\ntropics(n.)熱帶地區\ntropical fruit 熱帶水果\ntropical rainforest 熱帶雨林\nMangoes and papayas are tropical fruits.\n(芒果和木瓜都是熱帶水果。)\nSouthern Taiwan has a tropical climate.\n(台灣南部屬於熱帶氣候。)"],["trumpet","trumpet(n.)喇叭、小號\ntrumpeter(n.)小號手\nplay the trumpet 吹小號\nblow one's own trumpet 自吹自擂\nHe plays the trumpet in the school band.\n(他在學校樂隊吹小號。)\nShe never blows her own trumpet.\n(她從不自吹自擂。)"],["trunk","trunk(n.)樹幹、象鼻、汽車後車廂\n(無詞性變化)\ntree trunk 樹幹\ncar trunk 後車廂\nPut the suitcases in the trunk of the car.\n(把行李箱放進汽車後車廂。)\nAn elephant uses its trunk to drink water.\n(大象用鼻子喝水。)"],["truthful","truthful(adj.)誠實的、真實的\ntruth(n.)事實、真相\ntruthfully(adv.)誠實地\ntruthful answer 誠實的回答\nbe truthful with 對……誠實\nPlease give me a truthful answer.\n(請給我一個誠實的回答。)\nYou should always be truthful with your friends.\n(你應該永遠對朋友誠實。)"],["tub","tub(n.)浴缸、桶、盆\nbathtub(n.)浴缸\nhot tub 熱水浴缸\na tub of ice cream 一桶冰淇淋\nThe baby is playing in the tub.\n(寶寶在浴缸裡玩。)\nHe ate a whole tub of ice cream by himself.\n(他自己吃完了一整桶冰淇淋。)"],["tug","tug(n./v.)用力拉、拖\n(無詞性變化)\ntug of war 拔河\ntug at 拉扯\nOur class won the tug of war on sports day.\n(我們班在運動會拔河比賽中獲勝。)\nThe child tugged at his mother's sleeve.\n(那孩子拉了拉媽媽的袖子。)"],["tune","tune(n./v.)曲調、調音、調整頻道\n(無詞性變化)\nin tune 音準的、協調的\nstay tuned 敬請鎖定\nShe is humming a happy tune.\n(她正在哼一首快樂的曲子。)\nStay tuned for more news after the break.\n(廣告後更多新聞，敬請鎖定。)"],["tunnel","tunnel(n./v.)隧道、挖隧道\n(無詞性變化)\ngo through a tunnel 穿過隧道\nlight at the end of the tunnel 苦盡甘來的曙光\nIt takes about ten minutes to drive through the Hsuehshan Tunnel.\n(開車通過雪山隧道大約要十分鐘。)\nAfter months of hard work, we finally see light at the end of the tunnel.\n(經過幾個月的努力，我們終於看見了曙光。)"],["tutor","tutor(n./v.)家教、導師、個別指導\ntutorial(n./adj.)教學課程、輔導的\nprivate tutor 私人家教\nmath tutor 數學家教\nMy parents hired a math tutor for me.\n(我爸媽幫我請了一位數學家教。)\nShe tutors high school students in English.\n(她為高中生做英文家教。)"],["twin","twin(n.)雙胞胎之一\n(無詞性變化)\ntwin brother 雙胞胎兄弟\nidentical twins 同卵雙胞胎\nTom and his twin brother look exactly alike.\n(湯姆和他的雙胞胎兄弟長得一模一樣。)\nIt's hard to tell the identical twins apart.\n(很難分辨這對同卵雙胞胎。)"],["twist","twist(n./v.)扭轉、扭傷、意外轉折\ntwisted(adj.)扭曲的\ntwist one's ankle 扭傷腳踝\nplot twist 劇情轉折\nI twisted my ankle while playing basketball.\n(我打籃球時扭傷了腳踝。)\nThe movie has a surprising plot twist at the end.\n(這部電影結尾有個出人意料的劇情轉折。)"],["underlying","underlying(v.)作為……的基礎(underlie 的現在分詞)、潛在的、根本的\nunderlie(v.)構成……的基礎\nunderlying cause 根本原因\nunderlying problem 潛在的問題\nWe need to find the underlying cause of the problem.\n(我們必須找出這個問題的根本原因。)\nStress was the underlying reason for his poor sleep.\n(壓力是他睡不好的根本原因。)"],["underwear","underwear(n.)內衣褲\n(無詞性變化)\nclean underwear 乾淨的內衣褲\nthermal underwear 保暖內衣\nPack enough underwear for the five-day trip.\n(五天的旅行要帶足夠的內衣褲。)\nShe wears thermal underwear in winter.\n(她冬天會穿保暖內衣。)"],["union","union(n.)聯盟、工會、結合\nunite(v.)聯合\nlabor union 工會\nthe European Union 歐盟\nFrance is a member of the European Union.\n(法國是歐盟的成員國。)\nThe labor union asked for higher wages.\n(工會要求提高薪資。)"],["unique","unique(adj./n.)獨特的、獨一無二的、獨特的人或物\nuniqueness(n.)獨特性\nuniquely(adv.)獨特地\nunique style 獨特的風格\nunique to 某地特有的\nEvery person's fingerprints are unique.\n(每個人的指紋都是獨一無二的。)\nThis kind of bird is unique to Taiwan.\n(這種鳥是台灣特有的。)"],["unite","unite(v.)聯合、團結、統一\nunion(n.)聯盟\nunity(n.)團結\nunited(adj.)聯合的、團結的\nunite against 團結起來對抗\nunite as one 團結一致\nThe whole class united to win the contest.\n(全班團結一心贏得比賽。)\nPeople united against the new law.\n(人們團結起來反對新法律。)"],["unity","unity(n.)團結、統一、一致\nunite(v.)聯合\nnational unity 國家團結\na sense of unity 團結感\nTeam sports build a sense of unity.\n(團隊運動能建立團結感。)\nThe leader called for unity in hard times.\n(領導人在艱難時期呼籲團結。)"],["urban","urban(adj.)都市的、城市的\nurbanization(n.)都市化\nurban area 都市地區\nurban life 都市生活\nMore people now live in urban areas than in the countryside.\n(現在住在都市地區的人比住在鄉下的多。)\nUrban life is fast and busy.\n(都市生活步調快又忙碌。)"],["vacant","vacant(adj.)空的、未被占用的、茫然的\nvacancy(n.)空缺、空房\nvacant seat 空位\nvacant lot 空地\nIs this seat vacant?\n(這個位子有人坐嗎？)\nThe kids played soccer in a vacant lot.\n(孩子們在一塊空地上踢足球。)"],["van","van(n.)廂型車、貨車\n(無詞性變化)\ndelivery van 送貨車\ncamper van 露營車\nA delivery van stopped in front of our house.\n(一輛送貨車停在我們家門口。)\nWe rented a camper van for our road trip.\n(我們租了一輛露營車去公路旅行。)"],["vanish","vanish(v.)消失、絕跡\n(無詞性變化)\nvanish into thin air 消失得無影無蹤\nvanish from sight 從視線中消失\nThe magician made the coin vanish.\n(魔術師讓硬幣消失了。)\nMy keys seem to have vanished into thin air.\n(我的鑰匙好像憑空消失了。)"],["variety","variety(n.)多樣化、種類\nvarious(adj.)各種的\nvary(v.)變化\na variety of 各式各樣的\nvariety show 綜藝節目\nThe store sells a variety of snacks.\n(這家店販售各式各樣的零食。)\nMy grandparents enjoy watching variety shows.\n(我的祖父母喜歡看綜藝節目。)"],["various","various(adj.)各種的、不同的\nvariety(n.)多樣化\nvary(v.)變化\nvarious reasons 種種原因\nvarious kinds of 各種的\nHe was absent for various reasons.\n(他因為種種原因缺席。)\nThe museum has various kinds of old coins.\n(博物館裡有各種古錢幣。)"],["vary","vary(v.)變化、不同、改變\nvariety(n.)多樣化\nvarious(adj.)各種的\nvariation(n.)變化\nvary from A to B 從A到B不等\nvary in size 大小不一\nPrices vary from store to store.\n(價格因店而異。)\nThe weather in the mountains varies a lot.\n(山區的天氣變化很大。)"],["vase","vase(n.)花瓶\n(無詞性變化)\nflower vase 花瓶\nglass vase 玻璃花瓶\nShe put the roses in a glass vase.\n(她把玫瑰花插進玻璃花瓶裡。)\nThe cat knocked the vase off the table.\n(那隻貓把花瓶從桌上撞了下來。)"],["vehicle","vehicle(n.)車輛、交通工具、媒介\nvehicular(adj.)車輛的\nmotor vehicle 機動車輛\nelectric vehicle 電動車\nElectric vehicles are becoming more popular.\n(電動車越來越普及。)\nNo vehicles are allowed in this area.\n(這個區域禁止車輛進入。)"],["verse","verse(n.)詩、韻文、(歌曲的)段落\n(無詞性變化)\nin verse 用韻文寫的\nfirst verse 第一段歌詞\nThe play is written in verse.\n(這齣劇是用韻文寫成的。)\nLet's sing the first verse again.\n(我們再唱一次第一段吧。)"],["vest","vest(n.)背心\n(無詞性變化)\nlife vest 救生衣\ndown vest 羽絨背心\nEveryone must wear a life vest on the boat.\n(搭船時每個人都必須穿救生衣。)\nHe wore a warm down vest over his shirt.\n(他在襯衫外面穿了一件保暖的羽絨背心。)"],["victim","victim(n.)受害者、犧牲者\nvictimize(v.)使受害\nfall victim to 成為……的受害者\nflood victims 水災災民\nMany people donated money to the flood victims.\n(許多人捐款給水災災民。)\nDon't fall victim to online scams.\n(別成為網路詐騙的受害者。)"],["violence","violence(n.)暴力、猛烈\nviolent(adj.)暴力的\nviolently(adv.)猛烈地\ndomestic violence 家庭暴力\nschool violence 校園暴力\nViolence is never the answer to a problem.\n(暴力絕不是解決問題的方法。)\nThe school is working to stop school violence.\n(學校正努力杜絕校園暴力。)"],["violent","violent(adj.)暴力的、猛烈的、激烈的\nviolence(n.)暴力\nviolently(adv.)猛烈地\nviolent storm 猛烈的暴風雨\nviolent crime 暴力犯罪\nParents worry about violent video games.\n(家長們擔心暴力電玩遊戲。)\nA violent storm hit the island last night.\n(昨晚一場猛烈的暴風雨侵襲了這座島。)"],["violet","violet(adj./n.)紫羅蘭色的、紫羅蘭\n(無詞性變化)\nviolet flowers 紫羅蘭花\ndark violet 深紫色\nShe painted her room light violet.\n(她把房間漆成淡紫色。)\nViolets bloom in the spring.\n(紫羅蘭在春天開花。)"],["visible","visible(adj.)看得見的、明顯的\ninvisible(adj.)看不見的\nvisibility(n.)能見度\nvisible to the naked eye 肉眼可見\nclearly visible 清晰可見\nThe mountain is clearly visible on sunny days.\n(晴天時這座山清晰可見。)\nSome stars are not visible to the naked eye.\n(有些星星肉眼看不見。)"],["vision","vision(n.)視力、遠見、願景\nvisual(adj.)視覺的\nvisionary(adj./n.)有遠見的、有遠見的人\npoor vision 視力不好\na vision for the future 對未來的願景\nReading in the dark may harm your vision.\n(在黑暗中看書可能會傷害你的視力。)\nOur principal has a clear vision for the school.\n(我們校長對學校有清楚的願景。)"],["vitamin","vitamin(n.)維他命、維生素\n(無詞性變化)\nvitamin C 維他命C\ntake vitamins 服用維他命\nOranges are rich in vitamin C.\n(柳橙富含維他命C。)\nMy mother takes vitamins every morning.\n(我媽媽每天早上吃維他命。)"],["vivid","vivid(adj.)生動的、鮮明的、鮮豔的\nvividly(adv.)生動地、清楚地\nvivid memory 鮮明的記憶\nvivid colors 鮮豔的色彩\nI still have a vivid memory of my first day at school.\n(我對上學第一天仍記憶猶新。)\nThe painting is full of vivid colors.\n(這幅畫充滿鮮豔的色彩。)"],["vocabulary","vocabulary(n.)字彙、詞彙\n(無詞性變化)\nbuild one's vocabulary 增加字彙量\nvocabulary test 單字測驗\nReading novels helps build your vocabulary.\n(讀小說有助於增加你的字彙量。)\nWe have a vocabulary test every Friday.\n(我們每週五都有單字測驗。)"],["volleyball","volleyball(n.)排球\n(無詞性變化)\nplay volleyball 打排球\nbeach volleyball 沙灘排球\nWe play volleyball in PE class.\n(我們在體育課打排球。)\nBeach volleyball is popular in summer.\n(沙灘排球在夏天很受歡迎。)"],["volume","volume(n.)音量、容量、冊\nvoluminous(adj.)大量的、容量大的\nturn up the volume 調高音量\nvolume of traffic 交通流量\nCould you turn down the volume a little?\n(你可以把音量調小一點嗎？)\nThe library has over ten thousand volumes.\n(這間圖書館藏書超過一萬冊。)"],["voter","voter(n.)選民、投票者\nvote(v./n.)投票、選票\nfirst-time voter 首投族\nvoter turnout 投票率\nThere are many first-time voters in this election.\n(這次選舉有許多首投族。)\nVoter turnout was high this year.\n(今年的投票率很高。)"],["wage(s)","wage(n.)工資、薪水、wages(n.)工資(常用複數)\n(無詞性變化)\nminimum wage 基本工資\nearn a wage 賺取工資\nThe government raised the minimum wage this year.\n(政府今年調漲了基本工資。)\nWorkers asked for higher wages and shorter hours.\n(工人們要求更高的工資和更短的工時。)"],["wagon","wagon(n.)四輪馬車、貨車、手推車\n(無詞性變化)\ncovered wagon 篷車\nstation wagon 旅行車\nThe farmer loaded the hay onto the wagon.\n(農夫把乾草裝上馬車。)\nKids pulled a little red wagon full of toys.\n(孩子們拉著一台裝滿玩具的紅色小拖車。)"],["wander","wander(v./n.)漫遊、閒逛、走神\nwanderer(n.)流浪者\nwander around 四處閒逛\nmind wanders 思緒飄走\nWe wandered around the old streets of Jiufen.\n(我們在九份的老街四處閒逛。)\nMy mind began to wander during the long speech.\n(冗長的演講中我開始走神。)"],["warmth","warmth(n.)溫暖、熱情\nwarm(adj./v.)溫暖的、使暖和\nwarmth of the sun 陽光的溫暖\nfamily warmth 家庭溫暖\nThe cat enjoyed the warmth of the sun.\n(那隻貓享受著陽光的溫暖。)\nWe were moved by the warmth of the local people.\n(我們被當地人的熱情所感動。)"],["warn","warn(v.)警告、提醒\nwarning(n.)警告\nwarn someone of/about 警告某人……\nwarn someone not to 警告某人不要\nThe teacher warned us not to be late again.\n(老師警告我們不要再遲到。)\nThe news warned people about the coming typhoon.\n(新聞警告民眾颱風即將來襲。)"],["waterfall","waterfall(n.)瀑布\n(無詞性變化)\nbeautiful waterfall 美麗的瀑布\nhike to a waterfall 健行到瀑布\nShifen Waterfall is a famous spot in New Taipei.\n(十分瀑布是新北市的著名景點。)\nWe hiked for two hours to see the waterfall.\n(我們健行了兩個小時去看瀑布。)"],["wax","wax(n./v.)蠟、上蠟\nwaxy(adj.)似蠟的\ncandle wax 蠟燭蠟\nwax the floor 給地板打蠟\nThe candle wax dripped onto the table.\n(蠟燭的蠟滴到了桌上。)\nHe waxed his car until it was shiny.\n(他替車子打蠟，直到閃閃發亮。)"],["weaken","weaken(v.)削弱、使變弱\nweak(adj.)虛弱的\nweakness(n.)弱點\nweaken the body 使身體變虛弱\nthe typhoon weakens 颱風減弱\nStaying up late can weaken your body.\n(熬夜會使你的身體變虛弱。)\nThe typhoon weakened after it hit the mountains.\n(颱風撞上山脈後減弱了。)"],["wealthy","wealthy(adj.)富有的、富裕的\nwealth(n.)財富\nwealthy family 富裕的家庭\nthe wealthy 富人\nHe was born into a wealthy family.\n(他出生在一個富裕的家庭。)\nBeing wealthy does not always make people happy.\n(富有不一定會讓人快樂。)"],["weapon","weapon(n.)武器\nweaponry(n.)武器(總稱)\nnuclear weapon 核子武器\nsecret weapon 祕密武器\nCarrying weapons on a plane is not allowed.\n(搭飛機不得攜帶武器。)\nHer smile is her secret weapon.\n(她的微笑是她的祕密武器。)"],["weave","weave(v./n.)編織、織法\nweaver(n.)織布工\nweave a basket 編籃子\nweave through 穿梭於\nThe Atayal people are famous for weaving.\n(泰雅族以編織聞名。)\nThe motorcycle weaved through the traffic.\n(那輛機車在車陣中穿梭。)"],["web","web(n.)網、蜘蛛網、網路\nwebsite(n.)網站\nspider web 蜘蛛網\nsurf the Web 上網\nA spider web hung in the corner of the room.\n(房間角落掛著一張蜘蛛網。)\nI found the information on the Web.\n(我在網路上找到了這個資料。)"],["wed","wed(v.)結婚、與……結婚\nwedding(n.)婚禮\nnewly wed 新婚的\nbe wed to 與……結婚\nThe couple will wed in June.\n(那對情侶將在六月結婚。)\nThe newly wed couple went to Japan for their honeymoon.\n(那對新婚夫妻去日本度蜜月。)"],["weed","weed(n./v.)雜草、除草\n(無詞性變化)\npull weeds 拔草\nweed out 剔除\nGrandpa pulls weeds in the garden every morning.\n(爺爺每天早上在花園拔草。)\nThe coach weeded out the weaker players.\n(教練剔除了實力較弱的球員。)"],["weekly","weekly(adj./adv./n.)每週的、每週一次、週刊\nweek(n.)週\nweekly meeting 每週會議\nweekly magazine 週刊\nWe have a weekly meeting every Monday.\n(我們每週一開週會。)\nThe report is updated weekly.\n(這份報告每週更新一次。)"],["weep","weep(v.)哭泣、流淚\n(無詞性變化)\nweep for joy 喜極而泣\nweep bitterly 痛哭\nShe wept for joy when she got the news.\n(她得知消息時喜極而泣。)\nThe little girl wept over her lost dog.\n(小女孩為她走失的狗哭泣。)"],["wheat","wheat(n.)小麥\n(無詞性變化)\nwhole wheat 全麥\nwheat flour 麵粉\nWhole wheat bread is good for your health.\n(全麥麵包對健康有益。)\nBread and noodles are made from wheat flour.\n(麵包和麵條是用麵粉做的。)"],["whip","whip(n./v.)鞭子、鞭打、攪打\n(無詞性變化)\nwhipped cream 打發的鮮奶油\ncrack the whip 嚴加管教\nWhip the cream until it becomes thick.\n(把鮮奶油打到變濃稠。)\nThe man whipped the horse to make it run faster.\n(那個人鞭打馬匹讓牠跑快一點。)"],["whistle","whistle(n./v.)哨子、口哨、吹口哨\n(無詞性變化)\nblow a whistle 吹哨子\nwhistle a tune 吹口哨哼曲子\nThe referee blew the whistle to start the game.\n(裁判吹哨宣布比賽開始。)\nHe was whistling a happy tune on his way home.\n(他在回家路上吹著輕快的曲子。)"],["wicked","wicked(adj.)邪惡的、惡劣的、淘氣的\nwickedness(n.)邪惡\nwicked witch 邪惡的女巫\nwicked smile 不懷好意的笑容\nThe wicked witch put the princess to sleep.\n(邪惡的女巫讓公主陷入沉睡。)\nHe gave me a wicked smile.\n(他對我露出不懷好意的笑容。)"],["widen","widen(v.)加寬、擴大\nwide(adj.)寬的\nwidth(n.)寬度\nwiden the road 拓寬道路\nwiden the gap 擴大差距\nThe city plans to widen the road next year.\n(市政府計畫明年拓寬這條路。)\nHer eyes widened in surprise.\n(她驚訝得睜大了眼睛。)"],["wipe","wipe(v./n.)擦、擦拭\nwiper(n.)雨刷\nwipe off 擦掉\nwet wipes 濕紙巾\nPlease wipe the table after dinner.\n(晚餐後請擦桌子。)\nShe wiped the tears off her face.\n(她擦掉臉上的淚水。)"],["wisdom","wisdom(n.)智慧、明智\nwise(adj.)有智慧的\nwisdom tooth 智齒\nwords of wisdom 至理名言\nMy grandmother is a woman of great wisdom.\n(我奶奶是一位很有智慧的女性。)\nI had my wisdom tooth pulled last week.\n(我上週拔了智齒。)"],["wrap","wrap(v./n.)包、裹、包裝\nwrapper(n.)包裝紙\nwrapping(n.)包裝材料\nwrap a gift 包禮物\nwrap up 結束、包好\nShe wrapped the gift in red paper.\n(她用紅色的紙包裝禮物。)\nLet's wrap up the meeting now.\n(我們現在結束會議吧。)"],["wrist","wrist(n.)手腕\nwristwatch(n.)手錶\nsprain one's wrist 扭傷手腕\nwrist injury 手腕受傷\nHe hurt his wrist while playing tennis.\n(他打網球時傷了手腕。)\nShe wore a silver bracelet on her wrist.\n(她手腕上戴著一條銀手鍊。)"],["yearly","yearly(adj./adv.)每年的、每年一次\nyear(n.)年\nyearly event 年度活動\nyearly income 年收入\nThe school fair is a yearly event.\n(學校園遊會是一年一度的活動。)\nThe festival is held yearly in October.\n(這個節慶每年十月舉行。)"],["yell","yell(v./n.)大叫、吼叫\n(無詞性變化)\nyell at 對……大吼\nyell for help 大聲呼救\nPlease don't yell at your little brother.\n(請不要對你弟弟大吼。)\nThe boy yelled for help when he fell into the river.\n(男孩掉進河裡時大聲呼救。)"],["yolk","yolk(n.)蛋黃\n(無詞性變化)\negg yolk 蛋黃\nseparate the yolk 分離蛋黃\nI like eggs with soft yolks.\n(我喜歡蛋黃半熟的蛋。)\nSeparate the yolks from the whites first.\n(先把蛋黃和蛋白分開。)"],["youngster","youngster(n.)年輕人、小孩\nyoung(adj.)年輕的\nlocal youngsters 當地年輕人\ntalented youngster 有天分的年輕人\nThe park is full of youngsters on weekends.\n(週末公園裡滿是年輕人。)\nThe coach is training a group of talented youngsters.\n(教練正在訓練一群有天分的年輕人。)"],["zipper","zipper(n./v.)拉鍊、拉上拉鍊\nzip(v.)拉上拉鍊\nzip code 郵遞區號\npull up a zipper 拉上拉鍊\nThe zipper on my jacket is broken.\n(我外套上的拉鍊壞了。)\nPull up your zipper before you go out.\n(出門前把拉鍊拉上。)"],["zone","zone(n./v.)地帶、區域、劃分區域\n(無詞性變化)\ntime zone 時區\nno-parking zone 禁止停車區\nTaiwan and Japan are in different time zones.\n(台灣和日本處於不同的時區。)\nYou can't park here. It's a no-parking zone.\n(你不能停在這裡，這是禁止停車區。)"]],"4":[["abandon","abandon(v.)拋棄、放棄\nabandoned(adj.)被拋棄的、廢棄的\nabandonment(n.)拋棄、放棄\nabandon a plan 放棄計畫\nabandoned building 廢棄建築\nThe crew had to abandon the sinking ship.\n(船員們不得不棄船逃生。)\nMany abandoned dogs are waiting for new homes.\n(許多被遺棄的狗正在等待新家。)"],["absolute","absolute(adj.)絕對的、完全的\nabsolutely(adv.)絕對地、完全地\nabsolute truth 絕對的真理\nabsolute silence 一片寂靜\nThere was absolute silence in the exam room.\n(考場裡一片寂靜。)\nI have absolute trust in my best friend.\n(我完全信任我最好的朋友。)"],["absorb","absorb(v.)吸收、使專心\nabsorption(n.)吸收\nabsorbed(adj.)專心的\nabsorb water 吸水\nbe absorbed in 專注於\nPlants absorb water through their roots.\n(植物透過根部吸收水分。)\nHe was so absorbed in the novel that he missed his stop.\n(他太專注於那本小說，結果坐過站了。)"],["abstract","abstract(adj.)抽象的\nabstraction(n.)抽象概念\nabstract idea 抽象概念\nabstract art 抽象藝術\nLove is an abstract idea that is hard to explain.\n(愛是一個難以解釋的抽象概念。)\nI don't really understand abstract art.\n(我不太懂抽象藝術。)"],["academic","academic(adj.)學術的、學業的\nacademy(n.)學院、專科學校\nacademically(adv.)學業上\nacademic performance 學業表現\nacademic year 學年\nHer academic performance has improved this year.\n(她今年的學業表現進步了。)\nThe new academic year starts in September.\n(新學年從九月開始。)"],["accent","accent(n.)口音、重音\naccented(adj.)帶口音的\na strong accent 濃重的口音\nBritish accent 英國腔\nHe speaks English with a strong Spanish accent.\n(他說英文帶有濃重的西班牙口音。)\nWhere does the accent fall in this word?\n(這個字的重音在哪裡？)"],["acceptance","acceptance(n.)接受、認可\naccept(v.)接受\nacceptable(adj.)可接受的\nacceptance letter 錄取通知\ngain acceptance 獲得認可\nShe received an acceptance letter from the university.\n(她收到了大學的錄取通知書。)\nThe new idea slowly gained acceptance.\n(這個新想法慢慢獲得了認可。)"],["access","access(n./v.)接近、使用權、存取\naccessible(adj.)可接近的、可使用的\nhave access to 能使用、能接近\nInternet access 網路連線\nAll students have access to the school library.\n(所有學生都可以使用學校圖書館。)\nYou need a password to access this website.\n(你需要密碼才能進入這個網站。)"],["accidental","accidental(adj.)意外的、偶然的\naccident(n.)意外\naccidentally(adv.)意外地、不小心\naccidental death 意外死亡\naccidental discovery 意外的發現\nThe discovery of the medicine was accidental.\n(這種藥的發現是個意外。)\nI accidentally deleted the file.\n(我不小心把檔案刪掉了。)"],["accompany","accompany(v.)陪伴、伴隨、為⋯伴奏\ncompanion(n.)同伴\naccompaniment(n.)伴奏\nbe accompanied by 由⋯陪同\naccompany on the piano 用鋼琴伴奏\nChildren must be accompanied by an adult.\n(孩童必須由成人陪同。)\nShe accompanied her grandmother to the hospital.\n(她陪奶奶去醫院。)"],["accomplish(ment)","accomplish(v.)完成、達成、accomplishment(n.)成就\naccomplished(adj.)有造詣的、熟練的\naccomplish a goal 達成目標\na great accomplishment 偉大的成就\nWith teamwork, we accomplished the task on time.\n(靠著團隊合作，我們準時完成了任務。)\nWinning the prize was a great accomplishment for her.\n(得獎對她來說是一項了不起的成就。)"],["accountant","accountant(n.)會計師\naccount(n.)帳戶、帳目\naccounting(n.)會計學\ncertified accountant 合格會計師\nhire an accountant 聘請會計師\nMy mother works as an accountant at a bank.\n(我媽媽在銀行擔任會計。)\nThe company hired an accountant to check its records.\n(公司聘請了一位會計師查帳。)"],["accuracy","accuracy(n.)準確、精確\naccurate(adj.)準確的\naccurately(adv.)準確地\nwith accuracy 準確地\ncheck the accuracy 檢查正確性\nPlease check the accuracy of your answers.\n(請檢查你答案的正確性。)\nThe weather report was given with great accuracy.\n(這份氣象預報非常準確。)"],["accuse","accuse(v.)控告、指責\naccusation(n.)指控\naccuse... of 指控⋯犯了\nthe accused 被告\nHe was accused of stealing a bike.\n(他被指控偷了一輛腳踏車。)\nDon't accuse me of lying without proof.\n(沒有證據就別指責我說謊。)"],["acid","acid(n./adj.)酸、酸性的\nacidic(adj.)酸性的\nacid rain 酸雨\ncitric acid 檸檬酸\nAcid rain can damage forests and lakes.\n(酸雨會破壞森林和湖泊。)\nLemons contain a lot of citric acid.\n(檸檬含有大量檸檬酸。)"],["acquaintance","acquaintance(n.)熟人、認識、了解\nacquaint(v.)使認識、使熟悉\nmake one's acquaintance 結識某人\na casual acquaintance 泛泛之交\nHe is not a close friend, just an acquaintance.\n(他不是密友，只是認識的人。)\nI made her acquaintance at a summer camp.\n(我在夏令營認識了她。)"],["acquire","acquire(v.)獲得、習得\nacquisition(n.)獲得、習得\nacquire knowledge 獲得知識\nacquire a skill 習得技能\nChildren acquire language very quickly.\n(孩子學習語言非常快。)\nShe acquired many useful skills during her internship.\n(她在實習期間學到很多實用技能。)"],["adapt","adapt(v.)適應、改編\nadaptation(n.)適應、改編作品\nadaptable(adj.)能適應的\nadapt to 適應⋯\nbe adapted from 改編自\nIt took me a month to adapt to my new school.\n(我花了一個月適應新學校。)\nThe film was adapted from a popular novel.\n(這部電影改編自一本暢銷小說。)"],["addict","addict(n./v.)上癮者、使上癮\naddiction(n.)上癮、成癮\naddicted(adj.)上癮的\nbe addicted to 對⋯上癮\ngame addict 遊戲成癮者\nMany teenagers are addicted to their phones.\n(許多青少年對手機上癮。)\nHe used to be a game addict, but he has changed.\n(他以前是遊戲成癮者，但現在已經改變了。)"],["adequate","adequate(adj.)足夠的、適當的\nadequately(adv.)足夠地\nadequate sleep 充足的睡眠\nadequate supply 充足的供應\nTeenagers need adequate sleep to stay healthy.\n(青少年需要充足的睡眠以保持健康。)\nThe room is small but adequate for two people.\n(這房間雖小，但兩個人住剛好夠。)"],["adjust(ment)","adjust(v.)調整、適應、adjustment(n.)調整、適應\nadjustable(adj.)可調整的\nadjust to 適應⋯\nmake an adjustment 做調整\nYou can adjust the height of this chair.\n(你可以調整這張椅子的高度。)\nIt took him time to adjust to life in the city.\n(他花了一段時間才適應城市生活。)"],["admirable","admirable(adj.)令人欽佩的、值得讚賞的\nadmire(v.)欽佩、讚賞\nadmiration(n.)欽佩\nadmirable effort 令人欽佩的努力\nadmirable courage 令人敬佩的勇氣\nHer courage in the face of danger was admirable.\n(她面對危險時的勇氣令人欽佩。)\nHe made an admirable effort to help the poor.\n(他為幫助窮人付出了令人敬佩的努力。)"],["admiration","admiration(n.)欽佩、讚賞\nadmire(v.)欽佩、讚賞\nadmirable(adj.)令人欽佩的\nwith admiration 欽佩地\ndeep admiration 深深的欽佩\nThe students looked at the scientist with admiration.\n(學生們欽佩地看著那位科學家。)\nI have great admiration for doctors and nurses.\n(我非常欽佩醫生和護理師。)"],["admission","admission(n.)入場(許可)、入學許可、承認\nadmit(v.)承認、准許進入\nadmission fee 入場費\nfree admission 免費入場\nAdmission to the museum is free on Sundays.\n(週日博物館免費入場。)\nShe applied for admission to a top university.\n(她申請進入一所頂尖大學就讀。)"],["adopt","adopt(v.)收養、採用\nadoption(n.)收養、採用\nadopted(adj.)被收養的\nadopt a child 收養孩子\nadopt a plan 採用計畫\nThey adopted a cat from the animal shelter.\n(他們從動物收容所領養了一隻貓。)\nThe school adopted a new uniform policy.\n(學校採用了新的制服規定。)"],["agency","agency(n.)代理商、機構、仲介\nagent(n.)代理人\ntravel agency 旅行社\ngovernment agency 政府機構\nWe booked our trip through a travel agency.\n(我們透過旅行社預訂了行程。)\nThe agency helps people find jobs.\n(這家仲介公司幫助人們找工作。)"],["agent","agent(n.)代理人、經紀人、特務\nagency(n.)代理商、機構\ntravel agent 旅行業者\nsecret agent 特務\nThe singer's agent arranged the concert.\n(那位歌手的經紀人安排了演唱會。)\nHe plays a secret agent in the new movie.\n(他在新電影中飾演一名特務。)"],["aggressive","aggressive(adj.)具攻擊性的、積極進取的\naggression(n.)攻擊、侵略\naggressively(adv.)具侵略性地\naggressive behavior 攻擊性行為\naggressive dog 兇猛的狗\nStay away from that dog; it's aggressive.\n(離那隻狗遠一點，牠很兇。)\nThe company has an aggressive plan to expand.\n(那家公司有積極擴張的計畫。)"],["agreeable","agreeable(adj.)令人愉快的、欣然同意的\nagree(v.)同意\nagreement(n.)協議、同意\nagreeable weather 宜人的天氣\nbe agreeable to 同意⋯\nWe spent an agreeable evening with friends.\n(我們和朋友度過了一個愉快的夜晚。)\nIs your father agreeable to the plan?\n(你爸爸同意這個計畫嗎？)"],["alcohol","alcohol(n.)酒精、酒\nalcoholic(adj./n.)含酒精的、酗酒者\ndrink alcohol 喝酒\nalcohol-free 不含酒精的\nYou must not drive after drinking alcohol.\n(喝酒後絕對不可以開車。)\nClean the wound with alcohol first.\n(先用酒精清潔傷口。)"],["alert","alert(adj./v./n.)警覺的、使警覺、警報\nalertness(n.)警覺\nstay alert 保持警覺\non the alert 提高警覺\nDrivers must stay alert on the road.\n(駕駛人在路上必須保持警覺。)\nThe app alerts you when an earthquake is coming.\n(這個應用程式會在地震來臨時向你發出警報。)"],["allowance","allowance(n.)零用錢、津貼、允許量\nallow(v.)允許\nweekly allowance 每週零用錢\nmake allowances for 體諒、考慮到\nMy parents give me a weekly allowance.\n(我爸媽每週給我零用錢。)\nThe baggage allowance on this flight is 20 kilograms.\n(這班飛機的行李限額是二十公斤。)"],["alternative","alternative(adj./n.)替代的、另類的、替代方案\nalternatively(adv.)或者\nalternative energy 替代能源\nhave no alternative 別無選擇\nSolar power is a clean alternative to oil.\n(太陽能是石油的乾淨替代能源。)\nWe had no alternative but to cancel the trip.\n(我們別無選擇，只好取消旅行。)"],["amateur","amateur(adj./n.)業餘的、業餘愛好者\n(無詞性變化)\namateur photographer 業餘攝影師\namateur team 業餘隊伍\nHe is an amateur, but his photos are amazing.\n(他是業餘的，但他的照片很驚人。)\nShe plays in an amateur basketball team.\n(她在一支業餘籃球隊打球。)"],["ambiguous","ambiguous(adj.)模稜兩可的、含糊的\nambiguity(n.)模稜兩可\nambiguous answer 模稜兩可的回答\nambiguous meaning 含糊的意思\nHis ambiguous answer made us more confused.\n(他模稜兩可的回答讓我們更困惑。)\nThis sentence is ambiguous and needs to be rewritten.\n(這個句子意思不明確，需要改寫。)"],["ambitious","ambitious(adj.)有雄心的、野心勃勃的\nambition(n.)抱負、野心\nambitious goal 遠大的目標\nambitious plan 雄心勃勃的計畫\nShe is ambitious and wants to start her own company.\n(她很有抱負，想創辦自己的公司。)\nFinishing the project in a week is an ambitious goal.\n(一週內完成這個專案是個遠大的目標。)"],["amuse(ment)","amuse(v.)逗樂、使開心、amusement(n.)娛樂、樂趣\namusing(adj.)有趣的\namused(adj.)覺得好笑的\namusement park 遊樂園\nto one's amusement 令某人覺得好笑的是\nThe clown amused the children with funny tricks.\n(小丑用滑稽的把戲逗樂孩子們。)\nWe spent the whole day at the amusement park.\n(我們在遊樂園玩了一整天。)"],["analysis","analysis(n.)分析(複數 analyses)\nanalyze(v.)分析\nanalytical(adj.)分析的\ndata analysis 數據分析\nin the final analysis 歸根究柢\nThe scientist did a careful analysis of the water.\n(那位科學家仔細分析了這些水。)\nData analysis is an important skill today.\n(數據分析是現今很重要的技能。)"],["analyze","analyze(v.)分析\nanalysis(n.)分析\nanalyst(n.)分析師\nanalyze data 分析數據\nanalyze the problem 分析問題\nLet's analyze why we lost the game.\n(我們來分析一下為什麼輸了比賽。)\nThe students analyzed the results of the experiment.\n(學生們分析了實驗的結果。)"],["ancestor","ancestor(n.)祖先\nancestral(adj.)祖先的\nworship ancestors 祭祖\ncommon ancestor 共同祖先\nMany Taiwanese families honor their ancestors on Tomb Sweeping Day.\n(許多台灣家庭在清明節祭拜祖先。)\nMy ancestors came from Fujian.\n(我的祖先來自福建。)"],["anniversary","anniversary(n.)週年紀念日\n(無詞性變化)\nwedding anniversary 結婚週年紀念\nsilver anniversary 二十五週年紀念\nMy parents celebrated their wedding anniversary at a nice restaurant.\n(我爸媽在一家不錯的餐廳慶祝結婚週年。)\nThe school will celebrate its 60th anniversary next year.\n(學校明年將慶祝六十週年校慶。)"],["annoy","annoy(v.)使煩惱、惹惱\nannoyance(n.)惱怒\nannoying(adj.)惱人的\nannoyed(adj.)感到惱怒的\nbe annoyed with 對⋯生氣\nannoying noise 惱人的噪音\nHis loud music really annoys me.\n(他大聲放音樂真的讓我很煩。)\nShe was annoyed with her brother for taking her phone.\n(她因為弟弟拿走她的手機而生氣。)"],["annual","annual(adj.)每年的、年度的\nannually(adv.)每年\nannual meeting 年會\nannual income 年收入\nThe school holds an annual sports day in November.\n(學校每年十一月舉辦運動會。)\nThe festival is held annually in the spring.\n(這個節慶每年春天舉行。)"],["anxiety","anxiety(n.)焦慮、擔憂\nanxious(adj.)焦慮的、渴望的\nanxiously(adv.)焦急地\ntest anxiety 考試焦慮\nfeel anxiety about 對⋯感到焦慮\nMany students feel anxiety before big exams.\n(許多學生在大考前會感到焦慮。)\nDeep breathing can help reduce anxiety.\n(深呼吸可以幫助減輕焦慮。)"],["apology","apology(n.)道歉\napologize(v.)道歉\napologetic(adj.)道歉的、愧疚的\nmake an apology 道歉\naccept an apology 接受道歉\nHe made an apology for being late.\n(他為遲到道歉。)\nPlease accept my sincere apology.\n(請接受我誠摯的道歉。)"],["apparent","apparent(adj.)明顯的、表面上的\napparently(adv.)顯然、似乎\nfor no apparent reason 無緣無故\nit is apparent that 顯然⋯\nIt was apparent that she was very tired.\n(很明顯她非常疲累。)\nThe baby started crying for no apparent reason.\n(寶寶無緣無故地哭了起來。)"],["applicant","applicant(n.)申請人\napply(v.)申請\napplication(n.)申請\njob applicant 求職者\nsuccessful applicant 錄取者\nThere were over 100 applicants for the job.\n(這份工作有超過一百位申請人。)\nAll applicants must take an interview.\n(所有申請人都必須參加面試。)"],["application","application(n.)申請、應用、應用程式\napply(v.)申請、應用\napplicant(n.)申請人\napplication form 申請表\nfill out an application 填寫申請表\nPlease fill out the application form carefully.\n(請仔細填寫申請表。)\nThis phone application helps you learn new words.\n(這個手機應用程式能幫你學新單字。)"],["appoint(ment)","appoint(v.)任命、指定、appointment(n.)約會、預約、任命\n(無詞性變化)\nmake an appointment 預約\nbe appointed as 被任命為\nI made an appointment with the dentist for Friday.\n(我預約了星期五看牙醫。)\nShe was appointed as the new principal.\n(她被任命為新校長。)"],["appreciation","appreciation(n.)感激、欣賞、增值\nappreciate(v.)感激、欣賞\nappreciative(adj.)感激的\nin appreciation of 為了感謝⋯\nart appreciation 藝術鑑賞\nWe gave him a card in appreciation of his help.\n(我們送他一張卡片感謝他的幫忙。)\nThe course aims to develop students' music appreciation.\n(這門課旨在培養學生的音樂欣賞能力。)"],["appropriate","appropriate(adj.)適當的、合適的\nappropriately(adv.)適當地\ninappropriate(adj.)不適當的\nappropriate for 適合⋯\nappropriate behavior 合宜的行為\nJeans are not appropriate for a job interview.\n(牛仔褲不適合穿去面試。)\nPlease choose an appropriate word to fill in the blank.\n(請選一個適當的字填入空格。)"],["approval","approval(n.)贊成、批准、認可\napprove(v.)贊成、批准\nwith one's approval 經某人同意\nseek approval 尋求認可\nThe plan needs the principal's approval.\n(這個計畫需要校長的批准。)\nTeenagers often seek approval from their friends.\n(青少年經常尋求朋友的認同。)"],["aquarium","aquarium(n.)水族館、魚缸\n(無詞性變化)\nvisit an aquarium 參觀水族館\nhome aquarium 家用魚缸\nWe saw sharks and turtles at the aquarium.\n(我們在水族館看到鯊魚和海龜。)\nHe keeps tropical fish in his aquarium.\n(他在魚缸裡養熱帶魚。)"],["arch","arch(n./v.)拱門、拱形、使成拱形\n(無詞性變化)\nstone arch 石拱門\narch one's back 拱起背\nWe walked under a beautiful stone arch.\n(我們從一座美麗的石拱門下走過。)\nThe cat arched its back when it saw the dog.\n(那隻貓看到狗時拱起了背。)"],["arise","arise(v.)出現、發生、產生\n(無詞性變化)\nproblems arise 問題出現\narise from 起因於\nIf any problems arise, call me at once.\n(如果出現任何問題，馬上打電話給我。)\nMany accidents arise from careless driving.\n(許多事故起因於駕駛不小心。)"],["arms","arms(n.)武器、軍火\narm(v.)武裝\narmed(adj.)武裝的\narms race 軍備競賽\ntake up arms 拿起武器\nThe government stopped selling arms to that country.\n(政府停止對那個國家出售武器。)\nThe two countries were in an arms race.\n(那兩國當時正在進行軍備競賽。)"],["artificial","artificial(adj.)人造的、人工的、虛假的\nartificially(adv.)人工地\nartificial intelligence 人工智慧\nartificial flowers 人造花\nArtificial intelligence is changing the way we learn.\n(人工智慧正在改變我們學習的方式。)\nThis juice contains no artificial colors.\n(這種果汁不含人工色素。)"],["artistic","artistic(adj.)藝術的、有藝術天分的\nart(n.)藝術\nartist(n.)藝術家\nartistic talent 藝術天分\nartistic style 藝術風格\nShe has great artistic talent.\n(她很有藝術天分。)\nThe café is decorated in an artistic style.\n(那家咖啡廳裝潢得很有藝術風格。)"],["ashamed","ashamed(adj.)感到羞恥的、慚愧的\nshame(n.)羞恥\nbe ashamed of 對⋯感到羞愧\nfeel ashamed 感到慚愧\nHe felt ashamed of lying to his parents.\n(他對向父母說謊感到很慚愧。)\nYou should never be ashamed of who you are.\n(你永遠不該為自己是誰而感到羞愧。)"],["aspect","aspect(n.)方面、觀點、外觀\n(無詞性變化)\nevery aspect of 各方面\nan important aspect 重要的一面\nStress can affect every aspect of your life.\n(壓力會影響你生活的各個方面。)\nLet's look at the problem from a different aspect.\n(我們從另一個角度來看這個問題。)"],["aspirin","aspirin(n.)阿斯匹靈\n(無詞性變化)\ntake an aspirin 吃一顆阿斯匹靈\naspirin tablet 阿斯匹靈錠\nShe took an aspirin for her headache.\n(她吃了一顆阿斯匹靈止頭痛。)\nAsk a doctor before giving aspirin to children.\n(給孩童服用阿斯匹靈前要先問醫生。)"],["assemble","assemble(v.)集合、組裝\nassembly(n.)集會、組裝\nassemble furniture 組裝家具\nassemble in 在⋯集合\nAll students assembled in the hall for the ceremony.\n(所有學生在禮堂集合參加典禮。)\nIt took us two hours to assemble the bookshelf.\n(我們花了兩小時組裝這個書架。)"],["assembly","assembly(n.)集會、議會、組裝\nassemble(v.)集合、組裝\nschool assembly 朝會、全校集會\nassembly line 裝配線\nWe have a school assembly every Monday morning.\n(我們每週一早上有朝會。)\nHe works on an assembly line in a car factory.\n(他在汽車工廠的裝配線上工作。)"],["assign(ment)","assign(v.)分配、指派、assignment(n.)作業、任務\n(無詞性變化)\nassign a task 指派任務\nhand in an assignment 交作業\nThe teacher assigned us a group project.\n(老師分配給我們一項小組專題。)\nDon't forget to hand in your assignment by Friday.\n(別忘了在星期五前交作業。)"],["assistance","assistance(n.)協助、援助\nassist(v.)協助\nassistant(n.)助理\nfinancial assistance 經濟援助\nbe of assistance 有幫助\nIf you need any assistance, please let me know.\n(如果你需要任何協助，請告訴我。)\nThe poor family received financial assistance from the city.\n(那個貧困家庭獲得了市政府的經濟援助。)"],["associate","associate(adj./n./v.)副的、夥伴、聯想、交往\nassociation(n.)協會、關聯\nbe associated with 與⋯有關\nassociate professor 副教授\nMany people associate summer with the beach.\n(很多人會把夏天和海灘聯想在一起。)\nSmoking is associated with many health problems.\n(吸菸與許多健康問題有關。)"],["association","association(n.)協會、聯合、關聯\nassociate(v.)聯想、交往\nin association with 與⋯合作\nparents' association 家長會\nThe event was held in association with local schools.\n(這場活動是與當地學校合辦的。)\nShe joined the student association last year.\n(她去年加入了學生會。)"],["assurance","assurance(n.)保證、確信、把握\nassure(v.)保證、使確信\ngive an assurance 給予保證\nquality assurance 品質保證\nHe gave me his assurance that he would help.\n(他向我保證他會幫忙。)\nShe answered the questions with assurance.\n(她很有把握地回答了這些問題。)"],["assure","assure(v.)向⋯保證、使確信\nassurance(n.)保證\nassured(adj.)確定的、有把握的\nassure... of 向⋯保證\nrest assured 放心\nI assure you that the food is fresh.\n(我向你保證這食物很新鮮。)\nRest assured that we will take good care of your dog.\n(請放心，我們會好好照顧你的狗。)"],["athletic","athletic(adj.)運動的、體格健壯的\nathlete(n.)運動員\nathletics(n.)田徑運動\nathletic ability 運動能力\nathletic shoes 運動鞋\nMy brother is tall and athletic.\n(我哥哥又高又健壯。)\nShe has great athletic ability.\n(她的運動能力很強。)"],["atmosphere","atmosphere(n.)大氣、氣氛\natmospheric(adj.)大氣的、有氣氛的\nfriendly atmosphere 友善的氣氛\nthe earth's atmosphere 地球大氣層\nThe café has a warm and relaxing atmosphere.\n(那家咖啡廳有溫暖放鬆的氣氛。)\nPollution is harming the earth's atmosphere.\n(汙染正在危害地球的大氣層。)"],["atom","atom(n.)原子、微量\natomic(adj.)原子的\nhydrogen atom 氫原子\nsplit the atom 分裂原子\nEverything around us is made of atoms.\n(我們周遭的一切都是由原子構成的。)\nA water molecule has two hydrogen atoms.\n(一個水分子有兩個氫原子。)"],["atomic","atomic(adj.)原子的、原子能的\natom(n.)原子\natomic bomb 原子彈\natomic energy 原子能\nThe atomic bomb was first used in 1945.\n(原子彈在1945年首次被使用。)\nScientists are studying atomic energy for power.\n(科學家正在研究用原子能來發電。)"],["attach(ment)","attach(v.)貼上、附加、使依戀、attachment(n.)附件、依戀\nattached(adj.)附加的、依戀的\nbe attached to 依戀⋯\nemail attachment 電子郵件附件\nPlease attach a photo to your application.\n(請在申請表上附一張照片。)\nThe child is very attached to his grandmother.\n(那個孩子非常依戀他的奶奶。)"],["attraction","attraction(n.)吸引力、名勝\nattract(v.)吸引\nattractive(adj.)有吸引力的\ntourist attraction 觀光景點\nmain attraction 主要賣點\nTaipei 101 is a popular tourist attraction.\n(台北101是熱門的觀光景點。)\nThe main attraction of the city is its night markets.\n(這座城市最吸引人的是它的夜市。)"],["audio","audio(adj.)聲音的、音訊的\n(無詞性變化)\naudio file 音訊檔\naudio guide 語音導覽\nYou can download the audio files for this lesson.\n(你可以下載這一課的音訊檔。)\nThe museum offers a free audio guide.\n(博物館提供免費的語音導覽。)"],["authentic","authentic(adj.)真正的、道地的\nauthenticity(n.)真實性\nauthentic food 道地的食物\nauthentic document 真實文件\nThis restaurant serves authentic Italian food.\n(這家餐廳供應道地的義大利菜。)\nExperts say the painting is authentic.\n(專家說這幅畫是真跡。)"],["authority","authority(n.)權力、權威、當局(常用複數)\nauthorize(v.)授權\nauthoritative(adj.)權威的\nthe authorities 當局\nan authority on 在⋯方面的權威\nThe local authorities closed the road for safety.\n(地方當局為了安全封閉了道路。)\nShe is an authority on Taiwanese history.\n(她是台灣史方面的權威。)"],["autobiography","autobiography(n.)自傳\nbiography(n.)傳記\nautobiographical(adj.)自傳的\nwrite an autobiography 寫自傳\nfamous autobiography 知名自傳\nMany students need an autobiography for college applications.\n(許多學生申請大學時需要準備自傳。)\nThe singer published his autobiography last year.\n(那位歌手去年出版了他的自傳。)"],["autograph","autograph(n./v.)親筆簽名、簽名\n(無詞性變化)\nask for an autograph 要求簽名\nautograph book 簽名簿\nThe fans waited for hours to get his autograph.\n(粉絲們等了好幾個小時要他的簽名。)\nThe author autographed copies of her new book.\n(作者在她的新書上簽名。)"],["await","await(v.)等候、等待\n(無詞性變化)\nawait one's reply 等候某人回覆\neagerly await 熱切期待\nWe are eagerly awaiting the results of the exam.\n(我們正熱切等待考試結果。)\nA big surprise awaits you at home.\n(家裡有個大驚喜在等著你。)"],["bald","bald(adj.)禿頭的、光禿的\nbaldness(n.)禿頭\ngo bald 禿頭\nbald spot 禿的地方\nMy uncle started to go bald in his thirties.\n(我叔叔三十多歲就開始禿頭。)\nThe bald eagle is the national bird of the United States.\n(白頭海鵰是美國的國鳥。)"],["ballet","ballet(n.)芭蕾舞\nballerina(n.)芭蕾舞女伶\nballet dancer 芭蕾舞者\nballet class 芭蕾舞課\nShe has taken ballet classes since she was five.\n(她從五歲起就開始上芭蕾舞課。)\nWe watched a ballet performance at the National Theater.\n(我們在國家戲劇院觀賞了一場芭蕾舞演出。)"],["bandage","bandage(n./v.)繃帶、用繃帶包紮\n(無詞性變化)\napply a bandage 包上繃帶\nbandage a wound 包紮傷口\nThe nurse wrapped a bandage around my injured ankle.\n(護理師在我受傷的腳踝上纏了繃帶。)\nHe quickly bandaged the cut on his friend's arm.\n(他迅速包紮了朋友手臂上的傷口。)"],["bankrupt","bankrupt(adj./v./n.)破產的、使破產、破產者\nbankruptcy(n.)破產\ngo bankrupt 破產\ndeclare bankruptcy 宣告破產\nThe company went bankrupt after years of losses.\n(那家公司虧損多年後破產了。)\nBad investments nearly bankrupted the family.\n(錯誤的投資幾乎讓這個家庭破產。)"],["bargain","bargain(n./v.)便宜貨、協議、討價還價\n(無詞性變化)\na real bargain 真划算的東西\nbargain with 與…討價還價\nAt this price, the jacket is a real bargain.\n(以這個價格來說，這件夾克真的很划算。)\nTourists often bargain with vendors at night markets.\n(觀光客常在夜市和攤販討價還價。)"],["barrier","barrier(n.)障礙、柵欄、隔閡\n(無詞性變化)\nlanguage barrier 語言隔閡\nbreak down barriers 打破障礙\nThe language barrier made it hard for him to make friends abroad.\n(語言隔閡讓他在國外很難交到朋友。)\nPolice put up barriers to keep the crowd back.\n(警方架起柵欄擋住人群。)"],["basin","basin(n.)臉盆、盆地、流域\n(無詞性變化)\nwash basin 洗臉盆\nTaipei Basin 台北盆地\nTaipei is located in a basin surrounded by mountains.\n(台北位在一個群山環繞的盆地中。)\nShe filled the basin with warm water.\n(她把臉盆裝滿溫水。)"],["battery","battery(n.)電池\n(無詞性變化)\nbattery life 電池續航力\ncharge the battery 充電\nMy phone's battery dies quickly when I play games.\n(我玩遊戲時手機電池很快就沒電。)\nRemember to charge the battery before the trip.\n(旅行前記得把電池充飽。)"],["beggar","beggar(n.)乞丐\nbeg(v.)乞討、懇求\nstreet beggar 街頭乞丐\nbeggars can't be choosers 乞丐沒有挑選的權利\nA beggar sat outside the station asking for money.\n(一名乞丐坐在車站外乞討。)\nBeggars can't be choosers, so I took the last seat.\n(沒得挑剔，所以我坐了最後一個位子。)"],["behavior","behavior(n.)行為、舉止\nbehave(v.)表現、守規矩\nbehavioral(adj.)行為的\ngood behavior 良好行為\nhuman behavior 人類行為\nThe teacher praised the students for their good behavior.\n(老師稱讚學生們的良好表現。)\nScientists study animal behavior in the wild.\n(科學家研究野生動物的行為。)"],["bin","bin(n.)箱子、垃圾桶\n(無詞性變化)\nrecycling bin 資源回收桶\ntrash bin 垃圾桶\nPlease put empty bottles in the recycling bin.\n(請把空瓶放進資源回收桶。)\nHe threw the old letters into the trash bin.\n(他把舊信丟進垃圾桶。)"],["biography","biography(n.)傳記\nbiographer(n.)傳記作者\nbiographical(adj.)傳記的\nautobiography 自傳\nwrite a biography 撰寫傳記\nI am reading a biography of Steve Jobs.\n(我正在讀賈伯斯的傳記。)\nHer biography describes her difficult childhood.\n(她的傳記描述了她艱困的童年。)"],["biology","biology(n.)生物學\nbiologist(n.)生物學家\nbiological(adj.)生物的\nmarine biology 海洋生物學\nbiology class 生物課\nShe wants to study marine biology in college.\n(她想在大學念海洋生物學。)\nWe learned about cells in biology class.\n(我們在生物課學到細胞。)"],["blade","blade(n.)刀刃、刀片、葉片\n(無詞性變化)\nrazor blade 刮鬍刀片\nblade of grass 草葉\nBe careful—the blade of this knife is very sharp.\n(小心，這把刀的刀刃非常鋒利。)\nDew covered every blade of grass in the morning.\n(早晨露水覆蓋著每一片草葉。)"],["blend","blend(v./n.)混合、融合、混合物\nblender(n.)果汁機\nblend in 融入\na blend of 混合…\nBlend the bananas and milk until smooth.\n(把香蕉和牛奶攪拌到滑順。)\nThe new student tried hard to blend in with his classmates.\n(那位新同學努力融入同學之中。)"],["blessing","blessing(n.)祝福、幸事\nbless(v.)祝福、保佑\na blessing in disguise 因禍得福\ncount one's blessings 知足惜福\nMissing the bus turned out to be a blessing in disguise.\n(沒搭上公車結果反而因禍得福。)\nMy parents gave their blessing to my plan to study abroad.\n(我父母祝福我出國念書的計畫。)"],["blink","blink(v./n.)眨眼、閃爍\n(無詞性變化)\nin the blink of an eye 一眨眼間\nblink back tears 眨眼忍住淚水\nThe summer vacation was over in the blink of an eye.\n(暑假一眨眼就結束了。)\nThe lights on the tree blinked all night.\n(樹上的燈整晚閃爍著。)"],["bloom","bloom(n./v.)花、開花、繁盛\n(無詞性變化)\nin full bloom 盛開\ncome into bloom 開始開花\nThe cherry blossoms are in full bloom on Yangmingshan.\n(陽明山上的櫻花正盛開。)\nThese flowers only bloom in spring.\n(這些花只在春天開花。)"],["blossom","blossom(n./v.)(果樹的)花、開花、發展\n(無詞性變化)\ncherry blossoms 櫻花\nblossom into 發展成\nMany people go hiking to see the cherry blossoms.\n(許多人去健行賞櫻花。)\nTheir friendship blossomed into love.\n(他們的友誼發展成了愛情。)"],["boast","boast(v./n.)自誇、以擁有…自豪、誇耀\nboastful(adj.)自誇的\nboast about 吹噓…\nproud boast 引以為傲的事\nHe likes to boast about his test scores.\n(他喜歡吹噓自己的考試成績。)\nThe city boasts the tallest building in the country.\n(這座城市擁有全國最高的建築。)"],["bond","bond(n./v.)聯繫、羈絆、債券、結合\nbonding(n.)建立感情\nstrong bond 緊密的連結\nbond with 與…建立感情\nThere is a strong bond between the two sisters.\n(那兩姊妹之間的感情很深厚。)\nPlaying sports helps teammates bond with each other.\n(一起運動有助於隊友建立感情。)"],["bounce","bounce(v./n.)彈跳、反彈\nbouncy(adj.)有彈性的\nbounce back 恢復、反彈\nbounce a ball 拍球\nThe ball bounced off the wall and hit the window.\n(球從牆上彈開打到窗戶。)\nShe bounced back quickly after losing the game.\n(輸了比賽後她很快就振作起來。)"],["bracelet","bracelet(n.)手鐲、手鍊\n(無詞性變化)\ngold bracelet 金手鐲\nwear a bracelet 戴手鍊\nShe wore a silver bracelet her grandmother gave her.\n(她戴著祖母送她的銀手鍊。)\nI made a bracelet for my best friend's birthday.\n(我做了一條手鍊送給好朋友當生日禮物。)"],["breed","breed(n./v.)品種、繁殖、飼養\nbreeder(n.)飼養者\nbreeding(n.)繁殖、教養\nbreed of dog 狗的品種\nbreed animals 飼養動物\nThe golden retriever is a popular breed of dog.\n(黃金獵犬是很受歡迎的狗品種。)\nMosquitoes breed in standing water.\n(蚊子在積水中繁殖。)"],["bridegroom/groom","bridegroom(n.)新郎\ngroom(n./v.)新郎(口語)、馬夫、打扮\nbride and groom 新郎新娘\nhandsome bridegroom 英俊的新郎\nThe bridegroom looked nervous before the wedding.\n(新郎在婚禮前看起來很緊張。)\nGuests threw flower petals at the bride and groom.\n(賓客向新郎新娘撒花瓣。)"],["broke","broke(adj.)身無分文的、破產的\n(無詞性變化)\nflat broke 一文不名\ngo broke 破產\nI'm broke until I get paid next week.\n(我在下週領薪水前都身無分文。)\nMany small shops went broke during the pandemic.\n(許多小商店在疫情期間倒閉了。)"],["broom","broom(n.)掃帚\n(無詞性變化)\nsweep with a broom 用掃帚掃\nbroom closet 掃具櫃\nHe swept the classroom floor with a broom.\n(他用掃帚掃教室的地板。)\nIn the story, the witch flew on a broom.\n(故事裡，女巫騎著掃帚飛行。)"],["brutal","brutal(adj.)殘忍的、嚴酷的、直率的\nbrutality(n.)殘暴\nbrutally(adv.)殘忍地、毫不留情地\nbrutal attack 殘暴的攻擊\nbrutal honesty 毫不留情的坦白\nThe brutal heat made it hard to play outside.\n(酷熱讓人很難在戶外玩耍。)\nThe movie shows the brutal reality of war.\n(這部電影呈現出戰爭殘酷的現實。)"],["bulletin","bulletin(n.)公告、公報、快報\n(無詞性變化)\nbulletin board 布告欄\nnews bulletin 新聞快報\nThe exam schedule is posted on the bulletin board.\n(考試時程貼在布告欄上。)\nThe TV show was interrupted by a news bulletin.\n(電視節目被一則新聞快報打斷。)"],["burglar","burglar(n.)竊賊、闖空門者\nburglary(n.)入室竊盜\nburglar alarm 防盜警報器\ncatch a burglar 抓到竊賊\nA burglar broke into the house while the family was away.\n(這家人不在時，一名竊賊闖入屋內。)\nThe burglar alarm went off in the middle of the night.\n(防盜警報器在半夜響起。)"],["cabinet","cabinet(n.)櫥櫃、內閣\n(無詞性變化)\nkitchen cabinet 廚房櫥櫃\ncabinet member 內閣閣員\nShe keeps the medicine in a locked cabinet.\n(她把藥放在上鎖的櫃子裡。)\nThe new cabinet members were introduced to the public.\n(新任內閣閣員向大眾亮相。)"],["calculate","calculate(v.)計算、估計\ncalculation(n.)計算\ncalculator(n.)計算機\ncalculate the cost 計算成本\ncarefully calculated 精心計算的\nCan you calculate how much we spent on the trip?\n(你能算出我們這趟旅行花了多少錢嗎？)\nScientists calculated the distance to the star.\n(科學家計算出到那顆星星的距離。)"],["calculation","calculation(n.)計算、估算\ncalculate(v.)計算\nmake a calculation 進行計算\nrough calculation 粗略估算\nAccording to my calculation, we need 20 more chairs.\n(根據我的計算，我們還需要二十張椅子。)\nOne small mistake in the calculation led to the wrong answer.\n(計算中一個小錯誤導致了錯誤的答案。)"],["calorie","calorie(n.)卡路里、熱量\n(無詞性變化)\nlow-calorie 低熱量的\nburn calories 燃燒熱量\nRunning is a great way to burn calories.\n(跑步是燃燒熱量的好方法。)\nBubble tea is high in calories and sugar.\n(珍珠奶茶的熱量和糖分都很高。)"],["campaign","campaign(n./v.)運動、活動、競選、發起運動\ncampaigner(n.)活動人士\nelection campaign 競選活動\ncampaign against 發起反對……的運動\nThe school started a campaign to reduce plastic waste.\n(學校發起一項減少塑膠垃圾的活動。)\nThe candidates are busy with their election campaigns.\n(候選人們忙於競選活動。)"],["candidate","candidate(n.)候選人、應徵者\ncandidacy(n.)候選資格\npresidential candidate 總統候選人\nstrong candidate 有力人選\nThere are three candidates for class leader.\n(班長有三位候選人。)\nThe company interviewed five candidates for the job.\n(公司為這份工作面試了五位應徵者。)"],["cane","cane(n.)手杖、藤條、(植物的)莖\n(無詞性變化)\nwalking cane 手杖\nsugar cane 甘蔗\nMy grandfather walks with a cane.\n(我爺爺拄著手杖走路。)\nSugar cane was once an important crop in southern Taiwan.\n(甘蔗曾是台灣南部的重要作物。)"],["canoe","canoe(n./v.)獨木舟、划獨木舟\ncanoeing(n.)划獨木舟運動\npaddle a canoe 划獨木舟\ngo canoeing 去划獨木舟\nWe paddled a canoe across the lake.\n(我們划著獨木舟橫越湖面。)\nThey went canoeing on the river last weekend.\n(他們上週末去河上划獨木舟。)"],["capacity","capacity(n.)容量、能力、身分\ncapable(adj.)有能力的\nseating capacity 座位容量\nfull capacity 滿載\nThe stadium has a capacity of 50,000 people.\n(這座體育場可容納五萬人。)\nShe has a great capacity for learning languages.\n(她學習語言的能力很強。)"],["capital(ism)","capital(n.)首都、資本、大寫字母、capitalism(n.)資本主義\ncapitalist(n.)資本家\ncapital city 首都\ncapital letter 大寫字母\nTaipei is the capital of Taiwan.\n(台北是台灣的首都。)\nCapitalism is based on private ownership and free markets.\n(資本主義以私有制和自由市場為基礎。)"],["capitalist","capitalist(n.)資本家、資本主義者\ncapitalism(n.)資本主義\ncapitalistic(adj.)資本主義的\ncapitalist society 資本主義社會\ncapitalist economy 資本主義經濟\nThe factory was owned by a wealthy capitalist.\n(這間工廠為一位富有的資本家所有。)\nThe United States has a capitalist economy.\n(美國實行資本主義經濟。)"],["cargo","cargo(n.)貨物\n(無詞性變化)\ncargo ship 貨輪\ncargo plane 貨機\nThe cargo ship carried thousands of containers.\n(這艘貨輪載著數千個貨櫃。)\nThe workers unloaded the cargo at the port.\n(工人們在港口卸貨。)"],["carrier","carrier(n.)運送者、運輸公司、帶原者\ncarry(v.)攜帶、運送\nmail carrier 郵差\naircraft carrier 航空母艦\nThe mail carrier delivers letters every morning.\n(郵差每天早上送信。)\nMosquitoes can be carriers of disease.\n(蚊子可能是疾病的傳播者。)"],["carve","carve(v.)雕刻、切(肉)\ncarving(n.)雕刻品\ncarve wood 刻木頭\ncarve out 開創\nThe artist carved a beautiful bird out of wood.\n(這位藝術家用木頭雕出一隻美麗的鳥。)\nDad carved the turkey at Thanksgiving dinner.\n(爸爸在感恩節晚餐時切火雞。)"],["catalogue","catalogue(n./v.)目錄、編目錄\ncatalog(n.)目錄(美式拼法)\nproduct catalogue 產品目錄\nlibrary catalogue 圖書館館藏目錄\nShe looked through the catalogue to choose a new sofa.\n(她翻閱目錄挑選新沙發。)\nThe librarian catalogued all the new books.\n(圖書館員把所有新書編入目錄。)"],["category","category(n.)類別、種類\ncategorize(v.)分類\nfall into a category 屬於某一類\nage category 年齡組別\nThe books are arranged by category.\n(這些書按類別排列。)\nShe won first prize in the under-18 category.\n(她在十八歲以下組獲得第一名。)"],["cease","cease(v./n.)停止、終止\nceaseless(adj.)不停的\ncease fire 停火\nwithout cease 不停地\nThe factory ceased production last year.\n(這間工廠去年停止生產。)\nIt never ceases to amaze me how fast children learn.\n(孩子學得那麼快，總是讓我驚訝。)"],["celebration","celebration(n.)慶祝、慶典\ncelebrate(v.)慶祝\nin celebration of 為了慶祝\nbirthday celebration 生日慶祝\nThe whole town joined the New Year celebration.\n(全鎮的人都參加了新年慶典。)\nThey held a party in celebration of their victory.\n(他們舉辦派對慶祝勝利。)"],["chamber","chamber(n.)房間、議院、腔室\n(無詞性變化)\nchamber music 室內樂\nchamber of commerce 商會\nThe heart has four chambers.\n(心臟有四個腔室。)\nWe enjoyed an evening of chamber music.\n(我們享受了一晚的室內樂。)"],["championship","championship(n.)冠軍賽、錦標賽、冠軍頭銜\nchampion(n.)冠軍\nwin the championship 贏得冠軍\nworld championship 世界錦標賽\nOur school team won the basketball championship.\n(我們校隊贏得了籃球冠軍。)\nShe will compete in the world championship next month.\n(她下個月將參加世界錦標賽。)"],["characteristic","characteristic(n./adj.)特徵、特性、特有的\ncharacter(n.)性格、角色\ncharacterize(v.)以……為特徵\nmain characteristic 主要特徵\ncharacteristic of 為……所特有\nPatience is one of the characteristics of a good teacher.\n(耐心是好老師的特質之一。)\nThis dish has the characteristic flavor of Tainan food.\n(這道菜有台南料理特有的風味。)"],["charity","charity(n.)慈善、慈善機構、施捨\ncharitable(adj.)慈善的\ncharity event 慈善活動\ndonate to charity 捐給慈善機構\nThe money from the concert will go to charity.\n(音樂會的收入將捐給慈善機構。)\nShe works for a charity that helps poor children.\n(她在一個幫助貧童的慈善機構工作。)"],["chemistry","chemistry(n.)化學、(人與人之間的)默契\nchemical(adj./n.)化學的、化學物質\nchemist(n.)化學家\nchemistry class 化學課\ngood chemistry 默契很好\nWe did an interesting experiment in chemistry class.\n(我們在化學課上做了一個有趣的實驗。)\nThe two actors have great chemistry on screen.\n(這兩位演員在螢幕上很有默契。)"],["cherish","cherish(v.)愛惜、重視、懷念\n(無詞性變化)\ncherish the memory 懷念回憶\ncherish a dream 懷抱夢想\nI will always cherish the time we spent together.\n(我會永遠記得並重視我們在一起的時光。)\nWe should cherish our friendships.\n(我們應該愛惜友誼。)"],["chew","chew(v./n.)咀嚼、嚼\nchewy(adj.)有嚼勁的\nchewing gum 口香糖\nchew on 咀嚼、仔細思考\nChew your food well before you swallow.\n(吞下去之前要把食物嚼爛。)\nChewing gum is not allowed in class.\n(上課時不准嚼口香糖。)"],["choke","choke(v./n.)窒息、噎住、阻塞\n(無詞性變化)\nchoke on 被……噎到\nchoke back tears 強忍淚水\nThe child almost choked on a piece of candy.\n(那個孩子差點被一顆糖噎到。)\nShe choked back her tears and smiled.\n(她強忍淚水露出微笑。)"],["chorus","chorus(n.)合唱團、副歌、齊聲\nchoral(adj.)合唱的\nschool chorus 學校合唱團\nin chorus 齊聲地\nShe sings in the school chorus.\n(她參加學校合唱團。)\nEveryone sang along during the chorus.\n(大家在副歌時一起合唱。)"],["circular","circular(adj.)圓形的、循環的\ncircle(n.)圓圈\ncircular shape 圓形\ncircular economy 循環經濟\nThe table has a circular shape.\n(這張桌子是圓形的。)\nA circular economy aims to reduce waste.\n(循環經濟的目標是減少浪費。)"],["circulate","circulate(v.)循環、流通、傳播\ncirculation(n.)循環、發行量\ncirculate news 散布消息\nblood circulates 血液循環\nBlood circulates through the body.\n(血液在全身循環。)\nRumors about the new teacher circulated quickly.\n(關於新老師的傳言很快地傳開了。)"],["circulation","circulation(n.)循環、流通、發行量\ncirculate(v.)循環、流通\nblood circulation 血液循環\nin circulation 在流通中\nExercise improves blood circulation.\n(運動能促進血液循環。)\nThe magazine has a circulation of 100,000 copies.\n(這本雜誌的發行量是十萬本。)"],["circumstance","circumstance(n.)情況、環境\n(無詞性變化)\nunder no circumstances 絕不\nunder the circumstances 在這種情況下\nUnder no circumstances should you open the door.\n(無論如何你都不能開門。)\nHe did his best under difficult circumstances.\n(他在艱困的環境下盡了全力。)"],["civilian","civilian(adj./n.)平民的、平民\ncivil(adj.)公民的、民用的\ncivilian life 平民生活\ninnocent civilians 無辜百姓\nMany civilians were hurt in the war.\n(許多平民在戰爭中受傷。)\nAfter the army, he returned to civilian life.\n(退伍後，他回歸平民生活。)"],["civilization","civilization(n.)文明\ncivilize(v.)使文明化\ncivilized(adj.)文明的\nancient civilization 古文明\nmodern civilization 現代文明\nEgypt is home to one of the oldest civilizations.\n(埃及是最古老文明之一的發源地。)\nWriting played a key role in human civilization.\n(文字在人類文明中扮演關鍵角色。)"],["clarify","clarify(v.)澄清、闡明\nclarification(n.)澄清、說明\nclarity(n.)清晰\nclarify a point 說明某一點\nclarify the situation 澄清情況\nCould you clarify what you mean?\n(你能說明一下你的意思嗎？)\nThe teacher clarified the rules before the test.\n(老師在考試前說明規則。)"],["clash","clash(n./v.)衝突、撞擊聲、(顏色)不搭配\n(無詞性變化)\nclash with 與……衝突\nculture clash 文化衝突\nPolice clashed with protesters in the street.\n(警方在街頭與抗議者發生衝突。)\nYour red shirt clashes with your pink pants.\n(你的紅色上衣和粉紅色褲子不搭。)"],["classification","classification(n.)分類、類別\nclassify(v.)分類\nclassification system 分類系統\nfilm classification 電影分級\nThe classification of animals helps scientists study them.\n(動物分類有助於科學家研究牠們。)\nThis film has a classification of PG-13.\n(這部電影是輔導十三級。)"],["classify","classify(v.)分類、將……歸類\nclassification(n.)分類\nclassified(adj.)機密的、分類的\nclassify into 分成……類\nclassified information 機密資訊\nBooks in the library are classified by subject.\n(圖書館的書依主題分類。)\nScientists classify whales as mammals.\n(科學家把鯨魚歸類為哺乳類。)"],["claw","claw(n./v.)爪子、螯、用爪抓\n(無詞性變化)\nsharp claws 尖銳的爪子\nclaw machine 夾娃娃機\nThe cat scratched me with its sharp claws.\n(那隻貓用利爪抓傷了我。)\nHe spent all his coins on the claw machine.\n(他把所有硬幣都花在夾娃娃機上。)"],["cliff","cliff(n.)懸崖、峭壁\n(無詞性變化)\ncliff edge 懸崖邊\nsteep cliff 陡峭的懸崖\nThe Qingshui Cliff in Hualien is very famous.\n(花蓮的清水斷崖非常有名。)\nDon't stand too close to the edge of the cliff.\n(別站得太靠近懸崖邊。)"],["clumsy","clumsy(adj.)笨拙的\nclumsily(adv.)笨拙地\nclumsiness(n.)笨拙\nclumsy movement 笨拙的動作\nclumsy attempt 拙劣的嘗試\nI'm so clumsy that I broke another cup.\n(我真笨手笨腳，又打破了一個杯子。)\nThe puppy's clumsy steps made us laugh.\n(小狗笨拙的步伐讓我們發笑。)"],["coarse","coarse(adj.)粗糙的、粗俗的\ncoarsely(adv.)粗糙地\ncoarse sand 粗沙\ncoarse language 粗俗的話\nThe fabric feels coarse against my skin.\n(這塊布料貼在皮膚上感覺很粗糙。)\nPlease don't use coarse language in class.\n(上課時請不要講粗話。)"],["code","code(n./v.)密碼、代碼、規範、編碼\ncoding(n.)程式設計\ndress code 服裝規定\nQR code 行動條碼\nScan the QR code to pay.\n(掃描 QR 碼來付款。)\nStudents are learning to write computer code.\n(學生們正在學習寫程式碼。)"],["collapse","collapse(n./v.)倒塌、崩潰、昏倒\n(無詞性變化)\ncollapse of 某物的崩潰\non the verge of collapse 瀕臨崩潰\nThe old bridge collapsed during the earthquake.\n(那座舊橋在地震中倒塌了。)\nHe collapsed from heat after running the marathon.\n(他跑完馬拉松後中暑昏倒。)"],["colleague","colleague(n.)同事\n(無詞性變化)\nformer colleague 前同事\nwork colleague 工作上的同事\nMy mother gets along well with her colleagues.\n(我媽媽和她的同事們相處融洽。)\nHe discussed the plan with a colleague.\n(他和一位同事討論了這項計畫。)"],["combination","combination(n.)結合、組合、密碼組合\ncombine(v.)結合\nin combination with 與……結合\nperfect combination 完美組合\nSuccess is a combination of talent and hard work.\n(成功是天分與努力的結合。)\nI forgot the combination to my lock.\n(我忘了我的鎖的密碼。)"],["comedy","comedy(n.)喜劇\ncomedian(n.)喜劇演員\ncomic(adj.)喜劇的\nromantic comedy 浪漫喜劇\ncomedy show 喜劇節目\nWe watched a funny comedy last night.\n(我們昨晚看了一部好笑的喜劇。)\nRomantic comedies are popular among teenagers.\n(浪漫喜劇在青少年之間很受歡迎。)"],["commander","commander(n.)指揮官、司令\ncommand(v./n.)命令、指揮\nmilitary commander 軍事指揮官\ncommander in chief 總司令\nThe commander ordered his soldiers to retreat.\n(指揮官命令他的士兵撤退。)\nThe president is the commander in chief of the army.\n(總統是三軍統帥。)"],["comment","comment(n./v.)評論、意見、發表意見\ncommentary(n.)評論、實況報導\ncommentator(n.)評論員\nmake a comment 發表意見\nno comment 無可奉告\nThe teacher wrote some helpful comments on my essay.\n(老師在我的作文上寫了一些有幫助的評語。)\nHe refused to comment on the news.\n(他拒絕對這則新聞發表評論。)"],["commerce","commerce(n.)商業、貿易\ncommercial(adj./n.)商業的、廣告\ne-commerce 電子商務\ninternational commerce 國際貿易\nE-commerce has changed the way people shop.\n(電子商務改變了人們購物的方式。)\nThe city has long been a center of commerce.\n(這座城市長久以來一直是商業中心。)"],["commit","commit(v.)犯(罪)、承諾、投入\ncommitment(n.)承諾、投入\ncommitted(adj.)盡心盡力的\ncommit a crime 犯罪\ncommit oneself to 致力於\nThe man was arrested for committing a crime.\n(那名男子因犯罪而被捕。)\nShe committed herself to helping homeless animals.\n(她致力於幫助流浪動物。)"],["communication","communication(n.)溝通、通訊\ncommunicate(v.)溝通\ncommunicative(adj.)溝通的\ncommunication skills 溝通技巧\nmeans of communication 通訊方式\nGood communication is the key to a happy family.\n(良好的溝通是幸福家庭的關鍵。)\nSmartphones are the main means of communication today.\n(智慧型手機是現今主要的通訊工具。)"],["community","community(n.)社區、社群、共同體\n(無詞性變化)\nlocal community 當地社區\ncommunity service 社區服務\nStudents are required to do community service.\n(學生必須做社區服務。)\nThe online community shares tips about learning English.\n(這個網路社群分享學英文的訣竅。)"],["companion","companion(n.)同伴、伴侶\ncompanionship(n.)友誼、陪伴\ntraveling companion 旅伴\nconstant companion 形影不離的同伴\nMy dog has been my faithful companion for ten years.\n(我的狗十年來一直是我忠實的夥伴。)\nShe was a great traveling companion.\n(她是很棒的旅伴。)"],["competition","competition(n.)競爭、比賽\ncompete(v.)競爭\ncompetitive(adj.)競爭的\nfierce competition 激烈的競爭\nenter a competition 參加比賽\nShe won first place in the speech competition.\n(她在演講比賽中得到第一名。)\nThere is fierce competition among smartphone companies.\n(手機公司之間競爭激烈。)"],["competitive","competitive(adj.)競爭的、好勝的、有競爭力的\ncompete(v.)競爭\ncompetitiveness(n.)競爭力\ncompetitive price 有競爭力的價格\nhighly competitive 競爭激烈的\nThe job market is highly competitive.\n(就業市場競爭非常激烈。)\nHe is very competitive and hates to lose.\n(他非常好勝，很討厭輸。)"],["competitor","competitor(n.)競爭者、參賽者\ncompete(v.)競爭\ncompetition(n.)比賽\nmain competitor 主要競爭對手\nstrong competitor 強勁對手\nMore than 200 competitors took part in the race.\n(超過兩百名參賽者參加了這場賽跑。)\nThe company is losing customers to its competitors.\n(這家公司的客戶正被競爭對手搶走。)"],["complicate","complicate(v.)使複雜化\ncomplicated(adj.)複雜的\ncomplication(n.)複雜化、併發症\ncomplicate matters 使事情複雜\nfurther complicate 進一步複雜化\nDon't complicate things by changing the plan again.\n(別再改計畫把事情弄複雜了。)\nThe bad weather complicated the rescue work.\n(惡劣的天氣使救援工作更加複雜。)"],["compose","compose(v.)組成、作曲、撰寫、使鎮定\ncomposition(n.)作文、作品\ncomposer(n.)作曲家\nbe composed of 由……組成\ncompose oneself 使自己鎮定\nThe team is composed of ten members.\n(這支隊伍由十名成員組成。)\nMozart composed his first piece at the age of five.\n(莫札特五歲時就創作了他的第一首曲子。)"],["composer","composer(n.)作曲家\ncompose(v.)作曲\ncomposition(n.)樂曲\nfamous composer 著名作曲家\nfilm composer 電影配樂家\nBeethoven is one of the greatest composers in history.\n(貝多芬是史上最偉大的作曲家之一。)\nThe film composer wrote music for many popular movies.\n(這位配樂家為許多熱門電影寫了音樂。)"],["composition","composition(n.)作文、作品、組成\ncompose(v.)組成、作曲\nEnglish composition 英文作文\nchemical composition 化學成分\nWe have to write an English composition this week.\n(我們這週要寫一篇英文作文。)\nScientists studied the composition of the rock.\n(科學家研究了這塊岩石的組成成分。)"],["concentrate","concentrate(v.)專心、集中\nconcentration(n.)專心、集中\nconcentrate on 專注於\nconcentrate one's efforts 集中心力\nI can't concentrate on my homework with the TV on.\n(電視開著我沒辦法專心寫功課。)\nMost of the population is concentrated in big cities.\n(大部分人口集中在大城市。)"],["concentration","concentration(n.)專注力、集中、濃度\nconcentrate(v.)專心\nlose concentration 分心\nhigh concentration 高濃度\nLack of sleep can affect your concentration.\n(睡眠不足會影響你的專注力。)\nThe air has a high concentration of dust today.\n(今天空氣中的灰塵濃度很高。)"],["concept","concept(n.)概念、觀念\nconceptual(adj.)概念的\nbasic concept 基本概念\nconcept of time 時間概念\nIt took me a while to understand the concept.\n(我花了一些時間才理解這個概念。)\nThe concept of recycling is taught in elementary school.\n(回收的觀念在小學就有教了。)"],["concerning","concerning(prep.)關於\nconcern(n./v.)關心、涉及\nconcerning the matter 關於此事\nquestions concerning 關於……的問題\nI have some questions concerning the school trip.\n(我對校外教學有一些問題。)\nThe principal made an announcement concerning the new rules.\n(校長針對新規定發表了公告。)"],["concrete","concrete(adj./n./v.)具體的、混凝土、用混凝土鋪\nconcretely(adv.)具體地\nconcrete example 具體例子\nconcrete wall 水泥牆\nCan you give me a concrete example?\n(你能給我一個具體的例子嗎？)\nThe building is made of steel and concrete.\n(這棟建築由鋼筋和混凝土建成。)"],["conductor","conductor(n.)指揮、列車長、導體\nconduct(v.)指揮、進行、傳導\norchestra conductor 樂團指揮\nconductor of heat 熱的導體\nThe conductor raised his baton and the music began.\n(指揮舉起指揮棒，音樂隨即響起。)\nMetal is a good conductor of electricity.\n(金屬是電的良導體。)"],["conference","conference(n.)會議、研討會\nconfer(v.)商議\npress conference 記者會\nattend a conference 參加會議\nThe mayor held a press conference this morning.\n(市長今天早上召開了記者會。)\nMy teacher will attend an education conference in Tokyo.\n(我的老師將去東京參加一場教育研討會。)"],["confess","confess(v.)坦白、承認、懺悔\nconfession(n.)坦白、告解\nconfess to 承認(錯誤)\nconfess one's love 表白\nHe confessed that he had broken the window.\n(他坦承是他打破了窗戶。)\nShe finally confessed her feelings to him.\n(她終於向他表白了心意。)"],["confidence","confidence(n.)信心、自信、信任\nconfident(adj.)有信心的\nconfidential(adj.)機密的\nself-confidence 自信心\nlose confidence 失去信心\nPractice will give you more confidence.\n(練習能讓你更有自信。)\nI have full confidence in our team.\n(我對我們的隊伍充滿信心。)"],["confusion","confusion(n.)困惑、混亂\nconfuse(v.)使困惑\nconfused(adj.)困惑的\nin confusion 困惑地、混亂中\ncause confusion 引起混亂\nThe sudden change in schedule caused a lot of confusion.\n(行程突然改變造成許多混亂。)\nHe looked at me in confusion.\n(他困惑地看著我。)"],["congratulate","congratulate(v.)祝賀、恭喜\ncongratulation(n.)祝賀\ncongratulations(int.)恭喜\ncongratulate sb. on 恭喜某人……\nwarmly congratulate 熱烈祝賀\nWe congratulated her on winning the prize.\n(我們恭喜她得獎。)\nThe coach congratulated the players after the game.\n(比賽後教練向球員們道賀。)"],["congress","congress(n.)國會、代表大會\ncongressional(adj.)國會的\nmember of Congress 國會議員\npass Congress 經國會通過\nThe new law was passed by Congress.\n(這項新法律經國會通過。)\nShe was elected to Congress at the age of 35.\n(她三十五歲時當選國會議員。)"],["conquer","conquer(v.)征服、克服\nconquest(n.)征服\nconqueror(n.)征服者\nconquer fear 克服恐懼\nconquer the world 征服世界\nThe Roman army conquered much of Europe.\n(羅馬軍隊征服了歐洲大部分地區。)\nShe finally conquered her fear of speaking in public.\n(她終於克服了對公開演講的恐懼。)"],["conscience","conscience(n.)良心、良知\nconscientious(adj.)認真的、盡責的\nguilty conscience 良心不安\nclear conscience 問心無愧\nHe had a guilty conscience after lying to his mother.\n(他對媽媽說謊後感到良心不安。)\nI did my best, so I have a clear conscience.\n(我盡力了，所以問心無愧。)"],["consequence","consequence(n.)後果、結果、重要性\nconsequent(adj.)隨之發生的\nconsequently(adv.)因此\nas a consequence 因此\nface the consequences 承擔後果\nYou must be ready to face the consequences of your actions.\n(你必須準備好承擔自己行為的後果。)\nHe didn't study, and as a consequence, he failed.\n(他沒讀書，結果就考不及格。)"],["consequent","consequent(adj.)隨之發生的、作為結果的\nconsequence(n.)後果\nconsequently(adv.)因此\nconsequent loss 隨之而來的損失\nconsequent on 因……而發生的\nThe typhoon and the consequent floods destroyed many homes.\n(颱風及隨之而來的水災摧毀了許多房屋。)\nPrices rose, with a consequent drop in sales.\n(物價上漲，銷售量隨之下滑。)"],["conservative","conservative(adj./n.)保守的、保守派人士\nconserve(v.)保存、節約\nconservation(n.)保育、保存\nconservative view 保守的觀點\nconservative estimate 保守估計\nMy grandparents have very conservative views.\n(我的祖父母觀念非常保守。)\nBy a conservative estimate, the trip will cost 20,000 dollars.\n(保守估計，這趟旅行要花兩萬元。)"],["consist","consist(v.)組成、在於\nconsistent(adj.)一致的\nconsist of 由……組成\nconsist in 在於\nThe class consists of 30 students.\n(這個班由三十名學生組成。)\nHappiness consists in being content with what you have.\n(幸福在於知足。)"],["consistent","consistent(adj.)一致的、始終如一的\nconsistency(n.)一致性\nconsistently(adv.)一貫地\nbe consistent with 與……一致\nconsistent effort 持續的努力\nHis story is not consistent with the facts.\n(他的說法與事實不符。)\nConsistent practice is the key to learning a language.\n(持續練習是學好語言的關鍵。)"],["constitute","constitute(v.)構成、組成、設立\nconstitution(n.)憲法、體質\nconstitute a threat 構成威脅\nconstitute a majority 構成多數\nWomen constitute more than half of the staff.\n(女性占全體員工的一半以上。)\nPlastic waste constitutes a serious threat to sea life.\n(塑膠垃圾對海洋生物構成嚴重威脅。)"],["constitution","constitution(n.)憲法、體質、組成\nconstitutional(adj.)憲法的\nconstitute(v.)構成\namend the constitution 修憲\nstrong constitution 強健的體質\nThe constitution protects freedom of speech.\n(憲法保障言論自由。)\nHe has a strong constitution and rarely gets sick.\n(他體質強健，很少生病。)"],["construct","construct(v.)建造、構築\nconstruction(n.)建造、建築\nconstructive(adj.)建設性的\nconstruct a building 建造大樓\nconstruct a sentence 造句\nA new MRT line is being constructed in the city.\n(市內正在興建一條新的捷運線。)\nCan you construct a sentence with this word?\n(你能用這個字造一個句子嗎？)"],["construction","construction(n.)建造、建設、結構\nconstruct(v.)建造\nconstructive(adj.)建設性的\nunder construction 興建中\nconstruction site 工地\nThe new library is still under construction.\n(新圖書館仍在興建中。)\nWorkers must wear helmets at the construction site.\n(工人在工地必須戴安全帽。)"],["constructive","constructive(adj.)建設性的、有助益的\nconstruct(v.)建造\nconstructively(adv.)有建設性地\nconstructive criticism 建設性的批評\nconstructive suggestion 建設性的建議\nThank you for your constructive suggestions.\n(謝謝你提出有建設性的建議。)\nConstructive criticism can help you improve.\n(建設性的批評能幫助你進步。)"],["consult","consult(v.)諮詢、請教、查閱\nconsultant(n.)顧問\nconsultation(n.)諮詢\nconsult a doctor 看醫生\nconsult a dictionary 查字典\nYou should consult a doctor if the pain continues.\n(如果持續疼痛，你應該去看醫生。)\nI consulted a dictionary to check the spelling.\n(我查字典確認拼法。)"],["consultant","consultant(n.)顧問\nconsult(v.)諮詢\nconsultation(n.)諮詢\nbusiness consultant 企業顧問\nhire a consultant 聘請顧問\nThe company hired a consultant to solve the problem.\n(公司聘請了一位顧問來解決問題。)\nShe works as a financial consultant.\n(她是一名理財顧問。)"],["consume","consume(v.)消耗、消費、吃喝\nconsumer(n.)消費者\nconsumption(n.)消耗、消費\nconsume energy 消耗能源\ntime-consuming 費時的\nAir conditioners consume a lot of electricity.\n(冷氣機消耗大量電力。)\nWriting a research report is very time-consuming.\n(寫研究報告非常耗時。)"],["consumer","consumer(n.)消費者\nconsume(v.)消費\nconsumption(n.)消費\nconsumer rights 消費者權益\nconsumer goods 消費品\nConsumers are paying more attention to food safety.\n(消費者愈來愈注重食品安全。)\nThe law protects consumer rights.\n(這項法律保障消費者權益。)"],["container","container(n.)容器、貨櫃\ncontain(v.)包含、容納\nplastic container 塑膠容器\ncontainer ship 貨櫃船\nKeep the cookies in an airtight container.\n(把餅乾放在密封容器裡保存。)\nHuge container ships come in and out of Kaohsiung Port.\n(巨大的貨櫃船進出高雄港。)"],["content","content(n./adj.)內容、目錄、滿足的\ncontented(adj.)滿足的\nbe content with 對……滿足\ntable of contents 目錄\nThe content of this book is suitable for children.\n(這本書的內容適合兒童。)\nShe is content with her simple life.\n(她很滿足於自己簡單的生活。)"],["content(ment)","content(v.)使滿足、contentment(n.)滿足\ncontented(adj.)滿足的\ncontent oneself with 滿足於\na sense of contentment 滿足感\nHe contented himself with a simple meal.\n(他吃一頓簡單的餐就滿足了。)\nSpending time with family gives me a deep sense of contentment.\n(和家人相處讓我有深深的滿足感。)"],["contest","contest(n./v.)比賽、競賽、爭奪\ncontestant(n.)參賽者\nspeech contest 演講比賽\nbeauty contest 選美比賽\nHe won second prize in the English speech contest.\n(他在英文演講比賽中得到第二名。)\nThree candidates will contest the election.\n(三名候選人將角逐這次選舉。)"],["context","context(n.)上下文、背景、情境\ncontextual(adj.)上下文的\nin context 在上下文中\nhistorical context 歷史背景\nTry to guess the meaning of the word from the context.\n(試著從上下文猜出這個字的意思。)\nWe need to understand the historical context of the event.\n(我們需要了解這個事件的歷史背景。)"],["continual","continual(adj.)頻繁的、不斷重複的\ncontinually(adv.)不斷地\ncontinual interruptions 不斷的打擾\ncontinual complaints 頻繁的抱怨\nI'm tired of your continual complaints.\n(我受夠了你一再的抱怨。)\nContinual interruptions made it hard to study.\n(不斷的打擾讓人很難讀書。)"],["continuous","continuous(adj.)連續不斷的\ncontinuously(adv.)連續地\ncontinue(v.)繼續\ncontinuous rain 連續不停的雨\ncontinuous improvement 持續改進\nWe had three days of continuous rain.\n(我們這裡連續下了三天的雨。)\nThe machine makes a continuous noise.\n(這台機器發出持續不斷的噪音。)"],["contrary","contrary(n./adj.)相反、相反的\n(無詞性變化)\non the contrary 相反地\ncontrary to 與……相反\nContrary to popular belief, bats are not blind.\n(與一般看法相反，蝙蝠並不是瞎子。)\nHe isn't lazy; on the contrary, he works very hard.\n(他不懶惰；相反地，他非常努力。)"],["contrast","contrast(n./v.)對比、差異、形成對比\ncontrasting(adj.)對比鮮明的\nin contrast 相較之下\ncontrast with 與……形成對比\nIn contrast to her sister, she is very quiet.\n(和她姊姊相比，她非常文靜。)\nThe white house contrasts nicely with the blue sky.\n(白色房子和藍天形成美麗的對比。)"],["contribute","contribute(v.)貢獻、捐獻、促成\ncontribution(n.)貢獻\ncontributor(n.)貢獻者、投稿者\ncontribute to 有助於、導致\ncontribute money 捐錢\nExercise contributes to good health.\n(運動有助於身體健康。)\nEveryone contributed some money to buy a gift for the teacher.\n(每個人都出了些錢買禮物送老師。)"],["contribution","contribution(n.)貢獻、捐款、投稿\ncontribute(v.)貢獻\nmake a contribution 做出貢獻\nvaluable contribution 寶貴的貢獻\nShe made a great contribution to the success of the event.\n(她對活動的成功有很大的貢獻。)\nAll contributions to the charity are welcome.\n(歡迎各界捐款給這個慈善機構。)"],["convenience","convenience(n.)方便、便利\nconvenient(adj.)方便的\nconvenience store 便利商店\nat your convenience 在你方便時\nThere is a convenience store on every corner in Taipei.\n(台北幾乎每個街角都有便利商店。)\nPlease reply at your earliest convenience.\n(請在您方便時盡早回覆。)"],["convention","convention(n.)大會、慣例、公約\nconventional(adj.)傳統的、慣例的\nconvention center 會議中心\nsocial convention 社會慣例\nThe comic convention attracted thousands of fans.\n(動漫展吸引了數千名粉絲。)\nShaking hands is a social convention in many countries.\n(握手在許多國家是一種社交慣例。)"],["conventional","conventional(adj.)傳統的、慣例的、常規的\nconvention(n.)慣例\nconventionally(adv.)按慣例地\nconventional wisdom 一般看法\nconventional methods 傳統方法\nThe teacher uses both conventional and online teaching methods.\n(這位老師同時使用傳統與線上的教學方法。)\nElectric cars are replacing conventional cars.\n(電動車正在取代傳統汽車。)"],["converse","converse(v.)交談\nconversation(n.)對話\nconverse with 與……交談\nconverse in English 用英語交談\nShe can converse fluently in Japanese.\n(她能用日語流利地交談。)\nThe two leaders conversed for an hour.\n(兩位領袖交談了一個小時。)"],["convey","convey(v.)傳達、運送\nconveyor(n.)輸送帶、傳送者\nconvey a message 傳達訊息\nconvey feelings 表達感受\nMusic can convey feelings that words cannot.\n(音樂能傳達言語無法表達的感受。)\nPlease convey my thanks to your parents.\n(請代我向你的父母致謝。)"],["convince","convince(v.)說服、使相信\nconvinced(adj.)確信的\nconvincing(adj.)有說服力的\nconvince sb. of 使某人相信\nbe convinced that 確信\nI finally convinced my parents to let me go camping.\n(我終於說服爸媽讓我去露營。)\nShe is convinced that she will pass the exam.\n(她確信自己會通過考試。)"],["cooperate","cooperate(v.)合作、配合\ncooperation(n.)合作\ncooperative(adj.)合作的\ncooperate with 與……合作\ncooperate fully 全力配合\nThe two schools cooperated to hold the event.\n(這兩所學校合作舉辦這項活動。)\nPlease cooperate with the police.\n(請配合警方。)"],["cooperation","cooperation(n.)合作、協力\ncooperate(v.)合作\ncooperative(adj.)合作的\nin cooperation with 與……合作\ninternational cooperation 國際合作\nThank you for your cooperation.\n(謝謝您的合作。)\nThe festival was held in cooperation with the city government.\n(這個節慶活動是與市政府合作舉辦的。)"],["cooperative","cooperative(adj./n.)合作的、樂於配合的、合作社\ncooperate(v.)合作\ncooperation(n.)合作\ncooperative learning 合作學習\nschool cooperative 學校合作社\nThe students were very cooperative during the fire drill.\n(學生們在消防演習時非常配合。)\nI bought a pen at the school cooperative.\n(我在學校合作社買了一支筆。)"],["cope","cope(v.)應付、處理\n(無詞性變化)\ncope with 應付、處理\ncope with stress 應付壓力\nStudents need to learn how to cope with stress.\n(學生需要學習如何應付壓力。)\nThe hospital couldn't cope with so many patients.\n(醫院無法應付這麼多病人。)"],["copper","copper(n./adj.)銅、銅製的、銅色的\n(無詞性變化)\ncopper wire 銅線\ncopper coin 銅幣\nCopper is a good conductor of electricity.\n(銅是電的良導體。)\nThe old temple has a copper roof.\n(那座古廟有銅製的屋頂。)"],["cord","cord(n.)細繩、電線\ncordless(adj.)無線的\npower cord 電源線\nvocal cords 聲帶\nUnplug the power cord before cleaning the machine.\n(清理機器前先拔掉電源線。)\nShouting too much can hurt your vocal cords.\n(過度大喊會傷害你的聲帶。)"],["correspond","correspond(v.)符合、相當於、通信\ncorrespondence(n.)通信、符合\ncorrespondent(n.)特派員、通信者\ncorrespond to 相當於\ncorrespond with 與……相符、與……通信\nHis words do not correspond with his actions.\n(他言行不一。)\nI corresponded with a pen pal in Canada for years.\n(我和一位加拿大筆友通信多年。)"],["costume","costume(n.)服裝、戲服\n(無詞性變化)\nHalloween costume 萬聖節服裝\ncostume party 化裝舞會\nShe wore a witch costume for Halloween.\n(她萬聖節穿了女巫裝。)\nThe actors wore traditional costumes in the play.\n(演員們在劇中穿著傳統服裝。)"],["cottage","cottage(n.)小屋、農舍\n(無詞性變化)\ncountry cottage 鄉間小屋\nholiday cottage 度假小屋\nThey rented a small cottage by the lake.\n(他們在湖邊租了一間小屋。)\nMy dream is to live in a cottage in the countryside.\n(我的夢想是住在鄉間的小屋裡。)"],["council","council(n.)議會、委員會\ncouncilor(n.)議員\ncity council 市議會\nstudent council 學生會\nShe was elected president of the student council.\n(她當選學生會會長。)\nThe city council approved the new park plan.\n(市議會通過了新公園的計畫。)"],["counter","counter(n./v./adj./adv.)櫃檯、計數器、反擊、相反的\n(無詞性變化)\ncheck-in counter 報到櫃檯\nover the counter 不需處方(購藥)\nPlease pay at the counter.\n(請到櫃檯付款。)\nThis medicine can be bought over the counter.\n(這種藥不需處方就能買到。)"],["courageous","courageous(adj.)勇敢的\ncourage(n.)勇氣\ncourageously(adv.)勇敢地\ncourageous decision 勇敢的決定\ncourageous act 英勇行為\nThe courageous firefighter saved a child from the fire.\n(勇敢的消防員從火場中救出一名孩童。)\nIt was courageous of her to speak the truth.\n(她說出真相是很勇敢的。)"],["courtesy","courtesy(n.)禮貌、好意\ncourteous(adj.)有禮貌的\nout of courtesy 出於禮貌\ncourtesy call 禮貌性拜訪\nHe opened the door for her out of courtesy.\n(他出於禮貌為她開門。)\nIt's common courtesy to say thank you.\n(說謝謝是基本禮貌。)"],["coward","coward(n.)懦夫、膽小鬼\ncowardly(adj.)懦弱的\ncowardice(n.)膽小、怯懦\ncall sb. a coward 罵某人膽小鬼\nact like a coward 表現得像個懦夫\nDon't be a coward; tell her the truth.\n(別當膽小鬼，告訴她真相。)\nOnly a coward would run away from his friends in danger.\n(只有懦夫才會在朋友遇險時逃走。)"],["crack","crack(n./v.)裂縫、破裂、破解\ncracker(n.)餅乾、爆竹\ncrack down on 嚴厲打擊\ncrack a joke 說笑話\nThere is a crack in the wall after the earthquake.\n(地震後牆上出現了一道裂縫。)\nThe police are cracking down on drunk driving.\n(警方正在嚴厲取締酒駕。)"],["craft","craft(n.)手藝、工藝、工藝品\ncraftsman(n.)工匠\ncrafty(adj.)狡猾的\narts and crafts 美術工藝\ntraditional craft 傳統工藝\nThe market sells local arts and crafts.\n(這個市集販賣當地的工藝品。)\nMaking paper umbrellas is a traditional craft in Meinong.\n(製作紙傘是美濃的傳統工藝。)"],["creation","creation(n.)創造、創作、作品\ncreate(v.)創造\ncreative(adj.)有創意的\njob creation 創造就業\nthe creation of 某物的創造\nThe creation of the website took three months.\n(建置這個網站花了三個月。)\nThis dress is her latest creation.\n(這件洋裝是她最新的作品。)"],["creativity","creativity(n.)創造力、創意\ncreative(adj.)有創意的\ncreate(v.)創造\nencourage creativity 鼓勵創意\nshow creativity 展現創意\nArt classes help students develop their creativity.\n(美術課幫助學生發展創造力。)\nThe project requires both creativity and teamwork.\n(這個專題需要創意和團隊合作。)"],["creep","creep(v.)悄悄移動、爬行\ncreepy(adj.)令人毛骨悚然的\ncreep into 悄悄進入\ncreep up on 悄悄靠近\nThe cat crept toward the bird.\n(那隻貓悄悄地向小鳥靠近。)\nHe crept into the house so he wouldn't wake his parents.\n(他悄悄溜進屋裡，以免吵醒父母。)"],["critic","critic(n.)評論家、批評者\ncritical(adj.)批評的、關鍵的\ncriticize(v.)批評\nfilm critic 影評人\nharsh critic 嚴厲的批評者\nThe film critic gave the movie five stars.\n(影評人給了這部電影五顆星。)\nHe is one of the government's harshest critics.\n(他是政府最嚴厲的批評者之一。)"],["critical","critical(adj.)批評的、關鍵的、危急的\ncritic(n.)評論家\ncritically(adv.)批判地、危急地\ncritical thinking 批判性思考\nin critical condition 情況危急\nCritical thinking is an important skill for students.\n(批判性思考是學生重要的能力。)\nThe injured man is in critical condition.\n(那名傷者情況危急。)"],["criticism","criticism(n.)批評、評論\ncriticize(v.)批評\ncritic(n.)評論家\naccept criticism 接受批評\nconstructive criticism 建設性的批評\nHe can't take any criticism.\n(他完全無法接受批評。)\nThe new policy faced strong criticism from parents.\n(新政策遭到家長強烈批評。)"],["criticize","criticize(v.)批評、評論\ncriticism(n.)批評\ncritic(n.)評論家\ncriticize sb. for 因……批評某人\nbe widely criticized 受到廣泛批評\nDon't criticize others for their mistakes.\n(不要因別人犯錯就批評他們。)\nThe movie was criticized for being too violent.\n(這部電影因過於暴力而遭批評。)"],["cruelty","cruelty(n.)殘忍、殘酷行為\ncruel(adj.)殘忍的\nanimal cruelty 虐待動物\nact of cruelty 殘忍的行為\nAnimal cruelty is against the law.\n(虐待動物是違法的。)\nThe story shows the cruelty of war.\n(這個故事呈現了戰爭的殘酷。)"],["crunchy","crunchy(adj.)酥脆的、脆的\ncrunch(n./v.)嘎吱聲、嘎吱地咬嚼\ncrunchy snack 酥脆的零食\ncrunchy vegetables 爽脆的蔬菜\nI love crunchy peanut butter.\n(我很愛顆粒花生醬。)\nThese cookies are sweet and crunchy.\n(這些餅乾又甜又脆。)"],["crush","crush(n./v.)壓碎、壓垮、迷戀\ncrushing(adj.)壓倒性的\nhave a crush on 迷戀某人\ncrush ice 碎冰\nHe has a crush on a girl in his class.\n(他暗戀班上的一個女生。)\nThe car was crushed by a falling tree.\n(那輛車被倒下的樹壓扁了。)"],["cube","cube(n./v.)立方體、塊、切丁\ncubic(adj.)立方的\nice cube 冰塊\nsugar cube 方糖\nShe put some ice cubes in her drink.\n(她在飲料裡加了幾塊冰塊。)\nCube the potatoes before cooking them.\n(烹煮前先把馬鈴薯切丁。)"],["cue","cue(n./v.)暗示、提示、給……提示\n(無詞性變化)\non cue 恰好在這時\ntake one's cue from 學某人的樣\nThe actor waited for his cue to enter the stage.\n(那名演員等待上台的提示。)\nRight on cue, the bus arrived.\n(就在這時，公車正好到了。)"],["cunning","cunning(adj./n.)狡猾的、狡詐\ncunningly(adv.)狡猾地\ncunning plan 狡猾的計畫\nas cunning as a fox 像狐狸一樣狡猾\nThe fox in the story is very cunning.\n(故事裡的狐狸非常狡猾。)\nHe used cunning to win the game.\n(他耍詐贏了這場遊戲。)"],["curiosity","curiosity(n.)好奇心\ncurious(adj.)好奇的\nout of curiosity 出於好奇\nsatisfy one's curiosity 滿足好奇心\nOut of curiosity, I opened the box.\n(出於好奇，我打開了箱子。)\nCuriosity is the starting point of learning.\n(好奇心是學習的起點。)"],["curl","curl(n./v.)捲髮、捲曲、使捲曲\ncurly(adj.)捲曲的\ncurl up 蜷縮\ncurl one's hair 燙捲頭髮\nThe cat curled up on the sofa.\n(貓蜷縮在沙發上。)\nShe has beautiful blond curls.\n(她有一頭漂亮的金色捲髮。)"],["curse","curse(n./v.)詛咒、咒罵、禍害\ncursed(adj.)被詛咒的\nput a curse on 對……下咒\ncurse and swear 咒罵\nThe witch put a curse on the princess.\n(女巫對公主下了詛咒。)\nHe cursed when he missed the train.\n(他錯過火車時咒罵了一聲。)"],["curve","curve(n./v.)曲線、彎道、使彎曲\ncurved(adj.)彎曲的\nsharp curve 急彎\nlearning curve 學習曲線\nSlow down before the sharp curve.\n(過急彎前要減速。)\nThe road curves along the coast.\n(這條路沿著海岸蜿蜒。)"],["cushion","cushion(n./v.)墊子、坐墊、減輕(衝擊)\n(無詞性變化)\nsofa cushion 沙發靠墊\ncushion the impact 減輕衝擊\nShe sat on a soft cushion.\n(她坐在一個柔軟的墊子上。)\nThe soft grass cushioned his fall.\n(柔軟的草地減輕了他跌倒的衝擊。)"],["damp","damp(adj./n./v.)潮濕的、濕氣、使潮濕\ndampen(v.)使潮濕、使沮喪\ndampness(n.)潮濕\ndamp weather 潮濕的天氣\ndamp cloth 濕布\nWipe the table with a damp cloth.\n(用濕布擦桌子。)\nThe basement always feels damp in spring.\n(地下室在春天總是感覺很潮濕。)"],["deadline","deadline(n.)截止期限\n(無詞性變化)\nmeet a deadline 趕上截止期限\nmiss a deadline 錯過截止期限\nThe deadline for the report is next Friday.\n(報告的截止日是下週五。)\nI stayed up all night to meet the deadline.\n(我熬夜一整晚來趕上截止期限。)"],["declare","declare(v.)宣布、聲明、申報\ndeclaration(n.)宣言、聲明、申報\ndeclare war on 對⋯宣戰\ndeclare goods 申報物品\nThe government declared a state of emergency after the earthquake.\n(地震後政府宣布進入緊急狀態。)\nDo you have anything to declare at customs?\n(您在海關有任何物品要申報嗎？)"],["decoration","decoration(n.)裝飾、裝飾品\ndecorate(v.)裝飾\ndecorative(adj.)裝飾用的\nChristmas decorations 聖誕裝飾\nfor decoration 作為裝飾\nWe put up Christmas decorations in the living room.\n(我們在客廳掛上聖誕裝飾。)\nThe flowers on the table are just for decoration.\n(桌上的花只是用來裝飾的。)"],["defeat","defeat(n./v.)擊敗、戰勝、失敗\n(無詞性變化)\nadmit defeat 認輸\na narrow defeat 惜敗\nOur team defeated the champions in the final.\n(我們的隊伍在決賽中擊敗了衛冕冠軍。)\nHe refused to admit defeat even after losing three times.\n(就算輸了三次，他仍拒絕認輸。)"],["defend","defend(v.)防衛、保衛、為⋯辯護\ndefense(n.)防禦、辯護\ndefender(n.)防守者、辯護者\ndefend against 防禦⋯\ndefend oneself 為自己辯護、自衛\nThe soldiers fought bravely to defend their country.\n(士兵們英勇作戰保衛國家。)\nShe stood up and defended her friend in front of the class.\n(她在全班面前站出來為朋友辯護。)"],["defense","defense(n.)防禦、保衛、辯護\ndefend(v.)防衛、辯護\ndefensive(adj.)防禦的、戒備的\nnational defense 國防\nin defense of 為了保衛、為⋯辯護\nOur team has a strong defense this season.\n(我們隊這一季的防守很強。)\nHe spoke in defense of his classmate.\n(他為同學辯護。)"],["defensible","defensible(adj.)可防禦的、可辯護的、站得住腳的\ndefend(v.)防衛、辯護\ndefensible position 易守的陣地、站得住腳的立場\nmorally defensible 道德上站得住腳的\nHer decision to quit was perfectly defensible.\n(她決定辭職是完全說得過去的。)\nThe castle was built on a hill to make it more defensible.\n(這座城堡建在山丘上，讓它更易於防守。)"],["defensive","defensive(adj.)防禦的、戒備的、防衛心強的\ndefense(n.)防禦\ndefensively(adv.)防衛地\nget defensive 變得有防衛心\ndefensive driving 防禦性駕駛\nHe gets defensive whenever someone criticizes his work.\n(只要有人批評他的作品，他就會變得很防衛。)\nThe team changed to a more defensive strategy.\n(這支隊伍改採更保守的防守策略。)"],["definite","definite(adj.)明確的、確定的\ndefinitely(adv.)一定、絕對\ndefinition(n.)定義\ndefinite answer 明確的答覆\ndefinite article 定冠詞\nI need a definite answer by tomorrow.\n(我明天之前需要一個明確的答覆。)\nI will definitely come to your birthday party.\n(我一定會去你的生日派對。)"],["delicate","delicate(adj.)精緻的、脆弱的、微妙的、敏感的\ndelicacy(n.)佳餚、精緻、微妙\ndelicately(adv.)精巧地、小心地\ndelicate skin 細嫩的肌膚\ndelicate situation 微妙的處境\nHandle the glass with care; it's very delicate.\n(小心拿這個玻璃杯，它很易碎。)\nTalking about money with friends can be a delicate matter.\n(和朋友談錢可能是件敏感的事。)"],["delight","delight(n./v.)欣喜、樂事、使高興\ndelighted(adj.)高興的\ndelightful(adj.)令人愉快的\nto one's delight 令某人高興的是\ntake delight in 以⋯為樂\nTo my delight, I passed the driving test.\n(令我高興的是，我通過了駕照考試。)\nThe magic show delighted the children.\n(魔術表演讓孩子們非常開心。)"],["delightful","delightful(adj.)令人愉快的、討人喜歡的\ndelight(n./v.)欣喜、使高興\ndelightfully(adv.)令人愉快地\na delightful evening 愉快的夜晚\ndelightful surprise 令人驚喜的事\nWe spent a delightful afternoon by the lake.\n(我們在湖邊度過了一個愉快的下午。)\nHer grandmother is a delightful old lady.\n(她的奶奶是一位討人喜歡的老太太。)"],["demand","demand(n./v.)要求、需求、需要\ndemanding(adj.)要求高的、費力的\nsupply and demand 供給與需求\nin demand 有需求的、搶手的\nThe workers demanded higher pay.\n(工人們要求加薪。)\nGood engineers are always in demand.\n(優秀的工程師總是很搶手。)"],["demonstrate","demonstrate(v.)示範、證明、示威\ndemonstration(n.)示範、示威\ndemonstrator(n.)示威者、示範者\ndemonstrate how to 示範如何⋯\ndemonstrate against 示威反對⋯\nThe teacher demonstrated how to use the microscope.\n(老師示範如何使用顯微鏡。)\nThe study demonstrates that exercise improves memory.\n(這項研究證明運動能增進記憶力。)"],["demonstration","demonstration(n.)示範、示威遊行、證明\ndemonstrate(v.)示範、示威\ngive a demonstration 進行示範\nhold a demonstration 舉行示威\nThe salesman gave a demonstration of the new vacuum cleaner.\n(推銷員示範了新款吸塵器的用法。)\nThousands of people joined the demonstration downtown.\n(數千人參加了市中心的示威遊行。)"],["dense","dense(adj.)密集的、濃密的、稠密的\ndensity(n.)密度\ndensely(adv.)密集地\ndense fog 濃霧\ndensely populated 人口稠密的\nFlights were delayed because of the dense fog.\n(班機因為濃霧而延誤。)\nTaipei is one of the most densely populated cities in Asia.\n(臺北是亞洲人口最稠密的城市之一。)"],["depart","depart(v.)出發、離開\ndeparture(n.)出發、離開\ndepart from 從⋯出發、背離\ndepart for 前往⋯\nThe train departs from Taipei Station at 8:30.\n(火車在八點半從臺北車站出發。)\nOur flight to Tokyo departs in two hours.\n(我們飛往東京的班機兩小時後起飛。)"],["departure","departure(n.)出發、離開、背離\ndepart(v.)出發、離開\ndeparture time 出發時間\ndeparture lounge 候機室\nPlease arrive at the airport two hours before departure.\n(請在起飛前兩小時抵達機場。)\nHer sudden departure surprised everyone in the office.\n(她突然離職讓辦公室裡的每個人都很驚訝。)"],["dependent","dependent(adj./n.)依賴的、取決於⋯的、受撫養者\ndepend(v.)依賴、取決於\ndependence(n.)依賴\nbe dependent on 依賴⋯\nfinancially dependent 經濟上依賴的\nMany teenagers are still financially dependent on their parents.\n(許多青少年在經濟上仍依賴父母。)\nOur plans are dependent on the weather.\n(我們的計畫取決於天氣。)"],["depression","depression(n.)沮喪、憂鬱症、經濟蕭條\ndepress(v.)使沮喪\ndepressed(adj.)沮喪的\nsuffer from depression 罹患憂鬱症\nthe Great Depression 經濟大蕭條\nTalking to a doctor can help people with depression.\n(和醫生談談可以幫助憂鬱症患者。)\nMany people lost their jobs during the Great Depression.\n(經濟大蕭條期間許多人失業。)"],["deserve","deserve(v.)應得、值得\ndeserved(adj.)應得的、理所當然的\ndeserve to 值得⋯、應該⋯\nwell deserved 實至名歸的\nYou worked hard, so you deserve a break.\n(你很努力，所以你應該休息一下。)\nHer award was well deserved.\n(她得獎實至名歸。)"],["desperate","desperate(adj.)絕望的、拚命的、極需要的\ndesperately(adv.)拚命地、極度地\ndesperation(n.)絕望\nbe desperate for 極需要⋯\na desperate attempt 拚死一搏\nAfter walking for hours, we were desperate for water.\n(走了好幾個小時之後，我們極需要喝水。)\nHe made a desperate attempt to catch the last train.\n(他拚命想趕上最後一班火車。)"],["despite","despite(prep.)儘管、不管\n(無詞性變化)\ndespite the fact that 儘管⋯的事實\ndespite oneself 不由自主地\nDespite the heavy rain, the game continued.\n(儘管下大雨，比賽仍繼續進行。)\nShe smiled despite herself when she saw the puppy.\n(看到那隻小狗，她不由自主地笑了。)"],["destruction","destruction(n.)破壞、毀滅\ndestroy(v.)破壞\ndestructive(adj.)破壞性的\nmass destruction 大規模毀滅\nenvironmental destruction 環境破壞\nThe earthquake caused great destruction in the area.\n(地震對該地區造成嚴重的破壞。)\nWe must stop the destruction of the rainforests.\n(我們必須阻止雨林遭受破壞。)"],["detective","detective(n./adj.)偵探、刑警、偵探的\ndetect(v.)察覺、偵測\ndetective story 偵探小說\nprivate detective 私家偵探\nSherlock Holmes is the most famous detective in fiction.\n(福爾摩斯是小說中最有名的偵探。)\nI stayed up late reading a detective story.\n(我熬夜看一本偵探小說。)"],["determination","determination(n.)決心、堅定\ndetermine(v.)決定\ndetermined(adj.)下定決心的\nwith determination 堅決地\nstrong determination 堅定的決心\nWith great determination, she finished the marathon.\n(她憑著堅定的決心跑完了馬拉松。)\nHis determination to succeed impressed everyone.\n(他想要成功的決心讓大家印象深刻。)"],["device","device(n.)裝置、設備、手段\ndevise(v.)設計、發明\nelectronic device 電子裝置\nsafety device 安全裝置\nSmartphones are the most common electronic devices today.\n(智慧型手機是現今最常見的電子裝置。)\nThis device can measure your heart rate.\n(這個裝置可以測量你的心跳。)"],["devise","devise(v.)設計、想出、發明\ndevice(n.)裝置、設備\ndevise a plan 想出計畫\ndevise a method 設計方法\nThe students devised a plan to reduce waste at school.\n(學生們想出一個減少校園垃圾的計畫。)\nScientists devised a new way to clean the ocean.\n(科學家設計出一種清理海洋的新方法。)"],["devote","devote(v.)奉獻、致力於、把(時間、精力)用於\ndevoted(adj.)忠誠的、全心全意的\ndevotion(n.)奉獻、熱愛\ndevote oneself to 致力於⋯\ndevote time to 把時間花在⋯\nShe devoted her life to helping poor children.\n(她一生致力於幫助貧窮的孩子。)\nI devote two hours a day to practicing the piano.\n(我每天花兩個小時練鋼琴。)"],["dew","dew(n.)露水、露珠\ndewy(adj.)帶露水的、濕潤的\nmorning dew 晨露\ndrops of dew 露珠\nThe grass was wet with morning dew.\n(草地被晨露沾濕了。)\nDrops of dew shone like diamonds in the sun.\n(露珠在陽光下像鑽石般閃閃發亮。)"],["diagram","diagram(n./v.)圖解、圖表、用圖表示\ndiagrammatic(adj.)圖解的\ndraw a diagram 畫圖解\ntree diagram 樹狀圖\nThe teacher drew a diagram to explain how the heart works.\n(老師畫了一張圖來解釋心臟如何運作。)\nFollow the diagram to put the desk together.\n(依照圖解組裝書桌。)"],["differ","differ(v.)不同、意見不合\ndifference(n.)差異\ndifferent(adj.)不同的\ndiffer from 和⋯不同\ndiffer in 在⋯方面不同\nCustoms differ from country to country.\n(各國的習俗都不相同。)\nThe two brothers differ greatly in personality.\n(這兩兄弟的個性差異很大。)"],["digest","digest(n./v.)消化、理解、文摘\ndigestion(n.)消化\ndigestive(adj.)消化的\ndigest food 消化食物\ndigest information 消化(理解)資訊\nSome people find it hard to digest milk.\n(有些人很難消化牛奶。)\nIt took me a while to digest the bad news.\n(我花了一段時間才消化這個壞消息。)"],["digital","digital(adj.)數位的、數字的\ndigitally(adv.)數位地\ndigitize(v.)數位化\ndigital camera 數位相機\ndigital age 數位時代\nIn the digital age, information spreads very quickly.\n(在數位時代，資訊傳播得非常快。)\nShe took the photos with a digital camera.\n(她用數位相機拍了這些照片。)"],["dignity","dignity(n.)尊嚴、莊重\ndignified(adj.)有尊嚴的、莊重的\nhuman dignity 人性尊嚴\nwith dignity 有尊嚴地\nEveryone should be treated with dignity.\n(每個人都應該被有尊嚴地對待。)\nShe accepted the defeat with dignity.\n(她很有風度地接受了失敗。)"],["diligence","diligence(n.)勤奮、用功\ndiligent(adj.)勤奮的\ndiligently(adv.)勤奮地\nhard work and diligence 努力與勤奮\ndue diligence 盡職調查、應有的謹慎\nHer diligence finally paid off when she got into a top university.\n(她考上頂尖大學時，她的勤奮終於有了回報。)\nSuccess comes from diligence, not luck.\n(成功來自勤奮，而不是運氣。)"],["diligent","diligent(adj.)勤奮的、用功的\ndiligence(n.)勤奮\ndiligently(adv.)勤奮地\ndiligent student 用功的學生\nbe diligent in 在⋯方面勤奮\nHe is a diligent student who never misses a class.\n(他是個從不缺課的用功學生。)\nBe diligent in your studies, and you will see results.\n(認真讀書，你就會看到成果。)"],["diploma","diploma(n.)畢業證書、文憑\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh school diploma 高中畢業證書\nreceive a diploma 領取畢業證書\nShe proudly received her diploma at the graduation ceremony.\n(她在畢業典禮上驕傲地領取了畢業證書。)\nA high school diploma is required for this job.\n(這份工作需要高中畢業證書。)"],["diplomat","diplomat(n.)外交官、有手腕的人\ndiplomatic(adj.)外交的、有手腕的\ndiplomacy(n.)外交、交際手腕\ncareer diplomat 職業外交官\nforeign diplomat 外國外交官\nHer father is a diplomat who has lived in many countries.\n(她的爸爸是一位外交官，曾住過許多國家。)\nHe is a real diplomat and never upsets anyone.\n(他很會做人，從不得罪任何人。)"],["disability","disability(n.)失能、身心障礙\ndisabled(adj.)身心障礙的\npeople with disabilities 身心障礙者\nlearning disability 學習障礙\nThe building is designed for people with disabilities.\n(這棟建築是為身心障礙者設計的。)\nStudents with learning disabilities can get extra help.\n(有學習障礙的學生可以得到額外的協助。)"],["disadvantage","disadvantage(n./v.)缺點、不利條件、使處於不利地位\ndisadvantaged(adj.)弱勢的、處境不利的\nat a disadvantage 處於不利地位\nadvantages and disadvantages 優缺點\nOne disadvantage of living in the city is the noise.\n(住在城市的一個缺點是噪音。)\nStudents without computers are at a disadvantage.\n(沒有電腦的學生處於不利地位。)"],["disappoint(ment)","disappoint(v.)使失望、disappointment(n.)失望、令人失望的人或事\ndisappointed(adj.)感到失望的\ndisappointing(adj.)令人失望的\nto one's disappointment 令某人失望的是\nbe disappointed with 對⋯感到失望\nI don't want to disappoint my parents.\n(我不想讓我爸媽失望。)\nTo my disappointment, the concert was canceled.\n(令我失望的是，演唱會取消了。)"],["disaster","disaster(n.)災難、徹底的失敗\ndisastrous(adj.)災難性的\nnatural disaster 天災\na complete disaster 一場徹底的失敗\nEarthquakes and typhoons are common natural disasters in Taiwan.\n(地震和颱風是臺灣常見的天災。)\nOur first attempt at cooking was a complete disaster.\n(我們第一次嘗試煮飯完全是一場災難。)"],["discipline","discipline(n./v.)紀律、訓練、學科、懲戒\ndisciplined(adj.)有紀律的\nself-discipline 自律\nacademic discipline 學科\nSelf-discipline is the key to success.\n(自律是成功的關鍵。)\nThe teacher disciplined the students for cheating.\n(老師因為作弊懲處了那些學生。)"],["discourage(ment)","discourage(v.)使氣餒、勸阻、discouragement(n.)氣餒、勸阻\ndiscouraged(adj.)氣餒的\ndiscouraging(adj.)令人氣餒的\ndiscourage someone from 勸阻某人不要⋯\nfeel discouraged 感到氣餒\nDon't let one failure discourage you.\n(不要讓一次的失敗使你氣餒。)\nHis parents discouraged him from riding a motorcycle.\n(他的父母勸他不要騎機車。)"],["disguise","disguise(v./n.)偽裝、喬裝、掩飾\n(無詞性變化)\nin disguise 喬裝的、偽裝的\na blessing in disguise 因禍得福\nThe thief disguised himself as a delivery man.\n(小偷喬裝成送貨員。)\nMissing the bus was a blessing in disguise.\n(錯過公車反而因禍得福。)"],["disgust","disgust(n./v.)厭惡、反感、使厭惡\ndisgusting(adj.)令人作嘔的\ndisgusted(adj.)感到厭惡的\nin disgust 厭惡地\nbe disgusted by 對⋯感到厭惡\nShe looked at the dirty kitchen in disgust.\n(她厭惡地看著髒亂的廚房。)\nThe smell of the garbage disgusted everyone.\n(垃圾的臭味讓大家都很反感。)"],["dismiss","dismiss(v.)解散、讓⋯離開、解僱、不予理會\ndismissal(n.)解僱、解散\ndismiss a class 下課、讓學生離開\ndismiss an idea 不理會某個想法\nThe teacher dismissed the class ten minutes early.\n(老師提早十分鐘下課。)\nHe dismissed my suggestion as unrealistic.\n(他認為我的建議不切實際而不予理會。)"],["disorder","disorder(n./v.)混亂、失調、疾病、使混亂\ndisorderly(adj.)混亂的、無秩序的\nin disorder 混亂地\neating disorder 飲食失調\nAfter the party, the house was in complete disorder.\n(派對結束後，房子一片混亂。)\nLack of sleep can lead to many health disorders.\n(睡眠不足可能導致許多健康上的失調。)"],["dispute","dispute(n./v.)爭論、糾紛、對⋯提出異議\n(無詞性變化)\nin dispute 有爭議的\nsettle a dispute 解決爭端\nThe two countries are in a dispute over the island.\n(兩國為了那座島發生爭端。)\nNo one can dispute the fact that she is talented.\n(沒有人能否認她很有天分。)"],["distinct","distinct(adj.)不同的、明顯的、清楚的\ndistinction(n.)區別、卓越\ndistinctly(adv.)清楚地、明顯地\ndistinct from 與⋯不同\na distinct possibility 很有可能的事\nThe two languages are quite distinct from each other.\n(這兩種語言彼此差異相當大。)\nThere is a distinct smell of smoke in the room.\n(房間裡有一股明顯的煙味。)"],["distinguish","distinguish(v.)區分、辨別、使傑出\ndistinguished(adj.)傑出的、著名的\ndistinguishable(adj.)可區分的\ndistinguish A from B 區分A和B\ndistinguish between 區分⋯\nCan you distinguish right from wrong?\n(你能分辨是非嗎？)\nIt is hard to distinguish between the twins.\n(很難分辨這對雙胞胎。)"],["distinguished","distinguished(adj.)傑出的、著名的、高貴的\ndistinguish(v.)區分、使傑出\ndistinguished guest 貴賓\ndistinguished career 傑出的職業生涯\nWe welcomed several distinguished guests to the ceremony.\n(我們歡迎幾位貴賓蒞臨典禮。)\nThe professor had a distinguished career in science.\n(這位教授在科學界有傑出的職業生涯。)"],["distribute","distribute(v.)分發、分配、散布\ndistribution(n.)分配、分布\ndistributor(n.)經銷商\ndistribute flyers 發傳單\nevenly distributed 平均分布的\nVolunteers distributed food to the flood victims.\n(志工們分發食物給水災災民。)\nThe teacher distributed the test papers to the class.\n(老師把考卷發給全班。)"],["distribution","distribution(n.)分配、分發、分布\ndistribute(v.)分發、分配\ndistributor(n.)經銷商\nfood distribution 糧食分配\nthe distribution of wealth 財富分配\nThe unfair distribution of wealth causes many social problems.\n(財富分配不公造成許多社會問題。)\nThe map shows the distribution of rainfall in Taiwan.\n(這張地圖顯示臺灣的雨量分布。)"],["district","district(n.)區域、地區、行政區\n(無詞性變化)\nschool district 學區\nshopping district 購物區\nXinyi District is famous for Taipei 101.\n(信義區以臺北101聞名。)\nThey moved to a better school district.\n(他們搬到了一個比較好的學區。)"],["disturb","disturb(v.)打擾、擾亂、使不安\ndisturbance(n.)打擾、騷亂\ndisturbing(adj.)令人不安的\nDo not disturb. 請勿打擾。\ndisturb the peace 擾亂安寧\nPlease don't disturb me while I'm studying.\n(我讀書的時候請不要打擾我。)\nThe news about the accident disturbed many people.\n(這起事故的新聞讓許多人感到不安。)"],["diverse","diverse(adj.)多樣的、不同的\ndiversity(n.)多樣性\ndiversify(v.)使多樣化\nculturally diverse 文化多元的\ndiverse backgrounds 不同的背景\nTaiwan is a culturally diverse society.\n(臺灣是一個文化多元的社會。)\nOur club has members from diverse backgrounds.\n(我們的社團有來自不同背景的成員。)"],["diversity","diversity(n.)多樣性、差異\ndiverse(adj.)多樣的\ndiversify(v.)使多樣化\ncultural diversity 文化多樣性\nbiological diversity 生物多樣性\nThe island is famous for its biological diversity.\n(這座島以生物多樣性聞名。)\nOur school respects cultural diversity.\n(我們學校尊重文化多樣性。)"],["divine","divine(adj.)神的、神聖的、極好的\ndivinity(n.)神性、神學\ndivine power 神力\ndivine help 神助\nMany people pray for divine help during hard times.\n(許多人在艱困時期祈求神的幫助。)\nThe cake tasted absolutely divine.\n(這個蛋糕吃起來簡直棒極了。)"],["divorce","divorce(n./v.)離婚、與⋯離婚、分離\ndivorced(adj.)離婚的\nget a divorce 離婚\ndivorce rate 離婚率\nHis parents got a divorce when he was ten.\n(他十歲時父母離婚了。)\nThe divorce rate has risen in recent years.\n(近年來離婚率上升了。)"],["dodge","dodge(v./n.)閃避、躲避、推託\n(無詞性變化)\ndodge a ball 躲球\ndodge a question 迴避問題\nHe quickly dodged the ball.\n(他迅速閃過了球。)\nThe politician dodged the reporter's question.\n(那位政治人物迴避了記者的問題。)"],["dominant","dominant(adj.)主要的、占優勢的、支配的\ndominate(v.)支配、主宰\ndominance(n.)優勢、支配\ndominant role 主導角色\ndominant gene 顯性基因\nEnglish is the dominant language on the Internet.\n(英文是網路上的主要語言。)\nShe plays a dominant role in the team.\n(她在團隊中扮演主導的角色。)"],["dominate","dominate(v.)支配、主宰、在⋯中占優勢\ndominant(adj.)占優勢的\ndomination(n.)支配、統治\ndominate the market 主導市場\ndominate the conversation 主導對話\nA few big companies dominate the smartphone market.\n(少數幾家大公司主導智慧型手機市場。)\nHe always tries to dominate the conversation.\n(他總是想主導談話。)"],["draft","draft(n./v.)草稿、草擬、徵兵\n(無詞性變化)\nfirst draft 初稿\ndraft a letter 草擬一封信\nI finished the first draft of my essay last night.\n(我昨晚完成了作文的初稿。)\nThe lawyer drafted a new contract for us.\n(律師為我們草擬了一份新合約。)"],["dread","dread(n./v.)恐懼、害怕、擔憂\ndreadful(adj.)可怕的、糟透的\ndread + V-ing 害怕做⋯\nlive in dread of 生活在對⋯的恐懼中\nI dread going to the dentist.\n(我很怕去看牙醫。)\nShe was filled with dread before the final exam.\n(期末考前她心中充滿恐懼。)"],["drift","drift(v./n.)漂流、漂移、漸漸變得、趨勢\ndrifter(n.)流浪者\ndrift apart 漸行漸遠\ndrift off 漸漸睡著\nThe boat drifted slowly down the river.\n(小船沿著河慢慢漂流。)\nWe drifted apart after high school.\n(高中畢業後我們漸行漸遠。)"],["drill","drill(n./v.)鑽孔機、操練、演習、鑽孔\n(無詞性變化)\nfire drill 消防演習\nelectric drill 電鑽\nOur school holds a fire drill every semester.\n(我們學校每學期舉行一次消防演習。)\nThe worker drilled a hole in the wall.\n(工人在牆上鑽了一個洞。)"],["drowsy","drowsy(adj.)昏昏欲睡的\ndrowsiness(n.)睡意\ndrowsily(adv.)昏昏欲睡地\nfeel drowsy 覺得想睡\nmake someone drowsy 使某人想睡\nThis medicine may make you feel drowsy.\n(這種藥可能會讓你昏昏欲睡。)\nI always feel drowsy after lunch.\n(我午餐後總是昏昏欲睡。)"],["durable","durable(adj.)耐用的、持久的\ndurability(n.)耐用性\nduration(n.)持續時間\ndurable goods 耐久財\ndurable material 耐用的材料\nThese hiking boots are light and durable.\n(這雙登山靴又輕又耐用。)\nPlastic is cheap and durable, but it harms the environment.\n(塑膠便宜又耐用，但會危害環境。)"],["dusty","dusty(adj.)滿是灰塵的\ndust(n./v.)灰塵、撢去灰塵\ndusty road 塵土飛揚的路\ndusty room 布滿灰塵的房間\nWe found some dusty old books in the attic.\n(我們在閣樓裡發現一些布滿灰塵的舊書。)\nThe car was dusty after the long trip.\n(長途旅行後車子滿是灰塵。)"],["dye","dye(n./v.)染料、染色\ndyed(adj.)染過的\ndye one's hair 染頭髮\nnatural dye 天然染料\nShe dyed her hair purple during summer vacation.\n(她暑假時把頭髮染成紫色。)\nThe cloth was colored with natural dye.\n(這塊布是用天然染料染色的。)"],["dynamic","dynamic(adj.)充滿活力的、動態的、有活力的\ndynamics(n.)動力學、動態\ndynamically(adv.)動態地\ndynamic personality 充滿活力的個性\ndynamic economy 蓬勃的經濟\nOur new principal is a dynamic leader.\n(我們的新校長是一位充滿活力的領導者。)\nThe city has a dynamic and growing economy.\n(這座城市擁有蓬勃且不斷成長的經濟。)"],["dynasty","dynasty(n.)王朝、朝代\ndynastic(adj.)王朝的\nTang Dynasty 唐朝\nMing Dynasty 明朝\nMany famous poets lived during the Tang Dynasty.\n(許多有名的詩人生活在唐朝。)\nThe dynasty ruled China for nearly three hundred years.\n(這個王朝統治中國將近三百年。)"],["earnest","earnest(adj./n.)認真的、誠摯的、認真\nearnestly(adv.)認真地、誠懇地\nin earnest 認真地、正式地\nan earnest effort 誠摯的努力\nHe made an earnest effort to improve his grades.\n(他認真努力地提升自己的成績。)\nThe rain began in earnest after lunch.\n(午餐過後，雨開始下得很大。)"],["earphone","earphone(n.)耳機\n(無詞性變化)\nwear earphones 戴耳機\nwireless earphones 無線耳機\nShe always wears earphones on the bus.\n(她在公車上總是戴著耳機。)\nMy new wireless earphones have great sound.\n(我新買的無線耳機音質很好。)"],["economic","economic(adj.)經濟的、經濟上的\neconomically(adv.)經濟上\neconomic growth 經濟成長\neconomic crisis 經濟危機\nThe country has enjoyed rapid economic growth.\n(這個國家經濟快速成長。)\nMany families suffered during the economic crisis.\n(經濟危機期間，許多家庭受苦。)"],["economical","economical(adj.)節省的、經濟實惠的\neconomically(adv.)節省地\neconomical car 省油的車\nbe economical with 節省使用…\nTaking the MRT is an economical way to travel.\n(搭捷運是一種經濟實惠的交通方式。)\nMy mother is very economical with money.\n(我媽媽用錢很節省。)"],["economics","economics(n.)經濟學\n(無詞性變化)\nstudy economics 研讀經濟學\nhome economics 家政\nMy brother is studying economics in college.\n(我哥哥在大學念經濟學。)\nEconomics helps us understand how markets work.\n(經濟學幫助我們了解市場如何運作。)"],["economist","economist(n.)經濟學家\n(無詞性變化)\na leading economist 頂尖的經濟學家\neconomists predict 經濟學家預測\nEconomists predict that prices will rise next year.\n(經濟學家預測明年物價會上漲。)\nShe hopes to become a famous economist.\n(她希望成為知名的經濟學家。)"],["economy","economy(n.)經濟、節約\n(無詞性變化)\nglobal economy 全球經濟\neconomy class 經濟艙\nTourism is important to the local economy.\n(觀光業對當地經濟很重要。)\nWe flew economy class to save money.\n(我們為了省錢搭經濟艙。)"],["efficiency","efficiency(n.)效率、效能\nefficient(adj.)有效率的\nefficiently(adv.)有效率地\nenergy efficiency 能源效率\nimprove efficiency 提高效率\nThe new machine greatly improved our efficiency.\n(新機器大幅提高了我們的效率。)\nLED lights are known for their energy efficiency.\n(LED燈以節能聞名。)"],["elastic","elastic(adj./n.)有彈性的、鬆緊帶\nelasticity(n.)彈性\nelastic band 橡皮筋、鬆緊帶\nelastic material 有彈性的材質\nThese pants have an elastic waist.\n(這條褲子的腰部是鬆緊帶。)\nRubber is a very elastic material.\n(橡膠是非常有彈性的材料。)"],["electronics","electronics(n.)電子學、電子產品\nelectronic(adj.)電子的\nconsumer electronics 消費性電子產品\nelectronics store 電子產品店\nHe bought a new laptop at the electronics store.\n(他在電子產品店買了一台新筆電。)\nTaiwan is famous for its electronics industry.\n(臺灣以電子產業聞名。)"],["elegant","elegant(adj.)優雅的、高雅的\nelegance(n.)優雅\nelegantly(adv.)優雅地\nan elegant dress 優雅的洋裝\nelegant style 高雅的風格\nShe looked elegant in her long black dress.\n(她穿著黑色長禮服看起來很優雅。)\nThe hotel lobby was decorated in an elegant style.\n(飯店大廳裝潢得很高雅。)"],["elementary","elementary(adj.)基本的、初級的\nelement(n.)要素、元素\nelementary school 小學\nelementary level 初級程度\nMy sister is still in elementary school.\n(我妹妹還在念小學。)\nThis book is written for elementary learners.\n(這本書是為初學者寫的。)"],["eliminate","eliminate(v.)消除、淘汰\nelimination(n.)消除、淘汰\neliminate waste 減少浪費\nbe eliminated from 被…淘汰\nWe should eliminate plastic waste in our school.\n(我們應該消除校園裡的塑膠垃圾。)\nOur team was eliminated in the first round.\n(我們隊在第一輪就被淘汰了。)"],["elsewhere","elsewhere(adv.)在別處、到別處\n(無詞性變化)\nlook elsewhere 到別處找\nanywhere elsewhere 其他任何地方\nIf this shop is closed, we can eat elsewhere.\n(如果這家店關門，我們可以去別的地方吃。)\nPrices here are higher than elsewhere in the city.\n(這裡的物價比城市其他地方高。)"],["embarrass(ment)","embarrass(v.)使尷尬、使難堪、embarrassment(n.)尷尬、難堪\nembarrassed(adj.)感到尷尬的\nembarrassing(adj.)令人尷尬的\nfeel embarrassed 感到尷尬\nto one's embarrassment 令某人尷尬的是\nHis mother embarrassed him in front of his friends.\n(他媽媽在他朋友面前讓他很難堪。)\nHer face turned red with embarrassment.\n(她尷尬得臉都紅了。)"],["embassy","embassy(n.)大使館\nambassador(n.)大使\nthe U.S. Embassy 美國大使館\nembassy staff 大使館人員\nYou need to apply for a visa at the embassy.\n(你需要到大使館申請簽證。)\nThe embassy helped the travelers return home.\n(大使館協助旅客返國。)"],["emerge","emerge(v.)浮現、出現、顯露\nemergence(n.)出現、興起\nemerge from 從…出現\nnew problems emerge 新問題浮現\nThe sun emerged from behind the clouds.\n(太陽從雲層後面露了出來。)\nNew problems emerged after the plan started.\n(計畫開始後，新的問題浮現了。)"],["emphasis","emphasis(n.)強調、重點\nemphasize(v.)強調\nput emphasis on 強調、重視\nspecial emphasis 特別強調\nOur school puts great emphasis on reading.\n(我們學校非常重視閱讀。)\nThe teacher emphasized the importance of practice.\n(老師強調練習的重要性。)"],["empire","empire(n.)帝國、企業集團\nemperor(n.)皇帝\nthe Roman Empire 羅馬帝國\nbuild an empire 建立帝國\nThe Roman Empire lasted for hundreds of years.\n(羅馬帝國延續了數百年。)\nHe built a business empire from a small shop.\n(他從一家小店建立起商業帝國。)"],["enclose","enclose(v.)圍住、隨函附上\nenclosure(n.)圍場、附件\nplease find enclosed 隨信附上\nenclose a check 隨信附上支票\nI have enclosed a copy of my report.\n(我已隨信附上一份我的報告。)\nThe garden is enclosed by a tall wall.\n(這座花園被高牆圍住。)"],["encounter","encounter(n./v.)遭遇、偶遇、碰上\n(無詞性變化)\nencounter problems 遇到問題\na chance encounter 不期而遇\nWe encountered heavy traffic on the way home.\n(我們回家路上遇到嚴重塞車。)\nIt was a chance encounter with an old friend.\n(那是和老朋友的一次偶遇。)"],["endanger","endanger(v.)危及、使陷入危險\nendangered(adj.)瀕臨絕種的\nendangered species 瀕危物種\nendanger lives 危及生命\nDrunk driving endangers the lives of others.\n(酒駕會危及他人的生命。)\nThe black-faced spoonbill is an endangered species.\n(黑面琵鷺是瀕危物種。)"],["endure","endure(v.)忍受、持續\nendurance(n.)耐力、忍耐力\nendure pain 忍受痛苦\ncan't endure 無法忍受\nShe endured the pain without complaint.\n(她毫無怨言地忍受痛苦。)\nRunning a marathon requires great endurance.\n(跑馬拉松需要很好的耐力。)"],["enforce(ment)","enforce(v.)執行、實施、enforcement(n.)執行、實施\n(無詞性變化)\nenforce the law 執法\nlaw enforcement 執法(機關)\nThe police are responsible for enforcing the law.\n(警察負責執法。)\nStricter enforcement of traffic rules is needed.\n(需要更嚴格地執行交通規則。)"],["engineering","engineering(n.)工程、工程學\nengineer(n.)工程師\nelectrical engineering 電機工程\nengineering degree 工程學位\nHe wants to study engineering at university.\n(他想在大學念工程。)\nThe bridge is a great work of engineering.\n(這座橋是工程上的傑作。)"],["enlarge(ment)","enlarge(v.)擴大、放大、enlargement(n.)擴大、放大(的照片)\n(無詞性變化)\nenlarge a photo 放大照片\nenlarge the size 擴大尺寸\nCan you enlarge this photo for me?\n(你可以幫我放大這張照片嗎？)\nThe school plans to enlarge the library.\n(學校計劃擴建圖書館。)"],["enormous","enormous(adj.)巨大的、龐大的\nenormously(adv.)極大地\nan enormous amount 大量\nenormous pressure 龐大的壓力\nThe tree in the park is enormous.\n(公園裡的那棵樹非常巨大。)\nStudents face enormous pressure before exams.\n(考試前學生面臨龐大的壓力。)"],["ensure","ensure(v.)確保、保證\n(無詞性變化)\nensure safety 確保安全\nensure that 確保…\nPlease ensure that all windows are closed.\n(請確保所有窗戶都已關上。)\nWearing a helmet helps ensure your safety.\n(戴安全帽有助於確保你的安全。)"],["entertain(ment)","entertain(v.)娛樂、招待、entertainment(n.)娛樂、娛樂活動\nentertaining(adj.)有趣的、令人愉快的\nentertainer(n.)藝人、表演者\nentertain guests 招待客人\nentertainment industry 娛樂產業\nThe clown entertained the children at the party.\n(小丑在派對上逗孩子們開心。)\nWatching movies is my favorite form of entertainment.\n(看電影是我最喜歡的娛樂。)"],["enthusiasm","enthusiasm(n.)熱情、熱忱\nenthusiastic(adj.)熱情的、熱衷的\nwith enthusiasm 熱情地\nlack enthusiasm 缺乏熱忱\nShe talked about her trip with great enthusiasm.\n(她非常熱情地談論她的旅行。)\nThe students are enthusiastic about the school festival.\n(學生們對校慶非常熱衷。)"],["equality","equality(n.)平等、相等\nequal(adj.)平等的、相等的\ngender equality 性別平等\nracial equality 種族平等\nWe should fight for gender equality.\n(我們應該為性別平等而努力。)\nEveryone deserves equality before the law.\n(每個人在法律之前都應平等。)"],["equip(ment)","equip(v.)裝備、配備、equipment(n.)設備、器材\nequipped(adj.)配備…的\nbe equipped with 配備有…\nsports equipment 運動器材\nThe classroom is equipped with a projector.\n(這間教室配有投影機。)\nWe need new sports equipment for the gym.\n(體育館需要新的運動器材。)"],["era","era(n.)時代、紀元\n(無詞性變化)\na new era 新時代\nthe digital era 數位時代\nWe are living in the digital era.\n(我們生活在數位時代。)\nThe invention of the computer began a new era.\n(電腦的發明開啟了新時代。)"],["essential","essential(adj./n.)必要的、基本的、要素\nessentially(adv.)本質上、基本上\nessential to 對…不可或缺\nthe essentials 必需品、要點\nWater is essential to all living things.\n(水對所有生物都不可或缺。)\nPack only the essentials for the camping trip.\n(露營只要帶必需品就好。)"],["establish(ment)","establish(v.)建立、設立、establishment(n.)建立、機構\nestablished(adj.)已確立的、知名的\nestablish a company 創立公司\nestablish a relationship 建立關係\nThe school was established in 1946.\n(這所學校創立於1946年。)\nThe establishment of the new park took two years.\n(新公園的建設花了兩年。)"],["estimate","estimate(n./v.)估計、估算\nestimation(n.)估計、判斷\nrough estimate 粗略估計\nit is estimated that 據估計…\nIt is estimated that 500 people came to the concert.\n(據估計有五百人來參加演唱會。)\nCan you give me a rough estimate of the cost?\n(你能給我一個粗略的費用估計嗎？)"],["ethnic","ethnic(adj./n.)種族的、民族的、少數民族成員\nethnicity(n.)種族、民族\nethnic group 族群\nethnic food 異國料理、民族料理\nTaiwan has many different ethnic groups.\n(臺灣有許多不同的族群。)\nWe tried some ethnic food at the night market.\n(我們在夜市嘗試了一些異國料理。)"],["evaluate","evaluate(v.)評估、評價\nevaluation(n.)評估、評價\nevaluate performance 評估表現\ncarefully evaluate 仔細評估\nTeachers evaluate students in many different ways.\n(老師用許多不同方式評量學生。)\nWe need to evaluate the risks before we decide.\n(我們做決定前需要評估風險。)"],["evaluation","evaluation(n.)評估、評價\nevaluate(v.)評估、評價\nself-evaluation 自我評量\nperformance evaluation 績效評估\nThe teacher gave each student a written evaluation.\n(老師給每位學生一份書面評語。)\nSelf-evaluation helps you learn from mistakes.\n(自我評量能幫助你從錯誤中學習。)"],["eventual","eventual(adj.)最終的、最後的\neventually(adv.)最後、終於\nthe eventual winner 最後的贏家\neventually succeed 最終成功\nShe became the eventual winner of the contest.\n(她成為這場比賽最後的贏家。)\nAfter many tries, he eventually passed the test.\n(試了很多次之後，他終於通過了考試。)"],["evidence","evidence(n./v.)證據、證明\nevident(adj.)明顯的\nscientific evidence 科學證據\nlack of evidence 缺乏證據\nThere is no evidence that he stole the money.\n(沒有證據顯示他偷了錢。)\nScientists have found new evidence of water on Mars.\n(科學家發現了火星上有水的新證據。)"],["evident","evident(adj.)明顯的、顯而易見的\nevidently(adv.)明顯地\nevidence(n.)證據\nit is evident that 很明顯…\nself-evident 不言而喻的\nIt was evident that she was very tired.\n(很明顯她非常疲累。)\nHis love for music is evident in his songs.\n(他對音樂的熱愛在他的歌曲中顯而易見。)"],["exaggerate","exaggerate(v.)誇大、誇張\nexaggeration(n.)誇大、誇張\ngreatly exaggerate 過度誇大\nexaggerate the problem 誇大問題\nHe always exaggerates when he tells stories.\n(他講故事時總是誇大其詞。)\nIt is no exaggeration to say she saved my life.\n(說她救了我一命一點也不誇張。)"],["exception","exception(n.)例外、除外\nexceptional(adj.)特殊的、傑出的\nexcept(prep.)除了\nwith the exception of 除了…之外\nmake an exception 破例\nEveryone passed the test with the exception of Tom.\n(除了湯姆之外，大家都通過了考試。)\nThe teacher made an exception for me this time.\n(老師這次為我破例。)"],["exhaust","exhaust(n./v.)廢氣、使筋疲力盡、耗盡\nexhausted(adj.)筋疲力盡的\nexhausting(adj.)使人疲憊的\ncar exhaust 汽車廢氣\nexhaust resources 耗盡資源\nCar exhaust is a major cause of air pollution.\n(汽車廢氣是空氣汙染的主要原因。)\nI was exhausted after the long hike.\n(長途健行後我筋疲力盡。)"],["exhibit","exhibit(n./v.)展覽品、展出、表現出\nexhibition(n.)展覽、展覽會\nexhibit paintings 展出畫作\non exhibit 展出中\nThe museum is exhibiting paintings by local artists.\n(博物館正在展出本地藝術家的畫作。)\nThe child exhibited a great talent for music.\n(那個孩子展現出極高的音樂天分。)"],["expand","expand(v.)擴大、擴展、膨脹\nexpansion(n.)擴張、擴展\nexpand a business 擴展事業\nexpand one's knowledge 擴展知識\nThe company plans to expand into Japan.\n(這家公司計劃拓展到日本。)\nMetal expands when it is heated.\n(金屬受熱時會膨脹。)"],["expansion","expansion(n.)擴張、擴展、膨脹\nexpand(v.)擴大、擴展\nrapid expansion 快速擴張\neconomic expansion 經濟擴張\nThe rapid expansion of the city caused traffic problems.\n(城市快速擴張造成了交通問題。)\nThe airport expansion will be finished next year.\n(機場擴建工程明年將完工。)"],["experimental","experimental(adj.)實驗的、試驗性的\nexperiment(n./v.)實驗、做實驗\nexperimental results 實驗結果\nexperimental stage 試驗階段\nThe new medicine is still in the experimental stage.\n(新藥仍處於試驗階段。)\nThe band is known for its experimental music.\n(這個樂團以實驗性音樂聞名。)"],["explanation","explanation(n.)解釋、說明\nexplain(v.)解釋\ngive an explanation 提出解釋\na clear explanation 清楚的說明\nThe teacher gave a clear explanation of the rule.\n(老師清楚地解釋了這條規則。)\nThere must be an explanation for his strange behavior.\n(他奇怪的行為一定有原因。)"],["explosion","explosion(n.)爆炸、激增\nexplode(v.)爆炸\na loud explosion 巨大的爆炸聲\npopulation explosion 人口爆炸\nThe explosion broke all the windows nearby.\n(爆炸震碎了附近所有的窗戶。)\nThe world faced a population explosion last century.\n(上個世紀全世界面臨人口爆炸。)"],["explosive","explosive(adj./n.)爆炸性的、易爆的、炸藥\nexplode(v.)爆炸\nexplosion(n.)爆炸\nexplosive device 爆裂物\nan explosive issue 爆炸性的議題\nGasoline is highly explosive.\n(汽油非常容易爆炸。)\nThe police found explosives in the car.\n(警方在車上發現了炸藥。)"],["expose","expose(v.)暴露、揭露、使接觸\nexposure(n.)暴露、接觸\nbe exposed to 暴露於、接觸到\nexpose the truth 揭露真相\nDon't expose your skin to the sun for too long.\n(不要讓皮膚曝曬在陽光下太久。)\nThe reporter exposed the truth about the scandal.\n(記者揭露了那起醜聞的真相。)"],["exposure","exposure(n.)暴露、接觸、曝光\nexpose(v.)暴露、揭露\nexposure to 接觸…、暴露於…\nmedia exposure 媒體曝光\nToo much exposure to the sun can harm your skin.\n(過度曝曬會傷害皮膚。)\nEarly exposure to English helps children learn faster.\n(從小接觸英文能幫助孩子學得更快。)"],["extend","extend(v.)延長、延伸、擴大\nextension(n.)延長、分機\nextensive(adj.)廣泛的\nextend a deadline 延長期限\nextend one's hand 伸出手\nThe teacher extended the deadline by one week.\n(老師把截止日期延長了一週。)\nThe road extends all the way to the mountains.\n(這條路一路延伸到山區。)"],["extent","extent(n.)程度、範圍\n(無詞性變化)\nto some extent 在某種程度上\nthe full extent 全部範圍\nI agree with you to some extent.\n(我在某種程度上同意你。)\nWe don't yet know the extent of the damage.\n(我們還不知道損害的程度。)"],["facial","facial(adj.)臉部的、面部的\nface(n.)臉\nfacial expression 臉部表情\nfacial features 五官\nHer facial expression showed that she was angry.\n(她的表情顯示她很生氣。)\nThe twins have very similar facial features.\n(那對雙胞胎的五官非常相似。)"],["facility","facility(n.)設施、設備、能力\nfacilitate(v.)促進、使便利\nsports facilities 運動設施\npublic facilities 公共設施\nOur school has excellent sports facilities.\n(我們學校有很棒的運動設施。)\nPlease take care of public facilities.\n(請愛護公共設施。)"],["faithful","faithful(adj.)忠實的、忠誠的\nfaith(n.)信念、信仰\nfaithfully(adv.)忠實地\na faithful friend 忠實的朋友\nbe faithful to 對…忠誠\nDogs are faithful to their owners.\n(狗對主人很忠誠。)\nHe has been a faithful friend for many years.\n(他多年來一直是個忠實的朋友。)"],["fame","fame(n.)名聲、聲望\nfamous(adj.)有名的\nrise to fame 成名\nfame and fortune 名利\nThe singer rose to fame at the age of eighteen.\n(那位歌手十八歲就成名了。)\nFame and fortune do not always bring happiness.\n(名利不一定會帶來快樂。)"],["fantastic","fantastic(adj.)極好的、奇異的、空想的\nfantasy(n.)幻想\na fantastic idea 很棒的主意\nlook fantastic 看起來很棒\nWe had a fantastic time at the beach.\n(我們在海邊玩得很開心。)\nThat's a fantastic idea for the class party.\n(那是辦班級派對的絕佳點子。)"],["fantasy","fantasy(n.)幻想、奇幻作品\nfantastic(adj.)極好的、奇異的\nfantasy novel 奇幻小說\nlive in a fantasy world 活在幻想世界裡\nShe enjoys reading fantasy novels like Harry Potter.\n(她喜歡讀像《哈利波特》這樣的奇幻小說。)\nBecoming a millionaire is just a fantasy for most people.\n(成為百萬富翁對大多數人來說只是幻想。)"],["farewell","farewell(n.)告別、再會\n(無詞性變化)\nfarewell party 歡送會\nsay farewell to 向…道別\nWe held a farewell party for our teacher.\n(我們為老師舉辦了一場歡送會。)\nShe said farewell to her friends at the airport.\n(她在機場向朋友們道別。)"],["fasten","fasten(v.)繫緊、扣上、固定\nfastener(n.)扣件、拉鍊\nfasten your seat belt 繫好安全帶\nfasten a button 扣上鈕扣\nPlease fasten your seat belt before takeoff.\n(起飛前請繫好安全帶。)\nHe fastened the sign to the wall.\n(他把告示牌固定在牆上。)"],["fatal","fatal(adj.)致命的、毀滅性的\nfatally(adv.)致命地\nfatality(n.)死亡事故、死者\na fatal accident 致命的意外\na fatal mistake 致命的錯誤\nSpeeding often causes fatal accidents.\n(超速常造成致命車禍。)\nLeaving early was a fatal mistake for the team.\n(提早離開對這支隊伍是致命的錯誤。)"],["favorable","favorable(adj.)有利的、贊同的、良好的\nfavor(n./v.)恩惠、偏愛\nfavorable conditions 有利條件\na favorable impression 良好的印象\nThe weather was favorable for the boat race.\n(天氣對划船比賽很有利。)\nShe made a favorable impression on the interviewer.\n(她給面試官留下了良好的印象。)"],["fax","fax(n./v.)傳真、傳真機、用傳真發送\n(無詞性變化)\nfax machine 傳真機\nsend a fax 發傳真\nPlease fax the document to our office.\n(請把文件傳真到我們辦公室。)\nFew people use fax machines these days.\n(現在很少人使用傳真機了。)"],["feast","feast(n./v.)盛宴、宴會、盡情享用\n(無詞性變化)\na wedding feast 婚宴\nfeast on 盡情享用…\nWe had a big feast on Lunar New Year's Eve.\n(除夕夜我們吃了一頓豐盛的大餐。)\nThe children feasted on cake and ice cream.\n(孩子們盡情享用蛋糕和冰淇淋。)"],["feedback","feedback(n.)回饋、意見\n(無詞性變化)\ngive feedback 提供意見\npositive feedback 正面回饋\nThe teacher gave us useful feedback on our essays.\n(老師針對我們的作文給了有用的回饋。)\nWe welcome your feedback on our new menu.\n(歡迎對我們的新菜單提供意見。)"],["ferry","ferry(n./v.)渡輪、擺渡、運送\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a ferry 搭渡輪\nferry service 渡輪服務\nWe took a ferry to Penghu last summer.\n(去年夏天我們搭渡輪到澎湖。)\nBuses ferried the fans to the stadium.\n(公車把球迷載送到體育場。)"],["fertile","fertile(adj.)肥沃的、能生育的、豐富的\nfertilizer(n.)肥料\nfertility(n.)肥沃、生育力\nfertile land 肥沃的土地\na fertile imagination 豐富的想像力\nThe farmers grow rice on the fertile land.\n(農夫們在肥沃的土地上種稻。)\nThe writer has a fertile imagination.\n(那位作家有豐富的想像力。)"],["fetch","fetch(v./n.)取來、去拿來、賣得(價錢)\n(無詞性變化)\nfetch water 打水\nplay fetch 玩丟接遊戲(和狗)\nCould you fetch me a glass of water?\n(你可以幫我拿一杯水來嗎？)\nThe old painting fetched a high price.\n(那幅古畫賣得高價。)"],["fiction","fiction(n.)小說、虛構的事\nfictional(adj.)虛構的\nscience fiction 科幻小說\nfact and fiction 事實與虛構\nI enjoy reading science fiction.\n(我喜歡閱讀科幻小說。)\nThe story sounds true, but it is pure fiction.\n(這個故事聽起來像真的，但完全是虛構的。)"],["fierce","fierce(adj.)兇猛的、激烈的\nfiercely(adv.)兇猛地、激烈地\nfierce competition 激烈的競爭\na fierce dog 兇猛的狗\nThere is fierce competition for the scholarship.\n(這項獎學金競爭非常激烈。)\nThe fierce dog barked at the stranger.\n(那隻兇猛的狗對著陌生人吠叫。)"],["finance","finance(n./v.)財務、金融、資助\nfinancial(adj.)財務的、金融的\npersonal finance 個人理財\nfinance a project 資助計畫\nShe works in the finance department.\n(她在財務部門工作。)\nThe new library was financed by the city government.\n(新圖書館是由市政府出資興建的。)"],["financial","financial(adj.)財務的、金融的\nfinancially(adv.)財務上\nfinance(n.)財務、金融\nfinancial problems 財務問題\nfinancial support 經濟援助\nThe family is having financial problems.\n(那家人正面臨財務困難。)\nHe became financially independent after graduation.\n(他畢業後就經濟獨立了。)"],["fireplace","fireplace(n.)壁爐\n(無詞性變化)\nsit by the fireplace 坐在壁爐旁\na stone fireplace 石砌壁爐\nWe sat by the fireplace and drank hot chocolate.\n(我們坐在壁爐旁喝熱可可。)\nThe old house has a large stone fireplace.\n(那棟老房子有一座大型石砌壁爐。)"],["flatter","flatter(v.)奉承、討好、使顯得好看\nflattery(n.)奉承、恭維\nfeel flattered 感到受寵若驚\nflatter oneself 自以為\nHe flattered his boss to get a promotion.\n(他奉承老闆以求升遷。)\nI felt flattered when she asked for my advice.\n(她來問我的意見時，我感到受寵若驚。)"],["flea","flea(n.)跳蚤\n(無詞性變化)\nflea market 跳蚤市場\nflea bite 跳蚤咬痕\nI bought this old camera at a flea market.\n(我在跳蚤市場買了這台舊相機。)\nOur cat has fleas, so we took it to the vet.\n(我們的貓有跳蚤，所以帶牠去看獸醫。)"],["flee","flee(v.)逃走、逃離\n(無詞性變化)\nflee from 逃離…\nflee the country 逃離國家\nMany people fled their homes because of the war.\n(許多人因戰爭而逃離家園。)\nThe thief fled before the police arrived.\n(小偷在警察到達前逃走了。)"],["flexible","flexible(adj.)有彈性的、靈活的、易彎曲的\nflexibility(n.)彈性、靈活性\nflexible schedule 彈性的時間表\nflexible working hours 彈性工時\nMy job has flexible working hours.\n(我的工作有彈性工時。)\nDancers need to have flexible bodies.\n(舞者需要有柔軟的身體。)"],["fluent","fluent(adj.)流利的、流暢的\nfluency(n.)流利、流暢\nfluently(adv.)流利地\nfluent in English 英文流利\nfluent speaker 說話流利的人\nShe is fluent in English and Japanese.\n(她的英文和日文都很流利。)\nReading every day can improve your fluency.\n(每天閱讀能提升你的流暢度。)"],["flush","flush(v./n.)沖(馬桶)、臉紅、紅暈\n(無詞性變化)\nflush the toilet 沖馬桶\nflush with anger 氣得臉紅\nDon't forget to flush the toilet.\n(別忘了沖馬桶。)\nHer face flushed when everyone looked at her.\n(大家都看著她時，她臉紅了。)"],["foam","foam(n./v.)泡沫、泡棉、起泡沫\nfoamy(adj.)多泡沫的\nmilk foam 奶泡\nfoam box 保麗龍盒\nI like a latte with lots of milk foam.\n(我喜歡有很多奶泡的拿鐵。)\nThe waves foamed as they hit the rocks.\n(海浪拍打岩石時激起泡沫。)"],["forbid","forbid(v.)禁止、不許\nforbidden(adj.)被禁止的\nforbid sb. to 禁止某人做…\nstrictly forbidden 嚴格禁止\nMy parents forbid me to stay out late.\n(我父母禁止我在外面待到很晚。)\nSmoking is strictly forbidden in the building.\n(大樓內嚴格禁止吸菸。)"],["forecast","forecast(n./v.)預報、預測\nforecaster(n.)預報員\nweather forecast 氣象預報\nsales forecast 銷售預測\nThe weather forecast says it will rain tomorrow.\n(氣象預報說明天會下雨。)\nExperts forecast a hot summer this year.\n(專家預測今年夏天會很炎熱。)"],["formation","formation(n.)形成、構成、隊形\nform(v./n.)形成、形式\nrock formation 岩層\nin formation 排成隊形\nThe rock formations along the coast are amazing.\n(海岸沿線的岩石地形令人驚嘆。)\nThe birds flew south in a V formation.\n(鳥群排成V字形往南飛。)"],["formula","formula(n.)公式、配方、方案\nformulate(v.)制定、規劃\nmath formula 數學公式\na formula for success 成功的祕訣\nYou need to memorize this math formula.\n(你需要背下這個數學公式。)\nThere is no simple formula for success.\n(成功沒有簡單的公式。)"],["fort","fort(n.)堡壘、要塞\nfortress(n.)要塞、堡壘\nan old fort 古堡\nbuild a fort 建造堡壘\nFort San Domingo is a famous site in Tamsui.\n(紅毛城是淡水著名的景點。)\nThe children built a fort out of blankets.\n(孩子們用毯子搭了一座堡壘。)"],["fortunate","fortunate(adj.)幸運的\nfortunately(adv.)幸運地\nfortune(n.)運氣、財富\nbe fortunate enough to 很幸運能…\nless fortunate 較不幸的\nWe are fortunate to have such good teachers.\n(我們很幸運有這麼好的老師。)\nWe should help people who are less fortunate.\n(我們應該幫助比較不幸的人。)"],["fossil","fossil(n./adj.)化石、化石的\nfossilize(v.)使成化石\nfossil fuel 化石燃料\ndinosaur fossil 恐龍化石\nScientists found a dinosaur fossil in the desert.\n(科學家在沙漠中發現了恐龍化石。)\nBurning fossil fuels causes air pollution.\n(燃燒化石燃料會造成空氣汙染。)"],["foundation","foundation(n.)地基、基礎、基金會、粉底\nfound(v.)創立、建立\nlay the foundation 奠定基礎\na charity foundation 慈善基金會\nHard work lays the foundation for success.\n(努力奠定成功的基礎。)\nThe foundation helps poor children go to school.\n(這個基金會幫助貧困孩子上學。)"],["founder","founder(n.)創立者、創辦人\nfound(v.)創立\nco-founder 共同創辦人\nthe founder of 某機構的創辦人\nSteve Jobs was one of the founders of Apple.\n(賈伯斯是蘋果公司的創辦人之一。)\nThe school has a statue of its founder.\n(這所學校有一座創辦人的雕像。)"],["fragile","fragile(adj.)易碎的、脆弱的\nfragility(n.)脆弱\nfragile items 易碎物品\nfragile ecosystem 脆弱的生態系\nBe careful! The box contains fragile glasses.\n(小心！這個箱子裡有易碎的玻璃杯。)\nCoral reefs are part of a fragile ecosystem.\n(珊瑚礁屬於脆弱的生態系。)"],["frame","frame(n./v.)框架、畫框、給…裝框、陷害\nframework(n.)架構、框架\npicture frame 相框\nframe of mind 心境\nShe put our family photo in a wooden frame.\n(她把我們的全家福放進木製相框裡。)\nHe claimed that someone had framed him.\n(他聲稱有人陷害他。)"],["frequency","frequency(n.)頻率、次數\nfrequent(adj.)頻繁的\nfrequently(adv.)頻繁地\nhigh frequency 高頻率\nradio frequency 無線電頻率\nThe frequency of earthquakes in Taiwan is high.\n(臺灣地震發生的頻率很高。)\nBuses run with greater frequency during rush hour.\n(尖峰時段公車班次更密集。)"],["freshman","freshman(n.)新生、一年級生\n(無詞性變化)\nfreshman year 一年級\ncollege freshman 大一新生\nI joined the band in my freshman year.\n(我高一時加入了樂隊。)\nThe freshmen took a tour of the campus.\n(新生們參觀了校園。)"],["frost","frost(n./v.)霜、結霜\nfrosty(adj.)結霜的、冷淡的\nearly frost 早霜\ncovered with frost 覆蓋著霜\nThe grass was covered with frost this morning.\n(今天早上草地上覆蓋著一層霜。)\nFrost can damage young plants.\n(霜害會損害幼苗。)"],["frown","frown(n./v.)皺眉、蹙額\n(無詞性變化)\nfrown at 對…皺眉\nfrown upon 不贊成\nThe teacher frowned at the noisy students.\n(老師對吵鬧的學生皺起眉頭。)\nCheating is frowned upon in every school.\n(每所學校都不贊成作弊。)"],["frustrate","frustrate(v.)使挫折、使沮喪、阻撓\nfrustrated(adj.)感到挫折的\nfrustrating(adj.)令人沮喪的\nfeel frustrated 感到挫折\na frustrating experience 令人沮喪的經驗\nThe difficult math problem frustrated me.\n(這道困難的數學題讓我很挫折。)\nIt is frustrating to wait in line for hours.\n(排隊等好幾個小時真令人沮喪。)"],["frustration","frustration(n.)挫折、沮喪\nfrustrate(v.)使挫折\nin frustration 沮喪地\na sense of frustration 挫折感\nHe threw his pen down in frustration.\n(他沮喪地把筆丟在桌上。)\nLearning a new language can bring some frustration.\n(學習新語言可能會帶來一些挫折。)"],["fulfill(ment)","fulfill(v.)實現、履行、滿足、fulfillment(n.)實現、滿足感\n(無詞性變化)\nfulfill a dream 實現夢想\nfulfill a promise 履行承諾\nShe finally fulfilled her dream of becoming a doctor.\n(她終於實現了成為醫生的夢想。)\nHelping others gives me a sense of fulfillment.\n(幫助別人給我一種滿足感。)"],["functional","functional(adj.)功能性的、實用的、運作中的\nfunction(n./v.)功能、運作\nfunctional design 實用的設計\nfully functional 功能完全正常\nThe furniture is simple and functional.\n(這些家具簡單又實用。)\nIs the old computer still functional?\n(那台舊電腦還能用嗎？)"],["fundamental","fundamental(adj./n.)基本的、根本的、基本原則\nfundamentally(adv.)根本地\nfundamental rights 基本權利\nthe fundamentals 基本原理\nEducation is a fundamental right for every child.\n(受教育是每個孩子的基本權利。)\nYou must learn the fundamentals before you play a match.\n(比賽前你必須先學會基本功。)"],["funeral","funeral(n.)葬禮、喪禮\n(無詞性變化)\nattend a funeral 參加葬禮\nfuneral home 殯儀館\nMany people attended his grandfather's funeral.\n(許多人參加了他祖父的葬禮。)\nThe funeral will be held on Saturday.\n(葬禮將在星期六舉行。)"],["furious","furious(adj.)狂怒的、猛烈的\nfury(n.)狂怒\nfuriously(adv.)憤怒地、猛烈地\nbe furious with 對…大發雷霆\nfurious storm 猛烈的暴風雨\nMy dad was furious with me for lying.\n(我說謊讓爸爸非常生氣。)\nA furious storm hit the island last night.\n(昨晚一場猛烈的暴風雨侵襲這座島。)"],["furnish","furnish(v.)布置(家具)、提供\nfurnished(adj.)附家具的\nfurniture(n.)家具\nfully furnished 家具齊全的\nfurnish a room 為房間添置家具\nWe rented a fully furnished apartment.\n(我們租了一間家具齊全的公寓。)\nThey furnished the room with a bed and a desk.\n(他們在房間裡擺了一張床和一張書桌。)"],["furthermore","furthermore(adv.)此外、而且\n(無詞性變化)\nfurthermore, ... 此外，…\nand furthermore 而且\nThe hotel is cheap. Furthermore, it is close to the station.\n(這間飯店很便宜，此外，它離車站很近。)\nExercise is good for your body. Furthermore, it reduces stress.\n(運動對身體好，而且能減輕壓力。)"],["gallery","gallery(n.)畫廊、美術館、走廊\n(無詞性變化)\nart gallery 美術館、畫廊\nphoto gallery 相簿、攝影展覽\nWe spent the whole afternoon at the art gallery downtown.\n(我們在市中心的美術館待了一整個下午。)\nHer paintings are on display in a small gallery.\n(她的畫作正在一間小畫廊展出。)"],["gaze","gaze(n./v.)凝視、注視\n(無詞性變化)\ngaze at 凝視著…\na steady gaze 目不轉睛的凝視\nShe sat by the window, gazing at the stars.\n(她坐在窗邊，凝視著星星。)\nHe could not meet his father's angry gaze.\n(他不敢正視父親憤怒的眼神。)"],["gear","gear(n./v.)排檔、齒輪、裝備、使適合\n(無詞性變化)\ncamping gear 露營裝備\nchange gear 換檔\nRemember to bring your camping gear this weekend.\n(這個週末記得帶你的露營裝備。)\nThe program is geared toward beginners.\n(這個課程是為初學者設計的。)"],["gender","gender(n.)性別\n(無詞性變化)\ngender equality 性別平等\ngender roles 性別角色\nOur school holds lectures on gender equality every year.\n(我們學校每年都舉辦性別平等講座。)\nJobs should not be limited by gender.\n(工作不應該受到性別限制。)"],["gene","gene(n.)基因\ngenetic(adj.)基因的、遺傳的\ngenetics(n.)遺傳學\ngene therapy 基因療法\ncarry a gene 帶有某基因\nEye color is decided by our genes.\n(眼睛的顏色是由我們的基因決定的。)\nScientists found a gene linked to the disease.\n(科學家發現了一個和這種疾病有關的基因。)"],["generation","generation(n.)世代、一代人、產生\ngenerate(v.)產生\ngeneration gap 代溝\nfuture generations 後代子孫\nThere is a big generation gap between my grandpa and me.\n(我和我爺爺之間有很大的代溝。)\nWe must protect the earth for future generations.\n(我們必須為了後代子孫保護地球。)"],["generosity","generosity(n.)慷慨、大方\ngenerous(adj.)慷慨的\ngenerously(adv.)慷慨地\nthanks to one's generosity 多虧某人的慷慨\nshow generosity 表現慷慨\nWe thanked him for his generosity and kindness.\n(我們感謝他的慷慨與善良。)\nThanks to her generosity, the poor children got new books.\n(多虧她的慷慨，貧困的孩子們拿到了新書。)"],["genius","genius(n.)天才、天賦\n(無詞性變化)\na musical genius 音樂天才\na genius at/for 在…方面的天才\nMozart was a musical genius.\n(莫札特是個音樂天才。)\nMy cousin is a genius at solving math problems.\n(我表哥解數學題是個天才。)"],["genuine","genuine(adj.)真正的、真誠的\ngenuinely(adv.)真誠地\ngenuine leather 真皮\ngenuine interest 真正的興趣\nThis bag is made of genuine leather.\n(這個包包是真皮做的。)\nShe showed a genuine interest in helping others.\n(她對幫助別人展現出真誠的熱忱。)"],["germ","germ(n.)病菌、細菌、萌芽\n(無詞性變化)\nspread germs 傳播病菌\nkill germs 殺菌\nWashing your hands can stop germs from spreading.\n(洗手可以防止病菌傳播。)\nCover your mouth when you cough to avoid spreading germs.\n(咳嗽時要遮住嘴巴，避免傳播病菌。)"],["gifted","gifted(adj.)有天賦的、天資聰穎的\ngift(n.)禮物、天賦\ngifted students 資優生\ngifted in/at 在…方面有天賦\nShe is gifted at playing the piano.\n(她在彈鋼琴方面很有天賦。)\nThe school has a special class for gifted students.\n(這所學校為資優生開設了特別班。)"],["gigantic","gigantic(adj.)巨大的、龐大的\ngiant(n.)巨人\na gigantic wave 巨浪\ngigantic size 龐大的體型\nA gigantic wave hit the small fishing boat.\n(一道巨浪打中了那艘小漁船。)\nThe new shopping mall is gigantic.\n(那間新購物中心大得驚人。)"],["giggle","giggle(n./v.)咯咯地笑、傻笑\n(無詞性變化)\ngiggle at 對…咯咯笑\nget the giggles 笑個不停\nThe girls giggled at the funny picture.\n(女孩們看著那張好笑的圖片咯咯地笑。)\nWe couldn't stop giggling during the quiet class.\n(在安靜的課堂上我們忍不住一直偷笑。)"],["ginger","ginger(n.)薑\n(無詞性變化)\nginger tea 薑茶\nfresh ginger 生薑\nMy mom makes ginger tea when I catch a cold.\n(我感冒時媽媽會煮薑茶給我喝。)\nAdd some fresh ginger to the soup.\n(在湯裡加一點生薑。)"],["glimpse","glimpse(n./v.)瞥見、一瞥\n(無詞性變化)\ncatch a glimpse of 瞥見…\na glimpse into 對…的初步了解\nI caught a glimpse of the singer as she left.\n(那位歌手離開時我瞥見了她一眼。)\nThe museum gives us a glimpse into ancient life.\n(這間博物館讓我們一窺古代的生活。)"],["globe","globe(n.)地球、地球儀、球體\nglobal(adj.)全球的\naround the globe 全世界\na model globe 地球儀\nPeople around the globe watched the World Cup final.\n(全世界的人都觀看了世界盃決賽。)\nThe teacher pointed to Taiwan on the globe.\n(老師在地球儀上指出台灣的位置。)"],["glorious","glorious(adj.)光榮的、輝煌的、極好的\nglory(n.)榮耀\nglorious history 輝煌的歷史\nglorious weather 極好的天氣\nThe city has a long and glorious history.\n(這座城市有悠久而輝煌的歷史。)\nWe enjoyed a glorious sunny day at the beach.\n(我們在海邊度過了陽光燦爛的美好一天。)"],["goods","goods(n.)商品、貨物\n(無詞性變化)\nconsumer goods 消費品\nsporting goods 運動用品\nThe store sells sporting goods at low prices.\n(這家店以低價販賣運動用品。)\nThe goods will be delivered within three days.\n(這些貨物將在三天內送達。)"],["gown","gown(n.)禮服、長袍\n(無詞性變化)\nevening gown 晚禮服\ngraduation gown 畢業袍\nThe actress wore a beautiful evening gown.\n(那位女演員穿了一件美麗的晚禮服。)\nStudents wear graduation gowns at the ceremony.\n(學生們在典禮上穿著畢業袍。)"],["grace","grace(n./v.)優雅、風度、增光\ngraceful(adj.)優雅的\ngracious(adj.)親切的、有禮的\nwith grace 優雅地、得體地\nsaving grace 唯一可取之處\nThe dancer moved across the stage with grace.\n(那位舞者優雅地舞過舞台。)\nHe accepted the loss with grace.\n(他很有風度地接受了失敗。)"],["graceful","graceful(adj.)優雅的、得體的\ngrace(n.)優雅\ngracefully(adv.)優雅地\ngraceful movement 優雅的動作\na graceful exit 得體的退場\nThe swan looked graceful on the lake.\n(湖上的天鵝看起來很優雅。)\nShe is famous for her graceful dancing.\n(她以優雅的舞姿聞名。)"],["gracious","gracious(adj.)親切的、有禮的、優雅的\ngrace(n.)優雅、風度\ngraciously(adv.)親切地、有禮地\na gracious host 親切的主人\ngracious living 優雅的生活\nOur gracious host made us feel at home.\n(親切的主人讓我們感到賓至如歸。)\nShe gave a gracious smile to everyone.\n(她向大家露出親切的微笑。)"],["graduation","graduation(n.)畢業、畢業典禮\ngraduate(v./n.)畢業、畢業生\ngraduation ceremony 畢業典禮\nafter graduation 畢業後\nMy parents came to my graduation ceremony.\n(我爸媽來參加了我的畢業典禮。)\nWhat are your plans after graduation?\n(你畢業後有什麼計畫？)"],["grammar","grammar(n.)文法\ngrammatical(adj.)文法的\ngrammar mistake 文法錯誤\nEnglish grammar 英文文法\nPlease check your essay for grammar mistakes.\n(請檢查你的作文有沒有文法錯誤。)\nLearning grammar helps you write better sentences.\n(學文法能幫助你寫出更好的句子。)"],["grammatical","grammatical(adj.)文法上的、合乎文法的\ngrammar(n.)文法\ngrammatically(adv.)文法上\ngrammatical error 文法錯誤\ngrammatical structure 文法結構\nThis sentence is short but grammatical.\n(這個句子雖然短但合乎文法。)\nThe teacher corrected the grammatical errors in my essay.\n(老師訂正了我作文裡的文法錯誤。)"],["graph","graph(n./v.)圖表、用圖表示\ngraphic(adj.)圖像的、生動的\nbar graph 長條圖\nline graph 折線圖\nThe bar graph shows the students' test scores.\n(這張長條圖顯示學生的考試成績。)\nWe used a line graph to show the temperature changes.\n(我們用折線圖來表示溫度的變化。)"],["grateful","grateful(adj.)感激的\ngratitude(n.)感激\nbe grateful to sb. 感激某人\nbe grateful for sth. 感激某事\nI am grateful to my teacher for her help.\n(我很感激老師的幫忙。)\nWe should be grateful for what we have.\n(我們應該對自己擁有的心存感激。)"],["gratitude","gratitude(n.)感激、感謝\ngrateful(adj.)感激的\nexpress gratitude 表達感謝\na sense of gratitude 感恩的心\nI wrote a card to express my gratitude.\n(我寫了一張卡片來表達我的感謝。)\nShe smiled at him with gratitude.\n(她感激地對他微笑。)"],["grave","grave(n./adj.)墳墓、嚴重的、嚴肅的\ngravely(adv.)嚴重地\nvisit a grave 掃墓\ngrave danger 嚴重的危險\nWe visit our ancestors' graves on Tomb Sweeping Day.\n(我們在清明節去祭掃祖先的墳墓。)\nClimate change puts many animals in grave danger.\n(氣候變遷讓許多動物陷入嚴重的危險。)"],["greasy","greasy(adj.)油膩的\ngrease(n.)油脂\ngreasy food 油膩的食物\ngreasy hair 油膩的頭髮\nEating too much greasy food is bad for your health.\n(吃太多油膩的食物對健康不好。)\nThe plates were greasy after the barbecue.\n(烤肉後盤子都油油的。)"],["greeting(s)","greeting(n.)問候、招呼\ngreetings(n.)問候語、祝賀\ngreet(v.)問候、迎接\ngreeting card 賀卡\nexchange greetings 互相問候\nI sent my grandma a birthday greeting card.\n(我寄了一張生日賀卡給奶奶。)\nThe two old friends exchanged warm greetings.\n(兩位老朋友熱情地互相問候。)"],["grief","grief(n.)悲傷、悲痛\ngrieve(v.)悲傷\novercome with grief 悲痛欲絕\ndeep grief 深切的悲痛\nShe was overcome with grief when her dog died.\n(她的狗死去時，她悲痛欲絕。)\nTime can slowly heal our grief.\n(時間能慢慢撫平我們的悲傷。)"],["grind","grind(v./n.)磨碎、研磨、苦差事\nground(v.)磨碎(過去式、過去分詞)\ngrinder(n.)研磨機\ngrind coffee beans 磨咖啡豆\nthe daily grind 日常的苦差事\nMy father grinds coffee beans every morning.\n(我爸爸每天早上都磨咖啡豆。)\nStudying for exams every day can feel like a grind.\n(每天為考試讀書可能讓人覺得很辛苦。)"],["guarantee","guarantee(v./n.)保證、擔保、保固\n(無詞性變化)\nmoney-back guarantee 退款保證\nunder guarantee 在保固期內\nHard work does not always guarantee success.\n(努力不一定能保證成功。)\nThe laptop comes with a two-year guarantee.\n(這台筆電附有兩年保固。)"],["guardian","guardian(n.)監護人、守護者\nguard(v./n.)守衛\nlegal guardian 法定監護人\nguardian angel 守護天使\nStudents need a parent or guardian to sign the form.\n(學生需要家長或監護人在表格上簽名。)\nThe old tree is seen as the guardian of the village.\n(那棵老樹被視為村子的守護者。)"],["guilt","guilt(n.)內疚、罪惡感、有罪\nguilty(adj.)內疚的、有罪的\nfeel guilt 感到內疚\na sense of guilt 罪惡感\nHe felt a strong sense of guilt for lying to his mom.\n(他對媽媽說謊感到強烈的罪惡感。)\nThe court found no proof of his guilt.\n(法院找不到他有罪的證據。)"],["guilty","guilty(adj.)內疚的、有罪的\nguilt(n.)內疚、罪行\nfeel guilty about 對…感到內疚\nbe found guilty 被判有罪\nI feel guilty about forgetting my best friend's birthday.\n(我對忘記好友的生日感到內疚。)\nThe man was found guilty of stealing.\n(那名男子被判竊盜罪成立。)"],["gulf","gulf(n.)海灣、鴻溝\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Gulf of Mexico 墨西哥灣\na gulf between 兩者之間的鴻溝\nThe oil spill polluted the Gulf of Mexico.\n(石油外洩汙染了墨西哥灣。)\nThere is a wide gulf between the rich and the poor.\n(貧富之間存在著巨大的鴻溝。)"],["habitual","habitual(adj.)習慣性的、慣常的\nhabit(n.)習慣\nhabitually(adv.)習慣性地\na habitual liar 慣性說謊者\nhabitual behavior 習慣性行為\nNobody believes a habitual liar.\n(沒有人會相信一個習慣說謊的人。)\nHis habitual lateness made his boss angry.\n(他習慣性遲到讓老闆很生氣。)"],["halt","halt(n./v.)停止、中止\n(無詞性變化)\ncome to a halt 停下來\nbring to a halt 使停止\nThe bus came to a sudden halt in the middle of the road.\n(公車在路中間突然停了下來。)\nThe heavy rain halted the baseball game.\n(大雨使棒球比賽中止。)"],["handwriting","handwriting(n.)筆跡、手寫\n(無詞性變化)\nneat handwriting 工整的字跡\nmessy handwriting 潦草的字跡\nHer neat handwriting is easy to read.\n(她工整的字跡很容易閱讀。)\nI can't read the doctor's messy handwriting.\n(我看不懂醫生潦草的字跡。)"],["hardship","hardship(n.)艱難、困苦\n(無詞性變化)\nface hardship 面對困境\nfinancial hardship 經濟困難\nThe family faced many hardships after the war.\n(戰後這家人面臨了許多困苦。)\nHe never gave up, even in times of hardship.\n(即使在艱困的時候，他也從不放棄。)"],["hardware","hardware(n.)硬體、五金器具\nsoftware(n.)軟體\ncomputer hardware 電腦硬體\nhardware store 五金行\nMy uncle sells computer hardware and software.\n(我叔叔販售電腦硬體與軟體。)\nWe bought some nails at the hardware store.\n(我們在五金行買了一些釘子。)"],["harmony","harmony(n.)和諧、融洽、和聲\nharmonious(adj.)和諧的\nin harmony with 與…和諧\nlive in harmony 和睦相處\nPeople should live in harmony with nature.\n(人們應該與大自然和諧共處。)\nThe choir sang in perfect harmony.\n(合唱團唱出完美的和聲。)"],["harsh","harsh(adj.)嚴厲的、嚴酷的、刺耳的\nharshly(adv.)嚴厲地\nharsh words 嚴厲的話\nharsh weather 嚴酷的天氣\nThe coach's harsh words made him cry.\n(教練嚴厲的話讓他哭了出來。)\nFew plants can survive in such harsh weather.\n(很少植物能在這麼嚴酷的天氣中存活。)"],["haste","haste(n.)匆忙、急忙\nhasty(adj.)倉促的\nhasten(v.)加速、催促\nin haste 匆忙地\nHaste makes waste. 欲速則不達。\nShe left the house in haste and forgot her keys.\n(她匆忙出門，忘了帶鑰匙。)\nTake your time. Haste makes waste.\n(慢慢來，欲速則不達。)"],["hasten","hasten(v.)加速、催促、趕緊\nhaste(n.)匆忙\nhasty(adj.)倉促的\nhasten the process 加快過程\nhasten to add 趕緊補充\nWarm weather can hasten the growth of plants.\n(溫暖的天氣能加速植物生長。)\nI hasten to add that it was not his fault.\n(我得趕緊補充一點，那不是他的錯。)"],["hatred","hatred(n.)憎恨、仇恨\nhate(v.)恨、討厭\nfull of hatred 充滿仇恨\nhatred toward/of 對…的仇恨\nHis heart was full of hatred after the war.\n(戰爭過後他的心中充滿了仇恨。)\nLove is stronger than hatred.\n(愛比恨更強大。)"],["hawk","hawk(n.)鷹、主戰派\n(無詞性變化)\neyes like a hawk 眼光銳利\nwatch like a hawk 嚴密監視\nA hawk flew over the field looking for food.\n(一隻老鷹飛過田野尋找食物。)\nOur teacher watches us like a hawk during exams.\n(考試時老師像老鷹一樣緊盯著我們。)"],["helicopter","helicopter(n.)直升機\n(無詞性變化)\nrescue helicopter 救援直升機\nby helicopter 搭直升機\nThe injured climber was taken to the hospital by helicopter.\n(受傷的登山客被直升機送往醫院。)\nA rescue helicopter flew over the flooded village.\n(一架救援直升機飛過淹水的村莊。)"],["herd","herd(n./v.)獸群、牧群、放牧、聚集\nherder(n.)牧人\na herd of cattle 一群牛\nherd mentality 從眾心理\nA herd of cattle was eating grass on the hill.\n(一群牛正在山坡上吃草。)\nThe teacher herded the children onto the bus.\n(老師把孩子們趕上了遊覽車。)"],["hesitation","hesitation(n.)猶豫、躊躇\nhesitate(v.)猶豫\nwithout hesitation 毫不猶豫\na moment's hesitation 片刻的猶豫\nHe jumped into the river without hesitation to save the boy.\n(他毫不猶豫地跳進河裡救那個男孩。)\nAfter a moment's hesitation, she said yes.\n(猶豫片刻之後，她答應了。)"],["hive","hive(n.)蜂巢、蜂箱、熱鬧繁忙的地方\n(無詞性變化)\nbeehive 蜂窩、蜂巢\na hive of activity 一片忙碌的景象\nThousands of bees live in a single hive.\n(一個蜂巢裡住著數千隻蜜蜂。)\nThe kitchen was a hive of activity before the party.\n(派對開始前，廚房裡一片忙碌。)"],["homeland","homeland(n.)祖國、家鄉\n(無詞性變化)\nreturn to one's homeland 回到家鄉\ndefend one's homeland 保衛家園\nAfter many years abroad, he returned to his homeland.\n(在國外多年後，他回到了家鄉。)\nThe soldiers fought bravely to defend their homeland.\n(士兵們英勇作戰保衛家園。)"],["honeymoon","honeymoon(n./v.)蜜月、度蜜月\n(無詞性變化)\ngo on a honeymoon 去度蜜月\nhoneymoon period 蜜月期\nThe couple went to Bali on their honeymoon.\n(這對夫妻去峇里島度蜜月。)\nThe honeymoon period of the new president is over.\n(新總統的蜜月期已經結束了。)"],["hook","hook(n./v.)鉤子、掛鉤、鉤住、使著迷\nhooked(adj.)著迷的、上癮的\noff the hook 脫離困境\nbe hooked on 對…著迷\nHe hung his coat on the hook behind the door.\n(他把外套掛在門後的掛鉤上。)\nMy little sister is hooked on that cartoon.\n(我妹妹迷上了那部卡通。)"],["horizon","horizon(n.)地平線、眼界\nhorizontal(adj.)水平的\non the horizon 在地平線上、即將發生\nbroaden one's horizons 拓展視野\nThe sun slowly sank below the horizon.\n(太陽緩緩落到地平線下。)\nTraveling abroad can broaden your horizons.\n(出國旅行能拓展你的視野。)"],["horrify","horrify(v.)使驚嚇、使震驚\nhorrified(adj.)驚恐的\nhorror(n.)恐怖\nbe horrified at/by 對…感到震驚\nhorrifying news 駭人的消息\nWe were horrified by the news of the accident.\n(這起意外的消息讓我們大為震驚。)\nThe violent scenes in the movie horrified the audience.\n(電影中的暴力場面嚇壞了觀眾。)"],["hose","hose(n./v.)水管、用水管沖洗\n(無詞性變化)\ngarden hose 澆花水管\nhose down 用水管沖洗\nDad used a garden hose to water the plants.\n(爸爸用水管幫植物澆水。)\nWe hosed down the car after the trip.\n(旅行回來後我們用水管把車沖洗乾淨。)"],["household","household(n.)家庭、一家人\n(無詞性變化)\nhousehold chores 家事\nhousehold name 家喻戶曉的人物\nEvery member of the household should help with household chores.\n(家中每個成員都應該幫忙做家事。)\nThe singer became a household name in Taiwan.\n(那位歌手在台灣家喻戶曉。)"],["housework","housework(n.)家事\n(無詞性變化)\ndo housework 做家事\nshare the housework 分擔家事\nMy brother and I share the housework every weekend.\n(我和哥哥每個週末分擔家事。)\nDoing housework can be good exercise.\n(做家事也可以是不錯的運動。)"],["humanity","humanity(n.)人類、人性、人道\nhuman(adj./n.)人類的、人\nhumanities(n.)人文學科\ncrimes against humanity 違反人道罪\nthe future of humanity 人類的未來\nClimate change is a serious threat to humanity.\n(氣候變遷對人類是一大威脅。)\nHelping strangers shows our humanity.\n(幫助陌生人展現了我們的人性。)"],["humidity","humidity(n.)濕度、潮濕\nhumid(adj.)潮濕的\nhigh humidity 高濕度\nhumidity level 濕度\nThe high humidity in Taiwan makes summer feel hotter.\n(台灣的高濕度讓夏天感覺更熱。)\nUse a machine to control the humidity in your room.\n(用機器來控制房間的濕度。)"],["hurricane","hurricane(n.)颶風\n(無詞性變化)\nhurricane season 颶風季\nbe hit by a hurricane 遭颶風侵襲\nMany homes were destroyed when the hurricane hit Florida.\n(颶風侵襲佛州時，許多房屋被摧毀。)\nPeople stocked up on food before the hurricane season.\n(人們在颶風季來臨前囤積食物。)"],["hush","hush(n./v.)寂靜、使安靜\n(無詞性變化)\na sudden hush 突然的寂靜\nhush up 掩蓋、隱瞞\nA hush fell over the room when the principal walked in.\n(校長走進來時，房間裡突然一片寂靜。)\nThe mother hushed her crying baby.\n(那位媽媽哄她哭鬧的寶寶安靜下來。)"],["hydrogen","hydrogen(n.)氫\n(無詞性變化)\nhydrogen gas 氫氣\nhydrogen bomb 氫彈\nWater is made up of hydrogen and oxygen.\n(水是由氫和氧組成的。)\nSome new cars run on hydrogen instead of gasoline.\n(有些新型汽車使用氫而非汽油作為燃料。)"],["identical","identical(adj.)完全相同的、一模一樣的\nidentically(adv.)相同地\nidentical twins 同卵雙胞胎\nidentical to 與……完全相同\nThe two bags look identical, so I took the wrong one.\n(這兩個包包看起來一模一樣，所以我拿錯了。)\nHer answer was identical to mine.\n(她的答案和我的完全相同。)"],["identification","identification(n.)身分證明、識別、認同\nidentify(v.)識別\nidentity(n.)身分\nproof of identification 身分證明\nidentification card 身分證\nPlease show your identification at the counter.\n(請在櫃台出示你的身分證明。)\nFingerprints are often used for identification.\n(指紋常被用來辨識身分。)"],["identify","identify(v.)辨認、確認、認同\nidentification(n.)識別\nidentity(n.)身分\nidentify with 認同、產生共鳴\nidentify the problem 找出問題\nThe police identified the man from the video.\n(警方從影片中認出了那名男子。)\nMany teenagers identify with the main character.\n(許多青少年對主角產生共鳴。)"],["idiom","idiom(n.)成語、慣用語\nidiomatic(adj.)慣用的、道地的\nEnglish idiom 英文慣用語\nuse an idiom 使用成語\n'Break a leg' is an idiom that means 'good luck.'\n('Break a leg' 是一句意思為'祝好運'的慣用語。)\nUsing idioms correctly makes your English sound natural.\n(正確使用慣用語能讓你的英文聽起來更道地。)"],["idle","idle(adj./v.)閒置的、懶散的、無所事事、虛度\nidleness(n.)懶惰、閒散\nsit idle 閒坐著、閒置\nidle away 虛度光陰\nThe machines sat idle during the holiday.\n(假期期間機器都閒置著。)\nDon't idle away your summer vacation.\n(不要虛度你的暑假。)"],["idol","idol(n.)偶像\nidolize(v.)崇拜\npop idol 流行偶像\nteen idol 青少年偶像\nThe singer is an idol to many teenagers.\n(那位歌手是許多青少年的偶像。)\nFans waited for hours to see their idol.\n(粉絲們等了好幾個小時只為見偶像一面。)"],["ignorance","ignorance(n.)無知、不知道\nignorant(adj.)無知的\nignore(v.)忽視\nout of ignorance 出於無知\nignorance of the law 不懂法律\nHe made the mistake out of ignorance.\n(他是出於無知而犯錯。)\nIgnorance of the law is no excuse.\n(不懂法律不能當作藉口。)"],["ignorant","ignorant(adj.)無知的、不知道的\nignorance(n.)無知\nignore(v.)忽視\nignorant of 對……一無所知\nignorant person 無知的人\nMany people are ignorant of the dangers of smoking.\n(許多人不知道吸菸的危害。)\nI felt ignorant when I couldn't answer simple questions.\n(我答不出簡單的問題時覺得自己很無知。)"],["illustrate","illustrate(v.)說明、闡明、畫插圖\nillustration(n.)插圖、說明\nillustrator(n.)插畫家\nillustrate a point 說明觀點\nillustrate a book 為書畫插圖\nThe teacher used a story to illustrate her point.\n(老師用一個故事來說明她的觀點。)\nThis children's book was illustrated by a famous artist.\n(這本童書是由一位知名畫家繪製插圖。)"],["illustration","illustration(n.)插圖、圖解、實例\nillustrate(v.)說明、畫插圖\nillustrator(n.)插畫家\nby way of illustration 作為例證\ncolor illustration 彩色插圖\nThe book is full of beautiful illustrations.\n(這本書充滿了美麗的插圖。)\nThis chart is a clear illustration of the problem.\n(這張圖表清楚地說明了這個問題。)"],["imaginary","imaginary(adj.)想像的、虛構的\nimagine(v.)想像\nimagination(n.)想像力\nimaginary friend 想像出來的朋友\nimaginary world 虛構的世界\nAs a child, she had an imaginary friend.\n(她小時候有一個想像中的朋友。)\nThe story takes place in an imaginary world.\n(這個故事發生在一個虛構的世界。)"],["imaginative","imaginative(adj.)富有想像力的\nimagine(v.)想像\nimagination(n.)想像力\nimaginative child 富想像力的孩子\nimaginative design 富有創意的設計\nHer imaginative stories always surprise the class.\n(她富有想像力的故事總是讓全班驚豔。)\nThe building has a very imaginative design.\n(這棟建築的設計非常有創意。)"],["imitate","imitate(v.)模仿、仿效\nimitation(n.)模仿、仿製品\nimitator(n.)模仿者\nimitate someone's voice 模仿某人的聲音\nimitate the behavior 模仿行為\nChildren often imitate the behavior of their parents.\n(孩子常常模仿父母的行為。)\nHe can imitate the teacher's voice perfectly.\n(他能完美模仿老師的聲音。)"],["imitation","imitation(n.)模仿、仿製品\nimitate(v.)模仿\nimitation leather 人造皮革\ndo an imitation of 模仿某人\nThis bag is made of imitation leather.\n(這個包包是人造皮革製的。)\nHe did a funny imitation of our coach.\n(他滑稽地模仿了我們的教練。)"],["immigrant","immigrant(n.)(外來)移民\nimmigrate(v.)移入\nimmigration(n.)移民\nnew immigrant 新住民\nillegal immigrant 非法移民\nMany new immigrants in Taiwan come from Southeast Asia.\n(台灣許多新住民來自東南亞。)\nHis grandparents were immigrants from Italy.\n(他的祖父母是來自義大利的移民。)"],["immigrate","immigrate(v.)移入、(從外國)移居\nimmigrant(n.)移民\nimmigration(n.)移民\nimmigrate to 移民到\nimmigrate from 從……移民過來\nHer family immigrated to Canada ten years ago.\n(她的家人十年前移民到加拿大。)\nMany people immigrated to America for a better life.\n(許多人為了更好的生活移民到美國。)"],["immigration","immigration(n.)移民、入境管理\nimmigrate(v.)移入\nimmigrant(n.)移民\nimmigration office 移民署\ngo through immigration 通過入境審查\nIt took an hour to go through immigration at the airport.\n(在機場通過入境審查花了一個小時。)\nThe country changed its immigration policy.\n(這個國家改變了移民政策。)"],["impact","impact(n./v.)影響、衝擊、對……有影響\n(無詞性變化)\nhave an impact on 對……有影響\nenvironmental impact 環境衝擊\nSocial media has a huge impact on teenagers.\n(社群媒體對青少年有巨大的影響。)\nThe new rule will impact all students.\n(新規定將影響所有學生。)"],["imply","imply(v.)暗示、意味著\nimplication(n.)含意、影響\nimplied(adj.)暗示的\nimply that 暗示……\nclearly imply 明顯暗示\nAre you implying that I'm lying?\n(你是在暗示我說謊嗎？)\nHer silence implied that she was not happy.\n(她的沉默暗示她不高興。)"],["impose","impose(v.)強加、徵(稅)、實施\nimposition(n.)強加、負擔\nimpose a tax 課稅\nimpose on 強加於、占便宜\nThe government imposed a tax on sugary drinks.\n(政府對含糖飲料課稅。)\nParents should not impose their dreams on their children.\n(父母不應把自己的夢想強加在孩子身上。)"],["impression","impression(n.)印象、感想\nimpress(v.)使印象深刻\nimpressive(adj.)令人印象深刻的\nfirst impression 第一印象\nmake a good impression 留下好印象\nFirst impressions are very important in job interviews.\n(第一印象在工作面試中非常重要。)\nShe made a good impression on her new classmates.\n(她給新同學留下了好印象。)"],["incident","incident(n.)事件、事故\nincidental(adj.)附帶的\nincidentally(adv.)順便一提\nwithout incident 平安無事\nshooting incident 槍擊事件\nThe school reported the incident to the police.\n(學校將這起事件報警處理。)\nThe trip ended without incident.\n(這趟旅程平安無事地結束了。)"],["including","including(prep.)包括、包含\ninclude(v.)包括\ninclusive(adj.)包含的\nincluding tax 含稅\nnot including 不包括\nThe price is 500 dollars, including tax.\n(價格是五百元，含稅。)\nEveryone came, including my grandparents.\n(大家都來了，包括我的祖父母。)"],["incredible","incredible(adj.)難以置信的、驚人的\nincredibly(adv.)難以置信地、非常\nincredible view 令人驚嘆的景色\nincredible story 難以置信的故事\nThe view from the top of Yushan was incredible.\n(玉山山頂的景色令人驚嘆。)\nIt's incredible that he finished the race with a broken toe.\n(他腳趾骨折還跑完比賽，真令人難以置信。)"],["indication","indication(n.)跡象、指示、表明\nindicate(v.)指出、表明\nindicator(n.)指標\nclear indication 明顯的跡象\ngive an indication 表明\nThere is no indication that the rain will stop soon.\n(沒有跡象顯示雨很快就會停。)\nHer smile was a clear indication that she passed.\n(她的笑容明顯表示她通過了。)"],["infant","infant(n.)嬰兒、幼兒\ninfancy(n.)嬰兒期、初期\nnewborn infant 新生兒\ninfant formula 嬰兒配方奶粉\nInfants need to sleep for many hours a day.\n(嬰兒一天需要睡很多個小時。)\nThe nurse is taking care of a newborn infant.\n(護理師正在照顧一名新生兒。)"],["infection","infection(n.)感染、傳染病\ninfect(v.)感染\ninfectious(adj.)傳染性的\near infection 耳朵感染\nprevent infection 預防感染\nWash the cut to prevent infection.\n(清洗傷口以預防感染。)\nThe doctor gave him medicine for his ear infection.\n(醫生開藥治療他的耳朵感染。)"],["inflation","inflation(n.)通貨膨脹、充氣\ninflate(v.)充氣、使膨脹\nrate of inflation 通膨率\nhigh inflation 高通膨\nBecause of inflation, a bowl of noodles now costs more.\n(因為通貨膨脹，一碗麵現在變貴了。)\nThe government is trying to control inflation.\n(政府正設法控制通貨膨脹。)"],["influential","influential(adj.)有影響力的\ninfluence(n./v.)影響\ninfluential person 有影響力的人\nhighly influential 極具影響力\nShe is one of the most influential writers in Taiwan.\n(她是台灣最具影響力的作家之一。)\nParents are influential in shaping a child's values.\n(父母對塑造孩子的價值觀很有影響力。)"],["informative","informative(adj.)提供資訊的、有教育意義的\ninform(v.)通知\ninformation(n.)資訊\ninformative article 資訊豐富的文章\nhighly informative 非常有知識性\nThe museum tour was fun and informative.\n(博物館導覽既有趣又富有知識性。)\nI found the documentary very informative.\n(我覺得那部紀錄片很有教育意義。)"],["ingredient","ingredient(n.)原料、成分、要素\n(無詞性變化)\nmain ingredient 主要材料\nkey ingredient 關鍵要素\nFresh ingredients make the dish taste better.\n(新鮮的食材讓菜更好吃。)\nHard work is a key ingredient of success.\n(努力是成功的關鍵要素。)"],["initial","initial(adj./n./v.)最初的、(名字的)首字母、簽姓名首字母\ninitially(adv.)起初\ninitiate(v.)開始、發起\ninitial stage 初期階段\ninitial reaction 最初的反應\nMy initial reaction was surprise.\n(我最初的反應是驚訝。)\nHe signed the form with his initials.\n(他用姓名縮寫在表格上簽名。)"],["injure","injure(v.)使受傷、傷害\ninjury(n.)傷害\ninjured(adj.)受傷的\nseriously injured 受重傷\ninjure one's knee 傷到膝蓋\nThree people were seriously injured in the accident.\n(三人在事故中受重傷。)\nHe injured his knee while playing basketball.\n(他打籃球時傷到了膝蓋。)"],["innocence","innocence(n.)無罪、天真、清白\ninnocent(adj.)無辜的、天真的\nprove one's innocence 證明清白\nchildhood innocence 童真\nThe man tried hard to prove his innocence.\n(那名男子努力證明自己的清白。)\nI miss the innocence of my childhood.\n(我懷念童年的天真無邪。)"],["input","input(n./v.)輸入、投入、意見、輸入(資料)\noutput(n.)產出\ninput data 輸入資料\nvaluable input 寶貴的意見\nThank you for your input on our project.\n(謝謝你對我們專題提供的意見。)\nInput your password and press Enter.\n(輸入你的密碼後按下Enter鍵。)"],["insert","insert(v./n.)插入、嵌入、插入物\ninsertion(n.)插入\ninsert a card 插卡\ninsert a coin 投幣\nInsert your card into the machine.\n(把你的卡片插入機器。)\nInsert a coin and choose a drink.\n(投入硬幣並選擇飲料。)"],["inspection","inspection(n.)檢查、視察\ninspect(v.)檢查\ninspector(n.)檢查員\nsafety inspection 安全檢查\non closer inspection 經進一步檢查\nAll cars must pass a safety inspection.\n(所有車輛都必須通過安全檢查。)\nOn closer inspection, the painting turned out to be fake.\n(經進一步檢查，這幅畫原來是假的。)"],["inspiration","inspiration(n.)靈感、鼓舞、激勵人心的人或物\ninspire(v.)激勵\ninspirational(adj.)鼓舞人心的\nsource of inspiration 靈感來源\ndraw inspiration from 從……汲取靈感\nNature is a great source of inspiration for artists.\n(大自然是藝術家的重要靈感來源。)\nHer story is an inspiration to all of us.\n(她的故事激勵了我們所有人。)"],["inspire","inspire(v.)激勵、啟發、給予靈感\ninspiration(n.)靈感\ninspiring(adj.)鼓舞人心的\ninspire someone to 激勵某人去……\nbe inspired by 受……啟發\nMy English teacher inspired me to study abroad.\n(我的英文老師激勵我出國留學。)\nThe song was inspired by a true story.\n(這首歌的靈感來自一個真實故事。)"],["install","install(v.)安裝、設置\ninstallation(n.)安裝、設置\ninstall software 安裝軟體\ninstall a camera 安裝攝影機\nYou need to install the app before using it.\n(使用前你需要先安裝這個應用程式。)\nThe school installed new air conditioners in every classroom.\n(學校在每間教室都安裝了新冷氣。)"],["instinct","instinct(n.)本能、直覺\ninstinctive(adj.)本能的\ninstinctively(adv.)本能地\nsurvival instinct 求生本能\ntrust one's instincts 相信直覺\nBirds build nests by instinct.\n(鳥類靠本能築巢。)\nWhen in doubt, trust your instincts.\n(猶豫不決時，相信你的直覺。)"],["instruct","instruct(v.)指示、命令、教導\ninstruction(n.)指示、說明\ninstructor(n.)教練、講師\ninstruct someone to 指示某人做……\nas instructed 依照指示\nThe teacher instructed us to read chapter five.\n(老師指示我們閱讀第五章。)\nPlease fill out the form as instructed.\n(請依照指示填寫表格。)"],["instructor","instructor(n.)教練、講師、指導者\ninstruct(v.)教導\ninstruction(n.)指示\ndriving instructor 駕訓班教練\nyoga instructor 瑜伽老師\nMy driving instructor is very patient.\n(我的駕訓班教練非常有耐心。)\nShe works as a part-time yoga instructor.\n(她兼職擔任瑜伽老師。)"],["insult","insult(n./v.)侮辱、辱罵\ninsulting(adj.)侮辱的\npersonal insult 人身攻擊\nadd insult to injury 雪上加霜\nHe felt insulted when they laughed at his accent.\n(他們嘲笑他的口音時，他覺得受到侮辱。)\nTo add insult to injury, it started to rain.\n(更糟的是，天又開始下雨了。)"],["insurance","insurance(n.)保險、保險費\ninsure(v.)為……投保\nhealth insurance 健康保險\ninsurance company 保險公司\nTaiwan's National Health Insurance covers most people.\n(台灣的全民健康保險涵蓋大多數人。)\nYou should buy travel insurance before going abroad.\n(出國前你應該買旅遊保險。)"],["intellectual","intellectual(adj./n.)智力的、知識的、知識分子\nintellect(n.)智力\nintellectual property 智慧財產\nintellectual development 智力發展\nReading is important for children's intellectual development.\n(閱讀對兒童的智力發展很重要。)\nCopying music without permission violates intellectual property rights.\n(未經許可複製音樂侵犯了智慧財產權。)"],["intelligence","intelligence(n.)智力、智慧、情報\nintelligent(adj.)聰明的\nartificial intelligence 人工智慧\nemotional intelligence 情緒智商\nArtificial intelligence is changing the way we learn.\n(人工智慧正在改變我們學習的方式。)\nDon't insult my intelligence with such a silly excuse.\n(別用這麼蠢的藉口來侮辱我的智商。)"],["intend","intend(v.)打算、意欲\nintention(n.)意圖\nintended(adj.)預期的、計畫中的\nintend to 打算做……\nbe intended for 為……而設計\nI intend to study abroad after graduation.\n(我打算畢業後出國留學。)\nThis book is intended for beginners.\n(這本書是為初學者編寫的。)"],["intense","intense(adj.)強烈的、劇烈的、緊張的\nintensity(n.)強度\nintensely(adv.)強烈地\nintense heat 酷熱\nintense competition 激烈的競爭\nThe intense heat made it hard to sleep.\n(酷熱讓人難以入睡。)\nThere is intense competition to get into top universities.\n(進入頂尖大學的競爭十分激烈。)"],["intensity","intensity(n.)強度、強烈、激烈\nintense(adj.)強烈的\nintensify(v.)加強\nhigh intensity 高強度\nthe intensity of the light 光線的強度\nThe typhoon grew in intensity as it moved closer.\n(颱風越靠近強度越強。)\nHigh-intensity exercise can burn a lot of calories.\n(高強度運動可以燃燒大量熱量。)"],["intensive","intensive(adj.)密集的、加強的\nintensively(adv.)密集地\nintensive care unit 加護病房\nintensive course 密集課程\nShe took an intensive English course in the summer.\n(她暑假參加了英文密集課程。)\nThe patient was moved to the intensive care unit.\n(那名病人被轉入加護病房。)"],["intention","intention(n.)意圖、打算、目的\nintend(v.)打算\nintentional(adj.)故意的\ngood intentions 好意\nhave no intention of 無意……\nI have no intention of giving up.\n(我完全不打算放棄。)\nHe meant well; he had good intentions.\n(他是出於好意的。)"],["interact","interact(v.)互動、相互作用\ninteraction(n.)互動\ninteractive(adj.)互動的\ninteract with 與……互動\ninteract socially 社交互動\nTeachers should interact with students more in class.\n(老師在課堂上應該多和學生互動。)\nSome medicines can interact with each other.\n(有些藥物會彼此產生交互作用。)"],["interaction","interaction(n.)互動、相互作用\ninteract(v.)互動\ninteractive(adj.)互動的\nsocial interaction 社交互動\nface-to-face interaction 面對面互動\nOnline games cannot replace face-to-face interaction.\n(線上遊戲無法取代面對面的互動。)\nThe study looks at the interaction between parents and children.\n(這項研究探討父母與孩子之間的互動。)"],["interfere","interfere(v.)干涉、妨礙\ninterference(n.)干涉、干擾\ninterfere with 妨礙\ninterfere in 干涉\nDon't let your phone interfere with your studies.\n(別讓手機妨礙你的課業。)\nMy parents never interfere in my choices.\n(我父母從不干涉我的選擇。)"],["intermediate","intermediate(adj./n./v.)中級的、中間的、中級者、調解\n(無詞性變化)\nintermediate level 中級程度\nupper intermediate 中高級\nThis book is for students at the intermediate level.\n(這本書適合中級程度的學生。)\nShe passed the intermediate level of the GEPT.\n(她通過了全民英檢中級。)"],["interpret","interpret(v.)解釋、詮釋、口譯\ninterpretation(n.)解釋、詮釋\ninterpreter(n.)口譯員\ninterpret a dream 解夢\ninterpret for 為……翻譯\nPeople interpret the poem in many different ways.\n(人們對這首詩有許多不同的詮釋。)\nShe interpreted for the foreign guests at the meeting.\n(她在會議上為外賓擔任口譯。)"],["interruption","interruption(n.)中斷、打擾\ninterrupt(v.)打斷、打擾\nwithout interruption 不間斷地\nsorry for the interruption 抱歉打擾了\nShe studied for three hours without interruption.\n(她不間斷地讀了三個小時的書。)\nSorry for the interruption, but you have a phone call.\n(抱歉打擾，你有一通電話。)"],["intimate","intimate(adj./n.)親密的、詳盡的、密友\nintimacy(n.)親密\nintimate friend 密友\nintimate knowledge 深入的了解\nThey have been intimate friends since childhood.\n(他們從小就是親密的朋友。)\nThe guide has an intimate knowledge of the old town.\n(這位導遊對老城區瞭若指掌。)"],["intuition","intuition(n.)直覺、直觀\nintuitive(adj.)直覺的\nfemale intuition 女性的直覺\nrely on intuition 依靠直覺\nMy intuition told me something was wrong.\n(我的直覺告訴我有些不對勁。)\nGood players often rely on intuition during a game.\n(優秀的選手在比賽中常依靠直覺。)"],["invade","invade(v.)入侵、侵犯\ninvasion(n.)入侵\ninvader(n.)入侵者\ninvade a country 侵略一個國家\ninvade one's privacy 侵犯某人隱私\nThe army invaded the country in 1939.\n(軍隊在1939年入侵該國。)\nReading my diary invades my privacy.\n(看我的日記是侵犯我的隱私。)"],["invasion","invasion(n.)入侵、侵犯\ninvade(v.)入侵\nmilitary invasion 軍事入侵\ninvasion of privacy 侵犯隱私\nPosting someone's photo without permission is an invasion of privacy.\n(未經同意張貼別人的照片是侵犯隱私。)\nThe invasion led to a long war.\n(這次入侵導致了一場長期戰爭。)"],["invention","invention(n.)發明、發明物\ninvent(v.)發明\ninventor(n.)發明家\ninventive(adj.)有創意的\ngreat invention 偉大的發明\nthe invention of …的發明\nThe smartphone is one of the greatest inventions of our time.\n(智慧型手機是我們這個時代最偉大的發明之一。)\nNecessity is the mother of invention.\n(需要為發明之母。)"],["invest(ment)","invest(v.)投資、投入、investment(n.)投資\ninvestor(n.)投資者\ninvest in 投資於\na good investment 值得的投資\nMy parents invested a lot of money in my education.\n(我爸媽在我的教育上投資了很多錢。)\nLearning a second language is a good investment.\n(學習第二外語是很值得的投資。)"],["investigation","investigation(n.)調查、研究\ninvestigate(v.)調查\ninvestigator(n.)調查員\nunder investigation 調查中\ncarry out an investigation 進行調查\nThe cause of the fire is still under investigation.\n(火災的原因仍在調查中。)\nThe police carried out an investigation into the accident.\n(警方對這起事故進行了調查。)"],["involve(ment)","involve(v.)涉及、包含、使參與、involvement(n.)參與、牽涉\ninvolved(adj.)參與的、複雜的\nbe involved in 參與、涉及\nparental involvement 家長參與\nThe job involves a lot of traveling.\n(這份工作需要經常出差。)\nShe was involved in planning the school festival.\n(她參與了校慶的籌劃。)"],["isolate","isolate(v.)隔離、孤立\nisolation(n.)隔離\nisolated(adj.)孤立的、偏遠的\nisolate oneself 孤立自己\nisolated village 偏遠的村莊\nPatients with the disease were isolated from others.\n(患病的病人被與其他人隔離開來。)\nHe isolated himself after failing the exam.\n(考試失利後他把自己孤立起來。)"],["isolation","isolation(n.)隔離、孤立、孤獨\nisolate(v.)隔離\nisolated(adj.)孤立的\nin isolation 孤立地、單獨地\nsocial isolation 社會孤立\nSocial isolation is a problem for many elderly people.\n(社會孤立是許多長者面臨的問題。)\nYou can't study a word in isolation; look at the sentence.\n(你不能單獨學一個字，要看整個句子。)"],["issue","issue(n./v.)議題、問題、(期刊的)期、發行、發布\n(無詞性變化)\nenvironmental issue 環境議題\nissue a warning 發布警告\nClimate change is a global issue.\n(氣候變遷是全球性的議題。)\nThe weather bureau issued a typhoon warning this morning.\n(氣象局今天早上發布了颱風警報。)"],["jealousy","jealousy(n.)嫉妒、妒忌\njealous(adj.)嫉妒的\nfeel jealousy 感到嫉妒\nout of jealousy 出於嫉妒\nShe couldn't hide her jealousy when her friend won.\n(朋友得獎時，她掩飾不了自己的嫉妒。)\nHe said those mean words out of jealousy.\n(他是出於嫉妒才說了那些刻薄的話。)"],["keen","keen(adj.)熱衷的、渴望的、敏銳的\nkeenly(adv.)強烈地、敏銳地\nkeen on 熱衷於\nkeen sense of smell 敏銳的嗅覺\nMy brother is keen on playing basketball.\n(我弟弟熱衷於打籃球。)\nDogs have a keen sense of smell.\n(狗有敏銳的嗅覺。)"],["kettle","kettle(n.)水壺、茶壺\n(無詞性變化)\nelectric kettle 電熱水壺\nput the kettle on 燒開水\nI put the kettle on to make some tea.\n(我燒水準備泡茶。)\nThe electric kettle boils water in three minutes.\n(電熱水壺三分鐘就能把水煮開。)"],["kneel","kneel(v.)跪下、跪著\nknee(n.)膝蓋\nkneel down 跪下\nkneel on one knee 單膝跪地\nHe knelt on one knee and asked her to marry him.\n(他單膝跪地向她求婚。)\nShe knelt down to tie her little brother's shoes.\n(她跪下來幫弟弟綁鞋帶。)"],["knob","knob(n.)圓形把手、旋鈕\n(無詞性變化)\ndoor knob 門把\nturn the knob 轉動旋鈕\nHe turned the knob and opened the door slowly.\n(他轉動門把，慢慢地打開門。)\nTurn the knob to the right to make it louder.\n(把旋鈕向右轉可以讓聲音變大。)"],["labor","labor(n./v.)勞力、勞工、勞動、努力工作\nlaborer(n.)勞工\nlaborious(adj.)費力的\nlabor force 勞動力\nchild labor 童工\nChild labor is still a problem in some countries.\n(童工在某些國家仍是個問題。)\nThe farmers labored in the fields all day.\n(農夫們整天在田裡辛苦工作。)"],["laboratory/lab","laboratory(n.)實驗室\nlab(n.)實驗室(口語)\nscience laboratory 科學實驗室\nlab coat 實驗衣\nThe students did experiments in the science laboratory.\n(學生們在科學實驗室做實驗。)\nPlease wear your lab coat and safety glasses.\n(請穿上實驗衣並戴上護目鏡。)"],["lag","lag(n./v.)落後、延遲、時間差\n(無詞性變化)\njet lag 時差反應\nlag behind 落後\nI had terrible jet lag after flying to New York.\n(飛到紐約後我時差很嚴重。)\nSome students lag behind in math after the long break.\n(長假過後有些學生的數學進度落後。)"],["landmark","landmark(n.)地標、里程碑\n(無詞性變化)\nfamous landmark 著名地標\nlandmark decision 劃時代的決定\nTaipei 101 is the most famous landmark in Taipei.\n(台北101是台北最有名的地標。)\nThe moon landing was a landmark in human history.\n(登陸月球是人類歷史上的里程碑。)"],["landscape","landscape(n./v.)風景、景觀、美化環境\n(無詞性變化)\nnatural landscape 自然景觀\nlandscape painting 風景畫\nThe landscape of Taroko Gorge is breathtaking.\n(太魯閣峽谷的景觀令人屏息。)\nThe internet has changed the landscape of education.\n(網路改變了教育的面貌。)"],["largely","largely(adv.)主要地、大部分\nlarge(adj.)大的\nlargely due to 主要由於\nlargely ignored 大多被忽視\nHis success was largely due to hard work.\n(他的成功主要歸功於努力。)\nThe problem has been largely ignored by the public.\n(這個問題大多被大眾忽視了。)"],["launch","launch(v./n.)發射、推出、發起、發表\n(無詞性變化)\nlaunch a rocket 發射火箭\nproduct launch 產品發表會\nThe company will launch its new phone next month.\n(那家公司下個月將推出新手機。)\nTaiwan successfully launched a satellite into space.\n(台灣成功將一顆衛星發射到太空。)"],["lawful","lawful(adj.)合法的、法定的\nlaw(n.)法律\nunlawful(adj.)非法的\nlawful owner 合法擁有者\nlawful means 合法手段\nHe is the lawful owner of the house.\n(他是這棟房子的合法擁有者。)\nWe should solve problems by lawful means.\n(我們應該用合法的手段解決問題。)"],["lean","lean(v./adj.)倚靠、傾斜、瘦的、(肉)無油脂的\n(無詞性變化)\nlean against 靠在……上\nlean meat 瘦肉\nHe leaned against the wall and closed his eyes.\n(他靠在牆上閉起眼睛。)\nChoose lean meat if you want a healthy diet.\n(如果你想吃得健康，就選擇瘦肉。)"],["learned","learned(adj.)博學的、有學問的\nlearn(v.)學習\nlearning(n.)學問、學習\nlearned scholar 博學的學者\nlearned society 學會\nProfessor Lin is a learned scholar of Chinese history.\n(林教授是一位博學的中國史學者。)\nHe joined a learned society for physics.\n(他加入了一個物理學會。)"],["lecture","lecture(n./v.)演講、講課、訓斥\nlecturer(n.)講師\ngive a lecture 演講、講課\nlecture hall 演講廳\nThe professor gave a lecture on climate change.\n(教授做了一場關於氣候變遷的演講。)\nMy mom lectured me for coming home late.\n(我晚回家被媽媽訓了一頓。)"],["lecturer","lecturer(n.)講師、演講者\nlecture(n./v.)演講\nguest lecturer 客座講師\nsenior lecturer 資深講師\nThe guest lecturer shared her experience working abroad.\n(客座講師分享了她在國外工作的經驗。)\nHe works as a lecturer at a university in Tainan.\n(他在台南一所大學擔任講師。)"],["legend","legend(n.)傳說、傳奇人物\nlegendary(adj.)傳說的、傳奇的\naccording to legend 根據傳說\nliving legend 活傳奇\nAccording to legend, a dragon lived in this lake.\n(根據傳說，有一條龍住在這座湖裡。)\nMichael Jordan is a basketball legend.\n(麥可・喬丹是籃球界的傳奇人物。)"],["leisurely","leisurely(adj./adv.)悠閒的、從容不迫的、悠閒地\nleisure(n.)閒暇\nleisurely walk 悠閒的散步\nat a leisurely pace 以從容的步調\nWe took a leisurely walk along the river after dinner.\n(晚餐後我們沿著河邊悠閒地散步。)\nThey ate breakfast at a leisurely pace on Sunday.\n(週日他們慢條斯理地吃早餐。)"],["lengthen","lengthen(v.)加長、延長\nlength(n.)長度\nlong(adj.)長的\nlengthen the skirt 把裙子加長\nthe days lengthen 白天變長\nThe tailor lengthened my pants by two centimeters.\n(裁縫師把我的褲子加長了兩公分。)\nThe days lengthen as summer comes.\n(隨著夏天到來，白天變長了。)"],["liar","liar(n.)說謊者、騙子\nlie(v./n.)說謊、謊言\nterrible liar 很不會說謊的人\ncall someone a liar 說某人是騙子\nNobody believes him because he is a liar.\n(沒人相信他，因為他是個騙子。)\nShe's a terrible liar; her face always turns red.\n(她很不會說謊，臉總是會變紅。)"],["librarian","librarian(n.)圖書館員\nlibrary(n.)圖書館\nschool librarian 學校圖書館員\nask the librarian 詢問圖書館員\nThe librarian helped me find the book I needed.\n(圖書館員幫我找到我需要的書。)\nOur school librarian recommends a new book every week.\n(我們學校的圖書館員每週推薦一本新書。)"],["license","license(n./v.)執照、許可證、批准\nlicensed(adj.)有執照的\ndriver's license 駕照\nlicense plate 車牌\nMy brother got his driver's license last month.\n(我哥哥上個月拿到了駕照。)\nThe witness remembered the car's license plate number.\n(目擊者記得那輛車的車牌號碼。)"],["lifeguard","lifeguard(n.)救生員\n(無詞性變化)\nlifeguard on duty 值勤中的救生員\nbecome a lifeguard 成為救生員\nOnly swim when a lifeguard is on duty.\n(只在救生員值勤時游泳。)\nHe works as a lifeguard at the beach every summer.\n(他每年夏天在海灘擔任救生員。)"],["limitation","limitation(n.)限制、侷限、缺陷\nlimit(n./v.)限制\nlimited(adj.)有限的\ntime limitation 時間限制\nknow one's limitations 了解自己的能力極限\nEveryone has limitations, so ask for help when you need it.\n(每個人都有能力極限，需要時就尋求協助。)\nThe study has some limitations.\n(這項研究有一些侷限。)"],["linen","linen(n.)亞麻布、亞麻製品、床單桌巾類\n(無詞性變化)\nlinen shirt 亞麻襯衫\nbed linen 床單被套\nA linen shirt keeps you cool in hot weather.\n(亞麻襯衫在炎熱的天氣裡能讓你保持涼爽。)\nThe hotel changes the bed linen every day.\n(這家飯店每天更換床單被套。)"],["lipstick","lipstick(n.)口紅、唇膏\n(無詞性變化)\nwear lipstick 擦口紅\nred lipstick 紅色口紅\nShe put on some red lipstick before the party.\n(派對前她擦上了紅色口紅。)\nThe actress never goes out without lipstick.\n(那位女演員出門一定擦口紅。)"],["liquor","liquor(n.)烈酒、酒類\n(無詞性變化)\nliquor store 酒類專賣店\nhard liquor 烈酒\nSelling liquor to people under eighteen is illegal.\n(販賣酒類給未滿十八歲的人是違法的。)\nKaoliang is a famous liquor from Kinmen.\n(高粱酒是金門著名的烈酒。)"],["literary","literary(adj.)文學的、文藝的\nliterature(n.)文學\nliterate(adj.)識字的\nliterary work 文學作品\nliterary prize 文學獎\nHer novel won a famous literary prize.\n(她的小說贏得了一個著名的文學獎。)\nWe read several literary works in Chinese class.\n(我們在國文課讀了幾篇文學作品。)"],["literature","literature(n.)文學、文獻\nliterary(adj.)文學的\nEnglish literature 英國文學\nclassic literature 經典文學\nShe plans to study English literature in college.\n(她打算在大學念英國文學。)\nReading classic literature can broaden your mind.\n(閱讀經典文學能開闊你的視野。)"],["loan","loan(n./v.)貸款、借出、借貸\n(無詞性變化)\nstudent loan 學生貸款\nbank loan 銀行貸款\nHe took out a student loan to pay for college.\n(他申請學生貸款來支付大學學費。)\nMy friend loaned me his bike for the weekend.\n(我朋友週末把腳踏車借給我。)"],["lobster","lobster(n.)龍蝦\n(無詞性變化)\ngrilled lobster 烤龍蝦\nlobster tail 龍蝦尾\nWe had grilled lobster at a seafood restaurant.\n(我們在一家海鮮餐廳吃了烤龍蝦。)\nHis face turned as red as a lobster in the sun.\n(他的臉在太陽下曬得像龍蝦一樣紅。)"],["logic","logic(n.)邏輯、推理\nlogical(adj.)合邏輯的\nlogically(adv.)邏輯上\nfollow the logic 理解邏輯\nthe logic behind …背後的邏輯\nI don't understand the logic behind this rule.\n(我不懂這條規定背後的邏輯。)\nMath helps students develop logic.\n(數學幫助學生培養邏輯能力。)"],["logical","logical(adj.)合邏輯的、合理的\nlogic(n.)邏輯\nillogical(adj.)不合邏輯的\nlogical thinking 邏輯思考\nlogical conclusion 合理的結論\nIt's logical to bring an umbrella when it's cloudy.\n(陰天時帶傘是合理的。)\nProgramming helps develop logical thinking.\n(寫程式有助於培養邏輯思考。)"],["loosen","loosen(v.)鬆開、放鬆\nloose(adj.)鬆的\nloosen one's tie 鬆開領帶\nloosen the rules 放寬規定\nHe loosened his tie after the long meeting.\n(冗長的會議結束後，他鬆開了領帶。)\nThe school decided to loosen its rules on hairstyles.\n(學校決定放寬髮型的規定。)"],["lousy","lousy(adj.)糟糕的、差勁的\n(無詞性變化)\nlousy weather 糟糕的天氣\nfeel lousy 覺得很不舒服\nThe food at that restaurant was lousy.\n(那家餐廳的食物很難吃。)\nI feel lousy because I didn't sleep last night.\n(我昨晚沒睡，現在覺得很糟。)"],["loyal","loyal(adj.)忠誠的、忠實的\nloyalty(n.)忠誠\nloyally(adv.)忠誠地\nloyal friend 忠實的朋友\nloyal customer 忠實顧客\nDogs are known to be loyal to their owners.\n(狗以對主人忠誠而聞名。)\nShe has been a loyal customer of this store for years.\n(她多年來一直是這家店的忠實顧客。)"],["loyalty","loyalty(n.)忠誠、忠心\nloyal(adj.)忠誠的\nbrand loyalty 品牌忠誠度\nloyalty to 對……的忠誠\nHis loyalty to the team never changed.\n(他對球隊的忠誠從未改變。)\nMany stores offer loyalty cards to keep customers.\n(許多商店提供集點卡來留住顧客。)"],["luxurious","luxurious(adj.)奢華的、豪華的\nluxury(n.)奢侈品、奢華\nluxurious hotel 豪華飯店\nluxurious life 奢華的生活\nThey stayed in a luxurious hotel for their honeymoon.\n(他們度蜜月時住在一家豪華飯店。)\nThe movie star lives a luxurious life.\n(那位電影明星過著奢華的生活。)"],["luxury","luxury(n.)奢侈、奢侈品、奢華\nluxurious(adj.)奢華的\nluxury goods 奢侈品\nlive in luxury 過著奢華的生活\nFor many students, a new laptop is a luxury.\n(對許多學生來說，一台新筆電是奢侈品。)\nAfter a long week, a quiet weekend feels like a luxury.\n(忙了一整週後，安靜的週末感覺很奢侈。)"],["machinery","machinery(n.)機器(總稱)、機構、體制\nmachine(n.)機器\nheavy machinery 重型機械\nfarm machinery 農業機械\nThe factory bought new machinery last year.\n(那家工廠去年購買了新機器。)\nWorkers must be careful when using heavy machinery.\n(工人使用重型機械時必須小心。)"],["magnetic","magnetic(adj.)磁性的、有吸引力的\nmagnet(n.)磁鐵\nmagnetism(n.)磁性、魅力\nmagnetic field 磁場\nmagnetic personality 有魅力的個性\nThe earth has a strong magnetic field.\n(地球有強大的磁場。)\nShe has a magnetic personality that attracts friends.\n(她很有個人魅力，很容易吸引朋友。)"],["magnificent","magnificent(adj.)壯麗的、宏偉的、極好的\nmagnificence(n.)壯麗\nmagnificent view 壯麗的景色\nmagnificent building 宏偉的建築\nWe enjoyed a magnificent view from the mountaintop.\n(我們在山頂欣賞到壯麗的景色。)\nThe palace is a magnificent building.\n(那座宮殿是一棟宏偉的建築。)"],["makeup","makeup(n.)化妝品、化妝、組成\nmake up(v.)化妝、組成、編造\nwear makeup 化妝\nmakeup exam 補考\nShe doesn't wear makeup to school.\n(她上學不化妝。)\nStudents who were sick can take a makeup exam.\n(生病的學生可以參加補考。)"],["manual","manual(n./adj.)手冊、手工的、體力的\nmanually(adv.)手動地\nuser manual 使用手冊\nmanual labor 體力勞動\nRead the user manual before using the machine.\n(使用機器前先閱讀使用手冊。)\nFarming used to require a lot of manual labor.\n(以前農耕需要大量的體力勞動。)"],["manufacture","manufacture(n./v.)製造、製造業\nmanufacturer(n.)製造商\nmanufacturing(n.)製造業\nmanufacture cars 製造汽車\nbe manufactured in 在⋯製造\nThis company manufactures bicycles for export.\n(這家公司製造外銷用的腳踏車。)\nMost of these toys are manufactured in Asia.\n(這些玩具大多在亞洲製造。)"],["manufacturer","manufacturer(n.)製造商、廠商\nmanufacture(v.)製造\ncar manufacturer 汽車製造商\nleading manufacturer 主要製造商\nTaiwan has some of the world's leading chip manufacturers.\n(台灣擁有一些世界領先的晶片製造商。)\nContact the manufacturer if the product is broken.\n(如果產品壞了，請聯絡製造商。)"],["marathon","marathon(n.)馬拉松\n(無詞性變化)\nrun a marathon 跑馬拉松\nmarathon runner 馬拉松跑者\nMy uncle ran the Taipei Marathon last December.\n(我叔叔去年十二月跑了台北馬拉松。)\nRunning a marathon requires months of training.\n(跑馬拉松需要好幾個月的訓練。)"],["margin","margin(n.)頁邊空白、差距、利潤\nmarginal(adj.)邊緣的、少量的\nby a narrow margin 以些微差距\nin the margin 在頁邊空白處\nThe teacher wrote comments in the margin.\n(老師在頁邊空白處寫了評語。)\nOur team won by a narrow margin.\n(我們隊以些微差距獲勝。)"],["maturity","maturity(n.)成熟\nmature(adj./v.)成熟的、使成熟\nshow maturity 表現成熟\nreach maturity 達到成熟\nHe showed great maturity in handling the problem.\n(他處理問題時表現得非常成熟。)\nThese trees reach maturity in about ten years.\n(這些樹大約十年後成熟。)"],["maximum","maximum(adj./n.)最大的、最大量\nmaximize(v.)使最大化\nmaximum speed 最高速度\nto the maximum 到最大程度\nThe maximum speed on this road is 50 km per hour.\n(這條路的最高速限是每小時五十公里。)\nThis elevator holds a maximum of ten people.\n(這部電梯最多可載十人。)"],["measurable","measurable(adj.)可測量的、顯著的\nmeasure(v.)測量\nmeasurement(n.)測量、尺寸\nmeasurable goal 可衡量的目標\nmeasurable progress 顯著的進步\nSet a clear and measurable goal for your study plan.\n(為你的讀書計畫設定一個明確且可衡量的目標。)\nThe new teaching method led to measurable improvement.\n(新的教學方法帶來了顯著的進步。)"],["measure(s)","measure(n.)措施(常用複數 measures)、尺度、量\nmeasure(v.)測量\nmeasurement(n.)測量、尺寸\ntake measures 採取措施\nsafety measures 安全措施\nThe government took measures to prevent the flu.\n(政府採取措施預防流感。)\nSchools have strict safety measures during typhoons.\n(颱風期間學校有嚴格的安全措施。)"],["mechanic","mechanic(n.)技工、機械工\nmechanical(adj.)機械的\nmechanics(n.)力學、機械學\ncar mechanic 汽車修理工\nskilled mechanic 熟練的技工\nThe mechanic fixed my scooter in an hour.\n(技師在一小時內修好了我的機車。)\nHe works as a car mechanic in a small garage.\n(他在一家小修車廠當汽車修理工。)"],["mechanical","mechanical(adj.)機械的、機械式的\nmechanic(n.)技工\nmechanically(adv.)機械地\nmechanical problem 機械故障\nmechanical engineering 機械工程\nThe flight was delayed due to a mechanical problem.\n(班機因機械故障而延誤。)\nHe answered the questions in a mechanical way.\n(他機械式地回答問題。)"],["memorable","memorable(adj.)難忘的、值得紀念的\nmemory(n.)記憶\nmemorize(v.)記住\nmemorable experience 難忘的經驗\nmemorable moment 難忘的時刻\nThe graduation trip was a memorable experience.\n(畢業旅行是一次難忘的經驗。)\nIt was one of the most memorable moments of my life.\n(那是我人生中最難忘的時刻之一。)"],["memorial","memorial(adj./n.)紀念的、紀念物、紀念館\nmemory(n.)記憶\nmemorial service 追悼會\nwar memorial 戰爭紀念碑\nMany tourists visit the Chiang Kai-shek Memorial Hall.\n(許多觀光客參觀中正紀念堂。)\nA memorial service was held for the victims.\n(為罹難者舉行了追悼會。)"],["memorize","memorize(v.)記住、背誦\nmemory(n.)記憶\nmemorization(n.)記憶、背誦\nmemorize vocabulary 背單字\nmemorize a poem 背一首詩\nI memorize ten new words every day.\n(我每天背十個新單字。)\nShe memorized the whole poem for the contest.\n(她為了比賽背下了整首詩。)"],["merchant","merchant(n.)商人\nmerchandise(n.)商品\nmerchant ship 商船\nwealthy merchant 富商\nThe merchant sold silk and tea to foreign traders.\n(那位商人把絲綢和茶葉賣給外國貿易商。)\nMany merchants traveled along the Silk Road.\n(許多商人沿著絲路旅行。)"],["mercy","mercy(n.)仁慈、憐憫、寬恕\nmerciful(adj.)仁慈的\nmerciless(adj.)無情的\nat the mercy of 任由⋯擺布\nshow mercy 表現仁慈\nThe small boat was at the mercy of the storm.\n(那艘小船任由暴風雨擺布。)\nThe king showed mercy and set the prisoner free.\n(國王大發慈悲，釋放了那名囚犯。)"],["mere","mere(adj.)僅僅的、只不過的\nmerely(adv.)僅僅、只不過\na mere child 只是個孩子\nthe mere thought of 一想到⋯\nHe was a mere child when he left home.\n(他離家時只不過是個孩子。)\nThe mere thought of the exam makes me nervous.\n(一想到考試就讓我緊張。)"],["merit","merit(n.)優點、價值、功績\n(無詞性變化)\non merit 憑實力\nmerits and demerits 優缺點\nEach plan has its own merits.\n(每個計畫都有各自的優點。)\nStudents are chosen on merit, not on family background.\n(學生是憑實力而非家庭背景被選上的。)"],["messenger","messenger(n.)送信人、使者\nmessage(n.)訊息\nsend a messenger 派使者\nmessenger bag 郵差包\nThe king sent a messenger with the news.\n(國王派使者傳達這個消息。)\nDon't blame the messenger for bad news.\n(別因為壞消息而怪罪傳話的人。)"],["messy","messy(adj.)凌亂的、髒亂的、棘手的\nmess(n.)凌亂、困境\nmessy room 凌亂的房間\nmessy hair 亂髮\nMy brother's room is always messy.\n(我弟弟的房間總是很亂。)\nEating spaghetti can be messy for kids.\n(對小孩來說吃義大利麵常會弄得一團糟。)"],["microscope","microscope(n.)顯微鏡\nmicroscopic(adj.)極小的、顯微鏡的\nunder a microscope 在顯微鏡下\nelectron microscope 電子顯微鏡\nWe looked at the cells under a microscope.\n(我們在顯微鏡下觀察細胞。)\nThe microscope was a great help to biologists.\n(顯微鏡對生物學家幫助很大。)"],["mild","mild(adj.)溫和的、溫暖的、輕微的\nmildly(adv.)溫和地、稍微\nmild weather 溫和的天氣\nmild symptoms 輕微的症狀\nTaiwan has mild winters.\n(台灣的冬天很溫和。)\nHe only had a mild cold and soon got better.\n(他只是輕微感冒，很快就好了。)"],["mill","mill(n./v.)磨坊、工廠、磨碎\nmiller(n.)磨坊主人\npaper mill 造紙廠\nwindmill 風車\nThe old mill by the river is now a museum.\n(河邊那座舊磨坊現在是博物館。)\nFarmers took their wheat to the mill.\n(農夫們把小麥送到磨坊。)"],["millionaire","millionaire(n.)百萬富翁\nmillion(n.)百萬\nbecome a millionaire 成為百萬富翁\nself-made millionaire 白手起家的富翁\nHe became a millionaire before he was thirty.\n(他在三十歲前就成了百萬富翁。)\nEven millionaires can't buy happiness.\n(就算是百萬富翁也買不到快樂。)"],["miner","miner(n.)礦工\nmine(n.)礦坑\ncoal miner 煤礦工\ngold miner 淘金者\nCoal miners once worked hard in Jiufen and Ruifang.\n(以前煤礦工人在九份和瑞芳辛苦工作。)\nThe trapped miners were rescued after three days.\n(受困的礦工在三天後獲救。)"],["mineral","mineral(n.)礦物、礦物質\n(無詞性變化)\nmineral water 礦泉水\nvitamins and minerals 維生素和礦物質\nWould you like a bottle of mineral water?\n(你要一瓶礦泉水嗎？)\nVegetables are rich in vitamins and minerals.\n(蔬菜富含維生素和礦物質。)"],["minimum","minimum(adj./n.)最小的、最低限度\nminimize(v.)使減到最少\nminimal(adj.)極少的\nminimum wage 最低工資\nat a minimum 至少\nThe minimum wage in Taiwan goes up almost every year.\n(台灣的基本工資幾乎每年都調漲。)\nYou need a minimum of 60 points to pass.\n(你至少需要六十分才能及格。)"],["minister","minister(n.)部長、牧師\nministry(n.)(政府的)部\nprime minister 首相、總理\nMinister of Education 教育部長\nThe Minister of Education visited our school.\n(教育部長參訪了我們學校。)\nThe prime minister gave a speech on TV.\n(首相在電視上發表演說。)"],["ministry","ministry(n.)(政府的)部、牧師職務\nminister(n.)部長、牧師\nMinistry of Education 教育部\nMinistry of Health 衛生部\nThe Ministry of Education announced a new policy.\n(教育部宣布了一項新政策。)\nHe works for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\n(他在外交部工作。)"],["mischief","mischief(n.)惡作劇、淘氣、損害\nmischievous(adj.)淘氣的、惡作劇的\nget into mischief 調皮搗蛋\nfull of mischief 十分淘氣\nThe kids got into mischief while their parents were out.\n(爸媽出門時孩子們調皮搗蛋。)\nHis eyes were full of mischief.\n(他的眼神充滿了淘氣。)"],["miserable","miserable(adj.)悲慘的、痛苦的、糟糕的\nmisery(n.)痛苦、不幸\nfeel miserable 感到難受\nmiserable weather 糟糕的天氣\nI felt miserable when I had a high fever.\n(我發高燒時覺得非常難受。)\nThe refugees lived in miserable conditions.\n(難民們生活在悲慘的環境中。)"],["misfortune","misfortune(n.)不幸、厄運\nfortune(n.)運氣、財富\nsuffer misfortune 遭遇不幸\nhave the misfortune to 不幸⋯\nShe had the misfortune to lose her job.\n(她不幸失去了工作。)\nDon't laugh at other people's misfortune.\n(不要嘲笑別人的不幸。)"],["mislead","mislead(v.)誤導、欺騙\nmisleading(adj.)誤導的\nmislead the public 誤導大眾\nmisleading information 誤導性的資訊\nThe ad misled customers about the price.\n(那則廣告在價格上誤導了消費者。)\nBe careful of misleading information online.\n(小心網路上的誤導性資訊。)"],["misunderstand","misunderstand(v.)誤解、誤會\nmisunderstanding(n.)誤會\ncompletely misunderstand 完全誤解\nclear up a misunderstanding 澄清誤會\nPlease don't misunderstand me; I was only joking.\n(請別誤會我，我只是在開玩笑。)\nWe talked and cleared up the misunderstanding.\n(我們談過之後澄清了誤會。)"],["moderate","moderate(adj.)中等的、適度的、溫和的\nmoderately(adv.)適度地\nmoderation(n.)適度\nmoderate exercise 適度的運動\nin moderation 適量地\nDoctors suggest thirty minutes of moderate exercise a day.\n(醫生建議每天做三十分鐘適度的運動。)\nEating sweets in moderation is fine.\n(適量吃甜食是沒關係的。)"],["modest","modest(adj.)謙虛的、適度的、樸素的\nmodesty(n.)謙虛\nmodestly(adv.)謙虛地\nmodest about 對⋯很謙虛\na modest income 不多的收入\nHe is very modest about his success.\n(他對自己的成功非常謙虛。)\nThey live in a modest house in the countryside.\n(他們住在鄉下一間樸素的房子裡。)"],["modesty","modesty(n.)謙虛、樸素\nmodest(adj.)謙虛的\nwith modesty 謙虛地\nfalse modesty 假謙虛\nShe accepted the award with modesty.\n(她謙虛地接受了這個獎項。)\nModesty is considered a virtue in many cultures.\n(在許多文化中，謙虛被視為一種美德。)"],["monitor","monitor(n./v.)螢幕、班長、監視器、監控\n(無詞性變化)\nclass monitor 班長\nmonitor progress 監控進度\nOur class monitor helps the teacher every day.\n(我們的班長每天都幫老師的忙。)\nDoctors closely monitored his condition.\n(醫生密切監控他的病情。)"],["monument","monument(n.)紀念碑、紀念建築、古蹟\nmonumental(adj.)紀念性的、巨大的\nhistoric monument 歷史古蹟\nbuild a monument 建紀念碑\nA monument was built to honor the soldiers.\n(人們建了一座紀念碑來紀念那些士兵。)\nThe castle is a historic monument.\n(這座城堡是一處歷史古蹟。)"],["moreover","moreover(adv.)此外、而且\n(無詞性變化)\nand moreover 而且\nMoreover, ... 此外，⋯\nThe hotel is cheap. Moreover, it's close to the station.\n(這間旅館很便宜，而且離車站很近。)\nExercise keeps you fit. Moreover, it improves your mood.\n(運動讓你保持健康，此外還能改善心情。)"],["motivate","motivate(v.)激勵、促使\nmotivation(n.)動機\nmotivated(adj.)積極的、有動機的\nmotivate students 激勵學生\nbe motivated to 有動力去⋯\nGood teachers know how to motivate students.\n(好老師知道如何激勵學生。)\nShe was motivated to study harder after the test.\n(考試後她更有動力用功讀書。)"],["motivation","motivation(n.)動機、幹勁\nmotivate(v.)激勵\nmotive(n.)動機\nlack of motivation 缺乏動機\nstrong motivation 強烈的動機\nLack of motivation is a common problem for students.\n(缺乏動機是學生常見的問題。)\nHis motivation for learning Japanese is his love of anime.\n(他學日文的動機是因為熱愛動漫。)"],["mountainous","mountainous(adj.)多山的、巨大的\nmountain(n.)山\nmountainous area 山區\nmountainous country 多山的國家\nMuch of Taiwan is mountainous.\n(台灣大部分地區多山。)\nThe village is in a remote mountainous area.\n(那個村莊位於偏遠的山區。)"],["muddy","muddy(adj.)泥濘的、沾滿泥的\nmud(n.)泥巴\nmuddy road 泥濘的道路\nmuddy shoes 沾滿泥的鞋子\nTake off your muddy shoes before coming in.\n(進來前先脫掉你沾滿泥巴的鞋子。)\nThe road became muddy after the heavy rain.\n(大雨過後道路變得泥濘。)"],["mule","mule(n.)騾子、頑固的人\n(無詞性變化)\nas stubborn as a mule 非常固執\nride a mule 騎騾子\nThe farmer used a mule to carry the goods.\n(農夫用騾子載運貨物。)\nMy brother is as stubborn as a mule.\n(我哥哥固執得要命。)"],["multiple","multiple(adj.)多重的、多樣的\nmultiply(v.)乘、增加\nmultiple-choice question 選擇題\nmultiple times 多次\nThe test has 30 multiple-choice questions.\n(這份考卷有三十題選擇題。)\nShe has called him multiple times, but he didn't answer.\n(她打了好幾次電話給他，但他都沒接。)"],["murderer","murderer(n.)殺人兇手\nmurder(n./v.)謀殺\ncold-blooded murderer 冷血殺手\ncatch the murderer 抓到兇手\nThe police finally caught the murderer.\n(警方終於抓到了殺人兇手。)\nIn the novel, the murderer turns out to be the butler.\n(在小說中，兇手原來是管家。)"],["murmur","murmur(n./v.)低語、潺潺聲、喃喃地說\n(無詞性變化)\nmurmur of the stream 溪水潺潺聲\nmurmur to oneself 喃喃自語\nShe murmured something I couldn't hear.\n(她低聲說了些我聽不見的話。)\nWe fell asleep to the murmur of the stream.\n(我們在溪水的潺潺聲中睡著了。)"],["mutual","mutual(adj.)相互的、共同的\nmutually(adv.)相互地\nmutual respect 互相尊重\nmutual friend 共同的朋友\nGood friendship is based on mutual respect.\n(良好的友誼建立在互相尊重之上。)\nWe met through a mutual friend.\n(我們是透過一位共同的朋友認識的。)"],["mysterious","mysterious(adj.)神祕的、難以理解的\nmystery(n.)謎、神祕的事物\nmysteriously(adv.)神祕地\nmysterious stranger 神祕的陌生人\nmysterious disappearance 離奇失蹤\nA mysterious letter arrived without a name.\n(一封沒有署名的神祕信件寄來了。)\nThe ship disappeared under mysterious circumstances.\n(那艘船在離奇的情況下失蹤了。)"],["namely","namely(adv.)即、也就是\n(無詞性變化)\nnamely that 也就是說\ntwo reasons, namely... 兩個原因，即⋯\nOnly one student passed, namely Amy.\n(只有一個學生及格，那就是艾咪。)\nWe need two things, namely time and money.\n(我們需要兩樣東西，也就是時間和金錢。)"],["nationality","nationality(n.)國籍\nnation(n.)國家\nnational(adj.)國家的\ndual nationality 雙重國籍\nof different nationalities 不同國籍的\nWhat is your nationality?\n(你的國籍是什麼？)\nStudents of many nationalities study at this school.\n(許多不同國籍的學生在這所學校就讀。)"],["needy","needy(adj.)貧窮的、窮困的\nneed(n./v.)需要\nneedy families 貧困家庭\nthe needy 窮人\nThe charity gives food to needy families.\n(那個慈善團體提供食物給貧困家庭。)\nWe should help the needy in our community.\n(我們應該幫助社區中的窮人。)"],["neglect","neglect(n./v.)忽視、疏忽\nnegligence(n.)疏忽、過失\nneglected(adj.)被忽視的\nneglect one's duty 怠忽職守\nchild neglect 兒童疏於照顧\nDon't neglect your health because of work.\n(不要因為工作而忽略你的健康。)\nThe garden was in a state of neglect.\n(花園處於荒廢狀態。)"],["negotiate","negotiate(v.)談判、協商\nnegotiation(n.)談判\nnegotiator(n.)談判者\nnegotiate with 與⋯談判\nnegotiate a price 議價\nThe two countries agreed to negotiate a peace deal.\n(兩國同意就和平協議進行談判。)\nYou can negotiate the price at the night market.\n(你可以在夜市討價還價。)"],["nevertheless","nevertheless(adv.)然而、不過、儘管如此\n(無詞性變化)\nbut nevertheless 但儘管如此\nNevertheless, ... 然而，⋯\nIt was raining hard; nevertheless, the game went on.\n(雨下得很大，然而比賽仍繼續進行。)\nThe task was difficult. Nevertheless, we finished it.\n(這任務很困難，儘管如此我們還是完成了。)"],["nightmare","nightmare(n.)惡夢、可怕的經歷\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a nightmare 做惡夢\na living nightmare 活生生的惡夢\nI had a nightmare about being chased by a tiger.\n(我夢到被老虎追的惡夢。)\nDriving in the heavy traffic was a nightmare.\n(在擁擠的車流中開車簡直是場惡夢。)"],["noble","noble(adj./n.)高尚的、貴族的、貴族\nnobility(n.)貴族、高尚\nnoble cause 崇高的目標\nnoble family 貴族家庭\nHelping the poor is a noble cause.\n(幫助窮人是一項崇高的事業。)\nShe was born into a noble family.\n(她出身於貴族家庭。)"],["nonsense","nonsense(n.)胡說、廢話、荒謬的行為\nnonsensical(adj.)荒謬的\ntalk nonsense 胡說八道\ncomplete nonsense 一派胡言\nStop talking nonsense and get to work.\n(別再胡說八道，快去工作。)\nThe idea that the earth is flat is complete nonsense.\n(地球是平的這種想法完全是胡扯。)"],["nowadays","nowadays(adv.)現今、時下\n(無詞性變化)\nyoung people nowadays 現在的年輕人\nNowadays, ... 現在，⋯\nNowadays, most people use smartphones.\n(現今大多數人都使用智慧型手機。)\nYoung people nowadays rarely write letters.\n(現在的年輕人很少寫信。)"],["nuclear","nuclear(adj.)核子的、核能的\nnucleus(n.)核心、原子核\nnuclear power 核能\nnuclear weapon 核子武器\nSome people are against nuclear power plants.\n(有些人反對核能發電廠。)\nThe world should get rid of nuclear weapons.\n(全世界應該廢除核子武器。)"],["numerous","numerous(adj.)許多的、大量的\n(無詞性變化)\nnumerous times 無數次\nnumerous examples 許多例子\nI have told you numerous times to lock the door.\n(我已經跟你說過無數次要鎖門了。)\nThe book has received numerous awards.\n(這本書獲得了許多獎項。)"],["nursery","nursery(n.)托兒所、育嬰室、苗圃\nnurse(n./v.)護理師、照顧\nnursery school 幼稚園\nnursery rhyme 童謠\nMy little sister goes to nursery school.\n(我妹妹上幼稚園。)\nGrandma taught me many nursery rhymes.\n(奶奶教了我很多童謠。)"],["nutritious","nutritious(adj.)有營養的\nnutrition(n.)營養\nnutrient(n.)營養素\nnutritious food 營養的食物\nnutritious meal 營養的一餐\nStudents need a nutritious breakfast to focus in class.\n(學生需要營養的早餐才能專心上課。)\nBrown rice is more nutritious than white rice.\n(糙米比白米更有營養。)"],["obedience","obedience(n.)服從、順從\nobey(v.)服從\nobedient(adj.)服從的\nobedience training 服從訓練\nblind obedience 盲目服從\nThe dog went to obedience school for three months.\n(那隻狗去上了三個月的服從訓練課程。)\nThe army demands complete obedience.\n(軍隊要求絕對服從。)"],["obedient","obedient(adj.)服從的、順從的\nobey(v.)服從\nobedience(n.)服從\nobedient child 聽話的孩子\nobedient to 服從⋯\nThe obedient dog sat down when told to.\n(那隻聽話的狗一聽口令就坐下。)\nHe was an obedient child who never caused trouble.\n(他是個從不惹麻煩的乖孩子。)"],["objection","objection(n.)反對、異議\nobject(v.)反對\nobjectionable(adj.)令人反感的\nhave no objection to 不反對⋯\nraise an objection 提出異議\nI have no objection to your plan.\n(我不反對你的計畫。)\nSeveral parents raised objections to the new rule.\n(有幾位家長對新規定提出異議。)"],["objective","objective(n./adj.)目標、客觀的\nobjectively(adv.)客觀地\nobjectivity(n.)客觀性\nmain objective 主要目標\nobjective opinion 客觀的意見\nOur main objective is to improve students' reading.\n(我們的主要目標是提升學生的閱讀能力。)\nA judge should stay objective.\n(法官應該保持客觀。)"],["observation","observation(n.)觀察、評論\nobserve(v.)觀察、遵守\nobserver(n.)觀察者\nunder observation 在觀察中\nmake an observation 做出評論\nThe patient is still under observation in the hospital.\n(那位病人仍在醫院觀察中。)\nCareful observation is important in science.\n(仔細觀察在科學中很重要。)"],["obstacle","obstacle(n.)障礙、妨礙\n(無詞性變化)\novercome an obstacle 克服障礙\nobstacle course 障礙賽跑道\nShe overcame many obstacles to become a doctor.\n(她克服了許多障礙才成為醫生。)\nFear is the biggest obstacle to success.\n(恐懼是成功最大的障礙。)"],["obtain","obtain(v.)獲得、取得\nobtainable(adj.)可獲得的\nobtain information 取得資訊\nobtain permission 獲得許可\nYou must obtain permission before using the lab.\n(使用實驗室前必須先獲得許可。)\nHe obtained a scholarship to study abroad.\n(他獲得了出國留學的獎學金。)"],["occasional","occasional(adj.)偶爾的、臨時的\noccasion(n.)場合、時機\noccasionally(adv.)偶爾\noccasional showers 偶有陣雨\nan occasional visitor 偶爾來訪的客人\nThe forecast says there will be occasional showers.\n(氣象預報說會偶有陣雨。)\nI eat fast food only occasionally.\n(我只是偶爾吃速食。)"],["occupation","occupation(n.)職業、占領\noccupy(v.)占據\noccupational(adj.)職業的\nchoose an occupation 選擇職業\nmilitary occupation 軍事占領\nPlease write down your name and occupation.\n(請寫下你的姓名和職業。)\nTeaching is a rewarding occupation.\n(教書是一份有成就感的職業。)"],["occupy","occupy(v.)占據、占用、使忙碌\noccupation(n.)占領、職業\noccupied(adj.)被占用的、忙碌的\nbe occupied with 忙於⋯\noccupy a seat 占座位\nIs this seat occupied?\n(這個座位有人坐嗎？)\nShe is occupied with preparing for the exam.\n(她正忙著準備考試。)"],["offend","offend(v.)冒犯、觸怒\noffense(n.)冒犯、犯罪\noffensive(adj.)冒犯的\nbe offended by 被⋯冒犯\noffend someone 得罪某人\nI'm sorry if my words offended you.\n(如果我的話冒犯了你，我很抱歉。)\nShe was offended by his rude joke.\n(她被他無禮的玩笑冒犯了。)"],["offense","offense(n.)冒犯、罪行、進攻\noffend(v.)冒犯\noffensive(adj.)冒犯的、攻擊的\ntake offense 生氣、見怪\ncriminal offense 刑事罪\nNo offense, but I don't like your idea.\n(無意冒犯，但我不喜歡你的點子。)\nDrunk driving is a serious offense.\n(酒駕是一項嚴重的罪行。)"],["offensive","offensive(adj.)冒犯的、令人不快的、攻擊性的\noffend(v.)冒犯\noffense(n.)冒犯\noffensive language 冒犯的言語\noffensive smell 難聞的氣味\nPlease avoid using offensive language online.\n(請避免在網路上使用冒犯性的言語。)\nThere was an offensive smell coming from the trash can.\n(垃圾桶傳出一股難聞的氣味。)"],["opera","opera(n.)歌劇\noperatic(adj.)歌劇的\nopera house 歌劇院\nPeking opera 京劇\nWe went to see an opera at the National Theater.\n(我們到國家戲劇院看歌劇。)\nThe Sydney Opera House is famous around the world.\n(雪梨歌劇院舉世聞名。)"],["oppose","oppose(v.)反對\nopposition(n.)反對\nopposed(adj.)反對的\nbe opposed to 反對⋯\nstrongly oppose 強烈反對\nMany residents oppose the new factory.\n(許多居民反對蓋新工廠。)\nMy parents are opposed to my dyeing my hair.\n(我爸媽反對我染頭髮。)"],["option","option(n.)選擇、選項\noptional(adj.)可選擇的、非必修的\nhave no option but to 只好⋯\nkeep one's options open 保留選擇餘地\nWe had no option but to wait for the next bus.\n(我們只好等下一班公車。)\nThere are several options for students after graduation.\n(學生畢業後有幾種選擇。)"],["orbit","orbit(n./v.)軌道、繞⋯運行\norbital(adj.)軌道的\nin orbit 在軌道上\norbit the earth 繞地球運行\nThe moon orbits the earth.\n(月球繞著地球運行。)\nThe satellite was put into orbit last year.\n(那顆衛星去年被送入軌道。)"],["orchestra","orchestra(n.)管弦樂團\norchestral(adj.)管弦樂的\nsymphony orchestra 交響樂團\nplay in an orchestra 在樂團演奏\nShe plays the violin in the school orchestra.\n(她在學校管弦樂團拉小提琴。)\nThe orchestra performed beautifully last night.\n(樂團昨晚演出得很精彩。)"],["orientation","orientation(n.)新生訓練、方向、取向\norient(v.)使適應、定位\nfreshman orientation 新生訓練\ncareer orientation 職涯導向\nAll new students must attend orientation in August.\n(所有新生都必須參加八月的新生訓練。)\nThe course has a strong practical orientation.\n(這門課具有很強的實務導向。)"],["orphan","orphan(n./v.)孤兒、使成為孤兒\norphanage(n.)孤兒院\nbe orphaned 成為孤兒\nwar orphan 戰爭孤兒\nThe boy was orphaned at the age of five.\n(那個男孩五歲時就成了孤兒。)\nThe orphan was raised by his grandparents.\n(那個孤兒由祖父母撫養長大。)"],["otherwise","otherwise(adv.)否則、不然、在其他方面\n(無詞性變化)\nor otherwise 或相反\nunless otherwise noted 除非另有說明\nHurry up; otherwise, you'll be late.\n(快一點，不然你會遲到。)\nThe room is small, but otherwise it's perfect.\n(房間很小，但其他方面都很完美。)"],["outcome","outcome(n.)結果、成果\n(無詞性變化)\nfinal outcome 最終結果\nlearning outcome 學習成果\nNo one could predict the outcome of the election.\n(沒有人能預測選舉的結果。)\nWe are waiting for the outcome of the meeting.\n(我們正在等候會議的結果。)"],["outstanding","outstanding(adj.)傑出的、顯著的、未解決的\n(無詞性變化)\noutstanding student 傑出的學生\noutstanding performance 傑出的表現\nShe received an award for her outstanding performance.\n(她因傑出的表現而獲獎。)\nThere are still some outstanding problems to solve.\n(還有一些未解決的問題需要處理。)"],["oval","oval(adj./n.)橢圓形的、橢圓形\n(無詞性變化)\noval face 鵝蛋臉\noval table 橢圓桌\nShe has an oval face and big eyes.\n(她有一張鵝蛋臉和一雙大眼睛。)\nWe sat around an oval table in the meeting room.\n(我們圍坐在會議室的橢圓桌旁。)"],["overcoat","overcoat(n.)大衣\ncoat(n.)外套\nwool overcoat 羊毛大衣\nput on an overcoat 穿上大衣\nHe wore a heavy overcoat in the cold weather.\n(他在寒冷的天氣裡穿了一件厚大衣。)\nHang your overcoat on the hook by the door.\n(把你的大衣掛在門邊的掛鉤上。)"],["overcome","overcome(v.)克服、戰勝\n(無詞性變化)\novercome difficulties 克服困難\nbe overcome with 被⋯壓垮、充滿⋯\nShe worked hard to overcome her fear of speaking in public.\n(她努力克服在公開場合說話的恐懼。)\nHe was overcome with joy when he heard the news.\n(他聽到消息時欣喜若狂。)"],["overlook","overlook(v.)忽略、俯瞰、寬恕\n(無詞性變化)\noverlook a mistake 忽略錯誤、寬恕錯誤\noverlook the sea 俯瞰大海\nIt's easy to overlook small spelling mistakes.\n(很容易忽略小的拼字錯誤。)\nOur hotel room overlooks the sea.\n(我們的飯店房間可以俯瞰大海。)"],["overnight","overnight(adv./adj.)一夜之間、過夜、通宵的\n(無詞性變化)\nstay overnight 過夜\novernight success 一夜成名\nWe stayed overnight at a hotel near the airport.\n(我們在機場附近的旅館過了一夜。)\nThe singer became famous overnight.\n(那位歌手一夜之間爆紅。)"],["overthrow","overthrow(v.)推翻、打倒\n(無詞性變化)\noverthrow the government 推翻政府\noverthrow a king 推翻國王\nThe people rose up to overthrow the cruel king.\n(人民起義推翻了殘暴的國王。)\nThe army tried to overthrow the government.\n(軍方試圖推翻政府。)"],["oxygen","oxygen(n.)氧氣\n(無詞性變化)\noxygen mask 氧氣面罩\nlack of oxygen 缺氧\nPlants produce oxygen through photosynthesis.\n(植物透過光合作用產生氧氣。)\nClimbers often carry oxygen on high mountains.\n(登山客在高山上常攜帶氧氣。)"],["pace","pace(n./v.)步調、速度、踱步\n(無詞性變化)\nkeep pace with 跟上…\nat one's own pace 按自己的步調\nIt is hard to keep pace with changing technology.\n(要跟上日新月異的科技很困難。)\nHe paced up and down the room, waiting for the news.\n(他在房間裡來回踱步，等待消息。)"],["panel","panel(n.)小組、專門小組、面板、嵌板\n(無詞性變化)\nsolar panel 太陽能板\na panel of experts 專家小組\nThere are solar panels on the school roof.\n(學校屋頂上有太陽能板。)\nA panel of judges chose the winner of the contest.\n(一組評審選出了比賽的優勝者。)"],["parachute","parachute(n./v.)降落傘、跳傘\n(無詞性變化)\nopen a parachute 打開降落傘\nparachute jump 跳傘\nThe soldier opened his parachute and landed safely.\n(士兵打開降落傘，安全著陸。)\nSupplies were parachuted into the flooded village.\n(物資被空投到淹水的村莊。)"],["paragraph","paragraph(n.)段落\n(無詞性變化)\nthe first paragraph 第一段\ntopic sentence of a paragraph 段落主題句\nPlease read the first paragraph aloud.\n(請大聲朗讀第一段。)\nEach paragraph should have a clear main idea.\n(每個段落都應該有清楚的主旨。)"],["partial","partial(adj.)部分的、偏袒的\npartially(adv.)部分地\npartial success 部分成功\nbe partial to 偏愛…\nThe plan was only a partial success.\n(這個計畫只算部分成功。)\nMy grandmother is partial to sweet desserts.\n(我奶奶偏愛甜點。)"],["participation","participation(n.)參與、參加\nparticipate(v.)參與\nparticipant(n.)參與者\nactive participation 積極參與\nclass participation 課堂參與\nClass participation counts for 20% of your grade.\n(課堂參與佔你成績的百分之二十。)\nWe thank everyone for their participation in the event.\n(我們感謝大家參與這次活動。)"],["partnership","partnership(n.)合夥關係、合作關係\npartner(n.)夥伴、搭檔\nin partnership with 與…合作\nform a partnership 建立合作關係\nThe school works in partnership with local businesses.\n(這所學校與在地企業合作。)\nThe two companies formed a partnership last year.\n(這兩家公司去年建立了合作關係。)"],["passive","passive(adj.)被動的、消極的\npassively(adv.)被動地\npassive voice 被動語態\npassive attitude 消極的態度\nDon't be passive; ask questions in class.\n(不要被動，上課要發問。)\nWe learned how to use the passive voice today.\n(我們今天學了被動語態的用法。)"],["pasta","pasta(n.)義大利麵食\n(無詞性變化)\ncook pasta 煮義大利麵\npasta sauce 義大利麵醬\nMy mom cooked pasta with tomato sauce for dinner.\n(我媽媽晚餐煮了番茄醬義大利麵。)\nSpaghetti is one of the most popular kinds of pasta.\n(直麵是最受歡迎的義大利麵之一。)"],["paw","paw(n./v.)(動物的)腳掌、用爪子抓或碰\n(無詞性變化)\na dog's paw 狗的腳掌\npaw at 用爪子撥弄\nThe puppy hurt its paw while playing.\n(小狗玩耍時弄傷了腳掌。)\nThe cat pawed at the door to get in.\n(貓用爪子扒門想進來。)"],["peculiar","peculiar(adj.)奇怪的、特有的\npeculiarity(n.)特點、怪癖\npeculiar to 是…特有的\na peculiar smell 奇怪的味道\nThere is a peculiar smell coming from the kitchen.\n(廚房傳來一股奇怪的味道。)\nThis kind of bird is peculiar to Taiwan.\n(這種鳥是臺灣特有的。)"],["peep","peep(n./v.)偷看、窺視、瞥一眼\n(無詞性變化)\npeep through 從…偷看\ntake a peep at 偷看一眼\nThe kids peeped through the window at the party.\n(孩子們從窗戶偷看派對。)\nLet me take a peep at your new phone.\n(讓我看一眼你的新手機。)"],["peer","peer(n./v.)同儕、同輩、凝視\n(無詞性變化)\npeer pressure 同儕壓力\npeer at 凝視、仔細看\nTeenagers often feel peer pressure.\n(青少年常感受到同儕壓力。)\nShe peered at the tiny words on the screen.\n(她盯著螢幕上的小字仔細看。)"],["penalty","penalty(n.)處罰、罰款、罰球\npenalize(v.)處罰\ndeath penalty 死刑\npenalty kick 罰球、十二碼球\nThere is a heavy penalty for drunk driving.\n(酒駕會受到重罰。)\nHe scored the winning goal with a penalty kick.\n(他靠十二碼罰球踢進致勝球。)"],["percent","percent(n.)百分之…\n(無詞性變化)\nten percent 百分之十\na 50 percent discount 五折\nAbout 70 percent of the earth is covered by water.\n(地球約百分之七十被水覆蓋。)\nThe store is offering a 20 percent discount.\n(這家店正在打八折。)"],["percentage","percentage(n.)百分比、比例\npercent(n.)百分之…\na high percentage 高比例\npercentage of 某事物的百分比\nA high percentage of students passed the exam.\n(很高比例的學生通過了考試。)\nWhat percentage of your income do you save?\n(你把收入的百分之多少存起來？)"],["perfection","perfection(n.)完美、完善\nperfect(adj./v.)完美的、使完美\nperfectionist(n.)完美主義者\naim for perfection 追求完美\ncooked to perfection 煮得恰到好處\nThe steak was cooked to perfection.\n(這塊牛排煎得恰到好處。)\nNobody can achieve perfection in everything.\n(沒有人能在每件事上都做到完美。)"],["perfume","perfume(n./v.)香水、香氣、使充滿香味\n(無詞性變化)\nwear perfume 擦香水\na bottle of perfume 一瓶香水\nShe wore a light perfume to the party.\n(她擦了淡淡的香水去參加派對。)\nFlowers perfumed the air in the garden.\n(花朵讓花園的空氣充滿香氣。)"],["permanent","permanent(adj.)永久的、持久的\npermanently(adv.)永久地\npermanent job 固定工作\npermanent damage 永久損傷\nLoud music can cause permanent damage to your ears.\n(大聲的音樂可能對耳朵造成永久傷害。)\nShe is looking for a permanent job.\n(她正在找一份固定的工作。)"],["persuasion","persuasion(n.)說服、勸說\npersuade(v.)說服\npersuasive(adj.)有說服力的\npower of persuasion 說服力\nafter much persuasion 經過一番勸說\nAfter much persuasion, he agreed to join us.\n(經過一番勸說，他同意加入我們。)\nGood leaders have strong powers of persuasion.\n(好的領導者有很強的說服力。)"],["persuasive","persuasive(adj.)有說服力的\npersuade(v.)說服\npersuasion(n.)說服\npersuasive essay 論說文\npersuasive argument 有說服力的論點\nWe have to write a persuasive essay this week.\n(我們這週要寫一篇論說文。)\nHer speech was very persuasive.\n(她的演講非常有說服力。)"],["pessimistic","pessimistic(adj.)悲觀的\npessimist(n.)悲觀主義者\npessimism(n.)悲觀主義\nbe pessimistic about 對…悲觀\na pessimistic view 悲觀的看法\nHe is pessimistic about his chances of winning.\n(他對自己獲勝的機會感到悲觀。)\nDon't be so pessimistic; things will get better.\n(別那麼悲觀，事情會好轉的。)"],["pest","pest(n.)害蟲、討厭的人\npesticide(n.)殺蟲劑、農藥\npest control 病蟲害防治\ngarden pests 園藝害蟲\nFarmers use different methods to control pests.\n(農夫用不同方法來防治害蟲。)\nMy little brother can be a real pest sometimes.\n(我弟弟有時候真的很煩人。)"],["phenomenon","phenomenon(n.)現象\nphenomena(n.)現象(複數)\nphenomenal(adj.)非凡的\nnatural phenomenon 自然現象\nsocial phenomenon 社會現象\nA rainbow is a beautiful natural phenomenon.\n(彩虹是一種美麗的自然現象。)\nOnline shopping has become a global phenomenon.\n(網路購物已成為全球現象。)"],["philosopher","philosopher(n.)哲學家\nphilosophy(n.)哲學\nGreek philosopher 希臘哲學家\na great philosopher 偉大的哲學家\nSocrates was a famous Greek philosopher.\n(蘇格拉底是著名的希臘哲學家。)\nConfucius was a great Chinese philosopher.\n(孔子是偉大的中國哲學家。)"],["philosophical","philosophical(adj.)哲學的、達觀的\nphilosophy(n.)哲學\nphilosophically(adv.)達觀地\nphilosophical question 哲學問題\nbe philosophical about 對…看得開\nWhat is happiness? That is a philosophical question.\n(什麼是幸福？那是個哲學問題。)\nHe was philosophical about losing the game.\n(他對輸掉比賽看得很開。)"],["philosophy","philosophy(n.)哲學、人生觀\nphilosopher(n.)哲學家\nphilosophical(adj.)哲學的\nphilosophy of life 人生觀\nstudy philosophy 研讀哲學\nMy philosophy of life is to enjoy every day.\n(我的人生觀是享受每一天。)\nShe decided to study philosophy at university.\n(她決定在大學念哲學。)"],["photography","photography(n.)攝影、攝影術\nphotographer(n.)攝影師\nphotograph(n.)照片\nnature photography 自然攝影\nphotography club 攝影社\nHe joined the photography club in high school.\n(他高中時加入了攝影社。)\nPhotography is not allowed in this museum.\n(這間博物館禁止攝影。)"],["physical","physical(adj.)身體的、物質的、物理的\nphysically(adv.)身體上\nphysical education 體育課\nphysical activity 身體活動\nPhysical activity is good for your health.\n(身體活動對健康有益。)\nWe have physical education class twice a week.\n(我們每週上兩次體育課。)"],["physician","physician(n.)醫師、內科醫生\n(無詞性變化)\nfamily physician 家庭醫師\nconsult a physician 諮詢醫師\nYou should consult a physician if the pain continues.\n(如果疼痛持續，你應該去看醫生。)\nOur family physician knows our health history well.\n(我們的家庭醫師很清楚我們的健康史。)"],["physicist","physicist(n.)物理學家\nphysics(n.)物理學\na famous physicist 著名的物理學家\nnuclear physicist 核子物理學家\nAlbert Einstein was a famous physicist.\n(愛因斯坦是著名的物理學家。)\nShe dreams of becoming a physicist.\n(她夢想成為一位物理學家。)"],["physics","physics(n.)物理學\nphysical(adj.)物理的\nphysicist(n.)物理學家\nphysics class 物理課\nlaws of physics 物理定律\nPhysics is my favorite subject.\n(物理是我最喜歡的科目。)\nNothing can break the laws of physics.\n(沒有任何東西能違反物理定律。)"],["pickle","pickle(n.)醃黃瓜、醃菜\npickled(adj.)醃漬的\na jar of pickles 一罐醃黃瓜\nin a pickle 處於困境\nI don't like pickles in my hamburger.\n(我不喜歡漢堡裡有醃黃瓜。)\nI forgot my wallet and was in a real pickle.\n(我忘了帶錢包，陷入了困境。)"],["pioneer","pioneer(n./v.)先驅、拓荒者、開創\npioneering(adj.)開創性的\na pioneer in 某領域的先驅\npioneer a method 首創一種方法\nShe was a pioneer in women's education.\n(她是女性教育的先驅。)\nThe company pioneered the use of solar energy.\n(這家公司率先使用太陽能。)"],["plentiful","plentiful(adj.)大量的、豐富的\nplenty(n.)大量、充足\nplentiful supply 充足的供應\nplentiful food 豐富的食物\nFruit is plentiful in Taiwan during the summer.\n(臺灣夏天水果很豐富。)\nFresh water is not plentiful in desert areas.\n(沙漠地區的淡水並不充足。)"],["plot","plot(n./v.)情節、陰謀、密謀、小塊地\n(無詞性變化)\nthe plot of a movie 電影情節\nplot against 密謀對付\nThe plot of the movie was hard to follow.\n(這部電影的情節很難理解。)\nThey plotted to steal the jewels.\n(他們密謀偷竊珠寶。)"],["plum","plum(n.)李子、梅子\n(無詞性變化)\nplum tree 李樹、梅樹\nplum blossom 梅花\nThe plum blossom is the national flower of Taiwan.\n(梅花是中華民國的國花。)\nShe made jam from fresh plums.\n(她用新鮮李子做果醬。)"],["plumber","plumber(n.)水管工人\nplumbing(n.)水管設備、管線工程\ncall a plumber 叫水電工\na skilled plumber 技術好的水管工\nWe called a plumber to fix the leaking pipe.\n(我們打電話叫水電工來修漏水的水管。)\nThe plumber came quickly and fixed the sink.\n(水電工很快就來修好了水槽。)"],["poisonous","poisonous(adj.)有毒的\npoison(n./v.)毒藥、下毒\npoisonous snake 毒蛇\npoisonous gas 毒氣\nSome mushrooms are poisonous, so don't eat them.\n(有些蘑菇有毒，所以不要吃。)\nBe careful of poisonous snakes in the mountains.\n(在山上要小心毒蛇。)"],["polish","polish(n./v.)擦亮、磨光、亮光劑、潤飾\npolished(adj.)擦亮的、精練的\nnail polish 指甲油\npolish one's English 磨練英文\nHe polished his shoes before the interview.\n(他面試前把鞋子擦亮。)\nYou should polish your essay before handing it in.\n(交作文前你應該再潤飾一下。)"],["popularity","popularity(n.)受歡迎、普及\npopular(adj.)受歡迎的\ngain popularity 越來越受歡迎\npopularity among 在…之間受歡迎\nThe game gained popularity among teenagers.\n(這款遊戲在青少年間越來越受歡迎。)\nThe singer's popularity grew after the show.\n(那位歌手在節目播出後人氣上升。)"],["portable","portable(adj.)便於攜帶的、手提式的\n(無詞性變化)\nportable charger 行動電源\nportable speaker 攜帶式喇叭\nDon't forget to bring your portable charger.\n(別忘了帶你的行動電源。)\nThis portable speaker is light and easy to carry.\n(這個攜帶式喇叭又輕又方便帶。)"],["portray","portray(v.)描繪、描寫、扮演\nportrayal(n.)描繪、扮演\nportrait(n.)肖像、畫像\nportray sb. as 把某人描繪成…\nportray a character 飾演一個角色\nThe movie portrays him as a hero.\n(這部電影把他描繪成英雄。)\nThe actor portrayed a teacher in the drama.\n(那位演員在劇中飾演一位老師。)"],["possess","possess(v.)擁有、具有\npossession(n.)擁有、財產\npossessive(adj.)占有慾強的\npossess talent 具有天分\npossess a license 持有執照\nShe possesses a great talent for music.\n(她擁有極高的音樂天分。)\nYou must possess a license to drive a car.\n(你必須有駕照才能開車。)"],["possession","possession(n.)擁有、財產、所有物\npossess(v.)擁有\npersonal possessions 個人財物\nin possession of 擁有…\nThe fire destroyed all their possessions.\n(那場火燒毀了他們所有的財物。)\nHe was found in possession of stolen goods.\n(他被發現持有贓物。)"],["postage","postage(n.)郵資、郵費\npost(n./v.)郵件、郵寄\npostage stamp 郵票\npostage paid 郵資已付\nHow much is the postage for this letter?\n(這封信的郵資是多少？)\nThe postage to Japan is more expensive.\n(寄到日本的郵資比較貴。)"],["potential","potential(adj./n.)潛在的、可能的、潛力\npotentially(adv.)潛在地\nreach one's potential 發揮潛力\npotential danger 潛在危險\nEvery student has the potential to succeed.\n(每個學生都有成功的潛力。)\nWe must be aware of the potential dangers of the internet.\n(我們必須注意網路的潛在危險。)"],["precise","precise(adj.)精確的、準確的\nprecisely(adv.)精確地、正是\nprecision(n.)精確\nprecise instructions 明確的指示\nto be precise 精確地說\nThe teacher gave us precise instructions.\n(老師給了我們明確的指示。)\nThe train arrived at precisely nine o'clock.\n(火車正好在九點整抵達。)"],["predict","predict(v.)預測、預言\nprediction(n.)預測\npredictable(adj.)可預測的\npredict the future 預測未來\nhard to predict 難以預測\nNo one can predict the future.\n(沒有人能預測未來。)\nExperts predict that more people will work from home.\n(專家預測會有更多人在家工作。)"],["prediction","prediction(n.)預測、預言\npredict(v.)預測\nmake a prediction 做出預測\nweather prediction 天氣預測\nHis prediction about the game turned out to be right.\n(他對比賽的預測結果是對的。)\nIt is difficult to make predictions about the economy.\n(要預測經濟情勢很困難。)"],["pregnancy","pregnancy(n.)懷孕、懷孕期\npregnant(adj.)懷孕的\nduring pregnancy 懷孕期間\npregnancy test 驗孕\nWomen should not smoke during pregnancy.\n(女性在懷孕期間不應抽菸。)\nShe felt tired in the early months of her pregnancy.\n(她在懷孕初期感到很疲倦。)"],["pregnant","pregnant(adj.)懷孕的\npregnancy(n.)懷孕\nget pregnant 懷孕\npregnant women 孕婦\nMy aunt is pregnant with her second child.\n(我阿姨正懷著第二胎。)\nPlease give your seat to pregnant women.\n(請讓座給孕婦。)"],["presentation","presentation(n.)報告、簡報、呈現、贈送\npresent(v.)呈現、贈送\ngive a presentation 做報告\npresentation skills 簡報技巧\nI have to give a presentation in English class tomorrow.\n(我明天英文課要上台報告。)\nGood presentation skills are useful in any job.\n(良好的簡報技巧在任何工作中都很有用。)"],["preservation","preservation(n.)保存、保護\npreserve(v.)保存、保護\nhistoric preservation 古蹟保存\nfood preservation 食物保存\nThe preservation of old buildings is important.\n(保存老建築很重要。)\nSalt has long been used for food preservation.\n(鹽很早就被用來保存食物。)"],["preserve","preserve(v.)保存、保護、維持\npreservation(n.)保存\npreservative(n.)防腐劑\npreserve the environment 保護環境\npreserve traditions 保存傳統\nWe must work together to preserve the environment.\n(我們必須一起努力保護環境。)\nThe village has preserved its traditional culture.\n(這個村莊保存了其傳統文化。)"],["prevention","prevention(n.)預防、防止\nprevent(v.)預防、阻止\npreventive(adj.)預防的\ndisease prevention 疾病預防\ncrime prevention 犯罪防治\nPrevention is better than cure.\n(預防勝於治療。)\nThe government spends a lot on disease prevention.\n(政府在疾病預防上花了很多錢。)"],["prime","prime(adj./n.)主要的、最好的、全盛時期\n(無詞性變化)\nprime minister 首相、總理\nin one's prime 正值壯年、全盛時期\nThe prime minister will visit Taiwan next month.\n(那位首相下個月將訪問臺灣。)\nThe athlete was in his prime at the age of 25.\n(這名運動員在25歲時正處於巔峰期。)"],["primitive","primitive(adj.)原始的、簡陋的\n(無詞性變化)\nprimitive society 原始社會\nprimitive tools 原始工具\nPrimitive people used stone tools to hunt.\n(原始人使用石器打獵。)\nThe cabin was primitive, with no electricity.\n(那間小屋很簡陋，沒有電。)"],["priority","priority(n.)優先、優先事項\nprior(adj.)在先的\nprioritize(v.)優先處理\ntop priority 首要之務\ngive priority to 優先考慮\nYour health should be your top priority.\n(你的健康應該是首要之務。)\nBuses give priority to elderly passengers.\n(公車優先禮讓年長乘客。)"],["privacy","privacy(n.)隱私、私生活\nprivate(adj.)私人的\ninvade one's privacy 侵犯隱私\nprivacy policy 隱私權政策\nReading my diary is an invasion of my privacy.\n(看我的日記是侵犯我的隱私。)\nTeenagers need some privacy.\n(青少年需要一些隱私。)"],["privilege","privilege(n./v.)特權、榮幸、給予特權\nprivileged(adj.)享有特權的\na great privilege 莫大的榮幸\nspecial privileges 特權\nIt is a privilege to meet you.\n(能見到您是我的榮幸。)\nSenior students have some special privileges.\n(高年級學生享有一些特權。)"],["procedure","procedure(n.)程序、步驟、手續\nprocedural(adj.)程序上的\nstandard procedure 標準程序\nfollow the procedure 遵照程序\nPlease follow the safety procedures in the lab.\n(在實驗室裡請遵守安全程序。)\nApplying for a passport is a simple procedure.\n(申請護照的手續很簡單。)"],["proceed","proceed(v.)繼續進行、前往\nprocedure(n.)程序\nprocess(n.)過程\nproceed with 繼續進行…\nproceed to 前往…\nLet's proceed with the meeting.\n(我們繼續開會吧。)\nPassengers should proceed to Gate 5.\n(旅客請前往五號登機門。)"],["productive","productive(adj.)多產的、有成效的\nproductivity(n.)生產力\nproduct(n.)產品\na productive day 充實的一天\nproductive land 肥沃的土地\nI had a very productive day at the library.\n(我在圖書館度過了非常有效率的一天。)\nGetting enough sleep makes you more productive.\n(充足的睡眠讓你更有效率。)"],["profession","profession(n.)職業、專業\nprofessional(adj./n.)專業的、專業人士\nteaching profession 教職\nby profession 就職業而言\nShe is a lawyer by profession.\n(她的職業是律師。)\nNursing is a very demanding profession.\n(護理是非常辛苦的職業。)"],["professional","professional(adj./n.)專業的、職業的、專業人士\nprofessionally(adv.)專業地\nprofession(n.)職業\nprofessional athlete 職業運動員\nseek professional help 尋求專業協助\nHe wants to become a professional baseball player.\n(他想成為職業棒球選手。)\nIf you feel stressed, seek professional help.\n(如果你感到壓力很大，要尋求專業協助。)"],["profitable","profitable(adj.)有利潤的、有益的\nprofit(n./v.)利潤、獲益\nhighly profitable 利潤豐厚的\na profitable business 賺錢的生意\nSelling bubble tea is a profitable business.\n(賣珍珠奶茶是門賺錢的生意。)\nThe trip was a profitable learning experience.\n(這趟旅行是一次很有收穫的學習經驗。)"],["prominent","prominent(adj.)著名的、顯著的、突出的\nprominence(n.)卓越、顯著\na prominent figure 知名人物\nplay a prominent role 扮演重要角色\nHe is a prominent scientist in his field.\n(他是他所屬領域的知名科學家。)\nThe museum stands in a prominent position in the city.\n(這座博物館位於城市的顯眼位置。)"],["promising","promising(adj.)有前途的、有希望的\npromise(n./v.)承諾、有希望\na promising future 光明的前途\na promising young player 有潛力的年輕選手\nShe is a promising young pianist.\n(她是一位很有前途的年輕鋼琴家。)\nThe results of the test look promising.\n(測試結果看起來很有希望。)"],["promotion","promotion(n.)升遷、促銷、促進\npromote(v.)升遷、促銷、促進\nget a promotion 獲得升遷\nsales promotion 促銷\nMy father got a promotion last month.\n(我爸爸上個月升職了。)\nThe store is having a special promotion this weekend.\n(這家店這週末有特別促銷活動。)"],["prompt","prompt(v./adj./n.)促使、即時的、提示\npromptly(adv.)迅速地、準時地\nprompt action 迅速的行動\nprompt sb. to 促使某人做…\nThank you for your prompt reply.\n(謝謝你迅速回覆。)\nThe news prompted her to call her parents.\n(這則新聞促使她打電話給父母。)"],["pronunciation","pronunciation(n.)發音\npronounce(v.)發音\ncorrect pronunciation 正確的發音\npractice pronunciation 練習發音\nHer English pronunciation is very clear.\n(她的英文發音非常清楚。)\nListening to songs can help improve your pronunciation.\n(聽歌有助於改善你的發音。)"],["proposal","proposal(n.)提議、提案、求婚\npropose(v.)提議、求婚\nmake a proposal 提出建議\nmarriage proposal 求婚\nThe class rejected his proposal for a picnic.\n(全班否決了他去野餐的提議。)\nShe accepted his marriage proposal.\n(她接受了他的求婚。)"],["prosper","prosper(v.)繁榮、興盛、成功\nprosperity(n.)繁榮\nprosperous(adj.)繁榮的\nbusiness prospers 生意興隆\na city prospers 城市繁榮\nThe town prospered after the railway was built.\n(鐵路建成後，這個小鎮繁榮起來。)\nHer business prospered thanks to good service.\n(她的生意因為良好服務而興隆。)"],["prosperity","prosperity(n.)繁榮、興旺\nprosper(v.)繁榮\nprosperous(adj.)繁榮的\neconomic prosperity 經濟繁榮\npeace and prosperity 和平與繁榮\nThe country enjoyed years of peace and prosperity.\n(這個國家享有多年的和平與繁榮。)\nEducation is the key to future prosperity.\n(教育是未來繁榮的關鍵。)"],["prosperous","prosperous(adj.)繁榮的、興旺的\nprosper(v.)繁榮\nprosperity(n.)繁榮\na prosperous city 繁榮的城市\na prosperous new year 新年興旺\nTaipei has become a prosperous city.\n(臺北已成為一座繁榮的城市。)\nWe wish you a happy and prosperous new year.\n(祝你新年快樂、萬事興旺。)"],["protein","protein(n.)蛋白質\n(無詞性變化)\nrich in protein 富含蛋白質\nprotein shake 高蛋白飲品\nEggs and beans are rich in protein.\n(蛋和豆類富含蛋白質。)\nAthletes need more protein to build muscle.\n(運動員需要更多蛋白質來增加肌肉。)"],["protest","protest(n./v.)抗議、反對\nprotester(n.)抗議者\nprotest against 抗議…\nin protest 以示抗議\nThousands of people protested against the new law.\n(數千人抗議這項新法律。)\nThe workers walked out in protest.\n(工人們罷工離場以示抗議。)"],["psychological","psychological(adj.)心理的、心理學的\npsychologically(adv.)心理上\npsychological pressure 心理壓力\npsychological test 心理測驗\nExams can cause a lot of psychological pressure.\n(考試可能帶來很大的心理壓力。)\nWe took a fun psychological test in class.\n(我們在課堂上做了一個有趣的心理測驗。)"],["psychologist","psychologist(n.)心理學家\npsychology(n.)心理學\nchild psychologist 兒童心理學家\nsee a psychologist 看心理師\nThe school psychologist helps students with stress.\n(學校的心理師協助學生處理壓力。)\nPsychologists study how people think and behave.\n(心理學家研究人們如何思考與行為。)"],["psychology","psychology(n.)心理學、心理\npsychological(adj.)心理的\npsychologist(n.)心理學家\nstudy psychology 研讀心理學\nchild psychology 兒童心理學\nShe plans to major in psychology.\n(她打算主修心理學。)\nGood salespeople understand customer psychology.\n(好的業務員了解顧客心理。)"],["publication","publication(n.)出版、出版品、發表\npublish(v.)出版\ndate of publication 出版日期\na monthly publication 月刊\nThe publication of her first novel made her famous.\n(她的第一本小說出版後使她成名。)\nThe school magazine is a monthly publication.\n(校刊是一份月刊。)"],["publicity","publicity(n.)宣傳、知名度、公眾注意\npublic(adj./n.)公眾的、大眾\npublicize(v.)宣傳\nbad publicity 負面報導\nattract publicity 吸引關注\nThe movie got a lot of publicity before its release.\n(這部電影上映前做了大量宣傳。)\nThe scandal brought the company bad publicity.\n(醜聞讓公司受到負面報導。)"],["publish","publish(v.)出版、發表、公布\npublication(n.)出版\npublisher(n.)出版商\npublish a book 出版書籍\npublish results 公布結果\nHe published his first book at the age of 20.\n(他二十歲時出版了第一本書。)\nThe exam results will be published online.\n(考試結果將在網路上公布。)"],["publisher","publisher(n.)出版商、出版社\npublish(v.)出版\nbook publisher 圖書出版社\na major publisher 大型出版社\nShe sent her novel to several publishers.\n(她把小說寄給好幾家出版社。)\nThe publisher decided to print more copies.\n(出版社決定加印更多本。)"],["pursue","pursue(v.)追求、追趕、從事\npursuit(n.)追求、追趕\npursue a dream 追求夢想\npursue a career 從事某職業\nShe went abroad to pursue her dream.\n(她出國追求她的夢想。)\nThe police pursued the thief down the street.\n(警察沿街追捕小偷。)"],["pursuit","pursuit(n.)追求、追趕、消遣活動\npursue(v.)追求\nin pursuit of 追求…、追趕…\nthe pursuit of happiness 追求幸福\nMany people move to cities in pursuit of a better life.\n(許多人為了追求更好的生活而搬到城市。)\nReading is one of her favorite pursuits.\n(閱讀是她最喜歡的消遣之一。)"],["quarrel","quarrel(n./v.)爭吵、吵架\n(無詞性變化)\nquarrel with 和…吵架\nhave a quarrel 吵架\nThe twins often quarrel over toys.\n(那對雙胞胎常為了玩具吵架。)\nI had a quarrel with my best friend yesterday.\n(我昨天和最好的朋友吵了一架。)"],["quilt","quilt(n./v.)被子、棉被、縫製被子\n(無詞性變化)\na warm quilt 溫暖的被子\npatchwork quilt 拼布被\nI sleep under a thick quilt in winter.\n(冬天我蓋厚棉被睡覺。)\nMy grandmother made this patchwork quilt by hand.\n(我奶奶親手縫製了這條拼布被。)"],["quotation","quotation(n.)引文、語錄、報價\nquote(v./n.)引用、報價\nquotation marks 引號\na famous quotation 名言\nShe began her speech with a famous quotation.\n(她用一句名言開始她的演講。)\nPlease get a price quotation before you buy.\n(購買前請先取得報價。)"],["radar","radar(n.)雷達\n(無詞性變化)\nradar screen 雷達螢幕\nunder the radar 不受注意地\nThe plane disappeared from the radar screen over the ocean.\n(那架飛機在海洋上空從雷達螢幕上消失了。)\nThe small company grew quickly while staying under the radar.\n(那間小公司在不受注意的情況下迅速成長。)"],["rage","rage(n./v.)狂怒、盛怒、肆虐\n(無詞性變化)\nin a rage 盛怒之下\nroad rage 路怒症\nHe broke the cup in a fit of rage.\n(他在盛怒之下打破了杯子。)\nThe fire raged through the forest for three days.\n(大火在森林中肆虐了三天。)"],["rainfall","rainfall(n.)降雨量、降雨\n(無詞性變化)\nheavy rainfall 大量降雨\nannual rainfall 年降雨量\nHeavy rainfall caused landslides in the mountain areas.\n(大量降雨造成山區土石流。)\nTaiwan has a high annual rainfall compared with many countries.\n(和許多國家相比，台灣的年降雨量很高。)"],["raisin","raisin(n.)葡萄乾\n(無詞性變化)\nraisin bread 葡萄乾麵包\na handful of raisins 一把葡萄乾\nMy mother adds raisins to the cookies she bakes.\n(我媽媽在她烤的餅乾裡加了葡萄乾。)\nRaisin bread is one of my favorite breakfasts.\n(葡萄乾麵包是我最喜歡的早餐之一。)"],["realistic","realistic(adj.)實際的、務實的、逼真的\nrealism(n.)現實主義、寫實\nrealistically(adv.)實際地\nrealistic goal 實際的目標\nrealistic picture 寫實的描繪\nIt's important to set realistic goals for your studies.\n(為課業設定實際可行的目標很重要。)\nThe special effects in the movie look very realistic.\n(這部電影的特效看起來非常逼真。)"],["rebel","rebel(n./v.)叛亂者、反抗者、反叛\nrebellion(n.)叛亂、反抗\nrebellious(adj.)叛逆的\nrebel against 反抗\nrebel army 叛軍\nMany teenagers rebel against their parents' rules.\n(許多青少年反抗父母的規定。)\nThe rebels took control of the capital city.\n(叛軍控制了首都。)"],["recall","recall(v./n.)回想起、召回\n(無詞性變化)\nrecall a name 想起名字\nproduct recall 產品召回\nI can't recall where I put my keys.\n(我想不起來把鑰匙放在哪裡。)\nThe company announced a recall of the faulty cars.\n(那家公司宣布召回有瑕疵的汽車。)"],["reception","reception(n.)接待處、歡迎會、接收(訊號)\nreceptionist(n.)接待員\nreceive(v.)收到、接待\nwedding reception 婚宴\nreception desk 接待櫃台\nPlease leave your key at the reception desk.\n(請把鑰匙留在接待櫃台。)\nThe phone reception is poor in this building.\n(這棟大樓裡的手機收訊很差。)"],["recipe","recipe(n.)食譜、祕訣\n(無詞性變化)\nfollow a recipe 照著食譜做\nrecipe for success 成功的祕訣\nI followed my grandmother's recipe to make beef noodles.\n(我照著奶奶的食譜做牛肉麵。)\nHard work is the recipe for success.\n(努力是成功的祕訣。)"],["recognition","recognition(n.)認出、承認、表揚\nrecognize(v.)認出、承認\nface recognition 臉部辨識\nin recognition of 為表揚……\nMy phone uses face recognition to unlock.\n(我的手機用臉部辨識解鎖。)\nShe received an award in recognition of her volunteer work.\n(她獲頒獎項以表揚她的志工服務。)"],["recovery","recovery(n.)恢復、康復、復甦\nrecover(v.)恢復、康復\nmake a full recovery 完全康復\neconomic recovery 經濟復甦\nThe player made a full recovery after the knee surgery.\n(那位選手膝蓋手術後完全康復。)\nThe government hopes for a quick economic recovery.\n(政府希望經濟能迅速復甦。)"],["recreation","recreation(n.)娛樂、消遣\nrecreational(adj.)娛樂的、休閒的\nrecreation center 休閒中心\noutdoor recreation 戶外休閒活動\nThe park offers many kinds of outdoor recreation.\n(這座公園提供多種戶外休閒活動。)\nReading is my favorite form of recreation.\n(閱讀是我最喜歡的消遣。)"],["recycle","recycle(v.)回收、再利用\nrecycling(n.)回收\nrecyclable(adj.)可回收的\nrecycle plastic 回收塑膠\nrecycling bin 回收桶\nWe should recycle plastic bottles to protect the environment.\n(我們應該回收塑膠瓶來保護環境。)\nTaiwan is well known for its high recycling rate.\n(台灣以高回收率聞名。)"],["reduction","reduction(n.)減少、降低、折扣\nreduce(v.)減少、降低\nprice reduction 降價\nreduction in ……的減少\nThe store is offering a big price reduction this week.\n(這家店本週大降價。)\nThere has been a reduction in traffic accidents this year.\n(今年交通事故減少了。)"],["refer","refer(v.)提到、參考、轉介\nreference(n.)參考、提及\nreferee(n.)裁判\nrefer to 提到、參考、指的是\nrefer A to B 將A轉介給B\nThe word 'it' here refers to the old house.\n(這裡的「it」指的是那棟老房子。)\nYou may refer to your notes during the test.\n(考試時你可以參考筆記。)"],["reference","reference(n.)參考、參考資料、提及、推薦信\nrefer(v.)提到、參考\nreference book 參考書\nwith reference to 關於\nI borrowed some reference books from the library.\n(我從圖書館借了一些參考書。)\nMy teacher wrote a letter of reference for my college application.\n(我的老師為我的大學申請寫了一封推薦信。)"],["reflect","reflect(v.)反射、反映、反思\nreflection(n.)反射、倒影、反思\nreflective(adj.)反射的、沉思的\nreflect on 反思\nreflect light 反射光線\nThe calm lake reflected the mountains like a mirror.\n(平靜的湖面像鏡子一樣映出群山。)\nTake some time to reflect on what you have learned.\n(花些時間反思你學到了什麼。)"],["reflection","reflection(n.)倒影、反射、反思\nreflect(v.)反射、反映、反思\nreflection in the mirror 鏡中的倒影\non reflection 經過仔細考慮\nThe cat stared at its reflection in the mirror.\n(那隻貓盯著鏡中自己的倒影。)\nOn reflection, I think I made the wrong choice.\n(仔細想想，我覺得自己做錯了選擇。)"],["reform","reform(n./v.)改革、改進\nreformer(n.)改革者\neducation reform 教育改革\npolitical reform 政治改革\nThe new education reform has changed how students learn.\n(新的教育改革改變了學生學習的方式。)\nThe government promised to reform the tax system.\n(政府承諾改革稅制。)"],["refugee","refugee(n.)難民\nrefuge(n.)避難、避難所\nrefugee camp 難民營\nwar refugee 戰爭難民\nThousands of refugees fled the war to neighboring countries.\n(數千名難民逃離戰爭到鄰近國家。)\nVolunteers delivered food to the refugee camp.\n(志工把食物送到難民營。)"],["refund","refund(n./v.)退款、退還\nrefundable(adj.)可退款的\nfull refund 全額退款\nask for a refund 要求退款\nIf you are not satisfied, you can get a full refund.\n(如果你不滿意，可以獲得全額退款。)\nThe airline refunded our tickets because of the typhoon.\n(航空公司因颱風退還了我們的機票錢。)"],["refusal","refusal(n.)拒絕\nrefuse(v.)拒絕\nflat refusal 斷然拒絕\nrefusal to 拒絕做……\nHis refusal to help surprised everyone.\n(他拒絕幫忙讓大家很驚訝。)\nShe answered with a flat refusal.\n(她斷然拒絕了。)"],["regarding","regarding(prep.)關於、有關\nregard(v./n.)認為、尊重\nregardless(adv.)不管、無論\nregarding the matter 關於此事\nquestions regarding 有關……的問題\nIf you have any questions regarding the trip, please ask me.\n(如果你對這趟旅程有任何問題，請問我。)\nThe school sent a notice regarding the new dress code.\n(學校發出了一份關於新服裝規定的通知。)"],["register","register(v./n.)登記、註冊、名冊\nregistration(n.)登記、註冊\nregistered(adj.)已註冊的、掛號的\nregister for 報名\nregistered mail 掛號信\nYou need to register for the course before Friday.\n(你需要在星期五之前報名這門課。)\nI sent the important documents by registered mail.\n(我用掛號信寄出重要文件。)"],["registration","registration(n.)登記、註冊、報名\nregister(v./n.)登記、註冊\nregistration fee 報名費\nonline registration 線上報名\nOnline registration for the marathon starts next Monday.\n(馬拉松線上報名下週一開始。)\nThe registration fee includes a T-shirt and a medal.\n(報名費包含一件T恤和一面獎牌。)"],["regulate","regulate(v.)管理、調節、控制\nregulation(n.)規定、管制\nregulator(n.)管理者、調節器\nregulate temperature 調節溫度\nstrictly regulate 嚴格管制\nSweating helps the body regulate its temperature.\n(流汗幫助身體調節體溫。)\nThe government strictly regulates the sale of medicine.\n(政府嚴格管制藥品的販售。)"],["regulation","regulation(n.)規定、法規、管制\nregulate(v.)管理、調節\nsafety regulations 安全規定\nfollow regulations 遵守規定\nAll workers must follow the safety regulations.\n(所有工人都必須遵守安全規定。)\nNew regulations on plastic bags will take effect next year.\n(關於塑膠袋的新規定明年起生效。)"],["rejection","rejection(n.)拒絕、駁回\nreject(v.)拒絕、駁回\nfear of rejection 害怕被拒絕\nrejection letter 拒絕信\nHe was afraid of rejection, so he never asked her out.\n(他害怕被拒絕，所以從未約她出去。)\nShe received a rejection letter from the university.\n(她收到那所大學的拒絕信。)"],["relaxation","relaxation(n.)放鬆、休閒\nrelax(v.)放鬆\nrelaxed(adj.)放鬆的\nrelaxation techniques 放鬆技巧\nfor relaxation 為了放鬆\nI listen to music for relaxation after school.\n(放學後我聽音樂來放鬆。)\nDeep breathing is one of the easiest relaxation techniques.\n(深呼吸是最簡單的放鬆技巧之一。)"],["relevant","relevant(adj.)相關的、切題的\nrelevance(n.)關聯、相關性\nirrelevant(adj.)無關的\nrelevant information 相關資訊\nbe relevant to 與……有關\nPlease include only relevant information in your report.\n(你的報告裡請只放相關的資訊。)\nHis question is not relevant to today's topic.\n(他的問題與今天的主題無關。)"],["relieve","relieve(v.)減輕、緩和、使放心\nrelief(n.)放心、緩解\nrelieved(adj.)放心的\nrelieve stress 紓解壓力\nrelieve pain 減輕疼痛\nExercise is a good way to relieve stress.\n(運動是紓解壓力的好方法。)\nI was relieved to hear that you passed the exam.\n(聽到你通過考試，我鬆了一口氣。)"],["reluctant","reluctant(adj.)不情願的、勉強的\nreluctance(n.)不情願\nreluctantly(adv.)不情願地\nbe reluctant to 不情願做……\nreluctant agreement 勉強同意\nHe was reluctant to tell his parents about the bad grade.\n(他不願意把成績不好的事告訴父母。)\nShe reluctantly agreed to lend me her notes.\n(她勉強答應借我她的筆記。)"],["remark","remark(n./v.)評論、言論、談到\nremarkable(adj.)非凡的、值得注意的\nmake a remark 發表評論\nrude remark 無禮的言論\nHe made a rude remark about her new hairstyle.\n(他對她的新髮型說了很無禮的話。)\nMany visitors remarked on how clean the city was.\n(許多遊客都談到這座城市有多乾淨。)"],["remarkable","remarkable(adj.)非凡的、值得注意的、卓越的\nremarkably(adv.)非常地、顯著地\nremark(n./v.)評論、談到\nremarkable achievement 卓越的成就\nremarkable progress 顯著的進步\nWinning three gold medals is a remarkable achievement.\n(贏得三面金牌是一項卓越的成就。)\nHe has made remarkable progress in math this semester.\n(他這學期數學有顯著的進步。)"],["remedy","remedy(n./v.)治療法、補救辦法、補救\n(無詞性變化)\nhome remedy 偏方、居家療法\nremedy the situation 補救情況\nHot ginger tea is a popular home remedy for colds.\n(熱薑茶是治療感冒的常見偏方。)\nThe school took steps to remedy the problem.\n(學校採取措施來補救這個問題。)"],["renew","renew(v.)更新、續借、使恢復\nrenewal(n.)更新、續約\nrenewable(adj.)可再生的\nrenew a passport 換發護照\nrenew a contract 續約\nI need to renew my library books before Friday.\n(我需要在星期五前續借圖書館的書。)\nSolar power is a kind of renewable energy.\n(太陽能是一種再生能源。)"],["repetition","repetition(n.)重複、反覆\nrepeat(v.)重複\nrepetitive(adj.)重複的、單調的\nthrough repetition 透過反覆練習\navoid repetition 避免重複\nLearning new words takes a lot of repetition.\n(學習新單字需要大量的反覆練習。)\nTry to avoid repetition of the same words in your essay.\n(你的作文裡試著避免重複使用相同的字。)"],["representation","representation(n.)代表、表現、描繪\nrepresent(v.)代表、象徵\nrepresentative(n./adj.)代表、具代表性的\naccurate representation 準確的描繪\npolitical representation 政治代表權\nThe painting is a representation of life in old Taipei.\n(這幅畫描繪了舊時台北的生活。)\nWomen want more representation in government.\n(女性希望在政府中有更多代表。)"],["reputation","reputation(n.)名聲、聲譽\nreputable(adj.)聲譽好的\ngood reputation 好名聲\nhave a reputation for 以……聞名\nThe restaurant has a good reputation for its fresh seafood.\n(這家餐廳以新鮮海鮮享有好名聲。)\nOne mistake can damage a company's reputation.\n(一個錯誤就可能損害公司的聲譽。)"],["rescue","rescue(n./v.)救援、營救\nrescuer(n.)救援者\nrescue team 救援隊\ncome to the rescue 前來救援\nThe rescue team searched for the missing climbers all night.\n(救難隊整晚搜尋失蹤的登山客。)\nFirefighters rescued a cat from the burning house.\n(消防員從失火的房子裡救出一隻貓。)"],["research","research(n./v.)研究、調查\nresearcher(n.)研究人員\ndo research on 研究……\nresearch project 研究計畫\nScientists are doing research on new kinds of energy.\n(科學家正在研究新型態的能源。)\nWe researched the history of our town for the project.\n(我們為了專題研究了我們城鎮的歷史。)"],["researcher","researcher(n.)研究人員\nresearch(n./v.)研究\nmedical researcher 醫學研究人員\nteam of researchers 研究團隊\nA team of researchers discovered a new kind of frog.\n(一個研究團隊發現了一種新的青蛙。)\nMy aunt works as a medical researcher at a hospital.\n(我阿姨在一家醫院擔任醫學研究人員。)"],["resemble","resemble(v.)像、與……相似\nresemblance(n.)相似\nclosely resemble 非常相似\nresemble each other 彼此相似\nThe little girl closely resembles her mother.\n(那個小女孩長得非常像她的媽媽。)\nThe rock resembles an elephant's head.\n(那塊岩石像大象的頭。)"],["reservation","reservation(n.)預訂、保留、疑慮\nreserve(v./n.)預訂、保留\nmake a reservation 預訂\nwithout reservation 毫無保留地\nI made a reservation for dinner at seven.\n(我預訂了七點的晚餐。)\nShe supported the plan without reservation.\n(她毫無保留地支持這項計畫。)"],["resign","resign(v.)辭職、放棄\nresignation(n.)辭職、辭呈\nresigned(adj.)聽天由命的、順從的\nresign from 辭去\nresign oneself to 只好接受\nThe manager resigned from his job last month.\n(那位經理上個月辭職了。)\nHe resigned himself to staying home during the typhoon.\n(颱風期間他只好接受待在家裡。)"],["resignation","resignation(n.)辭職、辭呈、聽天由命\nresign(v.)辭職\nhand in one's resignation 遞辭呈\nletter of resignation 辭職信\nShe handed in her resignation to the boss this morning.\n(她今天早上向老闆遞出辭呈。)\nHe accepted the bad news with quiet resignation.\n(他默默地接受了這個壞消息。)"],["resistance","resistance(n.)抵抗、反抗、抵抗力\nresist(v.)抵抗\nresistant(adj.)有抵抗力的\nresistance to 對……的抵抗\nmeet with resistance 遭到反對\nThe new rule met with strong resistance from students.\n(新規定遭到學生強烈的反對。)\nRegular exercise can improve your resistance to illness.\n(規律運動能提升你對疾病的抵抗力。)"],["resolution","resolution(n.)決心、決議、解決、解析度\nresolve(v./n.)解決、決心\nNew Year's resolution 新年新希望\nhigh resolution 高解析度\nMy New Year's resolution is to exercise every day.\n(我的新年新希望是每天運動。)\nThis camera takes high resolution photos.\n(這台相機能拍出高解析度的照片。)"],["resolve","resolve(v./n.)解決、決心、決定\nresolution(n.)決心、解決\nresolve a problem 解決問題\nresolve a conflict 化解衝突\nThe two sides met to resolve the conflict.\n(雙方會面以化解衝突。)\nShe resolved to study harder after the failure.\n(失敗後她下定決心更用功讀書。)"],["respectable","respectable(adj.)值得尊敬的、體面的、可觀的\nrespect(n./v.)尊敬\nrespectable job 體面的工作\nrespectable score 可觀的分數\nHis parents want him to find a respectable job.\n(他父母希望他找份體面的工作。)\nOur team finished the race with a respectable time.\n(我們的隊伍以不錯的成績完成比賽。)"],["respectful","respectful(adj.)尊敬的、有禮貌的\nrespect(n./v.)尊敬\nrespectfully(adv.)尊敬地\nbe respectful to 對……有禮貌\nrespectful silence 肅靜以表敬意\nStudents should be respectful to their teachers.\n(學生應該尊敬老師。)\nThe crowd stood in respectful silence for one minute.\n(群眾肅立默哀一分鐘。)"],["restore","restore(v.)恢復、修復、歸還\nrestoration(n.)恢復、修復\nrestore order 恢復秩序\nrestore power 恢復供電\nWorkers restored the old temple to its original beauty.\n(工人將老廟宇修復成原本的美麗樣貌。)\nPower was restored a few hours after the typhoon.\n(颱風過後幾小時就恢復供電了。)"],["restriction","restriction(n.)限制、約束\nrestrict(v.)限制\nrestrictive(adj.)限制性的\nage restriction 年齡限制\nimpose restrictions on 對……加以限制\nThere is an age restriction for this movie.\n(這部電影有年齡限制。)\nThe city imposed restrictions on water use during the drought.\n(乾旱期間市政府對用水加以限制。)"],["retain","retain(v.)保持、保留、記住\nretention(n.)保留、記憶力\nretain heat 保溫\nretain information 記住資訊\nThis bottle can retain heat for twelve hours.\n(這個瓶子可以保溫十二小時。)\nTaking notes helps you retain information better.\n(做筆記幫助你更好地記住資訊。)"],["retire(ment)","retire(v.)退休、retirement(n.)退休\nretired(adj.)退休的\nretire from 從……退休\nearly retirement 提早退休\nMy grandfather retired from teaching at the age of 65.\n(我爺爺六十五歲時從教職退休。)\nShe plans to travel around the world after her retirement.\n(她打算退休後環遊世界。)"],["retreat","retreat(n./v.)撤退、退縮、靜修處\n(無詞性變化)\nbeat a retreat 匆忙撤退\nmountain retreat 山中隱居處\nThe army was forced to retreat after the battle.\n(戰役後軍隊被迫撤退。)\nThey spent the weekend at a quiet mountain retreat.\n(他們在寧靜的山中小屋度過週末。)"],["reunion","reunion(n.)團聚、重聚、同學會\nreunite(v.)重聚、再結合\nfamily reunion 家庭團聚\nclass reunion 同學會\nLunar New Year is a time for family reunion.\n(農曆新年是家人團聚的時刻。)\nWe had a class reunion ten years after graduation.\n(我們在畢業十年後舉辦了同學會。)"],["revenge","revenge(n./v.)報仇、復仇\n(無詞性變化)\ntake revenge on 向……報仇\nget revenge 報仇\nThe movie is about a man who takes revenge on his enemies.\n(這部電影講述一名男子向仇人報仇的故事。)\nOur team got revenge by winning this year's final.\n(我們隊贏得今年的決賽，報了一箭之仇。)"],["revise","revise(v.)修改、修訂、複習\nrevision(n.)修訂、複習\nrevise an essay 修改作文\nrevised edition 修訂版\nPlease revise your essay and hand it in again.\n(請修改你的作文再交一次。)\nThe revised edition of the dictionary includes many new words.\n(這本字典的修訂版收錄了許多新字。)"],["revision","revision(n.)修訂、修改、複習\nrevise(v.)修改、修訂\nmake revisions 做修改\nrevision of ……的修訂\nThe writer made several revisions before finishing the book.\n(作者在完成這本書之前做了好幾次修改。)\nThe revision of the law took two years.\n(這項法律的修訂花了兩年。)"],["revolution","revolution(n.)革命、重大變革、旋轉\nrevolutionary(adj./n.)革命的、革命者\nrevolve(v.)旋轉\nIndustrial Revolution 工業革命\ndigital revolution 數位革命\nThe Industrial Revolution changed the way people worked.\n(工業革命改變了人們工作的方式。)\nSmartphones have brought a revolution in communication.\n(智慧型手機帶來了通訊的革命。)"],["revolutionary","revolutionary(adj./n.)革命性的、革命的、革命者\nrevolution(n.)革命\nrevolutionary idea 革命性的想法\nrevolutionary change 革命性的改變\nThe invention of the Internet was a revolutionary change.\n(網際網路的發明是一項革命性的改變。)\nSun Yat-sen was a famous revolutionary.\n(孫中山是一位著名的革命家。)"],["reward","reward(n./v.)報酬、獎賞、獎勵\nrewarding(adj.)值得的、有益的\nreward for 對……的獎賞\nbe rewarded with 獲得……獎勵\nThe police offered a reward for information about the thief.\n(警方懸賞有關小偷的線索。)\nVolunteering at the hospital was a rewarding experience.\n(在醫院擔任志工是一次很有意義的經驗。)"],["rhyme","rhyme(n./v.)押韻、韻腳、押韻的詩\n(無詞性變化)\nnursery rhyme 童謠\nrhyme with 與……押韻\n'Cat' rhymes with 'hat'.\n('Cat' 和 'hat' 押韻。)\nChildren love singing nursery rhymes.\n(孩子們喜歡唱童謠。)"],["rhythm","rhythm(n.)節奏、韻律\nrhythmic(adj.)有節奏的\nsense of rhythm 節奏感\nrhythm of life 生活節奏\nShe has a good sense of rhythm, so she dances well.\n(她節奏感很好，所以舞跳得很棒。)\nLife in the countryside has a slower rhythm.\n(鄉下的生活節奏比較慢。)"],["riddle","riddle(n.)謎語、謎\n(無詞性變化)\nsolve a riddle 解謎語\nspeak in riddles 說話拐彎抹角\nCan you solve this riddle about animals?\n(你能解開這個關於動物的謎語嗎？)\nGuessing lantern riddles is a tradition of the Lantern Festival.\n(猜燈謎是元宵節的傳統。)"],["robber","robber(n.)強盜、搶匪\nrob(v.)搶劫\nrobbery(n.)搶劫\nbank robber 銀行搶匪\narmed robber 持械搶匪\nThe bank robber was caught by the police within an hour.\n(銀行搶匪在一小時內被警方抓到。)\nThe robbers ran away with a bag of cash.\n(搶匪帶著一袋現金逃走了。)"],["romance","romance(n.)戀情、浪漫、愛情小說\nromantic(adj.)浪漫的\nsummer romance 夏日戀情\nromance novel 愛情小說\nMy sister enjoys reading romance novels.\n(我姊姊喜歡看愛情小說。)\nTheir romance began when they met on a trip to Japan.\n(他們的戀情始於一趟日本旅行中的相遇。)"],["route","route(n./v.)路線、途徑、規劃路線\n(無詞性變化)\nbus route 公車路線\nthe best route 最佳路線\nThis bus route goes past the train station.\n(這條公車路線會經過火車站。)\nThe map app showed us the best route to the beach.\n(地圖應用程式顯示了去海邊的最佳路線。)"],["ruin","ruin(v./n.)毀壞、破壞、廢墟\n(無詞性變化)\nin ruins 成為廢墟\nruin one's day 毀了某人的一天\nThe rain ruined our plans for the picnic.\n(這場雨毀了我們的野餐計畫。)\nAfter the earthquake, the old town was in ruins.\n(地震過後，那座古鎮成了廢墟。)"],["rural","rural(adj.)鄉村的、農村的\n(無詞性變化)\nrural area 鄉村地區\nrural life 鄉村生活\nMany young people leave rural areas to find jobs in cities.\n(許多年輕人離開鄉村到城市找工作。)\nShe enjoys the quiet rural life in Hualien.\n(她喜歡花蓮寧靜的鄉村生活。)"],["rusty","rusty(adj.)生鏽的、生疏的\nrust(n./v.)鐵鏽、生鏽\nrusty nail 生鏽的鐵釘\nrusty English 生疏的英文\nBe careful not to step on that rusty nail.\n(小心不要踩到那根生鏽的鐵釘。)\nMy French is a little rusty because I haven't used it for years.\n(我的法文有點生疏了，因為好幾年沒用。)"],["sacrifice","sacrifice(n./v.)犧牲、祭品、獻祭\n(無詞性變化)\nmake sacrifices 做出犧牲\nsacrifice A for B 為了B犧牲A\nMy parents made many sacrifices for our education.\n(我爸媽為了我們的教育做了許多犧牲。)\nHe sacrificed his free time to help his classmates.\n(他犧牲自己的空閒時間來幫助同學。)"],["satellite","satellite(n.)衛星、人造衛星\n(無詞性變化)\nsatellite TV 衛星電視\nlaunch a satellite 發射衛星\nTaiwan successfully launched a weather satellite into space.\n(台灣成功發射了一枚氣象衛星進入太空。)\nThe moon is the earth's only natural satellite.\n(月球是地球唯一的天然衛星。)"],["satisfaction","satisfaction(n.)滿意、滿足\nsatisfy(v.)使滿意\nsatisfactory(adj.)令人滿意的\ncustomer satisfaction 顧客滿意度\njob satisfaction 工作滿意度\nShe felt great satisfaction after finishing the marathon.\n(跑完馬拉松後她感到非常滿足。)\nThe company cares a lot about customer satisfaction.\n(這家公司非常重視顧客滿意度。)"],["scarcely","scarcely(adv.)幾乎不、僅僅\nscarce(adj.)稀少的、缺乏的\nscarcely ever 幾乎從不\nscarcely... when 一…就\nI could scarcely believe my eyes when I saw the result.\n(看到結果時，我簡直不敢相信自己的眼睛。)\nWe had scarcely arrived when it started to rain.\n(我們一到達就開始下雨了。)"],["scenery","scenery(n.)風景、景色\nscene(n.)場景、景象\nscenic(adj.)風景優美的\nbeautiful scenery 美麗的風景\nenjoy the scenery 欣賞風景\nTaroko is famous for its beautiful mountain scenery.\n(太魯閣以美麗的山景聞名。)\nWe stopped the car to enjoy the scenery.\n(我們停車欣賞風景。)"],["scold","scold(v./n.)責罵、斥責\nscolding(n.)責罵\nscold sb. for sth. 因某事責罵某人\nget a scolding 挨罵\nMy mom scolded me for coming home late.\n(我媽媽因為我晚回家而罵我。)\nHe got a scolding from the teacher for sleeping in class.\n(他因為上課睡覺被老師罵了一頓。)"],["scoop","scoop(n./v.)勺子、一勺、獨家新聞、舀\n(無詞性變化)\na scoop of ice cream 一球冰淇淋\nscoop up 舀起、撈起\nI'd like two scoops of chocolate ice cream, please.\n(請給我兩球巧克力冰淇淋。)\nThe child scooped up some sand with his hands.\n(那孩子用雙手捧起了一些沙子。)"],["scratch","scratch(n./v.)抓痕、擦傷、抓、搔\n(無詞性變化)\nfrom scratch 從頭開始\nscratch one's head 搔頭、困惑\nThe cat scratched my arm when I picked it up.\n(我抱起貓的時候，牠抓了我的手臂。)\nWe built the website from scratch.\n(我們從零開始建立了這個網站。)"],["sculpture","sculpture(n./v.)雕刻、雕塑品、雕塑\nsculptor(n.)雕刻家\nstone sculpture 石雕\nbronze sculpture 銅雕\nThe park is full of stone sculptures by local artists.\n(公園裡到處都是當地藝術家的石雕作品。)\nShe studied sculpture at an art school in Italy.\n(她在義大利的一所藝術學校學雕塑。)"],["secure","secure(v./adj.)獲得、確保、安全的、穩固的\nsecurity(n.)安全、保全\nfeel secure 感到安心\nsecure a job 取得一份工作\nChildren need to feel safe and secure at home.\n(孩子們在家需要感到安全和安心。)\nShe worked hard and finally secured a job at a big company.\n(她努力工作，終於在一家大公司謀得職位。)"],["seize","seize(v.)抓住、奪取、沒收\nseizure(n.)奪取、沒收\nseize the chance 抓住機會\nseize power 奪取政權\nYou should seize the chance to study abroad.\n(你應該抓住出國念書的機會。)\nThe police seized a large amount of drugs.\n(警方查獲了大量毒品。)"],["settler","settler(n.)移居者、殖民者、開拓者\nsettle(v.)定居、解決\nsettlement(n.)定居地、解決\nearly settlers 早期移民\nEuropean settlers 歐洲移民\nEarly settlers built their homes near the river.\n(早期的移民在河邊建造家園。)\nThe settlers had to survive the cold winter.\n(那些開拓者必須熬過寒冷的冬天。)"],["severe","severe(adj.)嚴重的、嚴厲的、劇烈的\nseverely(adv.)嚴重地\nseverity(n.)嚴重性\nsevere weather 惡劣的天氣\nsevere pain 劇烈疼痛\nThe town was hit by a severe storm last night.\n(小鎮昨晚遭到強烈暴風雨侵襲。)\nHe felt a severe pain in his back.\n(他感到背部一陣劇痛。)"],["sew","sew(v.)縫、縫製\nsewing(n.)縫紉\nsew on 縫上\nsewing machine 縫紉機\nMy grandma sewed a button on my shirt.\n(我奶奶幫我把鈕扣縫回襯衫上。)\nShe learned to sew her own clothes.\n(她學會自己縫製衣服。)"],["shade","shade(n./v.)陰涼處、遮蔽、色調、遮陽\nshady(adj.)陰涼的\nin the shade 在陰涼處\nshades of 各種色調的\nLet's sit in the shade of that big tree.\n(我們去那棵大樹的樹蔭下坐吧。)\nShe shaded her eyes from the bright sun.\n(她遮住眼睛擋住刺眼的陽光。)"],["shady","shady(adj.)陰涼的、成蔭的、可疑的\nshade(n.)陰涼處\na shady spot 陰涼的地方\nshady business 可疑的生意\nWe found a shady spot under the trees for our picnic.\n(我們在樹下找到一個陰涼的地方野餐。)\nDon't get involved in his shady business.\n(別捲入他那可疑的生意。)"],["shameful","shameful(adj.)可恥的、丟臉的\nshame(n.)羞恥\nashamed(adj.)感到羞愧的\nshameful behavior 可恥的行為\na shameful secret 不可告人的祕密\nCheating on the test was a shameful thing to do.\n(考試作弊是件可恥的事。)\nIt is shameful to make fun of people in need.\n(嘲笑有困難的人是很可恥的。)"],["shave","shave(v./n.)刮(鬍子)、剃\nshaver(n.)電動刮鬍刀\nshave off 剃掉\na close shave 千鈞一髮\nMy father shaves every morning before work.\n(我爸爸每天早上上班前都會刮鬍子。)\nThat was a close shave; the car almost hit us.\n(真是千鈞一髮，那輛車差點撞到我們。)"],["shelter","shelter(n./v.)庇護所、避難處、遮蔽\n(無詞性變化)\nanimal shelter 動物收容所\ntake shelter 避難、躲避\nWe adopted our dog from an animal shelter.\n(我們從動物收容所領養了我們的狗。)\nPeople took shelter in the school during the flood.\n(水災期間人們在學校避難。)"],["shift","shift(n./v.)輪班、轉變、移動、轉移\n(無詞性變化)\nnight shift 夜班\nshift attention 轉移注意力\nMy mother works the night shift at the hospital.\n(我媽媽在醫院上夜班。)\nThere has been a shift in people's attitudes toward pets.\n(人們對寵物的態度已經有所轉變。)"],["sightseeing","sightseeing(n.)觀光、遊覽\nsightseer(n.)觀光客\ngo sightseeing 去觀光\nsightseeing tour 觀光行程\nWe went sightseeing in Tainan last weekend.\n(我們上週末去台南觀光。)\nThe hotel offers a sightseeing tour of the city.\n(飯店提供市區觀光行程。)"],["signature","signature(n./adj.)簽名、招牌的、特色的\nsign(v.)簽名\nsignature dish 招牌菜\ncollect signatures 收集簽名、連署\nThis beef noodle soup is the restaurant's signature dish.\n(這碗牛肉麵是這家餐廳的招牌菜。)\nPlease put your signature at the bottom of the form.\n(請在表格底部簽名。)"],["significance","significance(n.)重要性、意義\nsignificant(adj.)重要的、顯著的\nof great significance 非常重要的\nhistorical significance 歷史意義\nThe temple has great historical significance.\n(這座廟有重大的歷史意義。)\nFew people understood the significance of his discovery.\n(很少人理解他這項發現的重要性。)"],["sincerity","sincerity(n.)真誠、誠意\nsincere(adj.)真誠的\nsincerely(adv.)真誠地\nin all sincerity 非常真誠地\nshow sincerity 表現誠意\nI could feel the sincerity in his apology.\n(我能感受到他道歉中的誠意。)\nShe spoke with great sincerity about her mistakes.\n(她非常真誠地談到自己的錯誤。)"],["singular","singular(adj./n.)單數的、非凡的、單數\nplural(adj./n.)複數的、複數\nsingular form 單數形\nsingular noun 單數名詞\nThe singular form of 'children' is 'child'.\n(children的單數形是child。)\nUse a singular verb after 'everyone'.\n(在everyone後面要用單數動詞。)"],["site","site(n./v.)地點、場所、網站、設置\n(無詞性變化)\nconstruction site 工地\nhistoric site 古蹟\nWorkers must wear helmets at the construction site.\n(工人在工地必須戴安全帽。)\nThis old fort is one of Tainan's famous historic sites.\n(這座古堡是台南著名的古蹟之一。)"],["sketch","sketch(n./v.)素描、草圖、短劇、畫草圖\nsketchy(adj.)粗略的\nmake a sketch 畫素描\nsketch out 概述、草擬\nThe artist made a quick sketch of the old street.\n(這位畫家快速畫了一張老街的素描。)\nLet me sketch out my plan for the trip.\n(讓我大概說明一下我的旅行計畫。)"],["skyscraper","skyscraper(n.)摩天大樓\n(無詞性變化)\ntall skyscraper 高聳的摩天大樓\nbuild a skyscraper 興建摩天大樓\nTaipei 101 was once the tallest skyscraper in the world.\n(台北101曾經是世界上最高的摩天大樓。)\nThe city is full of modern skyscrapers.\n(這座城市到處都是現代化的摩天大樓。)"],["slight","slight(adj./n./v.)輕微的、少量的、輕視\nslightly(adv.)稍微\na slight change 些微的改變\nnot in the slightest 一點也不\nI have a slight headache today.\n(我今天有點頭痛。)\nThere was a slight change in the schedule.\n(行程有些微的變動。)"],["slogan","slogan(n.)標語、口號\n(無詞性變化)\nadvertising slogan 廣告標語\nshout slogans 喊口號\nThe company created a catchy advertising slogan.\n(這家公司想出了一句好記的廣告標語。)\nThe students shouted slogans during the march.\n(學生們在遊行中高喊口號。)"],["socket","socket(n.)插座、(眼)窩、凹槽\n(無詞性變化)\nelectric socket 電源插座\neye socket 眼窩\nDon't put your fingers into the electric socket.\n(不要把手指伸進電源插座裡。)\nPlease plug the charger into the socket.\n(請把充電器插進插座。)"],["software","software(n.)軟體\nhardware(n.)硬體\nsoftware engineer 軟體工程師\ninstall software 安裝軟體\nMy cousin works as a software engineer.\n(我表哥是一名軟體工程師。)\nYou need to install new software on your computer.\n(你需要在電腦上安裝新的軟體。)"],["solar","solar(adj.)太陽的、太陽能的\n(無詞性變化)\nsolar energy 太陽能\nsolar system 太陽系\nMany homes now use solar energy to make electricity.\n(現在許多家庭使用太陽能發電。)\nJupiter is the largest planet in the solar system.\n(木星是太陽系中最大的行星。)"],["spade","spade(n.)鏟子、(撲克牌)黑桃\n(無詞性變化)\ncall a spade a spade 直言不諱\nthe ace of spades 黑桃A\nHe dug a hole in the garden with a spade.\n(他用鏟子在花園裡挖了一個洞。)\nShe always calls a spade a spade.\n(她說話總是直言不諱。)"],["spare","spare(adj./v./n.)空閒的、備用的、撥出、饒恕、備品\n(無詞性變化)\nspare time 空閒時間\nspare tire 備胎\nWhat do you like to do in your spare time?\n(你空閒時喜歡做什麼？)\nCan you spare a few minutes to help me?\n(你能撥出幾分鐘幫我一下嗎？)"],["spark","spark(n./v.)火花、引發、激起\nsparkle(v.)閃耀\nspark interest 激起興趣\na spark of hope 一線希望\nThe teacher's story sparked my interest in history.\n(老師的故事激起了我對歷史的興趣。)\nA small spark can start a big forest fire.\n(一點小火花就能引發一場森林大火。)"],["spear","spear(n./v.)矛、長槍、用矛刺\n(無詞性變化)\nthrow a spear 擲矛\nspear fishing 魚叉捕魚\nAncient hunters used spears to catch animals.\n(古代獵人用矛捕捉動物。)\nThe fisherman speared a fish in the shallow water.\n(漁夫在淺水中用魚叉刺中了一條魚。)"],["species","species(n.)物種、種類(單複數同形)\n(無詞性變化)\nendangered species 瀕臨絕種的物種\nanimal species 動物物種\nThe Formosan black bear is an endangered species.\n(台灣黑熊是瀕臨絕種的物種。)\nScientists discovered a new species of frog in the forest.\n(科學家在森林裡發現了一種新的青蛙物種。)"],["spiritual","spiritual(adj.)精神的、心靈的、宗教的\nspirit(n.)精神、靈魂\nspiritual life 精神生活\nspiritual leader 精神領袖\nReading poems enriches my spiritual life.\n(讀詩豐富了我的精神生活。)\nMany people visit the temple for spiritual comfort.\n(許多人到廟裡尋求心靈的慰藉。)"],["splendid","splendid(adj.)壯麗的、極好的\nsplendor(n.)壯麗、輝煌\na splendid view 壯麗的景色\na splendid idea 絕妙的主意\nWe had a splendid view of the mountains from the hotel.\n(我們從飯店可以看到壯麗的山景。)\nThat's a splendid idea! Let's do it.\n(那真是個絕妙的主意！我們就這麼做吧。)"],["split","split(v./n.)分開、分攤、劈開、分裂\n(無詞性變化)\nsplit the bill 分攤帳單\nsplit up 分手、分開\nLet's split the bill after dinner.\n(晚餐後我們來分攤帳單吧。)\nThe teacher split the class into four groups.\n(老師把全班分成四組。)"],["sprinkle","sprinkle(v./n.)灑、撒、少量\nsprinkler(n.)灑水器\nsprinkle with 撒上…\na sprinkle of 少許…\nSprinkle some sugar on the strawberries.\n(在草莓上撒一些糖。)\nThe gardener sprinkled water on the flowers.\n(園丁在花上灑水。)"],["stab","stab(n./v.)刺、戳、刺傷、嘗試\nstabbing(adj.)刺痛的\nstab sb. in the back 背後捅刀、背叛\nhave a stab at 嘗試\nThe man was stabbed in the arm during the fight.\n(那名男子在打鬥中手臂被刺傷。)\nI've never cooked before, but I'll have a stab at it.\n(我從沒煮過飯，但我會試試看。)"],["statistic(s)","statistic(n.)統計數字\nstatistics(n.)統計資料、統計學\nstatistical(adj.)統計的\nofficial statistics 官方統計資料\naccording to statistics 根據統計\nAccording to statistics, more people are living alone.\n(根據統計，獨居的人越來越多。)\nMy sister majors in statistics at university.\n(我姊姊在大學主修統計學。)"],["status","status(n.)地位、身分、狀態\n(無詞性變化)\nsocial status 社會地位\nstatus symbol 身分地位的象徵\nIn the past, a car was seen as a status symbol.\n(過去汽車被視為身分地位的象徵。)\nYou can check the status of your order online.\n(你可以在網路上查詢訂單的狀態。)"],["stem","stem(n./v.)莖、梗、源自、阻止\n(無詞性變化)\nstem from 起源於、由…造成\nstem cell 幹細胞\nCut the flower stems before putting them in water.\n(把花放進水裡之前先修剪花莖。)\nHis fear of water stems from a childhood accident.\n(他怕水是源自童年的一次意外。)"],["stereo","stereo(n.)立體音響、立體聲\n(無詞性變化)\ncar stereo 汽車音響\nin stereo 以立體聲\nHe turned up the car stereo and sang along.\n(他把車上的音響調大聲，跟著一起唱。)\nThis old song was recorded in stereo.\n(這首老歌是用立體聲錄製的。)"],["stingy","stingy(adj.)小氣的、吝嗇的\n(無詞性變化)\nstingy with 對…小氣\na stingy boss 吝嗇的老闆\nDon't be so stingy; buy your friends a drink.\n(別那麼小氣，請你朋友喝杯飲料吧。)\nOur stingy boss never gives us a bonus.\n(我們那個小氣的老闆從不發獎金給我們。)"],["stocking(s)","stocking(n.)長襪\nstockings(n.)長襪(複數)\nChristmas stocking 聖誕襪\na pair of stockings 一雙長襪\nThe children hung their Christmas stockings by the fireplace.\n(孩子們把聖誕襪掛在壁爐旁。)\nShe wore a pair of black stockings with her dress.\n(她穿洋裝時搭配了一雙黑色長襪。)"],["strengthen","strengthen(v.)加強、增強\nstrength(n.)力量、長處\nstrong(adj.)強壯的\nstrengthen muscles 鍛鍊肌肉\nstrengthen relationships 加強關係\nSwimming can strengthen your muscles.\n(游泳可以強化你的肌肉。)\nThe exchange program strengthened the ties between the two schools.\n(這個交換計畫加強了兩校之間的關係。)"],["stripe","stripe(n.)條紋、線條\nstriped(adj.)有條紋的\nblack and white stripes 黑白條紋\nstars and stripes 星條旗\nZebras have black and white stripes.\n(斑馬身上有黑白相間的條紋。)\nHe wore a shirt with blue stripes.\n(他穿著一件藍色條紋襯衫。)"],["strive","strive(v.)努力、奮鬥\nstrife(n.)衝突\nstrive for 為…而努力\nstrive to do 努力做…\nWe should always strive for excellence.\n(我們應該永遠追求卓越。)\nShe strives to improve her English every day.\n(她每天努力提升自己的英文。)"],["stroke","stroke(n./v.)中風、一擊、筆畫、撫摸\n(無詞性變化)\na stroke of luck 一次好運\nhave a stroke 中風\nBy a stroke of luck, we caught the last train.\n(運氣很好，我們趕上了末班火車。)\nShe gently stroked the cat's back.\n(她輕輕撫摸那隻貓的背。)"],["submarine","submarine(n./adj.)潛水艇、海底的\n(無詞性變化)\nnuclear submarine 核子潛艇\nsubmarine cable 海底電纜\nThe submarine can stay underwater for months.\n(這艘潛水艇可以在水下停留好幾個月。)\nA submarine cable carries internet data between countries.\n(海底電纜在國家之間傳輸網路資料。)"],["sue","sue(v.)控告、提告\n(無詞性變化)\nsue sb. for sth. 因某事控告某人\nsue for damages 要求損害賠償\nThe singer sued the magazine for printing lies.\n(那位歌手控告雜誌刊登不實內容。)\nHe threatened to sue the company for damages.\n(他揚言要控告那家公司要求賠償。)"],["suggestion","suggestion(n.)建議、暗示\nsuggest(v.)建議\nmake a suggestion 提出建議\nat one's suggestion 依照某人的建議\nCan I make a suggestion about the class trip?\n(我可以對班遊提出一個建議嗎？)\nAt my teacher's suggestion, I joined the debate team.\n(依照老師的建議，我參加了辯論社。)"],["summarize","summarize(v.)總結、摘要\nsummary(n.)摘要\nsummarize the main points 歸納重點\nto summarize 總而言之\nPlease summarize the story in three sentences.\n(請用三句話總結這個故事。)\nThe teacher summarized the main points at the end of class.\n(老師在下課前歸納了重點。)"],["surgeon","surgeon(n.)外科醫生\nsurgery(n.)手術、外科\nplastic surgeon 整形外科醫生\nheart surgeon 心臟外科醫生\nMy uncle is a heart surgeon at a big hospital.\n(我舅舅是一家大醫院的心臟外科醫生。)\nThe surgeon spent five hours on the operation.\n(外科醫生花了五個小時進行這場手術。)"],["surgery","surgery(n.)手術、外科\nsurgeon(n.)外科醫生\nsurgical(adj.)外科的\nhave surgery 動手術\nplastic surgery 整形手術\nMy grandpa had surgery on his knee last month.\n(我爺爺上個月膝蓋動了手術。)\nShe is recovering well after the surgery.\n(她手術後恢復得很好。)"],["surrender","surrender(v./n.)投降、放棄、交出\n(無詞性變化)\nsurrender to 向…投降\nsurrender a weapon 交出武器\nThe enemy soldiers finally surrendered.\n(敵軍士兵最後投降了。)\nThe man was told to surrender his weapon to the police.\n(那名男子被要求向警方交出武器。)"],["surroundings","surroundings(n.)環境、周遭事物\nsurround(v.)圍繞\nsurrounding(adj.)周圍的\nnatural surroundings 自然環境\nget used to the new surroundings 習慣新環境\nIt took me a week to get used to my new surroundings.\n(我花了一週才習慣新環境。)\nThe hotel is in beautiful natural surroundings.\n(這間飯店位在美麗的自然環境中。)"],["suspicious","suspicious(adj.)可疑的、懷疑的\nsuspect(v./n.)懷疑、嫌犯\nsuspicion(n.)懷疑\nbe suspicious of 懷疑…\nsuspicious package 可疑包裹\nPlease report any suspicious package to the police.\n(如有任何可疑包裹請向警方報案。)\nMy mom was suspicious of the stranger's story.\n(我媽媽對那個陌生人的說法起了疑心。)"],["sway","sway(n./v.)搖擺、影響、支配\n(無詞性變化)\nsway in the wind 隨風搖曳\nbe swayed by 受…左右\nThe palm trees swayed gently in the wind.\n(椰子樹在風中輕輕搖曳。)\nDon't be swayed by other people's opinions.\n(別被別人的意見左右。)"],["syllable","syllable(n.)音節\n(無詞性變化)\nstressed syllable 重音節\nthe first syllable 第一個音節\nThe word 'banana' has three syllables.\n(banana這個字有三個音節。)\nPut the stress on the second syllable.\n(把重音放在第二個音節。)"],["sympathetic","sympathetic(adj.)同情的、有同理心的、贊同的\nsympathy(n.)同情\nsympathize(v.)同情\nbe sympathetic to/toward 對…表示同情\na sympathetic ear 願意傾聽的人\nMy friend is always sympathetic when I have problems.\n(每當我遇到問題，我朋友總是很體諒我。)\nThe teacher was sympathetic toward the sick student.\n(老師很同情那位生病的學生。)"],["sympathy","sympathy(n.)同情、慰問、贊同\nsympathetic(adj.)同情的\nsympathize(v.)同情\nfeel sympathy for 同情…\nexpress sympathy 表達慰問\nI feel deep sympathy for the families of the victims.\n(我對罹難者家屬深表同情。)\nWe sent a card to express our sympathy.\n(我們寄了一張卡片表達慰問。)"],["systematic","systematic(adj.)有系統的、有條理的\nsystem(n.)系統\nsystematically(adv.)有系統地\na systematic approach 有系統的方法\nsystematic study 有系統的研究\nYou need a systematic approach to learning vocabulary.\n(你需要一套有系統的方法來學單字。)\nThe police made a systematic search of the house.\n(警方對這棟房子進行了有系統的搜查。)"],["technician","technician(n.)技術人員、技師\ntechnical(adj.)技術的\nlab technician 實驗室技術員\ncomputer technician 電腦技術人員\nA computer technician came to fix the school's network.\n(一位電腦技術人員來修理學校的網路。)\nShe works as a lab technician at a hospital.\n(她在一家醫院擔任檢驗技術員。)"],["technological","technological(adj.)科技的、技術的\ntechnology(n.)科技\ntechnologically(adv.)科技上\ntechnological advances 科技進步\ntechnological changes 科技變革\nTechnological advances have changed the way we communicate.\n(科技進步改變了我們溝通的方式。)\nThe country is a world leader in technological development.\n(這個國家在科技發展方面居世界領先地位。)"],["telegraph","telegraph(n./v.)電報、電報機、打電報\ntelegram(n.)電報(訊息)\nsend a telegraph 發電報\ntelegraph pole 電線桿\nIn the past, people sent important news by telegraph.\n(過去人們用電報傳送重要的消息。)\nThe telegraph changed long-distance communication forever.\n(電報永遠改變了遠距離的通訊方式。)"],["telescope","telescope(n.)望遠鏡\n(無詞性變化)\nthrough a telescope 透過望遠鏡\nspace telescope 太空望遠鏡\nWe looked at the moon through a telescope.\n(我們透過望遠鏡觀察月亮。)\nThe space telescope sent back amazing pictures of distant stars.\n(太空望遠鏡傳回了遙遠星星的驚人照片。)"],["tendency","tendency(n.)傾向、趨勢\ntend(v.)傾向於\nhave a tendency to 有…的傾向\na growing tendency 日益增加的趨勢\nHe has a tendency to talk too much when he is nervous.\n(他緊張時容易話太多。)\nThere is a growing tendency for young people to shop online.\n(年輕人上網購物的趨勢日益增加。)"],["tense","tense(adj./v.)緊張的、拉緊的、使緊張\ntension(n.)緊張\ntense(n.)(文法)時態\ntense up 緊繃起來\na tense moment 緊張的時刻\nEveryone was tense before the final exam results came out.\n(期末考成績公布前，每個人都很緊張。)\nHis shoulders tensed up when he heard his name.\n(聽到自己的名字時，他的肩膀緊繃了起來。)"],["tension","tension(n.)緊張、緊張局勢、拉力\ntense(adj.)緊張的\nease tension 緩和緊張\ntension between 之間的緊張關係\nA good joke can help ease the tension in the room.\n(一個好笑話能幫助緩和房間裡的緊張氣氛。)\nThere is growing tension between the two countries.\n(兩國之間的緊張局勢日益升高。)"],["terror","terror(n.)恐懼、恐怖、恐怖行動\nterrify(v.)使恐懼\nterrorist(n.)恐怖分子\nin terror 驚恐地\na reign of terror 恐怖統治\nThe children screamed in terror when the lights went out.\n(燈熄滅時，孩子們驚恐地尖叫。)\nPeople lived in terror during the war.\n(戰爭期間人們生活在恐懼之中。)"],["theme","theme(n.)主題、題目\n(無詞性變化)\ntheme park 主題樂園\ntheme song 主題曲\nWe spent the whole day at a theme park.\n(我們在主題樂園玩了一整天。)\nThe theme of this year's school play is friendship.\n(今年校園話劇的主題是友誼。)"],["thorough","thorough(adj.)徹底的、仔細的\nthoroughly(adv.)徹底地\na thorough check 徹底的檢查\nthorough research 詳盡的研究\nThe mechanic gave my car a thorough check.\n(技師把我的車徹底檢查了一遍。)\nShe is very thorough in everything she does.\n(她做每件事都非常仔細。)"],["thoughtful","thoughtful(adj.)體貼的、深思的\nthought(n.)想法\nthoughtfully(adv.)體貼地、沉思地\na thoughtful gift 貼心的禮物\nIt's thoughtful of you 你真體貼\nIt was thoughtful of you to bring me some soup.\n(你帶湯來給我真是太體貼了。)\nHe gave me a thoughtful look before answering.\n(他回答之前若有所思地看了我一眼。)"],["tickle","tickle(v./n.)搔癢、使發癢、逗樂\nticklish(adj.)怕癢的\ntickle sb. 搔某人癢\nbe tickled pink 非常高興\nMy little sister laughed when I tickled her feet.\n(我搔妹妹的腳底時，她笑了起來。)\nThe wool sweater tickles my neck.\n(這件羊毛衣讓我的脖子發癢。)"],["timetable","timetable(n.)時刻表、時間表、課表\n(無詞性變化)\ntrain timetable 火車時刻表\nschool timetable 課表\nCheck the train timetable before you leave.\n(出發前先查一下火車時刻表。)\nAccording to our school timetable, we have PE on Tuesday.\n(根據課表，我們星期二有體育課。)"],["timid","timid(adj.)膽小的、害羞的\ntimidly(adv.)膽怯地\na timid smile 靦腆的微笑\ntimid animal 膽小的動物\nThe timid boy was afraid to speak in front of the class.\n(那個膽小的男孩不敢在全班面前說話。)\nRabbits are timid animals.\n(兔子是膽小的動物。)"],["tolerable","tolerable(adj.)可忍受的、尚可的\ntolerate(v.)忍受\nintolerable(adj.)無法忍受的\ntolerable pain 可忍受的疼痛\na tolerable level 可以接受的程度\nThe pain was tolerable after I took the medicine.\n(吃了藥之後，疼痛變得可以忍受。)\nThe food at the hotel was tolerable but not great.\n(飯店的食物還過得去，但不算好。)"],["tolerance","tolerance(n.)寬容、容忍、耐受力\ntolerant(adj.)寬容的\ntolerate(v.)容忍\nreligious tolerance 宗教包容\nzero tolerance 零容忍\nWe should show tolerance toward people with different opinions.\n(我們應該對意見不同的人展現包容。)\nThe school has zero tolerance for bullying.\n(學校對霸凌採取零容忍態度。)"],["tolerant","tolerant(adj.)寬容的、容忍的、耐…的\ntolerance(n.)寬容\ntolerate(v.)容忍\nbe tolerant of 容忍…\ndrought-tolerant 耐旱的\nMy parents are tolerant of my strange hobbies.\n(我爸媽對我奇怪的嗜好很包容。)\nCactuses are drought-tolerant plants.\n(仙人掌是耐旱的植物。)"],["tolerate","tolerate(v.)容忍、忍受\ntolerance(n.)寬容\ntolerable(adj.)可忍受的\ntolerate noise 忍受噪音\nwon't tolerate 不容許\nI can't tolerate the noise from the construction site anymore.\n(我再也受不了工地傳來的噪音了。)\nOur teacher will not tolerate cheating.\n(我們老師絕不容許作弊。)"],["tomb","tomb(n.)墳墓、墓穴\ntombstone(n.)墓碑\nancient tomb 古墓\nTomb Sweeping Day 清明節\nArchaeologists discovered an ancient tomb in Egypt.\n(考古學家在埃及發現了一座古墓。)\nPeople visit their family tombs on Tomb Sweeping Day.\n(人們在清明節去掃墓。)"],["tortoise","tortoise(n.)陸龜、烏龜\n(無詞性變化)\nthe tortoise and the hare 龜兔賽跑\ngiant tortoise 巨龜\nThe story of the tortoise and the hare teaches us to keep going.\n(龜兔賽跑的故事告訴我們要堅持下去。)\nGiant tortoises can live for more than 100 years.\n(巨龜可以活超過一百年。)"],["torture","torture(n./v.)折磨、拷問、酷刑\n(無詞性變化)\nbe tortured by 受…折磨\nsheer torture 純粹的折磨\nWaiting for the test results was sheer torture.\n(等待考試結果簡直是種折磨。)\nThe prisoner was tortured by the guards.\n(那名囚犯遭到警衛拷打。)"],["tragedy","tragedy(n.)悲劇、慘事\ntragic(adj.)悲劇的\na terrible tragedy 可怕的悲劇\nend in tragedy 以悲劇收場\nRomeo and Juliet is a famous tragedy by Shakespeare.\n(《羅密歐與茱麗葉》是莎士比亞著名的悲劇。)\nThe trip ended in tragedy when their car crashed.\n(他們的車子出事，這趟旅程以悲劇收場。)"],["tragic","tragic(adj.)悲慘的、悲劇的\ntragedy(n.)悲劇\ntragically(adv.)悲慘地\na tragic accident 悲慘的意外\ntragic hero 悲劇英雄\nThree people died in the tragic accident.\n(有三人在這起悲慘的意外中喪生。)\nThe movie has a tragic ending.\n(這部電影有個悲傷的結局。)"],["transfer","transfer(n./v.)轉移、轉學、轉帳、轉乘\n(無詞性變化)\ntransfer to 轉到…\nbank transfer 銀行轉帳\nShe transferred to a new school in Taichung.\n(她轉學到台中的一所新學校。)\nYou need to transfer to another train at Taipei Station.\n(你需要在台北車站轉乘另一班火車。)"],["transform","transform(v.)轉變、改變、改造\ntransformation(n.)轉變\ntransform A into B 把A轉變成B\ncompletely transform 徹底改變\nThe old factory was transformed into a museum.\n(那座舊工廠被改造成一間博物館。)\nSmartphones have transformed the way we live.\n(智慧型手機徹底改變了我們的生活方式。)"],["translate","translate(v.)翻譯、轉化\ntranslation(n.)翻譯\ntranslator(n.)譯者\ntranslate A into B 把A翻譯成B\ntranslate into action 付諸行動\nCan you translate this sentence into English?\n(你可以把這個句子翻譯成英文嗎？)\nIt's time to translate our ideas into action.\n(該是把我們的想法付諸行動的時候了。)"],["translation","translation(n.)翻譯、譯文\ntranslate(v.)翻譯\ntranslator(n.)譯者\nin translation 以譯本形式\nmachine translation 機器翻譯\nI read the Japanese novel in translation.\n(我讀的是那本日本小說的譯本。)\nMachine translation is getting better every year.\n(機器翻譯一年比一年進步。)"],["translator","translator(n.)譯者、翻譯員\ntranslate(v.)翻譯\ntranslation(n.)翻譯\nprofessional translator 專業譯者\nwork as a translator 擔任翻譯\nMy aunt works as a translator for a publishing company.\n(我阿姨在一家出版社擔任翻譯。)\nA good translator must understand both cultures well.\n(好的譯者必須對兩種文化都很了解。)"],["transportation","transportation(n.)交通運輸、交通工具\ntransport(v./n.)運輸\npublic transportation 大眾運輸\nmeans of transportation 交通工具\nTaking public transportation helps reduce air pollution.\n(搭乘大眾運輸有助於減少空氣汙染。)\nThe bicycle is a cheap means of transportation.\n(腳踏車是一種便宜的交通工具。)"],["tremble","tremble(v./n.)發抖、顫抖、搖晃\n(無詞性變化)\ntremble with fear 嚇得發抖\ntremble with cold 冷得發抖\nThe little girl was trembling with fear in the dark.\n(那個小女孩在黑暗中嚇得發抖。)\nThe ground trembled during the earthquake.\n(地震時地面搖晃了起來。)"],["tremendous","tremendous(adj.)巨大的、極好的\ntremendously(adv.)非常地\na tremendous amount of 大量的…\ntremendous success 極大的成功\nThe project took a tremendous amount of time and effort.\n(這個專案花了極大量的時間與心力。)\nThe concert was a tremendous success.\n(這場音樂會非常成功。)"],["tribal","tribal(adj.)部落的、種族的\ntribe(n.)部落\ntribal culture 部落文化\ntribal leader 部落領袖\nWe learned about tribal culture during our trip to Hualien.\n(我們在花蓮旅行時認識了部落文化。)\nThe tribal leader welcomed the visitors with a song.\n(部落領袖用一首歌歡迎訪客。)"],["triumph","triumph(n./v.)勝利、成功、獲勝\ntriumphant(adj.)勝利的、得意洋洋的\nin triumph 得意洋洋地\ntriumph over 戰勝…\nThe team returned home in triumph.\n(這支隊伍凱旋歸來。)\nShe triumphed over many difficulties to become a doctor.\n(她克服了許多困難，成為一名醫生。)"],["troublesome","troublesome(adj.)麻煩的、令人苦惱的\ntrouble(n./v.)麻煩\na troublesome problem 棘手的問題\ntroublesome neighbor 惹人厭的鄰居\nFilling out all these forms is really troublesome.\n(填寫這麼多表格真的很麻煩。)\nThe troublesome cough kept me awake all night.\n(惱人的咳嗽讓我整晚睡不著。)"],["tumble","tumble(v./n.)跌倒、滾落、暴跌\n(無詞性變化)\ntumble down 跌落、倒塌\ntake a tumble 跌一跤\nThe boy tumbled down the stairs but wasn't hurt.\n(男孩從樓梯上跌下來，但沒有受傷。)\nStock prices tumbled after the bad news.\n(壞消息傳出後股價暴跌。)"],["twig","twig(n.)細枝、嫩枝\n(無詞性變化)\ndry twigs 乾樹枝\na twig snaps 樹枝折斷\nWe gathered dry twigs to start a campfire.\n(我們收集乾樹枝來生營火。)\nA bird was building its nest with small twigs.\n(一隻鳥正用小樹枝築巢。)"],["universal","universal(adj./n.)普遍的、全世界的、通用的、普遍原則\nuniverse(n.)宇宙\nuniversally(adv.)普遍地\nuniversal language 共通的語言\nuniversal truth 普世真理\nMusic is often called a universal language.\n(音樂常被稱為共通的語言。)\nSmiling is a universal way to show friendliness.\n(微笑是全世界表達友善的共通方式。)"],["urge","urge(n./v.)強烈慾望、衝動、力勸、催促\nurgent(adj.)緊急的\nurge sb. to do 力勸某人做…\nhave an urge to 有股…的衝動\nThe doctor urged him to stop smoking.\n(醫生力勸他戒菸。)\nI had a sudden urge to eat ice cream.\n(我突然很想吃冰淇淋。)"],["urgent","urgent(adj.)緊急的、急迫的\nurgency(n.)緊急\nurgently(adv.)緊急地\nurgent matter 緊急的事\nin urgent need of 迫切需要\nI have an urgent matter to discuss with you.\n(我有一件緊急的事要和你討論。)\nThe flood victims are in urgent need of food and water.\n(水災災民迫切需要食物和飲水。)"],["usage","usage(n.)用法、使用、使用量\nuse(v./n.)使用\nword usage 字詞用法\nwater usage 用水量\nThis dictionary explains the usage of each word clearly.\n(這本字典清楚說明每個字的用法。)\nWe should try to reduce our water usage in summer.\n(我們夏天應該設法減少用水量。)"],["vacancy","vacancy(n.)空缺、空房、空位\nvacant(adj.)空的、未被占用的\njob vacancy 職缺\nno vacancy 客滿\nThe company has several job vacancies for engineers.\n(那家公司有幾個工程師的職缺。)\nWe drove past three hotels with 'No Vacancy' signs.\n(我們開車經過三家掛著「客滿」牌子的旅館。)"],["vain","vain(adj.)徒勞的、自負的、愛慕虛榮的\nvanity(n.)虛榮心\nin vain 徒勞無功\nvain attempt 徒勞的嘗試\nHe tried in vain to fix the broken printer.\n(他試著修理壞掉的印表機，卻徒勞無功。)\nShe is so vain that she checks the mirror every few minutes.\n(她很愛慕虛榮，每隔幾分鐘就照一次鏡子。)"],["vast","vast(adj.)廣大的、巨大的、大量的\nvastly(adv.)大大地、極其\nvast majority 絕大多數\nvast area 廣大的地區\nThe vast majority of students passed the exam.\n(絕大多數學生都通過了考試。)\nThe Sahara Desert covers a vast area of North Africa.\n(撒哈拉沙漠覆蓋北非廣大的地區。)"],["vegetarian","vegetarian(n.)素食者\nvegetable(n.)蔬菜\nvegetarian food 素食\nstrict vegetarian 嚴格的素食者\nMy aunt has been a vegetarian for over ten years.\n(我阿姨吃素已經超過十年了。)\nThere are many vegetarian restaurants in Taipei.\n(台北有很多素食餐廳。)"],["vessel","vessel(n.)船、容器、血管\n(無詞性變化)\nblood vessel 血管\nfishing vessel 漁船\nBlood vessels carry blood around the body.\n(血管將血液輸送到全身。)\nSeveral fishing vessels returned to the harbor before the typhoon.\n(颱風來臨前，好幾艘漁船返回了港口。)"],["violate","violate(v.)違反、侵犯\nviolation(n.)違反、侵犯\nviolator(n.)違反者\nviolate the law 違法\nviolate someone's privacy 侵犯某人隱私\nPosting someone's photo without permission may violate their privacy.\n(未經允許張貼別人的照片可能侵犯其隱私。)\nDrivers who violate traffic rules will be fined.\n(違反交通規則的駕駛人會被罰款。)"],["violation","violation(n.)違反、侵犯\nviolate(v.)違反、侵犯\ntraffic violation 交通違規\nhuman rights violation 侵犯人權\nHe got a ticket for a traffic violation.\n(他因交通違規收到一張罰單。)\nCopying others' work is a violation of school rules.\n(抄襲別人的作品違反校規。)"],["virtue","virtue(n.)美德、優點\nvirtuous(adj.)有道德的\nby virtue of 由於、憑藉\npatience is a virtue 耐心是一種美德\nHonesty is an important virtue.\n(誠實是一項重要的美德。)\nOne virtue of this phone is its long battery life.\n(這支手機的一大優點是電池續航力長。)"],["virus","virus(n.)病毒、電腦病毒\nviral(adj.)病毒的、(網路上)爆紅的\ncomputer virus 電腦病毒\nspread a virus 散播病毒\nThe virus spread quickly around the world.\n(這種病毒很快就傳遍全世界。)\nDon't open that file; it may contain a computer virus.\n(不要打開那個檔案，它可能含有電腦病毒。)"],["visual","visual(adj.)視覺的\nvisualize(v.)想像、使視覺化\nvisually(adv.)視覺上\nvisual arts 視覺藝術\nvisual aid 視覺輔助教具\nThe teacher used visual aids to explain the lesson.\n(老師使用視覺輔助教具講解這一課。)\nShe is interested in studying visual arts in college.\n(她有興趣在大學念視覺藝術。)"],["vital","vital(adj.)極重要的、生命的、充滿活力的\nvitality(n.)活力\nvital role 極重要的角色\nvital signs 生命徵象\nSleep plays a vital role in our health.\n(睡眠對我們的健康扮演極重要的角色。)\nIt is vital that you follow the safety rules.\n(你務必要遵守安全規定。)"],["voluntary","voluntary(adj.)自願的、義務的\nvolunteer(n./v.)志工、自願\nvoluntarily(adv.)自願地\nvoluntary work 志願服務工作\non a voluntary basis 以自願的方式\nJoining the cleaning team is voluntary.\n(加入打掃隊是自願的。)\nShe does voluntary work at the animal shelter every weekend.\n(她每個週末都在動物收容所做志工。)"],["volunteer","volunteer(n./v.)志工、自願者、自願\nvoluntary(adj.)自願的\nvolunteer work 志工服務\nvolunteer to 自願做…\nMany students volunteer at the library after school.\n(很多學生放學後在圖書館當志工。)\nTom volunteered to clean the classroom.\n(湯姆自願打掃教室。)"],["voyage","voyage(n./v.)航行、旅程、航海\n(無詞性變化)\nmaiden voyage 首航\nsea voyage 海上航行\nThe Titanic sank on its maiden voyage.\n(鐵達尼號在首航時沉沒了。)\nThe sailors voyaged across the Pacific Ocean.\n(水手們航行橫越太平洋。)"],["waken","waken(v.)喚醒、醒來\nwake(v.)醒來、叫醒\nawaken(v.)喚醒、喚起\nwaken someone up 叫醒某人\nbe wakened by 被…吵醒\nI was wakened by the sound of rain.\n(我被雨聲吵醒了。)\nPlease don't waken the baby; she just fell asleep.\n(請不要吵醒寶寶，她剛睡著。)"],["website","website(n.)網站\n(無詞性變化)\nofficial website 官方網站\nvisit a website 瀏覽網站\nYou can find more information on the school's official website.\n(你可以在學校官方網站上找到更多資訊。)\nThis website offers free English lessons.\n(這個網站提供免費的英文課程。)"],["welfare","welfare(n.)福利、福祉\n(無詞性變化)\nsocial welfare 社會福利\nanimal welfare 動物福利\nThe government should improve social welfare for the elderly.\n(政府應該改善老年人的社會福利。)\nShe cares a lot about animal welfare.\n(她非常關心動物福利。)"],["wink","wink(n./v.)眨眼、使眼色\n(無詞性變化)\nwink at 對…眨眼示意\nnot sleep a wink 一夜沒闔眼\nHe winked at me to show it was a joke.\n(他對我眨眼，表示那只是個玩笑。)\nI didn't sleep a wink before the exam.\n(考試前我整晚都沒闔眼。)"],["wit","wit(n.)機智、風趣、智力\nwitty(adj.)機智的、風趣的\nquick wit 反應機敏\nat one's wits' end 不知所措\nEveryone loves him for his quick wit.\n(大家都喜歡他反應機敏又風趣。)\nI'm at my wits' end with this math problem.\n(這道數學題讓我束手無策。)"],["witch/wizard","witch(n.)女巫\nwizard(n.)男巫、奇才\nwitch hunt 政治迫害、獵巫\ncomputer wizard 電腦奇才\nIn the story, a witch turned the prince into a frog.\n(故事中，一位女巫把王子變成了青蛙。)\nHarry Potter is a young wizard who studies at Hogwarts.\n(哈利波特是一位在霍格華茲就讀的年輕巫師。)"],["withdraw","withdraw(v.)提(款)、撤回、退出\nwithdrawal(n.)提款、撤退、退出\nwithdraw money 提款\nwithdraw from 退出…\nI need to withdraw some money from the ATM.\n(我需要從提款機領一些錢。)\nHe withdrew from the race because of an injury.\n(他因受傷退出比賽。)"],["witness","witness(n./v.)目擊者、證人、目擊、見證\n(無詞性變化)\nkey witness 關鍵證人\nwitness an accident 目擊事故\nThe police are looking for witnesses to the car accident.\n(警方正在尋找那起車禍的目擊者。)\nWe witnessed a beautiful sunrise from the top of Alishan.\n(我們在阿里山上見證了美麗的日出。)"],["workout","workout(n.)運動、鍛鍊\nwork out(v.)運動、健身、解決\ndaily workout 每日運動\nintense workout 高強度鍛鍊\nA 30-minute workout every day keeps me healthy.\n(每天運動三十分鐘讓我保持健康。)\nI felt tired but happy after the workout.\n(運動完後我覺得疲累但很開心。)"],["workplace","workplace(n.)工作場所、職場\n(無詞性變化)\nin the workplace 在職場上\nworkplace safety 職場安全\nGood communication skills are important in the workplace.\n(良好的溝通能力在職場上很重要。)\nThe company pays close attention to workplace safety.\n(那家公司非常重視職場安全。)"],["wreck","wreck(n./v.)殘骸、失事、毀壞、破壞\nwreckage(n.)殘骸\nshipwreck 船難\na nervous wreck 神經緊繃的人\nDivers found the wreck of an old ship on the seabed.\n(潛水員在海底發現一艘古老船隻的殘骸。)\nThe storm wrecked many houses near the coast.\n(暴風雨摧毀了海岸附近的許多房子。)"],["yawn","yawn(n./v.)打哈欠、呵欠\n(無詞性變化)\ngive a yawn 打個哈欠\nstifle a yawn 忍住哈欠\nHe yawned several times during the long meeting.\n(在冗長的會議中他打了好幾個哈欠。)\nYawning is contagious; when one person yawns, others often do too.\n(打哈欠會傳染，一個人打哈欠時，別人常常也會跟著打。)"],["youthful","youthful(adj.)年輕的、有朝氣的\nyouth(n.)青春、年輕人\nyouthful energy 青春活力\nyouthful appearance 年輕的外表\nMy grandmother still looks youthful at seventy.\n(我奶奶七十歲了看起來仍然很年輕。)\nThe students' youthful energy filled the classroom.\n(學生們的青春活力充滿了整間教室。)"]],"5":[["abnormal","abnormal(adj.)異常的、不正常的\nabnormality(n.)異常、反常\nabnormally(adv.)異常地\nabnormal behavior 異常行為\nabnormal weather 異常天氣\nThe doctor noticed some abnormal results in his blood test.\n(醫生注意到他的血液檢查中有些異常的結果。)\nScientists blame climate change for the abnormal weather this year.\n(科學家將今年的異常天氣歸咎於氣候變遷。)"],["abolish","abolish(v.)廢除、廢止\nabolition(n.)廢除\nabolish a law 廢除法律\nabolish slavery 廢除奴隸制度\nThe United States abolished slavery in 1865.\n(美國於1865年廢除了奴隸制度。)\nMany students hope the school will abolish the strict hair rules.\n(許多學生希望學校廢除嚴格的髮禁規定。)"],["abortion","abortion(n.)墮胎、人工流產\nabort(v.)中止、使流產\nabortion law 墮胎法\nlegalize abortion 使墮胎合法化\nThe debate over abortion laws remains heated in many countries.\n(在許多國家，關於墮胎法的辯論仍然十分激烈。)\nSome countries have recently changed their laws on abortion.\n(有些國家最近修改了有關墮胎的法律。)"],["abrupt","abrupt(adj.)突然的、唐突的、粗魯的\nabruptly(adv.)突然地\nabrupt change 突然的改變\nabrupt manner 唐突的態度\nThe meeting came to an abrupt end when the fire alarm went off.\n(火災警報響起時，會議戛然而止。)\nHis abrupt manner made the new employees feel uncomfortable.\n(他唐突的態度讓新進員工感到不自在。)"],["absurd","absurd(adj.)荒謬的、可笑的\nabsurdity(n.)荒謬\nabsurdly(adv.)荒謬地\nabsurd idea 荒謬的想法\nsound absurd 聽起來很荒謬\nIt sounds absurd to spend so much money on a phone case.\n(花那麼多錢買手機殼聽起來很荒謬。)\nAt first, people thought the idea of flying machines was absurd.\n(起初，人們認為飛行器的構想很荒謬。)"],["abundant","abundant(adj.)豐富的、充足的\nabundance(n.)豐富、充足\nabound(v.)大量存在、充滿\nabundant resources 豐富的資源\nabundant rainfall 充沛的雨量\nTaiwan has abundant rainfall, especially during the plum rain season.\n(臺灣雨量充沛，尤其是在梅雨季期間。)\nThe forest provides abundant food for many kinds of wildlife.\n(這片森林為許多種野生動物提供了充足的食物。)"],["abuse","abuse(n./v.)濫用、虐待、辱罵\nabusive(adj.)虐待的、辱罵的\ndrug abuse 濫用藥物\nabuse of power 濫用權力\nThe official was accused of abuse of power for personal gain.\n(那名官員被指控為了私利濫用職權。)\nAnimal protection groups are working to stop the abuse of stray dogs.\n(動物保護團體正致力於阻止虐待流浪狗的行為。)"],["accelerate","accelerate(v.)加速、促進\nacceleration(n.)加速、加速度\naccelerator(n.)油門、加速器\naccelerate growth 加速成長\naccelerate the process 加快進程\nThe driver accelerated suddenly to pass the truck in front of him.\n(駕駛突然加速超越前方的卡車。)\nNew technology has accelerated the process of globalization.\n(新科技加速了全球化的進程。)"],["accessible","accessible(adj.)可接近的、易取得的、易懂的\naccess(n./v.)使用權、接近、存取\naccessibility(n.)可及性、無障礙\neasily accessible 容易到達的\naccessible to the public 對大眾開放\nThe museum is easily accessible by MRT.\n(搭捷運很容易就能到達這座博物館。)\nThe government wants to make education accessible to every child.\n(政府希望讓每個孩子都能接受教育。)"],["accommodate","accommodate(v.)容納、提供住宿、適應、通融\naccommodation(n.)住宿、膳宿\naccommodating(adj.)樂於助人的、隨和的\naccommodate guests 容納客人\naccommodate needs 滿足需求\nThe new hotel can accommodate up to five hundred guests.\n(這家新飯店最多可容納五百位客人。)\nThe school tried to accommodate the needs of students with special requirements.\n(學校努力滿足有特殊需求學生的需要。)"],["accommodation","accommodation(n.)住宿、膳宿、和解\naccommodate(v.)容納、提供住宿\nfind accommodation 找住處\nstudent accommodation 學生宿舍\nIt can be difficult to find cheap accommodation in big cities.\n(在大城市裡要找到便宜的住處可能很困難。)\nThe price of the tour includes flights and accommodation.\n(旅遊團費用包含機票與住宿。)"],["accord","accord(n./v.)協議、一致、給予\naccordance(n.)一致、依照\naccordingly(adv.)相應地、因此\nof one's own accord 自願地、主動地\nin accordance with 依照\nHe cleaned his room of his own accord without being asked.\n(他沒被要求就主動打掃了自己的房間。)\nThe two countries signed a peace accord after years of conflict.\n(兩國在多年衝突後簽署了和平協議。)"],["accounting","accounting(n.)會計、會計學\naccount(n./v.)帳戶、說明、占……\naccountant(n.)會計師\naccounting firm 會計師事務所\naccounting department 會計部門\nMy sister studies accounting at university and wants to become an accountant.\n(我姊姊在大學念會計，想成為一名會計師。)\nPlease send all receipts to the accounting department by Friday.\n(請在星期五前將所有收據交給會計部門。)"],["acknowledge(ment)","acknowledge(v.)承認、致謝、確認收到、acknowledgment(n.)承認、致謝\nacknowledged(adj.)公認的\nacknowledge a mistake 承認錯誤\nin acknowledgment of 為感謝、為表彰\nHe finally acknowledged that he had made a serious mistake.\n(他終於承認自己犯了嚴重的錯誤。)\nShe received an award in acknowledgment of her years of volunteer work.\n(她獲頒獎項，以表彰她多年來的志工服務。)"],["acquaint","acquaint(v.)使熟悉、使認識\nacquaintance(n.)相識的人、認識\nacquainted(adj.)熟悉的、認識的\nacquaint oneself with 使自己熟悉\nbe acquainted with 認識、熟悉\nNew employees need time to acquaint themselves with the company rules.\n(新進員工需要時間熟悉公司規定。)\nAre you acquainted with the new manager?\n(你認識新來的經理嗎？)"],["acquisition","acquisition(n.)獲得、習得、收購、購得物\nacquire(v.)獲得、習得\nlanguage acquisition 語言習得\nrecent acquisition 新購得之物\nLanguage acquisition is easier for young children than for adults.\n(幼童學習語言比成人來得容易。)\nThe company announced its acquisition of a smaller tech firm.\n(這家公司宣布收購一家規模較小的科技公司。)"],["activist","activist(n.)社運人士、積極分子\nactive(adj.)積極的、活躍的\nactivism(n.)行動主義\nenvironmental activist 環保人士\nhuman rights activist 人權運動者\nThe young environmental activist gave a powerful speech at the conference.\n(那位年輕的環保人士在會議上發表了一場震撼人心的演講。)\nActivists gathered outside the building to protest the new policy.\n(社運人士聚集在大樓外抗議新政策。)"],["acute","acute(adj.)嚴重的、急性的、敏銳的\nacutely(adv.)強烈地、敏銳地\nacute pain 劇痛\nacute shortage 嚴重短缺\nThere is an acute shortage of nurses in many hospitals.\n(許多醫院面臨護理師嚴重短缺的問題。)\nDogs have an acute sense of smell.\n(狗的嗅覺非常敏銳。)"],["administration","administration(n.)管理、行政、政府當局\nadminister(v.)管理、執行、給予(藥物)\nadministrative(adj.)行政的、管理的\nbusiness administration 企業管理\nthe Biden administration 拜登政府\nHe decided to study business administration in college.\n(他決定在大學主修企業管理。)\nThe new administration promised to lower taxes.\n(新政府承諾要減稅。)"],["administrative","administrative(adj.)行政的、管理的\nadministration(n.)行政、管理\nadministrator(n.)管理者、行政人員\nadministrative staff 行政人員\nadministrative work 行政工作\nTeachers often complain about having too much administrative work.\n(老師們常抱怨行政工作太多。)\nThe administrative office is on the first floor of the main building.\n(行政辦公室在主大樓的一樓。)"],["administrator","administrator(n.)管理者、行政人員\nadminister(v.)管理、執行\nadministration(n.)管理、行政\nschool administrator 學校行政人員\nsystem administrator 系統管理員\nPlease contact the system administrator if you forget your password.\n(如果忘記密碼，請聯絡系統管理員。)\nThe hospital administrator is responsible for managing the budget.\n(醫院的行政主管負責管理預算。)"],["adolescent","adolescent(adj./n.)青少年的、青少年\nadolescence(n.)青春期\nadolescent years 青少年時期\nadolescent behavior 青少年行為\nAdolescents often care a lot about what their friends think.\n(青少年往往非常在意朋友的看法。)\nMany changes take place in the body during adolescence.\n(青春期時身體會發生許多變化。)"],["adore","adore(v.)熱愛、崇拜、非常喜歡\nadorable(adj.)可愛的、討人喜歡的\nadoration(n.)崇拜、愛慕\nadore children 非常喜愛孩子\nbe adored by fans 受粉絲崇拜\nMy little sister adores her new puppy and plays with it all day.\n(我妹妹非常喜愛她的新小狗，整天都跟牠玩。)\nThe singer is adored by millions of fans around the world.\n(這位歌手受到全世界數百萬粉絲的喜愛。)"],["adverse","adverse(adj.)不利的、有害的、相反的\nadversity(n.)逆境、困境\nadversely(adv.)不利地\nadverse effects 副作用、不良影響\nadverse weather conditions 惡劣天候\nSome medicines may have adverse effects on your stomach.\n(有些藥物可能會對你的胃產生不良影響。)\nThe flight was delayed due to adverse weather conditions.\n(由於天候惡劣，班機延誤了。)"],["advocate","advocate(n./v.)提倡者、擁護者、提倡、主張\nadvocacy(n.)擁護、提倡\nadvocate for 擁護、為……發聲\nstrong advocate 堅定的支持者\nShe is a strong advocate for animal rights.\n(她是動物權益的堅定擁護者。)\nMany doctors advocate regular exercise as a way to reduce stress.\n(許多醫生提倡規律運動作為減壓方式。)"],["affection","affection(n.)喜愛、情感、感情\naffectionate(adj.)充滿深情的、親切的\nshow affection 表達感情\ndeep affection 深厚的感情\nThe old man looked at his grandchildren with great affection.\n(老人以充滿慈愛的眼神看著他的孫子們。)\nCats show affection by rubbing against your legs.\n(貓會用磨蹭你的腿來表達好感。)"],["agenda","agenda(n.)議程、待議事項\n(無詞性變化)\non the agenda 在議程上\nhidden agenda 不可告人的目的\nWhat is the first item on the agenda for today's meeting?\n(今天會議議程上的第一項是什麼？)\nSome people suspected that he had a hidden agenda.\n(有些人懷疑他別有用心。)"],["aggression","aggression(n.)侵略、攻擊性行為\naggressive(adj.)侵略的、積極進取的\naggressor(n.)侵略者\nact of aggression 侵略行為\nsigns of aggression 攻擊性的跡象\nPlaying violent games may lead to aggression in some children.\n(玩暴力遊戲可能導致某些孩子出現攻擊行為。)\nThe invasion was condemned as an act of aggression.\n(這次入侵被譴責為一種侵略行為。)"],["agony","agony(n.)極度痛苦\nagonize(v.)苦惱、煩惱\nagonizing(adj.)令人痛苦的\nin agony 處於極度痛苦中\nagony of waiting 等待的煎熬\nThe injured player lay on the ground in agony.\n(受傷的球員痛苦地躺在地上。)\nWaiting for the exam results was pure agony for her.\n(等待考試結果對她而言是一種煎熬。)"],["agricultural","agricultural(adj.)農業的\nagriculture(n.)農業\nagricultural products 農產品\nagricultural land 農地\nTaiwan's agricultural products, such as mangoes, are popular overseas.\n(臺灣的農產品，例如芒果，在海外很受歡迎。)\nMuch agricultural land has been turned into factories.\n(許多農地已被改建成工廠。)"],["aisle","aisle(n.)走道、通道\n(無詞性變化)\naisle seat 靠走道座位\nwalk down the aisle 結婚、走紅毯\nI prefer an aisle seat on long flights.\n(長途飛行時我偏好靠走道的座位。)\nYou can find the cereal in aisle five of the supermarket.\n(你可以在超市的第五排走道找到穀片。)"],["alcoholic","alcoholic(adj./n.)含酒精的、酗酒者\nalcohol(n.)酒精、酒\nalcoholism(n.)酗酒、酒精中毒\nalcoholic drinks 酒精飲料\nnon-alcoholic 不含酒精的\nPeople under eighteen are not allowed to buy alcoholic drinks.\n(未滿十八歲的人不得購買酒精飲料。)\nThe restaurant offers a wide range of non-alcoholic drinks.\n(這家餐廳提供多種無酒精飲料。)"],["alien","alien(adj./n.)外國的、陌生的、外星人、外國人\nalienate(v.)使疏遠\nalien to 與……格格不入\nillegal alien 非法移民\nThe idea of working on weekends was completely alien to him.\n(週末工作的想法對他來說完全陌生。)\nDo you believe that aliens have visited the Earth?\n(你相信外星人曾造訪地球嗎？)"],["allergic","allergic(adj.)過敏的、極討厭的\nallergy(n.)過敏\nbe allergic to 對……過敏\nallergic reaction 過敏反應\nMy brother is allergic to peanuts, so we never cook with them.\n(我弟弟對花生過敏，所以我們從不用花生做菜。)\nShe had an allergic reaction after eating shrimp.\n(她吃了蝦子之後出現過敏反應。)"],["allergy","allergy(n.)過敏症\nallergic(adj.)過敏的\nfood allergy 食物過敏\npollen allergy 花粉過敏\nMany people suffer from pollen allergies in spring.\n(許多人在春天受花粉過敏所苦。)\nPlease tell the waiter if you have any food allergies.\n(如果您有任何食物過敏，請告訴服務生。)"],["alliance","alliance(n.)聯盟、同盟\nally(n./v.)盟友、結盟\nallied(adj.)同盟的\nform an alliance 結盟\nmilitary alliance 軍事同盟\nSeveral small companies formed an alliance to compete with the giant.\n(幾家小公司結盟以對抗那家大企業。)\nThe two countries signed a military alliance after the war.\n(兩國在戰後簽訂了軍事同盟。)"],["allocate","allocate(v.)分配、撥出\nallocation(n.)分配、配置\nallocate funds 撥款\nallocate time 分配時間\nThe government will allocate more funds to public education.\n(政府將撥出更多經費用於公共教育。)\nYou should allocate enough time for each subject when you study.\n(讀書時你應為每一科分配足夠的時間。)"],["ally","ally(n./v.)盟友、同盟國、結盟\nalliance(n.)聯盟\nallied(adj.)同盟的\nclose ally 親密盟友\nally with 與……結盟\nThe United States and Japan have been close allies for decades.\n(美國和日本數十年來一直是親密的盟友。)\nThe small party decided to ally itself with a larger one.\n(那個小黨決定與一個大黨結盟。)"],["alongside","alongside(prep./adv.)在旁邊、與……一起、並排\n(無詞性變化)\nwork alongside 與……並肩工作\nalongside each other 並排\nVolunteers worked alongside firefighters to help the victims.\n(志工與消防員並肩合作，協助受災者。)\nThe boat sailed alongside the coast for several hours.\n(那艘船沿著海岸航行了好幾個小時。)"],["alter","alter(v.)改變、修改\nalteration(n.)改變、修改\nalternative(adj./n.)替代的、替代方案\nalter a plan 更改計畫\nalter clothes 修改衣服\nWe had to alter our travel plans because of the typhoon.\n(因為颱風，我們不得不更改旅行計畫。)\nThe tailor altered the suit so that it fit me perfectly.\n(裁縫修改了這套西裝，讓它完全合我的身。)"],["alternate","alternate(adj./v./n.)輪流的、交替的、交替、替補者\nalternately(adv.)輪流地、交替地\nalternation(n.)交替、輪流\non alternate days 隔天、每隔一天\nalternate between 在……之間交替\nI go jogging on alternate days to give my legs a rest.\n(我隔天慢跑一次，讓雙腿休息。)\nHer mood alternated between hope and despair.\n(她的心情在希望與絕望之間交替。)"],["amend","amend(v.)修改、修正(法律等)\namendment(n.)修正案、修改\namends(n.)賠償、彌補\namend the law 修法\nmake amends 彌補、賠罪\nLawmakers voted to amend the traffic law last month.\n(立法委員上個月投票通過修改交通法規。)\nHe tried to make amends for his rude behavior by buying her lunch.\n(他請她吃午餐，想彌補自己無禮的行為。)"],["ample","ample(adj.)充足的、寬敞的\namply(adv.)充分地\nample time 充裕的時間\nample evidence 充分的證據\nThere will be ample time to ask questions after the presentation.\n(簡報結束後會有充裕的時間提問。)\nThe police found ample evidence to prove that he was guilty.\n(警方找到充分的證據證明他有罪。)"],["analyst","analyst(n.)分析師、分析者\nanalyze(v.)分析\nanalysis(n.)分析\nfinancial analyst 財務分析師\npolitical analyst 政治分析家\nFinancial analysts expect the stock market to rise next year.\n(財務分析師預期股市明年會上漲。)\nShe works as a data analyst for a large technology company.\n(她在一家大型科技公司擔任資料分析師。)"],["anonymous","anonymous(adj.)匿名的、無名的\nanonymity(n.)匿名\nanonymously(adv.)匿名地\nanonymous letter 匿名信\nremain anonymous 保持匿名\nAn anonymous donor gave one million dollars to the hospital.\n(一位匿名捐贈者捐了一百萬元給醫院。)\nThe writer wished to remain anonymous.\n(這位作者希望保持匿名。)"],["anticipate","anticipate(v.)預期、預料、期待\nanticipation(n.)預期、期待\nanticipate problems 預料到問題\nin anticipation of 預期、期待著\nWe did not anticipate so many people coming to the concert.\n(我們沒預料到會有這麼多人來聽演唱會。)\nThe children waited in eager anticipation of the holiday.\n(孩子們滿心期待地等著假期到來。)"],["antique","antique(adj./n.)古董的、古董\nantiquity(n.)古代、古物\nantique shop 古董店\nantique furniture 古董家具\nMy grandfather collects antique clocks from different countries.\n(我爺爺收藏來自不同國家的古董時鐘。)\nThis antique vase is worth a fortune.\n(這只古董花瓶價值不菲。)"],["applause","applause(n.)鼓掌、喝采\napplaud(v.)鼓掌、稱讚\nwarm applause 熱烈的掌聲\nburst into applause 爆出掌聲\nThe audience burst into applause at the end of the performance.\n(表演結束時，觀眾爆出熱烈掌聲。)\nLet's give a big round of applause to our guest speaker.\n(讓我們以熱烈的掌聲歡迎我們的演講嘉賓。)"],["appliance","appliance(n.)家電、器具\napply(v.)應用、申請\nhousehold appliance 家用電器\nkitchen appliance 廚房電器\nRemember to unplug electrical appliances before leaving on vacation.\n(出門度假前記得拔掉電器的插頭。)\nThe store offers discounts on kitchen appliances this week.\n(這家店本週廚房電器有打折。)"],["apt","apt(adj.)易於……的、恰當的、聰穎的\naptly(adv.)恰當地\naptitude(n.)天資、才能\nbe apt to 易於、傾向於\napt description 貼切的描述\nPeople are apt to make mistakes when they are tired.\n(人在疲累時容易犯錯。)\n'Busy bee' is an apt description of my mother.\n(用「忙碌的蜜蜂」來形容我媽媽非常貼切。)"],["architect","architect(n.)建築師、設計者\narchitecture(n.)建築、建築學\narchitectural(adj.)建築的\nfamous architect 知名建築師\nlandscape architect 景觀設計師\nThe architect designed the museum to look like a giant shell.\n(建築師將博物館設計成巨大貝殼的模樣。)\nHe was the chief architect of the new peace plan.\n(他是這項新和平計畫的主要策劃者。)"],["architecture","architecture(n.)建築、建築學、建築風格\narchitect(n.)建築師\narchitectural(adj.)建築的\nmodern architecture 現代建築\nstudy architecture 學建築\nTaipei 101 is a famous example of modern architecture.\n(臺北101是現代建築的知名範例。)\nShe went to Italy to study classical architecture.\n(她去義大利研讀古典建築。)"],["arena","arena(n.)競技場、舞臺、活動領域\n(無詞性變化)\nsports arena 體育館\npolitical arena 政治舞臺\nThe concert will be held at the city's largest sports arena.\n(演唱會將在城市最大的體育館舉行。)\nShe entered the political arena at a young age.\n(她年紀輕輕就踏入了政壇。)"],["arouse","arouse(v.)喚起、激起\narousal(n.)喚起、激發\narouse interest 引起興趣\narouse suspicion 引起懷疑\nThe strange noise aroused the curiosity of the children.\n(那奇怪的聲音激起了孩子們的好奇心。)\nHis nervous behavior aroused the suspicion of the police.\n(他緊張的舉動引起了警方的懷疑。)"],["array","array(n.)一系列、大量、陳列\n(無詞性變化)\na wide array of 各式各樣的\nan array of 一系列的\nThe night market offers a wide array of local snacks.\n(夜市提供各式各樣的在地小吃。)\nThe museum displays an impressive array of ancient art.\n(博物館陳列著一系列令人驚嘆的古代藝術品。)"],["arrogant","arrogant(adj.)傲慢的、自大的\narrogance(n.)傲慢\narrogantly(adv.)傲慢地\narrogant attitude 傲慢的態度\narrogant behavior 自大的行為\nHis arrogant attitude made it hard for him to make friends.\n(他傲慢的態度讓他很難交到朋友。)\nIt is arrogant to think you are always right.\n(認為自己永遠是對的是一種傲慢。)"],["articulate","articulate(v./adj.)清楚表達、口齒清晰的、善於表達的\narticulation(n.)清楚表達、發音\narticulate ideas 清楚表達想法\narticulate speaker 能言善道的講者\nShe was able to articulate her ideas clearly in the debate.\n(她在辯論中能清楚表達自己的想法。)\nHe is an articulate young man with a bright future.\n(他是個能言善道、前途光明的年輕人。)"],["ass","ass(n.)驢子、笨蛋\n(無詞性變化)\nmake an ass of oneself 出洋相\nstubborn as an ass 像驢子一樣固執\nHe made an ass of himself by singing loudly in the library.\n(他在圖書館大聲唱歌，讓自己出盡洋相。)\nIn the old story, the farmer rode an ass to the market.\n(在那則古老故事中，農夫騎著驢子去市場。)"],["assault","assault(n./v.)攻擊、襲擊、突擊\nassailant(n.)攻擊者\nphysical assault 人身攻擊\nlaunch an assault 發動攻擊\nThe man was arrested for assault after the fight in the bar.\n(那名男子在酒吧打架後因傷害罪被捕。)\nThe army launched an assault on the enemy's base at dawn.\n(軍隊在黎明時對敵軍基地發動突擊。)"],["assert","assert(v.)斷言、主張、維護(權利)\nassertion(n.)斷言、主張\nassertive(adj.)堅定自信的、果斷的\nassert oneself 堅持己見、表現自己\nassert one's rights 維護權利\nThe suspect continued to assert that he was innocent.\n(嫌疑人持續堅稱自己是無辜的。)\nYou need to learn to assert yourself in group discussions.\n(你需要學會在小組討論中表達自己的立場。)"],["assess(ment)","assess(v.)評估、評定、assessment(n.)評估、評價\nassessor(n.)評估者\nassess the damage 評估損害\nrisk assessment 風險評估\nExperts were sent to assess the damage caused by the earthquake.\n(專家被派去評估地震造成的損害。)\nTeachers use different kinds of assessment to check students' progress.\n(老師使用各種評量方式來檢視學生的進步。)"],["asset","asset(n.)資產、有價值的人或物\n(無詞性變化)\nvaluable asset 寶貴的資產\nassets and liabilities 資產與負債\nHer language skills are a valuable asset to the company.\n(她的語言能力是公司的寶貴資產。)\nThe family sold some of their assets to pay off the debt.\n(這家人變賣了部分資產來償還債務。)"],["assumption","assumption(n.)假設、假定、承擔\nassume(v.)假設、認為、承擔\nmake an assumption 做出假設\non the assumption that 假定……\nIt is dangerous to make assumptions about people based on their looks.\n(根據外表對人做出假設是很危險的。)\nWe planned the event on the assumption that it wouldn't rain.\n(我們是在假定不會下雨的前提下規劃這個活動。)"],["astonish(ment)","astonish(v.)使驚訝、astonishment(n.)驚訝\nastonishing(adj.)令人驚訝的\nastonished(adj.)感到驚訝的\nto one's astonishment 令某人驚訝的是\nbe astonished at 對……感到驚訝\nThe young pianist astonished the audience with her amazing skills.\n(那位年輕鋼琴家以驚人的技巧讓觀眾大為驚豔。)\nTo my astonishment, the shy boy won the speech contest.\n(令我驚訝的是，那個害羞的男孩贏得了演講比賽。)"],["athletics","athletics(n.)田徑運動、體育運動\nathlete(n.)運動員\nathletic(adj.)運動的、強健的\nathletics team 田徑隊\nathletics meet 田徑運動會\nShe joined the school athletics team and trained every morning.\n(她加入學校田徑隊，每天早上都去訓練。)\nThe national athletics meet attracts many talented young runners.\n(全國田徑運動會吸引了許多有天分的年輕跑者。)"],["attendance","attendance(n.)出席、出席人數\nattend(v.)出席、參加\nattendant(n.)服務員\ntake attendance 點名\nperfect attendance 全勤\nThe teacher takes attendance at the beginning of every class.\n(老師在每堂課開始時都會點名。)\nShe received an award for perfect attendance this semester.\n(她這學期因全勤而獲獎。)"],["attic","attic(n.)閣樓\n(無詞性變化)\nin the attic 在閣樓裡\nattic room 閣樓房間\nWe found a box of old family photos in the attic.\n(我們在閣樓裡找到一箱老舊的家族照片。)\nHe turned the attic into a small study room.\n(他把閣樓改造成一間小書房。)"],["attorney","attorney(n.)律師、代理人\n(無詞性變化)\ndefense attorney 辯護律師\nattorney general 檢察總長、司法部長\nThe defense attorney argued that her client was innocent.\n(辯護律師主張她的當事人是無辜的。)\nYou should talk to an attorney before signing the contract.\n(在簽約之前，你應該先諮詢律師。)"],["attribute","attribute(v.)把……歸因於、認為……是某人所作\nattribution(n.)歸因、歸屬\nattribute A to B 把A歸因於B\nbe attributed to 被認為是……所作\nShe attributes her success to hard work and good luck.\n(她將自己的成功歸因於努力和好運。)\nThis famous poem is attributed to Li Bai.\n(這首著名的詩被認為是李白所作。)"],["auction","auction(n./v.)拍賣、拍賣會、拍賣掉\nauctioneer(n.)拍賣師\nat auction 在拍賣會上\nonline auction 網路拍賣\nThe famous painting was sold at auction for ten million dollars.\n(那幅名畫在拍賣會上以一千萬元售出。)\nThey decided to auction off the old furniture.\n(他們決定把那批舊家具拍賣掉。)"],["authorize","authorize(v.)授權、批准\nauthority(n.)權威、當局\nauthorization(n.)授權、許可\nauthorized(adj.)經授權的\nauthorize payment 批准付款\nauthorized dealer 授權經銷商\nOnly the manager can authorize refunds over one thousand dollars.\n(只有經理能批准超過一千元的退款。)\nYou should buy the phone from an authorized dealer.\n(你應該向授權經銷商購買手機。)"],["autonomy","autonomy(n.)自治、自主權\nautonomous(adj.)自治的、自主的\npersonal autonomy 個人自主\nregional autonomy 地區自治\nTeenagers often want more autonomy in making their own decisions.\n(青少年常常希望在做決定時擁有更多自主權。)\nThe region was granted a high degree of autonomy.\n(該地區被賦予了高度自治權。)"],["awe","awe(n./v.)敬畏、驚嘆、使敬畏\nawesome(adj.)令人驚嘆的、很棒的\nawful(adj.)可怕的、糟糕的\nin awe of 對……敬畏\nstand in awe 肅然起敬\nWe stood in awe as we watched the sunrise from the top of Jade Mountain.\n(我們在玉山頂上看日出時心生敬畏。)\nThe young players were in awe of the famous coach.\n(年輕球員們對那位知名教練心懷敬畏。)"],["backyard","backyard(n.)後院\n(無詞性變化)\nin the backyard 在後院\nnot in my backyard 別在我家附近(鄰避)\nMy father planted several fruit trees in our backyard last spring.\n(我爸爸去年春天在我們家後院種了幾棵果樹。)\nMany residents oppose building a garbage plant in their own backyard.\n(許多居民反對在自家附近興建垃圾處理廠。)"],["ballot","ballot(n./v.)選票、無記名投票、投票表決\n(無詞性變化)\nsecret ballot 無記名投票\ncast a ballot 投票\nThe class leader was chosen by secret ballot this year.\n(今年班長是以無記名投票方式選出的。)\nMillions of citizens cast their ballots in the presidential election.\n(數百萬名公民在總統大選中投下了他們的選票。)"],["ban","ban(n./v.)禁令、禁止\n(無詞性變化)\na ban on 對…的禁令\nbe banned from 被禁止…\nThe government announced a ban on single-use plastic straws.\n(政府宣布禁止使用一次性塑膠吸管。)\nStudents are banned from using their phones during exams.\n(學生在考試期間禁止使用手機。)"],["banner","banner(n.)橫幅、旗幟、標語\n(無詞性變化)\nhang a banner 掛布條\nunder the banner of 打著…的旗號\nThe students hung a large banner to welcome the new principal.\n(學生們掛上一條大布條來歡迎新校長。)\nFans waved banners and shouted as the team entered the stadium.\n(球隊進場時，球迷們揮舞旗幟並大聲歡呼。)"],["barren","barren(adj.)貧瘠的、荒蕪的、不孕的\n(無詞性變化)\nbarren land 不毛之地\nbarren desert 荒涼的沙漠\nNothing could grow on the barren land after years of drought.\n(經過多年乾旱，這片貧瘠的土地上什麼都長不出來。)\nThe explorers walked for days across the barren desert.\n(探險家們在荒涼的沙漠中走了好幾天。)"],["batch","batch(n.)一批、一爐、一組\n(無詞性變化)\na batch of 一批…\nin batches 分批地\nMy mom baked a fresh batch of cookies for the school bazaar.\n(我媽媽為學校義賣烤了一批新鮮的餅乾。)\nThe new phones will be shipped to stores in batches.\n(新手機將分批運送到各家店面。)"],["behalf","behalf(n.)代表、利益\n(無詞性變化)\non behalf of 代表…\non sb.'s behalf 代表某人、為了某人\nOn behalf of our class, I would like to thank all the teachers.\n(我謹代表全班感謝所有的老師。)\nMy lawyer will speak on my behalf at the meeting.\n(我的律師將在會議上代表我發言。)"],["belongings","belongings(n.)財物、所有物\nbelong(v.)屬於\npersonal belongings 個人物品\npack one's belongings 收拾行李\nPlease take all your personal belongings with you when you leave the train.\n(下車時請攜帶您所有的隨身物品。)\nHe packed his belongings into two suitcases and moved out.\n(他把所有家當裝進兩個行李箱就搬出去了。)"],["beloved","beloved(adj./n.)心愛的、親愛的、心愛的人\nlove(v.)愛\nbeloved pet 心愛的寵物\ndearly beloved 最親愛的\nThe whole family was heartbroken when their beloved dog passed away.\n(心愛的狗過世時，全家人都非常傷心。)\nThe old singer is still beloved by fans of all ages.\n(那位資深歌手至今仍深受各年齡層歌迷的喜愛。)"],["beneficial","beneficial(adj.)有益的、有利的\nbenefit(n./v.)好處、得益\nbeneficiary(n.)受益人\nbeneficial to/for 對…有益\nmutually beneficial 互惠的\nGetting enough sleep is beneficial to both your body and your mind.\n(充足的睡眠對身體和心理都有益處。)\nThe two companies reached a mutually beneficial agreement.\n(這兩家公司達成了一項互惠的協議。)"],["betray","betray(v.)背叛、出賣、洩露\nbetrayal(n.)背叛\nbetray one's trust 辜負某人的信任\nbetray a secret 洩露祕密\nI will never forgive him for betraying my trust.\n(我永遠不會原諒他辜負了我的信任。)\nHer shaking voice betrayed how nervous she really was.\n(她顫抖的聲音洩露了她其實有多緊張。)"],["beware","beware(v.)當心、注意\n(無詞性變化)\nbeware of 小心…\nBeware of the dog. 內有惡犬。\nBeware of pickpockets when you travel in crowded places.\n(在擁擠的地方旅行時要小心扒手。)\nInternet users should beware of emails asking for personal information.\n(網路使用者應該留意要求提供個人資料的電子郵件。)"],["bias","bias(n./v.)偏見、偏袒、使有偏見\nbiased(adj.)有偏見的\nbias against 對…的偏見\ngender bias 性別偏見\nJudges must make decisions without any personal bias.\n(法官必須在沒有任何個人偏見的情況下做出判決。)\nSome news reports are biased in favor of one political party.\n(有些新聞報導偏袒某一個政黨。)"],["bid","bid(n./v.)出價、投標、努力爭取\nbidder(n.)出價者、投標者\nmake a bid 出價\nin a bid to 試圖…\nHe made a bid of five thousand dollars for the old painting.\n(他對那幅古畫出價五千元。)\nThe city cut taxes in a bid to attract more businesses.\n(該市降低稅收，試圖吸引更多企業進駐。)"],["biological","biological(adj.)生物的、生物學的、親生的\nbiology(n.)生物學\nbiologist(n.)生物學家\nbiological parents 親生父母\nbiological weapons 生物武器\nAfter growing up, she decided to look for her biological parents.\n(長大後，她決定尋找她的親生父母。)\nScientists study the biological effects of air pollution on children.\n(科學家研究空氣汙染對兒童造成的生物影響。)"],["bizarre","bizarre(adj.)古怪的、異乎尋常的\n(無詞性變化)\nbizarre behavior 古怪的行為\na bizarre story 離奇的故事\nEveryone was confused by his bizarre behavior at the party.\n(大家對他在派對上的古怪行為感到困惑。)\nThe newspaper reported a bizarre story about a cat that rode the bus every day.\n(報紙報導了一則有隻貓每天搭公車的離奇故事。)"],["blast","blast(n./v.)爆炸、一陣強風、大聲播放、炸開\n(無詞性變化)\na blast of 一陣…\nhave a blast 玩得很開心\nA blast of cold wind hit us as we opened the door.\n(我們一開門就被一陣冷風吹襲。)\nWe had a blast at the music festival last weekend.\n(我們上週末在音樂祭玩得超開心。)"],["blur","blur(n./v.)模糊的事物、使模糊\nblurry(adj.)模糊的\na blur of 一片模糊的…\nblur the line between 模糊…之間的界線\nWithout my glasses, everything is just a blur.\n(沒戴眼鏡時，所有東西都只是一片模糊。)\nSocial media has blurred the line between public and private life.\n(社群媒體模糊了公共生活與私人生活之間的界線。)"],["blush","blush(n./v.)臉紅、腮紅\n(無詞性變化)\nblush with embarrassment 尷尬得臉紅\nmake sb. blush 使某人臉紅\nShe blushed when her classmates praised her singing.\n(同學們稱讚她的歌聲時，她臉紅了。)\nHis sweet words made her blush with embarrassment.\n(他的甜言蜜語讓她害羞得臉紅。)"],["bodyguard","bodyguard(n.)保鑣、護衛\n(無詞性變化)\npersonal bodyguard 私人保鑣\nhire a bodyguard 雇用保鑣\nThe famous singer always travels with two bodyguards.\n(那位知名歌手總是帶著兩名保鑣出門。)\nThe rich businessman hired a bodyguard after receiving threats.\n(那位富商在收到威脅後雇用了一名保鑣。)"],["bolt","bolt(n./v.)門閂、螺栓、閃電、閂上、逃跑\n(無詞性變化)\na bolt of lightning 一道閃電\na bolt from the blue 晴天霹靂\nThe news of his sudden death came as a bolt from the blue.\n(他突然過世的消息宛如晴天霹靂。)\nThe frightened horse bolted when it heard the thunder.\n(受驚的馬聽到雷聲便狂奔逃跑。)"],["bonus","bonus(n.)獎金、紅利、額外的好處\n(無詞性變化)\nyear-end bonus 年終獎金\nan added bonus 額外的好處\nEmployees will receive a year-end bonus before the Lunar New Year.\n(員工將在農曆新年前領到年終獎金。)\nThe hotel is close to the beach, and the free breakfast is an added bonus.\n(這家飯店離海邊很近，免費早餐更是額外的好處。)"],["boom","boom(n./v.)繁榮、激增、隆隆聲、迅速發展\n(無詞性變化)\neconomic boom 經濟繁榮\nbaby boom 嬰兒潮\nThe country enjoyed an economic boom in the 1980s.\n(這個國家在一九八〇年代經歷了經濟繁榮。)\nOnline shopping has boomed in recent years.\n(網路購物近年來蓬勃發展。)"],["boost","boost(v./n.)提升、增加、促進、激勵\nbooster(n.)增強劑、加強針\nboost confidence 增強信心\nboost the economy 刺激經濟\nWinning the speech contest really boosted her confidence.\n(贏得演講比賽大大提升了她的自信心。)\nThe government hopes the new policy will give the economy a boost.\n(政府希望新政策能刺激經濟。)"],["booth","booth(n.)攤位、小隔間、亭子\n(無詞性變化)\nphone booth 電話亭\nticket booth 售票亭\nOur class set up a booth to sell drinks at the school fair.\n(我們班在校慶園遊會上設了一個攤位賣飲料。)\nThere are fewer and fewer phone booths on the streets these days.\n(現在街上的電話亭越來越少了。)"],["boredom","boredom(n.)無聊、厭倦\nbored(adj.)感到無聊的\nboring(adj.)令人無聊的\nout of boredom 出於無聊\nrelieve boredom 解悶\nHe started playing video games out of boredom during the long holiday.\n(長假期間，他出於無聊開始打電玩。)\nReading novels helps me relieve boredom on long train rides.\n(讀小說能幫我在漫長的火車旅程中解悶。)"],["bound","bound(v./n.)跳躍、以…為界、界限\nbound(adj.)一定的、受約束的、開往…的\nbe bound to 必然會…\nout of bounds 禁止進入、越界\nIf you keep practicing, you are bound to improve.\n(只要你持續練習，一定會進步。)\nThis area of the school is out of bounds to students after six p.m.\n(晚上六點以後，學生禁止進入校園的這個區域。)"],["boundary","boundary(n.)邊界、界限\n(無詞性變化)\nnational boundary 國界\nset boundaries 設定界限\nThe river forms a natural boundary between the two towns.\n(這條河形成兩個鎮之間的天然邊界。)\nIt is important to set clear boundaries in a friendship.\n(在友誼中設定清楚的界限是很重要的。)"],["boxer","boxer(n.)拳擊手\nbox(v.)拳擊\nboxing(n.)拳擊運動\nprofessional boxer 職業拳擊手\nboxer shorts 四角褲\nMuhammad Ali is one of the greatest boxers of all time.\n(穆罕默德·阿里是史上最偉大的拳擊手之一。)\nThe young boxer trains in the gym for six hours a day.\n(這位年輕拳擊手每天在健身房訓練六個小時。)"],["breakthrough","breakthrough(n.)突破、重大進展\n(無詞性變化)\na major breakthrough 重大突破\nmake a breakthrough 取得突破\nScientists have made a major breakthrough in cancer research.\n(科學家在癌症研究上取得了重大突破。)\nAfter months of practice, she finally had a breakthrough in her piano playing.\n(經過數月的練習，她的鋼琴演奏終於有了突破。)"],["briefcase","briefcase(n.)公事包\n(無詞性變化)\nleather briefcase 皮製公事包\ncarry a briefcase 提著公事包\nMy father carries an old leather briefcase to work every day.\n(我爸爸每天提著一個舊皮製公事包去上班。)\nHe opened his briefcase and took out a stack of documents.\n(他打開公事包，拿出一疊文件。)"],["bronze","bronze(n./adj.)青銅、銅牌、青銅色的\n(無詞性變化)\nbronze medal 銅牌\nBronze Age 青銅器時代\nOur school's team won a bronze medal in the national contest.\n(我們學校的隊伍在全國比賽中贏得一面銅牌。)\nThe museum displays bronze tools from ancient China.\n(博物館展示著來自古代中國的青銅器具。)"],["browse","browse(v./n.)瀏覽、隨意翻閱、逛\nbrowser(n.)瀏覽器\nbrowse the internet 瀏覽網路\nbrowse through 隨意翻閱\nI spent the afternoon browsing through magazines in the bookstore.\n(我花了一個下午在書店隨意翻閱雜誌。)\nMany people browse online stores before buying anything in person.\n(許多人在實體購物前會先瀏覽網路商店。)"],["bruise","bruise(n./v.)瘀傷、撞傷、使瘀傷\n(無詞性變化)\ncuts and bruises 割傷與瘀傷\na bruised ego 受挫的自尊\nHe fell off his bike and got a few cuts and bruises.\n(他從腳踏車上摔下來，受了一些割傷和瘀傷。)\nHandle the peaches carefully so you don't bruise them.\n(小心拿那些桃子，以免把它們碰傷。)"],["bulk","bulk(n.)大量、大部分、巨大的體積\nbulky(adj.)龐大的、笨重的\nin bulk 大量地、整批地\nthe bulk of 大部分的…\nBuying rice in bulk is cheaper for large families.\n(對大家庭來說，大量購買米比較便宜。)\nThe bulk of the work was done by volunteers.\n(大部分的工作是由志工完成的。)"],["bully","bully(n./v.)霸凌者、恃強欺弱的人、霸凌\nbullying(n.)霸凌\nschool bully 校園惡霸\nbe bullied 被霸凌\nStudents who are bullied should tell a teacher right away.\n(被霸凌的學生應該立刻告訴老師。)\nThe school has started a program to stop cyber bullying.\n(學校已推出一項防止網路霸凌的計畫。)"],["bureau","bureau(n.)局、處、事務所\n(無詞性變化)\nweather bureau 氣象局\ntourism bureau 觀光局\nThe Central Weather Bureau issued a typhoon warning this morning.\n(中央氣象局今天早上發布了颱風警報。)\nYou can get free maps from the tourism bureau.\n(你可以從觀光局拿到免費地圖。)"],["bureaucracy","bureaucracy(n.)官僚體制、官僚作風\nbureaucrat(n.)官僚\nbureaucratic(adj.)官僚的\ngovernment bureaucracy 政府官僚體系\ncut through bureaucracy 突破繁文縟節\nToo much bureaucracy slows down the decision-making process.\n(過多的官僚作風會拖慢決策的過程。)\nIt took months to cut through the bureaucracy and get the permit.\n(花了好幾個月突破繁瑣程序才拿到許可證。)"],["burial","burial(n.)埋葬、葬禮\nbury(v.)埋葬\nburial ground 墓地\nburial ceremony 葬禮\nThe ancient burial ground was discovered by local farmers.\n(那片古老的墓地是由當地農民發現的。)\nThe burial ceremony was attended only by close family members.\n(葬禮只有親近的家人出席。)"],["butcher","butcher(n./v.)屠夫、肉販、屠宰、殘殺\n(無詞性變化)\nbutcher shop 肉舖\nat the butcher's 在肉舖\nMy grandmother buys fresh pork from the butcher at the market.\n(我奶奶在市場向肉販買新鮮豬肉。)\nThe farmer butchered a pig for the village festival.\n(那位農夫為了村裡的節慶宰了一頭豬。)"],["calcium","calcium(n.)鈣\n(無詞性變化)\ncalcium intake 鈣攝取量\nrich in calcium 富含鈣質\nMilk and cheese are rich in calcium, which keeps your bones strong.\n(牛奶和起司富含鈣質，能讓骨骼強健。)\nOlder women are often advised to increase their calcium intake.\n(年長女性常被建議增加鈣的攝取量。)"],["canal","canal(n.)運河、(體內的)管道\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Panama Canal 巴拿馬運河\near canal 耳道\nTourists enjoy taking boat rides along the canals of Venice.\n(遊客喜歡沿著威尼斯的運河搭船遊覽。)\nThe Panama Canal connects the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans.\n(巴拿馬運河連接大西洋與太平洋。)"],["canvas","canvas(n./v.)帆布、畫布、遊說\n(無詞性變化)\ncanvas bag 帆布袋\noil on canvas 布面油畫\nShe carries her books in a sturdy canvas bag.\n(她用一個堅固的帆布袋裝書。)\nThe artist spent months painting on a huge canvas.\n(那位畫家花了好幾個月在一幅巨大的畫布上作畫。)"],["capability","capability(n.)能力、性能\ncapable(adj.)有能力的\nbeyond one's capability 超出能力範圍\nmilitary capability 軍事能力\nThe new smartphone has impressive camera capabilities.\n(這款新手機具有令人印象深刻的拍照性能。)\nSolving this problem alone is beyond my capability.\n(獨自解決這個問題超出我的能力範圍。)"],["carbon","carbon(n.)碳\n(無詞性變化)\ncarbon dioxide 二氧化碳\ncarbon footprint 碳足跡\nPlanting trees helps reduce the amount of carbon dioxide in the air.\n(種樹有助於減少空氣中的二氧化碳。)\nTaking public transportation can lower your carbon footprint.\n(搭乘大眾運輸可以降低你的碳足跡。)"],["carnival","carnival(n.)嘉年華會、狂歡節\n(無詞性變化)\ncarnival parade 嘉年華遊行\nRio Carnival 里約嘉年華\nMillions of people dance in the streets during the Rio Carnival.\n(里約嘉年華期間，數百萬人在街上跳舞。)\nOur school held a spring carnival with games and food stands.\n(我們學校舉辦了有遊戲和小吃攤的春季嘉年華。)"],["casino","casino(n.)賭場\n(無詞性變化)\ncasino resort 賭場度假村\nbuild a casino 興建賭場\nMacau is famous for its luxurious casinos and hotels.\n(澳門以豪華的賭場與飯店聞名。)\nResidents voted against the plan to build a casino on the island.\n(居民投票反對在島上興建賭場的計畫。)"],["cathedral","cathedral(n.)大教堂\n(無詞性變化)\nGothic cathedral 哥德式大教堂\ncathedral city 有大教堂的城市\nThe ancient cathedral attracts thousands of visitors every year.\n(那座古老的大教堂每年吸引數千名遊客。)\nNotre-Dame is one of the most famous Gothic cathedrals in the world.\n(聖母院是世界上最著名的哥德式大教堂之一。)"],["caution","caution(n./v.)小心、謹慎、警告\ncautious(adj.)謹慎的\nwith caution 謹慎地\ncaution against 警告不要\nDrivers should proceed with caution on wet and slippery roads.\n(駕駛在濕滑的路面上應謹慎行駛。)\nDoctors caution against taking too many painkillers.\n(醫生警告不要服用過多止痛藥。)"],["cautious","cautious(adj.)謹慎的、小心的\ncaution(n.)謹慎\ncautiously(adv.)謹慎地\nbe cautious about 對……謹慎\ncautious approach 謹慎的做法\nYou should be cautious about sharing personal information online.\n(在網路上分享個人資料時應該要謹慎。)\nThe government took a cautious approach to reopening the borders.\n(政府對開放邊境採取謹慎的做法。)"],["celebrity","celebrity(n.)名人、名氣\n(無詞性變化)\na famous celebrity 知名人士\ncelebrity culture 名人文化\nMany teenagers follow the daily lives of celebrities on social media.\n(許多青少年在社群媒體上追蹤名人的日常生活。)\nThe singer became an overnight celebrity after her video went viral.\n(那位歌手的影片爆紅後一夕成名。)"],["cemetery","cemetery(n.)墓地、公墓\n(無詞性變化)\npublic cemetery 公墓\nbe buried in a cemetery 葬在墓園\nMy family visits the cemetery every year during Tomb Sweeping Day.\n(我家每年清明節都會去墓園掃墓。)\nThe famous writer was buried in a quiet cemetery near his hometown.\n(那位知名作家被葬在他家鄉附近一座安靜的墓園。)"],["ceremony","ceremony(n.)典禮、儀式\nceremonial(adj.)儀式的\ngraduation ceremony 畢業典禮\nwedding ceremony 結婚典禮\nParents proudly watched their children at the graduation ceremony.\n(家長們在畢業典禮上自豪地看著孩子。)\nThe opening ceremony of the Olympics was watched by millions.\n(奧運開幕典禮有數百萬人觀看。)"],["certainty","certainty(n.)確定、必然的事\ncertain(adj.)確定的\ncertainly(adv.)當然\nwith certainty 確定地\na near certainty 幾乎確定的事\nNo one can predict the future with complete certainty.\n(沒有人能完全確定地預測未來。)\nIt is a near certainty that prices will rise next year.\n(明年物價上漲幾乎是確定的事。)"],["certificate","certificate(n./v.)證書、證明書、發證書給\ncertify(v.)證明\nbirth certificate 出生證明\naward a certificate 頒發證書\nYou need to show your birth certificate to apply for a passport.\n(申請護照需要出示出生證明。)\nEvery student who finished the course received a certificate.\n(每位完成課程的學生都獲得一張證書。)"],["chaos","chaos(n.)混亂\nchaotic(adj.)混亂的\nin chaos 一片混亂\ncause chaos 造成混亂\nThe sudden typhoon threw the whole city into chaos.\n(突如其來的颱風讓整座城市陷入一片混亂。)\nThe computer system failure caused chaos at the airport.\n(電腦系統故障在機場造成混亂。)"],["chapel","chapel(n.)小教堂、禮拜堂\n(無詞性變化)\nwedding chapel 婚禮教堂\nschool chapel 學校禮拜堂\nThe couple got married in a small chapel by the sea.\n(那對新人在海邊一間小教堂結婚。)\nStudents gather in the school chapel every Friday morning.\n(學生每週五早上聚集在學校禮拜堂。)"],["characterize","characterize(v.)以……為特徵、描述……的特性\ncharacter(n.)性格、特色\ncharacteristic(n./adj.)特徵、特有的\nbe characterized by 以……為特徵\ncharacterize as 把……描述為\nThe region is characterized by hot summers and mild winters.\n(這個地區的特色是夏季炎熱、冬季溫和。)\nCritics characterized the film as a masterpiece.\n(影評人將這部電影描述為傑作。)"],["chef","chef(n.)廚師、主廚\n(無詞性變化)\nhead chef 主廚\npastry chef 甜點師\nThe head chef created a special menu for the holiday season.\n(主廚為假期設計了特別菜單。)\nMy cousin dreams of becoming a pastry chef in Paris.\n(我表妹夢想在巴黎成為甜點師。)"],["choir","choir(n.)合唱團、唱詩班\n(無詞性變化)\nschool choir 學校合唱團\nsing in a choir 參加合唱團\nShe has sung in the school choir for three years.\n(她參加學校合唱團已經三年了。)\nThe choir performed beautifully at the Christmas concert.\n(合唱團在聖誕音樂會上表現得很精彩。)"],["chord","chord(n.)和弦、心弦\n(無詞性變化)\nguitar chord 吉他和弦\nstrike a chord 引起共鳴\nLearning a few basic chords is the first step to playing the guitar.\n(學會幾個基本和弦是彈吉他的第一步。)\nThe speech struck a chord with many young voters.\n(那場演說引起許多年輕選民的共鳴。)"],["chore","chore(n.)家務、雜事、討厭的工作\n(無詞性變化)\nhousehold chores 家務\ndo chores 做家事\nChildren should help with household chores like washing dishes.\n(孩子應該幫忙做洗碗之類的家事。)\nCleaning the bathroom is my least favorite chore.\n(打掃浴室是我最不喜歡的家事。)"],["chronic","chronic(adj.)慢性的、長期的\nchronically(adv.)長期地\nchronic disease 慢性病\nchronic shortage 長期短缺\nRegular exercise can lower the risk of chronic diseases.\n(規律運動能降低罹患慢性病的風險。)\nMany rural hospitals suffer from a chronic shortage of doctors.\n(許多偏鄉醫院長期缺乏醫生。)"],["chubby","chubby(adj.)圓胖的、胖嘟嘟的\n(無詞性變化)\nchubby cheeks 圓嘟嘟的臉頰\na chubby baby 胖嘟嘟的寶寶\nThe chubby baby smiled at everyone in the room.\n(那個胖嘟嘟的寶寶對房間裡的每個人微笑。)\nGrandma loves to pinch my little brother's chubby cheeks.\n(奶奶很愛捏我弟弟圓嘟嘟的臉頰。)"],["chunk","chunk(n.)厚塊、大部分\nchunky(adj.)厚實的\na chunk of 一大塊、一大部分\nin chunks 成塊地\nRent takes up a large chunk of his monthly salary.\n(房租佔了他月薪的一大部分。)\nCut the pineapple into chunks before serving.\n(上桌前把鳳梨切成塊。)"],["circuit","circuit(n.)電路、環行、巡迴\n(無詞性變化)\nelectrical circuit 電路\nshort circuit 短路\nA short circuit caused the fire in the old building.\n(短路引發了那棟老舊建築的火災。)\nStudents built a simple circuit to light a small bulb.\n(學生組裝了一個簡單的電路來點亮小燈泡。)"],["cite","cite(v.)引用、舉出(例子)\ncitation(n.)引用、引文\ncite an example 舉例\ncite a source 引用來源\nAlways cite your sources when you write a research paper.\n(寫研究報告時務必註明引用來源。)\nThe teacher cited several examples to explain the grammar rule.\n(老師舉了幾個例子來解釋這條文法規則。)"],["citizenship","citizenship(n.)公民身分、公民權\ncitizen(n.)公民\napply for citizenship 申請公民身分\ndual citizenship 雙重國籍\nShe holds dual citizenship in Taiwan and Canada.\n(她擁有台灣和加拿大的雙重國籍。)\nGood citizenship includes voting and obeying the law.\n(良好的公民素養包括投票與守法。)"],["civic","civic(adj.)市民的、公民的\n(無詞性變化)\ncivic duty 公民義務\ncivic center 市民中心\nVoting in elections is an important civic duty.\n(在選舉中投票是重要的公民義務。)\nThe concert will be held at the civic center downtown.\n(音樂會將在市中心的市民活動中心舉行。)"],["clarity","clarity(n.)清晰、清楚\nclarify(v.)闡明、澄清\nclear(adj.)清楚的\nwith clarity 清楚地\nlack of clarity 不夠清楚\nThe professor explained the complex theory with great clarity.\n(教授非常清楚地解釋了這個複雜的理論。)\nThe report was criticized for its lack of clarity.\n(這份報告因不夠清楚而受到批評。)"],["clause","clause(n.)子句、(法律)條款\n(無詞性變化)\nrelative clause 關係子句\na clause in the contract 合約中的條款\nA relative clause gives more information about a noun.\n(關係子句提供名詞的額外資訊。)\nRead every clause in the contract carefully before signing it.\n(簽約前要仔細閱讀合約中的每一項條款。)"],["cling","cling(v.)緊抓、黏著、堅守\n(無詞性變化)\ncling to 緊抓住、堅持\ncling together 緊緊靠在一起\nThe frightened child clung to her mother's arm.\n(那個受驚嚇的孩子緊抓著媽媽的手臂。)\nSome people still cling to old traditions.\n(有些人仍然堅守舊傳統。)"],["clinical","clinical(adj.)臨床的、冷靜客觀的\nclinic(n.)診所\nclinical trial 臨床試驗\nclinical experience 臨床經驗\nThe new vaccine is still in clinical trials.\n(這種新疫苗仍在臨床試驗階段。)\nMedical students gain clinical experience in hospitals.\n(醫學生在醫院累積臨床經驗。)"],["cluster","cluster(n./v.)群、串、聚集\n(無詞性變化)\na cluster of 一群、一串\ncluster around 聚集在周圍\nA cluster of small houses stood at the foot of the hill.\n(一群小房子坐落在山腳下。)\nFans clustered around the stage to see the singer.\n(歌迷聚集在舞台周圍看那位歌手。)"],["cocaine","cocaine(n.)古柯鹼\n(無詞性變化)\ncocaine addiction 古柯鹼成癮\ncocaine smuggling 古柯鹼走私\nPolice found a large amount of cocaine hidden in the ship.\n(警方在船上發現藏有大量古柯鹼。)\nCocaine is a highly addictive and illegal drug.\n(古柯鹼是一種極易成癮的非法毒品。)"],["coffin","coffin(n.)棺材、靈柩\n(無詞性變化)\nwooden coffin 木棺\na nail in the coffin 致命一擊\nThe coffin was carried slowly into the church.\n(靈柩被緩緩抬進教堂。)\nThe scandal was the final nail in the coffin of his career.\n(那件醜聞是他職業生涯的最後致命一擊。)"],["cognitive","cognitive(adj.)認知的\ncognition(n.)認知\ncognitive ability 認知能力\ncognitive development 認知發展\nReading to young children helps their cognitive development.\n(為幼兒朗讀有助於他們的認知發展。)\nLack of sleep can affect your cognitive abilities.\n(睡眠不足會影響你的認知能力。)"],["coherent","coherent(adj.)條理清楚的、連貫的\ncoherence(n.)連貫性\na coherent argument 條理分明的論點\ncoherent plan 一致的計畫\nYour essay needs a more coherent structure.\n(你的文章需要更有條理的結構。)\nHe was so tired that he couldn't give a coherent answer.\n(他累到無法給出有條理的回答。)"],["coincidence","coincidence(n.)巧合\ncoincide(v.)同時發生、一致\ncoincidental(adj.)巧合的\nby coincidence 碰巧\npure coincidence 純屬巧合\nBy coincidence, my new classmate lives on my street.\n(碰巧我的新同學就住在我家那條街。)\nIt was pure coincidence that we wore the same dress.\n(我們穿了同一件洋裝純屬巧合。)"],["collaboration","collaboration(n.)合作、協作\ncollaborate(v.)合作\ncollaborative(adj.)合作的\nin collaboration with 與……合作\nclose collaboration 密切合作\nThe project was completed in collaboration with a local university.\n(這個計畫是與當地大學合作完成的。)\nClose collaboration between teachers and parents benefits students.\n(師長與家長的密切合作對學生有益。)"],["collective","collective(adj./n.)集體的、共同的、集體\ncollectively(adv.)集體地\ncollective effort 集體努力\ncollective memory 集體記憶\nCleaning up the beach was a collective effort by the whole class.\n(淨灘是全班共同努力的成果。)\nThe war remains part of the nation's collective memory.\n(那場戰爭仍是這個國家集體記憶的一部分。)"],["collector","collector(n.)收藏家、收集者\ncollect(v.)收集\ncollection(n.)收藏品\nart collector 藝術收藏家\nstamp collector 集郵者\nThe painting was sold to a wealthy art collector.\n(那幅畫賣給了一位富有的藝術收藏家。)\nMy uncle is a serious stamp collector.\n(我叔叔是個認真的集郵者。)"],["colonial","colonial(adj./n.)殖民(地)的、殖民地居民\ncolony(n.)殖民地\ncolonize(v.)殖民\ncolonial rule 殖民統治\ncolonial period 殖民時期\nMany buildings from the colonial period still stand in the old town.\n(老城區仍保留許多殖民時期的建築。)\nThe country gained independence after years of colonial rule.\n(那個國家在多年殖民統治後獲得獨立。)"],["columnist","columnist(n.)專欄作家\ncolumn(n.)專欄、柱子\nnewspaper columnist 報紙專欄作家\nsports columnist 體育專欄作家\nThe columnist writes about education issues every Sunday.\n(那位專欄作家每週日撰寫教育議題。)\nShe became a popular newspaper columnist after college.\n(她大學畢業後成為受歡迎的報紙專欄作家。)"],["combat","combat(n./v.)戰鬥、對抗、打擊\ncombatant(n.)戰鬥人員\ncombat climate change 對抗氣候變遷\nin combat 在戰鬥中\nThe government launched a campaign to combat air pollution.\n(政府發起一項打擊空氣汙染的運動。)\nMany young soldiers were killed in combat.\n(許多年輕士兵在戰鬥中喪生。)"],["comedian","comedian(n.)喜劇演員\ncomedy(n.)喜劇\nstand-up comedian 單口喜劇演員\nfamous comedian 知名喜劇演員\nThe stand-up comedian made the whole audience laugh.\n(那位單口喜劇演員讓全場觀眾大笑。)\nHe dreams of becoming a comedian on television.\n(他夢想成為電視上的喜劇演員。)"],["commentary","commentary(n.)評論、實況報導\ncomment(n./v.)評論\nlive commentary 現場實況報導\npolitical commentary 政治評論\nWe listened to the live commentary of the baseball game on the radio.\n(我們收聽收音機上棒球比賽的現場轉播。)\nThe book offers a sharp commentary on modern society.\n(這本書對現代社會提出尖銳的評論。)"],["commentator","commentator(n.)評論員、實況播報員\ncomment(n./v.)評論\nsports commentator 體育主播\npolitical commentator 政治評論員\nThe sports commentator got excited when the player hit a home run.\n(球員擊出全壘打時，體育主播興奮不已。)\nPolitical commentators disagreed about the election results.\n(政治評論員對選舉結果意見分歧。)"],["commission","commission(n./v.)委員會、佣金、委託\ncommissioner(n.)委員、專員\non commission 按佣金計酬\ncommission a painting 委託作畫\nSalespeople at the store work on commission.\n(那家店的銷售人員按佣金計酬。)\nThe city commissioned an artist to design the new statue.\n(市政府委託一位藝術家設計新雕像。)"],["commitment","commitment(n.)承諾、投入、獻身\ncommit(v.)承諾、犯(罪)\ncommitted(adj.)投入的\nmake a commitment 做出承諾\ncommitment to 對……的投入\nThe company made a commitment to reduce plastic waste.\n(該公司承諾減少塑膠廢棄物。)\nHer commitment to helping others is truly admirable.\n(她對助人的投入真的令人欽佩。)"],["commodity","commodity(n.)商品、日用品\n(無詞性變化)\nbasic commodities 基本民生用品\ncommodity prices 商品價格\nRising commodity prices have made life harder for many families.\n(商品價格上漲讓許多家庭的生活更加艱難。)\nIn the desert, water is a precious commodity.\n(在沙漠中，水是寶貴的物資。)"],["communism","communism(n.)共產主義\ncommunist(n./adj.)共產主義者、共產主義的\nthe fall of communism 共產主義的瓦解\nunder communism 在共產主義下\nThe fall of communism in Eastern Europe changed world politics.\n(東歐共產主義的瓦解改變了世界政治。)\nMany people lost their property under communism.\n(許多人在共產主義統治下失去財產。)"],["communist","communist(adj./n.)共產主義的、共產黨員\ncommunism(n.)共產主義\nCommunist Party 共產黨\ncommunist country 共產國家\nCuba is one of the few remaining communist countries.\n(古巴是少數僅存的共產國家之一。)\nHe joined the Communist Party when he was young.\n(他年輕時加入了共產黨。)"],["commute","commute(v.)通勤\ncommuter(n.)通勤者\ncommute to work 通勤上班\ndaily commute 每日通勤\nShe commutes to Taipei by high-speed rail every day.\n(她每天搭高鐵通勤到台北。)\nMany people commute more than an hour each way.\n(許多人單程通勤超過一小時。)"],["commuter","commuter(n.)通勤者\ncommute(v.)通勤\ncommuter train 通勤列車\ndaily commuters 每日通勤族\nThe MRT is packed with commuters during rush hour.\n(尖峰時段捷運擠滿了通勤族。)\nMany commuters read the news on their phones on the train.\n(許多通勤族在火車上用手機看新聞。)"],["compact","compact(adj./n./v.)小巧的、緊密的、小型車、壓緊\n(無詞性變化)\ncompact car 小型車\ncompact design 輕巧設計\nThis camera is compact enough to fit in your pocket.\n(這台相機小巧到可以放進口袋。)\nThey bought a compact car that is easy to park in the city.\n(他們買了一台在市區好停車的小型車。)"],["comparable","comparable(adj.)可比較的、相當的\ncompare(v.)比較\ncomparison(n.)比較\ncomparable to 可與……相比\ncomparable quality 品質相當\nThe new model offers quality comparable to more expensive brands.\n(新款的品質可與更昂貴的品牌相比。)\nSalaries here are not comparable with those in big cities.\n(這裡的薪資無法與大城市相比。)"],["compassion","compassion(n.)同情、憐憫\ncompassionate(adj.)有同情心的\nshow compassion 表現同情\ncompassion for 對……的同情\nThe nurse treated every patient with kindness and compassion.\n(那位護理師以仁慈和同情心對待每位病患。)\nWe should show compassion for people in need.\n(我們應該對需要幫助的人表達同情。)"],["compassionate","compassionate(adj.)有同情心的、慈悲的\ncompassion(n.)同情\ncompassionate leave 喪假、事假\na compassionate person 富同情心的人\nShe is a compassionate person who always helps stray animals.\n(她是個有同情心的人，總是幫助流浪動物。)\nDoctors should be both skilled and compassionate.\n(醫生應該既有專業技術又有同理心。)"],["compatible","compatible(adj.)相容的、合得來的\ncompatibility(n.)相容性\nincompatible(adj.)不相容的\ncompatible with 與……相容\nhighly compatible 高度相容\nThis software is not compatible with older computers.\n(這套軟體與較舊的電腦不相容。)\nThe roommates turned out to be very compatible.\n(那兩位室友結果非常合得來。)"],["compel","compel(v.)強迫、迫使\ncompelling(adj.)令人信服的、引人入勝的\ncompulsion(n.)強迫\nbe compelled to 被迫\nfeel compelled to 覺得不得不\nHeavy rain compelled the organizers to cancel the concert.\n(大雨迫使主辦單位取消音樂會。)\nI felt compelled to tell her the truth.\n(我覺得不得不告訴她實話。)"],["compensate","compensate(v.)補償、彌補\ncompensation(n.)補償、賠償\ncompensate for 彌補\nbe compensated for 獲得……的賠償\nHard work can compensate for a lack of talent.\n(努力可以彌補天分的不足。)\nPassengers were compensated for the delayed flight.\n(乘客因班機延誤獲得補償。)"],["compensation","compensation(n.)補償、賠償金、報酬\ncompensate(v.)補償\nclaim compensation 要求賠償\nin compensation for 作為……的補償\nThe victims of the accident received compensation from the company.\n(事故受害者獲得公司的賠償。)\nHe received a free meal in compensation for the long wait.\n(他因久候而獲得一份免費餐點作為補償。)"],["competence","competence(n.)能力、勝任\ncompetent(adj.)能勝任的\nincompetence(n.)無能\nlanguage competence 語言能力\nprofessional competence 專業能力\nThe job requires a high level of competence in English.\n(這份工作要求很高的英文能力。)\nHer professional competence earned her a promotion.\n(她的專業能力為她贏得了升遷。)"],["competent","competent(adj.)有能力的、能勝任的\ncompetence(n.)能力\nincompetent(adj.)無能的\ncompetent at 擅長\na competent teacher 稱職的老師\nShe is a competent leader who makes wise decisions.\n(她是個做事明智、能力很強的領導者。)\nYou need to be competent at using computers for this job.\n(這份工作你需要能熟練使用電腦。)"],["complexity","complexity(n.)複雜性\ncomplex(adj.)複雜的\nthe complexity of 的複雜性\nincreasing complexity 日益增加的複雜度\nMany students underestimate the complexity of the problem.\n(許多學生低估了這個問題的複雜性。)\nThe complexity of modern life can cause a lot of stress.\n(現代生活的複雜度會造成很大的壓力。)"],["compliance","compliance(n.)遵守、順從\ncomply(v.)遵守\ncompliant(adj.)順從的、符合規定的\nin compliance with 遵照\nensure compliance 確保遵守\nAll factories must operate in compliance with safety regulations.\n(所有工廠都必須遵照安全法規運作。)\nInspectors check restaurants to ensure compliance with hygiene rules.\n(稽查員檢查餐廳以確保其遵守衛生規定。)"],["complication","complication(n.)併發症、複雜化的因素\ncomplicate(v.)使複雜\ncomplicated(adj.)複雜的\nserious complications 嚴重併發症\nfurther complications 進一步的麻煩\nThe surgery went well without any complications.\n(手術很順利，沒有任何併發症。)\nBad weather added another complication to our travel plans.\n(惡劣天氣讓我們的旅行計畫又多了一層麻煩。)"],["compliment","compliment(n./v.)讚美、恭維\ncomplimentary(adj.)讚美的、免費贈送的\npay a compliment 讚美\ntake it as a compliment 視為讚美\nMy teacher complimented me on my clear presentation.\n(老師稱讚我的報告很清楚。)\nThank you, I'll take that as a compliment.\n(謝謝，我就當作是讚美了。)"],["comply","comply(v.)遵守、依從\ncompliance(n.)遵守\ncomply with 遵守\nrefuse to comply 拒絕服從\nAll visitors must comply with the museum's rules.\n(所有參觀者都必須遵守博物館的規定。)\nThe company refused to comply with the court's order.\n(那家公司拒絕遵從法院的命令。)"],["component","component(n./adj.)成分、零件、組成的\n(無詞性變化)\nkey component 關鍵要素\nelectronic components 電子零件\nTrust is a key component of any healthy relationship.\n(信任是任何健康關係的關鍵要素。)\nTaiwan exports many electronic components to the world.\n(台灣向全世界出口許多電子零件。)"],["compound","compound(n./v./adj.)化合物、複合的、使惡化、(圍起的)場地\n(無詞性變化)\nchemical compound 化合物\ncompound word 複合字\nWater is a compound of hydrogen and oxygen.\n(水是氫和氧的化合物。)\nHis rude reply only compounded the problem.\n(他無禮的回答只讓問題更加惡化。)"],["comprehend","comprehend(v.)理解\ncomprehension(n.)理解力\ncomprehensive(adj.)全面的\nfail to comprehend 無法理解\nfully comprehend 完全理解\nIt is hard to comprehend how big the universe really is.\n(很難理解宇宙究竟有多大。)\nThe young child could not comprehend why his parents were upset.\n(那個小孩無法理解父母為何生氣。)"],["comprehension","comprehension(n.)理解、理解力\ncomprehend(v.)理解\nreading comprehension 閱讀理解\nbeyond comprehension 難以理解\nThe English exam includes a reading comprehension section.\n(英文考試包含閱讀理解題組。)\nThe scale of the disaster was beyond comprehension.\n(那場災難的規模令人難以想像。)"],["comprise","comprise(v.)包含、由……組成\n(無詞性變化)\nbe comprised of 由……組成\ncomprise the majority 構成多數\nThe committee comprises ten teachers and five students.\n(委員會由十位老師和五位學生組成。)\nWomen comprise more than half of the company's workforce.\n(女性佔該公司員工的一半以上。)"],["compromise","compromise(n./v.)妥協、讓步、危及\n(無詞性變化)\nreach a compromise 達成妥協\ncompromise on 在……讓步\nAfter a long discussion, the two sides reached a compromise.\n(經過長時間討論，雙方達成了妥協。)\nWe should never compromise our safety for speed.\n(我們絕不該為了速度而犧牲安全。)"],["compulsory","compulsory(adj.)義務的、強制的\n(無詞性變化)\ncompulsory education 義務教育\ncompulsory course 必修課\nTaiwan provides twelve years of compulsory education.\n(台灣提供十二年國民基本教育。)\nPhysical education is a compulsory course in high school.\n(體育是高中的必修課。)"],["conceal","conceal(v.)隱藏、隱瞞\nconcealment(n.)隱藏\nconceal the truth 隱瞞真相\nconceal one's feelings 隱藏感情\nShe tried hard to conceal her disappointment.\n(她努力掩飾自己的失望。)\nThe company was accused of concealing important information.\n(該公司被指控隱瞞重要資訊。)"],["concede","concede(v.)承認、讓步、認輸\nconcession(n.)讓步\nconcede defeat 認輸\nconcede that 承認……\nThe candidate conceded defeat on election night.\n(那位候選人在選舉當晚承認敗選。)\nHe reluctantly conceded that he had made a mistake.\n(他不情願地承認自己犯了錯。)"],["conceive","conceive(v.)構想、想像、懷孕\nconception(n.)概念、構想\nconcept(n.)概念\nconceive of 想像\nconceive an idea 構思想法\nIt is hard to conceive of life without the Internet.\n(很難想像沒有網路的生活。)\nThe idea for the app was conceived by two students.\n(這個應用程式的構想是由兩名學生想出來的。)"],["conception","conception(n.)概念、構想、受孕\nconceive(v.)構想、懷孕\na clear conception 清楚的概念\nfrom conception to completion 從構想到完成\nChildren often have a different conception of time.\n(孩子對時間往往有不同的概念。)\nThe project took three years from conception to completion.\n(這個計畫從構想到完成花了三年。)"],["condemn","condemn(v.)譴責、判刑\ncondemnation(n.)譴責\nstrongly condemn 強烈譴責\nbe condemned to 被判處\nWorld leaders strongly condemned the terrorist attack.\n(世界各國領袖強烈譴責這起恐怖攻擊。)\nThe prisoner was condemned to life in prison.\n(那名犯人被判處終身監禁。)"],["conduct","conduct(v./n.)進行、指揮、行為\nconductor(n.)指揮、導體、車掌\nconduct a survey 進行調查\ncode of conduct 行為準則\nThe class conducted a survey on students' sleeping habits.\n(全班針對學生睡眠習慣進行了一項調查。)\nHis conduct at the ceremony was praised by everyone.\n(他在典禮上的表現受到大家讚揚。)"],["confession","confession(n.)坦白、招供、懺悔\nconfess(v.)坦白、招認\nmake a confession 坦白\na full confession 完整招供\nHe made a confession that he had broken the window.\n(他坦白承認窗戶是他打破的。)\nThe suspect gave a full confession to the police.\n(嫌犯向警方完整招供。)"],["confidential","confidential(adj.)機密的\nconfidentiality(n.)機密性\nconfidential information 機密資訊\nstrictly confidential 嚴格保密\nPatients' medical records are strictly confidential.\n(病患的病歷是嚴格保密的。)\nPlease keep this information confidential.\n(請對這項資訊保密。)"],["confine","confine(v.)限制、侷限、監禁\nconfinement(n.)監禁、限制\nbe confined to 侷限於\nconfine oneself to 只限於\nPlease confine your answer to two hundred words.\n(請將你的回答限制在兩百字以內。)\nThe illness kept him confined to bed for a week.\n(這場病讓他臥床一週。)"],["conform","conform(v.)遵守、順從、符合\nconformity(n.)順從、一致\nconform to 遵守、符合\npressure to conform 從眾壓力\nTeenagers often feel pressure to conform to their peers.\n(青少年常感到要順從同儕的壓力。)\nAll products must conform to safety standards.\n(所有產品都必須符合安全標準。)"],["confront","confront(v.)面對、對抗、使面臨\nconfrontation(n.)對抗、衝突\nconfront a problem 面對問題\nbe confronted with 面臨\nWe must confront the problem instead of avoiding it.\n(我們必須面對問題，而不是逃避。)\nThe government is confronted with a serious economic crisis.\n(政府正面臨嚴重的經濟危機。)"],["confrontation","confrontation(n.)對抗、衝突\nconfront(v.)面對、對抗\navoid confrontation 避免衝突\nviolent confrontation 暴力衝突\nShe prefers to avoid confrontation with her coworkers.\n(她傾向避免和同事起衝突。)\nThe protest ended in a violent confrontation with the police.\n(抗議最後演變為與警方的暴力衝突。)"],["consecutive","consecutive(adj.)連續的\nconsecutively(adv.)連續地\nthree consecutive days 連續三天\nconsecutive wins 連勝\nIt has rained for five consecutive days.\n(已經連續下了五天雨。)\nThe team won the championship for the third consecutive year.\n(那支隊伍連續第三年奪得冠軍。)"],["consensus","consensus(n.)共識、一致意見\n(無詞性變化)\nreach a consensus 達成共識\ngeneral consensus 普遍共識\nThe class finally reached a consensus on where to go for the trip.\n(全班終於對旅行地點達成共識。)\nThere is a general consensus that smoking harms health.\n(大家普遍認同吸菸有害健康。)"],["consent","consent(n./v.)同意、許可\n(無詞性變化)\nparental consent 家長同意\nconsent to 同意\nStudents need parental consent to join the trip.\n(學生需要家長同意才能參加這次旅行。)\nShe finally consented to the plan.\n(她最後同意了這個計畫。)"],["conservation","conservation(n.)保護、保育、節約\nconserve(v.)保存、節約\nconservationist(n.)保育人士\nwildlife conservation 野生動物保育\nenergy conservation 節約能源\nWildlife conservation is important to protect endangered species.\n(野生動物保育對保護瀕危物種很重要。)\nThe school started a campaign for energy conservation.\n(學校發起了節約能源的活動。)"],["considerate","considerate(adj.)體貼的\nconsideration(n.)考慮、體貼\ninconsiderate(adj.)不體貼的\nconsiderate of 體貼……\nkind and considerate 和善體貼\nIt was considerate of you to bring me soup when I was sick.\n(你在我生病時帶湯給我真是體貼。)\nBe considerate of others and keep your voice down on the train.\n(在火車上要體貼他人，降低音量。)"],["constitutional","constitutional(adj./n.)憲法的、體質的、(健身)散步\nconstitution(n.)憲法、體質\nconstitutional right 憲法權利\nconstitutional reform 修憲\nFreedom of speech is a constitutional right in many countries.\n(言論自由在許多國家是憲法保障的權利。)\nThe government is discussing constitutional reform.\n(政府正在討論修憲。)"],["constraint","constraint(n.)限制、約束\nconstrain(v.)限制、約束\ntime constraints 時間限制\nbudget constraints 預算限制\nDue to time constraints, we could only visit two museums.\n(由於時間有限，我們只能參觀兩間博物館。)\nBudget constraints forced the school to cancel the trip.\n(預算限制迫使學校取消了旅行。)"],["consultation","consultation(n.)諮詢、商議、看診\nconsult(v.)諮詢、請教\nconsultant(n.)顧問\nin consultation with 與……商議\nfree consultation 免費諮詢\nThe plan was made in consultation with local residents.\n(這項計畫是與當地居民商議後制定的。)\nThe clinic offers a free consultation for new patients.\n(這家診所為初診病患提供免費諮詢。)"],["consumption","consumption(n.)消耗、消費、食用\nconsume(v.)消耗、食用\nconsumer(n.)消費者\nenergy consumption 能源消耗\nsugar consumption 糖分攝取\nTurning off unused lights can reduce energy consumption.\n(關掉沒在用的燈可以減少能源消耗。)\nDoctors recommend cutting down on sugar consumption.\n(醫生建議減少糖分攝取。)"],["contagious","contagious(adj.)傳染性的、有感染力的\ncontagion(n.)接觸傳染\nhighly contagious 高度傳染性的\ncontagious laughter 有感染力的笑聲\nThe flu is highly contagious, so please stay home if you are sick.\n(流感傳染性很高，生病時請待在家裡。)\nHer contagious laughter made everyone in the room smile.\n(她極具感染力的笑聲讓房間裡每個人都笑了。)"],["contaminate","contaminate(v.)汙染、弄髒\ncontamination(n.)汙染\ncontaminated water 受汙染的水\ncontaminate food 汙染食物\nChemicals from the factory contaminated the river.\n(工廠排放的化學物質汙染了河川。)\nWash your hands carefully to avoid contaminating the food.\n(仔細洗手以避免汙染食物。)"],["contemplate","contemplate(v.)沉思、考慮、凝視\ncontemplation(n.)沉思\ncontemplate doing 考慮做\ncontemplate the future 思考未來\nShe is contemplating studying abroad after graduation.\n(她正在考慮畢業後出國留學。)\nHe sat by the lake, contemplating the meaning of life.\n(他坐在湖邊沉思人生的意義。)"],["contemporary","contemporary(adj./n.)當代的、同時代的、同時代的人\n(無詞性變化)\ncontemporary art 當代藝術\ncontemporary of 與……同時代的人\nThe museum is showing an exhibition of contemporary art.\n(美術館正在舉辦當代藝術展。)\nShakespeare was a contemporary of Queen Elizabeth I.\n(莎士比亞與伊莉莎白一世是同時代的人。)"],["contempt","contempt(n.)輕視、鄙視\ncontemptuous(adj.)輕蔑的\nwith contempt 輕蔑地\nhold in contempt 鄙視\nHe looked at the cheater with contempt.\n(他輕蔑地看著那個作弊的人。)\nMany citizens hold corrupt politicians in contempt.\n(許多市民鄙視貪腐的政客。)"],["contend","contend(v.)競爭、爭奪、主張\ncontender(n.)競爭者\ncontention(n.)爭論、論點\ncontend for 爭奪\ncontend with 應付、對付\nFive teams are contending for the championship.\n(有五支隊伍正在爭奪冠軍。)\nFarmers have to contend with unpredictable weather every year.\n(農民每年都必須應付難以預測的天氣。)"],["continental","continental(adj.)大陸的、歐洲大陸的\ncontinent(n.)大陸、洲\ncontinental breakfast 歐陸式早餐\ncontinental climate 大陸型氣候\nThe hotel offers a free continental breakfast every morning.\n(飯店每天早上提供免費的歐陸式早餐。)\nPlaces with a continental climate have hot summers and cold winters.\n(大陸型氣候的地區夏季炎熱、冬季寒冷。)"],["contractor","contractor(n.)承包商、立約人\ncontract(n./v.)合約、訂約\nbuilding contractor 建築承包商\nhire a contractor 僱用承包商\nWe hired a contractor to repair the roof.\n(我們僱用了一位承包商來修屋頂。)\nThe building contractor promised to finish the project on time.\n(建築承包商承諾準時完工。)"],["contradiction","contradiction(n.)矛盾、反駁\ncontradict(v.)與……矛盾、反駁\ncontradictory(adj.)矛盾的\nin contradiction to 與……矛盾\na contradiction in terms 自相矛盾的說法\nHis actions are in contradiction to what he says.\n(他的行為與他說的話互相矛盾。)\nThere are several contradictions in the witness's story.\n(證人的說法中有幾處矛盾。)"],["controversial","controversial(adj.)有爭議的\ncontroversy(n.)爭議\ncontroversial issue 有爭議的議題\nhighly controversial 極具爭議的\nThe death penalty remains a controversial issue in Taiwan.\n(死刑在台灣仍是具爭議的議題。)\nThe movie's ending was highly controversial among fans.\n(這部電影的結局在影迷間極具爭議。)"],["controversy","controversy(n.)爭議、爭論\ncontroversial(adj.)有爭議的\ncause controversy 引起爭議\npolitical controversy 政治爭議\nThe new school uniform policy caused a lot of controversy.\n(新的校服政策引發了許多爭議。)\nThe singer's comments sparked controversy online.\n(那位歌手的言論在網路上引起爭議。)"],["conversion","conversion(n.)轉換、改變、改裝\nconvert(v.)轉換\nconversion rate 換算率、轉換率\nenergy conversion 能源轉換\nThe conversion of the old factory into a museum took two years.\n(把舊工廠改建成博物館花了兩年。)\nSolar panels allow the conversion of sunlight into electricity.\n(太陽能板能將陽光轉換成電力。)"],["convert","convert(v.)轉換、改變、改裝\nconversion(n.)轉換\nconvertible(adj.)可轉換的\nconvert into 轉換成\nconvert currency 兌換貨幣\nThey converted the garage into a small study room.\n(他們把車庫改裝成一間小書房。)\nYou can convert US dollars into NT dollars at the airport.\n(你可以在機場把美元兌換成新台幣。)"],["convict","convict(v./n.)判……有罪、囚犯\nconviction(n.)定罪、信念\nbe convicted of 被判……罪\nescaped convict 逃犯\nThe man was convicted of stealing a car.\n(那名男子被判竊車罪。)\nPolice are searching for an escaped convict.\n(警方正在搜捕一名逃犯。)"],["conviction","conviction(n.)信念、確信、定罪\nconvict(v.)判……有罪\nconvince(v.)說服\nstrong conviction 堅定的信念\nprevious conviction 前科\nShe spoke with deep conviction about protecting the environment.\n(她以堅定的信念談論保護環境。)\nHe had no previous convictions before this case.\n(在這起案件之前他沒有前科。)"],["coordinate","coordinate(v./n./adj.)協調、座標、同等的\ncoordination(n.)協調\ncoordinator(n.)協調者\ncoordinate efforts 協調努力\nmap coordinates 地圖座標\nThe teacher coordinated the activities for the school festival.\n(老師協調了校慶的各項活動。)\nRescue teams used GPS coordinates to find the lost hikers.\n(搜救隊利用GPS座標找到迷路的登山客。)"],["copyright","copyright(n./v.)著作權、版權、取得版權\n(無詞性變化)\ncopyright law 著作權法\nviolate copyright 侵犯著作權\nDownloading movies without permission may violate copyright law.\n(未經許可下載電影可能違反著作權法。)\nThe author holds the copyright to all her books.\n(那位作家擁有她所有著作的版權。)"],["core","core(n.)核心、果核\n(無詞性變化)\ncore values 核心價值\napple core 蘋果核\nHonesty is one of the core values of our school.\n(誠實是我們學校的核心價值之一。)\nHe threw the apple core into the trash can.\n(他把蘋果核丟進垃圾桶。)"],["corporate","corporate(adj.)公司的、企業的、團體的\ncorporation(n.)公司、企業\ncorporate culture 企業文化\ncorporate responsibility 企業責任\nMany young people prefer a relaxed corporate culture.\n(許多年輕人偏好輕鬆的企業文化。)\nCompanies are expected to take corporate social responsibility seriously.\n(企業被期望認真看待企業社會責任。)"],["corporation","corporation(n.)公司、企業、法人\ncorporate(adj.)公司的\nmultinational corporation 跨國企業\nlarge corporation 大企業\nShe works for a multinational corporation in Taipei.\n(她在台北的一家跨國企業工作。)\nLarge corporations have great influence on the economy.\n(大企業對經濟有很大的影響力。)"],["correlation","correlation(n.)相關性、關聯\ncorrelate(v.)相關、使相互關聯\nstrong correlation 高度相關\ncorrelation between 之間的相關性\nStudies show a strong correlation between sleep and academic performance.\n(研究顯示睡眠與學業表現高度相關。)\nThere is no clear correlation between height and intelligence.\n(身高和智力之間沒有明顯的相關性。)"],["correspondent","correspondent(n.)特派員、記者、通信者\ncorrespond(v.)通信、相符\ncorrespondence(n.)通信、一致\nforeign correspondent 駐外記者\nwar correspondent 戰地記者\nShe worked as a foreign correspondent in Japan for five years.\n(她曾在日本擔任駐外記者五年。)\nThe war correspondent risked his life to report the truth.\n(那位戰地記者冒著生命危險報導真相。)"],["corridor","corridor(n.)走廊、通道\n(無詞性變化)\nlong corridor 長廊\ndown the corridor 沿著走廊\nThe principal's office is at the end of the corridor.\n(校長室在走廊的盡頭。)\nStudents are not allowed to run in the corridors.\n(學生不准在走廊上奔跑。)"],["corrupt","corrupt(adj./v.)貪汙的、腐敗的、使腐化\ncorruption(n.)貪汙、腐敗\ncorrupt official 貪官\ncorrupt files 損毀檔案\nThe corrupt official was arrested for taking bribes.\n(那名貪官因收賄被捕。)\nPower can easily corrupt people.\n(權力很容易使人腐化。)"],["corruption","corruption(n.)貪汙、腐敗\ncorrupt(adj./v.)腐敗的、使腐化\nfight corruption 打擊貪腐\npolitical corruption 政治腐敗\nThe new mayor promised to fight corruption in the city government.\n(新市長承諾打擊市政府的貪腐。)\nPolitical corruption damages people's trust in the government.\n(政治腐敗會損害人民對政府的信任。)"],["counsel","counsel(n./v.)忠告、勸告、法律顧問、提供諮詢\ncounseling(n.)諮商、輔導\nseek counsel 尋求建議\ncounsel against 勸告不要\nMy teacher counseled me to think carefully before choosing a major.\n(老師勸我在選科系前仔細思考。)\nThe lawyer counseled against signing the contract.\n(律師勸告不要簽那份合約。)"],["counselor","counselor(n.)輔導老師、顧問\ncounsel(n./v.)勸告、諮詢\nschool counselor 學校輔導老師\ncareer counselor 生涯顧問\nYou can talk to the school counselor if you feel stressed.\n(如果你感到有壓力，可以找學校輔導老師談談。)\nA career counselor helped her choose the right university program.\n(一位生涯顧問幫她選擇了合適的大學科系。)"],["courteous","courteous(adj.)有禮貌的、謙恭的\ncourtesy(n.)禮貌\ncourteously(adv.)有禮貌地\ncourteous service 有禮的服務\nbe courteous to 對……有禮貌\nThe hotel staff were courteous and helpful.\n(飯店員工有禮貌又樂於助人。)\nAlways be courteous to others, even when you disagree.\n(即使意見不同，也要對他人保持禮貌。)"],["coverage","coverage(n.)新聞報導、涵蓋範圍、保險範圍\ncover(v./n.)涵蓋、報導\nmedia coverage 媒體報導\ninsurance coverage 保險給付範圍\nThe earthquake received wide media coverage around the world.\n(這場地震受到全球媒體廣泛報導。)\nMobile phone coverage is poor in the mountains.\n(山區的手機訊號涵蓋範圍很差。)"],["credibility","credibility(n.)可信度、信譽\ncredible(adj.)可信的\nlose credibility 失去信譽\ngain credibility 獲得信任\nThe politician lost credibility after he broke his promises.\n(那位政治人物食言後失去了信譽。)\nCiting reliable sources adds credibility to your report.\n(引用可靠的來源能增加報告的可信度。)"],["creek","creek(n.)小溪、小河\n(無詞性變化)\na small creek 小溪\ncreek bed 溪床\nThe children caught small fish in the creek behind the village.\n(孩子們在村子後面的小溪裡抓小魚。)\nWe followed the creek up into the mountains.\n(我們沿著小溪往山裡走。)"],["cripple","cripple(v./n.)使殘廢、嚴重損害、跛子\ncrippling(adj.)造成嚴重損害的\ncrippled by 因……而癱瘓\ncripple the economy 重創經濟\nThe long strike crippled the country's transportation system.\n(長時間的罷工癱瘓了該國的交通系統。)\nThe company was crippled by huge debts.\n(這家公司因龐大債務而一蹶不振。)"],["criterion/criteria","criterion(n.)標準、準則(單數)\ncriteria(n.)標準、準則(複數)\nselection criteria 選拔標準\nmeet the criteria 符合標準\nStudents must meet certain criteria to receive the scholarship.\n(學生必須符合特定標準才能獲得獎學金。)\nPrice is not the only criterion when buying a computer.\n(買電腦時價格不是唯一的標準。)"],["crucial","crucial(adj.)關鍵的、決定性的\ncrucially(adv.)關鍵地\ncrucial role 關鍵角色\ncrucial moment 關鍵時刻\nSleep plays a crucial role in memory and learning.\n(睡眠在記憶與學習中扮演關鍵角色。)\nThe goalkeeper made a save at the crucial moment.\n(守門員在關鍵時刻擋下了射門。)"],["crude","crude(adj.)粗糙的、未加工的、粗魯的\ncrudely(adv.)粗略地\ncrude oil 原油\ncrude joke 粗俗的笑話\nThe price of crude oil has risen sharply this year.\n(今年原油價格大幅上漲。)\nThe early humans made crude tools from stone.\n(早期人類用石頭製作粗糙的工具。)"],["cruise","cruise(n./v.)郵輪旅遊、巡航、緩慢行駛\ncruiser(n.)巡洋艦、遊艇\ngo on a cruise 搭郵輪旅遊\ncruise ship 郵輪\nMy grandparents went on a cruise to Japan last summer.\n(我的祖父母去年夏天搭郵輪去日本。)\nThe car cruised slowly along the coastal road.\n(那輛車沿著海岸公路緩緩行駛。)"],["crystal","crystal(n./adj.)水晶、結晶、清澈透明的\ncrystallize(v.)結晶、使具體化\ncrystal clear 清澈透明的、非常清楚的\nice crystals 冰晶\nThe water in the lake was crystal clear.\n(湖水清澈見底。)\nShe received a beautiful crystal vase as a wedding gift.\n(她收到一個漂亮的水晶花瓶作為結婚禮物。)"],["cuisine","cuisine(n.)菜餚、烹飪風格\n(無詞性變化)\nlocal cuisine 當地料理\nFrench cuisine 法式料理\nTrying the local cuisine is one of the best parts of traveling.\n(品嚐當地料理是旅行中最棒的部分之一。)\nThe restaurant is famous for its traditional Taiwanese cuisine.\n(這家餐廳以傳統台菜聞名。)"],["currency","currency(n.)貨幣、通用、流行\n(無詞性變化)\nforeign currency 外幣\ndigital currency 數位貨幣\nYou should exchange some foreign currency before your trip.\n(你應該在出發前兌換一些外幣。)\nThe idea gained currency among young people.\n(這個觀念在年輕人之間流行起來。)"],["curriculum","curriculum(n.)課程、全部課程\ncurricula(n.)課程(複數)\nschool curriculum 學校課程\nnational curriculum 國家課程綱要\nCoding has become part of the high school curriculum.\n(程式設計已成為高中課程的一部分。)\nThe new curriculum focuses on critical thinking skills.\n(新課綱著重於批判性思考能力。)"],["custody","custody(n.)監護權、拘留、保管\ncustodian(n.)管理人、監護人\nin custody 被拘留\ncustody of 的監護權\nAfter the divorce, the mother got custody of the children.\n(離婚後，母親取得了孩子的監護權。)\nThe suspect is now in police custody.\n(嫌犯目前遭警方拘留。)"],["customs","customs(n.)海關、關稅\ncustom(n.)習俗、風俗\ngo through customs 通關\ncustoms officer 海關人員\nIt took us an hour to go through customs at the airport.\n(我們在機場通關花了一個小時。)\nThe customs officer checked every bag carefully.\n(海關人員仔細檢查每一個行李。)"],["deadly","deadly(adj./adv.)致命的、極度的、極其\ndead(adj.)死的\ndeath(n.)死亡\ndeadly disease 致命的疾病\ndeadly serious 極為認真的\nSome mushrooms in the forest are deadly if eaten.\n(森林裡有些蘑菇吃了會致命。)\nHe was deadly serious about quitting his job to travel the world.\n(他是極為認真地想辭職去環遊世界。)"],["debris","debris(n.)殘骸、碎片、瓦礫\n(無詞性變化)\nspace debris 太空垃圾\nclear the debris 清除瓦礫\nRescue workers searched through the debris for survivors after the earthquake.\n(地震過後，救難人員在瓦礫堆中搜尋生還者。)\nSpace debris has become a serious threat to satellites.\n(太空垃圾已成為人造衛星的嚴重威脅。)"],["debut","debut(n.)首次登台、初次亮相、處女作\n(無詞性變化)\nmake one's debut 首次登場\ndebut album 首張專輯\nThe young singer made her debut on a TV talent show.\n(那位年輕歌手在電視選秀節目上首次亮相。)\nTheir debut album sold over a million copies in its first year.\n(他們的首張專輯第一年就賣出超過一百萬張。)"],["decay","decay(n./v.)腐爛、蛀蝕、衰敗\ndecayed(adj.)腐爛的、蛀壞的\ntooth decay 蛀牙\nurban decay 都市衰敗\nEating too much candy can lead to tooth decay.\n(吃太多糖果可能導致蛀牙。)\nThe old wooden house slowly decayed after years of neglect.\n(那棟老木屋經過多年無人照料後漸漸腐朽。)"],["deceive","deceive(v.)欺騙、蒙蔽\ndeception(n.)欺騙\ndeceit(n.)欺詐、欺騙\ndeceptive(adj.)騙人的、誤導的\ndeceive oneself 自欺欺人\nbe deceived by 被⋯欺騙\nDon't be deceived by his friendly smile.\n(別被他友善的笑容給騙了。)\nShe deceived her parents about where she was going that night.\n(她那晚對父母謊報了自己要去的地方。)"],["decent","decent(adj.)像樣的、體面的、正派的\ndecency(n.)體面、正派\ndecently(adv.)體面地、像樣地\ndecent job 像樣的工作\ndecent salary 還不錯的薪水\nAfter graduation, he found a decent job in a tech company.\n(畢業後，他在一家科技公司找到一份不錯的工作。)\nHe is a decent man who always treats others with respect.\n(他是個正派的人，總是尊重他人。)"],["declaration","declaration(n.)宣言、聲明、申報\ndeclare(v.)宣布、申報\nDeclaration of Independence 獨立宣言\ncustoms declaration 海關申報\nThe Declaration of Independence was signed in 1776.\n(《獨立宣言》在1776年簽署。)\nTravelers must fill out a customs declaration form before landing.\n(旅客在降落前必須填寫海關申報單。)"],["decline","decline(n./v.)下降、衰退、婉拒\n(無詞性變化)\ndecline an invitation 婉拒邀請\nin decline 衰退中\nThe number of births in Taiwan has declined sharply in recent years.\n(近年來臺灣的出生人數急劇下降。)\nShe politely declined the invitation to the party.\n(她禮貌地婉拒了派對的邀請。)"],["dedicate","dedicate(v.)奉獻、致力於、題獻\ndedication(n.)奉獻、專注\ndedicated(adj.)專注的、盡心盡力的\ndedicate oneself to 致力於⋯\ndedicate a book to 把書獻給⋯\nThe doctor dedicated his life to fighting cancer.\n(這位醫生畢生致力於對抗癌症。)\nThe author dedicated her new novel to her late mother.\n(作者將她的新小說獻給已故的母親。)"],["defendant","defendant(n.)被告\ndefend(v.)防衛、辯護\nplaintiff(n.)原告\nthe defendant's lawyer 被告律師\nfind the defendant guilty 判被告有罪\nThe jury found the defendant not guilty.\n(陪審團判定被告無罪。)\nThe defendant's lawyer asked for more time to prepare.\n(被告的律師要求更多時間準備。)"],["deficit","deficit(n.)赤字、不足額\n(無詞性變化)\nbudget deficit 預算赤字\ntrade deficit 貿易逆差\nThe government is trying to reduce the budget deficit.\n(政府正努力減少預算赤字。)\nThe country has had a trade deficit for five years in a row.\n(這個國家已連續五年出現貿易逆差。)"],["defy","defy(v.)違抗、公然反抗、無法(解釋等)\ndefiance(n.)反抗、蔑視\ndefiant(adj.)反抗的、挑釁的\ndefy the law 違抗法律\ndefy description 難以形容\nThe teenager defied his parents and went to the concert anyway.\n(那名青少年違抗父母，還是去了演唱會。)\nThe beauty of the sunrise defies description.\n(日出之美難以言喻。)"],["delegate","delegate(n./v.)代表、委派、授權\ndelegation(n.)代表團、授權\ndelegate tasks 分派任務\na delegate to the conference 會議代表\nA good leader knows how to delegate tasks to team members.\n(好的領導者懂得把任務分派給團隊成員。)\nEach school sent two delegates to the student conference.\n(每所學校派兩名代表參加學生會議。)"],["delegation","delegation(n.)代表團、授權、委派\ndelegate(n./v.)代表、委派\ntrade delegation 貿易代表團\nlead a delegation 率領代表團\nA trade delegation from Japan visited Taipei last week.\n(一個來自日本的貿易代表團上週訪問臺北。)\nEffective delegation allows managers to focus on important decisions.\n(有效的授權讓主管能專注於重要決策。)"],["deliberate","deliberate(adj./v.)故意的、深思熟慮的、仔細考慮\ndeliberately(adv.)故意地\ndeliberation(n.)深思熟慮、審議\na deliberate attempt 蓄意的企圖\ndeliberate on 仔細考慮⋯\nI'm sure it was a deliberate lie, not a mistake.\n(我確定那是蓄意的謊言，不是失誤。)\nThe committee deliberated for hours before reaching a decision.\n(委員會商議了好幾個小時才做出決定。)"],["democrat","democrat(n.)民主主義者、(Democrat)美國民主黨員\ndemocracy(n.)民主\ndemocratic(adj.)民主的\na true democrat 真正的民主主義者\nDemocrats and Republicans 民主黨與共和黨\nAs a true democrat, she believes every citizen's voice matters.\n(身為真正的民主主義者，她相信每位公民的聲音都很重要。)\nThe Democrats won a majority in the election.\n(民主黨在選舉中贏得多數席次。)"],["denial","denial(n.)否認、拒絕、否定\ndeny(v.)否認、拒絕\nin denial 拒絕承認(事實)\na flat denial 斷然否認\nHe is still in denial about his poor grades.\n(他仍不肯接受自己成績很差的事實。)\nThe company issued a firm denial of the rumors.\n(公司對謠言發出強烈否認。)"],["density","density(n.)密度、稠密\ndense(adj.)密集的\ndensely(adv.)密集地\npopulation density 人口密度\nhigh density 高密度\nHong Kong has one of the highest population densities in the world.\n(香港是世界上人口密度最高的地方之一。)\nWater has a higher density than oil.\n(水的密度比油高。)"],["depict","depict(v.)描繪、描述\ndepiction(n.)描繪、描述\ndepict A as B 把A描繪成B\nvividly depict 生動地描繪\nThe painting depicts a busy market in old Taipei.\n(這幅畫描繪了舊時臺北熱鬧的市集。)\nThe movie depicts the hero as a lonely but brave man.\n(電影把主角描繪成一個孤獨卻勇敢的人。)"],["deploy","deploy(v.)部署、調度、有效運用\ndeployment(n.)部署、調度\ndeploy troops 部署軍隊\ndeploy resources 調度資源\nThe government deployed soldiers to help with flood relief.\n(政府調派士兵協助救災。)\nThe company plans to deploy the new software next month.\n(公司計畫下個月部署這套新軟體。)"],["depress","depress(v.)使沮喪、使蕭條、壓下\ndepression(n.)沮喪、憂鬱症、不景氣\ndepressed(adj.)沮喪的\ndepressing(adj.)令人沮喪的\ndepress prices 壓低價格\ndepress the button 按下按鈕\nRainy weather always depresses me.\n(下雨天總是讓我心情低落。)\nThe bad news depressed the stock market for weeks.\n(這個壞消息使股市低迷了好幾週。)"],["deputy","deputy(n.)副手、代理人、副⋯\n(無詞性變化)\ndeputy mayor 副市長\ndeputy director 副主任、副處長\nThe deputy mayor attended the ceremony on behalf of the mayor.\n(副市長代表市長出席了典禮。)\nShe was promoted to deputy director last year.\n(她去年被升為副主任。)"],["derive","derive(v.)得到、源自、衍生\nderivation(n.)起源、衍生\nderivative(n./adj.)衍生物、衍生的\nderive from 源自⋯\nderive pleasure from 從⋯得到樂趣\nMany English words are derived from Latin.\n(許多英文字源自拉丁文。)\nShe derives great pleasure from helping others.\n(她從幫助他人中獲得極大的樂趣。)"],["descend","descend(v.)下降、下來、遺傳、源自\ndescent(n.)下降、血統\ndescendant(n.)後代、子孫\ndescend from 是⋯的後代\ndescend the stairs 走下樓梯\nThe plane began to descend toward the airport.\n(飛機開始朝機場下降。)\nShe is said to be descended from a famous scholar.\n(據說她是一位著名學者的後代。)"],["descriptive","descriptive(adj.)描述的、描寫的\ndescribe(v.)描述\ndescription(n.)描述\ndescriptive writing 描寫文\ndescriptive language 描述性語言\nOur teacher asked us to write a descriptive essay about our hometown.\n(老師要我們寫一篇描寫家鄉的文章。)\nThe author uses rich descriptive language to bring the scene to life.\n(作者運用豐富的描寫語言讓場景栩栩如生。)"],["despair","despair(n./v.)絕望、失望\ndesperate(adj.)絕望的、拚命的\nin despair 絕望地\ndespair of 對⋯感到絕望\nHe gave up in despair after failing the exam three times.\n(他考了三次都沒過後，絕望地放棄了。)\nNever despair; things will get better.\n(永遠不要絕望，事情會好轉的。)"],["destination","destination(n.)目的地、終點\ndestine(v.)注定\ntourist destination 觀光勝地\nfinal destination 最終目的地\nKenting is a popular tourist destination in summer.\n(墾丁是夏天熱門的觀光勝地。)\nWe finally reached our destination after a ten-hour drive.\n(經過十小時的車程，我們終於抵達目的地。)"],["destiny","destiny(n.)命運、天命\ndestined(adj.)注定的\ncontrol one's destiny 掌握自己的命運\nby destiny 命中注定\nShe believes that we can shape our own destiny.\n(她相信我們可以塑造自己的命運。)\nMeeting him was destiny, not chance.\n(遇見他是命中注定，不是偶然。)"],["destructive","destructive(adj.)破壞性的、毀滅性的\ndestroy(v.)破壞\ndestruction(n.)破壞\ndestructive power 破壞力\ndestructive behavior 破壞性行為\nThe typhoon was the most destructive storm in ten years.\n(這個颱風是十年來破壞力最強的暴風雨。)\nConstant criticism can be destructive to a child's confidence.\n(不斷的批評可能會摧毀孩子的自信。)"],["devotion","devotion(n.)奉獻、熱愛、忠誠\ndevote(v.)奉獻\ndevoted(adj.)忠誠的、全心全意的\ndevotion to 對⋯的熱愛、奉獻\nreligious devotion 虔誠\nHis devotion to his students made him a beloved teacher.\n(他對學生的全心奉獻使他成為一位受愛戴的老師。)\nThe dog showed great devotion to its owner.\n(這隻狗對主人非常忠誠。)"],["diagnose","diagnose(v.)診斷\ndiagnosis(n.)診斷\ndiagnostic(adj.)診斷的\nbe diagnosed with 被診斷出患有⋯\ndiagnose a problem 找出問題所在\nHe was diagnosed with diabetes at the age of forty.\n(他在四十歲時被診斷出罹患糖尿病。)\nThe mechanic quickly diagnosed the problem with my car.\n(技師很快就找出我車子的問題。)"],["diagnosis","diagnosis(n.)診斷\ndiagnose(v.)診斷\ndiagnostic(adj.)診斷的\nmake a diagnosis 做出診斷\nearly diagnosis 早期診斷\nEarly diagnosis of cancer can save many lives.\n(癌症的早期診斷可以拯救許多生命。)\nThe doctor made a diagnosis after checking the X-ray.\n(醫生看過X光片後做出了診斷。)"],["dialect","dialect(n.)方言\ndialectal(adj.)方言的\nlocal dialect 當地方言\nspeak a dialect 說方言\nMy grandparents speak to each other in the Hakka dialect.\n(我的祖父母彼此用客家話交談。)\nMany local dialects are disappearing as young people move to cities.\n(隨著年輕人移居城市，許多地方方言正在消失。)"],["diameter","diameter(n.)直徑\nradius(n.)半徑\nin diameter 直徑為⋯\nthe diameter of a circle 圓的直徑\nThe pizza is about thirty centimeters in diameter.\n(這個披薩的直徑大約三十公分。)\nTo find the area, first measure the diameter of the circle.\n(要算出面積，先量出圓的直徑。)"],["diaper","diaper(n.)尿布\n(無詞性變化)\nchange a diaper 換尿布\ndisposable diaper 紙尿布\nThe young father learned how to change a diaper.\n(這位年輕爸爸學會了怎麼換尿布。)\nDisposable diapers create a large amount of waste every year.\n(紙尿布每年製造大量的垃圾。)"],["digestion","digestion(n.)消化、消化力\ndigest(v.)消化\ndigestive(adj.)消化的\naid digestion 幫助消化\npoor digestion 消化不良\nDrinking warm water after meals can aid digestion.\n(飯後喝溫水可以幫助消化。)\nStress can have a negative effect on your digestion.\n(壓力可能對你的消化造成負面影響。)"],["dilemma","dilemma(n.)兩難、困境\n(無詞性變化)\nin a dilemma 進退兩難\nface a dilemma 面臨兩難\nI'm in a dilemma about whether to study abroad or stay home.\n(我在出國念書還是留在國內之間進退兩難。)\nDoctors often face moral dilemmas in their work.\n(醫生在工作中常面臨道德上的兩難。)"],["dimension","dimension(n.)尺寸、面向、維度、層面\ndimensional(adj.)⋯維的、⋯度空間的\nthree dimensions 三度空間、三維\na new dimension 新的面向\nPlease measure the dimensions of the room before buying furniture.\n(買家具前請先量好房間的尺寸。)\nSocial media has added a new dimension to how we communicate.\n(社群媒體為我們的溝通方式增添了新的面向。)"],["diminish","diminish(v.)減少、降低、貶低\ndiminution(n.)減少\ndiminish in value 價值降低\ndiminishing returns 報酬遞減\nThe pain gradually diminished after I took the medicine.\n(吃藥後疼痛漸漸減輕了。)\nNothing can diminish her achievements.\n(什麼也無法抹煞她的成就。)"],["diplomatic","diplomatic(adj.)外交的、圓滑的、有手腕的\ndiplomat(n.)外交官\ndiplomacy(n.)外交\ndiplomatic relations 外交關係\ndiplomatic answer 圓滑的回答\nThe two countries established diplomatic relations in 1990.\n(兩國在1990年建立外交關係。)\nShe gave a diplomatic answer to avoid hurting anyone's feelings.\n(她給了一個圓滑的回答，以免傷害任何人的感受。)"],["directory","directory(n.)名錄、電話簿、(電腦)目錄\n(無詞性變化)\ntelephone directory 電話簿\nfile directory 檔案目錄\nYou can find the store's number in the telephone directory.\n(你可以在電話簿裡找到這家店的號碼。)\nSave the file in the main directory.\n(把檔案存在主目錄裡。)"],["disapprove","disapprove(v.)不贊成、反對\ndisapproval(n.)不贊成、反對\napprove(v.)贊成\ndisapprove of 不贊成⋯\nstrongly disapprove 強烈反對\nMy parents disapprove of my staying up late to play games.\n(我爸媽不贊成我熬夜打電動。)\nThe teacher shook her head to show she disapproved.\n(老師搖搖頭表示不贊同。)"],["disclose","disclose(v.)揭露、透露、公開\ndisclosure(n.)揭露、透露\ndisclose information 透露資訊\nrefuse to disclose 拒絕透露\nThe company refused to disclose the details of the deal.\n(公司拒絕透露這筆交易的細節。)\nNever disclose your password to anyone online.\n(絕對不要在網路上把密碼透露給任何人。)"],["disconnect","disconnect(v.)切斷、斷開、使分離\ndisconnection(n.)斷開、分離\ndisconnected(adj.)斷開的、不連貫的\ndisconnect from 和⋯斷開\nget disconnected 斷線(電話、網路)\nWe got disconnected in the middle of our video call.\n(我們視訊通話到一半就斷線了。)\nSometimes it's good to disconnect from social media for a while.\n(有時暫時遠離社群媒體是好事。)"],["discourse","discourse(n.)論述、交談、演講\n(無詞性變化)\npolitical discourse 政治論述\npublic discourse 公共論述\nSocial media has changed the nature of political discourse.\n(社群媒體改變了政治論述的本質。)\nThe professor gave a long discourse on modern art.\n(教授針對現代藝術發表了一場長篇演講。)"],["discriminate","discriminate(v.)歧視、區別\ndiscrimination(n.)歧視、辨別力\ndiscriminatory(adj.)歧視的\ndiscriminate against 歧視⋯\ndiscriminate between 區分⋯\nIt is illegal to discriminate against people because of their age.\n(因年齡而歧視他人是違法的。)\nYoung children cannot always discriminate between fact and fiction.\n(幼童不一定能分辨事實與虛構。)"],["discrimination","discrimination(n.)歧視、辨別力\ndiscriminate(v.)歧視、區別\ndiscriminatory(adj.)歧視的\nracial discrimination 種族歧視\ndiscrimination against 對⋯的歧視\nThe law protects workers from discrimination in the workplace.\n(這項法律保護勞工免於在職場上受到歧視。)\nGender discrimination is still a problem in many countries.\n(性別歧視在許多國家仍是個問題。)"],["disrupt","disrupt(v.)擾亂、使中斷、顛覆\ndisruption(n.)中斷、混亂\ndisruptive(adj.)破壞性的、擾亂的\ndisrupt traffic 擾亂交通\ndisrupt a class 擾亂課堂秩序\nThe typhoon disrupted train services across the island.\n(颱風使全島的火車服務中斷。)\nHis loud phone call disrupted the whole class.\n(他大聲講電話擾亂了整個課堂。)"],["dissolve","dissolve(v.)溶解、解散、消失\ndissolution(n.)解散、溶解\ndissolve in water 溶於水\ndissolve a partnership 解除合夥關係\nStir the sugar until it completely dissolves in the tea.\n(攪拌糖直到它完全溶在茶裡。)\nThe band dissolved after their lead singer left.\n(主唱離開後，樂團就解散了。)"],["distinction","distinction(n.)區別、差異、卓越、殊榮\ndistinct(adj.)不同的、明顯的\ndistinctive(adj.)獨特的\nmake a distinction between 區分⋯\nwith distinction 以優異成績\nIt's important to make a distinction between facts and opinions.\n(區分事實與意見是很重要的。)\nShe graduated from university with distinction.\n(她以優異成績從大學畢業。)"],["distinctive","distinctive(adj.)獨特的、有特色的\ndistinct(adj.)不同的\ndistinction(n.)區別、特點\ndistinctive feature 獨特的特徵\ndistinctive style 獨特的風格\nThe singer has a very distinctive voice.\n(這位歌手有非常獨特的嗓音。)\nTainan is known for its distinctive local food.\n(臺南以獨具特色的在地小吃聞名。)"],["distract","distract(v.)使分心、轉移(注意力)\ndistraction(n.)令人分心的事物\ndistracted(adj.)分心的\ndistract someone from 使某人從⋯分心\neasily distracted 容易分心\nThe noise outside distracted me from my homework.\n(外面的噪音讓我無法專心寫作業。)\nSmartphones can easily distract students in class.\n(智慧型手機很容易讓學生上課分心。)"],["doctrine","doctrine(n.)教義、學說、主義\ndoctrinal(adj.)教義的、學說的\nreligious doctrine 宗教教義\npolitical doctrine 政治主張\nThe monks spent years studying Buddhist doctrine.\n(僧侶們花了多年研讀佛教教義。)\nThe president announced a new foreign policy doctrine.\n(總統宣布了一項新的外交政策主張。)"],["document","document(n./v.)文件、記錄、證明\ndocumentary(n./adj.)紀錄片、文件的\ndocumentation(n.)文件、證明資料\nofficial document 正式文件\ndocument the process 記錄過程\nPlease sign the document and return it by Friday.\n(請在文件上簽名並在週五前交回。)\nThe scientist carefully documented every step of the experiment.\n(那位科學家仔細記錄了實驗的每一個步驟。)"],["documentary","documentary(n./adj.)紀錄片、文件的、紀實的\ndocument(n./v.)文件、記錄\ndocumentary film 紀錄片\ndocumentary evidence 書面證據\nWe watched a documentary about climate change in class.\n(我們在課堂上看了一部關於氣候變遷的紀錄片。)\nThe lawyer presented documentary evidence to the court.\n(律師向法院提出書面證據。)"],["domain","domain(n.)領域、範圍、領土、網域\n(無詞性變化)\npublic domain 公共領域\ndomain name 網域名稱\nArtificial intelligence is no longer just the domain of scientists.\n(人工智慧已不再只是科學家的領域。)\nWe need to register a domain name for our website.\n(我們需要為網站註冊一個網域名稱。)"],["dome","dome(n./v.)圓頂、圓頂建築、使成圓頂形\ndomed(adj.)圓頂的\ngolden dome 金色圓頂\nTaipei Dome 臺北大巨蛋\nThe church is famous for its huge golden dome.\n(這座教堂以巨大的金色圓頂聞名。)\nThousands of fans gathered at the Taipei Dome for the baseball game.\n(數千名球迷聚集在臺北大巨蛋觀看棒球賽。)"],["donate","donate(v.)捐贈、捐獻\ndonation(n.)捐贈、捐款\ndonor(n.)捐贈者\ndonate blood 捐血\ndonate money to 捐錢給⋯\nMy father donates blood every three months.\n(我爸爸每三個月捐一次血。)\nThe students donated old books to a rural school.\n(學生們把舊書捐給一所偏鄉學校。)"],["donation","donation(n.)捐贈、捐款、捐贈物\ndonate(v.)捐贈\ndonor(n.)捐贈者\nmake a donation 捐款\norgan donation 器官捐贈\nShe made a donation to help the flood victims.\n(她捐了一筆款項幫助水災災民。)\nOrgan donation can save many lives.\n(器官捐贈能拯救許多生命。)"],["donor","donor(n.)捐贈者、捐血者、捐款人\ndonate(v.)捐贈\ndonation(n.)捐贈\nblood donor 捐血者\norgan donor 器官捐贈者\nThe hospital is looking for more blood donors.\n(醫院正在尋找更多的捐血者。)\nAn anonymous donor gave the school one million dollars.\n(一位匿名捐款人捐給學校一百萬元。)"],["doorway","doorway(n.)門口、出入口\n(無詞性變化)\nstand in the doorway 站在門口\nblock the doorway 擋住門口\nMy little sister stood in the doorway, waiting for me to come home.\n(我妹妹站在門口等我回家。)\nPlease don't block the doorway with your bags.\n(請不要用你的包包擋住出入口。)"],["dough","dough(n.)生麵糰、(俚)錢\ndoughy(adj.)麵糰似的、軟爛的\nknead the dough 揉麵糰\npizza dough 披薩麵糰\nKnead the dough for ten minutes until it becomes smooth.\n(揉麵糰十分鐘直到它變得光滑。)\nLet the pizza dough rest for an hour before baking.\n(烘烤前讓披薩麵糰靜置一小時。)"],["dreadful","dreadful(adj.)可怕的、糟透的、令人不快的\ndread(n./v.)恐懼、害怕\ndreadfully(adv.)非常、可怕地\ndreadful accident 可怕的意外\ndreadful weather 糟透的天氣\nWe had dreadful weather during our trip to Hokkaido.\n(我們去北海道旅行時天氣糟透了。)\nThe news of the dreadful accident shocked the whole country.\n(那起可怕意外的消息震驚了全國。)"],["driveway","driveway(n.)私人車道\n(無詞性變化)\npark in the driveway 停在車道上\na long driveway 一條長長的車道\nMy father parked the car in the driveway.\n(我爸爸把車停在家門前的車道上。)\nA long driveway led up to the old farmhouse.\n(一條長長的車道通往那間老農舍。)"],["drought","drought(n.)乾旱、旱災\n(無詞性變化)\nsevere drought 嚴重乾旱\nsuffer from drought 遭受旱災\nThe severe drought has caused water shortages in central Taiwan.\n(嚴重的乾旱已在中臺灣造成缺水。)\nFarmers lost most of their crops during the long drought.\n(在長期乾旱中，農民損失了大部分的農作物。)"],["ecological","ecological(adj.)生態的、生態學的\necology(n.)生態\necologist(n.)生態學家\necological balance 生態平衡\necological disaster 生態浩劫\nCutting down too many trees can upset the ecological balance of a region.\n(砍伐過多樹木會破壞一個地區的生態平衡。)\nThe oil spill was described as an ecological disaster for the coastline.\n(這起漏油事件被形容為海岸線的一場生態浩劫。)"],["ecology","ecology(n.)生態、生態學\necological(adj.)生態的\necologist(n.)生態學家\nmarine ecology 海洋生態\nthe ecology of 的生態\nShe plans to study marine ecology at a university in Taiwan.\n(她打算在台灣的大學研究海洋生態。)\nBuilding the new road could seriously damage the ecology of the wetland.\n(興建新道路可能會嚴重破壞濕地的生態。)"],["ecosystem","ecosystem(n.)生態系統\n(無詞性變化)\nmarine ecosystem 海洋生態系\nfragile ecosystem 脆弱的生態系統\nCoral reefs are among the most diverse ecosystems on Earth.\n(珊瑚礁是地球上最多樣化的生態系統之一。)\nIntroducing foreign species can harm a fragile ecosystem.\n(引進外來物種可能會危害脆弱的生態系統。)"],["ego","ego(n.)自我、自尊心、自負\negoism(n.)自我中心\nboost one's ego 增強自信、滿足虛榮心\na big ego 自負、自我膨脹\nWinning the award gave his ego a big boost.\n(得獎讓他的自尊心大大提升。)\nIt's hard to work with someone who has such a big ego.\n(和一個那麼自負的人共事很困難。)"],["elaborate","elaborate(adj./v.)精心製作的、詳盡的、詳細說明\nelaboration(n.)詳盡說明\nelaborate on 詳細說明…\nan elaborate plan 精心策劃的計畫\nCould you elaborate on your idea a little more?\n(你可以再詳細說明一下你的想法嗎？)\nThe students prepared an elaborate costume for the school play.\n(學生們為校園話劇準備了一套精心製作的服裝。)"],["eligible","eligible(adj.)有資格的、合格的\neligibility(n.)資格\nbe eligible for 有資格獲得…\nbe eligible to vote 有投票資格\nStudents with good grades are eligible for the scholarship.\n(成績優良的學生有資格申請這項獎學金。)\nIn Taiwan, citizens over the age of 18 are eligible to vote in referendums.\n(在台灣，年滿十八歲的公民有資格在公投中投票。)"],["eloquent","eloquent(adj.)雄辯的、有說服力的、口才好的\neloquence(n.)口才、雄辯\neloquently(adv.)雄辯地\nan eloquent speaker 口才很好的講者\nan eloquent speech 動人的演說\nThe eloquent speaker kept the audience's attention for an hour.\n(那位口才極好的講者吸引聽眾注意力長達一小時。)\nHer eloquent speech persuaded many people to donate money.\n(她動人的演說說服了許多人捐款。)"],["embrace","embrace(v./n.)擁抱、欣然接受、包含\n(無詞性變化)\nembrace change 擁抱改變\na warm embrace 溫暖的擁抱\nYoung people tend to embrace new technology quickly.\n(年輕人往往很快就接受新科技。)\nThe mother held her son in a warm embrace at the airport.\n(母親在機場給了兒子一個溫暖的擁抱。)"],["emission","emission(n.)排放、排放物\nemit(v.)排放、散發\ncarbon emissions 碳排放\nreduce emissions 減少排放\nMany countries have promised to reduce carbon emissions by 2050.\n(許多國家已承諾在2050年前減少碳排放。)\nElectric cars produce no exhaust emissions while driving.\n(電動車行駛時不會產生廢氣排放。)"],["endorse(ment)","endorse(v.)支持、贊同、代言、背書、endorsement(n.)支持、代言\n(無詞性變化)\ncelebrity endorsement 名人代言\nendorse a product 為產品代言\nThe famous athlete was paid millions to endorse the sports shoes.\n(那位知名運動員收了數百萬元為這款運動鞋代言。)\nThe plan won the endorsement of most teachers and parents.\n(這項計畫獲得了大多數老師和家長的支持。)"],["enterprise","enterprise(n.)企業、事業、進取心\nenterprising(adj.)有進取心的\nprivate enterprise 私人企業\nsmall and medium enterprises 中小企業\nSmall and medium enterprises play an important role in Taiwan's economy.\n(中小企業在台灣經濟中扮演重要角色。)\nStarting her own bakery was a risky enterprise.\n(開自己的麵包店是一項有風險的事業。)"],["enthusiastic","enthusiastic(adj.)熱心的、熱情的\nenthusiasm(n.)熱忱\nenthusiastically(adv.)熱情地\nbe enthusiastic about 對…熱衷\nan enthusiastic welcome 熱烈的歡迎\nHe is very enthusiastic about joining the school's robotics club.\n(他非常熱衷於加入學校的機器人社。)\nThe exchange students received an enthusiastic welcome from our class.\n(交換學生受到我們班熱烈的歡迎。)"],["entitle","entitle(v.)給…權利、使有資格、給…命名\nentitlement(n.)權利\nbe entitled to 有權…\na book entitled 一本名為…的書\nAll employees are entitled to two weeks of paid vacation.\n(所有員工都有權享有兩週的帶薪假。)\nShe wrote a book entitled 'Growing Up in Taipei'.\n(她寫了一本名為《在台北長大》的書。)"],["entity","entity(n.)實體、存在物\n(無詞性變化)\nlegal entity 法人\nseparate entity 獨立的個體\nThe two companies merged but remain separate legal entities.\n(這兩家公司合併了，但仍是各自獨立的法人。)\nThe school library operates as a separate entity from the main office.\n(學校圖書館是獨立於行政辦公室的單位。)"],["entrepreneur","entrepreneur(n.)企業家、創業者\nentrepreneurial(adj.)有創業精神的\nentrepreneurship(n.)創業精神\nyoung entrepreneur 年輕創業家\nsuccessful entrepreneur 成功的企業家\nThe young entrepreneur started her online business while still in college.\n(這位年輕創業家在大學時期就開始經營網路生意。)\nMany successful entrepreneurs failed several times before they succeeded.\n(許多成功的企業家在成功之前都失敗過好幾次。)"],["envious","envious(adj.)羨慕的、嫉妒的\nenvy(n./v.)羨慕、嫉妒\nbe envious of 羨慕…\nenvious eyes 羨慕的眼光\nMany classmates were envious of her perfect test scores.\n(許多同學都很羨慕她完美的考試成績。)\nHe looked at his friend's new bike with envious eyes.\n(他用羨慕的眼光看著朋友的新腳踏車。)"],["envision","envision(v.)想像、展望、預想\nvision(n.)願景、視力\nenvision a future 展望未來\nenvision doing 設想做…\nThe mayor envisions a city where everyone can ride bikes safely.\n(市長展望一個人人都能安全騎腳踏車的城市。)\nI never envisioned myself becoming a teacher.\n(我從沒想過自己會成為一名老師。)"],["epidemic","epidemic(n./adj.)流行病、傳染病、流行的\n(無詞性變化)\nflu epidemic 流感疫情\nan epidemic of 某事的大量蔓延\nThe government took quick action to stop the flu epidemic.\n(政府迅速採取行動遏止流感疫情。)\nSome experts say there is an epidemic of loneliness among young people.\n(有些專家說孤獨感正在年輕人之間蔓延。)"],["episode","episode(n.)(連續劇)一集、插曲、一段經歷\n(無詞性變化)\nthe latest episode 最新一集\nan unpleasant episode 不愉快的經歷\nI can't wait to watch the latest episode of the drama tonight.\n(我等不及今晚要看這部連續劇的最新一集。)\nShe wanted to forget that embarrassing episode in junior high school.\n(她想忘掉國中時那段尷尬的經歷。)"],["equation","equation(n.)方程式、等式、綜合考量\nequate(v.)把…視為同等\nsolve an equation 解方程式\nthe other side of the equation 問題的另一面\nThe students learned how to solve equations with two unknowns.\n(學生們學習如何解二元方程式。)\nMoney is only one part of the equation when choosing a job.\n(選擇工作時，薪水只是考量的一部分。)"],["equity","equity(n.)公平、公正、股權\nequitable(adj.)公平的\ngender equity 性別平等\neducational equity 教育公平\nThe government is working to improve educational equity in rural areas.\n(政府正努力提升偏鄉地區的教育公平。)\nGender equity in the workplace is still a goal for many countries.\n(職場的性別平等仍是許多國家努力的目標。)"],["equivalent","equivalent(n./adj.)相等物、對等詞、相等的\nequivalence(n.)相等\nbe equivalent to 相當於…\nthe equivalent of 相當於…的東西\nOne U.S. dollar is roughly equivalent to thirty New Taiwan dollars.\n(一美元大約相當於三十元新台幣。)\nThere is no exact English equivalent for this Chinese idiom.\n(這句中文成語沒有完全對等的英文說法。)"],["erect","erect(v./adj.)豎立、建造、直立的\nerection(n.)建造、豎立\nerect a statue 豎立雕像\nstand erect 挺直站立\nThe city erected a statue in honor of the brave firefighters.\n(市政府豎立了一座雕像來紀念英勇的消防員。)\nThe soldiers stood erect as the national anthem was played.\n(播放國歌時，士兵們挺直站立。)"],["errand","errand(n.)差事、跑腿\n(無詞性變化)\nrun errands 跑腿、辦雜事\non an errand 外出辦事\nI have to run some errands for my mom after school.\n(放學後我得幫我媽媽跑腿辦點事。)\nMy father went out on an errand and will be back soon.\n(我爸爸出門辦事了，很快就回來。)"],["erupt","erupt(v.)(火山)爆發、突然發生\neruption(n.)爆發\nvolcano erupts 火山爆發\nerupt into 突然爆發成…\nThe volcano erupted suddenly, forcing thousands of people to leave.\n(火山突然爆發，迫使數千人撤離。)\nThe crowd erupted into cheers when the team scored the winning goal.\n(球隊踢進致勝球時，群眾爆出歡呼聲。)"],["escalator","escalator(n.)電扶梯\nescalate(v.)逐步升級\ntake the escalator 搭電扶梯\nstand on the right of the escalator 站在電扶梯右側\nIn Taipei MRT stations, people usually stand on the right side of the escalator.\n(在台北捷運站，人們通常站在電扶梯的右側。)\nPlease hold the handrail when you take the escalator.\n(搭電扶梯時請握緊扶手。)"],["essence","essence(n.)本質、精髓、精華\nessential(adj.)必要的、本質的\nin essence 本質上\nthe essence of 的精髓\nIn essence, the two plans are almost the same.\n(本質上，這兩個計畫幾乎一樣。)\nKindness is the essence of true friendship.\n(善良是真正友誼的精髓。)"],["estate","estate(n.)地產、財產、莊園\n(無詞性變化)\nreal estate 房地產\nestate agent 房屋仲介\nReal estate prices in Taipei are among the highest in Taiwan.\n(台北的房地產價格是全台最高之一。)\nThe old man left his entire estate to his only grandson.\n(那位老人把所有財產都留給了他唯一的孫子。)"],["eternal","eternal(adj.)永恆的、永遠的\neternity(n.)永恆\neternally(adv.)永遠地\neternal love 永恆的愛\neternal life 永生\nThe couple promised each other eternal love on their wedding day.\n(這對新人在婚禮上互許永恆的愛。)\nThe poem describes the eternal beauty of nature.\n(這首詩描寫大自然永恆的美。)"],["ethic(s)","ethic(n.)倫理、道德觀\nethics(n.)倫理學、道德規範\nethical(adj.)道德的\nwork ethic 職業道德、敬業精神\nmedical ethics 醫學倫理\nHer strong work ethic earned her a quick promotion.\n(她強烈的敬業精神讓她很快就升遷了。)\nThe use of AI in schools raises many questions about ethics.\n(在學校使用人工智慧引發了許多倫理問題。)"],["ethical","ethical(adj.)道德的、倫理的、合乎道德的\nethics(n.)倫理\nethically(adv.)合乎道德地\nethical issue 倫理議題\nethical behavior 合乎道德的行為\nCloning humans raises serious ethical issues.\n(複製人引發了嚴重的倫理議題。)\nMany consumers prefer to buy from companies with ethical practices.\n(許多消費者偏好向經營合乎道德的公司購買商品。)"],["evolution","evolution(n.)演化、進化、發展\nevolve(v.)演化\nevolutionary(adj.)演化的\nthe theory of evolution 演化論\nthe evolution of 的發展\nDarwin is famous for his theory of evolution.\n(達爾文以他的演化論聞名。)\nThe museum shows the evolution of the telephone over the past century.\n(這間博物館展示了過去一世紀以來電話的演變。)"],["evolve","evolve(v.)演化、逐步發展\nevolution(n.)演化\nevolve from 從…演化而來\nevolve into 發展成…\nScientists believe that birds evolved from dinosaurs.\n(科學家相信鳥類是從恐龍演化而來的。)\nTheir small online shop has evolved into a large company.\n(他們的小網店已經發展成一家大公司。)"],["exaggeration","exaggeration(n.)誇張、誇大\nexaggerate(v.)誇張、誇大\nwithout exaggeration 毫不誇張地說\na slight exaggeration 有點誇張\nIt is no exaggeration to say that he is the best player on the team.\n(毫不誇張地說，他是隊上最好的球員。)\nSaying the test was impossible is a bit of an exaggeration.\n(說這次考試根本不可能考好，有點誇張了。)"],["exceed","exceed(v.)超過、超出\nexcess(n.)過量\nexcessive(adj.)過度的\nexceed the speed limit 超速\nexceed expectations 超出預期\nDrivers who exceed the speed limit will be fined.\n(超速的駕駛人將會被罰款。)\nThe results of the experiment exceeded our expectations.\n(實驗結果超出了我們的預期。)"],["exceptional","exceptional(adj.)傑出的、優秀的、例外的\nexception(n.)例外\nexceptionally(adv.)特別地、異常地\nexceptional talent 過人的天賦\nexceptional circumstances 特殊情況\nThe young violinist showed exceptional talent at an early age.\n(那位年輕小提琴家從小就展現出過人的天賦。)\nLate homework will only be accepted in exceptional circumstances.\n(只有在特殊情況下才會接受遲交的作業。)"],["excessive","excessive(adj.)過度的、過多的\nexcess(n.)過量\nexcessively(adv.)過度地\nexcessive use 過度使用\nexcessive drinking 過度飲酒\nExcessive use of smartphones may harm your eyesight.\n(過度使用智慧型手機可能會損害視力。)\nThe restaurant charged an excessive price for a simple bowl of noodles.\n(那家餐廳一碗簡單的麵卻收取過高的價格。)"],["exclaim","exclaim(v.)驚叫、呼喊\nexclamation(n.)驚嘆、感嘆詞\nexclaim in surprise 驚訝地叫出來\nexclamation mark 驚嘆號\n'What a beautiful view!' she exclaimed when she reached the top of the mountain.\n(她登上山頂時驚呼：「好美的景色！」)\nThe children exclaimed in delight when they saw the snow.\n(孩子們看到雪時開心地大叫。)"],["exclude","exclude(v.)排除、不包括\nexclusion(n.)排除\nexclusive(adj.)獨有的\nbe excluded from 被排除在…之外\nexcluding tax 不含稅\nNo student should be excluded from school activities because of their background.\n(任何學生都不應因為背景而被排除在學校活動之外。)\nThe price of the hotel room is three thousand dollars, excluding tax.\n(這間飯店房間的價格是三千元，不含稅。)"],["exclusive","exclusive(adj.)獨有的、獨家的、高級的\nexclusively(adv.)專門地、獨家地\nexclude(v.)排除\nexclusive interview 獨家專訪\nmutually exclusive 互相排斥的\nThe magazine published an exclusive interview with the famous director.\n(那本雜誌刊登了對這位知名導演的獨家專訪。)\nStudying hard and having fun are not mutually exclusive.\n(用功讀書和享受樂趣並不互相衝突。)"],["execute","execute(v.)執行、實行、處決\nexecution(n.)執行、處決\nexecutive(n.)主管\nexecute a plan 執行計畫\nbe executed for 因…被處決\nThe team executed the plan perfectly and won the game.\n(球隊完美執行計畫並贏得比賽。)\nIn the past, people could be executed for stealing bread.\n(在過去，偷麵包的人可能會被處決。)"],["execution","execution(n.)執行、實施、死刑\nexecute(v.)執行、處決\nexecutioner(n.)行刑者\nthe execution of a plan 計畫的執行\npublic execution 公開處決\nGood ideas are useless without careful execution.\n(好點子若沒有周詳的執行就毫無用處。)\nPublic executions were common in Europe hundreds of years ago.\n(幾百年前，公開處決在歐洲很常見。)"],["executive","executive(n./adj.)主管、行政官、執行的、行政的\nexecute(v.)執行\nchief executive officer (CEO) 執行長\nexecutive power 行政權\nShe became the chief executive officer of the company at age thirty-five.\n(她三十五歲時就成為了這家公司的執行長。)\nThe Executive Yuan is responsible for carrying out government policies.\n(行政院負責執行政府政策。)"],["exile","exile(n./v.)流亡、放逐、流亡者、流放\n(無詞性變化)\nin exile 流亡中\nbe exiled to 被流放到…\nThe writer lived in exile for twenty years before returning home.\n(那位作家流亡了二十年才回到故鄉。)\nNapoleon was exiled to a small island in the Atlantic Ocean.\n(拿破崙被流放到大西洋上的一座小島。)"],["exotic","exotic(adj./n.)異國風情的、外來的、外來品種\n(無詞性變化)\nexotic food 異國料理\nexotic species 外來物種\nWe tried some exotic food at the night market, like crocodile meat.\n(我們在夜市嘗試了一些異國食物，例如鱷魚肉。)\nExotic species can be a serious threat to local wildlife.\n(外來物種可能對當地野生動物造成嚴重威脅。)"],["expedition","expedition(n.)遠征、探險、探險隊\n(無詞性變化)\ngo on an expedition 去探險\na scientific expedition 科學考察\nThe team went on an expedition to the South Pole last winter.\n(這支隊伍去年冬天前往南極探險。)\nThe scientific expedition discovered several new kinds of plants.\n(這次科學考察發現了好幾種新的植物。)"],["expertise","expertise(n.)專業知識、專長\nexpert(n./adj.)專家、熟練的\ntechnical expertise 技術專長\nlack the expertise 缺乏專業知識\nThe project needs someone with expertise in computer programming.\n(這個專案需要具備電腦程式設計專長的人。)\nWe lack the expertise to repair the machine ourselves.\n(我們缺乏自己修理這台機器的專業知識。)"],["explicit","explicit(adj.)明確的、清楚的、露骨的\nexplicitly(adv.)明確地\nexplicit instructions 明確的指示\nexplicit content 露骨的內容\nThe teacher gave us explicit instructions about the project.\n(老師給了我們關於這份報告明確的指示。)\nThis movie is not suitable for children because of its explicit content.\n(這部電影因為內容露骨，不適合兒童觀看。)"],["exploit","exploit(v./n.)剝削、利用、開發、功績\nexploitation(n.)剝削、開發\nexploit workers 剝削勞工\nexploit natural resources 開發天然資源\nSome companies exploit workers by paying them very low wages.\n(有些公司以極低的工資剝削勞工。)\nWe should exploit natural resources in a sustainable way.\n(我們應該以永續的方式開發天然資源。)"],["exploration","exploration(n.)探險、探索、勘查\nexplore(v.)探索\nexplorer(n.)探險家\nspace exploration 太空探索\noil exploration 石油探勘\nSpace exploration has helped us learn more about our own planet.\n(太空探索幫助我們更了解自己的星球。)\nThe children enjoyed their exploration of the forest during summer camp.\n(孩子們在夏令營中很享受探索森林的過程。)"],["extension","extension(n.)延長、擴建、分機\nextend(v.)延長\nextensive(adj.)廣泛的\nextension number 分機號碼\ndeadline extension 延長期限\nPlease call me at extension 205 if you have any questions.\n(如有任何問題，請撥分機205找我。)\nThe teacher gave us a one-week extension on the report.\n(老師讓我們的報告延後一週繳交。)"],["extensive","extensive(adj.)廣泛的、大量的、廣大的\nextend(v.)延伸\nextensively(adv.)廣泛地\nextensive research 廣泛的研究\nextensive damage 大範圍的損害\nThe scientist did extensive research before publishing her findings.\n(這位科學家在發表研究結果前做了廣泛的研究。)\nThe earthquake caused extensive damage to buildings in the city.\n(地震對市區建築造成了大範圍的損害。)"],["exterior","exterior(n./adj.)外部、外表、外部的\ninterior(n./adj.)內部、內部的\nthe exterior of 的外觀\nexterior wall 外牆\nThe exterior of the old house was painted bright blue.\n(那棟老房子的外觀被漆成亮藍色。)\nWorkers are repairing the exterior walls of the library.\n(工人們正在修繕圖書館的外牆。)"],["external","external(adj./n.)外部的、外在的、外表\ninternal(adj.)內部的\nexternally(adv.)外部地\nexternal pressure 外部壓力\nfor external use only 僅供外用\nStudents often face external pressure from parents and teachers.\n(學生常常面臨來自家長和老師的外在壓力。)\nThis cream is for external use only, so do not swallow it.\n(這款藥膏僅供外用，請勿吞食。)"],["extinct","extinct(adj.)滅絕的、絕種的、熄滅的\nextinction(n.)滅絕\nbecome extinct 絕種\nextinct volcano 死火山\nDinosaurs became extinct about sixty-six million years ago.\n(恐龍大約在六千六百萬年前滅絕。)\nMany animals may become extinct if we don't protect their habitats.\n(如果我們不保護牠們的棲地，許多動物可能會絕種。)"],["extraordinary","extraordinary(adj.)非凡的、特別的、異常的\nextraordinarily(adv.)非常地、格外地\nextraordinary talent 非凡的才能\nextraordinary event 非比尋常的事件\nHelen Keller lived an extraordinary life despite being blind and deaf.\n(海倫·凱勒雖然又盲又聾，卻過著非凡的人生。)\nSeeing snow in Taipei would be an extraordinary event.\n(在台北看到下雪會是一件非比尋常的事。)"],["fabric","fabric(n.)布料、織物、結構\n(無詞性變化)\ncotton fabric 棉布\nthe fabric of society 社會結構\nThis shirt is made of soft cotton fabric.\n(這件襯衫是用柔軟的棉布製成的。)\nFamily values are an important part of the fabric of society.\n(家庭價值觀是社會結構中重要的一部分。)"],["fabulous","fabulous(adj.)極好的、驚人的、傳說中的\nfable(n.)寓言\na fabulous time 極愉快的時光\nfabulous wealth 驚人的財富\nWe had a fabulous time at the beach party last night.\n(我們昨晚在海灘派對上玩得非常愉快。)\nThe singer wore a fabulous dress at the award ceremony.\n(那位歌手在頒獎典禮上穿了一件超美的禮服。)"],["facilitate","facilitate(v.)促進、使便利\nfacility(n.)設施\nfacilitator(n.)協助者、引導者\nfacilitate learning 促進學習\nfacilitate communication 促進溝通\nGroup discussions can facilitate learning in the classroom.\n(分組討論能促進課堂上的學習。)\nThe new app was designed to facilitate communication between parents and teachers.\n(這款新應用程式是為了方便家長與老師溝通而設計的。)"],["faculty","faculty(n.)全體教職員、(大學)學院、能力\n(無詞性變化)\nfaculty members 教職員\nmental faculties 心智能力\nAll faculty members are invited to the meeting this Friday.\n(本週五的會議邀請全體教職員出席。)\nEven at ninety, my great-grandmother still has all her mental faculties.\n(我曾祖母即使九十歲了，頭腦仍然非常清楚。)"],["fascinate","fascinate(v.)使著迷、強烈吸引\nfascinating(adj.)迷人的\nfascination(n.)著迷\nbe fascinated by 對…著迷\nfascinating story 引人入勝的故事\nI have always been fascinated by stars and planets.\n(我一直對星星和行星深深著迷。)\nThe magician's tricks fascinated the young audience.\n(魔術師的把戲讓年輕的觀眾們看得入迷。)"],["fatigue","fatigue(n./v.)疲勞、疲倦、使疲勞\n(無詞性變化)\nmental fatigue 心理疲勞\nsuffer from fatigue 感到疲勞\nDriving for long hours without rest can cause fatigue and accidents.\n(長時間開車不休息可能導致疲勞與意外。)\nAfter the exam week, many students suffered from mental fatigue.\n(考試週結束後，許多學生都感到心理疲憊。)"],["federal","federal(adj.)聯邦的、聯邦政府的\nfederation(n.)聯邦、聯盟\nfederal government 聯邦政府\nfederal law 聯邦法律\nThe federal government of the United States is based in Washington, D.C.\n(美國聯邦政府設在華盛頓特區。)\nSelling these drugs is against federal law.\n(販賣這些藥物違反聯邦法律。)"],["fiber","fiber(n.)纖維、纖維質\n(無詞性變化)\ndietary fiber 膳食纖維\noptical fiber 光纖\nVegetables and fruits are rich in dietary fiber.\n(蔬菜和水果富含膳食纖維。)\nOptical fiber allows data to travel at very high speeds.\n(光纖讓資料能以極高速度傳輸。)"],["filter","filter(n./v.)過濾器、濾網、過濾\n(無詞性變化)\nwater filter 濾水器\nfilter out 過濾掉\nWe installed a water filter in the kitchen for clean drinking water.\n(我們在廚房裝了濾水器以取得乾淨的飲用水。)\nThe app can filter out spam messages automatically.\n(這款應用程式能自動過濾掉垃圾訊息。)"],["fiscal","fiscal(adj.)財政的、會計的\n(無詞性變化)\nfiscal year 會計年度\nfiscal policy 財政政策\nThe company's profits rose by ten percent in the last fiscal year.\n(這家公司在上一個會計年度獲利成長了百分之十。)\nThe government changed its fiscal policy to boost the economy.\n(政府調整財政政策以刺激經濟。)"],["fleet","fleet(n.)艦隊、船隊、車隊\n(無詞性變化)\na fleet of 一隊…\nfishing fleet 漁船隊\nThe company owns a fleet of electric buses.\n(這家公司擁有一支電動公車車隊。)\nThe fishing fleet returned to the harbor before the typhoon arrived.\n(漁船隊在颱風來臨前返回了港口。)"],["flexibility","flexibility(n.)彈性、靈活性、柔軟度\nflexible(adj.)有彈性的、靈活的\nshow flexibility 展現彈性\nimprove flexibility 增加柔軟度\nWorking from home gives employees more flexibility.\n(在家工作給予員工更多彈性。)\nDoing yoga regularly can improve your flexibility.\n(規律做瑜伽可以增加你身體的柔軟度。)"],["flip","flip(v./n.)輕拋、翻轉、快速翻動\n(無詞性變化)\nflip a coin 擲硬幣\nflip through 快速翻閱\nLet's flip a coin to decide who goes first.\n(我們擲硬幣決定誰先開始吧。)\nShe flipped through the magazine while waiting for the doctor.\n(她在等醫生時快速翻閱著雜誌。)"],["fluency","fluency(n.)流利、流暢\nfluent(adj.)流利的\nfluently(adv.)流利地\nfluency in 精通…(語言)\nimprove one's fluency 提升流利度\nFluency in English is required for this job.\n(這份工作要求英文流利。)\nReading aloud every day can help improve your fluency.\n(每天大聲朗讀能幫助提升你的流利度。)"],["fluid","fluid(n./adj.)液體、流體、流動的、不固定的\nfluidity(n.)流動性\ndrink plenty of fluids 多喝水\na fluid situation 變化不定的情勢\nWhen you have a cold, you should rest and drink plenty of fluids.\n(感冒時應該多休息並多喝水。)\nThe political situation is still fluid, so nobody knows what will happen.\n(政治情勢仍變化不定，所以沒有人知道會發生什麼事。)"],["forge","forge(v.)鍛造、偽造、建立(關係)\nforgery(n.)偽造、偽造品\nforge a friendship 建立友誼\nforge a signature 偽造簽名\nThe exchange program helped students forge friendships with people from other countries.\n(交換計畫幫助學生和其他國家的人建立友誼。)\nHe was caught trying to forge his father's signature on the report card.\n(他試圖在成績單上偽造爸爸的簽名，結果被抓到了。)"],["format","format(n./v.)格式、版式、形式、格式化\n(無詞性變化)\nfile format 檔案格式\nformat a disk 格式化磁碟\nPlease save your report in PDF format before you upload it.\n(上傳報告前請先存成PDF格式。)\nThe TV show changed its format to attract younger viewers.\n(這個電視節目改變了形式以吸引年輕觀眾。)"],["forum","forum(n.)論壇、討論會\n(無詞性變化)\nonline forum 網路論壇\npublic forum 公開論壇\nStudents can share their study tips on the school's online forum.\n(學生可以在學校的網路論壇上分享讀書技巧。)\nThe city held a public forum to discuss the new MRT line.\n(市政府舉辦了一場公開論壇討論新的捷運路線。)"],["foster","foster(adj./v.)寄養的、領養的、培養、促進\n(無詞性變化)\nfoster family 寄養家庭\nfoster creativity 培養創造力\nThe little girl was placed with a foster family after the accident.\n(意外發生後，那個小女孩被安置到一個寄養家庭。)\nTeachers should create a classroom that fosters creativity.\n(老師應該營造一個能培養創造力的教室環境。)"],["foul","foul(adj./n./v./adv.)骯髒的、難聞的、犯規、犯規地\n(無詞性變化)\nfoul smell 惡臭\ncommit a foul 犯規\nA foul smell came from the garbage truck.\n(垃圾車傳來一股惡臭。)\nThe basketball player committed his fifth foul and had to leave the game.\n(那名籃球員第五次犯規，必須退場。)"],["fraction","fraction(n.)分數、小部分、一點點\nfractional(adj.)極小的、分數的\na fraction of 一小部分的…\nin a fraction of a second 一瞬間\nThe online course costs only a fraction of the price of a regular class.\n(這門線上課程的費用只有一般課程的一小部分。)\nThe goalkeeper reacted in a fraction of a second.\n(守門員在一瞬間就做出了反應。)"],["fragment","fragment(n./v.)碎片、片段、使成碎片\nfragmentary(adj.)不完整的\nglass fragments 玻璃碎片\na fragment of 的片段\nBe careful not to step on the glass fragments on the floor.\n(小心不要踩到地上的玻璃碎片。)\nI can only remember fragments of the dream I had last night.\n(我只記得昨晚夢的片段。)"],["framework","framework(n.)框架、架構、體制\nframe(n.)框架\nlegal framework 法律架構\nwithin the framework of 在…的架構內\nThe new law provides a legal framework for protecting personal data.\n(新法提供了保護個人資料的法律架構。)\nThe workers built a wooden framework before pouring the concrete.\n(工人在灌水泥前先搭建了木製框架。)"],["franchise","franchise(n.)特許經營權、加盟店、系列作品\n(無詞性變化)\nfranchise store 加盟店\nmovie franchise 系列電影\nMy uncle opened a franchise store of a famous drink shop.\n(我叔叔開了一家知名飲料店的加盟店。)\nThe superhero movie franchise has earned billions of dollars.\n(這個超級英雄系列電影已經賺進了數十億美元。)"],["fraud","fraud(n.)詐騙、詐欺、騙子\nfraudulent(adj.)詐欺的\nphone fraud 電話詐騙\ncommit fraud 從事詐欺\nThe police warned elderly people about phone fraud.\n(警方提醒長者小心電話詐騙。)\nThe businessman was sent to prison for committing fraud.\n(那位商人因詐欺罪入獄。)"],["freight","freight(n./v.)貨物、貨運、運送\n(無詞性變化)\nfreight train 貨運列車\nby air freight 經由空運\nA long freight train passed slowly through the station.\n(一列長長的貨運列車緩緩駛過車站。)\nThe company sends its products to Europe by air freight.\n(這家公司將產品以空運寄往歐洲。)"],["frontier","frontier(n.)邊境、邊疆、(知識的)最前線\n(無詞性變化)\nthe frontiers of science 科學的尖端\ncross the frontier 越過邊境\nSpace is often called the final frontier of human exploration.\n(太空常被稱為人類探索的最後疆界。)\nScientists are pushing the frontiers of medical research.\n(科學家們不斷拓展醫學研究的領域。)"],["galaxy","galaxy(n.)星系、銀河\ngalactic(adj.)星系的\nthe Milky Way galaxy 銀河系\ndistant galaxy 遙遠的星系\nOur solar system is located in the Milky Way galaxy.\n(我們的太陽系位在銀河系之中。)\nThe space telescope took pictures of a galaxy billions of light-years away.\n(太空望遠鏡拍下了一個數十億光年外的星系。)"],["gasp","gasp(n./v.)喘氣、倒抽一口氣\n(無詞性變化)\ngasp for breath 上氣不接下氣\ngasp in surprise 驚訝得倒抽一口氣\nAfter running up the stairs, he was gasping for breath.\n(跑上樓梯後，他上氣不接下氣。)\nThe audience gasped in surprise when the magician disappeared.\n(魔術師消失時，觀眾驚訝得倒抽一口氣。)"],["gathering","gathering(n.)聚會、集會、收集\ngather(v.)聚集、收集\nfamily gathering 家庭聚會\nsocial gathering 社交聚會\nOur whole family has a big gathering during the Lunar New Year.\n(農曆新年期間我們全家會有一場大型聚會。)\nLarge public gatherings were banned during the epidemic.\n(疫情期間禁止大型公共集會。)"],["generate","generate(v.)產生、引起\ngeneration(n.)產生、世代\ngenerator(n.)發電機\ngenerate electricity 發電\ngenerate interest 引起興趣\nWind turbines generate electricity without polluting the air.\n(風力發電機發電時不會汙染空氣。)\nThe new science exhibit generated a lot of interest among students.\n(新的科學展覽引起了學生們極大的興趣。)"],["generator","generator(n.)發電機、產生器\ngenerate(v.)產生\npower generator 發電機\nbackup generator 備用發電機\nThe hospital uses a backup generator during power outages.\n(醫院在停電時會使用備用發電機。)\nThis website works as a random password generator.\n(這個網站可以用來隨機產生密碼。)"],["genetic","genetic(adj.)基因的、遺傳的\ngene(n.)基因\ngenetically(adv.)基因上\ngenetic engineering 基因工程\ngenetically modified food 基因改造食品\nSome diseases are caused by genetic factors.\n(有些疾病是由遺傳因素所引起的。)\nMany people are worried about the safety of genetically modified food.\n(許多人擔心基因改造食品的安全性。)"],["genetics","genetics(n.)遺傳學\ngenetic(adj.)遺傳的\ngeneticist(n.)遺傳學家\nmodern genetics 現代遺傳學\nthe father of genetics 遺傳學之父\nGregor Mendel is known as the father of modern genetics.\n(孟德爾被稱為現代遺傳學之父。)\nAdvances in genetics may help doctors cure many diseases.\n(遺傳學的進展可能幫助醫生治癒許多疾病。)"],["genre","genre(n.)類型、體裁、風格\n(無詞性變化)\nmusic genre 音樂類型\nliterary genre 文學體裁\nScience fiction is my favorite movie genre.\n(科幻片是我最喜歡的電影類型。)\nThe band mixes different music genres, such as jazz and hip-hop.\n(這個樂團融合了爵士和嘻哈等不同的音樂類型。)"],["glare","glare(n./v.)怒視、刺眼的光、怒目而視\nglaring(adj.)刺眼的、明顯的\nglare at 怒視…\nthe glare of the sun 刺眼的陽光\nThe teacher glared at the students who were talking in class.\n(老師怒視著在課堂上講話的學生。)\nShe put on sunglasses to protect her eyes from the glare of the sun.\n(她戴上太陽眼鏡保護眼睛免受刺眼陽光照射。)"],["gloomy","gloomy(adj.)陰暗的、憂鬱的、悲觀的\ngloom(n.)陰暗、憂鬱\ngloomy weather 陰沉的天氣\na gloomy future 黯淡的前景\nThe gloomy weather made everyone feel tired and sleepy.\n(陰沉的天氣讓每個人都覺得又累又想睡。)\nSome experts give a gloomy forecast for the economy next year.\n(有些專家對明年的經濟做出悲觀的預測。)"],["gorgeous","gorgeous(adj.)極美的、華麗的、令人愉快的\n(無詞性變化)\ngorgeous view 絕美的景色\ngorgeous weather 極好的天氣\nThe hotel room has a gorgeous view of Sun Moon Lake.\n(這間飯店房間可以看到日月潭的絕美景色。)\nThe bride looked gorgeous in her white wedding dress.\n(新娘穿著白色婚紗看起來美極了。)"],["grant","grant(n./v.)補助金、授予、准予、承認\n(無詞性變化)\ntake sth. for granted 把…視為理所當然\nresearch grant 研究補助金\nDon't take your parents' love for granted.\n(不要把父母的愛視為理所當然。)\nThe university granted her a full scholarship to study abroad.\n(大學提供她全額獎學金出國留學。)"],["graphic","graphic(adj./n.)圖像的、生動的、圖形\ngraph(n.)圖表\ngraphics(n.)圖像、繪圖\ngraphic design 平面設計\ngraphic description 生動的描述\nMy sister wants to study graphic design in college.\n(我姊姊想在大學念平面設計。)\nThe news report gave a graphic description of the accident.\n(新聞報導對那起事故做了生動的描述。)"],["gravity","gravity(n.)重力、地心引力、嚴重性\ngrave(adj.)嚴重的\nthe law of gravity 重力定律\nthe gravity of the situation 情勢的嚴重性\nNewton discovered the law of gravity after watching an apple fall.\n(牛頓在看到蘋果掉落後發現了重力定律。)\nThe students did not understand the gravity of the situation.\n(學生們並不了解情勢的嚴重性。)"],["greed","greed(n.)貪婪、貪心\ngreedy(adj.)貪婪的\nout of greed 出於貪婪\nhuman greed 人類的貪婪\nMany environmental problems are caused by human greed.\n(許多環境問題都是由人類的貪婪造成的。)\nHe stole the money out of greed, not because he needed it.\n(他偷錢是出於貪心，而不是因為需要。)"],["grieve","grieve(v.)悲傷、哀悼\ngrief(n.)悲傷\ngrieve for/over 為…悲傷\na grieving family 悲痛的家屬\nThe whole country grieved for the victims of the earthquake.\n(全國都為地震罹難者哀悼。)\nIt takes time for people to grieve after losing a loved one.\n(失去摯愛之後，人們需要時間去哀悼。)"],["grill","grill(n./v.)烤架、燒烤、盤問\ngrilled(adj.)烤過的\ngrilled chicken 烤雞\ngrill sb. about sth. 就某事盤問某人\nWe grilled corn and meat at the riverside for Mid-Autumn Festival.\n(中秋節時我們在河邊烤玉米和肉。)\nMy parents grilled me about where I had been all night.\n(我爸媽追問我整晚去了哪裡。)"],["grim","grim(adj.)嚴峻的、令人沮喪的、嚴肅的\ngrimly(adv.)嚴肅地、冷酷地\ngrim reality 殘酷的現實\ngrim news 令人沮喪的消息\nThe doctor's face was grim as he told us the news.\n(醫生告訴我們消息時神情嚴肅。)\nClimate scientists warn of a grim future if nothing changes.\n(氣候科學家警告，若不做出改變，未來將十分嚴峻。)"],["grip","grip(n./v.)緊握、掌握、控制、吸引住\ngripping(adj.)扣人心弦的\nget a grip on 控制住、掌握\nlose one's grip 失去控制\nGet a grip on yourself; panicking won't help.\n(冷靜一點，驚慌失措也沒有用。)\nThe child gripped his mother's hand tightly in the crowd.\n(那孩子在人群中緊緊抓住媽媽的手。)"],["gross","gross(adj./v./n.)總共的、噁心的、嚴重的、總收入\n(無詞性變化)\ngross domestic product (GDP) 國內生產毛額\ngross income 總收入\nTaiwan's gross domestic product grew steadily last year.\n(台灣去年的國內生產毛額穩定成長。)\nEww, that's gross! Don't put your dirty socks on the table.\n(噁，好噁心！不要把你的髒襪子放在桌上。)"],["guideline","guideline(n.)指導方針、準則\nguide(v./n.)引導、導遊\nfollow guidelines 遵守準則\nsafety guidelines 安全準則\nAll visitors must follow the safety guidelines in the laboratory.\n(所有訪客在實驗室都必須遵守安全準則。)\nThe school issued new guidelines on the use of AI in homework.\n(學校發布了關於在作業中使用人工智慧的新準則。)"],["gut","gut(n./v.)腸、直覺、勇氣、取出內臟、毀壞內部\nguts(n.)勇氣、膽量\ngutsy(adj.)有膽量的\ngut feeling 直覺\nhave the guts to 有勇氣做…\nMy gut feeling told me something was wrong.\n(我的直覺告訴我有些不對勁。)\nHe didn't have the guts to tell her the truth.\n(他沒有勇氣告訴她實話。)"],["habitat","habitat(n.)棲息地、自然環境\ninhabit(v.)居住於\nnatural habitat 自然棲地\nhabitat loss 棲地喪失\nHabitat loss is the biggest threat to many wild animals.\n(棲地喪失是許多野生動物面臨的最大威脅。)\nIt is better to see animals in their natural habitat than in a zoo.\n(在自然棲地看動物比在動物園看更好。)"],["haul","haul(v./n.)拖、拉、搬運、一次的收穫量\n(無詞性變化)\nhaul up 拖上來\nin the long haul 長期來看\nThe fishermen hauled their nets onto the boat.\n(漁夫們把漁網拖上船。)\nLearning a language takes effort, but it pays off in the long haul.\n(學語言需要努力，但長遠來看是值得的。)"],["hazard","hazard(n./v.)危險、危害、冒險提出\nhazardous(adj.)有危險的\nhealth hazard 健康危害\nfire hazard 火災隱患\nSmoking is a serious health hazard for both smokers and people around them.\n(吸菸對吸菸者及周遭的人都是嚴重的健康危害。)\nPiles of old newspapers in the hallway are a fire hazard.\n(走廊上堆積的舊報紙是一種火災隱患。)"],["heir","heir(n.)繼承人、後繼者\nheiress(n.)女繼承人\nheir to the throne 王位繼承人\nsole heir 唯一繼承人\nPrince William is heir to the British throne.\n(威廉王子是英國王位的繼承人。)\nAs the sole heir, she inherited her grandfather's entire fortune.\n(身為唯一繼承人，她繼承了祖父全部的財產。)"],["hence","hence(adv.)因此、從此以後\n(無詞性變化)\nhence the name 因此得名\ntwo years hence 兩年後\nThe island is shaped like a turtle, hence the name Turtle Island.\n(這座島的形狀像烏龜，因此得名龜山島。)\nThe road was blocked by a landslide; hence, we had to turn back.\n(道路被土石流阻斷，因此我們必須折返。)"],["herb","herb(n.)香草、草藥\nherbal(adj.)草藥的\nherbal tea 花草茶\nChinese herbs 中藥材\nMy grandmother grows herbs like basil and mint on her balcony.\n(我奶奶在陽台上種了羅勒和薄荷等香草。)\nSome people drink herbal tea to help them relax before bed.\n(有些人睡前喝花草茶來幫助放鬆。)"],["heritage","heritage(n.)遺產、傳統、文化遺產\n(無詞性變化)\ncultural heritage 文化遺產\nWorld Heritage Site 世界遺產\nThe old temple is an important part of the town's cultural heritage.\n(這座古廟是小鎮文化遺產中重要的一部分。)\nThe Great Wall of China is a famous World Heritage Site.\n(中國的萬里長城是著名的世界遺產。)"],["highlight","highlight(v./n.)強調、突顯、最精彩的部分\nhighlighter(n.)螢光筆\nthe highlight of 的最精彩部分\nhighlight the importance of 強調…的重要性\nThe fireworks show was the highlight of our trip to Taipei.\n(煙火秀是我們台北之旅最精彩的部分。)\nThe report highlights the importance of getting enough sleep.\n(這份報告強調充足睡眠的重要性。)"],["hockey","hockey(n.)曲棍球\n(無詞性變化)\nice hockey 冰上曲棍球\nfield hockey 草地曲棍球\nIce hockey is one of the most popular sports in Canada.\n(冰上曲棍球是加拿大最受歡迎的運動之一。)\nOur school's field hockey team won the national championship.\n(我們學校的曲棍球隊贏得了全國冠軍。)"],["honorable","honorable(adj.)可敬的、光榮的、正直的\nhonor(n./v.)榮譽、尊敬\nhonorably(adv.)光榮地、正直地\nan honorable man 正直的人\nhonorable mention 佳作、榮譽獎\nReturning the lost wallet was an honorable thing to do.\n(歸還遺失的錢包是一件值得敬佩的事。)\nMy drawing received an honorable mention in the art contest.\n(我的畫作在美術比賽中獲得了佳作。)"],["horizontal","horizontal(adj./n.)水平的、橫的、水平線\nhorizon(n.)地平線\nvertical(adj.)垂直的\nhorizontal line 水平線\nhorizontal axis 橫軸\nDraw a horizontal line across the middle of the page.\n(在頁面中間畫一條水平線。)\nThe horizontal axis of the graph shows the years.\n(這張圖表的橫軸表示年份。)"],["hormone","hormone(n.)荷爾蒙、激素\nhormonal(adj.)荷爾蒙的\ngrowth hormone 生長激素\nstress hormone 壓力荷爾蒙\nTeenagers go through many hormone changes during puberty.\n(青少年在青春期會經歷許多荷爾蒙變化。)\nGetting enough sleep helps the body produce growth hormone.\n(充足的睡眠有助於身體分泌生長激素。)"],["hostage","hostage(n.)人質\n(無詞性變化)\ntake sb. hostage 挾持某人為人質\nrelease hostages 釋放人質\nThe robbers took three bank workers hostage.\n(搶匪挾持了三名銀行員工作為人質。)\nAfter hours of talks, all the hostages were released safely.\n(經過數小時的談判，所有人質都被安全釋放。)"],["hostile","hostile(adj.)敵對的、懷有敵意的、不友善的\nhostility(n.)敵意\nbe hostile to 對…懷有敵意\nhostile environment 惡劣的環境\nThe villagers were hostile to the idea of building a factory nearby.\n(村民們強烈反對在附近蓋工廠的想法。)\nFew plants can survive in such a hostile environment.\n(很少植物能在如此惡劣的環境中生存。)"],["hostility","hostility(n.)敵意、敵對、戰爭行為\nhostile(adj.)敵對的\nhostility toward 對…的敵意\nopen hostility 公開的敵意\nHe felt hostility from his new classmates on the first day.\n(第一天他就感受到新同學對他的敵意。)\nThe two countries finally agreed to end their hostilities.\n(兩國終於同意停止敵對行動。)"],["housing","housing(n.)住房、住宅、房屋供給\nhouse(n./v.)房屋、收容\nhousing prices 房價\npublic housing 公共住宅、社會住宅\nHigh housing prices make it hard for young people to buy a home.\n(高房價讓年輕人很難買房。)\nThe city plans to build more public housing for low-income families.\n(市政府計畫為低收入家庭興建更多社會住宅。)"],["howl","howl(n./v.)嚎叫、怒吼、哀號\n(無詞性變化)\nhowl with laughter 捧腹大笑\nthe howl of the wind 風的呼嘯聲\nWe could hear wolves howling in the distance.\n(我們能聽到遠處狼群的嚎叫聲。)\nThe audience howled with laughter at the comedian's jokes.\n(觀眾被那位喜劇演員的笑話逗得捧腹大笑。)"],["hypothesis","hypothesis(n.)假說、假設\nhypotheses(n.)假說(複數)\nhypothetical(adj.)假設的\ntest a hypothesis 驗證假說\nsupport a hypothesis 支持假說\nScientists design experiments to test their hypotheses.\n(科學家設計實驗來驗證他們的假說。)\nThe new data supports the hypothesis that the climate is getting warmer.\n(新的數據支持了氣候正在變暖的假說。)"],["icon","icon(n.)圖示、偶像、象徵\niconic(adj.)代表性的、標誌性的\nfashion icon 時尚偶像\nclick on the icon 點選圖示\nClick on the icon at the top of the screen to open the app.\n(點選螢幕上方的圖示來開啟應用程式。)\nTaipei 101 has become an icon of Taiwan.\n(台北101已經成為台灣的象徵。)"],["ideology","ideology(n.)意識形態、思想體系\nideological(adj.)意識形態的\npolitical ideology 政治意識形態\nideological differences 意識形態的差異\nThe two parties have very different political ideologies.\n(這兩個政黨的政治意識形態大不相同。)\nIdeological differences sometimes make it hard for people to cooperate.\n(意識形態的差異有時讓人們很難合作。)"],["idiot","idiot(n.)白痴、傻瓜\nidiotic(adj.)愚蠢的\nfeel like an idiot 覺得自己像個傻瓜\na complete idiot 十足的笨蛋\nI felt like an idiot when I realized I had gone to the wrong classroom.\n(當我發現自己走錯教室時，覺得自己像個傻瓜。)\nOnly an idiot would drive that fast in heavy rain.\n(只有笨蛋才會在大雨中開那麼快。)"],["illusion","illusion(n.)錯覺、幻想、假象\nillusory(adj.)虛幻的\noptical illusion 視覺錯覺\nbe under the illusion that 誤以為…\nThis picture is an optical illusion; the two lines are actually the same length.\n(這張圖是一種視覺錯覺，兩條線其實一樣長。)\nHe was under the illusion that he could pass the test without studying.\n(他誤以為自己不用讀書就能通過考試。)"],["immense","immense(adj.)巨大的、極大的\nimmensely(adv.)極其、非常\nimmense pressure 巨大的壓力\nan immense amount of 大量的…\nSenior high school students often face immense pressure before the college entrance exam.\n(高中生在大學入學考試前常面臨巨大的壓力。)\nBuilding the bridge took an immense amount of time and money.\n(建造這座橋花費了大量的時間和金錢。)"],["immune","immune(adj.)免疫的、不受影響的、豁免的\nimmunity(n.)免疫力\nimmune system 免疫系統\nbe immune to 對…免疫、不受…影響\nRegular exercise can help strengthen your immune system.\n(規律運動有助於強化你的免疫系統。)\nNo one is completely immune to criticism.\n(沒有人能完全不受批評的影響。)"],["implement","implement(v./n.)實施、執行、工具\nimplementation(n.)實施、執行\nimplement a policy 實施政策\nfarm implements 農具\nThe school will implement a new uniform policy next semester.\n(學校下學期將實施新的制服規定。)\nThe museum displays old farm implements used by early settlers.\n(博物館展示早期移民使用過的舊農具。)"],["implication","implication(n.)可能的影響、含意、牽連\nimply(v.)暗示、意味\nhave implications for 對…有影響\nby implication 言下之意\nThe new law will have serious implications for small businesses.\n(新法將對小型企業造成嚴重的影響。)\nHe said the plan was risky and, by implication, that we should not try it.\n(他說這個計畫有風險，言下之意是我們不該嘗試。)"],["impulse","impulse(n.)衝動、推動力、脈衝\nimpulsive(adj.)衝動的\non impulse 一時衝動\nimpulse buying 衝動購物\nI bought these shoes on impulse, but I don't really need them.\n(我一時衝動買了這雙鞋，但其實並不需要。)\nOnline sales often encourage impulse buying.\n(網路特賣常常助長衝動購物。)"],["incentive","incentive(n./adj.)誘因、動機、獎勵的\n(無詞性變化)\ntax incentive 租稅優惠\nincentive to do 做…的動機\nThe government offers tax incentives to companies that use green energy.\n(政府對使用綠色能源的公司提供租稅優惠。)\nGood grades can be an incentive for students to study harder.\n(好成績可以成為學生更努力讀書的動力。)"],["incorporate","incorporate(v.)包含、納入、合併\nincorporation(n.)納入、合併\nincorporate A into B 把A納入B\nincorporated company 股份有限公司\nThe teacher incorporated games into her English lessons.\n(老師把遊戲融入她的英文課中。)\nThe new design incorporates many suggestions from students.\n(新的設計納入了許多學生的建議。)"],["index","index(n./v.)索引、指數、指標、編入索引\nindices(n.)指數(複數)\nprice index 物價指數\nindex finger 食指\nYou can find the word quickly by looking it up in the index.\n(你可以從索引中查找，很快就能找到這個字。)\nThe air quality index was very high in the city yesterday.\n(昨天市區的空氣品質指標非常高。)"],["indifferent","indifferent(adj.)漠不關心的、冷淡的、平庸的\nindifference(n.)冷漠\nbe indifferent to 對…漠不關心\nan indifferent attitude 冷淡的態度\nHow can people be indifferent to the suffering of others?\n(人們怎麼能對他人的苦難漠不關心呢？)\nHis indifferent attitude toward his studies worried his parents.\n(他對課業漠不關心的態度讓他父母很擔心。)"],["indigenous","indigenous(adj.)原住民的、本土的、原生的\n(無詞性變化)\nindigenous peoples 原住民族\nindigenous species 原生物種\nTaiwan has sixteen officially recognized indigenous peoples.\n(台灣有十六個官方認定的原住民族。)\nThe Formosan black bear is an indigenous species of Taiwan.\n(台灣黑熊是台灣的原生物種。)"],["indispensable","indispensable(adj.)不可或缺的、必需的\ndispensable(adj.)非必要的\nindispensable to/for 對…不可或缺\nan indispensable tool 不可或缺的工具\nSmartphones have become an indispensable tool in modern life.\n(智慧型手機已經成為現代生活中不可或缺的工具。)\nClean water is indispensable to human survival.\n(乾淨的水對人類生存是不可或缺的。)"],["indulge","indulge(v.)沉溺、縱容、盡情享受\nindulgence(n.)沉溺、放縱\nindulgent(adj.)縱容的\nindulge in 沉迷於、盡情享受\nindulge a child 寵溺孩子\nAfter the exam, I indulged in a big bowl of shaved ice.\n(考完試後，我盡情享受了一大碗剉冰。)\nGrandparents often indulge their grandchildren with sweets and toys.\n(祖父母常用糖果和玩具寵溺孫子女。)"],["inevitable","inevitable(adj.)不可避免的、必然的\ninevitably(adv.)不可避免地\nan inevitable result 必然的結果\nit is inevitable that 無可避免的是…\nMaking mistakes is an inevitable part of learning.\n(犯錯是學習過程中無可避免的一部分。)\nIt was inevitable that prices would rise after the typhoon.\n(颱風過後物價上漲是必然的。)"],["infect","infect(v.)傳染、感染、影響\ninfection(n.)感染\ninfectious(adj.)傳染性的\nbe infected with 感染…\ninfected wound 受感染的傷口\nThousands of people were infected with the virus last winter.\n(去年冬天有數千人感染了這種病毒。)\nHer laughter infected everyone in the room.\n(她的笑聲感染了房間裡的每一個人。)"],["infinite","infinite(adj.)無限的、無窮的\ninfinity(n.)無限\ninfinitely(adv.)無限地、極其\ninfinite patience 無比的耐心\ninfinite possibilities 無限的可能\nThe kindergarten teacher showed infinite patience with the children.\n(那位幼兒園老師對孩子們展現了無比的耐心。)\nYoung people have infinite possibilities for the future.\n(年輕人的未來有無限的可能。)"],["infrastructure","infrastructure(n.)基礎建設、公共設施\n(無詞性變化)\npublic infrastructure 公共基礎建設\ntransportation infrastructure 交通建設\nThe government plans to spend billions on public infrastructure.\n(政府計畫投入數十億元於公共基礎建設。)\nGood transportation infrastructure helps the economy grow.\n(良好的交通建設有助於經濟成長。)"],["inherent","inherent(adj.)固有的、內在的、天生的\ninherently(adv.)本質上\ninherent in 為…所固有\ninherent risk 固有的風險\nThere are risks inherent in every extreme sport.\n(每一項極限運動都有其固有的風險。)\nCuriosity is an inherent part of human nature.\n(好奇心是人性中固有的一部分。)"],["inherit","inherit(v.)繼承、遺傳、接手\ninheritance(n.)遺產、繼承\nheir(n.)繼承人\ninherit from 從…繼承\ninherit a fortune 繼承財產\nShe inherited her mother's talent for music.\n(她遺傳了母親的音樂天分。)\nHe inherited the family restaurant from his father.\n(他從父親那裡接手了家族餐廳。)"],["initiate","initiate(v./adj./n.)開始、發起、使入會、新入會者\ninitiation(n.)開始、入會儀式\ninitiative(n.)倡議、主動性\ninitiate a conversation 開啟對話\ninitiate a project 發起計畫\nShy students often find it hard to initiate a conversation.\n(害羞的學生常常很難主動開啟對話。)\nThe student council initiated a project to reduce plastic waste on campus.\n(學生會發起了一項減少校園塑膠垃圾的計畫。)"],["initiative","initiative(n./adj.)主動性、倡議、新方案、起始的\ninitiate(v.)發起\ntake the initiative 採取主動\non one's own initiative 主動地\nShe took the initiative to organize a beach cleanup.\n(她主動籌辦了一場淨灘活動。)\nThe city launched a new initiative to encourage people to ride bikes.\n(市政府推出一項鼓勵民眾騎腳踏車的新方案。)"],["inject","inject(v.)注射、注入、投入\ninjection(n.)注射\ninject sth. into 把…注入…\ninject money into 投入資金到…\nThe nurse injected the medicine into the patient's arm.\n(護理師把藥物注射到病人的手臂中。)\nThe new teacher injected fresh energy into the class.\n(新老師為班級注入了一股新的活力。)"],["injection","injection(n.)注射、打針、(資金)投入\ninject(v.)注射\ngive sb. an injection 幫某人打針\nan injection of cash 資金注入\nThe doctor gave the child an injection to lower his fever.\n(醫生幫那孩子打了一針退燒。)\nThe company needs an injection of cash to survive.\n(這家公司需要資金挹注才能生存下去。)"],["inning","inning(n.)(棒球)局\ninnings(n.)(板球)局、一局\nthe ninth inning 第九局\nthe top of the inning 上半局\nOur team scored three runs in the ninth inning and won the game.\n(我們隊在第九局得了三分，贏得了比賽。)\nThe pitcher was replaced in the bottom of the sixth inning.\n(那位投手在六局下半被換下場。)"],["innovation","innovation(n.)創新、新發明\ninnovate(v.)創新\ninnovative(adj.)創新的\ntechnological innovation 科技創新\nencourage innovation 鼓勵創新\nTechnological innovation has changed the way we learn.\n(科技創新改變了我們學習的方式。)\nThe company encourages innovation by rewarding new ideas.\n(這家公司以獎勵新點子的方式鼓勵創新。)"],["innovative","innovative(adj.)創新的、新穎的\ninnovation(n.)創新\ninnovate(v.)創新\ninnovative design 創新設計\ninnovative approach 創新的方法\nThe students came up with an innovative design for a solar-powered car.\n(學生們想出了一個太陽能車的創新設計。)\nOur teacher uses innovative approaches to make history lessons fun.\n(我們老師用創新的方法讓歷史課變得有趣。)"],["inquiry","inquiry(n.)詢問、調查、探究\ninquire(v.)詢問、調查\nmake inquiries 詢問、打聽\nan inquiry into 對…的調查\nWe received many inquiries about the summer camp.\n(我們接到許多關於夏令營的詢問。)\nThe government ordered an inquiry into the cause of the fire.\n(政府下令調查這場火災的起因。)"],["insane","insane(adj.)瘋狂的、荒唐的、精神失常的\ninsanity(n.)精神失常、瘋狂\ndrive sb. insane 把某人逼瘋\nan insane idea 瘋狂的主意\nThe noise from the construction site is driving me insane.\n(工地傳來的噪音快把我逼瘋了。)\nRiding a bike across Taiwan in three days sounds insane.\n(三天騎腳踏車環島聽起來很瘋狂。)"],["insight","insight(n.)洞察力、深刻見解\ninsightful(adj.)有洞察力的\ngain insight into 深入了解…\nvaluable insight 寶貴的見解\nVolunteering at the hospital gave me insight into a doctor's daily life.\n(在醫院當志工讓我深入了解醫生的日常生活。)\nThe speaker shared valuable insights about studying abroad.\n(講者分享了關於出國留學的寶貴見解。)"],["installation","installation(n.)安裝、設置、裝置藝術\ninstall(v.)安裝\nsoftware installation 軟體安裝\nart installation 裝置藝術\nThe installation of the new air conditioners will take two days.\n(安裝新冷氣將需要兩天的時間。)\nThe art installation in the park attracted many visitors.\n(公園裡的裝置藝術吸引了許多遊客。)"],["institute","institute(n./v.)機構、學院、研究所、設立、制定\ninstitution(n.)機構、制度\nresearch institute 研究機構\ninstitute a policy 制定政策\nShe works at a research institute that studies earthquakes.\n(她在一間研究地震的研究機構工作。)\nThe school instituted a new rule to ban phones in class.\n(學校制定了一項上課禁止使用手機的新規定。)"],["institution","institution(n.)機構、制度、慣例\ninstitute(n./v.)機構、設立\ninstitutional(adj.)機構的、制度上的\nfinancial institution 金融機構\neducational institution 教育機構\nBanks and insurance companies are financial institutions.\n(銀行和保險公司都是金融機構。)\nMarriage is one of the oldest social institutions.\n(婚姻是最古老的社會制度之一。)"],["intact","intact(adj.)完整無缺的、未受損的\n(無詞性變化)\nremain intact 保持完整\nfully intact 完好無缺\nAmazingly, the old temple remained intact after the earthquake.\n(令人驚訝的是，那座古廟在地震後仍完好無缺。)\nThe package arrived with everything inside intact.\n(包裹送達時裡面的東西都完好無損。)"],["integrate","integrate(v.)整合、使融入、結合\nintegration(n.)整合、融入\nintegrated(adj.)整合的\nintegrate into 融入…\nintegrate A with B 將A與B結合\nIt took the new students a few weeks to integrate into the class.\n(新同學花了幾週才融入班級。)\nThe course integrates science with art in creative ways.\n(這門課以富有創意的方式將科學與藝術結合。)"],["integration","integration(n.)整合、融合、融入\nintegrate(v.)整合\nsocial integration 社會融合\neconomic integration 經濟整合\nLanguage classes help the social integration of new immigrants.\n(語言課程有助於新移民融入社會。)\nThe integration of technology into education is happening quickly.\n(科技融入教育的速度正在加快。)"],["integrity","integrity(n.)正直、誠實、完整\n(無詞性變化)\na person of integrity 正直的人\nacademic integrity 學術誠信\nHe is a person of integrity who never breaks his promises.\n(他是個正直的人，從不食言。)\nCopying someone else's report is a violation of academic integrity.\n(抄襲別人的報告違反學術誠信。)"],["intensify","intensify(v.)加強、加劇\nintense(adj.)強烈的\nintensity(n.)強度\nintensify efforts 加緊努力\nthe storm intensifies 暴風雨增強\nThe typhoon is expected to intensify as it moves toward Taiwan.\n(這個颱風預計在朝台灣移動時增強。)\nThe police intensified their efforts to find the missing child.\n(警方加緊搜尋失蹤孩童。)"],["intent","intent(n./adj.)意圖、目的、專心的、決意的\nintention(n.)意圖\nintend(v.)打算\nbe intent on 專注於、決意要\nwith intent to 意圖…\nShe was so intent on her book that she didn't hear me come in.\n(她太專心看書，沒聽到我進來。)\nThe man was charged with breaking into the house with intent to steal.\n(那名男子被控意圖竊盜而闖入民宅。)"],["interference","interference(n.)干涉、干擾、妨礙\ninterfere(v.)干涉、妨礙\ninterference in 對…的干涉\nradio interference 無線電干擾\nTeenagers often dislike their parents' interference in their personal lives.\n(青少年常不喜歡父母干涉他們的私生活。)\nThe strange noise on the radio was caused by interference.\n(收音機裡奇怪的噪音是干擾造成的。)"],["interior","interior(adj./n.)內部的、內部、室內\nexterior(adj./n.)外部的、外部\ninterior design 室內設計\nthe interior of 的內部\nMy cousin works as an interior designer in Taichung.\n(我表姊在台中當室內設計師。)\nThe interior of the old church was beautifully decorated.\n(那座老教堂的內部裝飾得很美。)"],["interpretation","interpretation(n.)解釋、詮釋、口譯\ninterpret(v.)解釋、口譯\ninterpreter(n.)口譯員\nopen to interpretation 有多種解讀空間\nsimultaneous interpretation 同步口譯\nThe ending of the movie is open to interpretation.\n(這部電影的結局有很多解讀的空間。)\nEach actor gave a different interpretation of the same character.\n(每位演員對同一個角色都有不同的詮釋。)"],["interval","interval(n.)間隔、間距、中場休息\n(無詞性變化)\nat regular intervals 定期地、每隔一段時間\nat intervals of 每隔…\nBuses leave the station at regular intervals of ten minutes.\n(公車每隔十分鐘從車站發車。)\nThere will be a fifteen-minute interval between the two parts of the concert.\n(音樂會上下半場之間會有十五分鐘的中場休息。)"],["intervention","intervention(n.)干預、介入、調停\nintervene(v.)干預、介入\ngovernment intervention 政府干預\nearly intervention 及早介入\nWithout government intervention, housing prices may keep rising.\n(若沒有政府干預，房價可能會持續上漲。)\nEarly intervention can help children with learning difficulties.\n(及早介入能幫助有學習困難的孩子。)"],["investigator","investigator(n.)調查員、研究者\ninvestigate(v.)調查\ninvestigation(n.)調查\nprivate investigator 私家偵探\naccident investigator 事故調查員\nInvestigators are still trying to find out the cause of the plane crash.\n(調查人員仍在試圖找出墜機的原因。)\nShe hired a private investigator to find her lost brother.\n(她雇用了一名私家偵探尋找失散的哥哥。)"],["irony","irony(n.)諷刺、反諷、出乎意料的結果\nironic(adj.)諷刺的\nironically(adv.)諷刺的是\nthe irony is that 諷刺的是…\na touch of irony 一絲諷刺\nThe irony is that the fire station itself caught fire.\n(諷刺的是，消防局本身竟然失火了。)\nHe spoke with a touch of irony when he praised my cooking.\n(他稱讚我的廚藝時帶著一絲諷刺。)"],["journalism","journalism(n.)新聞業、新聞學、新聞工作\njournalist(n.)記者\njournal(n.)期刊、日誌\ninvestigative journalism 調查報導\nstudy journalism 念新聞系\nShe decided to study journalism because she wants to report the truth.\n(她決定念新聞系，因為她想報導真相。)\nGood investigative journalism can expose corruption in government.\n(好的調查報導可以揭發政府的貪腐。)"],["journalist","journalist(n.)記者、新聞工作者\njournalism(n.)新聞業\nfreelance journalist 自由記者\nsports journalist 體育記者\nThe journalist interviewed several students about the new school policy.\n(那位記者就學校新政策採訪了幾位學生。)\nMy aunt has worked as a sports journalist for ten years.\n(我阿姨擔任體育記者已經十年了。)"],["judicial","judicial(adj.)司法的、法院的\njudge(n./v.)法官、判斷\njudiciary(n.)司法部門\njudicial system 司法制度\nJudicial Yuan 司法院\nAn independent judicial system is important in a democracy.\n(獨立的司法制度在民主社會中非常重要。)\nThe Judicial Yuan is the highest judicial organ in Taiwan.\n(司法院是台灣最高的司法機關。)"],["jug","jug(n./v.)壺、罐、用壺燉\n(無詞性變化)\na jug of 一壺…\nwater jug 水壺\nShe poured a jug of lemonade for the guests.\n(她為客人倒了一壺檸檬汁。)\nPlease fill the water jug and put it on the table.\n(請把水壺裝滿放在桌上。)"],["jury","jury(n.)陪審團、評審團\njuror(n.)陪審員\nthe jury is still out 尚無定論\nserve on a jury 擔任陪審員\nThe jury found the man not guilty.\n(陪審團判定那名男子無罪。)\nThe jury is still out on whether the new policy will work.\n(這項新政策是否有效尚無定論。)"],["justify","justify(v.)證明…正當、為…辯護\njustification(n.)正當理由\njustified(adj.)正當的、有理由的\njustify one's decision 為自己的決定辯護\nThe end justifies the means. 為達目的不擇手段。\nHow can you justify spending so much money on a phone?\n(你要怎麼解釋花這麼多錢買一支手機是合理的？)\nNothing can justify violence against innocent people.\n(任何理由都不能讓對無辜者施暴變得正當。)"],["juvenile","juvenile(adj./n.)青少年的、幼稚的、少年\n(無詞性變化)\njuvenile delinquency 青少年犯罪\njuvenile court 少年法庭\nThe government is taking steps to reduce juvenile delinquency.\n(政府正採取措施減少青少年犯罪。)\nHis juvenile behavior embarrassed everyone at the party.\n(他幼稚的行為讓派對上的每個人都很尷尬。)"],["kidnap","kidnap(v.)綁架、誘拐\nkidnapper(n.)綁匪\nkidnapping(n.)綁架\nbe kidnapped 被綁架\nkidnap for ransom 擄人勒贖\nThe businessman's son was kidnapped on his way home from school.\n(那位商人的兒子在放學回家途中被綁架。)\nThe kidnappers demanded a large amount of money for the girl's release.\n(綁匪要求一大筆錢才肯釋放那名女孩。)"],["landlord","landlord(n.)房東、地主\nlandlady(n.)女房東\ntenant(n.)房客\nrent from a landlord 向房東租房\na strict landlord 嚴格的房東\nOur landlord raised the rent by five percent this year.\n(我們的房東今年把房租調漲了百分之五。)\nYou should tell your landlord if something in the apartment breaks.\n(如果公寓裡有東西壞了，你應該告訴房東。)"],["laser","laser(n.)雷射\n(無詞性變化)\nlaser pointer 雷射筆\nlaser surgery 雷射手術\nThe teacher used a laser pointer during the presentation.\n(老師在簡報時使用了雷射筆。)\nMany people have laser surgery to correct their eyesight.\n(許多人接受雷射手術來矯正視力。)"],["lawmaker","lawmaker(n.)立法者、立法委員\n(無詞性變化)\nlocal lawmakers 地方立法者\nlawmakers pass a bill 立法者通過法案\nLawmakers passed a new bill to protect animal rights.\n(立法委員通過了一項保護動物權益的新法案。)\nStudents wrote letters to lawmakers about climate change.\n(學生們寫信給立法委員表達對氣候變遷的關心。)"],["lawsuit","lawsuit(n.)訴訟\nsue(v.)控告\nfile a lawsuit 提起訴訟\nwin a lawsuit 打贏官司\nThe residents filed a lawsuit against the factory for polluting the river.\n(居民對那家汙染河川的工廠提起訴訟。)\nThe singer won the lawsuit and received a large sum of money.\n(那位歌手打贏了官司，獲得一大筆賠償金。)"],["layer","layer(n./v.)層、層次、分層放置\n(無詞性變化)\nozone layer 臭氧層\na thin layer of 一層薄薄的…\nThe ozone layer protects the earth from harmful sunlight.\n(臭氧層保護地球免受有害陽光的照射。)\nA thin layer of dust covered the old piano.\n(一層薄薄的灰塵覆蓋著那台舊鋼琴。)"],["league","league(n./v.)聯盟、聯賽、結盟\n(無詞性變化)\nmajor league 大聯盟\nin league with 與…勾結\nHe dreams of playing baseball in the major leagues one day.\n(他夢想有一天能在大聯盟打棒球。)\nThe police believe the guard was in league with the thieves.\n(警方認為那名警衛和小偷勾結。)"],["legacy","legacy(n.)遺產、遺留下來的事物\n(無詞性變化)\nleave a legacy 留下遺產\ncultural legacy 文化遺產\nThe great scientist left a legacy that still inspires young people today.\n(那位偉大的科學家留下的遺產至今仍激勵著年輕人。)\nPollution may be our generation's legacy to future generations.\n(汙染可能是我們這一代留給後代的遺產。)"],["legendary","legendary(adj.)傳說中的、傳奇的、極有名的\nlegend(n.)傳說、傳奇人物\na legendary figure 傳奇人物\nlegendary creature 傳說中的生物\nMichael Jordan is a legendary figure in basketball history.\n(麥可·喬丹是籃球史上的傳奇人物。)\nThe dragon is a legendary creature in many Asian cultures.\n(龍是許多亞洲文化中傳說中的生物。)"],["legislation","legislation(n.)法律、法規、立法\nlegislate(v.)立法\nlegislative(adj.)立法的\npass legislation 通過立法\nnew legislation 新法規\nThe government passed legislation to ban smoking in public places.\n(政府通過立法禁止在公共場所吸菸。)\nNew legislation will protect workers from long working hours.\n(新法規將保障勞工免於過長的工時。)"],["legislative","legislative(adj.)立法的、有立法權的\nlegislation(n.)立法\nlegislator(n.)立法者\nLegislative Yuan 立法院\nlegislative power 立法權\nThe Legislative Yuan is responsible for making laws in Taiwan.\n(立法院負責制定台灣的法律。)\nIn a democracy, legislative power belongs to the people's representatives.\n(在民主國家，立法權屬於人民的代表。)"],["legitimate","legitimate(adj./v.)合法的、正當的、合理的、使合法\nlegitimacy(n.)合法性、正當性\nlegitimately(adv.)合法地\nlegitimate reason 正當理由\nlegitimate business 合法的生意\nBeing sick is a legitimate reason for missing class.\n(生病是缺課的正當理由。)\nCustomers have a legitimate right to complain about poor service.\n(顧客有正當的權利抱怨服務品質不佳。)"],["lest","lest(conj.)以免、唯恐\n(無詞性變化)\nlest sb. (should) do 以免某人…\nlest we forget 以免我們遺忘\nShe wrote down the address lest she should forget it.\n(她把地址寫了下來，以免忘記。)\nThe museum was built lest we forget the lessons of the war.\n(這座博物館的建立是為了讓我們不忘記戰爭的教訓。)"],["liability","liability(n.)責任、負債、累贅\nliable(adj.)有責任的、易於…的\nlegal liability 法律責任\na liability to 對…是個負擔\nThe company accepted legal liability for the accident.\n(公司承擔了這起事故的法律責任。)\nThe injured player became a liability to the team.\n(那名受傷的球員成了球隊的負擔。)"],["likelihood","likelihood(n.)可能性\nlikely(adj.)可能的\nin all likelihood 很可能\nthe likelihood of 的可能性\nRegular exercise reduces the likelihood of heart disease.\n(規律運動可以降低罹患心臟病的可能性。)\nIn all likelihood, the game will be canceled because of the typhoon.\n(這場比賽很可能會因為颱風而取消。)"],["likewise","likewise(adv.)同樣地、也\n(無詞性變化)\ndo likewise 照著做\nNice to meet you. – Likewise. 很高興認識你。－我也是。\nHer father was a doctor, and she plans to do likewise.\n(她的父親是醫生，而她也打算從醫。)\nThe teacher worked hard, and the students were likewise eager to learn.\n(老師很努力，學生們也同樣渴望學習。)"],["loop","loop(n.)環、圈、迴路\n(無詞性變化)\nin the loop 了解內情、掌握最新消息\na loop of 一圈…\nPlease keep me in the loop about the plans for the school trip.\n(關於校外教學的計畫，請隨時讓我知道最新消息。)\nThe runners completed five loops around the park.\n(跑者們繞著公園跑了五圈。)"],["lounge","lounge(n./v.)休息室、交誼廳、閒逛、懶洋洋地躺\n(無詞性變化)\nairport lounge 機場貴賓室\nteachers' lounge 教師休息室\nWe waited for our flight in the airport lounge.\n(我們在機場貴賓室候機。)\nOn Sundays, my father likes to lounge on the sofa and watch TV.\n(星期天時我爸爸喜歡懶洋洋地躺在沙發上看電視。)"],["lump","lump(n./v.)塊、腫塊、把…混為一談\nlumpy(adj.)多塊狀的\na lump of sugar 一塊方糖\nlump together 混為一談、歸在一起\nShe put a lump of sugar in her coffee.\n(她在咖啡裡放了一塊方糖。)\nYou shouldn't lump all teenagers together as lazy.\n(你不該把所有青少年都一概說成懶惰。)"],["mainstream","mainstream(n.)主流\n(無詞性變化)\nmainstream media 主流媒體\nmainstream culture 主流文化\nOnline shopping has become part of the mainstream in recent years.\n(近年來網路購物已經成為主流的一部分。)\nMany young people get their news from social media instead of mainstream media.\n(許多年輕人從社群媒體而非主流媒體獲得新聞。)"],["maintenance","maintenance(n.)維修、保養、維持\nmaintain(v.)維持、保養\nregular maintenance 定期保養\nmaintenance cost 維修費用\nThe elevator is closed for maintenance this afternoon.\n(電梯今天下午因維修暫停使用。)\nRegular maintenance can make your car last much longer.\n(定期保養能讓你的車子用得更久。)"],["mammal","mammal(n.)哺乳動物\nmammalian(adj.)哺乳動物的\nmarine mammal 海洋哺乳動物\nlarge mammal 大型哺乳動物\nWhales and dolphins are mammals, not fish.\n(鯨魚和海豚是哺乳動物，不是魚類。)\nBats are the only mammals that can truly fly.\n(蝙蝠是唯一真正會飛的哺乳動物。)"],["mandate","mandate(n.)授權、命令、任期\nmandatory(adj.)強制的、義務的\na mandate to 做……的授權\ngovernment mandate 政府命令\nThe new government has a clear mandate to reform education.\n(新政府獲得明確授權進行教育改革。)\nThe mask mandate was lifted after the pandemic eased.\n(疫情趨緩後，口罩令便解除了。)"],["manifest","manifest(v./adj.)顯示、表明、明顯的\nmanifestation(n.)表現、顯示\nmanifest itself 顯現出來\nmanifest interest 表露興趣\nThe symptoms of the disease may not manifest for several years.\n(這種疾病的症狀可能好幾年都不會顯現。)\nHer talent for music manifested itself at an early age.\n(她的音樂天分很早就顯露出來了。)"],["manipulate","manipulate(v.)操縱、控制、巧妙處理\nmanipulation(n.)操縱\nmanipulative(adj.)善於操縱他人的\nmanipulate data 竄改資料\nmanipulate public opinion 操縱輿論\nSome advertisements try to manipulate people's emotions.\n(有些廣告試圖操縱人們的情緒。)\nThe scientist was accused of manipulating the results of the experiment.\n(那位科學家被指控竄改實驗結果。)"],["mansion","mansion(n.)大廈、豪宅、宅邸\n(無詞性變化)\nluxury mansion 豪華宅邸\nold mansion 古宅\nThe movie star lives in a huge mansion with a swimming pool.\n(那位電影明星住在一棟有游泳池的豪宅裡。)\nThe old mansion has been turned into a museum.\n(那座古宅已被改建成博物館。)"],["marine","marine(adj./n.)海洋的、海軍陸戰隊員\n(無詞性變化)\nmarine life 海洋生物\nmarine biologist 海洋生物學家\nPlastic pollution is a serious threat to marine life.\n(塑膠汙染對海洋生物是嚴重的威脅。)\nShe hopes to become a marine biologist and study coral reefs.\n(她希望成為海洋生物學家並研究珊瑚礁。)"],["masculine","masculine(adj./n.)男性的、有男子氣概的、陽性(詞)\nmasculinity(n.)男子氣概\nmasculine image 男性化形象\nmasculine voice 低沉的男性嗓音\nHe has a deep, masculine voice.\n(他有低沉、富男子氣概的嗓音。)\nTraditional ideas about masculine roles are changing in modern society.\n(現代社會中，關於男性角色的傳統觀念正在改變。)"],["massage","massage(n./v.)按摩\nmasseur(n.)按摩師\nfoot massage 腳底按摩\ngive sb. a massage 幫某人按摩\nAfter a long day of hiking, a foot massage feels wonderful.\n(健行一整天之後，做個腳底按摩感覺真棒。)\nShe massaged her father's shoulders to help him relax.\n(她幫爸爸按摩肩膀讓他放鬆。)"],["massive","massive(adj.)巨大的、大量的\nmass(n.)大量、團塊\nmassively(adv.)大規模地\nmassive amount 大量\nmassive earthquake 大地震\nA massive earthquake struck the area early this morning.\n(今天清晨一場大地震襲擊了該地區。)\nThe company spent a massive amount of money on advertising.\n(這家公司花了大筆金錢在廣告上。)"],["masterpiece","masterpiece(n.)傑作、名作\n(無詞性變化)\nliterary masterpiece 文學名著\ntrue masterpiece 真正的傑作\nThe Mona Lisa is considered Leonardo da Vinci's masterpiece.\n(《蒙娜麗莎》被視為達文西的傑作。)\nMany critics call this film a masterpiece of modern cinema.\n(許多影評人稱這部電影為現代電影的傑作。)"],["mattress","mattress(n.)床墊\n(無詞性變化)\nfirm mattress 硬床墊\nair mattress 充氣床墊\nA good mattress can improve the quality of your sleep.\n(好的床墊能改善你的睡眠品質。)\nWe slept on air mattresses during the camping trip.\n(露營期間我們睡在充氣床墊上。)"],["meantime","meantime(n./adv.)其間、同時\nmeanwhile(adv.)同時\nin the meantime 在此期間\nfor the meantime 暫時\nThe doctor will see you soon; in the meantime, please fill out this form.\n(醫生很快就會看診；在此期間，請填寫這張表格。)\nDinner won't be ready for an hour, so have some fruit in the meantime.\n(晚餐還要一個小時才好，你先吃點水果吧。)"],["mechanism","mechanism(n.)機制、機械裝置\nmechanical(adj.)機械的\nmechanic(n.)技工\ndefense mechanism 防衛機制\nsafety mechanism 安全裝置\nSweating is the body's natural mechanism for cooling down.\n(流汗是身體自然的降溫機制。)\nThe safety mechanism stops the machine if something goes wrong.\n(一旦出問題，安全裝置會讓機器停止運轉。)"],["medication","medication(n.)藥物、藥物治療\nmedicate(v.)用藥治療\nmedical(adj.)醫學的\ntake medication 服藥\non medication 正在服藥\nRemember to take your medication after meals.\n(記得飯後服藥。)\nSome medications can make you feel sleepy.\n(有些藥物會讓你昏昏欲睡。)"],["mentor","mentor(n.)導師、指導者\nmentorship(n.)指導關係\nact as a mentor 擔任導師\nmentor program 導師制度\nMy coach has been a great mentor to me over the years.\n(這些年來我的教練一直是我很好的導師。)\nThe school pairs each new teacher with an experienced mentor.\n(學校為每位新老師安排一位資深的指導者。)"],["merge","merge(v.)合併、融合\nmerger(n.)(公司)合併\nmerge with 與……合併\nmerge into 融入\nThe two small companies merged to form a larger one.\n(這兩家小公司合併成一家較大的公司。)\nDrivers must slow down where the two lanes merge.\n(在兩線道匯合處，駕駛必須減速。)"],["metaphor","metaphor(n.)隱喻、暗喻\nmetaphorical(adj.)隱喻的\nuse a metaphor 使用隱喻\nmetaphor for 象徵……的隱喻\nIn the poem, the journey is a metaphor for life.\n(在這首詩中，旅程是人生的隱喻。)\nWriters often use metaphors to make their ideas more vivid.\n(作家常使用隱喻讓想法更生動。)"],["metropolitan","metropolitan(adj./n.)大都市的、都會區居民\nmetropolis(n.)大都市\nmetropolitan area 都會區\nmetropolitan museum 大都會博物館\nMore than seven million people live in the Taipei metropolitan area.\n(超過七百萬人住在台北都會區。)\nHousing prices in metropolitan areas keep rising.\n(都會區的房價持續上漲。)"],["midst","midst(n./prep.)中間、當中\n(無詞性變化)\nin the midst of 在……之中\nin our midst 在我們之中\nIn the midst of the crisis, the mayor stayed calm.\n(在危機當中，市長保持冷靜。)\nShe found a quiet café in the midst of the busy city.\n(她在繁忙的城市中找到一間安靜的咖啡廳。)"],["migration","migration(n.)遷徙、移居\nmigrate(v.)遷徙\nmigrant(n.)移民、候鳥\nbird migration 鳥類遷徙\nmass migration 大規模移居\nEvery winter, birdwatchers gather to watch the migration of black-faced spoonbills.\n(每年冬天，賞鳥人士聚集觀賞黑面琵鷺的遷徙。)\nRural-to-urban migration has changed the population structure.\n(城鄉移居改變了人口結構。)"],["milestone","milestone(n.)里程碑、重要事件\n(無詞性變化)\nmajor milestone 重大里程碑\nreach a milestone 達到里程碑\nGraduating from high school is an important milestone in life.\n(高中畢業是人生中重要的里程碑。)\nThe invention of the internet was a milestone in human history.\n(網際網路的發明是人類歷史上的里程碑。)"],["miniature","miniature(adj./n.)小型的、縮圖、模型\nmini(adj.)迷你的\nin miniature 縮小的\nminiature model 微縮模型\nHe built a miniature model of the Taipei 101 building.\n(他製作了一個台北101的微縮模型。)\nThe theme park shows famous buildings in miniature.\n(這座主題樂園以縮小的形式展示著名建築。)"],["minimal","minimal(adj.)最小的、極少的\nminimum(n./adj.)最小量、最低的\nminimize(v.)減到最少\nminimal cost 極低的成本\nminimal effort 最少的力氣\nThe storm caused only minimal damage to the town.\n(暴風雨對小鎮只造成極少的損害。)\nShe prefers a minimal style with simple furniture.\n(她偏好家具簡單的極簡風格。)"],["minimize","minimize(v.)使減到最少、輕描淡寫\nminimum(n.)最小量\nminimal(adj.)最小的\nminimize the risk 將風險降到最低\nminimize waste 減少浪費\nWearing a helmet can minimize the risk of head injuries.\n(戴安全帽能將頭部受傷的風險降到最低。)\nWe should minimize the use of plastic bags.\n(我們應盡量減少使用塑膠袋。)"],["mint","mint(n.)薄荷、鑄幣廠、大筆錢\nminty(adj.)薄荷味的\nmint tea 薄荷茶\nin mint condition 嶄新的\nShe added some fresh mint leaves to the lemonade.\n(她在檸檬水裡加了一些新鮮薄荷葉。)\nThe old comic book is still in mint condition.\n(這本舊漫畫仍然完好如新。)"],["missionary","missionary(n./adj.)傳教士、傳教的\nmission(n.)任務、使命\nmissionary school 教會學校\nmissionary work 傳教工作\nGeorge Mackay was a missionary who founded schools and clinics in Tamsui.\n(馬偕是一位在淡水創辦學校和診所的傳教士。)\nMany early hospitals in Taiwan were set up by missionaries.\n(台灣許多早期的醫院是由傳教士建立的。)"],["moan","moan(n./v.)呻吟、抱怨\n(無詞性變化)\nmoan about 抱怨\nmoan in pain 痛苦地呻吟\nThe injured player lay on the ground, moaning in pain.\n(受傷的球員躺在地上痛苦地呻吟。)\nStop moaning about the homework and just do it.\n(別再抱怨作業了，去寫就對了。)"],["mock","mock(adj./v./n.)模擬的、嘲笑、模仿\nmockery(n.)嘲弄\nmock exam 模擬考\nmock sb. for 因……嘲笑某人\nWe will have a mock exam before the real one.\n(正式考試前我們會先有一次模擬考。)\nIt's unkind to mock others for their accents.\n(嘲笑別人的口音是很不厚道的。)"],["mode","mode(n.)方式、模式\n(無詞性變化)\nmode of transportation 交通方式\nairplane mode 飛航模式\nPlease switch your phone to airplane mode before takeoff.\n(起飛前請將手機切換成飛航模式。)\nThe bicycle is an eco-friendly mode of transportation.\n(腳踏車是環保的交通方式。)"],["modify","modify(v.)修改、調整、修飾\nmodification(n.)修改\nmodify a plan 修改計畫\ngenetically modified 基因改造的\nWe need to modify our plan because of the bad weather.\n(由於天氣不佳，我們需要修改計畫。)\nSome people avoid eating genetically modified food.\n(有些人避免食用基因改造食品。)"],["molecule","molecule(n.)分子\nmolecular(adj.)分子的\nwater molecule 水分子\nmolecule of oxygen 氧分子\nA water molecule is made up of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.\n(一個水分子由兩個氫原子和一個氧原子組成。)\nHeat makes molecules move faster.\n(熱會讓分子移動得更快。)"],["monopoly","monopoly(n.)壟斷、獨占\nmonopolize(v.)壟斷\nhave a monopoly on 壟斷……\nstate monopoly 國家專賣\nThe company had a monopoly on the market for years.\n(這家公司多年來壟斷這個市場。)\nNobody has a monopoly on good ideas.\n(好點子並不是某個人的專利。)"],["morality","morality(n.)道德、道德觀\nmoral(adj./n.)道德的、寓意\nimmorality(n.)不道德\npublic morality 公共道德\nsense of morality 道德感\nThe novel raises important questions about morality.\n(這本小說提出了關於道德的重要問題。)\nParents play a key role in teaching children morality.\n(父母在教導孩子道德方面扮演關鍵角色。)"],["mortality","mortality(n.)死亡率、必死性\nmortal(adj.)必死的、致命的\nimmortality(n.)不朽\ninfant mortality 嬰兒死亡率\nmortality rate 死亡率\nBetter health care has greatly reduced infant mortality.\n(更好的醫療照護大幅降低了嬰兒死亡率。)\nThe mortality rate of the disease is very low.\n(這種疾病的死亡率非常低。)"],["mortgage","mortgage(n.)抵押貸款、房貸\n(無詞性變化)\npay off a mortgage 還清房貸\ntake out a mortgage 申辦房貸\nMy parents took out a mortgage to buy our house.\n(我父母申辦了房貸來買我們的房子。)\nIt will take them twenty years to pay off the mortgage.\n(他們要花二十年才能還清房貸。)"],["motive","motive(n.)動機、目的\nmotivate(v.)激勵\nmotivation(n.)動機\nhidden motive 隱藏的動機\nmotive for 做……的動機\nThe police are still trying to find the motive for the crime.\n(警方仍在試圖找出犯案動機。)\nI wonder what his real motive for helping us was.\n(我很好奇他幫我們的真正動機是什麼。)"],["mount","mount(n./v.)山、登上、騎上、增加、安裝\nmountain(n.)山\nMount Jade 玉山\nmount a horse 騎上馬\nMount Jade is the highest mountain in Taiwan.\n(玉山是台灣最高的山。)\nPressure on students mounts as the exam gets closer.\n(隨著考試逼近，學生的壓力逐漸增加。)"],["mumble","mumble(v./n.)喃喃自語、含糊地說\n(無詞性變化)\nmumble an apology 含糊地道歉\nmumble to oneself 自言自語\nHe mumbled an apology and left the room.\n(他含糊地道了歉就離開了房間。)\nPlease speak clearly; don't mumble when you give a speech.\n(演講時請說清楚，不要含糊不清。)"],["municipal","municipal(adj.)市政的、市立的\nmunicipality(n.)直轄市、自治市\nmunicipal government 市政府\nmunicipal library 市立圖書館\nSongshan Senior High School is a municipal school in Taipei.\n(松山高中是台北市的市立學校。)\nThe municipal government plans to build more bike lanes.\n(市政府計畫興建更多自行車道。)"],["muscular","muscular(adj.)肌肉的、肌肉發達的\nmuscle(n.)肌肉\nmuscular body 健壯的身體\nmuscular strength 肌力\nAfter months of training, he became strong and muscular.\n(經過幾個月的訓練，他變得強壯又肌肉發達。)\nRegular exercise helps improve muscular strength.\n(規律運動有助於提升肌力。)"],["mustard","mustard(n.)芥末、芥菜\n(無詞性變化)\nmustard sauce 芥末醬\nmustard greens 芥菜\nHe likes to put mustard on his hot dog.\n(他喜歡在熱狗上加芥末醬。)\nMustard greens are a common vegetable in Taiwanese cooking.\n(芥菜是台灣料理中常見的蔬菜。)"],["myth","myth(n.)神話、迷思\nmythical(adj.)神話的、虛構的\nmythology(n.)神話學\nGreek myth 希臘神話\ncommon myth 常見迷思\nIt is a common myth that we only use ten percent of our brains.\n(認為人類只用了大腦百分之十是常見的迷思。)\nThe story of Hou Yi shooting the suns is an ancient Chinese myth.\n(后羿射日是一則中國古代神話。)"],["naive","naive(adj.)天真的、幼稚的\nnaivety(n.)天真\nnaively(adv.)天真地\nnaive belief 天真的想法\npolitically naive 政治上天真的\nIt was naive of me to believe everything I read online.\n(我相信網路上讀到的所有東西，真是太天真了。)\nShe asked a naive question, but the teacher answered it kindly.\n(她問了一個天真的問題，但老師親切地回答了。)"],["narrative","narrative(n./adj.)敘述、故事、敘事的\nnarrate(v.)敘述\nnarrator(n.)敘述者\nnarrative writing 記敘文\npersonal narrative 個人經歷敘述\nThe novel's narrative jumps between the past and the present.\n(這部小說的敘事在過去與現在之間跳躍。)\nWe were asked to write a narrative essay about a memorable trip.\n(我們被要求寫一篇關於難忘旅行的記敘文。)"],["nasty","nasty(adj.)令人不快的、惡劣的、嚴重的\nnastiness(n.)惡劣\nnasty smell 難聞的氣味\nnasty cold 重感冒\nThere's a nasty smell coming from the trash can.\n(垃圾桶散發出一股難聞的氣味。)\nShe was nasty to her classmates, so no one wanted to sit with her.\n(她對同學很惡劣，所以沒人想跟她坐。)"],["negotiation","negotiation(n.)談判、協商\nnegotiate(v.)談判\nnegotiator(n.)談判者\nunder negotiation 協商中\npeace negotiations 和平談判\nAfter weeks of negotiation, the two sides signed an agreement.\n(經過數週的談判，雙方簽署了協議。)\nThe price of the house is still under negotiation.\n(房子的價格仍在協商中。)"],["neutral","neutral(adj./n.)中立的、中性的、中立者\nneutrality(n.)中立\nneutralize(v.)使中和\nremain neutral 保持中立\nneutral color 中性色\nSwitzerland remained neutral during World War II.\n(瑞士在第二次世界大戰期間保持中立。)\nGray and beige are neutral colors that match everything.\n(灰色和米色是百搭的中性色。)"],["nominate","nominate(v.)提名、任命\nnomination(n.)提名\nnominee(n.)被提名人\nnominate sb. for 提名某人角逐……\nbe nominated as 被提名為\nThe film was nominated for five Golden Horse Awards.\n(這部電影獲得五項金馬獎提名。)\nOur class nominated Amy as the student council representative.\n(我們班提名艾咪擔任學生會代表。)"],["nomination","nomination(n.)提名、任命\nnominate(v.)提名\nreceive a nomination 獲得提名\nOscar nomination 奧斯卡提名\nThe actress received her first Oscar nomination this year.\n(這位女演員今年首度獲得奧斯卡提名。)\nThe party announced his nomination for mayor.\n(該黨宣布提名他角逐市長。)"],["nominee","nominee(n.)被提名人\nnominate(v.)提名\nnomination(n.)提名\naward nominee 入圍者\npresidential nominee 總統候選人\nAll the nominees for Best Actor were invited to the ceremony.\n(所有最佳男主角入圍者都受邀出席典禮。)\nThe nominee gave a speech after being chosen by the party.\n(被提名人在獲得黨內提名後發表演說。)"],["nonprofit","nonprofit(adj.)非營利的\nprofit(n.)利潤\nnonprofit organization 非營利組織\nnonprofit group 非營利團體\nShe volunteers at a nonprofit organization that helps stray animals.\n(她在一個幫助流浪動物的非營利組織當志工。)\nThe museum is run by a nonprofit foundation.\n(這間博物館由一個非營利基金會經營。)"],["norm","norm(n.)規範、標準、常態\nnormal(adj.)正常的\nsocial norm 社會規範\nthe norm 常態\nWorking from home has become the norm for many people.\n(在家工作已經成為許多人的常態。)\nDifferent cultures have different social norms.\n(不同文化有不同的社會規範。)"],["noticeable","noticeable(adj.)顯著的、明顯的\nnotice(v./n.)注意、通知\nnoticeably(adv.)顯著地\nnoticeable difference 明顯的差異\nnoticeable improvement 顯著的進步\nThere has been a noticeable improvement in her English.\n(她的英文有明顯的進步。)\nThe scar on his arm is barely noticeable now.\n(他手臂上的疤痕現在幾乎看不出來了。)"],["notify","notify(v.)通知、告知\nnotification(n.)通知\nnotify sb. of 通知某人……\nbe notified 收到通知\nPlease notify the teacher if you are going to be absent.\n(如果你要請假，請通知老師。)\nStudents will be notified of their exam results by email.\n(學生將透過電子郵件收到考試成績通知。)"],["notion","notion(n.)概念、想法、觀念\nnotional(adj.)概念上的\nthe notion that ……的觀念\nvague notion 模糊的概念\nThe notion that money brings happiness is not always true.\n(金錢帶來幸福的觀念不見得都正確。)\nI had no notion of how difficult the job would be.\n(我完全不知道這份工作會這麼困難。)"],["nowhere","nowhere(adv./pron.)無處、任何地方都不\n(無詞性變化)\nnowhere near 遠遠不及\nout of nowhere 突然冒出來\nA dog came running out of nowhere and scared me.\n(一隻狗突然衝出來嚇了我一跳。)\nMy essay is nowhere near finished.\n(我的作文還差得遠才寫完。)"],["nutrient","nutrient(n./adj.)養分、營養素、營養的\nnutrition(n.)營養\nnutritious(adj.)有營養的\nessential nutrients 必需營養素\nnutrient-rich 營養豐富的\nVegetables provide many essential nutrients for our bodies.\n(蔬菜為我們的身體提供許多必需的營養素。)\nPlants absorb nutrients from the soil through their roots.\n(植物透過根部從土壤中吸收養分。)"],["nutrition","nutrition(n.)營養、營養學\nnutritious(adj.)有營養的\nnutritionist(n.)營養師\ngood nutrition 良好營養\nnutrition facts 營養標示\nGood nutrition is important for growing teenagers.\n(良好的營養對成長中的青少年很重要。)\nAlways check the nutrition facts on food labels.\n(要記得查看食品標籤上的營養標示。)"],["obligation","obligation(n.)義務、責任\noblige(v.)迫使、使感激\nobligatory(adj.)義務的\nmoral obligation 道德義務\nbe under an obligation to 有義務做……\nParents have an obligation to take care of their children.\n(父母有照顧孩子的義務。)\nYou are under no obligation to buy anything.\n(你沒有義務一定要買東西。)"],["obscure","obscure(adj./v.)不清楚的、鮮為人知的、遮掩\nobscurity(n.)默默無聞、模糊\nobscure meaning 晦澀的意義\nobscure the view 遮住視線\nThe poem is full of obscure words that are hard to understand.\n(這首詩充滿難以理解的晦澀字詞。)\nTall buildings obscure the view of the mountains.\n(高樓遮住了山景。)"],["observer","observer(n.)觀察者、觀察員\nobserve(v.)觀察、遵守\nobservation(n.)觀察\nkeen observer 敏銳的觀察者\nindependent observer 獨立觀察員\nTo a casual observer, the twins look exactly the same.\n(對不經意看的人來說，這對雙胞胎長得一模一樣。)\nInternational observers were sent to monitor the election.\n(國際觀察員被派去監督這次選舉。)"],["odds","odds(n.)可能性、機率、賠率\n(無詞性變化)\nagainst all odds 克服萬難\nthe odds are 很有可能\nAgainst all odds, the small team won the championship.\n(這支小隊伍克服萬難贏得冠軍。)\nThe odds of winning the lottery are extremely low.\n(中樂透的機率極低。)"],["offering","offering(n.)祭品、供品、提供物\noffer(v./n.)提供\nmake an offering 獻上供品\nfood offering 食物供品\nPeople place food offerings on the table during Ghost Month.\n(人們在中元節時把食物供品擺在桌上。)\nThe restaurant's new menu offerings include several vegetarian dishes.\n(這家餐廳的新菜單包含幾道素食料理。)"],["olive","olive(adj./n.)橄欖色的、橄欖\n(無詞性變化)\nolive oil 橄欖油\nolive branch 橄欖枝(和平象徵)\nOlive oil is a healthy choice for cooking.\n(橄欖油是烹飪的健康選擇。)\nThe dove with an olive branch is a symbol of peace.\n(銜著橄欖枝的鴿子是和平的象徵。)"],["operational","operational(adj.)操作上的、運作中的\noperate(v.)操作、運作\noperation(n.)操作、手術\nfully operational 全面運作\noperational costs 營運成本\nThe new MRT line will be fully operational next year.\n(新的捷運線將在明年全面通車。)\nThe company is trying to reduce its operational costs.\n(這家公司正努力降低營運成本。)"],["opponent","opponent(n.)對手、反對者\noppose(v.)反對\nopposition(n.)反對\npolitical opponent 政敵\ndefeat an opponent 擊敗對手\nShe defeated her opponent in the final match.\n(她在決賽中擊敗了對手。)\nOpponents of the plan say it will harm the environment.\n(這項計畫的反對者說它會破壞環境。)"],["opposition","opposition(n.)反對、對立、反對黨\noppose(v.)反對\nopposite(adj.)相反的\nstrong opposition 強烈反對\nopposition party 反對黨\nThe plan to build a factory met strong opposition from local residents.\n(興建工廠的計畫遭到當地居民強烈反對。)\nThe opposition party criticized the new budget.\n(反對黨批評新的預算。)"],["opt","opt(v.)選擇\noption(n.)選擇\noptional(adj.)可選擇的\nopt for 選擇\nopt out of 選擇不參加\nMany students opt for science subjects in senior high school.\n(許多高中生選擇自然組的科目。)\nYou can opt out of the school trip if you have a good reason.\n(如果有正當理由，你可以選擇不參加校外教學。)"],["optimism","optimism(n.)樂觀、樂觀主義\noptimistic(adj.)樂觀的\noptimist(n.)樂觀者\ncautious optimism 審慎樂觀\na sense of optimism 樂觀的感覺\nShe faced her illness with courage and optimism.\n(她以勇氣和樂觀面對疾病。)\nThere is growing optimism that the economy will recover.\n(人們愈來愈樂觀地認為經濟將會復甦。)"],["optional","optional(adj.)可選擇的、非必須的\noption(n.)選擇\nopt(v.)選擇\noptional course 選修課\noptional extra 選配\nAttending the evening study session is optional.\n(參加晚自習是自由選擇的。)\nStudents can take optional courses in art or music.\n(學生可以選修美術或音樂課程。)"],["orchard","orchard(n.)果園\n(無詞性變化)\napple orchard 蘋果園\nfruit orchard 果園\nWe went strawberry picking at an orchard in Dahu.\n(我們到大湖的果園採草莓。)\nMy uncle owns a small orange orchard in the countryside.\n(我叔叔在鄉下擁有一座小柳丁園。)"],["organism","organism(n.)生物、有機體\norganic(adj.)有機的\nliving organism 生物\ntiny organism 微生物\nBacteria are tiny organisms that can only be seen under a microscope.\n(細菌是只能在顯微鏡下看見的微小生物。)\nAll living organisms need water to survive.\n(所有生物都需要水才能生存。)"],["originality","originality(n.)獨創性、創意\noriginal(adj.)原始的、獨創的\noriginally(adv.)原本\nshow originality 展現獨創性\nlack originality 缺乏創意\nThe judges praised the originality of her design.\n(評審讚揚她設計的獨創性。)\nThe movie was criticized for its lack of originality.\n(這部電影因缺乏新意而遭到批評。)"],["outfit","outfit(n./v.)全套服裝、裝備、配備\n(無詞性變化)\nnew outfit 新衣服\noutfit of the day 今日穿搭\nShe bought a new outfit for the graduation party.\n(她為畢業派對買了一套新衣服。)\nThe team was outfitted with new uniforms and equipment.\n(隊伍配備了新的制服和器材。)"],["outlet","outlet(n.)出口、發洩途徑、插座、暢貨中心\n(無詞性變化)\npower outlet 電源插座\noutlet mall 暢貨中心\nIs there a power outlet near the table?\n(桌子附近有電源插座嗎？)\nPlaying sports is a good outlet for stress.\n(運動是紓解壓力的好方法。)"],["output","output(n./v.)產量、輸出\n(無詞性變化)\nindustrial output 工業產量\noutput device 輸出裝置\nThe factory increased its output by 20 percent last year.\n(這間工廠去年產量增加了百分之二十。)\nThe printer is an output device of the computer.\n(印表機是電腦的輸出裝置。)"],["outsider","outsider(n.)局外人、外人\n(無詞性變化)\nfeel like an outsider 覺得自己是外人\nto an outsider 對外人來說\nWhen I moved to a new school, I felt like an outsider at first.\n(轉到新學校時，我一開始覺得自己像個外人。)\nTo an outsider, the rules of the game seem very confusing.\n(對局外人來說，這個遊戲的規則似乎很令人困惑。)"],["overall","overall(adj./adv./n.)全部的、整體來說、工作服\n(無詞性變化)\noverall situation 整體情況\noverall score 總分\nOverall, the school trip was a great success.\n(整體來說，這次校外教學非常成功。)\nHis overall grade improved a lot this semester.\n(他這學期的總成績進步很多。)"],["overhead","overhead(adv./adj./n.)在頭頂上、上方的、經常性開支\n(無詞性變化)\noverhead bin 頭頂置物櫃\noverhead costs 經常性開支\nA plane flew overhead as we were having a picnic.\n(我們野餐時，一架飛機從頭頂飛過。)\nPlease put your bags in the overhead bin.\n(請將您的行李放在上方的置物櫃。)"],["oversee","oversee(v.)監督、管理\noverseer(n.)監督者\noversee a project 監督計畫\noversee operations 管理營運\nThe principal oversees the daily operation of the school.\n(校長督導學校的日常運作。)\nAn engineer was hired to oversee the construction of the bridge.\n(聘請了一位工程師來監督橋梁的興建。)"],["overtake","overtake(v.)超越、趕上、突然降臨\n(無詞性變化)\novertake a car 超車\nbe overtaken by 被……侵襲\nIt is dangerous to overtake another car on a curve.\n(在彎道超車是很危險的。)\nOnline sales have overtaken sales in physical stores.\n(網路銷售已經超越實體店面的銷售。)"],["overturn","overturn(v./n.)翻倒、推翻\n(無詞性變化)\noverturn a decision 推翻決定\noverturned car 翻覆的車\nA truck overturned on the highway this morning.\n(今天早上一輛卡車在高速公路上翻覆。)\nThe higher court overturned the earlier decision.\n(上級法院推翻了先前的判決。)"],["overwhelm","overwhelm(v.)壓倒、使不知所措、淹沒\noverwhelming(adj.)壓倒性的、無法抗拒的\noverwhelmed(adj.)不知所措的\nbe overwhelmed by 被……壓得喘不過氣\noverwhelming majority 壓倒性多數\nI was overwhelmed by the amount of homework this week.\n(這週的作業量讓我喘不過氣。)\nThe proposal was supported by an overwhelming majority.\n(這項提案獲得壓倒性多數支持。)"],["parallel","parallel(adj./n./v.)平行的、相似處、與……相似\n(無詞性變化)\nparallel lines 平行線\ndraw a parallel between 比較……的相似之處\nThe road runs parallel to the river for several kilometers.\n(這條路與河流平行延伸好幾公里。)\nThe teacher drew a parallel between the two historical events.\n(老師比較了這兩個歷史事件的相似之處。)"],["participant","participant(n.)參與者、參加者\nparticipate(v.)參加\nparticipation(n.)參與\nactive participant 積極的參與者\nparticipants in ……的參加者\nAll participants in the contest will receive a certificate.\n(所有參賽者都會獲得一張證書。)\nShe was an active participant in class discussions.\n(她在課堂討論中是積極的參與者。)"],["particle","particle(n.)微粒、粒子、極少量\n(無詞性變化)\nfine particles 細懸浮微粒\ndust particles 灰塵顆粒\nFine particles in the air can cause serious breathing problems.\n(空氣中的細懸浮微粒可能造成嚴重的呼吸問題。)\nThere isn't a particle of truth in what he said.\n(他說的話沒有一點是真的。)"],["partly","partly(adv.)部分地、在某種程度上\npart(n.)部分\npartial(adj.)部分的、偏袒的\npartly cloudy 局部多雲\npartly because 部分是因為\nIt will be partly cloudy with a chance of rain this afternoon.\n(今天下午局部多雲，可能會下雨。)\nI failed the test partly because I didn't sleep well.\n(我考試沒過，部分是因為我沒睡好。)"],["passionate","passionate(adj.)熱情的、熱愛的、激昂的\npassion(n.)熱情、熱愛\npassionately(adv.)熱情地\nbe passionate about 熱愛……\npassionate speech 慷慨激昂的演說\nShe is passionate about protecting endangered animals.\n(她熱衷於保護瀕危動物。)\nThe student gave a passionate speech about climate change.\n(那位學生針對氣候變遷發表了一場慷慨激昂的演說。)"],["pastry","pastry(n.)糕點、酥皮點心\n(無詞性變化)\npastry chef 糕點師傅\npuff pastry 千層酥皮\nThe bakery sells delicious French pastries every morning.\n(那家麵包店每天早上販賣美味的法式糕點。)\nMy cousin is training to become a pastry chef in Paris.\n(我表姊正在巴黎受訓成為糕點師傅。)"],["patch","patch(n./v.)補丁、小塊區域、修補\npatchy(adj.)零散的、不均勻的\npatch up 修補、和解\nvegetable patch 小菜園\nMy grandmother sewed a patch on the knee of my jeans.\n(我奶奶在我的牛仔褲膝蓋處縫了一塊補丁。)\nThe two friends finally patched up their quarrel.\n(那兩個朋友終於和好了。)"],["patent","patent(n./adj./v.)專利、專利的、取得專利\n(無詞性變化)\napply for a patent 申請專利\npatent law 專利法\nThe engineer applied for a patent on his new invention.\n(那位工程師為他的新發明申請專利。)\nThe company patented its design to stop others from copying it.\n(那家公司為設計申請專利，以防止他人抄襲。)"],["pathetic","pathetic(adj.)可憐的、可悲的、差勁的\npathetically(adv.)可憐地、差勁地\npathetic excuse 拙劣的藉口\npathetic sight 可憐的景象\nThe lost puppy shivering in the rain was a pathetic sight.\n(那隻在雨中發抖的迷路小狗是一幅可憐的景象。)\nSaying the dog ate your homework is a pathetic excuse.\n(說狗吃了你的作業是個拙劣的藉口。)"],["patrol","patrol(n./v.)巡邏、巡邏隊\n(無詞性變化)\non patrol 巡邏中\npolice patrol 警察巡邏\nPolice officers patrol the night market every evening.\n(警察每天晚上在夜市巡邏。)\nThe coast guard sent a boat on patrol near the island.\n(海巡署派出一艘船在島嶼附近巡邏。)"],["patron","patron(n.)贊助者、資助人、老主顧\npatronage(n.)贊助、光顧\npatronize(v.)光顧、以高人一等的態度對待\npatron of the arts 藝術贊助者\nregular patron 老主顧\nThe wealthy businessman is a well-known patron of the arts.\n(那位富商是知名的藝術贊助者。)\nThe café offers discounts to its regular patrons.\n(這家咖啡店給老主顧打折。)"],["peasant","peasant(n.)農民、佃農\n(無詞性變化)\npeasant farmer 小農\npeasant uprising 農民起義\nIn the past, most peasants worked on land owned by rich landlords.\n(過去大多數農民在富有地主擁有的土地上耕作。)\nThe peasant uprising changed the history of the country.\n(那場農民起義改變了這個國家的歷史。)"],["pedal","pedal(n./v.)踏板、踩踏板\n(無詞性變化)\ngas pedal 油門\npedal a bike 騎腳踏車\nHe stepped on the gas pedal when the light turned green.\n(綠燈亮時他踩下油門。)\nShe pedaled hard to climb the steep hill.\n(她用力踩踏板爬上陡坡。)"],["pedestrian","pedestrian(n./adj.)行人、行人的、平淡無奇的\n(無詞性變化)\npedestrian crossing 行人穿越道\npedestrian zone 行人徒步區\nDrivers must stop for pedestrians at the crossing.\n(駕駛必須在行人穿越道前停車讓行人。)\nThe old street has become a pedestrian zone on weekends.\n(這條老街週末成為行人徒步區。)"],["penetrate","penetrate(v.)穿透、滲入、看穿\npenetration(n.)穿透、滲透\npenetrating(adj.)銳利的、有洞察力的\npenetrate the skin 穿透皮膚\npenetrate the market 打入市場\nSunlight could barely penetrate the thick forest.\n(陽光幾乎無法穿透茂密的森林。)\nThe company is trying to penetrate the Japanese market.\n(那家公司正試圖打入日本市場。)"],["pension","pension(n./v.)退休金、養老金\npensioner(n.)領退休金者\npension plan 退休金計畫\nretire on a pension 領退休金退休\nMy grandfather lives on his pension after retiring from teaching.\n(我爺爺從教職退休後靠退休金生活。)\nThe government is planning to reform the pension system.\n(政府正在計劃改革年金制度。)"],["perceive","perceive(v.)察覺、感知、認為\nperception(n.)感知、看法\nperceptive(adj.)有洞察力的\nperceive as 視為……\nperceive a change 察覺變化\nMany people perceive the Internet as a source of reliable information.\n(許多人把網路視為可靠的資訊來源。)\nDogs can perceive sounds that humans cannot hear.\n(狗能察覺人類聽不到的聲音。)"],["perception","perception(n.)感知、看法、認知\nperceive(v.)察覺、認為\nperceptive(adj.)有洞察力的\npublic perception 大眾觀感\nchange one's perception 改變某人的看法\nTraveling abroad changed my perception of different cultures.\n(出國旅行改變了我對不同文化的看法。)\nPublic perception of the new policy has been mostly positive.\n(大眾對新政策的觀感大致正面。)"],["performer","performer(n.)表演者、演出者\nperform(v.)表演、執行\nperformance(n.)表演、表現\nstreet performer 街頭藝人\ntalented performer 有才華的表演者\nA street performer was playing the violin outside the station.\n(一名街頭藝人在車站外拉小提琴。)\nShe is one of the most talented performers in the musical.\n(她是這部音樂劇中最有才華的演員之一。)"],["persist","persist(v.)堅持、持續存在\npersistence(n.)堅持、毅力\npersistent(adj.)堅持不懈的、持續的\npersist in 堅持……\nproblem persists 問題持續存在\nIf the pain persists, you should see a doctor.\n(如果疼痛持續，你應該去看醫生。)\nHe persisted in practicing the piano every day and finally won the contest.\n(他堅持每天練琴，最後贏得了比賽。)"],["personnel","personnel(n.)全體人員、人事部門\n(無詞性變化)\nmedical personnel 醫護人員\npersonnel department 人事部門\nOnly authorized personnel are allowed to enter this area.\n(只有經授權的人員才可進入此區域。)\nMedical personnel worked day and night during the outbreak.\n(疫情爆發期間，醫護人員日以繼夜地工作。)"],["perspective","perspective(n./adj.)觀點、看法、透視法\n(無詞性變化)\nfrom a different perspective 從不同觀點\nput things in perspective 正確看待事情\nTry to look at the problem from a different perspective.\n(試著從不同的角度看這個問題。)\nTalking with my grandmother helped me put things in perspective.\n(和奶奶聊天幫助我更客觀地看待事情。)"],["pessimism","pessimism(n.)悲觀、悲觀主義\npessimist(n.)悲觀者\npessimistic(adj.)悲觀的\ndeep pessimism 極度悲觀\npessimism about 對……的悲觀\nThere is growing pessimism about the future of the economy.\n(人們對經濟前景越來越悲觀。)\nHer pessimism made it hard for her to try new things.\n(她的悲觀讓她很難嘗試新事物。)"],["petition","petition(n.)請願書、請願\n(無詞性變化)\nsign a petition 在請願書上簽名\nonline petition 線上請願\nOver ten thousand people signed the petition to save the old tree.\n(超過一萬人在請願書上簽名，要求保留那棵老樹。)\nStudents started an online petition for a longer lunch break.\n(學生發起線上請願，爭取更長的午休時間。)"],["petty","petty(adj.)瑣碎的、小氣的、心胸狹窄的\npettiness(n.)瑣碎、小氣\npetty crime 輕微犯罪\npetty argument 雞毛蒜皮的爭吵\nDon't waste your time on petty arguments with your classmates.\n(不要把時間浪費在與同學雞毛蒜皮的爭吵上。)\nPetty crimes such as pickpocketing are common in tourist areas.\n(扒竊之類的輕微犯罪在觀光區很常見。)"],["phase","phase(n./v.)階段、時期、分階段進行\n(無詞性變化)\nfinal phase 最後階段\nphase out 逐步淘汰\nThe project is now in its final phase.\n(這項計畫目前處於最後階段。)\nThe government plans to phase out plastic straws by 2030.\n(政府計劃在二〇三〇年前逐步淘汰塑膠吸管。)"],["photographic","photographic(adj.)攝影的、照片的\nphotograph(n./v.)照片、拍照\nphotography(n.)攝影\nphotographic memory 過目不忘的記憶力\nphotographic equipment 攝影器材\nShe has a photographic memory and remembers every page she reads.\n(她過目不忘，讀過的每一頁都記得。)\nThe store sells all kinds of photographic equipment.\n(這家店販售各式攝影器材。)"],["pickup","pickup(n.)接送、取貨、小貨車\npick up(v.)撿起、接送\npickup truck 小貨車\npickup point 取貨點、接送點\nMy uncle drives a pickup truck to carry fruit to the market.\n(我叔叔開小貨車載水果到市場。)\nPlease wait at the pickup point near the hotel entrance.\n(請在飯店入口附近的接送點等候。)"],["pier","pier(n.)碼頭、突堤\n(無詞性變化)\nfishing pier 釣魚碼頭\nwalk along the pier 沿著碼頭散步\nWe walked along the pier and watched the sunset over the sea.\n(我們沿著碼頭散步，欣賞海上的夕陽。)\nThe ferry leaves from Pier 3 every hour.\n(渡輪每小時從三號碼頭出發。)"],["pillar","pillar(n.)柱子、支柱、中堅\n(無詞性變化)\nstone pillar 石柱\npillar of society 社會中堅\nThe temple roof is supported by carved stone pillars.\n(廟宇的屋頂由雕刻的石柱支撐。)\nTourism has become a pillar of the island's economy.\n(觀光業已成為這座島嶼經濟的支柱。)"],["pipeline","pipeline(n.)管線、輸送管、管道\npipe(n.)管子\noil pipeline 輸油管\nin the pipeline 在籌備中\nAn oil pipeline runs across the desert for hundreds of kilometers.\n(一條輸油管橫越沙漠綿延數百公里。)\nSeveral new projects are in the pipeline for next year.\n(有好幾項新計畫正在為明年籌備中。)"],["pirate","pirate(n./v.)海盜、盜版者、盜版\npiracy(n.)海盜行為、盜版\npirate ship 海盜船\npirated software 盜版軟體\nThe movie tells the story of a pirate searching for treasure.\n(這部電影講述一個海盜尋寶的故事。)\nUsing pirated software is illegal and can harm your computer.\n(使用盜版軟體是違法的，而且可能損害你的電腦。)"],["pitcher","pitcher(n.)投手、水壺\npitch(v./n.)投擲、音調\nstarting pitcher 先發投手\na pitcher of water 一壺水\nThe starting pitcher struck out ten batters in the game.\n(先發投手在比賽中三振了十名打者。)\nThe waiter brought a pitcher of iced water to our table.\n(服務生端了一壺冰水到我們桌上。)"],["placement","placement(n.)安置、放置、分班\nplace(n./v.)地方、放置\nplacement test 分級測驗\njob placement 職業安置\nAll new students must take an English placement test.\n(所有新生都必須參加英文分級測驗。)\nThe careful placement of furniture made the small room look bigger.\n(精心擺放的家具讓小房間看起來更大。)"],["plea","plea(n.)懇求、請求、答辯\nplead(v.)懇求、辯護\nmake a plea for 呼籲、懇求\nguilty plea 認罪答辯\nThe mayor made a plea for people to save water.\n(市長呼籲民眾節約用水。)\nDespite her desperate plea, the teacher did not change the grade.\n(儘管她苦苦懇求，老師並沒有更改成績。)"],["plead","plead(v.)懇求、辯護、承認(有罪或無罪)\nplea(n.)懇求、答辯\nplead with 懇求\nplead guilty 認罪\nThe boy pleaded with his parents to let him keep the puppy.\n(男孩懇求父母讓他養那隻小狗。)\nThe man pleaded guilty to stealing the car.\n(那名男子承認偷了那輛車。)"],["pledge","pledge(n./v.)誓言、保證、承諾\n(無詞性變化)\nmake a pledge 立誓\npledge support 承諾支持\nThe company pledged to cut its carbon emissions by half.\n(那家公司承諾將碳排放減半。)\nStudents made a pledge to keep the campus clean.\n(學生們立誓維護校園整潔。)"],["plunge","plunge(n./v.)跳入、驟降、陷入\n(無詞性變化)\ntake the plunge 毅然決定\nplunge into 跳入、陷入\nStock prices plunged after the bad news was announced.\n(壞消息公布後股價暴跌。)\nAfter years of thinking about it, he finally took the plunge and started his own business.\n(考慮多年後，他終於毅然決定自己創業。)"],["plural","plural(adj./n.)複數的、複數\nsingular(adj./n.)單數的、單數\nplural form 複數形\nplural noun 複數名詞\nThe plural form of 'child' is 'children'.\n('child' 的複數形是 'children'。)\nRemember to use a plural verb with a plural subject.\n(記得複數主詞要搭配複數動詞。)"],["poetic","poetic(adj.)詩的、詩意的、富有詩意的\npoet(n.)詩人\npoetry(n.)詩、詩集\npoetic language 詩意的語言\npoetic justice 惡有惡報、天理昭彰\nThe writer describes the mountains in beautiful poetic language.\n(作者用優美而富有詩意的語言描寫群山。)\nIt was poetic justice when the bully slipped on his own banana peel.\n(那個惡霸踩到自己丟的香蕉皮滑倒，真是惡有惡報。)"],["poke","poke(v./n.)戳、捅、刺\n(無詞性變化)\npoke fun at 取笑\npoke one's nose into 干涉、多管閒事\nHe poked me in the arm to wake me up in class.\n(他在課堂上戳我的手臂把我叫醒。)\nIt's not nice to poke fun at other people's accents.\n(取笑別人的口音是不好的。)"],["porch","porch(n.)門廊、走廊\n(無詞性變化)\nfront porch 前門廊\nsit on the porch 坐在門廊上\nMy grandparents like to sit on the front porch in the evening.\n(我爺爺奶奶喜歡傍晚坐在前門廊上。)\nThe delivery man left the package on our porch.\n(送貨員把包裹放在我們家門廊上。)"],["portfolio","portfolio(n.)作品集、文件夾、投資組合\n(無詞性變化)\nlearning portfolio 學習歷程檔案\ninvestment portfolio 投資組合\nSenior high students in Taiwan need to prepare a learning portfolio for college applications.\n(台灣高中生需要為大學申請準備學習歷程檔案。)\nThe designer showed her portfolio during the job interview.\n(那位設計師在求職面試時展示了她的作品集。)"],["practitioner","practitioner(n.)從業人員、開業者(醫生、律師等)\npractice(n./v.)實踐、執業、練習\ngeneral practitioner 一般科醫師、家庭醫師\nmedical practitioner 醫療從業人員\nYou should see a general practitioner if your cough continues.\n(如果你持續咳嗽，應該去看家庭醫師。)\nTraditional Chinese medicine practitioners often use herbs to treat patients.\n(中醫師常用草藥治療病人。)"],["precaution","precaution(n.)預防措施、防範\nprecautionary(adj.)預防的\ntake precautions 採取預防措施\nsafety precaution 安全防範措施\nTake precautions against mosquito bites when you hike in summer.\n(夏天健行時要做好防蚊措施。)\nAs a precaution, the school canceled all outdoor activities during the typhoon.\n(為了預防起見，學校在颱風期間取消所有戶外活動。)"],["predator","predator(n.)掠食者、捕食性動物\npredatory(adj.)掠食性的、掠奪性的\nnatural predator 天敵\ntop predator 頂級掠食者\nSharks are top predators in the ocean food chain.\n(鯊魚是海洋食物鏈中的頂級掠食者。)\nThe small fish hide among the rocks to escape from predators.\n(小魚躲在岩石間逃避掠食者。)"],["preference","preference(n.)偏好、喜好、優先\nprefer(v.)較喜歡\npreferable(adj.)更好的、較合意的\nhave a preference for 偏好……\npersonal preference 個人喜好\nChoosing between tea and coffee is a matter of personal preference.\n(選擇茶或咖啡純屬個人喜好。)\nMany students have a preference for online learning.\n(許多學生偏好線上學習。)"],["prejudice","prejudice(n./v.)偏見、使有偏見\nprejudiced(adj.)有偏見的\nracial prejudice 種族偏見\nprejudice against 對……的偏見\nWe should not have any prejudice against people from other cultures.\n(我們不應對來自其他文化的人抱持任何偏見。)\nThe book helped me overcome my prejudice against science fiction.\n(這本書幫助我克服了對科幻小說的偏見。)"],["preliminary","preliminary(adj./n.)初步的、預備的、預賽\n(無詞性變化)\npreliminary round 預賽\npreliminary results 初步結果\nOur team made it through the preliminary round of the competition.\n(我們隊通過了比賽的預賽。)\nPreliminary results show that the new medicine is effective.\n(初步結果顯示新藥有效。)"],["premature","premature(adj.)過早的、早產的、不成熟的\nprematurely(adv.)過早地\npremature baby 早產兒\npremature death 早逝\nThe premature baby had to stay in the hospital for two months.\n(那名早產兒必須在醫院住兩個月。)\nIt is premature to say who will win the election.\n(現在斷言誰會贏得選舉還言之過早。)"],["premier","premier(adj./n.)首要的、最好的、首相、行政院長\npremiere(n.)首映、首演\nPremier League 英格蘭超級足球聯賽\nthe Premier 行政院長、總理\nThe Premier announced new measures to support small businesses.\n(行政院長宣布支持小型企業的新措施。)\nThis hotel is one of the city's premier places to stay.\n(這家飯店是這座城市最頂級的住宿地點之一。)"],["premise","premise(n.)前提、(複數)房屋及土地\n(無詞性變化)\non the premise that 在……的前提下\non the premises 在場地內\nThe plan is based on the premise that everyone will cooperate.\n(這項計畫建立在每個人都會配合的前提上。)\nSmoking is not allowed anywhere on the premises.\n(場地內任何地方都禁止吸菸。)"],["premium","premium(n.)保險費、額外費用、獎金\n(無詞性變化)\ninsurance premium 保險費\nat a premium 稀缺的、難得的\nMy parents pay a monthly insurance premium for our health insurance.\n(我父母每月繳我們的健康保險費。)\nDuring the holidays, hotel rooms near the beach are at a premium.\n(假期期間，海邊附近的飯店房間一位難求。)"],["prescribe","prescribe(v.)開(藥方)、規定\nprescription(n.)處方、藥方\nprescribe medicine 開藥\nas prescribed 按照醫囑\nThe doctor prescribed some medicine for my sore throat.\n(醫生開了一些藥治療我的喉嚨痛。)\nTake the pills exactly as prescribed by your doctor.\n(請完全按照醫生指示服藥。)"],["prescription","prescription(n.)處方、藥方、處方藥\nprescribe(v.)開(藥方)\nprescription drug 處方藥\nfill a prescription 領藥、配藥\nYou need a prescription from a doctor to buy this medicine.\n(你需要醫生開的處方才能買這種藥。)\nI went to the pharmacy to fill my prescription.\n(我去藥局領處方藥。)"],["presidency","presidency(n.)總統職位、總統任期、會長職務\npresident(n.)總統、會長\npresidential(adj.)總統的\nrun for the presidency 競選總統\nduring one's presidency 在某人擔任總統期間\nMany important laws were passed during his presidency.\n(他擔任總統期間通過了許多重要法案。)\nShe decided to run for the presidency of the student council.\n(她決定競選學生會會長。)"],["presidential","presidential(adj.)總統的、總統職位的\npresident(n.)總統\npresidency(n.)總統職位\npresidential election 總統大選\npresidential candidate 總統候選人\nTaiwan holds a presidential election every four years.\n(台灣每四年舉行一次總統大選。)\nThe presidential candidates debated on TV last night.\n(總統候選人昨晚在電視上辯論。)"],["presumably","presumably(adv.)大概、據推測\npresume(v.)假定、推測\npresumably because 大概是因為\npresumably true 大概是真的\nThe flight was delayed, presumably because of the heavy fog.\n(班機延誤了，大概是因為濃霧。)\nPresumably, the new library will open before the next semester.\n(新圖書館大概會在下學期前開放。)"],["presume","presume(v.)假定、推測、冒昧\npresumably(adv.)大概\npresumption(n.)假定、推測\npresume that 推測……\nbe presumed dead 被推定死亡\nI presume that you have already finished your homework.\n(我猜你已經寫完作業了。)\nThe missing sailors were presumed dead after a month of searching.\n(經過一個月的搜尋，失蹤的船員被推定死亡。)"],["prevail","prevail(v.)盛行、普遍、獲勝\nprevailing(adj.)盛行的、普遍的\nprevalent(adj.)流行的、普遍的\nprevail over 戰勝\nprevailing wind 盛行風\nIn the end, justice prevailed over evil.\n(最後正義戰勝了邪惡。)\nThis custom still prevails in many rural villages.\n(這項習俗在許多鄉村地區仍然盛行。)"],["prey","prey(n./v.)獵物、捕食、受害者\n(無詞性變化)\nprey on 捕食、欺騙\nfall prey to 成為……的受害者\nOwls prey on mice and other small animals at night.\n(貓頭鷹在夜間捕食老鼠和其他小動物。)\nMany elderly people fall prey to phone scams.\n(許多長者成為電話詐騙的受害者。)"],["prior","prior(adj./adv./n.)先前的、優先的\npriority(n.)優先、優先事項\nprioritize(v.)排定優先順序\nprior to 在……之前\nprior knowledge 先備知識\nPlease arrive at the airport two hours prior to departure.\n(請在起飛前兩小時抵達機場。)\nNo prior knowledge of programming is needed for this course.\n(這門課不需要任何程式設計的先備知識。)"],["proclaim","proclaim(v.)宣布、聲明、顯示\nproclamation(n.)宣言、公告\nproclaim independence 宣布獨立\nproclaim oneself 自稱\nThe country proclaimed its independence in 1776.\n(該國於一七七六年宣布獨立。)\nThe singer proclaimed himself the king of pop music.\n(那位歌手自稱為流行音樂之王。)"],["productivity","productivity(n.)生產力、生產率\nproductive(adj.)多產的、有成效的\nproduct(n.)產品\nincrease productivity 提高生產力\nworker productivity 勞工生產力\nGetting enough sleep can greatly increase your productivity.\n(充足的睡眠能大幅提高你的效率。)\nNew technology has improved productivity in many factories.\n(新科技提升了許多工廠的生產力。)"],["profile","profile(n./v.)側面、簡介、輪廓、扼要介紹\n(無詞性變化)\nprofile picture 大頭貼\nkeep a low profile 保持低調\nHe changed his profile picture on social media yesterday.\n(他昨天換了社群媒體上的大頭貼。)\nAfter the scandal, the actor kept a low profile for months.\n(醜聞過後，那位演員低調了好幾個月。)"],["profound","profound(adj.)深刻的、深遠的、深奧的\nprofoundly(adv.)深刻地\nprofound impact 深遠的影響\nprofound knowledge 淵博的知識\nThe war had a profound impact on the lives of ordinary people.\n(那場戰爭對一般人的生活造成深遠的影響。)\nThe professor has profound knowledge of ancient Chinese history.\n(那位教授對中國古代史有淵博的知識。)"],["progressive","progressive(adj./n.)進步的、漸進的、改革派\nprogress(n./v.)進步、進展\nprogressively(adv.)逐漸地\nprogressive ideas 進步的思想\nprogressive tense 進行式\nThe new mayor is known for his progressive ideas on education.\n(新市長以他對教育的進步思想聞名。)\nThe patient's condition showed progressive improvement over the week.\n(病人的狀況在這週逐漸好轉。)"],["prohibit","prohibit(v.)禁止、阻止\nprohibition(n.)禁止、禁令\nprohibit A from B 禁止A做B\nstrictly prohibited 嚴格禁止\nSmoking is strictly prohibited inside the school campus.\n(校園內嚴格禁止吸菸。)\nThe law prohibits drivers from using their phones while driving.\n(法律禁止駕駛在開車時使用手機。)"],["projection","projection(n.)預測、投射、放映\nproject(v./n.)投射、預計、計畫\nprojector(n.)投影機\nsales projection 銷售預測\npopulation projection 人口推估\nAccording to the population projection, Taiwan will have fewer young people in the future.\n(根據人口推估，台灣未來的年輕人會越來越少。)\nThe teacher used a projection of the map on the wall.\n(老師把地圖投影在牆上。)"],["prolong","prolong(v.)延長、拖延\nprolonged(adj.)長期的、持久的\nprolong life 延長壽命\nprolonged period 長時間\nRegular exercise and a healthy diet can prolong your life.\n(規律運動和健康飲食可以延長壽命。)\nSitting for a prolonged period is bad for your back.\n(長時間久坐對背部不好。)"],["prone","prone(adj.)易於……的、有……傾向的、俯臥的\n(無詞性變化)\nbe prone to 容易……\naccident-prone 容易出意外的\nTaiwan is prone to earthquakes and typhoons.\n(台灣容易發生地震和颱風。)\nPeople who don't sleep enough are more prone to making mistakes.\n(睡眠不足的人比較容易犯錯。)"],["propaganda","propaganda(n.)宣傳、宣傳活動\n(無詞性變化)\npolitical propaganda 政治宣傳\npropaganda campaign 宣傳活動\nDuring the war, both sides used propaganda to influence the public.\n(戰爭期間，雙方都利用宣傳來影響大眾。)\nWe should learn to tell the difference between facts and propaganda.\n(我們應該學會分辨事實與宣傳。)"],["prophet","prophet(n.)先知、預言家\nprophecy(n.)預言\nprophetic(adj.)預言的、有預見的\nprophet of doom 悲觀預言者\nfalse prophet 假先知\nSome people called the scientist a prophet of doom.\n(有些人稱那位科學家為末日預言者。)\nIn the story, the prophet warned the king about the coming disaster.\n(故事中，先知警告國王即將來臨的災難。)"],["proportion","proportion(n./v.)比例、部分、使成比例\nproportional(adj.)成比例的\nin proportion to 與……成比例\na large proportion of 很大一部分的\nA large proportion of students in our school take the MRT to school.\n(我們學校很大一部分的學生搭捷運上學。)\nYour salary will increase in proportion to your experience.\n(你的薪水會依經驗比例增加。)"],["prosecution","prosecution(n.)起訴、檢方\nprosecute(v.)起訴、告發\nprosecutor(n.)檢察官\nface prosecution 面臨起訴\nthe prosecution 控方、檢方\nAnyone who damages public property may face prosecution.\n(任何毀損公物的人都可能面臨起訴。)\nThe prosecution presented new evidence in court.\n(檢方在法庭上提出新證據。)"],["prospect","prospect(n./v.)前景、可能性、勘探\nprospective(adj.)預期的、潛在的\njob prospects 就業前景\nprospect of ……的可能性\nLearning a second language can improve your job prospects.\n(學習第二外語可以提升你的就業前景。)\nThe prospect of studying abroad excites her a lot.\n(出國留學的可能性讓她非常興奮。)"],["province","province(n.)省、領域、範圍\nprovincial(adj.)省的、地方的、狹隘的\nCanadian province 加拿大的省\nwithin one's province 在某人的專業範圍內\nCanada is divided into ten provinces and three territories.\n(加拿大分為十個省和三個地區。)\nThat question is outside my province; ask the science teacher.\n(那個問題不在我的專業範圍內，去問自然老師吧。)"],["provision","provision(n.)提供、供應、條款、(複數)糧食\nprovide(v.)提供\nmake provision for 為……做準備\nprovision of services 服務的提供\nThe hikers carried enough provisions for a three-day trip.\n(登山客帶了足夠三天行程的糧食。)\nThe government is responsible for the provision of clean water.\n(政府負責提供乾淨的用水。)"],["provoke","provoke(v.)激起、引起、挑釁\nprovocation(n.)挑釁、激怒\nprovocative(adj.)挑釁的、引起爭議的\nprovoke anger 激起憤怒\nprovoke a reaction 引起反應\nHis rude comments provoked anger among the audience.\n(他無禮的言論激起觀眾的憤怒。)\nDon't provoke the dog, or it might bite you.\n(不要去挑釁那隻狗，否則牠可能會咬你。)"],["pulse","pulse(n./v.)脈搏、脈動、搏動\n(無詞性變化)\ntake one's pulse 量脈搏\npulse rate 脈搏速率\nThe nurse took my pulse and checked my blood pressure.\n(護理師幫我量脈搏和血壓。)\nHer pulse was racing as she waited for the exam results.\n(等待考試結果時她的心跳加速。)"],["purchase","purchase(n./v.)購買、購買的物品\npurchaser(n.)購買者\nmake a purchase 購買\nproof of purchase 購買證明\nPlease keep your receipt as proof of purchase.\n(請保留收據作為購買證明。)\nMy parents purchased a new car for the family last month.\n(我父母上個月為家裡買了一輛新車。)"],["pyramid","pyramid(n.)金字塔、角錐體\n(無詞性變化)\nEgyptian pyramids 埃及金字塔\nfood pyramid 飲食金字塔\nThe ancient Egyptian pyramids were built more than four thousand years ago.\n(古埃及金字塔建於四千多年前。)\nThe food pyramid shows how much of each food group we should eat.\n(飲食金字塔顯示每一類食物我們應攝取多少。)"],["qualify","qualify(v.)使具資格、取得資格\nqualification(n.)資格、條件\nqualified(adj.)合格的、有資格的\nqualify for 有資格參加……\nqualified teacher 合格教師\nOur school team qualified for the national finals.\n(我們校隊取得了全國決賽的資格。)\nYou need a teaching license to become a qualified teacher.\n(你需要教師證才能成為合格教師。)"],["quest","quest(n.)追尋、探索\n(無詞性變化)\nquest for 追求……\nin quest of 為了尋求……\nThe story follows a young hero on a quest for a magic sword.\n(這個故事描述一位年輕英雄尋找魔劍的旅程。)\nHumans will never stop their quest for knowledge.\n(人類永遠不會停止對知識的追求。)"],["questionnaire","questionnaire(n.)問卷、調查表\n(無詞性變化)\nfill out a questionnaire 填寫問卷\nonline questionnaire 線上問卷\nPlease take five minutes to fill out this questionnaire about school lunches.\n(請花五分鐘填寫這份關於學校午餐的問卷。)\nWe designed an online questionnaire for our research project.\n(我們為研究專題設計了一份線上問卷。)"],["quiver","quiver(n./v.)顫抖、抖動、箭袋\n(無詞性變化)\nquiver with fear 因恐懼而顫抖\nvoice quivers 聲音顫抖\nHer voice quivered as she thanked everyone at the graduation ceremony.\n(她在畢業典禮上向大家致謝時聲音顫抖。)\nThe leaves quivered in the cool morning breeze.\n(樹葉在涼爽的晨風中顫動。)"],["quota","quota(n.)配額、定額、名額\n(無詞性變化)\nimport quota 進口配額\nmeet a quota 達到定額\nEach salesperson has to meet a monthly sales quota.\n(每位業務員都必須達成每月的銷售定額。)\nThe university has a quota for international students each year.\n(這所大學每年有國際學生的名額限制。)"],["racism","racism(n.)種族歧視、種族主義\nracist(n./adj.)種族主義者、種族歧視的\nfight racism 對抗種族歧視\ninstitutional racism 制度性種族歧視\nMany athletes have spoken out publicly against racism in sports.\n(許多運動員公開發聲反對體壇的種族歧視。)\nThe school held a workshop to help students understand the harm of racism.\n(學校舉辦了一場工作坊，幫助學生了解種族歧視的危害。)"],["rack","rack(n./v.)架子、使痛苦\n(無詞性變化)\nshoe rack 鞋架\nrack one's brain 絞盡腦汁\nHe hung his wet towel on the rack in the bathroom.\n(他把濕毛巾掛在浴室的架子上。)\nI racked my brain but couldn't remember her name.\n(我絞盡腦汁還是想不起她的名字。)"],["radiation","radiation(n.)輻射、放射線\nradiate(v.)散發、輻射\nradioactive(adj.)放射性的\nradiation exposure 輻射暴露\nnuclear radiation 核輻射\nLong exposure to radiation can seriously damage human cells.\n(長時間暴露在輻射下會嚴重損害人體細胞。)\nSunscreen protects your skin from harmful ultraviolet radiation.\n(防曬乳能保護皮膚免受有害紫外線輻射。)"],["radical","radical(adj./n.)根本的、激進的、激進分子\nradically(adv.)徹底地\nradical change 根本的改變\nradical ideas 激進的想法\nThe new principal made radical changes to the school schedule.\n(新校長對學校的作息做了根本性的改變。)\nSome of his political views are considered too radical.\n(他的一些政治觀點被認為太過激進。)"],["ragged","ragged(adj.)破爛的、衣衫襤褸的、參差不齊的\nrag(n.)破布\nragged clothes 破爛的衣服\nragged edge 參差不齊的邊緣\nThe child in ragged clothes was begging for food.\n(那個衣衫襤褸的孩子正在乞討食物。)\nAfter running ten kilometers, his breathing was ragged.\n(跑完十公里後，他的呼吸變得急促不穩。)"],["raid","raid(n./v.)突襲、搜捕、劫掠\nraider(n.)襲擊者\npolice raid 警方突襲搜查\nair raid 空襲\nPolice carried out a raid on the illegal gambling house.\n(警方突襲搜查了那間非法賭場。)\nThe kids raided the fridge as soon as they got home.\n(孩子們一回到家就把冰箱搜刮一空。)"],["rail","rail(n.)欄杆、鐵軌、鐵路\nrailing(n.)欄杆\nhigh-speed rail 高速鐵路\nby rail 搭火車\nTaking the high-speed rail from Taipei to Kaohsiung saves a lot of time.\n(從台北搭高鐵到高雄可以省下很多時間。)\nHold onto the rail when you walk down the stairs.\n(下樓梯時請抓住扶手。)"],["rally","rally(n./v.)集會、重整、號召、(網球)對打\n(無詞性變化)\nhold a rally 舉行集會\nrally support 爭取支持\nThousands of people attended the rally for climate action.\n(數千人參加了支持氣候行動的集會。)\nThe captain rallied his teammates after they fell behind.\n(落後之後，隊長重新激勵隊友士氣。)"],["ranch","ranch(n./v.)大農場、牧場、經營牧場\nrancher(n.)牧場主人\ncattle ranch 養牛場\nranch house 牧場式平房\nHis family owns a large cattle ranch in Texas.\n(他的家族在德州擁有一座大型養牛場。)\nWe spent the summer riding horses on a ranch.\n(我們在一座牧場騎馬度過了夏天。)"],["random","random(adj.)隨機的、任意的\nrandomly(adv.)隨機地\nat random 隨機地\nrandom sample 隨機樣本\nThe teacher picked three students at random to answer the question.\n(老師隨機挑了三位學生回答問題。)\nThe researchers interviewed a random sample of 500 teenagers.\n(研究人員訪問了五百名隨機抽樣的青少年。)"],["ratio","ratio(n.)比例、比率\n(無詞性變化)\nthe ratio of A to B 兩者的比例\nstudent-teacher ratio 師生比\nThe ratio of boys to girls in our class is about two to one.\n(我們班男女生的比例大約是二比一。)\nSmaller classes have a lower student-teacher ratio.\n(小班制的師生比較低。)"],["rational","rational(adj.)理性的、合理的\nrationality(n.)理性\nrationally(adv.)理性地\nrational decision 理性的決定\nrational thinking 理性思考\nTry to stay calm and make a rational decision.\n(試著保持冷靜，做出理性的決定。)\nThere must be a rational explanation for what happened.\n(發生的事情一定有合理的解釋。)"],["rattle","rattle(v./n.)發出咯咯聲、使慌張、波浪鼓\n(無詞性變化)\nrattle the windows 使窗戶咯咯作響\nbaby rattle 嬰兒搖鈴\nThe strong wind rattled the windows all night.\n(強風整晚吹得窗戶咯咯作響。)\nShe was rattled by the difficult interview questions.\n(她被那些困難的面試問題弄得心慌意亂。)"],["realism","realism(n.)現實主義、寫實主義\nrealist(n.)現實主義者\nrealistic(adj.)實際的、逼真的\na sense of realism 現實感\nartistic realism 藝術寫實主義\nThe film is praised for its realism in depicting war.\n(這部電影因描繪戰爭的寫實而受到讚揚。)\nHer plan shows a healthy dose of realism.\n(她的計畫展現出相當程度的務實。)"],["realm","realm(n.)領域、範圍、王國\n(無詞性變化)\nwithin the realm of possibility 在可能範圍內\nthe realm of science 科學領域\nTraveling to Mars is now within the realm of possibility.\n(前往火星現在已經在可能的範圍內。)\nHer research opened up a new realm of study.\n(她的研究開拓了一個新的研究領域。)"],["rear","rear(adj./n.)後面的、後部、養育\n(無詞性變化)\nrear seat 後座\nrear a child 養育孩子\nPlease use the rear door when getting off the bus.\n(下公車時請走後門。)\nShe reared three children on her own.\n(她獨自養大了三個孩子。)"],["reassure","reassure(v.)使安心、消除疑慮\nreassurance(n.)安慰、保證\nreassuring(adj.)令人安心的\nreassure sb. that 向某人保證…\nreassuring smile 令人安心的微笑\nThe doctor reassured me that the surgery would go well.\n(醫生向我保證手術會很順利。)\nHer calm voice was reassuring to the nervous students.\n(她平靜的聲音讓緊張的學生安心不少。)"],["rebellion","rebellion(n.)叛亂、反抗\nrebel(n./v.)叛亂者、反抗\nrebellious(adj.)叛逆的\narmed rebellion 武裝叛亂\nteenage rebellion 青少年叛逆\nThe government sent troops to put down the rebellion.\n(政府派兵鎮壓叛亂。)\nDyeing his hair green was a small act of teenage rebellion.\n(把頭髮染成綠色是他小小的青春期叛逆行為。)"],["recession","recession(n.)經濟衰退、後退\nrecede(v.)後退、減弱\neconomic recession 經濟衰退\nin recession 處於衰退中\nMany people lost their jobs during the economic recession.\n(經濟衰退期間許多人失去了工作。)\nExperts warn that the country may slip into a recession.\n(專家警告這個國家可能陷入經濟衰退。)"],["recipient","recipient(n./adj.)接受者、領受者、接受的\nreceive(v.)接受、收到\naward recipient 得獎者\norgan recipient 器官受贈者\nShe was the youngest recipient of the science award.\n(她是那個科學獎最年輕的得主。)\nThe recipient of the letter never replied.\n(收信人從未回覆。)"],["recite","recite(v.)背誦、朗誦、列舉\nrecitation(n.)背誦\nrecital(n.)獨奏會、獨唱會\nrecite a poem 朗誦詩\nrecite from memory 憑記憶背誦\nEach student had to recite a poem in front of the class.\n(每位學生都得在全班面前朗誦一首詩。)\nHe recited the whole speech from memory.\n(他憑記憶背出整篇演講。)"],["recommend","recommend(v.)推薦、建議\nrecommendation(n.)推薦、建議\nhighly recommend 強力推薦\nrecommend that 建議…\nI highly recommend this book to anyone interested in history.\n(我強力推薦這本書給對歷史有興趣的人。)\nThe doctor recommended that he get more sleep.\n(醫生建議他多睡一點。)"],["recommendation","recommendation(n.)推薦、建議、推薦信\nrecommend(v.)推薦、建議\nletter of recommendation 推薦信\nmake a recommendation 提出建議\nI asked my teacher to write a letter of recommendation for me.\n(我請老師幫我寫一封推薦信。)\nWe chose this restaurant on a friend's recommendation.\n(我們依照朋友的推薦選了這間餐廳。)"],["recruit","recruit(v./n.)招募、新成員、新兵\nrecruitment(n.)招募\nrecruit volunteers 招募志工\nnew recruit 新成員\nThe club is recruiting new members this week.\n(社團這週正在招募新社員。)\nThe new recruits trained hard for three months.\n(新兵們刻苦訓練了三個月。)"],["refuge","refuge(n.)避難、庇護所\nrefugee(n.)難民\ntake refuge 避難\nwildlife refuge 野生動物保護區\nThe hikers took refuge in a cave during the storm.\n(登山客在暴風雨中躲進山洞避難。)\nFor her, the library was a quiet refuge from the busy city.\n(對她來說，圖書館是遠離喧囂城市的寧靜避風港。)"],["regardless","regardless(adj./adv.)不管、不顧\n(無詞性變化)\nregardless of 不論…\nregardless of the cost 不惜代價\nEveryone is welcome to join, regardless of age or background.\n(不論年齡或背景，歡迎所有人加入。)\nIt was raining hard, but they went ahead regardless.\n(雨下得很大，但他們仍不顧一切照常進行。)"],["regime","regime(n.)政權、政體、制度\n(無詞性變化)\nmilitary regime 軍事政權\npolitical regime 政治體制\nThe country suffered for decades under a military regime.\n(那個國家在軍事政權統治下受苦了數十年。)\nThe old regime collapsed after massive protests.\n(舊政權在大規模抗議後垮台。)"],["rehearsal","rehearsal(n.)排練、預演\nrehearse(v.)排練\ndress rehearsal 彩排\nin rehearsal 排練中\nThe band had a final rehearsal before the concert.\n(樂團在演唱會前做了最後一次排練。)\nThe dress rehearsal went smoothly last night.\n(昨晚的彩排進行得很順利。)"],["reinforce","reinforce(v.)加強、強化、增援\nreinforcement(n.)強化、增援\nreinforce learning 強化學習\nreinforced concrete 鋼筋混凝土\nRegular review helps reinforce what you learned in class.\n(定期複習有助於加強課堂所學。)\nThe bridge was reinforced with steel after the earthquake.\n(地震後這座橋以鋼材加以補強。)"],["reminder","reminder(n.)提醒、提醒物\nremind(v.)提醒、使想起\ngentle reminder 溫馨提醒\nserve as a reminder 作為提醒\nThis is a gentle reminder that the report is due on Friday.\n(溫馨提醒，報告星期五截止。)\nThe old photo serves as a reminder of our happy childhood.\n(這張舊照片讓人想起我們快樂的童年。)"],["removal","removal(n.)移除、除去、搬遷\nremove(v.)移除、拿走\nsnow removal 除雪\nhair removal 除毛\nThe removal of the old tree took the workers all day.\n(工人們花了一整天才移除那棵老樹。)\nThe city is responsible for garbage removal in this area.\n(市政府負責這個區域的垃圾清運。)"],["render","render(v.)使成為、給予、表現、翻譯\nrendering(n.)表演、詮釋\nrender sb. helpless 使某人無助\nrender assistance 提供協助\nThe heavy snow rendered the roads impassable.\n(大雪使道路無法通行。)\nVolunteers rendered help to the flood victims.\n(志工們為水災災民提供協助。)"],["rental","rental(n.)租金、出租、租賃\nrent(v./n.)租、租金\ncar rental 租車\nrental apartment 出租公寓\nWe arranged a car rental for our trip to Hualien.\n(我們為花蓮之旅安排了租車。)\nMonthly rental for apartments near the university is high.\n(大學附近公寓的月租金很高。)"],["repay","repay(v.)償還、報答\nrepayment(n.)償還\nrepay a loan 償還貸款\nrepay kindness 報答恩情\nIt took him five years to repay the loan.\n(他花了五年才還清貸款。)\nHow can I ever repay your kindness?\n(我要怎麼報答你的恩情呢？)"],["republican","republican(n./adj.)共和主義者、共和黨員、共和國的\nrepublic(n.)共和國\nRepublican Party 美國共和黨\nrepublican government 共和政府\nHe has voted for the Republican candidate in every election.\n(他每次選舉都投給共和黨候選人。)\nThe country adopted a republican form of government in 1912.\n(這個國家在一九一二年採行共和政體。)"],["resemblance","resemblance(n.)相似、相像\nresemble(v.)像、與…相似\nbear a resemblance to 和…相像\nstrong resemblance 非常相像\nShe bears a strong resemblance to her grandmother.\n(她和她祖母長得非常像。)\nThe story bears little resemblance to what actually happened.\n(這個故事和實際發生的事幾乎沒有相似之處。)"],["reservoir","reservoir(n.)水庫、蓄水池、儲藏\n(無詞性變化)\nwater reservoir 水庫\nFeitsui Reservoir 翡翠水庫\nThe water level in the reservoir dropped sharply during the drought.\n(乾旱期間水庫水位急遽下降。)\nFeitsui Reservoir supplies water to most of Taipei.\n(翡翠水庫供應台北大部分地區的用水。)"],["residence","residence(n.)住所、居住\nreside(v.)居住\nresidential(adj.)住宅的\npermanent residence 永久居留\nofficial residence 官邸\nThe president's official residence is heavily guarded.\n(總統官邸戒備森嚴。)\nHe has taken up residence in Tainan since he retired.\n(他退休後就定居在台南。)"],["resident","resident(n./adj.)居民、住院醫師、居住的\nreside(v.)居住\nlocal residents 當地居民\nresident doctor 住院醫師\nLocal residents complained about the noise from the construction.\n(當地居民抱怨施工的噪音。)\nShe has been a resident of this town for twenty years.\n(她在這個小鎮住了二十年。)"],["residential","residential(adj.)住宅的、居住的\nresidence(n.)住所\nresidential area 住宅區\nresidential building 住宅大樓\nFactories are not allowed in residential areas.\n(住宅區內不准設工廠。)\nThe new residential building has thirty floors.\n(那棟新住宅大樓有三十層。)"],["resort","resort(n./v.)度假勝地、手段、訴諸\n(無詞性變化)\nbeach resort 海灘度假村\nlast resort 最後手段\nWe stayed at a beach resort in Kenting.\n(我們住在墾丁的一間海灘度假村。)\nParents should never resort to violence to discipline their children.\n(父母絕不應該用暴力管教孩子。)"],["respondent","respondent(n.)回答者、受訪者、被告\nrespond(v.)回應\nresponse(n.)回應\nsurvey respondent 問卷受訪者\nmajority of respondents 多數受訪者\nMost respondents said they spend over three hours a day online.\n(大多數受訪者表示每天上網超過三小時。)\nThe survey asked respondents about their sleep habits.\n(這份調查詢問受訪者的睡眠習慣。)"],["resume","resume(v./n.)重新開始、繼續、履歷\nresume(n.)履歷(亦作résumé)\nresume work 恢復工作\nsend a résumé 寄履歷\nClasses will resume after the typhoon passes.\n(颱風過後將恢復上課。)\nShe sent her résumé to five companies.\n(她把履歷寄給了五家公司。)"],["retail","retail(n./adj./adv./v.)零售、零售的、以零售方式、零售\nretailer(n.)零售商\nretail price 零售價\nretail store 零售店\nThe retail price of this phone is higher than I expected.\n(這支手機的零售價比我預期的高。)\nOnline shopping has changed the retail industry dramatically.\n(網路購物大幅改變了零售業。)"],["revenue","revenue(n.)收入、稅收\n(無詞性變化)\ntax revenue 稅收\nadvertising revenue 廣告收入\nTourism is a major source of revenue for the island.\n(觀光是這座島嶼的主要收入來源。)\nThe company's revenue increased by twenty percent last year.\n(這家公司去年營收成長了百分之二十。)"],["reverse","reverse(v./adj./n.)反轉、倒退、相反的、相反\nreversal(n.)反轉\nreversible(adj.)可逆的、可兩面穿的\nin reverse 倒過來、反向\nreverse the decision 推翻決定\nThe court reversed its earlier decision.\n(法院推翻了先前的判決。)\nRead the numbers in reverse order.\n(把這些數字倒著唸。)"],["rhetoric","rhetoric(n.)修辭、修辭學、華麗空洞的言詞\nrhetorical(adj.)修辭的\npolitical rhetoric 政治辭令\nempty rhetoric 空話\nVoters are tired of empty political rhetoric.\n(選民厭倦了空洞的政治辭令。)\nThe speech was full of rhetoric but lacked real solutions.\n(那篇演講充滿華麗辭藻，卻缺乏實際解決方案。)"],["rib","rib(n./v.)肋骨、排骨、取笑\n(無詞性變化)\nbroken rib 肋骨斷裂\npork ribs 豬肋排\nHe broke two ribs in the car accident.\n(他在車禍中斷了兩根肋骨。)\nWe ordered grilled pork ribs for dinner.\n(我們晚餐點了烤豬肋排。)"],["ridge","ridge(n./v.)山脊、隆起、使隆起\n(無詞性變化)\nmountain ridge 山脊\nwalk along the ridge 沿著山脊走\nWe hiked along the ridge and enjoyed the view.\n(我們沿著山脊健行，欣賞風景。)\nThe sun rose slowly over the distant ridge.\n(太陽從遠方的山脊緩緩升起。)"],["ridiculous","ridiculous(adj.)荒謬的、可笑的\nridicule(v./n.)嘲笑\nridiculously(adv.)荒謬地\nridiculous idea 荒謬的想法\nlook ridiculous 看起來很可笑\nIt's ridiculous to pay that much for a T-shirt.\n(花那麼多錢買一件T恤太荒謬了。)\nI felt ridiculous in that bright pink costume.\n(穿著那套亮粉紅色的戲服我覺得很可笑。)"],["rifle","rifle(n./v.)步槍、翻找\n(無詞性變化)\nhunting rifle 獵槍\nrifle through 翻找\nThe soldier cleaned his rifle carefully.\n(那名士兵仔細清理他的步槍。)\nShe rifled through her bag looking for her keys.\n(她在包包裡翻找鑰匙。)"],["rigid","rigid(adj.)嚴格的、死板的、堅硬的\nrigidity(n.)嚴格、僵硬\nrigidly(adv.)嚴格地\nrigid rules 死板的規定\nrigid structure 堅固的結構\nThe school's rigid rules left students little freedom.\n(學校死板的規定讓學生幾乎沒有自由。)\nThe box is made of rigid plastic.\n(這個盒子是用硬塑膠做的。)"],["rim","rim(n./v.)邊緣、框、圍繞\n(無詞性變化)\nthe rim of a cup 杯緣\nglasses rim 眼鏡框\nThe ball rolled around the rim before dropping into the basket.\n(球在籃框上滾了一圈才掉進籃裡。)\nSalt was added to the rim of the glass.\n(杯緣上沾了一圈鹽。)"],["riot","riot(n./v.)暴動、騷亂、發生暴動\nriotous(adj.)暴亂的、喧鬧的\nriot police 鎮暴警察\nstart a riot 引發暴動\nRiot police were sent to control the angry crowd.\n(鎮暴警察被派去控制憤怒的群眾。)\nPrisoners rioted over the poor living conditions.\n(囚犯因惡劣的生活條件而發生暴動。)"],["rip","rip(v./n.)撕裂、扯破、裂口\n(無詞性變化)\nrip off 敲竹槓、剝削\nrip open 撕開\nHe ripped open the envelope to read the letter.\n(他撕開信封讀信。)\nPaying 500 dollars for that coffee was a total rip-off.\n(那杯咖啡要五百元，根本是敲竹槓。)"],["risky","risky(adj.)危險的、冒險的\nrisk(n./v.)風險、冒…的險\nrisky business 冒險的事\nrisky decision 冒險的決定\nSwimming in the river after heavy rain is very risky.\n(大雨後在河裡游泳非常危險。)\nInvesting all your money in one stock is a risky decision.\n(把所有錢都投資在一支股票上是冒險的決定。)"],["ritual","ritual(n./adj.)儀式、例行習慣、儀式的\n(無詞性變化)\nreligious ritual 宗教儀式\ndaily ritual 每日例行習慣\nMaking coffee in the morning is part of my daily ritual.\n(早上煮咖啡是我每天的例行習慣。)\nThe temple holds a special ritual during the Ghost Festival.\n(這間廟在中元節舉行特別的儀式。)"],["rival","rival(adj./n./v.)競爭的、對手、與…匹敵\nrivalry(n.)競爭、對抗\nrival team 敵隊\nmain rival 主要對手\nOur school beat its biggest rival in the final.\n(我們學校在決賽中擊敗了最大的對手。)\nFew cities can rival Paris for beauty.\n(在美麗程度上很少有城市能與巴黎匹敵。)"],["rod","rod(n.)桿、棒、竿\n(無詞性變化)\nfishing rod 釣竿\nmetal rod 金屬棒\nMy grandfather gave me his old fishing rod.\n(我爺爺把他的舊釣竿送給了我。)\nThe curtain hangs from a metal rod.\n(窗簾掛在一根金屬桿上。)"],["sacred","sacred(adj.)神聖的、宗教的、不可侵犯的\n(無詞性變化)\nsacred place 聖地\nsacred duty 神聖的職責\nThe mountain is considered a sacred place by the local tribe.\n(這座山被當地部落視為聖地。)\nFor him, family time on Sunday is sacred.\n(對他來說，星期天的家庭時光是不可侵犯的。)"],["saddle","saddle(n./v.)馬鞍、坐墊、使承擔(負擔)\n(無詞性變化)\nin the saddle 騎在馬上、掌權\nbe saddled with 背負…\nShe climbed into the saddle and rode off.\n(她跨上馬鞍騎馬離去。)\nMany graduates are saddled with heavy student loans.\n(許多畢業生背負著沉重的學貸。)"],["saint","saint(n./v.)聖人、聖徒、封為聖徒\nsaintly(adj.)聖潔的\npatron saint 守護聖徒\nbe no saint 並非完人\nShe has the patience of a saint with her little students.\n(她對年幼的學生有聖人般的耐心。)\nSaint Valentine's Day is celebrated on February 14.\n(聖瓦倫丁節在二月十四日慶祝。)"],["salmon","salmon(n./adj.)鮭魚、鮭魚肉色的\n(無詞性變化)\nsmoked salmon 燻鮭魚\nsalmon sushi 鮭魚壽司\nSalmon swim upstream to lay their eggs.\n(鮭魚會逆流而上產卵。)\nGrilled salmon is rich in healthy fats.\n(烤鮭魚富含健康的脂肪。)"],["salon","salon(n.)美髮院、沙龍、會客廳\n(無詞性變化)\nhair salon 美髮院\nbeauty salon 美容院\nShe gets her hair cut at a salon near the station.\n(她在車站附近的一家美髮院剪頭髮。)\nThe beauty salon is fully booked on weekends.\n(那家美容院週末都約滿了。)"],["sandal","sandal(n.)涼鞋\n(無詞性變化)\na pair of sandals 一雙涼鞋\nleather sandals 皮涼鞋\nHe wore a pair of sandals to the beach.\n(他穿了一雙涼鞋去海邊。)\nSandals are not allowed in the school laboratory.\n(學校實驗室內禁止穿涼鞋。)"],["scan","scan(n./v.)掃描、瀏覽、細看\nscanner(n.)掃描器\nscan a QR code 掃描QR碼\nbrain scan 腦部掃描\nScan the QR code to see the menu.\n(掃描QR碼即可查看菜單。)\nShe quickly scanned the newspaper for job ads.\n(她快速瀏覽報紙尋找徵才廣告。)"],["scandal","scandal(n.)醜聞、恥辱\nscandalous(adj.)可恥的、醜聞的\npolitical scandal 政治醜聞\ncause a scandal 引起醜聞\nThe minister resigned after the scandal was exposed.\n(醜聞曝光後，那位部長辭職了。)\nIt is a scandal that so much food goes to waste.\n(有這麼多食物被浪費真是可恥。)"],["scar","scar(n./v.)疤痕、創傷、留下傷痕\n(無詞性變化)\nleave a scar 留下疤痕\nemotional scars 心理創傷\nThe cut healed, but it left a small scar on his knee.\n(傷口癒合了，但在他膝蓋上留下一道小疤。)\nThe war scarred the whole generation emotionally.\n(那場戰爭在整個世代心中留下了創傷。)"],["scenario","scenario(n.)情節、劇本、可能的情況\n(無詞性變化)\nworst-case scenario 最壞的情況\npossible scenario 可能的情況\nIn the worst-case scenario, the event will be canceled.\n(最壞的情況是活動會取消。)\nThe teacher asked us to imagine a scenario without electricity.\n(老師要我們想像一個沒有電的情境。)"],["scent","scent(n./v.)香味、氣味、嗅出\nscented(adj.)有香味的\npleasant scent 宜人的香氣\non the scent 追蹤到線索\nThe scent of jasmine filled the garden.\n(茉莉花的香味瀰漫整個花園。)\nThe dog scented danger and began to bark.\n(那隻狗嗅出危險，開始吠叫。)"],["scheme","scheme(n./v.)計畫、方案、詭計、密謀\n(無詞性變化)\ncolor scheme 配色\nscheme to 密謀做…\nThe town launched a recycling scheme to reduce waste.\n(這個鎮推出一項回收方案以減少垃圾。)\nThey schemed to steal the company's secrets.\n(他們密謀竊取公司的機密。)"],["scope","scope(n.)範圍、機會、餘地\n(無詞性變化)\nbeyond the scope of 超出…範圍\nscope for improvement 改進的空間\nThis question is beyond the scope of today's lesson.\n(這個問題超出了今天課程的範圍。)\nThere is still plenty of scope for improvement in your essay.\n(你的文章仍有很大的進步空間。)"],["scramble","scramble(v./n.)爬、攀爬、爭奪、炒(蛋)\n(無詞性變化)\nscrambled eggs 炒蛋\nscramble for 爭搶\nShoppers scrambled for the discounted items.\n(購物者爭搶打折商品。)\nWe scrambled up the rocky hill to watch the sunrise.\n(我們手腳並用爬上岩石山丘看日出。)"],["scrap","scrap(n./v.)碎片、廢料、廢棄\n(無詞性變化)\nscrap paper 廢紙、計算紙\nscrap metal 廢金屬\nUse the back of scrap paper for your calculations.\n(用廢紙的背面來計算。)\nThe city decided to scrap the plan due to lack of money.\n(市政府因資金不足決定取消這項計畫。)"],["script","script(n./v.)劇本、腳本、筆跡、編寫劇本\nscriptwriter(n.)編劇\nfilm script 電影劇本\nwrite a script 寫劇本\nThe actors read through the script together.\n(演員們一起讀了一遍劇本。)\nShe scripted the school play herself.\n(她親自為學校話劇寫劇本。)"],["sector","sector(n.)部門、領域、扇形\n(無詞性變化)\nprivate sector 民間部門\npublic sector 公部門\nJobs in the technology sector are growing quickly.\n(科技業的工作機會正快速增加。)\nThe government is working with the private sector to create jobs.\n(政府正與民間企業合作創造就業機會。)"],["segment","segment(n./v.)部分、片段、分割\nsegmentation(n.)分割、區隔\nmarket segment 市場區隔\nline segment 線段\nYoung people are an important segment of the market.\n(年輕人是重要的市場族群。)\nDraw a line segment from point A to point B.\n(從A點到B點畫一條線段。)"],["seminar","seminar(n.)研討會、專題討論課\n(無詞性變化)\nattend a seminar 參加研討會\nhold a seminar 舉辦研討會\nOur teacher attended a seminar on AI in education.\n(我們老師參加了一場教育AI研討會。)\nThe university holds a seminar for new students every fall.\n(這所大學每年秋天為新生舉辦專題講座。)"],["senator","senator(n.)參議員\nsenate(n.)參議院\nUS senator 美國參議員\nstate senator 州參議員\nThe senator voted against the new tax bill.\n(那位參議員對新稅法投下反對票。)\nShe became the youngest senator in the state's history.\n(她成為該州史上最年輕的參議員。)"],["sensation","sensation(n.)感覺、轟動、轟動的事\nsensational(adj.)轟動的、聳動的\nburning sensation 灼熱感\ncause a sensation 引起轟動\nI felt a strange tingling sensation in my fingers.\n(我的手指有一種奇怪的刺痛感。)\nThe young singer became an overnight sensation online.\n(那位年輕歌手一夜之間在網路上爆紅。)"],["sensitivity","sensitivity(n.)敏感、靈敏度、體貼\nsensitive(adj.)敏感的\ncultural sensitivity 文化敏感度\nsensitivity to light 對光敏感\nThe topic should be handled with great sensitivity.\n(這個話題應該非常謹慎地處理。)\nSome people have a strong sensitivity to noise.\n(有些人對噪音非常敏感。)"],["sensor","sensor(n.)感應器、感測器\n(無詞性變化)\nmotion sensor 動作感應器\ntemperature sensor 溫度感測器\nThe lights turn on automatically thanks to a motion sensor.\n(多虧了動作感應器，燈會自動亮起。)\nSmartphones contain many sensors, such as GPS and cameras.\n(智慧型手機裡有許多感測器，像是GPS和相機。)"],["sentiment","sentiment(n.)情緒、觀點、感傷\nsentimental(adj.)感傷的、多愁善感的\npublic sentiment 民意\nanti-war sentiment 反戰情緒\nPublic sentiment turned against the new policy.\n(民意轉而反對這項新政策。)\nI share your sentiments about the importance of education.\n(我認同你對教育重要性的看法。)"],["sentimental","sentimental(adj.)感傷的、多愁善感的、情感上的\nsentiment(n.)情緒、感傷\nsentimental value 紀念價值\nget sentimental 變得感傷\nThis old watch isn't expensive, but it has great sentimental value.\n(這支舊手錶不貴，但很有紀念價值。)\nGrandpa gets sentimental when he looks at old photos.\n(爺爺看著舊照片時會變得很感傷。)"],["sequence","sequence(n./v.)順序、一連串、按順序排列\nsequential(adj.)連續的、按順序的\nin sequence 依序\na sequence of events 一連串事件\nPut the pictures in the correct sequence to tell the story.\n(把圖片按照正確的順序排列來說故事。)\nA strange sequence of events led to the accident.\n(一連串奇怪的事件導致了這場意外。)"],["series","series(n.)系列、一連串、影集\n(無詞性變化)\na series of 一連串的\nTV series 電視影集\nThe police are investigating a series of robberies.\n(警方正在調查一連串的搶案。)\nI stayed up late watching a Korean TV series.\n(我熬夜看韓劇。)"],["server","server(n.)伺服器、服務生\nserve(v.)服務、供應\nweb server 網頁伺服器\nserver down 伺服器當機\nThe website crashed because the server was overloaded.\n(網站因為伺服器超載而當機。)\nThe server brought us our drinks right away.\n(服務生立刻把飲料端來給我們。)"],["session","session(n.)一段時間、會議、開會期間\n(無詞性變化)\ntraining session 訓練課程\nin session 開會中、開庭中\nThe coach holds a training session every Saturday morning.\n(教練每週六早上舉行一次訓練。)\nParliament is now in session.\n(國會目前正在開會。)"],["setting","setting(n.)背景、環境、設定\nset(v.)設定、放置\nnatural setting 自然環境\nprivacy settings 隱私設定\nThe novel's setting is a small fishing village in Taiwan.\n(這本小說的背景是台灣的一個小漁村。)\nYou should check the privacy settings on your social media account.\n(你應該檢查社群帳號的隱私設定。)"],["shareholder","shareholder(n.)股東\nshare(n.)股份\nmajor shareholder 大股東\nshareholder meeting 股東大會\nThe shareholders voted to approve the merger.\n(股東們投票通過了這項合併案。)\nHe is the largest shareholder of the company.\n(他是這家公司最大的股東。)"],["shatter","shatter(v.)粉碎、使破滅\nshattered(adj.)極度疲憊的、心碎的\nshatter into pieces 碎成片片\nshatter dreams 使夢想破滅\nThe glass fell off the table and shattered into pieces.\n(玻璃杯從桌上掉下來摔得粉碎。)\nThe injury shattered his dream of playing professionally.\n(那次受傷粉碎了他打職業賽的夢想。)"],["shed","shed(v./n.)流出、脫落、去除、棚子\n(無詞性變化)\nshed tears 流淚\nshed light on 闡明、揭露\nThe new study sheds light on how sleep affects memory.\n(這項新研究揭示了睡眠如何影響記憶。)\nTrees shed their leaves in autumn.\n(樹木在秋天落葉。)"],["sheer","sheer(adj./adv.)全然的、純粹的、陡峭的、陡峭地\n(無詞性變化)\nsheer luck 純屬運氣\nsheer cliff 陡峭的懸崖\nHe passed the test by sheer luck.\n(他通過考試純屬運氣。)\nThe sheer size of the crowd surprised the organizers.\n(群眾的龐大規模令主辦單位大吃一驚。)"],["sheriff","sheriff(n.)(美國)郡警長\n(無詞性變化)\ncounty sheriff 郡警長\nlocal sheriff 當地警長\nThe sheriff arrested the suspect near the border.\n(警長在邊界附近逮捕了嫌犯。)\nIn old Western movies, the sheriff always wears a star badge.\n(在老西部片裡，警長總是配戴星形徽章。)"],["shield","shield(n./v.)盾、保護物、保護、遮擋\n(無詞性變化)\nshield from 保護免於…\nprotective shield 保護罩\nShe shielded her eyes from the bright sun.\n(她遮住眼睛擋住刺眼的陽光。)\nThe ozone layer acts as a shield against harmful rays.\n(臭氧層是抵擋有害射線的屏障。)"],["shiver","shiver(n./v.)顫抖、發抖\nshivery(adj.)發抖的\nshiver with cold 冷得發抖\nsend shivers down one's spine 令人毛骨悚然\nThe children stood shivering in the cold rain.\n(孩子們站在冰冷的雨中發抖。)\nThe ghost story sent shivers down my spine.\n(那個鬼故事讓我毛骨悚然。)"],["shortage","shortage(n.)短缺、不足\nshort(adj.)短缺的\nwater shortage 缺水\nlabor shortage 勞力短缺\nThe island often faces a water shortage in summer.\n(這座島嶼夏天常面臨缺水。)\nMany hospitals are dealing with a shortage of nurses.\n(許多醫院正面臨護理人力短缺。)"],["shove","shove(v./n.)推、擠、猛推\n(無詞性變化)\npush and shove 推擠\nshove into 把…塞進\nPeople pushed and shoved to get on the crowded train.\n(人們推擠著要擠上擁擠的列車。)\nHe shoved his clothes into the bag and rushed out.\n(他把衣服塞進包包就衝出門。)"],["shrug","shrug(n./v.)聳肩\n(無詞性變化)\nshrug one's shoulders 聳肩\nshrug off 不理會、對…不以為意\nWhen I asked where Tom was, she just shrugged.\n(我問湯姆在哪裡時，她只是聳聳肩。)\nHe shrugged off the criticism and kept working.\n(他對批評不以為意，繼續工作。)"],["shuttle","shuttle(n./v.)接駁車、太空梭、往返\n(無詞性變化)\nshuttle bus 接駁車\nspace shuttle 太空梭\nA free shuttle bus runs between the station and the stadium.\n(車站和體育館之間有免費接駁車。)\nPassengers were shuttled to the airport by van.\n(乘客們坐廂型車被接送到機場。)"],["sibling","sibling(n.)兄弟姊妹\n(無詞性變化)\nsibling rivalry 手足競爭\nolder sibling 哥哥或姊姊\nDo you have any siblings?\n(你有兄弟姊妹嗎？)\nSibling rivalry is common in families with young children.\n(手足競爭在有年幼孩子的家庭中很常見。)"],["siege","siege(n.)圍攻、包圍\nbesiege(v.)圍攻、圍困\nunder siege 被圍困\nlay siege to 圍攻\nThe city was under siege for several months.\n(這座城市被圍困了好幾個月。)\nThe army laid siege to the castle.\n(軍隊圍攻了城堡。)"],["skeleton","skeleton(n.)骨骼、骨架、骨幹\nskeletal(adj.)骨骼的\nhuman skeleton 人體骨骼\nskeleton staff 最基本人手\nThe museum displays the skeleton of a huge dinosaur.\n(博物館展示著一具巨大恐龍的骨骼。)\nOnly a skeleton staff works during the Lunar New Year holiday.\n(農曆年假期間只有最基本的人手上班。)"],["skull","skull(n.)頭骨、頭蓋骨\n(無詞性變化)\nfractured skull 頭骨骨折\nskull and crossbones 骷髏頭標誌\nA helmet protects your skull in an accident.\n(安全帽能在意外中保護你的頭骨。)\nThe pirate flag showed a skull and crossbones.\n(海盜旗上畫著骷髏頭和交叉骨頭。)"],["slam","slam(n./v.)猛關、猛擊、砰的一聲、抨擊\n(無詞性變化)\nslam the door 砰地關上門\nslam on the brakes 猛踩煞車\nShe slammed the door and ran upstairs.\n(她砰地關上門跑上樓。)\nThe driver slammed on the brakes to avoid hitting the dog.\n(司機猛踩煞車以免撞到狗。)"],["slap","slap(n./v./adv.)摑、拍打、恰好地\n(無詞性變化)\na slap in the face 一記耳光、侮辱\nslap on the back 拍背(表示鼓勵)\nBeing ignored by the judges felt like a slap in the face.\n(被評審忽視讓人覺得像挨了一記耳光。)\nHe slapped his friend on the back and congratulated him.\n(他拍拍朋友的背向他道賀。)"],["slavery","slavery(n.)奴隸制度、奴役\nslave(n.)奴隸\nabolish slavery 廢除奴隸制度\nmodern slavery 現代奴役\nSlavery was abolished in the United States in 1865.\n(美國在一八六五年廢除了奴隸制度。)\nMillions of people still live in conditions of modern slavery.\n(仍有數百萬人生活在現代奴役的處境中。)"],["slot","slot(n./v.)投幣口、狹縫、時段、插入\n(無詞性變化)\ntime slot 時段\nslot machine 吃角子老虎機\nInsert a coin into the slot to start the machine.\n(把硬幣投進投幣口啟動機器。)\nThe show was moved to a later time slot.\n(這個節目被移到較晚的時段。)"],["smash","smash(v./n.)打碎、猛擊、轟動的成功\nsmashing(adj.)極好的\nsmash into 猛撞上\nsmash hit 大受歡迎的作品\nThe car smashed into a tree on the icy road.\n(車子在結冰的路上猛然撞上一棵樹。)\nThe movie was a smash hit around the world.\n(這部電影在全世界大賣。)"],["smog","smog(n.)霧霾、煙霧\nsmoggy(adj.)煙霧瀰漫的\nheavy smog 嚴重霧霾\nsmog alert 霧霾警報\nHeavy smog covered the city for days.\n(嚴重的霧霾籠罩城市好幾天。)\nCar exhaust is a major cause of smog.\n(汽車廢氣是造成霧霾的主因之一。)"],["snatch","snatch(v./n.)搶奪、抓住、片段\n(無詞性變化)\nsnatch away 奪走\nbag snatching 搶皮包\nA thief snatched her purse and ran away.\n(一名小偷搶了她的錢包就跑。)\nI only heard snatches of their conversation.\n(我只聽到他們談話的片段。)"],["sneak","sneak(v./n.)偷偷溜走、偷偷做、鬼鬼祟祟的人\nsneaky(adj.)鬼鬼祟祟的\nsneak out 偷溜出去\nsneak peek 搶先看\nHe tried to sneak out of the house after midnight.\n(他半夜過後試圖偷偷溜出家門。)\nThe studio released a sneak peek of the new movie.\n(片商釋出了新電影的搶先看片段。)"],["sniff","sniff(v./n.)嗅、聞、抽鼻子\n(無詞性變化)\nsniff around 四處嗅、打探\ntake a sniff 聞一下\nThe dog sniffed the ground looking for food.\n(那隻狗在地上嗅來嗅去尋找食物。)\nShe took a sniff of the milk to see if it had gone bad.\n(她聞了一下牛奶，看看是否壞掉了。)"],["soak","soak(v./n.)浸泡、濕透、浸泡\nsoaking(adj.)濕透的\nsoak up 吸收\nget soaked 全身濕透\nSoak the beans in water overnight before cooking.\n(煮之前先把豆子泡水一晚。)\nWe got soaked on the way home without an umbrella.\n(我們沒帶傘，回家路上全身濕透。)"],["soar","soar(v.)高飛、猛增、高聳\n(無詞性變化)\nsoaring prices 飛漲的物價\nsoar into the sky 衝上天空\nAn eagle soared high above the valley.\n(一隻老鷹在山谷上空高飛。)\nHousing prices have soared in the past ten years.\n(過去十年房價飆漲。)"],["sob","sob(n./v.)啜泣、嗚咽\n(無詞性變化)\nsob story 博取同情的故事\nsob one's heart out 哭得肝腸寸斷\nThe little girl sobbed when she lost her puppy.\n(小女孩弄丟小狗時啜泣不已。)\nI heard quiet sobs coming from the next room.\n(我聽見隔壁房間傳來輕輕的啜泣聲。)"],["sober","sober(adj./v.)清醒的、未喝醉的、嚴肅的、使清醒\nsobriety(n.)清醒、節制\nstay sober 保持清醒\nsober up 醒酒\nMake sure the driver stays sober tonight.\n(確保今晚開車的人保持清醒。)\nThe news had a sobering effect on everyone in the room.\n(這個消息讓在場的每個人都冷靜下來。)"],["soften","soften(v.)使變軟、使緩和\nsoft(adj.)軟的\nsoften the blow 減輕打擊\nsoften one's tone 放軟語氣\nLeave the butter out to soften before baking.\n(烘焙前先把奶油放在室溫軟化。)\nShe softened her tone when she saw he was upset.\n(看到他難過，她放軟了語氣。)"],["sole","sole(adj./n./v.)唯一的、獨占的、鞋底、腳底、換鞋底\nsolely(adv.)唯一地、僅僅\nsole purpose 唯一目的\nsole survivor 唯一倖存者\nShe was the sole survivor of the plane crash.\n(她是那起空難的唯一倖存者。)\nThe soles of my shoes are worn out.\n(我的鞋底磨壞了。)"],["solo","solo(n./adv./adj.)獨奏、獨唱、單獨地、單獨的\nsoloist(n.)獨奏者\nsolo performance 獨奏\ngo solo 單飛、獨自進行\nShe played a beautiful piano solo at the concert.\n(她在音樂會上演奏了一首優美的鋼琴獨奏。)\nHe traveled solo around Europe for a month.\n(他獨自在歐洲旅行了一個月。)"],["sophisticated","sophisticated(adj.)精密的、複雜的、世故的、有品味的\nsophistication(n.)精緻、老練\nsophisticated technology 精密的科技\nsophisticated taste 高雅的品味\nModern cars are equipped with sophisticated computer systems.\n(現代汽車配備精密的電腦系統。)\nShe has a sophisticated taste in music and art.\n(她在音樂和藝術方面品味高雅。)"],["sophomore","sophomore(n.)(大學或高中)二年級學生\n(無詞性變化)\nsophomore year 二年級\ncollege sophomore 大二學生\nMy brother is a sophomore at National Taiwan University.\n(我哥哥是台大二年級學生。)\nHer sophomore year was much busier than her first.\n(她二年級比一年級忙得多。)"],["souvenir","souvenir(n.)紀念品\n(無詞性變化)\nsouvenir shop 紀念品店\nbuy souvenirs 買紀念品\nI bought some pineapple cakes as souvenirs for my friends.\n(我買了一些鳳梨酥當作送朋友的紀念品。)\nThe souvenir shop sells postcards and key chains.\n(那間紀念品店販售明信片和鑰匙圈。)"],["sovereignty","sovereignty(n.)主權、統治權\nsovereign(adj./n.)擁有主權的、君主\nnational sovereignty 國家主權\nclaim sovereignty 宣稱主權\nEvery nation has the right to protect its sovereignty.\n(每個國家都有權捍衛自己的主權。)\nSeveral countries claim sovereignty over the islands.\n(好幾個國家宣稱擁有這些島嶼的主權。)"],["sow","sow(v.)播種、散布\n(無詞性變化)\nsow seeds 播種\nsow doubt 散播懷疑\nFarmers sow rice seeds in early spring.\n(農夫在早春播下稻種。)\nHis comments sowed doubt in the minds of voters.\n(他的言論在選民心中種下懷疑。)"],["spacious","spacious(adj.)寬敞的\nspace(n.)空間\nspacious room 寬敞的房間\nspacious apartment 寬敞的公寓\nThe new library has a bright and spacious reading room.\n(新圖書館有一間明亮寬敞的閱覽室。)\nThey moved into a spacious apartment near the park.\n(他們搬進公園附近一間寬敞的公寓。)"],["sparkle","sparkle(v./n.)閃耀、發光、活力\nsparkling(adj.)閃閃發光的、氣泡的\nsparkling water 氣泡水\neyes sparkle 眼睛閃閃發亮\nHer eyes sparkled with excitement when she opened the gift.\n(她打開禮物時，眼睛興奮得閃閃發亮。)\nThe lake sparkled in the morning sunlight.\n(湖面在晨光中波光粼粼。)"],["specialist","specialist(n.)專家、專科醫生\nspecial(adj.)特別的\nspecialize(v.)專攻\nheart specialist 心臟科醫生\nspecialist in 在…方面的專家\nThe doctor referred him to a heart specialist.\n(醫生把他轉介給心臟科專科醫師。)\nShe is a specialist in early childhood education.\n(她是幼兒教育方面的專家。)"],["specialize","specialize(v.)專攻、專門從事\nspecialization(n.)專門化、專業\nspecialized(adj.)專門的\nspecialize in 專攻\nspecialized knowledge 專門知識\nThis restaurant specializes in seafood.\n(這家餐廳專賣海鮮。)\nShe plans to specialize in computer science in college.\n(她打算在大學專攻資訊科學。)"],["specialty","specialty(n.)專長、特產、招牌菜\nspecial(adj.)特別的\nlocal specialty 當地特產\nhouse specialty 招牌菜\nSun cakes are a local specialty of Taichung.\n(太陽餅是台中的地方特產。)\nMath is not my specialty, but I'll try my best.\n(數學不是我的專長，但我會盡力。)"],["specify","specify(v.)具體指定、詳細說明\nspecific(adj.)具體的、特定的\nspecification(n.)規格、說明\nspecify a date 指定日期\nunless otherwise specified 除非另有規定\nPlease specify your size when you place the order.\n(下訂單時請註明您的尺寸。)\nThe rules do not specify how long the speech should be.\n(規則沒有明確指定演講應該多長。)"],["specimen","specimen(n.)樣本、標本\n(無詞性變化)\nblood specimen 血液樣本\ncollect specimens 採集標本\nThe scientist collected insect specimens in the rainforest.\n(科學家在雨林採集昆蟲標本。)\nThe nurse took a blood specimen for testing.\n(護理師抽了血液樣本送去檢驗。)"],["spectacular","spectacular(adj./n.)壯觀的、驚人的、精采的表演\nspectacle(n.)奇觀、壯觀的場面\nspectacularly(adv.)壯觀地\nspectacular view 壯觀的景色\nspectacular success 驚人的成功\nThe fireworks over Taipei 101 were absolutely spectacular.\n(台北101的煙火真是壯觀極了。)\nThe team made a spectacular comeback in the last five minutes.\n(那支球隊在最後五分鐘上演驚人的逆轉。)"],["spectator","spectator(n.)觀眾、旁觀者\nspectate(v.)觀看\nspectator sport 觀賞性運動\nthousands of spectators 數千名觀眾\nThousands of spectators cheered as the runners crossed the finish line.\n(跑者衝過終點線時，數千名觀眾歡呼。)\nBaseball is a popular spectator sport in Taiwan.\n(棒球在台灣是受歡迎的觀賞性運動。)"],["spectrum","spectrum(n.)光譜、範圍、系列\n(無詞性變化)\na wide spectrum of 廣泛的…\npolitical spectrum 政治光譜\nThe survey covered a wide spectrum of opinions.\n(這份調查涵蓋了廣泛的意見。)\nA rainbow shows all the colors of the light spectrum.\n(彩虹呈現出光譜中所有的顏色。)"],["speculate","speculate(v.)推測、猜測、投機\nspeculation(n.)推測、投機\nspeculative(adj.)推測的、投機的\nspeculate about 對…推測\nspeculate on the stock market 炒股\nFans speculated about who would be the new team captain.\n(球迷們猜測誰會是新任隊長。)\nIt's too early to speculate on the cause of the fire.\n(現在推測火災的原因還太早。)"],["sphere","sphere(n.)球體、領域、範圍\nspherical(adj.)球形的\nsphere of influence 勢力範圍\npublic sphere 公共領域\nThe Earth is not a perfect sphere.\n(地球並不是完美的球體。)\nWomen have made great progress in the political sphere.\n(女性在政治領域有了很大的進展。)"],["spicy","spicy(adj.)辣的、加香料的\nspice(n.)香料\nspicy food 辣的食物\nspicy hot pot 麻辣鍋\nI can't eat spicy food, so I ordered the mild one.\n(我不能吃辣，所以點了小辣的。)\nSpicy hot pot is especially popular in winter.\n(麻辣鍋在冬天特別受歡迎。)"],["spine","spine(n.)脊椎、書脊、骨氣\nspinal(adj.)脊椎的\nspinal cord 脊髓\nsend chills down one's spine 令人不寒而慄\nSitting with poor posture can hurt your spine.\n(坐姿不良會傷害你的脊椎。)\nThe title is printed on the spine of the book.\n(書名印在書脊上。)"],["sponge","sponge(n./v.)海綿、用海綿擦、白吃白喝\nspongy(adj.)像海綿的、鬆軟的\nsponge cake 海綿蛋糕\nsponge off 依賴…過活\nShe wiped the table with a wet sponge.\n(她用濕海綿擦桌子。)\nHe is too old to keep sponging off his parents.\n(他年紀太大了，不該再靠父母過活。)"],["sponsor","sponsor(n./v.)贊助者、贊助、主辦\nsponsorship(n.)贊助\nmain sponsor 主要贊助商\nsponsor an event 贊助活動\nThe concert was sponsored by a local bank.\n(這場音樂會由一家地方銀行贊助。)\nThe team is looking for a new sponsor for next season.\n(這支隊伍正在為下一季尋找新的贊助商。)"],["sponsorship","sponsorship(n.)贊助、資助\nsponsor(n./v.)贊助者、贊助\ncorporate sponsorship 企業贊助\nseek sponsorship 尋求贊助\nThe school festival relies heavily on corporate sponsorship.\n(校慶活動很大程度依賴企業贊助。)\nThe athlete signed a sponsorship deal with a sports brand.\n(那位運動員和一家運動品牌簽了贊助合約。)"],["spouse","spouse(n.)配偶\nspousal(adj.)配偶的\nspouse and children 配偶與子女\nsurviving spouse 在世的配偶\nEmployees may bring their spouses to the company dinner.\n(員工可以攜配偶參加公司晚宴。)\nPlease write your spouse's name on the form.\n(請在表格上填寫配偶的姓名。)"],["squad","squad(n.)小隊、班、運動隊伍\n(無詞性變化)\nrescue squad 救援隊\nnational squad 國家隊\nThe rescue squad arrived within ten minutes.\n(救援隊在十分鐘內抵達。)\nHe was selected for the national squad at nineteen.\n(他十九歲時就入選國家隊。)"],["squash","squash(n./v.)南瓜類、壁球、壓扁\n(無詞性變化)\nplay squash 打壁球\nsquash into 擠進\nDon't put the eggs at the bottom or they'll get squashed.\n(別把蛋放在底下，否則會被壓扁。)\nTen of us squashed into the small elevator.\n(我們十個人擠進那部小電梯。)"],["squat","squat(adj./n./v.)矮胖的、蹲、深蹲、擅自占用\n(無詞性變化)\ndo squats 做深蹲\nsquat down 蹲下\nShe squatted down to talk to the little boy.\n(她蹲下來和那個小男孩說話。)\nDoing squats every day helps strengthen your legs.\n(每天做深蹲有助於強化腿部肌肉。)"],["stability","stability(n.)穩定、穩定性\nstable(adj.)穩定的\nstabilize(v.)使穩定\neconomic stability 經濟穩定\npolitical stability 政治穩定\nPolitical stability is important for economic growth.\n(政治穩定對經濟成長很重要。)\nChildren need a sense of stability in their lives.\n(孩子們的生活中需要安定感。)"],["stack","stack(n./v.)一疊、一堆、堆疊\n(無詞性變化)\na stack of 一疊…\nstack up 堆疊、累積\nThere is a stack of exam papers on the teacher's desk.\n(老師的桌上有一疊考卷。)\nPlease stack the chairs after the meeting.\n(會議結束後請把椅子疊起來。)"],["stain","stain(n./v.)汙漬、汙點、弄髒、染色\nstainless(adj.)不鏽的、無瑕的\ncoffee stain 咖啡漬\nstainless steel 不鏽鋼\nI spilled coffee and left a stain on my white shirt.\n(我打翻咖啡，在白襯衫上留下了汙漬。)\nThe scandal stained his reputation forever.\n(那樁醜聞永遠玷汙了他的名聲。)"],["stake","stake(n./v.)樁、利害關係、賭注、以…打賭\nstakeholder(n.)利害關係人\nat stake 處於危險中、攸關\nstake one's life on 以性命擔保\nWith the championship at stake, the players were under great pressure.\n(冠軍頭銜攸關，球員們承受很大的壓力。)\nI'd stake my reputation on his honesty.\n(我願以我的名譽擔保他的誠實。)"],["stall","stall(n./v.)攤位、熄火、拖延\n(無詞性變化)\nfood stall 小吃攤\nstall for time 拖延時間\nWe bought fried chicken from a stall at the night market.\n(我們在夜市的攤位買了炸雞。)\nThe car stalled in the middle of the road.\n(車子在路中間熄火了。)"],["stance","stance(n.)立場、態度、站姿\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a stance 表明立場\nfirm stance 堅定的立場\nThe government took a firm stance against drunk driving.\n(政府對酒駕採取堅定的立場。)\nThe golfer adjusted his stance before hitting the ball.\n(那位高爾夫球手在擊球前調整了站姿。)"],["startle","startle(v.)使驚嚇、使吃驚\nstartling(adj.)驚人的\nbe startled by 被…嚇一跳\nstartling discovery 驚人的發現\nI was startled by a loud knock on the door.\n(我被一陣很大的敲門聲嚇了一跳。)\nThe scientists made a startling discovery in the deep sea.\n(科學家在深海有了驚人的發現。)"],["statistical","statistical(adj.)統計的、統計學的\nstatistics(n.)統計數據、統計學\nstatistically(adv.)統計上\nstatistical data 統計資料\nstatistical analysis 統計分析\nThe report is based on statistical data from the past decade.\n(這份報告是根據過去十年的統計資料。)\nThere is no statistical difference between the two groups.\n(這兩組之間沒有統計上的差異。)"],["steer","steer(v./n.)駕駛、操縱、引導\nsteering wheel(n.)方向盤\nsteer clear of 避開\nsteer the conversation 引導話題\nShe steered the boat carefully through the rocks.\n(她小心地駕船穿過礁石。)\nYou should steer clear of strangers online who ask for money.\n(你應該避開網路上向你要錢的陌生人。)"],["stereotype","stereotype(n./v.)刻板印象、對…有刻板印象\nstereotypical(adj.)刻板的、典型的\ngender stereotype 性別刻板印象\nbreak stereotypes 打破刻板印象\nIt's a stereotype that boys are better at math than girls.\n(男生數學比女生好是一種刻板印象。)\nShe hopes to break stereotypes about female engineers.\n(她希望打破大家對女性工程師的刻板印象。)"],["stew","stew(n./v.)燉菜、燉、焦慮\n(無詞性變化)\nbeef stew 燉牛肉\nstew in one's own juice 自作自受\nMom made a pot of beef stew for dinner.\n(媽媽晚餐煮了一鍋燉牛肉。)\nStew the vegetables slowly over low heat.\n(用小火慢慢燉蔬菜。)"],["stimulate","stimulate(v.)刺激、激勵、促進\nstimulation(n.)刺激、激勵\nstimulus(n.)刺激物、激勵\nstimulate the economy 刺激經濟\nstimulate interest 激發興趣\nThe government cut taxes to stimulate the economy.\n(政府減稅以刺激經濟。)\nGood teachers know how to stimulate students' curiosity.\n(好老師懂得如何激發學生的好奇心。)"],["stimulus","stimulus(n.)刺激、刺激物、促進因素\nstimulate(v.)刺激\nstimulus package 經濟振興方案\nrespond to a stimulus 對刺激有反應\nThe eye responds to light as a stimulus.\n(眼睛會對光這種刺激產生反應。)\nThe government announced a large economic stimulus package.\n(政府宣布了大規模的經濟振興方案。)"],["stink","stink(n./v.)臭味、發臭、很糟\nstinky(adj.)臭的\nstinky tofu 臭豆腐\nstink of 發出…的臭味\nThe garbage in the kitchen stinks.\n(廚房裡的垃圾好臭。)\nStinky tofu smells terrible but tastes great.\n(臭豆腐聞起來很臭，但吃起來很美味。)"],["stock","stock(n.)存貨、股票、儲備\nstockholder(n.)股東\nin stock 有庫存\nstock market 股票市場\nSorry, this size is not in stock right now.\n(抱歉，這個尺寸目前沒有庫存。)\nHe lost a lot of money in the stock market.\n(他在股市賠了很多錢。)"],["storage","storage(n.)儲藏、儲存空間、倉庫\nstore(v.)儲存\nstorage space 儲存空間\ncloud storage 雲端儲存\nMy phone is running out of storage space.\n(我的手機儲存空間快不夠了。)\nWe keep old furniture in a storage room downstairs.\n(我們把舊家具放在樓下的儲藏室。)"],["straighten","straighten(v.)弄直、整理、改正\nstraight(adj./adv.)直的、直接地\nstraighten up 整理、坐直\nstraighten out 解決、理清\nPlease straighten up your room before the guests arrive.\n(客人來之前請把你的房間整理好。)\nShe straightened her hair before the party.\n(她在派對前把頭髮拉直。)"],["straightforward","straightforward(adj.)簡單明瞭的、坦率的\n(無詞性變化)\nstraightforward answer 直截了當的回答\nfairly straightforward 相當簡單\nThe instructions are clear and straightforward.\n(說明清楚又簡單明瞭。)\nHe is a straightforward person who always says what he thinks.\n(他是個坦率的人，總是有話直說。)"],["strain","strain(n./v.)壓力、拉傷、使緊張、過度使用\nstrained(adj.)緊張的、勉強的\neye strain 眼睛疲勞\nunder strain 承受壓力\nStaring at screens for hours can cause eye strain.\n(長時間盯著螢幕可能造成眼睛疲勞。)\nHe strained a muscle in his back while moving the desk.\n(他搬桌子時拉傷了背部肌肉。)"],["strand","strand(v./n.)使擱淺、使困住、一縷、一股\nstranded(adj.)被困住的\nbe stranded 被困住\na strand of hair 一縷頭髮\nHundreds of passengers were stranded at the airport by the typhoon.\n(數百名旅客因颱風受困機場。)\nShe brushed a strand of hair from her face.\n(她撥開臉上的一縷頭髮。)"],["strap","strap(n./v.)帶子、皮帶、用帶子綁住\n(無詞性變化)\nshoulder strap 肩帶\nstrap in 繫好安全帶\nThe strap of my backpack broke on the way to school.\n(我的背包肩帶在上學途中斷了。)\nMake sure the baby is strapped into the car seat.\n(確認寶寶已經被繫好在汽車安全座椅上。)"],["strategic","strategic(adj.)戰略的、策略上的\nstrategy(n.)策略\nstrategically(adv.)策略性地\nstrategic plan 策略計畫\nstrategic location 戰略位置\nTaiwan is in a strategic location in East Asia.\n(台灣位於東亞的戰略位置。)\nThe company made a strategic decision to focus on online sales.\n(公司做出策略性決定，專注於網路銷售。)"],["striking","striking(adj.)顯著的、引人注目的\nstrike(v.)打擊、使突然想到\nstrikingly(adv.)顯著地\nstriking contrast 鮮明的對比\nstriking similarity 驚人的相似\nThere is a striking contrast between the old town and the new city.\n(舊城區和新市區之間形成鮮明的對比。)\nShe is a woman of striking beauty.\n(她是位美貌出眾的女子。)"],["structural","structural(adj.)結構的、構造上的\nstructure(n.)結構\nstructurally(adv.)結構上\nstructural damage 結構損壞\nstructural engineer 結構工程師\nThe earthquake caused serious structural damage to the building.\n(地震對這棟建築造成了嚴重的結構損壞。)\nThe plan requires major structural changes to the school system.\n(這項計畫需要對學校制度進行重大的結構性改變。)"],["stumble","stumble(v./n.)絆倒、踉蹌、結巴、偶然發現\n(無詞性變化)\nstumble upon 偶然發現\nstumble over 被…絆倒、說話結巴\nI stumbled upon an interesting café while walking in the alley.\n(我在巷子裡散步時偶然發現一間有趣的咖啡館。)\nHe stumbled over a rock and almost fell.\n(他被石頭絆到，差點跌倒。)"],["sturdy","sturdy(adj.)堅固的、結實的、健壯的\nsturdily(adv.)堅固地\nsturdy shoes 耐穿的鞋子\nsturdy table 堅固的桌子\nWear sturdy shoes when you go hiking in the mountains.\n(去山上健行時要穿耐穿的鞋子。)\nThis sturdy old desk has lasted for fifty years.\n(這張堅固的舊書桌已經用了五十年。)"],["submit","submit(v.)提交、呈遞、屈服\nsubmission(n.)提交、屈服\nsubmit an application 提交申請\nsubmit to 屈服於、服從\nPlease submit your report by Friday.\n(請在星期五之前提交你的報告。)\nThey refused to submit to the unfair rules.\n(他們拒絕服從不公平的規定。)"],["subsequent","subsequent(adj.)隨後的、後來的\nsubsequently(adv.)隨後、後來\nsubsequent events 隨後發生的事\nsubsequent years 後來的幾年\nThe first test was easy, but subsequent ones were much harder.\n(第一次考試很簡單，但之後幾次就難多了。)\nHe was injured and subsequently missed the whole season.\n(他受了傷，隨後缺席了整個球季。)"],["subsidy","subsidy(n.)補助金、津貼\nsubsidize(v.)補助、資助\ngovernment subsidy 政府補助\nhousing subsidy 住房補貼\nFarmers receive government subsidies to grow certain crops.\n(農民種植某些作物可獲得政府補助。)\nThe city offers a subsidy for buying electric scooters.\n(市政府提供購買電動機車的補助。)"],["substantial","substantial(adj.)大量的、重大的、實質的\nsubstance(n.)物質、實質\nsubstantially(adv.)大幅地\nsubstantial amount 大量\nsubstantial progress 重大進展\nThe company spent a substantial amount of money on research.\n(這家公司在研究上花了大筆資金。)\nShe has made substantial progress in her English writing.\n(她的英文寫作有了大幅進步。)"],["substitute","substitute(n./v.)代替品、代替者、代替\nsubstitution(n.)代替、替換\nsubstitute teacher 代課老師\nsubstitute A for B 用A代替B\nWe had a substitute teacher because Ms. Lin was sick.\n(因為林老師生病，我們有一位代課老師。)\nYou can substitute honey for sugar in this recipe.\n(這個食譜中你可以用蜂蜜代替糖。)"],["subtle","subtle(adj.)微妙的、細微的、不明顯的\nsubtlety(n.)微妙、細微之處\nsubtly(adv.)微妙地\nsubtle difference 細微的差別\nsubtle hint 委婉的暗示\nThere is a subtle difference between these two colors.\n(這兩種顏色之間有細微的差別。)\nShe gave me a subtle hint that it was time to leave.\n(她委婉地暗示我該離開了。)"],["suburban","suburban(adj.)郊區的\nsuburb(n.)郊區\nsuburban area 郊區\nsuburban life 郊區生活\nMany families move to suburban areas for cheaper housing.\n(許多家庭為了較便宜的房子搬到郊區。)\nShe enjoys the quiet pace of suburban life.\n(她喜歡郊區生活寧靜的步調。)"],["successor","successor(n.)繼承者、接班人、後繼者\nsucceed(v.)繼承、接替\nsuccession(n.)繼承、連續\nsuccessor to 繼任者\nchoose a successor 選擇接班人\nThe CEO has not yet chosen his successor.\n(執行長尚未選定他的接班人。)\nThis model is the successor to last year's popular phone.\n(這款機型是去年熱門手機的後繼機種。)"],["suite","suite(n.)套房、一套、組曲\n(無詞性變化)\nhotel suite 飯店套房\nsoftware suite 套裝軟體\nThey stayed in a luxury suite on the top floor.\n(他們住在頂樓的豪華套房。)\nThe orchestra played a suite by Tchaikovsky.\n(管弦樂團演奏了柴可夫斯基的一組組曲。)"],["superb","superb(adj.)極好的、一流的\nsuperbly(adv.)極好地\nsuperb performance 精湛的表演\nsuperb quality 品質一流\nThe pianist gave a superb performance last night.\n(那位鋼琴家昨晚的演出非常精湛。)\nThe hotel offers superb views of the ocean.\n(這間飯店可以欣賞絕佳的海景。)"],["superstition","superstition(n.)迷信\nsuperstitious(adj.)迷信的\nold superstition 古老的迷信\nbelieve in superstition 相信迷信\nAccording to an old superstition, breaking a mirror brings bad luck.\n(根據古老的迷信，打破鏡子會帶來厄運。)\nMy grandmother is very superstitious about the number four.\n(我奶奶對數字四非常迷信。)"],["supervise","supervise(v.)監督、管理、指導\nsupervision(n.)監督\nsupervisor(n.)主管、指導者\nsupervise students 監督學生\nclosely supervise 嚴密監督\nTeachers take turns supervising students during lunch.\n(老師們輪流在午餐時間監督學生。)\nYoung children should be closely supervised near water.\n(在水邊應嚴密看顧幼童。)"],["supervision","supervision(n.)監督、管理、指導\nsupervise(v.)監督\nunder supervision 在監督之下\nadult supervision 大人陪同監督\nChildren under 12 must swim under adult supervision.\n(十二歲以下孩童必須在大人陪同下游泳。)\nThe project was completed under the supervision of Professor Chen.\n(這項計畫在陳教授的指導下完成。)"],["supervisor","supervisor(n.)主管、監督者、指導教授\nsupervise(v.)監督\nsupervisory(adj.)監督的\ndirect supervisor 直屬上司\nreport to a supervisor 向主管報告\nAsk your supervisor if you can leave early.\n(問問你的主管是否可以提早離開。)\nMy thesis supervisor gave me very helpful advice.\n(我的論文指導教授給了我非常有幫助的建議。)"],["supposedly","supposedly(adv.)據說、應該是\nsuppose(v.)猜想、假定\nsupposed(adj.)所謂的、應該的\nsupposedly true 據稱屬實\nsupposedly the best 號稱最好的\nThis restaurant is supposedly the best in town.\n(這家餐廳號稱是鎮上最好的。)\nThe package was supposedly sent last week, but it hasn't arrived.\n(包裹據說上週就寄出了，但還沒到。)"],["supreme","supreme(adj.)最高的、至高無上的、極度的\nsupremacy(n.)至高無上、優勢\nSupreme Court 最高法院\nsupreme effort 最大的努力\nThe case was finally decided by the Supreme Court.\n(這個案件最後由最高法院判決。)\nShe made a supreme effort to finish the marathon.\n(她竭盡全力跑完了馬拉松。)"],["surplus","surplus(n./adj.)過剩、盈餘、過剩的\n(無詞性變化)\ntrade surplus 貿易順差\nbudget surplus 預算盈餘\nThe country has a large trade surplus with the United States.\n(這個國家對美國有大量貿易順差。)\nSurplus food from the event was given to a local shelter.\n(活動剩餘的食物被捐給當地的收容所。)"],["surveillance","surveillance(n.)監視、監控\n(無詞性變化)\nsurveillance camera 監視器\nunder surveillance 受到監視\nSurveillance cameras recorded the thief entering the store.\n(監視器拍到小偷進入商店。)\nThe suspect has been under police surveillance for weeks.\n(那名嫌犯已遭警方監視好幾週。)"],["suspend","suspend(v.)暫停、使停學(職)、懸掛\nsuspension(n.)暫停、停學、懸吊\nsuspended(adj.)懸掛的、暫停的\nbe suspended from school 被停學\nsuspend service 暫停服務\nTrain service was suspended because of the typhoon.\n(因為颱風，火車停駛。)\nHe was suspended from school for three days for fighting.\n(他因打架被停學三天。)"],["sustain","sustain(v.)維持、支撐、遭受\nsustainable(adj.)可持續的\nsustain growth 維持成長\nsustain injuries 受傷\nIt is hard to sustain your energy without enough sleep.\n(睡眠不足很難維持精力。)\nThe driver sustained serious injuries in the crash.\n(那名駕駛在車禍中受了重傷。)"],["sustainable","sustainable(adj.)可持續的、永續的\nsustainability(n.)永續性\nsustain(v.)維持\nsustainable development 永續發展\nsustainable energy 永續能源\nOur school promotes sustainable development by reducing plastic use.\n(我們學校以減少塑膠使用來推動永續發展。)\nSolar power is a clean and sustainable energy source.\n(太陽能是一種乾淨且可永續的能源。)"],["swap","swap(v./n.)交換、交換物\n(無詞性變化)\nswap seats 換座位\nswap places 交換位置\nWould you mind swapping seats with me?\n(你介意和我換座位嗎？)\nWe held a book swap at school to share our old books.\n(我們在學校舉辦換書活動來分享舊書。)"],["symbolic","symbolic(adj.)象徵的、象徵性的\nsymbol(n.)象徵、符號\nsymbolize(v.)象徵\nsymbolic meaning 象徵意義\nsymbolic gesture 象徵性的舉動\nThe white dove is symbolic of peace.\n(白鴿象徵和平。)\nPlanting a tree was a symbolic gesture of hope for the future.\n(種樹是對未來懷抱希望的象徵性舉動。)"],["symptom","symptom(n.)症狀、徵兆\nsymptomatic(adj.)有症狀的、徵兆的\ncommon symptom 常見症狀\nshow symptoms 出現症狀\nFever and coughing are common symptoms of the flu.\n(發燒和咳嗽是流感的常見症狀。)\nRising crime may be a symptom of deeper social problems.\n(犯罪增加可能是更深層社會問題的徵兆。)"],["syndrome","syndrome(n.)症候群、典型表現\n(無詞性變化)\nDown syndrome 唐氏症\njet lag syndrome 時差症候群\nMany students suffer from Monday morning syndrome.\n(許多學生都有星期一早上症候群。)\nHe was diagnosed with a rare genetic syndrome.\n(他被診斷出罹患一種罕見的遺傳症候群。)"],["tackle","tackle(v.)處理、應付、擒抱\n(無詞性變化)\ntackle a problem 處理問題\ntackle climate change 對付氣候變遷\nThe government must tackle the problem of rising housing prices.\n(政府必須處理房價上漲的問題。)\nThe defender tackled the player and took the ball.\n(後衛擒抱那名球員並搶下了球。)"],["tactic(s)","tactic(n.)戰術、策略、tactics(n.)策略、手段(常用複數)\ntactical(adj.)戰術上的\nscare tactics 恐嚇手段\nchange tactics 改變策略\nThe coach changed tactics in the second half of the game.\n(教練在下半場改變了戰術。)\nDelaying the meeting was just a tactic to avoid the question.\n(延後會議只是迴避問題的手段。)"],["tangle","tangle(n./v.)糾結、混亂、使糾纏\ntangled(adj.)糾結的、複雜的\nin a tangle 糾結在一起、一團亂\ntangle with 與…爭吵\nMy headphone cords are always in a tangle.\n(我的耳機線總是纏成一團。)\nThe kitten got tangled in a ball of yarn.\n(小貓被一團毛線纏住了。)"],["tempt","tempt(v.)引誘、吸引、使想要\ntemptation(n.)誘惑\ntempting(adj.)誘人的\nbe tempted to 很想…\ntempting offer 誘人的提議\nI was tempted to skip class and go to the beach.\n(我很想翹課去海邊。)\nThe smell of fresh bread tempted me into the bakery.\n(新鮮麵包的香味吸引我走進麵包店。)"],["temptation","temptation(n.)誘惑、誘惑物\ntempt(v.)引誘\nresist temptation 抵抗誘惑\ngive in to temptation 屈服於誘惑\nIt's hard to resist the temptation of fried chicken late at night.\n(深夜很難抗拒炸雞的誘惑。)\nSmartphones are a big temptation for students during class.\n(智慧型手機對上課中的學生是很大的誘惑。)"],["terminal","terminal(n./adj.)航廈、終點站、末期的、終端的\nterminate(v.)終止\nairport terminal 機場航廈\nterminal illness 絕症、末期疾病\nOur flight leaves from Terminal 2.\n(我們的班機從第二航廈出發。)\nThe patient was told that his cancer was terminal.\n(那位病人被告知他的癌症已是末期。)"],["terrify","terrify(v.)使驚恐、使害怕\nterrified(adj.)感到驚恐的\nterrifying(adj.)令人驚恐的\nbe terrified of 非常害怕…\nterrifying experience 可怕的經歷\nLoud thunder terrifies my little dog.\n(巨大的雷聲讓我的小狗嚇壞了。)\nShe is terrified of speaking in front of large crowds.\n(她非常害怕在一大群人面前說話。)"],["testify","testify(v.)作證、證明\ntestimony(n.)證詞、證明\ntestify against 作證指控\ntestify to 證明\nThe witness agreed to testify against the suspect in court.\n(證人同意出庭作證指控嫌犯。)\nHer success testifies to years of hard work.\n(她的成功證明了多年的努力。)"],["texture","texture(n./v.)質地、口感、使具有紋理\ntextured(adj.)有紋理的\nsmooth texture 滑順的質地\nchewy texture 有嚼勁的口感\nTaiwanese people love the chewy texture of tapioca pearls.\n(台灣人喜愛粉圓有嚼勁的口感。)\nThis fabric has a soft and smooth texture.\n(這塊布料的質地柔軟滑順。)"],["theft","theft(n.)竊盜、偷竊\nthief(n.)小偷\nidentity theft 身分盜用\ncar theft 汽車竊盜\nIdentity theft is becoming more common online.\n(網路上的身分盜用越來越常見。)\nHe reported the theft of his bicycle to the police.\n(他向警方報案說腳踏車被偷了。)"],["theology","theology(n.)神學\ntheological(adj.)神學的\ntheologian(n.)神學家\nstudy theology 研讀神學\nChristian theology 基督教神學\nHe went to seminary to study theology.\n(他去神學院研讀神學。)\nThe professor wrote several books on Christian theology.\n(那位教授寫了好幾本關於基督教神學的書。)"],["theoretical","theoretical(adj.)理論上的、理論的\ntheory(n.)理論\ntheoretically(adv.)理論上\ntheoretical knowledge 理論知識\ntheoretical physics 理論物理學\nStudents need both theoretical knowledge and practical skills.\n(學生需要理論知識，也需要實作技能。)\nTime travel is only a theoretical possibility.\n(時光旅行只是一種理論上的可能。)"],["therapist","therapist(n.)治療師\ntherapy(n.)治療\nphysical therapist 物理治療師\nspeech therapist 語言治療師\nThe physical therapist helped him walk again after the accident.\n(物理治療師幫助他在意外後重新走路。)\nShe wants to become a speech therapist to help children.\n(她想成為語言治療師來幫助孩子。)"],["therapy","therapy(n.)治療、療法\ntherapeutic(adj.)治療的、有療效的\nphysical therapy 物理治療\nmusic therapy 音樂治療\nAfter the surgery, he needed months of physical therapy.\n(手術後，他需要好幾個月的物理治療。)\nMusic therapy can help patients relax and feel better.\n(音樂治療能幫助病人放鬆、感覺好一點。)"],["thereby","thereby(adv.)藉此、因此\n(無詞性變化)\nthereby reducing 藉此減少\nthereby causing 因而造成\nHe trained hard every day, thereby improving his speed.\n(他每天努力訓練，因而提升了速度。)\nThe city planted more trees, thereby reducing air pollution.\n(市政府種植更多樹木，藉此減少空氣汙染。)"],["thesis","thesis(n.)論文、論點\n(無詞性變化)\nmaster's thesis 碩士論文\nthesis statement 論點句、主旨句\nShe spent two years writing her master's thesis.\n(她花了兩年寫碩士論文。)\nA good essay begins with a clear thesis statement.\n(一篇好文章以清楚的主旨句開頭。)"],["thigh","thigh(n.)大腿\n(無詞性變化)\nthigh muscle 大腿肌肉\nchicken thigh 雞腿肉\nHe injured his thigh muscle during the race.\n(他在比賽中拉傷了大腿肌肉。)\nI ordered a grilled chicken thigh rice box for lunch.\n(我午餐點了烤雞腿飯便當。)"],["threshold","threshold(n.)門檻、起點、界限\n(無詞性變化)\non the threshold of 即將…、在…的開端\npain threshold 疼痛閾值\nYoung graduates are on the threshold of a new life.\n(年輕的畢業生正站在新生活的起點。)\nYour score must be above the threshold to pass.\n(你的分數必須超過門檻才能及格。)"],["thrill","thrill(n./v.)興奮、激動、使興奮\nthrilled(adj.)非常興奮的\nthrilling(adj.)令人興奮的\nthe thrill of 的刺激\nthrill seeker 尋求刺激的人\nRiding a roller coaster gives me a great thrill.\n(搭雲霄飛車讓我非常興奮刺激。)\nWe were thrilled to hear that we had won the contest.\n(聽到我們贏得比賽，我們都興奮極了。)"],["thriller","thriller(n.)驚悚片、驚悚小說\nthrill(n./v.)興奮、刺激\npsychological thriller 心理驚悚片\ncrime thriller 犯罪驚悚片\nI couldn't sleep after watching that psychological thriller.\n(看完那部心理驚悚片後我睡不著。)\nShe enjoys reading crime thrillers on long train rides.\n(她喜歡在長途火車旅程中讀犯罪驚悚小說。)"],["thrive","thrive(v.)繁榮、茁壯成長、興旺\nthriving(adj.)蓬勃發展的\nthrive on 從…中獲得成長或樂趣\nthriving business 興旺的生意\nThese plants thrive in warm, humid weather.\n(這些植物在溫暖潮濕的天氣中長得很茂盛。)\nSome people thrive on pressure and challenges.\n(有些人在壓力和挑戰下反而表現更好。)"],["throne","throne(n.)王位、寶座\ndethrone(v.)廢黜、取代\non the throne 在位\nheir to the throne 王位繼承人\nQueen Elizabeth II was on the throne for seventy years.\n(伊莉莎白二世在位七十年。)\nThe prince is the heir to the throne.\n(那位王子是王位繼承人。)"],["thrust","thrust(v./n.)猛推、刺、推力、要旨\n(無詞性變化)\nthrust into 推入、使陷入\nmain thrust 要點、主旨\nShe was suddenly thrust into the role of team leader.\n(她突然被推上隊長的位置。)\nThe main thrust of his speech was about education reform.\n(他演講的主旨是教育改革。)"],["tick","tick(n./v.)滴答聲、打勾、壁蝨、(時鐘)滴答響\n(無詞性變化)\ntick the box 在方格內打勾\ntick away 時間一分一秒流逝\nPlease tick the box if you agree to the terms.\n(如果同意條款，請在方格內打勾。)\nThe minutes ticked away as we waited for the results.\n(我們等待結果時，時間一分一秒過去。)"],["tile","tile(n./v.)磁磚、瓦片、鋪磁磚\n(無詞性變化)\nfloor tile 地磚\nroof tile 屋瓦\nThe bathroom floor is covered with white tiles.\n(浴室地板鋪著白色磁磚。)\nStrong winds blew several tiles off the roof.\n(強風把屋頂上幾片瓦片吹落。)"],["tin","tin(n./v.)錫、罐頭、裝罐\ntinned(adj.)罐裝的\ntin can 錫罐、罐頭\ncookie tin 餅乾鐵盒\nGrandma keeps her buttons in an old cookie tin.\n(奶奶把鈕扣放在一個舊餅乾鐵盒裡。)\nThe kids made a telephone with two tin cans and a string.\n(孩子們用兩個罐頭和一條繩子做了電話。)"],["toll","toll(n./v.)通行費、傷亡人數、損害、鳴(鐘)\n(無詞性變化)\ndeath toll 死亡人數\ntake a toll on 對…造成損害\nThe death toll from the earthquake continued to rise.\n(地震的死亡人數持續攀升。)\nWorking late every night took a toll on his health.\n(每晚熬夜工作損害了他的健康。)"],["torch","torch(n./v.)火炬、手電筒、放火燒\n(無詞性變化)\nOlympic torch 奧運聖火\npass the torch 傳承\nThe Olympic torch was carried through many cities.\n(奧運聖火被傳遞經過許多城市。)\nThe older generation must pass the torch to young leaders.\n(老一輩必須將重任傳承給年輕的領導者。)"],["torment","torment(n./v.)折磨、痛苦、使痛苦\ntormentor(n.)折磨者\nin torment 在痛苦中\ntorment by 被…折磨\nHe was in torment, unable to decide which school to choose.\n(他無法決定要選哪間學校，內心十分煎熬。)\nThe prisoners were tormented by hunger and cold.\n(囚犯們飽受飢寒折磨。)"],["tournament","tournament(n.)錦標賽、比賽\n(無詞性變化)\ntennis tournament 網球錦標賽\nwin the tournament 贏得錦標賽\nOur school won the national basketball tournament this year.\n(我們學校今年贏得全國籃球錦標賽。)\nTeams from twelve countries took part in the tournament.\n(來自十二個國家的隊伍參加了這場錦標賽。)"],["toxic","toxic(adj.)有毒的、有害的\ntoxin(n.)毒素\ntoxicity(n.)毒性\ntoxic waste 有毒廢棄物\ntoxic relationship 有害的關係\nThe factory was fined for dumping toxic waste into the river.\n(那家工廠因將有毒廢棄物倒入河中而被罰款。)\nIt took her years to leave that toxic relationship.\n(她花了好幾年才離開那段有害的關係。)"],["trait","trait(n.)特質、特徵\n(無詞性變化)\npersonality trait 人格特質\ngenetic trait 遺傳特徵\nHonesty is one of his best personality traits.\n(誠實是他最好的人格特質之一。)\nEye color is a genetic trait passed down from parents.\n(眼睛顏色是從父母遺傳下來的特徵。)"],["traitor","traitor(n.)叛徒、賣國賊\ntreason(n.)叛國罪\nbetray(v.)背叛\ntraitor to one's country 賣國賊\nbe called a traitor 被稱為叛徒\nHe was called a traitor for selling secrets to the enemy.\n(他因把機密賣給敵人而被稱為叛徒。)\nIn the story, the king's closest friend turns out to be a traitor.\n(在故事裡，國王最親近的朋友原來是個叛徒。)"],["transaction","transaction(n.)交易、處理\ntransact(v.)處理、交易\nonline transaction 線上交易\nbusiness transaction 商業交易\nAll online transactions on this site are protected.\n(此網站上的所有線上交易都受到保護。)\nThe bank charges a small fee for each transaction.\n(銀行每筆交易都收取一小筆手續費。)"],["transformation","transformation(n.)轉變、變形、改造\ntransform(v.)轉變、改造\ndigital transformation 數位轉型\nundergo a transformation 經歷轉變\nThe old factory underwent a transformation into an art center.\n(那座舊工廠經過改造成了藝術中心。)\nMany companies are going through digital transformation.\n(許多公司正在進行數位轉型。)"],["transit","transit(n./v.)運輸、過境、通過\ntransition(n.)轉變\npublic transit 大眾運輸\nin transit 運送途中\nTaipei has an excellent public transit system.\n(台北有很好的大眾運輸系統。)\nThe package was damaged in transit.\n(包裹在運送途中受損了。)"],["transition","transition(n.)轉變、過渡\ntransitional(adj.)過渡的\ntransition from A to B 從A轉變到B\nsmooth transition 順利過渡\nThe transition from junior high to senior high can be challenging.\n(從國中到高中的轉變可能充滿挑戰。)\nThe country is in transition to renewable energy.\n(這個國家正處於轉型為再生能源的過渡期。)"],["transmission","transmission(n.)傳染、傳播、播送、變速器\ntransmit(v.)傳送、傳染\ndisease transmission 疾病傳染\ndata transmission 資料傳輸\nWashing hands helps prevent the transmission of viruses.\n(洗手有助於防止病毒傳播。)\n5G networks allow much faster data transmission.\n(5G網路讓資料傳輸快得多。)"],["transparent","transparent(adj.)透明的、易懂的、公開的\ntransparency(n.)透明、透明度\ntransparent glass 透明玻璃\ntransparent process 公開透明的程序\nThe box is made of transparent plastic.\n(這個盒子是用透明塑膠做的。)\nCitizens want the government to be more transparent.\n(民眾希望政府更加公開透明。)"],["trauma","trauma(n.)創傷、損傷\ntraumatic(adj.)造成創傷的、痛苦的\nemotional trauma 心理創傷\nhead trauma 頭部外傷\nMany survivors suffered emotional trauma after the earthquake.\n(許多倖存者在地震後遭受心理創傷。)\nLosing his parents was a traumatic experience for him.\n(失去父母對他來說是很痛苦的經歷。)"],["treaty","treaty(n.)條約、協定\n(無詞性變化)\npeace treaty 和平條約\nsign a treaty 簽訂條約\nThe two countries signed a peace treaty after the war.\n(兩國在戰後簽訂了和平條約。)\nThe treaty aims to reduce nuclear weapons.\n(這項條約旨在減少核武。)"],["tribute","tribute(n.)致敬、讚揚、貢品\n(無詞性變化)\npay tribute to 向…致敬\ntribute concert 紀念音樂會\nFans paid tribute to the singer who passed away.\n(歌迷們向那位過世的歌手致敬。)\nThe statue was built as a tribute to the brave firefighters.\n(那座雕像是為了向英勇的消防員致敬而建。)"],["trigger","trigger(n./v.)扳機、起因、引發\n(無詞性變化)\npull the trigger 扣扳機\ntrigger an allergy 引發過敏\nDust can trigger an allergic reaction in some people.\n(灰塵可能引發某些人的過敏反應。)\nStress is often a trigger for headaches.\n(壓力常是引發頭痛的原因。)"],["trim","trim(v./n./adj.)修剪、削減、整潔的\n(無詞性變化)\ntrim the hedge 修剪樹籬\ntrim the budget 削減預算\nI need to trim my hair a little before the photo.\n(拍照前我需要稍微修剪一下頭髮。)\nThe school had to trim its budget this year.\n(學校今年必須削減預算。)"],["triple","triple(adj./v./n.)三倍的、三重的、使成三倍、三倍\n(無詞性變化)\ntriple the size 三倍大\ntriple jump 三級跳遠\nThe number of visitors has tripled since last year.\n(訪客人數從去年以來增加了三倍。)\nHe won a gold medal in the triple jump.\n(他在三級跳遠項目中贏得金牌。)"],["trivial","trivial(adj.)瑣碎的、不重要的\ntrivia(n.)瑣事、冷知識\ntrivial matter 瑣事\ntrivial mistake 小錯誤\nDon't waste your time arguing over trivial matters.\n(別浪費時間爭論瑣事。)\nWhat seems trivial to you may be important to others.\n(對你來說微不足道的事，對別人可能很重要。)"],["trophy","trophy(n.)獎盃、戰利品\n(無詞性變化)\nwin a trophy 贏得獎盃\ntrophy cabinet 獎盃櫃\nThe captain proudly lifted the trophy above his head.\n(隊長驕傲地把獎盃高舉過頭。)\nThe school's trophy cabinet is full of awards.\n(學校的獎盃櫃裡擺滿了獎項。)"],["tuition","tuition(n.)學費、教學\n(無詞性變化)\ntuition fees 學費\nprivate tuition 家教\nTuition fees at private universities are much higher.\n(私立大學的學費高得多。)\nShe works part-time to help pay her tuition.\n(她打工來幫忙支付學費。)"],["tumor","tumor(n.)腫瘤\n(無詞性變化)\nbrain tumor 腦瘤\nbenign tumor 良性腫瘤\nDoctors successfully removed the tumor from his lung.\n(醫生成功切除了他肺部的腫瘤。)\nFortunately, the tumor turned out to be benign.\n(幸好那個腫瘤是良性的。)"],["tuna","tuna(n.)鮪魚\n(無詞性變化)\ntuna sandwich 鮪魚三明治\ncanned tuna 鮪魚罐頭\nI made a tuna sandwich for lunch.\n(我做了一個鮪魚三明治當午餐。)\nPingtung is famous for its bluefin tuna.\n(屏東以黑鮪魚聞名。)"],["ultimate","ultimate(adj./n.)最終的、極致的、極品\nultimately(adv.)最後、終究\nultimate goal 最終目標\nthe ultimate in 極致的…\nHer ultimate goal is to become an astronaut.\n(她的最終目標是成為太空人。)\nUltimately, the decision is up to you.\n(最終，決定權在你。)"],["uncover","uncover(v.)揭露、發現、揭開\n(無詞性變化)\nuncover the truth 揭露真相\nuncover evidence 發現證據\nThe reporter worked for months to uncover the truth.\n(那位記者花了好幾個月揭露真相。)\nArchaeologists uncovered an ancient city under the sand.\n(考古學家在沙下發現一座古城。)"],["undergo","undergo(v.)經歷、遭受、接受(手術等)\n(無詞性變化)\nundergo surgery 接受手術\nundergo changes 經歷變化\nMy grandfather will undergo surgery next week.\n(我爺爺下週要接受手術。)\nTeenagers undergo many physical and emotional changes.\n(青少年會經歷許多生理和情緒上的變化。)"],["undergraduate","undergraduate(n.)大學生、大學部學生\n(無詞性變化)\nundergraduate degree 學士學位\nundergraduate student 大學部學生\nShe earned her undergraduate degree in economics.\n(她取得了經濟學的學士學位。)\nThe course is open to all undergraduates.\n(這門課開放給所有大學部學生修習。)"],["underline","underline(v./n.)畫底線、強調、底線\n(無詞性變化)\nunderline the key words 在關鍵字下畫線\nunderline the importance of 強調…的重要性\nUnderline the key words as you read the article.\n(閱讀文章時在關鍵字下畫線。)\nThe accident underlines the importance of wearing seat belts.\n(這起事故凸顯了繫安全帶的重要性。)"],["undermine","undermine(v.)破壞、削弱、損害\n(無詞性變化)\nundermine confidence 削弱信心\nundermine efforts 破壞努力\nConstant criticism can undermine a child's confidence.\n(不斷的批評會削弱孩子的自信。)\nFake news undermines public trust in the media.\n(假新聞損害了大眾對媒體的信任。)"],["undertake","undertake(v.)從事、承擔、著手進行\nundertaking(n.)任務、事業\nundertake a task 承擔任務\nundertake research 從事研究\nThe team undertook the difficult task of cleaning the beach.\n(團隊承擔了清理海灘的艱鉅任務。)\nShe plans to undertake research on ocean pollution.\n(她計畫從事海洋汙染的研究。)"],["undo","undo(v.)解開、取消、復原\n(無詞性變化)\nundo a button 解開鈕扣\nundo the damage 彌補損害\nPress Ctrl+Z to undo your last change.\n(按Ctrl+Z可以復原上一個動作。)\nIt will take years to undo the damage to the environment.\n(要彌補對環境的破壞需要好幾年。)"],["undoubtedly","undoubtedly(adv.)無疑地、確實地\ndoubt(n./v.)懷疑\nundoubted(adj.)無疑的\nundoubtedly the best 無疑是最好的\nundoubtedly true 確實如此\nShe is undoubtedly the best singer in our school.\n(她無疑是我們學校最會唱歌的人。)\nTechnology will undoubtedly change the way we learn.\n(科技無疑會改變我們學習的方式。)"],["unemployment","unemployment(n.)失業、失業率\nunemployed(adj.)失業的\nemployment(n.)就業\nunemployment rate 失業率\nyouth unemployment 青年失業\nThe unemployment rate rose during the economic crisis.\n(經濟危機期間失業率上升了。)\nYouth unemployment is a serious problem in many countries.\n(青年失業在許多國家都是嚴重的問題。)"],["unfold","unfold(v.)展開、打開、逐漸呈現\n(無詞性變化)\nunfold a map 打開地圖\nevents unfold 事件逐漸展開\nHe unfolded the map to find the way.\n(他打開地圖找路。)\nWe watched the story unfold on live TV.\n(我們在電視直播上看著事件逐漸發展。)"],["unlock","unlock(v.)開鎖、解開、釋放\n(無詞性變化)\nunlock the door 開門鎖\nunlock potential 激發潛能\nUse your fingerprint to unlock your phone.\n(用指紋解鎖你的手機。)\nGood education can unlock a child's potential.\n(良好的教育能激發孩子的潛能。)"],["unprecedented","unprecedented(adj.)前所未有的、空前的\nprecedent(n.)先例\nunprecedented challenge 前所未有的挑戰\non an unprecedented scale 規模空前\nThe pandemic brought unprecedented challenges to schools.\n(疫情為學校帶來前所未有的挑戰。)\nThe city saw unprecedented rainfall this summer.\n(這座城市今年夏天迎來前所未有的降雨量。)"],["update","update(n./v.)更新、最新消息、更新\nupdated(adj.)更新的\nsoftware update 軟體更新\nkeep sb. updated 隨時告知某人最新情況\nPlease update the app to the latest version.\n(請把應用程式更新到最新版本。)\nKeep me updated on your travel plans.\n(隨時告訴我你旅行計畫的最新狀況。)"],["upgrade","upgrade(v./n.)升級、提升、升級\n(無詞性變化)\nupgrade the system 升級系統\nget an upgrade 獲得升等\nThe school upgraded its computers over the summer.\n(學校在暑假期間升級了電腦。)\nWe got a free upgrade to business class.\n(我們免費升等到商務艙。)"],["utility","utility(n.)公用事業、效用、實用\nutilize(v.)利用\nutility bills 水電費\npublic utilities 公用事業\nOur utility bills are higher in the summer because of air conditioning.\n(因為開冷氣，我們夏天的水電費比較高。)\nWater and electricity are public utilities.\n(水和電是公用事業。)"],["utilize","utilize(v.)利用、使用\nutilization(n.)利用\nutility(n.)效用\nutilize resources 利用資源\nfully utilize 充分利用\nWe should fully utilize the school library's resources.\n(我們應該充分利用學校圖書館的資源。)\nSolar panels utilize sunlight to produce electricity.\n(太陽能板利用陽光發電。)"],["vacuum","vacuum(n./v.)真空、空白、用吸塵器清掃\n(無詞性變化)\nvacuum cleaner 吸塵器\nin a vacuum 在真空中、與世隔絕\nI vacuum my room every weekend.\n(我每個週末都用吸塵器打掃房間。)\nSound cannot travel in a vacuum.\n(聲音無法在真空中傳播。)"],["vague","vague(adj.)模糊的、含糊的\nvaguely(adv.)模糊地\nvagueness(n.)含糊\nvague answer 含糊的回答\nvague memory 模糊的記憶\nHe gave a vague answer when I asked about his plans.\n(我問他的計畫時，他給了個含糊的回答。)\nI have only a vague memory of my first day at school.\n(我對上學第一天只有模糊的記憶。)"],["valid","valid(adj.)有效的、正當的、合理的\nvalidity(n.)有效性\nvalidate(v.)證實、使有效\nvalid passport 有效護照\nvalid reason 正當理由\nMake sure your passport is valid for at least six months.\n(確認你的護照至少還有六個月效期。)\nBeing tired is not a valid reason for missing the exam.\n(累了不是缺考的正當理由。)"],["variable","variable(n./adj.)變數、可變的、多變的\nvary(v.)變化\nvariability(n.)可變性\nvariable weather 多變的天氣\nindependent variable 自變數\nThe weather in the mountains is highly variable.\n(山區的天氣非常多變。)\nIn this experiment, temperature is the independent variable.\n(在這個實驗中，溫度是自變數。)"],["variation","variation(n.)變化、變異、變奏\nvary(v.)變化\nvariation in 在…方面的變化\nregional variation 地區差異\nThere is a large variation in temperature between day and night.\n(日夜溫差很大。)\nThis dish is a modern variation of a traditional recipe.\n(這道菜是傳統食譜的現代變化版本。)"],["vein","vein(n.)靜脈、葉脈、風格\n(無詞性變化)\nin the same vein 以同樣風格\nblood vein 血管\nThe nurse found a vein and drew some blood.\n(護理師找到靜脈抽了一些血。)\nHis second novel is written in the same vein as the first.\n(他的第二本小說和第一本風格相同。)"],["vendor","vendor(n.)小販、攤販、供應商\nvend(v.)販賣\nstreet vendor 街頭小販\nvending machine 自動販賣機\nStreet vendors sell grilled corn at the night market.\n(夜市的小販賣烤玉米。)\nI bought a drink from the vending machine.\n(我在自動販賣機買了一瓶飲料。)"],["venture","venture(n./v.)冒險事業、新創事業、冒險前往\n(無詞性變化)\nbusiness venture 商業投資\njoint venture 合資企業\nOpening a café was his first business venture.\n(開咖啡店是他第一次的創業嘗試。)\nThe children ventured into the dark forest.\n(孩子們冒險走進黑暗的森林。)"],["venue","venue(n.)場地、會場\n(無詞性變化)\nconcert venue 演唱會場地\nchange the venue 更改地點\nThe venue for the concert has been changed due to rain.\n(演唱會的場地因雨而更改了。)\nTaipei Arena is a popular venue for big events.\n(台北小巨蛋是舉辦大型活動的熱門場地。)"],["verbal","verbal(adj./n.)口頭的、言語的、動狀詞\nverbally(adv.)口頭上\nverbal agreement 口頭協議\nverbal abuse 言語暴力\nThey made a verbal agreement but never signed a contract.\n(他們達成口頭協議，但從未簽約。)\nVerbal abuse can hurt as much as physical violence.\n(言語暴力造成的傷害不亞於肢體暴力。)"],["verdict","verdict(n.)判決、裁定、意見\n(無詞性變化)\nguilty verdict 有罪判決\nreach a verdict 做出裁決\nThe jury reached a guilty verdict after two days.\n(陪審團在兩天後做出有罪判決。)\nWhat's your verdict on the new restaurant?\n(你對那家新餐廳的評價如何？)"],["version","version(n.)版本、說法\n(無詞性變化)\nlatest version 最新版本\nEnglish version 英文版\nPlease download the latest version of the app.\n(請下載最新版本的應用程式。)\nHer version of the story is different from his.\n(她對這件事的說法和他的不同。)"],["versus","versus(prep.)對抗、與…相對\n(無詞性變化)\nA versus B 甲對乙\nhome versus away 主場對客場\nTonight's game is Taiwan versus Japan.\n(今晚的比賽是台灣對日本。)\nWe discussed the benefits of online versus in-person classes.\n(我們討論了線上課程與實體課程的優點。)"],["vertical","vertical(adj./n.)垂直的、直立的、垂直線\nvertically(adv.)垂直地\nvertical line 垂直線\nvertical garden 垂直花園\nDraw a vertical line down the middle of the page.\n(在頁面中間畫一條垂直線。)\nThe building has a beautiful vertical garden on its wall.\n(那棟建築的牆上有一座美麗的垂直花園。)"],["veteran","veteran(n.)老兵、退伍軍人、老手\n(無詞性變化)\nwar veteran 退伍老兵\nveteran teacher 資深教師\nThe war veteran shared his experiences with the students.\n(那位退伍老兵和學生分享他的經歷。)\nShe is a veteran teacher with thirty years of experience.\n(她是一位有三十年經驗的資深教師。)"],["via","via(prep.)經由、透過\n(無詞性變化)\nvia email 透過電子郵件\nvia Hong Kong 經由香港\nPlease send the file to me via email.\n(請透過電子郵件把檔案寄給我。)\nWe flew to London via Dubai.\n(我們經杜拜飛往倫敦。)"],["viable","viable(adj.)可行的、能存活的\nviability(n.)可行性\nviable option 可行的選擇\neconomically viable 經濟上可行\nSolar energy is a viable alternative to fossil fuels.\n(太陽能是取代化石燃料的可行方案。)\nThe plan is not economically viable.\n(這個計畫在經濟上不可行。)"],["vicious","vicious(adj.)兇惡的、惡毒的、猛烈的\nviciously(adv.)兇惡地\nvicious circle 惡性循環\nvicious dog 惡犬\nStaying up late and feeling tired the next day is a vicious circle.\n(熬夜和隔天疲倦形成惡性循環。)\nThe singer was hurt by vicious comments online.\n(那位歌手被網路上惡毒的留言傷害。)"],["viewer","viewer(n.)觀眾、觀看者\nview(v./n.)觀看、看法\nTV viewers 電視觀眾\nattract viewers 吸引觀眾\nThe show attracted millions of viewers.\n(這個節目吸引了數百萬名觀眾。)\nViewers can vote for their favorite singer online.\n(觀眾可以在網路上投票給最喜歡的歌手。)"],["viewpoint","viewpoint(n.)觀點、看法、觀景點\n(無詞性變化)\nfrom one's viewpoint 從某人的觀點\ndifferent viewpoints 不同的觀點\nFrom my viewpoint, the plan has several problems.\n(從我的觀點來看，這個計畫有好幾個問題。)\nIt's important to listen to different viewpoints.\n(傾聽不同的觀點很重要。)"],["vinegar","vinegar(n.)醋\n(無詞性變化)\nrice vinegar 米醋\nblack vinegar 烏醋\nAdd a little black vinegar to the soup.\n(在湯裡加一點烏醋。)\nVinegar can be used to clean windows.\n(醋可以用來清潔窗戶。)"],["virtual","virtual(adj.)虛擬的、實際上的\nvirtually(adv.)幾乎、實際上\nvirtual reality 虛擬實境\nvirtual tour 線上導覽\nVirtual reality allows students to explore ancient Rome.\n(虛擬實境讓學生能探索古羅馬。)\nThe museum offers a free virtual tour on its website.\n(博物館在網站上提供免費的線上導覽。)"],["visa","visa(n.)簽證\n(無詞性變化)\napply for a visa 申請簽證\nstudent visa 學生簽證\nYou need to apply for a student visa to study in the US.\n(到美國念書需要申請學生簽證。)\nTaiwanese passport holders can enter Japan without a visa.\n(持台灣護照的人可以免簽證入境日本。)"],["vocal","vocal(adj./n.)聲音的、直言的、主唱、歌聲\nvocalist(n.)歌手、主唱\nvocal cords 聲帶\nlead vocals 主唱\nShe was very vocal in her support for animal rights.\n(她大力發聲支持動物權利。)\nHe sings lead vocals in the school band.\n(他在學校樂團擔任主唱。)"],["volcano","volcano(n.)火山\nvolcanic(adj.)火山的\nactive volcano 活火山\nvolcanic eruption 火山爆發\nMount Fuji is actually an active volcano.\n(富士山其實是一座活火山。)\nDatun Mountain in Taipei was formed by a volcano.\n(台北的大屯山是由火山形成的。)"],["vomit","vomit(n./v.)嘔吐、嘔吐物\n(無詞性變化)\nfeel like vomiting 想吐\nvomit blood 吐血\nThe rough boat ride made me feel like vomiting.\n(搖晃的船程讓我覺得想吐。)\nThe child vomited after eating too much candy.\n(那個孩子吃了太多糖果後吐了。)"],["voucher","voucher(n.)抵用券、禮券、憑證\n(無詞性變化)\ngift voucher 禮券\ndiscount voucher 折價券\nThe government issued vouchers to boost spending.\n(政府發放振興券來刺激消費。)\nI used a gift voucher to buy these shoes.\n(我用禮券買了這雙鞋。)"],["vow","vow(n./v.)誓言、發誓\n(無詞性變化)\nwedding vows 婚禮誓詞\nmake a vow 立誓\nThe couple exchanged wedding vows in front of their families.\n(這對新人在家人面前交換婚禮誓詞。)\nHe vowed never to make the same mistake again.\n(他發誓絕不再犯同樣的錯。)"],["vulnerable","vulnerable(adj.)易受傷的、脆弱的\nvulnerability(n.)脆弱、弱點\nvulnerable to 容易受到…\nvulnerable groups 弱勢族群\nYoung children are especially vulnerable to the flu.\n(幼童特別容易感染流感。)\nThe program helps vulnerable groups such as the elderly.\n(這個計畫幫助像老人這樣的弱勢族群。)"],["warehouse","warehouse(n./v.)倉庫、存入倉庫\n(無詞性變化)\nwarehouse store 倉儲量販店\nstorage warehouse 儲藏倉庫\nThe online shop ships all its products from a huge warehouse.\n(那家網路商店的所有商品都從一座巨大的倉庫出貨。)\nMany families do their monthly shopping at warehouse stores.\n(許多家庭在倉儲量販店採買每月所需。)"],["warrior","warrior(n.)戰士、勇士\n(無詞性變化)\nbrave warrior 英勇的戰士\nroad warrior 經常出差的人\nThe ancient warriors fought bravely to protect their land.\n(古代戰士英勇作戰以保衛家園。)\nShe is a true warrior who never gives up in hard times.\n(她是個真正的勇士，在艱困時從不放棄。)"],["wary","wary(adj.)小心翼翼的、謹慎的、提防的\nwarily(adv.)謹慎地\nbe wary of 提防\nwary eye 警戒的眼光\nYou should be wary of strangers who ask for personal information online.\n(你應該提防在網路上索取個人資料的陌生人。)\nThe cat kept a wary eye on the dog in the yard.\n(那隻貓警戒地盯著院子裡的狗。)"],["weird","weird(adj.)怪異的、奇怪的\nweirdness(n.)怪異\nweird feeling 奇怪的感覺\nweird noise 怪聲\nI heard a weird noise coming from the kitchen last night.\n(昨晚我聽到廚房傳來一陣怪聲。)\nIt feels weird to be back at my old school after so many years.\n(這麼多年後回到母校感覺很奇怪。)"],["whatsoever","whatsoever(adj./pron.)任何的、絲毫(用於加強否定)\nwhatever(pron./adj.)無論什麼\nno doubt whatsoever 毫無疑問\nnothing whatsoever 什麼也沒有\nThere is no evidence whatsoever that he stole the money.\n(完全沒有證據顯示他偷了那筆錢。)\nI have no interest whatsoever in watching horror movies.\n(我對看恐怖片一點興趣也沒有。)"],["wheelchair","wheelchair(n.)輪椅\n(無詞性變化)\nin a wheelchair 坐輪椅\nwheelchair access 無障礙通道\nThe new library provides wheelchair access at every entrance.\n(新圖書館的每個入口都設有無障礙通道。)\nAfter the accident, he had to use a wheelchair for several months.\n(事故後，他有好幾個月必須坐輪椅。)"],["whereabouts","whereabouts(n./adv.)下落、行蹤、在哪裡\n(無詞性變化)\ncurrent whereabouts 目前下落\nwhereabouts unknown 下落不明\nThe police are still trying to find out the whereabouts of the missing hiker.\n(警方仍在設法查明失蹤登山客的下落。)\nWhereabouts in Taipei do you live?\n(你住在台北的哪一帶？)"],["whereas","whereas(conj.)然而、反之\n(無詞性變化)\nwhereas others 而其他人\nwhereas in the past 而在過去\nSome students prefer studying at night, whereas others focus better in the morning.\n(有些學生喜歡晚上讀書，而其他人則在早上比較專心。)\nMy brother loves sports, whereas I prefer reading.\n(我哥哥熱愛運動，而我比較喜歡閱讀。)"],["whine","whine(n./v.)抱怨、哀鳴、嘎吱聲\nwhiny(adj.)愛發牢騷的\nwhine about 抱怨\nthe whine of 的尖銳聲音\nStop whining about the homework and just get it done.\n(別再抱怨功課了，趕快把它寫完。)\nWe could hear the high-pitched whine of a mosquito in the dark.\n(黑暗中我們能聽到蚊子尖銳的嗡嗡聲。)"],["widespread","widespread(adj.)廣泛的、普遍的\n(無詞性變化)\nwidespread use 廣泛使用\nwidespread support 廣泛支持\nThe widespread use of smartphones has changed how we communicate.\n(智慧型手機的普及改變了我們溝通的方式。)\nThe new policy received widespread support from parents.\n(這項新政策獲得家長廣泛支持。)"],["wig","wig(n.)假髮\n(無詞性變化)\nwear a wig 戴假髮\ncurly wig 捲髮假髮\nThe actor wore a gray wig to play an old man in the play.\n(那位演員戴上灰色假髮在戲中飾演老人。)\nJudges in Britain traditionally wear white wigs in court.\n(英國的法官傳統上在法庭上戴白色假髮。)"],["wilderness","wilderness(n.)荒野、荒地\nwild(adj.)野生的\nin the wilderness 在荒野中\nwilderness area 荒野保護區\nThe hikers got lost in the wilderness for two days.\n(那些登山客在荒野中迷路了兩天。)\nSome people enjoy camping in the wilderness far from the city.\n(有些人喜歡在遠離城市的荒野中露營。)"],["wildlife","wildlife(n.)野生動物\n(無詞性變化)\nwildlife conservation 野生動物保育\nwildlife park 野生動物園\nPlastic waste in the ocean is a serious threat to wildlife.\n(海洋中的塑膠垃圾對野生動物是嚴重威脅。)\nThe national park is home to a rich variety of wildlife.\n(這座國家公園是多種野生動物的棲息地。)"],["windshield","windshield(n.)擋風玻璃\nwindscreen(n.)擋風玻璃(英式)\nwindshield wipers 雨刷\ncracked windshield 破裂的擋風玻璃\nA small stone hit the car and cracked the windshield.\n(一顆小石頭擊中車子，把擋風玻璃打裂了。)\nTurn on the windshield wipers when it starts to rain.\n(開始下雨時要打開雨刷。)"],["wither","wither(v.)枯萎、凋謝、衰弱\nwithered(adj.)枯萎的\nwither away 逐漸消亡\nwithered leaves 枯葉\nThe flowers withered because no one watered them.\n(那些花因為沒人澆水而枯萎了。)\nWithout community support, the old tradition may wither away.\n(少了社區的支持，這項老傳統可能會逐漸消失。)"],["witty","witty(adj.)機智的、詼諧的\nwit(n.)機智\nwittily(adv.)機智地\nwitty remark 妙語\nwitty speech 風趣的演說\nEveryone laughed at the speaker's witty remarks.\n(大家都被講者的妙語逗笑了。)\nOur English teacher is witty and always makes class fun.\n(我們的英文老師很風趣，總是讓課堂很有趣。)"],["workshop","workshop(n.)工作坊、研討會、工作室\n(無詞性變化)\nattend a workshop 參加工作坊\nwriting workshop 寫作工作坊\nOur school held a workshop on how to prepare for college interviews.\n(我們學校舉辦了一場準備大學面試的工作坊。)\nMy grandfather builds furniture in his small workshop.\n(我爺爺在他的小工作室裡做家具。)"],["worship","worship(n./v.)崇拜、禮拜\nworshipper(n.)崇拜者、禮拜者\nplace of worship 禮拜場所\nancestor worship 祭祖\nMany families in Taiwan practice ancestor worship during festivals.\n(台灣許多家庭在節日時祭拜祖先。)\nSome fans worship their idols and copy everything they do.\n(有些粉絲崇拜偶像，模仿他們的一舉一動。)"],["worthwhile","worthwhile(adj.)值得的、有價值的\nworth(adj./n.)值得的、價值\nworthwhile experience 值得的經驗\nmake it worthwhile 讓……值得\nVolunteering at the animal shelter was a worthwhile experience.\n(在動物收容所當志工是一次很有意義的經驗。)\nIt is worthwhile to spend time learning a second language.\n(花時間學習第二外語是值得的。)"],["worthy","worthy(adj.)值得的、有價值的、可敬的\nworth(adj./n.)值得的、價值\nbe worthy of 值得\nworthy cause 有意義的目標\nHer brave actions are worthy of our respect.\n(她英勇的行為值得我們尊敬。)\nThe students raised money for a worthy cause.\n(學生們為一項有意義的公益目標募款。)"],["yacht","yacht(n./v.)遊艇、駕遊艇\nyachting(n.)遊艇運動\nluxury yacht 豪華遊艇\nyacht club 遊艇俱樂部\nThe billionaire spent his vacation sailing on a luxury yacht.\n(那位億萬富翁搭著豪華遊艇度假。)\nKaohsiung is known for building high-quality yachts.\n(高雄以製造高品質遊艇聞名。)"],["yield","yield(v./n.)產生、出產、屈服、讓路、產量\n(無詞性變化)\nyield to 屈服於、讓路給\ncrop yield 作物產量\nDrivers must yield to pedestrians at crosswalks.\n(駕駛人在斑馬線前必須禮讓行人。)\nThe new farming method increased crop yields by twenty percent.\n(新的耕作方法使作物產量提高了百分之二十。)"]],"6":[["abbreviate","abbreviate(v.)縮寫、縮短\nabbreviation(n.)縮寫、縮寫字\nbe abbreviated to 縮寫為…\nabbreviated form 縮寫形式\nThe United Nations is often abbreviated to UN in news reports.\n(聯合國在新聞報導中常縮寫為UN。)\nBecause of the storm, the ceremony had to be abbreviated.\n(由於暴風雨，典禮只好縮短進行。)"],["abide","abide(v.)遵守、忍受\nabiding(adj.)持久的\nabide by 遵守\ncan't abide 無法忍受\nAll players must abide by the rules of the competition.\n(所有選手都必須遵守比賽規則。)\nShe can't abide people who are rude to service staff.\n(她無法忍受對服務人員無禮的人。)"],["aboriginal","aboriginal(adj./n.)原住民的、土著的、原住民\naborigine(n.)原住民\naboriginal culture 原住民文化\naboriginal people 原住民\nThe festival celebrates the music and dance of aboriginal culture in Taiwan.\n(這個節慶慶祝台灣原住民文化的音樂與舞蹈。)\nMany aboriginal languages are in danger of disappearing.\n(許多原住民語言正面臨消失的危機。)"],["abound","abound(v.)大量存在、充滿\nabundant(adj.)豐富的\nabound in/with 充滿…\nrumors abound 謠言四起\nRumors abound about the singer's retirement.\n(關於那位歌手退休的謠言四起。)\nThe coral reefs here abound with colorful fish.\n(這裡的珊瑚礁有大量色彩繽紛的魚。)"],["abstraction","abstraction(n.)抽象概念、抽象化、心不在焉\nabstract(adj./n.)抽象的、摘要\nabstract(v.)提取、抽象化\nmathematical abstraction 數學抽象概念\nin abstraction 抽象地\nJustice is an abstraction that is difficult to define precisely.\n(正義是一個很難精確定義的抽象概念。)\nHe stared out the window in a state of abstraction.\n(他心不在焉地凝視著窗外。)"],["abundance","abundance(n.)大量、豐富\nabundant(adj.)豐富的、充足的\nin abundance 大量、充足\nan abundance of 大量的…\nFruit grows in abundance on the island during the summer.\n(這座島嶼夏天盛產水果。)\nThe library offers an abundance of resources for research.\n(圖書館提供大量的研究資源。)"],["academy","academy(n.)學院、專科學校、研究院\nacademic(adj.)學術的\nmilitary academy 軍校\nAcademia Sinica 中央研究院\nHe was accepted into a prestigious military academy after graduation.\n(他畢業後被一所知名軍校錄取。)\nShe studied dance at a performing arts academy in London.\n(她在倫敦一所表演藝術學院學舞。)"],["accessory","accessory(n./adj.)配件、飾品、從犯、附屬的\n(無詞性變化)\nfashion accessories 時尚配件\nphone accessories 手機配件\nThe shop sells phone cases and other accessories.\n(那間店販售手機殼和其他配件。)\nA simple scarf can be the perfect accessory for a plain outfit.\n(一條簡單的圍巾可以是樸素服裝的完美配件。)"],["acclaim","acclaim(n./v.)稱讚、喝采、讚揚\nacclaimed(adj.)受讚譽的\ncritical acclaim 評論家的讚譽\nwidely acclaimed 廣受讚揚\nThe director's latest film received wide critical acclaim.\n(那位導演的新片獲得評論界廣泛讚譽。)\nHer novel was acclaimed as a masterpiece of modern literature.\n(她的小說被譽為現代文學的傑作。)"],["accordance","accordance(n.)一致、符合\naccord(n./v.)一致、協議\naccording(adv.)按照\nin accordance with 依照、根據\nin accordance with the law 依法\nThe decision was made in accordance with school regulations.\n(這項決定是依照校規做出的。)\nAll waste must be handled in accordance with the law.\n(所有廢棄物都必須依法處理。)"],["accordingly","accordingly(adv.)因此、相應地\naccording(adv.)按照\nact accordingly 相應地行動\nadjust accordingly 隨之調整\nThe weather may change quickly, so plan accordingly.\n(天氣可能變化很快，所以要事先做好相應的規劃。)\nPrices went up, and accordingly, sales dropped.\n(價格上漲了，銷量因而下滑。)"],["accountable","accountable(adj.)應負責任的\naccountability(n.)責任、問責\nhold sb. accountable 要某人負責\nbe accountable for 對…負責\nPoliticians must be held accountable for their promises.\n(政治人物必須為他們的承諾負責。)\nEach team member is accountable for a part of the project.\n(每位組員都要對專題中的一部分負責。)"],["accumulate","accumulate(v.)累積、積聚\naccumulation(n.)累積\naccumulative(adj.)累積的\naccumulate wealth 累積財富\naccumulate experience 累積經驗\nDust accumulates quickly on the shelves if you don't clean them.\n(如果不清理，灰塵很快就會在架子上堆積。)\nShe accumulated valuable experience by volunteering abroad.\n(她藉由到國外當志工累積了寶貴的經驗。)"],["accumulation","accumulation(n.)累積、積聚、堆積物\naccumulate(v.)累積\naccumulation of wealth 財富累積\nsnow accumulation 積雪\nThe accumulation of plastic waste in the ocean threatens marine life.\n(海洋中塑膠垃圾的堆積威脅著海洋生物。)\nLearning a language is a slow accumulation of small improvements.\n(學習語言是一點一滴進步的緩慢累積。)"],["accusation","accusation(n.)指控、控告\naccuse(v.)指控\nmake an accusation 提出指控\nfalse accusation 誣告\nHe strongly denied the accusation of cheating on the exam.\n(他強烈否認考試作弊的指控。)\nFalse accusations can seriously damage a person's reputation.\n(不實的指控會嚴重損害一個人的名譽。)"],["accustom","accustom(v.)使習慣\naccustomed(adj.)習慣的\nbe accustomed to 習慣於\naccustom oneself to 使自己習慣於\nIt took me weeks to accustom myself to the new time zone.\n(我花了好幾週才適應新的時區。)\nShe is accustomed to getting up early for morning practice.\n(她已經習慣早起參加晨練。)"],["acne","acne(n.)粉刺、痘痘、青春痘\n(無詞性變化)\nsuffer from acne 長痘痘\nacne scars 痘疤\nMany teenagers suffer from acne during puberty.\n(許多青少年在青春期長痘痘。)\nWashing your face gently can help prevent acne.\n(溫和地洗臉有助於預防痘痘。)"],["acre","acre(n.)英畝\nacreage(n.)英畝數、面積\nacres of land 數英畝的土地\nper acre 每英畝\nThe farm covers more than five hundred acres of land.\n(這座農場占地超過五百英畝。)\nAn acre is roughly equal to 4,047 square meters.\n(一英畝大約等於四千零四十七平方公尺。)"],["adaptation","adaptation(n.)適應、改編、改編作品\nadapt(v.)適應、改編\nadaptive(adj.)適應的\nfilm adaptation 電影改編版\nadaptation to 對…的適應\nThe film is an adaptation of a popular Japanese comic.\n(這部電影改編自一部受歡迎的日本漫畫。)\nThick fur is an adaptation to the extreme cold of the Arctic.\n(厚毛皮是對北極嚴寒的一種適應。)"],["addiction","addiction(n.)成癮、上癮、沉迷\naddict(n./v.)成癮者、使上癮\naddictive(adj.)使人上癮的\ninternet addiction 網路成癮\ndrug addiction 毒癮\nInternet addiction can affect students' sleep and grades.\n(網路成癮會影響學生的睡眠和成績。)\nSome mobile games are designed to be highly addictive.\n(有些手機遊戲被設計得非常容易讓人上癮。)"],["administer/administrate","administer(v.)管理、執行、給予(藥物)\nadministrate(v.)管理、經營(同administer)\nadministration(n.)管理、行政\nadminister a test 舉行測驗\nadminister medicine 給藥\nThe exam will be administered by the College Entrance Examination Center.\n(這項考試將由大學入學考試中心辦理。)\nThe nurse administered the medicine to the patient every four hours.\n(護理師每四小時給病人用一次藥。)"],["admiral","admiral(n.)海軍上將、艦隊司令\n(無詞性變化)\nrear admiral 海軍少將\nfleet admiral 海軍五星上將\nThe admiral led the fleet into the harbor.\n(海軍上將率領艦隊駛入港口。)\nHe rose from a young sailor to an admiral over thirty years.\n(他花了三十年從年輕水手晉升為海軍上將。)"],["adolescence","adolescence(n.)青春期\nadolescent(n./adj.)青少年、青春期的\nduring adolescence 在青春期\nearly adolescence 青春期早期\nMany physical and emotional changes take place during adolescence.\n(青春期會發生許多生理和情緒上的變化。)\nFriendships formed in adolescence often last a lifetime.\n(青春期結交的友誼往往維持一輩子。)"],["advisory","advisory(adj.)諮詢的、顧問的\nadvise(v.)建議\nadviser(n.)顧問\nadvisory committee 諮詢委員會\ntravel advisory 旅遊警示\nThe government set up an advisory committee on education reform.\n(政府成立了教育改革諮詢委員會。)\nThe weather bureau issued a heat advisory for southern Taiwan.\n(氣象署對南台灣發布高溫資訊。)"],["aesthetic","aesthetic(adj.)美學的、審美的、美感的\naesthetics(n.)美學\naesthetically(adv.)美學上\naesthetic value 美學價值\naesthetically pleasing 賞心悅目的\nThe new library was designed with both function and aesthetic value in mind.\n(新圖書館的設計兼顧了功能與美學價值。)\nThe garden is arranged in an aesthetically pleasing way.\n(這座花園布置得賞心悅目。)"],["affectionate","affectionate(adj.)充滿深情的、親切的\naffection(n.)喜愛、感情\naffectionately(adv.)親切地\naffectionate hug 深情的擁抱\naffectionate nickname 親暱的暱稱\nMy grandmother greeted me with an affectionate hug.\n(奶奶給了我一個溫暖的擁抱。)\nCats can be surprisingly affectionate toward their owners.\n(貓對主人可能出奇地黏人親暱。)"],["affiliate","affiliate(n.)分支機構、附屬機構、會員\naffiliate(v.)使隸屬、使加入\naffiliated(adj.)附屬的、有關聯的\naffiliated hospital 附屬醫院\nlocal affiliate 地方分支機構\nThe TV station is a local affiliate of a national network.\n(這家電視台是全國聯播網的地方分台。)\nShe works at a hospital affiliated with the university.\n(她在一家大學附設醫院工作。)"],["affirm","affirm(v.)斷言、證實、肯定\naffirmation(n.)斷言、肯定\naffirmative(adj.)肯定的\naffirm one's commitment 重申承諾\naffirmative answer 肯定的回答\nThe president affirmed the country's commitment to democracy.\n(總統重申國家對民主的承諾。)\nThe test results affirmed the doctor's original diagnosis.\n(檢驗結果證實了醫生原先的診斷。)"],["airtight","airtight(adj.)密封的、不透氣的、無懈可擊的\n(無詞性變化)\nairtight container 密封容器\nairtight alibi 無懈可擊的不在場證明\nStore the cookies in an airtight container to keep them fresh.\n(把餅乾存放在密封容器中以保持新鮮。)\nThe suspect had an airtight alibi for the night of the crime.\n(嫌犯在案發當晚有無懈可擊的不在場證明。)"],["airway","airway(n.)呼吸道、航線、航空公司\n(無詞性變化)\nclear the airway 暢通呼吸道\nBritish Airways 英國航空\nThe first step in first aid is to make sure the airway is clear.\n(急救的第一步是確保呼吸道暢通。)\nSmoke can irritate your airways and make breathing difficult.\n(煙霧會刺激呼吸道，使呼吸困難。)"],["algebra","algebra(n.)代數\nalgebraic(adj.)代數的\nlinear algebra 線性代數\nalgebra problem 代數題\nMany students find algebra more challenging than arithmetic.\n(許多學生覺得代數比算術更有挑戰性。)\nShe solved the algebra problem in just a few minutes.\n(她只花幾分鐘就解出那道代數題。)"],["alienate","alienate(v.)使疏遠、使不友善\nalienation(n.)疏遠、隔閡\nalienated(adj.)被疏遠的、疏離的\nalienate voters 失去選民支持\nfeel alienated 感到疏離\nHis rude comments alienated many of his old friends.\n(他無禮的言論讓許多老朋友疏遠了他。)\nNew immigrants sometimes feel alienated in a foreign culture.\n(新移民有時在異國文化中感到疏離。)"],["align","align(v.)使成一直線、使一致、結盟\nalignment(n.)排成直線、結盟\nalign with 與…一致、與…結盟\nalign the text 對齊文字\nMake sure the pictures are aligned before you print the poster.\n(印海報前確認圖片都已對齊。)\nThe school's goals are closely aligned with the new curriculum.\n(學校的目標與新課綱緊密一致。)"],["allege","allege(v.)宣稱、聲稱(無證據地)\nallegation(n.)指控、宣稱\nalleged(adj.)被指控的、據稱的\nallegedly(adv.)據稱\nallege that 聲稱…\nalleged crime 被指控的罪行\nThe newspaper alleged that the mayor had accepted bribes.\n(報紙聲稱市長收受了賄賂。)\nThe alleged thief was released due to lack of evidence.\n(那名涉嫌竊盜的人因證據不足而獲釋。)"],["alligator","alligator(n.)短吻鱷\n(無詞性變化)\nalligator skin 鱷魚皮\nAmerican alligator 美洲短吻鱷\nAlligators are commonly found in the swamps of Florida.\n(在佛羅里達的沼澤中常可以看到短吻鱷。)\nThe tourists watched an alligator sunbathing on the riverbank.\n(觀光客看著一隻短吻鱷在河岸上曬太陽。)"],["altitude","altitude(n.)高度、海拔\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh altitude 高海拔\naltitude sickness 高山症\nThe plane was flying at an altitude of 10,000 meters.\n(飛機在一萬公尺的高度飛行。)\nClimbers may suffer from altitude sickness on Jade Mountain.\n(登山客在玉山上可能會出現高山症。)"],["aluminum","aluminum(n.)鋁\n(無詞性變化)\naluminum foil 鋁箔紙\naluminum can 鋁罐\nWrap the sweet potatoes in aluminum foil before baking them.\n(烤地瓜之前先用鋁箔紙包起來。)\nAluminum cans should be put in the recycling bin.\n(鋁罐應該放進資源回收桶。)"],["ambiguity","ambiguity(n.)模稜兩可、含糊不清\nambiguous(adj.)模稜兩可的\nambiguously(adv.)含糊地\navoid ambiguity 避免歧義\nlegal ambiguity 法律上的模糊地帶\nGood writers choose their words carefully to avoid ambiguity.\n(好的作者會謹慎選字以避免語意不清。)\nThe ambiguity in the contract led to a long legal dispute.\n(合約中含糊不清之處引發了漫長的法律糾紛。)"],["amid/amidst","amid(prep.)在…之中、在…期間\namidst(prep.)在…之中(較文雅)\namid concerns 在各界憂慮聲中\namid the chaos 在一片混亂中\nThe concert went ahead amid concerns about the coming typhoon.\n(在各界對颱風的擔憂聲中，演唱會仍照常舉行。)\nShe remained calm amid the chaos after the earthquake.\n(地震過後一片混亂中，她依然保持冷靜。)"],["amplify","amplify(v.)放大、擴大、詳述\namplifier(n.)擴音器\namplification(n.)放大、擴大\namplify sound 放大聲音\namplify the effect 擴大效果\nThe microphone amplifies the speaker's voice so everyone can hear.\n(麥克風放大講者的聲音，讓大家都聽得到。)\nSocial media can amplify rumors within minutes.\n(社群媒體能在幾分鐘內把謠言擴散開來。)"],["analogy","analogy(n.)類比、相似之處\nanalogous(adj.)類似的\ndraw an analogy 做類比\nby analogy 用類推的方法\nThe teacher drew an analogy between the heart and a water pump.\n(老師把心臟比作抽水機。)\nBy analogy, we can understand how electricity flows through a circuit.\n(用類比的方法，我們可以理解電流如何在電路中流動。)"],["analytical","analytical(adj.)分析的、善於分析的\nanalyze(v.)分析\nanalysis(n.)分析\nanalytical skills 分析能力\nanalytical thinking 分析性思考\nStudying science helps students develop strong analytical skills.\n(學習科學能幫助學生培養很強的分析能力。)\nShe has an analytical mind and enjoys solving puzzles.\n(她頭腦善於分析，喜歡解謎。)"],["anchor","anchor(n./v.)錨、支柱、新聞主播、停泊、使固定\nanchorage(n.)停泊處\ndrop anchor 下錨、停泊\nnews anchor 新聞主播\nThe ship dropped anchor near the small island.\n(那艘船在小島附近下錨停泊。)\nShe has been the evening news anchor for ten years.\n(她擔任晚間新聞主播已經十年了。)"],["animate","animate(v./adj.)使有生氣、製作成動畫、有生命的\nanimation(n.)動畫、生氣\nanimated(adj.)動畫的、活躍的\nanimated film 動畫電影\nanimated discussion 熱烈的討論\nThe students had an animated discussion about climate change.\n(學生們針對氣候變遷進行了熱烈的討論。)\nThe studio spent three years animating the feature film.\n(這家工作室花了三年製作這部動畫長片。)"],["annoyance","annoyance(n.)惱怒、煩惱、令人煩惱的事\nannoy(v.)使惱怒\nannoying(adj.)令人惱怒的\nto one's annoyance 令某人惱怒的是\nminor annoyance 小麻煩\nTo my annoyance, the bus was late again this morning.\n(令我惱火的是，今天早上公車又誤點了。)\nThe constant noise from the construction site is a great annoyance.\n(工地持續的噪音是一大困擾。)"],["anthem","anthem(n.)國歌、讚歌、聖歌\n(無詞性變化)\nnational anthem 國歌\nsing the anthem 唱國歌\nEveryone stood up when the national anthem was played.\n(國歌響起時，大家都站了起來。)\nThe song became an anthem for a whole generation of young people.\n(那首歌成了一整個世代年輕人的代表歌曲。)"],["antibiotic","antibiotic(n./adj.)抗生素、抗生的\n(無詞性變化)\ntake antibiotics 服用抗生素\nantibiotic resistance 抗藥性\nThe doctor prescribed antibiotics for my throat infection.\n(醫生開了抗生素治療我的喉嚨感染。)\nOverusing antibiotics can lead to antibiotic resistance.\n(過度使用抗生素可能導致抗藥性。)"],["anticipation","anticipation(n.)期待、預期、預料\nanticipate(v.)預期、期待\nin anticipation of 預料到…、期待著…\neager anticipation 熱切期待\nFans waited in eager anticipation for the band to appear on stage.\n(歌迷們熱切期待樂團登台。)\nStores stocked up on water in anticipation of the typhoon.\n(商店預期颱風來襲而囤積了大量飲用水。)"],["antonym","antonym(n.)反義詞\nantonymous(adj.)反義的\nthe antonym of 某字的反義詞\nsynonyms and antonyms 同義詞與反義詞\nThe antonym of 'generous' is 'stingy'.\n(generous的反義詞是stingy。)\nLearning synonyms and antonyms helps expand your vocabulary.\n(學習同義詞和反義詞有助於擴充字彙量。)"],["applaud","applaud(v.)鼓掌、讚許\napplause(n.)掌聲\napplaud loudly 熱烈鼓掌\napplaud sb. for 為了…讚揚某人\nThe audience applauded loudly at the end of the performance.\n(表演結束時觀眾熱烈鼓掌。)\nWe applaud her for her courage to speak out.\n(我們讚揚她勇於發聲的勇氣。)"],["applicable","applicable(adj.)適用的、可應用的\napply(v.)應用、適用\napplicability(n.)適用性\napplicable to 適用於\nwhere applicable 在適用的情況下\nThese rules are applicable to all students in the school.\n(這些規定適用於全校所有學生。)\nPlease fill in your phone number where applicable.\n(如適用，請填寫你的電話號碼。)"],["apprentice","apprentice(n.)學徒、見習生\napprenticeship(n.)學徒期、學徒身分\napprentice chef 學徒廚師\nserve an apprenticeship 當學徒\nHe worked as an apprentice chef in a famous restaurant.\n(他在一家知名餐廳擔任學徒廚師。)\nShe served a three-year apprenticeship before opening her own shop.\n(她當了三年學徒才開了自己的店。)"],["approximate","approximate(adj./v.)大約的、近似的、接近\napproximately(adv.)大約\napproximation(n.)近似值\napproximate cost 大約的費用\napproximate number 大概的數目\nThe approximate cost of the school trip is 3,000 dollars.\n(校外教學的費用大約是三千元。)\nThe final result closely approximates our original estimate.\n(最後的結果非常接近我們原先的估計。)"],["archaeology","archaeology(n.)考古學\narchaeologist(n.)考古學家\narchaeological(adj.)考古學的\nmarine archaeology 水下考古學\narchaeological site 考古遺址\nShe became interested in archaeology after visiting Egypt.\n(她去過埃及後對考古學產生了興趣。)\nArchaeologists discovered pottery from 4,000 years ago at the site.\n(考古學家在遺址中發現了四千年前的陶器。)"],["archive","archive(n./v.)檔案、檔案館、存檔\narchival(adj.)檔案的\nnational archives 國家檔案館\narchive files 將檔案歸檔\nThe old photographs are kept in the city archives.\n(那些老照片被保存在市立檔案館裡。)\nRemember to archive your old emails to save space.\n(記得把舊郵件封存以節省空間。)"],["arithmetic","arithmetic(n./adj.)算術、計算、算術的\narithmetical(adj.)算術的\nbasic arithmetic 基礎算術\nmental arithmetic 心算\nChildren learn basic arithmetic in elementary school.\n(孩子們在小學學基礎算術。)\nShe is very good at mental arithmetic.\n(她心算非常厲害。)"],["ascend","ascend(v.)上升、登上、攀登\nascent(n.)上升、攀登\nascending(adj.)上升的\nascend the stairs 登上樓梯\nin ascending order 依遞增順序\nThe climbers began to ascend the mountain at dawn.\n(登山客在黎明時分開始攀登那座山。)\nPlease arrange the numbers in ascending order.\n(請將這些數字由小到大排列。)"],["aspire","aspire(v.)渴望、立志\naspiration(n.)抱負、志向\naspiring(adj.)有抱負的、想成為…的\naspire to 渴望達成…\naspiring artist 有志成為藝術家的人\nMany young people aspire to become social media influencers.\n(許多年輕人立志成為網紅。)\nThe program offers support to aspiring writers.\n(這個計畫為有志寫作的人提供支持。)"],["assassinate","assassinate(v.)暗殺、行刺\nassassination(n.)暗殺\nassassin(n.)刺客\nassassinate a leader 暗殺領袖\nassassination attempt 暗殺未遂\nPresident Lincoln was assassinated in 1865.\n(林肯總統在一八六五年遇刺身亡。)\nThe politician survived an assassination attempt last year.\n(那位政治人物在去年的暗殺行動中倖存。)"],["asthma","asthma(n.)氣喘\nasthmatic(adj.)氣喘的\nasthma attack 氣喘發作\nsuffer from asthma 患有氣喘\nAir pollution can trigger an asthma attack.\n(空氣汙染可能引發氣喘發作。)\nHe always carries an inhaler because he suffers from asthma.\n(他患有氣喘，所以總是隨身攜帶吸入器。)"],["astray","astray(adv./adj.)迷路地、離開正道地\n(無詞性變化)\ngo astray 迷路、誤入歧途、遺失\nlead sb. astray 把某人帶壞\nBad friends can easily lead young people astray.\n(損友很容易把年輕人帶壞。)\nThe letter went astray and never reached her.\n(那封信寄丟了，始終沒送到她手上。)"],["astronaut","astronaut(n.)太空人\n(無詞性變化)\nbecome an astronaut 成為太空人\nastronaut training 太空人訓練\nThe astronaut spent six months on the International Space Station.\n(那位太空人在國際太空站待了六個月。)\nAstronaut training includes learning to work in zero gravity.\n(太空人訓練包括學習在無重力狀態下工作。)"],["astronomer","astronomer(n.)天文學家\nastronomy(n.)天文學\namateur astronomer 業餘天文學家\nfamous astronomer 知名天文學家\nAstronomers have discovered a new planet outside our solar system.\n(天文學家發現了太陽系外的一顆新行星。)\nGalileo was one of the first astronomers to use a telescope.\n(伽利略是最早使用望遠鏡的天文學家之一。)"],["astronomy","astronomy(n.)天文學\nastronomer(n.)天文學家\nastronomical(adj.)天文學的、龐大的\nastronomy club 天文社\nastronomical cost 天文數字的費用\nMembers of the astronomy club meet on clear nights to observe the stars.\n(天文社社員會在晴朗的夜晚聚會觀星。)\nThe cost of the new stadium was astronomical.\n(新體育館的花費是個天文數字。)"],["attain(ment)","attain(v.)達到、獲得、attainment(n.)成就、達成\nattainable(adj.)可達到的\nattain a goal 達成目標\neducational attainment 教育程度\nWith hard work, she finally attained her goal of studying medicine.\n(憑藉努力，她終於達成就讀醫學系的目標。)\nEducational attainment is closely related to income levels.\n(教育程度與收入水準密切相關。)"],["attendant","attendant(n.)服務人員、侍者、隨從\nattend(v.)出席、照料\nflight attendant 空服員\nparking attendant 停車場管理員\nThe flight attendant showed us how to fasten our seat belts.\n(空服員示範如何繫好安全帶。)\nShe worked as a gas station attendant during summer vacation.\n(她暑假在加油站當服務員。)"],["audit","audit(n.)審計、查帳、稽核\naudit(v.)查帳、旁聽(課程)\nauditor(n.)審計員\nfinancial audit 財務審計\nenergy audit 能源稽核\nThe company hired an outside firm to carry out a financial audit.\n(公司聘請外部事務所進行財務審計。)\nI audited a philosophy course at the university last semester.\n(上學期我在大學旁聽了一門哲學課。)"],["auditorium","auditorium(n.)禮堂、會堂、觀眾席\n(無詞性變化)\nschool auditorium 學校禮堂\npacked auditorium 座無虛席的禮堂\nThe graduation ceremony will be held in the school auditorium.\n(畢業典禮將在學校禮堂舉行。)\nThe speaker received a standing ovation from the packed auditorium.\n(講者獲得滿座禮堂觀眾起立鼓掌。)"],["avert","avert(v.)避免、防止、轉移(目光)\n(無詞性變化)\navert a crisis 避免危機\navert one's eyes 移開目光\nQuick action by the pilot averted a disaster.\n(機長的迅速應變避免了一場災難。)\nShe averted her eyes during the scary scenes in the movie.\n(電影出現可怕畫面時，她把目光移開。)"],["aviation","aviation(n.)航空、飛行\naviator(n.)飛行員\ncivil aviation 民航\naviation industry 航空業\nThe aviation industry was hit hard during the pandemic.\n(航空業在疫情期間受到重創。)\nHe studied aviation engineering because he loves airplanes.\n(他因為熱愛飛機而攻讀航空工程。)"],["awesome","awesome(adj.)令人驚嘆的、很棒的\nawe(n./v.)敬畏、使敬畏\nawesome view 令人驚嘆的景色\ntotally awesome 超棒的\nThe view from the top of Taipei 101 is awesome.\n(從台北101頂樓看出去的景色令人驚嘆。)\nThanks for the gift—it's totally awesome!\n(謝謝你的禮物，真是太棒了！)"],["awhile","awhile(adv.)一會兒、片刻\n(無詞性變化)\nstay awhile 待一會兒\nrest awhile 休息片刻\nWhy don't you sit down and rest awhile?\n(你何不坐下來休息一會兒？)\nLet's wait awhile before we leave.\n(我們離開前再等一會兒吧。)"],["bachelor","bachelor(n.)單身漢、學士\n(無詞性變化)\nbachelor's degree 學士學位\neligible bachelor 黃金單身漢\nShe earned a bachelor's degree in computer science from National Taiwan University.\n(她取得了台灣大學資訊工程學士學位。)\nMy uncle remained a bachelor until he was forty-five.\n(我叔叔一直單身到四十五歲。)"],["backbone","backbone(n.)脊椎、骨幹、支柱、骨氣\n(無詞性變化)\nbackbone of the economy 經濟的支柱\nhave the backbone to 有骨氣去……\nSmall and medium-sized businesses are the backbone of Taiwan's economy.\n(中小企業是台灣經濟的支柱。)\nFew people had the backbone to stand up against the unfair decision.\n(很少人有勇氣站出來反對這個不公平的決定。)"],["badge","badge(n.)徽章、名牌、象徵\n(無詞性變化)\nname badge 名牌\nbadge of honor 榮譽的象徵\nAll visitors must wear a name badge while they are in the building.\n(所有訪客在大樓內都必須配戴名牌。)\nFor the young soldier, the scar was a badge of honor rather than shame.\n(對那位年輕士兵而言，這道疤痕是榮譽的象徵，而非恥辱。)"],["banquet","banquet(n./v.)宴會、盛宴、宴請\n(無詞性變化)\nwedding banquet 婚宴\nbanquet hall 宴會廳\nMore than three hundred guests attended the wedding banquet at the hotel.\n(超過三百位賓客出席了在飯店舉辦的婚宴。)\nThe company holds a year-end banquet to thank its employees for their hard work.\n(公司舉辦尾牙宴，感謝員工一整年的辛勞。)"],["barbarian","barbarian(adj./n.)野蠻的、未開化的、野蠻人\nbarbaric(adj.)野蠻的、殘暴的\nbarbarism(n.)野蠻、未開化\nbarbarian invasion 蠻族入侵\nbarbarian tribes 蠻族部落\nThe Great Wall was built partly to keep out barbarian invaders from the north.\n(長城的建造部分是為了抵禦北方的蠻族入侵者。)\nThe ancient Romans called people outside their empire barbarians.\n(古羅馬人把帝國以外的人稱為蠻族。)"],["bass","bass(n./adj.)低音、貝斯、低音的\n(無詞性變化)\nbass guitar 電貝斯\nbass voice 男低音\nHe plays bass guitar in a rock band with his high school friends.\n(他和高中朋友組了一個搖滾樂團，擔任貝斯手。)\nThe singer's deep bass voice filled the whole concert hall.\n(那位歌手深沉的低音響徹整個音樂廳。)"],["batter","batter(n./v.)麵糊、打擊手、連續猛擊\nbattered(adj.)破舊的、受虐的\npancake batter 鬆餅麵糊\nbatter down 擊倒、打破\nPour the pancake batter into the hot pan and cook it until golden.\n(把鬆餅麵糊倒入熱鍋，煎到呈金黃色。)\nHuge waves battered the coast during the powerful typhoon.\n(強烈颱風期間，巨浪不斷猛烈拍打海岸。)"],["beautify","beautify(v.)美化、使美麗\nbeauty(n.)美、美人\nbeautiful(adj.)美麗的\nbeautify the city 美化市容\nbeautify the environment 美化環境\nThe city government planted thousands of trees to beautify the riverside park.\n(市政府種了數千棵樹來美化河濱公園。)\nStudents painted murals on the walls to beautify their campus.\n(學生們在牆上畫壁畫來美化校園。)"],["beep","beep(n./v.)嗶嗶聲、發出嗶嗶聲\nbeeper(n.)呼叫器\nafter the beep 嗶聲之後\nbeep the horn 按喇叭\nPlease leave a message after the beep, and I will call you back.\n(請在嗶聲後留言，我會回電給你。)\nThe microwave beeped to let us know the food was ready.\n(微波爐嗶嗶作響，告訴我們食物已經好了。)"],["beforehand","beforehand(adv.)事先、預先\n(無詞性變化)\nknow beforehand 事先知道\nprepare beforehand 事先準備\nIf you are going to be late, please let me know beforehand.\n(如果你會遲到，請事先告訴我。)\nThe speech went smoothly because she had prepared well beforehand.\n(因為她事先做了充分準備，演講進行得很順利。)"],["beverage","beverage(n.)飲料\n(無詞性變化)\nalcoholic beverage 含酒精飲料\nhot beverage 熱飲\nSugary beverages are one of the main causes of tooth decay among teenagers.\n(含糖飲料是青少年蛀牙的主要原因之一。)\nThe sale of alcoholic beverages to people under eighteen is prohibited.\n(禁止販售含酒精飲料給未滿十八歲的人。)"],["bilateral","bilateral(adj.)雙邊的、雙方的、兩側的\n(無詞性變化)\nbilateral trade 雙邊貿易\nbilateral agreement 雙邊協定\nThe two countries signed a bilateral agreement to promote cultural exchange.\n(兩國簽署了一項促進文化交流的雙邊協定。)\nBilateral trade between Taiwan and Japan has grown steadily in recent years.\n(台日之間的雙邊貿易近年來穩定成長。)"],["blaze","blaze(n./v.)火焰、大火、熊熊燃燒、閃耀\nblazing(adj.)熾熱的、燃燒的\nblaze of glory 光榮的時刻\nblazing sun 烈日\nFirefighters struggled for hours to put out the blaze in the factory.\n(消防員奮戰了好幾個小時才撲滅工廠的大火。)\nThe farmers kept working under the blazing summer sun.\n(農夫們在炎炎夏日下持續工作。)"],["bleach","bleach(n./v.)漂白劑、漂白\n(無詞性變化)\nbleach one's hair 漂髮\nhousehold bleach 家用漂白水\nShe bleached her hair blonde during summer vacation.\n(她在暑假期間把頭髮漂成金色。)\nNever mix household bleach with other cleaning products, because it can produce toxic gas.\n(絕對不要把家用漂白水和其他清潔劑混合，因為可能會產生有毒氣體。)"],["blond/blonde","blond(n./adj.)金髮的、金髮的人\nblonde(n./adj.)金髮的、金髮女子\nblond hair 金髮\nblue-eyed blonde 碧眼金髮女子\nThe little boy with curly blond hair is my cousin from Australia.\n(那個有一頭金色捲髮的小男孩是我來自澳洲的表弟。)\nThe actress dyed her hair blonde for her new movie role.\n(那位女演員為了新電影角色把頭髮染成金色。)"],["blot","blot(v./n.)弄髒、吸乾、汙漬、汙點\n(無詞性變化)\nink blot 墨漬\nblot out 遮蔽、抹去\nThe scandal was a blot on the politician's otherwise clean record.\n(這起醜聞是那位政治人物原本清白紀錄上的一個汙點。)\nThick clouds blotted out the sun for most of the afternoon.\n(厚厚的雲層在下午大部分時間都遮蔽了太陽。)"],["blunt","blunt(adj./v.)鈍的、直率的、使變鈍\nbluntly(adv.)直率地、坦白地\nblunt knife 鈍刀\nto put it bluntly 坦白說\nThis knife is too blunt to cut the tomatoes properly.\n(這把刀太鈍了，切不好番茄。)\nTo put it bluntly, your essay needs a lot more work before you hand it in.\n(坦白說，你的作文在繳交之前還需要大幅修改。)"],["bodily","bodily(adj./adv.)身體的、肉體的、整個地\nbody(n.)身體\nbodily harm 身體傷害\nbodily functions 身體機能\nThe law protects citizens from threats of bodily harm.\n(法律保護公民免受身體傷害的威脅。)\nWater is essential for maintaining normal bodily functions.\n(水對維持正常的身體機能至關重要。)"],["booklet","booklet(n.)小冊子\nbook(n./v.)書、預訂\ninformation booklet 資訊手冊\ntest booklet 試題本\nEach new student received an information booklet about school rules.\n(每位新生都收到一本有關校規的資訊手冊。)\nPlease write your answers on the answer sheet, not in the test booklet.\n(請將答案寫在答案卡上，不要寫在試題本裡。)"],["bosom","bosom(n.)胸懷、內心、胸部\n(無詞性變化)\nbosom friend 知己、密友\nin the bosom of one's family 在家人的懷抱中\nThe two girls have been bosom friends since elementary school.\n(這兩個女孩從小學開始就是知心好友。)\nAfter years abroad, he was happy to be back in the bosom of his family.\n(在國外多年後，他很高興能回到家人的懷抱。)"],["boulevard","boulevard(n.)林蔭大道、大街\n(無詞性變化)\ntree-lined boulevard 綠樹成蔭的大道\nbroad boulevard 寬闊的大道\nWe strolled along the tree-lined boulevard on a quiet Sunday morning.\n(在一個寧靜的週日早晨，我們沿著綠樹成蔭的大道散步。)\nMany famous shops and cafés line the wide boulevard in Paris.\n(巴黎那條寬闊的林蔭大道兩旁有許多知名商店和咖啡館。)"],["boxing","boxing(n.)拳擊\nbox(v./n.)拳擊、盒子\nboxer(n.)拳擊手\nboxing match 拳擊比賽\nboxing gloves 拳擊手套\nHe took up boxing to stay fit and relieve stress after work.\n(他開始練拳擊，以保持身材並紓解下班後的壓力。)\nThousands of fans watched the boxing match on live TV.\n(數千名粉絲透過電視直播觀看了那場拳擊賽。)"],["boycott","boycott(n./v.)聯合抵制、杯葛\n(無詞性變化)\ncall for a boycott 呼籲抵制\nconsumer boycott 消費者抵制\nConsumers called for a boycott of the brand after the food safety scandal.\n(食安醜聞發生後，消費者呼籲抵制該品牌。)\nSeveral countries boycotted the Olympic Games for political reasons.\n(有幾個國家因政治因素杯葛奧運會。)"],["brace","brace(n./v.)支架、牙套、使做好準備\nbracing(adj.)令人振奮的、清新的\nbrace oneself for 做好……的準備\nwear braces 戴牙套\nResidents were told to brace themselves for the strong typhoon.\n(居民被告知要為強烈颱風做好準備。)\nMy sister has to wear braces on her teeth for two years.\n(我妹妹必須戴兩年牙套。)"],["brassiere/bra","brassiere(n.)胸罩、內衣\nbra(n.)胸罩(口語)\nsports bra 運動內衣\nbra size 胸罩尺寸\nFemale runners usually wear a sports bra for comfort and support.\n(女性跑者通常會穿運動內衣以求舒適和支撐。)\nThe word brassiere is rarely used today; most people simply say bra.\n(brassiere 這個字現在很少用，多數人只說 bra。)"],["breadth","breadth(n.)寬度、廣度\nbroad(adj.)寬的、廣泛的\nbroaden(v.)加寬、拓寬\nbreadth of knowledge 知識的廣度\nlength and breadth 長和寬、全境\nThe professor impressed us with the breadth of his knowledge.\n(那位教授知識之廣博令我們印象深刻。)\nThey traveled the length and breadth of Taiwan on their bicycles.\n(他們騎腳踏車走遍了台灣各地。)"],["breakdown","breakdown(n.)故障、崩潰、細目分析\nbreak down(v.)故障、崩潰、分解\nnervous breakdown 精神崩潰\nbreakdown of ……的破裂、分析\nOur car had a breakdown on the highway, so we had to call for help.\n(我們的車在高速公路上拋錨，所以只好求救。)\nThe report includes a detailed breakdown of how the money was spent.\n(這份報告包含了經費使用的詳細分析。)"],["breakup","breakup(n.)分手、解散、瓦解\nbreak up(v.)分手、解散\npainful breakup 痛苦的分手\nbreakup of the band 樂團解散\nAfter a painful breakup, she decided to focus on her studies.\n(經歷一段痛苦的分手後，她決定專心念書。)\nFans were shocked by the sudden breakup of the popular band.\n(那個受歡迎的樂團突然解散，讓歌迷們十分震驚。)"],["bribe","bribe(n./v.)賄賂、賄款\nbribery(n.)行賄、受賄\naccept a bribe 收賄\nbribe someone into 收買某人做……\nThe official was arrested for accepting bribes from a construction company.\n(那名官員因收受營建公司的賄賂而被捕。)\nThe mother tried to bribe her son into doing homework with ice cream.\n(那位媽媽試圖用冰淇淋收買兒子去寫功課。)"],["brink","brink(n.)邊緣、初始\n(無詞性變化)\non the brink of 瀕臨……\nbrink of extinction 瀕臨絕種\nMany species of frogs are on the brink of extinction because of habitat loss.\n(許多種青蛙因棲地消失而瀕臨絕種。)\nThe two countries were on the brink of war before the talks began.\n(談判開始前，兩國已處於戰爭邊緣。)"],["broaden","broaden(v.)擴大、拓寬\nbroad(adj.)寬的、廣泛的\nbreadth(n.)寬度、廣度\nbroaden one's horizons 開拓視野\nbroaden the road 拓寬道路\nStudying abroad can greatly broaden your horizons.\n(出國留學能大幅開拓你的視野。)\nThe city plans to broaden the road to reduce traffic jams.\n(市政府計劃拓寬道路以減少交通壅塞。)"],["brochure","brochure(n.)小冊子、宣傳手冊\n(無詞性變化)\ntravel brochure 旅遊手冊\nfree brochure 免費手冊\nThe travel agent gave us a brochure with information about tours to Europe.\n(旅行社業務給了我們一本介紹歐洲行程的手冊。)\nYou can pick up a free brochure about the museum at the front desk.\n(你可以在服務台索取免費的博物館簡介手冊。)"],["broil","broil(v.)燒烤、炙烤、酷熱\nbroiler(n.)烤架、烤箱、肉雞\nbroiled fish 烤魚\nbroil the steak 烤牛排\nMy father broiled the salmon with lemon and salt for dinner.\n(我爸爸晚餐用檸檬和鹽炙烤鮭魚。)\nBroiled chicken is a healthier choice than fried chicken.\n(烤雞比炸雞是更健康的選擇。)"],["brook","brook(n.)小溪、小河\n(無詞性變化)\nbabbling brook 潺潺小溪\nmountain brook 山澗\nWe sat by the babbling brook and listened to the birds singing.\n(我們坐在潺潺的小溪旁，聆聽鳥兒歌唱。)\nThe children caught small fish in the clear mountain brook.\n(孩子們在清澈的山澗裡抓小魚。)"],["broth","broth(n.)清湯、肉湯\n(無詞性變化)\nchicken broth 雞湯\nbeef broth 牛肉高湯\nWhen I had a cold, my grandmother made me a bowl of warm chicken broth.\n(我感冒時，奶奶替我煮了一碗溫熱的雞湯。)\nThe secret of good beef noodles lies in the rich broth.\n(好吃牛肉麵的祕訣在於濃郁的湯頭。)"],["brotherhood","brotherhood(n.)兄弟情誼、手足之情、同業團體\nbrother(n.)兄弟\nbrotherly(adj.)兄弟般的\nsense of brotherhood 兄弟情誼\nuniversal brotherhood 四海之內皆兄弟\nPlaying on the same team gave the players a strong sense of brotherhood.\n(在同一支隊伍打球讓球員們產生了深厚的兄弟情誼。)\nThe festival celebrates peace and the brotherhood of all people.\n(這個節慶歌頌和平與四海一家的情誼。)"],["bulky","bulky(adj.)龐大的、笨重的\nbulk(n.)大量、大部分、體積\nbulky item 大型物品\nbulky furniture 笨重的家具\nBulky items such as sofas cannot be thrown away with regular garbage.\n(沙發等大型物品不能和一般垃圾一起丟棄。)\nThe winter jacket is warm but too bulky to pack in a small suitcase.\n(這件冬季外套很保暖，但太笨重，放不進小行李箱。)"],["bureaucrat","bureaucrat(n.)官僚、公務員\nbureaucracy(n.)官僚體制\nbureaucratic(adj.)官僚的\nsenior bureaucrat 高階官員\nfaceless bureaucrat 無名小官僚\nSome people complain that decisions are made by bureaucrats who don't understand local needs.\n(有些人抱怨決策是由不了解地方需求的官僚所制定的。)\nA senior bureaucrat from the ministry explained the new policy to the press.\n(部會的一名高階官員向媒體說明新政策。)"],["bypass","bypass(n./v.)繞道、旁路、繞過、規避\n(無詞性變化)\nheart bypass 心臟繞道手術\nbypass the city center 繞過市中心\nThe new highway allows drivers to bypass the crowded city center.\n(新的公路讓駕駛人可以繞過擁擠的市中心。)\nSome students tried to bypass the school's Internet filter.\n(有些學生試圖規避學校的網路過濾系統。)"],["caffeine","caffeine(n.)咖啡因\ncaffeinated(adj.)含咖啡因的\ndecaffeinated(adj.)去除咖啡因的\ncaffeine intake 咖啡因攝取量\ncaffeine-free 不含咖啡因的\nDrinking too much caffeine late at night can make it hard to fall asleep.\n(深夜攝取過多咖啡因會讓人難以入睡。)\nMany students rely on caffeine to stay awake while studying for exams.\n(許多學生在準備考試時依賴咖啡因來保持清醒。)"],["calculator","calculator(n.)計算機\ncalculate(v.)計算\ncalculation(n.)計算\nscientific calculator 工程用計算機\npocket calculator 口袋型計算機\nStudents are not allowed to use calculators on the math section of the exam.\n(學生在考試的數學部分不准使用計算機。)\nShe quickly added up the bill on her calculator.\n(她用計算機很快地算出帳單總額。)"],["calligraphy","calligraphy(n.)書法\ncalligrapher(n.)書法家\nChinese calligraphy 中國書法\npractice calligraphy 練書法\nMy grandfather practices Chinese calligraphy every morning to calm his mind.\n(我爺爺每天早上練書法來沉澱心情。)\nThe art exhibition features beautiful works of calligraphy from the Tang Dynasty.\n(這場藝術展展出唐朝優美的書法作品。)"],["cape","cape(n.)海角、岬、披肩、斗篷\n(無詞性變化)\nCape of Good Hope 好望角\nred cape 紅色斗篷\nEluanbi is a famous cape at the southern tip of Taiwan.\n(鵝鑾鼻是位於台灣最南端的著名海角。)\nIn the movie, the superhero wears a long red cape.\n(電影中，那位超級英雄披著一件長長的紅色斗篷。)"],["capsule","capsule(n.)膠囊、太空艙\n(無詞性變化)\ntime capsule 時光膠囊\nspace capsule 太空艙\nOur class buried a time capsule to be opened in twenty years.\n(我們班埋了一個時光膠囊，二十年後再打開。)\nTake one capsule with water after each meal.\n(每餐飯後配水服用一顆膠囊。)"],["caption","caption(n./v.)(圖片的)說明文字、字幕、加上說明\n(無詞性變化)\nphoto caption 照片說明\nwrite a caption 寫說明文字\nShe spent ten minutes thinking of a clever caption for her Instagram post.\n(她花了十分鐘想一句巧妙的文字搭配她的 Instagram 貼文。)\nThe photo was captioned 'Sunset over Tamsui River.'\n(這張照片的說明文字是「淡水河上的夕陽」。)"],["captive","captive(adj./n.)被俘虜的、被關住的、俘虜\ncaptivity(n.)囚禁\ncaptivate(v.)迷住\nhold someone captive 囚禁某人\ncaptive audience 不得不聽的聽眾\nThe rebels held the journalists captive for three months.\n(叛軍將那些記者囚禁了三個月。)\nPassengers on a long flight are a captive audience for advertisers.\n(長途班機上的乘客是廣告商無處可逃的觀眾。)"],["captivity","captivity(n.)囚禁、圈養\ncaptive(adj./n.)被俘的、俘虜\nin captivity 被囚禁、被圈養\nrelease from captivity 從囚禁中釋放\nAnimals born in captivity may not survive if released into the wild.\n(圈養出生的動物若被野放，可能無法存活。)\nThe hostages were finally released after two years of captivity.\n(人質在被囚禁兩年後終於獲釋。)"],["cardboard","cardboard(n.)硬紙板、厚紙板\n(無詞性變化)\ncardboard box 紙箱\nrecycle cardboard 回收紙板\nWe packed all our books into cardboard boxes before moving.\n(搬家前我們把所有的書裝進紙箱。)\nThe students built a model city out of recycled cardboard.\n(學生們用回收的厚紙板搭建了一座模型城市。)"],["cardinal","cardinal(n./adj.)樞機主教、紅雀、基本的、首要的\n(無詞性變化)\ncardinal rule 基本原則\ncardinal number 基數\nThe cardinal rule of science is that results must be tested and repeated.\n(科學的基本原則是結果必須經過檢驗並可重複。)\nA cardinal is a senior official in the Catholic Church.\n(樞機主教是天主教會的高階神職人員。)"],["carefree","carefree(adj.)無憂無慮的\n(無詞性變化)\ncarefree days 無憂無慮的日子\ncarefree childhood 無憂無慮的童年\nI often think back to the carefree days of my childhood.\n(我常常回想起童年無憂無慮的日子。)\nThe students looked relaxed and carefree after their final exams.\n(期末考結束後，學生們看起來放鬆又無憂無慮。)"],["caretaker","caretaker(n.)看護、照顧者、管理員\n(無詞性變化)\nfull-time caretaker 全職照顧者\nschool caretaker 學校工友\nAfter her father's stroke, she became his full-time caretaker.\n(她父親中風後，她成了他的全職照顧者。)\nThe caretaker locks the school gate every night at ten.\n(管理員每晚十點鎖上校門。)"],["carton","carton(n.)紙盒、紙箱\n(無詞性變化)\nmilk carton 牛奶紙盒\na carton of eggs 一盒蛋\nPlease rinse the milk carton before putting it in the recycling bin.\n(把牛奶紙盒放進回收桶前請先沖洗乾淨。)\nMom asked me to buy a carton of eggs on my way home.\n(媽媽要我回家路上買一盒蛋。)"],["cashier","cashier(n.)收銀員、出納員\ncash(n./v.)現金、兌現\npay the cashier 付錢給收銀員\ncashier counter 收銀台\nPlease pay the cashier at the front of the store.\n(請到店門口的收銀台付款。)\nShe works part-time as a cashier at a convenience store.\n(她在便利商店兼職當收銀員。)"],["casualty","casualty(n.)傷亡人員、受害者\ncasual(adj.)偶然的、非正式的\nheavy casualties 慘重的傷亡\ncasualty figures 傷亡人數\nThe earthquake caused heavy casualties in the mountain villages.\n(那場地震在山區村莊造成慘重傷亡。)\nSmall businesses were the first casualties of the economic crisis.\n(小型企業是這次經濟危機的首批受害者。)"],["catastrophe","catastrophe(n.)大災難、災禍\ncatastrophic(adj.)災難性的\nnatural catastrophe 天災\nenvironmental catastrophe 環境浩劫\nScientists warn that rising sea levels could lead to a global catastrophe.\n(科學家警告海平面上升可能導致全球性大災難。)\nThe oil spill was an environmental catastrophe for the coastline.\n(這次漏油事件對海岸線而言是一場環境浩劫。)"],["cater","cater(v.)提供餐飲、迎合、滿足需要\ncatering(n.)外燴\ncaterer(n.)外燴業者\ncater to 迎合、滿足\ncater a party 為派對提供外燴\nThe restaurant caters to customers who prefer vegetarian food.\n(這家餐廳迎合偏好素食的顧客。)\nA local company catered the wedding banquet.\n(一家當地公司承辦了這場婚宴的餐飲。)"],["caterpillar","caterpillar(n.)毛毛蟲\n(無詞性變化)\nhungry caterpillar 好餓的毛毛蟲\ncaterpillar stage 幼蟲階段\nA caterpillar eventually turns into a beautiful butterfly.\n(毛毛蟲最終會變成美麗的蝴蝶。)\nThe caterpillars ate almost all the leaves on the lemon tree.\n(毛毛蟲幾乎吃光了檸檬樹上所有的葉子。)"],["cavity","cavity(n.)蛀牙、蛀洞、腔、洞\n(無詞性變化)\ndental cavity 蛀牙\nchest cavity 胸腔\nEating too much sugar can cause cavities in your teeth.\n(吃太多糖會導致蛀牙。)\nThe dentist found two cavities during my checkup.\n(牙醫在檢查時發現我有兩顆蛀牙。)"],["celery","celery(n.)芹菜\n(無詞性變化)\ncelery stick 芹菜條\nstir-fried celery 炒芹菜\nCelery is low in calories and high in fiber.\n(芹菜熱量低而且纖維含量高。)\nShe dipped a celery stick into the peanut butter.\n(她把一根芹菜條沾上花生醬。)"],["cellular","cellular(adj.)細胞的、蜂巢式(行動)通訊的\ncell(n.)細胞\ncellular phone 行動電話\ncellular structure 細胞結構\nScientists study the cellular structure of plants under a microscope.\n(科學家在顯微鏡下研究植物的細胞結構。)\nCellular networks allow us to use the Internet almost anywhere.\n(行動網路讓我們幾乎在任何地方都能上網。)"],["Celsius","Celsius(n.)攝氏\n(無詞性變化)\ndegrees Celsius 攝氏度\nCelsius scale 攝氏溫標\nWater boils at 100 degrees Celsius at sea level.\n(在海平面，水在攝氏一百度沸騰。)\nThe temperature in Taipei reached 38 degrees Celsius yesterday.\n(台北昨天的氣溫高達攝氏三十八度。)"],["cement","cement(n./v.)水泥、黏合劑、鞏固\n(無詞性變化)\ncement floor 水泥地\ncement a relationship 鞏固關係\nThe workers mixed sand and cement to make concrete.\n(工人們把沙和水泥混合製成混凝土。)\nThe trip helped cement the friendship between the two classes.\n(這趟旅行有助於鞏固兩班之間的友誼。)"],["census","census(n.)人口普查\n(無詞性變化)\nnational census 全國人口普查\ncensus data 人口普查資料\nThe government conducts a national census every ten years.\n(政府每十年進行一次全國人口普查。)\nAccording to census data, the population of the city is getting older.\n(根據人口普查資料，這座城市的人口正在老化。)"],["ceramic","ceramic(adj./n.)陶瓷的、陶瓷製品\nceramics(n.)陶瓷藝術、陶藝\nceramic tile 瓷磚\nceramic bowl 陶瓷碗\nYingge is famous for its handmade ceramic products.\n(鶯歌以手工陶瓷製品聞名。)\nThe bathroom floor is covered with white ceramic tiles.\n(浴室地板鋪著白色瓷磚。)"],["certify","certify(v.)證明、認證、發證書給\ncertificate(n.)證書\ncertification(n.)認證\ncertified(adj.)經認證的\ncertified teacher 合格教師\ncertify as 認證為\nThis document certifies that you have completed the course.\n(本文件證明你已修畢此課程。)\nOnly certified electricians are allowed to do this kind of work.\n(只有合格的電工才能做這類工作。)"],["chairperson/chair/chairman/chairwoman","chairperson(n.)主席(性別中立)\nchair(n.)主席\nchairman(n.)主席(男)、董事長\nchairwoman(n.)女主席\nelect a chairperson 選出主席\nchairman of the board 董事長\nThe committee elected a new chairperson at its first meeting.\n(委員會在第一次會議中選出新主席。)\nThe chairman of the company announced his retirement yesterday.\n(那家公司的董事長昨天宣布退休。)"],["champagne","champagne(n.)香檳酒\n(無詞性變化)\na bottle of champagne 一瓶香檳\nchampagne toast 香檳舉杯慶祝\nThey opened a bottle of champagne to celebrate their victory.\n(他們開了一瓶香檳慶祝勝利。)\nGuests raised their glasses for a champagne toast to the newlyweds.\n(賓客們舉起香檳杯向新人敬酒。)"],["chant","chant(n./v.)反覆吟唱、呼口號、讚美詩\n(無詞性變化)\nchant slogans 呼口號\nBuddhist chant 佛教誦經\nThe fans chanted the player's name as he walked onto the field.\n(那位球員走進球場時，球迷們齊聲高喊他的名字。)\nWe could hear the monks chanting in the temple.\n(我們能聽到僧侶在寺裡誦經。)"],["charitable","charitable(adj.)慈善的、寬厚的\ncharity(n.)慈善、慈善機構\ncharitable organization 慈善機構\ncharitable donation 慈善捐款\nShe donates part of her salary to charitable organizations every year.\n(她每年把一部分薪水捐給慈善機構。)\nTry to be charitable when judging other people's mistakes.\n(評斷別人的錯誤時，試著寬厚一點。)"],["checkup","checkup(n.)健康檢查、檢查\ncheck(v./n.)檢查\nannual checkup 年度健康檢查\ndental checkup 牙齒檢查\nDoctors recommend getting a medical checkup at least once a year.\n(醫生建議至少每年做一次健康檢查。)\nI have a dental checkup next Monday afternoon.\n(我下週一下午要做牙齒檢查。)"],["chemist","chemist(n.)化學家、藥劑師(英式)\nchemistry(n.)化學\nchemical(adj./n.)化學的、化學物質\nresearch chemist 研究化學家\norganic chemist 有機化學家\nMarie Curie was a famous chemist who won two Nobel Prizes.\n(居禮夫人是一位曾獲兩座諾貝爾獎的知名化學家。)\nThe chemist developed a new material that can absorb carbon dioxide.\n(那位化學家開發出一種能吸收二氧化碳的新材料。)"],["chestnut","chestnut(n./adj.)栗子、栗樹、栗色的\n(無詞性變化)\nroasted chestnuts 糖炒栗子\nchestnut hair 栗色頭髮\nThe smell of roasted chestnuts filled the street in winter.\n(冬天街上瀰漫著糖炒栗子的香味。)\nThe girl with chestnut hair is our new classmate.\n(那位栗色頭髮的女孩是我們的新同學。)"],["chili","chili(n.)辣椒\n(無詞性變化)\nchili sauce 辣椒醬\nchili pepper 辣椒\nHe added a spoonful of chili sauce to his noodles.\n(他在麵裡加了一湯匙辣椒醬。)\nThai food often uses fresh chili peppers and lime.\n(泰國菜常使用新鮮辣椒和萊姆。)"],["chimpanzee","chimpanzee(n.)黑猩猩\nchimp(n.)黑猩猩(口語)\nwild chimpanzee 野生黑猩猩\nchimpanzee behavior 黑猩猩的行為\nJane Goodall spent decades studying wild chimpanzees in Africa.\n(動物學家古德花了數十年在非洲研究野生黑猩猩。)\nChimpanzees are able to use simple tools to find food.\n(黑猩猩能夠使用簡單的工具來找食物。)"],["chirp","chirp(n./v.)(鳥、蟲)啁啾聲、發出啁啾聲\nchirpy(adj.)活潑快樂的\nbirds chirp 鳥兒啁啾\nthe chirp of crickets 蟋蟀的唧唧聲\nI woke up to the sound of birds chirping outside my window.\n(我在窗外鳥兒的啁啾聲中醒來。)\nThe chirp of crickets filled the quiet summer night.\n(蟋蟀的唧唧聲充滿了寧靜的夏夜。)"],["cholesterol","cholesterol(n.)膽固醇\n(無詞性變化)\nhigh cholesterol 高膽固醇\ncholesterol level 膽固醇濃度\nEating too much fried food can raise your cholesterol level.\n(吃太多油炸食物會使膽固醇升高。)\nThe doctor advised him to eat more vegetables to lower his cholesterol.\n(醫生建議他多吃蔬菜以降低膽固醇。)"],["cigar","cigar(n.)雪茄\ncigarette(n.)香菸\nsmoke a cigar 抽雪茄\nCuban cigar 古巴雪茄\nThe old man sat on the porch, slowly smoking a cigar.\n(那位老人坐在門廊上，慢慢地抽著雪茄。)\nCigar smoke filled the small room and made me cough.\n(雪茄的煙霧充滿了小房間，嗆得我直咳嗽。)"],["civilize","civilize(v.)使文明、教化\ncivilization(n.)文明\ncivilized(adj.)文明的、有禮的\ncivilized society 文明社會\ncivilized behavior 有禮貌的行為\nIn a civilized society, people settle disputes through discussion rather than violence.\n(在文明社會中，人們透過討論而非暴力解決爭端。)\nColonists once believed they had a duty to civilize other peoples, a view now widely criticized.\n(殖民者曾認為自己有責任教化其他民族，這種觀點如今廣受批評。)"],["clam","clam(n.)蛤蜊、蚌\n(無詞性變化)\nclam soup 蛤蜊湯\nclam up 閉口不言\nMom made a pot of clam soup with ginger.\n(媽媽煮了一鍋加薑的蛤蜊湯。)\nWhenever the teacher asks about the broken window, he clams up.\n(每當老師問起打破的窗戶，他就閉口不言。)"],["clasp","clasp(v./n.)緊握、扣住、扣環、緊握\n(無詞性變化)\nclasp one's hands 雙手緊握\nnecklace clasp 項鍊扣環\nShe clasped her hands together and prayed for her sick grandmother.\n(她雙手緊握，為生病的奶奶祈禱。)\nThe clasp on my necklace broke, so I had to get it repaired.\n(我項鍊的扣環壞了，所以得拿去修理。)"],["clearance","clearance(n.)清除、出清、許可、間隙\nclear(v./adj.)清除、清楚的\nclearance sale 清倉大拍賣\nsecurity clearance 安全許可\nThe department store is having a clearance sale this weekend.\n(那家百貨公司這個週末舉辦清倉大拍賣。)\nThe pilot was waiting for clearance to take off.\n(機長正在等待起飛許可。)"],["climax","climax(n./v.)高潮、頂點、達到高潮\nclimactic(adj.)高潮的\nreach a climax 達到高潮\nthe climax of the story 故事的高潮\nThe concert reached its climax when the band played their most famous song.\n(樂團演奏他們最有名的歌曲時，音樂會達到高潮。)\nThe climax of the novel comes when the detective finally reveals the killer.\n(小說的高潮出現在偵探終於揭露兇手的時候。)"],["clockwise","clockwise(adv./adj.)順時針方向地、順時針方向的\ncounterclockwise(adv./adj.)逆時針方向地\nturn clockwise 順時針轉\nclockwise direction 順時針方向\nTurn the knob clockwise to increase the volume.\n(把旋鈕順時針轉以調高音量。)\nThe runners circled the track in a counterclockwise direction, not clockwise.\n(跑者們沿著跑道逆時針方向而非順時針方向繞圈。)"],["clone","clone(n./v.)複製品、複製生物、複製\ncloning(n.)複製技術\nhuman cloning 複製人技術\nclone an animal 複製動物\nDolly the sheep was the first mammal to be cloned from an adult cell.\n(桃莉羊是第一隻由成體細胞複製出來的哺乳動物。)\nMany cheap smartphones are simply clones of popular brands.\n(許多廉價智慧型手機只不過是知名品牌的仿製品。)"],["closure","closure(n.)關閉、結束、了結\nclose(v.)關閉\nroad closure 道路封閉\nschool closure 停課、學校關閉\nThe road closure caused heavy traffic during rush hour.\n(道路封閉在尖峰時段造成嚴重塞車。)\nTalking with her ex-boyfriend helped her find closure.\n(和前男友談過之後，她終於能夠釋懷。)"],["coalition","coalition(n.)聯盟、聯合政府\n(無詞性變化)\ncoalition government 聯合政府\nform a coalition 組成聯盟\nThe two parties formed a coalition after neither won a majority.\n(兩黨在都沒有取得多數席次後組成了聯盟。)\nA coalition of environmental groups protested against the new factory.\n(環保團體聯盟抗議興建新工廠。)"],["coastline","coastline(n.)海岸線\ncoast(n.)海岸\nrocky coastline 岩岸\nalong the coastline 沿著海岸線\nWe rode our bikes along the beautiful coastline of eastern Taiwan.\n(我們沿著台灣東部美麗的海岸線騎腳踏車。)\nRising sea levels are slowly changing the island's coastline.\n(海平面上升正慢慢改變島嶼的海岸線。)"],["collision","collision(n.)碰撞、衝突\ncollide(v.)碰撞、衝突\nhead-on collision 迎面相撞\ncollision with 與…相撞\nThree people were injured in a head-on collision on the highway.\n(公路上一起迎面相撞的車禍造成三人受傷。)\nThe ship was badly damaged in a collision with an iceberg.\n(那艘船與冰山相撞後嚴重受損。)"],["colloquial","colloquial(adj.)口語的、白話的\ncolloquialism(n.)口語用語\ncolloquially(adv.)口語地\ncolloquial English 口語英文\ncolloquial expression 口語說法\n'Gonna' is a colloquial form of 'going to' and should be avoided in formal writing.\n('Gonna' 是 'going to' 的口語形式，在正式寫作中應避免使用。)\nWatching TV dramas is a good way to learn colloquial English.\n(看影集是學習口語英文的好方法。)"],["comet","comet(n.)彗星\n(無詞性變化)\nHalley's Comet 哈雷彗星\ncomet tail 彗尾\nHalley's Comet can be seen from Earth about every 76 years.\n(從地球上大約每七十六年可以看到一次哈雷彗星。)\nAstronomers discovered a new comet heading toward the sun.\n(天文學家發現了一顆朝太陽前進的新彗星。)"],["commonplace","commonplace(adj./n.)平凡的、常見的、司空見慣的事\n(無詞性變化)\nbecome commonplace 變得司空見慣\ncommonplace event 平常的事\nOnline classes, once rare, have now become commonplace.\n(曾經少見的線上課程現在已經變得司空見慣。)\nElectric scooters are now a commonplace sight in Taiwanese cities.\n(電動機車如今在台灣城市中隨處可見。)"],["commonwealth","commonwealth(n.)聯邦、共和國、國協\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Commonwealth (of Nations) 大英國協\nCommonwealth Games 大英國協運動會\nCanada and Australia are both members of the Commonwealth.\n(加拿大與澳洲都是大英國協的成員。)\nAthletes from over seventy nations compete in the Commonwealth Games.\n(來自七十多個國家的運動員參加大英國協運動會。)"],["communicative","communicative(adj.)溝通的、健談的\ncommunicate(v.)溝通\ncommunication(n.)溝通、通訊\ncommunicative skills 溝通技巧\ncommunicative approach 溝通式教學法\nTeachers today often use a communicative approach to teaching English.\n(現今的老師常用溝通式教學法來教英文。)\nHe is usually quiet, but he becomes quite communicative when talking about baseball.\n(他平常很安靜，但一聊到棒球就變得很健談。)"],["comparative","comparative(adj.)比較的、相對的\ncompare(v.)比較\ncomparison(n.)比較\ncomparatively(adv.)比較地、相對地\ncomparative study 比較研究\ncomparative form 比較級\nShe wrote a comparative study of education systems in Taiwan and Finland.\n(她寫了一篇台灣與芬蘭教育制度的比較研究。)\nThe comparative form of 'good' is 'better.'\n('good' 的比較級是 'better'。)"],["compass","compass(n./v.)指南針、圓規、範圍、包圍\n(無詞性變化)\nmoral compass 道德準則\na pair of compasses 一副圓規\nHikers should carry a map and compass in case their phones lose signal.\n(登山客應攜帶地圖和指南針，以防手機沒有訊號。)\nUse a pair of compasses to draw a circle with a radius of five centimeters.\n(用圓規畫一個半徑五公分的圓。)"],["compile","compile(v.)編纂、彙編、編譯(程式)\ncompilation(n.)彙編、合輯\ncompile a list 列出清單\ncompile data 彙整資料\nThe teacher compiled a list of useful websites for our research project.\n(老師為我們的研究專題彙整了一份實用網站清單。)\nBefore running the program, you need to compile the C++ code.\n(在執行程式之前，你需要先編譯 C++ 程式碼。)"],["complement","complement(v./n.)補足、與…相配、補充物\ncomplementary(adj.)互補的\ncomplement each other 相輔相成\na perfect complement to 與…完美搭配\nThe two singers' voices complement each other beautifully.\n(這兩位歌手的歌聲相得益彰。)\nThis white wine is a perfect complement to seafood dishes.\n(這款白酒與海鮮料理是完美的搭配。)"],["complexion","complexion(n.)膚色、氣色、局面\n(無詞性變化)\nfair complexion 白皙的膚色\nchange the complexion of 改變…的局面\nShe has a fair complexion and burns easily in the sun.\n(她的膚色白皙，容易被太陽曬傷。)\nThe new evidence changed the whole complexion of the case.\n(新證據改變了整個案件的局面。)"],["comprehensive","comprehensive(adj.)全面的、綜合的、廣泛的\ncomprehension(n.)理解\ncomprehend(v.)理解\ncomprehensive study 全面研究\ncomprehensive high school 綜合高中\nThe report gives a comprehensive overview of air pollution in Taiwan.\n(這份報告全面概述了台灣的空氣汙染。)\nBefore the exam, we did a comprehensive review of everything we had learned.\n(考試前，我們全面複習了所學的所有內容。)"],["compute","compute(v.)計算、估算\ncomputation(n.)計算\ncomputer(n.)電腦\ncompute the cost 計算成本\ncompute the average 計算平均值\nThe program can compute the average score of the class in seconds.\n(這個程式能在幾秒內計算出全班的平均分數。)\nEngineers computed the cost of building the new bridge.\n(工程師們計算了興建新橋的成本。)"],["computerize","computerize(v.)使電腦化、用電腦處理\ncomputerization(n.)電腦化\ncomputerized(adj.)電腦化的\ncomputerize records 將紀錄電腦化\nfully computerized 完全電腦化的\nThe library has computerized all its records to make searching easier.\n(圖書館已將所有紀錄電腦化，讓查詢更方便。)\nMost factories today use computerized systems to control production.\n(現今大多數工廠使用電腦化系統來控制生產。)"],["comrade","comrade(n.)同志、戰友、夥伴\ncomradeship(n.)同志情誼\ncomrade in arms 戰友\nold comrade 老戰友\nThe soldier risked his life to save a wounded comrade.\n(那名士兵冒著生命危險救了一位受傷的戰友。)\nYears later, the old comrades met again to remember the war.\n(多年後，老戰友們重聚，緬懷那場戰爭。)"],["concession","concession(n.)讓步、特許權、優惠\nconcede(v.)承認、讓步\nmake concessions 做出讓步\ntax concession 稅賦優惠\nBoth sides had to make concessions to reach an agreement.\n(雙方都必須做出讓步才能達成協議。)\nStudents and seniors can buy concession tickets at a lower price.\n(學生和長者可以較低價格購買優待票。)"],["concise","concise(adj.)簡潔的、簡明的\nconcisely(adv.)簡潔地\nclear and concise 清楚而簡潔\nconcise summary 簡明摘要\nYour essay should be clear and concise, no longer than 300 words.\n(你的作文應該清楚簡潔，不超過三百字。)\nShe gave a concise summary of the main points of the meeting.\n(她簡明扼要地總結了會議的重點。)"],["condense","condense(v.)濃縮、凝結、精簡\ncondensation(n.)凝結、濃縮\ncondensed(adj.)濃縮的\ncondensed milk 煉乳\ncondense into 濃縮成…\nWater vapor condenses into tiny drops on the cold window.\n(水蒸氣在冰冷的窗戶上凝結成小水滴。)\nCan you condense your ten-page report into a one-page summary?\n(你能把十頁的報告精簡成一頁的摘要嗎？)"],["confederation","confederation(n.)聯邦、聯盟、同盟\nconfederate(adj./n.)同盟的、同盟者\nform a confederation 組成聯盟\nconfederation of states 邦聯\nSeveral tribes formed a confederation to defend their land.\n(幾個部落組成聯盟來保衛他們的土地。)\nSwitzerland is officially known as the Swiss Confederation.\n(瑞士的正式國名是瑞士聯邦。)"],["congressman/congresswoman","congressman(n.)(美國)國會議員、眾議員(男)\ncongresswoman(n.)(美國)國會議員、眾議員(女)\ncongress(n.)國會、代表大會\nelect a congressman 選出國會議員\nlocal congressman 地方選出的眾議員\nThe congressman promised to create more jobs in his district.\n(那位眾議員承諾要在他的選區創造更多工作機會。)\nThe congresswoman spoke strongly in favor of the new education bill.\n(那位女眾議員強烈表態支持新的教育法案。)"],["conquest","conquest(n.)征服、征服地、戰利品\nconquer(v.)征服、克服\nconqueror(n.)征服者\nthe conquest of 對…的征服\nSpanish conquest 西班牙的征服\nThe Spanish conquest of the Aztec Empire took place in the 16th century.\n(西班牙征服阿茲特克帝國發生在十六世紀。)\nThe conquest of Mount Everest in 1953 was a historic achievement.\n(1953年攀登聖母峰成功是一項歷史性成就。)"],["conscientious","conscientious(adj.)認真的、盡責的、本著良心的\nconscientiously(adv.)認真地\nconscience(n.)良心\nconscientious student 認真的學生\nconscientious objector 良心拒服兵役者\nShe is a conscientious student who always finishes her assignments on time.\n(她是個認真的學生，總是準時完成作業。)\nA conscientious doctor double-checks every prescription.\n(一位盡責的醫生會再三檢查每一張處方。)"],["conserve","conserve(v./n.)節約、保存、保護、蜜餞\nconservation(n.)保育、節約\nconservative(adj.)保守的\nconserve energy 節約能源\nconserve water 節約用水\nWe can conserve energy by turning off lights when we leave a room.\n(離開房間時關燈，就能節約能源。)\nDuring the drought, residents were asked to conserve water.\n(乾旱期間，居民被要求節約用水。)"],["consolation","consolation(n.)安慰、慰藉\nconsole(v.)安慰\nconsolatory(adj.)安慰的\nconsolation prize 安慰獎\nwords of consolation 安慰的話\nAlthough our team lost, we won a consolation prize.\n(雖然我們隊輸了，但我們得到了安慰獎。)\nHer friends' support was a great consolation to her after the loss.\n(在失去親人後，朋友們的支持給了她極大的慰藉。)"],["console","console(n./v.)控制台、遊戲主機、安慰\nconsolation(n.)安慰\nconsole someone 安慰某人\ngame console 遊戲主機\nShe tried to console her friend after he failed the audition.\n(朋友試鏡失敗後，她試著安慰他。)\nMy brother saved money for months to buy a new game console.\n(我弟弟存了好幾個月的錢買一台新的遊戲主機。)"],["consonant","consonant(n.)子音\nvowel(n.)母音\nconsonant sound 子音\nconsonant cluster 子音群\nThe word 'strength' begins with three consonants.\n('strength' 這個字以三個子音開頭。)\nSome learners find it hard to pronounce consonant clusters in English.\n(有些學習者覺得英文的子音群很難發音。)"],["conspiracy","conspiracy(n.)陰謀、共謀\nconspire(v.)密謀、共謀\nconspirator(n.)陰謀者\nconspiracy theory 陰謀論\nconspiracy to 密謀做…\nMany conspiracy theories spread quickly on social media without any evidence.\n(許多陰謀論在毫無證據的情況下迅速在社群媒體上傳開。)\nThe men were arrested for conspiracy to rob a bank.\n(那些男子因密謀搶劫銀行而被捕。)"],["contention","contention(n.)爭論、論點、競爭\ncontend(v.)爭奪、主張\ncontentious(adj.)有爭議的\nbone of contention 爭論的焦點\nin contention for 有望爭奪…\nThe use of nuclear power remains a major bone of contention in Taiwan.\n(核能的使用在台灣仍是主要的爭論焦點。)\nAfter winning five games in a row, our team is now in contention for the title.\n(連贏五場之後，我們隊現在有望爭奪冠軍。)"],["contestant","contestant(n.)參賽者、競爭者\ncontest(n./v.)比賽、爭奪\ntalent show contestant 才藝表演參賽者\nquiz show contestant 益智節目參賽者\nEach contestant has three minutes to give a speech.\n(每位參賽者有三分鐘的演講時間。)\nThe youngest contestant surprised the judges with her amazing voice.\n(最年輕的參賽者以她驚人的歌聲讓評審大為驚豔。)"],["continuity","continuity(n.)連續性、連貫性\ncontinue(v.)繼續\ncontinuous(adj.)連續的\nsense of continuity 連續感\nensure continuity 確保連貫性\nHaving the same teacher for three years provides continuity in students' learning.\n(三年由同一位老師任教，能讓學生的學習具有連貫性。)\nThe new manager promised continuity in the company's policies.\n(新任經理承諾公司政策將保持一貫。)"],["contradict","contradict(v.)反駁、與…矛盾\ncontradiction(n.)矛盾\ncontradictory(adj.)矛盾的\ncontradict oneself 自相矛盾\ncontradict the evidence 與證據相矛盾\nThe witness's story contradicted the evidence found at the scene.\n(那名證人的說法與現場找到的證據相矛盾。)\nHe often contradicts himself when he tries to explain why he was late.\n(他試圖解釋為何遲到時常常自相矛盾。)"],["convene","convene(v.)召開、召集、聚集\nconvention(n.)會議、慣例\nconvene a meeting 召開會議\nconvene a committee 召集委員會\nThe principal convened an emergency meeting after the typhoon damaged the gym.\n(颱風損壞體育館後，校長召開了緊急會議。)\nWorld leaders will convene in Paris next month to discuss climate change.\n(世界各國領袖下個月將齊聚巴黎討論氣候變遷。)"],["coral","coral(n./adj.)珊瑚、珊瑚色的\n(無詞性變化)\ncoral reef 珊瑚礁\ncoral bleaching 珊瑚白化\nRising ocean temperatures are causing serious damage to coral reefs.\n(海水溫度上升正對珊瑚礁造成嚴重破壞。)\nKenting is a popular place for divers to see colorful coral.\n(墾丁是潛水客觀賞繽紛珊瑚的熱門地點。)"],["corpse","corpse(n.)屍體\n(無詞性變化)\nfind a corpse 發現屍體\nidentify a corpse 指認屍體\nThe police found a corpse floating in the river early this morning.\n(今天清晨警方在河中發現一具漂浮的屍體。)\nIn the mystery novel, the detective examines the corpse for clues.\n(在這本推理小說中，偵探檢查屍體尋找線索。)"],["correspondence","correspondence(n.)通信、信件、一致、相符\ncorrespond(v.)通信、相符\ncorrespondent(n.)通訊記者、通信者\nin correspondence with 與…通信\nclose correspondence 密切的相符\nThe two scientists kept up a regular correspondence for many years.\n(這兩位科學家多年來保持定期通信。)\nThere is a close correspondence between hours of study and test results.\n(讀書時數與考試成績之間有密切的相關。)"],["cosmetic","cosmetic(adj.)美容的、表面的、裝飾性的\ncosmetics(n.)化妝品\ncosmetic surgery 整形手術\ncosmetic changes 表面上的改變\nThe new government only made cosmetic changes to the old policy.\n(新政府只對舊政策做了表面上的修改。)\nCosmetic surgery has become increasingly popular among young people.\n(整形手術在年輕人之間越來越受歡迎。)"],["cosmetics","cosmetics(n.)化妝品\ncosmetic(adj.)美容的\ncosmetics company 化妝品公司\nuse cosmetics 使用化妝品\nMany cosmetics companies no longer test their products on animals.\n(許多化妝品公司不再用動物做產品測試。)\nShe spends a lot of money on cosmetics and skin care products.\n(她花很多錢在化妝品和保養品上。)"],["counterpart","counterpart(n.)對應的人或物、對手\n(無詞性變化)\nforeign counterpart 外國的對等官員\none's counterpart in …的對應者\nThe Minister of Education met with his Japanese counterpart to discuss student exchanges.\n(教育部長與日本的教育部長會面，討論學生交流事宜。)\nTaiwanese students often study longer hours than their Western counterparts.\n(台灣學生的讀書時數往往比西方學生還長。)"],["coupon","coupon(n.)優惠券、折價券\n(無詞性變化)\ndiscount coupon 折價券\nredeem a coupon 使用優惠券\nWith this coupon, you can get 20 percent off your next purchase.\n(憑這張優惠券，下次購物可享八折優惠。)\nShe collects coupons from newspapers to save money on groceries.\n(她從報紙上收集折價券，以節省購買日用品的花費。)"],["courtyard","courtyard(n.)庭院、天井\n(無詞性變化)\ninner courtyard 內院\ntraditional courtyard house 傳統合院\nTraditional Taiwanese courtyard houses are built around an open central space.\n(台灣傳統的合院環繞著中央的空地而建。)\nThe children played badminton in the courtyard after dinner.\n(孩子們晚飯後在院子裡打羽毛球。)"],["cowardly","cowardly(adj.)膽小的、懦弱的\ncoward(n.)懦夫、膽小鬼\ncowardice(n.)懦弱\ncowardly act 懦弱的行為\ncowardly attack 卑鄙的攻擊\nBullying people online while hiding your identity is a cowardly act.\n(隱藏身分在網路上霸凌他人是懦弱的行為。)\nHe was ashamed of his cowardly decision to run away instead of helping.\n(他對自己選擇逃跑而不出手幫忙的懦弱決定感到羞愧。)"],["cozy","cozy(adj.)舒適的、溫馨的\ncoziness(n.)舒適\ncozy room 舒適的房間\ncozy atmosphere 溫馨的氣氛\nThe small café has a cozy atmosphere, perfect for reading on rainy days.\n(這間小咖啡館氣氛溫馨，很適合在雨天看書。)\nWe spent a cozy evening by the fire drinking hot chocolate.\n(我們在爐火旁喝著熱可可，度過了一個溫馨的夜晚。)"],["crackdown","crackdown(n.)取締、鎮壓\ncrack down(v.)取締、嚴厲打擊\ncrackdown on 取締…\npolice crackdown 警方取締\nThe police launched a crackdown on drunk driving during the holidays.\n(假期期間，警方展開取締酒駕的行動。)\nThe government's crackdown on fake news has raised concerns about freedom of speech.\n(政府取締假新聞的行動引發了對言論自由的擔憂。)"],["cracker","cracker(n.)餅乾(薄脆)、鞭炮\ncrack(v./n.)使破裂、裂縫\ncheese and crackers 起司配餅乾\nsoda cracker 蘇打餅乾\nShe had some crackers and cheese as an afternoon snack.\n(她吃了一些餅乾配起司當下午的點心。)\nSoda crackers are easy on the stomach when you feel sick.\n(身體不舒服時，蘇打餅乾對腸胃比較溫和。)"],["cram","cram(v.)塞滿、臨時抱佛腳\n(無詞性變化)\ncram school 補習班\ncram for an exam 為考試臨時抱佛腳\nMany students cram for exams the night before instead of studying regularly.\n(許多學生不平時讀書，而是在考前一晚臨時抱佛腳。)\nAfter school, he goes straight to cram school until nine at night.\n(放學後，他直接去補習班上課到晚上九點。)"],["cramp","cramp(n./v.)抽筋、限制、妨礙\ncramped(adj.)狹窄的、擁擠的\nleg cramp 腿抽筋\nmuscle cramp 肌肉痙攣\nHe got a leg cramp while swimming and had to be helped out of the pool.\n(他游泳時腿抽筋，只好被扶出泳池。)\nStretching before exercise can help prevent muscle cramps.\n(運動前伸展有助於預防肌肉抽筋。)"],["crater","crater(n./v.)火山口、隕石坑、坑洞、形成坑洞\n(無詞性變化)\nvolcanic crater 火山口\nimpact crater 撞擊坑\nVisitors can hike up to the edge of the volcanic crater.\n(遊客可以健行到火山口的邊緣。)\nThe surface of the moon is covered with thousands of craters.\n(月球表面布滿了數以千計的坑洞。)"],["credible","credible(adj.)可信的、可靠的\ncredibility(n.)可信度\ncredibly(adv.)可信地\ncredible source 可靠的來源\ncredible evidence 可信的證據\nAlways check whether the information comes from a credible source.\n(務必確認資訊是否來自可靠的來源。)\nThe police found no credible evidence to support his story.\n(警方找不到可信的證據來支持他的說法。)"],["crocodile","crocodile(n.)鱷魚\n(無詞性變化)\ncrocodile tears 假慈悲、鱷魚的眼淚\ncrocodile skin 鱷魚皮\nA huge crocodile was lying motionless on the riverbank.\n(一隻巨大的鱷魚一動也不動地躺在河岸上。)\nDon't believe his apology; those are just crocodile tears.\n(別相信他的道歉，那不過是假惺惺的眼淚。)"],["crossing","crossing(n.)十字路口、穿越處、橫越\ncross(v.)穿越\npedestrian crossing 行人穿越道\nborder crossing 過境處\nAlways use the pedestrian crossing when you cross a busy road.\n(穿越繁忙的馬路時務必走行人穿越道。)\nThe crossing from Keelung to Matsu takes about eight hours by boat.\n(從基隆搭船橫渡到馬祖大約需要八小時。)"],["crutch","crutch(n.)拐杖、精神支柱、依靠\n(無詞性變化)\non crutches 拄著拐杖\nemotional crutch 精神寄託\nAfter breaking his ankle, he had to walk on crutches for six weeks.\n(他腳踝骨折後，得拄著拐杖走路六週。)\nSome students use their phones as a crutch instead of thinking for themselves.\n(有些學生把手機當作依靠，而不是自己思考。)"],["cub","cub(n.)幼獸(熊、獅、虎等)、新手\n(無詞性變化)\nbear cub 小熊\ncub reporter 菜鳥記者\nThe mother bear stayed close to protect her cubs.\n(母熊待在附近保護她的小熊。)\nAs a cub reporter, she was sent to cover small local events.\n(身為菜鳥記者，她被派去採訪地方上的小活動。)"],["cucumber","cucumber(n.)小黃瓜、黃瓜\n(無詞性變化)\nas cool as a cucumber 非常冷靜\ncucumber salad 涼拌小黃瓜\nEven under pressure, she remained as cool as a cucumber.\n(即使在壓力下，她依然非常沉著冷靜。)\nWe ordered cucumber salad and beef noodles for lunch.\n(我們午餐點了涼拌小黃瓜和牛肉麵。)"],["cultivate","cultivate(v.)耕種、栽培、培養\ncultivation(n.)耕作、培養\ncultivated(adj.)有教養的、栽培的\ncultivate the land 耕種土地\ncultivate a habit 培養習慣\nIt takes time and effort to cultivate a good reading habit.\n(培養良好的閱讀習慣需要時間和努力。)\nFarmers in this area cultivate rice and tea on the hillsides.\n(這個地區的農民在山坡上種植稻米和茶。)"],["cumulative","cumulative(adj.)累積的、漸增的\naccumulate(v.)累積\ncumulatively(adv.)累積地\ncumulative effect 累積效應\ncumulative total 累計總數\nThe cumulative effect of small daily habits can be huge over time.\n(日積月累下來，日常小習慣的累積效應可能相當驚人。)\nYour final grade is based on cumulative scores from the whole semester.\n(你的學期總成績是根據整學期累積的分數計算。)"],["curb","curb(n./v.)路緣、抑制、控制\n(無詞性變化)\ncurb spending 控制開銷\npull over to the curb 靠邊停車\nThe government introduced new measures to curb air pollution.\n(政府推出了新措施來抑制空氣汙染。)\nThe taxi driver pulled over to the curb to let us out.\n(計程車司機靠邊停車讓我們下車。)"],["curfew","curfew(n.)宵禁、門禁時間\n(無詞性變化)\nimpose a curfew 實施宵禁\nbreak curfew 違反門禁\nThe government imposed a curfew after the riots broke out.\n(暴動發生後，政府實施了宵禁。)\nMy parents set a curfew of ten o'clock on school nights.\n(我爸媽規定上學日晚上十點是門禁時間。)"],["curry","curry(n.)咖哩、咖哩菜餚\n(無詞性變化)\ncurry rice 咖哩飯\ncurry powder 咖哩粉\nJapanese curry rice is one of my favorite comfort foods.\n(日式咖哩飯是我最喜歡的療癒美食之一。)\nAdd a spoonful of curry powder to give the soup more flavor.\n(加一匙咖哩粉讓湯更有風味。)"],["customary","customary(adj.)習慣上的、慣例的\ncustom(n.)習俗、習慣\ncustomarily(adv.)按照慣例\nit is customary to 按照慣例會…\ncustomary practice 慣例\nIn Taiwan, it is customary to give red envelopes during the Lunar New Year.\n(在台灣，農曆新年時習慣發紅包。)\nIt is customary for the host to make a short speech before dinner.\n(按照慣例，主人在晚宴前會簡短致詞。)"],["cynical","cynical(adj.)憤世嫉俗的、懷疑的\ncynic(n.)憤世嫉俗者\ncynicism(n.)憤世嫉俗\ncynical about 對…抱持懷疑\ncynical attitude 憤世嫉俗的態度\nMany young voters have become cynical about politics.\n(許多年輕選民已對政治感到失望懷疑。)\nDespite his cynical attitude, he volunteers at the shelter every weekend.\n(儘管他態度憤世嫉俗，他每個週末仍去收容所當志工。)"],["dazzle","dazzle(v./n.)使目眩、使讚嘆、耀眼的光\ndazzling(adj.)耀眼的、令人驚豔的\nbe dazzled by 被……迷住\ndazzle the audience 令觀眾驚豔\nThe audience was dazzled by the dancers' amazing performance.\n(觀眾被舞者們精采的表演深深吸引。)\nThe bright headlights of the truck dazzled me for a moment.\n(卡車刺眼的大燈讓我一時睜不開眼。)"],["deafen","deafen(v.)使聾、震耳欲聾\ndeaf(adj.)聾的\ndeafening(adj.)震耳欲聾的\ndeafening noise 震耳欲聾的噪音\ndeafening silence 令人難堪的沉默\nThe crowd's cheers deafened us when the team scored the winning goal.\n(球隊踢進致勝球時，群眾的歡呼聲震耳欲聾。)\nWorking near the loud machines without earplugs may deafen you.\n(在吵雜機器旁工作不戴耳塞可能會讓你聽力受損。)"],["decisive","decisive(adj.)決定性的、果斷的\ndecide(v.)決定\ndecision(n.)決定\ndecisively(adv.)果斷地\ndecisive moment 關鍵時刻\ndecisive victory 決定性的勝利\nA good leader must be decisive in times of crisis.\n(好的領導者在危機時刻必須果斷。)\nHis goal in the final minute proved decisive.\n(他在最後一分鐘的進球成為致勝關鍵。)"],["dedication","dedication(n.)奉獻、專注、獻詞\ndedicate(v.)奉獻、致力於\ndedicated(adj.)專注的、盡心盡力的\ndedication to 對……的奉獻\nhard work and dedication 努力與奉獻\nThe nurse was praised for her dedication to her patients.\n(那位護理師因為對病人的盡心奉獻而受到讚揚。)\nBecoming a professional pianist requires years of dedication.\n(成為職業鋼琴家需要多年的專注投入。)"],["deduct","deduct(v.)扣除、減去\ndeduction(n.)扣除、推論\ndeductible(adj.)可扣除的\ndeduct points 扣分\ndeduct from 從……中扣除\nThe teacher will deduct points if you hand in your homework late.\n(如果你遲交作業，老師會扣分。)\nTaxes are automatically deducted from his monthly salary.\n(稅金會自動從他的月薪中扣除。)"],["deem","deem(v.)認為、視為\n(無詞性變化)\ndeem it necessary 認為有必要\nbe deemed (to be) 被視為\nThe building was deemed unsafe after the earthquake.\n(這棟建築在地震後被認定為不安全。)\nThe principal will take whatever action he deems necessary.\n(校長將採取他認為必要的任何措施。)"],["default","default(n./v.)預設值、違約、不履行\n(無詞性變化)\nby default 預設地、因對方缺席\ndefault setting 預設設定\nThe phone's default language is English, but you can change it.\n(這支手機的預設語言是英文，但你可以更改。)\nThe company defaulted on its loan and went bankrupt.\n(這家公司拖欠貸款後破產了。)"],["defect","defect(n./v.)缺陷、瑕疵、叛逃\ndefective(adj.)有缺陷的\ndefector(n.)叛逃者\nbirth defect 先天缺陷\nproduct defect 產品瑕疵\nThe company recalled thousands of cars because of a defect in the brakes.\n(由於煞車有瑕疵，這家公司召回了數千輛汽車。)\nDuring the Cold War, some scientists defected to the West.\n(冷戰期間，有些科學家叛逃到西方國家。)"],["defiance","defiance(n.)違抗、蔑視、反抗\ndefy(v.)違抗、蔑視\ndefiant(adj.)違抗的\nin defiance of 不顧、違抗\nact of defiance 反抗行為\nThe students held the protest in defiance of the school's ban.\n(學生們不顧學校的禁令舉行抗議。)\nHe raised his fist as an act of defiance.\n(他舉起拳頭表示反抗。)"],["definitive","definitive(adj.)決定性的、最權威的\ndefinite(adj.)明確的\ndefinitively(adv.)決定性地\ndefinitive answer 確切的答覆\ndefinitive guide 權威指南\nScientists have not yet found a definitive answer to the question.\n(科學家尚未找到這個問題的確切答案。)\nThis book is considered the definitive guide to Taiwanese birds.\n(這本書被視為台灣鳥類最權威的指南。)"],["dental","dental(adj.)牙齒的、牙科的\ndentist(n.)牙醫\ndental care 牙齒保健\ndental floss 牙線\nGood dental care can prevent many problems later in life.\n(良好的牙齒保健能預防日後許多問題。)\nUsing dental floss every day helps keep your gums healthy.\n(每天使用牙線有助於保持牙齦健康。)"],["deplete","deplete(v.)耗盡、使枯竭\ndepletion(n.)耗盡、枯竭\ndeplete resources 耗盡資源\nozone depletion 臭氧層破洞\nOverfishing has seriously depleted fish populations in the ocean.\n(過度捕撈已嚴重耗盡海洋中的魚群數量。)\nHuman activities are depleting the earth's natural resources.\n(人類的活動正在耗盡地球的自然資源。)"],["deprive","deprive(v.)剝奪、使喪失\ndeprivation(n.)剝奪、匱乏\ndeprived(adj.)貧困的、被剝奪的\ndeprive sb. of 剝奪某人的……\nsleep deprivation 睡眠不足\nToo much homework deprives students of time to rest.\n(過多的作業剝奪了學生休息的時間。)\nSleep deprivation can affect your memory and concentration.\n(睡眠不足會影響你的記憶力和專注力。)"],["descent","descent(n.)下降、血統、出身\ndescend(v.)下降\ndescendant(n.)後代\nof ... descent ……血統的\nsteep descent 陡坡\nThe plane began its descent into Taoyuan Airport.\n(飛機開始下降準備降落桃園機場。)\nShe is of Japanese descent but grew up in Taiwan.\n(她有日本血統，但在台灣長大。)"],["despise","despise(v.)鄙視、看不起\ndespicable(adj.)可鄙的\ndespise sb. for 因……鄙視某人\nopenly despise 公然鄙視\nShe despises people who lie to get what they want.\n(她鄙視那些為達目的而說謊的人。)\nDon't despise others just because they are poor.\n(不要只因為別人貧窮就看不起他們。)"],["destined","destined(adj.)命中注定的、預定前往的\ndestiny(n.)命運\ndestination(n.)目的地\nbe destined to 注定要\ndestined for 開往……的、注定……\nWith her talent, she seems destined to become a great writer.\n(憑她的天分，她似乎注定會成為偉大的作家。)\nThe ship was destined for Japan.\n(這艘船預定駛往日本。)"],["detach","detach(v.)分開、拆下\ndetached(adj.)分開的、超然的\ndetachment(n.)分離、超然\ndetach from 從……分離\ndetached house 獨棟住宅\nPlease detach the form and return it to your teacher.\n(請撕下這張表格交給你的老師。)\nHe tries to detach himself from his emotions when making decisions.\n(他做決定時會試著讓自己不受情緒影響。)"],["detain","detain(v.)拘留、扣留、耽擱\ndetention(n.)拘留、課後留校\ndetainee(n.)被拘留者\nbe detained by 被……拘留\ndetain for questioning 拘留問訊\nThe suspect was detained by the police for questioning.\n(嫌犯被警方拘留問訊。)\nI'm sorry I'm late; I was detained by a meeting.\n(抱歉我遲到了，我被一個會議耽擱了。)"],["detention","detention(n.)拘留、課後留校\ndetain(v.)拘留\ndetention center 拘留所\nget detention 被罰留校\nHe got detention for talking during the exam.\n(他因為考試時講話而被罰留校。)\nThe men were held in a detention center for several days.\n(那些男子被關在拘留所好幾天。)"],["deter","deter(v.)阻止、威懾\ndeterrent(n.)威懾力量、嚇阻物\ndeterrence(n.)嚇阻\ndeter sb. from 阻止某人做……\ndeter crime 遏止犯罪\nHeavy fines are meant to deter people from littering.\n(高額罰款是為了嚇阻人們亂丟垃圾。)\nNothing could deter her from pursuing her dream.\n(沒有什麼能阻止她追求夢想。)"],["detergent","detergent(n.)清潔劑、洗衣精\n(無詞性變化)\nlaundry detergent 洗衣精\ndish detergent 洗碗精\nAdd a cup of laundry detergent before starting the washing machine.\n(啟動洗衣機前先加入一杯洗衣精。)\nSome detergents contain chemicals that pollute rivers.\n(有些清潔劑含有會汙染河川的化學物質。)"],["devour","devour(v.)狼吞虎嚥、吞噬、如飢似渴地閱讀\n(無詞性變化)\ndevour a meal 狼吞虎嚥地吃一頓\ndevour books 如飢似渴地看書\nThe hungry boys devoured the whole pizza in five minutes.\n(那群飢餓的男孩五分鐘就把整個披薩吃光了。)\nShe devoured every Harry Potter book as soon as it came out.\n(每本《哈利波特》一出版，她就迫不及待地讀完。)"],["diabetes","diabetes(n.)糖尿病\ndiabetic(adj./n.)糖尿病的、糖尿病患者\ntype 2 diabetes 第二型糖尿病\nrisk of diabetes 糖尿病風險\nDrinking too many sugary drinks increases the risk of diabetes.\n(喝太多含糖飲料會增加罹患糖尿病的風險。)\nPeople with diabetes need to check their blood sugar regularly.\n(糖尿病患者需要定期檢查血糖。)"],["dictate","dictate(v.)口述、命令、支配\ndictation(n.)聽寫、口述\ndictator(n.)獨裁者\ndictate a letter 口述信件\ndictate terms 規定條件\nThe manager dictated a letter to his secretary.\n(經理向祕書口述了一封信。)\nThe weather will dictate whether we hold the event outdoors.\n(天氣將決定我們是否在戶外舉辦活動。)"],["dictation","dictation(n.)聽寫、口述\ndictate(v.)口述\ntake dictation 做聽寫、記錄口述\ndictation test 聽寫測驗\nWe have an English dictation test every Friday.\n(我們每週五都有英文聽寫測驗。)\nThe secretary took dictation during the meeting.\n(祕書在會議中記錄口述內容。)"],["dictator","dictator(n.)獨裁者\ndictatorship(n.)獨裁政權\ndictatorial(adj.)獨裁的\nmilitary dictator 軍事獨裁者\noverthrow a dictator 推翻獨裁者\nThe people finally overthrew the dictator after years of protests.\n(經過多年的抗議，人民終於推翻了獨裁者。)\nThe dictator controlled the media and silenced his critics.\n(那名獨裁者控制媒體並壓制批評者。)"],["dictatorship","dictatorship(n.)獨裁政權、專政\ndictator(n.)獨裁者\nmilitary dictatorship 軍事獨裁\nunder a dictatorship 在獨裁統治下\nThe country was ruled by a military dictatorship for decades.\n(這個國家數十年來由軍事獨裁政權統治。)\nFreedom of speech is often limited under a dictatorship.\n(在獨裁統治下，言論自由經常受到限制。)"],["diesel","diesel(n.)柴油、柴油引擎\n(無詞性變化)\ndiesel engine 柴油引擎\ndiesel fuel 柴油\nMany old trucks run on diesel and cause serious air pollution.\n(許多老舊卡車使用柴油，造成嚴重空氣汙染。)\nThe city plans to replace its diesel buses with electric ones.\n(市政府計畫把柴油公車換成電動公車。)"],["differentiate","differentiate(v.)區別、區分\ndifferentiation(n.)區別、分化\ndifferent(adj.)不同的\ndifferentiate between 區分\ndifferentiate A from B 把 A 與 B 區分開來\nYoung children cannot always differentiate between fantasy and reality.\n(年幼的孩子不一定能區分幻想與現實。)\nWhat differentiates this phone from others is its long battery life.\n(這支手機與眾不同之處在於電池續航力很長。)"],["diplomacy","diplomacy(n.)外交、交際手腕\ndiplomat(n.)外交官\ndiplomatic(adj.)外交的、圓滑的\ninternational diplomacy 國際外交\nwith diplomacy 圓融地\nThe conflict between the two countries was solved through diplomacy.\n(兩國間的衝突透過外交途徑解決了。)\nShe handled the angry customer with great diplomacy.\n(她非常圓融地處理了那位生氣的顧客。)"],["directive","directive(n.)指令、命令\ndirect(v.)指揮、指示\ndirection(n.)方向、指示\nissue a directive 發布指令\ngovernment directive 政府指令\nThe school received a directive from the Ministry of Education.\n(學校收到教育部的一項指令。)\nAll staff must follow the new safety directive.\n(所有員工都必須遵守新的安全指令。)"],["disable","disable(v.)使失去能力、使傷殘、停用\ndisabled(adj.)身心障礙的、被停用的\ndisability(n.)身心障礙\ndisable a function 停用功能\ndisabled parking 身障停車位\nYou can disable the notifications in the phone's settings.\n(你可以在手機的設定中停用通知。)\nThe accident disabled him, but he never gave up on his dreams.\n(這場意外使他身體傷殘，但他從未放棄夢想。)"],["disastrous","disastrous(adj.)災難性的、極糟的\ndisaster(n.)災難\ndisastrously(adv.)災難性地\ndisastrous effect 災難性的影響\ndisastrous result 極糟的結果\nThe typhoon had a disastrous effect on the farmers' crops.\n(颱風對農民的作物造成了災難性的影響。)\nCheating on the exam could lead to disastrous results.\n(考試作弊可能導致極為嚴重的後果。)"],["disbelief","disbelief(n.)不相信、懷疑\ndisbelieve(v.)不相信\nin disbelief 不敢置信地\nshake one's head in disbelief 不可置信地搖頭\nShe stared at her exam results in disbelief.\n(她不敢置信地盯著自己的考試成績。)\nThe fans watched in disbelief as their team lost the final.\n(球迷們難以置信地看著自己的隊伍輸掉決賽。)"],["discard","discard(v./n.)丟棄、拋棄、被拋棄之物\n(無詞性變化)\ndiscard old clothes 丟棄舊衣\ndiscard a theory 揚棄理論\nPlease discard used batteries in the special recycling bins.\n(請把用過的電池丟進專用的回收桶。)\nScientists discarded the old theory after new evidence was found.\n(發現新證據後，科學家們揚棄了舊理論。)"],["discharge","discharge(n./v.)排放、出院、解雇、履行\n(無詞性變化)\nbe discharged from hospital 出院\ndischarge waste 排放廢棄物\nMy grandmother was discharged from the hospital yesterday.\n(我奶奶昨天出院了。)\nThe factory was fined for discharging waste into the river.\n(這間工廠因將廢棄物排入河中而被罰款。)"],["disciple","disciple(n.)門徒、追隨者、弟子\ndiscipleship(n.)門徒身分\nloyal disciple 忠實的追隨者\ndisciple of ……的信徒\nConfucius had many disciples who spread his teachings.\n(孔子有許多傳播他學說的弟子。)\nHe is a devoted disciple of the famous chef.\n(他是那位名廚忠實的追隨者。)"],["disciplinary","disciplinary(adj.)紀律的、懲戒的、學科的\ndiscipline(n./v.)紀律、懲戒\ndisciplinary action 懲處\ninterdisciplinary 跨學科的\nThe school will take disciplinary action against students who bully others.\n(學校將對霸凌他人的學生採取懲處措施。)\nThe project requires an interdisciplinary approach combining science and art.\n(這個專題需要結合科學與藝術的跨學科方法。)"],["disclosure","disclosure(n.)揭露、透露、公開\ndisclose(v.)揭露、透露\npublic disclosure 公開揭露\ndisclosure of information 資訊揭露\nThe disclosure of personal data without permission is illegal.\n(未經允許揭露個人資料是違法的。)\nCompanies must make full disclosure of their financial situation.\n(公司必須完整公開其財務狀況。)"],["discomfort","discomfort(n./v.)不適、不舒服、使不安\ncomfort(n.)舒適\nuncomfortable(adj.)不舒服的\nphysical discomfort 身體不適\ncause discomfort 造成不適\nYou may feel some discomfort after the dental treatment.\n(牙齒治療後你可能會感到一些不適。)\nHe shifted in his seat, clearly in discomfort.\n(他在座位上挪動身子，顯然很不自在。)"],["discreet","discreet(adj.)謹慎的、低調的\ndiscretion(n.)謹慎、斟酌權\ndiscreetly(adv.)謹慎地\nbe discreet about 對……保密、低調\ndiscreet inquiry 私下打聽\nPlease be discreet and don't tell anyone about the surprise party.\n(請保密，別告訴任何人這個驚喜派對。)\nShe gave him a discreet signal to stop talking.\n(她不動聲色地示意他別再說了。)"],["disgrace","disgrace(n./v.)恥辱、丟臉、使蒙羞\ndisgraceful(adj.)可恥的\nin disgrace 丟臉地、失寵\nbring disgrace on 使……蒙羞\nThe politician resigned in disgrace after the scandal.\n(那位政治人物在醜聞後丟臉地辭職了。)\nHis cheating brought disgrace on the whole team.\n(他的作弊行為讓整個隊伍蒙羞。)"],["dismay","dismay(n./v.)沮喪、驚愕、使灰心\ndismayed(adj.)沮喪的、驚愕的\nto one's dismay 令某人沮喪的是\nin dismay 驚慌地\nTo our dismay, the concert was canceled because of the typhoon.\n(令我們沮喪的是，演唱會因颱風取消了。)\nShe looked at the broken vase in dismay.\n(她驚慌地看著破掉的花瓶。)"],["dispensable","dispensable(adj.)非必要的、可有可無的\nindispensable(adj.)不可或缺的\ndispense(v.)分配、省去\ndispensable item 非必需品\nbe considered dispensable 被視為可有可無\nIn a tight budget, eating out is a dispensable expense.\n(在預算吃緊時，外食是可以省下的開銷。)\nNo member of our team is dispensable; everyone plays an important role.\n(我們隊上沒有人是可有可無的，每個人都扮演重要角色。)"],["dispense","dispense(v.)分配、發放、配藥\ndispenser(n.)自動販賣機、分配器\ndispensable(adj.)非必要的\ndispense with 省去、免除\nwater dispenser 飲水機\nThe machine dispenses hot and cold drinks.\n(這台機器供應冷熱飲料。)\nLet's dispense with the formalities and get straight to the point.\n(我們省去那些客套，直接切入重點吧。)"],["disposable","disposable(adj./n.)用完即丟的、可支配的、拋棄式用品\ndispose(v.)處理、丟棄\ndisposal(n.)處置\ndisposable cups 免洗杯\ndisposable income 可支配所得\nMany shops no longer provide disposable plastic straws.\n(許多店家已不再提供一次性塑膠吸管。)\nPeople with more disposable income tend to travel more.\n(可支配所得較多的人往往比較常旅行。)"],["disposal","disposal(n.)處置、處理、支配權\ndispose(v.)處理、丟棄\nwaste disposal 廢棄物處理\nat one's disposal 任某人支配\nProper waste disposal is important for protecting the environment.\n(妥善處理廢棄物對保護環境很重要。)\nThe library has many resources at your disposal.\n(圖書館有許多資源可供你使用。)"],["dispose","dispose(v.)處理、丟棄、使傾向\ndisposal(n.)處置\ndisposable(adj.)用完即丟的\ndispose of 處理、丟棄\nbe disposed to 傾向於\nPlease dispose of your trash properly after the picnic.\n(野餐後請妥善處理你的垃圾。)\nThe government is looking for a safe way to dispose of nuclear waste.\n(政府正在尋找安全處理核廢料的方法。)"],["dissent","dissent(n.)異議、不同意見\ndissenter(n.)持異議者\ndissenting(adj.)持異議的\nvoice dissent 表達異議\npolitical dissent 政治異議\nIn a democracy, people are free to express dissent.\n(在民主社會中，人們可以自由表達異議。)\nThe decision was passed with little dissent.\n(這項決議幾乎沒有異議就通過了。)"],["distraction","distraction(n.)分心、使分心的事物、消遣\ndistract(v.)使分心\ndistracted(adj.)分心的\nwithout distraction 不受干擾地\ndrive sb. to distraction 使某人心煩意亂\nSmartphones can be a big distraction when you are studying.\n(讀書時，智慧型手機可能是很大的干擾。)\nI need a quiet place to work without distraction.\n(我需要一個不受干擾的安靜地方工作。)"],["distress","distress(n./v.)痛苦、苦惱、危難、使苦惱\ndistressed(adj.)苦惱的\ndistressing(adj.)令人痛苦的\nin distress 處於危難中、苦惱\ndistress signal 求救信號\nThe coast guard rescued a fishing boat in distress.\n(海巡人員救援了一艘遇險的漁船。)\nThe news of the accident caused great distress to the family.\n(這起意外的消息讓那個家庭非常痛苦。)"],["disturbance","disturbance(n.)干擾、騷亂、失調\ndisturb(v.)打擾\ndisturbing(adj.)令人不安的\ncause a disturbance 引起騷動\nsleep disturbance 睡眠障礙\nThe noisy neighbors caused a disturbance late at night.\n(吵鬧的鄰居深夜引起了騷動。)\nConstruction work nearby is a constant disturbance to our classes.\n(附近的施工持續干擾我們上課。)"],["diversify","diversify(v.)使多樣化、多元發展\ndiversity(n.)多樣性\ndiverse(adj.)多樣的\ndiversification(n.)多樣化\ndiversify the economy 使經濟多元化\ndiversify into 擴展業務至\nThe farm diversified by opening a café for visitors.\n(這座農場透過為遊客開設咖啡廳來多元經營。)\nCountries that rely on one industry should diversify their economies.\n(仰賴單一產業的國家應該讓經濟多元化。)"],["diversion","diversion(n.)轉移、改道、消遣\ndivert(v.)轉移、使改道\ntraffic diversion 交通改道\ncreate a diversion 轉移注意力\nThere is a traffic diversion because of the road repairs.\n(因為道路維修，交通改道了。)\nOne thief created a diversion while the other stole the wallet.\n(一個小偷轉移注意力，另一個趁機偷走錢包。)"],["divert","divert(v.)轉移、使改道、使轉向\ndiversion(n.)轉移、改道\ndivert attention 轉移注意力\ndivert traffic 使交通改道\nThe flight was diverted to Kaohsiung because of bad weather.\n(由於天氣惡劣，該班機改降高雄。)\nHe told a joke to divert attention from his mistake.\n(他講了個笑話來轉移大家對他錯誤的注意。)"],["dividend","dividend(n.)股息、紅利、好處\ndivide(v.)分配、分開\npay a dividend 發放股利\npay dividends 帶來好處\nThe company pays its shareholders a dividend every year.\n(這家公司每年發放股利給股東。)\nYour hard work in high school will pay dividends in the future.\n(你在高中時的努力將來會帶來回報。)"],["doom","doom(n./v.)厄運、毀滅、注定(失敗)\ndoomed(adj.)注定失敗的\nbe doomed to 注定要\ndoom and gloom 悲觀絕望\nThe plan was doomed to fail from the very beginning.\n(這個計畫從一開始就注定失敗。)\nMany people predicted doom for the company, but it survived.\n(許多人預言這家公司會倒閉，但它撐了下來。)"],["dormitory/dorm","dormitory(n.)宿舍\ndorm(n.)宿舍(口語)\nstudent dormitory 學生宿舍\ndorm room 宿舍房間\nMost first-year students live in the school dormitory.\n(大多數一年級學生住在學校宿舍。)\nI share a dorm room with three classmates.\n(我和三位同學共住一間宿舍房間。)"],["downward","downward(adj.)向下的、下降的\ndownwards(adv.)向下地\ndownward trend 下降趨勢\ndownward spiral 惡性循環\nThe birth rate in Taiwan has shown a downward trend for years.\n(台灣的出生率多年來呈現下降趨勢。)\nAfter losing his job, his life went into a downward spiral.\n(失業後，他的生活陷入了惡性循環。)"],["downward/downwards","downward(adv.)向下地\ndownwards(adv.)向下地(英式常用)\nlook downward 向下看\nface downward 臉朝下\nThe road slopes gently downward toward the sea.\n(這條路緩緩向下延伸到海邊。)\nPlace the cards face downwards on the table.\n(把卡片正面朝下放在桌上。)"],["doze","doze(v./n.)打瞌睡、小睡\ndozy(adj.)昏昏欲睡的\ndoze off 打瞌睡\nhave a doze 小睡一下\nI dozed off in class because I stayed up late last night.\n(我昨晚熬夜，所以上課打瞌睡。)\nGrandpa likes to have a doze in his chair after lunch.\n(爺爺喜歡午餐後在椅子上小睡一下。)"],["drastic","drastic(adj.)激烈的、徹底的、嚴厲的\ndrastically(adv.)大幅地、徹底地\ndrastic change 劇烈的變化\ndrastic measures 激烈的措施\nThe government took drastic measures to stop the spread of the virus.\n(政府採取激烈措施阻止病毒擴散。)\nClimate change has caused drastic changes in weather patterns.\n(氣候變遷導致天氣型態劇烈改變。)"],["draught","draught(n.)氣流、通風、一飲(英式拼法)\ndraft(n.)氣流、草稿(美式拼法)\ndraughty(adj.)有冷風吹進的\ncold draught 冷風\ndraught beer 生啤酒\nClose the window; there's a cold draught coming in.\n(把窗戶關上，有冷風吹進來了。)\nThe old house is full of draughts in winter.\n(那間老房子冬天到處都有冷風灌進來。)"],["dresser","dresser(n.)梳妝臺、五斗櫃、穿著……的人\ndress(v./n.)穿衣、洋裝\nchest of drawers 五斗櫃\nsmart dresser 衣著講究的人\nShe keeps her socks in the top drawer of the dresser.\n(她把襪子放在五斗櫃最上層的抽屜。)\nMy uncle is a smart dresser who always wears a suit.\n(我叔叔衣著講究，總是穿西裝。)"],["dressing","dressing(n.)調味醬、敷料、穿衣\ndress(v.)穿衣、包紮、調味\nsalad dressing 沙拉醬\ndressing room 更衣室\nWould you like Thousand Island or Caesar dressing on your salad?\n(你的沙拉要淋千島醬還是凱撒醬？)\nThe nurse changed the dressing on his wound every day.\n(護理師每天替他更換傷口的敷料。)"],["dual","dual(adj.)雙重的、兩部分的\nduality(n.)二元性\ndual role 雙重角色\ndual citizenship 雙重國籍\nShe plays a dual role as a teacher and a mother.\n(她身兼老師與母親的雙重角色。)\nThis car has dual airbags for extra safety.\n(這輛車配有雙安全氣囊，更加安全。)"],["dubious","dubious(adj.)可疑的、半信半疑的\ndubiously(adv.)懷疑地\ndubious claim 可疑的說法\nbe dubious about 對……存疑\nBe careful of websites that make dubious health claims.\n(要小心那些提出可疑健康說法的網站。)\nI'm dubious about whether the plan will really work.\n(我對這個計畫是否真的可行感到存疑。)"],["duration","duration(n.)持續時間、期間\ndurable(adj.)耐用的\nfor the duration of 在……期間\nshort duration 短時間\nPlease turn off your phones for the duration of the exam.\n(考試期間請將手機關機。)\nThe duration of the flight from Taipei to Tokyo is about three hours.\n(台北到東京的飛行時間約三小時。)"],["dusk","dusk(n.)黃昏、薄暮\ndusky(adj.)昏暗的\nat dusk 在黃昏時\nfrom dawn to dusk 從早到晚\nThe streetlights come on at dusk.\n(路燈在黃昏時亮起。)\nThe farmers work in the fields from dawn to dusk.\n(農夫們從早到晚都在田裡工作。)"],["dwarf","dwarf(n./v.)矮人、侏儒、使相形見絀\n(無詞性變化)\nSnow White and the Seven Dwarfs 白雪公主與七矮人\nbe dwarfed by 被……比得渺小\nThe old temple is dwarfed by the tall buildings around it.\n(這座古廟在周圍高樓的對比下顯得渺小。)\nIn the story, the dwarfs welcomed Snow White into their home.\n(在故事中，小矮人們歡迎白雪公主住進他們家。)"],["dwell","dwell(v.)居住、老是想著\ndwelling(n.)住處\ndweller(n.)居民\ndwell on 老是想著、詳述\ncity dweller 都市居民\nDon't dwell on your past mistakes; learn from them and move on.\n(別老想著過去的錯誤，從中學習然後繼續前進。)\nAncient people dwelled in caves to protect themselves from wild animals.\n(古代人住在洞穴裡以躲避野獸。)"],["dwelling","dwelling(n.)住處、住宅\ndwell(v.)居住\ndweller(n.)居民\ndwelling place 住所\ncave dwelling 穴居處\nThe archaeologists discovered ancient dwellings near the river.\n(考古學家在河邊發現了古代的住所。)\nTraditional Atayal dwellings were built with bamboo and wood.\n(傳統泰雅族住屋是以竹子和木頭建造的。)"],["eccentric","eccentric(adj./n.)古怪的、怪人\neccentricity(n.)古怪、怪癖\neccentric behavior 古怪的行為\nan eccentric old man 古怪的老人\nThe eccentric artist always wears a purple hat, even at dinner.\n(那位古怪的藝術家總是戴著紫色帽子，連吃晚餐時也不例外。)\nHis eccentric behavior made his neighbors curious about his past.\n(他古怪的舉動讓鄰居對他的過去感到好奇。)"],["eclipse","eclipse(n./v.)日蝕、月蝕、使黯然失色\n(無詞性變化)\nsolar eclipse 日蝕\nlunar eclipse 月蝕\nThousands of people gathered to watch the total solar eclipse.\n(數千人聚集觀看日全蝕。)\nHer success was soon eclipsed by her younger sister's achievements.\n(她的成就很快就被妹妹的成就比下去了。)"],["edible","edible(adj.)可食用的\ninedible(adj.)不可食用的\nedible mushrooms 可食用的菇類\nedible oil 食用油\nNot all wild mushrooms are edible, so never pick them without an expert.\n(並非所有野菇都能吃，所以沒有專家陪同千萬別採。)\nThe cake was decorated with edible flowers from the garden.\n(這個蛋糕用花園裡的食用花裝飾。)"],["editorial","editorial(adj./n.)編輯的、社論\neditor(n.)編輯\nedit(v.)編輯\neditorial board 編輯委員會\nnewspaper editorial 報紙社論\nThe newspaper published an editorial criticizing the new tax policy.\n(這份報紙刊登了一篇批評新稅制的社論。)\nShe joined the editorial team of the school magazine this year.\n(她今年加入了校刊的編輯團隊。)"],["electrician","electrician(n.)電工、電氣技師\nelectric(adj.)電的\nelectricity(n.)電\ncall an electrician 叫電工\nlicensed electrician 合格電工\nWe called an electrician to fix the faulty wiring in the kitchen.\n(我們請電工來修理廚房有問題的電線。)\nOnly a licensed electrician should install the new lights.\n(只有合格的電工才能安裝新的燈具。)"],["elevate","elevate(v.)提升、抬高、使晉升\nelevation(n.)海拔、提升\nelevator(n.)電梯\nelevate the status 提升地位\nelevated highway 高架道路\nGood music can elevate your mood after a stressful day.\n(好的音樂能在壓力大的一天後提振你的心情。)\nThe village sits at an elevation of 2,000 meters above sea level.\n(這個村莊位於海拔兩千公尺處。)"],["emigrant","emigrant(n.)(移出的)移民、移居外國者\nemigrate(v.)移居外國\nemigration(n.)移居外國\nTaiwanese emigrants 臺灣移民\nan emigrant family 移民家庭\nMany emigrants left Europe for America in the nineteenth century.\n(十九世紀時，許多移民離開歐洲前往美洲。)\nThe emigrants struggled to adapt to the language and culture of their new home.\n(這些移民努力適應新家園的語言和文化。)"],["emigrate","emigrate(v.)移居外國\nemigrant(n.)移民\nemigration(n.)移居外國\nemigrate to 移民到…\nemigrate from 從…移出\nHis family emigrated to Canada when he was ten years old.\n(他十歲時全家移民到加拿大。)\nMany young people emigrate in search of better job opportunities.\n(許多年輕人為了尋找更好的工作機會而移居國外。)"],["emigration","emigration(n.)移居外國、移民出境\nemigrate(v.)移居外國\nmass emigration 大規模移民\nemigration policy 移民出境政策\nThe war led to a wave of mass emigration from the region.\n(戰爭導致該地區出現一波大規模移民潮。)\nEmigration has caused a shortage of skilled workers in the country.\n(人口外移導致該國缺乏技術工人。)"],["encyclopedia","encyclopedia(n.)百科全書\nencyclopedic(adj.)百科全書式的、知識淵博的\nonline encyclopedia 線上百科全書\na walking encyclopedia 活百科\nBefore the internet, students looked up facts in a printed encyclopedia.\n(在網路出現之前，學生在紙本百科全書中查資料。)\nMy grandfather knows so much that we call him a walking encyclopedia.\n(我爺爺懂得很多，我們稱他為活百科。)"],["endeavor","endeavor(n./v.)努力、嘗試、致力\n(無詞性變化)\nendeavor to 努力去…\nhuman endeavor 人類的努力\nWe will endeavor to answer all your questions within two days.\n(我們會盡力在兩天內回覆你所有的問題。)\nSpace exploration is one of the greatest human endeavors.\n(太空探索是人類最偉大的努力之一。)"],["endowment","endowment(n.)捐贈、捐款、天賦\nendow(v.)捐贈、賦予\nbe endowed with 天生具有…\nendowment fund 捐贈基金\nThe university received a large endowment from a wealthy alumnus.\n(這所大學收到一位富有校友的大筆捐款。)\nShe is endowed with a remarkable talent for languages.\n(她天生具有非凡的語言天分。)"],["endurance","endurance(n.)耐力、忍耐力\nendure(v.)忍受、持續\nendurable(adj.)可忍受的\nphysical endurance 體力、耐力\nbeyond endurance 忍無可忍\nLong-distance swimming requires great strength and endurance.\n(長距離游泳需要很強的力量和耐力。)\nThe noise from the construction site was beyond endurance.\n(工地傳來的噪音令人忍無可忍。)"],["enhance(ment)","enhance(v.)提高、增強、enhancement(n.)提高、增強\n(無詞性變化)\nenhance the quality 提升品質\nenhance one's image 提升形象\nReading widely can enhance your writing skills and vocabulary.\n(廣泛閱讀能提升你的寫作能力和字彙量。)\nThe new software brought a great enhancement to image quality.\n(新軟體大幅提升了影像品質。)"],["enlighten(ment)","enlighten(v.)啟發、開導、enlightenment(n.)啟發、啟蒙\nenlightening(adj.)有啟發性的\nthe Enlightenment 啟蒙運動\nspiritual enlightenment 心靈啟發\nThe documentary enlightened me about the problem of ocean pollution.\n(這部紀錄片讓我了解海洋汙染的問題。)\nThe Enlightenment changed the way Europeans thought about reason and freedom.\n(啟蒙運動改變了歐洲人對理性與自由的看法。)"],["enrich(ment)","enrich(v.)使豐富、使富裕、enrichment(n.)豐富、充實\n(無詞性變化)\nenrich one's life 豐富人生\nenrichment program 增廣課程\nTraveling abroad can greatly enrich your understanding of other cultures.\n(出國旅行能大大豐富你對其他文化的了解。)\nThe school offers enrichment programs in art and science after class.\n(學校在課後提供藝術與科學的增廣課程。)"],["enroll(ment)","enroll(v.)註冊、入學、登記、enrollment(n.)註冊、入學人數\n(無詞性變化)\nenroll in 註冊參加…\nstudent enrollment 學生人數\nShe enrolled in an online course to learn basic programming.\n(她報名了一門線上課程來學習基礎程式設計。)\nStudent enrollment has dropped because of the low birth rate.\n(由於少子化，學生入學人數下降了。)"],["equalize","equalize(v.)使相等、使平等、扳平比分\nequal(adj.)相等的\nequality(n.)平等\nequalize opportunities 使機會平等\nequalize the score 扳平比分\nThe government hopes to equalize educational opportunities in rural areas.\n(政府希望讓偏鄉的教育機會更平等。)\nOur team equalized the score just two minutes before the end.\n(我們隊在比賽結束前兩分鐘扳平了比分。)"],["equate","equate(v.)把…等同、使相等\nequation(n.)方程式、等同\nequate A with B 把A等同於B\nsolve an equation 解方程式\nMany people wrongly equate wealth with happiness.\n(許多人錯誤地把財富等同於幸福。)\nYou should not equate good grades with true intelligence.\n(你不應該把好成績和真正的聰明畫上等號。)"],["escort","escort(n./v.)護送者、護衛隊、護送、陪同\n(無詞性變化)\npolice escort 警察護送\nescort sb. to 護送某人到…\nThe singer arrived at the stadium under police escort.\n(那位歌手在警察護送下抵達體育場。)\nA staff member escorted the visitors to the meeting room.\n(一位工作人員陪同訪客前往會議室。)"],["esteem","esteem(n./v.)尊重、尊敬、認為\nself-esteem(n.)自尊心\nhold sb. in high esteem 非常尊敬某人\nlow self-esteem 自卑、缺乏自信\nThe doctor is held in high esteem by everyone in the village.\n(那位醫生受到村裡每個人的高度尊敬。)\nPraise from teachers can help build students' self-esteem.\n(老師的稱讚有助於建立學生的自信心。)"],["eternity","eternity(n.)永恆、無窮的時間\neternal(adj.)永恆的\nfor eternity 永遠\nseem like an eternity 彷彿過了很久\nWaiting for the exam results seemed like an eternity.\n(等待考試結果彷彿過了一輩子那麼久。)\nThe ancient Egyptians believed the soul would live for eternity.\n(古埃及人相信靈魂會永遠存在。)"],["evacuate","evacuate(v.)撤離、疏散\nevacuation(n.)撤離、疏散\nevacuate a building 疏散大樓人員\nevacuation route 疏散路線\nResidents were evacuated before the typhoon hit the coast.\n(颱風襲擊海岸前，居民已被撤離。)\nDuring the fire drill, all students evacuated the building in three minutes.\n(在消防演習中，所有學生在三分鐘內疏散出大樓。)"],["evergreen","evergreen(adj./n.)常綠的、常青的、常綠植物\n(無詞性變化)\nevergreen tree 常綠樹\nevergreen forest 常綠林\nPine trees are evergreens that stay green throughout the year.\n(松樹是一年四季都保持翠綠的常綠植物。)\nHer songs have become evergreen classics loved by every generation.\n(她的歌已成為受各世代喜愛的不朽經典。)"],["evoke","evoke(v.)喚起、引起\nevocative(adj.)喚起回憶的\nevoke memories 喚起回憶\nevoke a response 引起反應\nThe smell of fresh bread evokes memories of my grandmother's kitchen.\n(新鮮麵包的香味喚起我對奶奶廚房的回憶。)\nThe photograph evoked strong feelings of sadness among the viewers.\n(這張照片在觀眾心中引起強烈的悲傷。)"],["examinee","examinee(n.)應試者、考生\nexaminer(n.)主考官\nexamination(n.)考試\nexaminee number 准考證號碼\nexaminees are required to 考生必須…\nAll examinees must bring their admission tickets to the test center.\n(所有考生都必須攜帶准考證到考場。)\nThe examinees waited nervously outside the classroom.\n(考生們緊張地在教室外等候。)"],["examiner","examiner(n.)主考官、檢查員\nexamine(v.)檢查、考試\nexaminee(n.)考生\ndriving examiner 駕照考官\nmedical examiner 法醫\nThe examiner asked me to describe a picture in English.\n(主考官要我用英文描述一張圖片。)\nThe driving examiner said I had passed the road test.\n(駕照考官說我通過了路考。)"],["excel","excel(v.)擅長、勝過、表現優異\nexcellence(n.)卓越\nexcellent(adj.)極好的\nexcel in/at 擅長…\nacademic excellence 學業優異\nShe excels in both mathematics and music.\n(她在數學和音樂方面都表現優異。)\nThe school is known for its academic excellence.\n(這所學校以學業卓越聞名。)"],["excerpt","excerpt(n./v.)摘錄、節錄\n(無詞性變化)\nan excerpt from 摘錄自…\nread an excerpt 朗讀一段節錄\nThe teacher read us an excerpt from a famous novel.\n(老師為我們朗讀了一部名著的節錄。)\nThis passage is excerpted from a speech by Martin Luther King Jr.\n(這段文字節錄自馬丁·路德·金恩的演講。)"],["excess","excess(adj./n.)過量的、多餘的、過量\nexcessive(adj.)過度的\nexcessively(adv.)過度地\nin excess of 超過…\nexcess weight 多餘的體重\nDrinking alcohol to excess can seriously damage your health.\n(過量飲酒會嚴重損害健康。)\nPassengers must pay extra for excess baggage.\n(乘客的行李超重必須額外付費。)"],["exclusion","exclusion(n.)排除、排斥\nexclude(v.)排除\nexclusive(adj.)獨家的、排外的\nsocial exclusion 社會排斥\nto the exclusion of 排除…、而不顧…\nHe studied computer science to the exclusion of everything else.\n(他專心研讀資訊科學，其他什麼都不管。)\nSocial exclusion can make teenagers feel lonely and anxious.\n(社交排擠可能使青少年感到孤單和焦慮。)"],["exempt","exempt(adj.)被免除的、豁免的\nexemption(n.)免除、豁免\nexempt from 免除…\ntax-exempt 免稅的\nStudents with excellent grades are exempt from the final exam.\n(成績優異的學生可以免考期末考。)\nBooks and newspapers are exempt from this new tax.\n(書籍和報紙不需課徵這項新稅。)"],["exert","exert(v.)運用、施加(影響、壓力)\nexertion(n.)盡力、費力\nexert influence 發揮影響力\nexert pressure on 對…施壓\nParents exert a strong influence on their children's values.\n(父母對孩子的價值觀有很大的影響。)\nThe group exerted pressure on the government to protect the forest.\n(這個團體向政府施壓要求保護森林。)"],["expenditure","expenditure(n.)支出、花費、經費\nexpend(v.)花費\nexpense(n.)費用\ngovernment expenditure 政府支出\nreduce expenditure 減少支出\nThe city has increased its expenditure on public transportation.\n(這座城市增加了在大眾運輸上的支出。)\nWe need to reduce expenditure if we want to save for the trip.\n(如果我們想存錢去旅行，就得減少開支。)"],["expiration","expiration(n.)期滿、截止、到期\nexpire(v.)到期\nexpiration date 有效期限、到期日\nupon expiration 到期時\nAlways check the expiration date before you buy milk.\n(買牛奶前一定要檢查有效期限。)\nUpon expiration of the contract, both sides may decide whether to renew it.\n(合約到期時，雙方可決定是否續約。)"],["expire","expire(v.)到期、失效\nexpiration(n.)到期\nexpired(adj.)過期的\nexpired food 過期食品\nthe visa expires 簽證到期\nMy passport will expire next month, so I need to renew it.\n(我的護照下個月到期，所以需要換新。)\nThe store was fined for selling expired food to customers.\n(這家店因販賣過期食品給顧客而被罰款。)"],["extract","extract(n./v.)萃取物、摘錄、拔出、提取\nextraction(n.)提取、拔出\nextract information 擷取資訊\nvanilla extract 香草精\nThe dentist had to extract two of my teeth.\n(牙醫必須拔掉我兩顆牙。)\nOil is extracted from olives by pressing them.\n(橄欖油是藉由壓榨橄欖萃取出來的。)"],["extracurricular","extracurricular(adj.)課外的\ncurriculum(n.)課程\nextracurricular activities 課外活動\nextracurricular clubs 課外社團\nJoining extracurricular activities helps students develop leadership skills.\n(參加課外活動有助於學生培養領導能力。)\nUniversities often look at applicants' extracurricular experience.\n(大學常會參考申請者的課外經驗。)"],["eyelash/lash","eyelash(n.)睫毛\nlash(n.)睫毛\nlong eyelashes 長睫毛\nfalse eyelashes 假睫毛\nThe baby has long, curly eyelashes.\n(那個嬰兒有又長又捲的睫毛。)\nShe put on false eyelashes before going on stage.\n(她上台前戴上了假睫毛。)"],["eyelid","eyelid(n.)眼皮、眼瞼\n(無詞性變化)\ndouble eyelid 雙眼皮\nheavy eyelids 沉重的眼皮\nMy eyelids felt heavy after studying until midnight.\n(念書念到半夜後，我的眼皮變得好沉重。)\nShe was born with double eyelids, just like her mother.\n(她天生就是雙眼皮，跟她媽媽一樣。)"],["eyesight","eyesight(n.)視力\n(無詞性變化)\npoor eyesight 視力不佳\nlose one's eyesight 失明\nStaring at screens for hours can harm your eyesight.\n(長時間盯著螢幕可能傷害你的視力。)\nMy grandfather wears glasses because of his poor eyesight.\n(我爺爺因為視力不好而戴眼鏡。)"],["fable","fable(n.)寓言、虛構的故事\nfabulous(adj.)極好的、驚人的\nAesop's Fables 伊索寓言\nthe moral of a fable 寓言的寓意\nThe fable of the tortoise and the hare teaches us not to be proud.\n(龜兔賽跑的寓言教導我們不要驕傲。)\nMany of Aesop's fables use animals to teach moral lessons.\n(許多伊索寓言用動物來傳達道德教訓。)"],["faction","faction(n.)派系、黨派\nfactional(adj.)派系的\nrival factions 敵對派系\npolitical faction 政治派系\nThe party split into two rival factions after the election.\n(選舉後，這個政黨分裂成兩個敵對派系。)\nFighting between factions weakened the government.\n(派系之間的鬥爭削弱了政府。)"],["Fahrenheit","Fahrenheit(n.)華氏溫度\n(無詞性變化)\ndegrees Fahrenheit 華氏…度\nFahrenheit scale 華氏溫標\nWater boils at 212 degrees Fahrenheit.\n(水在華氏212度沸騰。)\nAmericans usually measure temperature in Fahrenheit rather than Celsius.\n(美國人通常用華氏而非攝氏來測量溫度。)"],["falter","falter(v.)蹣跚、搖晃、支吾、衰退\n(無詞性變化)\nvoice falters 聲音發顫\neconomy falters 經濟衰退\nHer voice faltered as she told the sad story.\n(她講述這個悲傷故事時聲音顫抖。)\nSales began to falter after the new competitor entered the market.\n(新的競爭者進入市場後，銷售開始下滑。)"],["familiarity","familiarity(n.)熟悉、通曉、親密\nfamiliar(adj.)熟悉的\nfamiliarize(v.)使熟悉\nfamiliarity with 對…的熟悉\nFamiliarity breeds contempt. 熟悉生輕慢\nHer familiarity with the local language made the trip much easier.\n(她對當地語言的熟悉讓旅途輕鬆許多。)\nNew students should familiarize themselves with the school rules.\n(新生應該熟悉校規。)"],["fascination","fascination(n.)著迷、魅力、吸引力\nfascinate(v.)使著迷\nfascinating(adj.)迷人的\nfascination with 對…的著迷\nhold a fascination for 對…有吸引力\nHis fascination with space led him to study astronomy.\n(他對太空的著迷使他去攻讀天文學。)\nDinosaurs hold a special fascination for many children.\n(恐龍對許多孩子有一種特別的吸引力。)"],["feasible","feasible(adj.)可行的、行得通的\nfeasibility(n.)可行性\na feasible plan 可行的計畫\nfeasibility study 可行性研究\nWe need to find a feasible solution to the parking problem.\n(我們需要為停車問題找出可行的解決辦法。)\nBuilding a bridge across the river is not economically feasible.\n(在河上建橋在經濟上並不可行。)"],["feeble","feeble(adj.)虛弱的、微弱的、無力的\nfeebly(adv.)虛弱地\na feeble voice 微弱的聲音\na feeble excuse 站不住腳的藉口\nThe old man answered in a feeble voice.\n(那位老人用微弱的聲音回答。)\nSaying the dog ate your homework is a feeble excuse.\n(說狗吃了你的作業是個站不住腳的藉口。)"],["feminine","feminine(adj./n.)女性的、有女人味的、陰性\nfemininity(n.)女性特質\nfeminine qualities 女性特質\nfeminine style 女性化的風格\nThe dress has a soft and feminine design.\n(這件洋裝的設計柔美又有女人味。)\nIn French, every noun is either masculine or feminine.\n(在法文中，每個名詞都分陽性或陰性。)"],["fertility","fertility(n.)肥沃、繁殖力、生育力\nfertile(adj.)肥沃的\nfertilize(v.)施肥、使受精\nsoil fertility 土壤肥沃度\nfertility rate 生育率\nTaiwan has one of the lowest fertility rates in the world.\n(臺灣的生育率是全世界最低的之一。)\nFarmers rotate crops to keep the fertility of the soil.\n(農民輪作作物以保持土壤的肥沃。)"],["fertilizer","fertilizer(n.)肥料\nfertilize(v.)施肥\nfertile(adj.)肥沃的\nchemical fertilizer 化學肥料\norganic fertilizer 有機肥料\nMany farmers now use organic fertilizer instead of chemicals.\n(許多農民現在改用有機肥料而不用化學肥料。)\nToo much fertilizer can pollute rivers and lakes.\n(過多的肥料可能汙染河川和湖泊。)"],["fiancé/fiance","fiancé(n.)未婚夫\nfiance(n.)未婚夫(不加重音符號的寫法)\nher fiancé 她的未婚夫\nintroduce one's fiancé 介紹未婚夫\nShe introduced her fiancé to her family at the dinner party.\n(她在晚宴上把未婚夫介紹給家人。)\nHer fiancé proposed to her on the beach at sunset.\n(她的未婚夫在夕陽下的海灘向她求婚。)"],["fin","fin(n.)鰭、鰭狀物\n(無詞性變化)\nshark fin 魚翅、鯊魚鰭\ntail fin 尾鰭\nMany people now refuse to eat shark fin soup to protect sharks.\n(現在許多人為了保護鯊魚而拒吃魚翅湯。)\nThe fish moved its fins slowly as it swam near the rocks.\n(那條魚在岩石附近游動時緩緩擺動牠的鰭。)"],["finite","finite(adj.)有限的\ninfinite(adj.)無限的\nfinite resources 有限的資源\na finite number 有限的數量\nOil and coal are finite resources that will eventually run out.\n(石油和煤炭是終究會耗盡的有限資源。)\nWe only have a finite amount of time, so let's use it wisely.\n(我們的時間有限，所以要善加利用。)"],["firecracker","firecracker(n.)鞭炮、爆竹\n(無詞性變化)\nset off firecrackers 放鞭炮\na string of firecrackers 一串鞭炮\nPeople set off firecrackers to celebrate the Lunar New Year.\n(人們放鞭炮慶祝農曆新年。)\nThe loud firecrackers frightened the dogs in the neighborhood.\n(響亮的鞭炮聲嚇壞了附近的狗。)"],["fireproof","fireproof(adj.)防火的、耐火的\n(無詞性變化)\nfireproof door 防火門\nfireproof material 防火材料\nImportant documents are kept in a fireproof safe.\n(重要文件保存在防火保險箱裡。)\nThe new building was constructed with fireproof materials.\n(這棟新大樓是用防火建材建造的。)"],["fishery","fishery(n.)漁業、漁場\nfisherman(n.)漁夫\nfishery resources 漁業資源\ncoastal fishery 沿岸漁業\nOverfishing has seriously damaged the local fishery.\n(過度捕撈嚴重破壞了當地的漁業。)\nThe government is taking steps to protect fishery resources.\n(政府正採取措施保護漁業資源。)"],["flake","flake(n./v.)薄片、雪花、剝落\nflaky(adj.)易剝落的、成片的\nsnowflake 雪花\ncorn flakes 玉米片\nSnowflakes fell gently on the mountain village.\n(雪花輕輕飄落在山村上。)\nThe old paint on the wall has started to flake off.\n(牆上的舊油漆開始剝落了。)"],["flaw","flaw(n./v.)缺陷、瑕疵、使有缺陷\nflawless(adj.)完美無瑕的\nflawed(adj.)有缺陷的\na fatal flaw 致命缺點\na flaw in the plan 計畫中的漏洞\nThe engineers found a serious flaw in the design of the bridge.\n(工程師發現這座橋的設計有嚴重的缺陷。)\nHer English is almost flawless after years of practice.\n(經過多年練習，她的英文幾乎完美無瑕。)"],["flourish","flourish(v./n.)繁榮、茂盛、揮舞\n(無詞性變化)\nbusiness flourishes 生意興隆\nwith a flourish 誇張地、大張旗鼓地\nPlants flourish in warm and humid weather.\n(植物在溫暖潮濕的天氣中長得茂盛。)\nArt and literature flourished during the Tang Dynasty.\n(藝術和文學在唐朝蓬勃發展。)"],["flunk","flunk(v./n.)考不及格、當掉、不及格\n(無詞性變化)\nflunk a test 考試不及格\nflunk out 因成績不及格而退學\nHe flunked his math test because he didn't study at all.\n(他因為完全沒讀書，數學考試不及格。)\nIf you keep skipping classes, you might flunk out of college.\n(如果你一直翹課，可能會被大學退學。)"],["foe","foe(n.)敵人、仇敵\n(無詞性變化)\nfriend or foe 是敵是友\na bitter foe 死敵\nThe two former foes finally shook hands and made peace.\n(這兩個昔日的仇敵終於握手言和。)\nIn the story, the hero must defeat his ancient foe.\n(在這個故事裡，英雄必須打敗他的宿敵。)"],["folklore","folklore(n.)民間傳說、民俗\nfolk(adj./n.)民間的、人們\nlocal folklore 地方傳說\nChinese folklore 中國民間傳說\nAccording to local folklore, a dragon once lived in the lake.\n(根據當地傳說，曾經有一條龍住在湖裡。)\nThe museum displays objects related to Taiwanese folklore.\n(這座博物館展出與臺灣民俗相關的物品。)"],["formidable","formidable(adj.)可怕的、難對付的、令人敬畏的\nformidably(adv.)令人生畏地\na formidable opponent 難纏的對手\na formidable task 艱鉅的任務\nThe champion is a formidable opponent for any young player.\n(這位冠軍對任何年輕選手來說都是難纏的對手。)\nRebuilding the city after the earthquake was a formidable task.\n(地震後重建城市是一項艱鉅的任務。)"],["formulate","formulate(v.)規劃、制定、清楚表達\nformulation(n.)制定、表述\nformula(n.)公式\nformulate a plan 擬定計畫\nformulate a policy 制定政策\nThe committee formulated a new plan to reduce traffic jams.\n(委員會擬定了一項減少塞車的新計畫。)\nIt took her some time to formulate her answer clearly.\n(她花了一點時間才清楚地組織好她的回答。)"],["forsake","forsake(v.)拋棄、遺棄、放棄\nforsaken(adj.)被遺棄的\nforsake one's friends 拋棄朋友\na godforsaken place 荒涼的地方\nHe promised that he would never forsake his family.\n(他承諾永遠不會拋棄家人。)\nShe forsook her comfortable life in the city to help farmers in the mountains.\n(她放棄城市的舒適生活去幫助山區的農民。)"],["forthcoming","forthcoming(adj.)即將到來的、現成的、樂於提供資訊的\n(無詞性變化)\nthe forthcoming election 即將到來的選舉\nforthcoming book 即將出版的書\nThe students are busy preparing for the forthcoming exams.\n(學生們正忙著準備即將到來的考試。)\nThe witness was not very forthcoming about what he had seen.\n(那位證人對於他所看到的事不太願意多說。)"],["fortify","fortify(v.)加強防禦、強化、增強\nfortification(n.)防禦工事\nfortified with vitamins 添加維生素\nfortify a city 加強城市的防禦\nThe soldiers fortified the castle against the coming attack.\n(士兵們加強了城堡的防禦，以應付即將來臨的攻擊。)\nThis cereal is fortified with iron and vitamins.\n(這種穀片添加了鐵質和維生素。)"],["fowl","fowl(n.)家禽、禽類\n(無詞性變化)\ndomestic fowl 家禽\nwild fowl 野禽\nChickens, ducks, and geese are common domestic fowl.\n(雞、鴨和鵝是常見的家禽。)\nThe farmer raises fowl and pigs on his land.\n(那位農夫在他的土地上養家禽和豬。)"],["fracture","fracture(n./v.)骨折、裂縫、使破裂\n(無詞性變化)\nbone fracture 骨折\nfracture one's arm 手臂骨折\nHe fractured his arm when he fell off his bike.\n(他從腳踏車上摔下來時手臂骨折了。)\nThe X-ray showed a small fracture in her ankle.\n(X光片顯示她的腳踝有輕微骨折。)"],["fragrance","fragrance(n.)香味、芳香、香水\nfragrant(adj.)芳香的\nsweet fragrance 甜美的香氣\nfragrance-free 無香料的\nThe fragrance of jasmine filled the garden in the evening.\n(傍晚時，茉莉花的香氣瀰漫整座花園。)\nThis soap is fragrance-free, so it is good for sensitive skin.\n(這塊肥皂不含香料，所以適合敏感肌膚。)"],["fragrant","fragrant(adj.)芳香的、香的\nfragrance(n.)香味\nfragrant flowers 芳香的花朵\nfragrant tea 香氣四溢的茶\nThe fragrant smell of coffee woke me up this morning.\n(今天早上咖啡的香氣把我喚醒。)\nOsmanthus flowers are small but very fragrant.\n(桂花雖小卻非常芳香。)"],["frantic","frantic(adj.)發狂似的、狂亂的、忙亂的\nfrantically(adv.)發狂似地、拚命地\nfrantic search 瘋狂搜尋\nfrantic with worry 急得發狂\nThe mother was frantic with worry when her child went missing.\n(孩子失蹤時，那位母親急得快發瘋了。)\nHe searched frantically for his passport before the flight.\n(登機前他拚命地找他的護照。)"],["freak","freak(n./v.)怪人、狂熱者、異常的事、(使)抓狂\nfreaky(adj.)怪異的\nfreak out 嚇壞、抓狂\na control freak 控制狂\nMy sister freaked out when she saw a cockroach in her room.\n(我姊姊看到房間裡有蟑螂時嚇壞了。)\nHe is a fitness freak who goes to the gym every day.\n(他是個健身狂，每天都上健身房。)"],["freeway","freeway(n.)高速公路\n(無詞性變化)\non the freeway 在高速公路上\nfreeway exit 高速公路出口\nTraffic on the freeway was heavy during the holiday weekend.\n(連假期間高速公路上的車流量很大。)\nTake the next freeway exit to get to the airport.\n(從下一個高速公路出口下去就能到機場。)"],["friction","friction(n.)摩擦、摩擦力、不和\n(無詞性變化)\ncause friction 引起摩擦\nfriction between 之間的不和\nFriction between the tires and the road helps the car stop.\n(輪胎與路面之間的摩擦力幫助車子停下來。)\nDifferent opinions about money caused friction between the two partners.\n(對金錢的不同看法造成兩位合夥人之間的摩擦。)"],["fume","fume(v./n.)發怒、冒煙、(有害的)煙、氣體\n(無詞性變化)\nexhaust fumes 廢氣\nfume at/over 對…發怒\nBreathing in exhaust fumes every day is bad for your lungs.\n(每天吸入廢氣對肺部有害。)\nShe was fuming over the rude comments posted online.\n(她對網路上無禮的留言感到非常憤怒。)"],["fury","fury(n.)狂怒、暴怒、猛烈\nfurious(adj.)狂怒的\nin a fury 盛怒之下\nthe fury of the storm 暴風雨的猛烈\nHe left the room in a fury after the argument.\n(爭吵之後他怒氣沖沖地離開了房間。)\nThe village was hit by the full fury of the typhoon.\n(這個村莊遭受颱風猛烈的侵襲。)"],["fuse","fuse(n./v.)保險絲、導火線、熔合、融合\nfusion(n.)融合、核融合\nblow a fuse 燒斷保險絲、大發脾氣\nfusion cuisine 創意融合料理\nThe lights went out because a fuse had blown.\n(因為保險絲燒斷了，燈都熄了。)\nThe restaurant fuses Japanese and Italian cooking styles.\n(這家餐廳融合了日式與義式的烹調風格。)"],["fuss","fuss(n./v.)大驚小怪、小題大作、忙亂\nfussy(adj.)挑剔的、大驚小怪的\nmake a fuss about 對…大驚小怪\na fussy eater 挑食的人\nDon't make such a fuss about a small scratch.\n(別為了一點小擦傷大驚小怪。)\nMy little brother is a fussy eater who refuses to eat vegetables.\n(我弟弟很挑食，不肯吃蔬菜。)"],["gallop","gallop(n./v.)(馬)疾馳、飛奔\n(無詞性變化)\nat a gallop 疾馳著\ngallop across 飛奔越過\nThe horses galloped across the open field.\n(馬兒們飛奔越過空曠的原野。)\nThe knight rode away at a gallop to deliver the message.\n(騎士策馬疾馳而去傳遞消息。)"],["gangster","gangster(n.)歹徒、幫派分子\ngang(n.)幫派\ngangster movie 黑幫電影\na notorious gangster 惡名昭彰的歹徒\nThe film tells the story of a gangster in 1930s Chicago.\n(這部電影講述1930年代芝加哥一名幫派分子的故事。)\nThe police finally arrested the gangster after a long investigation.\n(經過長期調查，警方終於逮捕了那名歹徒。)"],["garment","garment(n.)衣服、服裝\n(無詞性變化)\ngarment industry 成衣業\na woolen garment 毛料衣物\nThe garment industry employs many workers in Southeast Asia.\n(成衣業在東南亞僱用了許多勞工。)\nPlease read the care label before washing the garment.\n(清洗這件衣物前請先閱讀洗滌標籤。)"],["gauge","gauge(n./v.)測量儀器、標準、測量、估計\n(無詞性變化)\nfuel gauge 油表\ngauge public opinion 評估輿論\nThe fuel gauge shows that we are almost out of gas.\n(油表顯示我們快沒油了。)\nThe survey was designed to gauge students' interest in the new club.\n(這份調查是為了評估學生對新社團的興趣。)"],["gay","gay(adj./n.)同性戀的、快樂的、同性戀者\n(無詞性變化)\ngay rights 同志權益\ngay marriage 同性婚姻\nTaiwan became the first place in Asia to legalize gay marriage.\n(臺灣成為亞洲第一個同性婚姻合法化的地方。)\nIn older novels, the word 'gay' often simply means cheerful.\n(在較舊的小說中，gay這個字常常只是指愉快的。)"],["geographical","geographical(adj.)地理的、地理學的\ngeography(n.)地理\ngeographically(adv.)地理上\ngeographical location 地理位置\ngeographical features 地理特徵\nTaiwan's geographical location makes it a hub for shipping in Asia.\n(臺灣的地理位置使其成為亞洲的航運樞紐。)\nMountains and rivers are important geographical features of the island.\n(山脈和河流是這座島重要的地理特徵。)"],["geometry","geometry(n.)幾何學\ngeometric(adj.)幾何的\ngeometry class 幾何課\ngeometric shapes 幾何圖形\nWe learned how to calculate the area of triangles in geometry class.\n(我們在幾何課上學了如何計算三角形的面積。)\nThe carpet is decorated with colorful geometric patterns.\n(這塊地毯上有色彩繽紛的幾何圖案。)"],["glacier","glacier(n.)冰河\nglacial(adj.)冰河的、冰冷的\nmelting glaciers 融化的冰河\nglacier national park 冰河國家公園\nGlobal warming is causing glaciers around the world to melt.\n(全球暖化正導致世界各地的冰河融化。)\nWe took a boat tour to see the huge glaciers in Alaska.\n(我們搭船遊覽觀賞阿拉斯加的巨大冰河。)"],["glamorous","glamorous(adj.)富有魅力的、光鮮亮麗的\nglamour(n.)魅力\na glamorous lifestyle 光鮮亮麗的生活\na glamorous movie star 迷人的電影明星\nBeing a model may look glamorous, but it is actually hard work.\n(當模特兒看似光鮮亮麗，其實非常辛苦。)\nShe wore a glamorous gown to the award ceremony.\n(她穿著一襲迷人的禮服出席頒獎典禮。)"],["glamour","glamour(n.)魅力、誘惑力\nglamorous(adj.)富有魅力的\nthe glamour of Hollywood 好萊塢的魅力\nadd glamour to 為…增添魅力\nMany young people are attracted by the glamour of show business.\n(許多年輕人被演藝圈的光環所吸引。)\nThe bright lights added glamour to the evening party.\n(明亮的燈光為晚會增添了華麗的氣氛。)"],["gleam","gleam(n./v.)微光、閃爍、閃現\n(無詞性變化)\na gleam of hope 一線希望\ngleam with 閃耀著…\nHer eyes gleamed with excitement when she opened the gift.\n(她打開禮物時，眼中閃耀著興奮的光芒。)\nAfter weeks of searching, there was finally a gleam of hope.\n(經過數週的搜尋，終於出現了一線希望。)"],["glide","glide(v./n.)滑行、滑翔、溜\nglider(n.)滑翔機\nglide across 滑過…\nglide through the air 在空中滑翔\nThe swans glided gracefully across the lake.\n(天鵝優雅地滑過湖面。)\nThe eagle glided through the air without moving its wings.\n(老鷹不拍動翅膀就在空中滑翔。)"],["glitter","glitter(n./v.)閃爍、閃光、亮片\nglittering(adj.)閃閃發光的、輝煌的\nAll that glitters is not gold. 閃亮的不一定都是金子\nglitter in the sun 在陽光下閃閃發光\nThe lake glittered in the morning sun.\n(湖水在晨光中閃閃發亮。)\nThe children decorated their cards with glue and glitter.\n(孩子們用膠水和亮片裝飾他們的卡片。)"],["gloom","gloom(n./v.)陰暗、憂鬱、使憂鬱\ngloomy(adj.)陰暗的、憂鬱的\ndoom and gloom 悲觀氣氛\na gloomy day 陰沉的一天\nA sense of gloom spread through the team after the defeat.\n(戰敗後，整支隊伍瀰漫著沮喪的氣氛。)\nThe gloomy weather made everyone want to stay indoors.\n(陰沉的天氣讓大家都想待在室內。)"],["goalkeeper","goalkeeper(n.)守門員\ngoalie(n.)守門員(口語)\na brilliant goalkeeper 出色的守門員\ngoalkeeper gloves 守門員手套\nThe goalkeeper made an amazing save in the last minute of the game.\n(守門員在比賽最後一分鐘做出了驚人的撲救。)\nOur team's goalkeeper is tall and quick to react.\n(我們隊的守門員又高反應又快。)"],["goodwill","goodwill(n.)善意、友好、商譽\n(無詞性變化)\na gesture of goodwill 善意的表示\ngoodwill ambassador 親善大使\nThe two countries exchanged gifts as a gesture of goodwill.\n(兩國互贈禮物以表達善意。)\nThe famous actress was named a UNICEF goodwill ambassador.\n(那位知名女演員被任命為聯合國兒童基金會親善大使。)"],["gorilla","gorilla(n.)大猩猩\n(無詞性變化)\nmountain gorilla 山地大猩猩\na group of gorillas 一群大猩猩\nGorillas live in the forests of central Africa.\n(大猩猩生活在中非的森林裡。)\nMountain gorillas are endangered because of habitat loss and hunting.\n(山地大猩猩因棲地流失和獵捕而瀕臨絕種。)"],["gospel","gospel(n.)福音、真理、信條\n(無詞性變化)\ngospel music 福音音樂\ntake sth. as gospel 對某事深信不疑\nThe choir sang gospel songs at the Christmas concert.\n(合唱團在聖誕音樂會上演唱福音歌曲。)\nDon't take everything you read online as gospel.\n(不要對網路上讀到的每件事都深信不疑。)"],["grapefruit","grapefruit(n.)葡萄柚\n(無詞性變化)\ngrapefruit juice 葡萄柚汁\npink grapefruit 紅肉葡萄柚\nI drink a glass of grapefruit juice with my breakfast every morning.\n(我每天早上吃早餐時都喝一杯葡萄柚汁。)\nGrapefruit tastes a little bitter, but it is rich in vitamin C.\n(葡萄柚嚐起來有點苦，但富含維生素C。)"],["graze","graze(v.)吃草、放牧、擦傷\n(無詞性變化)\ngraze on grass 吃草\ngraze one's knee 擦傷膝蓋\nSheep were grazing peacefully on the green hills.\n(羊群在綠色山丘上悠閒地吃草。)\nShe fell off her scooter and grazed her knee.\n(她從滑板車上摔下來，擦傷了膝蓋。)"],["grease","grease(n./v.)油脂、潤滑油、塗油\ngreasy(adj.)油膩的\ngreasy food 油膩的食物\ngrease the pan 在鍋子上抹油\nGrease the pan with butter before pouring in the batter.\n(倒入麵糊前先在烤盤上抹奶油。)\nEating too much greasy food is bad for your health.\n(吃太多油膩的食物對健康不好。)"],["groan","groan(n./v.)呻吟、抱怨、發出嘎吱聲\n(無詞性變化)\ngroan in pain 痛苦地呻吟\nlet out a groan 發出呻吟聲\nThe students groaned when the teacher announced another test.\n(老師宣布又要考試時，學生們一片哀號。)\nThe injured player lay on the field, groaning in pain.\n(受傷的球員躺在場上痛苦地呻吟。)"],["growl","growl(n./v.)(動物)低吼、咆哮、低聲抱怨\n(無詞性變化)\ngrowl at 對…低吼\nstomach growls 肚子咕嚕叫\nThe dog growled at the stranger standing by the gate.\n(那隻狗對站在門口的陌生人低吼。)\nMy stomach growled loudly during the quiet exam.\n(安靜的考試中，我的肚子咕嚕咕嚕地大聲叫。)"],["grumble","grumble(v./n.)抱怨、發牢騷、抱怨聲\n(無詞性變化)\ngrumble about 抱怨…\nwithout a grumble 毫無怨言\nHe always grumbles about the food in the school cafeteria.\n(他總是抱怨學校餐廳的食物。)\nShe did all the housework without a grumble.\n(她毫無怨言地做完了所有家事。)"],["hacker","hacker(n.)駭客\nhack(v.)入侵(電腦系統)\nhacking(n.)駭客行為\ncomputer hacker 電腦駭客\nhacker attack 駭客攻擊\nA hacker broke into the company's system and stole customer data.\n(一名駭客入侵公司的系統並竊取了客戶資料。)\nThe bank hired experts to protect its website from hacker attacks.\n(那家銀行聘請專家保護網站免受駭客攻擊。)"],["hail","hail(n./v.)冰雹、下冰雹、歡呼、招呼\n(無詞性變化)\nhail a taxi 招計程車\nbe hailed as 被譽為\nHeavy hail damaged many cars parked along the street last night.\n(昨晚的大冰雹損壞了許多停在路邊的車。)\nThe young scientist was hailed as a hero after her discovery.\n(那位年輕科學家在有所發現後被譽為英雄。)"],["hamper","hamper(v.)妨礙、阻礙\n(無詞性變化)\nhamper efforts 阻礙努力\nhamper progress 妨礙進展\nHeavy rain hampered the rescue workers' efforts to reach the village.\n(大雨妨礙了救難人員抵達村莊的行動。)\nA lack of funding has seriously hampered the progress of the research.\n(資金短缺嚴重阻礙了研究的進展。)"],["handicap","handicap(n./v.)障礙、不利條件、妨礙\nhandicapped(adj.)身心障礙的\nphysical handicap 身體障礙\nbe handicapped by 受…所阻礙\nNot speaking the local language can be a real handicap when traveling.\n(旅行時不會說當地語言可能是很大的不利條件。)\nThe team was handicapped by injuries to two key players.\n(球隊因兩名主力球員受傷而處於劣勢。)"],["handicraft","handicraft(n.)手工藝、手工藝品\n(無詞性變化)\ntraditional handicrafts 傳統手工藝品\nhandicraft market 手工藝市集\nTourists often buy traditional handicrafts as souvenirs in Lukang.\n(遊客在鹿港常會買傳統手工藝品當作紀念品。)\nThe village is famous for its bamboo handicrafts made by local artists.\n(這個村莊以當地藝術家製作的竹編手工藝品聞名。)"],["harass(ment)","harass(v.)騷擾、侵擾、harassment(n.)騷擾\n(無詞性變化)\nsexual harassment 性騷擾\nonline harassment 網路騷擾\nThe singer complained that photographers kept harassing her family.\n(那位歌手抱怨攝影師一直騷擾她的家人。)\nThe school has clear rules to deal with online harassment among students.\n(學校有明確的規定來處理學生之間的網路騷擾。)"],["harden","harden(v.)使變硬、變得冷酷、使堅定\nhard(adj.)硬的\nhardened(adj.)變硬的、冷酷無情的\nharden one's heart 硬起心腸\nharden into 變硬成為\nThe melted chocolate will harden as it cools down.\n(融化的巧克力冷卻後會變硬。)\nYears of hardship had hardened him into a cold and silent man.\n(多年的艱苦使他變成一個冷漠寡言的人。)"],["harmonica","harmonica(n.)口琴\n(無詞性變化)\nplay the harmonica 吹口琴\nharmonica band 口琴隊\nMy grandfather taught me how to play the harmonica when I was ten.\n(我十歲時，爺爺教我吹口琴。)\nShe joined the school harmonica band and practiced every afternoon.\n(她加入學校的口琴隊，每天下午都練習。)"],["harness","harness(n./v.)馬具、安全吊帶、駕馭、利用\n(無詞性變化)\nharness energy 利用能源\nsafety harness 安全吊帶\nMany countries are trying to harness wind and solar energy.\n(許多國家正努力利用風能與太陽能。)\nClimbers must wear a safety harness at all times.\n(攀岩者必須全程穿戴安全吊帶。)"],["haunt","haunt(v./n.)(鬼魂)出沒、縈繞心頭、常去的地方\nhaunted(adj.)鬧鬼的\nhaunting(adj.)縈繞心頭的\nhaunted house 鬼屋\nfavorite haunt 常去的地方\nPeople say the old house on the hill is haunted by a ghost.\n(人們說山丘上那棟老房子有鬼出沒。)\nThe memory of the accident continued to haunt him for years.\n(那場意外的記憶多年來一直縈繞在他心頭。)"],["headphone(s)","headphone(n.)耳機、headphones(n.)頭戴式耳機\n(無詞性變化)\nwear headphones 戴耳機\nnoise-canceling headphones 降噪耳機\nHe always wears headphones on the MRT to avoid the noise.\n(他搭捷運時總是戴著耳機以隔絕噪音。)\nListening to loud music through headphones can damage your hearing.\n(用耳機聽很大聲的音樂可能會損害聽力。)"],["healthful","healthful(adj.)有益健康的\nhealth(n.)健康\nhealthy(adj.)健康的\nhealthful diet 有益健康的飲食\nhealthful food 健康食品\nA healthful diet should include plenty of fresh fruits and vegetables.\n(有益健康的飲食應該包含大量新鮮蔬果。)\nWalking in fresh air is a simple and healthful habit.\n(在新鮮空氣中散步是簡單又有益健康的習慣。)"],["hearty","hearty(adj.)熱忱的、豐盛的、衷心的\nheartily(adv.)熱情地、盡情地\nhearty meal 豐盛的一餐\nhearty welcome 熱烈的歡迎\nAfter the long hike, we enjoyed a hearty meal at a local restaurant.\n(長途健行後，我們在當地餐廳享用了一頓豐盛的餐點。)\nThe exchange students received a hearty welcome from their host families.\n(交換學生受到寄宿家庭熱烈的歡迎。)"],["hedge","hedge(n./v.)樹籬、防範措施、避免正面回答\n(無詞性變化)\nhedge against 防範、對沖\ntrim the hedge 修剪樹籬\nMy father spent the whole afternoon trimming the hedge in the garden.\n(我爸爸花了整個下午修剪花園裡的樹籬。)\nWhen reporters asked about the scandal, the minister hedged and changed the subject.\n(記者詢問醜聞時，部長避重就輕並轉移話題。)"],["heighten","heighten(v.)提高、增強、加劇\nheight(n.)高度\nheightened(adj.)提高的\nheighten awareness 提高意識\nheighten tension 加劇緊張\nThe campaign aims to heighten public awareness of ocean pollution.\n(這項活動旨在提高大眾對海洋汙染的意識。)\nThe dramatic music heightened the tension in the final scene of the movie.\n(戲劇性的配樂增強了電影最後一幕的緊張感。)"],["hemisphere","hemisphere(n.)半球、大腦半球\n(無詞性變化)\nNorthern Hemisphere 北半球\nleft hemisphere 左腦\nWhen it is summer in the Northern Hemisphere, it is winter in Australia.\n(北半球是夏天時，澳洲正值冬天。)\nThe left hemisphere of the brain is closely linked to language.\n(大腦的左半球與語言能力密切相關。)"],["heroic","heroic(adj./n.)英勇的、英雄的、英雄式的言行\nhero(n.)英雄\nheroism(n.)英勇行為\nheroic act 英勇的行為\nheroic effort 英勇的努力\nThe firefighter received a medal for his heroic act during the fire.\n(那位消防員因在火災中的英勇行為而獲頒獎章。)\nDespite their heroic efforts, the doctors could not save the patient.\n(儘管醫生們盡了最大努力，仍未能救回那名病人。)"],["heroin","heroin(n.)海洛因\n(無詞性變化)\nheroin addiction 海洛因成癮\nheroin smuggling 海洛因走私\nCustoms officers found a large amount of heroin hidden in the suitcase.\n(海關人員在行李箱中發現大量藏匿的海洛因。)\nThe documentary shows how heroin addiction can destroy a family.\n(這部紀錄片呈現海洛因成癮如何摧毀一個家庭。)"],["heterosexual","heterosexual(adj./n.)異性戀的、異性戀者\nheterosexuality(n.)異性戀\nheterosexual couple 異性伴侶\nheterosexual relationship 異性關係\nThe survey included both heterosexual and same-sex couples.\n(這項調查同時涵蓋了異性伴侶與同性伴侶。)\nThe law gives same-sex couples the same rights as heterosexual couples.\n(這項法律賦予同性伴侶與異性伴侶相同的權利。)"],["hierarchy","hierarchy(n.)階級制度、等級體系\nhierarchical(adj.)階級制的\nsocial hierarchy 社會階級\nin the hierarchy 在階級體系中\nIn the past, the social hierarchy decided what jobs people could have.\n(在過去，社會階級決定了人們能從事什麼工作。)\nShe quickly moved up the company's hierarchy because of her ability.\n(她憑藉能力在公司的階級體系中迅速晉升。)"],["hijack","hijack(v./n.)劫持(交通工具)、挾持、劫機事件\nhijacker(n.)劫機者\nhijack a plane 劫機\nhijack a conversation 搶走話題\nArmed men tried to hijack the plane shortly after it took off.\n(起飛後不久，武裝分子企圖劫持那架飛機。)\nHe always hijacks the conversation and talks only about himself.\n(他總是搶走話題，只談論自己的事。)"],["hoarse","hoarse(adj.)(聲音)沙啞的\nhoarsely(adv.)沙啞地\ngo hoarse 嗓子變啞\nhoarse voice 沙啞的聲音\nAfter cheering for three hours at the game, my voice went hoarse.\n(在比賽中加油三個小時後，我的聲音都啞了。)\nThe teacher spoke in a hoarse voice because she had a bad cold.\n(老師因重感冒而聲音沙啞。)"],["homosexual","homosexual(adj./n.)同性戀的、同性戀者\nhomosexuality(n.)同性戀\nhomosexual couple 同性伴侶\nhomosexual rights 同志權益\nIn 2019, Taiwan became the first place in Asia to legalize marriage for homosexual couples.\n(2019 年，台灣成為亞洲第一個讓同性伴侶婚姻合法化的地方。)\nThe class discussed how attitudes toward homosexual people have changed over time.\n(全班討論了社會對同性戀者的態度如何隨時間改變。)"],["honorary","honorary(adj.)榮譽的、名譽的\nhonor(n.)榮譽\nhonorary degree 榮譽學位\nhonorary citizen 榮譽市民\nThe university awarded the famous writer an honorary degree.\n(那所大學頒給這位知名作家榮譽學位。)\nThe coach was made an honorary citizen of the city after the victory.\n(那位教練在獲勝後被授予榮譽市民的身分。)"],["hospitable","hospitable(adj.)好客的、宜人的\nhospitality(n.)好客、款待\ninhospitable(adj.)不好客的、荒涼的\nhospitable people 好客的人們\nbe hospitable to 對…好客\nThe local people were so hospitable that we felt at home.\n(當地人非常好客，讓我們感到賓至如歸。)\nThe warm climate makes the island hospitable to many kinds of plants.\n(溫暖的氣候使這座島適合許多種植物生長。)"],["hospitality","hospitality(n.)好客、殷勤款待、餐旅業\nhospitable(adj.)好客的\nwarm hospitality 熱情款待\nhospitality industry 餐旅業\nThank you for your warm hospitality during our stay in Tainan.\n(謝謝你們在我們停留台南期間的熱情款待。)\nShe plans to study hospitality management and work in a hotel.\n(她打算讀餐旅管理並在飯店工作。)"],["hospitalize","hospitalize(v.)使住院\nhospital(n.)醫院\nhospitalization(n.)住院\nbe hospitalized for 因…住院\nhospitalized patients 住院病人\nHe was hospitalized for a week after the serious car accident.\n(他在嚴重車禍後住院了一個星期。)\nSeveral students were hospitalized after eating spoiled food at the camp.\n(幾名學生在營隊吃了壞掉的食物後住院。)"],["hostel","hostel(n.)青年旅館、招待所\n(無詞性變化)\nyouth hostel 青年旅館\nstay at a hostel 住青年旅館\nBackpackers often stay at youth hostels to save money.\n(背包客常住青年旅館來省錢。)\nThe hostel near the station was clean, cheap, and full of travelers.\n(車站附近的青年旅館乾淨、便宜，而且住滿了旅客。)"],["hover","hover(v./n.)盤旋、徘徊、搖擺不定\n(無詞性變化)\nhover over 在…上空盤旋\nhover around 在…左右徘徊\nA helicopter hovered over the building during the rescue.\n(救援期間，一架直升機在大樓上空盤旋。)\nTemperatures hovered around 35 degrees for most of the week.\n(這週大部分時間氣溫都在三十五度上下徘徊。)"],["humiliate","humiliate(v.)羞辱、使丟臉\nhumiliation(n.)羞辱\nhumiliating(adj.)丟臉的、屈辱的\npublicly humiliate 公開羞辱\nfeel humiliated 感到受辱\nThe coach humiliated the player by shouting at him in front of everyone.\n(教練當眾對那名球員大吼，讓他顏面盡失。)\nLosing the game 10 to 0 was a humiliating experience for the team.\n(以十比零輸球對球隊來說是一次屈辱的經驗。)"],["hunch","hunch(n./v.)直覺、預感、弓起背\n(無詞性變化)\nhave a hunch 有預感\nhunch over 駝背、彎身\nI have a hunch that our team is going to win today.\n(我有預感我們隊今天會贏。)\nSitting hunched over a phone for hours is bad for your back.\n(駝著背滑手機好幾個小時對背部不好。)"],["hurdle","hurdle(n./v.)障礙、欄架、跨越障礙\nhurdler(n.)跨欄選手\novercome a hurdle 克服障礙\nclear a hurdle 跨過欄架\nPassing the entrance exam was the first hurdle on his way to medical school.\n(通過入學考試是他進入醫學院路上的第一道關卡。)\nShe won the gold medal in the 100-meter hurdles.\n(她在一百公尺跨欄中奪得金牌。)"],["hybrid","hybrid(adj./n.)混合的、雜交的、混種、混合物\nhybridize(v.)使雜交\nhybrid car 油電混合車\nhybrid of 混合體\nHybrid cars use both gasoline and electricity to save energy.\n(油電混合車同時使用汽油和電力來節省能源。)\nThe new course is a hybrid of online and classroom learning.\n(這門新課程結合了線上學習與課堂學習。)"],["hygiene","hygiene(n.)衛生、衛生學\nhygienic(adj.)衛生的\npersonal hygiene 個人衛生\nfood hygiene 食品衛生\nWashing your hands often is an important part of personal hygiene.\n(經常洗手是個人衛生的重要一環。)\nThe restaurant was fined for poor food hygiene.\n(那家餐廳因食品衛生不佳而被罰款。)"],["hypocrite","hypocrite(n.)偽君子、虛偽的人\nhypocrisy(n.)虛偽\nhypocritical(adj.)虛偽的\ntotal hypocrite 十足的偽君子\ncall sb. a hypocrite 說某人虛偽\nHe tells others to save energy but drives everywhere, so people call him a hypocrite.\n(他叫別人節能卻到哪都開車，所以大家說他是偽君子。)\nI don't want to be a hypocrite who says one thing and does another.\n(我不想當個說一套做一套的偽君子。)"],["iceberg","iceberg(n.)冰山\n(無詞性變化)\nthe tip of the iceberg 冰山一角\nhit an iceberg 撞上冰山\nThe Titanic sank after it hit an iceberg in 1912.\n(鐵達尼號在 1912 年撞上冰山後沉沒。)\nThe cases we know about are just the tip of the iceberg.\n(我們所知道的案例只是冰山一角。)"],["illuminate","illuminate(v.)照亮、闡明、啟發\nillumination(n.)照明、闡明\nilluminating(adj.)富啟發性的\nbrightly illuminated 燈火通明\nilluminate the problem 闡明問題\nAt night, thousands of lights illuminate Taipei 101.\n(夜晚，成千上萬盞燈照亮台北 101。)\nThe professor used simple examples to illuminate the difficult theory.\n(教授用簡單的例子闡明那個艱澀的理論。)"],["imminent","imminent(adj.)即將發生的、迫近的\nimminence(n.)迫近\nimminent danger 迫在眉睫的危險\nimminent threat 迫切的威脅\nDark clouds and strong winds warned us that a storm was imminent.\n(烏雲和強風警告我們暴風雨即將來臨。)\nThe old bridge was closed because it was in imminent danger of collapse.\n(那座舊橋因隨時可能倒塌而被封閉。)"],["imperative","imperative(adj./n.)極重要的、必要的、命令的、必要之事\n(無詞性變化)\nit is imperative that 務必…\nmoral imperative 道德義務\nIt is imperative that we take action to reduce plastic waste.\n(我們務必採取行動減少塑膠垃圾。)\nProtecting children's safety is a moral imperative for every society.\n(保護兒童安全是每個社會的道德義務。)"],["imperial","imperial(adj.)帝國的、皇帝的\nempire(n.)帝國\nemperor(n.)皇帝\nimperial palace 皇宮\nimperial family 皇室\nTourists line up every day to visit the Imperial Palace in Tokyo.\n(遊客每天排隊參觀東京的皇居。)\nThe museum displays treasures used by the imperial family of China.\n(這間博物館展出中國皇室使用過的寶物。)"],["implicit","implicit(adj.)含蓄的、暗示的、絕對的\nimplicitly(adv.)含蓄地、絕對地\nimplicit meaning 言外之意\nimplicit trust 絕對信任\nThere was an implicit criticism in his polite comment.\n(他那句客氣的評論中隱含著批評。)\nThe team has implicit trust in their captain's decisions.\n(隊員們絕對信任隊長的決定。)"],["imposing","imposing(adj.)壯觀的、雄偉的、氣勢逼人的\nimpose(v.)強加\nimposing building 雄偉的建築\nimposing figure 威風凜凜的人物\nThe Presidential Office is an imposing building in central Taipei.\n(總統府是台北市中心一座雄偉的建築。)\nThe tall, serious principal was an imposing figure to new students.\n(那位高大嚴肅的校長對新生來說很有威嚴。)"],["imprison(ment)","imprison(v.)監禁、使入獄、imprisonment(n.)監禁、徒刑\nprison(n.)監獄\nlife imprisonment 無期徒刑\nbe imprisoned for 因…入獄\nThe man was imprisoned for ten years for robbing a bank.\n(那名男子因搶劫銀行被判入獄十年。)\nThe judge sentenced the killer to life imprisonment.\n(法官判處那名兇手無期徒刑。)"],["incline","incline(v./n.)傾向於、使傾斜、斜坡\ninclination(n.)傾向、意願\ninclined(adj.)傾向於…的\nbe inclined to 傾向於\nsteep incline 陡坡\nI am inclined to agree with you, but I need more information.\n(我傾向於同意你，但我需要更多資訊。)\nThe bikers slowed down as they rode up the steep incline.\n(自行車騎士騎上陡坡時放慢了速度。)"],["inclusive","inclusive(adj.)包含在內的、包容的\ninclude(v.)包含\ninclusion(n.)包含、融合\ninclusive education 融合教育\nall-inclusive 費用全包的\nThe school promotes inclusive education for students of all abilities.\n(這所學校推動讓各種能力的學生一起學習的融合教育。)\nWe booked an all-inclusive trip, so meals and tickets are already paid for.\n(我們訂了全包式旅遊，所以餐點和門票都已付清。)"],["incur","incur(v.)招致、引起、蒙受\n(無詞性變化)\nincur costs 產生費用\nincur anger 招致憤怒\nYou will incur a late fee if you return the book after the due date.\n(如果在到期日後還書，你將被收取逾期費。)\nThe new policy incurred the anger of many local residents.\n(新政策引起許多當地居民的憤怒。)"],["indifference","indifference(n.)冷漠、漠不關心\nindifferent(adj.)漠不關心的\nindifferently(adv.)冷漠地\nindifference to 對…的冷漠\nwith indifference 冷淡地\nMany people showed indifference to the problem of climate change.\n(許多人對氣候變遷問題漠不關心。)\nShe listened to his excuses with complete indifference.\n(她完全冷淡地聽著他的藉口。)"],["indignant","indignant(adj.)憤慨的、義憤的\nindignation(n.)憤慨\nindignantly(adv.)憤慨地\nindignant at 對…感到憤慨\nindignant protest 憤慨的抗議\nThe customers were indignant at being treated so rudely by the staff.\n(顧客對於遭到店員如此無禮的對待感到憤慨。)\n'I did not cheat!' the student replied indignantly.\n(「我沒有作弊！」那個學生憤慨地回答。)"],["induce","induce(v.)誘使、引起、導致\ninducement(n.)誘因\ninduction(n.)歸納法、就職\ninduce sb. to 誘使某人\ninduce sleep 誘發睡意\nNothing could induce him to change his mind about the plan.\n(沒有任何事能讓他改變對這個計畫的想法。)\nSome medicines may induce sleep, so don't drive after taking them.\n(有些藥物會引起睡意，所以服用後別開車。)"],["industrialize","industrialize(v.)使工業化\nindustrial(adj.)工業的\nindustrialization(n.)工業化\nrapidly industrialize 快速工業化\nindustrialized countries 工業化國家\nTaiwan industrialized rapidly in the second half of the twentieth century.\n(台灣在二十世紀下半葉迅速工業化。)\nIndustrialized countries produce much more carbon dioxide than poor nations.\n(工業化國家排放的二氧化碳遠多於貧窮國家。)"],["infectious","infectious(adj.)傳染性的、有感染力的\ninfect(v.)傳染\ninfection(n.)感染\ninfectious disease 傳染病\ninfectious laugh 有感染力的笑聲\nDoctors are working hard to stop the spread of infectious diseases.\n(醫生們正努力阻止傳染病的擴散。)\nHer infectious laugh made everyone in the room smile.\n(她富有感染力的笑聲讓房裡每個人都笑了。)"],["infer","infer(v.)推論、推斷\ninference(n.)推論\ninfer from 從…推斷\nmake an inference 做出推論\nFrom his silence, I inferred that he was not happy with the result.\n(從他的沉默中，我推斷他對結果並不滿意。)\nReaders can infer the main idea from the first paragraph.\n(讀者可以從第一段推論出主旨。)"],["inflict","inflict(v.)施加(打擊、傷害等)、使承受\ninfliction(n.)施加、痛苦\ninflict damage 造成損害\ninflict pain on 使…承受痛苦\nThe typhoon inflicted serious damage on farms in southern Taiwan.\n(颱風對南台灣的農田造成嚴重損害。)\nBullies often inflict pain on others to feel powerful.\n(霸凌者常藉由使他人痛苦來感覺自己強大。)"],["inhabit","inhabit(v.)居住於、棲息於\ninhabitant(n.)居民\nhabitat(n.)棲息地\ninhabit an area 居住在某地區\ndensely inhabited 人口稠密的\nMany rare birds inhabit the wetlands along the west coast.\n(許多稀有鳥類棲息在西海岸的濕地。)\nThe island was once inhabited by only a few fishing families.\n(這座島曾經只有少數幾戶漁民居住。)"],["inhabitant","inhabitant(n.)居民、棲息的動物\ninhabit(v.)居住於\nlocal inhabitants 當地居民\noriginal inhabitants 原住民、原始居民\nThe town has about five thousand inhabitants, most of whom are farmers.\n(這個鎮大約有五千名居民，其中大多數是農民。)\nThe original inhabitants of the island had their own language and culture.\n(這座島的原始居民有自己的語言和文化。)"],["injustice","injustice(n.)不公正、不公平的事\njustice(n.)正義\nunjust(adj.)不公正的\nsocial injustice 社會不公\nfight injustice 對抗不公\nMany young people joined the protest to fight social injustice.\n(許多年輕人參加抗議活動來對抗社會不公。)\nHe felt a deep sense of injustice when he was punished for something he didn't do.\n(他因沒做過的事受罰時，深感不公平。)"],["inland","inland(adj./adv./n.)內陸的、在內陸、內陸地區\n(無詞性變化)\ninland areas 內陸地區\nmove inland 向內陸移動\nThe typhoon weakened as it moved inland over the mountains.\n(颱風向內陸移動越過山脈後減弱了。)\nInland areas usually have hotter summers than coastal cities.\n(內陸地區的夏天通常比沿海城市炎熱。)"],["innumerable","innumerable(adj.)無數的、數不清的\nnumerous(adj.)眾多的\ninnumerable stars 無數的星星\ninnumerable times 無數次\nOn a clear night in the mountains, you can see innumerable stars.\n(在山上晴朗的夜晚，你可以看到無數的星星。)\nThe scientist repeated the experiment innumerable times before she succeeded.\n(那位科學家重複實驗了無數次才成功。)"],["inquire","inquire(v.)詢問、打聽、調查\ninquiry(n.)詢問、調查\ninquire about 詢問有關…\ninquire into 調查\nI called the hotel to inquire about room prices for next weekend.\n(我打電話到飯店詢問下週末的房價。)\nThe committee will inquire into the causes of the accident.\n(委員會將調查這起意外的原因。)"],["insistence","insistence(n.)堅持、強調\ninsist(v.)堅持\ninsistent(adj.)堅持的\nat sb.'s insistence 在某人的堅持下\ninsistence on 堅持…\nAt my mother's insistence, I wore a jacket even though it was warm.\n(在媽媽的堅持下，雖然天氣暖和我還是穿了外套。)\nHis insistence on doing everything by himself slowed the whole team down.\n(他堅持凡事親力親為，拖慢了整個團隊。)"],["instinctive","instinctive(adj.)本能的、直覺的\ninstinct(n.)本能\ninstinctively(adv.)本能地\ninstinctive reaction 本能反應\ninstinctive fear 本能的恐懼\nPulling your hand away from something hot is an instinctive reaction.\n(碰到燙的東西時把手縮回是一種本能反應。)\nShe instinctively covered her head when the shelf began to fall.\n(架子開始倒下時，她本能地護住頭部。)"],["intake","intake(n.)攝取量、吸入、招收人數\n(無詞性變化)\ncalorie intake 卡路里攝取量\nsugar intake 糖分攝取\nDoctors advise people to reduce their daily sugar intake.\n(醫生建議人們減少每天的糖分攝取。)\nThe school plans to increase its student intake next year.\n(這所學校計畫明年增加招生人數。)"],["intellect","intellect(n.)智力、才智、知識分子\nintellectual(adj./n.)智力的、知識分子\nintelligent(adj.)聰明的\nsharp intellect 敏銳的才智\na person of great intellect 才智過人的人\nEinstein was a man of great intellect and imagination.\n(愛因斯坦是一位才智與想像力兼具的人。)\nReading widely helps develop both your intellect and your character.\n(廣泛閱讀有助於培養你的才智與品格。)"],["interpreter","interpreter(n.)口譯員、詮釋者\ninterpret(v.)口譯、詮釋\ninterpretation(n.)解釋、口譯\nsign language interpreter 手語翻譯員\nthrough an interpreter 透過口譯員\nThe president spoke to the foreign guests through an interpreter.\n(總統透過口譯員與外賓交談。)\nA sign language interpreter stood beside the speaker during the press conference.\n(記者會期間，一位手語翻譯員站在發言人身旁。)"],["intersection","intersection(n.)十字路口、交叉點\nintersect(v.)相交、交叉\nbusy intersection 繁忙的十字路口\nat the intersection 在十字路口\nTurn left at the next intersection, and you will see the museum.\n(在下一個路口左轉，你就會看到博物館。)\nTwo cars crashed at the busy intersection near our school.\n(兩輛車在我們學校附近繁忙的十字路口相撞。)"],["intervene","intervene(v.)干預、介入、調停\nintervention(n.)干預、介入\nintervene in 介入…\nintervene between 在…之間調停\nThe teacher had to intervene when the two students started fighting.\n(那兩名學生開始打架時，老師不得不介入。)\nThe government decided not to intervene in the price war.\n(政府決定不介入這場價格戰。)"],["intimacy","intimacy(n.)親密、親近\nintimate(adj.)親密的\nemotional intimacy 情感上的親密\na sense of intimacy 親密感\nThe small café has a warm sense of intimacy that customers love.\n(這家小咖啡館有一種顧客喜愛的溫馨親密感。)\nSharing secrets can build intimacy between close friends.\n(分享秘密能拉近好朋友之間的距離。)"],["intimidate","intimidate(v.)恐嚇、威脅、使膽怯\nintimidation(n.)恐嚇\nintimidating(adj.)令人生畏的\nfeel intimidated 感到膽怯\nintimidate witnesses 恐嚇證人\nDon't let the size of the other team intimidate you.\n(別讓對手的體型嚇倒你。)\nSpeaking in front of the whole school can be intimidating at first.\n(一開始在全校面前說話可能會讓人膽怯。)"],["intonation","intonation(n.)語調、聲調\nintone(v.)吟誦\nrising intonation 上揚的語調\nfalling intonation 下降的語調\nIn English, yes-no questions usually end with a rising intonation.\n(在英文中，是非問句通常以上揚語調結尾。)\nHer intonation made it clear that she was joking.\n(從她的語調明顯聽得出來她在開玩笑。)"],["intrigue","intrigue(n./v.)陰謀、詭計、激起興趣\nintriguing(adj.)引人入勝的\npolitical intrigue 政治陰謀\nbe intrigued by 對…很感興趣\nThe novel is full of political intrigue and surprising twists.\n(這本小說充滿了政治陰謀和出人意料的轉折。)\nI was intrigued by the strange symbols carved on the old stone.\n(我對那塊古老石頭上刻的奇怪符號很感興趣。)"],["intrude","intrude(v.)闖入、侵入、打擾\nintruder(n.)入侵者\nintrusion(n.)侵擾\nintrude on 打擾、侵犯\nintrude into 闖入\nI'm sorry to intrude, but there is an urgent call for you.\n(抱歉打擾，但有一通找你的緊急電話。)\nReporters should not intrude on people's private lives.\n(記者不應侵犯他人的私生活。)"],["intruder","intruder(n.)入侵者、闖入者\nintrude(v.)闖入\nintrusion(n.)侵入\narmed intruder 武裝入侵者\ncatch an intruder 抓到闖入者\nThe alarm went off when an intruder broke into the house at midnight.\n(半夜有人闖入屋內時，警報器響了起來。)\nThe dog barked loudly to warn its owner of the intruder.\n(那隻狗大聲吠叫，警告主人有人闖入。)"],["invaluable","invaluable(adj.)無價的、極寶貴的\nvalue(n.)價值\nvaluable(adj.)有價值的\ninvaluable experience 寶貴的經驗\ninvaluable help 極大的幫助\nWorking as a volunteer gave me invaluable experience in dealing with people.\n(擔任志工讓我在與人相處方面獲得寶貴的經驗。)\nYour advice has been invaluable to me during this difficult time.\n(在這段艱難時期，你的建議對我來說非常寶貴。)"],["invariably","invariably(adv.)總是、一向\ninvariable(adj.)不變的\nalmost invariably 幾乎總是\ninvariably late 總是遲到\nWhen he is nervous, he invariably starts talking too fast.\n(他一緊張，總是會開始講太快。)\nOur weekend plans are invariably canceled because of the rain.\n(我們的週末計畫總是因下雨而取消。)"],["inventory","inventory(n./v.)存貨、清單、盤點\n(無詞性變化)\ntake inventory 盤點存貨\ninventory list 存貨清單\nThe store closes early once a month to take inventory.\n(這家店每個月提早關門一次以盤點存貨。)\nThe manager made a detailed inventory of all the computers in the office.\n(經理把辦公室裡所有電腦列出一份詳細的清單。)"],["ironic","ironic(adj.)諷刺的、反諷的\nirony(n.)諷刺\nironically(adv.)諷刺地\nit is ironic that 諷刺的是\nironic smile 嘲諷的微笑\nIt is ironic that the fire station itself burned down.\n(諷刺的是，消防局本身竟然燒毀了。)\nIronically, the health expert was the first to catch the flu.\n(諷刺的是，那位健康專家是第一個得流感的。)"],["irritable","irritable(adj.)易怒的、急躁的\nirritate(v.)激怒\nirritability(n.)易怒\nbecome irritable 變得煩躁\nirritable mood 煩躁的心情\nLack of sleep can make people irritable and less focused.\n(睡眠不足會讓人變得易怒且不專心。)\nHe gets irritable when he is hungry, so we always bring snacks.\n(他一餓就會變得暴躁，所以我們總會帶點零食。)"],["irritate","irritate(v.)激怒、使惱怒、刺激(皮膚等)\nirritation(n.)惱怒、刺激\nirritating(adj.)令人惱火的\nirritate the skin 刺激皮膚\nbe irritated by 對…感到惱怒\nHer habit of interrupting others really irritates me.\n(她打斷別人說話的習慣真的讓我很惱火。)\nSome soaps contain chemicals that may irritate sensitive skin.\n(有些肥皂含有可能刺激敏感肌膚的化學物質。)"],["isle","isle(n.)島、小島\nislet(n.)小島\nthe British Isles 英倫諸島\ntropical isle 熱帶小島\nThey spent their honeymoon on a quiet tropical isle.\n(他們在一座寧靜的熱帶小島上度蜜月。)\nThe British Isles include Great Britain, Ireland, and many smaller islands.\n(英倫諸島包括大不列顛島、愛爾蘭島以及許多小島。)"],["itch","itch(n./v.)癢、渴望、發癢\nitchy(adj.)發癢的\nhave an itch 發癢\nitch to 渴望做…\nMosquito bites made my arms itch all night.\n(蚊子叮咬讓我的手臂癢了一整晚。)\nAfter months of studying, I'm itching to go on a trip.\n(讀了幾個月的書後，我很想去旅行。)"],["ivy","ivy(n.)常春藤\n(無詞性變化)\ncovered in ivy 爬滿常春藤\nIvy League 常春藤聯盟\nThe walls of the old library are covered in green ivy.\n(那座老圖書館的牆上爬滿了綠色的常春藤。)\nShe hopes to study at an Ivy League university in the United States.\n(她希望能就讀美國的常春藤聯盟大學。)"],["jade","jade(n.)玉、翡翠\n(無詞性變化)\njade bracelet 玉鐲\njade market 玉市\nMy grandmother gave me a jade bracelet as a birthday gift.\n(奶奶送我一只玉鐲當作生日禮物。)\nThe Jadeite Cabbage is one of the most famous treasures in the National Palace Museum.\n(翠玉白菜是故宮博物院最著名的館藏之一。)"],["janitor","janitor(n.)工友、管理員\n(無詞性變化)\nschool janitor 學校工友\nwork as a janitor 擔任管理員\nThe school janitor fixed the broken window in our classroom.\n(學校工友修好了我們教室破掉的窗戶。)\nHe worked as a janitor at night to pay for his college education.\n(他晚上當清潔管理員來支付大學學費。)"],["jasmine","jasmine(n.)茉莉、茉莉花\n(無詞性變化)\njasmine tea 茉莉花茶\njasmine flowers 茉莉花\nThe sweet smell of jasmine filled the garden in the evening.\n(傍晚時，茉莉花的香甜氣味瀰漫整座花園。)\nMy mother likes to drink a cup of jasmine tea after dinner.\n(我媽媽喜歡在晚餐後喝一杯茉莉花茶。)"],["jingle","jingle(n./v.)叮噹聲、廣告歌曲、發出叮噹聲\n(無詞性變化)\njingle bells 叮噹鈴\nadvertising jingle 廣告歌曲\nThe keys in his pocket jingled as he walked down the hall.\n(他走過走廊時，口袋裡的鑰匙叮噹作響。)\nThat catchy advertising jingle has been stuck in my head all day.\n(那首朗朗上口的廣告歌一整天都在我腦中揮之不去。)"],["jockey","jockey(n./v.)賽馬騎師、操作者、謀取(地位)\n(無詞性變化)\ndisc jockey 電台或舞會的音樂主持人(DJ)\njockey for position 爭奪有利位置\nThe jockey guided his horse to victory in the final race.\n(那位騎師在最後一場比賽中策馬奪冠。)\nSeveral companies are jockeying for position in the electric car market.\n(好幾家公司正在電動車市場中爭奪有利地位。)"],["jolly","jolly(adj./adv./v./n.)愉快的、非常、哄騙、歡樂\njollity(n.)歡樂\njolly good 非常好\njolly old man 快活的老人\nSanta Claus is often described as a jolly old man with a white beard.\n(聖誕老人常被描述成一位留著白鬍子的快活老人。)\nWe had a jolly time singing songs around the campfire.\n(我們圍著營火唱歌，度過了歡樂的時光。)"],["joyous","joyous(adj.)充滿歡樂的、快樂的\njoy(n.)歡樂\njoyously(adv.)快樂地\njoyous occasion 喜慶的場合\njoyous celebration 歡慶\nThe wedding was a joyous occasion for both families.\n(這場婚禮對兩家人來說都是喜慶的場合。)\nCrowds filled the streets for a joyous celebration after the team's victory.\n(球隊獲勝後，人群湧上街頭歡慶。)"],["junction","junction(n.)交叉點、交流道、匯合處\njoin(v.)連接\nrailway junction 鐵路樞紐\nhighway junction 交流道\nTake the highway and exit at the next junction for Hsinchu.\n(上高速公路後，在下一個交流道下往新竹。)\nThe town grew quickly because it was an important railway junction.\n(這個鎮因為是重要的鐵路樞紐而迅速發展。)"],["kin","kin(n./adj.)親屬、家族、有親屬關係的\nkinship(n.)親屬關係\nnext of kin 最近親屬\nkith and kin 親朋好友\nThe hospital contacted the patient's next of kin after the accident.\n(意外發生後，醫院聯絡了病人的最近親屬。)\nDuring the Lunar New Year, many people return home to visit their kin.\n(農曆新年期間，許多人返鄉探望親人。)"],["kindle","kindle(v.)點燃、激起\nkindling(n.)引火物\nkindle a fire 生火\nkindle interest 激起興趣\nWe used dry leaves and small sticks to kindle a fire at the campsite.\n(我們在營地用乾葉子和小樹枝生火。)\nA trip to the science museum kindled his interest in space.\n(一趟科學博物館之旅激起了他對太空的興趣。)"],["knowledgeable","knowledgeable(adj.)知識淵博的、有見識的\nknowledge(n.)知識\nknowledgeably(adv.)有見識地\nknowledgeable about 對…很了解\nknowledgeable staff 專業的工作人員\nOur history teacher is very knowledgeable about ancient Chinese culture.\n(我們的歷史老師對中國古代文化非常了解。)\nThe museum guide was friendly and knowledgeable, answering all our questions.\n(博物館導覽員親切又博學，回答了我們所有的問題。)"],["lad","lad(n.)少年、小伙子\n(無詞性變化)\na young lad 年輕小伙子\nthe lads 哥兒們\nThe old fisherman taught the young lad how to tie strong knots.\n(老漁夫教那個年輕小伙子如何打牢固的結。)\nHe has been a hardworking lad since he was a child.\n(他從小就是個勤奮的孩子。)"],["landlady","landlady(n.)女房東、(旅館等的)女老闆\nlandlord(n.)房東\nfriendly landlady 和善的女房東\npay rent to the landlady 付房租給女房東\nOur landlady lives downstairs and often brings us homemade cookies.\n(我們的女房東住在樓下，常常拿自製餅乾給我們。)\nI have to pay the rent to my landlady by the fifth of each month.\n(我每個月五號前必須付房租給女房東。)"],["landslide","landslide(n.)山崩、土石流、(選舉)壓倒性勝利\n(無詞性變化)\nlandslide victory 壓倒性勝利\ncause a landslide 引起山崩\nHeavy rain from the typhoon caused a landslide that blocked the mountain road.\n(颱風帶來的豪雨引發山崩，阻斷了山路。)\nThe candidate won the election by a landslide.\n(那位候選人以壓倒性勝利贏得選舉。)"],["latitude","latitude(n.)緯度、(行動等的)自由\nlatitudinal(adj.)緯度的\nhigh latitudes 高緯度地區\nlatitude and longitude 經緯度\nThe Tropic of Cancer passes through Chiayi at a latitude of about 23.5 degrees north.\n(北回歸線在北緯約23.5度處穿過嘉義。)\nOur teacher gives us a lot of latitude in choosing research topics.\n(老師給我們很大的自由選擇研究題目。)"],["lavish","lavish(adj.)奢華的、慷慨的、過分大方的\nlavishly(adv.)奢華地、慷慨地\nlavish lifestyle 奢華的生活方式\nlavish praise 大力讚揚\nThe movie star threw a lavish party at a five-star hotel.\n(那位電影明星在五星級飯店舉辦了一場奢華的派對。)\nThe coach was lavish in his praise of the young players.\n(教練對年輕球員讚不絕口。)"],["layman","layman(n.)外行人、門外漢、普通信徒\nlayperson(n.)外行人(中性用法)\nin layman's terms 用淺顯易懂的話來說\nto the layman 對外行人來說\nCan you explain the theory in layman's terms?\n(你能用淺顯易懂的話解釋這個理論嗎？)\nTo the layman, these legal documents are very hard to understand.\n(對外行人來說，這些法律文件非常難懂。)"],["layout","layout(n.)布局、版面設計、格局\nlay out(v.)安排、規劃\npage layout 版面設計\nfloor layout 平面格局\nI love the open layout of this apartment.\n(我很喜歡這間公寓的開放式格局。)\nThe designer changed the layout of the magazine's front page.\n(設計師改變了雜誌封面的版面配置。)"],["lease","lease(n.)租約、租賃契約\nleaseholder(n.)承租人\nsign a lease 簽租約\na one-year lease 一年的租約\nWe signed a two-year lease on the apartment near the university.\n(我們簽下了大學附近那間公寓的兩年租約。)\nWhen the lease expires, the landlord may raise the rent.\n(租約到期時，房東可能會漲房租。)"],["legislator","legislator(n.)立法委員、立法者\nlegislate(v.)立法\nlegislation(n.)法律、立法\nelect a legislator 選出立法委員\nstate legislator 州議員\nSeveral legislators proposed a new law to protect stray animals.\n(幾位立法委員提出一項保護流浪動物的新法案。)\nThe legislator promised to improve public transportation in his district.\n(那位立法委員承諾改善他選區的大眾運輸。)"],["lengthy","lengthy(adj.)冗長的、漫長的\nlength(n.)長度\nlengthen(v.)加長、延長\nlengthy discussion 冗長的討論\nlengthy process 漫長的過程\nAfter a lengthy discussion, the committee finally reached an agreement.\n(經過冗長的討論，委員會終於達成協議。)\nApplying for a visa can be a lengthy process.\n(申請簽證可能是個漫長的過程。)"],["lesbian","lesbian(adj.)女同性戀的、女同性戀者\n(無詞性變化)\nlesbian couple 女同性戀伴侶\ngay and lesbian rights 同志權益\nThe novel tells the story of a lesbian couple fighting for the right to marry.\n(這本小說講述一對女同志伴侶爭取婚姻權利的故事。)\nTaiwan became the first place in Asia where gay and lesbian couples could legally marry.\n(臺灣成為亞洲第一個同性伴侶可以合法結婚的地方。)"],["lessen","lessen(v.)減少、減輕\nless(adj./adv.)較少的、較少地\nlessen the impact 減輕衝擊\nlessen the pain 減輕疼痛\nPlanting more trees can lessen the effects of air pollution.\n(多種樹可以減輕空氣汙染的影響。)\nThe doctor gave him medicine to lessen the pain.\n(醫生給他藥來減輕疼痛。)"],["lethal","lethal(adj.)致命的、致死的\nlethally(adv.)致命地\nlethal dose 致死劑量\nlethal weapon 致命武器\nMixing these two chemicals can produce a lethal gas.\n(混合這兩種化學物質可能產生致命氣體。)\nDrunk driving can be lethal to both drivers and pedestrians.\n(酒駕對駕駛人和行人都可能是致命的。)"],["liable","liable(adj.)有法律責任的、易於⋯的\nliability(n.)責任、負債\nbe liable for 對⋯負有法律責任\nbe liable to 易於⋯、很可能⋯\nParents may be liable for damage caused by their children.\n(父母可能要對孩子造成的損害負法律責任。)\nThis old bridge is liable to collapse in a strong earthquake.\n(這座老橋在強烈地震中很可能會倒塌。)"],["liberate","liberate(v.)解放、使獲得自由\nliberation(n.)解放\nliberal(adj.)開明的、自由主義的\nliberated(adj.)獲得解放的\nliberate from 使從⋯中解放\nliberate a city 解放城市\nThe soldiers liberated the prisoners from the camp.\n(士兵們把囚犯從營中解放出來。)\nTechnology can liberate people from boring and repetitive work.\n(科技能讓人們從無聊重複的工作中解放出來。)"],["liberation","liberation(n.)解放、解放運動\nliberate(v.)解放\nwomen's liberation 婦女解放運動\nnational liberation 民族解放\nThe women's liberation movement fought for equal rights in the 1960s.\n(婦女解放運動在1960年代爭取平等權利。)\nQuitting the stressful job gave her a sense of liberation.\n(辭掉那份壓力大的工作讓她有種解脫的感覺。)"],["lieutenant","lieutenant(n.)中尉、副手、副職官員\n(無詞性變化)\nsecond lieutenant 少尉\nlieutenant governor 副州長\nAfter graduating from the military academy, he became a second lieutenant.\n(他從軍校畢業後成為一名少尉。)\nThe general trusted his lieutenant to lead the troops.\n(將軍信任他的副手來率領部隊。)"],["lifelong","lifelong(adj.)終身的、畢生的\n(無詞性變化)\nlifelong learning 終身學習\nlifelong friend 一輩子的朋友\nLifelong learning is essential in today's fast-changing world.\n(在當今快速變遷的世界中，終身學習是不可或缺的。)\nShe and I have been lifelong friends since kindergarten.\n(她和我從幼稚園起就是一輩子的好朋友。)"],["lighten","lighten(v.)減輕、使變亮、使輕鬆\nlight(adj./n.)輕的、光\nlighten the load 減輕負擔\nlighten up 放輕鬆\nRobots can lighten the workload of nurses in hospitals.\n(機器人可以減輕醫院護理師的工作量。)\nLighten up! It's just a game, not a matter of life and death.\n(放輕鬆！這只是遊戲，又不是生死攸關的事。)"],["limp","limp(n./v.)跛行、一跛一跛地走\nlimply(adv.)無力地\nwalk with a limp 跛著腳走路\nlimp off the field 跛著腳離場\nThe player limped off the field after hurting his ankle.\n(那名球員扭傷腳踝後一跛一跛地離開球場。)\nEver since the accident, he has walked with a slight limp.\n(自從那次意外後，他走路就有點跛。)"],["liner","liner(n.)郵輪、客輪、襯墊、眼線筆\nline(n./v.)線、排隊、襯裡\nocean liner 遠洋客輪\ntrash can liner 垃圾袋\nThe ocean liner carried over two thousand passengers across the Atlantic.\n(那艘遠洋客輪載著兩千多名乘客橫渡大西洋。)\nPut a plastic liner in the trash can before you throw away food waste.\n(丟廚餘之前先在垃圾桶裡套上塑膠袋。)"],["linger","linger(v.)逗留、徘徊、持續存在\nlingering(adj.)揮之不去的、拖延的\nlinger on 持續存在、繼續逗留\nlinger in the air 瀰漫不散(氣味等)\nThe smell of fried food lingered in the kitchen for hours.\n(炸物的味道在廚房裡久久不散。)\nFans lingered outside the stadium long after the concert ended.\n(演唱會結束許久後，歌迷仍在體育場外逗留。)"],["lining","lining(n.)襯裡、內襯、內層\nline(v.)加襯裡\nsilver lining 一線希望\nstomach lining 胃壁\nEvery cloud has a silver lining.\n(每片烏雲都鑲著銀邊；黑暗中總有一線希望。)\nThe coat has a warm wool lining for the winter.\n(這件大衣有保暖的羊毛內襯，適合冬天穿。)"],["liter","liter(n.)公升\n(無詞性變化)\na liter of 一公升的⋯\nliters per minute 每分鐘幾公升\nAdults should drink about two liters of water a day.\n(成年人一天應該喝大約兩公升的水。)\nThis car uses about six liters of gas per hundred kilometers.\n(這輛車每一百公里大約耗油六公升。)"],["literacy","literacy(n.)讀寫能力、識字、(某領域的)素養\nliterate(adj.)識字的\nilliteracy(n.)文盲、不識字\nliteracy rate 識字率\nmedia literacy 媒體素養\nTaiwan has a literacy rate of nearly one hundred percent.\n(臺灣的識字率幾乎達到百分之百。)\nMedia literacy helps students tell real news from fake news.\n(媒體素養幫助學生分辨真假新聞。)"],["literal","literal(adj.)字面上的、逐字的、照字面的\nliterally(adv.)照字面地、簡直\nliteral meaning 字面意義\nliteral translation 直譯\nThe literal meaning of the idiom is quite different from its real meaning.\n(這個成語的字面意思和它真正的意思相差很大。)\nI was literally shaking with fear during the horror movie.\n(看恐怖片時我簡直怕到發抖。)"],["literate","literate(adj./n.)識字的、有讀寫能力的、有學問的人\nliteracy(n.)讀寫能力\nilliterate(adj.)不識字的\ncomputer literate 懂電腦的\nhighly literate 學識淵博的\nIn today's job market, almost every employee needs to be computer literate.\n(在現今的就業市場，幾乎每位員工都需要懂電腦。)\nOnly a small number of people were literate in ancient times.\n(在古代只有少數人識字。)"],["livestock","livestock(n.)家畜、牲畜\n(無詞性變化)\nraise livestock 飼養家畜\nlivestock farming 畜牧業\nMany farmers in the area raise livestock such as pigs and cattle.\n(這個地區的許多農民飼養豬、牛等家畜。)\nThe flood killed hundreds of livestock in the village.\n(洪水造成村裡數百頭牲畜死亡。)"],["lizard","lizard(n.)蜥蜴\n(無詞性變化)\nhouse lizard 壁虎\npet lizard 寵物蜥蜴\nA small lizard was resting on the warm rock in the afternoon sun.\n(一隻小蜥蜴在午後陽光下的溫暖石頭上休息。)\nSome lizards can grow back their tails after losing them.\n(有些蜥蜴斷尾後還能再長出來。)"],["locker","locker(n.)置物櫃、寄物櫃\nlock(n./v.)鎖、上鎖\nlocker room 更衣室\ncoin locker 投幣式置物櫃\nI left my textbook in my locker at school.\n(我把課本留在學校的置物櫃裡了。)\nThe players changed their clothes in the locker room before the game.\n(球員們在比賽前於更衣室換衣服。)"],["lodge","lodge(n./v.)小屋、山莊、借住、提出(申訴)\nlodging(n.)住宿\nmountain lodge 山中小屋\nlodge a complaint 提出申訴\nWe stayed in a cozy mountain lodge during our trip to Alishan.\n(我們去阿里山旅行時住在一間舒適的山中小屋。)\nSeveral customers lodged a complaint about the poor service.\n(幾位顧客對服務不佳提出了申訴。)"],["lofty","lofty(adj.)崇高的、高聳的、高傲的\nloft(n.)閣樓\nlofty ideals 崇高的理想\nlofty mountains 高聳的山\nThe young doctor had lofty ideals about helping the poor.\n(那位年輕醫生懷抱著幫助窮人的崇高理想。)\nLofty mountains surround the peaceful village.\n(高聳的群山環繞著這座寧靜的村莊。)"],["logo","logo(n.)商標、標誌\n(無詞性變化)\ncompany logo 公司標誌\ndesign a logo 設計標誌\nThe company's logo is a simple blue bird.\n(那家公司的標誌是一隻簡單的藍色小鳥。)\nOur art club held a contest to design a new school logo.\n(我們的美術社舉辦比賽來設計新的校徽。)"],["lonesome","lonesome(adj.)寂寞的、孤單的、人跡罕至的\nlonely(adj.)寂寞的\nfeel lonesome 感到寂寞\na lonesome road 一條荒涼的路\nShe felt lonesome after all her friends moved away.\n(朋友們都搬走後，她感到很寂寞。)\nThe old man walked down the lonesome road at night.\n(那位老人在夜裡走在荒涼的路上。)"],["longevity","longevity(n.)長壽、壽命、持久\n(無詞性變化)\nthe secret of longevity 長壽的祕訣\nincrease longevity 延長壽命\nA healthy diet and regular exercise are the keys to longevity.\n(健康的飲食和規律的運動是長壽的關鍵。)\nOkinawa is famous for the longevity of its people.\n(沖繩以居民長壽聞名。)"],["longitude","longitude(n.)經度\nlongitudinal(adj.)經度的、縱向的\ndegrees of longitude 經度的度數\nline of longitude 經線\nTaiwan lies at about 121 degrees east longitude.\n(臺灣位於東經約121度。)\nSailors needed accurate clocks to find their longitude at sea.\n(水手們需要精準的時鐘才能在海上測出經度。)"],["lotion","lotion(n.)乳液、化妝水、塗劑\n(無詞性變化)\nbody lotion 身體乳液\nsuntan lotion 防曬乳\nDon't forget to put on suntan lotion before going to the beach.\n(去海灘之前別忘了擦防曬乳。)\nApply some body lotion after your shower to keep your skin soft.\n(洗完澡後擦些身體乳液以保持皮膚柔嫩。)"],["lottery","lottery(n.)樂透、彩券、抽獎、碰運氣的事\n(無詞性變化)\nwin the lottery 中樂透\nlottery ticket 彩券\nHe spends a lot of money on lottery tickets, hoping to get rich overnight.\n(他花很多錢買彩券，希望一夜致富。)\nGetting a good roommate in college is a bit of a lottery.\n(在大學能不能遇到好室友有點靠運氣。)"],["lotus","lotus(n.)蓮花、荷花\n(無詞性變化)\nlotus pond 荷花池\nlotus seeds 蓮子\nEvery summer, the lotus pond in Baihe is full of pink flowers.\n(每年夏天，白河的荷花池都開滿粉紅色的花。)\nMy grandmother makes a sweet soup with lotus seeds.\n(我奶奶會用蓮子煮甜湯。)"],["loudspeaker","loudspeaker(n.)擴音器、揚聲器、喇叭\n(無詞性變化)\nover the loudspeaker 透過擴音器\nportable loudspeaker 攜帶式擴音器\nThe principal made an announcement over the loudspeaker.\n(校長透過擴音器宣布了一則消息。)\nA loudspeaker on the truck played music to attract customers.\n(卡車上的喇叭播放音樂以吸引顧客。)"],["lucrative","lucrative(adj.)賺錢的、有利可圖的\n(無詞性變化)\nlucrative business 賺錢的生意\nlucrative contract 獲利豐厚的合約\nSelling Taiwanese drinks abroad has become a lucrative business.\n(在國外賣臺灣飲料已成為一門賺錢的生意。)\nShe turned down a lucrative job offer to work for a charity.\n(她拒絕了一份高薪工作，去慈善機構服務。)"],["lullaby","lullaby(n.)搖籃曲\n(無詞性變化)\nsing a lullaby 唱搖籃曲\na gentle lullaby 輕柔的搖籃曲\nThe mother sang a soft lullaby to put her baby to sleep.\n(那位母親唱著輕柔的搖籃曲哄寶寶入睡。)\nThe sound of the rain was like a lullaby to me.\n(雨聲對我來說就像一首搖籃曲。)"],["lunar","lunar(adj.)月亮的、陰曆的\n(無詞性變化)\nlunar calendar 農曆\nlunar eclipse 月蝕\nChinese New Year falls on the first day of the lunar calendar.\n(農曆新年在農曆的第一天。)\nMany people stayed up late to watch the total lunar eclipse.\n(許多人熬夜觀看月全蝕。)"],["lure","lure(n./v.)誘惑、吸引力、誘餌、引誘\nalluring(adj.)誘人的\nlure someone into 誘使某人做⋯\nthe lure of 的誘惑\nOnline scams often lure victims with promises of easy money.\n(網路詐騙常以輕鬆賺錢為誘餌引誘受害者。)\nThe lure of big city life draws many young people away from their hometowns.\n(大城市生活的吸引力使許多年輕人離開家鄉。)"],["lush","lush(adj.)茂盛的、蒼翠的、豪華的\nlushness(n.)茂盛\nlush green 綠意盎然的\nlush vegetation 茂密的植被\nThe hills were covered in lush green forests after the rainy season.\n(雨季過後，山丘上覆蓋著蒼翠繁茂的森林。)\nHualien is known for its lush valleys and clear rivers.\n(花蓮以蒼翠的山谷和清澈的河流聞名。)"],["madam/ma’am","madam(n.)女士、夫人(尊稱)\nma'am(n.)女士(madam 的口語縮寫)\nDear Madam 敬啟者(書信用)\nExcuse me, ma'am. 不好意思，女士。\nCan I help you find anything, madam?\n(女士，需要我幫您找什麼嗎？)\nExcuse me, ma'am, you dropped your wallet.\n(不好意思，女士，您的錢包掉了。)"],["magnify","magnify(v.)放大、擴大、誇大\nmagnification(n.)放大(率)\nmagnifying glass 放大鏡\nmagnify the problem 誇大問題\nUse a magnifying glass to look at the tiny insects more closely.\n(用放大鏡更仔細地觀察這些小昆蟲。)\nSocial media can magnify small mistakes into big scandals.\n(社群媒體可能把小錯誤放大成大醜聞。)"],["maiden","maiden(adj./n.)首次的、未婚的、少女\n(無詞性變化)\nmaiden voyage 處女航\nmaiden name 婚前姓氏\nThe Titanic sank on its maiden voyage in 1912.\n(鐵達尼號在1912年的處女航中沉沒。)\nShe kept her maiden name after she got married.\n(她婚後保留了婚前的姓氏。)"],["mainland","mainland(n.)大陸、本土\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Chinese mainland 中國大陸\nmainland China 中國大陸\nMany tourists take ferries from the mainland to the island.\n(許多遊客從本土搭渡輪到島上。)\nPenghu is about fifty kilometers away from the mainland of Taiwan.\n(澎湖距離臺灣本島大約五十公里。)"],["majestic","majestic(adj.)雄偉的、莊嚴的、壯麗的\nmajesty(n.)雄偉、陛下\nmajestically(adv.)雄偉地\nmajestic mountains 雄偉的山脈\nmajestic view 壯麗的景色\nWe were amazed by the majestic view of Taroko Gorge.\n(太魯閣峽谷的壯麗景色讓我們驚嘆不已。)\nA majestic eagle flew high above the valley.\n(一隻雄偉的老鷹高飛在山谷上空。)"],["majesty","majesty(n.)雄偉、壯麗、(Majesty)陛下\nmajestic(adj.)雄偉的、莊嚴的\nYour Majesty 陛下(稱呼)\nthe majesty of nature 大自然的壯麗\nThe guests bowed and said, 'Good evening, Your Majesty.'\n(賓客們鞠躬說：「晚安，陛下。」)\nStanding at the top of Jade Mountain, I felt the majesty of nature.\n(站在玉山頂上，我感受到大自然的壯麗。)"],["manuscript","manuscript(n.)手稿、原稿\n(無詞性變化)\noriginal manuscript 原始手稿\nsubmit a manuscript 投稿\nThe museum displays the original manuscript of the famous poem.\n(博物館展出那首名詩的原始手稿。)\nThe writer submitted her manuscript to three publishers.\n(那位作家將她的原稿投給三家出版社。)"],["maple","maple(n.)楓樹、楓木\n(無詞性變化)\nmaple leaf 楓葉\nmaple syrup 楓糖漿\nThe maple leaf is the national symbol of Canada.\n(楓葉是加拿大的國家象徵。)\nWe had pancakes with maple syrup for breakfast.\n(我們早餐吃了淋上楓糖漿的鬆餅。)"],["mar","mar(v.)損毀、破壞、損害\n(無詞性變化)\nmar the beauty 破壞美感\nmarred by 因⋯而美中不足\nThe beautiful beach was marred by piles of plastic waste.\n(美麗的海灘被成堆的塑膠垃圾破壞了。)\nThe wedding was marred by heavy rain, but everyone still had fun.\n(婚禮因大雨而美中不足，但大家還是玩得很開心。)"],["marginal","marginal(adj.)微小的、邊緣的、頁邊的\nmargin(n.)邊緣、頁邊空白、差額\nmarginally(adv.)稍微、略微\nmarginal increase 微幅增加\nmarginal notes 旁註、頁邊筆記\nThere was only a marginal improvement in his grades this semester.\n(他這學期的成績只有微幅進步。)\nShe wrote marginal notes in her textbook while studying.\n(她讀書時在課本的頁邊寫筆記。)"],["martial","martial(adj.)戰爭的、軍事的、尚武的\n(無詞性變化)\nmartial arts 武術\nmartial law 戒嚴令\nTaiwan lifted martial law in 1987 after thirty-eight years.\n(臺灣在實施三十八年後於1987年解除戒嚴。)\nMany students learn martial arts such as taekwondo and kung fu.\n(許多學生學習跆拳道和功夫等武術。)"],["marvel","marvel(n./v.)奇蹟、令人驚奇的事物、對⋯感到驚奇\nmarvelous(adj.)令人驚嘆的、極好的\nmarvel at 對⋯感到驚嘆\na marvel of engineering 工程奇蹟\nVisitors marvel at the size of the ancient pyramids.\n(遊客們對古老金字塔的規模感到驚嘆。)\nTaipei 101 is considered a marvel of modern engineering.\n(臺北101被認為是現代工程的奇蹟。)"],["mastery","mastery(n.)精通、掌握、控制\nmaster(n./v.)主人、大師、精通\nmasterful(adj.)熟練的、高超的\nmastery of 精通⋯\nachieve mastery 達到精通\nHer mastery of three languages helped her get a job at the airline.\n(她精通三種語言，幫助她在航空公司找到工作。)\nIt takes years of practice to achieve mastery of the violin.\n(要精通小提琴需要多年的練習。)"],["mediate","mediate(v.)調解、斡旋\nmediation(n.)調解\nmediator(n.)調解人\nmediate a dispute 調解糾紛\nmediate between 在⋯之間調停\nThe teacher tried to mediate between the two students who were fighting.\n(老師試著在兩個吵架的學生之間調解。)\nA neutral country offered to mediate the dispute between the two nations.\n(一個中立國提議調解兩國之間的爭端。)"],["medieval","medieval(adj.)中世紀的、老舊過時的\n(無詞性變化)\nmedieval castle 中世紀城堡\nmedieval history 中世紀史\nWe visited a medieval castle during our trip to Germany.\n(我們去德國旅行時參觀了一座中世紀城堡。)\nHis ideas about women's roles are positively medieval.\n(他對女性角色的看法簡直老舊過時。)"],["meditate","meditate(v.)冥想、沉思、打坐\nmeditation(n.)冥想、沉思\nmeditative(adj.)沉思的\nmeditate on 沉思⋯\nmeditate daily 每天冥想\nShe meditates for twenty minutes every morning to reduce stress.\n(她每天早上冥想二十分鐘來減輕壓力。)\nThe old monk sat quietly and meditated on the meaning of life.\n(老和尚靜靜坐著，沉思人生的意義。)"],["meditation","meditation(n.)冥想、沉思、打坐\nmeditate(v.)冥想、沉思\npractice meditation 練習冥想\ndeep meditation 深度冥想\nStudies show that meditation can improve concentration and reduce anxiety.\n(研究顯示冥想可以提升專注力並減輕焦慮。)\nHe found peace through daily meditation.\n(他透過每天冥想找到了內心的平靜。)"],["melancholy","melancholy(n./adj.)憂鬱、憂愁、憂鬱的、令人傷感的\nmelancholic(adj.)憂鬱的\na sense of melancholy 一股憂傷\nmelancholy music 憂傷的音樂\nA feeling of melancholy came over him as he looked at old photos.\n(看著舊照片時，一股憂傷湧上他的心頭。)\nThe rainy autumn evening put her in a melancholy mood.\n(秋天下雨的夜晚讓她心情憂鬱。)"],["mentality","mentality(n.)心態、思維方式\nmental(adj.)心理的、精神的\nwinning mentality 求勝心態\nvictim mentality 受害者心態\nSuccessful athletes usually have a strong winning mentality.\n(成功的運動員通常有強烈的求勝心態。)\nWe need to change the mentality that grades are everything.\n(我們必須改變「成績就是一切」的心態。)"],["merchandise","merchandise(n./v.)商品、貨物、推銷\nmerchant(n.)商人\nofficial merchandise 官方周邊商品\ngeneral merchandise 雜貨、百貨\nFans lined up for hours to buy the band's official merchandise.\n(粉絲們排隊好幾個小時購買樂團的官方周邊商品。)\nThe store merchandises its products cleverly to attract young people.\n(這家店巧妙地推銷商品以吸引年輕人。)"],["mermaid","mermaid(n.)美人魚\n(無詞性變化)\nThe Little Mermaid 小美人魚\nmermaid statue 美人魚雕像\nThe Little Mermaid is one of Hans Christian Andersen's most famous stories.\n(《小美人魚》是安徒生最有名的故事之一。)\nTourists take pictures of the mermaid statue in Copenhagen.\n(遊客在哥本哈根拍攝美人魚雕像。)"],["migrant","migrant(n./adj.)移居者、移工、候鳥、移居的\nmigrate(v.)遷移、移居\nmigration(n.)遷移、移居\nmigrant workers 移工\nmigrant birds 候鳥\nMany migrant workers in Taiwan come from Southeast Asia.\n(臺灣許多移工來自東南亞。)\nMigrant birds stop at the wetlands on their way south every winter.\n(每年冬天候鳥南飛途中會在溼地停留。)"],["mimic","mimic(v./n.)模仿、模仿者、擅長模仿的人\nmimicry(n.)模仿、擬態\nmimic someone's voice 模仿某人的聲音\na talented mimic 很會模仿的人\nThe parrot can mimic the sound of a ringing phone.\n(這隻鸚鵡會模仿電話鈴響的聲音。)\nHe is a talented mimic who can copy any teacher's voice.\n(他很會模仿，可以學任何一位老師的聲音。)"],["mingle","mingle(v.)混合、(社交場合中)與人交談周旋\n(無詞性變化)\nmingle with 與⋯交際、混入⋯\nmingle with the crowd 混入人群\nAt the party, she mingled with guests from different countries.\n(在派對上，她和來自不同國家的賓客交際。)\nThe smell of coffee mingled with the scent of fresh bread.\n(咖啡的香味和新鮮麵包的香氣混合在一起。)"],["miraculous","miraculous(adj.)奇蹟般的、不可思議的\nmiracle(n.)奇蹟\nmiraculously(adv.)奇蹟似地\nmiraculous recovery 奇蹟般的康復\nmiraculous escape 奇蹟般的脫險\nThe doctors were amazed by her miraculous recovery after the accident.\n(醫生們對她車禍後奇蹟般的康復感到驚訝。)\nMiraculously, nobody was hurt in the fire.\n(奇蹟似地，沒有人在火災中受傷。)"],["miscellaneous","miscellaneous(adj.)各式各樣的、雜項的\n(無詞性變化)\nmiscellaneous items 雜物\nmiscellaneous expenses 雜費\nThe drawer is full of miscellaneous items like batteries, keys, and rubber bands.\n(抽屜裡塞滿了電池、鑰匙、橡皮筋等雜物。)\nPlease list your miscellaneous expenses at the end of the report.\n(請在報告最後列出你的雜項開支。)"],["mischievous","mischievous(adj.)淘氣的、惡作劇的、有惡意的\nmischief(n.)惡作劇、淘氣\nmischievously(adv.)淘氣地\nmischievous smile 調皮的笑容\nmischievous child 淘氣的小孩\nThe mischievous boy hid his sister's shoes before school.\n(那個淘氣的男孩在上學前把姊姊的鞋子藏起來。)\nShe gave me a mischievous smile, and I knew she was planning something.\n(她對我露出調皮的笑容，我就知道她在打什麼主意。)"],["mistress","mistress(n.)女主人、情婦、精通⋯的女子\nmaster(n.)主人\nmistress of the house 一家的女主人\nhave a mistress 有情婦\nThe dog ran happily to greet its mistress at the door.\n(那隻狗開心地跑到門口迎接女主人。)\nIn the novel, the king's secret mistress plays an important role.\n(在這本小說中，國王的祕密情婦扮演重要的角色。)"],["mobilize","mobilize(v.)動員、調動、組織\nmobilization(n.)動員\nmobile(adj.)可移動的\nmobilize troops 動員軍隊\nmobilize support 爭取支持\nThe government mobilized thousands of soldiers to help after the earthquake.\n(地震後政府動員了數千名士兵協助救災。)\nThe students mobilized support for the campaign through social media.\n(學生們透過社群媒體為這項活動爭取支持。)"],["modernization","modernization(n.)現代化\nmodernize(v.)使現代化\nmodern(adj.)現代的\neconomic modernization 經濟現代化\nthe modernization of 對⋯的現代化\nThe modernization of the railway system has made travel much faster.\n(鐵路系統的現代化讓交通變得快速許多。)\nRapid modernization has changed the way people live in rural areas.\n(快速的現代化改變了鄉村地區人們的生活方式。)"],["modernize","modernize(v.)使現代化、更新\nmodernization(n.)現代化\nmodern(adj.)現代的\nmodernize facilities 更新設施\nmodernize the economy 使經濟現代化\nThe school plans to modernize its library with digital equipment.\n(學校計畫用數位設備將圖書館現代化。)\nThe country spent billions to modernize its army.\n(這個國家花了數十億來使軍隊現代化。)"],["momentum","momentum(n.)動力、氣勢、動量\n(無詞性變化)\ngain momentum 聲勢漸增\nlose momentum 失去動力\nThe campaign to ban plastic straws is gaining momentum around the world.\n(禁用塑膠吸管的運動在全球聲勢漸增。)\nOur team lost momentum after the star player got hurt.\n(明星球員受傷後，我們的隊伍就失去了氣勢。)"],["monarch","monarch(n.)君主、帝王\nmonarchy(n.)君主政體、君主國\nabsolute monarch 專制君主\nreigning monarch 在位君主\nQueen Elizabeth II was the longest-reigning monarch in British history.\n(伊莉莎白二世是英國史上在位最久的君主。)\nIn the past, the monarch had absolute power over the people.\n(過去君主對人民擁有絕對的權力。)"],["monetary","monetary(adj.)貨幣的、金融的、金錢的\nmoney(n.)錢\nmonetary policy 貨幣政策\nmonetary value 金錢價值\nThe central bank changed its monetary policy to control inflation.\n(中央銀行改變貨幣政策以控制通貨膨脹。)\nThe old letters have little monetary value, but they mean a lot to me.\n(這些舊信沒什麼金錢價值，但對我意義重大。)"],["monotony","monotony(n.)單調、無變化\nmonotonous(adj.)單調的、乏味的\nbreak the monotony 打破單調\nthe monotony of daily life 日常生活的單調\nListening to music helps break the monotony of the long bus ride.\n(聽音樂有助於打破長途巴士旅程的單調。)\nHe quit the job because he could no longer stand the monotony.\n(他辭掉那份工作，因為再也受不了那種單調。)"],["monstrous","monstrous(adj.)可怕的、駭人的、巨大的、荒謬的\nmonster(n.)怪物\nmonstrous crime 駭人的罪行\nmonstrous waves 巨浪\nThe monstrous waves destroyed many houses along the coast.\n(巨浪摧毀了沿岸許多房屋。)\nIt is monstrous to treat animals so cruelly.\n(如此殘忍地對待動物實在駭人聽聞。)"],["moody","moody(adj.)喜怒無常的、心情不好的、陰鬱的\nmood(n.)心情\nmoodiness(n.)喜怒無常\nmoody teenager 喜怒無常的青少年\nmoody atmosphere 陰鬱的氣氛\nTeenagers can be moody when they don't get enough sleep.\n(青少年睡眠不足時可能會喜怒無常。)\nThe film's moody music makes the story feel even sadder.\n(電影陰鬱的配樂讓故事感覺更加悲傷。)"],["morale","morale(n.)士氣、鬥志\n(無詞性變化)\nboost morale 提振士氣\nlow morale 士氣低落\nThe coach's speech boosted the team's morale before the final.\n(教練的演說在決賽前提振了全隊的士氣。)\nLong working hours have led to low morale among the staff.\n(工時過長導致員工士氣低落。)"],["mortal","mortal(adj./n.)終究會死的、致命的、凡人\nmortality(n.)死亡率、必死性\nimmortal(adj.)不朽的、長生不死的\nmortal danger 致命的危險\nmere mortals 凡夫俗子\nAll living things are mortal and will die someday.\n(所有生物都終將一死。)\nThe soldiers knew they were in mortal danger.\n(士兵們知道自己身處致命的危險中。)"],["motherhood","motherhood(n.)母親身分、母性\nmother(n.)母親\nmotherly(adj.)母親般的、慈愛的\nthe joys of motherhood 為人母的喜悅\nbalance work and motherhood 兼顧工作與母職\nShe found it hard to balance her career and motherhood.\n(她發現要兼顧事業和母職很不容易。)\nThe book describes the joys and challenges of motherhood.\n(這本書描述了身為母親的喜悅與挑戰。)"],["motto","motto(n.)座右銘、格言、校訓\n(無詞性變化)\nschool motto 校訓\npersonal motto 個人座右銘\nOur school motto encourages students to be honest and diligent.\n(我們的校訓鼓勵學生誠實勤奮。)\n'Never give up' has always been my personal motto.\n(「永不放棄」一直是我的座右銘。)"],["mound","mound(n./v.)土堆、小丘、一堆、堆積\n(無詞性變化)\npitcher's mound 投手丘\na mound of 一大堆⋯\nThe pitcher walked to the mound and prepared to throw.\n(投手走上投手丘準備投球。)\nThere was a mound of dirty laundry in the corner of his room.\n(他房間角落堆著一大堆髒衣服。)"],["mourn","mourn(v.)哀悼、悲痛\nmourning(n.)哀悼、服喪\nmourner(n.)哀悼者\nmourn for 為⋯哀悼\nmourn the loss of 為失去⋯而悲傷\nThe whole nation mourned the death of the beloved leader.\n(全國人民哀悼這位受愛戴的領袖逝世。)\nShe is still mourning the loss of her pet dog.\n(她仍為失去愛犬而傷心。)"],["mournful","mournful(adj.)悲傷的、令人哀傷的\nmourn(v.)哀悼\nmournfully(adv.)悲傷地\nmournful music 哀傷的音樂\nmournful expression 悲傷的神情\nThe mournful sound of the violin brought tears to my eyes.\n(小提琴哀傷的聲音讓我熱淚盈眶。)\nHe looked at the empty house with a mournful expression.\n(他帶著悲傷的神情看著那間空屋。)"],["mow","mow(v.)割(草)\nmower(n.)割草機\nmow the lawn 割草坪\nlawn mower 割草機\nMy father asked me to mow the lawn every Sunday.\n(我爸爸要我每個星期天割草坪。)\nThe noise of the lawn mower woke me up early this morning.\n(割草機的噪音今天一大早就把我吵醒了。)"],["muse","muse(n.)靈感來源、繆思女神\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Muses 繆思女神們\none's muse 某人的靈感來源\nThe singer said his wife was the muse behind many of his love songs.\n(那位歌手說他的妻子是他許多情歌背後的靈感來源。)\nIn Greek myths, the nine Muses inspire art, music, and poetry.\n(在希臘神話中，九位繆思女神啟發了藝術、音樂和詩歌。)"],["mustache","mustache(n.)小鬍子、八字鬍\n(無詞性變化)\ngrow a mustache 留小鬍子\nthick mustache 濃密的八字鬍\nMy uncle decided to grow a mustache to look more mature.\n(我叔叔決定留小鬍子讓自己看起來更成熟。)\nThe man with the thick mustache turned out to be the detective.\n(那個留著濃密八字鬍的男人原來就是偵探。)"],["mute","mute(adj./v./n.)沉默的、無聲的、使靜音、啞巴\nmuted(adj.)減弱的、柔和的\nmute button 靜音鍵\nremain mute 保持沉默\nPlease mute your microphone when you are not speaking in the online meeting.\n(線上會議中沒有發言時，請將麥克風靜音。)\nShe remained mute when the reporters asked about her private life.\n(當記者問到她的私生活時，她保持沉默。)"],["nag","nag(v./n.)嘮叨、不斷抱怨、愛嘮叨的人\nnagging(adj.)嘮叨的、揮之不去的\nnag someone to 嘮叨某人去做⋯\nnagging pain 揮之不去的疼痛\nMy mom keeps nagging me to clean up my room.\n(我媽一直嘮叨要我整理房間。)\nI've had a nagging feeling all day that I forgot something important.\n(我一整天都有種揮之不去的感覺，好像忘了什麼重要的事。)"],["narrate","narrate(v.)敘述、講述、旁白\nnarration(n.)敘述、旁白\nnarrative(n./adj.)敘事、敘事的\nnarrator(n.)敘述者\nnarrate a story 講述故事\nnarrate a documentary 為紀錄片旁白\nThe famous actor narrated the documentary about ocean life.\n(那位知名演員為這部海洋生物紀錄片擔任旁白。)\nThe story is narrated by a ten-year-old girl.\n(這個故事是由一個十歲女孩敘述的。)"],["narrator","narrator(n.)敘述者、旁白者\nnarrate(v.)敘述\nnarrative(n.)敘事\nfirst-person narrator 第一人稱敘述者\nunreliable narrator 不可靠的敘述者\nThe narrator of the novel tells the story from a dog's point of view.\n(這本小說的敘述者從一隻狗的觀點講故事。)\nThe narrator's calm voice made the film even more moving.\n(旁白沉穩的聲音讓這部片更加動人。)"],["nationalism","nationalism(n.)民族主義、國家主義\nnationalist(n./adj.)民族主義者、民族主義的\nnational(adj.)國家的、民族的\nrising nationalism 高漲的民族主義\na sense of nationalism 民族意識\nRising nationalism can sometimes lead to conflicts between countries.\n(高漲的民族主義有時會導致國與國之間的衝突。)\nThe Olympic Games often stir up strong feelings of nationalism.\n(奧運常常激起強烈的民族情感。)"],["navigate","navigate(v.)導航、航行、找到方向、處理(困難)\nnavigation(n.)導航、航海\nnavigator(n.)領航員\nnavigate through 在⋯中找到出路\nnavigate the website 瀏覽網站\nEarly sailors used the stars to navigate across the ocean.\n(早期的水手利用星星在海上導航。)\nIt took me a while to navigate the school's new online system.\n(我花了一段時間才摸熟學校的新線上系統。)"],["navigation","navigation(n.)導航、航海、航行\nnavigate(v.)導航\nnavigational(adj.)導航的\nnavigation system 導航系統\nsatellite navigation 衛星導航\nThe car's navigation system guided us to the hotel without any problems.\n(車上的導航系統順利地帶我們到飯店。)\nBefore GPS, navigation at sea was much more difficult.\n(在全球定位系統出現之前，海上航行困難得多。)"],["nearsighted","nearsighted(adj.)近視的、目光短淺的\nnearsightedness(n.)近視\nfarsighted(adj.)遠視的、有遠見的\nbecome nearsighted 變成近視\nnearsighted policy 短視的政策\nMany students become nearsighted because they spend too much time on their phones.\n(許多學生因為花太多時間滑手機而近視。)\nCutting the education budget is a nearsighted decision.\n(刪減教育預算是一個短視的決定。)"],["nickel","nickel(n./v.)鎳、(美國、加拿大的)五分錢硬幣\n(無詞性變化)\na nickel 一枚五分錢硬幣\nnickel and dime 斤斤計較、一點一點地榨取\nA nickel is worth five cents in the United States.\n(在美國，一枚五分錢硬幣值五分錢。)\nNickel is often used to make coins and batteries.\n(鎳常被用來製造硬幣和電池。)"],["nostril","nostril(n.)鼻孔\n(無詞性變化)\nflare one's nostrils 張大鼻孔(表示憤怒等)\nleft nostril 左鼻孔\nThe horse flared its nostrils and began to run.\n(那匹馬張大鼻孔，開始奔跑。)\nBreathe in slowly through your nostrils and out through your mouth.\n(用鼻孔慢慢吸氣，再用嘴巴吐氣。)"],["notable","notable(adj./n.)值得注意的、著名的、名人\nnotably(adv.)顯著地、尤其\nnotable for 以⋯著稱\na notable exception 一個明顯的例外\nThe town is notable for its beautiful old temples.\n(這個小鎮以美麗的古廟著稱。)\nMost of the students passed the test, with a few notable exceptions.\n(大部分學生都通過了考試，只有少數明顯的例外。)"],["notorious","notorious(adj.)惡名昭彰的、聲名狼藉的\nnotoriety(n.)惡名\nnotoriously(adv.)出了名地(用於負面)\nbe notorious for 因⋯而惡名昭彰\nnotorious criminal 惡名昭彰的罪犯\nThis road is notorious for its heavy traffic during rush hour.\n(這條路以尖峰時段交通壅塞而出名。)\nThe police finally caught the notorious criminal after years of searching.\n(經過多年搜捕，警方終於抓到了那名惡名昭彰的罪犯。)"],["nourish(ment)","nourish(v.)滋養、養育、培養、nourishment(n.)營養、養分\nnourishing(adj.)有營養的、滋補的\nnourish the skin 滋潤肌膚\nnourish the mind 滋養心靈\nReading good books can nourish the mind.\n(閱讀好書能滋養心靈。)\nPlants get nourishment from the soil, water, and sunlight.\n(植物從土壤、水和陽光中獲得養分。)"],["novice","novice(n.)新手、初學者\n(無詞性變化)\ncomplete novice 完全的新手\nnovice driver 新手駕駛\nI'm a complete novice at cooking, so please be patient with me.\n(我做菜完全是新手，所以請對我有耐心。)\nThis ski slope is perfect for novices.\n(這條滑雪道非常適合初學者。)"],["nucleus","nucleus(n.)核心、原子核、細胞核\nnuclear(adj.)核子的、原子能的\nnuclei(n.)核心、細胞核(複數)\ncell nucleus 細胞核\nthe nucleus of 的核心\nThe nucleus controls the activities of the cell.\n(細胞核控制細胞的活動。)\nThese five players form the nucleus of the national team.\n(這五名球員構成國家隊的核心。)"],["nude","nude(adj./n.)裸體的、裸體畫、裸體\nnudity(n.)裸體\nnude painting 裸體畫\nin the nude 裸體地\nThe museum displays several famous nude paintings from the Renaissance.\n(博物館展出幾幅文藝復興時期著名的裸體畫。)\nThe ancient Greek statue shows a nude athlete throwing a discus.\n(這座古希臘雕像呈現一名擲鐵餅的裸體運動員。)"],["nurture","nurture(v./n.)養育、培育、培養、教養\n(無詞性變化)\nnature and nurture 先天與後天\nnurture talent 培育人才\nGood teachers nurture their students' curiosity and creativity.\n(好老師會培養學生的好奇心和創造力。)\nScientists still debate whether personality comes from nature or nurture.\n(科學家仍在爭論個性是來自先天還是後天的教養。)"],["oasis","oasis(n.)綠洲、宜人之處(複數 oases)\n(無詞性變化)\ndesert oasis 沙漠綠洲\nan oasis of calm 寧靜的世外桃源\nThe exhausted travelers finally reached an oasis in the desert.\n(筋疲力盡的旅人終於抵達了沙漠中的一片綠洲。)\nThe small park is an oasis of calm in the busy city.\n(這座小公園是繁忙都市中的一片寧靜綠洲。)"],["oath","oath(n.)誓言、宣誓、咒罵\n(無詞性變化)\ntake an oath 宣誓\nunder oath 在宣誓下(作證)\nThe new president took an oath to protect the constitution.\n(新任總統宣誓維護憲法。)\nWitnesses must tell the truth under oath in court.\n(證人在法庭上宣誓後必須說實話。)"],["oatmeal","oatmeal(n.)燕麥片、燕麥粥\noat(n.)燕麥(常用複數 oats)\na bowl of oatmeal 一碗燕麥粥\ninstant oatmeal 即食燕麥片\nA bowl of oatmeal with fruit makes a healthy breakfast.\n(一碗加了水果的燕麥粥是健康的早餐。)\nOatmeal is rich in fiber and keeps you full for hours.\n(燕麥富含纖維，能讓你飽足好幾個小時。)"],["oblige","oblige(v.)強迫、迫使、施恩於\nobligation(n.)義務、責任\nobligatory(adj.)義務的、強制的\nbe obliged to 不得不⋯\nI'm much obliged. 非常感激。\nDrivers are obliged by law to wear seat belts.\n(依法規定，駕駛人必須繫安全帶。)\nI felt obliged to help him after all he had done for me.\n(在他為我做了那麼多之後，我覺得有義務幫他。)"],["obsess","obsess(v.)使著迷、使困擾\nobsession(n.)著迷、執念\nobsessive(adj.)著迷的、強迫性的\nbe obsessed with 對⋯著迷\nobsessed fan 狂熱粉絲\nHe is obsessed with getting perfect scores on every test.\n(他執著於每次考試都要拿滿分。)\nMany teenagers are obsessed with checking social media.\n(許多青少年熱衷於查看社群媒體。)"],["obstinate","obstinate(adj.)固執的、頑固的、難以去除的\nobstinacy(n.)固執\nobstinate refusal 斷然拒絕\nobstinate stain 頑強的汙漬\nThe obstinate old man refused to listen to his doctor's advice.\n(那位固執的老人拒絕聽從醫生的建議。)\nIt took hours to remove the obstinate stain from the carpet.\n(花了好幾個小時才把地毯上頑強的汙漬清除。)"],["occurrence","occurrence(n.)發生、事件\noccur(v.)發生\ncommon occurrence 常見的事\nrare occurrence 罕見的事\nTraffic jams are a common occurrence in big cities.\n(塞車在大城市是常見的事。)\nSnow in Taipei is a very rare occurrence.\n(台北下雪是非常罕見的事。)"],["octopus","octopus(n.)章魚\n(無詞性變化)\ngrilled octopus 烤章魚\noctopus balls 章魚燒\nAn octopus can change its color to hide from enemies.\n(章魚能改變顏色以躲避敵人。)\nWe ordered grilled octopus at the seafood restaurant.\n(我們在海鮮餐廳點了烤章魚。)"],["odor","odor(n.)氣味、臭味\nodorless(adj.)無味的\nbody odor 體臭\nunpleasant odor 難聞的氣味\nAn unpleasant odor came from the trash can in the kitchen.\n(廚房的垃圾桶傳來一股難聞的氣味。)\nCarbon monoxide is dangerous because it has no odor.\n(一氧化碳很危險，因為它沒有氣味。)"],["offshore","offshore(adj.)近海的、離岸的、境外的\n(無詞性變化)\noffshore wind farm 離岸風場\noffshore island 離島\nTaiwan is building many offshore wind farms to produce clean energy.\n(台灣正在興建許多離岸風場來生產乾淨能源。)\nKinmen and Matsu are offshore islands of Taiwan.\n(金門和馬祖是台灣的離島。)"],["offspring","offspring(n.)後代、子女(單複數同形)\n(無詞性變化)\nproduce offspring 繁衍後代\nhealthy offspring 健康的後代\nParents naturally want the best for their offspring.\n(父母自然希望給子女最好的。)\nSea turtles leave their offspring alone soon after laying eggs.\n(海龜產卵後不久便讓後代自生自滅。)"],["operative","operative(adj.)運作中的、有效的\noperate(v.)運作、動手術\noperation(n.)運作、手術\nbecome operative 開始生效\nthe operative word 關鍵字眼\nThe new train line will become operative next year.\n(新的鐵路線將於明年開始營運。)\nThe rule is still operative, so we must follow it.\n(這項規定仍然有效，所以我們必須遵守。)"],["oppress","oppress(v.)壓迫、使沉重\noppression(n.)壓迫\noppressive(adj.)壓迫的、悶熱的\noppressed people 受壓迫的人民\nfeel oppressed 感到壓抑\nThe cruel ruler oppressed the poor for decades.\n(那位殘暴的統治者壓迫窮人長達數十年。)\nShe felt oppressed by the heavy pressure of exams.\n(她被沉重的考試壓力壓得喘不過氣。)"],["oppression","oppression(n.)壓迫、壓制、沉悶\noppress(v.)壓迫\noppressive(adj.)壓迫的\npolitical oppression 政治壓迫\nfight against oppression 反抗壓迫\nThe people finally rose up against years of oppression.\n(人民終於起身反抗多年來的壓迫。)\nMany writers have described life under political oppression.\n(許多作家描寫過在政治壓迫下的生活。)"],["ordeal","ordeal(n.)嚴酷的考驗、痛苦的經歷\n(無詞性變化)\ngo through an ordeal 經歷苦難\nterrible ordeal 可怕的折磨\nThe hikers were exhausted after their ordeal in the mountains.\n(那些登山客在山中歷經磨難後筋疲力盡。)\nPreparing for the college entrance exam can be a real ordeal.\n(準備大學入學考試可能是一場真正的考驗。)"],["orderly","orderly(adj./n.)有秩序的、整齊的、(醫院)勤務員\norder(n./v.)秩序、命令\norderliness(n.)整齊\nin an orderly manner 有秩序地\norderly room 整齊的房間\nThe students left the building in an orderly manner during the fire drill.\n(消防演習時學生們有秩序地離開大樓。)\nThe hospital orderly helped move the patient to another room.\n(醫院勤務員協助把病人移到另一間病房。)"],["organizer","organizer(n.)組織者、主辦人、收納盒\norganize(v.)組織、籌辦\norganization(n.)組織\nevent organizer 活動主辦人\ndesk organizer 桌上收納盒\nThe organizers expect over ten thousand people at the festival.\n(主辦單位預計將有超過一萬人參加這個節慶。)\nAs the event organizer, she handled every detail carefully.\n(身為活動主辦人，她仔細處理每個細節。)"],["orient","orient(n./v.)東方、使適應、使朝向\norientation(n.)方向、新生訓練\noriental(adj.)東方的\norient oneself 確定方位、適應\nbe oriented toward 以⋯為導向\nIt took me a few days to orient myself in the new city.\n(我花了幾天才熟悉這座新城市。)\nThe program is oriented toward helping beginners.\n(這個課程以幫助初學者為導向。)"],["oriental","oriental(adj./n.)東方的、東方人\norient(n.)東方\noriental culture 東方文化\noriental art 東方藝術\nThe museum has a large collection of oriental art.\n(這間博物館收藏了大量東方藝術品。)\nMany Western tourists are interested in oriental culture.\n(許多西方遊客對東方文化很感興趣。)"],["originate","originate(v.)起源、發源、創始\norigin(n.)起源\noriginal(adj.)原始的、原創的\noriginate from 起源於\noriginate in 發源於\nBubble tea originated in Taiwan in the 1980s.\n(珍珠奶茶於1980年代起源於台灣。)\nThe idea originated from a conversation between two students.\n(這個想法起源於兩名學生之間的一次對話。)"],["ornament","ornament(n./v.)裝飾品、裝飾\nornamental(adj.)裝飾用的\nChristmas ornament 聖誕裝飾品\nornamental plant 觀賞植物\nWe hung colorful ornaments on the Christmas tree.\n(我們在聖誕樹上掛了五彩繽紛的裝飾品。)\nThe old temple is ornamented with beautiful carvings.\n(那座古廟飾有精美的雕刻。)"],["orphanage","orphanage(n.)孤兒院\norphan(n.)孤兒\ngrow up in an orphanage 在孤兒院長大\nvolunteer at an orphanage 在孤兒院當志工\nHe grew up in an orphanage and later became a successful doctor.\n(他在孤兒院長大，後來成為一位成功的醫生。)\nOur class volunteered at a local orphanage last winter.\n(我們班去年冬天到當地的孤兒院當志工。)"],["orthodox","orthodox(adj.)正統的、傳統的、東正教的\northodoxy(n.)正統觀念\northodox method 傳統方法\nOrthodox Church 東正教會\nThe teacher used an unusual rather than an orthodox method.\n(那位老師使用的是一種特殊而非傳統的方法。)\nHis ideas challenged the orthodox views of the time.\n(他的想法挑戰了當時的正統觀點。)"],["ounce","ounce(n.)盎司(重量單位)、少量\n(無詞性變化)\nan ounce of gold 一盎司黃金\nnot an ounce of 一點也沒有\nThe price of an ounce of gold has risen sharply this year.\n(今年一盎司黃金的價格大幅上漲。)\nHe doesn't have an ounce of patience with lazy people.\n(他對懶惰的人一點耐心也沒有。)"],["outbreak","outbreak(n.)(疾病、戰爭等的)爆發\nbreak out(v.)爆發\noutbreak of war 戰爭爆發\ndisease outbreak 疾病爆發\nThe outbreak of the flu forced the school to close for a week.\n(流感爆發迫使學校停課一週。)\nMany families fled the country after the outbreak of war.\n(戰爭爆發後許多家庭逃離了這個國家。)"],["outgoing","outgoing(adj.)外向的、友善的、即將離職的\n(無詞性變化)\noutgoing personality 外向的個性\noutgoing president 即將卸任的總統\nWith her outgoing personality, she makes friends easily.\n(她個性外向，很容易交到朋友。)\nThe outgoing principal gave a moving farewell speech.\n(即將卸任的校長發表了感人的告別演說。)"],["outing","outing(n.)出遊、短途旅行\n(無詞性變化)\nfamily outing 家庭出遊\nschool outing 校外教學\nOur family went on an outing to Yangmingshan last Sunday.\n(我們全家上週日到陽明山出遊。)\nThe class outing was canceled because of the typhoon.\n(班級出遊因颱風而取消了。)"],["outlaw","outlaw(n./v.)罪犯、亡命之徒、宣布⋯為非法\n(無詞性變化)\noutlaw smoking 禁止吸菸\na famous outlaw 知名的亡命之徒\nMany countries have outlawed smoking in public places.\n(許多國家已明令禁止在公共場所吸菸。)\nThe movie tells the story of a famous outlaw in the Wild West.\n(這部電影講述蠻荒西部一位知名亡命之徒的故事。)"],["outlook","outlook(n.)觀點、看法、前景\n(無詞性變化)\npositive outlook 積極的人生觀\neconomic outlook 經濟前景\nDespite her illness, she keeps a positive outlook on life.\n(儘管生病，她仍保持積極的人生觀。)\nExperts say the economic outlook for next year is uncertain.\n(專家表示明年的經濟前景不明朗。)"],["outnumber","outnumber(v.)數量上超過、比⋯多\n(無詞性變化)\nbe outnumbered by 在數量上少於⋯\noutnumber... by two to one 以二比一的比例超過⋯\nIn our class, girls outnumber boys by two to one.\n(我們班女生人數是男生的兩倍。)\nThe soldiers were badly outnumbered but refused to give up.\n(士兵們寡不敵眾，但拒絕投降。)"],["outrage","outrage(n./v.)憤慨、暴行、激怒\noutrageous(adj.)駭人聽聞的\npublic outrage 公憤\nexpress outrage 表達憤慨\nThe decision to cut down the old trees caused public outrage.\n(砍伐老樹的決定引發了公憤。)\nMany people were outraged by the cruel treatment of animals.\n(許多人對虐待動物的行為感到憤慨。)"],["outrageous","outrageous(adj.)駭人聽聞的、令人憤慨的、離譜的\noutrage(n.)憤慨\noutrageously(adv.)離譜地\noutrageous price 離譜的價格\noutrageous behavior 令人憤慨的行為\nThey charged an outrageous price for a simple meal.\n(一頓簡單的餐點他們竟收取離譜的價格。)\nHis outrageous behavior at the party shocked everyone.\n(他在派對上駭人的行為讓大家都很震驚。)"],["outright","outright(adj./adv.)完全的、直率的、徹底地、當場\n(無詞性變化)\nwin outright 完勝\noutright lie 徹頭徹尾的謊言\nWhat he told you was an outright lie.\n(他告訴你的完全是謊言。)\nShe refused the offer outright without a second thought.\n(她想都沒想就斷然拒絕了這個提議。)"],["outset","outset(n.)開始、開端\n(無詞性變化)\nat the outset 一開始\nfrom the outset 從一開始\nFrom the outset, we knew the project would be difficult.\n(我們從一開始就知道這個計畫會很困難。)\nMake your goals clear at the outset of the semester.\n(在學期一開始就把你的目標訂清楚。)"],["outskirts","outskirts(n.)郊區、市郊\n(無詞性變化)\non the outskirts of 在⋯的郊區\ncity outskirts 城市郊區\nThey moved to a quiet house on the outskirts of Taichung.\n(他們搬到台中郊區一間安靜的房子。)\nThe new stadium was built on the outskirts of the city.\n(新體育場蓋在城市的郊區。)"],["outward","outward(adj.)外表的、向外的\noutwardly(adv.)表面上\noutward appearance 外表\noutward journey 去程\nDon't judge people by their outward appearance.\n(不要以貌取人。)\nDespite her outward calm, she was very nervous inside.\n(儘管她外表平靜，內心卻非常緊張。)"],["outward/outwards","outward(adv.)向外、往外\noutwards(adv.)向外、往外(同 outward)\nspread outward 向外擴散\nopen outwards 向外開\nThe door of the emergency exit opens outward.\n(緊急出口的門是向外開的。)\nThe city has been expanding outwards for decades.\n(這座城市數十年來不斷向外擴張。)"],["overdo","overdo(v.)做得過火、過度使用\noverdone(adj.)煮過頭的、過度的\noverdo it 做得過度、過度勞累\noverdo the salt 鹽放太多\nExercise is good for you, but don't overdo it.\n(運動對你有益，但不要過度。)\nThe chef overdid the salt, so the soup tasted terrible.\n(廚師鹽放太多，所以湯很難喝。)"],["overflow","overflow(n./v.)溢出、氾濫、過剩\n(無詞性變化)\noverflow with 充滿⋯\noverflow the banks 河水漫過堤岸\nAfter days of heavy rain, the river overflowed its banks.\n(連日大雨後，河水漫過了堤岸。)\nHer heart was overflowing with joy on graduation day.\n(畢業那天她的心中充滿了喜悅。)"],["overhear","overhear(v.)無意中聽到、偷聽到\n(無詞性變化)\noverhear a conversation 無意間聽到對話\nbe overheard 被人聽到\nI happened to overhear my parents talking about a trip to Japan.\n(我碰巧聽到爸媽在討論去日本旅行的事。)\nBe careful what you say; you might be overheard.\n(說話小心點，可能會被人聽到。)"],["overlap","overlap(n./v.)重疊、部分相同\n(無詞性變化)\noverlap with 與⋯重疊\na large overlap 大部分重疊\nThe two classes overlap, so I can only take one of them.\n(這兩門課時間重疊，所以我只能選其中一門。)\nThere is some overlap between biology and chemistry.\n(生物和化學之間有一些重疊的內容。)"],["overwork","overwork(n./v.)過勞、工作過度\noverworked(adj.)工作過度的\ndie from overwork 過勞死\noverworked and underpaid 工作過量且薪水過低\nOverwork can lead to serious health problems.\n(工作過度可能導致嚴重的健康問題。)\nNurses are often overworked during flu season.\n(流感季節時護理師常常工作過量。)"],["oyster","oyster(n.)牡蠣、蚵仔\n(無詞性變化)\noyster omelet 蚵仔煎\noyster sauce 蠔油\nOyster omelets are one of the most popular night market snacks.\n(蚵仔煎是最受歡迎的夜市小吃之一。)\nThe world is your oyster, so go out and explore it.\n(世界任你闖蕩，勇敢出去探索吧。)"],["ozone","ozone(n.)臭氧\n(無詞性變化)\nozone layer 臭氧層\nozone hole 臭氧層破洞\nThe ozone layer protects the earth from harmful UV rays.\n(臭氧層保護地球免受有害的紫外線傷害。)\nCertain chemicals have caused a hole in the ozone layer.\n(某些化學物質造成了臭氧層破洞。)"],["packet","packet(n.)小包、小袋、一包\npack(n./v.)包裹、打包\na packet of 一包…\nsugar packet 糖包\nShe tore open a packet of instant noodles for a late-night snack.\n(她撕開一包泡麵當作宵夜。)\nFollow the instructions printed on the back of the seed packet.\n(請依照種子包背面印的說明操作。)"],["paddle","paddle(n./v.)槳、用槳划、涉水\n(無詞性變化)\npaddle a canoe 划獨木舟\nstand-up paddle board 立式划槳\nWe paddled our canoe slowly along the quiet river.\n(我們沿著寧靜的河流慢慢划著獨木舟。)\nThe children paddled in the shallow water at the beach.\n(孩子們在海邊的淺水中玩水。)"],["paperback","paperback(n.)平裝書\nhardcover(n.)精裝書\nin paperback 平裝版\na cheap paperback 便宜的平裝書\nThe novel will be available in paperback next month.\n(這本小說下個月將推出平裝版。)\nI prefer paperbacks because they are lighter and cheaper.\n(我比較喜歡平裝書，因為它們比較輕也比較便宜。)"],["paradox","paradox(n.)矛盾、似非而是的論點、自相矛盾的人事物\nparadoxical(adj.)矛盾的\nparadoxically(adv.)矛盾地\na strange paradox 奇怪的矛盾\nthe paradox of choice 選擇的矛盾\nIt is a paradox that the more choices we have, the harder it is to decide.\n(選擇越多反而越難做決定，這真是個矛盾。)\nParadoxically, the busiest people often find time to help others.\n(矛盾的是，最忙碌的人往往能找到時間幫助別人。)"],["paralyze","paralyze(v.)使癱瘓、使麻痺\nparalysis(n.)癱瘓、麻痺\nparalyzed(adj.)癱瘓的\nbe paralyzed by fear 嚇得動彈不得\nparalyze traffic 使交通癱瘓\nThe heavy snowstorm paralyzed traffic across the entire city.\n(大風雪使整座城市的交通陷入癱瘓。)\nHe was paralyzed from the waist down after the car accident.\n(那場車禍後，他腰部以下癱瘓了。)"],["parliament","parliament(n.)國會、議會\nparliamentary(adj.)國會的\nmember of parliament 國會議員\npass through parliament 經國會通過\nThe new law must be approved by parliament before it takes effect.\n(新法律必須經國會通過才能生效。)\nShe was elected to parliament at the age of thirty.\n(她三十歲時當選國會議員。)"],["pastime","pastime(n.)消遣、娛樂\n(無詞性變化)\na favorite pastime 最喜歡的消遣\nnational pastime 全民休閒活動\nReading comics is one of my favorite pastimes on weekends.\n(看漫畫是我週末最喜歡的消遣之一。)\nBaseball is often called America's national pastime.\n(棒球常被稱為美國的國民休閒運動。)"],["patriot","patriot(n.)愛國者\npatriotic(adj.)愛國的\npatriotism(n.)愛國心\na true patriot 真正的愛國者\na sense of patriotism 愛國情操\nHe was remembered as a true patriot who fought for his country.\n(他被人們緬懷為一位為國奮戰的真正愛國者。)\nThe national anthem filled the crowd with a strong sense of patriotism.\n(國歌讓群眾心中充滿強烈的愛國情操。)"],["patriotic","patriotic(adj.)愛國的\npatriot(n.)愛國者\npatriotism(n.)愛國心\npatriotic songs 愛國歌曲\npatriotic spirit 愛國精神\nThe crowd sang patriotic songs during the national celebration.\n(在國家慶典上，群眾高唱愛國歌曲。)\nFans waved flags to show their patriotic spirit at the Olympics.\n(球迷在奧運會上揮舞國旗展現愛國精神。)"],["peacock","peacock(n.)(雄)孔雀\npeahen(n.)雌孔雀\nas proud as a peacock 像孔雀一樣驕傲\npeacock feathers 孔雀羽毛\nThe peacock spread its beautiful tail feathers to attract attention.\n(孔雀展開美麗的尾羽吸引目光。)\nAfter winning the prize, he walked around as proud as a peacock.\n(得獎後，他像孔雀一樣驕傲地四處走動。)"],["pebble","pebble(n.)小圓石、鵝卵石\npebbly(adj.)多卵石的\npebble beach 礫石灘\nsmooth pebbles 光滑的鵝卵石\nThe children collected smooth pebbles along the riverbank.\n(孩子們沿著河岸撿光滑的鵝卵石。)\nQixingtan in Hualien is famous for its beautiful pebble beach.\n(花蓮的七星潭以美麗的礫石灘聞名。)"],["peek","peek(n./v.)偷看、窺視\n(無詞性變化)\ntake a peek at 偷看一下\nsneak a peek 偷瞄一眼\nDon't peek at the answers before you finish the quiz.\n(做完小考之前不要偷看答案。)\nShe took a quick peek at her birthday present before the party.\n(派對開始前，她偷偷瞄了一眼她的生日禮物。)"],["pending","pending(adj.)懸而未決的、待決的、即將發生的\n(無詞性變化)\npending approval 等待批准\npending case 未決案件\nThe final decision is still pending until the manager returns.\n(在經理回來之前，最終決定仍懸而未決。)\nMy visa application is pending approval from the embassy.\n(我的簽證申請正在等待大使館核准。)"],["peninsula","peninsula(n.)半島\npeninsular(adj.)半島的\nthe Korean Peninsula 朝鮮半島\nthe Hengchun Peninsula 恆春半島\nKenting National Park is located on the Hengchun Peninsula.\n(墾丁國家公園位於恆春半島。)\nItaly is a long peninsula shaped like a boot.\n(義大利是一個形狀像靴子的狹長半島。)"],["perch","perch(n./v.)棲木、高處、(鳥)棲息、坐在高處\n(無詞性變化)\nperch on 棲息在…\na bird's perch 鳥的棲木\nA small bird perched on the branch outside my window.\n(一隻小鳥停在我窗外的樹枝上。)\nThe old castle is perched on top of a steep hill.\n(那座古堡坐落在陡峭的山頂上。)"],["peril","peril(n./v.)(嚴重的)危險、危及\nperilous(adj.)危險的\nin peril 在危險中\nat one's peril 自行承擔風險\nThe sailors were in great peril during the violent storm.\n(在猛烈的暴風雨中，水手們身陷極大的危險。)\nYou ignore the safety rules at your own peril.\n(你若忽視安全規則，後果自負。)"],["perish","perish(v.)死亡、毀滅、腐爛\nperishable(adj.)易腐壞的\nperish in a fire 死於火災\nperishable food 易腐壞的食物\nHundreds of people perished in the earthquake.\n(數百人在地震中喪生。)\nPerishable food such as milk should be kept in the refrigerator.\n(牛奶等容易腐壞的食物應存放在冰箱裡。)"],["permissible","permissible(adj.)可允許的、許可的\npermit(v./n.)允許、許可證\npermission(n.)許可\npermissible level 容許標準\nlegally permissible 法律允許的\nThe pollution in the river was far above the permissible level.\n(河川的汙染遠超過容許標準。)\nIs it permissible to use a calculator during the exam?\n(考試時可以使用計算機嗎？)"],["persevere","persevere(v.)堅持不懈、不屈不撓\nperseverance(n.)毅力、堅忍\npersevere with/in 堅持…\nwith perseverance 憑著毅力\nIf you persevere with your practice, your English will improve.\n(如果你堅持練習，英文就會進步。)\nHer perseverance finally paid off when she won the competition.\n(當她贏得比賽時，她的毅力終於得到了回報。)"],["persistence","persistence(n.)堅持、持續、固執\npersist(v.)堅持、持續\npersistent(adj.)堅持的\nwith persistence 堅持不懈地\npatience and persistence 耐心與毅力\nLearning a musical instrument requires patience and persistence.\n(學習樂器需要耐心和毅力。)\nThanks to his persistence, the team finally solved the problem.\n(多虧了他的堅持，團隊終於解決了問題。)"],["persistent","persistent(adj.)持續的、堅持不懈的、固執的\npersist(v.)堅持\npersistently(adv.)持續地\npersistent cough 久咳不癒\na persistent problem 持續存在的問題\nYou should see a doctor if you have a persistent cough.\n(如果久咳不癒，你應該去看醫生。)\nThe salesman was so persistent that I finally bought the product.\n(那位業務員非常鍥而不捨，最後我還是買了那項產品。)"],["petrol","petrol(n.)汽油(英式)\n(無詞性變化)\npetrol station 加油站\nrun out of petrol 汽油用完\nWe stopped at a petrol station to fill up the tank.\n(我們在加油站停下來加滿油。)\nThe price of petrol has risen sharply this year.\n(今年汽油價格大幅上漲。)"],["petroleum","petroleum(n.)石油\n(無詞性變化)\npetroleum products 石油製品\ncrude petroleum 原油\nPlastic is made from petroleum, a non-renewable resource.\n(塑膠是由石油這種不可再生資源製成的。)\nMany countries in the Middle East depend on petroleum exports.\n(許多中東國家仰賴石油出口。)"],["pharmacist","pharmacist(n.)藥劑師\npharmacy(n.)藥局、藥學\nask a pharmacist 詢問藥師\nlicensed pharmacist 有執照的藥師\nThe pharmacist explained how often I should take the medicine.\n(藥師解釋了我應該多久吃一次藥。)\nIf you have questions about side effects, ask your pharmacist.\n(如果對副作用有疑問，請詢問你的藥師。)"],["pharmacy","pharmacy(n.)藥局、藥學\npharmacist(n.)藥劑師\npharmaceutical(adj.)製藥的\na 24-hour pharmacy 二十四小時藥局\nstudy pharmacy 攻讀藥學\nI picked up my prescription at the pharmacy near the hospital.\n(我在醫院附近的藥局領了處方藥。)\nShe plans to study pharmacy at university next year.\n(她打算明年在大學攻讀藥學。)"],["pianist","pianist(n.)鋼琴家、鋼琴師\npiano(n.)鋼琴\na talented pianist 有天分的鋼琴家\nconcert pianist 演奏會鋼琴家\nThe young pianist gave a brilliant performance at the concert hall.\n(那位年輕鋼琴家在音樂廳的演出非常精彩。)\nShe practices four hours a day because she wants to be a concert pianist.\n(她每天練琴四小時，因為她想成為演奏會鋼琴家。)"],["pickpocket","pickpocket(n.)扒手\n(無詞性變化)\nbeware of pickpockets 小心扒手\na skilled pickpocket 熟練的扒手\nBeware of pickpockets in crowded places like night markets.\n(在夜市等擁擠的地方要小心扒手。)\nA pickpocket stole my wallet while I was on the crowded train.\n(我在擁擠的火車上時，錢包被扒手偷走了。)"],["pilgrim","pilgrim(n.)朝聖者、香客\npilgrimage(n.)朝聖、朝聖之旅\nmake a pilgrimage 去朝聖\nreligious pilgrims 宗教朝聖者\nThousands of pilgrims follow the Mazu procession every spring.\n(每年春天都有數千名香客跟隨媽祖遶境。)\nFor many music fans, visiting the singer's hometown is a kind of pilgrimage.\n(對許多樂迷來說，造訪那位歌手的故鄉是一種朝聖之旅。)"],["pimple","pimple(n.)青春痘、粉刺\npimply(adj.)長滿青春痘的\nget pimples 長痘痘\nsqueeze a pimple 擠痘痘\nMany teenagers get pimples on their faces during puberty.\n(許多青少年在青春期臉上會長痘痘。)\nDon't squeeze your pimples, or they may leave scars.\n(不要擠痘痘，否則可能會留下疤痕。)"],["pinch","pinch(n./v.)捏、擰、一撮、夾痛\n(無詞性變化)\na pinch of salt 一小撮鹽\nin a pinch 在緊要關頭\nAdd a pinch of salt to bring out the sweetness of the fruit.\n(加一小撮鹽來帶出水果的甜味。)\nI had to pinch myself to make sure I wasn't dreaming.\n(我得捏自己一下，確定我不是在作夢。)"],["plague","plague(n.)瘟疫、鼠疫、災害\n(無詞性變化)\nthe Black Plague 黑死病\na plague of 大量的(有害的)…\nThe plague killed millions of people in Europe during the Middle Ages.\n(中世紀時，瘟疫在歐洲奪走了數百萬條人命。)\nThe farmers suffered from a plague of locusts that destroyed their crops.\n(農民遭受蝗災，作物全被摧毀。)"],["plantation","plantation(n.)農園、大農場、種植園\nplant(n./v.)植物、種植\ntea plantation 茶園\nrubber plantation 橡膠園\nWe visited a tea plantation in Alishan and learned how tea is made.\n(我們參觀了阿里山的一座茶園，學習茶葉的製作過程。)\nMany workers on the sugar plantations lived in poor conditions.\n(許多甘蔗園的工人生活條件很差。)"],["playwright","playwright(n.)劇作家\nplay(n.)戲劇\na famous playwright 著名劇作家\na young playwright 年輕劇作家\nShakespeare is the most famous playwright in the English language.\n(莎士比亞是英語世界最著名的劇作家。)\nThe young playwright's first play was a huge success.\n(那位年輕劇作家的第一部劇作大獲成功。)"],["plow","plow(n./v.)犁、耕地、費力前進\n(無詞性變化)\nplow the field 犁田\nplow through 費力地完成、穿過\nIn the past, farmers used water buffalo to plow their fields.\n(過去農夫用水牛來犁田。)\nI had to plow through a pile of homework over the weekend.\n(我週末得費力地寫完一大堆作業。)"],["pneumonia","pneumonia(n.)肺炎\n(無詞性變化)\ncatch pneumonia 罹患肺炎\nsevere pneumonia 嚴重肺炎\nHis cold turned into pneumonia, so he had to stay in the hospital.\n(他的感冒轉成肺炎，所以必須住院。)\nElderly people are encouraged to get vaccinated against pneumonia.\n(長者被鼓勵接種肺炎疫苗。)"],["polar","polar(adj.)極地的、南北極的、正好相反的\npole(n.)極、極地\npolar bear 北極熊\npolar opposites 截然相反\nPolar bears are losing their habitat as the Arctic ice melts.\n(隨著北極冰層融化，北極熊正在失去棲息地。)\nThe two brothers are polar opposites in personality.\n(這兩兄弟的個性截然相反。)"],["ponder","ponder(v.)仔細考慮、沉思\n(無詞性變化)\nponder over/on 仔細思考…\nponder the question 思考這個問題\nShe pondered the question for a long time before answering.\n(她思考了這個問題很久才回答。)\nAfter graduation, he pondered over what career he should choose.\n(畢業後，他仔細思考該選擇什麼職業。)"],["pony","pony(n.)小馬\n(無詞性變化)\nride a pony 騎小馬\npony tail 馬尾(髮型)\nThe children took turns riding a pony at the farm.\n(孩子們在農場輪流騎小馬。)\nShe tied her long hair into a ponytail before the race.\n(比賽前她把長髮綁成馬尾。)"],["populate","populate(v.)居住於、構成人口\npopulation(n.)人口\npopulated(adj.)有人居住的\ndensely populated 人口稠密的\nsparsely populated 人口稀少的\nTaipei is one of the most densely populated cities in Taiwan.\n(臺北是臺灣人口最稠密的城市之一。)\nThe island was once populated by only a few fishing families.\n(這座島曾經只有幾戶漁民居住。)"],["porter","porter(n.)搬運工、行李員、門房\n(無詞性變化)\nhotel porter 飯店行李員\nairport porter 機場行李搬運員\nThe hotel porter carried our heavy suitcases up to the room.\n(飯店行李員把我們沉重的行李搬到房間。)\nPorters help climbers carry supplies up the mountain.\n(挑夫幫登山者把補給品背上山。)"],["posture","posture(n./v.)姿勢、態度、擺姿態\n(無詞性變化)\ngood posture 良好的姿勢\nsitting posture 坐姿\nPoor posture while using your phone can cause neck pain.\n(使用手機時姿勢不良可能導致頸部疼痛。)\nThe government adopted a firm posture in the trade negotiations.\n(政府在貿易談判中採取了強硬的態度。)"],["potent","potent(adj.)強有力的、有效力的\npotency(n.)效力、力量\na potent drug 強效藥物\na potent symbol 強而有力的象徵\nThis medicine is very potent, so follow the instructions carefully.\n(這種藥藥效很強，請仔細遵照說明服用。)\nThe flag has become a potent symbol of freedom for the people.\n(這面旗幟已成為人民追求自由的強烈象徵。)"],["poultry","poultry(n.)家禽、禽肉\n(無詞性變化)\npoultry farm 養雞場、家禽養殖場\npoultry products 禽肉製品\nThe poultry farm raises thousands of chickens and ducks.\n(這座家禽養殖場飼養了數千隻雞和鴨。)\nPoultry should be cooked thoroughly to kill harmful bacteria.\n(禽肉應該徹底煮熟以殺死有害細菌。)"],["preach","preach(v.)講道、說教、宣揚\npreacher(n.)傳教士\npreach to 對…說教\npractice what you preach 以身作則\nMy parents always preach about the importance of saving money.\n(我爸媽總是對存錢的重要性說教。)\nA good leader should practice what he preaches.\n(好的領導者應該以身作則。)"],["precede","precede(v.)在…之前、先於\npreceding(adj.)前面的、在前的\nprecedent(n.)先例\nprecede sth. with 在…之前先…\nthe preceding chapter 前一章\nA short speech by the principal preceded the award ceremony.\n(頒獎典禮之前有校長的簡短致詞。)\nThe answer to this question can be found in the preceding paragraph.\n(這個問題的答案可以在前一段找到。)"],["precedent","precedent(n.)先例、前例\nunprecedented(adj.)前所未有的\nset a precedent 開先例\nwithout precedent 史無前例\nThe court's decision set an important precedent for future cases.\n(法院的判決為未來的案件立下了重要先例。)\nThe pandemic caused unprecedented changes in the way we work.\n(疫情對我們的工作方式造成前所未有的改變。)"],["precision","precision(n.)精確、精準\nprecise(adj.)精確的\nprecisely(adv.)精確地\nwith precision 精確地\nprecision instruments 精密儀器\nThe surgeon performed the operation with great precision.\n(外科醫生非常精準地完成了手術。)\nTaiwan is known for producing precision machinery.\n(臺灣以生產精密機械聞名。)"],["predecessor","predecessor(n.)前任、前輩、前身\nsuccessor(n.)繼任者\none's predecessor 某人的前任\nthe predecessor of 某物的前身\nThe new principal is much stricter than her predecessor.\n(新校長比她的前任嚴格得多。)\nThe new phone is lighter and faster than its predecessor.\n(這款新手機比前一代更輕更快。)"],["prehistoric","prehistoric(adj.)史前的\nprehistory(n.)史前時代\nprehistoric times 史前時代\nprehistoric animals 史前動物\nScientists discovered prehistoric tools in a cave in eastern Taiwan.\n(科學家在臺灣東部的一個洞穴中發現了史前工具。)\nDinosaurs are the most famous prehistoric animals.\n(恐龍是最有名的史前動物。)"],["premiere","premiere(n.)首映、首演\n(無詞性變化)\nworld premiere 全球首映\nmovie premiere 電影首映會\nFans waited for hours outside the theater for the movie premiere.\n(影迷在戲院外等了好幾個小時參加電影首映會。)\nThe musical will have its world premiere in London next spring.\n(這齣音樂劇明年春天將在倫敦全球首演。)"],["preside","preside(v.)主持、擔任主席\npresident(n.)總統、會長\npresidency(n.)總統職位\npreside over 主持…\npreside at a meeting 主持會議\nThe principal presided over the graduation ceremony.\n(校長主持了畢業典禮。)\nThe judge who presided at the trial was known for being fair.\n(主持審判的法官以公正著稱。)"],["prestige","prestige(n.)聲望、威望\nprestigious(adj.)有聲望的\na prestigious university 名校\ngain prestige 獲得聲望\nWinning the international award brought the school great prestige.\n(贏得這項國際獎項為學校帶來極高的聲望。)\nHe was accepted by a prestigious university in the United States.\n(他被美國一所名校錄取了。)"],["preventive","preventive(adj./n.)預防的、預防措施\nprevent(v.)預防\nprevention(n.)預防\npreventive measures 預防措施\npreventive medicine 預防醫學\nThe government took preventive measures to stop the spread of the disease.\n(政府採取了預防措施來阻止疾病擴散。)\nRegular checkups are an important part of preventive medicine.\n(定期健康檢查是預防醫學的重要一環。)"],["preview","preview(n./v.)預告片、預習、預覽\n(無詞性變化)\nmovie preview 電影預告\npreview the lesson 預習課程\nStudents are encouraged to preview the lesson before class.\n(鼓勵學生在上課前預習課程。)\nThe preview of the new movie made everyone excited.\n(新電影的預告讓大家都很興奮。)"],["priceless","priceless(adj.)無價的、極寶貴的\nprice(n.)價格\npriceless treasure 無價之寶\npriceless experience 寶貴的經驗\nThe museum's collection includes many priceless works of art.\n(博物館的收藏包括許多無價的藝術品。)\nSpending time with my grandparents is a priceless experience.\n(和祖父母相處是一段無比寶貴的經驗。)"],["privatize","privatize(v.)使私有化、使民營化\nprivatization(n.)私有化、民營化\nprivatize state-owned companies 將國營企業民營化\nthe privatization of 某事物的民營化\nThe government decided to privatize the national airline.\n(政府決定將國家航空公司民營化。)\nThe privatization of public services remains a controversial issue.\n(公共服務的民營化仍是個具爭議的議題。)"],["probe","probe(n.)探查、調查、探測器\n(無詞性變化)\nspace probe 太空探測器\na probe into 對…的調查\nThe space probe sent back clear photos of Mars.\n(太空探測器傳回了火星的清晰照片。)\nThe police launched a probe into the cause of the fire.\n(警方對火災原因展開調查。)"],["procession","procession(n.)隊伍、行列、遊行\nproceed(v.)前進\nfuneral procession 送葬隊伍\nreligious procession 宗教遶境\nThe Mazu procession attracts thousands of believers every year.\n(媽祖遶境每年吸引數千名信眾。)\nA long procession of cars followed the bride's car to the hotel.\n(一長列車隊跟在新娘車後面前往飯店。)"],["proficiency","proficiency(n.)精通、熟練\nproficient(adj.)精通的、熟練的\nlanguage proficiency 語言能力\nproficiency test 能力檢定\nMany universities require proof of English proficiency.\n(許多大學要求提供英語能力證明。)\nShe is proficient in three languages, including Spanish.\n(她精通三種語言，包括西班牙文。)"],["prohibition","prohibition(n.)禁止、禁令\nprohibit(v.)禁止\na prohibition on/against 對…的禁令\nsmoking prohibition 禁菸令\nThere is a strict prohibition on smoking in all public buildings.\n(所有公共建築內都嚴格禁止吸菸。)\nThe government announced a prohibition against fishing in the area.\n(政府宣布禁止在該區域捕魚。)"],["propel","propel(v.)推進、驅使\npropeller(n.)螺旋槳\npropulsion(n.)推進力\nbe propelled by 由…推動\npropel sb. to fame 使某人成名\nThe boat is propelled by a small engine.\n(這艘船由一具小型引擎推進。)\nThe hit song propelled the young singer to fame overnight.\n(那首熱門歌曲讓這位年輕歌手一夕成名。)"],["prose","prose(n.)散文\n(無詞性變化)\nprose and poetry 散文與詩\na prose writer 散文作家\nThe author is famous for her beautiful and simple prose.\n(這位作家以優美而簡潔的散文聞名。)\nWe read both poetry and prose in our literature class.\n(我們在文學課上讀了詩和散文。)"],["prosecute","prosecute(v.)起訴、告發\nprosecution(n.)起訴、檢方\nprosecutor(n.)檢察官\nbe prosecuted for 因…被起訴\nthe prosecution 檢方\nThe driver was prosecuted for drunk driving.\n(那名駕駛因酒駕被起訴。)\nThe prosecutor presented strong evidence in court.\n(檢察官在法庭上提出了有力的證據。)"],["prospective","prospective(adj.)預期的、未來的、潛在的\nprospect(n.)前景、可能性\nprospective students 未來的學生\nprospective buyers 潛在買家\nThe university holds an open day for prospective students.\n(這所大學為有意就讀的學生舉辦校園開放日。)\nSeveral prospective buyers came to look at the house this weekend.\n(這週末有好幾位潛在買家來看房子。)"],["prototype","prototype(n.)原型、雛型\n(無詞性變化)\nbuild a prototype 打造原型\na working prototype 可運作的原型\nThe engineers built a prototype of the electric car for testing.\n(工程師們打造了電動車的原型以進行測試。)\nOur team presented a working prototype at the science fair.\n(我們團隊在科展上展示了一個可運作的原型。)"],["proverb","proverb(n.)諺語、俗語\nproverbial(adj.)諺語的、眾所皆知的\nan old proverb 古老的諺語\nas the proverb goes 俗話說\nAs the proverb goes, 'Practice makes perfect.'\n(俗話說：「熟能生巧。」)\nEvery culture has proverbs that teach lessons about life.\n(每個文化都有傳達人生道理的諺語。)"],["provincial","provincial(adj./n.)省的、地方的、鄉下的、外省人、鄉下人\nprovince(n.)省\nprovincial government 省政府\nprovincial attitude 狹隘的觀念\nThe provincial government announced new measures to protect farmland.\n(省政府宣布了保護農地的新措施。)\nTraveling abroad helped him overcome his provincial way of thinking.\n(出國旅行幫助他克服了狹隘的思考方式。)"],["provisional","provisional(adj.)暫時的、臨時的\nprovisionally(adv.)暫時地\nprovisional government 臨時政府\nprovisional license 臨時駕照\nA provisional government was formed after the revolution.\n(革命後成立了臨時政府。)\nThe schedule is provisional and may change next week.\n(這份行程是暫定的，下週可能會變動。)"],["psychiatry","psychiatry(n.)精神病學、精神醫學\npsychiatrist(n.)精神科醫師\npsychiatric(adj.)精神病學的\nchild psychiatry 兒童精神醫學\npsychiatric hospital 精神科醫院\nShe decided to specialize in psychiatry after medical school.\n(醫學院畢業後，她決定專攻精神醫學。)\nThe psychiatrist listened carefully to the patient's concerns.\n(精神科醫師仔細聆聽病患的困擾。)"],["psychic","psychic(adj.)通靈的、超自然的、心靈的\n(無詞性變化)\npsychic powers 超能力\npsychic abilities 通靈能力\nThe woman claimed to have psychic powers and could predict the future.\n(那名女子聲稱自己有超能力，能預知未來。)\nScientists remain doubtful about the existence of psychic abilities.\n(科學家對通靈能力是否存在仍抱持懷疑。)"],["psychotherapy","psychotherapy(n.)心理治療\npsychotherapist(n.)心理治療師\nundergo psychotherapy 接受心理治療\ngroup psychotherapy 團體心理治療\nPsychotherapy can help people cope with stress and emotional problems.\n(心理治療能幫助人們應付壓力與情緒問題。)\nThe psychotherapist uses art to help children express their feelings.\n(這位心理治療師用藝術幫助孩子表達自己的感受。)"],["publicize","publicize(v.)宣傳、公布\npublicity(n.)宣傳\npublic(adj.)公開的\npublicize an event 宣傳活動\nwidely publicized 廣為宣傳的\nThe students made posters to publicize the charity concert.\n(學生們製作海報宣傳慈善音樂會。)\nThe scandal was widely publicized in the media.\n(這起醜聞被媒體大幅報導。)"],["puff","puff(n./v.)一陣(煙、氣)、噴煙、喘氣\npuffy(adj.)腫脹的、蓬鬆的\na puff of smoke 一縷煙\ncream puff 泡芙\nA puff of smoke rose from the chimney.\n(一縷煙從煙囪升起。)\nHe was huffing and puffing after running up five flights of stairs.\n(他跑上五層樓梯後氣喘吁吁。)"],["punctual","punctual(adj.)準時的、守時的\npunctuality(n.)準時、守時\npunctually(adv.)準時地\nbe punctual for 準時參加…\npunctual payment 按時付款\nJapanese trains are famous for being punctual.\n(日本的火車以準時聞名。)\nPunctuality is an important quality in the workplace.\n(守時是職場上很重要的特質。)"],["purify","purify(v.)淨化、使純淨\npurification(n.)淨化\npure(adj.)純淨的\npurify water 淨化水\nair purifier 空氣清淨機\nThis machine purifies water by removing harmful chemicals.\n(這台機器藉由去除有害化學物質來淨化水。)\nMany families use an air purifier during seasons of poor air quality.\n(許多家庭在空氣品質不佳的季節使用空氣清淨機。)"],["purity","purity(n.)純淨、純度、純潔\npure(adj.)純淨的\npurify(v.)淨化\nhigh purity 高純度\npurity of heart 心靈純潔\nThe gold has a purity of 99.9 percent.\n(這塊黃金的純度達百分之九十九點九。)\nIn many cultures, white is a symbol of purity.\n(在許多文化中，白色象徵純潔。)"],["quake","quake(v./n.)震動、顫抖、地震\nearthquake(n.)地震\nquake with fear 嚇得發抖\na strong quake 強烈地震\nThe building quaked violently during the strong earthquake.\n(強烈地震時，大樓劇烈搖晃。)\nThe little boy was quaking with fear during the thunderstorm.\n(雷雨時那個小男孩嚇得直發抖。)"],["qualification","qualification(n.)資格、學歷、條件\nqualify(v.)使有資格\nqualified(adj.)有資格的、合格的\nacademic qualifications 學歷\nmeet the qualifications 符合資格\nApplicants must meet all the qualifications listed in the job ad.\n(應徵者必須符合職缺廣告上列出的所有資格。)\nShe is highly qualified to teach English at our school.\n(她非常有資格在我們學校教英文。)"],["radiant","radiant(adj./n.)容光煥發的、燦爛的、輻射的、發光體\nradiance(n.)光輝、容光煥發\na radiant smile 燦爛的笑容\nradiant energy 輻射能\nThe bride looked radiant in her white wedding dress.\n(新娘穿著白色婚紗，看起來容光煥發。)\nShe greeted every guest with a radiant smile.\n(她以燦爛的笑容迎接每一位賓客。)"],["radiate","radiate(v./adj.)散發、輻射、放射狀的\nradiation(n.)輻射\nradiator(n.)暖氣片、散熱器\nradiate heat 散發熱\nradiate confidence 散發自信\nThe stove radiated enough heat to warm the whole room.\n(火爐散發的熱足以讓整個房間暖和起來。)\nThe new captain radiated confidence as she led the team onto the field.\n(新隊長帶領隊伍上場時散發著自信。)"],["radioactive","radioactive(adj.)放射性的、有輻射的\nradioactivity(n.)放射性\nradioactive waste 核廢料\nradioactive material 放射性物質\nStoring radioactive waste safely is a serious problem for many countries.\n(安全貯存核廢料是許多國家面臨的嚴重問題。)\nWorkers must wear protective suits when handling radioactive materials.\n(工人處理放射性物質時必須穿防護衣。)"],["radish","radish(n.)蘿蔔、小紅蘿蔔\n(無詞性變化)\nwhite radish 白蘿蔔\nradish cake 蘿蔔糕\nRadish cake is a popular dish during the Lunar New Year in Taiwan.\n(蘿蔔糕是臺灣農曆新年期間很受歡迎的料理。)\nMy grandmother grows white radishes in her backyard garden.\n(我奶奶在後院菜園裡種白蘿蔔。)"],["radius","radius(n.)半徑、範圍\nradii(n.)半徑(複數)\nwithin a radius of 在…半徑範圍內\nthe radius of a circle 圓的半徑\nThere are five convenience stores within a radius of one kilometer.\n(方圓一公里內有五家便利商店。)\nTo find the area of a circle, you need to know its radius.\n(要算出圓的面積，你需要知道它的半徑。)"],["rap","rap(n.)饒舌音樂、敲擊聲、責備\nrapper(n.)饒舌歌手\nrap music 饒舌音樂\na rap on the door 敲門聲\nRap music became popular among young people in the 1990s.\n(饒舌音樂在1990年代開始受到年輕人歡迎。)\nWe heard a sharp rap on the door late at night.\n(深夜我們聽到一陣急促的敲門聲。)"],["rash","rash(n./adj.)疹子、輕率的、魯莽的\nrashly(adv.)輕率地\nskin rash 皮疹\na rash decision 輕率的決定\nDon't make a rash decision when you are angry.\n(生氣時不要做出輕率的決定。)\nShe developed a red rash after eating seafood.\n(她吃了海鮮後起了紅疹。)"],["ratify","ratify(v.)批准、正式認可\nratification(n.)批准\nratify a treaty 批准條約\nratify an agreement 批准協議\nBoth countries must ratify the treaty before it can take effect.\n(兩國都必須批准該條約，條約才能生效。)\nThe agreement was ratified by the legislature last week.\n(該協議上週已由立法機關批准。)"],["realization","realization(n.)領悟、認識、實現\nrealize(v.)了解、實現\ncome to the realization 逐漸領悟\nthe realization of a dream 夢想的實現\nHe came to the realization that health is more important than money.\n(他逐漸領悟到健康比金錢更重要。)\nOpening her own bakery was the realization of a lifelong dream.\n(開一家自己的麵包店是她畢生夢想的實現。)"],["reap","reap(v.)收割、收穫、獲得\n(無詞性變化)\nreap the benefits 獲得好處\nreap what you sow 種瓜得瓜、自食其果\nStudents who study regularly will reap the benefits at exam time.\n(平時規律念書的學生在考試時就會嚐到甜頭。)\nAs the saying goes, you reap what you sow.\n(俗話說，種什麼因就得什麼果。)"],["reckless","reckless(adj.)魯莽的、不顧後果的\nrecklessly(adv.)魯莽地\nrecklessness(n.)魯莽\nreckless driving 魯莽駕駛\nreckless behavior 不顧後果的行為\nReckless driving is one of the main causes of traffic accidents.\n(魯莽駕駛是交通事故的主要原因之一。)\nHe spent his money recklessly and soon had nothing left.\n(他揮霍無度，很快就一無所有。)"],["reckon","reckon(v.)認為、估計、計算\nreckoning(n.)計算、清算\nreckon on 指望…\nreckon with 處理、對付\nI reckon it will take about two hours to get there.\n(我估計到那裡大約要兩個小時。)\nDo you reckon he will accept our invitation?\n(你認為他會接受我們的邀請嗎？)"],["reconcile","reconcile(v.)使和解、調和、使接受\nreconciliation(n.)和解、調和\nreconcile with 與…和解\nbe reconciled to 勉強接受…\nAfter years of silence, the two brothers finally reconciled.\n(經過多年不說話，兩兄弟終於和解了。)\nIt is hard to reconcile a busy career with family life.\n(要兼顧忙碌的工作和家庭生活很困難。)"],["recreational","recreational(adj.)娛樂的、休閒的\nrecreation(n.)娛樂、消遣\nrecreational activities 休閒活動\nrecreational facilities 休閒設施\nThe park offers many recreational activities such as cycling and fishing.\n(這座公園提供許多休閒活動，例如騎單車和釣魚。)\nThe new community center includes a pool and other recreational facilities.\n(新的社區中心包括泳池和其他休閒設施。)"],["redundancy","redundancy(n.)多餘、冗詞、裁員\nredundant(adj.)多餘的、被裁員的\navoid redundancy 避免贅字\nbe made redundant 被裁員\nGood writers avoid redundancy and choose their words carefully.\n(好的作家會避免贅字並謹慎選擇用詞。)\nHundreds of workers were made redundant when the factory closed.\n(工廠關閉時，數百名員工被裁員。)"],["reef","reef(n.)礁、暗礁\n(無詞性變化)\ncoral reef 珊瑚礁\nGreat Barrier Reef 大堡礁\nCoral reefs are home to thousands of species of marine life.\n(珊瑚礁是數千種海洋生物的家。)\nRising ocean temperatures are damaging the Great Barrier Reef.\n(海水溫度上升正在破壞大堡礁。)"],["referee","referee(n./v.)裁判、擔任裁判\n(無詞性變化)\nfootball referee 足球裁判\nreferee a match 擔任比賽裁判\nThe referee blew the whistle to end the first half.\n(裁判吹哨結束上半場。)\nMy uncle has refereed basketball games for over twenty years.\n(我舅舅擔任籃球比賽裁判已經二十多年了。)"],["referendum","referendum(n.)公民投票、公投\n(無詞性變化)\nhold a referendum 舉行公投\na referendum on 針對…的公投\nThe country held a referendum on whether to change its energy policy.\n(該國針對是否改變能源政策舉行了公投。)\nThe result of the referendum surprised many political experts.\n(公投結果讓許多政治專家感到意外。)"],["refine(ment)","refine(v.)精煉、改善、使優雅、refinement(n.)精煉、改進、優雅\nrefined(adj.)精煉的、有教養的\nrefinery(n.)精煉廠\nrefined sugar 精製糖\nrefine one's skills 精進技巧\nShe spent months refining her speech for the competition.\n(她花了好幾個月修改她的比賽演講稿。)\nEating too much refined sugar is bad for your teeth.\n(吃太多精製糖對牙齒不好。)"],["reflective","reflective(adj.)反射的、沉思的、反映…的\nreflect(v.)反射、反映、反省\nreflection(n.)倒影、反省\nreflective vest 反光背心\nin a reflective mood 陷入沉思\nRoad workers must wear reflective vests at night.\n(道路工人晚上必須穿反光背心。)\nAfter the trip, she was in a quiet and reflective mood.\n(旅行結束後，她安靜地陷入沉思。)"],["refresh(ment)","refresh(v.)使恢復精神、更新、refreshment(n.)恢復精神、提神物\nrefreshing(adj.)令人神清氣爽的\nrefresh one's memory 喚起記憶\nrefresh the page 重新整理頁面\nA short nap will refresh you after a long morning of classes.\n(上了一早上的課後，小睡一下能讓你恢復精神。)\nLet me refresh your memory about what we discussed last week.\n(讓我幫你回想一下我們上週討論的內容。)"],["refreshment(s)","refreshment(n.)恢復精神、提神物、refreshments(n.)茶點、點心飲料\nrefresh(v.)使恢復精神\nlight refreshments 簡單的茶點\nserve refreshments 供應茶點\nLight refreshments will be served after the lecture.\n(演講結束後將供應簡單的茶點。)\nThe hikers stopped at a small shop for some refreshment.\n(登山客在一家小店停下來稍作休息、吃點東西。)"],["refute","refute(v.)反駁、駁斥\nrefutation(n.)反駁\nrefute a claim 駁斥說法\nrefute an argument 反駁論點\nThe scientist used new data to refute the old theory.\n(那位科學家用新數據駁斥了舊理論。)\nThe company quickly refuted the rumors about its financial problems.\n(公司迅速駁斥了有關其財務問題的謠言。)"],["rehabilitate","rehabilitate(v.)使康復、使恢復正常生活、修復\nrehabilitation(n.)復健、康復、修復\nrehabilitation center 復健中心\nrehabilitate patients 使病人康復\nThe program helps rehabilitate injured athletes so they can compete again.\n(這項計畫協助受傷的運動員復健，讓他們能再次參賽。)\nAfter the surgery, he needed months of rehabilitation to walk normally.\n(手術後，他需要好幾個月的復健才能正常走路。)"],["rehearse","rehearse(v.)排練、預演\nrehearsal(n.)排練、彩排\ndress rehearsal 彩排\nrehearse a play 排練戲劇\nThe drama club rehearsed the play every afternoon for a month.\n(戲劇社一個月來每天下午都在排練這齣戲。)\nWe had a dress rehearsal the day before the graduation ceremony.\n(畢業典禮的前一天我們進行了彩排。)"],["reign","reign(n./v.)統治時期、統治、盛行\n(無詞性變化)\nduring the reign of 在…統治期間\nreign supreme 居於首位\nMany great buildings were built during the reign of Queen Victoria.\n(許多宏偉的建築是在維多利亞女王統治期間建造的。)\nSilence reigned in the classroom after the teacher's announcement.\n(老師宣布之後，教室裡一片寂靜。)"],["rejoice","rejoice(v.)欣喜、高興\nrejoicing(n.)歡騰、喜悅\nrejoice at/over 為…感到欣喜\nrejoice in 樂於…\nThe whole town rejoiced at the news of the team's victory.\n(全鎮都為球隊獲勝的消息而歡欣鼓舞。)\nFans rejoiced in the streets after the national team won the championship.\n(國家隊奪冠後，球迷們在街頭歡慶。)"],["relay","relay(n./v.)接力賽、轉達、轉播\n(無詞性變化)\nrelay race 接力賽\nrelay a message 轉達訊息\nOur class won first place in the 400-meter relay race.\n(我們班在四百公尺接力賽中得到第一名。)\nPlease relay this message to the rest of the team.\n(請把這則訊息轉達給隊上其他人。)"],["relentless","relentless(adj.)不懈的、無情的、持續不斷的\nrelentlessly(adv.)不停地、無情地\nrelentless pressure 持續不斷的壓力\nrelentless pursuit 不懈的追求\nThe relentless rain caused flooding in several parts of the city.\n(持續不斷的大雨導致城市多處淹水。)\nHer relentless pursuit of excellence made her a top athlete.\n(她對卓越的不懈追求使她成為頂尖運動員。)"],["reliance","reliance(n.)依賴、信賴\nrely(v.)依賴\nreliant(adj.)依賴的\nreliance on 對…的依賴\nheavy reliance 嚴重依賴\nThe country is trying to reduce its reliance on imported oil.\n(該國正試圖減少對進口石油的依賴。)\nToo much reliance on smartphones may affect our ability to concentrate.\n(過度依賴智慧型手機可能影響我們的專注力。)"],["reliant","reliant(adj.)依賴的、依靠的\nreliance(n.)依賴\nself-reliant(adj.)自立的\nbe reliant on 依賴…\nheavily reliant 高度依賴\nThe island is heavily reliant on tourism for its income.\n(這座島的收入高度依賴觀光業。)\nLiving alone taught him to become more self-reliant.\n(獨自生活讓他學會更加自立。)"],["relic","relic(n.)遺物、遺跡、遺俗\n(無詞性變化)\nancient relics 古代遺物\na relic of the past 過去的遺物\nThe museum displays relics from the Ming Dynasty.\n(這座博物館展出明朝的文物。)\nThe old typewriter is a relic of a time before computers.\n(這台舊打字機是電腦問世之前的時代遺物。)"],["remainder","remainder(n.)剩餘部分、餘數\nremain(v.)剩下、保持\nremaining(adj.)剩餘的\nthe remainder of 其餘的…\nfor the remainder of 在…剩下的時間\nShe spent the remainder of her vacation reading at home.\n(她把剩下的假期都用來在家看書。)\nWhen you divide 10 by 3, the remainder is 1.\n(當你把十除以三時，餘數是一。)"],["reminiscent","reminiscent(adj.)使人聯想起的、懷舊的\nreminisce(v.)追憶、緬懷\nreminiscence(n.)回憶\nbe reminiscent of 讓人想起…\nreminisce about 回憶…\nThe taste of this soup is reminiscent of my mother's cooking.\n(這碗湯的味道讓我想起媽媽的手藝。)\nThe old classmates spent the evening reminiscing about their school days.\n(老同學們整晚都在回憶學生時代。)"],["renowned","renowned(adj.)著名的、有聲譽的\nrenown(n.)名聲、聲望\nbe renowned for 以…聞名\nworld-renowned 世界知名的\nTaiwan is renowned for its delicious street food.\n(臺灣以美味的街頭小吃聞名。)\nThe concert featured a world-renowned violinist from Germany.\n(這場音樂會邀請了一位來自德國的世界知名小提琴家。)"],["reproduce","reproduce(v.)繁殖、複製、再現\nreproduction(n.)繁殖、複製品\nreproductive(adj.)生殖的\nreproduce quickly 快速繁殖\nreproduce a painting 複製畫作\nRabbits can reproduce very quickly if they are not controlled.\n(如果不加以控制，兔子可以繁殖得非常快。)\nThe painting in the hotel lobby is a reproduction of a famous work.\n(飯店大廳的那幅畫是一幅名作的複製品。)"],["reptile","reptile(n./adj.)爬蟲類動物、爬蟲類的\nreptilian(adj.)爬蟲類的\nreptile house 爬蟲館\ncold-blooded reptiles 冷血的爬蟲類\nSnakes, lizards, and turtles are all reptiles.\n(蛇、蜥蜴和烏龜都是爬蟲類。)\nReptiles often lie in the sun to warm their bodies.\n(爬蟲類常躺在陽光下讓身體變暖。)"],["resent(ment)","resent(v.)憤恨、怨恨、resentment(n.)憤恨、怨恨\nresentful(adj.)憤恨的\nresent being 對被…感到不滿\nfeel resentment toward 對…感到怨恨\nTeenagers often resent being treated like little children.\n(青少年常常不滿被當成小孩對待。)\nUnfair treatment can create deep resentment among employees.\n(不公平的待遇可能在員工之間造成很深的怨恨。)"],["reside","reside(v.)居住、存在於\nresidence(n.)住所、居住\nresident(n.)居民\nreside in 居住在…\npermanent residence 永久居留\nMost of his relatives now reside in Kaohsiung.\n(他大部分的親戚現在住在高雄。)\nLocal residents complained about the noise from the new factory.\n(當地居民抱怨新工廠的噪音。)"],["resistant","resistant(adj.)抵抗的、有抵抗力的、耐…的\nresist(v.)抵抗\nresistance(n.)抵抗、抵抗力\nwater-resistant 防水的\nresistant to 對…有抵抗力\nThis watch is water-resistant up to fifty meters.\n(這支錶可防水至五十公尺。)\nSome bacteria have become resistant to common antibiotics.\n(有些細菌已對常見的抗生素產生抗藥性。)"],["respective","respective(adj.)分別的、各自的\nrespectively(adv.)分別地、各自地\ntheir respective homes 他們各自的家\nrespective fields 各自的領域\nAfter the party, the guests returned to their respective homes.\n(派對結束後，賓客們各自回家。)\nTom and Mary scored 85 and 92 points respectively.\n(湯姆和瑪莉分別得了85分和92分。)"],["restoration","restoration(n.)恢復、修復、重建\nrestore(v.)恢復、修復\nrestoration work 修復工程\nthe restoration of 某事物的恢復\nThe restoration of the old temple took nearly three years.\n(這座古廟的修復花了將近三年。)\nEveryone welcomed the restoration of electricity after the typhoon.\n(颱風過後電力恢復，大家都很高興。)"],["restrain","restrain(v.)抑制、克制、阻止\nrestraint(n.)克制、約束\nrestrain oneself 克制自己\nrestrain sb. from 阻止某人做…\nShe could hardly restrain her excitement when she heard the news.\n(聽到這個消息時，她幾乎無法抑制自己的興奮。)\nThe police had to restrain the angry man from attacking others.\n(警方必須制止那名憤怒的男子攻擊他人。)"],["restraint","restraint(n.)克制、節制、約束\nrestrain(v.)抑制\nshow restraint 表現克制\nwithout restraint 毫無節制地\nBoth sides were asked to show restraint and avoid violence.\n(雙方都被要求保持克制、避免暴力。)\nChildren in cars must be secured with proper safety restraints.\n(車內的孩童必須用適當的安全裝置固定。)"],["retort","retort(n./v.)反駁、回嘴\n(無詞性變化)\na sharp retort 尖銳的反駁\nretort angrily 憤怒地反駁\n'It's none of your business,' she retorted angrily.\n(「不關你的事。」她憤怒地反駁。)\nHis clever retort made the whole class laugh.\n(他機智的回嘴讓全班哄堂大笑。)"],["retrieve","retrieve(v.)取回、找回、檢索\nretrieval(n.)取回、檢索\nretrieve data 擷取資料\ninformation retrieval 資訊檢索\nI managed to retrieve the lost files from my old computer.\n(我設法從舊電腦中找回了遺失的檔案。)\nThe dog ran into the lake to retrieve the ball.\n(那隻狗跑進湖裡把球叼回來。)"],["revelation","revelation(n.)揭露、透露、啟示\nreveal(v.)揭露、透露\na shocking revelation 驚人的揭露\ncome as a revelation 令人大開眼界\nThe revelation that the mayor had lied shocked the public.\n(市長說謊一事被揭露後震驚了大眾。)\nVisiting the science museum was a revelation for the young students.\n(參觀科學博物館讓年輕學生大開眼界。)"],["revival","revival(n.)復甦、復興、重新流行\nrevive(v.)使復甦\neconomic revival 經濟復甦\na revival of interest 重新引起興趣\nThere has been a revival of interest in vinyl records among young people.\n(年輕人對黑膠唱片重新燃起興趣。)\nThe government hopes the new policy will lead to an economic revival.\n(政府希望新政策能帶動經濟復甦。)"],["revive","revive(v.)使甦醒、使復活、使復興\nrevival(n.)復甦、復興\nrevive the economy 振興經濟\nrevive a tradition 恢復傳統\nThe doctors managed to revive the man who had stopped breathing.\n(醫生們成功救醒了那名停止呼吸的男子。)\nThe village is trying to revive its traditional festivals to attract tourists.\n(這個村莊正努力恢復傳統節慶來吸引觀光客。)"],["revolt","revolt(n./v.)反叛、起義、使反感\nrevolting(adj.)令人作嘔的\nrise in revolt 起義\nrevolt against 反抗…\nThe farmers rose in revolt against the unfair taxes.\n(農民們起義反抗不公平的稅收。)\nThe smell of the rotten fish was absolutely revolting.\n(腐爛的魚的味道令人極度作嘔。)"],["revolve","revolve(v.)旋轉、繞轉、以…為中心\nrevolution(n.)革命、公轉\nrevolving(adj.)旋轉的\nrevolve around 繞著…轉、以…為中心\nrevolving door 旋轉門\nThe earth revolves around the sun once a year.\n(地球每年繞太陽公轉一圈。)\nHer whole life seems to revolve around her children.\n(她整個生活似乎都圍繞著她的孩子打轉。)"],["rigorous","rigorous(adj.)嚴格的、嚴謹的、嚴酷的\nrigorously(adv.)嚴格地\nrigor(n.)嚴格、嚴謹\nrigorous training 嚴格的訓練\nrigorous testing 嚴格的測試\nAstronauts must go through years of rigorous training.\n(太空人必須經過多年嚴格的訓練。)\nAll new medicines undergo rigorous testing before they are sold.\n(所有新藥在上市前都要經過嚴格的測試。)"],["ripple","ripple(n./v.)漣漪、波紋、起漣漪\n(無詞性變化)\nripple effect 連鎖效應\na ripple of laughter 一陣笑聲\nThe stone created small ripples on the surface of the pond.\n(石頭在池塘水面上激起小小的漣漪。)\nRising oil prices have a ripple effect on the whole economy.\n(油價上漲對整體經濟產生連鎖效應。)"],["rivalry","rivalry(n.)競爭、對抗\nrival(n./v.)對手、與…匹敵\nfierce rivalry 激烈的競爭\nsibling rivalry 手足之爭\nThere is a fierce rivalry between the two schools' basketball teams.\n(這兩所學校的籃球隊之間競爭非常激烈。)\nSibling rivalry is common in families with more than one child.\n(手足之爭在有多個孩子的家庭中很常見。)"],["roam","roam(v./n.)漫步、閒逛、漫遊\nroaming(n.)(手機)漫遊\nroam the streets 在街上閒逛\nroam freely 自由漫遊\nWild deer roam freely in the national park.\n(野鹿在國家公園裡自由地漫遊。)\nWe spent the afternoon roaming the narrow streets of the old town.\n(我們整個下午都在老城區的窄巷裡閒逛。)"],["robust","robust(adj.)強健的、堅固的、穩健的\nrobustly(adv.)強健地\nrobust health 健壯的身體\nrobust economy 穩健的經濟\nMy grandfather is still in robust health at the age of ninety.\n(我爺爺九十歲了身體依然硬朗。)\nThe new phone has a robust design that can survive a fall.\n(這款新手機設計堅固，摔落也不易損壞。)"],["rotate","rotate(v.)旋轉、輪流、輪換\nrotation(n.)旋轉、輪流\nrotate around 繞…旋轉\nrotate crops 輪作\nThe earth rotates on its axis once every 24 hours.\n(地球每二十四小時繞地軸自轉一次。)\nTeam members rotate the job of cleaning the classroom every week.\n(組員每週輪流負責打掃教室。)"],["rotation","rotation(n.)旋轉、自轉、輪流\nrotate(v.)旋轉、輪流\nin rotation 輪流地\ncrop rotation 輪作\nThe rotation of the earth causes day and night.\n(地球的自轉造成了白天和黑夜。)\nFarmers use crop rotation to keep the soil healthy.\n(農民採用輪作來保持土壤健康。)"],["royalty","royalty(n.)王室成員、王權、版稅\nroyal(adj.)皇家的\nbe treated like royalty 受到貴賓級款待\nreceive royalties 收取版稅\nWe were treated like royalty at the luxury hotel.\n(我們在那家豪華飯店受到了貴賓級的款待。)\nThe author receives royalties every time her book is sold.\n(這位作家的書每賣出一本，她就能收到版稅。)"],["rubbish","rubbish(n.)垃圾、廢物、胡說\n(無詞性變化)\nrubbish bin 垃圾桶\ntalk rubbish 胡說八道\nPlease put your rubbish in the bin before leaving the park.\n(離開公園前請把垃圾丟進垃圾桶。)\nDon't believe him; he is talking rubbish.\n(別相信他，他在胡說八道。)"],["rugged","rugged(adj.)崎嶇的、粗獷的、堅固耐用的\nruggedness(n.)崎嶇、粗獷\nrugged coastline 崎嶇的海岸線\nrugged mountains 崎嶇的山脈\nThe east coast of Taiwan is famous for its rugged coastline.\n(臺灣東海岸以崎嶇的海岸線聞名。)\nThis rugged laptop is designed for use in extreme conditions.\n(這台耐用的筆電是為極端環境下使用而設計的。)"],["ruthless","ruthless(adj.)無情的、殘忍的\nruthlessly(adv.)無情地\nruthlessness(n.)無情、殘忍\na ruthless dictator 冷酷無情的獨裁者\nruthless competition 殘酷的競爭\nThe ruthless dictator punished anyone who disagreed with him.\n(那個冷酷無情的獨裁者懲罰任何反對他的人。)\nSmall shops struggle to survive in the ruthless competition with big chains.\n(小商店在與大型連鎖店的殘酷競爭中艱難求生。)"],["salute","salute(n./v.)敬禮、致敬、表揚\n(無詞性變化)\nmilitary salute 軍禮\nsalute the flag 向國旗敬禮\nThe soldiers saluted the general as he walked past them.\n(將軍經過時，士兵們向他敬禮。)\nThe ceremony was held to salute the doctors and nurses who fought the pandemic.\n(這場典禮是為了向對抗疫情的醫護人員致敬而舉辦的。)"],["salvage","salvage(v.)搶救、挽救、打撈\nsalvation(n.)拯救、救助\nsalvage operation 打撈行動\nsalvage the situation 挽救局面\nDivers tried to salvage valuable items from the sunken ship.\n(潛水員試著從沉船中打撈有價值的物品。)\nThe coach made several changes to salvage the team's disappointing season.\n(教練做了幾項調整，試圖挽救球隊令人失望的球季。)"],["sanitation","sanitation(n.)公共衛生、衛生設備\nsanitary(adj.)衛生的、清潔的\nsanitize(v.)消毒\npoor sanitation 衛生條件不佳\nsanitation worker 清潔隊員\nPoor sanitation can lead to the spread of serious diseases.\n(衛生條件不佳可能導致嚴重疾病的散播。)\nSanitation workers collect garbage in our neighborhood every evening.\n(清潔隊員每天傍晚到我們社區收垃圾。)"],["savage","savage(adj./n./v.)野蠻的、兇猛的、野蠻人、猛烈攻擊\nsavagely(adv.)兇猛地、殘忍地\nsavagery(n.)野蠻、殘暴\nsavage attack 兇猛的攻擊\nsavage criticism 猛烈的批評\nThe villagers were frightened by the savage attack of the wild dogs.\n(村民們被野狗兇猛的攻擊嚇壞了。)\nThe director's new film was savaged by critics.\n(這位導演的新片遭到影評人猛烈抨擊。)"],["scenic","scenic(adj.)風景優美的、景色的\nscene(n.)景色、場景\nscenery(n.)風景\nscenic spot 風景區、景點\nscenic route 景觀路線\nSun Moon Lake is one of the most popular scenic spots in Taiwan.\n(日月潭是臺灣最受歡迎的風景區之一。)\nWe took the scenic route along the east coast instead of the highway.\n(我們沒走高速公路，而是沿著東海岸走景觀路線。)"],["scorn","scorn(n./v.)輕蔑、鄙視、不屑\nscornful(adj.)輕蔑的\npour scorn on 對……嗤之以鼻\nwith scorn 輕蔑地\nSome people poured scorn on his idea, but it turned out to be a great success.\n(有些人對他的點子嗤之以鼻，但結果卻非常成功。)\nShe scorned the offer because she thought it was unfair.\n(她不屑這個提議，因為她認為它不公平。)"],["scrape","scrape(v./n.)刮、擦傷、刮擦聲、困境\nscraper(n.)刮刀\nscrape off 刮掉\nscrape through 勉強通過\nHe scraped the old paint off the wall before repainting it.\n(他重新油漆前先把牆上的舊漆刮掉。)\nShe fell off her bike and scraped her knee on the road.\n(她從腳踏車上摔下來，膝蓋在路面上擦傷了。)"],["screwdriver","screwdriver(n.)螺絲起子\nscrew(n./v.)螺絲、旋緊\nelectric screwdriver 電動螺絲起子\nuse a screwdriver 用螺絲起子\nYou will need a small screwdriver to open the back of the remote control.\n(你需要一支小的螺絲起子才能打開遙控器的背蓋。)\nHe tightened the loose screws with a screwdriver.\n(他用螺絲起子把鬆掉的螺絲鎖緊。)"],["scroll","scroll(n./v.)卷軸、捲動(螢幕)\n(無詞性變化)\nscroll down 向下捲動\nancient scroll 古代卷軸\nScroll down to the bottom of the page to find the contact information.\n(往下捲動到頁面底部就能找到聯絡資訊。)\nThe museum displays ancient scrolls painted during the Song dynasty.\n(博物館展出宋代繪製的古代卷軸。)"],["scrutiny","scrutiny(n.)仔細檢查、審查\nscrutinize(v.)仔細檢查、審視\nunder scrutiny 受到審查\nclose scrutiny 嚴密檢視\nThe government's new policy is under close scrutiny by the public.\n(政府的新政策正受到大眾的嚴密檢視。)\nEvery detail of the report was subject to careful scrutiny.\n(報告中的每個細節都經過仔細審查。)"],["sculptor","sculptor(n.)雕刻家、雕塑家\nsculpture(n.)雕刻、雕塑品\nsculpt(v.)雕刻、雕塑\nfamous sculptor 知名雕塑家\nwood sculptor 木雕師\nJu Ming is a world-famous Taiwanese sculptor known for his Taichi series.\n(朱銘是世界知名的臺灣雕塑家，以太極系列聞名。)\nThe sculptor spent three years completing the giant stone statue.\n(這位雕刻家花了三年完成那座巨大的石像。)"],["seagull/gull","seagull(n.)海鷗\ngull(n.)海鷗(同 seagull)\na flock of seagulls 一群海鷗\nseagulls circling 海鷗盤旋\nA flock of seagulls followed the fishing boat back to the harbor.\n(一群海鷗跟著漁船回到港口。)\nBe careful, or the gulls might steal the food from your hand.\n(小心點，否則海鷗可能會搶走你手中的食物。)"],["seduce","seduce(v.)引誘、誘惑、勾引\nseduction(n.)誘惑\nseductive(adj.)誘人的\nbe seduced by 被……誘惑\nseduce customers 吸引顧客\nMany young people are seduced by the promise of easy money.\n(許多年輕人被輕鬆賺錢的承諾所誘惑。)\nThe store uses bright lights and music to seduce customers into buying more.\n(這家店利用明亮的燈光和音樂來吸引顧客多買一些。)"],["selective","selective(adj.)有選擇性的、挑剔的\nselect(v.)挑選\nselection(n.)選擇、精選\nselectively(adv.)選擇性地\nselective memory 選擇性記憶\nbe selective about 對……很挑剔\nHe seems to have a selective memory when it comes to his promises.\n(說到他的承諾，他似乎有選擇性記憶。)\nShe is very selective about the friends she spends time with.\n(她對於要和哪些朋友相處非常挑剔。)"],["serene","serene(adj.)寧靜的、安詳的、平靜的\nserenity(n.)寧靜、平靜\nserenely(adv.)安詳地\nserene smile 安詳的微笑\nserene lake 寧靜的湖泊\nThe serene lake reflected the mountains like a mirror.\n(寧靜的湖面像鏡子一樣映照出群山。)\nDespite the chaos around her, she remained calm and serene.\n(儘管周遭一片混亂，她依然冷靜而安詳。)"],["sergeant","sergeant(n.)士官、中士、巡佐\n(無詞性變化)\npolice sergeant 警佐\ndrill sergeant 教育班長\nThe drill sergeant shouted orders at the new soldiers.\n(教育班長對著新兵大聲下達命令。)\nHe was promoted to sergeant after five years of service.\n(服役五年後，他晉升為士官。)"],["serial","serial(adj.)連續的、一系列的、連載的\nseries(n.)系列、連續\nserial number 序號\nserial killer 連續殺人犯\nPlease write down the serial number printed on the back of the device.\n(請寫下印在裝置背面的序號。)\nThe novel was first published as a serial in a weekly magazine.\n(這部小說最初是在週刊上連載的。)"],["sermon","sermon(n.)講道、說教\n(無詞性變化)\ndeliver a sermon 講道\npreach a sermon 布道\nThe priest delivered a moving sermon about forgiveness.\n(神父發表了一場關於寬恕的感人講道。)\nI don't need another sermon about my messy room.\n(我不需要再聽一次有關我房間亂七八糟的說教。)"],["serving","serving(n.)一份(食物)\nserve(v.)供應、服務\nserver(n.)服務生、伺服器\na serving of 一份\nsecond serving 第二份、再來一份\nDoctors recommend eating at least five servings of fruit and vegetables a day.\n(醫生建議每天至少吃五份蔬果。)\nThe cake was so delicious that everyone asked for a second serving.\n(蛋糕太好吃了，每個人都要求再來一份。)"],["setback","setback(n.)挫折、阻礙、倒退\n(無詞性變化)\nsuffer a setback 遭遇挫折\nmajor setback 重大挫折\nThe team suffered a major setback when their best player got injured.\n(最佳球員受傷，讓球隊遭受重大挫折。)\nDon't let one small setback stop you from chasing your dreams.\n(別讓一次小挫折阻止你追逐夢想。)"],["shabby","shabby(adj.)破舊的、衣衫襤褸的、卑劣的\nshabbily(adv.)破舊地、卑鄙地\nshabby clothes 破舊的衣服\nshabby treatment 不公平的待遇\nThe old man wore a shabby coat with holes in the sleeves.\n(那位老人穿著一件袖子有破洞的破舊外套。)\nThe employees complained about the shabby treatment they received from the company.\n(員工們抱怨公司對他們的不公平待遇。)"],["sharpen","sharpen(v.)削尖、磨利、使敏銳、加強\nsharp(adj.)鋒利的、敏銳的\nsharpener(n.)削鉛筆機、磨刀器\nsharpen a pencil 削鉛筆\nsharpen one's skills 精進技能\nPlease sharpen your pencils before the exam begins.\n(考試開始前請先把鉛筆削好。)\nReading English newspapers can help you sharpen your language skills.\n(閱讀英文報紙可以幫助你精進語言能力。)"],["shaver","shaver(n.)電動刮鬍刀\nshave(v./n.)刮鬍子、剃\nelectric shaver 電動刮鬍刀\nrechargeable shaver 充電式刮鬍刀\nMy father bought a new electric shaver for his business trip.\n(我爸爸為了出差買了一支新的電動刮鬍刀。)\nRemember to charge your shaver before you pack it.\n(打包前記得把刮鬍刀充好電。)"],["shortcoming","shortcoming(n.)缺點、短處\n(無詞性變化)\novercome shortcomings 克服缺點\nserious shortcoming 嚴重缺陷\nEveryone has shortcomings, but we can learn to improve them.\n(每個人都有缺點，但我們可以學著改進。)\nThe report pointed out several shortcomings in the new system.\n(報告指出了新系統的幾項缺陷。)"],["shortsighted","shortsighted(adj.)近視的、目光短淺的\nshortsightedness(n.)近視、短視\nshortsighted policy 短視的政策\nshortsighted view 短淺的看法\nCutting the education budget would be a shortsighted decision.\n(刪減教育預算會是一個目光短淺的決定。)\nMany students become shortsighted from staring at screens too long.\n(許多學生因長時間盯著螢幕而近視。)"],["shred","shred(n./v.)碎片、少量、撕碎、切絲\nshredder(n.)碎紙機\nshred documents 用碎紙機銷毀文件\nnot a shred of 一點也沒有\nThe company shreds all confidential documents before throwing them away.\n(這家公司在丟棄機密文件前都會先用碎紙機銷毀。)\nThere is not a shred of evidence to support his claim.\n(沒有絲毫證據能支持他的說法。)"],["shriek","shriek(n./v.)尖叫、尖叫聲\n(無詞性變化)\nshriek with laughter 尖聲大笑\nlet out a shriek 發出一聲尖叫\nThe girls shrieked with excitement when their favorite singer appeared on stage.\n(最喜歡的歌手登臺時，女孩們興奮地尖叫。)\nShe let out a shriek when she saw a cockroach in the kitchen.\n(她在廚房看到一隻蟑螂時發出一聲尖叫。)"],["shrub","shrub(n.)灌木\nshrubbery(n.)灌木叢\nplant shrubs 種灌木\nevergreen shrub 常綠灌木\nThe gardener trimmed the shrubs along the path into neat shapes.\n(園丁把小徑旁的灌木修剪成整齊的形狀。)\nSmall birds often build their nests in thick shrubs.\n(小鳥常在茂密的灌木中築巢。)"],["shuffle","shuffle(v.)洗(牌)、拖著腳走、搬來移去\n(無詞性變化)\nshuffle the cards 洗牌\nshuffle one's feet 拖著腳步走\nHe shuffled the cards carefully before dealing them to the players.\n(他在發牌給玩家前仔細地洗牌。)\nThe tired old man shuffled slowly across the room.\n(那位疲倦的老人拖著腳步慢慢走過房間。)"],["shutter","shutter(n./v.)百葉窗、快門、關閉\n(無詞性變化)\nshutter speed 快門速度\nclose the shutters 關上百葉窗\nPhotographers use a fast shutter speed to capture moving objects.\n(攝影師使用高速快門來捕捉移動中的物體。)\nWe closed the shutters to keep out the strong afternoon sun.\n(我們關上百葉窗，擋住午後強烈的陽光。)"],["simplicity","simplicity(n.)簡單、樸素、單純\nsimple(adj.)簡單的\nsimplify(v.)簡化\nfor the sake of simplicity 為了簡單起見\nbeauty of simplicity 簡約之美\nThe design of the phone is admired for its simplicity and elegance.\n(這款手機的設計以簡約優雅受到讚賞。)\nFor the sake of simplicity, we will round the numbers to whole numbers.\n(為了簡單起見，我們會把數字四捨五入到整數。)"],["simplify","simplify(v.)簡化、使簡單\nsimple(adj.)簡單的\nsimplification(n.)簡化\nsimplify the process 簡化流程\ngreatly simplify 大幅簡化\nThe new app greatly simplifies the process of booking train tickets.\n(這個新應用程式大幅簡化了訂火車票的流程。)\nThe teacher simplified the story so that younger students could understand it.\n(老師簡化了這個故事，讓年紀較小的學生也能理解。)"],["simultaneous","simultaneous(adj.)同時的、同時發生的\nsimultaneously(adv.)同時地\nsimultaneous interpretation 同步口譯\nsimultaneous events 同時發生的事件\nThe conference provided simultaneous interpretation in five languages.\n(這場會議提供五種語言的同步口譯。)\nThere were simultaneous protests in several major cities around the world.\n(世界上好幾個大城市同時發生了抗議活動。)"],["skeptical","skeptical(adj.)懷疑的、多疑的\nskeptic(n.)懷疑論者\nskepticism(n.)懷疑態度\nbe skeptical about/of 對……抱持懷疑\nremain skeptical 仍持懷疑態度\nMany scientists remain skeptical about the claims made in the advertisement.\n(許多科學家仍對廣告中的說法抱持懷疑態度。)\nI was skeptical of his excuse, but I didn't say anything.\n(我對他的藉口半信半疑，但什麼也沒說。)"],["skim","skim(v./n.)略讀、瀏覽、撇去(浮沫)、掠過\n(無詞性變化)\nskim through 快速瀏覽\nskim milk 脫脂牛奶\nSkim through the article first to get the main idea before reading it carefully.\n(先快速瀏覽文章抓住大意，再仔細閱讀。)\nShe skimmed the fat off the top of the soup.\n(她撇去湯上面的浮油。)"],["slang","slang(n./v.)俚語、謾罵\nslangy(adj.)俚語的\nstreet slang 街頭俚語\nslang word 俚語用字\nTeenagers often use slang that their parents do not understand.\n(青少年常用父母聽不懂的俚語。)\nYou should avoid using slang in formal writing.\n(在正式寫作中應避免使用俚語。)"],["slash","slash(v./n.)砍、劃破、大幅削減、斜線\n(無詞性變化)\nslash prices 大幅降價\nslash the budget 大砍預算\nThe store slashed prices by fifty percent during the year-end sale.\n(這家店在年終特賣時降價五成。)\nSomeone slashed the tires of his car last night.\n(昨晚有人劃破了他的車胎。)"],["slaughter","slaughter(n./v.)屠宰、屠殺、大敗\nslaughterhouse(n.)屠宰場\nmass slaughter 大屠殺\nslaughter animals 屠宰動物\nThe farmers slaughter the pigs before the Lunar New Year.\n(農民在農曆新年前宰殺豬隻。)\nThe war led to the slaughter of thousands of innocent people.\n(這場戰爭導致數千名無辜民眾慘遭屠殺。)"],["slay","slay(v.)殺死、殺害\nslayer(n.)殺手\nslay a dragon 屠龍\nbe slain in battle 戰死沙場\nIn the legend, the brave knight slew the dragon and saved the princess.\n(傳說中，勇敢的騎士殺死了惡龍並救出公主。)\nThousands of soldiers were slain in the battle.\n(數千名士兵在這場戰役中陣亡。)"],["sloppy","sloppy(adj.)草率的、邋遢的、稀爛的\nsloppily(adv.)草率地\nsloppy work 草率的工作\nsloppy handwriting 潦草的字跡\nThe teacher refused to accept the sloppy homework and asked him to do it again.\n(老師拒收那份草率的作業，要他重寫。)\nHis sloppy appearance made a bad impression at the interview.\n(他邋遢的外表在面試時給人不好的印象。)"],["slum","slum(n./v.)貧民窟、過簡陋的生活\n(無詞性變化)\nlive in a slum 住在貧民窟\nslum area 貧民區\nMillions of people in large cities still live in crowded slums.\n(大城市中仍有數百萬人住在擁擠的貧民窟裡。)\nThe charity builds schools for children in slum areas.\n(這個慈善團體為貧民區的孩童興建學校。)"],["slump","slump(n./v.)暴跌、低迷、癱坐、垂頭\n(無詞性變化)\neconomic slump 經濟衰退\nslump in sales 銷售量下滑\nThe company suffered a sharp slump in sales after the scandal.\n(醜聞爆發後，這家公司的銷售量大幅下滑。)\nExhausted after the game, he slumped into a chair.\n(比賽後他筋疲力盡地癱坐在椅子上。)"],["sly","sly(adj.)狡猾的、會意的、淘氣的\nslyly(adv.)狡猾地、會心地\nsly smile 狡黠的微笑\non the sly 偷偷地\nIn many fables, the fox is described as a sly animal.\n(在許多寓言裡，狐狸都被描寫成狡猾的動物。)\nShe gave me a sly smile, as if she knew my secret.\n(她對我露出狡黠的微笑，好像知道我的祕密似的。)"],["smuggle","smuggle(v.)走私、偷帶\nsmuggler(n.)走私者\nsmuggling(n.)走私\nsmuggle drugs 走私毒品\nsmuggle into 偷運進\nCustoms officers caught a man trying to smuggle rare birds into the country.\n(海關人員逮到一名試圖走私稀有鳥類入境的男子。)\nThe kids smuggled snacks into the movie theater.\n(孩子們偷偷把零食帶進電影院。)"],["sneaker(s)","sneaker(n.)運動鞋(單隻)、sneakers(n.)運動鞋(一雙)\nsneak(v.)偷偷地走、潛行\na pair of sneakers 一雙運動鞋\nrunning sneakers 跑步鞋\nI bought a new pair of sneakers for the school sports day.\n(我為了學校運動會買了一雙新的運動鞋。)\nWearing comfortable sneakers is important if you walk a lot.\n(如果你常走路，穿一雙舒適的運動鞋很重要。)"],["sneaky","sneaky(adj.)鬼鬼祟祟的、偷偷摸摸的、卑鄙的\nsneak(v.)偷偷地走、潛行\nsneakily(adv.)偷偷地\nsneaky trick 卑鄙的伎倆\nsneaky way 偷偷摸摸的方式\nIt was sneaky of him to read my messages without asking.\n(他沒問就偷看我的訊息，真是鬼鬼祟祟。)\nThe advertisement used a sneaky trick to make the price look lower.\n(這則廣告用了一個卑劣的伎倆，讓價格看起來比較低。)"],["sneeze","sneeze(n./v.)噴嚏、打噴嚏\n(無詞性變化)\ncough and sneeze 咳嗽和打噴嚏\nnot to be sneezed at 不可小看\nPlease cover your mouth when you cough or sneeze.\n(咳嗽或打噴嚏時請遮住口鼻。)\nA prize of ten thousand dollars is not to be sneezed at.\n(一萬元的獎金可不能小看。)"],["snore","snore(v./n.)打鼾、鼾聲\nsnoring(n.)打鼾\nsnore loudly 大聲打鼾\nloud snore 很大的鼾聲\nMy roommate snores so loudly that I can hardly fall asleep.\n(我的室友打鼾太大聲，讓我幾乎睡不著。)\nHis loud snores could be heard from the next room.\n(從隔壁房間都能聽到他很大的鼾聲。)"],["sociable","sociable(adj.)好交際的、友善的\nsociety(n.)社會\nsociability(n.)社交性、合群\nsociable person 好交際的人\nsociable atmosphere 融洽的氣氛\nShe is a sociable person who makes friends easily.\n(她是個好交際的人，很容易交到朋友。)\nDolphins are sociable animals that live in groups.\n(海豚是群居的社會性動物。)"],["socialism","socialism(n.)社會主義\nsocialist(n./adj.)社會主義者、社會主義的\ndemocratic socialism 民主社會主義\nprinciples of socialism 社會主義原則\nSocialism emphasizes the fair distribution of wealth in society.\n(社會主義強調社會財富的公平分配。)\nThe students compared socialism and capitalism in their history class.\n(學生們在歷史課上比較社會主義與資本主義。)"],["socialist","socialist(n.)社會主義者\nsocialism(n.)社會主義\nsocialist party 社會黨\nsocialist country 社會主義國家\nHe described himself as a socialist who believed in equality.\n(他形容自己是相信平等的社會主義者。)\nThe socialist party won several seats in the election.\n(社會黨在選舉中贏得了幾個席次。)"],["socialize","socialize(v.)交際、交往、使社會化\nsocial(adj.)社會的、社交的\nsocialization(n.)社會化\nsocialize with 與……交際\nlearn to socialize 學習與人相處\nJoining a club is a good way to socialize with people who share your interests.\n(加入社團是與志同道合的人交流的好方法。)\nPuppies need to be socialized with other dogs at an early age.\n(小狗需要在年幼時就和其他狗社會化。)"],["sociology","sociology(n.)社會學\nsociologist(n.)社會學家\nsociological(adj.)社會學的\nstudy sociology 研讀社會學\nprofessor of sociology 社會學教授\nShe majored in sociology because she was interested in human behavior.\n(她主修社會學，因為她對人類行為很感興趣。)\nSociology helps us understand how society shapes people's lives.\n(社會學幫助我們了解社會如何形塑人們的生活。)"],["solemn","solemn(adj.)莊嚴的、嚴肅的、鄭重的\nsolemnly(adv.)莊嚴地、鄭重地\nsolemnity(n.)莊嚴、嚴肅\nsolemn ceremony 莊嚴的典禮\nsolemn promise 鄭重的承諾\nThe national anthem was played during the solemn ceremony.\n(在莊嚴的典禮中奏起了國歌。)\nHe made a solemn promise to take care of his younger brother.\n(他鄭重承諾會照顧弟弟。)"],["solidarity","solidarity(n.)團結、一致\nsolid(adj.)堅固的、可靠的\nshow solidarity 表達團結支持\nin solidarity with 聲援、與……團結一致\nPeople around the world showed solidarity with the earthquake victims.\n(世界各地的人都向地震災民表達了支持。)\nThe workers went on strike in solidarity with their colleagues.\n(工人們罷工以聲援他們的同事。)"],["solitary","solitary(adj./n.)單獨的、孤獨的、隱居者\nsolitude(n.)孤獨、獨處\nsolitary life 獨居生活\nsolitary confinement 單獨監禁\nThe old artist lived a solitary life in the mountains.\n(那位老藝術家在山中過著獨居生活。)\nTigers are solitary animals that usually hunt alone.\n(老虎是獨居動物，通常單獨狩獵。)"],["solitude","solitude(n.)孤獨、獨處、幽靜\nsolitary(adj.)單獨的、孤獨的\nin solitude 獨自地\nenjoy solitude 享受獨處\nSome writers prefer to work in solitude without any distractions.\n(有些作家喜歡在不受打擾的情況下獨自工作。)\nAfter a busy week, she enjoyed the solitude of a quiet walk by the sea.\n(忙碌一週後，她享受在海邊獨自散步的寧靜。)"],["soothe","soothe(v.)安撫、緩和、減輕(痛苦)\nsoothing(adj.)撫慰的、使人平靜的\nsoothe a baby 安撫嬰兒\nsoothe the pain 減輕疼痛\nThe mother sang softly to soothe her crying baby.\n(那位母親輕聲唱歌來安撫哭鬧的嬰兒。)\nThis cream can help soothe the pain of sunburn.\n(這款乳霜有助於緩解曬傷的疼痛。)"],["sorrowful","sorrowful(adj.)悲傷的、哀傷的\nsorrow(n.)悲傷\nsorrowfully(adv.)悲傷地\nsorrowful eyes 哀傷的眼神\nsorrowful news 令人悲傷的消息\nThe dog looked at its owner with sorrowful eyes.\n(那隻狗以哀傷的眼神望著主人。)\nThe whole village was shocked by the sorrowful news of the accident.\n(整個村莊都被那起意外的悲傷消息震驚了。)"],["sovereign","sovereign(adj./n.)擁有主權的、至高無上的、君主\nsovereignty(n.)主權\nsovereign state 主權國家\nsovereign power 最高權力\nEvery sovereign state has the right to make its own laws.\n(每個主權國家都有權制定自己的法律。)\nThe sovereign ruled the kingdom for more than forty years.\n(那位君主統治王國超過四十年。)"],["spacecraft/spaceship","spacecraft(n.)太空船、太空飛行器\nspaceship(n.)太空船(同 spacecraft)\nlaunch a spacecraft 發射太空船\nunmanned spacecraft 無人太空船\nThe unmanned spacecraft sent back amazing photos of Mars.\n(這艘無人太空船傳回了令人驚嘆的火星照片。)\nIn the movie, aliens arrived on Earth in a giant spaceship.\n(電影中，外星人乘坐一艘巨大的太空船抵達地球。)"],["span","span(n./v.)期間、跨度、範圍、橫跨、持續\n(無詞性變化)\nattention span 專注時間\nlife span 壽命\nYoung children usually have a short attention span.\n(幼兒的專注時間通常很短。)\nHer career as a singer spanned more than thirty years.\n(她的歌手生涯橫跨了三十多年。)"],["sparrow","sparrow(n.)麻雀\n(無詞性變化)\nhouse sparrow 家麻雀\na flock of sparrows 一群麻雀\nA group of sparrows was looking for food on the playground.\n(一群麻雀在操場上覓食。)\nSparrows are among the most common birds in Taiwanese cities.\n(麻雀是臺灣城市中最常見的鳥類之一。)"],["spectacle","spectacle(n.)壯觀景象、奇觀、場面\nspectacular(adj.)壯觀的\nspectacles(n.)眼鏡\na magnificent spectacle 壯麗的景象\nmake a spectacle of oneself 出洋相\nThe fireworks over Taipei 101 were an amazing spectacle on New Year's Eve.\n(跨年夜臺北101上空的煙火是一場驚人的盛大景象。)\nStop shouting and don't make a spectacle of yourself in public.\n(別再大吼了，不要在公共場合出洋相。)"],["spiral","spiral(adj./n./v.)螺旋形的、螺旋、盤旋上升或下降、急遽變化\n(無詞性變化)\nspiral staircase 螺旋梯\nspiral out of control 失去控制、急遽惡化\nWe climbed the spiral staircase to the top of the lighthouse.\n(我們爬上螺旋梯到燈塔頂端。)\nPrices began to spiral out of control during the economic crisis.\n(經濟危機期間，物價開始失控飆漲。)"],["splendor","splendor(n.)壯麗、輝煌、光彩\nsplendid(adj.)壯麗的、極好的\nnatural splendor 自然的壯麗\nin all its splendor 極其壯麗\nTourists come from around the world to see the splendor of Taroko Gorge.\n(遊客從世界各地前來欣賞太魯閣峽谷的壯麗景色。)\nThe palace has been restored to its former splendor.\n(這座宮殿已恢復昔日的輝煌。)"],["spokesperson/spokesman/spokeswoman","spokesperson(n.)發言人\nspokesman(n.)男發言人\nspokeswoman(n.)女發言人\ngovernment spokesperson 政府發言人\nofficial spokesman 官方發言人\nA spokesperson for the company said the problem would be fixed soon.\n(公司的發言人表示問題將很快獲得解決。)\nThe spokeswoman refused to answer any questions about the scandal.\n(那位女發言人拒絕回答任何有關醜聞的問題。)"],["spontaneous","spontaneous(adj.)自發的、自然的、即興的\nspontaneously(adv.)自發地\nspontaneity(n.)自發性\nspontaneous applause 自發的掌聲\nspontaneous decision 一時興起的決定\nThe audience broke into spontaneous applause when the singer appeared.\n(歌手一出現，觀眾便自發地鼓起掌來。)\nOur trip to Kenting was a spontaneous decision made on Friday night.\n(我們的墾丁之旅是星期五晚上一時興起決定的。)"],["sportsman/sportswoman","sportsman(n.)運動員、運動家\nsportswoman(n.)女運動員\nsportsmanship(n.)運動家精神\nprofessional sportsman 職業運動員\ntrue sportsman 真正的運動家\nHe is a true sportsman who always respects his opponents.\n(他是個總是尊重對手的真正運動家。)\nShe was named the best sportswoman of the year.\n(她被選為年度最佳女運動員。)"],["sportsmanship","sportsmanship(n.)運動家精神、運動員精神\nsportsman(n.)運動員\ngood sportsmanship 良好的運動家精神\nshow sportsmanship 展現運動家精神\nThe team showed good sportsmanship by shaking hands with the winners.\n(這支隊伍與獲勝者握手，展現了良好的運動家精神。)\nCoaches should teach young players the importance of sportsmanship.\n(教練應教導年輕選手運動家精神的重要性。)"],["spotlight","spotlight(n./v.)聚光燈、眾所矚目、使突出\n(無詞性變化)\nin the spotlight 受到矚目\nsteal the spotlight 搶盡風頭\nThe young actress has been in the spotlight since her first movie.\n(這位年輕女演員從第一部電影開始就備受矚目。)\nThe documentary spotlights the problem of plastic pollution in the ocean.\n(這部紀錄片突顯了海洋塑膠汙染的問題。)"],["spur","spur(v./n.)激勵、刺激、促進、馬刺、激勵因素\n(無詞性變化)\non the spur of the moment 一時衝動、心血來潮\nspur on 激勵\nOn the spur of the moment, we decided to go to the beach.\n(一時興起，我們決定去海邊。)\nThe fans' cheers spurred the players on to victory.\n(球迷的歡呼激勵球員們奪得勝利。)"],["stabilize","stabilize(v.)使穩定、穩定\nstable(adj.)穩定的\nstability(n.)穩定性\nstabilize prices 穩定物價\nstabilize the economy 穩定經濟\nThe government took measures to stabilize prices after the typhoon.\n(颱風過後，政府採取措施穩定物價。)\nThe patient's condition has stabilized after the operation.\n(手術後病人的情況已趨於穩定。)"],["stagger","stagger(v./n.)搖晃、蹣跚、使震驚、錯開\nstaggering(adj.)驚人的\nstagger to one's feet 搖搖晃晃地站起來\nstagger working hours 錯開上班時間\nThe injured man staggered to his feet and asked for help.\n(那名受傷男子搖搖晃晃地站起來求救。)\nThe company decided to stagger working hours to reduce crowding.\n(公司決定錯開上班時間以減少擁擠。)"],["staple","staple(n./v.)主食、主要產品、釘書針、用釘書機釘\nstapler(n.)釘書機\nstaple food 主食\nstaple together 用釘書針釘在一起\nRice is the staple food in many Asian countries.\n(米飯是許多亞洲國家的主食。)\nPlease staple the pages together before you hand in your report.\n(繳交報告前，請先用釘書機把頁面釘在一起。)"],["starvation","starvation(n.)飢餓、餓死\nstarve(v.)挨餓、餓死\ndie of starvation 餓死\nstarvation diet 極端節食\nThousands of people died of starvation during the famine.\n(饑荒期間有數千人餓死。)\nDoctors warn that a starvation diet can be harmful to your health.\n(醫生警告極端節食可能對健康有害。)"],["statesman","statesman(n.)政治家\nstatesmanship(n.)政治家的才能\ngreat statesman 偉大的政治家\nelder statesman 政界元老\nAbraham Lincoln is remembered as one of the greatest statesmen in history.\n(林肯被譽為史上最偉大的政治家之一。)\nA true statesman cares about the future of the nation, not just the next election.\n(真正的政治家關心國家的未來，而不只是下一場選舉。)"],["stationary","stationary(adj.)靜止的、固定的、不動的\n(無詞性變化)\nstationary vehicle 靜止的車輛\nstationary bike 室內健身腳踏車\nThe car crashed into a stationary truck parked on the roadside.\n(那輛汽車撞上一輛停在路邊的靜止卡車。)\nI ride a stationary bike at the gym three times a week.\n(我每週在健身房騎三次室內腳踏車。)"],["stationery","stationery(n.)文具、信紙\n(無詞性變化)\nstationery store 文具店\nschool stationery 學校文具\nI need to buy some stationery before the new semester starts.\n(新學期開始前我需要買一些文具。)\nShe wrote the thank-you letter on beautiful stationery.\n(她在精美的信紙上寫了感謝信。)"],["stature","stature(n.)身高、身材、聲望、地位\n(無詞性變化)\nsmall in stature 個子矮小\ngain stature 提高聲望\nAlthough small in stature, he was a powerful basketball player.\n(雖然個子矮小，他卻是個實力強大的籃球員。)\nThe scientist's stature grew after she won the international award.\n(這位科學家贏得國際大獎後，聲望隨之提高。)"],["statute","statute(n.)法令、法規、成文法\nstatutory(adj.)法定的\nunder the statute 依照法規\nstatute of limitations 追訴時效\nThe new statute protects the rights of workers who work overtime.\n(這項新法規保障加班勞工的權益。)\nThe case could not be brought to court because of the statute of limitations.\n(由於已過追訴時效，此案無法提起訴訟。)"],["stepchild","stepchild(n.)繼子、繼女\nstepson(n.)繼子\nstepdaughter(n.)繼女\nraise a stepchild 撫養繼子女\nstepchildren and parents 繼子女與父母\nHe treats his stepchild as if she were his own daughter.\n(他對待繼女就像自己的親生女兒一樣。)\nBuilding trust with a stepchild can take a lot of time and patience.\n(與繼子女建立信任可能需要許多時間和耐心。)"],["stepfather","stepfather(n.)繼父\n(無詞性變化)\ncaring stepfather 體貼的繼父\nbecome a stepfather 成為繼父\nHer stepfather taught her how to ride a bike when she was six.\n(她六歲時，繼父教她騎腳踏車。)\nHe has a good relationship with his stepfather.\n(他和繼父的關係很好。)"],["stepmother","stepmother(n.)繼母\n(無詞性變化)\nwicked stepmother 惡毒的繼母\nloving stepmother 慈愛的繼母\nIn the story of Cinderella, the wicked stepmother treated her badly.\n(在灰姑娘的故事裡，惡毒的繼母對她很壞。)\nUnlike in fairy tales, my stepmother is kind and supportive.\n(不像童話故事裡那樣，我的繼母既和善又支持我。)"],["stimulation","stimulation(n.)刺激、激勵\nstimulate(v.)刺激、激勵\nstimulus(n.)刺激物、促進因素\nmental stimulation 智力刺激\neconomic stimulation 經濟刺激\nPuzzles and reading provide mental stimulation for the elderly.\n(拼圖和閱讀能為長者提供腦力刺激。)\nBabies need plenty of stimulation to help their brains develop.\n(嬰兒需要大量刺激來幫助大腦發展。)"],["strait","strait(n.)海峽、困境(常用複數)\n(無詞性變化)\nTaiwan Strait 臺灣海峽\nin dire straits 陷入困境\nThe Taiwan Strait separates Taiwan from mainland China.\n(臺灣海峽將臺灣與中國大陸分隔開來。)\nAfter losing his job, the family was in dire straits.\n(他失業後，全家陷入了困境。)"],["strangle","strangle(v.)勒死、扼殺、抑制\nstrangulation(n.)勒死、窒息\nstrangle growth 抑制成長\nstrangle to death 勒死\nToo many rules may strangle creativity in the classroom.\n(過多的規定可能扼殺課堂上的創造力。)\nThe vine slowly strangled the tree it was growing on.\n(藤蔓慢慢地把它所攀附的樹木纏死。)"],["stray","stray(adj./v./n.)迷路的、走失的、偏離、流浪動物\n(無詞性變化)\nstray dog 流浪狗\nstray from the topic 離題\nThe volunteers rescue stray dogs and find new homes for them.\n(志工們救援流浪狗，並為牠們尋找新家。)\nPlease don't stray from the topic during the discussion.\n(討論時請不要離題。)"],["stride","stride(n./v.)大步、闊步走、進展\n(無詞性變化)\nmake great strides 有長足的進步\ntake... in stride 從容應付\nMedical science has made great strides in the past fifty years.\n(過去五十年來，醫學有了長足的進步。)\nShe strode confidently onto the stage to give her speech.\n(她自信地大步走上舞臺發表演說。)"],["stroll","stroll(n./v.)散步、閒逛、漫步\nstroller(n.)嬰兒推車、散步者\ntake a stroll 散步\nstroll along 沿著……漫步\nAfter dinner, we took a stroll along the riverside park.\n(晚餐後，我們沿著河濱公園散步。)\nTourists strolled through the old street, tasting local snacks.\n(遊客們漫步在老街上，品嚐當地小吃。)"],["stun","stun(v.)使震驚、使昏迷、使目瞪口呆\nstunning(adj.)令人驚豔的、極美的\nstunned(adj.)震驚的\nstun gun 電擊槍\nbe stunned by 被……震驚\nEveryone was stunned by the news that the famous singer had retired.\n(那位知名歌手退休的消息讓每個人都震驚不已。)\nThe view from the top of the mountain was absolutely stunning.\n(從山頂望出去的景色美得令人驚嘆。)"],["stutter","stutter(n./v.)口吃、結巴\n(無詞性變化)\nspeak with a stutter 說話結巴\nstutter nervously 緊張地結巴\nHe tends to stutter when he is nervous in front of a crowd.\n(他在人群前緊張時容易結巴。)\nDespite his stutter, he became an excellent public speaker.\n(儘管有口吃，他仍成為一位出色的演說家。)"],["stylish","stylish(adj.)時髦的、有風格的\nstyle(n./v.)風格、設計\nstylishly(adv.)時髦地\nstylish clothes 時髦的衣服\nstylish design 時尚的設計\nShe always wears stylish clothes that suit her personality.\n(她總是穿著符合自己個性的時髦衣服。)\nThe new café has a stylish design that attracts many young people.\n(這家新咖啡廳有著時尚的設計，吸引了許多年輕人。)"],["subjective","subjective(adj./n.)主觀的、主格\nsubject(n.)主題、科目、主詞\nsubjectivity(n.)主觀性\nsubjective opinion 主觀意見\nhighly subjective 非常主觀的\nJudging art is highly subjective because everyone has different tastes.\n(評斷藝術非常主觀，因為每個人品味不同。)\nTry not to let your subjective feelings affect your decision.\n(盡量不要讓主觀感受影響你的決定。)"],["subordinate","subordinate(adj./n./v.)次要的、下級的、部屬、使從屬\nsubordination(n.)從屬、下級\nsubordinate to 從屬於、次於\nsubordinate clause 從屬子句\nA good manager listens to the opinions of his subordinates.\n(好的經理會傾聽部屬的意見。)\nIn his view, personal interests should be subordinate to the needs of the team.\n(在他看來，個人利益應次於團隊的需要。)"],["subscribe","subscribe(v.)訂閱、訂購、同意\nsubscription(n.)訂閱、訂購\nsubscriber(n.)訂閱者\nsubscribe to a channel 訂閱頻道\nsubscribe to a view 贊同某觀點\nDon't forget to subscribe to our channel for more videos.\n(別忘了訂閱我們的頻道以觀看更多影片。)\nI don't subscribe to the idea that money can buy happiness.\n(我不認同金錢能買到幸福的想法。)"],["subscription","subscription(n.)訂閱、訂閱費、會費\nsubscribe(v.)訂閱\nsubscriber(n.)訂閱者\nannual subscription 年度訂閱\ncancel a subscription 取消訂閱\nMy family pays for an annual subscription to a music streaming service.\n(我家付費訂閱了一年的音樂串流服務。)\nShe canceled her magazine subscription because she no longer had time to read it.\n(她取消了雜誌訂閱，因為她已經沒時間看了。)"],["subsidize","subsidize(v.)補助、資助、津貼\nsubsidy(n.)補助金、津貼\nsubsidize education 補助教育\ngovernment-subsidized 政府補助的\nThe government subsidizes public transportation to keep ticket prices low.\n(政府補助大眾運輸，讓票價維持在低價。)\nMany farmers rely on government-subsidized loans.\n(許多農民仰賴政府補助的貸款。)"],["succession","succession(n.)連續、接連、繼承\nsucceed(v.)成功、繼承\nsuccessor(n.)繼承者、接班人\nin succession 連續地\na succession of 一連串的\nThe team won three championships in succession.\n(這支隊伍連續贏得三次冠軍。)\nA succession of typhoons hit the island last summer.\n(去年夏天一連串的颱風侵襲了這座島嶼。)"],["successive","successive(adj.)連續的、接連的\nsuccession(n.)連續、繼承\nsuccessively(adv.)連續地\nsuccessive years 連續幾年\nsuccessive governments 歷屆政府\nThe company has made a profit for five successive years.\n(這家公司已連續五年獲利。)\nSuccessive governments have failed to solve the housing problem.\n(歷屆政府都未能解決住房問題。)"],["suffocate","suffocate(v.)窒息、使窒息、壓制\nsuffocation(n.)窒息\nsuffocating(adj.)令人窒息的\nsuffocate to death 窒息而死\nsuffocating heat 令人窒息的高溫\nPlastic bags should be kept away from small children so they do not suffocate.\n(塑膠袋應遠離幼童，以免他們窒息。)\nThe crowded train was hot and suffocating during rush hour.\n(尖峰時段擁擠的火車又熱又令人窒息。)"],["suitcase","suitcase(n.)手提箱、行李箱\n(無詞性變化)\npack a suitcase 打包行李箱\ncarry-on suitcase 登機箱\nI packed my suitcase the night before the trip.\n(我在旅行前一晚打包了行李箱。)\nHer suitcase was too heavy, so she had to pay an extra fee at the airport.\n(她的行李箱太重，所以必須在機場支付額外費用。)"],["summon","summon(v.)召喚、傳喚、鼓起(勇氣)\nsummons(n.)傳票、召喚\nsummon up courage 鼓起勇氣\nbe summoned to court 被傳喚出庭\nHe finally summoned up the courage to ask her out.\n(他終於鼓起勇氣約她出去。)\nThe student was summoned to the principal's office.\n(那名學生被叫到校長室。)"],["superficial","superficial(adj.)表面的、膚淺的、淺薄的\nsuperficially(adv.)表面上\nsuperficial wound 皮肉傷\nsuperficial knowledge 膚淺的知識\nLuckily, the cut on his arm was only superficial.\n(幸好他手臂上的傷口只是皮肉傷。)\nDon't judge people by superficial things like their clothes.\n(不要以衣著這種表面的東西來評斷他人。)"],["superintendent","superintendent(n.)主管、監督人、督學\nsuperintend(v.)監督、主管\npolice superintendent 警察局長\nschool superintendent 教育局長、督學\nThe building superintendent fixed the broken elevator.\n(大樓管理員修好了故障的電梯。)\nThe school superintendent visited several schools to check their facilities.\n(督學走訪了幾所學校以檢查設施。)"],["superiority","superiority(n.)優越、優勢\nsuperior(adj./n.)較好的、上級\nsense of superiority 優越感\nsuperiority over 勝過……的優勢\nHis sense of superiority made him unpopular with his classmates.\n(他的優越感讓他不受同學歡迎。)\nThe team showed clear superiority over its opponents in the final.\n(這支隊伍在決賽中展現了明顯勝過對手的實力。)"],["superstitious","superstitious(adj.)迷信的\nsuperstition(n.)迷信\nsuperstitious belief 迷信觀念\nbe superstitious about 對……迷信\nSome people are superstitious about the number four.\n(有些人對數字四很迷信。)\nMy grandmother is superstitious and never sweeps the floor on New Year's Day.\n(我奶奶很迷信，從不在大年初一掃地。)"],["supplement","supplement(n./v.)補充、補充品、增刊、增補\nsupplementary(adj.)補充的、額外的\ndietary supplement 營養補充品\nsupplement one's income 增加收入\nMany people take vitamin supplements to stay healthy.\n(許多人服用維他命補充品以保持健康。)\nHe works part-time on weekends to supplement his income.\n(他週末兼差以增加收入。)"],["suppress","suppress(v./n.)鎮壓、抑制、隱瞞\nsuppression(n.)鎮壓、抑制\nsuppress a smile 忍住笑\nsuppress the truth 隱瞞真相\nShe tried hard to suppress a smile when he made a silly mistake.\n(他犯了愚蠢的錯時，她努力忍住不笑。)\nThe army was sent to suppress the protest.\n(軍隊被派去鎮壓抗議活動。)"],["surge","surge(n./v.)激增、洶湧、湧現\n(無詞性變化)\na surge in 激增\nsurge forward 向前湧去\nThere has been a surge in demand for electric cars recently.\n(最近電動車的需求激增。)\nThe crowd surged forward when the gates opened.\n(大門一打開，人群便向前湧去。)"],["surgical","surgical(adj.)外科的、手術的\nsurgery(n.)手術、外科\nsurgeon(n.)外科醫生\nsurgical mask 醫療口罩\nsurgical operation 外科手術\nPeople wore surgical masks to protect themselves during the flu season.\n(流感季節期間人們戴醫療口罩保護自己。)\nThe surgical team worked for ten hours to save the patient's life.\n(手術團隊花了十個小時搶救病人的性命。)"],["surname","surname(n.)姓氏\n(無詞性變化)\ncommon surname 常見姓氏\nfamily surname 家族姓氏\nChen and Lin are the two most common surnames in Taiwan.\n(陳和林是臺灣最常見的兩個姓氏。)\nPlease write your surname in capital letters on the form.\n(請在表格上以大寫字母填寫您的姓氏。)"],["surpass","surpass(v.)超越、勝過\nunsurpassed(adj.)無人能及的\nsurpass expectations 超出預期\nsurpass oneself 超越自我\nThe success of the movie surpassed everyone's expectations.\n(這部電影的成功超出了所有人的預期。)\nShe hopes to surpass her personal best in the next race.\n(她希望在下一場比賽中超越自己的最佳成績。)"],["suspense","suspense(n.)懸疑、焦慮、懸而未決\nsuspenseful(adj.)懸疑的、緊張刺激的\nkeep... in suspense 讓……懸著一顆心\nsuspense novel 懸疑小說\nPlease don't keep us in suspense; tell us who won!\n(別讓我們乾著急了，快告訴我們誰贏了！)\nThe movie is full of suspense until the very last scene.\n(這部電影直到最後一幕都充滿懸疑。)"],["suspension","suspension(n.)暫停、停職、停學、懸掛\nsuspend(v.)暫停、懸掛、停職\nsuspension bridge 吊橋\nsuspension from school 停學處分\nThe student received a three-day suspension for fighting.\n(那名學生因打架被處以停學三天。)\nThe Golden Gate Bridge is a famous suspension bridge in San Francisco.\n(金門大橋是舊金山一座著名的吊橋。)"],["swamp","swamp(n./v.)沼澤、淹沒、使應接不暇\nswampy(adj.)沼澤的、濕軟的\nbe swamped with 忙得不可開交、被……淹沒\nmangrove swamp 紅樹林沼澤\nAlligators and many kinds of birds live in the swamp.\n(短吻鱷和許多種鳥類住在沼澤裡。)\nI'm swamped with homework this week and can't go out.\n(我這週作業多到應接不暇，沒辦法出去。)"],["swarm","swarm(n./v.)一大群、蜂群、成群移動、擠滿\n(無詞性變化)\na swarm of bees 一群蜜蜂\nbe swarming with 擠滿\nA swarm of bees attacked the hikers in the forest.\n(一群蜜蜂在森林裡攻擊了登山客。)\nThe night market was swarming with tourists on Saturday night.\n(星期六晚上的夜市擠滿了觀光客。)"],["symbolize","symbolize(v.)象徵、代表\nsymbol(n.)象徵、符號\nsymbolic(adj.)象徵性的\nsymbolize peace 象徵和平\nsymbolize hope 象徵希望\nThe white dove symbolizes peace in many cultures.\n(在許多文化中，白鴿象徵和平。)\nIn Chinese culture, the color red symbolizes good luck and happiness.\n(在中華文化中，紅色象徵好運與喜慶。)"],["symmetry","symmetry(n.)對稱、均衡\nsymmetrical(adj.)對稱的\nperfect symmetry 完美的對稱\nlack of symmetry 不對稱\nThe Taj Mahal is famous for its perfect symmetry.\n(泰姬瑪哈陵以其完美的對稱而聞名。)\nMany people find faces with symmetry more attractive.\n(許多人覺得對稱的臉孔更有吸引力。)"],["sympathize","sympathize(v.)同情、贊同、支持\nsympathy(n.)同情、贊同\nsympathetic(adj.)同情的\nsympathize with 同情、體諒\ndeeply sympathize 深表同情\nI sympathize with you, but there is nothing I can do to help.\n(我很同情你，但我也幫不上忙。)\nMany people sympathized with the workers' demands for better pay.\n(許多人支持工人要求加薪的訴求。)"],["symphony","symphony(n.)交響曲、交響樂團\nsymphonic(adj.)交響樂的\nsymphony orchestra 交響樂團\nBeethoven's Ninth Symphony 貝多芬第九號交響曲\nWe went to the National Concert Hall to hear the symphony orchestra.\n(我們去國家音樂廳聆聽交響樂團演奏。)\nBeethoven's Ninth Symphony is often performed at the end of the year.\n(貝多芬第九號交響曲常在年底演出。)"],["synonym","synonym(n.)同義字、同義詞\nsynonymous(adj.)同義的、密切相關的\nantonym(n.)反義字\nbe synonymous with 與……同義、代名詞\nfind a synonym 找同義字\n'Happy' and 'glad' are synonyms.\n('happy' 和 'glad' 是同義字。)\nFor many people, the brand name is synonymous with quality.\n(對許多人來說，這個品牌就是品質的代名詞。)"],["synthetic","synthetic(adj./n.)合成的、人造的、合成物\nsynthesize(v.)合成、綜合\nsynthesis(n.)合成、綜合\nsynthetic fiber 合成纖維\nsynthetic material 合成材料\nMany sports clothes are made of synthetic fibers that dry quickly.\n(許多運動服是由快乾的合成纖維製成。)\nNatural rubber has largely been replaced by synthetic materials.\n(天然橡膠大多已被合成材料取代。)"],["syrup","syrup(n.)糖漿、果汁\nsyrupy(adj.)糖漿般的、甜膩的\nmaple syrup 楓糖漿\ncough syrup 止咳糖漿\nI like to pour maple syrup over my pancakes.\n(我喜歡在鬆餅上淋楓糖漿。)\nThe doctor gave the child some cough syrup.\n(醫生給了那個孩子一些止咳糖漿。)"],["tan","tan(n./adj./v.)曬黑的膚色、棕褐色的、曬黑\ntanned(adj.)曬黑的\nget a tan 曬黑\nsuntan lotion 防曬乳\nShe came back from Kenting with a deep tan.\n(她從墾丁回來時曬得一身黝黑。)\nHe wore a tan jacket and dark blue jeans to the party.\n(他穿著棕褐色夾克和深藍色牛仔褲去參加派對。)"],["tedious","tedious(adj.)冗長乏味的、單調的\ntedium(n.)單調乏味\ntediously(adv.)乏味地\ntedious task 乏味的工作\ntedious lecture 冗長無趣的演講\nCopying the same words a hundred times is a tedious task.\n(把同樣的字抄寫一百遍是件乏味的工作。)\nThe lecture was so tedious that several students fell asleep.\n(那堂課冗長乏味到好幾個學生都睡著了。)"],["telecommunications","telecommunications(n.)電信、遠距通訊\ntelecommunication(n.)電信\ntelecommunications industry 電信業\ntelecommunications company 電信公司\nThe telecommunications industry has changed rapidly since smartphones appeared.\n(自從智慧型手機問世後，電信業變化迅速。)\nMy uncle works as an engineer for a telecommunications company.\n(我叔叔在一家電信公司擔任工程師。)"],["teller","teller(n.)銀行出納員、講述者\ntell(v.)講述、告訴\nbank teller 銀行行員\nfortune teller 算命師\nThe bank teller counted the money carefully before handing it to me.\n(銀行行員在把錢交給我之前仔細清點了一遍。)\nA fortune teller at the night market told me that I would be lucky this year.\n(夜市裡的一位算命師告訴我，我今年會很幸運。)"],["tempo","tempo(n.)節奏、速度、拍子\n(無詞性變化)\nfast tempo 快節奏\ntempo of life 生活步調\nThe song starts slowly, but the tempo increases toward the end.\n(這首歌開頭很慢，但節奏在接近尾聲時加快。)\nMany people move to the countryside to escape the fast tempo of city life.\n(許多人搬到鄉下，以逃離城市生活的快速步調。)"],["tenant","tenant(n./v.)房客、承租人、租用\ntenancy(n.)租賃、租期\nlandlord and tenant 房東與房客\ntenant farmer 佃農\nThe landlord asked the tenants to pay the rent by the fifth of each month.\n(房東要求房客每月五號前繳交房租。)\nThe new tenants moved into the apartment upstairs last week.\n(新房客上週搬進了樓上的公寓。)"],["tentative","tentative(adj.)暫時的、試探性的、猶豫不決的\ntentatively(adv.)暫時地、試探性地\ntentative plan 暫定計畫\ntentative step 試探性的一步\nWe have made a tentative plan to visit Japan next summer.\n(我們暫定明年夏天去日本。)\nThe baby took a few tentative steps toward her mother.\n(寶寶猶豫地朝媽媽走了幾步。)"],["terrace","terrace(n./v.)露臺、梯田、使成梯田\nterraced(adj.)梯田式的、階梯狀的\nrice terraces 梯田\noutdoor terrace 戶外露臺\nWe had breakfast on the terrace overlooking the sea.\n(我們在俯瞰大海的露臺上吃早餐。)\nThe rice terraces in the mountains look beautiful in spring.\n(山上的梯田在春天看起來很美。)"],["textile","textile(n./adj.)紡織品、紡織的\ntexture(n.)質地、紋理\ntextile industry 紡織業\ntextile factory 紡織廠\nTaiwan's textile industry is famous for producing high-tech sportswear fabrics.\n(臺灣的紡織業以生產高科技運動服布料聞名。)\nThe old textile factory has been turned into an art center.\n(那座老紡織廠已改建為藝術中心。)"],["thereafter","thereafter(adv.)此後、之後\n(無詞性變化)\nshortly thereafter 不久之後\nand thereafter 此後\nHe moved to Tainan in 2010 and lived there for ten years thereafter.\n(他於2010年搬到臺南，此後在那裡住了十年。)\nThe rain started at noon, and the game was canceled shortly thereafter.\n(中午開始下雨，不久之後比賽就取消了。)"],["thermometer","thermometer(n.)溫度計、體溫計\n(無詞性變化)\ndigital thermometer 電子體溫計\nthermometer reading 溫度計讀數\nThe nurse used a digital thermometer to take my temperature.\n(護理師用電子體溫計幫我量體溫。)\nThe thermometer showed that it was thirty-eight degrees outside.\n(溫度計顯示外面氣溫是三十八度。)"],["tilt","tilt(n./v.)傾斜、偏向、使傾斜\n(無詞性變化)\ntilt one's head 歪著頭\nat full tilt 全速地\nThe puppy tilted its head when it heard a strange sound.\n(小狗聽到奇怪的聲音時歪了歪頭。)\nThe picture on the wall is tilted slightly to the left.\n(牆上的畫稍微向左傾斜。)"],["tiptoe","tiptoe(n./v.)腳尖、踮著腳走\n(無詞性變化)\non tiptoe 踮著腳尖\ntiptoe out of 躡手躡腳地走出\nShe stood on tiptoe to reach the book on the top shelf.\n(她踮起腳尖去拿書架最上層的書。)\nHe tiptoed out of the room so as not to wake the baby.\n(他躡手躡腳地走出房間，以免吵醒寶寶。)"],["tiresome","tiresome(adj.)令人厭煩的、無聊的\ntire(v.)使疲倦、厭倦\ntiresome job 令人厭煩的工作\ntiresome person 討人厭的人\nListening to his endless complaints is really tiresome.\n(聽他沒完沒了地抱怨真的很煩人。)\nFilling out all these forms is a tiresome but necessary job.\n(填寫這些表格是件令人厭煩但必要的工作。)"],["token","token(n.)代幣、象徵、標誌、紀念品\n(無詞性變化)\nas a token of 作為……的象徵\nby the same token 同樣地\nPlease accept this small gift as a token of our appreciation.\n(請收下這份小禮物，聊表我們的謝意。)\nIn the past, you needed a token to ride the subway in some cities.\n(過去在某些城市，搭地鐵需要使用代幣。)"],["tornado","tornado(n.)龍捲風\n(無詞性變化)\ntornado warning 龍捲風警報\nbe hit by a tornado 遭龍捲風侵襲\nThe town was badly damaged after being hit by a powerful tornado.\n(這個小鎮遭強烈龍捲風侵襲後嚴重受損。)\nWhen the tornado warning sounded, everyone hid in the basement.\n(龍捲風警報響起時，大家都躲進了地下室。)"],["torrent","torrent(n.)急流、洪流、(言語等)連發\ntorrential(adj.)猛烈的、傾盆的\ntorrential rain 傾盆大雨\na torrent of 一連串的\nTorrential rain caused serious flooding in southern Taiwan.\n(傾盆大雨在南臺灣造成嚴重水災。)\nThe singer received a torrent of criticism after the concert was canceled.\n(演唱會取消後，那位歌手遭到一連串批評。)"],["trademark","trademark(n.)商標、特徵、標誌\n(無詞性變化)\nregistered trademark 註冊商標\ntrademark smile 招牌笑容\nThe company sued the factory for using its trademark without permission.\n(那家公司控告該工廠未經許可使用其商標。)\nWearing a black turtleneck became Steve Jobs's trademark.\n(穿黑色高領衫成了賈伯斯的招牌特色。)"],["transcript","transcript(n.)成績單、文字紀錄、謄本\ntranscribe(v.)謄寫、轉錄\nofficial transcript 正式成績單\ninterview transcript 訪談逐字稿\nYou need to submit your high school transcript when applying to universities.\n(申請大學時你需要繳交高中成績單。)\nThe reporter read the transcript of the president's speech carefully.\n(記者仔細閱讀了總統演講的文字稿。)"],["transmit","transmit(v.)傳送、傳播、傳染\ntransmission(n.)傳送、傳播、變速器\ntransmitter(n.)發射器\ntransmit signals 傳送訊號\ntransmit diseases 傳播疾病\nMosquitoes can transmit diseases such as dengue fever.\n(蚊子會傳播登革熱等疾病。)\nThe satellite transmits signals back to the Earth every few minutes.\n(衛星每隔幾分鐘就將訊號傳回地球。)"],["transplant","transplant(n./v.)移植、移居\ntransplantation(n.)移植\norgan transplant 器官移植\nheart transplant 心臟移植\nThe patient needed a heart transplant to survive.\n(這位病患需要心臟移植才能存活。)\nThe young trees were transplanted to a larger garden.\n(那些小樹被移植到一座更大的花園。)"],["treasury","treasury(n.)國庫、財政部、寶庫\ntreasure(n./v.)寶藏、愛惜\nnational treasury 國庫\na treasury of 寶庫\nThe money for the new highway will come from the national treasury.\n(新公路的經費將來自國庫。)\nThe museum is a treasury of ancient Chinese art.\n(這座博物館是中國古代藝術的寶庫。)"],["trek","trek(n./v.)長途跋涉、艱苦的旅行\ntrekking(n.)健行、徒步旅行\nmountain trek 山區健行\ntrek across 徒步穿越\nThe hikers went on a three-day trek through the mountains.\n(登山客進行了為期三天的山區健行。)\nWe had to trek across the desert to reach the ancient city.\n(我們必須徒步穿越沙漠才能抵達那座古城。)"],["trifle","trifle(n./v.)瑣事、少量、輕視、玩弄\ntrifling(adj.)微不足道的\na trifle 有點、稍微\ntrifle with 玩弄、輕視\nDon't get angry over such a trifle.\n(別為了這種小事生氣。)\nHe is not a man to be trifled with.\n(他可不是個能被輕視的人。)"],["trillion","trillion(n.)兆\n(無詞性變化)\na trillion dollars 一兆元\ntrillions of 數兆的\nThe government's budget this year is more than two trillion dollars.\n(政府今年的預算超過兩兆元。)\nThere are trillions of cells in the human body.\n(人體內有數兆個細胞。)"],["tropic","tropic(n./adj.)回歸線、熱帶地區、熱帶的\ntropical(adj.)熱帶的\nTropic of Cancer 北回歸線\nthe tropics 熱帶地區\nThe Tropic of Cancer passes through Chiayi in southern Taiwan.\n(北回歸線通過臺灣南部的嘉義。)\nMany colorful birds live in the tropics.\n(許多色彩繽紛的鳥類生活在熱帶地區。)"],["trout","trout(n.)鱒魚\n(無詞性變化)\nrainbow trout 虹鱒\ntrout fishing 釣鱒魚\nMy father caught a big rainbow trout in the mountain stream.\n(我爸爸在山溪裡釣到一條大虹鱒。)\nThe restaurant serves grilled trout with lemon and herbs.\n(這家餐廳供應搭配檸檬與香草的烤鱒魚。)"],["trustee","trustee(n.)受託人、理事\ntrust(n./v.)信任、信託\nboard of trustees 董事會、理事會\nappoint a trustee 指定受託人\nThe board of trustees decided to build a new library for the university.\n(董事會決定為大學興建一座新圖書館。)\nHis uncle was appointed as a trustee to manage the family's money.\n(他叔叔被指定為受託人，負責管理家族的財產。)"],["tuck","tuck(v./n.)塞進、捲起、收攏、褶\n(無詞性變化)\ntuck in 把(衣服)塞好、給(小孩)蓋好被子\ntuck away 藏起、收起\nPlease tuck in your shirt before the school ceremony.\n(學校典禮前請把襯衫紮好。)\nShe tucked her children into bed and read them a story.\n(她幫孩子們蓋好被子，並唸了一個故事給他們聽。)"],["turmoil","turmoil(n.)騷動、混亂、動盪\n(無詞性變化)\nin turmoil 處於混亂中\npolitical turmoil 政治動盪\nThe country was in turmoil after the sudden death of its leader.\n(該國領導人猝逝後，全國陷入一片混亂。)\nHer mind was in turmoil as she waited for the test results.\n(她等待檢查結果時，心裡一團亂。)"],["twilight","twilight(n.)黃昏、暮色、衰退期\n(無詞性變化)\nat twilight 在黃昏時\ntwilight years 晚年\nThe city lights began to shine at twilight.\n(黃昏時城市燈火開始亮起。)\nThe famous actor spent his twilight years in a small village.\n(那位知名演員在一個小村莊度過晚年。)"],["twinkle","twinkle(n./v.)閃爍、閃耀\n(無詞性變化)\ntwinkle in one's eye 眼中閃爍的光芒\nstars twinkle 星光閃爍\nStars twinkled in the clear night sky above the mountains.\n(群山上方晴朗的夜空中星光閃爍。)\nGrandpa told the joke with a twinkle in his eye.\n(爺爺眼裡閃著光芒說了那個笑話。)"],["unanimous","unanimous(adj.)全體一致的、無異議的\nunanimously(adv.)全體一致地\nunanimity(n.)全體一致\nunanimous decision 一致的決定\nunanimous vote 全票通過\nThe committee reached a unanimous decision to support the plan.\n(委員會一致決定支持這項計畫。)\nThe proposal was passed by a unanimous vote.\n(這項提案以全票通過。)"],["unconditional","unconditional(adj.)無條件的、絕對的\nunconditionally(adv.)無條件地\ncondition(n.)條件\nunconditional love 無條件的愛\nunconditional surrender 無條件投降\nParents usually give their children unconditional love.\n(父母通常給予孩子無條件的愛。)\nJapan's unconditional surrender in 1945 ended World War II.\n(日本在1945年無條件投降，結束了第二次世界大戰。)"],["underestimate","underestimate(v./n.)低估、輕視\nestimate(v./n.)估計\noverestimate(v.)高估\nunderestimate the cost 低估成本\nnever underestimate 永遠別小看\nNever underestimate the power of hard work.\n(永遠不要低估努力的力量。)\nWe underestimated how long it would take to finish the project.\n(我們低估了完成這個專案所需的時間。)"],["underneath","underneath(prep./adv./n./adj.)在……下面、在底下、底部\n(無詞性變化)\nunderneath the surface 在表面之下\nfrom underneath 從底下\nThe cat is hiding underneath the sofa.\n(那隻貓躲在沙發底下。)\nHe seems tough, but underneath he is a very kind person.\n(他看起來很強悍，但內心其實是個非常善良的人。)"],["underpass","underpass(n.)地下道\noverpass(n.)天橋、高架道路\npedestrian underpass 行人地下道\nthrough the underpass 穿過地下道\nUse the underpass to cross the busy road safely.\n(利用地下道安全地穿越繁忙的馬路。)\nThe underpass was flooded after the heavy rain.\n(大雨過後，地下道淹水了。)"],["underway","underway(adv.)在進行中、已開始\n(無詞性變化)\nbe well underway 進展順利、已在進行\nget underway 開始\nPreparations for the school anniversary are already well underway.\n(校慶的籌備工作已經順利進行中。)\nThe meeting got underway at exactly nine o'clock.\n(會議在九點整準時開始。)"],["unification","unification(n.)統一、聯合\nunify(v.)統一\nunified(adj.)統一的\nnational unification 國家統一\nGerman unification 德國統一\nGerman unification took place in 1990 after the fall of the Berlin Wall.\n(德國在柏林圍牆倒塌後於1990年統一。)\nQin Shi Huang is known for the unification of China in 221 BC.\n(秦始皇以在西元前221年統一中國聞名。)"],["unify","unify(v.)統一、使一致\nunification(n.)統一\nunified(adj.)統一的\nunify the country 統一國家\nunify efforts 整合力量\nThe coach tried to unify the team after their painful loss.\n(在慘痛落敗後，教練試圖讓全隊團結一致。)\nThe company wants to unify all its services into one app.\n(這家公司想把所有服務整合到同一個應用程式中。)"],["unveil","unveil(v.)揭幕、揭露、首次公開\nveil(n./v.)面紗、遮掩\nunveil a statue 為雕像揭幕\nunveil a plan 公布計畫\nThe mayor unveiled a statue of the famous poet in the park.\n(市長在公園為那位知名詩人的雕像揭幕。)\nThe company will unveil its latest smartphone next week.\n(這家公司下週將發表最新款智慧型手機。)"],["upright","upright(adv./adj./n.)直立地、筆直的、正直的、豎立物\n(無詞性變化)\nsit upright 坐直\nupright citizen 正直的公民\nPlease keep your seat in the upright position during takeoff.\n(起飛時請將椅背豎直。)\nHe was known as an honest and upright judge.\n(他以誠實正直的法官而聞名。)"],["uprising","uprising(n.)起義、暴動\nrise(v./n.)上升、起義\narmed uprising 武裝起義\npopular uprising 民眾起義\nThe uprising was quickly put down by the government.\n(這場起義很快就被政府鎮壓了。)\nThe history teacher explained the causes of the peasant uprising.\n(歷史老師解釋了那場農民起義的原因。)"],["upward","upward(adj.)向上的、上升的\nupwards(adv.)向上地\ndownward(adj.)向下的\nupward trend 上升趨勢\nupward movement 向上移動\nThere has been an upward trend in housing prices over the past ten years.\n(過去十年來房價呈上升趨勢。)\nThe hot-air balloon began its slow upward journey into the morning sky.\n(熱氣球開始緩緩向上升入晨空。)"],["upward/upwards","upward(adv.)向上、往上\nupwards(adv.)向上(同 upward)\nlook upward 抬頭往上看\nupwards of 超過、多於\nThe children looked upward to watch the fireworks.\n(孩子們抬頭往上看煙火。)\nUpwards of a thousand people attended the concert in the park.\n(超過一千人參加了公園裡的音樂會。)"],["urgency","urgency(n.)緊急、迫切\nurgent(adj.)緊急的\nurgently(adv.)緊急地\nsense of urgency 緊迫感\na matter of urgency 緊急事件\nThere is a growing sense of urgency about climate change.\n(人們對氣候變遷的緊迫感與日俱增。)\nThe problem should be dealt with as a matter of urgency.\n(這個問題應作為緊急事項立即處理。)"],["usher","usher(v./n.)引領、迎來、招待員、帶位員\n(無詞性變化)\nusher in 迎來、開創\nusher someone to 引導某人到\nThe waiter ushered us to a table near the window.\n(服務生帶我們到靠窗的座位。)\nThe invention of the smartphone ushered in a new era of communication.\n(智慧型手機的發明開創了通訊的新時代。)"],["utensil","utensil(n.)器具、用具\n(無詞性變化)\nkitchen utensils 廚房用具\neating utensils 餐具\nBringing your own eating utensils helps reduce plastic waste.\n(自備餐具有助於減少塑膠垃圾。)\nThe store sells all kinds of kitchen utensils, from knives to spatulas.\n(這家店販售各式廚房用具，從刀子到鍋鏟都有。)"],["utter","utter(adj./v.)完全的、徹底的、說出、發出(聲音)\nutterly(adv.)完全地\nutterance(n.)說出的話、發言\nutter a word 說一句話\nutter nonsense 一派胡言\nShe left the room without uttering a single word.\n(她一句話也沒說就離開了房間。)\nWhat he said about the test being canceled was utter nonsense.\n(他說考試取消的事根本是一派胡言。)"],["vaccine","vaccine(n.)疫苗\nvaccinate(v.)接種疫苗\nvaccination(n.)疫苗接種\nflu vaccine 流感疫苗\ndevelop a vaccine 研發疫苗\nScientists worked hard to develop a vaccine against the new virus.\n(科學家們努力研發對抗新病毒的疫苗。)\nElderly people are encouraged to get the flu vaccine every year.\n(長者被鼓勵每年接種流感疫苗。)"],["vanilla","vanilla(n.)香草\n(無詞性變化)\nvanilla ice cream 香草冰淇淋\nvanilla extract 香草精\nWould you like chocolate or vanilla ice cream?\n(你想要巧克力還是香草冰淇淋？)\nAdd a teaspoon of vanilla extract to the cake mixture.\n(在蛋糕麵糊中加入一茶匙香草精。)"],["vanity","vanity(n.)虛榮心、自負、空虛\nvain(adj.)虛榮的、徒勞的\nout of vanity 出於虛榮\nvanity fair 名利場\nShe bought the expensive bag out of vanity, not need.\n(她買那個昂貴的包包是出於虛榮，而非需要。)\nHis vanity made him unable to admit his mistakes.\n(他的自負使他無法承認自己的錯誤。)"],["vapor","vapor(n.)蒸氣、霧氣\nvaporize(v.)使蒸發\nevaporate(v.)蒸發\nwater vapor 水蒸氣\nvapor trail 飛機凝結尾\nClouds are formed when water vapor cools in the air.\n(水蒸氣在空氣中冷卻時便會形成雲。)\nWe could see the vapor trail left by the plane in the blue sky.\n(我們能看到飛機在藍天中留下的凝結尾。)"],["veil","veil(n./v.)面紗、遮蔽物、掩飾\nunveil(v.)揭幕、揭露\nveiled(adj.)蒙面紗的、隱約的\nwedding veil 新娘頭紗\na veil of mist 一層薄霧\nThe bride wore a long white veil at the wedding.\n(新娘在婚禮上戴著一條白色長頭紗。)\nThe mountain was hidden behind a veil of mist in the early morning.\n(清晨時，那座山隱藏在一層薄霧之後。)"],["velvet","velvet(n./adj.)天鵝絨、絲絨、柔軟光滑的\nvelvety(adj.)天鵝絨般的、柔滑的\nvelvet dress 絲絨洋裝\nred velvet cake 紅絲絨蛋糕\nShe wore an elegant black velvet dress to the concert.\n(她穿著一件優雅的黑色絲絨洋裝去聽音樂會。)\nThe red velvet curtains in the old theater were replaced last year.\n(老劇院裡的紅色天鵝絨布幕去年換新了。)"],["versatile","versatile(adj.)多才多藝的、多用途的\nversatility(n.)多才多藝、多功能\nversatile actor 戲路寬廣的演員\nversatile tool 多功能工具\nHe is a versatile actor who can play both comedy and drama.\n(他是位戲路寬廣的演員，喜劇和劇情片都能演。)\nEggs are a versatile ingredient that can be cooked in many ways.\n(蛋是一種用途廣泛的食材，可用多種方式烹調。)"],["veterinarian/vet","veterinarian(n.)獸醫\nvet(n.)獸醫(口語)\nveterinary(adj.)獸醫的\ntake a pet to the vet 帶寵物看獸醫\nveterinary clinic 動物醫院\nThe veterinarian gave our dog a full check-up and some vaccines.\n(獸醫幫我們的狗做了全身檢查並施打疫苗。)\nMy cat hasn't been eating well, so I'm taking her to the vet tomorrow.\n(我的貓最近食慾不好，所以我明天要帶牠去看獸醫。)"],["veto","veto(n./v.)否決、否決權\n(無詞性變化)\nveto power 否決權\nveto a bill 否決法案\nThe president used his veto to block the new tax law.\n(總統動用否決權阻擋了新稅法。)\nMy parents vetoed my plan to travel alone during summer vacation.\n(我爸媽否決了我暑假獨自旅行的計畫。)"],["vibrate","vibrate(v.)震動、振動\nvibration(n.)震動\nvibrant(adj.)充滿活力的、鮮豔的\nphone vibrates 手機震動\nvibrate with 因……而震動\nPlease set your phone to vibrate during the performance.\n(表演期間請將手機設為震動模式。)\nThe windows vibrated as the heavy trucks passed by.\n(重型卡車駛過時，窗戶隨之震動。)"],["vibration","vibration(n.)震動、振動、感受\nvibrate(v.)震動\nfeel the vibration 感受到震動\nsound vibration 聲波振動\nWe could feel the vibration of the earthquake even on the tenth floor.\n(即使在十樓，我們也能感受到地震的震動。)\nSound is created by the vibration of air.\n(聲音是由空氣振動產生的。)"],["vice","vice(n.)惡行、缺點、罪惡\nvicious(adj.)惡毒的、兇猛的\nvirtue and vice 美德與惡行\nvice president 副總統、副總裁\nLaziness is his greatest vice.\n(懶惰是他最大的缺點。)\nThe story teaches children the difference between virtue and vice.\n(這個故事教導孩子分辨美德與惡行。)"],["victor","victor(n.)勝利者、征服者\nvictory(n.)勝利\nvictorious(adj.)勝利的\nemerge as the victor 成為勝利者\nto the victor go the spoils 勝者為王\nAfter a long and difficult match, she emerged as the victor.\n(經過一場漫長艱難的比賽，她成為了勝利者。)\nHistory is often written by the victors.\n(歷史往往是由勝利者書寫的。)"],["vigor","vigor(n.)活力、精力、氣勢\nvigorous(adj.)精力充沛的、強而有力的\nvigorously(adv.)有力地\nwith vigor 精力充沛地\nrenewed vigor 重新振作\nThe team started the second half with renewed vigor.\n(全隊以重新振作的士氣展開下半場比賽。)\nEven at eighty, my grandfather still works in the garden with great vigor.\n(即使已經八十歲，我爺爺仍精力充沛地在花園裡工作。)"],["vigorous","vigorous(adj.)精力充沛的、強而有力的、激烈的\nvigor(n.)活力\nvigorously(adv.)有力地\nvigorous exercise 劇烈運動\nvigorous debate 激烈的辯論\nDoctors recommend at least twenty minutes of vigorous exercise three times a week.\n(醫生建議每週至少做三次、每次二十分鐘的劇烈運動。)\nThe new policy led to a vigorous debate in the legislature.\n(新政策在立法院引發激烈的辯論。)"],["villa","villa(n.)別墅\n(無詞性變化)\nholiday villa 度假別墅\nluxury villa 豪華別墅\nThe family rented a villa by the sea for the summer vacation.\n(那家人在暑假時租了一間海邊的別墅。)\nThe wealthy businessman owns a luxury villa in the mountains.\n(那位富商在山上擁有一棟豪華別墅。)"],["villain","villain(n.)壞人、惡棍、反派角色\nvillainous(adj.)邪惡的\nplay the villain 飾演反派\nthe villain of the piece 罪魁禍首\nThe actor is famous for playing villains in action movies.\n(那位演員以在動作片中飾演反派而聞名。)\nIn the end, the hero defeated the villain and saved the city.\n(最後，英雄打敗了壞人，拯救了城市。)"],["vine","vine(n.)藤蔓、葡萄藤\nvineyard(n.)葡萄園\ngrape vine 葡萄藤\nclimbing vine 攀爬藤蔓\nGreen vines covered the walls of the old house.\n(綠色藤蔓爬滿了那棟老房子的牆。)\nThe farmer checks the grape vines every morning.\n(農夫每天早上都檢查葡萄藤。)"],["vineyard","vineyard(n.)葡萄園\nvine(n.)藤蔓、葡萄藤\nvisit a vineyard 參觀葡萄園\nfamily-owned vineyard 家族經營的葡萄園\nWe visited a vineyard in Changhua and picked fresh grapes.\n(我們參觀了彰化的一座葡萄園，還採了新鮮葡萄。)\nThe family has owned this vineyard for over a hundred years.\n(這個家族擁有這座葡萄園已超過一百年。)"],["violinist","violinist(n.)小提琴家、小提琴手\nviolin(n.)小提琴\ntalented violinist 有天分的小提琴家\nsolo violinist 小提琴獨奏家\nThe young violinist won first prize in the international competition.\n(那位年輕小提琴家在國際比賽中奪得首獎。)\nShe practices for hours every day because she wants to be a professional violinist.\n(她每天練習好幾個小時，因為她想成為職業小提琴家。)"],["virgin","virgin(n./adj.)處女、原始的、未開發的、未使用過的\nvirginity(n.)童貞\nvirgin forest 原始森林\nextra virgin olive oil 特級初榨橄欖油\nThe mountain is covered by virgin forest that has never been cut down.\n(這座山覆蓋著從未被砍伐過的原始森林。)\nExtra virgin olive oil is often used in salads.\n(特級初榨橄欖油常用於沙拉中。)"],["vitality","vitality(n.)活力、生命力\nvital(adj.)極重要的、生命的\nfull of vitality 充滿活力\neconomic vitality 經濟活力\nThe children's laughter filled the old house with vitality.\n(孩子們的笑聲讓老房子充滿了活力。)\nSmall businesses are important to the economic vitality of a city.\n(小型企業對城市的經濟活力很重要。)"],["vocation","vocation(n.)職業、天職、使命感\nvocational(adj.)職業的\nsense of vocation 使命感\nfind one's vocation 找到天職\nShe felt that teaching was her true vocation.\n(她覺得教書是她真正的天職。)\nDoctors need a strong sense of vocation to work such long hours.\n(醫生需要強烈的使命感才能長時間工作。)"],["vocational","vocational(adj.)職業的、職業訓練的\nvocation(n.)職業、天職\nvocational school 職業學校、技職學校\nvocational training 職業訓練\nHe chose to attend a vocational school to learn auto repair.\n(他選擇就讀技職學校學習汽車修護。)\nThe government offers free vocational training for people who lose their jobs.\n(政府為失業者提供免費的職業訓練。)"],["vowel","vowel(n.)母音\nconsonant(n.)子音\nvowel sound 母音\nshort vowel 短母音\nThe English alphabet has five vowels: a, e, i, o, and u.\n(英文字母中有五個母音：a、e、i、o、u。)\nPay attention to the short vowel sounds when you read these words.\n(念這些單字時請注意短母音的發音。)"],["wag","wag(v./n.)搖擺、搖動(尾巴)\n(無詞性變化)\nwag its tail 搖尾巴\nwag a finger 搖手指(表示責備)\nThe dog wagged its tail happily when its owner came home.\n(主人回家時，狗開心地搖著尾巴。)\nThe teacher wagged her finger at the students who were talking in class.\n(老師對著上課講話的學生搖手指表示責備。)"],["walnut","walnut(n.)核桃、胡桃木\n(無詞性變化)\nwalnut tree 核桃樹\nwalnut furniture 胡桃木家具\nWalnuts are rich in healthy fats that are good for the brain.\n(核桃富含有益大腦的健康脂肪。)\nThe antique table is made of solid walnut.\n(這張古董桌是用實心胡桃木做的。)"],["ward","ward(n./v.)病房、行政區、受監護人、避開\nwarden(n.)看守人、典獄長\nhospital ward 醫院病房\nward off 擋開、防止\nThe nurse checks on the patients in the ward every two hours.\n(護理師每兩個小時巡視一次病房裡的病人。)\nSome people believe that garlic can ward off evil spirits.\n(有些人相信大蒜可以驅邪。)"],["wardrobe","wardrobe(n.)衣櫥、全部服裝、戲服\n(無詞性變化)\nbuilt-in wardrobe 嵌入式衣櫥\nsummer wardrobe 夏季服裝\nShe hung all her dresses neatly in the wardrobe.\n(她把所有洋裝整齊地掛在衣櫥裡。)\nIt's time to update my wardrobe for the new season.\n(該為新季節添購新衣服了。)"],["warrant","warrant(n.)令狀、搜索票、正當理由\nwarranty(n.)保固、保證書\nsearch warrant 搜索票\narrest warrant 逮捕令\nThe police obtained a search warrant before entering the house.\n(警方在進入那棟房子之前先取得了搜索票。)\nThere is no warrant for such rude behavior.\n(這種無禮的行為毫無正當理由。)"],["warranty","warranty(n.)保固、保證書\nwarrant(n.)令狀、正當理由\nunder warranty 在保固期內\none-year warranty 一年保固\nMy laptop is still under warranty, so the repair is free.\n(我的筆電還在保固期內，所以維修是免費的。)\nThe washing machine comes with a two-year warranty.\n(這台洗衣機附有兩年保固。)"],["waterproof","waterproof(adj./v.)防水的、使防水\nwater(n./v.)水、澆水\nwaterproof jacket 防水外套\nwaterproof watch 防水手錶\nBring a waterproof jacket in case it rains on the mountain.\n(帶件防水外套，以防山上下雨。)\nThis watch is waterproof up to fifty meters.\n(這支手錶可防水達五十公尺。)"],["weary","weary(adj./v.)疲倦的、厭倦的、使疲倦\nweariness(n.)疲倦、厭倦\nwearily(adv.)疲倦地\nweary of 厭倦\nweary traveler 疲憊的旅人\nThe weary travelers finally arrived at the hotel late at night.\n(疲憊的旅客們終於在深夜抵達飯店。)\nPeople are growing weary of the endless political arguments.\n(人們越來越厭倦無止盡的政治爭論。)"],["wharf","wharf(n./v.)碼頭、停靠碼頭\n(無詞性變化)\nFisherman's Wharf 漁人碼頭\nalong the wharf 沿著碼頭\nWe watched the sunset at Tamsui Fisherman's Wharf.\n(我們在淡水漁人碼頭看夕陽。)\nThe ship was unloaded at the wharf early in the morning.\n(那艘船一大早就在碼頭卸貨。)"],["whiskey/whisky","whiskey(n.)威士忌\nwhisky(n.)威士忌(英式拼法)\nScotch whisky 蘇格蘭威士忌\na glass of whiskey 一杯威士忌\nTaiwanese whisky has won several international awards in recent years.\n(臺灣威士忌近年來贏得了好幾項國際大獎。)\nHe ordered a glass of whiskey with ice at the bar.\n(他在酒吧點了一杯加冰塊的威士忌。)"],["wholesale","wholesale(adj./adv./n./v.)批發的、大規模的、以批發方式、批發\nwholesaler(n.)批發商\nretail(n./v.)零售\nwholesale price 批發價\nwholesale market 批發市場\nRestaurants usually buy vegetables at wholesale prices.\n(餐廳通常以批發價購買蔬菜。)\nThe fruit is sold wholesale to supermarkets across the country.\n(這些水果以批發方式銷售給全國的超市。)"],["wholesome","wholesome(adj.)有益健康的、有益身心的\nwholesomeness(n.)有益健康\nwholesome food 健康的食物\nwholesome entertainment 有益身心的娛樂\nMy grandmother always cooks simple but wholesome meals for us.\n(我奶奶總是為我們準備簡單卻健康的餐點。)\nThe TV channel aims to provide wholesome entertainment for families.\n(這個電視頻道致力於提供有益身心的闔家娛樂。)"],["widow/widower","widow(n.)寡婦\nwidower(n.)鰥夫\nwidowed(adj.)喪偶的\nbecome a widow 守寡\nelderly widower 年長的鰥夫\nShe became a widow at the age of fifty and raised her three children alone.\n(她五十歲時守寡，獨自撫養三個孩子。)\nThe elderly widower lives with his daughter's family.\n(那位年長的鰥夫和女兒一家同住。)"],["withhold","withhold(v.)保留、扣留、拒絕給予\nwithholding(n.)扣繳、扣留\nwithhold information 隱瞞資訊\nwithhold payment 暫緩付款\nThe police decided to withhold the victim's name from the public.\n(警方決定不對外公布被害者的姓名。)\nThe company withheld payment until the work was finished properly.\n(公司在工作確實完成前暫緩付款。)"],["woe","woe(n.)悲哀、苦惱、災難\nwoeful(adj.)悲哀的、糟糕的\ntale of woe 悲慘的遭遇\nfinancial woes 財務困境\nHe told me a long tale of woe about losing his wallet and phone.\n(他向我訴說了一段弄丟錢包和手機的悲慘遭遇。)\nThe airline's financial woes forced it to cancel many flights.\n(那家航空公司的財務困境迫使它取消了許多航班。)"],["woodpecker","woodpecker(n.)啄木鳥\n(無詞性變化)\nwoodpecker pecks 啄木鳥啄木\ngreen woodpecker 綠啄木鳥\nWe heard a woodpecker tapping on a tree in the forest.\n(我們在森林裡聽到一隻啄木鳥在啄樹。)\nWoodpeckers use their strong beaks to find insects inside trees.\n(啄木鳥用強壯的喙找出樹裡面的昆蟲。)"],["workforce","workforce(n.)勞動力、全體員工\n(無詞性變化)\nskilled workforce 技術勞動力\nenter the workforce 進入職場\nMany young people enter the workforce right after graduating from college.\n(許多年輕人大學一畢業就進入職場。)\nThe company plans to reduce its workforce by ten percent.\n(這家公司計畫裁減百分之十的員工。)"],["wrestle","wrestle(v./n.)摔角、扭打、努力解決\nwrestler(n.)摔角選手\nwrestling(n.)摔角運動\nwrestle with 努力解決、與……搏鬥\nwrestle someone to the ground 把某人摔倒在地\nThe police officer wrestled the thief to the ground.\n(警察把小偷摔倒在地上。)\nShe has been wrestling with the difficult math problem for an hour.\n(她已經為這道難解的數學題苦思了一個小時。)"],["wrinkle","wrinkle(n./v.)皺紋、皺褶、使起皺\nwrinkled(adj.)有皺紋的、起皺的\nwrinkle-free 免燙的、無皺的\nfine wrinkles 細紋\nMy grandmother has many wrinkles, but her smile is still beautiful.\n(我奶奶有很多皺紋，但她的笑容依然美麗。)\nHang your shirt up so it won't wrinkle.\n(把襯衫掛起來，才不會起皺。)"],["yearn","yearn(v.)渴望、思念\nyearning(n.)渴望、思慕\nyearn for 渴望\nyearn to 渴望做\nMany people working overseas yearn for home during the holidays.\n(許多在海外工作的人在節日期間特別思念家鄉。)\nShe has always yearned to travel around the world.\n(她一直渴望環遊世界。)"],["yoga","yoga(n.)瑜伽\n(無詞性變化)\npractice yoga 練瑜伽\nyoga class 瑜伽課\nMy mother practices yoga every morning to stay healthy and relaxed.\n(我媽媽每天早上練瑜伽，以保持健康和放鬆。)\nShe signed up for a yoga class at the community center.\n(她報名了社區活動中心的瑜伽課。)"],["yogurt","yogurt(n.)優格、優酪乳\n(無詞性變化)\nplain yogurt 原味優格\nfrozen yogurt 霜凍優格\nI usually eat plain yogurt with fresh fruit for breakfast.\n(我早餐通常吃原味優格配新鮮水果。)\nYogurt contains good bacteria that are helpful for digestion.\n(優格含有對消化有幫助的好菌。)"],["zoom","zoom(v./n.)急速移動、(鏡頭)拉近或拉遠、急升\n(無詞性變化)\nzoom in 拉近鏡頭、放大\nzoom past 呼嘯而過\nYou can zoom in on the map to see the street names more clearly.\n(你可以把地圖放大，看清楚街道名稱。)\nA sports car zoomed past us on the highway.\n(一輛跑車在高速公路上從我們旁邊呼嘯而過。)"]]};
